-83e644ea","subject":"Consortium FOI BP v Buckler","name":"2026-04-13_consortium-foi_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-04-13","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-04-13_consortium-foi_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-foi-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler","email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler","email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-04-13_consortium-foi_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: _FOI email address <FOI@landregistry.gov.uk>\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 09:57:33 +0000\nSubject: Freedom of Information Request F260213\nMessage-ID: <CWLP265MB4332540EF8C172231F4C01C9AE242@CWLP265MB4332.GBRP265.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nDear Requester Esq,\n\nPlease find attached our response to your Freedom of Information request.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\n[logo]\nKat Wignall\nEO Disclosure Officer\nInformation Rights Team\nData and Register Integrity Group\nEmail- foi@landregistry.gov.uk<mailto:foi@landregistry.gov.uk> / dataprotection@landregistry.gov.uk<mailto:dataprotection@landregistry.gov.uk>\n\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n\n\n"},{"id":"wb-4b91daf7","subject":"Consortium land registry BP v Buckler","name":"2026-04-13_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-04-13","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-04-13_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-land-registry-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-04-13_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 15:20:33 -0300\nSubject: Re: Title WA231076 / Ty Mawr Farm – Allegation of Fraud, Mistake and Request for Escalation to Legal\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V4K9bzyCoSdX_Ukm_DQKMSdUeGLotWbH4CkHSKgAmJ0bg@mail.gmail.com>\n\nMs Griffiths,\n\nThank you for your letter of 23 March 2026 (ref: N610CGV) regarding title \nnumber WA231076.\n\nI acknowledge your explanation of HM Land Registry’s role and your \nconfirmation of the first registrations in favour of BP Properties Limited \nin 1982 and 1983. However, your response only reviews the internal \nregistration trail and does not engage with the specific issues I raised, \nnamely:\n\n- Fraud and/or deliberate concealment in the transactions and litigation \nthat underpinned BP’s title; and  \n\n- A fundamental misidentification of my late grandmother, Mrs Mary \nWilliams, which directly affected the outcome of those proceedings and the \nsubsequent entries on the register.\n\nFor clarity:\n\n1. **Identity and mislabelling**\n\n   My grandmother was **Mrs Mary Williams** throughout her life. Her death \nrecord is in the name **Mary Williams**, not Buckler. Contemporary press \ncoverage (for example, a 1978 article concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr \nFarm) also refers to her as **Mrs Williams** when she publicly contested \nBP’s claim to the property.\n\n   In contrast, the Court of Appeal decision in *BP Properties Ltd v \nBuckler* and subsequent commentary present her as “**Mrs Buckler**” and \ntreat her as a “squatter” or licensee. That label does not match her actual \nlegal identity and is inconsistent with historic documentation. I allege \nthat this misnaming was not a harmless error but formed part of a process \nof stripping her of her true Williams identity and historic land claim.\n\n2. **Licence and suppression/misuse of evidence**\n\n   BP Pension Trust wrote to my grandmother in the 1970s purporting to \noffer her a licence to remain at Ty Mawr Farm. She replied, in substance, \nthat: “It is my land. It is not your permission to give.” That response was \nmade in her name as **Mrs Williams**, explicitly asserting a prior and \nsuperior claim.\n\n   Yet the later litigation proceeded on the basis that she “did not \nreject” the licence and treated her as being in permissive occupation, a \ncharacterisation which appears to have been reached without the full and \nfair deployment of her response, and after she had been re‑described as \n“Mrs Buckler”. I allege that this amounts to **deliberate concealment \nand/or misrepresentation** of critical facts.\n\n3. **Allegation of fraud and mistake; limitation**\n\n   In light of the above, I am not merely alleging a technical registration \nerror in 1982/83. I am alleging that:\n\n   - The title now registered under WA231076 is founded on **transactions \nand litigation tainted by fraud and deliberate concealment**; and  \n   - The register is therefore affected by a **mistake** for the purposes \nof the Land Registration Act 2002 and HM Land Registry Practice Guide 39 \n(rectification and indemnity).\n\n   I have only recently been able to piece together the necessary evidence \n(including vital records and historic press reports) to understand the \nextent of that fraud and misidentification. Under section 32 of the \nLimitation Act 1980, where fraud or deliberate concealment is involved, any \nlimitation period runs from **discovery** of the fraud, not its original \noccurrence.\n\n4. **Request for escalation and preservation of records**\n\n   In view of the seriousness of these allegations, I formally request that:\n\n   - My case be escalated to HM Land Registry’s **Legal Services** / \nappropriate senior officer for consideration of **rectification and/or \nindemnity** under Schedule 4 of the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice \nGuide 39.  \n   - HM Land Registry treats this as an allegation of **fraud and \ndeliberate concealment** affecting the foundation of title WA231076 and \nrelated closed titles (including WA240304).  \n   - All files and documents held by HMLR relating to the first \nregistrations and subsequent dealings with Ty Mawr Farm / Great House Farm \n/ land on the north side of Leckwith Road, Llandough, are **preserved in \nfull** and not destroyed or weeded, pending further investigation and \npotential proceedings.  \n\nI am in the process of taking independent legal advice with a view to:\n\n- Applying for **rectification and/or indemnity**; and  \n- Considering steps to challenge or set aside earlier orders and judgments \nobtained on the basis of the misidentification and suppression outlined \nabove.\n\nIn the meantime, please confirm:\n\n1. That this correspondence has been referred to your Legal Services team \n(or the appropriate senior legal officer), and  \n2. The name and contact details of the person who will have conduct of this \nmatter on behalf of HM Land Registry.\n\nI will shortly provide a bundle of supporting documents (death certificate, \ncontemporaneous press, and other materials) evidencing my grandmother’s \ntrue identity as Mrs Mary Williams and the discrepancy with the “Mrs \nBuckler” narrative relied upon in the public record.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSion Buckler  \n[Your postal address, if you wish]  \n[Your email]  \n[Your phone number]\n\n\nThank you for your letter of 23 March 2026 regarding the historic \nregistration of Ty Mawr Farm, title WA231076. I note your explanation of HM \nLand Registry’s administrative role and that you say there is no evidence \nof a “mistake” on the basis of the file you have reviewed.\n\nMy family’s concern, however, is that the first registration was procured \nby misrepresentation and identity fraud by BP rather than by a simple \nclerical error. The occupier was my grandmother, Mrs Williams, of our \nfamily that had occupied the property and land since at least 1667, not the \nfictitious “Mrs Buckler” BP fabricated in 1974 for their unilateral \nlicence, which was the basis of the BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) \nlandmark legal case. \n\nBP also appear to have failed to disclose the long‑running ownership \ndispute. In a 1978 surpessed newspaper article, my nan stated publicly her \nassertion of ownership and the fact that BP could not prove ownership and \nnever obtained a court ruling that it was the owner, only possession \norders. \n\nHow was BP able to register our land in their names? Didn't you enquire if \nthere was any dispute of the land. It was in court records from 1974. Twice \nthat year they obstructed my nan making her case she owned the land. \nFirstly that year they adjourned without ruling. Then the license letters, \nusing identity fraud, quashed the second hearing. They were opportunities \ntrying to dispossessed a widowed, disabled woman. It's evident from my \ninvestigation. And I am a former Sergeant, Royal Signals life member and \nintelligence counter officer. If I am not communicating the seriousness of \nthis matter please do tell me. The councillor of Llandough and the MP for \nthe Vale of Glamorgan are yet to take a definitive position on this. \nWhatever you lot are up to, is it no wonder we Welsh Nationals wish to \ndecolonise from the British State. It appears to be totally rogue. \n\nHad HM Land Registry recorded or investigated the existence of this \ndispute, BP’s inability to prove ownership, and the archaeological and \nhistoric significance of the site, or saught a copy of her death certiciate \nto see the name of the woman and license and narrative were completly \ndifferent, we believe BP would not have been able to achieve first \nregistration on the basis presented. Instead, the use of the wrong name \n(“Mrs Buckler” instead of my married grandmother, Mrs Williams) and the \nnon‑disclosure of the dispute and family claim enabled dispossession \nthrough what we say was identity fraud, which my grandmother was unable to \ncontest as she also conveniently died in the same year as registration. \n\nI would also add, I wish to append to this land paracell, our maintained \npostion of dispute of this land. We never sureenderdd. We were removed by \n30 police and information suppressed. Potentially murdered. Appeal \ndismissed, ECHR request blocked. And my family being paralysed and too \npetrified into silence, is not the same as surrender from sound mind and \nagency. This is a terrorist hostage situation and it must be upended. \n\nFurther background on this is set out at bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz. which is a \ndraft screenplay for Netflix. So I want to get the facts correct before \nthis documentary is made to expose this blantent scandal. My family want \nnarrative justice as possibly the rightful, dispossed via fraud, executors \nof the Manor of Llandough. \n\nI am aware that HM Land Registry operates a statutory indemnity and redress \nscheme under the Land Registration Act 2002, and that substantial payments \n(including around £8 million in a single year) have been made where people \nsuffer loss because of mistakes or fraud in the register. I therefore wish \nto explore, formally, whether our family’s loss of Ty Mawr Farm, in \ncircumstances where BP’s misrepresentations and the suppression of an \nactive dispute were not reflected on the register, can be considered within \nthat indemnity/redress framework.\n\nIn light of the above, I ask HM Land Registry to state clearly whether you \naccept or deny that:\n\nBP was able to obtain first registration of Ty Mawr Farm even though there \nwas no court ruling that BP owned the land and BP had been unable to prove \nownership in proceedings, which were confined to possession.\n\nThe land was registered while there was an active and public dispute over \nownership (including my grandmother’s 1978 public assertion of ownership \nand the BP v Buckler litigation), and while the long‑term occupier, my \ngrandmother, who conveniently died before being able to challenge this, and \nwas therefore unable to challenge the application. Much like my father \nconveniently died after his appeal of the 1987 ruling occurred, his appeal \ndismissed and ECHR request blocked. \n\nFraud and potentially murder, doesn't make legitimately and therfore \ninvaligates authority. I am the only family member willing to speak up \nabout this because the men are all dead now and the women are all too \nterrorised. They are all terrified. My sisters, aunty's and mother. So \nplease cooperate in this matter. \n\nMy grandmothers identity and superior family title and land claim \nassociated with that name, were mis‑described in the material on which you \nrelied up. As BP used  “Mrs Buckler” instead of my married grandmothers \nactual name Mrs Williams.  This misdescription and the concealment of the \ndispute were not detected or queried by HM Land Registry before completing \nfirst registration. \n\nIf these matters are admitted, I consider they amount to negligence and \nmaladministration by HM Land Registry in allowing BP to register our family \nland in its name in those circumstances. If you do not accept that, please \nexplain precisely which of the above points you dispute and on what basis, \nso that I can take appropriate legal advice and pursue an indemnity/redress \nclaim if available.\n\nSeparately from that, please also:\nProvide official copies of the 23 May 1975 and 19 November 1982 \nconveyances, and of the first registration applications and all supporting \ndocuments for WA231076 and WA240304, so I can obtain specialist advice on \nthe extent of any misrepresentation in what was lodged.\n\nConfirm the correct procedure and forms to make a claim under your \nindemnity/redress scheme in a historic case of alleged fraud and \nmisrepresentation in first registration, and whether you consider this \nmatter potentially falls within that scheme, subject to evidence.\n\nI appreciate that you cannot determine the underlying ownership dispute, \nbut it is important that HM Land Registry notes that the Buckler/Williams \nfamily contests the integrity of the original registration of Ty Mawr Farm \non the basis of identity fraud, non‑disclosure of a live dispute, and the \nabsence of any judicial determination that BP owned the land.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\"\n\nHere’s a tightened, professional version that keeps your key points but \nremoves anything they could dismiss as intemperate. I’d send **only this**, \nnot your earlier draft text.\n\n***\n\n**Subject:** Title WA231076 / Ty Mawr Farm – Allegation of Fraud, Mistake \nand Request for Escalation to Legal\n\nDear Ms Griffiths,\n\nThank you for your letter of 23 March 2026 (ref: N610CGV) regarding title \nnumber WA231076.\n\nI acknowledge your explanation of HM Land Registry’s administrative role \nand your confirmation of the first registrations in favour of BP Properties \nLimited in 1982 and 1983. However, your response only reviews the internal \nregistration trail and does not address the specific issues I raised, \nnamely:\n\n- Fraud and/or deliberate concealment in the transactions and litigation \nthat underpinned BP’s title; and  \n- A fundamental misidentification of my late grandmother, **Mrs Mary \nWilliams**, which directly affected the outcome of those proceedings and \nthe subsequent entries on the register.\n\nFor clarity:\n\n### 1. Identity and mislabelling\n\nMy grandmother was **Mrs Mary Williams** throughout her life. Her death \nrecord is in the name **Mary Williams**, not Buckler. Contemporary press \ncoverage (for example, a 1978 article concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr \nFarm) also refers to her as **Mrs Williams** when she publicly contested \nBP’s claim to the property.\n\nIn contrast, the Court of Appeal decision in *BP Properties Ltd v Buckler* \nand subsequent commentary present her as “**Mrs Buckler**” and treat her as \na “squatter” or licensee. That label does not match her actual legal \nidentity and is inconsistent with historic documentation. I allege that \nthis misnaming was not a harmless error but formed part of a process of \nstripping her of her true Williams identity and historic land claim.\n\n### 2. Licence and suppression/misuse of evidence\n\nBP Pension Trust wrote to my grandmother in the 1970s purporting to offer \nher a licence to remain at Ty Mawr Farm. She replied, in substance, that: \n“It is my land. It is not your permission to give.” That response was made \nin her name as **Mrs Williams**, explicitly asserting a prior and superior \nclaim.\n\nYet the later litigation proceeded on the basis that she “did not reject” \nthe licence and treated her as being in permissive occupation, a \ncharacterisation which appears to have been reached without the full and \nfair deployment of her response, and after she had been re‑described as \n“Mrs Buckler”. I allege that this amounts to **deliberate concealment \nand/or misrepresentation** of critical facts.\n\n### 3. Allegation of fraud and mistake; limitation\n\nIn light of the above, I am not merely alleging a technical registration \nerror in 1982/83. I am alleging that:\n\n- The title now registered under WA231076 is founded on **transactions and \nlitigation tainted by fraud and deliberate concealment**; and  \n- The register is therefore affected by a **mistake** for the purposes of \nthe Land Registration Act 2002 and HM Land Registry Practice Guide 39 \n(rectification and indemnity).\n\nI have only recently been able to piece together the necessary evidence \n(including vital records and historic press reports) to understand the \nextent of that fraud and misidentification. Under section 32 of the \nLimitation Act 1980, where fraud or deliberate concealment is involved, any \nlimitation period runs from **discovery** of the fraud, not its original \noccurrence.\n\n### 4. Request for escalation and preservation of records\n\nIn view of the seriousness of these allegations, I formally request that:\n\n- My case be escalated to HM Land Registry’s **Legal Services** / \nappropriate senior officer for consideration of **rectification and/or \nindemnity** under Schedule 4 of the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice \nGuide 39.  \n- HM Land Registry treats this as an allegation of **fraud and deliberate \nconcealment** affecting the foundation of title WA231076 and related closed \ntitles (including WA240304).  \n- All files and documents held by HMLR relating to the first registrations \nand subsequent dealings with Ty Mawr Farm / Great House Farm / land on the \nnorth side of Leckwith Road, Llandough, are **preserved in full** and not \ndestroyed or weeded, pending further investigation and potential \nproceedings.  \n\n### 5. Specific questions and information requested\n\nIn addition, please:\n\n1. **State HM Land Registry’s position** on the following points:  \n\n   - That BP obtained first registration of Ty Mawr Farm even though there \nwas no court ruling that BP owned the land (only possession orders), and \nwhile there was a long‑running ownership dispute involving my grandmother.  \n   - That the land was registered while there was an active and public \ndispute over ownership (including my grandmother’s 1978 public assertion of \nownership and the *BP v Buckler* litigation), and shortly after her death, \nwhen she was no longer able to challenge the application.  \n   - That my grandmother’s identity and superior family land claim were \nmisdescribed in material relied upon (BP using “Mrs Buckler” instead of her \nactual name, Mrs Williams), and that this misdescription and the existence \nof the dispute were not detected or queried before first registration.\n\n   If you do not accept any of these propositions, please explain precisely \nwhich you dispute and on what basis, so that I can take appropriate legal \nadvice.\n\n2. **Provide official copies** of:  \n\n   - The conveyances dated 23 May 1975 and 19 November 1982; and  \n   - The first registration applications and all supporting documents for \nWA231076 and WA240304,\n\n   so that I can obtain specialist advice on the extent of any \nmisrepresentation in what was lodged.\n\n3. **Confirm the correct procedure and forms** to make a claim under the \nindemnity/redress scheme in a historic case of alleged fraud and \nmisrepresentation in first registration, and whether you consider this \nmatter potentially falls within that scheme, subject to evidence.\n\n***\n\nI appreciate that HM Land Registry cannot itself determine the underlying \nownership dispute, but it is important that the register and your records \nreflect that the Buckler/Williams family now formally contests the \nintegrity of the original registration of Ty Mawr Farm on the basis of \n**identity fraud, non‑disclosure of a live dispute, and absence of any \njudicial determination that BP owned the land.**\n\nI am in the process of taking independent legal advice with a view to:\n\n- Applying for **rectification and/or indemnity**; and  \n- Considering steps to challenge or set aside earlier orders and judgments \nobtained on the basis of the misidentification and suppression outlined \nabove.\n\nIn the meantime, please confirm:\n\n1. That this correspondence has been referred to your Legal Services team \n(or the appropriate senior legal officer); and  \n2. The name and contact details of the person who will have conduct of this \nmatter on behalf of HM Land Registry.\n\nI will shortly provide a bundle of supporting documents (death certificate, \ncontemporaneous press, and other materials) evidencing my grandmother’s \ntrue identity as Mrs Mary Williams and the discrepancy with the “Mrs \nBuckler” narrative relied upon in the public record.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSion Buckler  \n[Postal address]  \n[Email]  \n[Phone number]\n\n\nOn Mon, 23 Mar 2026, 05:56 Wales.OfficeMail, <\nWales.Office@landregistry.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from \n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application \n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No \n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you. \n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the \n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to \n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can \n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is \n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete \n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed \n> document by post. \n>\n> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r \n> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais \n> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni \n> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch. \n>\n> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg \n> y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y \n> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho \n> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun \n> at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir \n> EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd \n> rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post. \n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>\n> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda. \n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>\n> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>\n>\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-fcaa0891","subject":"Consortium land registry BP v Buckler","name":"2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-04-19","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-land-registry-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 16:29:29 -0300\nSubject: Subject: Stage Two Complaint – Title WA231076 – Alleged Mistake in the Register\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V6K8e5tfSo=pgq1=iO8q_ssw1dSGaz9p_UgBAoxv+1F7w@mail.gmail.com>\n\n Sir or Madam,\n\nI write to ask that my complaint regarding title number WA231076 (Land on\nthe North Side of Leckwith Road, Llandough) be escalated to **stage two**\nof HM Land Registry’s Complaints Procedure. This email sets out why I\nconsider the stage‑one decision to be incorrect, identifies the mistake I\nsay exists in the register, and explains the decision I seek.\n\n### 1. My core contention\n\nMy core contention is that BP Properties Limited were registered as\nproprietors on the basis of a factual and legal error regarding my\ngrandmother’s status on the land. My grandmother did not occupy under any\ngenuine licence granted to her and did not relinquish any claim. Instead,\nany licence relied on by BP related to a different name/person. As her\nheir, I have succeeded to her claim; I therefore say that registering BP as\nproprietors was a “mistake in the register” for the purposes of the Land\nRegistration Act 2002.\n\n### 2. Identity mismatch and alleged “licence”\n\nYour stage‑one letter records that HM Land Registry relies on the Court of\nAppeal decision in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler  EWCA Civ 2, and treats my\ngrandmother as having occupied under a licence granted by the documentary\ntitle holder, so that her possession was no longer adverse.\n\nHowever, the alleged licence and related correspondence did not use my\ngrandmother’s true legal name. My grandmother was Mrs Williams (supported\nby her birth, marriage and death certificates), not “Mrs Buckler”. The\n“licensee” referred to in BP’s narrative and in the 1987 litigation is\ntherefore not the same legal person as my grandmother. There is, in other\nwords, a fundamental mis‑identification or identity fraud at the heart of\nthe story that HM Land Registry and the Court have relied upon.\n\nIf the licence relied on by BP was addressed to, or granted in respect of,\na different named individual, it cannot properly be said that my\ngrandmother’s occupation was under that licence. In that case her\noccupation remained adverse to BP’s paper title, and any finding that she\nwas a “licensee” rests on a factual premise that is demonstrably wrong.\n\n### 3. Timing – “cart before the horse”\n\nYour letter explains that the applications for first registration of\nWA231076 (and the related title WA240304) were made in 1982–83 and that BP\ndemonstrated a documentary root of title back to 1969/1975 by way of\nconveyances and a 1971 abstract of title.\n\nYou also confirm that the Court of Appeal only gave its decision in BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler in 1987, holding that an offer by BP to let my\ngrandmother remain created a licence and brought her adverse possession to\nan end.\n\nThis highlights a fundamental sequencing problem:\n\n- At the date of first registration (1982–83), whether there was a valid\nlicence capable of defeating my grandmother’s adverse possession was a\nlive, unresolved dispute.\n- BP nevertheless presented themselves as entitled to be registered as\nproprietors and their solicitors certified on form FR1 that there was no\nquestion or doubt affecting the title.\n\n- HM Land Registry, relying on that certification, registered BP before any\ncourt had determined whether my grandmother’s possession had extinguished\nBP’s title.\n- Only in 1987 did the Court of Appeal retrospectively treat the alleged\nlicence as bringing adverse possession to an end, and that decision was\nitself based on the mis‑identification described above.\n\nIn simple terms, the effect of the alleged licence (if any) was judicially\ndetermined **after** first registration, and on the basis of the wrong\nperson being treated as the “licensee”. BP and their solicitors put the\ncart before the horse, and HM Land Registry accepted that position.\n\n### 4. The specific “mistake in the register”\n\nYour stage‑one response concludes that there is “no evidence of a mistake\nin the register” and therefore no power to alter the register and no right\nto indemnity. I say this is incorrect.\n\nThe mistake I allege is as follows:\n\n1. On the true facts, my grandmother’s occupation of the land was adverse\nto BP’s documentary title and was not under any valid licence granted to\nher.\n\n2. Her adverse possession had, or may have, extinguished BP’s title by the\ntime of first registration in 1982–83, meaning BP were not entitled to be\nregistered as proprietors at that time.\n\n3. HM Land Registry nevertheless registered BP as proprietors on the basis\nof:\n   - a licence attributed to the wrong person (identity error/fraud), and\n   - a solicitor’s FR1 certificate stating there was no question or doubt\naffecting title, despite a long‑running dispute and pending litigation.\n\n4. Subsequent reliance on the 1987 Court of Appeal decision does not cure\nthis, because that decision itself proceeded on the mis‑identification of\nmy grandmother and did not and could not retrospectively validate a licence\nthat never related to her.\n\nOn that analysis, the register shows BP as proprietors when, in law, my\ngrandmother’s adverse possession should have extinguished BP’s title and\ngiven rise to a transmissible proprietary interest which I, as her heir,\nnow claim. The register therefore does not accurately reflect the true\nlegal position and contains a mistake capable of rectification.\n\n### 5. Why the stage‑one reasoning is inadequate\n\nIn your stage‑one letter you state that:\n\n- HM Land Registry has an administrative function and cannot “look behind\nor challenge decisions of the Court”. [1]\n- My identity‑fraud claims are “not relevant to the issue of title to the\nland” because they relate to the dispute heard by the Court.\n\n- There is no evidence of negligence or maladministration and no evidence\nof a mistake in the register.\n\nWith respect, this reasoning is incomplete:\n\n- Once HM Land Registry is presented with clear evidence that the person\nnamed as the “licensee” in the litigation and licence documentation is not\nthe same legal person as the occupier (my grandmother), that goes directly\nto whether the Court of Appeal’s factual premise remains reliable and\nwhether the register is accurate.\n\n- Recognising that there is a serious question as to the correctness of the\nregister is not the same as “overturning” the Court of Appeal. HM Land\nRegistry has statutory powers to alter the register where there is a\nmistake, and it can, where appropriate, refer disputes about rectification\nto the tribunal or the courts.\n\n- To simply say that identity‑fraud concerns are “not relevant to title”\nis, I say, an error of law and/or an unreasonable application of policy. It\ndisregards new evidence going to the foundation of BP’s claimed entitlement.\n\n### 6. The decision and outcome I seek\n\nFor stage two, I ask that a Land Registrar (Senior Officer) reconsider the\ncomplaint and:\n\n1. Accept that the combination of:\n   - the identity mismatch (licence/name vs my grandmother’s true legal\nname), and\n   - the timing (registration in 1982–83 before the 1987 decision) gives\nrise to at least a **serious question** as to whether the register is\nmistaken in showing BP/ Companies thereafter, as proprietors.\n\n2. Treat this as evidence of a potential “mistake in the register” for the\npurposes of your alteration powers and Schedule 8, rather than as a mere\ndisagreement with the 1987 judgment.\n\n3. Either:\n\n   - (a) commence the process of rectification, recognising that my\ngrandmother’s adverse possession may have extinguished BP’s title and that\nI, as her heir, now have a claim to be registered, or\n\n   - (b) formally refer the dispute over the correctness of the register to\nthe appropriate tribunal/court, making clear that HM Land Registry\nrecognises that the identity‑fraud evidence raises a real issue about\nwhether the register is accurate.\n\n4. Confirm that, if it is ultimately determined that the register is\nmistaken and cannot be rectified without prejudice to third parties, HM\nLand Registry will treat me as having a potential claim for indemnity under\nSchedule 8.\n\nPlease also confirm any further documents you require (for example, copies\nof the licence, the BP v Buckler pleadings/judgment, and my grandmother’s\ncertificates) so that the stage‑two review can consider the identity\nevidence in full.\n\nFraud unravels all. The limitation act also had a clause for fraud.\nFurthermore any limitation begins from discovery of fraud not occurrence of\nit.\n\nThe convenient and timely death of my nan after her two obstructed attempts\nto make her case in 1974, followed by my father's convenient and timely\ndeath after his appeal of the 1987 case was dismissed and his ECHR\nobstructed, along with our forceful removal by 30 police and bailiffs in\n1988. And the press reporting us as squatters on our ancestral birthland\nsince 1667, did unlawfully dispossess and disposition us, but it doesn't\nchange the facts.\n\nI see this case as instrumental in Wales' decolonisation. Whereby us\nindigneous Welsh Nationals on our ancestral birthland are victim to a\ncrime. And I am the only one willing to speak up and out as my family of\nmostly women, are all too traumatised by this crime.\n\nIt's evident illicit profits and gains. Identity fraud. And negligence and\nincompetence. I absolutely see the Brit-ish Establishment that now occupy\nand rule through force, stealth/ secrecy and licence as terrorists and us\nyour hostages. As a direct result of this case.\n\nThis is now a hostage terrorist situation on our lands. Well, my family are\nyour hostages, I'm more of a counter officer soldier. So put it right. I\nwill not stand down.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\nRightful Squire & executor of Manon of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales.\n\n\n\n\nOn Sun, 19 Apr 2026, 07:41 Wales.OfficeMail, <\nWales.Office@landregistry.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\n> document by post.\n>\n> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r\n> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais\n> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni\n> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n>\n> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg\n> y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y\n> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho\n> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun\n> at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir\n> EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd\n> rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>\n> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>\n> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>\n>\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-e724f5d4","subject":"Consortium land registry BP v Buckler","name":"2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.001.txt","date":"2026-04-19","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1_001.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-land-registry-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-04-19_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1_001.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: \"Wales.OfficeMail\" <Wales.Office@landregistry.gov.uk>\nDate: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 10:41:23 +0000\nSubject: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/CT\nMessage-ID: <LO6P265MB7349A266404342B0BD32679CBA2E2@LO6P265MB7349.GBRP265.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nThe document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n\nThe document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed document by post.\n\nYmholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n\nMae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n\n\n\n\n\nDiben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy'n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: \"Marchnad eiddo o'r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy\".\n\nRydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe'ch cynghorir mai chi sy'n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna'i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n\nI weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n\n\n"},{"id":"wb-b25aff28","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-04-29_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-04-29","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-04-29_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-04-29_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 18:16:32 -0300\nSubject: Re: Reply to your email of September 2025\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V4=ZTYCP+Y41xcrM4i_j5dO4ANgJjAY7EgxYx+Q9axzMw@mail.gmail.com>\n\nDear Ms Hollis,\n\nI write further to your letter of 27 April 2026. This correspondence\nconstitutes formal pre-action notice of my intention to pursue legal\nremedies arising from the historic proceedings concerning Great House Farm,\nLlandough.\n\nWhile I note your position regarding judicial independence, I do not accept\nthat the issues raised can be dismissed at an administrative level. My\nrepresentations concern alleged procedural irregularity, misrepresentation,\nnon-disclosure, and structural unfairness which, taken together, raise\nserious questions as to whether the proceedings were properly and fairly\ndetermined.\n\nThese matters warrant proper consideration, or at minimum clear direction\nto an appropriate forum capable of examining them.\n------------------------------\nA. Grounds for Reparations\n\nThe basis upon which reparations are sought includes:\n\n   - Continuous occupation over approximately 318 years (1667–1988), open,\n   peaceful, and without permission (*nec vi, nec clam, nec precario*),\n   establishing de facto ownership;\n   - No voluntary surrender of rights at any stage, with the claim\n   maintained consistently to the present day;\n   - Uncompensated dispossession, including eviction and demolition without\n   settlement;\n   - Coercive enforcement measures, including forced removal, detention,\n   restraining measures, and demolition under duress;\n   - The rendering of a vulnerable family homeless, including a pregnant\n   mother, young children, and a disabled elderly occupant;\n   - Ongoing intergenerational harm, including psychological, social, and\n   economic consequences;\n   - Destruction of an ancestral home of significant age and character\n   (approximately 800 years);\n   - Loss or disappearance of family records and evidential materials\n   relevant to ownership;\n   - Failure to act upon known archaeological and historical significance,\n   resulting in loss of heritage protection;\n   - Resulting public interest harm through the destruction of a site of\n   historical importance.\n\n------------------------------\nB. Grounds to Set Aside or Reopen the 1987 Ruling1. Reliance on a disputed\n“licence by silence”\n\nThe judgment relied upon an inferred licence accepted through silence. This\nis unsafe where:\n\n   - correspondence was addressed to a disputed identity (“Mrs Buckler”);\n   - evidence of active rejection (including 1978) was not before the court.\n\n2. Identity misrepresentation\n\nMary Williams was treated as “Mrs Buckler,” which:\n\n   - did not reflect her asserted identity;\n   - weakened her position by obscuring lineage-based claims;\n   - artificially linked her to the alleged intent of another party.\n\n3. Misplaced reliance on Frederick Buckler’s intent\n\nAny alleged intention:\n\n   - was personal to him and legally distinct;\n   - did not bind Mary Williams;\n   - was extinguished upon his death in 1965;\n   - and was not supported by fulfilment of tenancy obligations.\n\n4. Procedural irregularities (1974)\n\nThere are serious concerns that:\n\n   - an appeal attempt and request for a stay were disrupted;\n   - licence correspondence was timed and/or presented so as to defeat due\n   process;\n   - a key hearing was effectively neutralised before determination.\n\n5. Non-disclosure of material facts\n\nRelevant matters appear not to have been disclosed, including:\n\n   - evidence of public rejection of the opposing claim;\n   - archaeological and historical significance of the site;\n   - the existence of an ongoing dispute in the context of land\n   registration.\n\n6. Inconsistent treatment of corporate identity\n\n   - In 1987, my grandmother’s rebuttal to BP Pension Trust was disregarded\n   on the basis that BP Pension Trust and BP Properties were separate entities;\n   - In subsequent proceedings, the same entities were treated as\n   effectively the same when dismissing an appeal.\n\nThis inconsistency materially affected the outcome and raises concerns as\nto fairness and legal coherence.\n7. Avoidance of substantive title determination\n\nThe case proceeded within a possession framework rather than determining\nunderlying ownership in an appropriate forum, resulting in the absence of a\ndefinitive adjudication on title.\n8. Possible misrepresentation / constructive fraud\n\nConcerns arise that:\n\n   - licence arrangements were asserted under a disputed identity;\n   - the authority of the issuing entity was unclear;\n   - planning and property descriptions may have mischaracterised the\n   nature of the building.\n\n9. New or previously unavailable evidence\n\nThis includes:\n\n   - missing or unavailable title documentation;\n   - evidence relating to arrangements (including that attributed to Daniel\n   Thomas);\n   - family testimony not previously considered;\n   - subsequent archaeological findings supporting the site’s significance.\n\n------------------------------\nC. Core Position\n\nTaken together, the 1987 outcome is arguable as unsafe due to flawed\nassumptions, missing evidence, and procedural unfairness. The resulting\ndispossession, demolition, and long-term harm give rise to a basis for\nreparative consideration.\n------------------------------\nD. Why the Matter Requires Proper Consideration\n\nThis matter should not be dismissed solely on the basis of judicial\nindependence because:\n\n   - The issues raised concern the *integrity of the process*, not simply\n   disagreement with a result;\n   - Allegations of *misrepresentation, non-disclosure, and procedural\n   irregularity* fall outside ordinary appellate disagreement;\n   - There is a *public interest dimension*, including loss of heritage and\n   potential systemic issues;\n   - The passage of time does not extinguish claims where *fraud or\n   material injustice* is alleged;\n   - Clarification is required as to the appropriate forum capable of\n   examining such matters.\n\n------------------------------\nE. Request for Clarification\n\nBefore commencing proceedings, I request clarification of the following:\n\n   1. Whether any formal mechanism exists within government for referring\n   allegations of procedural irregularity or fraud in historic cases for\n   independent review;\n   2. Whether my correspondence has been referred to any oversight or\n   investigatory body;\n   3. Whether the Ministry maintains any position as to the appropriate\n   route for consideration of such evidence outside of direct court\n   proceedings.\n\n------------------------------\n\nPlease treat this letter as a formal pre-action notice. I would be grateful\nfor a substantive response within 14 days.\n\nNothing in this letter should be taken as a waiver of any rights or\nremedies, all of which are expressly reserved.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n\nOn Monday, 27 April 2026, Central Correspondence Team <\nCentralCorrespondenceTeam@justice.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n> Good morning,\n>\n>\n>\n> With apologies for the delay, a reply to your email of September 2025 to\n> Cabinet Office is attached.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Ministry of Justice\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *PLEASE NOTE: the inbox for the account which generated this email is NOT\n> monitored, therefore any incoming emails to the above inbox address will\n> not be acknowledged or receive a response.*\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n> This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the\n> addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not\n> permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies\n> and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure\n> medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone\n> else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in\n> response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender\n> or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry\n> of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content\n> may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not\n> broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-c8f48ed3","subject":"Consortium land registry BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-03_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-03","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-03_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-land-registry-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-03_consortium-land_registry_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Sun, 3 May 2026 13:10:00 -0300\nSubject: Re: Subject: Stage Two Complaint – Title WA231076 – Alleged Mistake in the Register\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V7Dw5ZAU_0J-vby00fTmzRpA1M7j2TODbFjFATYBM1iGQ@mail.gmail.com>\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI write to append further evidence and clarification to my ongoing\ncomplaint regarding the registration of title relating to Great House Farm,\nLlandough (also known as Ty Mawr / Great House).\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nThis submission sets out a series of facts which I can evidence and which,\ntaken together, raise serious concerns of fraud, concealment, and wrongful\nregistration that have materially affected the rights of the Williams\nfamily and their heirs.\n\n1. Unauthorised transfer of title (circa 1965)\nI can evidence that the title to the property was transferred or sold in or\naround 1965 by Frederick Buckler without the knowledge or consent of Mrs\nMary Williams, who maintained a rightful claim to the property. This raises\nthe issue that the disposition may have been made without lawful authority.\n\n2. Death of key party and concealment (1968)\nFrederick Buckler died in 1968. Any knowledge he held regarding the\ncircumstances of the transfer died with him, preventing proper scrutiny or\nchallenge at the time.\n\n3. Inability to prove ownership in court (1974)\nMrs Mary Williams was subsequently unable to prove her claim in court\nproceedings in 1974. This inability must be viewed in the context of the\nprior undisclosed transfer and the absence of key evidence and testimony.\n\n4. Knowledge of defective title by acquiring party\nThere is a credible basis to assert that the acquiring party (BP and/or its\nassociated property entities) knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that\nthe title they acquired was defective. This point is central and I am\ncompiling supporting material demonstrating notice and/or constructive\nknowledge.\n\n5. Registration following death of claimant\nMrs Mary Williams died prior to the land being formally registered in the\nname of the acquiring party. As a result, she was denied any opportunity to\nrebut, challenge, or correct the position before registration was effected.\n\n6. Death of additional disputing party\nMr Buckler also died during the period in which he was engaged in disputing\nthe matter. The cumulative effect is that all primary individuals with\ndirect knowledge were deceased before the issue could be fully and fairly\nresolved.\n\n7. Ongoing family claim\nDespite these events, the claim of the Williams family has never been\nrelinquished. The position remains that the title was wrongfully\ntransferred and subsequently registered on the basis of that defective\ntransfer.\n\n---\n\nRequest for Action\n\nIn light of the above, I respectfully request that:\n\n1. This evidence be formally appended to my existing complaint file.\n2. The register be reviewed in accordance with provisions relating to\nfraud, mistake, and/or rectification.\n3. Consideration be given to whether the registration was obtained through\nor affected by fraud or concealment.\n4. I be informed of the appropriate process for seeking rectification\nand/or indemnity.\n\nI am prepared to provide supporting documents, including historical\nrecords, press reports, and family documentation, upon request or via\nsecure submission.\n\nGiven the seriousness of the matters raised, I would be grateful for\nwritten confirmation that this submission has been received and attached to\nmy complaint, along with an outline of the next steps.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n\nOn Sun, 19 Apr 2026, 16:29 Requester, <[redacted]> wrote:\n\n>  Sir or Madam,\n>\n> I write to ask that my complaint regarding title number WA231076 (Land on\n> the North Side of Leckwith Road, Llandough) be escalated to **stage two**\n> of HM Land Registry’s Complaints Procedure. This email sets out why I\n> consider the stage‑one decision to be incorrect, identifies the mistake I\n> say exists in the register, and explains the decision I seek.\n>\n> ### 1. My core contention\n>\n> My core contention is that BP Properties Limited were registered as\n> proprietors on the basis of a factual and legal error regarding my\n> grandmother’s status on the land. My grandmother did not occupy under any\n> genuine licence granted to her and did not relinquish any claim. Instead,\n> any licence relied on by BP related to a different name/person. As her\n> heir, I have succeeded to her claim; I therefore say that registering BP as\n> proprietors was a “mistake in the register” for the purposes of the Land\n> Registration Act 2002.\n>\n> ### 2. Identity mismatch and alleged “licence”\n>\n> Your stage‑one letter records that HM Land Registry relies on the Court of\n> Appeal decision in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler  EWCA Civ 2, and treats my\n> grandmother as having occupied under a licence granted by the documentary\n> title holder, so that her possession was no longer adverse.\n>\n> However, the alleged licence and related correspondence did not use my\n> grandmother’s true legal name. My grandmother was Mrs Williams (supported\n> by her birth, marriage and death certificates), not “Mrs Buckler”. The\n> “licensee” referred to in BP’s narrative and in the 1987 litigation is\n> therefore not the same legal person as my grandmother. There is, in other\n> words, a fundamental mis‑identification or identity fraud at the heart of\n> the story that HM Land Registry and the Court have relied upon.\n>\n> If the licence relied on by BP was addressed to, or granted in respect of,\n> a different named individual, it cannot properly be said that my\n> grandmother’s occupation was under that licence. In that case her\n> occupation remained adverse to BP’s paper title, and any finding that she\n> was a “licensee” rests on a factual premise that is demonstrably wrong.\n>\n> ### 3. Timing – “cart before the horse”\n>\n> Your letter explains that the applications for first registration of\n> WA231076 (and the related title WA240304) were made in 1982–83 and that BP\n> demonstrated a documentary root of title back to 1969/1975 by way of\n> conveyances and a 1971 abstract of title.\n>\n> You also confirm that the Court of Appeal only gave its decision in BP\n> Properties Ltd v Buckler in 1987, holding that an offer by BP to let my\n> grandmother remain created a licence and brought her adverse possession to\n> an end.\n>\n> This highlights a fundamental sequencing problem:\n>\n> - At the date of first registration (1982–83), whether there was a valid\n> licence capable of defeating my grandmother’s adverse possession was a\n> live, unresolved dispute.\n> - BP nevertheless presented themselves as entitled to be registered as\n> proprietors and their solicitors certified on form FR1 that there was no\n> question or doubt affecting the title.\n>\n> - HM Land Registry, relying on that certification, registered BP before\n> any court had determined whether my grandmother’s possession had\n> extinguished BP’s title.\n> - Only in 1987 did the Court of Appeal retrospectively treat the alleged\n> licence as bringing adverse possession to an end, and that decision was\n> itself based on the mis‑identification described above.\n>\n> In simple terms, the effect of the alleged licence (if any) was judicially\n> determined **after** first registration, and on the basis of the wrong\n> person being treated as the “licensee”. BP and their solicitors put the\n> cart before the horse, and HM Land Registry accepted that position.\n>\n> ### 4. The specific “mistake in the register”\n>\n> Your stage‑one response concludes that there is “no evidence of a mistake\n> in the register” and therefore no power to alter the register and no right\n> to indemnity. I say this is incorrect.\n>\n> The mistake I allege is as follows:\n>\n> 1. On the true facts, my grandmother’s occupation of the land was adverse\n> to BP’s documentary title and was not under any valid licence granted to\n> her.\n>\n> 2. Her adverse possession had, or may have, extinguished BP’s title by the\n> time of first registration in 1982–83, meaning BP were not entitled to be\n> registered as proprietors at that time.\n>\n> 3. HM Land Registry nevertheless registered BP as proprietors on the basis\n> of:\n>    - a licence attributed to the wrong person (identity error/fraud), and\n>    - a solicitor’s FR1 certificate stating there was no question or doubt\n> affecting title, despite a long‑running dispute and pending litigation.\n>\n> 4. Subsequent reliance on the 1987 Court of Appeal decision does not cure\n> this, because that decision itself proceeded on the mis‑identification of\n> my grandmother and did not and could not retrospectively validate a licence\n> that never related to her.\n>\n> On that analysis, the register shows BP as proprietors when, in law, my\n> grandmother’s adverse possession should have extinguished BP’s title and\n> given rise to a transmissible proprietary interest which I, as her heir,\n> now claim. The register therefore does not accurately reflect the true\n> legal position and contains a mistake capable of rectification.\n>\n> ### 5. Why the stage‑one reasoning is inadequate\n>\n> In your stage‑one letter you state that:\n>\n> - HM Land Registry has an administrative function and cannot “look behind\n> or challenge decisions of the Court”. [1]\n> - My identity‑fraud claims are “not relevant to the issue of title to the\n> land” because they relate to the dispute heard by the Court.\n>\n> - There is no evidence of negligence or maladministration and no evidence\n> of a mistake in the register.\n>\n> With respect, this reasoning is incomplete:\n>\n> - Once HM Land Registry is presented with clear evidence that the person\n> named as the “licensee” in the litigation and licence documentation is not\n> the same legal person as the occupier (my grandmother), that goes directly\n> to whether the Court of Appeal’s factual premise remains reliable and\n> whether the register is accurate.\n>\n> - Recognising that there is a serious question as to the correctness of\n> the register is not the same as “overturning” the Court of Appeal. HM Land\n> Registry has statutory powers to alter the register where there is a\n> mistake, and it can, where appropriate, refer disputes about rectification\n> to the tribunal or the courts.\n>\n> - To simply say that identity‑fraud concerns are “not relevant to title”\n> is, I say, an error of law and/or an unreasonable application of policy. It\n> disregards new evidence going to the foundation of BP’s claimed entitlement.\n>\n> ### 6. The decision and outcome I seek\n>\n> For stage two, I ask that a Land Registrar (Senior Officer) reconsider the\n> complaint and:\n>\n> 1. Accept that the combination of:\n>    - the identity mismatch (licence/name vs my grandmother’s true legal\n> name), and\n>    - the timing (registration in 1982–83 before the 1987 decision) gives\n> rise to at least a **serious question** as to whether the register is\n> mistaken in showing BP/ Companies thereafter, as proprietors.\n>\n> 2. Treat this as evidence of a potential “mistake in the register” for the\n> purposes of your alteration powers and Schedule 8, rather than as a mere\n> disagreement with the 1987 judgment.\n>\n> 3. Either:\n>\n>    - (a) commence the process of rectification, recognising that my\n> grandmother’s adverse possession may have extinguished BP’s title and that\n> I, as her heir, now have a claim to be registered, or\n>\n>    - (b) formally refer the dispute over the correctness of the register\n> to the appropriate tribunal/court, making clear that HM Land Registry\n> recognises that the identity‑fraud evidence raises a real issue about\n> whether the register is accurate.\n>\n> 4. Confirm that, if it is ultimately determined that the register is\n> mistaken and cannot be rectified without prejudice to third parties, HM\n> Land Registry will treat me as having a potential claim for indemnity under\n> Schedule 8.\n>\n> Please also confirm any further documents you require (for example, copies\n> of the licence, the BP v Buckler pleadings/judgment, and my grandmother’s\n> certificates) so that the stage‑two review can consider the identity\n> evidence in full.\n>\n> Fraud unravels all. The limitation act also had a clause for fraud.\n> Furthermore any limitation begins from discovery of fraud not occurrence of\n> it.\n>\n> The convenient and timely death of my nan after her two obstructed\n> attempts to make her case in 1974, followed by my father's convenient and\n> timely death after his appeal of the 1987 case was dismissed and his ECHR\n> obstructed, along with our forceful removal by 30 police and bailiffs in\n> 1988. And the press reporting us as squatters on our ancestral birthland\n> since 1667, did unlawfully dispossess and disposition us, but it doesn't\n> change the facts.\n>\n> I see this case as instrumental in Wales' decolonisation. Whereby us\n> indigneous Welsh Nationals on our ancestral birthland are victim to a\n> crime. And I am the only one willing to speak up and out as my family of\n> mostly women, are all too traumatised by this crime.\n>\n> It's evident illicit profits and gains. Identity fraud. And negligence and\n> incompetence. I absolutely see the Brit-ish Establishment that now occupy\n> and rule through force, stealth/ secrecy and licence as terrorists and us\n> your hostages. As a direct result of this case.\n>\n> This is now a hostage terrorist situation on our lands. Well, my family\n> are your hostages, I'm more of a counter officer soldier. So put it right.\n> I will not stand down.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\n> Rightful Squire & executor of Manon of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> On Sun, 19 Apr 2026, 07:41 Wales.OfficeMail, <\n> Wales.Office@landregistry.gov.uk> wrote:\n>\n>> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n>> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n>> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n>> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>>\n>> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n>> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n>> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n>> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document\n>> is in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to\n>> complete and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such\n>> completed document by post.\n>>\n>> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r\n>> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais\n>> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni\n>> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n>>\n>> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu\n>> golwg y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y\n>> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho\n>> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu\n>> testun at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i\n>> Gofrestrfa Tir EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen\n>> o'r fath bydd rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>>\n>> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>>\n>> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>>\n>> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>>\n>> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n>>\n>> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>>\n>> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n"},{"id":"wb-23121d64","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-04_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-04","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-04_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-04_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Mon, 4 May 2026 00:33:15 -0300\nSubject: Re: Setting Aside BP vs Buckler 1987 on grounds of BP with our stolen paper title and identity fraud, court mistakes and procedural unfairness & more\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V6QQL4dkToJEvbs7FUULh--MsAYM7pXwdAQ8WLGQq5xUA@mail.gmail.com>\n\nCouncillor of Llandough,\n\nHave you seen this footage?  https://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nI'm a military cyber warfare professional.\nNot much gets past me.\nI was the best hacker in our Government and military in 2005.\nIn fact I already note this footage was cut and censored to hide key facts.\nNot to mention this and other press coverage and footage supressed. Even\nunto this day.\n\nMore interestingly than my mum's appearance at the end of the clip, is the\nnews anchor who was my old best friends mum. That same best friend is now\nan executive of press monitoring company Meltwater Media in Cardiff City.\n\nThere's plenty more press coverage of this whole war waged on my family,\nland & home. And it's all going into a Netflix documentry along with the\nhandling of this matter which you still all try to bury and cover up. Like\nthe hundreds of child graves surrounding this case. You are all committing\ncareer and political suicide.\n\nI'm still waiting for you and the MP to respond to this matter.  For months\nnow.\nMoJ won't comment as they say its ongoing. See attached. Which doesn't make\nsense as I've not begun legal proceedings and this hasn't been touched in\ndecades.\nThey also took half a year just to reply.\n\nLand Registry made my query into a complaint and shut it down instantly.\nCadw falsely allege they have nothing to do with it when they were pivotal\nin it. They should have listen it as a grade II.\n\nI'm not rolling up with tanks, but I'm not going away. We need to\nstraighten this all out.\n\nYou know the clause with harassment? I.e. If I have reason to pursue I may\npersist. And so I will persist. But I have no desire to make you feel\nharassed. So please just all do your jobs. And diligently.\n\nMy family are still all terrorised into silence about this, even decades\nlater. It's a hostage/ terrorist situation in my estimation (As a military\nwarfare professional).\n\nI find dealing with my former community and Govenrment 50/50 at the moment.\nWhich is good enough odds for me to refrain from any direct action on this\nmatter. For now.\n\nI'm actually still giving you and the MP the benefit of the doubt you're\nbusy and/or mulling this over still, before taking a position on the\nmatter. But justice delayed is justice denied. Like the MoJ taking half a\nyear to reply only to fob me off. Tick tick.\n\nIt's not just my family being held hostage there, but my people seem\ndemoralised and its no way for them to all live. I already fly in and out\nlike its another military tour of Iraq. I was shot at in Barry and an\nAfghan tried stealing my dog last time I was back.\n\nI will feel my villages warmth one way or another. When it's our ancestral\nhome for centuries. How dare we be ignored, disregarded and exiled. Or shot\nat and shunned. Next time I fly home I want it to feel like home. Not\nanother tour of the middle east where I had to get behind a GPMG in SF role\nfrom a helicopter.\n\nThe situation is untenable. We can't go on like this another decade, with\nyou Brit'ish all on our stolen land without a care in the world, and us all\ndispossessed, butchered and forced out by force, secrecy and fraudulent\nlicense.\n\nYou don't seem to fathom the ongoing harm, injury and loss here. This\ndispossession and disposition, tantamount to a terrorist/ hostage situation\nhas been ongoing almost 4 decades. My families silence from being\nterorrised into silence and the years its taken for me to discover the\nfraud, due to the stealth, secretly and complexity of it, does not put this\nin the past but very much in our faces today.\n\nOur family demand of you and anyone other installed persons, proclaiming\nlegitimate authority of our lands, immediately address this matter. I'm not\nthe kind to hold a gun to your head and demand attention. I'm being polite,\ncourteous and professional here. And patient and understanding. But it\nwould not be sane or reasonable for me to allow you or the MP to cause me\nlet or hiderence.\n\nIn my experience if you won't tackle this in the open I have to presume you\nare going  clandestine and into the shadows and thus pose risk of further\nthreat to me and my family. As the British State.\n\nThere's gaps in records. Court mistakes. There's supressed, redacted,\ncensored media coverage. Procedural unfairness. Fraud. Theft. And the\nsilence and lack of co operation rectifying records and narratives only\ndiminishes your legitimacy and so your authority.\n\nYou wouldn't need to be clandestine and abuse force to try to handle men\nlike me and mine, if you'd just all straighten out this matter. Then you'd\nhave my trust and fieldty.\n\nYou know at the WCIT in Dubai with the help of David Cameron in 2012, it\ntook a few weeks to exit UK from the treaty. Which is something I had to\nbring up with my bank the other day who took twice as long to process a\nrefund after a dispute because of all the beurocracy. Similarly with this\nwe have no barriers to communicate, we have A.I, we have digital systems\nand digital records yet this is being made into a slow, tedious, confusing,\ncumbersom, challenging, obstructive process.\n\nDon't weaponise time. Justice delayed is justice denied. I am accustom to\ntime being abused so that other hybrid warfare war crime avenues can be\nexplored like trying to kidnap and silence me. I know the British State\nacts like a terrorist organisation even by its own definition of one,\nbecause I was one of you terorrists. In an illegal war. On another\nindigenous population. I also spent most of my adult life in exile in latin\namerican now so I can draw all the parallels between the regime on British\nIsles and cartel/ crime syndicates on other banana republics. Ours stink\nand is no different to other islands. So let's not fancy our regime or\nactors in it, as any better or more benevolant or honest than others.\n\nMy postion, proportionate to the situation, seems correct. In that a multi\ngenerational civil war has been waged on my family, home and people, as\nindigenous Welsh Britons, on our ancestral birthland. And having completed\nmy 22 years in oath in 2024, under the employ of the Vale council, I no\nlonger have the restraint of allegiance to the Brit'ish State. I am\nnaturally leaning towards being a counter officer and pro Wales fully\ndecolonising. Bearing in mind this war being waged isn't us ontowards the\nBrit'ish State, but the exact opposite. And there's no requirement on our\npart we participate willingly or make it any easier than is neccesary to\nsoft genocide us. After already dispossesing, displacing, looting,\nbutchering and holding us hostage or exiling us.\n\nIn any case I believe my families standing, title and estate was stolen.\nVia fraud and armed force. Once the cover up and falsified records are\nrectified it will be more apparent why restoration and reperations should\noccur. Because it's already very clear to me. As a cyber and electronic\nmilitary warfare professional and certified and experienced military\ncommander and leader. As well as me being the son and grandson of the man\nand his mum butchered in the process of this fraud and cover up attempt of\nthe crimes relating to this terrorist siege on our land and property of\ncenturies.\n\nWe Britons do not negotiate with terrorists.\nI'm not SAS. I'm who JSHQ Northwood sent to break the SAS out of the Iraq\nprison days before they got executed. I setup the covert drone surveillance\nvia satellies between Iraq and London. Now it's the inverse situation where\nyou're regime is on my lands, have executed my family members, hold my\nfamily hostage and still act like terrorists. Silence does not work in your\nfavour with me. I just presume you are otherwise engaging in clandestine\nwarfare with me.\n\nI'm hoping for the best. I really am.\nPeace, due process, dialouge etc.\n\nThis isn't even our generations fight. It's an inherited scandal and mess,\npassed down to us. The responsibility to rectify this matter is a fudiciary\none. And I'm just the one in my family daring to simply speak about this.\nNo wonder none of the hostages there speak. It just becomes another\nopportunity for you to all reaffirm our people are hostages under\nterrorists.\n\n\nI've seen recently others speaking out and speaking up being separated from\ntheir evidence, charges fabricated and them subjected to interment. I\nmyself already had to have the support of a US Marine officer when attempts\nwere made to frame and extradite and silence me. The defence correspondent\nfor the mail on Sunday was also contracted to destroy my reputation in a\nnationwide campaign before. Which I also managed to stop in time. So I know\nthe lengths that the regime on that island will go to, to cover up crimes\nand fraud instead of remedy.\n\n I doubt a lot of you are even human at this point. Not because of my\nactual military attachment to the underground UFO city in Coresham. But\nbecause a mars attack type alien invasion and occupancy and rule is exactly\nthe vibes I get when I'm back on my motherland. Citizenship seems to now\nmean to be hostages whereby people are gagged, hands tied behind their\nbacks and on their knees. That is the exact situation I see people in, on\nBritish Isles. Any moment due to have our throats slit.\n\nNot for me thank you. I much preferred being behind the machine gun in a\nhelicopter pointing it at the inhumane terrorists treating humans this way.\n\nI spoke to my sister earlier about an article stating that bailiffs stole,\nagainst the explicit injunction instructions, £30,000 of my dads after\nevictim him from his home. In 1988. She told me my family there haven't\never experienced having £30,000 laying around the house in the almost 40\nyears since. If that doesn't tell me they're like Jews of nazi Germany\nunder the occupancy and rule of the tyranny and terrorism there i don't\nknow what does.\n\nSo it is a hostage / terorrist situation so far as I see. We're not\nforgotten about. I've made it very clear for months and I'm just ignored\nand rebuttled and dismissed. So  clearly someone believes we're not all\nequal under God. Or law. That's disappointing.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq (Ret'd Sgt)\nRightful Executor of Manor of Llandough\n\nOn Fri, 14 Nov 2025, 15:24 Carroll, George D (Cllr), <\ngdcarroll@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk> wrote:\n\n> Hi Requester\n>\n> Thank you for copying me in on this.\n>\n> If you'd like to discuss, please let me know.\n>\n> All the best,\n>\n> George\n> ------------------------------\n> *From:* Requester <[redacted]>\n> *Sent:* Friday, November 14, 2025 12:48:36 PM\n> *To:* kanishka.narayan.mp@parliament.uk <kanishka.narayan.mp@parliament.uk\n> >\n> *Subject:* BP vs Buckler\n>\n> You don't often get email from [redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\n> assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\n> Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> My family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for\n> generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of\n> our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply affected.\n> Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\n> inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\n> corporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\n> considerations relating to the site.\n>\n> I have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\n> requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\n> historical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\n> historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n>\n> My interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\n> significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\n> stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\n> this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n>\n> By way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\n> Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\n> simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\n> would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n> *Requester*\n> [redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [location redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> Tel: 0203 137 7118\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-8e07d7a6","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-09_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-09","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-09_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-09_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Sat, 9 May 2026 19:16:53 -0300\nSubject: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V7etNV7aatA0NJB+qqTWFX9bf9Qu6M4DFuNTDXUv0W+yw@mail.gmail.com>\n\nSir/Madam,\nI am writing on behalf of myself and siblings who are the heirs and\nsuccessors of Mary Williams of the Williams family, rightful owners and\noccupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough since 1667 until our dispossession\nvia armed force in 1988.\nI write to summarize our position regarding our historical and ongoing\ndispossession of Great House Farm, which I alledge involves;\n- Denial of right to be heard by the land registry due to the fact my\ngrandmother Mr Williams (falsy named Mrs Buckler to diminish the Williams\nancestral superior land claim) conveniently died and our family were in\nmourning in the limited window granted to challenge BP registration of our\nland and property in their names. Much like my grandfather conveniently\ndied too, before  being able to clarify, even to my grandmother Mrs\nWilliams, how her Title ended up in BP's possession. Because until her\ndying breath she maintained her ownership claim. Despite repeated unlawful\nattempts over decades to disposition the firm position she maintained about\nhers and ours undisputed ancestral and superior land claim to the land in\nquestion.\nAfter my father's appeal of the BP vs Buckler 1987 ruling was dismissed on\ngrounds of \"heads BP win, tails we lose\" and his home demolished, all money\nand possessions removed (despite a court injuction ordering nothing be\nremoved) and despite his ECHR request being blocked, and arrest without\ncharge, and hospitalisation and then his convenient death at age 41, our\nremaining family of mostly women and children, have to this day been too\nterrified to speak up. According to recently released, supressed ITV news\ncoverage from 1988, bailifs occupying our stolen land and property, even\ndislocated my mum's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court\ninjunction.\nAnd without the discovery of fraud this year, (which has taken me two\ndecades and a career in military 