are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2026 16:17:41 -0300\nSubject: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V47Uyuy3ASSyaAKeCBdTH5KqsaQgt=Z4scn87Syo==0DQ@mail.gmail.com>\n\nSirs/ Ma'ams,\n\nI write on behalf of myself and my siblings, who are the heirs and\nsuccessors of Mary Williams of the Williams family, the rightful owners and\noccupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough, since 1667 until our unlawful,\nunconstitution and inhumane dispossession by armed force in 1988. For which\nwe remain dispossessed, defrauded and without justice or even narrative\njustice, unto this day. The public also lost a site of historic and\narchelogical significants and were lied to about what went on. The land\nlooted too, which is a loss to our nation and people.\n\nI apologise if any of this is incoherent. I am the only member of my family\nwilling to speak out; the rest, who are nearly all women (sisters, mum,\naunties etc), are petrified of the repercussions, given what happened to\nour family in the 1980s. Or dead from this. My father, nan, grandad and\npossibly great grandad and maybe more, all potentially murdered.\n\nAll this is also chilling in that the playbook used here, could be\nindustrial scale and nationwide  and have occured to other families too.\nOur case might be the foundations for a class action for the public.\n\nI write to summarise our position regarding the historical and ongoing\ndispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough, following the landmark legal\ncase *BP v Buckler* [1987], which I allege involved:\n\n- **Denial of the right to be heard by the Land Registry.** My grandmother,\nMary Williams (falsely named \"Mrs Buckler\" on the licence letter produced\nby BP in 1974, in order to diminish the Williams ancestral superior land\nclaim), conveniently died while our family was in mourning during the\nlimited window granted by the Land Registry to challenge BP's registration\nof our land and property in their name in 1982/83. Similarly, my\ngrandfather died before he was able to clarify—even to my grandmother—how\nher fee simple absolute title deed ended up in BP's possession. Until her\ndying breath, she maintained her ownership claim, despite repeated unlawful\nattempts over decades to dislodge the firm position she held regarding her\nand our undisputed ancestral and superior land claim. The official records\nand narrative are wrong; there are court errors, suppressed evidence,\nprocedural unfairness, fraud, and the list goes on.\n\nThe *BP v Buckler* [1987] ruling applied the licence my deceased\ngrandmother held to my father and mother. They never had, nor entered into,\nany such agreement with BP. The ruling also alleged that my grandmother\naccepted BP's licence letters by non-response, which was untrue. It further\nstated that any objection should have been directed to the BP Pension Trust\nrather than the claimant, BP Properties, which were deemed separate\ncompanies. Yet in my father's subsequent appeal against the *BP v Buckler*\nruling, his appeal was dismissed on the grounds that the BP companies were\neffectively the same—so \"heads BP wins, tails we lose.\" Our 800-year-old\nhome was then demolished and all money and possessions removed, despite a\ncourt injunction ordering that nothing be removed. My father's ECHR\napplication was blocked; he was arrested without charge, hospitalised, and\nthen he conveniently died at the age of 41. Our remaining family,\nconsisting mostly of women and children, have to this day been too\nterrified to speak about this case because of the decades of crimes\ncommitted against our household by the British State. It was synonymous\nwith a battle or war. I say this as a military warfare professional and\nIraq War veteran: a certified and experienced military commander and\nleader. I concluded my military career with honours as an Acting Sergeant.\nMy profession is cyber and electronic warfare.\n\nAccording to recently declassified, previously suppressed ITV news coverage\nfrom 1988, bailiffs occupied our stolen land and property, and even\ndislocated my mother's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court\ninjunction. I also question how ITV came to declassify and publish this\nfootage to YouTube a few months ago, after the months I have spent seeking\ninformation. That did not go unnoticed. There is liability there, and I do\nnot accept ITV's belief that this quiet release of suppressed news coverage\nmakes the matter right—though the action is appreciated. How did it come to\nbe suppressed in the first place? And why is it cut abruptly, at what\nappears to be SAS performing a siege on my family home and dislocating my\npregnant mother's shoulder?\n\nWithout my discovery of fraud this year—which has taken me two decades, a\ncareer in military cyber and electronic warfare, and recent innovations in\nAI to discover and unravel—we had no redress or recourse due to the statute\nof limitations and the passage of time, notwithstanding that we were all\ntoo traumatised, like hostages under terrorists, to speak out. We have\nreceived no support to this day for what we were subjected to.\n\nThis whole affair, even to this day, represents scandalous treatment of me\nand my family. We never surrendered our claim. The manorial titles of the\nManor of Llandough are rightfully ours. The fee simple absolute title has\nbeen ours for over a century, a fact that is also suppressed and withheld\nfrom the defrauded—and implicated—Land Registry.\n\nI am also a war veteran who left my military career with honours and was\nemployed until 2024 under the Vale of Glamorgan Council / Welsh Government.\nI completed my 22 years' service oath *bona fide*. I am an indigenous Welsh\nBriton, and this is my ancestral birthland (established 1667). The\ndisrespect shown by the Vale MP and Llandough Councillor in simply ignoring\nme and this matter is abhorrent.\n\nITV coverage (suppressed until recent months) also reports that neighbours\ndescribed the eviction as an \"SAS-style operation\" to remove us by force in\n1988 (myself included). The men in the video do look like SAS. I have\nsubmitted an FOI request to the MOD. Shareholders of mine are SAS, so I\nshall find out one way or another, even if I receive an NCND reply. This\nmatter was also raised in Parliament, who classified and disposed of the\nrecords.\n\nMargaret Thatcher's administration at the time (the British Government) was\nevidently assisting BP in clawing assets for the UK Government's sale and\nexit at the time, which might explain how 30 police—and possibly SAS—were\nused to rip us from our home and land. The human rights violations remain\nunanswered.\n\nThe Land Registry ultimately had checks and balances lifted and total free\nrein during Thatcher's reign, while BP's lawyers evidently committed\nperjury in their declarations to the Land Registry, withholding information\nfrom it and supplying it with false information.\n\nAll the while, Welsh television was simultaneously interviewing Gaddafi in\nLibya in 1988, where he accused Thatcher and the British State of being the\nreal terrorists, not him. My oath ended in 2024; I am also a Welsh\nnational. I have no allegiance to the British State. If it acts like my\nenemy, it is my enemy. I am absolutely a Welsh national and counter-officer\nnow that it is so evident the British State waged civil war upon us\nindigenous Britons—me and my family included—on our ancestral birthland.\n\nOther media coverage alleged by UK courts to exist from 1974 seems\nnon-existent or suppressed too. Much is behind paywalls. This whole case\nneeds to be in the public eye. I have put everyone I can think of on notice.\n\nFraud and procedural unfairness are ultimately rampant in the case of my\nfamily's dispossession. Aside from all my family members dying at\nconvenient junctures instrumental in the windows to change the outcome, I\nstill have major concerns regarding how the MOJ took months to respond only\nto fob me off last week; how the MP fobbed me off and will not provide a\nproper response; how CADW and Llandough Parish allege this is nothing to do\nwith them, despite CADW failing to list the farmhouse as Grade II so it\ncould be demolished (as per a 1,700-signature petition, which was\npractically the whole town at the time); the current councillor for\nLlandough failing to reply properly; and the fact that the National\nArchives report gaps, missing records, and suppressed records.\nNotwithstanding that Marconi was staying with us while inventing radio, and\nthe town will not even put a plaque up to commemorate this, which is\nfurther erasure of the history and known (but suppressed) archaeological\nand historic significance of the site. In BP's planning application\nrecords, they state that our 800-year-old former courthouse home was merely\nan old, dilapidated building.\n\nNotwithstanding the suppression of the 1870 Roman soldier remains we\ndiscovered when changing our floor from stone to timber, also suppressed to\nhide the site's archaeological significance so that housing development\ncould be unlawfully approved. BP did not even seek a ruling on ownership;\nthey only sought possession, most likely so that the discovery and\nsignificance of the site's archaeology could be pretended not to be known\nuntil the excavation of our land in 1994—which is further evidence of\nblatant conspiracy and fraud.\n\nThese are the actions of a crime or terrorist network, seeking to install a\nterrorist cell or camp. It is worse than simply the British colonising\nWales.\n\nNotwithstanding the child graves secretly moved from the church next door\nduring the excavation, which seemed to take ten years to be properly\nreported on, and even then their numbers in the report appear to be\nunderrepresented.\n\nThe scandal continues endlessly. There are court errors too. The fancy\nLatin words diminish and falsely describe my grandmother's land claim and\nsuperior ownership (it was \"older than man can remember,\" not merely a\n\"claim to the land\"). The language used by the court clearly demonstrates\nbias prior to the ruling—language implying that my late grandmother, Mrs\nWilliams (*not* Mrs Buckler, as they falsely named her in document fraud),\nwas imagining her ancestral superior land claim, in order to discredit her\nthrough carefully selected judicial wording.\n\nMy siblings and I remain the heirs and successors and landowners. Nothing\nhas lawfully broken or undone that claim. We demand that the fraud,\ncorruption, gaps in records, false records, and myriad crimes committed\nagainst us be addressed and not ignored. There should be a Senedd public\ninquiry into this. My family should not be dispossessed a second longer. We\nare seriously looking at £100 million in reparations if the truth of this\nmatter becomes known, given the scale of the scandal and injustice.\n\nIn 1667 we acquired the land and property in a 999-year lease (virtual\nfreehold). In the early 1900s we obtained the superior paper title—free and\nclear, outright equitable ownership—via the deal with Bute Estate quarryman\nDaniel Thomas, which led to the tree-planting ceremony to affirm this in\nhistory. *(See attached.)*\n\nFrederick Buckler's transfer of Mrs Williams's equitable title to BP and\ntheir predecessors, without her knowledge or consent, is not legitimate and\nshould never have stood, nor does it stand to reason. His inability to\nclarify the details of the alleged transaction due to his convenient death\nafterwards does not make it right, as Mary Williams maintained her position\nafter his death. It was never his title to sell, even if he did. My\ngrandmother was left unable to prove her standing, and the 1974 hearing was\nadjourned. The dismissal of the second hearings in 1974 due to the licence\nletter issued by BP (resorting to identity and document fraud) does not\nnegate the fact that there was never a ruling stating BP owned our land,\ndespite their purchasing my grandmother's stolen fee simple absolute title\ndeed. BP only ever sought possession. They could not obtain a ruling\nbecause it would have meant discovery, unveiling the archaeological\nsignificance that would have prevented land and housing development.\n\nThis was a coordinated campaign of fraud, stealth, and administrative\nerasure spanning decades, employing force, secrecy, and fraudulent licence.\nBy hook and by crook we were dispossessed of our land. Thatcher—and\npotentially the SAS—make it, at the least, an allodial/eminent domain\nseizure, in which case we should still be due compensation.\n\nI fail to see the proclaimed authority of the other men on my land,\nalleging themselves to be a government and citizens rather than terrorists,\nwho both ostracised and held my family hostage, if legitimacy does not\nexist. You need legitimacy to claim authority.\n\n**Summary of the Fraudulent Dispossession:**\n\n**The Title Theft:** Evidence supports that a \"Title-for-Quarrying\"\nagreement existed with Daniel Thomas of the Bute Estate. We obtained this\nfee simple absolute title lawfully, but it was later secretly and\nfraudulently taken and sold back to Bute / Western Ground Rents / BP\nwithout the knowledge or consent of the rightful owner, Mary Williams.\nParliament even stated on record how criminal Western Ground Rents were.\n\n**Procedural Fraud (The 1974 Licence):** The 1987 Court of Appeal ruling\nwas predicated on a unilateral \"licence letter\" issued by the landlords'\nsolicitors. We reject this ruling. It should be set aside on grounds of\nfraud.\n\n**Identity Erasure:** Throughout all legal proceedings, Mary Williams was\nintentionally misidentified as \"Mrs Buckler.\" This was a calculated tactic\nto strip her of her ancestral \"Williams\" lineage and the superior land\nrights and claim associated with it.\n\n**Exploitation of Mortality:**\n- **Frederick Buckler:** Died before the circumstances of how Mary was\ndispossessed of her title—and how the other parties regained possession\nafter the lawful Daniel Thomas (and/or Anthony Williams) dealings with Bute\nEstate—could be clarified. This is inconsequential, much like Mary's own\ndeath; neither changed her position on the matter, which she did voice,\ndespite what the 1987 ruling falsely alleges.\n- **Mary Williams:** Died during the precise two-week window required to\nrebut the Land Registry's registration of the land in BP's name—a window we\nbelieve was exploited to finalise this theft. At minimum, this is the case;\nit is more likely she was murdered. Her husband before her too. And my\nfather, William Buckler, given the convenient timing of all their\ndeaths—not to mention the unfair dismissal of my father's appeal, the\nblocking of his ECHR request, the theft and demolition of his property and\nour home prior to his death.\n\n**Our Position:**\nThe Williams family (now the Buckler family) has never ceased our claim. We\nmaintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the\ncurrent registered titles are poisoned by this original fraud. We seek full\nreparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman\narchaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right\nto a fair trial.\n\nPlease provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this\nmatter within 14 days. Please also hold to account those taking steps back\ninto the shadows, as this only makes the matter more clandestine and\ntherefore makes me very jumpy as a military warfare professional. I already\nfly in and out as if on another tour of the Middle East, and my family\nremain hostages under terrorists.\n\nI would also ask that Companies House, who have recently tried to\ncriminalise me, give me some space. They gave me three options to submit\nID: a questionnaire with passport and driving licence (which I provided);\nPost Office verification; or Digital ID. I chose the first option. They\nwill not accept it. But I will not be lured to a location of their\nchoosing, nor will I put any of their tracking ID applications on my\ndevices. I do not trust the regime on that island. Until this and another\nunnamed matter of similar scale is resolved, I consider the British\nGovernment a terrorist organisation and do not recognise its authority. My\nfamily there are hostages under said terrorists. And Church View Close,\nLlandough—23 houses—is a terrorist cell/camp on my land.\n\nMarconi was staying with us in Llandough when he invented radio. This too\nwas covered up. Cardiff City will not put a plaque naming Marconi as the\ninventor on the statue of a radio at Cardiff Bay—not even a plaque to\ncommemorate it. Llandough should be a tourist attraction based on this fact\nalone, rather than the occupying terrorist network's cell of 23 houses, as\nI see it.\n\nRegards,\n\n**Requester Esq.** (Ret'd Sgt)\nOn behalf of and as one of the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams, Great\nHouse Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n---\n"},{"id":"wb-19fa6aa3","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-11_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-11","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-11_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-11_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: \"Griffiths, Eleri\" <Eleri.Griffiths@senedd.cymru>\nDate: Mon, 11 May 2026 15:14:37 +0000\nSubject: ATB/RE: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <CW1P123MB8645D7449BD843D35072CCAE9A382@CW1P123MB8645.GBRP123.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for writing to Heledd.  She has asked me to respond on her behalf.  We were sorry to read of your difficulties.  Unfortunately, we are unable to offer help with your case.  From May the 8th Heledd became a Senedd Member for Pontypridd Cynon Merthyr.  I used the postcode CF71 7LR to check your constituency with this tool Welsh Parliament<https://constituency.senedd.wales/> and found you live in Pen-y-bont Bro Morgannwg.\n\nYour local Senedd Members are:\n\nSarah Rees (Plaid Cymru) Sarah Rees MS<https://senedd.wales/people/sarah-rees-ms/>\nAndrew RT Davies ( Conservative) Andrew RT Davies MS<https://senedd.wales/people/andrew-rt-davies-ms/> (Copied in already)\nSarah Murphy (Labour) sarah.murphy-ms@senedd.wales<mailto:sarah.murphy-ms@senedd.wales>\nMark Hooper (Plaid Cymru) Mark.Hooper-AS@Senedd.Cymru<mailto:Mark.Hooper-AS@Senedd.Cymru>\nSarah Cooper-Lesadd (Reform UK) (Sorry I cannot find this address yet)\nGareth Thomas (Reform UK) (Sorry I cannot find this address yet)\n\nIf you check back on the Senedd website tomorrow all addresses should be available.   This is the link Find a Member Search<https://senedd.wales/find-a-member-of-the-senedd>\n\nI hope this is useful.\n\nYours Sincerely\nEleri\n\nEleri Griffiths\nRheolwr Polisi, Gwaith Achos ac Ymgyrchu\nPolicy, Casework and Campaigns Manager\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DCE161.3FEF31B0]\n\n\n\nSwyddfa Heledd Fychan AS\nPontypridd Cynon Merthyr\nOffice of Heledd Fychan MS\nPontypridd Cynon Merthyr\n\n\nEleri.Griffiths@Senedd.Cymru<mailto:Eleri.Griffiths@Senedd.Cymru>\n0300 200 6304\n[cidimage003.png@01D7B515.6AAE7DC0]<https://www.facebook.com/HeleddFychanPlaidCymru/>\n[Llun yn cynnwys testun, olwyn, gêr, awyr y nos  Wedi cynhyrchu’r disgrifiad yn awtomatig]<https://twitter.com/heleddfychan>\n[Icon  Description automatically generated]<https://www.instagram.com/heledd_plaid/>\n\nOs nad wyf ar gael cysylltwch â  / If I am not available please contact\nheledd.fychan@senedd.cymru<mailto:heledd.fychan@senedd.cymru> 01443 853 214\n\n\nCaiff yr wybodaeth bersonol yr ydych wedi’i darparu ei thrin yn ôl gofynion GDPR. Os ydych am dderbyn copi o’n Hysbysiad Preifatrwydd, mynnwch gopi drwy ymateb i’r e-bost hwn.\n\nThe personal data you have provided will be treated in accordance with GDPR. If you would like to receive a copy of our GDPR Privacy Notice, you can request one by replying to this email\n\n\n\n\nOddi wrth: Requester <[redacted]>\nAnfonwyd: 09 May 2026 23:17\nAt: pensions@bp.com; ukgeneralenquiries@bp.com\nCopi/Cc: IDRP@bp.com; reportafraud@landregistry.gov.uk; complaints@gov.wales; ask@ombudsman-wales.org.uk; cadw@gov.wales; stephen.doughty.mp@parliament.uk; huw.thomas.ms@senedd.wales; anna.brychan.ms@senedd.wales; joseph.martin.ms@senedd.wales; anthony.slaughter.ms@senedd.wales; gcarroll@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk; Paul Egan <clerk@llandough-cc.co.uk>; commissioner@south-wales.police.uk; heritage@cardiff.gov.uk; Swyddfa Heledd Fychan AS - Office of Heledd Fychan MS <heledd.fychan@senedd.wales>; rhys.ab.owen@senedd.wales; James, Joel <joel.james@senedd.wales>; Swyddfa Andrew RT Davies - Office of Andrew RT Davies <andrewrt.davies@senedd.wales>; democratic@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk; leader@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\nPwnc: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n[https://senedd.wales/media/obuo0sep/senedd_logo_xs.png]\nE-mail protection couldn't recognize this email as this is the first time you received an email from this sender [redacted]\n\nSir/Madam,\nI am writing on behalf of myself and siblings who are the heirs and successors of Mary Williams of the Williams family, rightful owners and occupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough since 1667 until our dispossession via armed force in 1988.\nI write to summarize our position regarding our historical and ongoing dispossession of Great House Farm, which I alledge involves;\n- Denial of right to be heard by the land registry due to the fact my grandmother Mr Williams (falsy named Mrs Buckler to diminish the Williams ancestral superior land claim) conveniently died and our family were in mourning in the limited window granted to challenge BP registration of our land and property in their names. Much like my grandfather conveniently died too, before  being able to clarify, even to my grandmother Mrs Williams, how her Title ended up in BP's possession. Because until her dying breath she maintained her ownership claim. Despite repeated unlawful attempts over decades to disposition the firm position she maintained about hers and ours undisputed ancestral and superior land claim to the land in question.\nAfter my father's appeal of the BP vs Buckler 1987 ruling was dismissed on grounds of \"heads BP win, tails we lose\" and his home demolished, all money and possessions removed (despite a court injuction ordering nothing be removed) and despite his ECHR request being blocked, and arrest without charge, and hospitalisation and then his convenient death at age 41, our remaining family of mostly women and children, have to this day been too terrified to speak up. According to recently released, supressed ITV news coverage from 1988, bailifs occupying our stolen land and property, even dislocated my mum's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court injunction.\nAnd without the discovery of fraud this year, (which has taken me two decades and a career in military cyber and electronic warfare and the recent innovations in A.I to discover) we had no redress recourse due to the statute of limitation and time passed, ever had we not all been too traumatised like hostages under terrorists to speak out. This whole thing, even unto this day is scandalous treatment of me and my family. Not withstanding I am a war veteran, who left my military career with honours and was employed until 2024 under the Vale of Glamorgan Council/ Welsh Govenrment. Finished my 22 years in Oath BONAFIDE.\nITV coverage supressed until recent months also says neighbours report it was like an SAS Style Operation to remove us by force in 1988. And the men in the video do look SAS. I have subbmitee a FOI to the MOD.\nAnd Margaret Thatchers administration at the time (you Brit'ish) were evidently helping BP claw assets for the UK Governments exit at the time. Which might explain how 30 police and maybe SAS were used to rip us from our home and land.\nLand registry ultimately had check balances lifted and total free reign, while BPs lawyers commited purgergy in their declarations to them; withholding information from and supplying to the land registry false information.\nAll the while Welsh TV simultaneously interviewed Ghadaffi in Lybia in 1988, who report him accusing Thatcher and the Brit'ish State of being the real terrorists, not him. My oath ended in 2024, I'm also a Welsh National. I have no allegiance to the British State. If it acts like my enemy, its my enemy.\nOther media coverage alleged by UK courts to exist from 1974 seems non existence or suppressed too.\nFraud and proceedural unfairness are ultimately rampant in the case of my families dispossession. Aside from all my family members dying at all the convenient junctures instrumental to change the outcome of our dispossession, I still have major concerns with how the MOJ just took months to respond only to fob me off last week. Or how the MP fobbed me off and will not provide a proper response. Or how CADW alledge this is nothing to do with them despite failing to list the farm house as a grade II so it couldn't be demolished. As per a 1700 signature petition, which was practically the whole town at the time. Or the current councillor for Llandough failing to properly reply. Or the fact the national archives report gaps and missing and supressed records. Not withstanding Marconi was staying with us while inventing radio and the town won't even out a plaque up to make that known. Which is more erasure of the history. Like in BPs planning application saying our 800 year old former court house home was just an old delapitated building.\nNot withstanding the supression of the 1870 roman soldier we discovered when changing our floor from stone to timber. Also supressed to hide the sites archaeological significants so housing development could be unlawfully approved. And BP didn't even seek a ruling on ownership, they only saught possession, most likely so that the discovery and significant of the sites archaeological significants could be pretended to not be known until the excavation of our land in 1994. Which is just more evidence of the blatant conspiracy and fraud.\nThis is all the actions of a crime or terrorist network. To install a terrorist cell/ camp. It's worse than just the Brit'ish colonising Wales.\nNot withstanding the child graves secretly moved from the church next door during the exhivation seem to take 10 years to be properly reported on and even then their numbers in the report seem to be under represented.\nThe scandal just goes on and on. It's the gift that keeps giving. There's court mistakes too. The fancy latin words deminish and falsely describe my nans land claim and superior ownership. And language used clearly shows a bias before a ruling. Language used to imply she is almost imagining her ancestral superior land claim to discredit her in the carefully selected wording used by the judge. In court records that use the false legal fiction name fabricated by BP in their license letters document fraud, instead of her actual name. Evidently to shy away from the Williams name and its superior inpenitrable and unbreakable land claim. For which we remain the heirs and successors.\n1667 we aquired the land and property in a 999 year leasehold. And in the early 1900's obtained the superior paper title, free and clear outright equitable ownership, via the deal with Bute Estates quarryman Daniel Thomas. Which led to the tree planting ceremony to affirm this in history.\nFredrick Bucklers transfer of Mrs Williams title to BP and their predecessors without her knowledge or consent isn't legitimate and so has no authority. Him not being able to clarify that transaction due to dying doesn't make it right as Mary Williams maintained her position after his death. She just couldn't prove what she claimed without title. And the adjournment and dismissal of the two hearings in 1974 where she made her case, but without getting the ruling doesn't negate the facts.\nThis was a coordinated campaign of fraud, stealth, and administrative erasure. Over decades.\nSummary of the Fraudulent Dispossession:\n\n  *   The Title Theft: Evidence supports that a \"Title-for-Quarrying\" agreement existed with Daniel Thomas of the Bute Estate. We maintain this title was later secretly and fraudulently sold back to the landlords by Frederick Buckler without the knowledge or consent of the rightful owner, Mary Williams.\n  *   Procedural Fraud (The 1974 License): The 1987 Court of Appeal ruling was predicated on a unilateral \"license letter\" issued by the landlords’ solicitors. We reject this document as a fraudulent instrument of stealth designed to bypass adverse possession rights without Mary Williams’ agreement.\n  *   Identity Erasure: Throughout all legal proceedings, Mary Williams was intentionally misidentified as \"Mrs. Buckler.\" This was a calculated tactic to strip her of her ancestral \"Williams\" lineage and the superior land rights associated with it.\n  *   Exploitation of Mortality:\n\n     *   Frederick Buckler: Died before the truth of the title sale could be brought to light.\n     *   Mary Williams: Died during the precise 2-week window required to rebut the Land Registry’s registration of the land in BP’s name—a window we believe was exploited to finalize a theft.\n     *   William Buckler: His untimely death following the unfair dismissal of his appeal effectively blocked our path to the ECHR.\nOur Position:\nThe Williams family has never ceased its claim. We maintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the current registered titles are \"poisoned\" by this original fraud. We are now seeking full reparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman archaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right to a fair trial.\nPlease provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this matter within 14 days.\nRegards,\nSion Buckler\nOn behalf of and one of the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams\n"},{"id":"wb-8e5cc071","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-12_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-12","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-12_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-12_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Tue, 12 May 2026 08:18:38 -0300\nSubject: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V4uNits_Tj_URFdX2mBEJpmn9bZZdp2tyB0MwZBo1qgyg@mail.gmail.com>\n\nSirs/ Ma'ams,\n\nI write on behalf of myself and my siblings, who are the heirs and\nsuccessors of the late Mary Williams of the Williams family, the rightful\nowners and occupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough, since 1667 until our\nunlawful, unconstitution, brutal and inhumane dispossession by armed force\nin 1988. With press and courts falsly labelling and treating us as\nsquatters in favor of the false narrative of those who stole my disabled,\nwidow nans fee simple absolute title. For which we remain dispossessed,\ndefrauded and without justice or even narrative justice, unto this day. The\npublic also lost a site of historic and archelogical significants and were\nlied to about what went on. The land looted of artefacts too, which is a\nloss to our nation and people.\n\nI apologise if any of this is incoherent. I am the only member of my family\nwilling to speak out; the rest, who are nearly all women (sisters, mum,\naunties etc), are petrified of the repercussions, given what happened to\nour family in the 1980s. Or dead from this. My father, nan, grandad and\npossibly great grandad and maybe more, all potentially murdered.\n\nAll this is also chilling in that the playbook used here, could be\nindustrial scale and nationwide and have occured to other families too. Our\ncase might be the foundations for a class action for the public.\n\nI write to summarise our position regarding the historical and ongoing\ndispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough, following the landmark legal\ncase *BP v Buckler* [1987], which I allege involved a myriad of fraud,\ntheft, crimes and proceedural unfairness, gaps in records, supressed and\nconcealed records, human rights violations and literally almost every\ninjustice imaginable; not withstanding it was over decades for our family;\n\n- **Denial of the right to be heard by the Land Registry.** My grandmother,\nMary Williams (falsely named \"Mrs Buckler\" on the licence letter produced\nby BP in 1974, in order to diminish the Williams ancestral superior land\nclaim), conveniently died while our family was in mourning during the\nlimited window granted by the Land Registry to challenge BP's registration\nof our land and property in their name in 1982/83. Similarly, my\ngrandfather died before he was able to clarify—even to my grandmother—how\nher fee simple absolute title deed ended up in BP's possession. Until her\ndying breath, she maintained her ownership claim, despite repeated unlawful\nattempts over decades to dislodge the firm position she held regarding her\nand our undisputed ancestral and superior land claim. The official records\nand narrative are wrong; there are court errors, suppressed evidence,\nprocedural unfairness, fraud, and the list goes on.\n\nThe *BP v Buckler* [1987] ruling applied the licence my deceased\ngrandmother held to my father and mother. They never had, nor entered into,\nany such agreement with BP. The ruling also alleged that my grandmother\naccepted BP's licence letters by non-response, which was untrue. It further\nstated that any objection should have been directed to the BP Pension Trust\nrather than the claimant, BP Properties, which were deemed separate\ncompanies. Yet in my father's subsequent appeal against the *BP v Buckler*\nruling, his appeal was dismissed on the grounds that the BP companies were\neffectively the same—so \"heads BP wins, tails we lose.\" Our 800-year-old\nhome was then demolished and all money and possessions removed, despite a\ncourt injunction ordering that nothing be removed. My father's ECHR\napplication was blocked; he was arrested without charge, hospitalised, and\nthen he conveniently died at the age of 41. Our remaining family,\nconsisting mostly of women and children, have to this day been too\nterrified to speak about this case because of the decades of crimes\ncommitted against our household by the British State. It was synonymous\nwith a battle or war. I say this as a military warfare professional and\nIraq War veteran: a certified and experienced military commander and\nleader. I concluded my military career with honours as an Acting Sergeant.\nMy profession is cyber and electronic warfare.\n\nAccording to recently declassified, previously suppressed ITV news coverage\nfrom 1988, bailiffs occupied our stolen land and property, and even\ndislocated my mother's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court\ninjunction. I also question how ITV came to declassify and publish this\nfootage to YouTube a few months ago, after the months I have spent seeking\ninformation. That did not go unnoticed. There is liability there, and I do\nnot accept ITV's belief that this quiet release of suppressed news coverage\nmakes the matter right—though the action is appreciated. How did it come to\nbe suppressed in the first place? And why is it cut abruptly, at what\nappears to be SAS performing a siege on my family home and dislocating my\npregnant mother's shoulder?\n\nWithout my discovery of fraud this year—which has taken me two decades, a\ncareer in military cyber and electronic warfare, and recent innovations in\nAI to discover and unravel—we had no redress or recourse due to the statute\nof limitations and the passage of time, notwithstanding that we were all\ntoo traumatised, like hostages under terrorists, to speak out. We have\nreceived no support to this day for what we were subjected to.\n\nThis whole affair, even to this day, represents scandalous treatment of me\nand my family. We never surrendered our claim. The manorial titles of the\nManor of Llandough are rightfully ours. The fee simple absolute title has\nbeen ours for over a century, a fact that is also suppressed and withheld\nfrom the defrauded—and implicated—Land Registry.\n\nI am also a war veteran who left my military career with honours and was\nemployed until 2024 under the Vale of Glamorgan Council / Welsh Government.\nI completed my 22 years' service oath *bona fide*. I am an indigenous Welsh\nBriton, and this is my ancestral birthland (established 1667). The\ndisrespect shown by the Vale MP and Llandough Councillor in simply ignoring\nme and this matter is abhorrent.\n\nITV coverage (suppressed until recent months) also reports that neighbours\ndescribed the eviction as an \"SAS-style operation\" to remove us by force in\n1988 (myself included). The men in the video do look like SAS. I have\nsubmitted an FOI request to the MOD. Shareholders of mine are SAS, so I\nshall find out one way or another, even if I receive an NCND reply. This\nmatter was also raised in Parliament, who classified and disposed of the\nrecords.\n\nMargaret Thatcher's administration at the time (the British Government) was\nevidently assisting BP in clawing assets for the UK Government's sale and\nexit at the time, which might explain how 30 police—and possibly SAS—were\nused to rip us from our home and land. The human rights violations remain\nunanswered.\n\nThe Land Registry ultimately had checks and balances lifted and total free\nrein during Thatcher's reign, while BP's lawyers evidently committed\nperjury in their declarations to the Land Registry, withholding information\nfrom it and supplying it with false information.\n\nAll the while, Welsh television was simultaneously interviewing Gaddafi in\nLibya in 1988, where he accused Thatcher and the British State of being the\nreal terrorists, not him. My oath ended in 2024; I am also a Welsh\nnational. I have no allegiance to the British State. If it acts like my\nenemy, it is my enemy. I am absolutely a Welsh national and counter-officer\nnow that it is so evident the British State waged civil war upon us\nindigenous Britons—me and my family included—on our ancestral birthland.\n\nOther media coverage alleged by UK courts to exist from 1974 seems\nnon-existent or suppressed too. Much is behind paywalls. This whole case\nneeds to be in the public eye. I have put everyone I can think of on notice.\n\nFraud and procedural unfairness are ultimately rampant in the case of my\nfamily's dispossession. Aside from all my family members dying at\nconvenient junctures instrumental in the windows to change the outcome, I\nstill have major concerns regarding how the MOJ took months to respond only\nto fob me off last week; how the MP fobbed me off and will not provide a\nproper response; how CADW and Llandough Parish allege this is nothing to do\nwith them, despite CADW failing to list the farmhouse as Grade II so it\ncould be demolished (as per a 1,700-signature petition, which was\npractically the whole town at the time); the current councillor for\nLlandough failing to reply properly; and the fact that the National\nArchives report gaps, missing records, and suppressed records.\nNotwithstanding that Marconi was staying with us while inventing radio, and\nthe town will not even put a plaque up to commemorate this, which is\nfurther erasure of the history and known (but suppressed) archaeological\nand historic significance of the site. In BP's planning application\nrecords, they state that our 800-year-old former courthouse home was merely\nan old, dilapidated building.\n\nNotwithstanding the suppression of the 1870 Roman soldier remains we\ndiscovered when changing our floor from stone to timber, also suppressed to\nhide the site's archaeological significance so that housing development\ncould be unlawfully approved. BP did not even seek a ruling on ownership;\nthey only sought possession, most likely so that the discovery and\nsignificance of the site's archaeology could be pretended not to be known\nuntil the excavation of our land in 1994—which is further evidence of\nblatant conspiracy and fraud.\n\nThese are the actions of a crime or terrorist network, seeking to install a\nterrorist cell or camp. It is worse than simply the British colonising\nWales.\n\nNotwithstanding the child graves secretly moved from the church next door\nduring the excavation, which seemed to take ten years to be properly\nreported on, and even then their numbers in the report appear to be\nunderrepresented.\n\nThe scandal continues endlessly. There are court errors too. The fancy\nLatin words diminish and falsely describe my grandmother's land claim and\nsuperior ownership (it was \"older than man can remember,\" not merely a\n\"claim to the land\"). The language used by the court clearly demonstrates\nbias prior to the ruling—language implying that my late grandmother, Mrs\nWilliams (*not* Mrs Buckler, as they falsely named her in document fraud),\nwas imagining her ancestral superior land claim, in order to discredit her\nthrough carefully selected judicial wording.\n\nMy siblings and I remain the heirs and successors and landowners. Nothing\nhas lawfully broken or undone that claim. We demand that the fraud,\ncorruption, gaps in records, false records, and myriad crimes committed\nagainst us be addressed and not ignored. There should be a Senedd public\ninquiry into this. My family should not be dispossessed a second longer. We\nare seriously looking at £100 million in reparations if the truth of this\nmatter becomes known, given the scale of the scandal and injustice.\n\nIn 1667 we acquired the land and property in a 999-year lease (virtual\nfreehold). In the early 1900s we obtained the superior paper title—free and\nclear, outright equitable ownership—via the deal with Bute Estate quarryman\nDaniel Thomas, which led to the tree-planting ceremony to affirm this in\nhistory. *(See attached.)*\n\nFrederick Buckler's transfer of Mrs Williams's equitable title to BP and\ntheir predecessors, without her knowledge or consent, is not legitimate and\nshould never have stood, nor does it stand to reason. His inability to\nclarify the details of the alleged transaction due to his convenient death\nafterwards does not make it right, as Mary Williams maintained her position\nafter his death. It was never his title to sell, even if he did. My\ngrandmother was left unable to prove her standing, and the 1974 hearing was\nadjourned. The dismissal of the second hearings in 1974 due to the licence\nletter issued by BP (resorting to identity and document fraud) does not\nnegate the fact that there was never a ruling stating BP owned our land,\ndespite their purchasing my grandmother's stolen fee simple absolute title\ndeed. BP only ever sought possession. They could not obtain a ruling\nbecause it would have meant discovery, unveiling the archaeological\nsignificance that would have prevented land and housing development.\n\nThis was a coordinated campaign of fraud, stealth, and administrative\nerasure spanning decades, employing force, secrecy, and fraudulent licence.\nBy hook and by crook we were dispossessed of our land. Thatcher—and\npotentially the SAS—make it, at the least, an allodial/eminent domain\nseizure, in which case we should still be due compensation.\n\nI fail to see the proclaimed authority of the other men on my land,\nalleging themselves to be a government and citizens rather than terrorists,\nwho both ostracised and held my family hostage, if legitimacy does not\nexist. You need legitimacy to claim authority.\n\n**Summary of the Fraudulent Dispossession:**\n\n**The Title Theft:** Evidence supports that a \"Title-for-Quarrying\"\nagreement existed with Daniel Thomas of the Bute Estate. We obtained this\nfee simple absolute title lawfully, but it was later secretly and\nfraudulently taken and sold back to Bute / Western Ground Rents / BP\nwithout the knowledge or consent of the rightful owner, Mary Williams.\nParliament even stated on record how criminal Western Ground Rents were.\n\n**Procedural Fraud (The 1974 Licence):** The 1987 Court of Appeal ruling\nwas predicated on a unilateral \"licence letter\" issued by the landlords'\nsolicitors. We reject this ruling. It should be set aside on grounds of\nfraud.\n\n**Identity Erasure:** Throughout all legal proceedings, Mary Williams was\nintentionally misidentified as \"Mrs Buckler.\" This was a calculated tactic\nto strip her of her ancestral \"Williams\" lineage and the superior land\nrights and claim associated with it.\n\n**Exploitation of Mortality:**\n- **Frederick Buckler:** Died before the circumstances of how Mary was\ndispossessed of her title—and how the other parties regained possession\nafter the lawful Daniel Thomas (and/or Anthony Williams) dealings with Bute\nEstate—could be clarified. This is inconsequential, much like Mary's own\ndeath; neither changed her position on the matter, which she did voice,\ndespite what the 1987 ruling falsely alleges.\n- **Mary Williams:** Died during the precise two-week window required to\nrebut the Land Registry's registration of the land in BP's name—a window we\nbelieve was exploited to finalise this theft. At minimum, this is the case;\nit is more likely she was murdered. Her husband before her too. And my\nfather, William Buckler, given the convenient timing of all their\ndeaths—not to mention the unfair dismissal of my father's appeal, the\nblocking of his ECHR request, the theft and demolition of his property and\nour home prior to his death.\n\n**Our Position:**\nThe Williams family (now the Buckler family) has never ceased our claim. We\nmaintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the\ncurrent registered titles are poisoned by this original fraud. We seek full\nreparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman\narchaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right\nto a fair trial.\n\nPlease provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this\nmatter within 14 days. Please also hold to account those taking steps back\ninto the shadows, as this only makes the matter more clandestine and\ntherefore makes me very jumpy as a military warfare professional. I already\nfly in and out as if on another tour of the Middle East, and my family\nremain hostages under terrorists.\n\nI would also ask that Companies House, who have recently tried to\ncriminalise me, give me some space. They gave me three options to submit\nID: a questionnaire with passport and driving licence (which I provided);\nPost Office verification; or Digital ID. I chose the first option. They\nwill not accept it. But I will not be lured to a location of their\nchoosing, nor will I put any of their tracking ID applications on my\ndevices. I do not trust the regime on that island. Until this and another\nunnamed matter of similar scale is resolved, I consider the British\nGovernment a terrorist organisation and do not recognise its authority. My\nfamily there are hostages under said terrorists. And Church View Close,\nLlandough—23 houses—is a terrorist cell/camp on my land.\n\nMarconi was staying with us in Llandough when he invented radio. This too\nwas covered up. Cardiff City will not put a plaque naming Marconi as the\ninventor on the statue of a radio at Cardiff Bay—not even a plaque to\ncommemorate it. Llandough should be a tourist attraction based on this fact\nalone, rather than the occupying terrorist network's cell of 23 houses, as\nI see it.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\nOn behalf of (and as one of) the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams,\nGreat House Farm, Manor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nCurrent Address: [redacted]\n\n---\n"},{"id":"wb-383c9f92","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-12_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-12","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-12_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-12_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: \"Griffiths, Eleri\" <Eleri.Griffiths@senedd.cymru>\nDate: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:09:55 +0000\nSubject: ATB/RE: ATB/RE: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <CW1P123MB86459FBCD6D0B8A8F685BA6C9A392@CW1P123MB8645.GBRP123.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nHi Requester\n\nI used your correct postcode and you are actually in a Caerdydd Penarth NOT Penybont Bro Morgannwg so the contacts in the previous email are wrong.\n\nYour Senedd Members are\n\nLeticia Gonzalez MS Plaid Cymru ( no known email yet)\nAnna Brychan MS Plaid Cymru Anna.Brychan-MS@senedd.wales<mailto:Anna.Brychan-MS@senedd.wales>\nKiera Marshall MS Plaid Cymru (no known email yet)\nHuw Thomas ( Labour) No known email yet\nJoe Martin (Reform UK)   Joe.Martin-MS@senedd.wales<mailto:%20%20Joe.Martin-MS@senedd.wales%0d>\n\nSorry for giving you the incorrect information – for your interest the postcode was provided by Royal Mail Postcode finder when I typed in the address of Great House Farm.\n\nBest wishes\n\nEleri\n\n\nOddi wrth: Requester <[redacted]>\nAnfonwyd: 11 May 2026 18:52\nAt: Griffiths, Eleri <Eleri.Griffiths@senedd.cymru>\nPwnc: Re: ATB/RE: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nThanks.\n\nFYI that post code is unknown to me.\nCF71 7LR.\n\nMy post code is [redacted].\n([redacted]).\n\nBut I appreciate the prompt reply and thank you.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Hywel Buckler\n\nOn Mon, 11 May 2026, 12:14 Griffiths, Eleri, <Eleri.Griffiths@senedd.cymru<mailto:Eleri.Griffiths@senedd.cymru>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for writing to Heledd.  She has asked me to respond on her behalf.  We were sorry to read of your difficulties.  Unfortunately, we are unable to offer help with your case.  From May the 8th Heledd became a Senedd Member for Pontypridd Cynon Merthyr.  I used the postcode CF71 7LR to check your constituency with this tool Welsh Parliament<https://constituency.senedd.wales/> and found you live in Pen-y-bont Bro Morgannwg.\n\nYour local Senedd Members are:\n\nSarah Rees (Plaid Cymru) Sarah Rees MS<https://senedd.wales/people/sarah-rees-ms/>\nAndrew RT Davies ( Conservative) Andrew RT Davies MS<https://senedd.wales/people/andrew-rt-davies-ms/> (Copied in already)\nSarah Murphy (Labour) sarah.murphy-ms@senedd.wales<mailto:sarah.murphy-ms@senedd.wales>\nMark Hooper (Plaid Cymru) Mark.Hooper-AS@Senedd.Cymru<mailto:Mark.Hooper-AS@Senedd.Cymru>\nSarah Cooper-Lesadd (Reform UK) (Sorry I cannot find this address yet)\nGareth Thomas (Reform UK) (Sorry I cannot find this address yet)\n\nIf you check back on the Senedd website tomorrow all addresses should be available.   This is the link Find a Member Search<https://senedd.wales/find-a-member-of-the-senedd>\n\nI hope this is useful.\n\nYours Sincerely\nEleri\n\nEleri Griffiths\nRheolwr Polisi, Gwaith Achos ac Ymgyrchu\nPolicy, Casework and Campaigns Manager\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DCE1FF.3DFE5360]\n\n\n\nSwyddfa Heledd Fychan AS\nPontypridd Cynon Merthyr\nOffice of Heledd Fychan MS\nPontypridd Cynon Merthyr\n\n\nEleri.Griffiths@Senedd.Cymru<mailto:Eleri.Griffiths@Senedd.Cymru>\n0300 200 6304\n[cidimage003.png@01D7B515.6AAE7DC0]<https://www.facebook.com/HeleddFychanPlaidCymru/>\n[Llun yn cynnwys testun, olwyn, gêr, awyr y nos    Wedi cynhyrchu’r disgrifiad yn awtomatig]<https://twitter.com/heleddfychan>\n[Icon    Description automatically generated]<https://www.instagram.com/heledd_plaid/>\n\nOs nad wyf ar gael cysylltwch â  / If I am not available please contact\nheledd.fychan@senedd.cymru<mailto:heledd.fychan@senedd.cymru> 01443 853 214\n\n\nCaiff yr wybodaeth bersonol yr ydych wedi’i darparu ei thrin yn ôl gofynion GDPR. Os ydych am dderbyn copi o’n Hysbysiad Preifatrwydd, mynnwch gopi drwy ymateb i’r e-bost hwn.\n\nThe personal data you have provided will be treated in accordance with GDPR. If you would like to receive a copy of our GDPR Privacy Notice, you can request one by replying to this email\n\n\n\n\nOddi wrth: Requester <[redacted]<mailto:[redacted]>>\nAnfonwyd: 09 May 2026 23:17\nAt: pensions@bp.com<mailto:pensions@bp.com>; ukgeneralenquiries@bp.com<mailto:ukgeneralenquiries@bp.com>\nCopi/Cc: IDRP@bp.com<mailto:IDRP@bp.com>; reportafraud@landregistry.gov.uk<mailto:reportafraud@landregistry.gov.uk>; complaints@gov.wales<mailto:complaints@gov.wales>; ask@ombudsman-wales.org.uk<mailto:ask@ombudsman-wales.org.uk>; cadw@gov.wales<mailto:cadw@gov.wales>; stephen.doughty.mp@parliament.uk<mailto:stephen.doughty.mp@parliament.uk>; huw.thomas.ms@senedd.wales<mailto:huw.thomas.ms@senedd.wales>; anna.brychan.ms@senedd.wales<mailto:anna.brychan.ms@senedd.wales>; joseph.martin.ms@senedd.wales<mailto:joseph.martin.ms@senedd.wales>; anthony.slaughter.ms@senedd.wales<mailto:anthony.slaughter.ms@senedd.wales>; gcarroll@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:gcarroll@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>; Paul Egan <clerk@llandough-cc.co.uk<mailto:clerk@llandough-cc.co.uk>>; commissioner@south-wales.police.uk<mailto:commissioner@south-wales.police.uk>; heritage@cardiff.gov.uk<mailto:heritage@cardiff.gov.uk>; Swyddfa Heledd Fychan AS - Office of Heledd Fychan MS <heledd.fychan@senedd.wales<mailto:heledd.fychan@senedd.wales>>; rhys.ab.owen@senedd.wales<mailto:rhys.ab.owen@senedd.wales>; James, Joel <joel.james@senedd.wales<mailto:joel.james@senedd.wales>>; Swyddfa Andrew RT Davies - Office of Andrew RT Davies <andrewrt.davies@senedd.wales<mailto:andrewrt.davies@senedd.wales>>; democratic@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:democratic@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>; leader@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:leader@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\nPwnc: Formal Notice Follow Up: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n[https://senedd.wales/media/obuo0sep/senedd_logo_xs.png]\nE-mail protection couldn't recognize this email as this is the first time you received an email from this sender [redacted]<http://gmail.com/>\n\nSir/Madam,\nI am writing on behalf of myself and siblings who are the heirs and successors of Mary Williams of the Williams family, rightful owners and occupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough since 1667 until our dispossession via armed force in 1988.\nI write to summarize our position regarding our historical and ongoing dispossession of Great House Farm, which I alledge involves;\n- Denial of right to be heard by the land registry due to the fact my grandmother Mr Williams (falsy named Mrs Buckler to diminish the Williams ancestral superior land claim) conveniently died and our family were in mourning in the limited window granted to challenge BP registration of our land and property in their names. Much like my grandfather conveniently died too, before  being able to clarify, even to my grandmother Mrs Williams, how her Title ended up in BP's possession. Because until her dying breath she maintained her ownership claim. Despite repeated unlawful attempts over decades to disposition the firm position she maintained about hers and ours undisputed ancestral and superior land claim to the land in question.\nAfter my father's appeal of the BP vs Buckler 1987 ruling was dismissed on grounds of \"heads BP win, tails we lose\" and his home demolished, all money and possessions removed (despite a court injuction ordering nothing be removed) and despite his ECHR request being blocked, and arrest without charge, and hospitalisation and then his convenient death at age 41, our remaining family of mostly women and children, have to this day been too terrified to speak up. According to recently released, supressed ITV news coverage from 1988, bailifs occupying our stolen land and property, even dislocated my mum's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court injunction.\nAnd without the discovery of fraud this year, (which has taken me two decades and a career in military cyber and electronic warfare and the recent innovations in A.I to discover) we had no redress recourse due to the statute of limitation and time passed, ever had we not all been too traumatised like hostages under terrorists to speak out. This whole thing, even unto this day is scandalous treatment of me and my family. Not withstanding I am a war veteran, who left my military career with honours and was employed until 2024 under the Vale of Glamorgan Council/ Welsh Govenrment. Finished my 22 years in Oath BONAFIDE.\nITV coverage supressed until recent months also says neighbours report it was like an SAS Style Operation to remove us by force in 1988. And the men in the video do look SAS. I have subbmitee a FOI to the MOD.\nAnd Margaret Thatchers administration at the time (you Brit'ish) were evidently helping BP claw assets for the UK Governments exit at the time. Which might explain how 30 police and maybe SAS were used to rip us from our home and land.\nLand registry ultimately had check balances lifted and total free reign, while BPs lawyers commited purgergy in their declarations to them; withholding information from and supplying to the land registry false information.\nAll the while Welsh TV simultaneously interviewed Ghadaffi in Lybia in 1988, who report him accusing Thatcher and the Brit'ish State of being the real terrorists, not him. My oath ended in 2024, I'm also a Welsh National. I have no allegiance to the British State. If it acts like my enemy, its my enemy.\nOther media coverage alleged by UK courts to exist from 1974 seems non existence or suppressed too.\nFraud and proceedural unfairness are ultimately rampant in the case of my families dispossession. Aside from all my family members dying at all the convenient junctures instrumental to change the outcome of our dispossession, I still have major concerns with how the MOJ just took months to respond only to fob me off last week. Or how the MP fobbed me off and will not provide a proper response. Or how CADW alledge this is nothing to do with them despite failing to list the farm house as a grade II so it couldn't be demolished. As per a 1700 signature petition, which was practically the whole town at the time. Or the current councillor for Llandough failing to properly reply. Or the fact the national archives report gaps and missing and supressed records. Not withstanding Marconi was staying with us while inventing radio and the town won't even out a plaque up to make that known. Which is more erasure of the history. Like in BPs planning application saying our 800 year old former court house home was just an old delapitated building.\nNot withstanding the supression of the 1870 roman soldier we discovered when changing our floor from stone to timber. Also supressed to hide the sites archaeological significants so housing development could be unlawfully approved. And BP didn't even seek a ruling on ownership, they only saught possession, most likely so that the discovery and significant of the sites archaeological significants could be pretended to not be known until the excavation of our land in 1994. Which is just more evidence of the blatant conspiracy and fraud.\nThis is all the actions of a crime or terrorist network. To install a terrorist cell/ camp. It's worse than just the Brit'ish colonising Wales.\nNot withstanding the child graves secretly moved from the church next door during the exhivation seem to take 10 years to be properly reported on and even then their numbers in the report seem to be under represented.\nThe scandal just goes on and on. It's the gift that keeps giving. There's court mistakes too. The fancy latin words deminish and falsely describe my nans land claim and superior ownership. And language used clearly shows a bias before a ruling. Language used to imply she is almost imagining her ancestral superior land claim to discredit her in the carefully selected wording used by the judge. In court records that use the false legal fiction name fabricated by BP in their license letters document fraud, instead of her actual name. Evidently to shy away from the Williams name and its superior inpenitrable and unbreakable land claim. For which we remain the heirs and successors.\n1667 we aquired the land and property in a 999 year leasehold. And in the early 1900's obtained the superior paper title, free and clear outright equitable ownership, via the deal with Bute Estates quarryman Daniel Thomas. Which led to the tree planting ceremony to affirm this in history.\nFredrick Bucklers transfer of Mrs Williams title to BP and their predecessors without her knowledge or consent isn't legitimate and so has no authority. Him not being able to clarify that transaction due to dying doesn't make it right as Mary Williams maintained her position after his death. She just couldn't prove what she claimed without title. And the adjournment and dismissal of the two hearings in 1974 where she made her case, but without getting the ruling doesn't negate the facts.\nThis was a coordinated campaign of fraud, stealth, and administrative erasure. Over decades.\nSummary of the Fraudulent Dispossession:\n\n  *   The Title Theft: Evidence supports that a \"Title-for-Quarrying\" agreement existed with Daniel Thomas of the Bute Estate. We maintain this title was later secretly and fraudulently sold back to the landlords by Frederick Buckler without the knowledge or consent of the rightful owner, Mary Williams.\n  *   Procedural Fraud (The 1974 License): The 1987 Court of Appeal ruling was predicated on a unilateral \"license letter\" issued by the landlords’ solicitors. We reject this document as a fraudulent instrument of stealth designed to bypass adverse possession rights without Mary Williams’ agreement.\n  *   Identity Erasure: Throughout all legal proceedings, Mary Williams was intentionally misidentified as \"Mrs. Buckler.\" This was a calculated tactic to strip her of her ancestral \"Williams\" lineage and the superior land rights associated with it.\n  *   Exploitation of Mortality:\n\n     *   Frederick Buckler: Died before the truth of the title sale could be brought to light.\n     *   Mary Williams: Died during the precise 2-week window required to rebut the Land Registry’s registration of the land in BP’s name—a window we believe was exploited to finalize a theft.\n     *   William Buckler: His untimely death following the unfair dismissal of his appeal effectively blocked our path to the ECHR.\nOur Position:\nThe Williams family has never ceased its claim. We maintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the current registered titles are \"poisoned\" by this original fraud. We are now seeking full reparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman archaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right to a fair trial.\nPlease provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this matter within 14 days.\nRegards,\nSion Buckler\nOn behalf of and one of the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams\n"},{"id":"wb-03049af4","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-13_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-13","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-13_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-13_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Swyddfa Joe Martin AS - Office of Joe Martin MS <Joe.Martin-MS@senedd.wales>\nDate: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:36:14 +0000\nSubject: Re: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nMessage-ID: <LO3P123MB357917198A075E5ECA2D2DD4D5062@LO3P123MB3579.GBRP123.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email. I am currently in the process of setting up a constituency office, and will reply to your email in full as soon as possible.\n\nKind regards,\n\nJoe Martin MS\n\n\nSent from Outlook for iOS<https://aka.ms/o0ukef>\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[redacted]>\nSent: Tuesday, May 12, 2026 12:18:38 PM\nTo: Swyddfa Joe Martin AS - Office of Joe Martin MS <Joe.Martin-MS@senedd.wales>; Anna.Brychan-MS@senedd.wales <Anna.Brychan-MS@senedd.wales>\nSubject: Resolution of Historical Dispossession and Fraud – Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n[https://senedd.wales/media/obuo0sep/senedd_logo_xs.png]        E-mail protection couldn't recognize this email as this is the first time you received an email from this sender [redacted]\n\nSirs/ Ma'ams,\n\nI write on behalf of myself and my siblings, who are the heirs and successors of the late Mary Williams of the Williams family, the rightful owners and occupiers of Great House Farm, Llandough, since 1667 until our unlawful, unconstitution, brutal and inhumane dispossession by armed force in 1988. With press and courts falsly labelling and treating us as squatters in favor of the false narrative of those who stole my disabled, widow nans fee simple absolute title. For which we remain dispossessed, defrauded and without justice or even narrative justice, unto this day. The public also lost a site of historic and archelogical significants and were lied to about what went on. The land looted of artefacts too, which is a loss to our nation and people.\n\nI apologise if any of this is incoherent. I am the only member of my family willing to speak out; the rest, who are nearly all women (sisters, mum, aunties etc), are petrified of the repercussions, given what happened to our family in the 1980s. Or dead from this. My father, nan, grandad and possibly great grandad and maybe more, all potentially murdered.\n\nAll this is also chilling in that the playbook used here, could be industrial scale and nationwide and have occured to other families too. Our case might be the foundations for a class action for the public.\n\nI write to summarise our position regarding the historical and ongoing dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough, following the landmark legal case *BP v Buckler* [1987], which I allege involved a myriad of fraud, theft, crimes and proceedural unfairness, gaps in records, supressed and concealed records, human rights violations and literally almost every injustice imaginable; not withstanding it was over decades for our family;\n\n- **Denial of the right to be heard by the Land Registry.** My grandmother, Mary Williams (falsely named \"Mrs Buckler\" on the licence letter produced by BP in 1974, in order to diminish the Williams ancestral superior land claim), conveniently died while our family was in mourning during the limited window granted by the Land Registry to challenge BP's registration of our land and property in their name in 1982/83. Similarly, my grandfather died before he was able to clarify—even to my grandmother—how her fee simple absolute title deed ended up in BP's possession. Until her dying breath, she maintained her ownership claim, despite repeated unlawful attempts over decades to dislodge the firm position she held regarding her and our undisputed ancestral and superior land claim. The official records and narrative are wrong; there are court errors, suppressed evidence, procedural unfairness, fraud, and the list goes on.\n\nThe *BP v Buckler* [1987] ruling applied the licence my deceased grandmother held to my father and mother. They never had, nor entered into, any such agreement with BP. The ruling also alleged that my grandmother accepted BP's licence letters by non-response, which was untrue. It further stated that any objection should have been directed to the BP Pension Trust rather than the claimant, BP Properties, which were deemed separate companies. Yet in my father's subsequent appeal against the *BP v Buckler* ruling, his appeal was dismissed on the grounds that the BP companies were effectively the same—so \"heads BP wins, tails we lose.\" Our 800-year-old home was then demolished and all money and possessions removed, despite a court injunction ordering that nothing be removed. My father's ECHR application was blocked; he was arrested without charge, hospitalised, and then he conveniently died at the age of 41. Our remaining family, consisting mostly of women and children, have to this day been too terrified to speak about this case because of the decades of crimes committed against our household by the British State. It was synonymous with a battle or war. I say this as a military warfare professional and Iraq War veteran: a certified and experienced military commander and leader. I concluded my military career with honours as an Acting Sergeant. My profession is cyber and electronic warfare.\n\nAccording to recently declassified, previously suppressed ITV news coverage from 1988, bailiffs occupied our stolen land and property, and even dislocated my mother's shoulder for simply serving them a lawful court injunction. I also question how ITV came to declassify and publish this footage to YouTube a few months ago, after the months I have spent seeking information. That did not go unnoticed. There is liability there, and I do not accept ITV's belief that this quiet release of suppressed news coverage makes the matter right—though the action is appreciated. How did it come to be suppressed in the first place? And why is it cut abruptly, at what appears to be SAS performing a siege on my family home and dislocating my pregnant mother's shoulder?\n\nWithout my discovery of fraud this year—which has taken me two decades, a career in military cyber and electronic warfare, and recent innovations in AI to discover and unravel—we had no redress or recourse due to the statute of limitations and the passage of time, notwithstanding that we were all too traumatised, like hostages under terrorists, to speak out. We have received no support to this day for what we were subjected to.\n\nThis whole affair, even to this day, represents scandalous treatment of me and my family. We never surrendered our claim. The manorial titles of the Manor of Llandough are rightfully ours. The fee simple absolute title has been ours for over a century, a fact that is also suppressed and withheld from the defrauded—and implicated—Land Registry.\n\nI am also a war veteran who left my military career with honours and was employed until 2024 under the Vale of Glamorgan Council / Welsh Government. I completed my 22 years' service oath *bona fide*. I am an indigenous Welsh Briton, and this is my ancestral birthland (established 1667). The disrespect shown by the Vale MP and Llandough Councillor in simply ignoring me and this matter is abhorrent.\n\nITV coverage (suppressed until recent months) also reports that neighbours described the eviction as an \"SAS-style operation\" to remove us by force in 1988 (myself included). The men in the video do look like SAS. I have submitted an FOI request to the MOD. Shareholders of mine are SAS, so I shall find out one way or another, even if I receive an NCND reply. This matter was also raised in Parliament, who classified and disposed of the records.\n\nMargaret Thatcher's administration at the time (the British Government) was evidently assisting BP in clawing assets for the UK Government's sale and exit at the time, which might explain how 30 police—and possibly SAS—were used to rip us from our home and land. The human rights violations remain unanswered.\n\nThe Land Registry ultimately had checks and balances lifted and total free rein during Thatcher's reign, while BP's lawyers evidently committed perjury in their declarations to the Land Registry, withholding information from it and supplying it with false information.\n\nAll the while, Welsh television was simultaneously interviewing Gaddafi in Libya in 1988, where he accused Thatcher and the British State of being the real terrorists, not him. My oath ended in 2024; I am also a Welsh national. I have no allegiance to the British State. If it acts like my enemy, it is my enemy. I am absolutely a Welsh national and counter-officer now that it is so evident the British State waged civil war upon us indigenous Britons—me and my family included—on our ancestral birthland.\n\nOther media coverage alleged by UK courts to exist from 1974 seems non-existent or suppressed too. Much is behind paywalls. This whole case needs to be in the public eye. I have put everyone I can think of on notice.\n\nFraud and procedural unfairness are ultimately rampant in the case of my family's dispossession. Aside from all my family members dying at convenient junctures instrumental in the windows to change the outcome, I still have major concerns regarding how the MOJ took months to respond only to fob me off last week; how the MP fobbed me off and will not provide a proper response; how CADW and Llandough Parish allege this is nothing to do with them, despite CADW failing to list the farmhouse as Grade II so it could be demolished (as per a 1,700-signature petition, which was practically the whole town at the time); the current councillor for Llandough failing to reply properly; and the fact that the National Archives report gaps, missing records, and suppressed records. Notwithstanding that Marconi was staying with us while inventing radio, and the town will not even put a plaque up to commemorate this, which is further erasure of the history and known (but suppressed) archaeological and historic significance of the site. In BP's planning application records, they state that our 800-year-old former courthouse home was merely an old, dilapidated building.\n\nNotwithstanding the suppression of the 1870 Roman soldier remains we discovered when changing our floor from stone to timber, also suppressed to hide the site's archaeological significance so that housing development could be unlawfully approved. BP did not even seek a ruling on ownership; they only sought possession, most likely so that the discovery and significance of the site's archaeology could be pretended not to be known until the excavation of our land in 1994—which is further evidence of blatant conspiracy and fraud.\n\nThese are the actions of a crime or terrorist network, seeking to install a terrorist cell or camp. It is worse than simply the British colonising Wales.\n\nNotwithstanding the child graves secretly moved from the church next door during the excavation, which seemed to take ten years to be properly reported on, and even then their numbers in the report appear to be underrepresented.\n\nThe scandal continues endlessly. There are court errors too. The fancy Latin words diminish and falsely describe my grandmother's land claim and superior ownership (it was \"older than man can remember,\" not merely a \"claim to the land\"). The language used by the court clearly demonstrates bias prior to the ruling—language implying that my late grandmother, Mrs Williams (*not* Mrs Buckler, as they falsely named her in document fraud), was imagining her ancestral superior land claim, in order to discredit her through carefully selected judicial wording.\n\nMy siblings and I remain the heirs and successors and landowners. Nothing has lawfully broken or undone that claim. We demand that the fraud, corruption, gaps in records, false records, and myriad crimes committed against us be addressed and not ignored. There should be a Senedd public inquiry into this. My family should not be dispossessed a second longer. We are seriously looking at £100 million in reparations if the truth of this matter becomes known, given the scale of the scandal and injustice.\n\nIn 1667 we acquired the land and property in a 999-year lease (virtual freehold). In the early 1900s we obtained the superior paper title—free and clear, outright equitable ownership—via the deal with Bute Estate quarryman Daniel Thomas, which led to the tree-planting ceremony to affirm this in history. *(See attached.)*\n\nFrederick Buckler's transfer of Mrs Williams's equitable title to BP and their predecessors, without her knowledge or consent, is not legitimate and should never have stood, nor does it stand to reason. His inability to clarify the details of the alleged transaction due to his convenient death afterwards does not make it right, as Mary Williams maintained her position after his death. It was never his title to sell, even if he did. My grandmother was left unable to prove her standing, and the 1974 hearing was adjourned. The dismissal of the second hearings in 1974 due to the licence letter issued by BP (resorting to identity and document fraud) does not negate the fact that there was never a ruling stating BP owned our land, despite their purchasing my grandmother's stolen fee simple absolute title deed. BP only ever sought possession. They could not obtain a ruling because it would have meant discovery, unveiling the archaeological significance that would have prevented land and housing development.\n\nThis was a coordinated campaign of fraud, stealth, and administrative erasure spanning decades, employing force, secrecy, and fraudulent licence. By hook and by crook we were dispossessed of our land. Thatcher—and potentially the SAS—make it, at the least, an allodial/eminent domain seizure, in which case we should still be due compensation.\n\nI fail to see the proclaimed authority of the other men on my land, alleging themselves to be a government and citizens rather than terrorists, who both ostracised and held my family hostage, if legitimacy does not exist. You need legitimacy to claim authority.\n\n**Summary of the Fraudulent Dispossession:**\n\n**The Title Theft:** Evidence supports that a \"Title-for-Quarrying\" agreement existed with Daniel Thomas of the Bute Estate. We obtained this fee simple absolute title lawfully, but it was later secretly and fraudulently taken and sold back to Bute / Western Ground Rents / BP without the knowledge or consent of the rightful owner, Mary Williams. Parliament even stated on record how criminal Western Ground Rents were.\n\n**Procedural Fraud (The 1974 Licence):** The 1987 Court of Appeal ruling was predicated on a unilateral \"licence letter\" issued by the landlords' solicitors. We reject this ruling. It should be set aside on grounds of fraud.\n\n**Identity Erasure:** Throughout all legal proceedings, Mary Williams was intentionally misidentified as \"Mrs Buckler.\" This was a calculated tactic to strip her of her ancestral \"Williams\" lineage and the superior land rights and claim associated with it.\n\n**Exploitation of Mortality:**\n- **Frederick Buckler:** Died before the circumstances of how Mary was dispossessed of her title—and how the other parties regained possession after the lawful Daniel Thomas (and/or Anthony Williams) dealings with Bute Estate—could be clarified. This is inconsequential, much like Mary's own death; neither changed her position on the matter, which she did voice, despite what the 1987 ruling falsely alleges.\n- **Mary Williams:** Died during the precise two-week window required to rebut the Land Registry's registration of the land in BP's name—a window we believe was exploited to finalise this theft. At minimum, this is the case; it is more likely she was murdered. Her husband before her too. And my father, William Buckler, given the convenient timing of all their deaths—not to mention the unfair dismissal of my father's appeal, the blocking of his ECHR request, the theft and demolition of his property and our home prior to his death.\n\n**Our Position:**\nThe Williams family (now the Buckler family) has never ceased our claim. We maintain that the land was taken through criminal stealth and that the current registered titles are poisoned by this original fraud. We seek full reparations for the loss of ancestral wealth, the destruction of the Roman archaeological site on the property, and the systematic denial of our right to a fair trial.\n\nPlease provide a formal response and update regarding your position on this matter within 14 days. Please also hold to account those taking steps back into the shadows, as this only makes the matter more clandestine and therefore makes me very jumpy as a military warfare professional. I already fly in and out as if on another tour of the Middle East, and my family remain hostages under terrorists.\n\nI would also ask that Companies House, who have recently tried to criminalise me, give me some space. They gave me three options to submit ID: a questionnaire with passport and driving licence (which I provided); Post Office verification; or Digital ID. I chose the first option. They will not accept it. But I will not be lured to a location of their choosing, nor will I put any of their tracking ID applications on my devices. I do not trust the regime on that island. Until this and another unnamed matter of similar scale is resolved, I consider the British Government a terrorist organisation and do not recognise its authority. My family there are hostages under said terrorists. And Church View Close, Llandough—23 houses—is a terrorist cell/camp on my land.\n\nMarconi was staying with us in Llandough when he invented radio. This too was covered up. Cardiff City will not put a plaque naming Marconi as the inventor on the statue of a radio at Cardiff Bay—not even a plaque to commemorate it. Llandough should be a tourist attraction based on this fact alone, rather than the occupying terrorist network's cell of 23 houses, as I see it.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\nOn behalf of (and as one of) the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Manor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nCurrent Address: [redacted]\n\n---\n"},{"id":"wb-cd0a0a56","subject":"Consortium correspondence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-14","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-correspondence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: South Wales Police Commissioner - GM <COMMISSIONER@south-wales.police.uk>\nDate: Thu, 14 May 2026 08:36:04 +0000\nSubject: Our Reference: LPB/26/0781\nMessage-ID: <CWXP123MB52995A1A54873EF81D6467FDEC072@CWXP123MB5299.GBRP123.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nThank you for your e-mail received 10 May 2026, addressed to the South Wales Police and Crime Commissioner.\n\nThe Commissioner and her Team very much welcome correspondence from the public and use this to aid our understanding of the issues important to our communities and monitor developing themes within the public experiences shared. This feedback is used to support the Chief Constable in shaping South Wales Police's priorities and services through understanding and responding to our communities' needs.\n\nWe are sorry to hear of the difficulties you have been experiencing; however we must advise that South Wales Police and the South Wales Police and Crime Commissioner are two separate organisations. The Commissioner and her team do not have access to Police systems to allocate members of staff to respond to matters as operational policing matters remain the responsibility of the Chief Constable, however we can advise that reports and concerns regarding operational policing matters can be reported to South Wales Police by dialling 101 or by using their website<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/tua/tell-us-about/soh/seen-or-heard/>. You can also give crime information anonymously to Crimestoppers<https://crimestoppers-uk.org/>.\n\nI trust this guidance will be of assistance to you.\n\nYours sincerely,\nElinor\n[cid:image001.png@01DCE384.AC4C6BF0]\nSWP59089\nSwyddog Cymorth Sicrwydd a Chydymffurfiaeth | Assurance and Compliance Support Officer\nComisiynydd yr Heddlu a Throseddu De Cymru | South Wales Police and Crime Commissioner\nFfôn/Phone: [redacted]\n[cid:image012.png@01DCE385.12DA1570]<https://www.comisiynydddecymru.org.uk/blaenoriaethaur-comisiynwyr/cynllun-heddlu-troseddu-a-chyfiawnder-de-cymru-2025-29/>[cid:image013.png@01DCE385.12DA1570]<https://www.comisiynydddecymru.org.uk/cymorth-a-chefnogaeth/cysylltwch-a-ni/>[cid:image014.png@01DCE385.12DA1570]<https://www.southwalescommissioner.org.uk/help-and-support/contact-us/>\n[A black background with blue text  AI-generated content may be incorrect.]\n[An orange and white logo  AI-generated content may be incorrect.]\n\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg ac yn Saesneg.\nByddwn yn ymateb yn eich iaith o ddewis.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. We will respond in your language of choice.\n\n\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/.\n"},{"id":"wb-6926a330","subject":"Consortium correspondence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.002.txt","date":"2026-05-14","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1_002.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-correspondence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-14_consortium-correspondence_bpvsbuckler__en_v0-0-1_002.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Support <info@crunchbase.com>\nDate: Thu, 14 May 2026 01:03:08 +0000\nSubject: [Request Received]\nMessage-ID: <0027RP1V7MK_6a051f4caaa36_988252d4d2c818_sprut@zendesk.com>\n\n##- Please type your reply above this line -##\n\n<img src=\"https://theme.zdassets.com/theme_assets/1324366/b7410f9cf3aea41d5098a84f0eb1c30df0864e3d.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;\">\n\n<p>Thanks for reaching out to us! Your request (2794823) has been received and is being reviewed by the Crunchbase team. Please allow up to 2 business days for our team to get back to you.</p>\n\nLooking for info about how to edit a Crunchbase profile, learn about Crunchbase subscriptions, need help with billing, or more? Visit the <a href=\"https://support.crunchbase.com/hc/en-us\">Crunchbase Knowledge Center</a> for our FAQs and helpful articles!\n\nLooking to seek help from or start conversations with other users? Check out our new <a href=\"https://support.crunchbase.com/hc/en-us/community/topics\">Crunchbase User Community</a> for this and more!\n\nTo add additional comments, just reply to this email.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------\nThis email is a service from Crunchbase Support Center.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[0027RP-1V7MK]"},{"id":"wb-1aed763b","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-14_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-14","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-14_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-14_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Thu, 14 May 2026 15:40:04 -0300\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987 Thatcher & SAS\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V4AsCV+BOx05Sx0_HjZE8oM0cSB2ga4vN6PrYztuB7BMg@mail.gmail.com>\n\nI am writing regarding this video and case;\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nThis appears to be previously suppressed or unaired ITV footage relating to\nthe 1987–1988 BP/Buckler dispossession case. I was a toddler at the time\nand that is my mum on TV.\n\nI am now a former military cyber warfare professional. I left my military\ncareer with honours. I spent the last 2 years of my 22 years in oath\nemployed by the Welsh Government/ Vale of Glamorgan Council up until 2024.\nI am bonafide.\n\nThe material allegedly contains significant evidence contradicting the\naccepted public narrative surrounding the events, including possible\nprocedural irregularities and the treatment of the family involved. Maybe\neven SAS in addition to the newspaper reports of 30 police to remove my\npregnant mum, terminally ill dad and siblings and me who were toddlers at\nthe time. The footage and associated materials have only recently come into\ncirculation and may be of substantial public interest.\n\nI am seeking to preserve the material properly and ensure it is\nindependently authenticated and reviewed by experienced investigative\njournalists. I also possess supporting historical documentation and\ntimelines connected to the case.\n\nAt this stage I am requesting confidential contact with an investigative\nproducer or journalist before wider disclosure. Original copies and\nprovenance information can be made available.\n\nMy family held virtual freehold (999 year lease) of the land from 1667. In\nthe late 1800's after Marconi stayed with us in our 800 year old former\ncourt house 10 bedroom home, while inventing radio, we did a deal with Bute\nEstate and Quarryman contractor Daniel Thomas, allowing our farmland to be\nquarried in exchange for the manorial fee simple absolute title. Which my\ngrandmother Mrs Williams held.\n\nDaniel Thomas died. Mary's dad and husband died. And the title was stolen\nfrom Mary Williams. And in the window Mary had go rebuttle BP registering\nher land with the land registry in 1982 after committing purgergy and\nwithholding information from the land registry (and erazing the name\nWilliams falsly alleging she was Mrs Buckler in fraudulent license letters\nin 1974 after obstructing Mrs Williams having her day in court and ruling\nin 1974) Mrs Mary Williams conveniently died too.\n\nThe fraudulent license letter terms were then applied to my parents who had\nno such agreement with BP in BP vs Buckler 1987. My dad appealed on grounds\nBP Pension Trust should have been the claimant not BP Properties Ltd. The\nappeal was dismissed on grounds they were effectively the same company. But\nwhen that same judge awarded BP possession he said my nans rebuttle of BP\nPension Trusts claim didn't count as the claimant BP Properties was a\nseparate company. My dads ECHR request was blocked then ge conveniently\ndied age 42 in 1991.\n\nMy councillor for Llandough wont reply.\nMy Brit'ish Muslim MP wont reply.\nCadw say its nothing to do with them after ignoring a petition and delaying\ninstead of listing our home as a grade II so it couldn't be demolished. The\nnation archives say theres gaps in the Bute records which support we held\nmanorial fee simple absolute title until it was stolen. My nan maintained\nunwaiveeingly she was the owner until her convenient abrupt death in 1982.\n\nWe got title fair and square. BP never got a ruling their claim with our\nstolen title was more superior. Press labelled us squatters. SAS appeared\nto have been used by Thatcher to force us out. But our claim remains and\nunchallenged. And now I have proven fraud, fraud unravels all. And the\nlimitation clock only begin from discovery not occurance of the fraud.\n\nSince we got title and did our tree planting ceremony to celebrate. We have\nbeen the subject of a death of a thousands cuts for decades. Proceedural\nunfairness, court mistakes, supressed coverage. And I am trying to speak to\nMinistry of Justice (who just took 6 months to reply only to dismiss me)\nand land registry (who converted my query and concern into a complaint only\nto dismiss it as resolved having done nothing). Thatcher lifted any check\nbalances they had to do at the time so that BP were able to register our\nland in their names.\n\nThis is an outrage. There were child graves in the church next to us which\nwere quietly moves, no press coverage. A decade until the exhivation in\n1994 was reported and the child graves under states in the report by a\nmatter of hundreds. The 1870 roman soldier we reported was also surpessed,\nso to  to this day is Marconi's stay with us while inventing radio. All so\nthey could get planning permission to build the 23 houses there on our\nstolen land. Instead of listing our home as a Grade II they called it an\nold ruin barn and building in the planning applications. They pretended not\nto know about the sites archelogical and historic significants to build\nhouses. The excavation was one of burials biggest recorded in welsh\nhistory. Under our farm was a lot of history with many artifacts now in\nmuseums. So we were looted.\n\nMy family are too terrified to speak out. Like insigenous welsh hostages\nunder Brit'ish colonial rule and terrorists. Its absurd in 2026 but\nevidently the danger is real.\n\nI find it no coincidence when I placed everyone on notice about this fraud\nI discovered companies house rejected my valid passport and driving license\nand fined me for not providing ID after providing it then alledge I will be\ncriminalised if I dont install a digital id tracking app or go into a post\noffice.\n\nPlease investigate and you will find the 1,000 cuts I speak off. But we are\nstill here (Yma o Hyd). My brother Rhys is the rightful Lord of Manor of\nLlandough. My two sisters Lady's. We will seek reperations through our\nfamily lawyer but we want this fought in the open and not in the shadows in\nclandestine civil war ways. I am a military cyber and electronic warfare\nprofessional and I have the corrupt Brit'ish State who put my family\nthrough all this for the last century, dead to rights. No matter all of\ntheir murder, fraud, lawfare, procedural unfairness, court \"mistakes\" ,\ncollusion with BP, abuse of power and human rights violations.\n\nThis was an act and decleration of civil war upon us. I am in effect now a\ncounter officer in this matter.\n\nI am currently at the Welsh Settlement in Argentina to rebuild a replica of\nmy farm for it to be somewhat open to the public. So this story can be told\nand shared forever. Here they celebrate Welsh culture and history unlike\nthe colonised Wales that still tries to bury this. In Cardiff Bay theres a\nstatute of Radio with no plaque to name Marconi as he was right wing.\nCardiff council openly confess this. Meanwhile there's not even a park\nbench plaque in Llandough to commemorate Marconi was ever there let alone\nit being the birthplace of Radio. Just 23 charscterless houses and a parish\nwho also ignore this like the councillor and MP.\n\nI urge you to investigate and report.\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\n[redacted]\n\nFYI my aunty is Shan Cothi.\nMy uncle founded Tigertailz.\nMy grandad was Ray Smith who starred in TV series  Dempsey and Makepeace.\nMy other uncle is Joshua Richards who is Buewolf in Emmerdale and starred\nin Troy with Brad Pitt.\n\nWe are the land.\n"},{"id":"wb-1c1ec99f","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-15","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Fri, 15 May 2026 22:06:01 -0700\nSubject: FORMAL NOTICE: State-Sanctioned Dispossession of Great House Farm (Former Estate WA231076)\nMessage-ID: 19e2f2d5abfb3f85\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI am writing as the rightful executor of the estate, administering my family trust and estate, concerning the state-sanctioned dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough. Our investigation has confirmed that our fee simple absolute manorial title (which is distinct from the virtual freehold 999-year lease we acquired in 1667) was never sold, surrendered, or extinguished.\n\nOur title was stolen, and we put you on notice that the statute of limitations has not passed, as it commences from the discovery of the fraud, not the occurrence of it. We maintain that the 'Death of a Thousand Cuts' we suffered—a combination of procedural unfairness, abuse of power, fraud, concealment, perjury, gaps in records, and court mistakes—is evidence of a conspiracy to dispossess us of our lawful inheritance.\n\nWe hereby put the State on notice regarding:\n1. The deliberate stalling of the Cadw emergency listing process in 1988, which directly facilitated the demolition of the farm.\n2. The removal of Williams/Buckler title documentation from Cardiff Library in 1984, which remains an unexplained erasure of public records.\n3. The procedural unfairness of the 1987 Court of Appeal judgment which denied our rightful claim through inconsistent judicial logic.\n\nWe are formally requesting the production of all records held by the National Archives, Cadw, and Vale of Glamorgan Council regarding these events. \n\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n[redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-7b165ece","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.001.txt","date":"2026-05-15","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.001.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-15_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.001.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Fri, 15 May 2026 22:07:18 -0700\nSubject: FORMAL NOTICE: Unlawful Dispossession of Great House Farm (Former Estate WA231076)\nMessage-ID: 19e2f2e84ffead06\n\nDear Legal Team,\n\nI am writing as the rightful executor of the estate, administering my family trust and estate, concerning the unlawful dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough. Our investigation has confirmed that our fee simple absolute manorial title (which is distinct from the virtual freehold 999-year lease we acquired in 1667) was never sold, surrendered, or extinguished.\n\nOur title was stolen, and we put you on notice that the statute of limitations has not passed, as it commences from the discovery of the fraud, not the occurrence of it. We maintain that the 'Death of a Thousand Cuts' we suffered—a combination of procedural unfairness, abuse of power, fraud, concealment, perjury, gaps in records, and court mistakes—is evidence of a conspiracy to dispossess us of our lawful inheritance.\n\nWe put you on formal notice of the following findings:\n1. The 1916 'tenancy' was a legal fiction used to facilitate land seizure.\n2. The 1987 BP v Buckler judgment relied on judicial manipulation where BP Pension Trust and BP Properties were inconsistently ruled as separate and identical entities to suit BP's interest (\"Heads/Tails\" fraud).\n3. The 1988 demolition of Great House Farm was a bad-faith act to destroy evidence.\n4. Essential title documents were stolen from public custody in 1984.\n\nWe hereby demand the production of:\n- All internal records regarding the 1938 Western Ground Rents reversion conveyance.\n- All internal BP/BP Properties documentation regarding the 1974 'Licence to Occupy' operation.\n\nWe await your response within 14 days.\n\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n[redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-40f6107e","subject":"Consortium formal notice BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-16_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-16","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-16_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-formal-notice-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-16_consortium-formal_notice_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Sat, 16 May 2026 02:02:21 -0300\nSubject: FORMAL NOTICE: State-Sanctioned Dispossession of Great House Farm (Former Estate WA231076)\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V6qvtSmUiOL=bAM9eQyGtSj_mHR_m-YzHCFk-8AU0sNVQ@mail.gmail.com>\n\nSirs/Mesdames,\n\nI am writing on behalf of the heirs of Mary Williams concerning the state-sanctioned dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough. Our investigation has uncovered that the family's superior manorial title was undermined through a series of \"Death of a Thousand Cuts\" (DoaTC) events, involving public institutions.\n\nWe hereby put the State on notice regarding:\n1. The deliberate stalling of the Cadw emergency listing process in 1988, which directly facilitated the demolition of the farm.\n2. The removal of Williams/Buckler title documentation from Cardiff Library in 1984, which remains an unexplained erasure of public records.\n3. The procedural unfairness of the 1987 Court of Appeal judgment which denied the family's rightful claim through inconsistent judicial logic.\n\nWe are formally requesting the production of all records held by the National Archives, Cadw, and Vale of Glamorgan Council regarding these events. We maintain that the title to Great House Farm remains rightfully with the family and has never been lawfully surrendered.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-668f2a60","subject":"Consortium evidence BP v Buckler","name":"2026-05-17_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","date":"2026-05-17","dateStatus":"filename-date-unverified","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/2026-05-17_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","threadSlug":"consortium-evidence-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bpvsbuckler"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["bpvsbuckler"],"sourcePath":"text/2026-05-17_consortium-evidence_bpvsbuckler_en_v0.0.1.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"From: Requester <[redacted]>\nDate: Sun, 17 May 2026 01:11:13 -0300\nSubject: BP vs Buckler, Great House Farm, Llandough\nMessage-ID: <CAAuJ3V4LnwrosJy0ZxmJ9Ssd_4vhBVZSYF1ap3c+E-jgjG4aag@mail.gmail.com>\n\nTo whom it may concern,\n\nI am writing as the child of Branwen and William (“Billy”) Buckler\nregarding the destruction of Great House Farm, Llandough, and the\nlong-running dispute surrounding BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987].\n\nI have compiled a substantial historical archive, including newspaper\nreports, court references, family testimony, archaeological material,\nestate history, and public records relating to Great House Farm (“Ty\nMawr”), a site associated with medieval, monastic, and Roman occupation.\n\nThe archive is currently being made into a website at:\n\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nThe material raises serious unresolved questions regarding:\n\n• The treatment of us Williams/Buckler family’s longstanding occupation and\nasserted ownership claims. • The repeated use of possession proceedings\nwithout a full adjudication of superior title. • Missing or allegedly\nsuppressed title documentation connected to Bute estate transfers and later\ntransactions. • The demolition of an allegedly medieval structure during an\nactive heritage controversy. • Whether the archaeological significance of\nthe site was fully disclosed during planning and demolition processes. •\nThe wider public interest and cultural significance of the site and its\ndestruction.\n\nIt's looking to me like my family actually did obtain fee simple absolute\nand manorial title. Then it was stolen and attempts were made by the\npossessor of the stolen title, to make my family lessee's / tenants as we\nwere when we were on the virtual freehold (999 year lease) aquired in 1667.\nThereafter it appears to be a death of a thousand cuts of proceedural\nunfairness, audacity, fraud, court \"mistakes\" , purgery and more.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nContemporaneous newspaper coverage from the 1970s and 1980s demonstrates\nthat these concerns were publicly known at the time, including heritage\nobjections, petitions, and public claims of ancestral ownership.\n\nI am requesting:\n\n   1. Review and preservation consideration of all surviving records\n   connected to Great House Farm.\n   2. Clarification as to whether any formal heritage review or\n   investigation into the demolition process was ever completed.\n   3. Guidance regarding access to archival and planning materials relevant\n   to the site.\n   4. Consideration of whether this matter warrants renewed historical or\n   heritage examination.\n\nI appreciate that some claims remain disputed or unproven, and I am not\nasking recipients to accept every allegation as established fact. However,\nI believe the totality of the historical material warrants serious review\nrather than dismissal.\n\nI would be grateful for acknowledgement of receipt and guidance on the\nappropriate next steps.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\n\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n"},{"id":"wb-5782a260","subject":"A survey of manor of Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_a-survey-of-manor-of-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_a-survey-of-manor-of-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"a-survey-of-manor-of-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_a-survey-of-manor-of-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/digitisations/19c0f1a9-1d60-44df-9e73-d79911dbf7ed/sequence/item:33/zxy:7.454,0.246,0.968?q=Great%20House%20farm%2C%20llandough\n\nSent from [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) for Android."},{"id":"wb-53dbeca3","subject":"Atb re cais am ddeiseb ac ymchwiliad cyhoeddus achos buckler","name":"0000-00-00_atb_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_atb_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"atb-re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_atb_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester,\r\n\r\nDiolch am eich neges.\r\n\r\nFel dwedodd Lara, y ffordd gorau nawr bydd i greu deiseb trwy ein system arlein. https://deisebau.senedd.cymru/deisebau/gwirio\r\n\r\nMwy o manylion yma,\r\n\r\nGareth\r\n\r\n\r\nOddi wrth: Requester <[redacted]>\r\nAnfonwyd: 17 February 2026 13:32\r\nAt: Petitions Committee | Y Pwyllgor Deisebau <petitions@senedd.wales>\r\nPwnc: Re: Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)\r\n\r\n\r\nLara,\r\n\r\nDiolch am eich arweiniad.\r\n\r\nRwyf wedi mireinio fy mhethos arfaethedig ymhellach er mwyn ehangu ei gwmpas. Mae'n cynnwys nawr alwadau am ymchwiliad i achosion hanesyddol tebyg lluosog yng Nghymru, gan gynnwys archwilio problemau systemig posibl fel twyll, gorthrymu tystiolaeth, neu anwybyddu/gweithio o amgylch gwarchodaethau amaethyddol a threftadaeth mewn anghytundebau meddiannu anghyfreithlon—gan o bosibl atal y cloc cyfyngu ar feddiannu anghyfreithlon yn anghyfreithlon neu yn anghyfansoddiadol—tra'n defnyddio Fferm Great House (BP v Buckler 1987) fel prif enghraifft.\r\n\r\nMae'r ffocws yn parhau i fod yn gadarn ar faterion datganoledig: polisi amgylchedd hanesyddol Cymru, gwarchodaethau amaethyddol, rôl CADW, a diwygiadau i fynd i'r afael ag unrhyw fylchau a nodir, heb geisio ailymweld â dyfarniadau llys penodol.\r\n\r\nRwy'n cadarnhau bod gennyf gyfeiriad yng Nghymru: [redacted]. Rwy'n etholwr yn Nyffryn Morgannwg ac rwyf wedi ysgrifennu at yr AS presennol a'r Cynghorydd Carroll yn Llandochau; maent yn ymwybodol o'r mater a chredaf eu bod yn edrych i mewn iddo.\r\n\r\nOs caiff ei fframio fel hyn—gan bwysleisio \"dosbarth\" posibl o ffermydd/teuluoedd Cymreig yr effeithir arnynt a methiannau polisi ehangach—a ydych chi'n credu y byddai'n bodloni'r safonau'n ddigonol i ennill sylw'r Pwyllgor a mynd ymlaen i gyflwyno/cyhoeddi?\r\n\r\nNid yw twyll byth yn rhy bell yn y gorffennol, gan nad yw'r cyfnod cyfyngu yn berthnasol mewn amgylchiadau o'r fath ac fe'i datodolir i gyd yn ôl y gyfraith. Mae hefyd yn gyfyngedig o'r dyddiad y cafodd ei ddarganfod—ac rwyf newydd ei ddarganfod—ac nid o ddyddiad y twyll honedig.\r\n\r\nEr gwaethaf hynny, rydym yn dal yn deulu Cymreig brodorol dadfeddiannol ar ein tir geni hynafiaid. Rydym yn dal yma.\r\n\r\nOs na, pa gamau eraill y byddech chi'n eu hargymell (er enghraifft, ymgysylltu ag Aelod o'r Senedd, adrannau Llywodraeth Cymru fel CADW, neu sianeli eraill ar gyfer codi materion systemig tir/amaethyddol)?\r\n\r\nByddai unrhyw gyngor ar gryfhau'r geiriad neu'r dystiolaeth ategol yn cael ei werthfawrogi'n fawr cyn i mi gyflwyno.\r\n\r\nDiolch—mae'r mater hwn o bwysigrwydd sylweddol i gyfanrwydd diwylliannol, amaethyddol a hanesyddol Cymru.\r\n\r\nCofion cynhes,\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\n...................  [SAESNEG/ ENGLISH] .....................\r\n\r\nThanks for your guidance.\r\n\r\nI've further refined my proposed petition to broaden its scope, incorporating calls for an inquiry into multiple similar historical cases in Wales. This includes examining the possibility of systemic issues like fraud, suppression of evidence, or ignoring/working around agricultural and heritage protections in adverse possession disputes—potentially to unlawfully or unconstitutionally stop limitation clock on adverse possession—while using the Great House Farm (BP v Buckler 1987) as a key example. The focus remains on devolved matters: Welsh historic environment policy, agricultural safeguards, CADW's role, and reforms to address gaps without revisiting specific court judgments.\r\n\r\nAnd yes I have an address, it's [redacted]. I am a constituent in the Vale of Glamorgan and I have written to the current MP and councillor Carroll in Llandough, they are aware and I trust they are looking into it.\r\n\r\nIf framed this way—emphasizing a possible \"class\" of affected Welsh farms/families and broader policy failures—do you believe it would meet the standards to gain the Committee's attention and proceed to submission/publication?\r\n\r\nFraud is never too far in the past as the statute of limitation doesn't apply in such circumstances and furthermore it unravels all according to law. It is also only limited from the date it was discovered and I recently discovered, not from the date of occurrence of the alleged fraud.\r\n\r\nNotwithstanding we are still an dispossessed indigenous Welsh family on our ancestral birthland. We are still here.\r\n\r\nFailing that, what alternative steps do you recommend (e.g., approaching a Member of the Senedd, Welsh Government departments like CADW, or other channels for raising systemic land/agricultural issues)?\r\n\r\nAny advice on strengthening wording or evidence would be appreciated before submission.\r\n\r\nThank you—this matter holds significant importance for Welsh cultural, agricultural, and historical integrity.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler [redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-77fd8a01","subject":"Atisn 27021","name":"0000-00-00_atisn-27021_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_atisn-27021_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_atisn-27021_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Mike, I see, silly me.\r\n\r\nThank you for your email and for confirming receipt and handling of ATISN\r\n27021.\r\n\r\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I would be grateful if searches include both\r\ndigital and archived/historical records held by Cadw, the Welsh Government,\r\nand any predecessor bodies or contracted advisors.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your response by 25 June 2026.\r\n\r\nYours sincerely,\r\nSion Buckler\r\n\r\nOn Tue, 2 Jun 2026 at 02:17, <Michael.Weatherhead@gov.wales> wrote:\r\n\r\n> Good morning Requester,\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> My name is Mike Weatherhead. My details are at the end of the below email.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Thanks\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> -Mike\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> *From:* Requester <[redacted]>\r\n> *Sent:* 01 June 2026 23:08\r\n> *To:* Weatherhead, Michael (LCC - Cadw) <Michael.Weatherhead@gov.wales>\r\n> *Subject:* Re: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr.\r\n> Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (ATISN 27021)\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Thank you.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Might I have your name please?\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Force/Stealth & Secrecy is the basis of the concern I'm raising.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Regards,\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Requester\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> On Mon, 1 Jun 2026, 12:58 , <Michael.Weatherhead@gov.wales> wrote:\r\n>\r\n> Dear Requester,\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> *Great House Farm, Llandough*\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Thank you for your request which I received on 1 June 2026. You asked for:\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>    1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\r\n>    2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\r\n>    reports concerning the building.\r\n>    3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\r\n>    authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\r\n>    concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\r\n>    protection of the property.\r\n>    4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\r\n>    statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\r\n>    5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\r\n>    archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\r\n>    6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing,\r\n>    preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the\r\n>    property.\r\n>    7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\r\n>    representations seeking preservation of the building.\r\n>    8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by\r\n>    Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> You will receive a response by 25 June 2026. If you have any queries\r\n> about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address\r\n> below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future\r\n> correspondence *(ATISN 27021).*\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> The request you sent me contains personal information about you - for\r\n> example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data\r\n> processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data\r\n> Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public\r\n> task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a\r\n> response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your\r\n> request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your\r\n> personal information and all other information relating to your request for\r\n> three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your\r\n> personal information will then be disposed of securely.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Under data protection legislation, you have the right:\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>    - to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access\r\n>    it\r\n>    - to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\r\n>    - to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\r\n>    - for (in certain circumstances) your data to be ‘erased’\r\n>    - to (in certain circumstances) data portability\r\n>    - to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office\r\n>    (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> For further information about the information which the Welsh Government\r\n> holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR,\r\n> please see contact details below:\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Data Protection Officer\r\n>\r\n> Welsh Government\r\n>\r\n> Cathays Park\r\n>\r\n> CARDIFF\r\n>\r\n> CF10 3NQ\r\n>\r\n> Email: DataProtectionOfficer@gov.wales\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> The contact details for the Information Commissioner’s Office are:\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Wycliffe House\r\n>\r\n> Water Lane\r\n>\r\n> Wilmslow\r\n>\r\n> Cheshire\r\n>\r\n> SK9 5AF\r\n>\r\n> Website: www.ico.org.uk\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Any information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or\r\n> Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh\r\n> Government’s Disclosure Log (at\r\n> https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en\r\n> ).\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Yours sincerely,\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Mike Weatherhead\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Arweinydd Tîm Gwaith Achosion / Casework Team Leader\r\n>\r\n> Polisi a Gwarchod / Policy and Protection\r\n>\r\n> Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment Inspectorate\r\n>\r\n> Cadw\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> *From:* Requester <[redacted]>\r\n> *Sent:* 28 May 2026 06:29\r\n> *To:* Freedom of Information Officer <Freedom.ofinformation@gov.wales>;\r\n> Listed Buildings / Adeiladau Rhestredig <listedbuildings@gov.wales>\r\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth,\r\n> Vale of Glamorgan\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Dear Freedom of Information Officer,\r\n>\r\n> I am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw\r\n> concerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr),\r\n> Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\r\n>\r\n> I request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\r\n>\r\n>    1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\r\n>    2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\r\n>    reports concerning the building.\r\n>    3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\r\n>    authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\r\n>    concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\r\n>    protection of the property.\r\n>    4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\r\n>    statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\r\n>    5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\r\n>    archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\r\n>    6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing,\r\n>    preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the\r\n>    property.\r\n>    7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\r\n>    representations seeking preservation of the building.\r\n>    8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by\r\n>    Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\r\n>\r\n> For the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than\r\n> an explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\r\n>\r\n> If any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I\r\n> would be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the\r\n> records.\r\n>\r\n> I would prefer the information in electronic form.\r\n>\r\n> Yours faithfully,\r\n>\r\n> Requester Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant). Heir & Successors of Mary Williams,\r\n> Great House Farm, Llandough\r\n>\r\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\r\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\r\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd yn\r\n> esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich\r\n> preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb\r\n> yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg\r\n> yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this\r\n> email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the\r\n> protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then\r\n> our Privacy Notice\r\n> <https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en>\r\n> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your\r\n> privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence\r\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\r\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\r\n>\r\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\r\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\r\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd\r\n> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu\r\n> eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon\r\n> ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn\r\n> Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh\r\n> Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh\r\n> Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the\r\n> Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice\r\n> <https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en>\r\n> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your\r\n> privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence\r\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\r\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\r\n>\r\n"},{"id":"wb-3754fdee","subject":"Automatic reply BP v Buckler great house far