":"text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Automatic reply: BP vs Buckler\nFrom: NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP)\nDate: Fri, 14 Nov 2025 12:49 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHello,\n\nThank you for reaching out to me. This is just a quick note to confirm that we’ve received your email.\n\nAs your MP for the Vale of Glamorgan, my priority is supporting local constituents who need help with urgent issues. I receive a high volume of emails every day, so while I will do my best to get back to you as soon as possible, there may be a slight delay—especially if you’re contacting me about policy matters or upcoming legislation. Please know that your message has been logged, and I’ll respond as soon as I can.\n\nConstituency Casework\n\nIf you need my help with a personal case, please make sure your email includes:\n✔ Your full name\n✔ Your full address (including postcode)\n✔ A contact method (email or phone)\n✔ Details of your case (including any relevant reference numbers)\n\nA member of my casework team will be in touch as soon as possible.\n\nAm I Your MP?\n\nDue to parliamentary protocol, I can only take up casework for people living in the Vale of Glamorgan. If you’re unsure whether I’m your MP, you can check by entering your postcode here: findyourmp.parliament.uk<http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>.\n\nGetting in Touch\n\nThe best way to contact me is by email. My office is open Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 5 PM, and we’ll do our best to respond as soon as we can.\n\nYou can also keep up with my work here:\n📌 Facebook: [KanishkafortheVale]\n📌 Instagram: [@valekanishka]\n📌 X (Twitter): [@KanishkaNarayan]\n\nEmergency Contacts\n\nIf you need urgent assistance, here are some useful contacts:\n📞 NHS Wales (Non-Emergency Medical Advice): 111\n🚨 Emergency Services (Police, Fire, Ambulance): 999\n🏥 Mental Health Support (Samaritans Cymru): [phone redacted]\n🏠 Homelessness Support (Shelter Cymru): [phone redacted]\n👮 South Wales Police (Non-Emergency): 101\n\nThanks again for getting in touch—I really appreciate hearing from people across our community. My team and I look forward to assisting you.\n\nBest wishes,\nKanishka\n\n\nKanishka Narayan MP\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\nParliamentary Private Secretary to the Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs\n\n\n\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data.\n"},{"id":"wb-cf4b93b3","subject":"Automatic reply enquiry re potential acquiring authority rou","name":"0000-00-00_automatic-reply-enquiry-re-potential-acquiring-authority-rou_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-enqu