ishes,\nKanishka\nKanishka Narayan MP\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\nMinister for AI and Online Safety\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data.\n"},{"id":"wb-e85d3ff6","subject":"Automatic reply subject FOI location access to historical co","name":"0000-00-00_automatic-reply-subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-co_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-co_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"automatic-reply-subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-co","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-co_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Automatic reply: Subject: FOI - Location & Access to Historical Court Records (Great House Farm, Llandough)\nFrom: Disclosure Team\nDate: Sun, 07 Jun 2026 14:15 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is an automated confirmation that your email has been received by the Disclosure Team (Ministry of Justice) mailbox. Please be aware, this team deals with a high volume of emails.\n\n\n\nPlease note this email address is for requests for recorded information under the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) and non-offender subject access requests under Data Protection Act 2018 (DPA)/General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).\n\n\n\nFreedom of Information requests\n\nYou can expect a response within 20 working days.\n\n\n\nSubject Access Requests\n\nYou can expect an initial response within 1 calendar month.\n\n\n\nAny other types of queries/requests, will be handled accordingly.\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n"},{"id":"wb-cc91208f","subject":"Automatic reply title fraud and procedural concealment churc","name":"0000-00-00_automatic-reply-title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-churc_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-churc_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"automatic-reply-title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-churc","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_automatic-reply-title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-churc_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Automatic reply: Title Fraud and Procedural Concealment – Church View Close, Llandough (formerly Great House Farm/ \"Ty Mawr\")\nFrom: NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP)\nDate: Mon, 16 Feb 2026 17:32 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHello,\n\nThank you for reaching out to me. This is just a quick note to confirm that we’ve received your email.\n\nAs your MP for the Vale of Glamorgan, my priority is supporting local constituents who need help with urgent issues. I receive a high volume of emails every day, so while I will do my best to get back to you as soon as possible, there may be a slight delay—especially if you’re contacting me about policy matters or upcoming legislation. Please know that your message has been logged, and I’ll respond as soon as I can.\n\nConstituency Casework\n\nIf you need my help with a personal case, please make sure your email includes:\n✔ Your full name\n✔ Your full address (including postcode)\n✔ A contact method (email or phone)\n✔ Details of your case (including any relevant reference numbers)\n\nA member of my casework team will be in touch as soon as possible.\n\nAm I Your MP?\n\nDue to parliamentary protocol, I can only take up casework for people living in the Vale of Glamorgan. If you’re unsure whether I’m your MP, you can check by entering your postcode here: <http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/> findyourmp.parliament.uk<http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>.\n\nGetting in Touch\n\nThe best way to contact me is by email. My office is open Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 5 PM, and we’ll do our best to respond as soon as we can.\n\nYou can also keep up with my work here:\n📌 Facebook: [KanishkafortheVale]\n📌 Instagram: [@valekanishka]\n📌 X (Twitter): [@KanishkaNarayan]\n\nEmergency Contacts\n\nIf you need urgent assistance, here are some useful contacts:\n📞 NHS Wales (Non-Emergency Medical Advice): 111\n🚨 Emergency Services (Police, Fire, Ambulance): 999\n🏥 Mental Health Support (Samaritans Cymru): [phone redacted]\n🏠 Homelessness Support (Shelter Cymru): [phone redacted]\n👮 South Wales Police (Non-Emergency): 101\n\nThanks again for getting in touch—I really appreciate hearing from people across our community. My team and I look forward to assisting you.\n\nBest wishes,\nKanishka\n\n\n\nKanishka Narayan MP\n\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\n\nMinister for AI and Online Safety\n\n\n\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data.\n"},{"id":"wb-3945bcba","subject":"Bp properties ltd v buckler request for opinion limitation a","name":"0000-00-00_bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-request-for-opinion-limitation-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-request-for-opinion-limitation-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-request-for-opinion-limitation-a","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-request-for-opinion-limitation-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler – Request for Opinion (Limitation Act 1980 s.32)\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Wed, 05 Nov 2025 05:59 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Mr Thomas,\n\nI am seeking a preliminary opinion regarding potential grounds to reopen\nthe case BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 31 July 1987),\nconcerning Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan.\n\nThere appear to be two material issues:\n\n1. Corporate Party Identification:\nCorrespondence relevant to the dispute was exchanged with BP Pension Trust\nLtd, while litigation and enforcement proceeded under BP Properties Ltd.\nThe Court treated these entities as separate when assessing notice but\neffectively identical in dismissing the appeal and enforcing possession.\nThis inconsistency may constitute a mistake or misrepresentation under\nLimitation Act 1980, Section 32.\n\n\n2. Effect of the 1974 Letters:\nThe Court found that unilateral letters in 1974 granting a licence to\noccupy rent-free for life converted possession from adverse to licensed.\nHowever, I understand there is no evidence that this licence was ever\naccepted. If acceptance did not occur, adverse possession may have\ncontinued and the running of limitation may not have been interrupted as\nthe judgment assumes.\n\n\nI would be grateful for:\n\nYour view on whether these issues may be sufficient to apply to set aside\nor reopen enforcement, or otherwise seek remedy or restitution; and\n\nYour guidance on next procedural steps.\n\n\nI can provide Judgment text and Newspaper records of the demolition (1988)\netc.\n\nThank you for your consideration.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSion Hywel Buckler\n[phone redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-1f61018c","subject":"Bp v buckler 1987 and the 1982 land registration of great ho","name":"0000-00-00_bp-v-buckler-1987-and-the-1982-land-registration-of-great-ho_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-v-buckler-1987-and-the-1982-land-registration-of-great-ho_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-and-the-1982-land-registration-of-great-ho","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-v-buckler-1987-and-the-1982-land-registration-of-great-ho_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI'm writing in relation to land formerly known as *Great House Farm,\r\nLlandough (Vale of Glamorgan)*, subsequently developed for residential use\r\nand historically connected with the proceedings culminating in *BP v\r\nBuckler (Court of Appeal, 1987)*.\r\n\r\nI appreciate that the Local Planning Authority is not responsible for\r\ndetermining land ownership, nor am I asking it to do so. My purpose is to\r\nplace on record a *chronological summary of unresolved land-governance\r\nissues* which may be material to the integrity of the planning history\r\nrelied upon for that site.\r\n\r\nIn brief and as reflected in public records:\r\n\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   In *July 1974*, proceedings involving my grandmother and BP both\r\n   asserting ownership, were adjourned and did not result in a judicial final\r\n   determination.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   On *31 October 1974*, a further listed hearing did not proceed\r\n   substantively, following correspondence sent that morning by BP entities.\r\n   No judgment on title was issued. My nan requested the audience with the\r\n   judge the day before, with her lawyer. But that got leaked, the press\r\n   descended on our farm (not that I can find evidence of news articles from\r\n   said press), and the following morning the two letters from BP arrived to\r\n   our solicitor, effectively squashing the court hearing and audience with\r\n   the judge my nan had sought, to make her case of ownership. Her reply to\r\n   both BP letters (one from BP Pension Trust Ltd and one from BP Properties\r\n   Ltd), that morning of the 31st of October, was also 'I own the land'.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   Throughout this period, my grandmother was *excluded from dealings*\r\n   concerning land we asserted we owned, while the opposing party\r\ncontinued to *assert\r\n   ownership*, notwithstanding the absence of a concluded judicial finding.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   In or around *1982*, the land was registered in BP’s name, despite the\r\n   earlier proceedings never having resolved the competing claims nor having\r\n   resulted in findings adverse to my grandmother.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   My grandmother then died in *1983*, after the registration had taken\r\n   place, without compensation and without any final adjudication of her claim.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   In the *1987 appeal*, the Court referred to correspondence as having\r\n   been replied to (albeit not to the correct corporate entity - which is\r\n   ultimately why we lost BP vs Buckler 1987), yet in my fathers appeal that\r\n   followed, whereby he argued that surely BP Pension Trust should have been\r\n   the claimant not BP Properties, the same judge from the case dismissed the\r\n   appeal citing that both companies were effectively the same. This is all\r\n   evidence on the face of the public record of these proceedings.\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   By that stage, and in the absence of a documentary title which had\r\n   effectively been overtaken by registration, my family was driven to advance\r\n   arguments in adverse possession as a *fallback position*, which itself\r\n   should have assured our continued occupancy.\r\n\r\nThe cumulative effect was that my family was *displaced*, the land was\r\ndeveloped, and no compensation was ever paid, despite ownership never\r\nhaving been conclusively decided in court. Whether intentionally or not,\r\nthe process operated in a manner where asserted ownership became treated as\r\nsettled fact.\r\n\r\nI am not alleging misconduct, nor am I seeking retrospective remedies from\r\nthe Authority. I am simply asking whether, given the above sequence, it\r\nwould be appropriate for the Authority to:\r\n\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   note that historic planning decisions were taken on the basis of *assumed\r\n   title*, and\r\n   -\r\n\r\n   record that the underlying ownership dispute was *never finally\r\n   adjudicated*, for the sake of transparency and future governance\r\n   integrity.\r\n\r\nThis correspondence is intended to be factual, measured, and\r\nnon-adversarial. I am happy to supply references to the relevant hearings,\r\nregistrations, or judgments if that assists your records. But what I'm\r\nhighlighting here is all on public record and in the public eye.\r\n\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n"},{"id":"wb-09d1cc7c","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 documentary","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-documentary","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm exploring doing a documentary about legal case BP Vs Buckler 1987.\r\n\r\nI'm the son of the defendant, my late dad William Buckler.\r\n\r\nMy last employer and source of income, for my last 22 years in Oath, was\r\nthe Vale of Glamorgan council.\r\n\r\nI have a UK company and would like to make a documentary about this case.\r\nAnd I'm now seeking co-financeers for this project.\r\n\r\nPlease email/ call me if you have interest in this project.\r\n\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\nDirector\r\nDATRO Consortium Ltd\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-6d602fe1","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 FOI request","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-foi-request_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-foi-request_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-foi-request","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-foi-request_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am writing to make a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\r\n\r\nAt your earliest convenience please would you provide me copies of all\r\ninformation held by Cadw relating to Great House Farm, formerly occupied by\r\nmy Buckler / Williams family, which was subject to a refusal to list and\r\nsubsequent demolition in or around the late 1980s.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, I request disclosure of the following:\r\n\r\n1. All records, assessments, reports, site visit notes, photographs,\r\ndesk-based evaluations, or recommendations produced by or for Cadw in\r\nrelation to Great House Farm, including any material connected to decisions\r\nnot to list the building.\r\n\r\n2. All internal correspondence (including letters, memoranda, emails, and\r\nbriefing notes) held by Cadw that relate to:\r\nThe heritage significance of Great House Farm\r\n\r\n3. The decision not to list the building\r\nAny consideration of archaeological, historical, or associative significance\r\nAny communications between Cadw and third parties (including local\r\nauthorities, developers, landowners, or commercial entities) concerning\r\nGreat House Farm prior to demolition\r\n\r\n4. Records of any archaeological notifications, alerts, or discoveries\r\nassociated with Great House Farm, whether before or after demolition,\r\nincluding references to artefacts later recovered during excavations in the\r\nearly 1990s.\r\n\r\n5. Any documentation referring to historical associations between Great\r\nHouse Farm and early radio or wireless experimentation, including any\r\nmention of Guglielmo Marconi or related activity in the Cardiff Bay /\r\nLavernock / surrounding area that may have been considered or dismissed.\r\n\r\n6. Policy or guidance documents in force at the time (1980s) that governed\r\nCadw’s criteria for listing historic farmhouses or buildings with\r\nassociative historical value.\r\n\r\n7. If any information is withheld, please specify the exemption relied upon\r\nand provide the reasoning as required under the Act.\r\n\r\nI would prefer to receive the information electronically, by email.\r\n\r\nPlease confirm receipt of this request too.\r\n\r\nI understand that under the Freedom of Information Act you're required to\r\nrespond within 20 working days. It's not that urgent so please take the\r\ntime you need, within reason, and keep me updated where possible.\r\n\r\nAnd if you have any questions, queries or concerns please feel free to\r\nreach out to me too.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n[redacted]\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-5bdbbf6f","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 great house farm 20","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-great-house-farm-20_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-great-house-farm-20_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-great-house-farm-20","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-great-house-farm-20_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI'm a Welsh Christian from Wales. Here in Puerto Madryn. My last employer\r\nwas the Welsh Government. Before that I had a career in the military.\r\n\r\nI grew up in an 800 year old farm near Cardiff in Wales. Called Great House\r\nFarm in Llandough, Cardiff. Which my family occupied for 400 years.\r\n\r\nWe lost possession of this farm to BP, in 1987. After they claimed they\r\nwere the rightful owners. They took possession through the courts, evicted\r\nus, then demolished our farm. My dads appeal was dismissed. His application\r\nto ECHR was blocked. And then he died.\r\n\r\nI am now in Puerto Madryn. I came here with a childhood dream, to rebuild\r\nmy family farm here. I want to construct an exact replica of my families\r\nfarm here. To honour my family.\r\n\r\nFurthermore Marconi was also staying with my family in Wales, at our old\r\nfarm, the day he invited radio. And a lot of Roman burials were exhevated\r\nfrom our family land and placed into museums, after it was demolished.\r\n\r\nWe are only now learning, from advances in AI, that our Welsh farm may have\r\nbeen stolen from us, through lawfare, fraud and concealment. A huge\r\ninjustice and a potentially huge lawsuit against BP and the British\r\nEstablishment, if this is true. It looks to be true.\r\n\r\nIf anyone here would like to help me establish in Argentina and achieve my\r\ngoals here, I would very much appreciate assistance. I am new here. I don't\r\nknow anyone here. I speak a little Spanish. Fluent Welsh. And English.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your replies,\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n\r\nSion Hywel Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n[redacted] (WhatsApp)\r\n"},{"id":"wb-5d23f57f","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 request for academic perspective on histo","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-request-for-academic-perspective-on-histo_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-request-for-academic-perspective-on-histo_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-request-for-academic-perspective-on-histo","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-request-for-academic-perspective-on-histo_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am.\r\n\r\nI'm writing to ask whether you might be willing to offer a brief academic\r\nperspective on a legal history question involving land law and land\r\nregistration.\r\n\r\nThe issue concerns a land registration made around 1982 that later\r\nunderpinned the case *BP v Buckler (1987)*. There was never a definitive\r\ncourt determination of ownership prior to the registration, and competing\r\nclaims existed from my family at the time. Subsequent case law appears to\r\ncontain internal inconsistencies regarding corporate identity and\r\ncorrespondence that materially affected outcomes.\r\n\r\nI am not seeking legal advice, representation, or advocacy, merely an\r\nacademic view on whether a title that has never been clearly adjudicated by\r\nthe courts can later be treated as settled fact — and whether this\r\nsituation highlights any doctrinal or structural concerns within land\r\nregistration law or legal scholarship.\r\n\r\nI can provide a short factual timeline and key documents if helpful. Any\r\nthoughts you might share would be greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n"},{"id":"wb-89ffd7a0","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 thatcher sas","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-thatcher-sas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-thatcher-sas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987-thatcher-sas","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-thatcher-sas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"I am writing regarding this video and case;\r\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nThis appears to be previously suppressed or unaired ITV footage relating to\r\nthe 1987–1988 BP/Buckler dispossession case. I was a toddler at the time\r\nand that is my mum on TV.\r\n\r\nI am now a former military cyber warfare professional. I left my military\r\ncareer with honours. I spent the last 2 years of my 22 years in oath\r\nemployed by the Welsh Government/ Vale of Glamorgan Council up until 2024.\r\nI am bonafide.\r\n\r\nThe material allegedly contains significant evidence contradicting the\r\naccepted public narrative surrounding the events, including possible\r\nprocedural irregularities and the treatment of the family involved. Maybe\r\neven SAS in addition to the newspaper reports of 30 police to remove my\r\npregnant mum, terminally ill dad and siblings and me who were toddlers at\r\nthe time. The footage and associated materials have only recently come into\r\ncirculation and may be of substantial public interest.\r\n\r\nI am seeking to preserve the material properly and ensure it is\r\nindependently authenticated and reviewed by experienced investigative\r\njournalists. I also possess supporting historical documentation and\r\ntimelines connected to the case.\r\n\r\nAt this stage I am requesting confidential contact with an investigative\r\nproducer or journalist before wider disclosure. Original copies and\r\nprovenance information can be made available.\r\n\r\nMy family held virtual freehold (999 year lease) of the land from 1667. In\r\nthe late 1800's after Marconi stayed with us in our 800 year old former\r\ncourt house 10 bedroom home, while inventing radio, we did a deal with Bute\r\nEstate and Quarryman contractor Daniel Thomas, allowing our farmland to be\r\nquarried in exchange for the manorial fee simple absolute title. Which my\r\ngrandmother Mrs Williams held.\r\n\r\nDaniel Thomas died. Mary's dad and husband died. And the title was stolen\r\nfrom Mary Williams. And in the window Mary had go rebuttle BP registering\r\nher land with the land registry in 1982 after committing purgergy and\r\nwithholding information from the land registry (and erazing the name\r\nWilliams falsly alleging she was Mrs Buckler in fraudulent license letters\r\nin 1974 after obstructing Mrs Williams having her day in court and ruling\r\nin 1974) Mrs Mary Williams conveniently died too.\r\n\r\nThe fraudulent license letter terms were then applied to my parents who had\r\nno such agreement with BP in BP vs Buckler 1987. My dad appealed on grounds\r\nBP Pension Trust should have been the claimant not BP Properties Ltd. The\r\nappeal was dismissed on grounds they were effectively the same company. But\r\nwhen that same judge awarded BP possession he said my nans rebuttle of BP\r\nPension Trusts claim didn't count as the claimant BP Properties was a\r\nseparate company. My dads ECHR request was blocked then ge conveniently\r\ndied age 42 in 1991.\r\n\r\nMy councillor for Llandough wont reply.\r\nMy Brit'ish Muslim MP wont reply.\r\nCadw say its nothing to do with them after ignoring a petition and delaying\r\ninstead of listing our home as a grade II so it couldn't be demolished. The\r\nnation archives say theres gaps in the Bute records which support we held\r\nmanorial fee simple absolute title until it was stolen. My nan maintained\r\nunwaiveeingly she was the owner until her convenient abrupt death in 1982.\r\n\r\nWe got title fair and square. BP never got a ruling their claim with our\r\nstolen title was more superior. Press labelled us squatters. SAS appeared\r\nto have been used by Thatcher to force us out. But our claim remains and\r\nunchallenged. And now I have proven fraud, fraud unravels all. And the\r\nlimitation clock only begin from discovery not occurance of the fraud.\r\n\r\nSince we got title and did our tree planting ceremony to celebrate. We have\r\nbeen the subject of a death of a thousands cuts for decades. Proceedural\r\nunfairness, court mistakes, supressed coverage. And I am trying to speak to\r\nMinistry of Justice (who just took 6 months to reply only to dismiss me)\r\nand land registry (who converted my query and concern into a complaint only\r\nto dismiss it as resolved having done nothing). Thatcher lifted any check\r\nbalances they had to do at the time so that BP were able to register our\r\nland in their names.\r\n\r\nThis is an outrage. There were child graves in the church next to us which\r\nwere quietly moves, no press coverage. A decade until the exhivation in\r\n1994 was reported and the child graves under states in the report by a\r\nmatter of hundreds. The 1870 roman soldier we reported was also surpessed,\r\nso to  to this day is Marconi's stay with us while inventing radio. All so\r\nthey could get planning permission to build the 23 houses there on our\r\nstolen land. Instead of listing our home as a Grade II they called it an\r\nold ruin barn and building in the planning applications. They pretended not\r\nto know about the sites archelogical and historic significants to build\r\nhouses. The excavation was one of burials biggest recorded in welsh\r\nhistory. Under our farm was a lot of history with many artifacts now in\r\nmuseums. So we were looted.\r\n\r\nMy family are too terrified to speak out. Like insigenous welsh hostages\r\nunder Brit'ish colonial rule and terrorists. Its absurd in 2026 but\r\nevidently the danger is real.\r\n\r\nI find it no coincidence when I placed everyone on notice about this fraud\r\nI discovered companies house rejected my valid passport and driving license\r\nand fined me for not providing ID after providing it then alledge I will be\r\ncriminalised if I dont install a digital id tracking app or go into a post\r\noffice.\r\n\r\nPlease investigate and you will find the 1,000 cuts I speak off. But we are\r\nstill here (Yma o Hyd). My brother Rhys is the rightful Lord of Manor of\r\nLlandough. My two sisters Lady's. We will seek reperations through our\r\nfamily lawyer but we want this fought in the open and not in the shadows in\r\nclandestine civil war ways. I am a military cyber and electronic warfare\r\nprofessional and I have the corrupt Brit'ish State who put my family\r\nthrough all this for the last century, dead to rights. No matter all of\r\ntheir murder, fraud, lawfare, procedural unfairness, court \"mistakes\" ,\r\ncollusion with BP, abuse of power and human rights violations.\r\n\r\nThis was an act and decleration of civil war upon us. I am in effect now a\r\ncounter officer in this matter.\r\n\r\nI am currently at the Welsh Settlement in Argentina to rebuild a replica of\r\nmy farm for it to be somewhat open to the public. So this story can be told\r\nand shared forever. Here they celebrate Welsh culture and history unlike\r\nthe colonised Wales that still tries to bury this. In Cardiff Bay theres a\r\nstatute of Radio with no plaque to name Marconi as he was right wing.\r\nCardiff council openly confess this. Meanwhile there's not even a park\r\nbench plaque in Llandough to commemorate Marconi was ever there let alone\r\nit being the birthplace of Radio. Just 23 charscterless houses and a parish\r\nwho also ignore this like the councillor and MP.\r\n\r\nI urge you to investigate and report.\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\nFYI my aunty is Shan Cothi.\r\nMy uncle founded Tigertailz.\r\nMy grandad was Ray Smith who starred in TV series  Dempsey and Makepeace.\r\nMy other uncle is Joshua Richards who is Buewolf in Emmerdale and starred\r\nin Troy with Brad Pitt.\r\n\r\nWe are the land.\r\n"},{"id":"wb-f9966743","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987 incident 251111 000063","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987-incident-251111-000063_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckle