rom our Support site, click https://support.britishlegion.org.uk/app/account/questions/detail/i_id/1269697/track/AvO42Qp8Dv8S~QjsGqUe~yL3w_cq9S75Mv8k~zj~PP~t/\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSubject\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nBP vs Buckler 1987\n\nDiscussion Thread\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nResponse By E-mail (Carol Bullock) (02/12/2025 09.18 AM)     \nGood Morning Requester \n \nThank you for contacting the RBL War Pension and Armed Forces Compensation Scheme Team. \n \n Unfortunately as our Manager Mark Linton advised on 12th November 2025 we are unable to assist you in civil claims in regard to litigation in legal property ownership disputes and would recommend you speak to an independent solicitor to obtain legal advice on any legal recourse.\n \nBelow is a link to the services that RBL offer and if you feel any of these would be of benefit I would encourage you to reach out to us regarding those  https://www.britishlegion.org.uk/get-support/how-we-help.   \n \nI will keep your case open with us for now in case.  If however your case has been passed to the War Pensions and Armed Forces Compensation Scheme team in error please let me know so I am not contacting you unnecessarily causing you any issues. \n \nBest wishes \n \nCarol Bullock\nRBL War Pensions and Armed Forces Compensation Scheme Team \n \n\n\nResponse By E-mail (Mark Linton) (12/11/2025 09.59 AM)     \nDear Requester\n \nif your case is in relation to a claim for a War Pension then we may be able to assist you - if the case is for any other form of litigation then we cannot assist\n \nPlease advise further details\n \nMark Linton\nWP&AFCS Manager \n\n\nChat By Chat (Chris) (11/11/2025 10.31 AM)     \nChris: Hi, my name is Chris. How may I help you?\nSion Buckler: Hey. AI is telling me I should sue BP and the British Government for a legal case my family lost many years ago. It's telling me there's fraud and concealment, which is grounds to re-open the case. Needless to say this wont be easy. I'm ex forces, I thought I'd begin with you. The case is public. It's BP vs Buckler 1987\nChris: good morning sion\nSion Buckler: Good morning.\nChris: thank you for information,To allow me to help you, would you please provide the following information and confirm you are happy for this to be stored and shared within the relevant Royal British Legion departments?\n\nConsent: Yes/No \nFull Name:\nTelephone number:\nAddress:\nPost Code:\n \nSion Buckler: Yes. Requester. [phone redacted]. [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan. [postcode redacted].\nSion Buckler: My old service ID: 25148537\nChris: thank you just bear with me a moment\nChris: Date of birth:\nNational Insurance Number: \nBranch of armed Forces: (Army, RAF, Navy, Marines)\nService number:\nRegiment:\nEnlistment Date:\nDischarge Date:\nName whilst Serving:\n \nSion Buckler: 24/10/1984 , Army. 25148537. Royal Signals. July 2002 - July 2007. Or there abouts. Name whilst serving: Requester Hywel Buckler (nickname: Noel)\nSion Buckler: NI number: JE340808A\nChris: thank you\nChris: just uploading this on\nChris: so what we can do today is pass this on to a case worker\nChris: who will be in touch to assist you futher on what you can with this]\nChris: how would you like be contacted please?\nSion Buckler: email: [email redacted]\nChris: thank you\nChris: i pop on the notes contact you via email\nChris: anything else i can help you with today?\nSion Buckler: Thanks. That's all. Enjoy your week\nChris: saem you as you\nChris: \n\nThank you for contacting the Royal British Legion Advice and Information Line. Our Live Chat facility is open 8am till 8pm Monday to Sunday if you need any other assistance.\n\nAlternately you can contact us directly on [phone redacted] our lines are open 8am till 8pm Monday to Sunday.\n\n\nSystem: 'Requester' is currently 'Absent'. Approximately 120 seconds until disconnect.\nSystem: Concluded by Agent\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion Reference # 251111-000063\n       Date Created: 11/11/2025 10.31 AM\n  Date Last Updated: 02/12/2025 09.18 AM\n             Status: Waiting\n\n\n[---002:003600:21033---]\n"},{"id":"wb-4364ae14","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm the son of William Buckler, from the 34 year legal battle with BP.\r\nBP vs Buckler 1987\r\n\r\nI'm a certified and experienced military commander & leader.\r\nI served in the middle east.\r\nAnd left my military career in cyber & electronic warfare with honours.\r\nI just finished 22 years in Oath. Last 2 under the Welsh Government.\r\n\r\nI'd very much like to speak to you.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-332bd842","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 05:08 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI'm seeking guidance on whether a concern I have may fall within the remit\nof maladministration by public bodies.\n\nThe issue relates to a land registration made in 1982 which appears to have\nbeen relied upon by courts and enforcement authorities despite there being\nno definitive judicial determination of ownership at the time, and despite\nunresolved competing claims.\n\nI am not seeking compensation or a ruling on ownership at this stage. I am\nseeking an independent view on whether administrative process failures may\nhave occurred and whether it would be appropriate for the matter to be\nexamined further.\n\nI would be grateful for advice on whether this is something your office can\nconsider, or whether another oversight body would be more appropriate.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-d693dbab","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 05:09 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI'm writing to notify your office of a potential inconsistency across\nrelated judicial decisions arising from the same underlying land dispute.\n\nI am not making a complaint and I am not alleging misconduct. Rather, I\nwish to place on record that in closely related proceedings, the same judge\nappears to have treated the legal identity of two related corporate\nentities inconsistently, with material consequences for the outcome.\n\nThis inconsistency directly affected whether correspondence was deemed\neffective and whether a party was said to have failed to respond, despite\nfindings elsewhere acknowledging that a response was in fact made.\n\nI submit this solely for awareness and record, in case it is relevant to\nstandards, training, or internal review.\n\nYours faithfully,\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-5dc1f53c","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 05:10 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI'm writing to ask whether my family’s experience may be relevant to the\nCommission’s interest in systemic human rights issues.\n\nThe matter concerns forced removal from land following civil proceedings\nthat relied upon a land registration made without definitive adjudication\nof ownership, subsequent denial of effective access to further remedy, and\nthe destruction of our home preventing re-entry.\n\nI am not requesting intervention or litigation. I am seeking to understand\nwhether this experience engages Convention principles and whether it is\nappropriate for it to be logged or considered as part of broader systemic\nanalysis.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-56f6ee5d","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 05:18 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI'm writing to raise a point of awareness concerning a historical land\nregistration that appears to have been relied upon by public authorities\ndespite the absence of a definitive judicial determination of ownership at\nthe time it was entered on the register.\n\nI am not seeking legal advice or intervention. My purpose is simply to flag\na concern as to whether the State may, in some circumstances, rely upon a\nregistered title that was based on assertion rather than adjudication.\n\nIf this is not appropriate for your department, I would be grateful if you\ncould indicate whether another public body would be better placed to note\nthe issue.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-1dfa1c9e","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-5.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-5.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-5.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 05:52 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI am writing to ask whether a historical land dispute may be of interest\nfrom a professional or law-reform perspective.\n\nThe case involved reliance on registered title obtained prior to definitive\nadjudication, and subsequent judicial reasoning that appears internally\ninconsistent regarding party identity and correspondence.\n\nI am not seeking advocacy or review. I am simply asking whether such issues\nfall within areas the Bar Council monitors in relation to procedural\nfairness and the development of land law.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-7193d19d","subject":"BP v Buckler great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI'm Requester. Son of William Buckler of the landmark legal case BP Vs\r\nBuckler 1987.\r\n\r\nI am at the Welsh settlement in Argentina, attempting to rebuild a replica\r\nof my families former 800 year old farm here.\r\n\r\nOur farm outside Cardiff, which my family occupied since 1667, was where\r\nMarconi invented radio. It should have been a Grade II listen building. We\r\nshould have never been forced from it. It should have never been bulldozed\r\ndown.\r\n\r\n\r\nMy family should have at least been compensated or seen justice. Instead my\r\nfather's appeal was dismissed. His ECHR request blocked and then he died in\r\n1991 at age just 41 - my age today.\r\n\r\nThere's a number of reasons us indigenous Briton Welsh farmers got forced\r\nfrom our ancestral birthland of 400 years via force, secrecy/ stealth and\r\nlicense. When we operated with non of these and remained in honour.\r\n\r\n1. Ownership was never determined in a court. Possession was saught but BP\r\nnever saught clarification on the true owners.\r\n\r\nMy nans tried making her case that we were the owners, inspire of our fall\r\nback legal defence of adverse pissesion.\r\n\r\nMy nans audience with the judge in July 1974 was ajourned. Her request for\r\nan audience with the judge to appeal and make her claim to the land in\r\nOctober 30th was squashed too, by license letters alledgedly sent by BP\r\nthat morning, but not received until November 4th. The court stepped back\r\nin November 1974, alledging the matter was sufficiently de-escelated due to\r\nBP's license offer. But that was an inadvertent way of ruling in BP's\r\nfavour without ruling on the matter. So the license offer upheld, my nans\r\nappeal and claim to land ownership unheard/ blocked yet again.\r\n\r\nThe press also appeared around my nan and home after it was leaked our\r\nfamily solicitor made the appeal to the judge on the 30th October 1974. For\r\na hearing the next day. Odd coincidence. Where's any of that press\r\ncoverage? Suppressed? Another odd coincidence. We're they even real press.\r\nIn any case, real or not, the BP license letters afterwards gave the\r\nappearance of a retreate by BP, when in actual fact it was forcing a\r\nlicense, unlawfully and unconditionally onto my one legged, wheelchair\r\nbound grandmother.\r\n\r\nIf ever my nan was silent, it was because the courts, her own solicitor,\r\nmaybe even husband, and BP were all incrementally deminishing her position.\r\nHer reason for an amputated legal was a blood clot caused from the stress.\r\nFurthermore they cut the electric, water, poisoned our river and cows.\r\n\r\nThose BP letters of license might have worked with my grandad Frederick\r\nBuckler. As he did express intent to entertain license offers. But that\r\nintent, by law, will have died with him in the late 60's. My nan was a\r\nWilliams. She kept and maintained her maiden name. But the court and press\r\nand BP would  nevertheless refer to my nan as Mrs Buckler. Since no\r\nWilliams ever showed intent. Only Frederick Buckler. And so it was\r\nimportant they force upon my nan the name Buckler, and the narrative the\r\n\"Buckler's\" expressed intent.\r\n\r\nAnd contrary to claims my nan aquiessed and even accepted the license by\r\nremaining silent, as falsly alleged and ill advised by her solicitor, she\r\ndid no such thing.\r\n\r\n2. I found an article from 1978 showing my nan arranged a petition.\r\nArranged and open day. And claimed publically \"it's my house\". Our families\r\nhome since 1667. See attached.\r\n\r\nThe press say 'open day' in hyphens, as if to belittle my nans attempts to\r\nsave our home from possession, demolition and housing development.\r\n\r\nSo too, does the judge in the 87 case against my late father, use language\r\nlike my nan '“Conceived the notion” we held title - suggesting our title\r\nclaim might be fanciful or ungrounded.\r\n\r\nBut recently I have found evidence of the exchange which happened between\r\nSir Mark Wood and Marquess of Bute as my nan alledged. Whereby we received\r\ntitle, as it was promised to us in exchange (as agricultural tenants) if we\r\npermit quarrying to occur on the farmland.\r\n\r\nThe deal with us was not honoured. Daniel Thomas is believed to have died\r\nin 1915. Our title is believed to have been stolen from our home by a house\r\nguest, not fully known to us. And a copy of the title in our name, stolen\r\nfrom the public library. Albeit they left the index card.\r\n\r\nWhen land registry begun, BP Properties Ltd didn't just race to register in\r\n1982 (my nan dying age 65 in 1983), despite women in our family living even\r\nunto 101, but BP and the land registry didn't lodge that the title claim\r\nwas in dispute as they should have. Nor had they had confirmation by a\r\ncourt that they were the superior owners. As it was never decided in a\r\ncourt, it was actually actively avoided as my family held superior title\r\nand claim which they couldn't challenge. Not by stealing our titles. Not by\r\ntrying to force, stealth or license.\r\n\r\n3. BP should not have been awarded possession of our land in the landmark\r\nlegal case in 1987. The intent argument was disproven in the appeal my late\r\nfather filed afterwards. And for reasons I mentioned above. And while the\r\njudge ruled in BP's favor, citing any rejection my nan made to BP Pensions\r\nTrust Ltd didn't count, as the claimant and self-proclaimed licensor was BP\r\nProperties Ltd and the two were separate companies. The same justice\r\ndismissed my dads appeal citing both companies were effectively the same.\r\nSo a case of heads they win, tails we lose.\r\n\r\nI've tried bringing this up with authorities all my life. And I'm forever\r\nblocked and ignored, or my enquiries are absorbed and deflected. My family\r\nwant our justice. And compensation.\r\n\r\nI'm a war veteran. Ieft my military career with honours. I finished 22\r\nyears in Oath. Last 2 employed under the Welsh government (Vale Council)\r\n2022-24. I am bona fide.\r\n\r\nIt's an oborrant situation on British Isles. I've spent most of my adult\r\nlife abroad because we seem to have just been overrun by extreme\r\nanti-indigenous leftists, non-indigenous and corporations. It's always\r\ntotal silence when I bring this matter up. As I've stated, it's so bad I'm\r\njust rebuilding a replica of my farm at the Welsh settlement in Argentina\r\nnow. Who care to celebrate the house radio was invented in. And my story\r\nrights. And me, a living member of this family and whole matter.\r\n\r\nIt's evident history is being buried and rewritten by the anti-christian,\r\nanti-indigenous, anti-welsh Regime occupying British isles. As there's a\r\nstatute in Cardiff of a radio which expressly won't name the inventor\r\nMarconi as he was far right. I wonder if that's why a multi generation\r\nlawfare campaign was waged on my farm and farm where Marconi invented\r\nradio. Or was it the burials and treasures under our farmland that were\r\nexhevated in 1994? Or the value of the land overlooking Cardiff bay, which\r\nwas later sold on to developers.\r\n\r\nSomeone even hypothesised that BP and the Brit-ISH/ BritLESS State took\r\ntheir time with our family so that we would upkeep the farmhouse and\r\nStewart the land and defend it, until it had reached maturity for value\r\nextrapolation. Which is plausible all things considered. And would go\r\nlengths to show you the depth of evil us harvested indigenous Britons are\r\nfighting.\r\n\r\nI am a certified and experienced military commander and leader. And the\r\nfarm story I've given you here is just one of a long line of unjust events.\r\nMy house in 40 Lombard Street, Barry was stolen in 2012 in a similar way.\r\nAnd my 36 day old boy was abducted from my home in Stockeld Park in 2013,\r\nnever to be seen again. And all that happened since then was failed\r\nattempts to discredit, frame, kidnap, censor and silence me. So it's like a\r\ncivil war has been waged on us, which is why I only fly in and our of\r\nBritain now, like it's another tour of the middle east.\r\n\r\nThe danger is real. I keep my daughter and wife off the island now, not\r\njust my self. I even exported my dog to our place in the Caribbean after I\r\ncaught an Afghan in my garden in Wales, trying to steal him. One of the 97\r\nAfghans secretly housed in StAthan, near our 11 home village of Monknash,\r\nwhich the Government were trying to deny existed.\r\n\r\nI hope someone follows up on this story of BP Vs Buckler 1987. And asks all\r\nthe questions that should have been asked throughout. And to this day.\r\n\r\nI won't accept the illegal occupation. At some point as a now counter\r\nofficer, we Welsh, who are already seeking to decolonise, will need to\r\nfight back by asserting boundaries upon this trespass. I should not have\r\nbeen forced off my own ancestral birthland. Out of my own home. Out of my\r\nson's life. Not as someone in honour and bona fide. As stated I have made\r\nnew lives in the Caribbean and here in Argentina. But only while justice is\r\ndelayed back home in Wales. But that delay is now decades. DECADES !! It's\r\nabsolute insanity.\r\n\r\nPlease report !!\r\nInvestigate.\r\n\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-d894074f","subject":"BP v Buckler great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler, Great House Farm, Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sun, 17 May 2026 04:11 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTo whom it may concern,\n\nI am writing as the child of Branwen and William (“Billy”) Buckler\nregarding the destruction of Great House Farm, Llandough, and the\nlong-running dispute surrounding BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987].\n\nI have compiled a substantial historical archive, including newspaper\nreports, court references, family testimony, archaeological material,\nestate history, and public records relating to Great House Farm (“Ty\nMawr”), a site associated with medieval, monastic, and Roman occupation.\n\nThe archive is currently being made into a website at:\n\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nThe material raises serious unresolved questions regarding:\n\n• The treatment of us Williams/Buckler family’s longstanding occupation and\nasserted ownership claims. • The repeated use of possession proceedings\nwithout a full adjudication of superior title. • Missing or allegedly\nsuppressed title documentation connected to Bute estate transfers and later\ntransactions. • The demolition of an allegedly medieval structure during an\nactive heritage controversy. • Whether the archaeological significance of\nthe site was fully disclosed during planning and demolition processes. •\nThe wider public interest and cultural significance of the site and its\ndestruction.\n\nIt's looking to me like my family actually did obtain fee simple absolute\nand manorial title. Then it was stolen and attempts were made by the\npossessor of the stolen title, to make my family lessee's / tenants as we\nwere when we were on the virtual freehold (999 year lease) aquired in 1667.\nThereafter it appears to be a death of a thousand cuts of proceedural\nunfairness, audacity, fraud, court \"mistakes\" , purgery and more.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nContemporaneous newspaper coverage from the 1970s and 1980s demonstrates\nthat these concerns were publicly known at the time, including heritage\nobjections, petitions, and public claims of ancestral ownership.\n\nI am requesting:\n\n   1. Review and preservation consideration of all surviving records\n   connected to Great House Farm.\n   2. Clarification as to whether any formal heritage review or\n   investigation into the demolition process was ever completed.\n   3. Guidance regarding access to archival and planning materials relevant\n   to the site.\n   4. Consideration of whether this matter warrants renewed historical or\n   heritage examination.\n\nI appreciate that some claims remain disputed or unproven, and I am not\nasking recipients to accept every allegation as established fact. However,\nI believe the totality of the historical material warrants serious review\nrather than dismissal.\n\nI would be grateful for acknowledgement of receipt and guidance on the\nappropriate next steps.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\n\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n"},{"id":"wb-ab2d691e","subject":"BP v Buckler","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\r\nassistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\r\nProperties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\r\n\r\nMy family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for generations.\r\nThe events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of our home and\r\nland, and left several members of my family deeply affected. Recent\r\nresearch I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\r\ninconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\r\ncorporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\r\nconsiderations relating to the site.\r\n\r\nI have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\r\nrequesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\r\nhistorical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\r\nhistorical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\r\n\r\nMy interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\r\nsignificance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\r\nstayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\r\nthis should form part of our preserved historical record.\r\n\r\nBy way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\r\nForces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\r\nsimply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\r\nwould be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\r\n\r\nYours sincerely,\r\n\r\n\r\n*Requester*\r\n[redacted]\r\nTel: 0203 137 7118\r\n"},{"id":"wb-eaed83ec","subject":"BP v Buckler","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler\nFrom: Hywel Apbuckler\nDate: Wed, 17 Aug 2016 03:06 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nI just discovered you. This page\n<https://www.hcrlaw.com/people/jane-mayglothling/> told me about you.\nThis article <https://www.hcrlaw.com/blog/what-is-a-possessory-title/> sent\nme to that page after I Google'd the terms 'possessory title' .\n\nI am the son of William Buckler. Of the 'BP vs Buckler' case of adverse\npossession.\nI am now 31 years old and in Oath to defend rights and freedoms (Gov ID:\n25148537).\n\nNot many people are aware of the true story of this case. I'm now able to\nexpose the truth thanks to skills I acquired in my career as a Cyber\nWarfare/ Security Engineer.\n\nBP did a back hand deal with an archaeological firm who discovered roman\nburials under our family farm land. The 34 year campaign to remove us from\nour land and steal the gold which lay beneath (to sell to museums) was a\nscandal of that time and still not public information. But the scandal runs\ndeeper.\n\nMy father died never fully understanding his inalienable or inherent birth\nrights. I single highhandedly wrote the same amount of code it takes to fly\na US drone or F22 Fighter Jet last year, so reading through and\nunderstanding the Bill of Rights, Magna Carta and the UK's 750 'statute'\nrules wasn't too difficult for me.\n\nWhat I concluded from it all, was that democracy is not voting for the\nleader and rule makers of the society we are members of. Democracy is in\nfact, a free British Subjects right to leave, join or form any society we\nchoose (with any 'statute' rules we consent to be governed by -\nindividually!).\n\nThe 1801 UK \"Society\" (Regime) now closer resembles an Evil, Tyrannical,\nNationwide Cult, which doesn't serve and defend with the allodial title of\nGreat Britain we afford it. Its statute rules, in a lot of cases, actually\nviolate the laws of the land. We are systematically being\nenslaved-from-birth (made members of this society by child abduction and\nforce) and harvested of everything we once had e.g. land, liberty, wealth,\nproperty and even each other.\n\nSo I vow to 'renounce' membership/ citizenship from Britain's new No.1\nEnemy (The 1801 UK \"Society\") and join/form a new British Society. Which I\nhave done!!\n\nThe 2015 United Technocracy Society was founded and financed by myself and\n50 other British Subjects, most in Oath and still in active duty. We have a\nstronghold with a defense force and are unofficially a British Protectorate\n(protecting our societies members from UK Regime oppression, austerity,\ngenocide, interment, touchless torture etc). I will be inviting my\nCommander-In-Chief to give our new Act of Union Her Royal Assent and I will\nseek Royal Charter once we reach 5,000 members.\n\nI never know how much liberty or life I have remaining making this stand\nagainst the UK Regime. As it is one of the most powerful in the world. I\nrecently had a safe house raided by secret services, I've lost two Private\nMilitary Security Contractors and my driver was in a Diana-style RTA. But I\nhonor my Oath and Father and I am determine to see through what I began as\nit is both legal and lawful and fully warranted.\n\nGoogle awarded my Technocratic System of Governance two patents in January\nso we're off to a good start. And we've sold our first 'Neo-Dome' today.\nWhich provides free internet and electricity to those moving Off-Grid. For\neach 5 we sell we're able to create a new mesh network and a 6th dome will\nbe erected for schools, churches and hospitals. I plan to resettle\n(proclaim)back my birth land, once my colonies and defense force have grown\nin strength and numbers.\n\nYes I am a threat to society! The 1801 UK \"Society\" specifically. But it's\nbeen more than a threat to our country, families, wealth and children's\nfuture for many years and someone has to put an end to it! I'm willing and\nable to be the John Gault people needs. I'm a proficient military commander\nand leader, cyber security expect (hacker) and I've made more progress for\nthe freeman movement than Dean Clifford, Roger Hayes or John Harris ever\ndid.\n\nThank you for your time reading this.\nI hope you and others alike will pick the right side when the time comes.\n\nKind Regards,\n\nHywel ApBuckler\nPrime Technocrat\nUnited Technocracy, GB\nskype: hywel.buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-408f901f","subject":"Cais am ddeiseb ac ymchwiliad cyhoeddus achos buckler v bp 1","name":"0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Aelodau Anrhydeddus y Senedd,\r\n\r\nRwy’n ysgrifennu atoch i dynnu eich sylw at yr hyn yr wyf yn ei ystyried yn\r\nanghyfiawnder hanesyddol difrifol, yn ymwneud â’m teulu, y Bucklers, a\r\ndinistr Great House Farm yn Llandough — safle fferm a chartref o dros 800\r\nmlynedd o hanes, gan gynnwys cysylltiadau mynachaidd a chysylltiad\r\nuniongyrchol â Guglielmo Marconi yn ystod datblygiad cynnar radio.\r\n\r\nMae’r mater hwn yn codi cwestiynau difrifol ynghylch hawliau tir,\r\ngweithdrefnau cyfreithiol, cofrestru tir, a hawliau dynol yng Nghymru.\r\n\r\nEr enghraifft, mewn datganiad i’r wasg yn 1974, dywedodd fy nain yn\r\ngyhoeddus: *“It’s my home.”* Mae’r datganiad hwn, sydd yn fater o gofnod\r\ncyhoeddus, yn gwrth-ddweud yn uniongyrchol ganfyddiad Llys Apêl 1987 yn *BP\r\nv Buckler*, lle dywedwyd ei bod wedi bod yn “ddistaw” ac wedi derbyn\r\ntrwydded BP a gyhoeddwyd yn 1974.\r\n\r\nYn yr un achos, gwrthodwyd apêl fy nhad ar y sail bod BP Pension Trust Ltd\r\na BP Properties Ltd yn “effeithiol yr un cwmni”. Fodd bynnag, yn y\r\ndyfarniad yr oedd yn ei herio, nododd y barnwr nad oedd ymatebion fy nain i\r\nBP Pension Trust Ltd yn cyfrif gan mai BP Properties Ltd oedd yr hawlydd,\r\nac mai cwmnïau ar wahân oeddent. Yn ymarferol, roedd hyn yn arwain at\r\nsefyllfa “pen y cwmni’n ennill, cynffon y teulu’n colli”.\r\n\r\nYn sgil hyn, cafodd fy nhad ei dynnu o’i wely ysbyty, ei garcharu heb\r\ngyhuddiad, a gosodwyd gorchymyn atal arno i’w atal rhag meddiannu ac\r\namddiffyn ein fferm 800 oed rhag cael ei dymchwel. Cafodd ei gais i’r Llys\r\nHawliau Dynol Ewropeaidd ei rwystro cyn iddo farw yn 1991, yn ddim ond 41\r\noed.\r\n\r\nAr y sail hon, rwy’n gofyn yn ffurfiol am *Ddeiseb i sefydlu Ymchwiliad\r\nCyhoeddus* i’r achos hwn, fel mater o ddwyn tir hanesyddol ac o dorri\r\nhawliau dynol yng Nghymru.\r\n\r\nRwy’n weithiwr proffesiynol ym maes seiber a rhyfela electronig milwrol.\r\nMae technolegau AI pwerus bellach ar gael i bob un ohonom, ac nid oes\r\nunrhyw reswm technegol pam na ellid archwilio’r mater hwn yn llawn ac yn\r\ndrylwyr. Mae’r hyn a ddigwyddodd i’m teulu yn ymddangos fel anghyfiawnder\r\ndwys, aml-genhedlaethol, ac yn debyg i ffurf ar “lawfare”, lle y trinwyd fy\r\nnheulu fel llafur di-dâl i gynnal ased tir hyd nes yr oedd yn gyfleus i’w\r\nariannu. Mae’n arwyddocaol bod bron pob cam yn ein herbyn wedi digwydd ar\r\nyr eiliad olaf posibl.\r\n\r\nCeir honiadau bod sylw sylweddol yn y wasg yn 1974 o blaid fy nain a’n\r\nteulu, ynghyd â deiseb o tua 1,700 o bobl yn ceisio atal dymchwel y fferm.\r\nYmhellach, mae’n ymddangos bod CADW wedi methu ag ymyrryd lle dylai’r safle\r\nfod wedi cael statws Adeilad Rhestredig Gradd II.\r\n\r\nNid wyf yn sicr a gofnodwyd erioed yn briodol yn y Gofrestrfa Tir fod y tir\r\n— a gofrestrwyd gan BP yn 1982 — dan anghydfod. Yn fy nealltwriaeth i,\r\ncafodd ei drin fel pe na bai mewn anghydfod o gwbl. Nid oes unrhyw lys wedi\r\npenderfynu’n derfynol mai BP oedd perchnogion cyfreithiol y tir; cafodd\r\nhynny ei honni yn hytrach na’i brofi.\r\n\r\nMae hefyd fater pwysig o hanes diwylliannol. Arhosodd Marconi gyda’n teulu\r\nyn y fferm wrth iddo ddatblygu radio. Mae cynghorwyr a’r plwyf yn Llandough\r\nyn gwrthod cydnabod hyn. Rwy’n deall bod Marconi yn cael ei ystyried yn\r\nwleidyddol eithafol ar y dde, ac, fel y gwelir yn achos y cerflun radio ym\r\nMae Caerdydd, mae ei rôl hanesyddol yn cael ei hailysgrifennu. Mae’n\r\nrhesymol tybio bod ein teulu wedi cael ei ddal mewn ymgyrch wleidyddol\r\nehangach o’r chwith yn erbyn y dde, ac mai am roi llety i Marconi y bu i ni\r\nwynebu canlyniadau canrif o hyd — problemau nad oedd yn bodoli yn y tair\r\ncanrif flaenorol yr oeddem wedi byw ar y fferm.\r\n\r\nRoedd mam Marconi hefyd yn Jamerson o gwmni wisgi Gwyddelig Jameson. Rwy’n\r\ngofyn i chi gynnal eich ymchwil eich hun, gwneud eich ymholiadau eich hun,\r\na dod i’ch casgliadau eich hun — ond yn anad dim, peidiwch â chaniatáu i\r\nhanes gael ei ailysgrifennu yma.\r\n\r\nMae fy nheulu bellach yn archwilio opsiynau ar gyfer siarad cyhoeddus,\r\nhawliau stori, a dogfennaeth. Yn nhermau cysylltiadau teuluol: fy nhaid\r\noedd Ray Smith o Dempsey and Makepeace; mae fy modryb yn Shan Cothi; a\r\ndechreuodd fy ewythr y band Tigertailz.\r\n\r\nRwy’n disgrifio’r sefyllfa hon fel gwarthus. Mae fy nheulu’n mynnu\r\ncyfiawnder am gael ein dadleoli a’n dwyn o’n tir a’n heiddo gan y Sefydliad\r\nPrydeinig a BP, gyda phrin unrhyw amddiffyniad dan y gyfraith. Rydym yn\r\ndeulu Cymreig brodorol, Cymraeg eu hiaith, wedi byw yng Nghaerdydd, Bro\r\nMorgannwg, a’r fferm yn Llandough ers cannoedd o flynyddoedd.\r\n\r\nO’r hyn y gallaf ei gasglu, ceir dwsinau o achosion posibl o dwyll a\r\nchuddio gwybodaeth, sy’n golygu nad yw statud cyfyngiadau yn berthnasol o\r\nreidrwydd. I’r rhai sy’n cefnogi dad-drefedigaethu Cymru ac annibyniaeth,\r\nprin y ceir enghraifft gliriach na *BP v Buckler (1987)* o’r hyn a\r\nddigwyddodd i deulu ffermio Cymreig wrth herio’r Wladwriaeth Brydeinig a\r\nchorfforaeth fawr. Nid yw eraill wedi codi’r mater hwn, yn bennaf oherwydd\r\ntrawma cenhedlaethol.\r\n\r\nRwyf wedi profi fy hun. Gadewais fy ngyrfa filwrol gydag anrhydedd, gan\r\ngwblhau fy llw 22 mlynedd. Cefais fy nghyflogi’n bona fide gan Gyngor Bro\r\nMorgannwg a Llywodraeth Cymru hyd at 2024. Gwasanaethais mewn rhyfeloedd yn\r\ny Dwyrain Canol. Fodd bynnag, nid yw’r anghyfiawnder fferm yn fater unigol.\r\n\r\nYn 2013, cafodd fy mab 36 diwrnod oed ei gipio, ac nid wyf erioed wedi ei\r\nweld ers hynny. Cafodd tŷ ei ddwyn oddi arnaf (40 Lombard Street, Y Barri).\r\nYn 2023, cefais fy ngadael i gysgu mewn pabell tra roedd bron i 100 o\r\nAfghanistaniaid yn cael eu lletya’n dawel wrth ymyl ein pentref o 11 tŷ,\r\ntra roedd yn rhaid imi aros yno i ofalu am fy nain gan na allai gofalwyr ei\r\nchyrraedd.\r\n\r\nO ganlyniad, rwyf bellach yn byw yn yr hyn a elwir yn Setliad Cymreig yn yr\r\nAriannin. Rwyf wedi fy nisodli ac wedi fy dadleoli i’r eithaf. Serch hynny,\r\nrwy’n ddiolchgar fy mod wedi goroesi gyda’m rhyddid, fy mywyd, a’m henw da\r\nyn gymharol gyfan. Serch hynny, hoffwn fod wedi aros yng Nghymru, fel\r\nCymro, gyda safon a chynhaliaeth bywyd deg.\r\n\r\nMae fy ngwraig a minnau’n amharod i ganiatáu i’n merch hyd yn oed gamu ar\r\nYnysoedd Prydain o ystyried yr hyn a glywn sy’n digwydd yno. Yn 2024,\r\nallforiais hyd yn oed fy nghi o Abertawe i’n heiddo yn y Caribî ar ôl i\r\nunigolyn Afghanistan fod yng ngardd fy nheulu yng Nghymru, gan geisio ei\r\nddwyn.\r\n\r\nGofynnaf i’r Senedd gymryd y mater hwn o ddifrif, ac ystyried sefydlu\r\nYmchwiliad Cyhoeddus llawn, tryloyw ac annibynnol. Nid er budd fy nheulu yn\r\nunig y mae hyn, ond er uniondeb hanes, cyfiawnder tir, a hawliau dynol yng\r\nNghymru.\r\n\r\nYn gywir,\r\n\r\n*Requester Hywel Buckler*\r\n\r\n*----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*\r\n\r\nSirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am writing to you regarding a significant historical injustice involving\r\nmy family, the Bucklers, and the destruction of Great House Farm (an\r\n800-year-old site of monastic and Marconi history).\r\n\r\nFor example, in a 1974 press statement my grandmother said publically 'It's\r\nmy home'—that directly contradicts the 1987 Court of Appeal ruling that she\r\nwas 'silent' and accepted of BP license issued in 1974. My dad's appeal for\r\nthe BP vs Buckler 1987 case also got dismissed on grounds both BP Pension\r\nTrust Ltd and BP Properties Ltd were effectively the same company. But in\r\nthe ruling he was appealing, the judge said that my nans replies to BP\r\nPensions Trust Ltd didn't count as BP Properties Ltd were the claimant, and\r\nthe two were seperate companies. So it was heads they win, tails we lose.\r\nMy dad was ripped from his hospital bed, jailed without charge and slapped\r\nwith a restraining order to keep him from occupying and defending our 800\r\nyear old farm from being bulldozed down. His ECHR request blocked before he\r\ndied in 1991 aged just 41.\r\n\r\nI am requesting a *Petition for a Public Inquiry* into this case as a\r\nmatter of historical land theft and human rights violations in Wales.\r\n\r\nI'm a military cyber and electronic warfare professional. We all have very\r\npowerful AI technology at our disposal which can make light work out of all\r\nof this. My family suffered an incredible injustice. It also appears to be\r\nmulti-generational warfare/ lawfare. Whereby we were treated as free labour\r\nto upkeep the asset of the land and property until it was ripe to be cashed\r\nin. I say this as every action against us seemed to be last minute.\r\n\r\nThere was allegedly press covering the 74 case and supporting my nan and\r\nfamily and farm. There was a petition of 1700 people trying to defend us\r\nand the farm from demolishment. CADW looked the other way when it should\r\nhave been a Grade II listed building. I could go on and on and on.\r\n\r\nI'm not even sure the land registry recorded that our land, being\r\nregistered in 1982 by BP , was in dispute. I believe it was treated as if\r\nit wasn't dispited. No court actually definitively determined that BP were\r\nthe landowners. It was just asserted.\r\n\r\nMarconi stayed with our family at our farm when inventing radio. The\r\ncouncillors and parish at Llandough won't even acknowledge this. I\r\nunderstand Marconi was far right and so, like the radio statute at Cardiff\r\nBay has confirmed, he is being re-written out of history.  It stands to\r\nreason that our family was caught in this political campaign of left vs\r\nright. And for helping Marconi we found ourselves experiencing a century of\r\nproblems afterwards. Which didn't exist for the 3 centuries we were at our\r\nfarm before letting far right marconi stay with us. Marconi's mother was\r\nalso Jamerson of the Irish Whiskey company.\r\n\r\nDo your own homework. Make your own enquiries. Draw your own conclusions.\r\n\r\n But please do not let history be rewritten here. My family are exploring\r\noptions for public speaking, story rights, and a documentary etc.\r\n\r\nMy grandfather was Ray Smith, of Dempsey and Makepeace. My aunty Shan\r\nCothi. My uncle started the band tigertailz.\r\n\r\nThis is an outrage and my family demands justice for being displaced and\r\nstolen from, land and property, by the British Establishment/ BP -  with\r\nlittle to no protections under law. And we're indigenous to the land,\r\nWelsh, Welsh speaking, Welsh family. Resident in Cardiff / Vale and that\r\nfarm in Llandough for HUNDREDS OF YEARS.\r\n\r\nThere's tens of counts of fraud and concealment from what I can gather.\r\nWhich means the statute of limitation doesn't apply in this instance. I\r\nknow some are in favour of Wales decolonising and gaining independence. I\r\nthink there's no better example of BP vs Buckler 1987 and what has happened\r\nto my family. Nobody else will bring this up because there's generational\r\ntrauma. Notwithstanding we, a welsh farming family, are speaking up and\r\nagainst the British State and BP.\r\n\r\nBut I've proven myself. Leaving my military career with honours. Finishing\r\nmy 22 years Oath, bona fide, employed by the Vale of Glamorgan Council,\r\nWelsh Government until 2024. I served in the wars in the middle east. I\r\ndon't know what is going on, on that island. But the farm injustice isn't\r\nthe only matter. My 36 day old son was abducted in 2013 and I've never seen\r\nhim since. I had a house stolen (40 Lombard Street, Barry). And in 2023 I\r\nwas left to sleep in a tent, while almost 100 afghans were secretly housed\r\nnext to our 11 home village. Where I had to be to care for my grandmother,\r\nas no carers couldn't reach her. So I'm currently at the Welsh Settlement\r\nin Argentina. So I'm as displaced and replaced as I can be to cater for the\r\ninsanity that's going on, on that island. And grateful I've managed to\r\nsurvive it all with my liberty and life and reputation somewhat still\r\nintact. But I would have actually liked to have remained in Wales as a\r\nWelshman. And have some quality and standard of life. My wife and I are\r\nreluctant for our daughter to even step foot on the British Isles with what\r\nwe're hearing that's going on there lately. And I even exported my dog from\r\nSwansea to our place in the Caribbean in 2024 after an afghan was in my\r\nfamily's garden in Wales, trying to steal him.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your reply,\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Hywel Buckler\r\n"},{"id":"wb-c52361b1","subject":"Cais am ddeiseb ac ymchwiliad cyhoeddus achos buckler v bp 1","name":"0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Wed, 04 Feb 2026 06:37 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMP,\n\nFurther to my last email, please would you;\n\n- Pose a Parliamentary Question to the UK Government about the historical\ncase or current land registration policies.\n\n- Request a debate on historical property disputes.\n\n- Refer me to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman a I have\nevidence of maladministration by a public body (e.g. Land Registry, court,\ncouncil, CADW etc).\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n[phone redacted]\n\nOn Sun, 1 Feb 2026, 09:13 NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP), <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Hello,\n>\n> Thank you for reaching out to me. This is just a quick note to confirm\n> that we’ve received your email.\n>\n> As your MP for the Vale of Glamorgan, my priority is supporting local\n> constituents who need help with urgent issues. I receive a high volume of\n> emails every day, so while I will do my best to get back to you as soon as\n> possible, there may be a slight delay—especially if you’re contacting me\n> about policy matters or upcoming legislation. Please know that your message\n> has been logged, and I’ll respond as soon as I can.\n> Constituency Casework\n>\n> If you need my help with a personal case, please make sure your email\n> includes:\n> ✔ Your full name\n> ✔ Your full address (including postcode)\n> ✔ A contact method (email or phone)\n> ✔ Details of your case (including any relevant reference numbers)\n>\n> A member of my casework team will be in touch as soon as possible.\n> Am I Your MP?\n>\n> Due to parliamentary protocol, I can only take up casework for people\n> living in the *Vale of Glamorgan*. If you’re unsure whether I’m your MP,\n> you can check by entering your postcode here:*\n> <http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>**findyourmp.parliament.uk\n> <http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>*.\n> Getting in Touch\n>\n> The best way to contact me is by email. My office is open Monday to\n> Friday, 9 AM to 5 PM, and we’ll do our best to respond as soon as we can.\n>\n> You can also keep up with my work here:\n> 📌 *Facebook:* [KanishkafortheVale]\n> 📌 *Instagram:* [@valekanishka]\n> 📌 *X (Twitter):* [@KanishkaNarayan]\n> Emergency Contacts\n>\n> If you need urgent assistance, here are some useful contacts:\n> 📞 *NHS Wales (Non-Emergency Medical Advice):* 111\n> 🚨 *Emergency Services (Police, Fire, Ambulance):* 999\n> 🏥 *Mental Health Support (Samaritans Cymru):* [phone redacted]\n> 🏠 *Homelessness Support (Shelter Cymru):* [phone redacted]\n> 👮 *South Wales Police (Non-Emergency):* 101\n>\n> Thanks again for getting in touch—I really appreciate hearing from people\n> across our community. My team and I look forward to assisting you.\n>\n> Best wishes,\n> Kanishka\n>\n>\n>\n> *Kanishka Narayan MP*\n>\n> Member of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\n>\n> Minister for AI and Online Safety\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> UK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended\n> recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and\n> delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is\n> not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability\n> is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail.\n> This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used\n> for sensitive data.\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-8a5b2eec","subject":"Cais am ddeiseb ac ymchwiliad cyhoeddus achos buckler v bp 1","name":"0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-bbc393dc","subject":"Cais am gyngor cyfreithiol Tŷ Mawr Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-t-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-6f137bb2","subject":"Church view close Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_church-view-close-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_church-view-close-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"church-view-close-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_church-view-close-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI'm piecing together something I experienced in Llandough in 1988. From\r\npublic record, my research and family testemony. And media.\r\n\r\nThis is ongoing but here's a video of where my mind at is so far. It's\r\nlooking very aweful. I just thought I'd share this to invite you to\r\ncomment/ advise on any of this case.\r\n\r\nMy family seem to have been murdered into silence. But have never\r\nsurrendered claim to land in Llandough. Our home, my home, since 1667.\r\n\r\nI am trying to communicate this story and please understand its\r\nchallenging. There's trauma, anger/ upset and it's fragmented across family\r\nand various historic govenrment archives. It's collosal and multi\r\ngenerational too.\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nWebsite below. I will work to get all these evidence onto this website so\r\nthere's a chrononical timeline and central location for the evidence.\r\n\r\nThis matter is unresolved in many ways and I feel it needs to be handled. I\r\nfeel it's unacceptable all this could have been allowed to have happened\r\nand gone on and buried or ignored for decades.\r\n\r\nFor authority to be authority there in South Wales, there must be\r\nlegitimacy. Be legitimate about this is all I ask.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n"},{"id":"wb-d522330a","subject":"Clarification required FOI EIR request case ref 00210772","name":"0000-00-00_clarification-required-foi_eir-request-case-ref-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_clarification-required-foi_eir-request-case-ref-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"clarification-required-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00210772","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_clarification-required-foi_eir-request-case-ref-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDear Requester\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWe write further in relation to your request for information, referenced above.\r\n\r\nThe relevant service area have requested we ask the below. We would be grateful if you could provide some clarification on the following point(s):\r\n\r\nPlease can we ask for a plan showing the locations? We have found great house farm but the request includes Ty Mawr / Great House Estate and we are not clear the extent of the site being queried. \r\n\r\n\r\nThis will help us to identify and locate the information you are seeking and ensure we provide you with the most relevant response.\r\n\r\nPlease note that the statutory response deadline is paused while we await your clarification. Once we receive your response, we will resume processing your request.\r\n\r\nIf we do not hear from you within [e.g. 2 months], we may consider the request closed\r\n\r\nYours sincerely,\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nInformation Governance Officer/ Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\r\n\r\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\r\n\r\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\r\n\r\ntel / ffôn: 01446 700111\r\n\r\ne-mail / e-bost: foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk or dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\r\n\r\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\r\n\r\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\r\n\r\nFollow us on Twitter /Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\r\n"},{"id":"wb-0754fcc1","subject":"Coflein government archives evidence for great house farm ty","name":"0000-00-00_coflein-government-archives-evidence-for-great-house-farm-ty_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_coflein-government-archives-evidence-for-great-house-farm-ty_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"coflein-government-archives-evidence-for-great-house-farm-ty","scopeTopics":["family"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["family"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_coflein-government-archives-evidence-for-great-house-farm-ty_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Evidence from Coflein.gov.uk (RCAHMW) for Great House Farm, Llandough (NPRN 20182):\n\nSite Details:\nNPRN 20182\nMap Reference: ST17SE\nGrid Reference: ST1681073310\nUnitary Authority: The Vale of Glamorgan\nOld County: Glamorgan\nCommunity: Llandough\nType Of Site: DWELLING\nPeriod: Post Medieval\n\nDescription:\n1. Demolished December 1988.\n2. A farmhouse of limestone construction of uncertain date. Internal details suggest that the house was C17, however certain features suggest that the core of the house may have been medieval. The house was altered and reconstructed by the Bute estate in the C19, and much of the exterior would seem to have dated from this period. (Source: Site File notes by Richard Suggett)\nJ Hill 26/04/2004\n3. Early medieval cemetery excavated, on land adjacent to Great House Farm, by Cotswold Archaeology, 1994.\n\nRelated Archives (text descriptions only):\n- Archive Number 6524751: Glamorgan Gwent Archaeological Trust report \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: comments and recommendations on the planning application, assessment of the archaeological implications of development,\" dated August 1990. Planning application no. 89/01396/OUT. Medium: Graphic, Text, Cartographic.\n- Archive Number 6416853: Plans relating to the excavation of an early-medieval monastic cemetery on land at Great House Farm, Llandough. Entitled 'Llandough Publication Report'. Produced by Cotswold Archaeology: Project Number 0381; Site Code LLAN94.\n- Archive Number 6500905: Set of microfiche copies of records produced during the 1997 excavation of land at Great House Farm, Llandough, carried out by K. Watson. Medium: Cartographic, Graphic, Text, Photo.\n- Archive Number 6048941: Ink drawing showing plan of Great House Farm, Llandough, showing periods of construction. Scale 1:100. Additions made 12/12/1988.\n- Archive Number 6048946: Photocopy of a newspaper article concerning the demolition of Great House Farm, Llandough.\n- Archive Number 6048944: Two newspaper cuttings concerning the proposed demolition of Great House Farm, Llandough. One taken from the Western Mail, dated 19/11/1974 and one from the Daily Telegraph dated 16/04/1974.\n- Archive Number 6048937: Copy of a newspaper concerning the proposed demolition of Great House Farm, Llandough.\n- Archive Number 6048942: Descriptive account of Great House Farm, Llandough.\n- Archive Number 6048938: Photocopy of a newspaper article concerning the demolition of Great House Farm, Llandough.\n- Archive Number 6048945: Descriptive account of Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nNo direct PDF or image attachments were available for download from the listings page. Request full archives from RCAHMW/GlamRO for potential evidence supporting family title and history."},{"id":"wb-d65895e7","subject":"Communication concerning the destruction of great house farm","name":"0000-00-00_communication-concerning-the-destruction-of-great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_communication-concerning-the-destruction-of-great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"communication-concerning-the-destruction-of-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_communication-concerning-the-destruction-of-great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"My dad was William Buckler in the legal case BP vs Buckler 1987. I have\r\nconcerns to raise about this whole ordeal.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis was not just an eviction — it’s a layered heritage injustice:\r\n\r\nDisplacement of an indigenous family (Bucklers) under imposed UK\r\nnationality law.\r\n\r\nErasure of cultural memory (Roman burials, child graves, farming heritage).\r\n\r\nSuppression of scientific history (Marconi’s stay, linked to the invention\r\nof radio).\r\n\r\nIgnored community objections (local petitions against demolition, which\r\nthemselves are part of “intangible cultural heritage”).\r\n\r\nNo memorialisation (the new development has no plaque, no marker\r\nacknowledging the history).\r\n\r\nII. Facts of the Case\r\n\r\n1. Eviction and Demolition (1987):\r\n\r\nThe Buckler family were evicted from Great House Farm following litigation\r\nbrought by BP, supported by UK authorities.\r\n\r\nThe farm was demolished against the wishes of the local community.\r\n\r\nMy family maintained we always owned it. I believe the whole legal case was\r\na kangaroo court. And my family and the public were outsmarted. I believe\r\nevidence exists proving my family actually did become equitable title\r\nholders of the farm. And did own it. We were not squatters living rent free\r\nfor decades as was suggested in the court documents. Which is itself an\r\nabsurd claim.\r\n\r\n2. Imposed Nationality:\r\n\r\nAt the time of eviction, Mrs. Buckler was a Welsh national with ancestral\r\nties to the land.\r\n\r\nShe did not freely consent to become a UK citizen; British citizenship was\r\nimposed under the British Nationality Act 1948 and 1981.\r\n\r\nThis imposition extinguished her indigenous status in law, but not in fact.\r\n\r\nThe court proceedings never considered her as an indigenous Welsh person,\r\nnor her ancestral rights to the land.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Cultural & Scientific Significance:\r\n\r\nGreat House Farm is historically significant as a residence of Guglielmo\r\nMarconi during his pioneering experiments leading to the invention of radio.\r\n\r\nThe site also contained Roman burials and child graves, representing unique\r\narchaeological heritage.\r\n\r\nDespite this, no plaque or marker exists on the new development to\r\nacknowledge Marconi’s presence or the heritage of the land.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Community Opposition:\r\n\r\nLocal residents petitioned against the demolition of the farm in 1987.\r\n\r\nObjections raised by the community were disregarded.\r\n\r\nThe demolition destroyed not only a building, but also the intangible\r\ncultural heritage of the community’s relationship with the farm and its\r\nhistory.\r\n\r\n\r\nCADW refused to list the building as protected.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIII. Grounds for Complaint\r\n\r\nViolation of the 1970 UNESCO Convention: The destruction and concealment of\r\ncultural property (Roman burials, graves, artifacts) constitutes illicit\r\nremoval and suppression of heritage.\r\n\r\nViolation of the 1972 World Heritage Convention: Sites of outstanding\r\nuniversal value (Marconi’s residence, archaeological burials) were\r\ndemolished without recognition or protection.\r\n\r\nViolation of Indigenous/Minority Rights: The Buckler family, as indigenous\r\nWelsh nationals, were displaced through the imposition of foreign\r\nnationality law and denied ancestral rights to their land.\r\n\r\nViolation of Intangible Heritage (2003 Convention): The petitions and\r\nobjections of the community are part of cultural memory, yet no recognition\r\nor preservation exists.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIV. Relief Requested\r\n\r\nWe respectfully request that UNESCO:\r\n\r\n1. Acknowledge the destruction of Great House Farm as a cultural and\r\nhistorical loss to Wales and humanity.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Investigate the circumstances of the eviction and demolition, including\r\nthe role of BP and the UK government.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Recommend that the site be marked with a plaque or memorial\r\nacknowledging its historical significance (Marconi, Roman burials, Buckler\r\nfamily).\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Call upon the UK government to release any records concerning\r\narchaeological excavations or heritage suppression at the site.\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Recognise the Buckler family and local community as bearers of an\r\nintangible cultural heritage unjustly erased.\r\n\r\n\r\nMy family were displaced and tresspasses in a rotten way. I am seeking any\r\njustice for what I perceive to be hybrid human rights violations and war\r\ncrimes upon my family. And a most certain conspiracy against us.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your reply,\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\nCEO\r\nDATRO Security Group\r\nDATRO Consortium Ltd\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-a14a5100","subject":"Confirm your FOI request to hm courts and tribunals service","name":"0000-00-00_confirm-your-foi-request-to-hm-courts-and-tribunals-service_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_confirm-your-foi-request-to-hm-courts-and-tribunals-service_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"confirm-your-foi-request-to-hm-courts-and-tribunals-service","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_confirm-your-foi-request-to-hm-courts-and-tribunals-service_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Confirm your FOI request to HM Courts and Tribunals Service\nFrom: (name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com address)\nDate: Wed, 28 Jan 2026 06:40 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSion Buckler,\n\nYou just tried to sign up to WhatDoTheyKnow, when you already have an account. Your name and password have been left as they previously were. Please click on the link below.\n\nThen your FOI request to HM Courts and Tribunals Service will be sent and published.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/c/8hvhnz06816ks0fo5rb\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n"},{"id":"wb-798d0000","subject":"Confirm your FOI request to ministry of justice","name":"0000-00-00_confirm-your-foi-request-to-ministry-of-justice_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI 