thout confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-d789475c","subject":"Dude in Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_dude-in-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_dude-in-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"dude-in-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_dude-in-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Dude in Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 23 May 2023 16:29 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nhttps://vm.tiktok.com/ZM2LqeDJa/\n"},{"id":"wb-058eea3f","subject":"EIR request historic water supply records for great house fa","name":"0000-00-00_eir-request-historic-water-supply-records-for-great-house-fa_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_eir-request-historic-water-supply-records-for-great-house-fa_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"eir-request-historic-water-supply-records-for-great-house-fa","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_eir-request-historic-water-supply-records-for-great-house-fa_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear EIR Team,\r\n\r\nUnder the Environmental Information Regulations, please provide all records\r\nof water supply applications, connections, refusals, correspondence, or\r\nservice issues for Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff),\r\nparticularly involving my late gran Mary Williams or our Buckler family in\r\nthe 1900s-1980s. Include any notes on dairy operations, health impacts, or\r\nestate disputes (Western Ground Rents/Bute).\r\n\r\nThis supports family historical research into occupation and equitable\r\ntitle claims tied to a Daniel Thomas quarry deal. Thank you.\r\n\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Ret'd Sergeant\r\n"},{"id":"wb-28d3265e","subject":"EIR FOI request 00210772","name":"0000-00-00_eir_foi-request-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_eir_foi-request-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"eir-foi-request-00210772","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_eir_foi-request-00210772_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\r\n\r\nThe Council's Information Governance Team works collaboratively, and requests are managed collectively across the team rather than by individual officers. For this reason, correspondence is not issued under individual names. The team is managed by Evelyn Morgan who is the Council's Data Protection Officer/Information Manager.\r\n\r\nWe appreciate the detailed correspondence you have provided to date and understand that this matter is of importance to you. We have received multiple items of correspondence from you, including earlier requests relating to the legal case of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler. Work had already been undertaken to review this request and we were in the process of preparing a response when your more recent correspondence was received. We were aiming to ensure that all appropriate lines of enquiry had been explored before providing a response.\r\n\r\nAt this stage, we would like to clarify that the Vale of Glamorgan Council does not hold records relating to this historic legal matter. Neither the Council nor its predecessor authorities, the Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council or the former South Glamorgan County Council were involved in the case of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler. From the information available, it appears this was a private legal matter between BP Properties Ltd and the Buckler family. We also recognise that your enquiries extend beyond the Council and have been shared with a number of organisations. Some of the information you are seeking is more likely to be held elsewhere and not with the Council. Some information that may have historically been retained by the Council may now be held by the Glamorgan Archives but only in relation to historical land ownership, tenancy records, or court administrative deposits. Some information may also be obtainable from the Land Registry, but we can see that they have been included in your correspondence.\r\n\r\nIn terms of information the Council may hold, this is most likely limited to planning related records. As previously advised, in order for our Planning colleagues to conduct accurate searches, they have requested a copy of the relevant site plan. Without this, there is a risk that any searches undertaken may not capture all relevant records.  We note that this does not mean there are records just that in trying to cover every possibility we have asked for a site plan to complete this aspect of our enquiries.  There may not be anything held but, we are trying to search for you.  It is entirely a matter for you as to whether you provide a site plan. If you do not wish to provide one you do not have to but that will restrict our enquiries as it will be difficult to pin down the correct area.\r\n\r\nWe are looking to assist in providing you with a full response as soon as possible with the information that is held by the Council. Your cooperation in providing the requested plan will help us progress this matter efficiently.\r\n\r\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\r\n\r\nKind regards\r\n\r\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\r\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\r\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\r\ntel / ffôn: 01446 700111\r\ne-mail / e-bost: foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk or dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\r\n\r\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\r\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\r\n\r\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\r\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\r\n\r\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\r\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\r\n\r\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\r\n\r\nFrom: Requester <[redacted]>\r\nSent: 01 June 2026 23:10\r\nTo: FOI Unit <FoiUnit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\r\nSubject: Re: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)\r\n\r\nWhat is your name please?\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n\r\nOn Mon, 1 Jun 2026, 10:52 FOI Unit, <FoiUnit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:FoiUnit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>> wrote:\r\nDear Mr Buckler\r\n\r\nThank you for the below. We note its contents in relation to Freedom of Information however, we wrote to you (copy attached) seeking clarification on a previous request received by you which relates to the same matter.\r\n\r\nWe are unable to progress your request until this clarification has been received.\r\n\r\nKind regards\r\n\r\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\r\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\r\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\r\ntel / ffôn: 01446 700111\r\ne-mail / e-bost: foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk> or dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\r\n\r\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\r\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\r\n\r\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\r\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\r\n\r\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\r\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\r\n\r\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\r\n\r\nFrom: Requester <[redacted]<mailto:[redacted]>>\r\nSent: 29 May 2026 19:48\r\nTo: Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <Glamro@cardiff.gov.uk<mailto:Glamro@cardiff.gov.uk>>\r\nSubject: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)\r\n\r\nLEGAL NOTICE TO RECIPIENTS:\r\nTake notice that this request is issued in anticipation of formal legal proceedings and the filing of an official report regarding systemic institutional fraud, land misconduct, and the unlawful concealment of historic preservation data. You are under a strict legal duty to preserve all physical and electronic records, metadata, correspondence, maps, and erased files relating to this site. Any spoliation, deletion, or withholding of data will be cited in subsequent court filings.\r\nDear Freedom of Information Officer,\r\nRE: Information Request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the Environmental Information Regulations 2004\r\nI am writing to request access to historical records, internal correspondence, planning briefs, and assessments held by your organization regarding Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth/Cardiff (demolished December 1988), and the historical occupancy of the Buckler family.\r\nStatutory Mandate on Accessibility & Charging Fees:\r\nI am aware that previous attempts to locate this data have resulted in directives to visit physical archives in person or use paywalled, commercial third-party web portals. Please be advised of the following statutory obligations:\r\n\r\n  1.  Under EIR Regulation 8, fees cannot act as an unreasonable barrier or deterrent to access. Because my family was historically displaced from this site and I am executing this request remotely, forcing physical attendance or demanding payment constitutes an unlawful obstacle.\r\n  2.  Public authorities are required to supply information in the format requested. I require all documents to be delivered digitally via email attachment or secure electronic download link, free of charge, as specified by the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) guidelines for data already held electronically.\r\nPlease provide all recorded information matching the following points:\r\n1. Tenant/Ownership Identification and the 1880 Report\r\n\r\n  *   Any documents, archival notes, or registry indexes citing the William/ Buckler family line (who occupied and farmed the house across four generations).\r\n  *   Clarification on whether my family members were formally cited as the legal owners, long-term tenants, or registered reporters of the 1880 discovery under the dining room floor.\r\n  *   Any explicit records indicating gaps, deleted metadata, or missing volumes in your authority's archive concerning the tenancy, land-dispute maps, or agricultural heritage of Great House Farm between 1950 and 1989.\r\n2. Statutory Protection and Cadw's Assessments\r\n\r\n  *   Given that the site's extreme archaeological value (a 1st-to-4th-century Roman precursor villa and a massive early medieval monastic settlement) was verified by rescue operations as early as 1979, what are the recorded reasons why Cadw failed to place a statutory Schedule or Protection Order on the standing fabric of Great House Farm before its demolition?\r\n  *   All internal correspondence, risk assessments, or ministerial briefs evaluating the preservation value of the sub-medieval direct-entry farmhouse core before it was levelled.\r\n3. Planning Approvals and Local Authority Governance\r\n\r\n  *   All minutes, planning committee files, and consultation responses from the local authority that granted planning permission and housing development rights on this specific acreage.\r\n  *   Direct information explaining how the council approved planning permission for a private housing development in light of the documented historical evidence surrounding the immediate parish boundary.\r\n4. Institutional Concealment and Historical \"Ignorance\"\r\n\r\n  *   Records showing exactly where and at what stage of the planning process this archaeological evidence should have been brought up but was not, which ultimately allowed developers and public bodies to claim they were unaware of the land's deep significance until after the farmhouse was destroyed and housing development began.\r\n  *   Any environmental impact assessments, historic environment register (HER) lookups, or developer briefs filed between 1980 and 1990 regarding the footprint of Great House Farm.\r\nIf any part of this request is refused under the guise of commercial sensitivity or archival limitations, you are required by law to state the exact statutory exemption applied and provide a formal internal review pathway.\r\nI expect your response within the statutory 20-working-day timeframe.\r\nKind regards,\r\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---------- Forwarded message ----------\r\nFrom: FOI Unit <FoiUnit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:FoiUnit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>>\r\nTo: \"[redacted]<mailto:[redacted]>\" <[redacted]<mailto:[redacted]>>\r\nCc:\r\nBcc:\r\nDate: Thu, 28 May 2026 11:04:26 +0000\r\nSubject: Clarification required - FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00210772\r\nDear Requester\r\n\r\nWe write further in relation to your request for information, referenced above.\r\n\r\nThe relevant service area have requested we ask the below. We would be grateful if you could provide some clarification on the following point(s):\r\nPlease can we ask for a plan showing the locations? We have found great house farm but the request includes Ty Mawr / Great House Estate and we are not clear the extent of the site being queried.\r\n\r\nThis will help us to identify and locate the information you are seeking and ensure we provide you with the most relevant response.\r\n\r\nPlease note that the statutory response deadline is paused while we await your clarification. Once we receive your response, we will resume processing your request.\r\n\r\nIf we do not hear from you within [e.g. 2 months], we may consider the request closed\r\nYours sincerely,\r\n\r\n\r\nInformation Governance Officer/ Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\r\n\r\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\r\n\r\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\r\n\r\ntel / ffôn: 01446 700111\r\n\r\ne-mail / e-bost: foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:foiunit@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk> or dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<mailto:dpo@valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\r\n\r\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\r\n\r\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<http://en-gb.facebook.com/valeofglamorganlife>\r\n\r\nFollow us on Twitter /Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\r\n"},{"id":"wb-0eb2c550","subject":"Enquiry ref marconi and buckler family","name":"0000-00-00_enquiry-ref-marconi-and-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_enquiry-ref-marconi-and-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"enquiry-ref-marconi-and-buckler-family","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_enquiry-ref-marconi-and-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am Requester, the son of William Buckler.\r\nMy father fought BP in the legal case: BP vs Buckler 1987.\r\nI wish to notify you of a scandal concerning this case and Marconi.\r\n\r\nMarconi was staying with my family at our farm (Great House Farm,\r\nLlandough, Wales) when he invented the first working radio.\r\nAfter BP stole our farm via lawfare. And demolished it. Our 800 farm was\r\nalmost immediately bulldozed down, and covered with 23 houses.\r\nTo this day there is not even a plaque to commemorate or acknowledge\r\nMarconi was ever there, or radio was invented from this location.\r\nAs you can see when I bring this up with my local parish and councillors\r\nthe response is not cooperation or compassion or just.\r\n\r\nThe entire case is suspect. The way the farm was taken from us is suspect.\r\nWhat was exhevtated from under the ground was suspect.\r\nMy fathers appeal was dismissed, which was also suspect. Basically when BP\r\nProperties were the claimant, the judge stated my grandmother's response to\r\nBP didn't count as her response was to BP Pension Trust Ltd (the alleged\r\npossessor), which didn't count as them and BP Properties were seperate\r\ncompanies. Also this was after my nan died, so she was unable to defend her\r\nposition. But until the day she died she maintained we owned our farm. But\r\nin my dads appearance, where he raised the issue the claimant was not the\r\nalleged possessor, it was dismissed citing the two companies were basically\r\nthe same.\r\nSo it was a case of 'heads they win, tails we lose' and this entire case is\r\nriddled with fraud, concealment and scandal.\r\nMy fathers appeal to the European Court of Human Rights was shut down by\r\nour Government too. Also suspect.\r\nHe then died very abruptly and young. The age me and my older brother are\r\nnow.\r\n\r\nI wish to spearhead a lawsuit and sue BP and the British Government.\r\nUnder the UK Limitation Act clause concerning fraud and concealment I am\r\nable to re-open this case.\r\n\r\nThe Italian government may wish to investigate this by its own accord.\r\nBut I appear to have made the most ground in this investigation because of\r\nmy connection to this case.\r\nAnd my background in military cyber warfare, which helps me utilize\r\ntechnologies to aggregate the data.\r\nMy last employer, upon completion of my 22 Years in Oath to the Crown last\r\nyear, was the Welsh Government.\r\n\r\nIf the Italian Government would like to sponsor or endorse my work, I would\r\nbe grateful.\r\nI think it would be poetic justice if you were to assist me in this\r\nendeavour.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-554fe03e","subject":"Enquiry BP v Buckler","name":"0000-00-00_enquiry-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_enquiry-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"enquiry-bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_enquiry-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI try to access videos and I'm prevented saying I need to register and/or\r\nbe in clip corner.\r\n\r\nI'm currently in Patagonia. For my own safety. I'm making the allegation\r\nthat it was BP and British State fraud, theft and consealment of evidence\r\nthat led to my family being dispossessed of our land of centuries.\r\n\r\nHelp me out please.\r\nSee attach the footage I seek.\r\n\r\nAllegedly there was also coverage in 1974 too. I seek that too.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\r\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-e060b1d6","subject":"Enquiry 260214 5794105","name":"0000-00-00_enquiry-260214-5794105_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_enquiry-260214-5794105_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"enquiry-260214-5794105","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_enquiry-260214-5794105_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-c850bdb2","subjec