spondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_fwd-setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hwyl Bronwen,\r\n\r\nI speak fluent Welsh but will keep this in English as I'm a military cyber\r\nand electronic warfare professional and use A.I which is learning from this\r\ncase for a possible class action lawsuit scaling.\r\n\r\nI'm writing to raise a long-standing family grievance concerning the events\r\nsurrounding BP v Buckler (1987), and what I believe to be the dispossession\r\nand marginalisation of my indigenous Welsh family from our ancestral\r\nbirthland and heritage. Our title appears to have been stolen after Marconi\r\nstayed with us while inventing radio, then for the last century we appear\r\nto have suffered decades of supressed info, court \"mistakes\" , proceedural\r\nunfairness, conveniently timed deaths, gaps in records, abuse of power,\r\nhuman rights violations and what I now see to be fraud. Fraud unravels all.\r\nAnd limitation applies from discovery not occurance of the fraud.\r\n\r\nMy family history concerns Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough, and the\r\nBuckler / Williams lineage connected to the property and surrounding lands.\r\nFrom family records, historical material, local reporting, and documents\r\nreferenced through my research, I believe there are unresolved questions\r\nregarding title history, possession, treatment of the family, and the\r\nhandling of allegations and complaints raised over the years.\r\n\r\nMy concern is not only the legal events themselves, but the broader\r\nhistorical context. The period during and following the Thatcher era saw\r\nmajor industrial, land, and economic changes in Wales. From my perspective,\r\nthese changes disproportionately affected Welsh communities and families\r\nwith long-standing local roots and historical connections to land.\r\n\r\nI believe BP v Buckler (1987) should be revisited as part of a wider\r\nhistorical review of:\r\n\r\n• Chain of custody and title history relating to the property and lands\r\n• Historical ownership claims and succession issues\r\n• Any council records, correspondence, reports, or discussions concerning\r\nthe matter\r\n• Allegations reportedly raised but not fully investigated\r\n• The treatment and displacement of local Welsh families connected to the\r\nland\r\n\r\nI respectfully request access to all available records, archives, minutes,\r\ncorrespondence, title documents, and related materials concerning the\r\nproperty and associated disputes. I am being ignored by the MP and\r\nCouncillor and Land Registry converted my query to a complaint only to mark\r\nit as solved and squash it. Ministry of Justice took 6 months to reply only\r\nto dismiss me. ITV ignore me but quietly declassified supressed footage\r\nrecently:\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nI am working on a website to put together the full timeline and full\r\nevidence for a Netflix documentry. Or a Welsh studio and producer if\r\npossible. My family want narrative and legal justice. They are terrified\r\ninto silence. I am 7000 miles away in Patagonia just to bring this matter\r\nup, since the British State has already tried Force, Stealth/ Secrecy and\r\nfraudulent License and other clandestine strikes from the shadows, instead\r\nof addressing this out in the open. I also require of the Senedd a public\r\nenquiry. Our Nation and Herritage was defrauded, not just my family.\r\n\r\nMy intention is historical clarification, transparency, and preservation of\r\nWelsh heritage and family history.\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\n\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-ccc04355","subject":"Fwd Tŷ Mawr casa grande Llandough gales","name":"0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"fwd-t-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Fwd: Tŷ Mawr (Casa Grande), Llandough, Gales\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 02 Jun 2026 05:10 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nDate: Tue, 2 Jun 2026, 02:08\nSubject: Tŷ Mawr (Casa Grande), Llandough, Gales\nTo: <[email redacted]>\nCc: <[email redacted]>\n\n\nA la atención del Ministerio del Interior de la Nación:\nMe dirijo a usted con el propósito de solicitar formalmente mi radicación\nen la región de la Patagonia y presentar una petición para la concesión de\ntierras destinadas a un proyecto de preservación histórica y cultural.\nActualmente me encuentro en territorio argentino tras haber sido desposeído\ny exiliado de mi hogar solariego de 800 años de antigüedad ubicado en\nLlandough, Gales. Si bien la propiedad de la tierra sigue bajo disputa\nlegal debido a alegaciones de fraude, el Estado británico tomó posesión de\nlos terrenos y demolió la residencia señorial de 10 habitaciones antes de\nque se pudieran aplicar las debidas protecciones patrimoniales. Denuncio\npúblicamente que el Estado británico continúa suprimiendo nuestra herencia\ny ocupando tierras robadas.\nMi intención es establecerme definitivamente en la Patagonia y reconstruir\nuna réplica exacta de dicha residencia de 10 habitaciones. Este espacio\nfuncionará como un museo abierto al público para celebrar la cultura galesa\ny conmemorar un hito histórico de gran relevancia: la estancia de Guglielmo\nMarconi en nuestra propiedad original mientras realizaba los experimentos\nque llevaron a la invención de la radio.\nPor lo tanto, solicito formalmente que se me otorguen tierras de una\nextensión equivalente a la propiedad original en Llandough, con la\nautorización legal para bautizar este nuevo asentamiento con el nombre de\nLlandough.\nQuedo a su entera disposición para presentar la documentación\ncorrespondiente.\nAtentamente,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿\nEr sylw Gweinidogaeth y Materion Mewnol:\nYsgrifennaf atoch er mwyn gwneud cais ffurfiol i ymsefydlu yn rhanbarth\nPatagonia ac i gyflwyno cais am ddarn o dir ar gyfer prosiect i warchod\nhanes a threftadaeth.\nRwyf ar hyn o bryd yn yr Ariannin ar ôl cael fy niarddel a mynd i alltud\no'm cartref maenoraidd 800 oed yn Llandochau (Llandough), Cymru. Er bod\nperchnogaeth y tir yn dal i gael ei herio'n gyfreithiol oherwydd honiadau o\ndwyll, cymerodd y wladwriaeth Brydeinig feddiant o'r safle a dymchwel y tŷ\nmaenor 10 ystafell wely cyn y gellid gweithredu amddiffyniadau treftadaeth\npriodol. Rwyf yn honni bod y wladwriaeth Brydeinig yn parhau i sipresio ein\ntreftadaeth tra eu bod yn meddiannu ein tir a ddygwyd oddi arnom.\nFy mwriad yw setlo'n barhaol ym Mhatagonia ac adeiladu replica union o'r tŷ\nmaenor 10 ystafell wely hwnnw. Bydd y lle hwn yn gweithredu fel amgueddfa\nagored i'r cyhoedd i ddathlu diwylliant Cymru ac i goffau carreg filltir\nhanesyddol o bwys mawr: cyfnod Guglielmo Marconi yn aros gyda ni yn ein\ncartref gwreiddiol tra ei fod yn dyfeisio'r radio.\nFelly, rwyf yn gofyn yn ffurfiol i chi roi tir i mi sydd yr un maint â'r\nsafle gwreiddiol yn Llandochau, ac i gael yr awdurdod cyfreithiol i enwi'r\nsafle hwn yn Llandochau.\nRwyf yn parhau i fod ar gael i gyflwyno'r dogfennau perthnasol.\nYn gywir,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿\nFor the attention of the Ministry of the Interior:\nI am writing to you to formally request residency in the Patagonia region\nand to submit a petition for a land concession dedicated to a historical\nand cultural preservation project.\nI am currently located within Argentine territory after being dispossessed\nand exiled from my 800-year-old manorial home in Llandough, Wales. While\nthe ownership of the land remains under legal dispute due to my allegations\nof fraud and abuse of power, the British state took possession of the\nproperty and demolished the 10-bedroom manor house before proper heritage\nprotections could be applied. I publicly allege that the British state\ncontinues to suppress our heritage while they occupy our stolen land.\nMy intention is to settle permanently in Patagonia and rebuild an exact\nreplica of that 10-bedroom manorial residence. This space will operate as a\nmuseum open to the public to celebrate Welsh culture and commemorate a\nhistorical milestone of great relevance: the period when Guglielmo Marconi\nstayed with us at our original property while conducting the experiments\nthat led to the invention of the radio.\nTherefore, I formally request that I be granted land of an equivalent size\nto the original property in Llandough, along with the legal authority to\nname this new settlement Llandough.\nI remain entirely at your disposal to submit all corresponding\ndocumentation.\nSincerely,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n"},{"id":"wb-5ebeba97","subject":"Fwd Tŷ Mawr casa grande Llandough gales","name":"0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"fwd-t-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_fwd-ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubjec