on from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-de8e9ae8","subject":"Great house farm williams buckler","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-williams-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am researching land ownership history relating to Llandough (Great House\r\nFarm / Ty Mawr area) and surrounding parcels.\r\nI am specifically seeking:\r\n\r\nBute Estate records for Llandough / Penarth / Cardiff outskirts\r\n\r\nAny conveyances, land exchanges, or “swap” agreements involving the Bute\r\nestate and a Daniel Thomas (late 1800s–early 1900s)\r\n\r\nAny quarrying agreements or mineral extraction leases connected to the\r\nproperty (including conditions of land reversion after quarrying)\r\n\r\nAny records of Western Ground Rents taking over Bute estate interests circa\r\nearly 1900s\r\n\r\nPlease advise:\r\n\r\nWhether such records exist in your catalogue\r\n\r\nWhich reference numbers or collections I should request\r\n\r\nWhether any material is restricted or off-site\r\nI am particularly interested in estate papers, deeds, correspondence, and\r\nmaps relating to land transfers or long leases.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\n"},{"id":"wb-aa1544b5","subject":"Great house farm reparations","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-reparations_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-reparations_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-reparations","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-reparations_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-e0300e85","subject":"Great house farm Tŷ Mawr Llandough further evidence of 1988","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-further-evidence-of-1988_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-further-evidence-of-1988_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-further-evidence-of-1988","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-further-evidence-of-1988_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough – Further Evidence of 1988 Involvement & Request for Comprehensive Records (Ref: Previous Enquiries incl. 21 May 2026)\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sun, 07 Jun 2026 07:11 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Cadw Team / Mr Michael Weatherhead / Listed Buildings Team,\n\nThank you for your assistance to date with my enquiries regarding Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including the heritage assessment\nmaterials provided on 21 May 2026.\n\nThis is a matter of profound personal and historic importance to the\nWilliams/Buckler family descendants. Mary Williams maintained until her\ndeath in 1983 that the family held ownership of the house following\narrangements with Daniel Thomas involving the quarry on the land, with the\nsurrounding farmland subject to a lease that defaulted. The family had\noccupied the property for centuries, with strong local and press\nrecognition of their longstanding connection.\n\nI attach a copy of a contemporary newspaper article from the *South Wales\nEcho* dated 3 December 1988 (\"History fight to save farm\" by Peter Bibby).\nIt reports that officials from Cadw were actively considering an appeal to\nthe Secretary of State for Wales to protect the farmhouse as a listed\nbuilding. A Cadw spokeswoman is quoted on evaluating spot-listing and\nemergency procedures due to its historic significance (parts potentially\ndating to the 12th-13th century), with plans for an inspector's site visit\nand discussion with the Royal Commission on Ancient and Historical\nMonuments. This occurred amid the family's legal battle and imminent\ndemolition.\n\nIn light of this clear evidence of Cadw's involvement at the critical time,\nI would be most grateful for a thorough review and full disclosure of *all*\nheld records, correspondence, assessments, site notes, photographs,\ninternal memos, or communications relating to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr\nfrom the 1970s to 1990s. This includes any listing considerations, heritage\nevaluations, interactions with the Vale of Glamorgan Council, BP\nProperties, or the family, and details of any records transferred to other\narchives (such as RCAHMW or Glamorgan Archives).\n\nI appreciate Cadw’s focused remit on the historic environment and kindly\nrequest that searches extend across all relevant teams and archives to\nensure nothing is overlooked. This would greatly assist our efforts to\ndocument and substantiate the family’s historic position in this sensitive\nmatter.\n\nThank you once again for your understanding and support. I look forward to\nyour substantive response at the earliest opportunity, and remain available\nfor any clarification that may assist.\n\nKind regards,\n\n*Requester* bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz [address redacted] [postcode redacted] (On\nbehalf of the Williams / Buckler family descendants)\n"},{"id":"wb-db38646e","subject":"Great house farm Llandough williams buckler family","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-family","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-family_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-8a0ffd21","subject":"Great house farm Llandough nr penarth vale of glamorgan","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am, Please cite the link displaying the record of petition of\r\ndemolition of great house farm in Llandough near Penarth. I have a\r\nnewspaper article from 1978 citing the petition. It says 1,000 signatures,\r\nin other references it says 1700. Regards, Requester\r\n"},{"id":"wb-1b9467b6","subject":"Great house farm Llandough wales","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-wales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-wales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough-wales","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough-wales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'ams,\r\n\r\nI am Requester, grandson of Mary Doreen Williams (née Williams), who \r\nlived at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales \r\nuntil her death in 1983. My family has maintained continuous occupation of \r\nthe site since at least 1667 until 1988, with a key equitable arrangement \r\nvia the Daniel Thomas quarry deal (c.1876 and/or 1895–1915) that we believe \r\nsecured ownership of the house and garden separate from the surrounding \r\nleased farmland.\r\n\r\nDespite this, the property was subject to possession actions by BP \r\nentities, culminating in demolition in 1988. The full title and ownership \r\nhave never received a definitive court ruling on the equitable claim. But \r\nmy grandmother maintained absolute title and that was undefeated all of her \r\nlife. Until her conveniently timed death the fortnight BP registered her \r\nland into their names with the Land Registry in 1983. Regardless of the \r\nmatter never being adjudicated. Ultimately Nan’s title got stolen; they \r\npurchased it. Which didn't change anything due to our firmly established \r\nstanding and position in our town.\r\n\r\nI am compiling a detailed chronological timeline with evidence on my \r\nwebsite to support upcoming formal legal adjudication on who truly owns the \r\nsite — including Roman villa and monastic remains beneath, which has never \r\noccurred. BP and the British State (synonymous in 1987) merely awarded \r\nthemselves possession against a petition, after withholding and suppressing \r\nand destroying evidence, fraud, court \"mistakes\", procedural unfairness and \r\nabuse of power and what appears to be murder, against a disabled widow \r\npensioner, last in her matriarchy. And her son, my terminally ill father. \r\nWho they tore from his hospital bed, detained without charge, restrained \r\nfrom returning home, while they demolished it with my pregnant mum and us \r\nchildren inside.\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nPlease forgive me in advance for my furious writing as I research what my \r\nfamily were subjected to, beyond what we even knew at the time.\r\n\r\nYour expertise in Welsh history, quarrying, manorial estates, archaeology, \r\nor heritage would be invaluable. Any guidance, archive leads, or historical \r\ncontext you can provide would greatly assist in my research. I require \r\nsupport in this endeavour.\r\nSupport can also include a donation to the website \r\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz, which helps co-fund this work and bring the \r\nfull story to light. It's also a branch on GitHub called bpvsbuckler on \r\nmonorepo unclehowell/datro where developers can submit pull requests to \r\npropose changes.\r\nThis is my personal story — I was a child on the site during these events — \r\nand my family has been deeply affected, with my father and grandmother's \r\ndeaths occurring at critical times while challenging the process. We \r\nbelieve the true historical and archaeological importance of the manor \r\nhouse site was downplayed and is concealed to this day, and we want the \r\ncomplete narrative told.\r\n\r\nWe were there since 1667 and owned it. Yet we got labelled squatters and \r\n\"evicted\" as \"tenants\" in 1988. ITV explicitly excluded that my mum was \r\npregnant with us 3 toddlers. More so the presenter was like my second mum \r\ngrowing up: Nichola Hayward Thomas. Her son was my best friend. And she \r\nnever mentioned to me she covered this story of us. And that footage was \r\nburied and only recently stealthily released on YouTube ITV archives after \r\ndecades of suppression.\r\n\r\nMy Nan’s appeal in the news in 1974 was also excluded from the 1987 \r\nhearing, where the judge ruled in favour of BP citing my Nan \"conceived the \r\nnotion\" we owned our home. And that she accepted BP licence letters despite \r\nrejecting them in the suppressed 1974 press article. And in the 1975 \r\nconveyance. I spoke to the Land Registry who have no clear answer how they \r\ndid not see the land BP registered was being challenged by the \r\nowner/occupier. Who conveniently died the month, even the fortnight, BP did \r\nthe conveyance to merge our home and garden land (since 1667) into their \r\ntitle of the surrounding farmland we leased for 3 centuries.\r\n\r\nMy family have never recovered and the last 38 years have brought us no \r\njustice or peace or remedy. I have enquired about a public enquiry from the \r\nSenedd. My family are still too terrified to speak up or out because of the \r\nconveniently timed deaths. My little sister, now 40, had nightmares after I \r\ncalled her to ask her about this. They're all like hostages under the \r\noccupation of terrorists after a literal act of terrorism, in that SAS \r\n(military), undercover as BP bailiffs, appear to have been used to \r\ndispossess us by UK State and BP (synonymous at the time) as part of their \r\n£7Billion deal.\r\n\r\nI even suspect our case is not isolated and this could be a nationwide \r\nclass action. Which resulted in many many indigenous, even manorial \r\noutright property and land owners like ourselves, being dispossessed by \r\ntheft and abuse of power of Government and corporate greed individuals, to \r\nenrich themselves and their families' private estates. Leaving ours in \r\nruins and faithless and in decades of living hell and generational trauma.\r\n\r\nI left my military career with honours and finished my 22 years in Oath \r\nrecently under the local council/Welsh Government. I'm now in Patagonia in \r\na cabin to research all of this and reconnect with my Welsh language and \r\nculture where it's becoming increasingly prohibited under the British.\r\nBefore I flew here people in Wales were being arrested for preaching from \r\nthe bible, flying the Welsh flag, commenting online about being replaced \r\netc. 99% of British MP's refuse to even sign an EDM to condemn decapitating \r\nChristians. There's a Rosary Shrine with my family crest in a church in \r\nEngland. Where people can go and pray for the good estate of the Bucklers. \r\nOur coat of arms is in stained glass and our family Shield is on the tomb \r\nthere. It's as if a demonic realm has plagued our lands and just keeps \r\nspreading and spreading. I've already now spent more of my adult life \r\noverseas than in Britain which is why I'm maybe still free, alive, bona \r\nfide and in full honours, despite being a practical counter officer in a \r\ncivil war being waged on us.\r\n\r\nI would welcome any advice or assistance in pursuing justice for this \r\nlongstanding Welsh family, history and heritage claim.\r\nI am also on my 13th year in exile. I only worked under the Welsh \r\nGovernment 2022/2024 while caring for my nan who died after taking the \r\nvaccine, notwithstanding 2 years of suffering what I believe was \r\nGuillain-Barré syndrome. I flew from New York back to Wales to care for her \r\n(after 8 years in exile before that), then flew back out after she died. \r\nTaking my dog abroad too after one of the 97 Afghans secretly housed \r\noutside of our 11 home village in Monknash, was in my garden trying to \r\nsteal him. I was also expected to sleep in a tent by the Council when I \r\nflew back, despite the 97 Afghans being housed and given multiple times the \r\namount of tax I paid those years. I was horrified I even had to care for my \r\nnan, but Monknash is so far from Barry where the healthcare workers all \r\nare, they couldn't reach her to care for her.\r\nThe danger is real there, especially challenging the state narrative and \r\nreporting even half of what is going on. There's not even a plaque to \r\ncommemorate Marconi staying with us while inventing radio. Not even on the \r\npark bench there. They removed the tree we planted on our land to \r\ncommemorate our ownership, despite us still being owners. Nor is there a \r\ntourist board for the Roman Villa and Monastery under the 20 houses. The \r\ncouncillor for the town won't even reply to me or address any of this. \r\nActing as any hostile illegal occupier would. MoD and MoJ all haven't \r\nreplied. MP's play silly games. CADW claimed to have nothing to do with it, \r\nnot realising I'd been collecting evidence for the last 20 years.\r\n\r\nIn Cardiff Bay the council have the statue of a radio with no naming of the \r\ninventor as he was right wing politically. According to Cardiff council \r\nthemselves that is. The whole thing is an outrage. It's also Wales' largest \r\nand most significant burial site. The injustice here is not just upon my \r\nbrutally displaced family, but generations to come and our Welsh history \r\nand heritage. There's gaps in records, court \"mistakes\", procedural \r\nunfairness. Suppression. Fraud. It's decades and decades of lawfare. What \r\nand why are they so desperate to hide?\r\nMarconi’s apprentice journalled that the success of their experiment was \r\ndue to the zinc poles and copper and dragging it through lots of mud more \r\nso than the radio itself. Experiments were already underway before Marconi \r\narrived to stay with our family in our house. My great grandad Mr Williams, \r\ntook Marconi and equipment to Lavernock point by horse and cart. And a Mr \r\nWilliams was documented in newspapers at the time as having been erecting \r\nthe mast on the day of the experiment. Quartz and copper was discovered in \r\nthe excavation under our farm. All this is documented and public record. \r\nLike the Roman soldier we discovered changing our floor from stone to \r\ntimber in 1870/80.\r\n\r\nThis and the Roman Villa there and the effort for decades to bury us and \r\nthe archaeological and historic significance all leads to another theory, \r\nwhich I won't go into on this email. But to get planning permission to \r\nbuild houses, I don't think so. There is a very important story to be told \r\nabout Great House Farm, Llandough in the Vale of Glamorgan. And I would \r\nencourage anyone with a vested interest in the topics I've discussed to \r\nlook into that location. And help me produce a chronological timeline of \r\nevents for public record.\r\n\r\nMy source code for my repo is on 1,000 year film buried in a Scandinavian \r\nold mine. As part of the GitHub Arctic project. And these backups will \r\noccur again they say. It would be nice to get this all organised and into \r\ntheir next time capsule deposit.\r\nThank you for your time and expertise.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n02032377118\r\n"},{"id":"wb-217c73e1","subject":"Great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\r\n\r\nI am seeking representation and initial advice regarding the 1987 case BP\r\nProperties Ltd v Buckler, which concerned Great House Farm, Llandough —\r\nproperty long occupied by my family. I believe, among a myriad of\r\narguments, that the judgment was reached through a procedural inconsistency\r\namounting to bias or error in law, which may justify reopening under CPR\r\n52.30 and Limitations Act Section 32.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSummary of the issue\r\n\r\nIn the 1987 case, the court ruled against my grandmother on the basis that\r\nshe did not formally reject an offer made by BP Properties Ltd, and treated\r\nthat as tacit acceptance. However, she had already explicitly rejected\r\nprior licence attempts by BP Pension Trust Ltd, a related BP entity, before\r\nBP Properties Ltd appeared as claimant.\r\n\r\nThe judge ruled that BP Properties Ltd was a distinct legal entity, and\r\ntherefore her prior rejection of BP Pension Trust Ltd’s offer was legally\r\nirrelevant.\r\n\r\nLater, in my father’s appeal, he argued that the wrong BP company had been\r\nthe claimant — that BP Pension Trust Ltd, not BP Properties Ltd, held the\r\nrelevant interest.\r\nThe appellate court dismissed his appeal, ruling that “BP companies are all\r\neffectively one and the same” for the purposes of upholding the judgment.\r\n\r\nThis is a clear double standard:\r\n\r\nWhen it benefited BP, the court treated the companies as separate.\r\n\r\nWhen it benefited our family, they were treated as the same entity.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis contradictory reasoning — “heads BP wins, tails the Bucklers lose” —\r\nrepresents either judicial bias, procedural irregularity, or corruption by\r\nomission, and undermines the fairness of the original proceedings.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGrounds for reopening\r\n\r\nUnder CPR 52.30, a final judgment can be reopened if necessary to avoid\r\nreal injustice, in exceptional circumstances, where no alternative remedy\r\nexists.\r\nMy argument is that:\r\n\r\nThe 1987 decision and subsequent appeal were tainted by inconsistent\r\napplication of corporate identity principles, creating real injustice.\r\n\r\nThe appeal court’s own language evidences bias and unequal treatment\r\nbetween parties.\r\n\r\nThis meets the “exceptional circumstances” threshold.\r\n\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the Supreme Court ruling in Takhar v Gracefield Developments\r\nLtd [2019] UKSC 13 confirms that a judgment obtained through fraud or\r\nconcealment can be set aside even decades later — “fraud unravels all.”\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLimitation Act 1980 – Section 32\r\n\r\nPursuant to s.32(1)(b):\r\n\r\n> “Where any fact relevant to the plaintiff’s right of action has been\r\ndeliberately concealed by the defendant, the period of limitation shall not\r\nbegin to run until the plaintiff has discovered the concealment or could\r\nwith reasonable diligence have discovered it.”\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI have only recently obtained and cross-referenced records revealing these\r\ncontradictions in corporate treatment and procedural handling — thus,\r\nlimitation does not bar action.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRequested scope of representation\r\n\r\nAssess the viability of a CPR 52.30 petition to reopen or set aside BP v\r\nBuckler (1987).\r\n\r\nReview the documentary record (Land Registry files, local authority\r\narchives, excavation permissions, HTV Wales coverage, etc.).\r\n\r\nIf viable, initiate a claim for rectification of title and potential\r\ncultural property recovery of artefacts excavated during BP’s occupation of\r\nthe disputed land.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAttachments available upon request\r\n\r\nLand Registry and microfiche title extracts (pre- and post-1987)\r\n\r\nLocal authority and archaeological licensing records (1985–1988)\r\n\r\nMedia and correspondence evidence of procedural bias and conflict\r\n\r\nChronology of BP company interactions with the Buckler family\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nPlease confirm conflicts and whether one of your dispute resolution\r\npartners can offer an initial consultation. I am prepared to provide a full\r\nevidentiary bundle immediately upon engagement.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and consideration.\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-a237df7b","subject":"Great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:57 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nGood Sirs,\n\nI'm writing to you both as elected representatives because, frankly, the\ninstitutional dysfunction I am uncovering is becoming quite extraordinary.\n\nMy family — including the last remaining members of my dispossessed Welsh\nfamily in South Wales — have spent 38 years living with the consequences of\nwhat happened to our home and land. They have been frightened into silence,\nwhile the institutions responsible for safeguarding justice, heritage and\npublic accountability appear, time and again, to have preferred discretion,\nobfuscation and exquisitely worded emails to the rather unfashionable\nconcept of actually answering the questions.\n\nI have now spent considerable time reconstructing what happened. The deeper\nI dig, the more the story appears to unravel.\n\nWe were not merely separated from a house. We were separated from ancestral\nland, family history and heritage. And now the woodland on that land is\nbeing cleared for a development of 133 homes.\n\nOne might reasonably ask: *whose history is being developed over, and whose\nhistory is being erased?*\n\nWhatever one's political position, the fact remains that possession being\nawarded through historical court proceedings does not magically make every\nunderlying question of title, evidence, procedure or institutional conduct\ndisappear. A court order is not an archaeological dig, a title\ninvestigation, or a certificate of immaculate institutional behaviour.\n\nI attach a summary of my grievances concerning CADW, particularly its\nhistoric involvement in this matter. I also attach a mock court application\nwhich I have been developing alongside AI-assisted legal research, not as a\nsubstitute for legal advice, but as a means of stress-testing the evidence\nand identifying the questions that require proper legal determination.\n\nI hope you will read them carefully.\nThis is considerably larger than one parcel of land\n\nThe parcel my family occupied — Church View Close — may ultimately prove to\nbe only one piece of a much larger story.\n\nThe same apparent pattern of irregularity that I am investigating in\nrelation to our parcel appears potentially relevant to:\n\n   - the parcel we leased immediately to the east, now proposed for the\n   133-home development;\n   - the playing fields subsequently acquired by the council;\n   - the 33 acres associated with the limeworks; and\n   - potentially the underlying question of whether the Marquess of Bute\n   possessed the freehold interest that has subsequently been assumed.\n\nThat last question is obviously not something I intend to settle by\nrhetorical flourish. It is precisely the sort of question that should be\nsettled by *documents, title records and evidence*.\n\nOne relevant public-record reference is here:\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/2020_01590_hyb\n<https://reference-url-citation.invalid/0>\n\nThat is the point of my investigation.\n\nI am not asking anybody to accept my conclusions simply because I have\nreached them.\n\n*I am asking institutions to produce the evidence.*\nWhat happened to my family cannot simply be filed away\n\nWhat happened to my family and our home in the 1980s was, in its human\nconsequences, devastating. From my perspective, it amounted to an assault\non our family itself. And decades of it. At least mid 40's by Western\nGround Rents and onwards.\n\nFor decades there has been no meaningful after-support, no meaningful\nattempt at reconciliation, no reparative process and, above all, no\nsatisfactory account of what actually happened.\n\nInstead, the historical record appears fragmented, inaccessible and in\nplaces remarkably difficult to obtain.\n\nCADW is only one of numerous agencies about which my representatives are\nnow compiling material.\n\nThe emerging picture includes questions concerning procedural fairness,\ncourt proceedings, evidential failures, institutional decision-making,\nheritage protection and the apparent absence of effective oversight.\n\nThe more documents I obtain, the more questions arise.\n\nAnd I am increasingly uncomfortable with the proposition that *the\ndescendants of the people affected should have to conduct the investigation\nthemselves simply to discover what the institutions already ought to know.*\n\nIt is particularly distressing that I am having to investigate matters\nsurrounding my own father's and grandmother's lives and deaths in this way.\nI am asking for accountability, not theatre\n\nI appreciate that public bodies have procedures.\n\nI appreciate that officials have workloads.\n\nI appreciate that nobody likes receiving an inconvenient historical file\nwith several decades' worth of questions attached to it.\n\nBut carefully crafted sentences, selective disclosure, unexplained\nomissions and silence are not substitutes for accountability.\n\nI have repeatedly encountered what appears to be a culture of concealment,\nstealth and institutional defensiveness. Sometimes I receive an answer.\nSometimes I receive an answer to a question I did not ask. Sometimes I\nreceive an exquisitely polished paragraph which manages, with almost\nbreathtaking elegance, to avoid answering the actual question.\n\nIt is rather like asking for the keys to the filing cabinet and being\nhanded a brochure about the importance of filing cabinets.\n\nThat may be administratively impressive.\n\nIt is not an answer.\nI am asking you to intervene\n\nI do not expect either of you to determine the merits of my family's\nhistorical or legal claims yourselves.\n\nI am asking you to ensure that the matter receives *proper independent\nscrutiny*.\n\nSpecifically, I am asking you to assist in ensuring that:\n\n   1. relevant surviving records are identified and preserved;\n   2. agencies holding potentially material records provide substantive\n   answers rather than procedural evasions;\n   3. the historical involvement of CADW and other public bodies is\n   properly examined;\n   4. the underlying title, conveyancing and land-history evidence is\n   obtained wherever it survives;\n   5. any allegations of procedural unfairness or institutional failure are\n   referred to the appropriate independent bodies where necessary; and\n   6. my family is finally given a meaningful opportunity to establish,\n   through evidence, what actually happened.\n\nI have no interest in mythology.\n\nI want the documents.\n\nI want the chronology.\n\nI want the title deeds.\n\nI want the correspondence.\n\nI want the decisions.\n\nI want to know who knew what, when they knew it, what they did with that\ninformation, and why.\n\nIf the evidence ultimately disproves some of my suspicions, so be it.\n\n*But the evidence must first be allowed to speak.*\nAnd yes, I am angry\n\nI make no apology for that.\n\nI served this country. I spent years working in public service. I have\nworked for the Vale Council. I have served in the military and operated in\ncircumstances considerably more dangerous than sending an email to a public\nauthority.\n\nI am therefore perfectly capable of distinguishing between legitimate\nadministration and institutional stonewalling.\n\nI am no longer asking to be placated.\n\nI am asking for cooperation in recovering whatever evidence remains and\nallowing it to be examined properly.\n\nThe local community members who have contacted me have long memories. Many\nremain convinced that something about this episode was profoundly wrong. I\nintend to establish exactly what happened — not through rumour, grievance\nor inherited mythology, but through the surviving documentary record.\n\nAnd if the record contradicts me, I will accept that.\n\nBut if the record supports my family, then somebody is eventually going to\nhave to explain why it took a descendant *38 years, hundreds of enquiries\nand an obscene amount of archival digging* to uncover it.\n\nThat is not an acceptable model of public accountability.\nSo, gentlemen — enough of the situationship.\n\nWhatever happened to:\n\n*“We don't negotiate with terrorists”?*\n\nIs there peace?\n\n*No.*\n\nIs there peace?\n\n*No.*\n\nIs there peace?\n\n*No.*\n\nThere is, however, apparently an absolutely fabulous quantity of\nbureaucracy.\n\nWhat there has not yet been is accountability.\n\nI therefore ask you, gentlemen, to address this matter with the seriousness\nit deserves and to assist my family in obtaining the answers that have been\ndenied to us for far too long.\n\nI am not asking for special treatment.\n\nI am asking for the truth.\n\nAnd if the institutions involved have nothing to hide, then surely they\nshould have nothing to fear from producing the documents.\n\nRegards,\n\n\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergeant)\n"},{"id":"wb-fbf9b4d2","subject":"Great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:45 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Civic Trust,\n\nI am researching the 1989 planning application for the development of\nChurch View Close, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and in particular the treatment\nof the historic Great House Farm farmhouse.\n\nThe surviving planning officer's report records that representations were\nreceived from the *Civic Trust* and the *Barry Preservation Society*, but\nthe report does not set out the substance of those representations.\n\nI therefore request any records held by the Civic Trust concerning the 1989\nplanning application, including:\n\n   - the letter, objection, representation or submission made by the Civic\n   Trust concerning the application;\n   - any comments specifically concerning the retention, demolition,\n   alteration or preservation of the *Great House Farm farmhouse*;\n   - any photographs, plans, notes, minutes, correspondence or internal\n   records relating to the farmhouse or the application;\n   - correspondence with Vale of Glamorgan/Barry Council, the developer,\n   GGAT, Cadw or any other body concerning the historic or archaeological\n   significance of the farmhouse/site;\n   - the date on which the Trust became aware of the proposal and the date\n   and method by which its representation was submitted; and\n   - any subsequent correspondence concerning the fate or demolition of the\n   farmhouse.\n\nI am particularly interested in establishing *what the Civic Trust said in\n1989 about whether Great House Farm farmhouse should be retained*, and the\nevidence or reasons given for that position.\n\nThe planning application concerned the site at Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nsubsequently developed as Church View Close. The relevant planning records\ndescribe the site as formerly containing Great House Farm.\n\nPlease provide copies of any records you hold, preferably as scanned PDFs\nor images. If the original records are no longer held, please state that\nand, if known, identify where they were transferred or deposited.\n\nThis is a historical research request concerning records from 1989.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-77792011","subject":"Great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:23 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nRoyal Commission,\n\nI am researching the demolition of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr),\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, in December 1988 (HER reference GGAT02038s / ST\n1681 7331).\n\nI am seeking to establish whether the Royal Commission was consulted or\nnotified before the farmhouse was demolished.\n\nContemporary reports from 3 December 1988 state that Cadw was considering\nemergency protection/listing of Great House Farm and that a Cadw inspection\nwas being arranged, including discussion with the Royal Commission for\nAncient and Historical Monuments.\n\nThe farmhouse was then demolished on 6 December 1988.\n\nI understand that the statutory framework at the time included provisions\nconcerning the recording of historic buildings before authorised\ndemolition. I would therefore be grateful if you could check your records\nand confirm:\n\n   1.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission received any notification, consultation,\n   referral or request for advice concerning Great House Farm before its\n   demolition in December 1988.\n   2.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission was asked to inspect, photograph, record or\n   otherwise document the building before demolition.\n   3.\n\n   Whether any correspondence exists between the Royal Commission, Cadw,\n   the local planning authority, BP Properties Ltd, or their representatives\n   concerning the proposed demolition.\n   4.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission was given an opportunity to complete or\n   supplement its earlier recording of the farmhouse before demolition.\n   5.\n\n   Whether your records contain any photographs, measured drawings,\n   reports, field notes or other documentation relating specifically to the\n   farmhouse immediately before its demolition.\n   6.\n\n   If records exist, I would be grateful for the relevant reference numbers\n   and, where possible, copies.\n\nFor context, the Royal Commission had already recorded Great House Farm\narchitecturally in 1974. Contemporary material indicates that the building\nwas subsequently under consideration for emergency listing shortly before\nits destruction.\n\nThere is also an important chronology concerning the occupation and\npossession of the property: my late father William Buckler had lodged\nEuropean Commission of Human Rights application 14464/88 on 3 May 1988; BP\nobtained possession on 29 November 1988; demolition began on 6 December\n1988; and the Strasbourg application was registered on 12 December 1988.\n\nI am not asking the Royal Commission to express an opinion on the ownership\ndispute or the legality of the demolition. I am simply seeking to\nestablish, from your records, whether the Commission was notified or\nconsulted and what opportunity, if any, it was given to record the building\n(our home since 1667) before it was destroyed?\n\nGiven the historical and archaeological significance subsequently\nidentified at the site, I would particularly appreciate confirmation of\nwhether any pre-demolition recording was requested or undertaken.\n\nRegards\n\n\n,\n\n\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergeant)\n\nRoyal Signals Cyber/ Electronic Warfare Professional and Life Member\n"},{"id":"wb-319b7591","subject":"Great house farm williams buckler family Llandough vale of g","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-g_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-g_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-g","scopeTopics":["morgan","family"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["morgan","family"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-g_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir / Madam,\r\n\r\nTo all those whom it concerns, BCC'd into this email.\r\n\r\nI write to request disclosure under the Freedom of Information Act 2000\r\nand, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\r\n\r\nThis request concerns Great House Farm / Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough,\r\nassociated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records.\r\nMy family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House\r\nFarm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our\r\nownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling\r\nof ownership, only possession.\r\n\r\nIt's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And\r\nwhen BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title,\r\nmy nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry\r\nwindow to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and\r\ndocument/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his\r\nappeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR\r\nrequest blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from\r\nstopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed\r\nforce officers and possible SAS.\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\r\n\r\nI understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of\r\nWales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations\r\nand planning files, including references already identified as:\r\n\r\n• Great House Farm HER site entry – GGAT03586s\r\n• Land at Great House Farm HER event entry – GGATE003872\r\n• The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\r\n\r\nPlease provide copies of, or access to:\r\n\r\n   1. All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House\r\n   Estate, Llandough including:\r\n\r\n• surveys\r\n• reports\r\n• site notes\r\n• photographs\r\n• maps\r\n• aerial imagery\r\n• GIS layers\r\n• archive material\r\n• annotations\r\n• title references\r\n• occupancy references\r\n• landscape records\r\n• archaeological observations.\r\n\r\n   2. All internal and external correspondence involving:\r\n\r\n• RCAHMW / NMRW\r\n• Cadw\r\n• GGAT / Heneb\r\n• Vale of Glamorgan Council\r\n• BP Properties Ltd\r\n• developers\r\n• planning authorities\r\n• landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\r\n\r\n   3. Any documents discussing:\r\n\r\n• estate ownership\r\n• occupation history\r\n• family occupation or association\r\n• agricultural use\r\n• commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\r\n• estate boundaries\r\n• title history\r\n• acquisition history\r\n• disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\r\n• estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title\r\nalteration.\r\n\r\n   4.\r\n\r\n   Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872, including\r\n   the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\r\n   5.\r\n\r\n   Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or\r\n   family associations, including references to the Williams family where\r\n   present within archives.\r\n   6.\r\n\r\n   Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance, dates\r\n   and retention schedules.\r\n   7.\r\n\r\n   File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further\r\n   related material not already listed.\r\n\r\nPlease provide information electronically where possible.\r\n\r\nIf any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and\r\nprovide the public interest assessment.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-4a438c71","subject":"Great house farm church view close Llandough nr penarth vale","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Freedom of Information Officer,\r\n\r\nI am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw\r\nconcerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr),\r\nLlandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\r\n\r\nI request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\r\n\r\n   1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\r\n   2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\r\n   reports concerning the building.\r\n   3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\r\n   authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\r\n   concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\r\n   protection of the property.\r\n   4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\r\n   statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\r\n   5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\r\n   archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\r\n   6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation\r\n   notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\r\n   7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\r\n   representations seeking preservation of the building.\r\n   8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw\r\n   or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\r\n\r\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than\r\nan explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\r\n\r\nIf any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I\r\nwould be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the\r\nrecords.\r\n\r\nI would prefer the information in electronic form.\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant). Heir & Successors of Mary Williams,\r\nGreat House Farm, Llandough\r\n"},{"id":"wb-b10d3cab","subject":"Great house farm church view close Llandough nr penarth vale","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 28 May 2026 05:29 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFreedom of Information Officer,\n\nI am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw\nconcerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr),\nLlandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\n\nI request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\n\n   1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n   2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\n   reports concerning the building.\n   3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\n   authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\n   concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\n   protection of the property.\n   4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\n   statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n   5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\n   archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n   6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation\n   notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n   7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\n   representations seeking preservation of the building.\n   8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw\n   or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than\nan explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\n\nIf any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I\nwould be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the\nrecords.\n\nI would prefer the information in electronic form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant). Heir & Successors of Mary Williams,\nGreat House Farm, Llandough\n"},{"id":"wb-0e2356d4","subject":"Great house farm","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"I have a wild story for you.\r\n\r\nI was working in cyber and electronic warfare in the military as an acting\r\nsergeant in 2007. I left to start a security group. I was voted the top\r\nhacker in British Defence in 2005. I got head hunted a lot.\r\n\r\nI'm from Llandough near Cardiff. But I was living in Stockeld Park in Leeds\r\nwith my son and his mum in 2013. I discovered his mum and family were in a\r\ncult. So I tried whisleblowing and the state tried to kidnap and silence\r\nme. This included 3 lots of police, 5 military and a helicopter sent to the\r\nip address they traced me to.\r\n\r\nBut I'm a military warfare professional so I escaped and evaded capture. I\r\neventually ended up on a caribbean island in exile. All the way until 2022\r\nwhen I was exhonourated and returned. It wasn't the state who confirmed\r\nwhat I was saying was true about these Epstein Class types and grooming\r\nscandals in UK, they were the ones working to bury it and cover it up.\r\n\r\nSo I worked back under the welsh Govenrment/ Vale Council 2022 to 2024.\r\nThen moved to the Welsh Settlement here in argentina. So I left my military\r\ncareer with honours and finished my 22 in Oath and I'm bonafide. But my son\r\nis still abducted and missing/ hidden, if he's even still alive. They all\r\njust go silent about that when I query it, having failed to kidnap and\r\nsilence me.\r\n\r\nBut more interestingly is another matter I've been investigating now I have\r\nsuch little trust for the British State and that I'm not alone in Wales\r\nquest to decolonise. The other matter is my families century long battle\r\nwith BP over farm land we had in Llandough since 1667.\r\n\r\nI recently got some ITV surpessed footage declassified. It shows my mum on\r\nTV (and old best friends mum as the news Anchor Nichola Haywood Thomas). It\r\nseems to show and imply SAS were used to dispossess us of our farm. This\r\nfollows a lot of proceedural unfairness, fraud, court \"mistakes\". And so I\r\nhave dug and dug into the backstory of landmark legal case BP vs Buckler\r\n1987.\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nIt transpires my family aquired the virtual freehold (999 year lease) in\r\n1667. And by the mid to late 1800's / early 1900's we had obtained the\r\nmanorial fee simple absolute title from Bute Estate. My nan maintained this\r\nuntil her death in 1982. Despite a 1978 article stating it being supressed.\r\nAnd despite her paper title being stolen and sold to BP. And despite\r\ncountless attempts by courts to block her in 1974 from receiving a ruling\r\nshe owned the land. And so on and so on.\r\n\r\nThey not only spent decades trying to make out we were tenants with our\r\nstolen title. They reported us as squatters, while suppressing the fact we\r\nowned it and had lived there since 1667. So that they could evict us with\r\narmed force. All so BP could build houses. They also supressed the\r\narchelogical and historic significants of the site.\r\n\r\nMarconi stayed with us while inventing radio. This is still surpessed. They\r\nalso suppressed our report of discovering a roman soldier under our floor\r\nin 1870. And CADW didn't list our 800 year old farmhouse as a grade II\r\nbuilding like they should have, resulting in it being demolished.\r\n\r\nSo my family and I are the rightful heirs of this claim to Manor of\r\nLlandough and the British State , even unto this day are still doing\r\neverything to bury their crimes against me and my family. Like my nan\r\nconveniently died in the week window she had to challenge BP registering\r\nour land in their name at the land registry in 1982. My dads appeal of the\r\n87 ruling was dismissed and his ECHR blocked and he died age just 42 in\r\n1991 too. And back when the title was stolen my grandad Fredrick Buckler\r\ndied right before BP purchased our stolen title from Western Ground Rents ,\r\nso was unable to rebuttle the story that he was the one who stole my nan's\r\ntitle and pawned it to Western Ground Rents. Which even if true, doesn't\r\nmake her stolen title their lawful possession. And even if it did, doesn't\r\nmean her ancestral multi centurial occupation doesn't count. So the way\r\nthey got around that was to issue a license for my nan to live there until\r\nshe dies, but falsly named her Mrs Buckler on those licenses. A legal name\r\nthey created which didnt have the family name and claim to the land my nans\r\nactual name (Mrs Williams) had.\r\n\r\nI am putting together a website using A.I to consolidate all the evidence\r\nand timeline narration and storyline now.\r\n\r\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n\r\nI have put most departments in Wales on notice and called for a public\r\nenquiry and investigation. But there is such a push back to dismiss this\r\nand keep it buried and hidden from the public. I am horrified at how this\r\nis being handled. The Llandough Councillor and MP won't even respond. Land\r\nregistry converted my query into a complaint only to close it as resolved\r\nwithout properly addressing it. Its clear Thatcher gave them a pass to\r\nignore proper checks , while my nan was murdered to prevent her challenging\r\nBP's registration of our land in their names. While BP commited purgergy\r\nand withheld info from the Land Registry to get their application in,\r\nunchallenged.\r\n\r\nI am looking for all support I can for this. My family are terrified into\r\nsilence and have been for decades.\r\n\r\nMy brother is the rightful Lord of Manor of Llandough and in exile in\r\nIreland. I was exiled over another matter. I have two sisters too who would\r\nbe the rightful Lady's of Manor of Llandough. My mum and aunties and\r\ncousins are all still alive and gave me testemony. But we're all scattered\r\nto the wind. And our land is illegally occupied by the British State.\r\n\r\nThere's gaps in the Bute records showing their did not hold title when we\r\nclaim to have. We have been erased from record. There is also photo\r\nevidence of a tree planting ceremony when we aquired the absolute title.\r\nAnd the way in which we aquired it, from a deal with Bute quarryman Daniel\r\nThomas, who awarded us the title in exchange for our permission to quarry\r\nour farm, all stands to reason. Not withstanding my nan Mary Williams\r\nmaintained our superior land claim until her death in 1982 age 65.\r\n\r\nThere was hundreds of child graves also moved from the church in Llandough\r\nin 1994. Which was not only not reported on at the time, but the report\r\ntook 10 years to release and still under reports the number of child graves\r\nby hundreds. Llandough not only refuses to celebrate radio was invented\r\nthere by Marconi, but refuses to acknowledge marconi or my families\r\nexistence there. Which is natural of illegal occupiers not wanting\r\nquestions to be asked. But more so the radio statute in Cardiff Bay has had\r\nthe name Marconi removed from it as he was right wing politically. Cardiff\r\ncouncil openly admit this.\r\n\r\nThe roman burials exhivated from under our farm, along with all the\r\nartifacts looted, which are now in museums, was wales biggest discover and\r\ndig in history, but they pretended to not know until after dispossessing us\r\nand getting planning permission to develop houses. But this was theatrics\r\nand untrue. They knew all along they wouldn't get permission to build\r\nhouses if it was known how significant the site was to Welsh History so\r\nthey supresssed the info. More than this BP only ever saught possession of\r\nour farm with our stolen title and never a ruling they owned it, because\r\nthat would have meant discovery which would have unveiled the archelogical\r\nand historic significants and prevented planning. And they lied to the\r\nplanning department saying our 800 year old 10 bedroom former court house\r\nhome was old sheds and delapidated buildings to demolish.\r\n\r\nI really hope to get narrative justice for my family. And public support.\r\nBecause the British State occupying and ruling is not happy I unravelled\r\nthe fraud here and is obstructive. But I also fear they are again, like\r\nwith the case of me exposing the Epstein Class and spending 8 years in\r\nexile already, I fear they are again trying to get to me before I expose\r\nthem. In the 6 months I waited for the Ministry of Justice to reply, only\r\nfor their to dismiss me, I got asked by companies house for ID, but my\r\nvalid passport and driving licence is supposedly no good and I should go to\r\na post office or download their digital ID tracking app. I don't find this\r\nsuspicious. Then they alledged their website got hacked as if to imply it\r\nwas me.\r\n\r\nMy family notably challenged BP and the British State the last century, but\r\nwithout force, stealth/ secrecy or license. Whereas they wage war on us\r\nwith force, strikes from the shadows and fraudulent licence. I just want\r\nthis to all be handled in the public eye so it doesn't get more cloak and\r\ndagger, clandestine and hybrid warfare. The councillor in 1988 already\r\nraised concerned someone would get killed before my dad died. I'm not\r\nfearful for my life as I'm warfare professional and proved myself difficult\r\nfor the Brit'ish State to capture and kill already. But I have them dead to\r\nrights again and unlike the Epstein Class fights, I don't want this battle\r\nto be fought in the shadows.\r\n\r\nEveryone should care because this is likely a class action. This\r\ndispossesion and death by a thousand cuts thereafter to try to cover up\r\ntheir crime, likely has happened to all our families nationwide in the\r\npast. But there's no limitation on the fraud from when it occured. The\r\nclock for the statute of limitation begins from discovery of the fraud and\r\nI've only just discovered all their fraud.\r\n\r\nSo I'm wondering who else nationwide might feel they've been dispossessed\r\nof their land and home through lawfare. I have teams of lawyers and I will\r\ngladly make my case a class action.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\nExecutor of Manor of Llandough,\r\nVale of Glamorgan, Wales\r\n"},{"id":"wb-4d02a102","subject":"Great house farm","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-f06c376b","subject":"Great house farm","name":"0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_great-house-farm_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related fil