ame dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Land Registry\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 29 Dec 2022 22:53 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs,\n\nIn 2006 I took out a 109k GBP mortgage on the property (address 40 Lombard\nStreet, Barry).\nThe mortgage was with Manchester Building Society (MBS).\nIn 2011/12 I had arrears, which I paid. To the tune of 7K GBP.\nBut MBS also wanted 3.5k in fees for the admin/ reminder letters etc.\nI said I would pay 2k GBP, but I felt 3.5k GBP was unreasonable.\n\nInstead of being reasonable, MBS decided to abruptly return my arrears to\nmy bank and took possession of my home.\nThey did not say in their application to the courts that it was a human\nrights issue (to take my home and make me homeless).\nThis I[m told was intentional in order the case get processed by the wrong\ntype of court e.g. a court that was favourable to them and not a court\nwhere my inherent and inalienable rights as a British Subject are a factor\nto be considered.\nFurthermore MBS attempted to place a charge on my grandmothers property\nand/or get her to remortgage with them, in order she pay the shortfall from\nthe auction. Fortunately the ombudsman defended my grandmother and made MBS\npay my grandmother 1k GBP in damaged for the alarm and distress they caused\nher.\n\nIn recent years I did receive a final statement from MBS, which gives some\nindication of the timeline. I also take this opportunity to add that a\ncontributing factor to why I was in arrears in the first place was because\nI was not granted a payment holiday when required, which I'm sure was\nactually a term of the mortgage, which MBS failed to honour.\n\nUpon requesting a land registry record for the property today I discovered\nI'm not even recorded as being on the property at all. Despite owning it\nbetween 2006 and 2012. I also have a detailed credit report, which does not\nshow me having had that property either.\n\nI believe serious fraud has occurred upon my person. And if this was the\ncase, I'm wondering what my options are to clear all this up so that I may\ntake out a  new mortgage and become a homeowner again.\n\nKind Regards,\n\nSion Buckler\n"},{"id":"wb-57be6cc4","subject":"New response to your FOI request 1988 dispossession of great","name":"0000-00-00_new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request '1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family' that you made to Ministry of Defence.\r\n\r\nTo view the response, click on the link below.\r\n\r\nht