on on this service is provided\n> below.\n>\n>\n>\n> Once you have sufficiently clarified the relevant land in which you would\n> like this information for, we will proceed with your request.\n>\n>\n>\n> To assist you in accessing information held by HMLR, please be aware the\n> information you have requested is held within our registers that are open\n> to public inspection and accessible via statutory routes of access. This\n> means that we are unable to provide access to this information via an\n> Environmental Information Regulations (EIR) or a Freedom of Information Act\n> 2000 (FOIA) request and it is likely a refusal notice will be issued for\n> this information.\n>\n>\n>\n> Information about how to apply to inspect or obtain official copies is\n> contained with practice guide 11:\n>\n>\n> www.gov.uk/government/publications/inspection-and-application-for-official-copies/practice-guide-11-inspection-and-application-for-official-copies\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Our Customer Support colleagues are trained to handle queries which relate\n> to information that is held on the register of title\n>\n> If you require any assistance in completing the application form or to\n> determine which documents to order, please contact our Customer Support\n> Team who will be able to assist you with your query.\n>\n>\n>\n> Their contact details are as follows:\n>\n>\n>\n> English language phone [phone redacted]\n>\n> Welsh language phone [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> Telephone lines are open between 08:00 and 17:00 Monday to Friday This\n> does not include Bank Holidays.\n>\n> Website: www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry\n>\n>\n>\n> *What is the Index Map?*\n>\n> HM Land Registry keeps a computerised 'index map' based on the Ordnance\n> Survey map. This computerised map provides an index of the land in every\n> registered title and pending application for first registration.\n>\n>\n>\n> *Applying for an Index Map Search*\n>\n> You apply for an official search of the index map using form SIM\n> <https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/index-map-application-for-an-official-search-sim>\n> .\n>\n> This will need to be printed, completed and sent to our Standard address\n> <https://www.gov.uk/guidance/hm-land-registry-address-for-applications#standard-addresses>\n> .\n>\n> You must attach a plan to show the land that you are interested in, it\n> should:\n>\n>\n>\n>    -      be drawn to scale\n>    -      be based on the current large scale Ordnance Survey map\n>    -      indicate scale and north point\n>    -      show property extent with suitable colouring and position in\n>    relation to nearby roads and other features plans of flats and maisonettes\n>         indicate floor level (if any) of the property.\n>    -\n>\n> You can also search by map on our Search for land and property information\n> <https://www.gov.uk/search-property-information-land-registry> service.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: logo]\n>\n> *Amanda Whittaker *\n> *PC.foi Disclosure Officer*\n>\n> *Information Rights Team*\n>\n> Data Group\n>\n> Data and Register Integrity Group\n>\n> Email: [email redacted] / [email redacted]\n> GOV.UK <https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry> |\n> @HMLandRegistry <https://twitter.com/HMLandRegistry> | LinkedIn\n> <http://www.linkedin.com/company/land-registry> | Facebook\n> <http://www.facebook.com/pages/Land-Registry/343223435769541>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 February 2026 01:03\n> *To:* _FOI email address <[email redacted]>;\n> [email redacted]\n> *Subject:* Subject: Freedom of Information Request - Ty Mawr (Great\n> House), Llandough, near Penarth (1938-1987)\n>\n>\n>\n> Some people who received this message don't often get email from\n> [email redacted]. Learn why this is important\n> <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n>\n>\n> I understand you may already be busy, so please don't feel overwhelmed by\n> this FOI request—I'm conducting my own diligence and happy for you to take\n> the full statutory 20 working days to respond.\n>\n>\n>\n> Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, I request copies of all\n> records, correspondence, memoranda, internal notes, minutes, file notes,\n> land registration applications, objections, or communications held by HM\n> Land Registry from 1 January 1938 to 31 December 1987 relating to:Ty Mawr\n> (Great House), Llandough, near Penarth, South Glamorgan (also known as\n> Great House Farm).\n>\n>\n>\n> Land registration applications, title transfers, or dealings involving\n> Mountjoy Ltd, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Pension Trust Ltd, and/or BP\n> Properties Ltd (including the 1938 auction/reversion conveyance and 1969\n> sale).\n>\n>\n>\n> Interactions, notices, proceedings, tenancy offers, licences (e.g., 1974\n> unilateral lifetime licence letters), or disputes involving Mrs Mary\n> Williams (also referred to as Mrs Buckler), Mr Frederick Buckler, or\n> Williams/Buckler family occupiers—particularly the 1962 Cardiff County\n> Court possession proceedings (Dec 11 order by Judge Temple Morris QC).\n>\n>\n>\n> Any possession proceedings, adverse possession claims, or title objections\n> connected to the property (e.g., 1955 High Court, 1962 Cardiff County\n> Court, 1974 actions).\n>\n>\n>\n> Please include archived, off-site, or scanned records where applicable.If\n> exemptions apply (e.g., Section 40 personal data), specify which and why.\n> If costs exceed the appropriate limit, advise how to refine (e.g.,\n> prioritize 1955-1987 or 1962/1974 events).\n>\n>\n>\n> I look forward to your response within 20 working days.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester Esq. Sgt (Ret'd)\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-c30e06e1","subject":"Re external cais am gyngor cyfreithiol Tŷ Mawr Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-t-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: RE: [EXTERNAL] Cais am Gyngor Cyfreithiol – Ty Mawr, Llandough\nFrom: Emily Wellington\nDate: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 17:04 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nGood afternoon Mr Buckler,\n\nThank you for your enquiry and voicemail.\n\nFor us to provide a fee quotation we will require sight of some further documents. Please send these through and we can assess if we are able to assist further.\n\nWhilst we do not provide legal advice through the medium of Welsh, my colleague Rhys Evans is a fluent Welsh speaker and is happy to discuss matters through the medium of Welsh.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nKind regards,\nEmily\n\n\n​​​​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 13 February 2026 01:33\nTo: UZZI Consulting <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nCc: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Hello <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Cais am Gyngor Cyfreithiol – Ty Mawr, Llandough\n\n\nAnnwyl Syr/Fadam,\n\nYsgrifennaf i ofyn am gyngor cyfreithiol mewn perthynas â mater cymhleth yn ymwneud â Thŷ Mawr (Great House Farm), Llandough.\n\nYn gryno, mae’r mater yn codi’r cwestiynau canlynol:\n\n  *   Diffyg penderfyniad barnwrol ar berchnogaeth cyn achos meddiant yn y 1980au;\n  *   Cofrestru cyntaf yn 1982 a allai gynnwys “camgymeriad” o fewn ystyr Atodlen 4 Deddf Cofrestru Tir 2002;\n  *   Amnewid neu anghysondeb hunaniaeth yn y disgrifiad cyfreithiol;\n  *   Cwestiynau ynghylch ystyriaeth a datgeliad treftadaeth archaeolegol.\n\nRwy’n ceisio:\n\n  1.  Barn gynnar ar hyfywedd unrhyw gais i adolygu neu gywiro’r gofrestr;\n  2.  Asesiad o’r sefyllfa gyfyngu (limitation);\n  3.  Cyngor ar gamau cyn-weithredu priodol.\n\nRwyf wedi atodi crynodeb gweithredol byr er hwylustod.\n\nByddwn yn ddiolchgar am gyfle i drefnu ymgynghoriad cychwynnol. Rwy’n barod i dalu am gyngor cychwynnol ffurfiol.\n\nYn gywir,\n\nSion Buckler\n[address redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[Evolve:cb628be1-368d-44fb-9e69-22ad06858d51]\n"},{"id":"wb-2e4dc46f","subject":"Re external re wcr website enquiry","name":"0000-00-00_re-external-re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-external-re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"external-re-wcr-website-enquiry","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-external-re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon Requester,\r\n\r\nI have forwarded this email and its attachments to my colleague in the Dispute Resolution team. They will review and will confirm whether they will be able to assist in due course.\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\nJess\r\n\r\n\r\nJessica Williams\r\nLegal Assistant\r\nDDI\r\nEmail\r\n01522 515947\r\nJessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk\r\nwilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk\r\nThe Maltings, 11-15 Brayford Wharf East, Lincoln, LN5 7AY\r\nRanked in - Lawyer UK 200 • Top Tier Firm - Legal 500 UK • Leading Firm - Chambers UK\r\n​IMPORTANT PLEASE READ:\r\n​TERMS OF BUSINESS:\r\n​\r\n​Please note that our new Terms of Business released on 1 December 2025 can be found at\r\n​(https://www.wilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk/terms-of-business).  ​These were revised to reflect the change to Financial Services\r\n​Compensation Scheme deposit protection limit which has ​risen to £120.000.​​\r\n​\r\n​CYBER CRIME ALERT:\r\n \r\n​You will be aware from recent press coverage email scams and cybercrime are becoming more prevalent and despite security ​\r\n​measures ​being in place, emails can be hacked and the contents altered. This email has been checked for potential computer ​viruses \r\n​using Mimecast technology. You should carry out your own virus check before opening any attachment. We accept no ​liability for any \r\n​loss or damage, which may be caused by software viruses or interception or interruption of this email. \r\n \r\n​For payments to us:\r\n​Before transferring any money to us electronically, please call the individual who has conduct of the matter on the telephone number \r\n​you regularly use, to verify that you have the correct bank account details. We will never notify you of a change to our bank details by \r\n​email. If you receive an email of this nature, do not make any payment to the account stated and please immediately contact our \r\n​Accounts Department on 01472 262626. We will not be liable if you transfer money to an incorrect bank account. \r\n \r\n​For payments to you:\r\n​If you wish to notify us of a change to your bank details to those originally provided, please note we will not accept this information by \r\n​email without speaking to you to confirm the change and we will also need a bank statement or other evidence to confirm the account \r\n​details. \r\n\r\n​Wilkin Chapman Rollits is a trading name of Wilkin Chapman LLP a limited liability partnership incorporated in England and Wales with \r\n​registered number OC343261 and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority under number 509655. Our ​registered\r\n​office is at Cartergate House, 26 Chantry Lane, Grimsby, DN31 2LJ. A list of members may be inspected at this address. The term \r\n​Partner is used to refer to a member of Wilkin Chapman LLP. Wilkin Chapman LLP does not accept service of documents by e-mail or \r\n​fax, and the use of e-mail does not imply that it is willing to do so, unless otherwise expressly agreed.\r\n\r\n​This e-mail and its contents are confidential, protected by law and legally privileged. Only access by the addressee is authorised. Any \r\n​liability (in negligence, contract or otherwise) arising from any third party taking any action, or refraining from taking any action on the \r\n​basis of any of the information contained in this e-mail is hereby excluded. If you are not the intended addressee, please notify the \r\n​sender immediately by replying to the email and delete the email from your system. Do not discuss, disclose the contents to any person, \r\n​or store or copy the information in any medium or use it for any purpose whatsoever. Copyright in this e-mail (and any attachments \r\n​created by Wilkin Chapman LLP) belongs to Wilkin Chapman LLP which asserts the right to be identified as such and hereby objects to \r\n​any misuse thereof.\r\nFrom: Requester <[redacted]>\r\nSent: 08 December 2025 12:38\r\nTo: Jessica Williams <Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk>\r\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Re: WCR Website Enquiry\r\n\r\nThis Message originated outside your organisation.\r\n________________________________\r\nNo problem about Martin's case, understood, thanks for your prompt reply Jess.\r\n\r\nI don't mean to appear litigious, but the other matter I have is BP vs Buckler 1987. My dad appealed it, it was dismissed. He then sought ECHR, blocked. He then died. The trauma on our family frightened and immobilised everyone from seeking justice. Even unto this day.\r\n\r\nI found a lot of fraud & concealment in this case. There's also a lot of media coverage in archives. I wondered if the clause in the limitations act could allow me to reopen the case on these grounds. The museum confirmed to be last week all the items exhevated from under our farm after it was stolen from us.\r\n\r\nI'll give you one of the 12 arguments I have where it concerns clauses in the limitation act to reopen the case. My nan fought off the alleged possessor, BP Pensions Trust Ltd, for many years - and  maintained equitable title ownership of our 800 year old farm. But the judge ruled that BP Properties Ltd, the claimant in the 1987 case, were ignored. And the BP companies were seperate, so rejecting one doesn't inherently meaning rejecting the other. And so their letter of offer, a license to stay at \"their\" farm until she died, upheld and stopped the clock on adverse possession. Which was the position of our family (since our title deeds had gone missing from our home and copy gone from the public library during all this multi generational lawfare).\r\n\r\nBut in my dads appeal (point 3/3) he argued BP Pensions Trust should have been the claimant, not BP Properties Ltd. To which the judges dismissed the appeal citing - both BP companies are basically the same.\r\n\r\nSo a blatant case of \"Heads they win, tails we lose\". Not to mention the relationship between British Government and BP in those years being a huge bias.\r\n\r\nFurthermore my nan wasn't alive to defend her position in 87. And no evidence was presented of the alleged letter from BP to stop the clock of adverse possession. Yet the case was won on the fact a letter of rejection, from a now dead woman, wasn't able to be presented. It is insane how BP took possession of our family farm of 400 years of occupancy.\r\n\r\nOur farm was prime real estate, overlooking Cardiff bay. This is an Erin Brokovitch scale scandal. It gets more wild. In my research I discovered Marconi stayed with us while inventing Radio. My great grandad took him via horse & cart every day, to Lavenock Point Penarth, to conduct his radio experiments - including the day of the first successful broadcast. There's not even a plaque there today to commemorate that Llandough is the birthplace of radio. I'm also a decorated Royal Signals veteran (honourable discharge). Just 23 houses built over the site now. CADW expressly rejected a petition at the time too, which would afford our 800 year old farm protection from demolishment. Not only was the farm demolished, it was done during the night and early morning after the lawfare in the court which is an evident act of  desperation and relentlessness.\r\n\r\nMy family would like justice. I believe we have a strong case. The councillor of Llandough is very interested. I just need legal representation to take this forward.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your reply on that matter too if you wouldn't mind. I did call and leave a message about it last week as well.\r\n\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\n[cid:image001.jpg@01DC6849.4DC13040]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOn Mon, 8 Dec 2025, 07:07 Jessica Williams, <Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk<mailto:Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk>> wrote:\r\nGood morning Requester,\r\n\r\nI write in response to your website enquiry received by me this morning – apologies for the delay in reverting to you. Unfortunately, this does not appear to be a matter we would be able to assist with as we do not have a Criminal Law department.\r\n\r\nYou may be able to find assistance through Forces Law<https://forceslaw.com/contact/>. They are essentially a switchboard of multiple different firms of solicitors, all with military knowledge. Alternatively, Op NOVA<https://www.forcesemployment.org.uk/programmes/op-nova/contact/> may be able to assist. They are a charity who support veterans in contact with the justice system.\r\n\r\nThank you for your enquiry, and apologies we cannot be of assistance at this time.\r\n\r\nBest wishes,\r\nJess\r\n[cid:image002.png@01DC6849.4DC13040]\r\n\r\n​​​​\r\nJessica Williams\r\nLegal Assistant\r\nDDI\r\nEmail\r\n01522 515947\r\nJessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk<mailto:Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nwilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk<http://wilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk>\r\n\r\nThe Maltings, 11‑15<https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g> Brayford<https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2