ge D (Cllr)\n<[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Hi Requester\n>\n> Thank you for copying me in on this.\n>\n> If you'd like to discuss, please let me know.\n>\n> All the best,\n>\n> George\n> ________________________________\n> From: Requester <[email redacted]>\n> Sent: Friday, November 14, 2025 12:48:36 PM\n> To: [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n> Subject: BP vs Buckler\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important\n>\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987), relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> My family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply affected. Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding corporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage considerations relating to the site.\n>\n> I have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal, historical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n>\n> My interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n>\n> By way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n> Requester\n> [address redacted]\n> [location redacted]\n> [postcode redacted]\n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-605cd651","subject":"Re BP v Buckler","name":"0000-00-00_re-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-bp-vs-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-994633d3","subject":"Re cais am ddeiseb ac ymchwiliad cyhoeddus achos buckler v b","name":"0000-00-00_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-b_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-b_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-b","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-b_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:32 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLara,\n\nDiolch am eich arweiniad.\n\nRwyf wedi mireinio fy mhethos arfaethedig ymhellach er mwyn ehangu ei\ngwmpas. Mae'n cynnwys nawr alwadau am ymchwiliad i achosion hanesyddol\ntebyg lluosog yng Nghymru, gan gynnwys archwilio problemau systemig posibl\nfel twyll, gorthrymu tystiolaeth, neu anwybyddu/gweithio o amgylch\ngwarchodaethau amaethyddol a threftadaeth mewn anghytundebau meddiannu\nanghyfreithlon—gan o bosibl atal y cloc cyfyngu ar feddiannu anghyfreithlon\nyn anghyfreithlon neu yn anghyfansoddiadol—tra'n defnyddio Fferm Great\nHouse (BP v Buckler 1987) fel prif enghraifft.\n\nMae'r ffocws yn parhau i fod yn gadarn ar faterion datganoledig: polisi\namgylchedd hanesyddol Cymru, gwarchodaethau amaethyddol, rôl CADW, a\ndiwygiadau i fynd i'r afael ag unrhyw fylchau a nodir, heb geisio ailymweld\nâ dyfarniadau llys penodol.\n\nRwy'n cadarnhau bod gennyf gyfeiriad yng Nghymru: [address redacted].\nRwy'n etholwr yn Nyffryn Morgannwg ac rwyf wedi ysgrifennu at yr AS\npresennol a'r Cynghorydd Carroll yn Llandochau; maent yn ymwybodol o'r\nmater a chredaf eu bod yn edrych i mewn iddo.\n\nOs caiff ei fframio fel hyn—gan bwysleisio \"dosbarth\" posibl o\nffermydd/teuluoedd Cymreig yr effeithir arnynt a methiannau polisi\nehangach—a ydych chi'n credu y byddai'n bodloni'r safonau'n ddigonol i\nennill sylw'r Pwyllgor a mynd ymlaen i gyflwyno/cyhoeddi?\n\nNid yw twyll byth yn rhy bell yn y gorffennol, gan nad yw'r cyfnod cyfyngu\nyn berthnasol mewn amgylchiadau o'r fath ac fe'i datodolir i gyd yn ôl y\ngyfraith. Mae hefyd yn gyfyngedig o'r dyddiad y cafodd ei ddarganfod—ac\nrwyf newydd ei ddarganfod—ac nid o ddyddiad y twyll honedig.\n\nEr gwaethaf hynny, rydym yn dal yn deulu Cymreig brodorol dadfeddiannol ar\nein tir geni hynafiaid. Rydym yn dal yma.\n\nOs na, pa gamau eraill y byddech chi'n eu hargymell (er enghraifft,\nymgysylltu ag Aelod o'r Senedd, adrannau Llywodraeth Cymru fel CADW, neu\nsianeli eraill ar gyfer codi materion systemig tir/amaethyddol)?\n\nByddai unrhyw gyngor ar gryfhau'r geiriad neu'r dystiolaeth ategol yn cael\nei werthfawrogi'n fawr cyn i mi gyflwyno.\n\nDiolch—mae'r mater hwn o bwysigrwydd sylweddol i gyfanrwydd diwylliannol,\namaethyddol a hanesyddol Cymru.\n\nCofion cynhes,\nSion Buckler\n[address redacted]\n\n...................  [SAESNEG/ ENGLISH] .....................\n\nThanks for your guidance.\n\nI've further refined my proposed petition to broaden its scope,\nincorporating calls for an inquiry into multiple similar historical cases\nin Wales. This includes examining the possibility of systemic issues like\nfraud, suppression of evidence, or ignoring/working around agricultural and\nheritage protections in adverse possession disputes—potentially to\nunlawfully or unconstitutionally stop limitation clock on adverse\npossession—while using the Great House Farm (BP v Buckler 1987) as a key\nexample. The focus remains on devolved matters: Welsh historic environment\npolicy, agricultural safeguards, CADW's role, and reforms to address gaps\nwithout revisiting specific court judgments.\n\nAnd yes I have an address, it's [address redacted]. I am a constituent\nin the Vale of Glamorgan and I have written to the current MP and\ncouncillor Carroll in Llandough, they are aware and I trust they are\nlooking into it.\n\nIf framed this way—emphasizing a possible \"class\" of affected Welsh\nfarms/families and broader policy failures—do you believe it would meet the\nstandards to gain the Committee's attention and proceed to\nsubmission/publication?\n\nFraud is never too far in the past as the statute of limitation doesn't\napply in such circumstances and furthermore it unravels all according to\nlaw. It is also only limited from the date it was discovered and I recently\ndiscovered, not from the date of occurrence of the alleged fraud.\n\nNotwithstanding we are still an dispossessed indigenous Welsh family on our\nancestral birthland. We are still here.\n\nFailing that, what alternative steps do you recommend (e.g., approaching a\nMember of the Senedd, Welsh Government departments like CADW, or other\nchannels for raising systemic land/agricultural issues)?\n\nAny advice on strengthening wording or evidence would be appreciated before\nsubmission.\n\nThank you—this matter holds significant importance for Welsh cultural,\nagricultural, and historical integrity.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler [address redacted]\n\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-c48f00db","subject":"Re cais am gyngor cyfreithiol Tŷ Mawr Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_re-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"cais-am-g