add flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>>\n>> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n>>\n>> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>>\n>> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n"},{"id":"wb-0da64085","subject":"Re tid 7760490 freedom of information request requester buckler","name":"0000-00-00_re-tid-7760490-freedom-of-information-request-requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-tid-7760490-freedom-of-information-request-requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"tid-7760490-freedom-of-information-request-requester-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-tid-7760490-freedom-of-information-request-requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: TID [7760490] - Freedom of Information Request - Requester\nFrom: GoSkippy Insurance\nDate: Thu, 25 Apr 2024 20:10 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThank you for contacting GoSkippy Insurance. We aim to respond to\nall e-mails within 2 working days.\n\nGoSkippy Insurance | Customer Service\n\nLysander House, Catbrain Lane, Cribbs Causeway, Bristol, [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone: [phone redacted] | Website: www.goskippy.com \n( http://www.goskippy.com/ )\n\nhttps://sbgl.logicalware.com/uploads/inline?file_key=uploads%2Finline%2FTNMefgPD6TjM_gZpx4MKSQ-image.png\n"},{"id":"wb-b61e4bf3","subject":"Re title WA231076 Tŷ Mawr farm allegation of fraud mistake a","name":"0000-00-00_re-title-wa231076-ty-mawr-farm-allegation-of-fraud-mistake-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-title-wa231076-ty-mawr-farm-allegation-of-fraud-mistake-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"title-wa231076-t-mawr-farm-allegation-of-fraud-mistake-a","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-title-wa231076-ty-mawr-farm-allegation-of-fraud-mistake-a_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-dd1bdb31","subject":"Re wcr website enquiry","name":"0000-00-00_re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"wcr-website-enquiry","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-wcr-website-enquiry_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"No problem about Martin's case, understood, thanks for your prompt reply\r\nJess.\r\n\r\nI don't mean to appear litigious, but the other matter I have is BP vs\r\nBuckler 1987. My dad appealed it, it was dismissed. He then sought ECHR,\r\nblocked. He then died. The trauma on our family frightened and immobilised\r\neveryone from seeking justice. Even unto this day.\r\n\r\nI found a lot of fraud & concealment in this case. There's also a lot of\r\nmedia coverage in archives. I wondered if the clause in the limitations act\r\ncould allow me to reopen the case on these grounds. The museum confirmed to\r\nbe last week all the items exhevated from under our farm after it was\r\nstolen from us.\r\n\r\nI'll give you one of the 12 arguments I have where it concerns clauses in\r\nthe limitation act to reopen the case. My nan fought off the alleged\r\npossessor, BP Pensions Trust Ltd, for many years - and  maintained\r\nequitable title ownership of our 800 year old farm. But the judge ruled\r\nthat BP Properties Ltd, the claimant in the 1987 case, were ignored. And\r\nthe BP companies were seperate, so rejecting one doesn't inherently meaning\r\nrejecting the other. And so their letter of offer, a license to stay at\r\n\"their\" farm until she died, upheld and stopped the clock on adverse\r\npossession. Which was the position of our family (since our title deeds had\r\ngone missing from our home and copy gone from the public library during all\r\nthis multi generational lawfare).\r\n\r\nBut in my dads appeal (point 3/3) he argued BP Pensions Trust should have\r\nbeen the claimant, not BP Properties Ltd. To which the judges dismissed the\r\nappeal citing - both BP companies are basically the same.\r\n\r\nSo a blatant case of \"Heads they win, tails we lose\". Not to mention the\r\nrelationship between British Government and BP in those years being a huge\r\nbias.\r\n\r\nFurthermore my nan wasn't alive to defend her position in 87. And no\r\nevidence was presented of the alleged letter from BP to stop the clock of\r\nadverse possession. Yet the case was won on the fact a letter of rejection,\r\nfrom a now dead woman, wasn't able to be presented. It is insane how BP\r\ntook possession of our family farm of 400 years of occupancy.\r\n\r\nOur farm was prime real estate, overlooking Cardiff bay. This is an Erin\r\nBrokovitch scale scandal. It gets more wild. In my research I discovered\r\nMarconi stayed with us while inventing Radio. My great grandad took him via\r\nhorse & cart every day, to Lavenock Point Penarth, to conduct his radio\r\nexperiments - including the day of the first successful broadcast. There's\r\nnot even a plaque there today to commemorate that Llandough is the\r\nbirthplace of radio. I'm also a decorated Royal Signals veteran (honourable\r\ndischarge). Just 23 houses built over the site now. CADW expressly rejected\r\na petition at the time too, which would afford our 800 year old farm\r\nprotection from demolishment. Not only was the farm demolished, it was done\r\nduring the night and early morning after the lawfare in the court which is\r\nan evident act of  desperation and relentlessness.\r\n\r\nMy family would like justice. I believe we have a strong case. The\r\ncouncillor of Llandough is very interested. I just need legal\r\nrepresentation to take this forward.\r\n\r\nI look forward to your reply on that matter too if you wouldn't mind. I did\r\ncall and leave a message about it last week as well.\r\n\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOn Mon, 8 Dec 2025, 07:07 Jessica Williams, <Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk>\r\nwrote:\r\n\r\n> Good morning Requester,\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> I write in response to your website enquiry received by me this morning –\r\n> apologies for the delay in reverting to you. Unfortunately, this does not\r\n> appear to be a matter we would be able to assist with as we do not have a\r\n> Criminal Law department.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> You may be able to find assistance through Forces Law\r\n> <https://forceslaw.com/contact/>. They are essentially a switchboard of\r\n> multiple different firms of solicitors, all with military knowledge.\r\n> Alternatively, Op NOVA\r\n> <https://www.forcesemployment.org.uk/programmes/op-nova/contact/> may be\r\n> able to assist. They are a charity who support veterans in contact with the\r\n> justice system.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Thank you for your enquiry, and apologies we cannot be of assistance at\r\n> this time.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Best wishes,\r\n>\r\n> Jess\r\n>   ​​​​\r\n> Jessica Williams\r\n> Legal Assistant\r\n> DDI\r\n> Email\r\n> 01522 515947\r\n> Jessica.Williams@wcrlaw.co.uk\r\n>\r\n> wilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk\r\n>\r\n> The Maltings, 11‑15\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  Brayford\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  Wharf\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  East,\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  Lincoln,\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  LN5\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>  7AY\r\n> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/11%E2%80%9115+Brayford+Wharf+East,+Lincoln,+LN5+7AY?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>\r\n> [image: LinkedIn] <https://www.linkedin.com/company/wilkinchapmanrollits/>\r\n> [image: Facebook] <https://www.facebook.com/WilkinChapmanRollits>\r\n> [image: Instagram] <https://instagram.com/wilkinchapmanrollits>\r\n> [image: YouT] <https://www.youtube.com/@wilkinchapmanrollits>\r\n> Ranked in ‑ Lawyer UK 200 • Top Tier Firm ‑ Legal 500 UK • Leading Firm ‑\r\n> Chambers UK\r\n> ​IMPORTANT PLEASE READ:\r\n> ​TERMS OF BUSINESS:\r\n> ​\r\n> ​\r\n> Please note that our new Terms of Business released on 1 December 2025 can be found at\r\n> ​(https://www.wilkinchapmanrollits.co.uk/terms-of-business).\r\n> ​These were revised to reflect the change to Financial Services\r\n> ​Compensation Scheme deposit protection limit which has\r\n> ​risen to £120.000.​​\r\n> ​\r\n> ​CYBER CRIME ALERT:\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> ​You will be aware from recent press coverage email scams and cybercrime are becoming more prevalent and despite security ​\r\n>\r\n> ​measures ​being in place, emails can be hacked and the contents altered. This email has been checked for potential computer ​viruses\r\n>\r\n> ​using Mimecast technology. You should carry out your own virus check before opening any attachment. We accept no ​liability for any\r\n>\r\n> ​loss or damage, which may be caused by software viruses or interception or interruption of this email.\r\n>\r\n> ​For payments to us:\r\n>\r\n> ​Before transferring any money to us electronically, please call the individual who has conduc