the use of e‑mail does not imply that it is willing to do so, unless otherwise expressly agreed.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> ​This e‑mail and its contents are confidential, protected by law and legally privileged. Only access by the addressee is authorised. Any\r\n>\r\n> ​liability (in negligence, contract or otherwise) arising from any third party taking any action, or refraining from taking any action on the\r\n>\r\n> ​basis of any of the information contained in this e‑mail is hereby excluded. If you are not the intended addressee, please notify the\r\n>\r\n> ​sender immediately by replying to the email and delete the email from your system. Do not discuss, disclose the contents to any person,\r\n>\r\n> ​or store or copy the information in any medium or use it for any purpose whatsoever. Copyright in this e‑mail (and any attachments\r\n>\r\n> ​created by Wilkin Chapman LLP) belongs to Wilkin Chapman LLP which asserts the right to be identified as such and hereby objects to\r\n> ​any misuse thereof.\r\n>\r\n"},{"id":"wb-92bb9a58","subject":"Re williams title estate Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_re-williams-title-estate-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-williams-title-estate-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"williams-title-estate-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-williams-title-estate-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"\r\n\r\nPaul,\r\n\r\nIf I've erred in writing to you again I anticipate in advance, your \r\nforgiveness. \r\n\r\nFurther to our last correspondence, I'm writing to make a new request in \r\nseeking your assistance in identifying any records held by the Council \r\nrelating to one or two physical features and commemorative or heritage \r\nitems in the Llandough / Leckwith Road area.\r\n\r\nIn particular, I would be grateful for information on the following:\r\n\r\n*Tree planting*\r\nDoes the Council hold any records of a tree (the one shown in the attached \r\nphoto), including its exact location, maintenance history, and/or removal \r\nor relocation.\r\n\r\n*Stone or marker on the green*\r\nThe origin, purpose, and installation details of the millennium stone \r\nlocated on the green, and whether it originated from our land and former \r\nGreat House. If not, out of just pure curiousity, can you tell me where it \r\noriginate? If not from our land then where?\r\n\r\nI explicitly say “our land” (present tense), not former land, for two \r\nreasons:\r\n\r\nFirstly, we have never surrendered our land ownership claim, nor has it \r\nbeen lawfully or even properly legally extinguished. My late nan, even \r\nbefore falling back to her advised adverse possession claim, maintained and \r\nproved to a court she owned it. She was then dispossed of that proof but \r\nher ancestral \"Williams Title\" and name claim prevailed. \r\n\r\nThen BP's license letters to a purposefully inacurately titled \"Mrs \r\nBuckler\" to sever her land claim as a living woman, also layed a time bomb. \r\nBut that doesn't hold water as I will explain later.\r\n\r\nFinally my nans conveniently timed death in the two weeks she will have had \r\nto challenge BP's registration of our land in their names, gave the \r\nappearance of no contest. But it's my undertanding that BP commited purgery \r\nwitholding from (and providing false) information, to the land registry, \r\nwhile Thatcher lifted normal dudiligence guardrails; effectively allowing \r\nthe land registry to look the other way while the corporation did this. \r\n\r\nThe whole license letter agreement was also with a non existence legal \r\nfiction \"Mrs Buckler\" which BP imagined up in 1974 to quash my nans \r\naudience with a judge she requested. After courts already adjourning her \r\naudience with the judge earlier in 1974.  Its arguable if her audience with \r\nthe judge was even quashed by these letters, as the hearing appears to have \r\nbeen quashed first and the reason actually came later. So block a disabled, \r\nwidowed, pensioners audience with a judge and figure out a reason later. \r\nThat reason being the famous BP license letters. Which also appeared to \r\nhave been sent afterwards and backdated. This was  desperate and criminal. \r\nNot to mention identity fraud, considering it was creating joinder with a \r\nlegal fiction without the rights the living woman Mrs Williams had. With no \r\nmeeting of the minds either. And to add more insult to injury it was falsly \r\nalledged BP were backing off due to the bad press. Who supported my nan and \r\nthis scandal. \r\n\r\nThen later in 1987 the court applied this alledged agremeent with BP and my \r\nnan to my parents who entered into no such agreement with BP. And the \r\nruling stated my nan (now dead from 1983 and unable to defend her claim) \r\naccepted the license letters due to a non response. Which is itself a \r\nstretch of the imagination. But also untrue as in 1974 a publication was \r\nmade by the press. See attached. But this evidence was supressed and so not \r\nin the court hearing in 1987. Does this read to you like acceptable through \r\nsilence? She's literally screaming top of her lungs to the world. What a \r\nsham all this is. What a rap ship. The only class in this act of what is \r\nnow Church View Close, was my nan. \r\n\r\nFurthermore the judge in BP vs Buckler 1987. Who stated she'd \"imagined\" \r\nher ownership, which was an easy downplay of our standing to make, seeing \r\nas my nan was too dead (possibly murdered) to defend herself - he said that \r\neven my nans contest of BP, would have been to BP Pension Trust not the \r\nplaintiff BP Properties and they were two separate companies. Yet in my \r\nfather's appeal he pointed out BP Pension Trust should have been the \r\nplaintiff to which that same judge replied both BP companies are \r\neffectively the same. A blatant \"heads BP win, tails we lose\". I can't even \r\nunderstand how all the legal minds criticising this for the last 3 decades \r\nhaven't raised any of these concerns. I guess nobody cares enough about \r\ndisabled or elderly enough to care how they could be treated in these ways. \r\nAgain my family, still terrorised into silence, have also been told for \r\ndecades that times past and nothing can be done about this. But fraud is \r\nthe new discovery and it unravels ALL !!\r\n\r\nBecause we all tolerated this our children will be next. As the song goes. \r\nAnd I have a wife son and daughter. I am not tolerating this. I already \r\ndon't let my daughter step foot in that realm of so much sinister, \r\ngatekeeping of false records and narratives and protection of the worst \r\nkinds of people who are eating away at our lands and communies from the \r\ninside. \r\n\r\nHow I am so easily ignored by those alledgedly serving and defending and \r\nclaiming to be a democracy there, is where I feel I maybe on a completely \r\nalternate plane of reality. I don't undertand the disconnect as I in full \r\nmental and physical health. I left my military career with full honours. I \r\ncomplete my 22 in Oath under the employ of the Vale Council in 2024. I am \r\nbonafide. I also know war having served in the middle east. Not withstand I \r\nam most assuredly, along with my family, the rightful holders of lordship \r\nof the manor of Llandough. Demolishing the manor house in a terorist act \r\ndoesn't change that. \r\n\r\nThis pathogen/cancer like fraud and bad faith and actors, more so those who \r\nprotect it all after I've brought it to all your attentions it is the sort \r\nof stuff that lead to the \"battleground\" and \"warzone\" the newspapers of \r\n1988 described Llandough as being. With one councillor warning on record he \r\nwas almost certain someone would get killed. While Parliment stated \r\npublicly BP Pension Trust would not be happy to learn what was going on in \r\nSouth Wales (to children and grandchildren of a possibly murdered \r\npensioner). Even the MP at the time sided with us. And my dad did die like \r\nwas warned. But not in battle, but afterwards. Which is common. His death \r\nfighting this cruel first war (in a series of cruel wars soon to ensue) was \r\nsoon after his appeal of the 1987 ruling was wrongfully dismissed and his \r\nECHR request was blocked and his home bulldozed down. After he was ripped \r\nfrom his hospital bed and jailed without charge to purposefully prevent him \r\ndefending his home from being demolished. \r\n\r\nITV, who failed to report my mum was even pregnant with 3 children. In \r\nfootage that just took 38 years to see the light of day. Maybe because it \r\nstated and showed SAS being used and this whole Thatcher/ BP crime on my \r\nfamily, Llandough and even our nations herritage & history. Or that it \r\nhighlighted the lands premium real estate value overlooking Cardiff Bay. \r\n(Before being abruptly cut/ edited). So there's clearly more and ongoing \r\nsupression of information. And even worse is how ITV just quietly published \r\nthis to YouTube. This rabbit hole goes even further since I got back from \r\nexile in 2022 to find the news anchor Nichola Haywood Thomas dying and dead \r\ntoo before being able to talk to her about that. And that lady was like a \r\nsecond mum to me growing up as her son Tom and I were best friends. What is \r\ninteresting is how even practically  living with Tom and his mum in Cardiff \r\nfor a time, she never mentioned that news coverage or footage. Which I find \r\nvery odd too.\r\n\r\nDoes nobody els there want to fight this evil and have a chance of making \r\nit old to your beds dying of natural causes surrounded by family. It's \r\nsomething we see less and less. And I say this as a certified and \r\nexperienced military commander and leader and warfare professional. It is \r\nnot normal. We are already in a hybrid war and its getting less and less \r\nhybrid by the week. \r\n\r\nI was both there through all that in Llandough in 1988 and by 2005 I was in \r\nan actual warzone in the middle east. And you should know from me, the Iraq \r\nsoldiers I encountered while flying through villages behind a machine gun \r\non a helicopter, just broke through Belgium and are heading to UK. And I'm \r\nfairly confident our beach in Monknash in Wales was recently made exposed \r\nto import firearms and migrants. I ran that beach car park 2022-2024 and \r\nhave my police Axon bodycam and CCTV footage. So I would hope my family and \r\nour community heal from our divide and conquer in 1988 swift and sure so we \r\ncan put this behind us and to bed sooner than later. Or we will most \r\ncertain die as individuals at an increasing rate to what we already are. \r\nAnd I know, even while flying around, Llandough is seeing specific \r\ninstances of the concerns I'm raising. Moving the British Legion closer \r\ninwards won't help. The Brit'ish are the issue for us indigenous Britons \r\nand Welsh and our actual guests, friends and family who aren't. I already \r\nexported my dog from Dinas Powys to my place in the Caribbean after an \r\nafghan was in my garden trying to steal him. 97 were secretly housed by the \r\nVale Council near our 11 home village of Monknash at the time. Absolutely \r\nno response to my report of one trying to steal my dog as they were more \r\nconcerned about keeping it secret from the public. Not withstanding I was \r\nexpected to sleep in a tent that same year, flying back from New York to \r\ncare for my other nan. The Brit'ish is already waging war on our \r\ncommunities. I'm 100% a counter officer now. I pray Wales decolonises and \r\nScotland renounces and ireland Unites and England at least gets its own \r\nparliament. I heard yesterday UK police giving a public warning to prepare \r\nto be shot at and run and hide. Not that you should run and hide unless \r\nyou're a woman or child. Also knives you run from, guns you run towards. \r\nThe Brit'ish is forever depopulating indigenous Britons. But like I'm \r\nproving with our land in Llandough. We are the land. And regimes do come \r\nand go on our small pale island. \r\n\r\nIf my alledged own hometown community want to treat sons of Llandough how \r\nI've been. Which is buried alive and exiled as a toddler. So let's start \r\nwith the fact nobody even knows me in Llandough as I am basically presumed \r\ndead since birth by Llandough. I was sent to war to die as a teen by Blair. \r\nNot withstanding that I was then exiled between leaving my military career \r\nwith honours in 2007 and serving under the welsh government in 2022, after \r\nwhisleblowing on the epstein class in 2013. 8 years I was on a caribbean \r\nisland with my girlfriend Dr Carrie Madej. Just to survive the 3 pairs of \r\ncorrupt UK police, 5 lots of corrupt UK soldiers and the helicopter sent \r\nafter me to Monknash, to try to kidnap and silence me. No charges. No \r\nwarrant for my arrest. Just the cover up of ritualistic child abuse of my \r\nabducted boy. After failing to ransom me with him. I know precisely the \r\nthreat of wickedness and torture everyone is held hostage under there, in \r\nthat realm. My son is still abducted and missing, presumed dead. 13 years \r\nlater. There's no justice or child protection or other system back there. \r\nJust the illusion of it, while the inverse is occurring. \r\n\r\nWe can only truly count on our communities, tribes and family. \r\n\r\nBut I digress. To resume what  I was saying beforehand, the statute of \r\nlimitation with this matter between my family and BP would normally have \r\napplied had it not been for my discovery and allegation of fraud and \r\nwithholding and suppression of information that resulted in our \r\ndisplacement from our land and home.\r\n\r\nMy two private security close protection officers when I got exiled until \r\n2022, were both 3 time decorated gulf war veterans. One an airforce MP from \r\nDerby. The other a US Marine Lt. Col Curtis Van Sant. Curtis was also a \r\npolice Sergeant in Miami and professor of criminal psychology. While in a \r\nsafe house in Santo Domingo, DR  - before we obtained the video evidence of \r\nmy 36 day old boys abductors and captors performing rituals on him. Before \r\nthe corrupt UK police tried calling me to surrender, having failed to try \r\nto kidnap and silence and frame and extradite me. Before all that we had \r\nshreds of evidence. Nothing individually constituted a crime of any \r\nvelocity. But Curtis, being a professor of criminal psychology knew all the \r\nsigns were there. Like some of the images on their computers. Or the animal \r\nclothes they would dress my abducted boy in. Or the tactics attempted to \r\ntry using my abducted child to handle or ransom me. \r\n\r\nThat's the perfect crime Thatcher and BP (the Brit'ish) hoped it would be \r\non our town of Llandough and my disabled widowed pensioner nan. My nans \r\ntitle stolen then it was a death of a thousand cuts over decades. Court \r\nmistakes. Proceedural unfairness. Supression of information. Fake news, \r\nfasly labelling us squatters. All designed to fly under the radar of \r\nanything constituting a crime. But a crime has been commited on Llandough. \r\nPerhaps like we say in Llandovery where Rhys and I went to private boarding \r\nschool before I got into military intelligence,  Llandough has old \r\nLlandoughians like Llandovery has old Llandoverians. I see some online \r\nnever forever our family and farm which warms my heart. Many kind words on \r\nsocial media from people who would come and feed our horses and so forth. \r\n\r\nBut I digressed again. The second reason I say I own the land. Which might \r\nget the wet fish of a Councillor or MP you have there to show a pulse, is \r\nthe Land Registry recently wrote back to me indicating that my nan, Mary \r\nWilliams, was not incorrect in our claim of ownership of the land. They \r\nalso do not dispute that we owned the farm, nor that evidence of our \r\nownership didn't exist. They reaffirmed that no court ruled against my nans \r\nownership claim on its merits, but simply state they will not “look behind” \r\nthe court decision that awarded BP possession and are not the body to \r\ninvestigate historical ownership. Their position is essentially that they \r\nwill not investigate this, rather than that they have investigated and \r\ndetermined our claim to be false. Key historical questions therefore remain \r\nunanswered.\r\n\r\nOur families forced removal from our land and home in Llandough, since \r\n1667, because us OWNERS refused to play the role of hostage tenant to the \r\nterrorist thieves keeping our stolen title from us, is not a final ruling \r\nor settled. Mere possession was awarded to BP. So even if I'd liked what \r\nthey'd done to our place, ownership remains undetermined and unresolved. \r\nForced removed doesn't change that. Time doesn't change that. Raveling \r\ndoesn't change that. Court mistakes, fraud, purgergy, suppressing \r\ninformation. Nothing done, including rewriting and supressing history after \r\nthe fact, has truly changed the fact that our families position remains \r\nunchanged and has remained unchanged and unwaivering since my grandmother \r\nfirst said, as she said until her dying breath, as my dad did until his \r\ndying breath, as I will until my dying breath; We are that land. It is \r\nours. \r\n\r\nHad the alledged fraud or consealment not occurred, we would have had \r\nlittle basis to revisit this. However, fraud and so forth is a clause in \r\nthe limitation act for good reason, and so the limitation clock has only \r\nrecently begun: from my discovery of this alledged fraud upon my family, \r\nnot the time of occurrence of it. So we are into this for at least the next \r\n6 years. People will be remembered for their roles in these next 6 years. \r\n\r\nIf it's any consolation, I'm working to rebuild a replica of the Welsh \r\nSettlement in Argentina. And here where the Welsh language and culture and \r\nhistory, along with Italians which Marconi was, will not only tell the \r\nstory of BP vs Buckler up until 1988. But these next 6 years will more than \r\ncertainly be on the open house tour. It's already a damming chapter for the \r\nBrit'ish and even Welsh Govenrment under British occupancy and rule, how \r\nmuch effort went into burying my nan, dad, farm and herritage and history. \r\nArgentina doesn't shy away from how wicked the British treat us Welsh too. \r\nDecapitation Committee was the exact phrase supporters of Michael Jones \r\nused. The man who helped found this colony in Patagonia. \r\n\r\nMakers of leaders, be careful of the kinds of leaders you're creating. 99% \r\nof Brit'ish MP's just refused to sign an EDM to condemn decapitating \r\nChristians. You have Bonnie Blue openly turning her baby shower into a \r\ngolden shower. Your real is hell. And the four horsemen \r\n\r\nI would expect Llandough community to be more enthustiatic than me for a \r\nfull and accurate understanding of the towns local history. I know my \r\nfamily would appreciate feeling that villages warmth again. Notwithstanding \r\nthe last 3+ decades in which I believe, at least in this case alone, \r\nthere's been a realm of suppression, scandal, abuse of power, procedural \r\nunfairness, and miscarriage of justice holding hostages, all of which \r\nproved life threatening untoward my late father, William Buckler, and my \r\nlate nan, Mrs Williams. \r\n\r\nWe are simply now seeking records in the hands of elected fiduciaries be \r\nfactual, coherent, truthful and given the proper optics and focus — which \r\nsurely you'll agree is not outside the basic benevolence of the realm I, \r\nuntil recently, naively believed we all, other than BP perhaps, all existed \r\nwithin. \r\n\r\nThese concerns of fraud and consealment/ supression of information which I \r\nrecently identified and alledge, are both troubling but also an opportunity \r\nto heal and clarify matters fully, rather than allow further untenable \r\ndishonour, shame, suppression and uncertainty. I simply seek accurate \r\nrecords and true accounts of history be held by public bodies. Or else the \r\nacting authorities there lacks legitimacy and subsiquenlty defeats your own \r\nalledged authority. In which case Church View Close is merely a Terrorist \r\nCell or Camp, in a Terrorist Network, following the 1988 Act of Terrorism \r\nto displace my family while our intersecting matriarchy/ dynasty was at its \r\nmost vunerable. Those same terrorist which demolished and replaced our \r\nmanorial 800 year old home with shelter for the aforementioned realms \r\nhostage or officers doesn't change these facts; and so constitute fair \r\ngame, in what is effectively a lawless Society of our own silence and \r\naquiessance. \r\n\r\n*Plaques or commemorative markers*\r\nI also wonder whether there are, or have ever been:\r\n\r\n   - any plaques or memorials installed in the area\r\n   - any records of proposed but uninstalled plaques\r\n   - any references to Guglielmo Marconi or related local heritage \r\n   recognition (including Marconi Avenue, which I have already noted).\r\n\r\n*Land and maintenance responsibilities*\r\nFinally, I would be grateful for clarification of land and maintenance \r\nresponsibilities for the green, Church View Close, and the immediate \r\nsurrounding area. Whether these are maintained by the Council or another \r\nauthority, and whether records exist regarding changes over time.\r\n\r\n*Council records referencing local involvement*\r\nWhether Council minutes, correspondence, or historical notes contain any \r\nreferences to myself or members of my family in connection with local \r\nevents, commemorative activities, or the features described above.\r\n\r\nIf any such records exist, I would be grateful if you could advise how I \r\nmay access copies.\r\n\r\nIf this request would be more appropriately handled as a formal Subject \r\nAccess Request under data protection legislation, please advise and I will \r\nsubmit it in the correct format.\r\n\r\nIf the Council does not hold such records, I would be grateful if you could \r\nconfirm this and, where possible, direct me to the relevant authority.\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and assistance.\r\n\r\nYours sincerely,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-d3289583","subject":"Re your ref edd our ref WA231076 a 216 kh","name":"0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_kh_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_kh_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-kh","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_kh_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/KH\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 19:22 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKaren,\n\nThanks for your reply.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 21 Apr 2026 at 16:00, Coventry.OfficeMail\n<[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed document by post.\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-2d6a7405","subject":"Re your ref edd our ref WA231076 a 216 lg","name":"0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_lg_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_lg_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-lg","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_lg_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Griffiths,\r\n\r\nThanks for your letter of 23 March 2026 regarding the historic registration\r\nof Ty Mawr Farm, title WA231076. I note your explanation of HM Land\r\nRegistry’s administrative role and that you say there is no evidence of a\r\n“mistake” on the basis of the file you have reviewed.\r\n\r\nMy family’s concern, however, is that the first registration was procured\r\nby misrepresentation and identity fraud by BP, rather than by a simple\r\nclerical error. The occupier was my grandmother, Mrs Williams, from a\r\nfamily that had occupied the property and land since at least 1667, not the\r\nfictitious “Mrs Buckler” BP fabricated in 1974 for their unilateral\r\nlicence, which was the basis of the BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) case.\r\nBP also appears to have failed to disclose the long‑running ownership\r\ndispute. In a 1978 suppressed newspaper article, my grandmother publicly\r\nasserted her ownership and stated that BP could not prove ownership and had\r\nnever obtained a court ruling that it was the owner, only possession orders.\r\n\r\nHow was BP able to register our land in its name? Did HM Land Registry\r\nenquire whether there was any dispute over the land, given that the dispute\r\nappears in court records from 1974? Twice that year BP obstructed my\r\ngrandmother from making her case that she owned the land: first, the\r\nhearing was adjourned without a ruling; then the licence letters, using\r\nidentity fraud, prevented the second hearing from taking place. These were\r\nopportunities to dispossess a widowed, disabled woman.\r\nHad HM Land Registry recorded or investigated the existence of this\r\ndispute, BP’s inability to prove ownership, the archaeological and historic\r\nsignificance of the site, or sought a copy of my grandmother’s death\r\ncertificate to see that the name on the licence and narrative were\r\ncompletely different, we believe BP would not have been able to achieve\r\nfirst registration on the basis presented. Instead, the use of the wrong\r\nname (“Mrs Buckler” instead of my married grandmother, Mrs Williams) and\r\nthe non‑disclosure of the dispute and family claim enabled dispossession\r\nthrough what we say was identity fraud, which my grandmother was unable to\r\ncontest as she also died in the same year as registration.\r\n\r\nI wish to append to this land parcel our maintained position of dispute. We\r\nnever surrendered. We were removed by around 30 police officers and\r\ninformation was suppressed. My family being paralysed by fear and silence\r\nis not the same as surrender from sound mind and agency.\r\nFurther background is set out at bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz. My family wants\r\nnarrative justice as the possibly rightful, dispossessed via fraud,\r\nexecutors of the Manor of Llandough.\r\n\r\nI am aware that HM Land Registry operates a statutory indemnity and redress\r\nscheme under the Land Registration Act 2002, and that substantial payments\r\n(including around £8 million in a single year) have been made where people\r\nsuffer loss because of mistakes or fraud in the register. I therefore wish\r\nto explore, formally, whether our family’s loss of Ty Mawr Farm, in\r\ncircumstances where BP’s misrepresentations and the suppression of an\r\nactive dispute were not reflected on the register, can be considered within\r\nthat indemnity/redress framework.\r\n\r\nIn light of the above, I ask HM Land Registry to state clearly whether you\r\naccept or deny that:\r\nBP was able to obtain first registration of Ty Mawr Farm even though there\r\nwas no court ruling that BP owned the land and BP had been unable to prove\r\nownership in proceedings, which were confined to possession.\r\n\r\nThe land was registered while there was an active and public dispute over\r\nownership (including my grandmother’s 1978 public assertion of ownership\r\nand the BP v Buckler litigation), and while the long‑term occupier, my\r\ngrandmother, had died and was therefore unable to challenge the application.\r\n\r\nMy grandmother’s identity and superior family title and land claim\r\nassociated with that name were mis‑described in the material on which you\r\nrelied, as BP used “Mrs Buckler” instead of my married grandmother’s actual\r\nname, Mrs Williams, and that this misdescription and the concealment of the\r\ndispute were not detected or queried by HM Land Registry before completing\r\nfirst registration.�\r\nIf these matters are admitted, I consider they amount to negligence and\r\nmaladministration by HM Land Registry in allowing BP to register our family\r\nland in its name in those circumstances. If you do not accept that, please\r\nexplain precisely which of the above points you dispute and on what basis,\r\nso that I can take appropriate legal advice and pursue an indemnity/redress\r\nclaim if available.\r\nSeparately from that, please also:\r\nProvide official copies of the 23 May 1975 and 19 November 1982\r\nconveyances, and of the first registration applications and all supporting\r\ndocuments for WA231076 and WA240304, so I can obtain specialist advice on\r\nthe extent of any misrepresentation in what was lodged.\r\n\r\nConfirm the correct procedure and forms to make a claim under your\r\nindemnity/redress scheme in a historic case of alleged fraud and\r\nmisrepresentation in first registration, and whether you consider this\r\nmatter potentially falls within that scheme, subject to evidence.\r\n\r\nI appreciate that you cannot determine the underlying ownership dispute,\r\nbut it is important that HM Land Registry notes that the Buckler/Williams\r\nfamily contests the integrity of the original registration of Ty Mawr Farm\r\non the basis of identity fraud, non‑disclosure of a live dispute, and the\r\nabsence of any judicial determination that BP owned the land.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\n\r\nOn Mon, 23 Mar 2026, 05:56 Wales.OfficeMail, <\r\nWales.Office@landregistry.gov.uk> wrote:\r\n\r\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\r\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\r\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\r\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\r\n>\r\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\r\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\r\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\r\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\r\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\r\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\r\n> document by post.\r\n>\r\n> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r\r\n> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais\r\n> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni\r\n> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\r\n>\r\n> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg\r\n> y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y\r\n> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho\r\n> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun\r\n> at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir\r\n> EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd\r\n> rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\r\n>\r\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\r\n>\r\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\r\n>\r\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\r\n>\r\n> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebos