date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_mc_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-mc","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076_a_216_mc_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/MC\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 26 May 2026 17:18 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Mr Gill,\n\nThank you for your response dated 25 May 2026 regarding title WA231076.\n\nI note your statement that HM Land Registry considered my grandmother to be\nthe same individual despite the use of different surnames and that “there\nis a marriage certificate to show this”.\n\nPlease could you clarify:\n\n   1. Was a marriage certificate actually lodged with HM Land Registry as\n   part of the registration evidence relied upon by HM Land Registry, or are\n   you referring to information held elsewhere?\n   2. If such a certificate formed part of the registration evidence\n   considered by HM Land Registry, please identify the document relied upon\n   and whether copies may be requested.\n   3. Prior correspondence and BP licence letters before 1974, to my\n   understanding, referred to my grandmother as Mrs Williams. I am therefore\n   trying to understand the evidential chain relied upon and how identity\n   continuity was established.\n\nI also wish to clarify that my purpose has been to query and understand the\nhistorical record and registration process. I did not submit this as a\ncomplaint; my intention was to seek clarification and challenge aspects of\nthe historical narrative where I believe evidence may be incomplete or\ndisputed.\n\nMy concerns extend beyond the surname issue. I remain concerned about\nwhether all appropriate checks and safeguards were applied at the time of\nregistration and whether the underlying evidence was fully scrutinised.\n\nI understand HM Land Registry’s position that it records interests\npresented to it and is not a forum for determining disputes. However, I am\nstill gathering evidence and attempting to understand how these events\noccurred and whether any procedural irregularities existed.\n\nAt present I am not asking HM Land Registry to accept my conclusions. I am\nrequesting transparency regarding the evidence and process relied upon.\n\nThank you again for your reply.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n\nOn Mon, 25 May 2026 at 13:16, Birkenhead.OfficeMail <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\n> document by post.\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-6cfb2a7b","subject":"Re external cais am gyngor cyfreithiol Tŷ Mawr Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-t-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-external-cais-am-gyngor-cyfreithiol-ty-mawr-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: [EXTERNAL] Cais am Gyngor Cyfreithiol – Ty Mawr, Llandough\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 18:06 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHi,\n\nThanks for your reply.\nI can correspond in English, but for the case I'd like it to all be in\nWelsh.\nI feel that's important.\n\nBut all are welcome to assist my family in this endeavour.\nThis will take, at least, a village.\n\nSion\n\nOn Tue, 17 Feb 2026 at 14:04, Emily Wellington <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Good afternoon Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry and voicemail.\n>\n>\n>\n> For us to provide a fee quotation we will require sight of some further\n> documents. Please send these through and we can assess if we are able to\n> assist further.\n>\n>\n>\n> Whilst we do not provide legal advice through the medium of Welsh, my\n> colleague Rhys Evans is a fluent Welsh speaker and is happy to discuss\n> matters through the medium of Welsh.\n>\n>\n>\n> I look forward to hearing from you.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Emily\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> ​​​​\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 13 February 2026 01:33\n> *To:* UZZI Consulting <[email redacted]>\n> *Cc:* [email redacted]; Hello <[email redacted]>;\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted]\n> *Subject:* [EXTERNAL] Cais am Gyngor Cyfreithiol – Ty Mawr, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> Annwyl Syr/Fadam,\n>\n> Ysgrifennaf i ofyn am gyngor cyfreithiol mewn perthynas â mater cymhleth\n> yn ymwneud â Thŷ Mawr (Great House Farm), Llandough.\n>\n> Yn gryno, mae’r mater yn codi’r cwestiynau canlynol:\n>\n>    - Diffyg pend