errorist cell/camp on my land.\n\nMarconi was staying with us in Llandough when he invented radio. This too\nwas covered up. Cardiff City will not put a plaque naming Marconi as the\ninventor on the statue of a radio at Cardiff Bay—not even a plaque to\ncommemorate it. Llandough should be a tourist attraction based on this fact\nalone, rather than the occupying terrorist network's cell of 23 houses, as\nI see it.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\nOn behalf of (and as one of) the Heirs and Successors of Mary Williams,\nGreat House Farm, Manor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nCurrent Address: [address redacted]\n\n---\n"},{"id":"wb-a1d81f58","subject":"Response to national archives case number cas 313954 y6c0h3","name":"0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Response to National Archives case number CAS-313954-Y6C0H3 CRM:022601115\nFrom: RESO Records Enquiries\nDate: Fri, 06 Feb 2026 13:07 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for clarifying the nature of your enquiry.\n\nIn answer to your main enquiry, in general we would not add notes to, or review, records in light of unresolved disputes or other matters. The records are left to speak for themselves. In fact, those records are often incomplete and patchwork in character, meaning that they may not enable the enquirer to know what the final determination or outcome of any dispute was.\n\nSince you refer to a reported Court of Appeal (Civil Division) case, I have conducted a quick search of our, admittedly limited holdings. The main record series in which you might expect to find archival material here are J 157<https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C9764>, J 83<https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C9691> and J 84<https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C9692>. Unfortunately, none contain records relevant to the case.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nCharlotte Smith﻿\n\nPrincipal Records Specialist, Modern Legal Records\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk<http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/>\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n\nTo clarify my original enquiry, I am specifically concerned with the historical record surrounding the case of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2, which involved a disputed land dispossession at Great House Farm in Llandough, South Glamorgan. This stemmed from earlier proceedings in 1974, including an adjourned case in July and an appeal attempt on October 31st that was impacted by correspondence from BP the same day. Following the 1987 ruling, there was forced removal, demolition of our family home, and archaeological activity on the site, despite ongoing questions about the adjudication of ownership prior to land registration.\n\nMy question is not solely about locating ownership or court documents (though any guidance on whether The National Archives holds physical files from these proceedings would be welcome), but rather whether circumstances like these—where ownership was disputed and not fully resolved before registration or excavation—raise any considerations for the integrity or completeness of the archival record. For instance, do such disputes prompt reviews or annotations in historical land records, or are there protocols for archiving related materials from corporate entities like BP or local authorities involved?\n\nI understand your resources are focused on national-level holdings, but any further direction would greatly assist my research.\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"},{"id":"wb-b3cd477e","subject":"Response to national archives case number cas 313954 y6c0h3","name":"0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-8648c2ae","subject":"Response to enquiry at the national archives case number cas","name":"0000-00-00_response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number: CAS-313954-Y6C0H3 CRM:052900508\nFrom: RESO Records Enquiries\nDate: Fri, 06 Feb 2026 10:28 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nIt is unlikely The National Archives holds the records of this type of case, and the Central Land Registry<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry>, who hold records of land registration, is a separate body. Some records of land ownership can be found among records at local or county archives.\n\nI recommend you consult our guide to searching for records of Land ownership records and deeds: an overview - The National Archives<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/research-guides/land-ownership-records-and-deeds-an-overview/>. Regarding the court cases you mention, I also recommend you consult: Civil court cases: Chancery Division since 1875 - The National Archives<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/research-guides/civil-court-cases-chancery-division-since-1875/>, and you may also find Civil courts: appeal cases after 1875 - The National Archives<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/research-guides/civil-courts-appeal-cases-after-1875/> of use to your research. These guides will help you to use our catalogue<https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/>, or other online sources, effectively and focus your search.\n\nRecords are represented in our online catalogue by a title, a reference and a brief description. When you search our catalogue using keywords you are searching across these titles and descriptions, rather than the contents of the records themselves. By clicking on any search result, you can see whether the record is available online or if you need to visit us to view the original. You can also request copies of records from their catalogue description page.\n\nIf the record is held by another archive, you will need to contact them directly to find out how you can access it.\n\nYou can also watch this video<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tz4f--o3zUU> for more advice on using our online catalogue.\n\nYou are welcome to visit us<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/about/visit-us/> to continue your research here in person, where access to our records is free of charge. Before you visit, please check our website for information regarding our opening hours<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/about/visit-us/opening-times/> and ID requirements<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/about/visit-us/researching-here/do-i-need-a-readers-ticket/>. If you are unable to visit, or would like someone to pursue this research on your behalf, please see the available paid search options<https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/paying-for-research/> on our website.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRobert Fleming﻿\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk<http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/>\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 31 January 2026 05:59\nTo: Contact Centre <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Concern regarding historical record following disputed land dispossession\n\n        You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI'm writing to raise a concern regarding the integrity of the historical record following disputed dispossession of land i.e. BP vs Buckler 1987\n\nAfter forced removal and demolition of our home, archaeological excavation and removal of items took place on land whose ownership had never been conclusively adjudicated at the time of registration. BP asserted it, but it was never determined in a ruling beforehand as the July 1974 case between BP and my grandmother was adjourned and the October 31st 1974 appeal and audience with a judge she made just 24 hours before, was squashed by letters sent by BP that same morning.\n\nI am not making allegations here, simply stating facts about this landmark legal case. And asking whether this type of circumstance is relevant to archival or historical record considerations.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler\n\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"},{"id":"wb-e3cd1132","subject":"See attached whisleblow a sgt buckler","name":"0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblow-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblow-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"see-attached-whisleblow-a-sgt-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblow-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-31fcecff","subject":"See attached whisleblower a sgt buckler","name":"0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblower-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblower-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"see-attached-whisleblower-a-sgt-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_see-attached-whisleblower-a_sgt-buckler_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-2c410fcc","subject":"Setting aside BP v Buckler 1987 on grounds of fraud","name":"0000-00-00_setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"setting-aside-bp-v-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hwyl,\r\n\r\nI speak fluent Welsh but will keep this in English as I'm a military cyber\r\nand electronic warfare professional and use A.I which is learning from this\r\ncase for a possible class action lawsuit scaling.\r\n\r\nI'm writing to raise a long-standing family grievance concerning the events\r\nsurrounding BP v Buckler (1987), and what I believe to be the dispossession\r\nand marginalisation of my indigenous Welsh family from our ancestral\r\nbirthland and heritage. Our title appears to have been stolen after Marconi\r\nstayed with us while inventing radio, then for the last century we appear\r\nto have suffered decades of supressed info, court \"mistakes\" , proceedural\r\nunfairness, conveniently timed deaths, gaps in records, abuse of power,\r\nhuman rights violations and what I now see to be fraud. Fraud unravels all.\r\nAnd limitation applies from discovery not occurance of the fraud.\r\n\r\nMy family history concerns Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough, and the\r\nBuckler / Williams lineage connected to the property and surrounding lands.\r\nFrom family records, historical material, local reporting, and documents\r\nreferenced through my research, I believe there are unresolved questions\r\nregarding title history, possession, treatment of the family, and the\r\nhandling of allegations and complaints raised over the years.\r\n\r\nMy concern is not only the legal events themselves, but the broader\r\nhistorical context. The period during and following the Thatcher era saw\r\nmajor industrial, land, and economic changes in Wales. From my perspective,\r\nthese changes disproportionately affected Welsh communities and families\r\nwith long-standing local roots and historical connections to land.\r\n\r\nI believe BP v Buckler (1987) should be revisited as part of a wider\r\nhistorical review of:\r\n\r\n• Chain of custody and title history relating to the property and lands\r\n• Historical ownership claims and succession issues\r\n• Any council records, correspondence, reports, or discussions concerning\r\nthe matter\r\n• Allegations reportedly raised but not fully investigated\r\n• The treatment and displacement of local Welsh families connected to the\r\nland\r\n\r\nI respectfully request access to all available records, archives, minutes,\r\ncorrespondence, title documents, and related materials concerning the\r\nproperty and associated disputes. I am being ignored by the MP and\r\nCouncillor and Land Registry converted my query to a complaint only to mark\r\nit as solved and squash it. Ministry of Justice took 6 months to reply only\r\nto dismiss me. ITV ignore me but quietly declassified supressed footage\r\nrecently:\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\r\n\r\nI am working on a website to put together the full timeline and full\r\nevidence for a Netflix documentry. Or a Welsh studio and producer if\r\npossible. My family want narrative and legal justice. They are terrified\r\ninto silence. I am 7000 miles away in Patagonia just to bring this matter\r\nup, since the British State has already tried Force, Stealth/ Secrecy and\r\nfraudulent License and other clandestine strikes from the shadows, instead\r\nof addressing this out in the open. I also require of the Senedd a public\r\nenquiry. Our Nation and Herritage was defrauded, not just my family.\r\n\r\nMy intention is historical clarification, transparency, and preservation of\r\nWelsh heritage and family history.\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\r\n\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-3d3a9d0e","subject":"Requester buckler nec vi nec clam nec precario heir successor to","name":"0000-00-00_requester-nec-vi-nec-clam-nec-precario-heir-successor-to_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_requester-nec-vi-nec-clam-nec-precario-heir-successor-to_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"quester-buckler-nec-vi-nec-clam-nec-precario-heir-successor-to","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_requester-nec-vi-nec-clam-nec-precario-heir-successor-to_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs / Ma’am,\r\n\r\nI write from the Welsh settlement in Patagonia, Argentina, with respect,\r\nand for the attention of His Majesty King Charles III and the appropriate\r\nofficers of the Royal Household.\r\n\r\nI write as a Welsh national, a father, and a former public servant. I\r\nconcluded twenty-two years in oath in 2024, including a career in the\r\nmilitary, also serving in the Middle East and leaving colour service with\r\nhonours. I recently completed employment under the Welsh Government (Vale\r\nof Glamorgan Council). I now write in a private capacity, not under oath,\r\nand not in any adversarial posture, but in good faith and with the\r\nintention that the historic record be accurately preserved.\r\n\r\nMy purpose in writing is to place on record serious concerns regarding the\r\nhistorical treatment, documentation, and subsequent erasure of my family’s\r\nancestral estate, Tŷ Mawr (Great House Farm), Llandough, in the Vale of\r\nGlamorgan.\r\n\r\nTŷ Mawr was an historic monastic grange and site of Roman antiquity. From\r\n1667, it was held in continuous occupation and stewardship by my fathers\r\nsides maternal family, the Williams family, later intersecting with the\r\nBuckler line through marriage. For over three centuries, my forebears\r\noccupied, worked, and maintained this land. I was born there.\r\n\r\nPrior to enlisting in Signals Intelligence roles and encountering senior\r\nnational and royal figures in the course of official duties, I was educated\r\nin Wales, including at Llandovery College, which I attended under the\r\nGovernment-run Assisted Places Scheme, having been selected on academic\r\nmerit. On my mothers side, my late grandfather, the Welsh BAFTA-winning\r\nactor Ray Smith, carried the same Welsh cultural identity into public life.\r\nMy wider family has likewise contributed to Welsh cultural life, including\r\nmy aunt Shan Cothi, the opera singer, and her husband/ my late uncle;\r\nJustin Smith, founder of the Welsh band Tigertailz and directed a major\r\n'visit wales' campaign for the tourist board. These details are to\r\ndemonstrate continuity of Welsh cultural life rooted in this family and\r\nplace. I'm also a fluent speak Welsh, I named my daugher Delyth, and I do\r\nmuch for the continuity of Welsh cultural life.\r\n\r\nIn 1974, my grandmother on my fathers side; Mary Williams, initiated\r\nproceedings concerning the title to Tŷ Mawr. Those proceedings were\r\nadjourned and later that same year effectively extinguished without\r\nsubstantive resolution. Critically, my grandmother never adopted her\r\nhusband’s surname; she remained Mary Williams throughout her life. That\r\nname was not incidental. It was the living link to the 1667 acquisition of\r\nthe farm and to our family’s long occupation.\r\n\r\nDuring later proceedings, the name “Mrs Buckler” was ascribed to her in\r\ncourt records. This misidentification had material consequences. It severed\r\nthe documentary continuity of the Williams line and undermined both our de\r\nfacto occupation and any consideration of adverse possession. This\r\nmisnaming remains, to my knowledge, uncorrected in the public record.\r\n\r\nIn 1988, my family was forcibly removed from Tŷ Mawr, having been\r\ncharacterised as squatters despite centuries of occupation. Our home — an\r\n800-year-old farmhouse — was demolished shortly thereafter. I was four\r\nyears old. I witnessed the destruction alongside my siblings and parents.\r\nWe were not permitted to retrieve belongings or family records. Centuries\r\nof family material history were lost.\r\n\r\nOf particular concern is that the site had long been associated with Roman\r\nremains. In 1870, a Roman burial was reportedly uncovered on the land, a\r\nfact later omitted or minimised in official descriptions of the site.\r\nFollowing the demolition of the farmhouse, and prior to residential\r\ndevelopment, it emerged that the land contained what is now understood to\r\nbe the largest Roman burial site excavated in Wales, with over 1,000\r\nburials. Had this been properly recorded and acknowledged earlier,\r\nstatutory archaeological protections should have applied.\r\n\r\nThe effect of these events has been the near-total erasure of the historic\r\nand indigenous Welsh continuity of Tŷ Mawr from public narrative and\r\nrecord. The land now forms part of a modern housing development, without\r\nacknowledgment of its significance or of the family that occupied it for\r\nover three centuries.\r\n\r\nI wish to be clear: my primary concern is not confrontation, but correction\r\n— correction of the historical record, acknowledgment of documented\r\nirregularities, and preservation of truth for future generations. My family\r\nhas carried the consequences of these events for decades, including\r\nsignificant trauma, and many remain reluctant to come forward.\r\n\r\nI hold a forensic analysis estimating the financial losses associated with\r\nTŷ Mawr at approximately £101.2 million, but the greater matter is not\r\nmonetary. It is the restoration of narrative accuracy and the\r\nacknowledgment of indigenous Welsh continuity at this site and my families\r\nstanding in our local community thereafter. The generational trauma is so\r\ndeep, even last week my mother refused to discuss this, even privately.\r\n\r\nI do not write to demand action from His Majesty personally, nor do I\r\npresume upon the Crown. I write so that it cannot later be said that these\r\nmatters were unknown or unrecorded. I respectfully request that this\r\ncorrespondence be retained as a notice of concern regarding historic record\r\nintegrity, misidentification of parties, and the suppression or omission of\r\nmaterial archaeological and cultural facts.\r\n\r\nMy intention is also to rebuild an exact replica of Great House Farm in\r\nPatagonia, where the Welsh community here has welcomed the preservation of\r\nthis history. This project is intended as an act of cultural conservation,\r\nnot protest.\r\n\r\nI remain respectful of the Crown’s constitutional role and of the King\r\npersonally. My request is simply that the truth of Tŷ Mawr — its history,\r\nits people, and its erasure — is not allowed to disappear entirely from the\r\nhistorical record.\r\n\r\nI certify that I write in good faith, with full mental capacity, and\r\nwithout hostility. I seek only truth, acknowledgment, and preservation of\r\nhistory.\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\nSion Hywel Buckler\r\n[redacted], Wales\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-3d85129b","subject":"Requester buckler","name":"0000-00-00_requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"quester-buckler","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_requester_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm from Cardiff, with a military background.\r\nI'm married with a wife, daughter and little dog - (currently all in the\r\nCaribbean).\r\nMy Address is [redacted], Wales. [redacted]\r\n\r\nI was awarded life membership to the Royal Signals as recent as 2017.\r\n(Britain's and the British military's home of Cyber Professionals)\r\nI've been a Director of various companies for 15+ years.\r\nA recent request for a DBS certificate also shows I've never committed,\r\nbeen suspected of, charged with, or arrested for a crime.\r\nI've also never been bankrupt. And I served in Iraq and I left the military\r\nwith honours.\r\nSo please trust what I have to say to you today. It's serious and true.\r\n\r\nIn 2013, my 36-day-old son, with my ex partner, was abducted from my home\r\nin Stockeld Park, Leeds. I have never seen him since.\r\nInstead of assisting, the UK Government attempted to suppress it and bury\r\nme with the truth.\r\n\r\nIf you act like my enemy, you are my enemy.\r\nSo I hired private military security (US Marine Lieutenant Colonel Curtis\r\nVan Sant and British Airforce MP Leon Allen) to push back,\r\ntreating the UK Government no differently to other child snatching\r\nterrorist groups like the Taliban or ISIS.\r\nWith my expertise in military cyber warfare, I evaded corrupt police kidnap\r\nand obtained video evidence.\r\nVideo evidence of my abducted son in a ritual, conducted shortly after his\r\nabduction - I got this from 4,000 miles away.\r\n\r\nThen in 2015 Police called, but refused to just say how or where my\r\nabducted son was.\r\nThey not only spent the whole call trying to get me to purger myself and\r\ngive away my location,\r\nBut it was revealed from the call recording - a plot was in motion to try\r\nto frame me for terrorism (as to abuse terrorism law powers) to extradite\r\nand silence me.\r\nHere's some of that evidence: https://docsend.com/view/s/6mtvrameqkqzja78\r\n\r\nI spent eight years in exile all together - gathering evidence of these\r\nsick corrupt people in the UK Regime,\r\ngetting to them without them being able to get to me. Neither I, nor the\r\ncorrupt UK Regime are backing down.\r\nAgents in ski masks even raided a friend's police station in Derby,\r\nsnatching his phone, attempting to read our messages.\r\n\r\nToday - 12+ years later, I still have no proof-of-life of knowledge of the\r\nfate of my son. He remains abducted and missing.\r\nThe UK Government likely knows the truth, but is either gagged or too\r\nspineless to disclose it.\r\nI've been left waiting and hoping, like Madeleine McCann's parents.\r\nBut this terrorist organisation we call the UK - has the audacity, aplomb\r\nand nerve to keep up its sadism - even after I exposed it.\r\nLike it's still plotting to get away with silencing me and covering up\r\ncrimes against mine and my son's humanity.\r\n\r\nThe Otley-based family cult, responsible for rituals on my son (and other\r\nchildren in their care before my son) was caught harming another child.\r\nThis cult operated freely for years while I was in exile trying to stay\r\nfree and alive, specifically due to the cover-up efforts and all the\r\ncorrupt people on their payroll.\r\nSo other children and people have been harmed as a direct result of my\r\nchild's abductors, abusers and captors not ending up behind bars.\r\n\r\nStill no investigation seems to have happened, just ongoing attempts to\r\nsuppress the truth.\r\n(not even a witness statement taken, from the witness at my home the day of\r\nmy son's abduction).\r\nMy military community all now knows the truth, but the police appear beyond\r\ncorrupt, negligent, or incompetent.\r\nI don't know why I went into exile, I should have just stayed in Britain\r\nwith my private military security contractors and executed a coup or civil\r\nwar.\r\nHad I done that, I'd have actually made sure my son's fate was determined,\r\nhis abusers punished and the negligent, incompetent, corrupt UK Government\r\nwould have surely been pushed off a cliff and at the bottom of the sea\r\nwhere it belongs by now.  My mistake was trusting my own government was my\r\nally - not our enemy as it transpired to be.\r\nI thought it would serve and defend me and my son, as I once served and\r\ndefended it in uniform. What a circus UK Government is.\r\n\r\nIn any case I consider the exposure of crimes committed against other\r\nchildren other than my son,\r\nafter they finished with my son (because police were too busy covering up\r\ntheir crimes than jailing them), testament enough that I was exonerated,\r\nSo in 2022 I returned to Britain.\r\nUpon returning from exile, I was treated with silent respect by some. Like\r\nthe stakes remain high, with enemies everywhere.\r\nFrom 2022 until mid last year, I worked under the Welsh Government's Vale\r\nof Glamorgan Direct Payments Scheme doing adult care.\r\n\r\nGiven these circumstances, including the added addition of the unlawful\r\ntheft of land (BP vs Buckler 1987) and theft of my first house,\r\nI view the UK Government and its loyalists as a terrorist organisation\r\noccupying Britain. Which just keeps raping and pillaging my families.\r\n\r\nI didn't leave exile for Britain after exoneration. I actually flew to\r\nAmerica.\r\nI mainly returned to Britain from America in 2022, because my nan was\r\ndying; And she passed away last year. I also consider that a genocide by\r\nthe UK Regime.\r\nFor all the reasons above I keep myself, my wife, child, dog, and assets as\r\nfar from Britain as possible until significant change occurs.\r\nAnd consider us now in a state of civil war.\r\n\r\nAnd no. My daughter is a British Subject, but no I will not be registering\r\nher into the UK Regime.\r\nI never even gave consent for the UK Regime to govern my son - it was done\r\nby way of abduction and enslavement.\r\nAnd I do not give my consent for the UK to govern my daughter.\r\nIt's why I keep her far from Britain or being able to be abducted and\r\nenslaved, like was done to my son.\r\n\r\nI'm writing all this today because I live and breathe what I'm disclosing,\r\nso please don't belittle or reduce all this down to military and legal\r\nrhetoric.\r\nChatGPT tells me there's a solid legal basis for calling out the UK\r\nGovernment as being a terrorist organisation that's annihilating our\r\nfreedom and sovereignty.\r\nRead more here:\r\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1xtP15riHMWHEfc4Zn3MEMmY2-7kEUFVFQuAgTS983ms\r\n\r\nMost notably the UK Home Offices FormRN no longer allows a renouncing UK\r\ncitizen to revert back to a free human and/or sovereign British subject, as\r\nwe were at birth (prior to registration into UK Society). The only option\r\nis transfer to another regime, effectively constituting this being\r\nentrapment, enslavement and human trafficking.\r\nThe aforementioned changes, made discreetly without a vote, eradicates our\r\nfreedom and sovereignty.\r\n\r\nI've filed formal complaints, reported all this to my old (and now new) MP,\r\nbut the Home Office ignores them.\r\nI'm even raising all this with the international human rights and amity\r\ninternational now.\r\nThe UK Regime appears to largely consist of corrupt terrorists, spineless\r\nor silent cowards or people too heavily indoctrinated or occupied to\r\nperform their function of government.\r\nWithout reinstating the ability to renounce citizenship, the UK Government\r\nis engaging in enslavement, exploitation, and human trafficking, akin to\r\nISIS or the Taliban.\r\nRestoring this check and balance is essential to prevent further war crimes\r\nand human rights violations.\r\nThe 1801 Act of Union, albeit established by a 24-year-old prime minister,\r\nwas designed with this check/ balance in mind - And its removal is\r\ndevastating.\r\n\r\nThe UK Government is not only evolving into a terrorist organisation in my\r\nestimation, but foreign interests and control is increasing - making this\r\nan urgent national security matter in my estimation too. The right of free\r\npeople to join at will (or waiver the benefits and leave), must be restored\r\nto prevent enslavement and unlawful detainment/ human trafficking.\r\nWithout restoration of mutual agreement, this trespass on our freedom and\r\nsovereignty that's occurring, will further decimate the people, union and\r\ncountry.\r\n\r\nFeel free to email me back or call and leave a voice message.\r\nI check into my voicemail when I'm able.\r\n\r\nSion Buckler\r\nFounder & CEO\r\nDATRO Security Group\r\n[redacted]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-a792806f","subject":"Subject FOI location access to historical court records grea","name":"0000-00-00_subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-court-records-grea_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-court-records-grea_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-court-records-grea","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_subject-foi-location-access-to-historical-court-records-grea_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Please advise on the current location and access options for records of\r\nproceedings involving Great House Farm, Mary Williams/Buckler/Western\r\nGround Rents/BP (1915 eviction attempt, 1955/1962 possession orders). Focus\r\non title/equitable interest evidence.\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Ret'd Sgt\r\n"},{"id":"wb-e2787d4d","subject":"Subject freedom of information request Tŷ Mawr great house l","name":"0000-00-00_subject-freedom-of-information-request-ty-mawr-great-house-l_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"FOI / EIR correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_subject-freedom-of-information-request-ty-mawr-great-house-l_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"subject-freedom-of-information-request-t-mawr-great-house-l","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_subject-freedom-of-information-request-ty-mawr-great-house-l_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Madam,\r\n\r\nI understand you may already be busy, so please don't feel overwhelmed by\r\nthis FOI request—I'm conducting my own diligence and happy for you to take\r\nthe full statutory 20 working days to respond.\r\n\r\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000, I request copies of all records,\r\ncorrespondence, memoranda, internal notes, minutes, file notes, land\r\nregistration applications, objections, or communications held by HM Land\r\nRegistry from 1 January 1938 to 31 December 1987 relating to:Ty Mawr (Great\r\nHouse), Llandough, near Penarth, South Glamorgan (also known as Great House\r\nFarm).\r\n\r\nLand registration applications, title transfers, or dealings involving\r\nMountjoy Ltd, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Pension Trust Ltd, and/or BP\r\nProperties Ltd (including the 1938 auction/reversion conveyance and 1969\r\nsale).\r\n\r\nInteractions, notices, proceedings, tenancy offers, licences (e.g., 1974\r\nunilateral lifetime licence letters), or disputes involving Mrs Mary\r\nWilliams (also referred to as Mrs Buckler), Mr Frederick Buckler, or\r\nWilliams/Buckler family occupiers—particularly the 1962 Cardiff County\r\nCourt possession proceedings (Dec 11 order by Judge Temple Morris QC).\r\n\r\nAny possession proceedings, adverse possession claims, or title objections\r\nconnected to the property (e.g., 1955 High Court, 1962 Cardiff County\r\nCourt, 1974 actions).\r\n\r\nPlease include archived, off-site, or scanned records where applicable.If\r\nexemptions apply (e.g., Section 40 personal data), specify which and why.\r\nIf costs exceed the appropriate limit, advise how to refine (e.g.,\r\nprioritize 1955-1987 or 1962/1974 events).\r\n\r\nI look forward to your response within 20 working days.\r\n\r\nYours faithfully,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. Sgt (Ret'd)\r\n"},{"id":"wb-5a9dd1bb","subject":"Subject research enquiry great house farm Llandough williams","name":"0000-00-00_subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams","scopeTopics":["email","ghf"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email","ghf"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Enquiries,\r\n\r\nPlease search and advise on/provide access to: Bute Estate collections,\r\nmaps, title references, family papers, or manuscripts relating to Great\r\nHouse Farm, Llandough; Daniel Thomas quarry deal/swap; John/Mary Williams\r\noccupation/ownership claims.\r\n\r\nFor generational land history and reparations research. Copies/fees welcome.\r\n\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Ret'd Sgt\r\n"},{"id":"wb-2e24c77e","subject":"Subject stage two complaint title WA231076 alleged mistake i","name":"0000-00-00_subject-stage-two-complaint-title-wa231076-alleged-mistake-i_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Land Registry correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_subject-stage-two-complaint-title-wa231076-alleged-mistake-i_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"subject-stage-two-complaint-title-wa231076-alleged-mistake-i","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_subject-stage-two-complaint-title-wa231076-alleged-mistake-i_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Subject: Stage Two Complaint – Title WA231076 – Alleged Mistake in the Register\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 19:29 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSir or Madam,\n\nI write to ask that my complaint regarding title number WA231076 (Land on\nthe North Side of Leckwith Road, Llandough) be escalated to **stage two**\nof HM Land Registry’s Complaints Procedure. This email sets out why I\nconsider the stage‑one decision to be incorrect, identifies the mistake I\nsay exists in the register, and explains the decision I seek.\n\n### 1. My core contention\n\nMy core contention is that BP Properties Limited were registered as\nproprietors on the basis of a factual and legal error regarding my\ngrandmother’s status on the land. My grandmother did not occupy under any\ngenuine licence granted to her and did not relinquish any claim. Instead,\nany licence relied on by BP related to a different name/person. As her\nheir, I have succeeded to her claim; I therefore say that registering BP as\nproprietors was a “mistake in the register” for the purposes of the Land\nRegistration Act 2002.\n\n### 2. Identity mismatch and alleged “licence”\n\nYour stage‑one letter records that HM Land Registry relies on the Court of\nAppeal decision in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler  EWCA Civ 2, and treats my\ngrandmother as having occupied under a licence granted by the documentary\ntitle holder, so that her possession was no longer adverse.\n\nHowever, the alleged licence and related correspondence did not use my\ngrandmother’s true legal name. My grandmother was Mrs Williams (supported\nby her birth, marriage and death certificates), not “Mrs Buckler”. The\n“licensee” referred to in BP’s narrative and in the 1987 litigation is\ntherefore not the same legal person as my grandmother. There is, in other\nwords, a fundamental mis‑identification or identity fraud at the heart of\nthe story that HM Land Registry and the Court have relied upon.\n\nIf the licence relied on by BP was addressed to, or granted in respect of,\na different named individual, it cannot properly be said that my\ngrandmother’s occupation was under that licence. In that case her\noccupation remained adverse to BP’s paper title, and any finding that she\nwas a “licensee” rests on a factual premise that is demonstrably wrong.\n\n### 3. Timing – “cart before the horse”\n\nYour letter explains that the applications for first registration of\nWA231076 (and the related title WA240304) were made in 1982–83 and that BP\ndemonstrated a documentary root of title back to 1969/1975 by way of\nconveyances and a 1971 abstract of title.\n\nYou also confirm that the Court of Appeal only gave its decision in BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler in 1987, holding that an offer by BP to let my\ngrandmother remain created a licence and brought her adverse possession to\nan end.\n\nThis highlights a fundamental sequencing problem:\n\n- At the date of first registration (1982–83), whether there was a valid\nlicence capable of defeating my grandmother’s adverse possession was a\nlive, unresolved dispute.\n- BP nevertheless presented themselves as entitled to be registered as\nproprietors and their solicitors certified on form FR1 that there was no\nquestion or doubt affecting the title.\n\n- HM Land Registry, relying on that certification, registered BP before any\ncourt had determined whether my grandmother’s possession had extinguished\nBP’s title.\n- Only in 1987 did the Court of Appeal retrospectively treat the alleged\nlicence as bringing adverse possession to an end, and that decision was\nitself based on the mis‑identification described above.\n\nIn simple terms, the effect of the alleged licence (if any) was judicially\ndetermined **after** first registration, and on the basis of the wrong\nperson being treated as the “licensee”. BP and their solicitors put the\ncart before the horse, and HM Land Registry accepted that position.\n\n### 4. The specific “mistake in the register”\n\nYour stage‑one response concludes that there is “no evidence of a mistake\nin the register” and therefore no power to alter the register and no right\nto indemnity. I say this is incorrect.\n\nThe mistake I allege is as follows:\n\n1. On the true facts, my grandmother’s occupation of the land was adverse\nto BP’s documentary title and was not under any valid licence granted to\nher.\n\n2. Her adverse possession had, or may have, extinguished BP’s title by the\ntime of first registration in 1982–83, meaning BP were not entitled to be\nregistered as proprietors at that time.\n\n3. HM Land Registry nevertheless registered BP as proprietors on the basis\nof:\n   - a licence attributed to the wrong person (identity error/fraud), and\n   - a solicitor’s FR1 certificate stating there was no question or doubt\naffecting title, despite a long‑running dispute and pending litigation.\n\n4. Subsequent reliance on the 1987 Court of Appeal decision does not cure\nthis, because that decision itself proceeded on the mis‑identification of\nmy grandmother and did not and could not retrospectively validate a licence\nthat never related to her.\n\nOn that analysis, the register shows BP as proprietors when, in law, my\ngrandmother’s adverse possession should have extinguished BP’s title and\ngiven rise to a transmissible proprietary interest which I, as her heir,\nnow claim. The register therefore does not accurately reflect the true\nlegal position and contains a mistake capable of rectification.\n\n### 5. Why the stage‑one reasoning is inadequate\n\nIn your stage‑one letter you state that:\n\n- HM Land Registry has an administrative function and cannot “look behind\nor challenge decisions of the Court”. [1]\n- My identity‑fraud claims are “not relevant to the issue of title to the\nland” because they relate to the dispute heard by the Court.\n\n- There is no evidence of negligence or maladministration and no evidence\nof a mistake in the register.\n\nWith respect, this reasoning is incomplete:\n\n- Once HM Land Registry is presented with clear evidence that the person\nnamed as the “licensee” in the litigation and licence documentation is not\nthe same legal person as the occupier (my grandmother), that goes directly\nto whether the Court of Appeal’s factual premise remains reliable and\nwhether the register is accurate.\n\n- Recognising that there is a serious question as to the correctness of the\nregister is not the same as “overturning” the Court of Appeal. HM Land\nRegistry has statutory powers to alter the register where there is a\nmistake, and it can, where appropriate, refer disputes about rectification\nto the tribunal or the courts.\n\n- To simply say that identity‑fraud concerns are “not relevant to title”\nis, I say, an error of law and/or an unreasonable application of policy. It\ndisregards new evidence going to the foundation of BP’s claimed entitlement.\n\n### 6. The decision and outcome I seek\n\nFor stage two, I ask that a Land Registrar (Senior Officer) reconsider the\ncomplaint and:\n\n1. Accept that the combination of:\n   - the identity mismatch (licence/name vs my grandmother’s true legal\nname), and\n   - the timing (registration in 1982–83 before the 1987 decision) gives\nrise to at least a **serious question** as to whether the register is\nmistaken in showing BP/ Companies thereafter, as proprietors.\n\n2. Treat this as evidence of a potential “mistake in the register” for the\npurposes of your alteration powers and Schedule 8, rather than as a mere\ndisagreement with the 1987 judgment.\n\n3. Either:\n\n   - (a) commence the process of rectification, recognising that my\ngrandmother’s adverse possession may have extinguished BP’s title and that\nI, as her heir, now have a claim to be registered, or\n\n   - (b) formally refer the dispute over the correctness of the register to\nthe appropriate tribunal/court, making clear that HM Land Registry\nrecognises that the identity‑fraud evidence raises a real issue about\nwhether the register is accurate.\n\n4. Confirm that, if it is ultimately determined that the register is\nmistaken and cannot be rectified without prejudice to third parties, HM\nLand Registry will treat me as having a potential claim for indemnity under\nSchedule 8.\n\nPlease also confirm any further documents you require (for example, copies\nof the licence, the BP v Buckler pleadings/judgment, and my grandmother’s\ncertificates) so that the stage‑two review can consider the identity\nevidence in full.\n\nFraud unravels all. The limitation act also had a clause for fraud.\nFurthermore any limitation begins from discovery of fraud not occurrence of\nit.\n\nThe convenient and timely death of my nan after her two obstructed attempts\nto make her case in 1974, followed by my father's convenient and timely\ndeath after his appeal of the 1987 case was dismissed and his ECHR\nobstructed, along with our forceful removal by 30 police and bailiffs in\n1988. And the press reporting us as squatters on our ancestral birthland\nsince 1667, did unlawfully dispossess and disposition us, but it doesn't\nchange the facts.\n\nI see this case as instrumental in Wales' decolonisation. Whereby us\nindigneous Welsh Nationals on our ancestral birthland are victim to a\ncrime. And I am the only one willing to speak up and out as my family of\nmostly women, are all too traumatised by this crime.\n\nIt's evident illicit profits and gains. Identity fraud. And negligence and\nincompetence. I absolutely see the Brit-ish Establishment that now occupy\nand rule through force, stealth/ secrecy and licence as terrorists and us\nyour hostages. As a direct result of this case.\n\nThis is now a hostage terrorist situation on our lands. Well, my family are\nyour hostages, I'm more of a counter officer soldier. So put it right. I\nwill not stand down.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\nRightful Squire & executor of Manon of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, Wales.\n\n\n\n\nOn Sun, 19 Apr 2026, 07:41 Wales.OfficeMail, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\n> document by post.\n>\n> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r\n> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais\n> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni\n> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n>\n> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg\n> y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y\n> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho\n> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun\n> at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir\n> EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd\n> rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>\n> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>\n> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>\n>\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-bab21111","subject":"Support for the great house farm Tŷ Mawr Llandough heritage","name":"0000-00-00_support-for-the-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-heritage_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_support-for-the-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-heritage_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"support-for-the-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-heritage","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_support-for-the-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-heritage_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"\r\n\r\nSir / Madam,\r\n\r\nI am currently developing an independent heritage research project focused \r\non the history of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, and its \r\nsurrounding landscape.\r\n\r\nThe aim of this work is to carefully bring together historical, \r\narchaeological, and documentary evidence to better understand the full \r\ntimeline of the site, and to make this information accessible to the public \r\nin a clear and engaging way. Hence website https://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n\r\nAs part of the project, I am planning:\r\n\r\n   - A detailed digital reconstruction and Augmented reality guided tour of \r\n   the Llandough site\r\n\r\n\r\n   - A public-facing archive of gathered historical evidence and \r\n   interpretations\r\n\r\n\r\n   - A physical scale model / replica of the farm, to be created in \r\n   Patagonia as part of a wider educational and cultural display\r\n\r\n\r\n   - Open public access to the findings, continuing the tradition of shared \r\n   community heritage work\r\n\r\nThe project is intended as an open heritage initiative, with the goal of \r\neducation, preservation of local history, and public engagement.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to support this work, donations can be made directly \r\nthrough the website:\r\n*[insert your website link here]*\r\n\r\nAll contributions will go toward research, digitisation of records, \r\nmodelling work, and public presentation of the findings.\r\n\r\nI appreciate any support you are able to offer and welcome anyone \r\ninterested in the history of Llandough and the wider area to follow the \r\nproject as it develops.\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n\r\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sgt)\r\n\r\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n\r\n\r\n"},{"id":"wb-99afb156","subject":"Thank you for reaching out re BP v Buckler 1987 documentary","name":"0000-00-00_thank-you-for-reaching-out-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_thank-you-for-reaching-out-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"thank-you-for-reaching-out-re-bp-v-buckler-1987-documentary","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_thank-you-for-reaching-out-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata