le=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><a href=\"[email redacted] style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\">[email redacted]</a><br><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Learn more about our program opportunities <a href=\"https://www.sundance.org/programs/documentary-film/\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/meips/ADKq_NaDzI0Wq6BixWrqZ6cBDnEa_gJKduSRw1QPX7IgohedRrQFIDlFh4y9fTvmzeD6Ihqgh2cqh2hAe6oKfO0sYidZ7fM2WMRfUlSw9-djLXlzqS-FZQm95CXPL56dJEFFGjNhDPn3GeVsgb1YhA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://www.sundance.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/SFF26_EmailSignature-MID-REZ-2.png\"><br></div></div><br/>\n"},{"id":"wb-fba0c99c","subject":"Thank you for your email re BP v Buckler 1987 documentary","name":"0000-00-00_thank-you-for-your-email-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_thank-you-for-your-email-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"thank-you-for-your-email-re-bp-v-buckler-1987-documentary","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_thank-you-for-your-email-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Thank you for your email Re: BP vs Buckler 1987 - Documentary\nFrom: Hello You\nDate: Tue, 28 Oct 2025 23:05 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Sender,\n\nThank you for getting in touch with us here at Doc Society!\n\nUnfortunately, we are unable to respond personally to your email. Due\nto the high number of enquiries we receive, we cannot accept proposals\nor watch content that has not been submitted through the official\napplication process. We do not engage in partnerships with studios or\nproduction companies for commissioned content creation. Please find\nkey information below on our programmes, funds and resources available\nto documentary filmmakers.\n\nWe recommend that you register for our monthly newsletter for\nup-to-date news and fund opening dates. Sign up at the bottom of this\npage: http://www.docsociety.org/#mailout\n\n\nOur Funds\nEach fund is listed on our website and details how to apply, the\ncriteria, and fund opening dates. All up-to-date information can be\nfound on these linked below. If you have completed an application and\nhave a question, please use the messaging tool in the application\nsystem. It’s easy and will likely get a faster response from us! Visit\nhttps://app.docsociety.org. Login with your credentials (your user\nname is your email). Once you are logged in, scroll down the page\nuntil you find your application module. Click on the Send Message\nbutton. Write to us! We will respond as soon as possible:\n\nThe BFI Doc Society Fund (for UK feature documentaries) - CLOSED for\nDocumentary Feature Film Applications, OPEN for Immersive non fiction,\nInformation on how to apply https://bfi.docsociety.org/bfi-doc-features/\n\nThe BFI Research and Development (RAD) Fund - CLOSED-\nFor early development of documentary and immersive projects for\ndirectors and producers based in the UK.\nhttps://bfi.docsociety.org/bfi-doc-rad/\n\nThe Climate Story Fund - CLOSED\nhttps://climatestoryfund.org/apply/\n\nBFI Made of Truth fund for short documentaries is now - CLOSED\nhttps://bfi.docsociety.org/bfi-doc-shorts/\n\nBig Tech Narrative Initiative Showcase CLOSED\nhttps://democracystoryunit.org/big-tech/\n\nThe Threshold Fund, European Documentary Journalism Fund, New\nPerspectives Fellowship, BFI Ripple Effect Fund, BFI Doc Society\nProduction Fund SOS, Bertha Journalism Fund, Genesis Fund and Circle\nFund are no longer active funds within Doc Society and will not\nreopen.\n\nFind out more about the projects we’ve supported in the past here:\nhttps://docsociety.org/films/\n\nGood Pitch\nGot a project in the making with strong social impact goals? Find out\nall about our global\nGood Pitch and Good Pitch Local events and programmes\nhttps://goodpitch.org/\n\nGIPA\nLearn more about the Global Impact Producers Alliance here.\nhttps://globalimpactproducers.org/\n\nFollow Us\nRegularly check in on Doc Society social media for other opportunities\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/TheDocSociety\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/thedocsociety\n\n\nThank you for keeping in touch and for keeping our storytelling ecosystem going,\nDoc Society\n\n-- \nFollow us on social media and subscribe to our *newsletter\n<https://docsociety.org/#mailout>* for the latest Doc Society updates,\nindustry news, events and fund opportunities:\nTwitter <http://twitter.com/TheDocSociety> | Facebook\n<http://facebook.com/TheDocSociety> | Instagram\n<https://www.instagram.com/thedocsociety/>\n\n<http://www.docsociety.org>\n\nThe people formerly known as BRITDOC\nWondering why are we using a new name?  <https://docsociety.org/docsociety/>\n"},{"id":"wb-4cf7fe5d","subject":"Thanks for reaching out re BP v Buckler 1987 documentary","name":"0000-00-00_thanks-for-reaching-out-re-bp-vs-buckler-1987-documentary_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateS