>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<img src=\"https://customervoice.microsoft.com/eur/dist/api/invite/outbound/wRKV-Z_9dUSYlpoLPNxQ7DzjL1w_oLhGkn_gR9vKBGRUNTJYMTUzQkNFSkZZNUVMQkRHVTFWTUJCMy4u/5c2fe33c-a03f-46b8-927f-e047dbca0464/f99512c1-fd9f-4475-9896-9a0b3cdc50ec/77c69bab-4500-48dc-a8da-bd4b87b67a2f/GBR/370cdb98-f6f4-4c08-89aa-01e33d21cd07/amwyUG9ZeGlsbEZTVmhkclRPZ0piS1FwbmIyNzRWOTJEa0VUcEdkbkU9/0/639077945290000000\" alt=\"\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" border=\"0\" style=\"height:1px !important;width:1px !important;border-width:0 !important;margin-top:0 !important;margin-bottom:0 !important;margin-right:0 !important;margin-left:0 !important;padding-top:0 !important;padding-bottom:0 !important;padding-right:0 !important;padding-left:0 !important;\">"},{"id":"wb-2fcb0123","subject":"The williams family marconi farm ymholiad cofnodion teulu te","name":"0000-00-00_the-williams-family-marconi-farm-ymholiad-cofnodion-teulu-te_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_the-williams-family-marconi-farm-ymholiad-cofnodion-teulu-te_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"the-williams-family-marconi-farm-ymholiad-cofnodion-teulu-te","scopeTopics":["family"],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":["family"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_the-williams-family-marconi-farm-ymholiad-cofnodion-teulu-te_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"Welsh (Cymraeg)\r\n\r\n*Annwyl Bugeiliaid a Chyfeillion,*\r\n\r\nRwyf yn ysgrifennu atoch i ofyn am eich cymorth. Cyrhaeddais Puerto Madryn\r\ny llynedd gyda’r nod o ailadeiladu fferm fy nheulu, y teulu Williams.\r\n\r\nRoedd y fferm hon yn eiddo i ni ers 1667, ac roedd yn safle hanesyddol lle\r\nbu Marconi yn dyfeisio’r radio. Yn anffodus, cawsom ein troi allan ym 1988\r\ngan BP, sydd bellach wedi adeiladu tai ar ein tir. Rydym bellach wedi\r\ndatgelu twyll a chelach o ran y digwyddiadau hyn. Mae ein cyfreithiwr\r\nwrthi’n cychwyn achos cyfreithiol i ddarparu iawndal o £200 miliwn am ein\r\ndiarddel o’r tir.\r\n\r\nRwyf yn chwilio am unrhyw gofnodion, tystysgrifau, neu wybodaeth yn eich\r\narchifau a allai gadarnhau ein llinach a'n hawl i’r tir hwn. Mae hwn yn\r\nfater o gyfiawnder i’r teulu cyn i’r genhedlaeth hon basio draw.\r\n\r\nDiolch yn fawr am eich help.\r\n\r\n*Yn gywir,* *Bob [Your Surname]*\r\n------------------------------\r\nSpanish (Español)\r\n\r\n*Estimados Pastores y Amigos:*\r\n\r\nLes escribo para solicitar su ayuda. Llegué a Puerto Madryn el año pasado\r\ncon el objetivo de reconstruir la granja de mi familia, la familia Williams.\r\n\r\nEsta granja fue nuestra propiedad y ocupación desde 1667, y fue el sitio\r\nhistórico donde Marconi inventó la radio. Lamentablemente, fuimos\r\ndesalojados en 1988 por la empresa BP, que posteriormente construyó\r\nviviendas en nuestras tierras. Hemos expuesto el fraude y el ocultamiento\r\ndetrás de este caso. Nuestro abogado está iniciando procedimientos legales\r\npara demandar por 200 millones de libras por desposesión.\r\n\r\nBusco cualquier registro, certificado o información en sus archivos que\r\npueda confirmar nuestro linaje y nuestro derecho a estas tierras. Este es\r\nun acto de justicia para nuestra familia antes de que sea demasiado tarde\r\npara nuestros mayores.\r\n\r\nMuchas gracias por su tiempo y colaboración.\r\n\r\n*Atentamente,*\r\nSion Hywel Buckler\r\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\r\n[redacted]\r\n[redacted]\r\n\r\n[image: 492340134_122193631400112242_6487893391323682583_n.jpg][image:\r\n492889702_122193631334112242_8056921153707903085_n.jpg]\r\n"},{"id":"wb-b9acd093","subject":"Title fraud and procedural concealment church view close lla","name":"0000-00-00_title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-church-view-close-lla_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-church-view-close-lla_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-church-view-close-lla","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_title-fraud-and-procedural-concealment-church-view-close-lla_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Title Fraud and Procedural Concealment – Church View Close, Llandough (formerly Great House Farm/ \"Ty Mawr\")\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Mon, 16 Feb 2026 17:31 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCouncillor Carroll & co,\n\nI write regarding potential gaps in the Council's planning and\nrecord-keeping processes relating to Great House Farm, Llandough, which was\ndemolished in 1988 following the 1987 Court of Appeal decision in BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler.\n\nRecent evidence suggests the Council may wish to examine its own position\non this matter, as it raises questions about procedural compliance and\nrecord integrity that could expose the authority to wider scrutiny.\n\nCORE ISSUES\n\n**1. Identity and Procedural Integrity**\n\nThe 1987 judgment turned on a 1974 licence addressed to \"Mrs Buckler\". My\ngrandmother, Mary Williams, did not use or accept this designation.\nContemporaneous evidence (1978 newspaper article attached) records her\nasserting ownership under her correct name.\n\nIf the 1987 court was not presented with this evidence, the judgment may\nrest on an incomplete factual record. This raises procedural fairness\nconcerns relevant to any future review of the decision.\n\n**2. Heritage Information and Statutory Compliance**\n\nThe site's archaeological significance was documented by 1978 (Roman\nburials, monastic associations). Yet professional excavations in 1994\nrevealed 1,026 early medieval burials and monastic structures—findings that\nshould have prompted evaluation under the Ancient Monuments and\nArchaeological Areas Act 1979.\n\nCritical question: Did the Council conduct or require prior archaeological\nassessment before granting permissions to demolish? If not, this represents\na potential gap in statutory process that may affect the validity of the\npermissions granted.\n\n**3. Land Registry Disclosure**\n\nBP registered title in 1982 based on the disputed licence. The Council\nshould establish:\n- Whether any dispute notice or heritage caution was lodged;\n- Whether the Council disclosed relevant heritage information to the Land\nRegistry;\n- What planning records exist from 1978–1988 regarding the site's known\narchaeological potential.\n\n**4. Corporate Identity Inconsistency**\n\nDuring my father's appeal, the court treated BP Properties Ltd and BP\nPension Trust Ltd inconsistently—as separate entities when convenient, then\nas one when dismissing his claim. This raises questions about how\nthoroughly the litigation was scrutinised and whether the Council's records\nreflect this uncertainty.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS TO THE COUNCIL\n\nThese issues go beyond a single historical dispute. They touch on:\n\n- **Planning record integrity**: Whether heritage information was\nadequately documented and acted upon;\n- **Procedural compliance**: Whether statutory protections (Ancient\nMonuments Act) were properly applied;\n- **Institutional liability**: Whether decisions were made on incomplete or\nmisleading information;\n- **Precedent risk**: Whether similar vulnerabilities may exist in other\nhistorical planning decisions.\n\nREQUESTS\n\nI ask the Council to:\n\n1. **Commission a review** of the planning permissions granted between\n1978–1988 for Great House Farm, specifically examining what heritage and\narchaeological information was available to decision-makers and how it was\nhandled.\n\n2. **Refer this matter to the Monitoring Officer** for examination of\nprocedural compliance and record integrity.\n\n3. **Establish** what correspondence, cautions, or dispute notices exist in\nrelation to this site's title or heritage status.\n\n4. **Clarify the Council's current protocol** for handling historical title\ndisputes, previously unknown heritage information, or allegations of\nmaterial non-disclosure in past planning processes—to prevent recurrence.\n\nI am not asking the Council to reverse the 1987 judgment or disturb current\nresidents. I am asking it to ensure its own records are accurate and its\nown processes are defensible.\n\nI attach the 1978 article and supporting documents, and am available to\nmeet or provide further information.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nSion Buckler, Sgt (Ret'd)\nExecutor for the Manor of Llandough\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-e4305369","subject":"Tŷ Mawr casa grande Llandough gales","name":"0000-00-00_ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"t-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_ty-mawr-casa-grande-llandough-gales_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Tŷ Mawr (Casa Grande), Llandough, Gales\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 02 Jun 2026 05:08 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nA la atención del Ministerio del Interior de la Nación:\nMe dirijo a usted con el propósito de solicitar formalmente mi radicación\nen la región de la Patagonia y presentar una petición para la concesión de\ntierras destinadas a un proyecto de preservación histórica y cultural.\nActualmente me encuentro en territorio argentino tras haber sido desposeído\ny exiliado de mi hogar solariego de 800 años de antigüedad ubicado en\nLlandough, Gales. Si bien la propiedad de la tierra sigue bajo disputa\nlegal debido a alegaciones de fraude, el Estado británico tomó posesión de\nlos terrenos y demolió la residencia señorial de 10 habitaciones antes de\nque se pudieran aplicar las debidas protecciones patrimoniales. Denuncio\npúblicamente que el Estado británico continúa suprimiendo nuestra herencia\ny ocupando tierras robadas.\nMi intención es establecerme definitivamente en la Patagonia y reconstruir\nuna réplica exacta de dicha residencia de 10 habitaciones. Este espacio\nfuncionará como un museo abierto al público para celebrar la cultura galesa\ny conmemorar un hito histórico de gran relevancia: la estancia de Guglielmo\nMarconi en nuestra propiedad original mientras realizaba los experimentos\nque llevaron a la invención de la radio.\nPor lo tanto, solicito formalmente que se me otorguen tierras de una\nextensión equivalente a la propiedad original en Llandough, con la\nautorización legal para bautizar este nuevo asentamiento con el nombre de\nLlandough.\nQuedo a su entera disposición para presentar la documentación\ncorrespondiente.\nAtentamente,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁷󠁬󠁳󠁿\nEr sylw Gweinidogaeth y Materion Mewnol:\nYsgrifennaf atoch er mwyn gwneud cais ffurfiol i ymsefydlu yn rhanbarth\nPatagonia ac i gyflwyno cais am ddarn o dir ar gyfer prosiect i warchod\nhanes a threftadaeth.\nRwyf ar hyn o bryd yn yr Ariannin ar ôl cael fy niarddel a mynd i alltud\no'm cartref maenoraidd 800 oed yn Llandochau (Llandough), Cymru. Er bod\nperchnogaeth y tir yn dal i gael ei herio'n gyfreithiol oherwydd honiadau o\ndwyll, cymerodd y wladwriaeth Brydeinig feddiant o'r safle a dymchwel y tŷ\nmaenor 10 ystafell wely cyn y gellid gweithredu amddiffyniadau treftadaeth\npriodol. Rwyf yn honni bod y wladwriaeth Brydeinig yn parhau i sipresio ein\ntreftadaeth tra eu bod yn meddiannu ein tir a ddygwyd oddi arnom.\nFy mwriad yw setlo'n barhaol ym Mhatagonia ac adeiladu replica union o'r tŷ\nmaenor 10 ystafell wely hwnnw. Bydd y lle hwn yn gweithredu fel amgueddfa\nagored i'r cyhoedd i ddathlu diwylliant Cymru ac i goffau carreg filltir\nhanesyddol o bwys mawr: cyfnod Guglielmo Marconi yn aros gyda ni yn ein\ncartref gwreiddiol tra ei fod yn dyfeisio'r radio.\nFelly, rwyf yn gofyn yn ffurfiol i chi roi tir i mi sydd yr un maint â'r\nsafle gwreiddiol yn Llandochau, ac i gael yr awdurdod cyfreithiol i enwi'r\nsafle hwn yn Llandochau.\nRwyf yn parhau i fod ar gael i gyflwyno'r dogfennau perthnasol.\nYn gywir,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿🏴󠁧󠁢󠁥󠁮󠁧󠁿\nFor the attention of the Ministry of the Interior:\nI am writing to you to formally request residency in the Patagonia region\nand to submit a petition for a land concession dedicated to a historical\nand cultural preservation project.\nI am currently located within Argentine territory after being dispossessed\nand exiled from my 800-year-old manorial home in Llandough, Wales. While\nthe ownership of the land remains under legal dispute due to my allegations\nof fraud and abuse of power, the British state took possession of the\nproperty and demolished the 10-bedroom manor house before proper heritage\nprotections could be applied. I publicly allege that the British state\ncontinues to suppress our heritage while they occupy our stolen land.\nMy intention is to settle permanently in Patagonia and rebuild an exact\nreplica of that 10-bedroom manorial residence. This space will operate as a\nmuseum open to the public to celebrate Welsh culture and commemorate a\nhistorical milestone of great relevance: the period when Guglielmo Marconi\nstayed with us at our original property while conducting the experiments\nthat led to the invention of the radio.\nTherefore, I formally request that I be granted land of an equivalent size\nto the original property in Llandough, along with the legal authority to\nname this new settlement Llandough.\nI remain entirely at your disposal to submit all corresponding\ndocumentation.\nSincerely,\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz https://wa.me/5491176322115\n"},{"id":"wb-8a7641b0","subject":"Undeliverable BP v Buckler great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_undeliverable-bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_undeliverable-bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","threadSlug":"undeliverable-bp-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_undeliverable-bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[https://products.office.com/en-us/CMSImages/Office365Logo_Orange.png?version=b8d100a9-0a8b-8e6a-88e1-ef488fee0470]\r\nYour message to Correspondence.Jack.Sargeant@gov.wales couldn't be delivered.\r\nCorrespondence.Jack.Sargeant wasn't found at gov.wales.\r\n[redacted]  Office 365      Correspondence.Jack.. . .\r\nAction Required                 Recipient\r\nUnknown To address\r\n\r\nHow to Fix It\r\nThe address may be misspelled or may not exist. Try one or more of the following:\r\n\r\n  *   Send the message again following these steps: In Outlook, open this non-delivery report (NDR) and choose Send Again from the Report ribbon. In Outlook on the web, select this NDR, then select the lin