ification to ensure my\nunderstanding of the record set is accurate before any further request is\nmade under statutory access routes.\n\nI am seeking confirmation of the composition and scope of the first\nregistration file(s), specifically what material is held, recorded, or\nidentifiable as forming part of the application record at the time of\nregistration.\n\nTo avoid duplication or misunderstanding, could you please confirm the\nfollowing factual points only in relation to the actual file contents held\nby HM Land Registry:\nWhether a complete first registration application file is still held for\nWA231076 and WA240304, including any supporting bundle of documents\nsubmitted at the time of registration.\n\nWhether the file(s) include an index, schedule, or equivalent record\nidentifying the documents that formed part of the application (whether\nretained or not retained).\n\nWhether the file(s) contain any recorded material of any kind (including\ncorrespondence, requisitions, internal notes, or annotations) relating to\nany dispute, objection, or competing claim concerning the property known as\nGreat House Farm / Ty Mawr.\n\nWhether the file(s) contain any notation indicating that documents were\n“not retained”, “copy filed”, or otherwise recorded as not forming part of\nthe permanent archive.\n\nThis request is limited strictly to confirmation of the existence and scope\nof records held, rather than a request for reassessment of historical\nmatters or legal conclusions.\n\nI would be grateful if this clarification can be provided so that any\nsubsequent FOI or inspection request can be properly scoped to the actual\nrecords held.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nSion Buckler Esq. (Ret’d Sergeant)\nHeir & Successor to Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of\nGlamorgan C/O [address redacted] [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n\nOn Tue, 2 Jun 2026, 01:56 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am writing to request clarification regarding first registration files\n> relating to title WA231076 and WA240304.\n>\n> This request is not a complaint, request for reconsideration, or\n> application for rectification. I am seeking only clarification of the\n> documents and records held on the first registration file(s), and the\n> material relied upon in the registration process.\n>\n> Please confirm and/or provide the following:\n>\n> The full list of documents and evidence held on the first registration\n> file(s) for WA231076 and WA240304, including the application form (FR1),\n> transfer/conveyance deed(s), and any supporting abstract, epitome, or\n> statement of title.\n>\n> Whether any requisitions, objections, cautions, notices, or third-party\n> claims were received or recorded during the first registration process.\n>\n> Whether the file contains any correspondence, notes, or other documents of\n> any description referring to a dispute, competing claim, or challenge\n> concerning Mary Williams / Mary Buckler or Great House Farm / Ty Mawr.\n>\n> Whether any personal documents (including but not limited to identity,\n> marital, or probate records) relating to Mary Williams / Mary Buckler were\n> submitted as part of the application or retained on file, and if so whether\n> they were relied upon in the registration decision.\n>\n> A schedule or index of the documentary evidence relied upon to support\n> first registration, including any statement that copies were not retained\n> or are no longer held.\n>\n> Whether any document referred to in the registration process is noted as\n> “copy filed”, “not retained”, or similarly annotated.\n>\n> If this request is not the appropriate route for access to the above\n> material, please advise on the correct procedure for inspection or\n> obtaining copies of the first registration file contents.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant)\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-62518fe3","subject":"Your ref edd our ref WA231076 a 216 ct","name":"0000-00-00_your-ref-edd-o