assification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-18018267","subject":"BP v Buckler 1987","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-1987_en_v0.0.0.00-6.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: BP vs Buckler 1987\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:32 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSirs,\n\nI discovered fraud and concealment in landmark legal case BP vs Buckler\n1987. I believe my case is not unique or restricted to me and my family.\n\nThe courts and BP awarded themselves possession of our land in their\ncourts. We maintain we own the land.\n\nMy pregnant mum, other infant brother and sister and terminally ill dad\nwere dragged out of our 800 year old home. The first time we'd been out of\nour home as a family since the 16th century. And it was demolished in front\nof us. In fact, demolition began while we were still in it.\n\nMy MP or local councillor wont reply to my discovery of fraud and\nconcealment. After being caught in a lie and admitting destroying evidence\nCADW are now all on holiday. The council clerk took his retirement. South\nWales police deny holding records and want to speak not email. I left them\nmy phone number to my voicemail. Nothing left. The council didn't reply to\ntheir own deadline to respond to my FOI. There's a lot of gatekeeping. Last\nweek for the third time my sister has tried to visit archieves to see\nrecords and is rail roaded each time. My brother is now flying from ireland\nto try to view records for a 4th time.\n\nI believe what has occured in our case and others. Is that ownership\ndisputes of land were manufactures. Our title deeds went missing from our\nhome, so too did a public library copy. The courts then shelved the\nownership dispute and awarded possession. This is where BP and their deep\npockets and lawfare all went to work. My disabled widowed nan didn't stand\na chance. But she fought well for decades.\n\nThe scandal here is huge because it was a matter of public interest then,\nits a matter of national history and herritage too. Marconi stayed in our\nhome while inventing radio. There were 1,026 burials exhivated and moved\nduring housing development. The site sits on a monestry and roman villa.\nAll covered up in lieu of 20 houses. Peerless Jim world champion boxer also\nfought his first fight in our barns.\n\nI'll try to publish all my findings:\nhttps://youtube.com/@sionbuckler5713?si=KLtcTMB8CWZuu0Hq\n\nFraud unravels all. And the statute of limitation is on discovery, not\noccurance of fraud. So while many of us find our lands occupied via\npossession, even from birth, we may own the land. And land registry call it\na \"mistake\" we're not on our own land records. But its no mistake. They\nlooked the other way in our case. In conjunction with BP concealing\ninformation.\n\nI actually think the Senedd should do a public enquiry into this erazure of\nour history and herritage and denial and existence of it. They almost got\naway with this too. ITV quietly declassified some footage onto YouTube\narchieves a few months ago. But the damage is done. The cover up attempt\nhas been ongoing for decades. And is still ongoing by the looks of it.\n\nOur family got thrown into the street. To live in a caravan. No trauma\ncouncilling. No after support. No reporations. ECHR (Buckler vs United\nKingdom) was deniel in lieu of BP's rights. They literally broke our\npregnant mums shoulder. BP bailiffs appear to have been under cover\nmilitary. My dad convenieny died prior to housing development approval on\nour stolen land. My nan conveniently died in the 2 weeks she had to\nchallenge BP registering our land in their names at the land registry in\n1983.\n\nI am a former Signals cyber and electronic warfare professional. I'm\ncurrently at the welsh Settlement in South Argentina where they celebrate\nour culture and history. I'm attempting to rebuild our home here. The\nethnic cleansing just gets worse and worse back there. My last employer was\nthe Vale of Glamorgan/ Welsh Govenrment too, up until 2024.\n\nI just thought I'd let you all know. Find your ancestral birthland.\nIdentify the way in which we were dispossessed, after ownership dispute\narising. Identify the fraud/ consealment/ hybrid warfare. Fraud unravels\nall.\n\nThis is how indigenous britons on our ancestral birthland make another\nstand. And a worthwhile one. I also say this as a bona fide military\ncommander and leader. In Cyprus the Turks and Greeks would return with\norigional deeds to land and reclaim it. And the UN would have to give up\nits possession of that land. It's practically a loophole to decolonise in\nUK.\n\nRegards,\n\nSion Buckler\n[phone redacted]\n"},{"id":"wb-12a809c6","subject":"BP v Buckler great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-b1027465","subject":"BP v Buckler great house farm Llandough","name":"0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","threadSlug":"bp-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"related-case-source","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","classifica