-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Case correspondence / related source","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-fw-manor-of-llandough-mdr-entries_en_v0.0.0.00-5.txt","threadSlug":"fw-manor-of-llandough-mdr-entries","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-fw-manor-of-llandough-mdr-entries_en_v0.0.0.00-5.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-6c467061","subject":"Re great house farm church view close Llandough nr penarth v","name":"0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (ATISN 27021)\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:03 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHi Mike,\n\nAppreciate the reply.\n\nI kindly request an internal review of the response provided under ATISN\n27021.\n\nI am grateful for the release of the two inspection photographs dated 29\nJuly 1988. However, I am not satisfied that the searches undertaken were\nsufficient to establish that no other relevant records are held or can be\naccounted for.\n\nThe response states that Great House Farm was visited and assessed for\nlisting by Cadw inspectors, but that the only surviving records are two\nphotographs. It further states that any associated records may have been\ntransferred to the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments\nof Wales or destroyed under the Public Records Act 1958.\n\nI respectfully submit that this conclusion appears difficult to reconcile\nwith the contemporary evidence.\n\nContemporary newspaper reports from December 1988 record that:\n\nCadw was actively considering emergency listing (\"spot-listing\") procedures\nin relation to Great House Farm;\n\nCadw inspectors visited the site;\nCadw assessed the architectural and archaeological significance of the\nproperty;\nCadw communicated a decision that the building did not warrant statutory\nprotection.\n\nThese activities would ordinarily be expected to generate records such as\ninspection notes, recommendations, assessments, correspondence, memoranda,\nlisting files, briefing notes, internal communications, or decision records.\n\nIn addition, a surviving family witness who was present during the\ninspection recalls that a written assessment was produced and supplied to\nthe family. The witness recalls that the assessment concluded that,\nalthough the site was old, the building had undergone substantial\nalteration over the centuries and was therefore not considered sufficiently\nsignificant for listing.\n\nThis recollection appears broadly consistent with the reasoning attributed\nto Cadw in contemporary press reports.\nI therefore request clarification of the following:\n\nWere searches undertaken for inspection notes, site notes, assessment\nreports, recommendations, listing files, briefing papers, internal\nmemoranda, correspondence, and decision records relating to Great House\nFarm?\nWere accession records, transfer schedules, disposal schedules, or archive\ncatalogues searched to determine whether such records once existed?\n\nIf records were transferred to RCAHMW, please identify any transfer\nreferences, accession numbers, file references, or other metadata recording\nthat transfer.\nIf records were destroyed, please identify the disposal authority,\nretention schedule, and date of destruction.\n\nIf no written assessment, recommendation, report, or decision record ever\nexisted, please explain how Cadw reached and communicated conclusions\nregarding the architectural and archaeological significance of the property.\n\nI am not seeking reconsideration of the 1988 listing decision itself.\nRather, I seek clarification regarding the apparent absence of records\nrelating to a matter that was publicly reported at the time as being under\nactive consideration by Cadw and which resulted in a communicated decision.\n\nThank you for undertaking an internal review.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergenant)\nCyber & Electronic Warfare Professional\nLife Member of the Royal Signals\n\n\nOn Thu, 11 Jun 2026, 12:54 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your request which I received on 1 June 2026, and your\n> follow-up request received on 8 June 2026.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please see attached response and documents.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mike Weatherhead\n>\n>\n> Arweinydd Tîm Gwaith Achosion / Casework Team Leader\n>\n> Polisi a Gwarchod / Policy and Protection\n>\n> Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment Inspectorate\n>\n> Cadw\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Weatherhead, Michael (LCC - Cadw)\n> *Sent:* 01 June 2026 16:59\n> *To:* 'Requester' <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* RE: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr.\n> Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (ATISN 27021)\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> *Great House Farm, Llandough*\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your request which I received on 1 June 2026. You asked for:\n>\n>\n>\n>    1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n>    2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\n>    reports concerning the building.\n>    3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\n>    authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\n>    concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\n>    protection of the property.\n>    4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\n>    statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n>    5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\n>    archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n>    6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing,\n>    preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the\n>    property.\n>    7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\n>    representations seeking preservation of the building.\n>    8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by\n>    Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n> You will receive a response by 25 June 2026. If you have any queries\n> about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address\n> below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future\n> correspondence *(ATISN 27021).*\n>\n>\n>\n> The request you sent me contains personal information about you - for\n> example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data\n> processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data\n> Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public\n> task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a\n> response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your\n> request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your\n> personal information and all other information relating to your request for\n> three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your\n> personal information will then be disposed of securely.\n>\n>\n>\n> Under data protection legislation, you have the right:\n>\n>\n>\n>    - to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access\n>    it\n>    - to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\n>    - to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\n>    - for (in certain circumstances) your data to be ‘erased’\n>    - to (in certain circumstances) data portability\n>    - to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office\n>    (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\n>\n>\n>\n> For further information about the information which the Welsh Government\n> holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR,\n> please see contact details below:\n>\n>\n>\n> Data Protection Officer\n>\n> Welsh Government\n>\n> Cathays Park\n>\n> CARDIFF\n>\n> [postcode redacted]\n>\n> Email: [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> The contact details for the Information Commissioner’s Office are:\n>\n>\n>\n> Wycliffe House\n>\n> Water Lane\n>\n> Wilmslow\n>\n> Cheshire\n>\n> [postcode redacted]\n>\n> Website: www.ico.org.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> Any information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or\n> Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh\n> Government’s Disclosure Log (at\n> https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en\n> ).\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mike Weatherhead\n>\n>\n> Arweinydd Tîm Gwaith Achosion / Casework Team Leader\n>\n> Polisi a Gwarchod / Policy and Protection\n>\n> Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment Inspectorate\n>\n> Cadw\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 28 May 2026 06:29\n> *To:* Freedom of Information Officer <[email redacted]>;\n> Listed Buildings / Adeiladau Rhestredig <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth,\n> Vale of Glamorgan\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Freedom of Information Officer,\n>\n> I am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw\n> concerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr),\n> Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\n>\n> I request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\n>\n>    1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n>    2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\n>    reports concerning the building.\n>    3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\n>    authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\n>    concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\n>    protection of the property.\n>    4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\n>    statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n>    5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\n>    archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n>    6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing,\n>    preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the\n>    property.\n>    7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\n>    representations seeking preservation of the building.\n>    8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by\n>    Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n>\n> For the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than\n> an explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\n>\n> If any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I\n> would be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the\n> records.\n>\n> I would prefer the information in electronic form.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester Esq. (Ret'd Sergeant). Heir & Successors of Mary Williams,\n> Great House Farm, Llandough\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd\n> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu\n> eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon\n> ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn\n> Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh\n> Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh\n> Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the\n> Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice\n> <https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en>\n> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your\n> privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\n>\n"},{"id":"wb-1a5353a8","subject":"Re great house farm church view close Llandough nr penarth v","name":"0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","threadSlug":"great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-v_en_v0.0.0.00-4.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-340811fd","subject":"Re great house farm Llandough nr penarth vale of glamorgan","name":"0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Council and local authority correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan_en_v0.0.0.00-3.txt","threadSl