xt archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llando_en_v0.0.0.00-9.txt","threadSlug":"rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llando","scopeTopics":["morgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["morgan"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llando_en_v0.0.0.00-9.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-cb9e213c","subject":"Re response to enquiry at the national archives case number","name":"0000-00-00_re-response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_re-response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_re-response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Re: Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464\nFrom: Requester\nDate: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:54 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Patricia Reynolds,\n\nThank you for your response of 30 July 2026 (Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6).\n\nI note your advice that The National Archives is not the primary repository\nfor the material described in my original enquiry. However, my enquiry also\nconcerns whether The National Archives holds any recorded information\nrelating to the existence, transfer, retention, destruction, or absence of\nsuch records.\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000, I request confirmation of any\nrecorded information held by The National Archives relating to Great House\nFarm / Ty Mawr, Llandough (Glamorgan), including historical references\nunder alternative descriptions such as Cedfin or equivalent contemporary\ndescriptions.\n\nSpecifically, please confirm whether The National Archives holds:\n\n   1. *Manorial and estate records*\n\nAny catalogue entries, Manorial Documents Register information, finding\naids, transfer records, or related documentation concerning:\n\n   - the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan);\n   - pre-1667 references to occupants, customary tenants, holdings,\n   surveys, rentals, terriers, or court rolls;\n   - Vaughan family estate holdings at Llandough;\n   - Great House Farm / Ty Mawr or any earlier description of the holding.\n\nPlease include any references to HMC9/311 or related archival series.\n\n   2. *Records concerning disposal, destruction, or transfer of records*\n\nAny recorded information showing:\n\n   - whether records relating to Great House Farm, Llandough, the Bute\n   Estate, Vaughan family papers, or associated land records were ever\n   transferred to The National Archives;\n   - whether any such records were destroyed, and if so:\n      - what records were destroyed;\n      - when they were destroyed;\n      - under which retention schedule, disposal authority, or policy;\n      - which body authorised or carried out the destruction.\n\nIf no such records are held, please confirm whether any disposal or\ntransfer records indicate that relevant material was never deposited or was\ndestroyed elsewhere.\n\n   3. *Legal and court records*\n\nAny central court records, indexes, correspondence, or administrative\nrecords concerning:\n\n   - possession or title disputes involving Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n   - Western Ground Rents Ltd;\n   - BP Pension Trust Ltd;\n   - BP Properties Ltd;\n   - Mountjoy Ltd;\n   - the proceedings connected with *BP Properties Ltd v Buckler* [1987]\n   EWCA Civ 2.\n\n\n   4. *Estate transfers and ownership records*\n\nAny government-held correspondence, files, or records relating to:\n\n   - the Bute Estate;\n   - the 1938 sale or transfer of Great House Farm;\n   - Western Ground Rents Ltd acquisition;\n   - BP Pension Trust/BP Properties involvement;\n   - any government department involvement in the property.\n\n\n   5. *Family correspondence and related records*\n\nAny correspondence, reports, enquiries, or administrative records held by\nThe National Archives involving:\n\n   - Mary Williams;\n   - Fred Buckler;\n   - William Buckler;\n   - the Williams/Buckler family;\n   - Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n   - Bute Estate representatives;\n   - Western Ground Rents;\n   - BP entities.\n\n\n   6. *1980–1988 period and demolition/eviction matters*\n\nAny records concerning:\n\n   - the public campaign regarding Great House Farm;\n   - parliamentary correspondence or government enquiries;\n   - the 1988 eviction/demolition;\n   - Cadw or government communications;\n   - European Commission of Human Rights Application 14464/88 (Buckler v\n   United Kingdom).\n\nIf any relevant information is held, please provide catalogue references,\ndescriptions, and access arrangements.\n\nIf no relevant information is held, please confirm:\n\n   - the searches undertaken;\n   - the catalogues, databases, and record series searched;\n   - whether any relevant records were ever held and subsequently\n   transferred, destroyed, or disposed of.\n\nI am pursuing parallel enquiries with the National Library of Wales,\nGlamorgan Archives and other repositories. This request is specifically\ndirected at recorded information held by The National Archives.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergeant)\nRoyal Signals Cyber & Electronic Warfare Professional and Life Member\n\nOn Thu, 30 Jul 2026, 10:56 Contact Centre, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Thank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n>\n> I'm afraid we are not the right place to come to for your enquiry. We hold\n> historical records sent to us by central government departments and law\n> courts for permanent preservation. I regret, therefore, that I'm unable to\n> help you with your enquiry.\n>\n> I suggest you contact The National Library of Wales\n> <https://www.library.wales/>.\n>\n> I wish you every success with your research.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Patricia Reynolds\n>\n> Remote Enquiries Duty Officer\n> www.nationalarchives.gov.uk\n>\n> Please complete our brief, three question survey\n> <https://emea.dcv.ms/1PncPtnWn7> to let us know what you think about your\n> recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n>\n> *Enquiry:*\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n>\n> *EXTERNAL*: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded\n> information held by the National Library of Wales:\n> Any manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents\n> for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that\n> list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later\n> known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\n> Any estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or\n> surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings)\n> that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of\n> land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\n> Any catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify\n> pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the\n> family’s holding at this property.\n> Please confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the\n> relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or\n> advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state\n> the exemption(s) relied upon.\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n> Requester (Ret'd Sergeant)\n>\n> Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\n> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n> National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it\n> are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are\n> addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this\n> email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions,\n> conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do\n> not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither\n> given nor endorsed by it.\n> -------------------------------------------------------