TRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas","scopeTopics":["email"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["email"],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_response-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"available","text":"[Recovered on 19 Oct 2026 from the original email in the family's Gmail, because this archive file was missing. Matched to this entry by its subject line; where several emails share a subject, the order within the group is not certain. Email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses are redacted.]\n\nSubject: Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464\nFrom: Contact Centre\nDate: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:56 UTC\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nI'm afraid we are not the right place to come to for your enquiry. We hold historical records sent to us by central government departments and law courts for permanent preservation. I regret, therefore, that I'm unable to help you with your enquiry.\n\nI suggest you contact The National Library of Wales<https://www.library.wales/>.\n\nI wish you every success with your research.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nPatricia Reynolds\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk<http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/>\n\nPlease complete our brief, three question survey<https://emea.dcv.ms/1PncPtnWn7> to let us know what you think about your recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded information held by the National Library of Wales:\nAny manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\nAny estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings) that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\nAny catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the family’s holding at this property.\nPlease confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state the exemption(s) relied upon.\n\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nSion Buckler (Ret'd Sergeant)\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n"},{"id":"wb-97026147","subject":"Response to national archives case number cas 313954 y6c0h3","name":"0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Heritage and archives correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","threadSlug":"sponse-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":"text/0000-00-00_response-to-national-archives-case-number-cas-313954-y6c0h3_en_v0.0.0.00-2.txt","classificationNote":"Indexed from the public Wayback text catalogue by case-related filename and/or existing public catalogue tags. The classification is a finding aid, not proof that every record is an email; inspect the original source before relying on metadata. Filename dates are not asserted as sent dates without confirmation from the source.","textStatus":"not-recovered","text":null,"textNotice":"Original text not yet recovered: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"wb-4cd0760a","subject":"Setting aside BP v Buckler 1987 on grounds of fraud","name":"0000-00-00_setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-on-grounds-of-fraud_en_v0.0.0.00-1.txt","date":null,"dateStatus":"date-not-stated-or-filename-placeholder","category":"Court and legal correspondence","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"DATRO Wayback public text archive","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/text/0000-00-00_setting-aside-bp-vs-buckler-1987-