overed: the archived source file for this record is missing. See sourceUrl."},{"id":"gm-1a18bf4bdca7fa49","subject":"Automated Response: Email address not supported","name":"Automated Response: Email address not supported","date":"2026-10-30T08:37:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a18bf4bdca7fa49.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a18bf4bdca7fa49-automated-response-email-address-not-supported","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a18bf4bdca7fa49","direction":"received","from":"HM Land Registry - Do Not Reply","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["261029-6904545"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a18bf4bdca7fa49.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Enquiry Reference: 261029-6904545\n\nDear Customer\n\nThis email address is no longer supported.\n\nOur Contact HM Land Registry<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&utm_term=> page has comprehensive help pages for most enquiries.\n\nThis is an automated response and no action will be taken with your enquiry.\n\nPlease do not reply to this email. This mailbox is not monitored.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNid yw’r cyfeiriad ebost hwn yn cael ei gynnal mwyach.\n\nMae gan ein tudalen Cysylltu â Chofrestrfa Tir EF<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry.cy> dudalennau cymorth cynhwysfawr ar gyfer y rhan fwyaf o ymholiadau.\n\nYmateb awtomataidd yw hwn ac ni chymerir unrhyw gamau gyda’ch ymholiad.\n\nPeidiwch ag ateb yr ebost hwn. Nid yw’r blwch negeseuon ebost hwn yn cael ei fonitro.\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a1894085ac5ba9d","subject":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","name":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","date":"2026-10-29T20:01:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1894085ac5ba9d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1894085ac5ba9d-your-submission-to-libanswers-was-received","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1894085ac5ba9d","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["9816877"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1894085ac5ba9d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester,\n\nYour question was submitted successfully to the National Library of Wales enquiries service / Cyflwynwyd eich cwestiwn yn llwyddiannus i Wasanaeth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru\n\nDue to high demand and some resource challenges, there may be some delay in responding to enquiries at present. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nOherwydd lefel uchel y galw a rhai heriau adnoddau, bydd oedi gydag ymateb i ymholiadau ar hyn o bryd. Yr ydym yn ymddiheuro am unrhyw anghyfleuster a achosir gan hyn ac fe fyddwn yn darparu diweddariad cyn gynted ag y medrwn.\n\nWe will contact you as soon as possible. In the meantime, perhaps you can visit our FAQs <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com>\nByddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted â phosibl! Yn y cyfamser, efallai yr hoffech chi chwlio ein  FAQs  <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com> perthnasol gall ateb eich cwestiwn.\n\n\n\nWe welcome calls and correspondence in Welsh. You will receive a response in Welsh and correspondence in Welsh will not result in a delay./ Rydym yn croesawu galwadau a gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwch yn derbyn ymateb yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 29 2026, 07:58PM via Email\nEnquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth:"},{"id":"gm-1a1893deb4a12e56","subject":"Enquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth: Bute Estate records and related items (several items)","name":"Enquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth: Bute Estate records and related items (several items)","date":"2026-10-29T19:58:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1893deb4a12e56.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526f6d8a1233b-enquiry-9816877-great-house-farm-t-mawr-cedfin-llandough-juxta-penarth-bute-estate-records-and-related-items-several-ite","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526f6d8a1233b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["9816877"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1893deb4a12e56.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Enquiries team,  Further to my research enquiry of 27 September 2026 and enquiry 9816877, and my preservation notice of 28 September, I need to identify and examine three records urgently to test the title history and rule out suspected fraud or concealment. I do not allege wrongdoing by the Library or any individual.  The records are: (1) a reported 1926 conveyance to Cardiff Corporation and its plan; (2) the 1926 formation and company records of Mountjoy Ltd / Mountjoy Limited associated with the Bute estate; and (3) the 1938 Bute or Mountjoy conveyance to Western Ground Rents Ltd and its plan. A 1965 school-site contract refers to a conveyance on sale dated 25 December 1938; its parties and extent remain to be checked. Please confirm or correct these identifications.  For each, does the Library hold or has it held an original, copy, plan, abstract or reference? Please identify its current custodian, location, collection and item reference, any retention, preservation, litigation hold or stop, and anyone else who may have held or copied it. Please identify the catalogues, collections and indexes checked, including GB 0210 BUTE and D153 / D219 where appropriate, and whether any physical file was examined. If transferred or destroyed, please provide the recorded date, authority and destination. Please provide copies if held or explain the free inspection route and any cost before work is undertaken.  Thank you for your reply of 30 September that the Library does not routinely destroy, transfer or dispose of historical documents. Please preserve all three records and related indexes in your custody, without destruction, disposal or transfer without a recorded handover while the enquiry is open, and confirm their status.  The farm is Great House Farm / Great House / Greathouse / Tŷ Mawr / Ty Mawr / Ty-mawr / Ty Mawr Farm beside St Dochdwy&#39;s Church, Llandough-juxta-Penarth near Penarth and Cardiff, later Church View Close. Please also search Llandough Home Farm, Land Doc Home Farm, Cydfin, Cedfin, Cydwin, Cedwyn, Cedfyn, Cefin, Church Farm, Llandough Church Farm, Llandough Farm, Bute Estate, Mountjoy, Western Ground Rents, Landoche-juxta-Cardif, Llandochau, Leckwith and Penarth. These are search leads, not proof of a shared title; please distinguish the separate Llandough Farm and exclude Llandough near Cowbridge. Full farm, estate and locality forms and qualifications: https://cedwyn.bucklerfamily.estate/nomenclature/  Thank you for your help.  Kind regards,  Requester  https://cedwyn.bucklerfamily.estate"},{"id":"gm-1a1893bf53cbef20","subject":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","name":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","date":"2026-10-29T19:56:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1893bf53cbef20.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd-your-communication-with-companies-house-ref-coh2382411x","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd","direction":"received","from":"enquiries","institutions":[],"refs":["COH2382411X"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1893bf53cbef20.json","textStatus":"available","text":"The Companies House Enquiries Team has received your email.\nA response will be with you shortly.\nPlease note our opening hours - Monday - Friday 08.30 - 18.00 excluding Bank Holidays\n\n\nMae Tim Ymholiadau Ty'r Cwmniau wedi derbyn eich neges e-bost.\nAnfonir ateb atoch cyn bo hir.\nNodwch ein horiau agor - Llun - Gwener 08.30 - 18.00  ac eithrio Gwyliau Banc\n\n\n[Companies House Footer Image]\n\nFor details on how your personal data is handled by Companies House, please see our privacy policy -https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/companies-house/about/personal-information-charter\n\nThis message and any attachments are intended for the persons named as addressees only and may contain confidential information. In addition they may be protected by copyright. If you receive it in error, notify us, delete it and do not make use of or copy it. You must not copy, disseminate or otherwise distribute or publish this message, except for the purposes for which this message is intended, without our consent. Please note that this e-mail has been created in the knowledge that Internet e-mail is not a 100% secure communications medium. We advise that you understand and accept this lack of security when e-mailing us. For company information, guidance and how to file documents online, please visit our website www.companieshouse.gov.uk. This message has been scanned for viruses"},{"id":"gm-1a1893a0d4b8573c","subject":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","name":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","date":"2026-10-29T19:54:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1893a0d4b8573c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd-your-communication-with-companies-house-ref-coh2382411x","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[],"refs":["COH2382411X"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1893a0d4b8573c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Companies House,  Re: COH2382411X and my preservation and supply request of 10 October 2026  Thank you for your reply of 12 October. I need to identify and examine three records urgently to test the title history and rule out suspected fraud or concealment. I do not allege wrongdoing by any recipient:  1. A reported 1926 conveyance to Cardiff Corporation, including its plan; 2. The 1926 formation and company records for Mountjoy Ltd / Mountjoy Limited, associated with the Bute estate; 3. The 1938 Bute or Mountjoy conveyance to Western Ground Rents Ltd, including its plan. A 1965 school-site contract refers to a conveyance on sale dated 25 December 1938; its parties and extent remain to be checked.  Please confirm or correct each identification, including the correct Mountjoy company number and the identity of Western Ground Rents Ltd connected to the 1938 sale. My enquiry of 20 October used company number 00342092; your 12 October reply gave 09760885. Please check whether these refer to different companies and identify the correct historical company.  For each record, please say whether you hold or have held it, including copies, indexes and predecessor or archive files; the current custodian, location, series and reference; whether any retention, preservation, litigation hold or stop applies; and who else may have handled or copied it. Please identify the registers, indexes, systems and dates searched, and any destruction or transfer record. If held, please provide a copy or explain the free inspection route and any charge before work is undertaken.  Please preserve the records and related indexes, including electronic and archived material, and do not destroy or dispose of them or transfer them without a recorded handover while my enquiry is open. Please confirm whether a hold is in place.  The site is Great House Farm / Great House / Greathouse / Tŷ Mawr / Ty Mawr / Ty-mawr / Ty Mawr Farm, beside St Dochdwy&#39;s Church, Llandough-juxta-Penarth near Penarth and Cardiff, later Church View Close. Please also search Llandough Home Farm, Land Doc Home Farm, Cydfin, Cedfin, Cydwin, Cedwyn, Cedfyn, Cefin, Church Farm, Llandough Church Farm, Llandough Farm, Bute Estate, Mountjoy, Western Ground Rents, Landoche-juxta-Cardif, Llandochau, Leckwith and Penarth. These are search leads, not proof of a shared title; please distinguish the separate Llandough Farm and exclude Llandough near Cowbridge. The complete farm, estate and locality search forms and their qualifications are at https://cedwyn.bucklerfamily.estate/nomenclature/  Thank you for your help.  Yours faithfully,  Requester  https://cedwyn.bucklerfamily.estate"},{"id":"gm-1a188e9f7c98cf55","subject":"Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","name":"Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","date":"2026-10-29T18:26:36Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a188e9f7c98cf55.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988-personal-research","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71","direction":"received","from":"Viewers Requests","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a188e9f7c98cf55.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Viewer Requests\n\n-This is an automated response-\n\nThank you for your email to ITV Viewers Requests - this service is only for\nviewers wishing to obtain copies of ITV programmes past and present.\n\nFor any other query or questions about ITV or its content please contact\nour\n\nViewer Services team at:  [email redacted] , who will be very happy\nto answer your enquiry.\n\n\n   -\n\n   For copies of ITV programmes please complete the following viewer\n   request order form.\n\n\n\n   -\n\n   Only digital files of the programmes can be supplied (no DVDs etc)\n\n\n\n   -\n\n   All orders are subject to payment, to cover the cost to supply the\n   content -\n\n\nPrice List Per Programme\n\nUp to 15 mins: £70\n\nUp to 30 mins £95\n\nUp to 60 mins £145\n\nUp to 90 mins £195\n\nOver 90 mins £245\n\nPlease note that due to the large volume of requests only fully completed\nforms will be accepted and only complete programmes can be supplied (not\nclips of programmes)\n\n\n\nViewers Request Form (Please click and complete)\n<https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeYsGJiLW2WZND1dioj56n4iSAln1uhkXJ2XTs0tnNXlgv0aw/viewform?usp=sf_link>\n\n\n\nThank You\n\nITV Viewer Requests\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nViewers Requests | *ITV plc*\n[email redacted]\n\nITV plc Head Office Tel [phone redacted] itv.com <http://www.itv.com/>\n\nPlease consider the environment before printing this email\n\n-- \n <htt"},{"id":"gm-1a188e9e63686fb9","subject":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","name":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","date":"2026-10-29T18:26:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a188e9e63686fb9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988-personal-research","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a188e9e63686fb9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear ITV Viewers Requests,  Further search terms for my email of 10 October 2026, “Archive search request - Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff - December 1988 (personal research)”  I am following up on that request after ITV Clipsales advised that personal and academic research enquiries should be sent to this address. New information has come to light about historical farm, estate and locality nomenclature, including the 1881 census wording “Llandough Home Farm”. Please associate the terms below with my existing request and rerun or extend the relevant archive checks for the regional or national news coverage filmed or transmitted in late November and December 1988 concerning the farmhouse possession or demolition and adjoining site. The original request’s subject and period remain unchanged.  The intended site is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr beside St Dochdwy’s Church at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, near Penarth and Cardiff, Vale of Glamorgan. Please use the site identifiers as the primary means of disambiguation: Heneb/GGAT HER GGAT02038s; RCAHMW NPRN 20182; grid reference ST16707335; and the later development address Church View Close, [postcode redacted]. The relevant mapping references are County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW, including 38-1-608 and 38-1-334. The approximate reference in my original email was ST 168 733.  Farm and farmhouse search forms  Please consider “Great House Farm”; “Great House Farm, Llandough”; “Great House Farm (GGAT02038s)”; “Great House”; “Great house”; “Greathouse”; “Tŷ Mawr”; “Ty Mawr”; “Ty-mawr”; “Ty Mawr Farm”; “Ty Mawr (Great House)”; “Ty Mawr, Penarth Road, Llandough”; “Cydfin Farm”; “Cydfin Farm or Ty Mawr Farm, (107 a.)”; “Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm”; “Cedfin”; “Cydwin”; “Cedwyn”; “Cedfyn”; “Cefin”; “Llandough Home Farm”; “Land Doc Home Farm”; “R-W-S-S Farm / Reese’s Farm”; “Llandough Church Farm”; “Church Farm”; “former Great House Farm”; “a 3.4 acre site located adjacent St. Dochdwy Parish Church”; and “LLANDOUGH FARM (Ideal Homes Wales)”. “Ty-mawr” is also recorded on an Ordnance Survey 25-inch map, although the edition and its precise relationship to the site have not been confirmed.  These are candidate search strings, not interchangeable names or proof that each record concerns the same building, parcel or holding. The checked 1881 census image reads “Llandough Home Farm”; “Land Doc Home Farm” is a reported competing transcription. The checked page does not contain “R-W-S-S Farm / Reese’s Farm”. “Cydwin” and “Cedwyn” are reported research leads whose underlying 16th-century documents have not been verified; “Cedfyn” and “Cefin” are retained as search forms without a confirmed primary occurrence. “Llandough Church Farm” and “Church Farm” are source-specific terms whose connection to this site is not established. The Bute catalogue lists “Cydfin Farm or Ty Mawr Farm, (107 a.)” within a 1552 - 1824 catalogue range, which is not a specific date for that wording. The 1824 Stewart survey, plan 19, records “Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm” (Glamorgan Archives DB/E/1). “LLANDOUGH FARM” appears on the 1994 Ideal Homes Wales plan for the development site, but other records use Llandough Farm for a separate farmstead; please distinguish by mapped location.  Wider estate search forms  For relevant records about the surrounding area, please also consider “Cedwyn Estate”, “Cydwin”, “Cydfin Farm or Ty Mawr Farm, (107 a.)”, “Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm” and “Cwm Cydfin Wood”. “Cedwyn Estate” is the family’s working name for the wider historic estate, not a period name established by the records cited here. “Cydwin” is a reported lead from a 1547 family research note whose underlying document is not held. “Cwm Cydfin Wood” appears in a 1902 Bute sale catalogue. These are search aids for relevant site and surrounding-area records; they do not establish that all terms denote the same holding or prove the estate’s extent or title.  Locality and administrative search forms  Please also consider “Llandough-juxta-Penarth”; “Llandough near Penarth”; “Llandough near Cardiff”; “Llandough, Penarth”; “Llandough, Cardiff”; “Llandough”; “Landoche-juxta-Cardif”; “Llandough / Leckwith”; “Penarth Road, Llandough”; “Urban District of Penarth”; “Llandochau”; “CF64”; and “Church View Close, [postcode redacted]”. “Landoche-juxta-Cardif” is a historical locator for the manor, not proof that every holding recorded under it is this farm. “Llandough / Leckwith” is neighbouring parish and manorial context, not another name for the farm. The locality forms are aids to retrieval and should be kept separate from the farm and estate names. Llandough near Cowbridge and Llandow are outside the scope of this request and should be excluded as false matches.  Please record which terms and archive indexes or catalogues were checked, and tell me whether any relevant item, production record or alternative custod