":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your further email regarding your request, reference FOI2026/23886.\n\nWe have considered the additional information you have provided, including the alternative historical names and locality descriptions for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr. We note that you have confirmed that the scope and period of your original request remain unchanged.\n\nThe additional information does not change our response of 21 October 2026. Defra maintains its position that the information requested is not held by the Department.\n\nAs advised in our original response, the information may be held by the Welsh Government. You may therefore wish to contact the Welsh Government directly:\n\nhttps://www.gov.wales/contact-welsh-government#52148\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nInformation Rights Team\nDepartment for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs\n\nEmail: Information [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nSeacole Building, 4th Floor, 2 Marsham Street, London, [postcode redacted]\n\n\n\nFrom: [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\nSent: 29 October 2026 12:16\nTo: SM-Defra-Information Requests (DEFRA) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Le"},{"id":"gm-1a18790e834b0c5b","subject":"[LLGC Cymraeg] FOI request — ITV/HTV Report Wales holdings: Llandough protests 11 April &amp; 1 November 1974 (CAN 2775 item 4; CAN 2904 item 8)","name":"[LLGC Cymraeg] FOI request — ITV/HTV Report Wales holdings: Llandough protests 11 April &amp; 1 November 1974 (CAN 2775 item 4; CAN 2904 item 8)","date":"2026-10-29T12:09:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a18790e834b0c5b.txt",