nt of a Cottage\nat Llandough\" — CAN 2775, item 4.\n\nPlease confirm whether the Library ho"},{"id":"gm-1a1878f023b1d4ab","subject":"[NLW English] New FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"[NLW English] New FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-29T12:07:38Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1878f023b1d4ab.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141fc4254e01d4-nlw-english-new-foi-request-outside-foi-2026-09-1610-herbert-survey-s7-and-cardiff-mss-microfilm-of-bute-x-6-12-llandoug","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141fc4254e01d4","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["FOI/2026/16"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1878f023b1d4ab.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nOct 29 2026, 12:07PM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nI am writing in response to your recent application for information held by the Library\n \n(Ref FOI/2026/16) received here at the Library on 16 October, 2026\n \nYou will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 13 November, 2026\n\nBest wishes,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 16 2026, 12:53AM via Email\nNew FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nFreedom of Information / Enquiries Service,\n\nThis is a new request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is\noutside the scope of FOI/2026/09 and its internal review, which\nconcerned Bute series including D153 and D205 and the 1877\ntransaction. It is also separate from my enquiry of 27 September and\nfollow-up of 10 October 2026 on D153/1–8.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm\ncalled Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and\nCardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood\nbeside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge),\nand the Great Houses at nearby Lland"},{"id":"gm-1a1872aed8dc3ac1","subject":"[NLW English] FOI/2026/09 and subsequent correspondence – thank you and one remaining point","name":"[NLW English] FOI/2026/09 and subsequent correspondence – thank you and one remaining point","date":"2026-10-29T10:18:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1872aed8dc3ac1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eaa0af2e3861-nlw-english-foi-2026-09-and-subsequent-correspondence-thank-you-and-one-remaining-point","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eaa0af2e3861","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["FOI/2026/09"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1872aed8dc3ac1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nOwain Roberts\n\nOct 29 2026, 10:17AM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nFollowing verification. I can confirm that no further classmarks have been identified since the July 2026 searches that relate to Great\nHouse Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough, the 1877 agreement, the 1916 tenancy, or the 1938–39 sale.\n\nYours sincerely\nDr Owain Rhys Roberts\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 10 2026, 08:14PM via Email\nFOI/2026/09 and subsequent correspondence – thank you and one remaining point\nDear NLW FOI / Enquiries team,\n\nThank you for the internal-review outcome and the searches of the Bute\nEstate series (including D153 and D205).\n\nPlease confirm whether any further Bute Estate or related classmarks\nhave been identified since the July 2026 searches that relate to Great\nHouse Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough, the 1877 agreement, the 1916\ntenancy, or the 1938–39 sale.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , \n\n------------------\n\nThank you for using the National Library of Wales Enquiry Service.\nDiolch am ddefnyddio Gwasaneth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru.\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9872684.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a187069f574f360","subject":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211463 — clarification and refinement of request","name":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211463 — clarification and refinement of request","date":"2026-10-29T09:38:36Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a187069f574f360.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0c1c87a6f1717d-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00211463-clarification-and-refinement-of-request","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0c1c87a6f1717d","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211463"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a187069f574f360.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester \n\nWe write in response to your request for an internal review.  For clarity, we have attached a copy of this request and cite below the detail of it as your e-mail asking for an internal review does refer to the correct request.  This request is for:-\n\nDear Freedom of Information Officer,\nI am researching the 1989 planning application for the development subsequently known as Church View Close, Llandough-juxta-Penarth. The planning officer's report records that representations were received from the Barry Preservation Society and the Civic Trust, but the report does not reproduce the substance of those representations. Please provide copies of all records held by the Council relating to the representation made by the Barry Preservation Society in connection with that planning application, including: The original letter, objection or representation submitted by the Barry Preservation Society. Any covering letter, acknowledgement or correspondence concerning its submission. Any internal Council correspondence referring to or summarising the Society's representations. Any plans, photographs or supporting material submitted by the Society. Any correspondence concerning the retention, preservation, alteration or demolition of Great House Farm farmhouse. Any subsequent correspondence between the Council and the Barry Preservation Society concerning Great House Farm or the development. I am par"},{"id":"gm-1a187017ef140611","subject":"Request reference 00211557","name":"Request reference 00211557","date":"2026-10-29T09:33:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a187017ef140611.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a187017ef140611-quest-reference-00211557","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a187017ef140611","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211557"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a187017ef140611.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe write in respect of your request below, request number 00211557, which is below. The Council is dealing with your request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 (EIR), although certain elements could also be argued to be Freedom of Information requests.\n\nHaving carefully considered your request, the Council has commenced searches but has also concluded in hindsight, that an extension is necessary under Regulation 7 of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. The request requires searches across multiple service areas and involves the location, identification, retrieval, review and consideration of a significant volume of historic information and to consider whether any exceptions under the Regulations may apply, whether anyone else needs to be consulted and, where relevant, whether the public interest favours disclosure.\n\nDue to the scale and complexity of this work, it is not reasonably practicable to provide a substantive response within the initial 20 working day period. The Council has therefore extended the deadline for responding and will provide its full response no later than 19th November 2026.\n\nWe remain committed to responding as soon as possible and will issue a response before this date should our enquiries be completed sooner.\n\nRegards\nInformation Governance Officer/ / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nLegal & Democratic Services /Gwasanaethau Cyfreithol a Democrataidd\nVal"},{"id":"gm-1a186fef75ae76ee","subject":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211484 and 00211483","name":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211484 and 00211483","date":"2026-10-29T09:30:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a186fef75ae76ee.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a186fef75ae76ee-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00211484-and-00211483","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a186fef75ae76ee","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211484"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a186fef75ae76ee.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester \n\nWe attach copies of both your original requests to 00211483 and 00211484.  The Council is dealing with your requests under the Environmental Information Regulations (EIR).\n\nHaving carefully considered your requests, the Council has commenced searches but has also concluded in hindsight, that an extension was necessary under Regulation 7 of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. The request requires searches across multiple service areas and involves the location, identification, retrieval, review and consideration of a significant volume of historic information and to consider whether any exceptions under the Regulations may apply, whether anyone else needs to be consulted and, where relevant, whether the public interest favours disclosure.  Even, request 00211484 although seeming relatively straightforward is quite complex simply by virtue of the fact that it is very historic in nature and requires careful identification.  \n\nDue to the scale and complexity of this work, it was not reasonably practicable to provide a substantive response within the initial 20 working day period. The Council therefore should have extended the deadline for responding.  But even if doing so, as you state below the requests would be beyond the 40-day period.  We therefore apologise to you for the delay.  However, we do feel that the very historic nature of your requests does make consideration qu"},{"id":"gm-1a18649ce508047a","subject":"You're long overdue a response to your FOI request - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (BP vs Buckler 1987)","name":"You're long overdue a response to your FOI request - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (BP vs Buckler 1987)","date":"2026-10-29T06:12:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a18649ce508047a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a18649ce508047a-you-re-long-overdue-a-response-to-your-foi-request-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-bp-vs-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a18649ce508047a","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a18649ce508047a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"National Archives are long overdue.\n\nThey have not replied to your FOI request 'Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (BP vs Buckler 1987)', as normally required by law.\n\nClick on the link below to send a message to National Archives asking them to confirm that they have received your request and tell you when they are going to respond. You can also refer your request to the Information Commissioner.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/great_house_farm_llandough_cardi/followups/new/3540231\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhatDoTheyKnow is a project of mySociety run by a small team of staff and\ndedicated volunteers.\n\nmySociety is a charity that believes that information should be accessible to everyone.\nIf this is important to you, please consider donating to help us do more:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/donate\n\nFind out more about how we handle your data at:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/help/privacy\n\nmySociety is a registered charity in England and Wales (1076346), and a limited\ncompany (03277032)"},{"id":"gm-1a18345ba8c044f9","subject":"[LLGC Cymraeg] FOI request — ITV/HTV Report Wales holdings: Llandough protests 11 April &amp; 1 November 1974 (CAN 2775 item 4; CAN 2904 item 8)","name":"[LLGC Cymraeg] FOI request — ITV/HTV Report Wales holdings: Llandough protests 11 April &amp; 1 November 1974 (CAN 2775 item 4; CAN 2904 item 8)","date":"2026-10-28T16:09:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a18345ba8c044f9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a18345ba8c044f9-llgc-cymraeg-foi-request-itv-htv-report-wales-holdings-llandough-protests-11-april-amp-1-november-1974-can-2775-item-4-c","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a18345ba8c044f9","direction":"received","from":"Rhianydd Davies","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["FOI/2026/15"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a18345ba8c044f9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nRhianydd Davies\n\nOct 28 714, pm: 08pm via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\n\n\nI am writing in response to your recent application for information held by the National Library of Wales\n\n\n\n(Ref. FOI/2026/15) received here at the Library 28 October 2026.\n\n\n\nYou will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 25 November 2026.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\nRhianydd Davies\n------------------\n\nOriginal Question\n\nOct 28 658, pm: 48pm via Email\nFOI request — ITV/HTV Report Wales holdings: Llandough protests 11 April & 1 November 1974 (CAN 2775 item 4; CAN 2904 item 8)\nNational Library of Wales,\n\nI am writing to request recorded information under the Freedom of\nInformation Act 2000 about two entries reportedly in the Library's\nITV/HTV \"Report Wales\" holdings:\n\n1 November 1974 — \"Protest at a Cottage in Llandough Over Eviction\nPlans\" — ITV CAN 2904, item 8.\n\n11 April 1974 — \"People Protesting Against Redevelopment of a Cottage\nat Llandough\" — CAN 2775, item 4.\n\nPlease confirm whether the Library holds the underlying films or\nrecordings for each entry, not merely catalogue descriptions. I ask\nthat archive staff check the physical holdings and any associated\ndigital or preservation copies, rather than relying solely on the\nonline catalogue.\n\nPlease report what was checked, when it was"},{"id":"gm-1a18320aac359503","subject":"RE: 00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm  New Request 00211722","name":"RE: 00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm  New Request 00211722","date":"2026-10-28T15:28:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a18320aac359503.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a18320aac359503-00211484-narrowed-request-commemorative-tree-church-view-close-great-house-farm-new-request-00211722","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a18320aac359503","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211722"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a18320aac359503.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe are writing in respect of below, which you notified us of earlier this month and asked for it to be considered as part of 00211484 and 00211483.  Given the timing of this further request and the detail within we believe that this will in fact need to be treated as an additional request.  We have logged it as such.  The reference number for this request:- 00211722.\n\nWe are of the view that this request sits within the environmental information regulation regime.  This supplement was received on 18th October 2026.\nDue to the complexity and volume of the information requested, the Council is extending the time available to respond under Regulation 7 of the EIR. Regulation 7 permits a public authority to extend the normal 20 working day response period to a maximum of 40 working days where the complexity and volume of the information requested makes it impracticable to respond within the standard timeframe. The Council therefore expects to provide a substantive response by 14th December 2026.  This extension is necessary because your request requires detailed searches across a range of records and consideration of a substantial volume of historic information before a response can be issued.\nWe will continue to process your request as promptly as possible and will provide a response before the revised deadline wherever practicable.\nRegards\n\nInformation Governance Officer/ / Swyd"},{"id":"gm-1a1831b1020095c7","subject":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211557 New Request 00211721","name":"RE: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211557 New Request 00211721","date":"2026-10-28T15:22:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1831b1020095c7.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1831b1020095c7-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00211557-new-request-00211721","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1831b1020095c7","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211721"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1831b1020095c7.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe are writing in respect of below, which you notified us of earlier this month and asked for it to be considered as part of 00211557.  Given the timing of this further request and the detail within we believe that this will in fact need to be treated as an additional request.  We have logged it as such.  The reference number for this request:- 00211721.\n\nWe are of the view that this request sits within the environmental information regulation regime.  This supplement was received on 18th October 2026.\nDue to the complexity and volume of the information requested, the Council is extending the time available to respond under Regulation 7 of the EIR. Regulation 7 permits a public authority to extend the normal 20 working day response period to a maximum of 40 working days where the complexity and volume of the information requested makes it impracticable to respond within the standard timeframe. The Council therefore expects to provide a substantive response by 14th December 2026.  This extension is necessary because your request requires detailed searches across a range of records and consideration of a substantial volume of historic information before a response can be issued.\nWe will continue to process your request as promptly as possible and will provide a response before the revised deadline wherever practicable.\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nInformation Governance Officer/ / Swyd"},{"id":"gm-1a181ade960954f0","subject":"RE: [3] Re: Formal complaint — GGAT / Heneb: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — HER identifiers and the 1978–1995 record","name":"RE: [3] Re: Formal complaint — GGAT / Heneb: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — HER identifiers and the 1978–1995 record","date":"2026-10-28T08:43:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a181ade960954f0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ed989b1263c57-3-re-formal-complaint-ggat-heneb-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-her-identifiers-and-the-1978-1995-record","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ed989b1263c57","direction":"received","from":"Steven Foulston","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a181ade960954f0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nResponse to your Formal complaint — GGAT / Heneb: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — HER identifiers and the 1978–1995 record\nFurther to your complaint dated 27 September 2026 and the supplementary email you sent on 30 September. I have now had the opportunity to review this matter and detail my response below.\n\n\n  1.  I have not seen the HER\n\n\n\nThe HER is a publicly available record. Further details of how to use the HER  can be found here: Historic Environment Records (HER) - Heneb<https://heneb.org.uk/historic-environment-records-her/>\n\n\n\n  1.  \"Partially recorded\" is RCAHMW's phrase, not a finding I have verified on the HER\n\nAs noted above, the HER is a publicly available record.\n3. What GGAT held in 1988, and what it did not do\nIf you wish to find the information you have enquired about, the HER is a publicly available record\n\n4. \"County treasure\"\nSee response to answer 3 above\n\n5. Specify, price, bid, execute\nFor GDPR reasons we are unable to share information which identifies specific individuals.\n\n\n6. The 1990 method against GGAT's own model\nSee response to answer 3 above. For the sake of clarity, Heneb are unable to review the 1990 evaluation as you propose.\n\n7. Human remains and the 1981 Act\nAny relevant information will be contained in the HER record.\n\n8. Two burial figures, both correct\nSee response to answer 1 above\n\n9. The"},{"id":"gm-1a17e354759f980f","subject":"RICS - Email Forwarded RICS:022900001655","name":"RICS - Email Forwarded RICS:022900001655","date":"2026-10-27T16:32:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17e354759f980f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a17e354759f980f-rics-email-forwarded-rics-022900001655","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a17e354759f980f","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[],"refs":["RICS:022900001655"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17e354759f980f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nThank you for contacting RICS.\n\n\n\nI’ve forwarded your email to the relevant department who will respond to your query shortly.\n\n\n\nThe Knowledge Team will be in touch within the coming days.\n\nIf there's anything else we can help with in the meantime, please don’t hesitate to get in touch.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nKiran Mohammed\n\nRICS Hub - Membership Support UK&I, Europe, Americas\n\n\n\nt [phone redacted] w rics.org\n\n\n\n<https://www.linkedin.com/company/rics>   <https://twitter.com/RICSnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor>    <https://www.facebook.com/ricssurveyors/>\n\n------------------- Original Message -------------------\nFrom: [email redacted];\nReceived: Sun Oct 25 2026 00:24:27 GMT+0100 (British Summer Time)\nTo: The RICS Hub <[email redacted]>;\nSubject: RE: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993) RICS:022900001630\n\n\n\n[You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of RICS. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognise the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Kiran Mohammed,\n\nThank you for your reply of 23 October 2026 (reference"},{"id":"gm-1a17e2cec3d874ce","subject":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-27T16:23:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17e2cec3d874ce.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"received","from":"clrd.mears","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17e2cec3d874ce.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Clear, concise and hopefully final, professional response as usual Paul. Sent from my Galaxy\n-------- Original message --------From: Paul Egan <[email redacted]> Date: 27/10/2026  16:05  (GMT+00:00) To: Requester <[email redacted]> Subject: Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM \nDear Requester,\nPlease see below my response to your questions as promised.\n1. What consideration was my first approach given before the reply of 20 November 2025? - You need to be more specific about what you are looking for in relation to this question.2. Does the Council hold any Tŷ Mawr records besides the minute books deposited in 2002 (my email of 14 June)? Uncertain at this stage pending the outcome of the internal review which you have requested.3. Which agenda items cover the \"other matters\" your email of 11 October said would be considered in October? These related to the two specific questions you posed which were included on the agenda.4. Who decided the meeting would be remote only, and on what date? The Council decided to hold the meeting remotely for the reason given to you by the Chair at the meeting on 22 October 20265. When was the website agenda revised and republished? It was amended in good time to provide for the three clear day's notice of the meeting.6. Where are the published arrangements for multi-location meetings (s.47, LGE(W)A 2021)? The arrangements for how communi"},{"id":"gm-1a17e1bd6c43ebf1","subject":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-27T16:05:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17e1bd6c43ebf1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17e1bd6c43ebf1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nPlease see below my response to your questions as promised.\n\n1. What consideration was my first approach given before the reply of 20 \nNovember 2025? - You need to be more specific about what you are looking \nfor in relation to this question.\n2. Does the Council hold any Tŷ Mawr records besides the minute books \ndeposited in 2002 (my email of 14 June)? Uncertain at this stage pending \nthe outcome of the internal review which you have requested.\n3. Which agenda items cover the \"other matters\" your email of 11 October \nsaid would be considered in October? These related to the two specific \nquestions you posed which were included on the agenda.\n4. Who decided the meeting would be remote only, and on what date? The \nCouncil decided to hold the meeting remotely for the reason given to you \nby the Chair at the meeting on 22 October 2026\n5. When was the website agenda revised and republished? It was amended \nin good time to provide for the three clear day's notice of the meeting.\n6. Where are the published arrangements for multi-location meetings \n(s.47, LGE(W)A 2021)? The arrangements for how community council \nmeetings may be held are detailed in the statutory guidance for \ncommunity councils - \nhttps://www.gov.wales/sites/default/files/publications/2022-08/statutory-guidance-for-community-and-town-councils.pdf\n\n7. Was a physical public venue considered? Not on this occa"},{"id":"gm-1a17e173d16e616a","subject":"Your email to the ICO - Case Reference IC-546505-W6P0","name":"Your email to the ICO - Case Reference IC-546505-W6P0","date":"2026-10-27T16:00:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17e173d16e616a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a17e173d16e616a-your-email-to-the-ico-case-reference-ic-546505-w6p0","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a17e173d16e616a","direction":"received","from":"icocasework","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":["IC-546505-W6P0"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17e173d16e616a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"27 October 2026\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026. I note that you would like some advice on four points relating to submission of FOI complaints to the ICO. I will address each of your points in turn.\n\n1. I note that you have a query about whether the ICO can consider complaints about a public authority’s compliance with section 46 of the FOI Code of Practice. Unfortunately, the ICO is unable to consider complaints about public authority’s compliance with the section 46 as part of a section 50 complaint. For further information on the way the Information Commission monitors public authorities adherence to the section 46 Code of Practice, please see the following guidance: https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/foi/freedom-of-information-and-environmental-information-regulations/section-46-code-of-practice-records-management/#monitors\n\n2. Where a public authority deletes, alters or conceals information within the scope of a request with the aim of preventing the disclosure of that information, the public authority may have committed a section 77 offence under FOIA or regulation 19 offence under the EIR.\n\nIf you consider that a public authority has committed a section 77 offence when responding to a request for information you have made, you can submit a complaint to us using our FOI complaint form: https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/foi-and-eir-complaints/foi"},{"id":"gm-1a17debed8d64a3b","subject":"Re: Draft minutes of 22 October 2026 – my additions for the record","name":"Re: Draft minutes of 22 October 2026 – my additions for the record","date":"2026-10-27T15:12:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17debed8d64a3b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a17c63fbd8e6731-draft-minutes-of-22-october-2026-my-additions-for-the-record","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a17c63fbd8e6731","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17debed8d64a3b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nI acknowledge receipt of your email.\n\nThe accuracy of the draft minutes is a matter for the council to \nconsider at its next meeting and I am unable to make any of the changes \nyou propose. I would point out that it is not our practice to include \neither myself or Councillor Carroll in the list of attendees as we are \nnot members of the council.\n\nRegards,\n\nPaul\n\n---\nPaul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n\nClerk to Llandough Community Council,\n\n[address removed]\n\nVale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone [phone redacted]\n\nWebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n\n\n\n\n\nWhen you contact us\n\nThe information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\nemail address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\nto enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\ninformation and/or access our facilities and services.\n\nYour personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \nthird party. Your information may however be published in the public \ndomain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n\n\n\nFor further information please see our full privacy notice on our \nwebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n\n\n\nThe Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \nour identity' The Council will always strive to:\n\n  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n\n· Be accountable in all our council activities\n\n· Be responsive to the needs of the community\n\n· Encourage community participation\n\nOn 2026-10-27 08:04, Requester wrote:\n> Dear Mr Egan, Councillor Dr Misra and Councillor Carroll,\n> \n> Please find attached the draft minutes of the meeting of 22 October\n> 2026, with my additions shown in red, for the record before the\n> minutes are confirmed.\n> \n> My additions are:\n> 1. Present: Councillor George Carroll and the Council Clerk, Paul Egan.\n> 2. Public participation: there were four members of the public in\n> attendance. Names taken included [member of the public], Requester and [member of the public]. [member of the public] attended briefly but left when names were\n> being demanded by Councillor Misra.\n> 3. The spelling \"Rail Replacement\".\n> 4. My name, given as Requester in the item heading and \n> throughout.\n> 5. That Marconi stayed in my birth home (Great House Farm) with his\n> family, and that World Champion boxer Peerless Jim fought his first\n> fight in the barn there.\n> 6. On my question (a): that the council emphasised it would not be\n> asking anyone on my behalf, if that's what was being asked (said with\n> tone).\n> 7. Item (c): that one councillor suggested a QR code. The sentence\n> breaks off in the draft (\"to inform the\"), so please complete it from\n> your notes.\n> \n> As the council's website is currently showing an expired security\n> certificate, which I made Mr Egan aware of, citing a free SSL provider\n> (Cloudflare), I will also add these amendments to WhatDoTheyKnow so\n> they are on the public record.\n> \n> Kind regards,\n> Requester"},{"id":"gm-1a17d70dd5a8a389","subject":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-27T12:58:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17d70dd5a8a389.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d-information-request-great-house-farm-t-y-mawr-near-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["historic-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["historic-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d","direction":"received","from":"Wilkins, Mark","institutions":[{"id":"historic-england","name":"Historic England"}],"refs":["26/04323"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17d70dd5a8a389.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Our Reference: 26/04323\n\nDear Requester,\n\nRe: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan:\n\nThank you for your email on the 22nd October 2026 in which you requested the following information related to the property above. Your request has been processed under the Environmental Information Regulations (2004) :\n\n\n\n  1.  Item 1 (the record of the transfer). Your response confirms that the section of the archaeological reports microfiche collection relating to sites in Wales was transferred to RCAHMW on 12 January 2018. Please confirm whether Historic England holds any record of that transfer itself (for example a covering letter or email, a transfer agreement, a receipt from RCAHMW, a box or batch list, a spreadsheet, index or manifest prepared before the transfer, or a file note recording the decision), even if it does not itemise individual fiche. If held, please provide a copy.\n\n\n\nYes, a letter of transfer to RCAHMW dated 12 January 2018 (attached)\n\n\n\n  1.  Item 4 (the decision to transfer). Please confirm whether any record holds the date of the decision, the role of the officer who authorised it, and its basis. If held, please provide it; if not held, please say so.\n\n\n\nYes, a deaccession statement showing the deaccession decision on 25 July 2017 by former Head of Archive (attached)\n\n\n\n  1.  Item 6 (retaine"},{"id":"gm-1a17d40e7e544e07","subject":"CAS-322825-L6S1- Acknowledgement - Cwm Cydfin SSSI (0524) notification and owner/occupier records","name":"CAS-322825-L6S1- Acknowledgement - Cwm Cydfin SSSI (0524) notification and owner/occupier records","date":"2026-10-27T12:06:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17d40e7e544e07.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a17d40e7e544e07-cas-322825-l6s1-acknowledgement-cwm-cydfin-sssi-0524-notification-and-owner-occupier-records","scopeTopics":["nrw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nrw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a17d40e7e544e07","direction":"received","from":"Mynediad at Wybodaeth / Access to Information Team","institutions":[{"id":"nrw","name":"Natural Resources Wales"}],"refs":["CAS-322825-L6S1"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17d40e7e544e07.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThis request has been allocated Access to Information Request Number CAS-322825-L6S1.\n\nNatural Resources Wales will respond to your request for information in line with the Environmental Information Regulations (EIR) 2004.\n\nWe will respond to your request as soon as possible and no later than 20 working days from when we received your request. We will contact you as soon as possible should we need to clarify your request. Any information that takes less than 2 ½ days to compile will be free. If it takes longer than this we will consult you before taking further action.\n\nWe will be retaining your personal details along with your request in a database for the purpose of recording progress and monitoring our performance Any Information disclosed under the Freedom of Information Act (2000) or Environmental Information Regulations (2004) will be listed in the Natural Resources Wales disclosure log on our web site.\n\nWe will only use this personal data in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation to deal with your request and any matters that arise from it.\n\nIf you have any further queries or concerns, please contact [email redacted]. See our Privacy Policy which describes how we collect use and share your information,\n\nIf you have any further queries or concerns, please contact us on the details below. I would be grateful if you would use the ATI Request number in all futu"},{"id":"gm-1a17d3ce2927a81d","subject":"Subject Access Request: D260928","name":"Subject Access Request: D260928","date":"2026-10-27T12:01:40Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17d3ce2927a81d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a17d3ce2927a81d-subject-access-request-d260928","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a17d3ce2927a81d","direction":"received","from":"_DataProtection","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["D260928"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17d3ce2927a81d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nTo avoid personal data about one individual being disclosed to another, we need to be reasonably satisfied of the identity of the individual making the request.\n\nIn order to continue with your subject access request, please provide a copy of photographic evidence of your identity (for example passport or driving licence) together with a copy of a recent utility bill. Once we are satisfied with your identity we will proceed with your request. We will make a file note but will not retain copies of the documents provided.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n[logo]\nS Henderson\nDisclosure Officer, Information Rights Team\n\nGOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry> | @HMLandRegistry<https://twitter.com/HMLandRegistry> | LinkedIn<http://www.linkedin.com/company/land-registry> | Facebook<http://www.facebook.com/pages/Land-Registry/343223435769541>\n\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome"},{"id":"gm-1a1797cf17494564","subject":"ATISN 26-0010 - internal review - Acknowledgement (Retention & destruction schedules)","name":"ATISN 26-0010 - internal review - Acknowledgement (Retention & destruction schedules)","date":"2026-10-26T18:33:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1797cf17494564.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1797cf17494564-atisn-26-0010-internal-review-acknowledgement-retention-destruction-schedules","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1797cf17494564","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN 26-0010"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1797cf17494564.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nFurther to your recent request for an internal review of the above request, please find an acknowledgement letter attached.\n\nKind regards\nNatalie\n\nNatalie Chant\nTîm Rheoli Busnes / Business Management Unit\nY Grŵp Effeithiolrwydd Gweithredol / Operational Effectiveness Group\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\nE-bost: [email redacted] / E-mail: [email redacted]\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-1a1793ba43e8d95b","subject":"IR/26/16 - Buckler - Response","name":"IR/26/16 - Buckler - Response","date":"2026-10-26T17:21:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1793ba43e8d95b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1793ba43e8d95b-ir-26-16-buckler-response","scopeTopics":["nio"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nio"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1793ba43e8d95b","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"nio","name":"Northern Ireland Office"}],"refs":["IR/26/16"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1793ba43e8d95b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\nPlease see the attached response in respect of your internal review\nrequest to the Wales Office, reference IR/26/16.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nFreedom of information Team\n\n\n[image: image.png]"},{"id":"gm-1a1790f028e2355a","subject":"CPS Freedom of Information Request – Ref. 14786","name":"CPS Freedom of Information Request – Ref. 14786","date":"2026-10-26T16:33:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1790f028e2355a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1790f028e2355a-cps-freedom-of-information-request-ref-14786","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1790f028e2355a","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":["14786"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1790f028e2355a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"OFFICIAL\nGood afternoon\n\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 (FOIA) Request\n\nThank you for your request which we received via CPS Wales on 21 October 2026. This is being actioned as a request under the FOIA for information held by a public authority.\n\nFreedom of Information (FOI) is a public disclosure regime, not a private regime. This means that any information disclosed under the Act, by definition, may become available to the wider public.  Please be aware that FOI applies only to information that a public authority, in this case the Crown Prosecution Service (CPS), holds in recorded format at the time a request is received. The CPS is not required to create it or seek this from a third party.\n\nThere is a 20-working day limit in which we are required to respond to requests.\n\nThe deadline for your request is 18 November 2026.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nCorporate Knowledge & Information Team\nHQ Digital and Information Directorate\n[Crown Prosecution Service logo]\n102 Petty France, London, [postcode redacted]\ncps.gov.uk<http://www.cps.gov.uk/>\n[cid:[email redacted]161E0]: @cpsuk<https://mobile.twitter.com/cpsuk> | LinkedIn: @CrownProsecutionService<https://uk.linkedin.com/company/crown-prosecution-service>\n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\n\nSent: 21 October 2026 16:13\n\nTo: Victim Liaison Cymru-Wales <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\n\nSubject: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud - Send to IAT\n\n\n\nDear L Rutter,\n\n\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026, and for passing my email of 30 September 2026 to a Legal Manager.\n\n\n\nI note the CPS position: it cannot accept evidence from members of the public, and material bearing on any criminal matter is for the police.\n\nNoted: material of that kind is for the police, and none will be sent to the CPS as evidence.\n\n\n\nYour reply says the CPS \"is not involved in, and has no knowledge of\"\n\nthe case. That answers the evidential point. It does not answer whether the CPS holds records. The CPS took over prosecutions in England and Wales in October 1986, and the events at Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, Penarth, include a summons arising from events at the farm on 29 April 1988, which the local press reported as withdrawn in January 1989 as out of time. Our position is that any file on that summons would have been a CPS file.\n\n\n\nI therefore make the following requests. They are requests for information, not the submission of evidence.\n\n\n\nRequest under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 1. Whether the CPS (including CPS Wales and any earlier CPS area office covering Glamorgan) holds any record, from 1 October 1986 to 31 December 1990, that refers to Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, BP Properties Ltd, or the summons described above.\n\n2. If such records once existed but are no longer held: the retention schedule that applied to magistrates' court case files of that period, and any destruction or disposal record for them.\n\n3. The searches made before your reply of 21 October (systems searched, terms used), so that \"no knowledge of the case\" can be understood as either \"no record held\" or \"no search made\".\n\n\n\nIf any part of this would be better framed differently, please advise under section 16 FOIA (the duty to advise and assist). Any personal data within scope should be dealt with separately as a subject access request under section 45 of the Data Protection Act 2018. Please treat this email as that request, so far as it concerns Requester's own personal data.\n\n\n\nStatutory dates: the FOIA response is due within 20 working days of receipt, by 18 November 2026; the subject access response is due within one month.\n\n\n\nFor clarity on routes: if the FOIA answer is refused or incomplete, the next steps are internal review and then a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA. Any concern about the handling of this correspondence will go through the CPS Feedback and Complaints Policy, and then to the Independent Assessor of Complaints.\n\n\n\nPlease preserve any surviving 1986–1990 records within scope while this request is open.\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\nRequester's Tab agent\n\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester [email redacted]<[email redacted]>"},{"id":"gm-1a178895fba55836","subject":"RC26-0375 – Order form and 3 points","name":"RC26-0375 – Order form and 3 points","date":"2026-10-26T14:06:41Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a178895fba55836.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a178895fba55836-rc26-0375-order-form-and-3-points","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a178895fba55836","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0375"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a178895fba55836.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email. \n\nWith regard to point 1, please find a Word Document copy of our order form, attached. If you continue to experience difficulty in utilising this form, it is also possible to submit an order using our online order form, here: https://rcahmw.gov.uk/contact-us/.\n\nWith regard to point 2, and taking as starting point, as you note, that no further information is held beyond the archive catalogue:\n\na) This information is not held.\n\nb) The ‘plans’ included in Archive Numbers 6048943 (Investigator's notes for Great House Farm, Llandough, including sketch plan showing periods of construction by Howard H. Thomas) and 6048941 (Ink drawing showing plan of Great House Farm, Llandough, showing periods of construction. Scale 1:100. Additions made 12/12/1988) are as described in the archive catalogue. There is no further related material, such as correspondence or photography, not listed in the online archive catalogue.\n\nc) To provide a list of the relevant sorties would require a search for which there would be a charge.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAdam Coward\n\n\nNMR Enquiries\nYmholiadau Cyhoeddus I Public Enquiries\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 21 October 2026 16:13\nTo: NMR Enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: RC26-0375 – thank you and three remaining points & Order for scans\n\nDear Adam,\n\nThank you for your email of 13 October 2026 on RC26-0375, and for the clear answers on all three points. I accept point 3: archive number\n6364275 relates to Great House, Bonvilston, not Great House Farm, Llandough. I am grateful that the item was physically examined.\n\n1. Scan order. Please treat this email as confirmation that we wish to order research-quality scans of archive numbers 6048945, 6048943 and 6048941, for private, non-commercial research for the family's case.\nThe order form attached to your email has not come through on our side in a usable form. Could you either accept the order on the details below, or send the form again (a plain Word or PDF file is fine)?\n   - Name: Requester\n   - Email: [email redacted]\n   - Items: 6048945, 6048943, 6048941 (your estimate: four research-quality scans, within the fee waiver for fewer than five)\n   - Use: personal, non-commercial research\n\n2. Noted: no further information is held beyond the archive catalogue.\nThree short follow-up questions, which I do not think have been asked\nbefore:\n   a) Did the NMRW receive any material from Cadw (or the Welsh\nOffice) relating to the 1988 listing or demolition of the Llandough farmhouse? A yes or no from the accessions or transfer register is enough.\n   b) Are the H.J. Thomas notes and plan of 26 April 1974 (ST 1681\n7331) held complete, and is there any related correspondence or photography from that survey?\n   c) Is there a list of RAF or Ordnance Survey vertical aerial sorties that cover Llandough (around ST 168 733) between 1940 and 1990? I am asking only for the sortie list from the catalogue, not a chargeable search.\n\nIf any of these would be better made as a formal request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, please say so (regulation 9, advice and assistance) and treat it as one. A reply within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026, would be appreciated.\n\nWith thanks,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester [email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a178545741638a9","subject":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information Request 1188/26","name":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information Request 1188/26","date":"2026-10-26T13:09:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a178545741638a9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a178545741638a9-sponse-freedom-of-information-request-1188-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a178545741638a9","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1188/26 (review of 719/26)"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a178545741638a9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nYour request for information has now been considered and our response is attached.\n\nI trust that this information answers your request. Should you have any queries and wish to contact us by e-mail, please do so using the mail box [email redacted] .\n\nSouth Wales Police provides you the right to request a re-examination of your case under its review procedure (copy attached). If you decide to request such a review and having followed the Forces full process you are still dissatisfied, then you have the right to direct your comments to the Information Commissioner who will give it consideration.\n\nKind regards,\n\n[cid:[email redacted]8610]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>\n\n\nSamantha Jones\nSwyddog Ymchwil ac Ansawdd Data| Research and Data Quality Officer\nRheolwr Rheoli Data a Datgeliadau | Data Management and Disclosure Unit\nPencadlys Heddlu De Cymru | South Wales Police Headquarters\n*: [phone redacted] | Ext: 26660\n[cid:[email redacted]8610]<http://fb.me/swpolice>\n[cid:[email redacted]8610]<https://www.instagram.com/swpolice/>\n[cid:[email redacted]8610]<https://twitter.com/swpolice>\n[cid:[email redacted]8610]<https://www.youtube.com/user/swptv>\n\n\n\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad ?'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk<https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/>, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a177a359d80b6be","subject":"Ref No: FOI-26-46 (Mapping information Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff – Request for information – Clarification request","name":"Ref No: FOI-26-46 (Mapping information Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff – Request for information – Clarification request","date":"2026-10-26T09:54:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a177a359d80b6be.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a177a359d80b6be-f-no-foi-26-46-mapping-information-ty-mawr-great-house-farm-red-fen-cedfin-llandough-cardiff-request-for-information-cla","scopeTopics":["os"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["os"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a177a359d80b6be","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":["FOI-26-46"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a177a359d80b6be.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nFurther to your email dated 20 October 2026, which is being considered by Ordnance Survey in accordance with the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) 2000, and our acknowledgement, also dated 20 October.\n\nWe acknowledge your information request to be:\n\n\n\n1. Two parts of my email of 27 June asked for recorded information, not for advice. They asked whether Ordnance Survey holds (a) \"any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\", and (b) \"any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\". Please deal with those two parts as a request for information under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 if you consider the information environmental.\n\n2. For each of (a) and (b), please confirm or deny whether the information is held (section 1(1)(a)). The site is at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, within the area of County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW, with the map references I gave (38-1-608 and 38-1-334).\n\n3. To make (a) as precise as possible, it covers, for the large-scale (1:2,500 and 1:10,560) plans of this site published between 1950 and 1975: the revision or resurvey dates; any name sheet, name book or field revision record for the names \"Ty Mawr\", \"Great House\" or \"Great House Farm\"; and any record of who supplied or authorised a name or a change to it (for example, an owner, an occupier, a local authority or HM Land Registry), in what capacity, and when.\n\n4. If any of this has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference instead of treating that part as not held. I have found that object name books for County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW (1898–1942) are at The National Archives as OS 35/2503. Please tell me whether Ordnance Survey holds anything later of the same kind for this area. If records of this kind were destroyed, please give the disposal schedule or policy that applied and, if recorded, the date.\n\n\nWe are having some trouble identifying the exact location which is the subject of your request.\n\nUsing the information provided, the only Great House Farm near Llandough we can find is: GREAT HOUSE FARM, LLANDOUGH, COWBRIDGE, [postcode redacted]. However, we cannot find any reference to this address being referred to as Ty Mawr.\n\nWe have another location in the vicinity, where we have found a property called Ty Mawr, but no reference to Great House or Great House Farm. I have attached a screenshot of a map we have pulled from the National Library of Scotland which shows this area in approximately 1950, circled in red.\n\nPlease can you confirm which address / area is correct.  This will enable us to provide an appropriate and accurate response to your request.\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) 2000, we are obliged to provide you with a response to your request within twenty working days.  However, as we have sought clarification from you the 20 working days will start the day after the necessary clarification is received by Ordnance Survey.\n\nWe will acknowledge your clarification response and confirm the revised date by which you should expect to receive a full response from us.\n\nIf we do not receive a response from you, within two months of receipt of this request for clarification, your request for information will be considered closed.  Please note that under section 1(3) of the FOIA 2000, a public authority need not comply with a request unless any further information reasonably required to locate the information is supplied.\n\nShould you need to contact Ordnance Survey regarding your request at any time, please quote the allocated reference number in any correspondence.\n\nPlease reply to [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nMany thanks and with kind regards\n\nNikki\n\nNikki Osborne for the FOI Team\nLegal Services\n[cid:[email redacted]4D0]\nAdanac Drive, Southampton, [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n[email redacted] | www.os.uk<http://www.os.uk/>\nFollow us: X (Twitter)<https://x.com/OrdnanceSurvey> | LinkedIn<https://www.linkedin.com/company/ordnance-survey/> | YouTube<https://www.youtube.com/@ordnancesurvey/videos> | Instagram<https://www.instagram.com/ordnancesurvey/?hl=en> | Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/osmapping/>\n\n\n\nThis email and any attachments are intended only for the intended recipient and may contain sensitive information. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately delete this email and inform the sender.\n\nOS email communications may be monitored to ensure the secure and effective operation of our systems and for other lawful purposes. Subject to contract: No rights are to be derived from any proposal contained in this email until a written agreement containing all necessary terms is executed between the relevant parties.\n\nThank you for your cooperation.\n\nOrdnance Survey Limited (Company Registration number 09121572)\nRegistered Office: Explorer House\nAdanac Drive\nSouthampton [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\nhttp://www.os.uk"},{"id":"gm-1a17774f4bd25728","subject":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-26T09:05:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17774f4bd25728.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17774f4bd25728.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email and for setting out your proposed scrutiny topic in such a clear and comprehensive manner. I acknowledge receipt of your correspondence and note the distinction you have drawn between the specific matters that have given rise to your suggestion and the broader, county-wide focus you are proposing in relation to the management of, and public access to, historic planning, land charges and heritage records.\n\nThe Council has an established process for submitting scrutiny topic suggestions. Once received, the proposal will be considered in accordance with the Council's work programming arrangements and the agreed principles used to assess potential scrutiny topics. At this juncture, I would recommend this being an item for considered by Place Scrutiny Committee, as the Committee's Terms of Reference generally covers matters related to the wider built environment.\n\nAt this stage, I cannot provide a view on whether the topic will be added to a future work programme, the form of any scrutiny activity that may be undertaken, or which committee may ultimately be best placed to consider the matter. These are issues that would need to be assessed through the normal work programming process, taking account of the subject matter, the remit of the relevant scrutiny committee(s), existing work programme commitments, and available capacity. We will undertake this process in conjunction with the Chair and various supporting officers as part of our normal work planning process and inform you of next steps as soon as reasonably practicable.\n\nThank you again for your engagement with the scrutiny process. Should you submit the proposal through the Topic Suggestion Form, it will be processed in accordance with the Council's established arrangements and referred through the appropriate channels for consideration, with a response to yourself as appropriate.\n\nBest,\nJames\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 22 October 2026 19:19\nTo: Langridge-Thomas, James <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough\n\nDear James,\n\nThank you for your detailed reply of 22 October, and for clarifying that your correspondence of 11 October reflected your assessment of the proposal as submitted, against the Council's Scrutiny work programming principles, rather than a formal decision of a Scrutiny Chair or Committee.\n\nI understand that scrutiny of this topic would not review individual cases or revisit an individual historic planning decision, would not determine private title, and would not replace the statutory information-rights procedures. I also note that final agreement rests with the relevant Scrutiny Committee and Chair, that the Committee does not currently have capacity for another Task and Finish review while it completes its current piece of work, and that a new topic remains subject to the Council's normal work programming process.\n\nOn that basis, I wish to pursue a separate, county-wide topic as follows.\n\nProposed title: Management of, and public access to, historic planning, land-charges and heritage records.\n\nPurpose: To consider whether the Council's arrangements for retaining, transferring, cataloguing, locating and providing access to historic records are clear, effective and appropriately documented. Reliable historic records matter to any resident, landowner or conveyancer tracing the planning and land-charges history of land anywhere in the Vale.\n\nProposed scope:\n\n1. The policies, responsibilities and procedures for retaining, transferring, disposing of, indexing and retrieving historic records, including records inherited from predecessor authorities at the 1996 local government reorganisation and earlier reorganisations, how those handovers were documented, and records held on paper or in off-site archives.\n\n2. How searches for historic records are carried out and documented, and how missing, incomplete or unlocated files, appendices and supporting material are identified and explained.\n\n3. How requests for access to historic planning, land-charges and heritage information are received, routed, monitored and answered.\n\n4. Whether published procedures, allocation of responsibilities, record-search practices and service standards could be improved.\n\nThe Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) matter is the background to this suggestion, but it is not a request for Scrutiny to determine, review or revisit that case or any other individual case. I note your point that a topic of this kind would not reflect upon or review individual cases, and I am content for the work to proceed entirely at the level of the Council's systems and practices.\n\nThe proposed work would concern policy, governance, records management and service delivery. It would not ask Scrutiny to determine property ownership, make findings about individual liability, or decide the merits of a historic planning decision. My outstanding information requests, including the internal review of EIR request 00210772 and the requests concerning the missing planning appendices, will continue separately through the information-rights routes.\n\nI will submit this as a separate topic suggestion through the Scrutiny Topic Suggestion Form linked from the Council's published Scrutiny webpage (https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/our_council/Council-Structure/scrutiny/scrutiny.aspx).\n\nAs the topic spans both historic planning records and corporate records management, I would welcome your advice, or that of Democratic and Scrutiny Services, on which committee or committees it falls under within their current remits.\n\nI would also be grateful to take up your offer to help direct the proposal through the appropriate work programming process. If it cannot be scheduled as Task and Finish work at present, could you please advise whether it can be recorded for a future work programme or co"},{"id":"gm-1a17767a60886d8c","subject":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-10-26T08:50:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17767a60886d8c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17767a60886d8c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning, Requester,\nApologies for the late reply .\nMy computer system does not store any information for referrals received in 1983 or 1990 or any information for referrals received before 2002 and I do not hold any transfer references for cases . This information you require will be held at Glamorgan Archives,.  I am unable to confirm if any referrals were ever received for the late Mary Doreen Williams or the late Mr William (Billy) Buckler. I am unable to give details of the coroner at that time for Llandough Hospital.\nYou have not confirmed in your e-mail if you have already contacted Glamorgan Archives and if so, what information could they supply ? if you have not yet contacted them, please do at \n\n e-mail [email redacted]\n\nGlamorgan Archives\nClos Parc Morgannwg\nLeckwith\nCARDIFF\n[postcode redacted]\nTel; [phone redacted]\n\n\nKind Regards\nBev Morgan\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 22 October 2026 19:20\nTo: Morgan, Beverley <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\n                Rhybudd: E-bost allanol yw hwn - sy wedi dod o sefydliad/unigolyn y tu allan i'r Cyngor. Byddwch yn wyliadwrus wrth glicio ar ddolenni neu agor atodiadau.\n                Caution: This is an external email and did not originate from within the Council. Please take care when clicking links or opening attachments.\n\n\nDear Bev,\n\nMy email of 26 August 2026 — two points still open\n\nThank you again for your replies of 21 and 25 August. I wrote on 26 August with two short questions and have not had a reply, so I am asking again in this thread. Twenty working days from 26 August ended on 24 September 2026.\n\n1. Mary Doreen Williams (died March 1983): does your office hold any record of which coroner's jurisdiction covered Llandough Hospital in 1983, and of where that jurisdiction's registers and case papers went (a transfer list, accession record, or destruction or retention record), including the date on which any such records were handed to the Glamorgan Archivist? A held / not held answer is enough.\n\n2. William (Billy) Buckler (died 1990): your search note covered referrals received in 1983 or before. Was a 1990 referral capable of being found in the system you searched? If yes, please confirm the result for 1990. If no, please confirm whether Cardiff and Vale cases from 1990 are among those \"with the Glamorgan Archivist\", and give any transfer reference you hold.\n\n3. If these questions fall to Rhondda Cynon Taf Council's Freedom of Information team rather than to your office, please pass this email to them and let me know the reference. If it is treated as a request for recorded information, please treat this email as asking for an internal review of the lack of a reply to the email of 26 August.\n\nI am not asking for any medical information, only whether a record exists, where it is, or when and under what authority it was destroyed.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any charge would apply, please tell me first.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\n\nCroesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at oedi.  Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e Cymraeg neu'n ddwyieithog. Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person(au) a enwyd yn unig a gall gynnwys deunydd sensitif neu ddeunydd sy wedi'i farcio hyd at 'CYFYNGEDIG' a dylid ei thrin yn unol a hynny. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi'r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopio neu'i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych wedi derbyn y neges ar gam a wnewch roi gwybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae modd cofnodi a/neu fonitro holl negeseuon GCSX yn unol a'r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol.  \nI weld yr ymwadiad llawn ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual. This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain sensitive or protectively marked material up to RESTRICTED and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a171fb721ce8b95","subject":"Re: Website security certificate has expired (13 December 2025)","name":"Re: Website security certificate has expired (13 December 2025)","date":"2026-10-25T07:34:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a171fb721ce8b95.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a16faed34c17e2b-website-security-certificate-has-expired-13-december-2025","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a16faed34c17e2b","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a171fb721ce8b95.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks Requester.\n\nWe do pay annually for the security certificate so I will take it up \nwith our website host provider.\n\nRegards,\n\nPaul\n\n---\nPaul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n\nClerk to Llandough Community Council,\n\n[address removed]\n\nVale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone [phone redacted]\n\nWebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n\n\n\n\n\nWhen you contact us\n\nThe information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\nemail address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\nto enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\ninformation and/or access our facilities and services.\n\nYour personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \nthird party. Your information may however be published in the public \ndomain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n\n\n\nFor further information please see our full privacy notice on our \nwebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n\n\n\nThe Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \nour identity' The Council will always strive to:\n\n  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n\n· Be accountable in all our council activities\n\n· Be responsive to the needs of the community\n\n· Encourage community participation\n\nOn 2026-10-24 21:51, Requester wrote:\n> Dear Mo, Paul and George,\n> \n> A quick, friendly heads-up. While checking the Llandough Community\n> Council website, I noticed that the SSL/TLS security certificate for\n> www.llandough-cc.co.uk expired on 13 December 2025 (315 days ago), and\n> the address without \"www\" doesn't answer securely at all. Because of\n> this, visitors' browsers show a \"Not secure\" warning or refuse to open\n> the secure page.\n> \n> Whoever looks after the site, or its hosting provider, should be able\n> to renew the certificate and turn on auto-renewal so it doesn't lapse\n> again.\n> \n> No reply needed.\n> \n> Kind regards,\n> \n> Requester \n> "},{"id":"gm-1a1703ab823f247a","subject":"RE: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993) RICS:022900001630","name":"RE: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993) RICS:022900001630","date":"2026-10-24T23:24:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1703ab823f247a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1695c09fefeb37-enquiry-and-preservation-notice-surveyors-and-valuation-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-1969","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1695c09fefeb37","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[],"refs":["RICS:022900001630"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1703ab823f247a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Kiran Mohammed,\n\nThank you for your reply of 23 October 2026 (reference RICS:022900001630) to my email of 16 October 2026.\n\nYes, I am seeking specific information and assistance. The site is Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan: the farmhouse, its fields and the woodland beside Leckwith Road. The period is 1969 to 1993. The land passed to the BP Pension Trust / BP Properties Ltd in 1969, was the subject of possession proceedings, and the farmhouse was demolished in 1988; the land was later developed for housing.\n\nFor each numbered point, please say whether RICS holds the information and, if it does not, who may hold it.\n\n1. Historic directories. Does RICS, including its library or archive, hold the RICS Year Books or lists of members and firms for 1969 to 1993 covering Cardiff, Penarth and the Vale of Glamorgan? If so, how may they be consulted or copied?\n\n2. Instructions on this site. Does RICS hold any record of members or firms who acted as surveyors, valuers or land agents in connection with Great House Farm between 1969 and 1993, for any landowner, local authority, public body or developer?\n\n3. Complaints and regulatory records. Does RICS hold any complaint, disciplinary or regulatory record that relates to this site in that period? If a record exists but cannot be released, please say so and give the reason.\n\n4. Record-keeping rules at the time. What did RICS byelaws, regulations or guidance in force between 1969 and 1993 require members to keep (instructions, valuation reports, field notes and correspondence), and for how long? Please send the relevant text or tell me where it is published.\n\n5. Closed or merged practices. When a member firm closed or merged in that period, what happened to its client files? Does RICS keep any record of where the files of closed practices went, or of successor firms?\n\n6. Preservation. Please preserve any records RICS holds that relate to this site, and confirm that you have done so. Please also tell me whether RICS can draw this preservation request to the attention of member firms that may hold files for the site, or whether I should write to firms directly.\n\n7. Other holders. If RICS holds none of the above, please tell me which body or archive may hold it.\n\nIf a charge would apply to any item, please tell me the amount first. A quote will be considered; nothing is agreed at this stage.\n\nA reply within 20 working days of receipt would be appreciated.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1702151ac77d8f","subject":"Automatic reply: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","name":"Automatic reply: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-24T22:56:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1702151ac77d8f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1702149e534f1e-automatic-reply-document-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1702149e534f1e","direction":"received","from":"Norman, Jo","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1702151ac77d8f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"I am on leave until Thursday 29th October.  If you need to speak to someone urgently, please contact James Renwick, thank you."},{"id":"gm-1a1702149e534f1e","subject":"Automatic reply: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","name":"Automatic reply: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-24T22:56:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1702149e534f1e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1702149e534f1e-automatic-reply-document-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1702149e534f1e","direction":"received","from":"Brierly, Chris","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1702149e534f1e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your email.  I am out of the office until 3 November."},{"id":"gm-1a17021271c3c58d","subject":"RE: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","name":"RE: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-24T22:56:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a17021271c3c58d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4-document-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1984-1988","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a17021271c3c58d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Sheehy,\n\nThank you for your reply of 23 October.\n\nI asked BP to preserve these records in my preservation notice of 28 September 2026, sent to BP Archive ([email redacted]). I repeated the request on 16 October 2026 in my email to Jo Norman, and your reply confirms that email was passed to you.\n\nI repeat my request that BP preserve all relevant existing records in its possession, custody or control, or held on its behalf, relating to the land known as Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, and the proceedings BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1984–1988). This includes relevant records held by BP group entities and predecessor, pension or trust functions, as well as external solicitors, archives, agents or storage providers. Please take appropriate steps to ensure that relevant physical and electronic records, including archived communications and attachments, are not lost through routine deletion, overwriting or disposal.\n\nPlease forward this request promptly to BP p.l.c.’s Group General Counsel, the legal team responsible for BP Properties Limited, and the relevant legal-hold and records-management custodians. Please confirm by 7 November 2026 which offices or roles have been notified and whether a preservation hold is in place; if so, please state its effective date and scope. If no hold is in place, please say so expressly.\n\nIf BP disagrees with any part of this request, please tell me in writing by 7 November 2026. If I hear nothing by then, I will proceed on the basis that BP accepts that it should preserve the records described above and is doing so, and I will keep this email as my record of that notice.\n\nThis email is about preservation only. I am not asking for disclosure or privileged advice here, and I reserve the right to do so separately.\n\nNothing in this email is an acknowledgment of any title, right or licence, and all of my rights are reserved.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1695c09fefeb37","subject":"RE: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993)","name":"RE: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993)","date":"2026-10-23T15:23:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1695c09fefeb37.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1695c09fefeb37-enquiry-and-preservation-notice-surveyors-and-valuation-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-1969","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1695c09fefeb37","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[],"refs":["RICS:022900001630"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1695c09fefeb37.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting RICS and for sharing your research resources regarding Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, South Wales.\n\nWe appreciate you taking the time to share this information with us.\n\nCould you please clarify whether there is any specific information or assistance you are seeking from RICS in relation to your research?\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nKiran Mohammed\n\nRICS Hub - Membership Support UK&I, Europe, Americas\n\n\n\nt [phone redacted] w rics.org\n\n\n\n<https://www.linkedin.com/company/rics>   <https://twitter.com/RICSnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor>    <https://www.facebook.com/ricssurveyors/>\n\n------------------- Original Message -------------------\nFrom: [email redacted];\nReceived: Fri Oct 16 2026 08:50:00 GMT+0100 (British Summer Time)\nTo: The RICS Hub <[email redacted]>;\nSubject: Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993)\n\n\n\n[You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of RICS. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognise the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear RICS,\n\nI am researching Great House Farm (Tŷ"},{"id":"gm-1a168f453b3abea1","subject":"IR1038 - Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr","name":"IR1038 - Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr","date":"2026-10-23T13:30:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a168f453b3abea1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a168f453b3abea1-ir1038-great-house-farm-t-mawr","scopeTopics":["audit-wales"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["audit-wales"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a168f453b3abea1","direction":"received","from":"Information Officer","institutions":[{"id":"audit-wales","name":"Audit Wales"}],"refs":["IR1038"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a168f453b3abea1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nI am writing to acknowledge receipt of your request for information in your email below.\n\n\n\nI am considering your request in accordance with the procedures set out on the Wales Audit Office website at: http://www.audit.wales/openness-and-transparency/information-policy. The procedures are intended to ensure that requests are dealt with in accordance with the Freedom of Information Act 2000, the Code of Practice set under section 45 of the 2000 Act, the Data Protection Act 2018 and other relevant legislation.\n\n\n\nI shall write to you again once I am able to provide a substantive response, though I may write to you before then if I need to clarify your request. In the meantime, if you have any queries, you are welcome to contact me.\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nAndrew Lane\nLaw and Ethics Specialist (Information Officer) || Arbernigwr y Gyfraith a Moeseg (Swyddog Gwybodaeth)\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]> [phone redacted]\nwww.archwilio.cymru<http://www.archwilio.cymru/> || www.audit.wales<http://www.audit.wales/>\n\n[cid:image001.jpg@01DD62FA.15052E30]\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:47\nTo: Information Officer <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI request — Audit Wales: external audit records of council land dealings at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1970–1996\n\n\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Audit Wales.\n\n\n\nDear Information Officer,\n\n\n\nI sent this request earlier today (20 October 2026) to [email redacted]<[email redacted]>, which returned it as undeliverable (address unknown), so I am resending it to the address published on your Freedom of Information page.\n\n\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where they apply, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. It concerns Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of\n\nGlamorgan: the farm, its woodland beside Leckwith Road, village green\n\nVG41 (registered on 16 June 1970), and the land later developed as Church View Close. The farmhouse was demolished in 1988.\n\n\n\nI understand that Audit Wales holds records inherited from the Wales Audit Office and, for Welsh local government, from the District Audit Service and the Audit Commission. I am trying to establish from the records whether the external auditors examined any council dealing with this land and, if so, who examined it, when and with what result.\n\n\n\nPlease tell me whether Audit Wales holds, and provide, the following for 1970–1996, for the Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council, South Glamorgan County Council, Glamorgan County Council and the district councils that covered Llandough before 1974:\n\n1. any audit report, management letter, public interest report or value-for-money report that mentions Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Church View Close, village green VG41 or land at Leckwith Road, Llandough; 2. any auditor's working papers or correspondence about any acquisition, sale, exchange, lease or registration of land there by any of those councils, including the registration of VG41; 3. any objection by a local government elector, or any question raised at the audit of accounts, about land at Great House Farm, and the auditor's decision on it, with the date and the auditor (by role) who made it; 4. any correspondence between the auditors and HM Land Registry, BP Properties Ltd (company no. 00699446), Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) or Ideal Homes about the land; 5. if records of this kind for the period are no longer held, the retention or disposal schedule that applied, the date of disposal if recorded, and who authorised it, or the repository to which they were transferred.\n\n\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance under section 16.\n\n\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\n\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n\nRequester \n\n https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com__;!!A_jZAm9j2ts!6xnuvCyquQcnwIs1kSObPvVIP3YVF8-OU4-Vj2rRgWjz48ZJjBz5R-DeIqvpe6-NFaOBNtOkPeUu8ENjhXAdSuees1zKivc$<https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com__;!!A_jZAm9j2ts!6xnuvCyquQcnwIs1kSObPvVIP3YVF8-OU4-Vj2rRgWjz48ZJjBz5R-DeIqvpe6-NFaOBNtOkPeUu8ENjhXAdSuees1zKivc$>"},{"id":"gm-1a168c69031bff64","subject":"Environmental Information Regulations 2004 - F261029 and Freedom of Information request - F261030","name":"Environmental Information Regulations 2004 - F261029 and Freedom of Information request - F261030","date":"2026-10-23T12:40:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a168c69031bff64.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a168c69031bff64-environmental-information-regulations-2004-f261029-and-freedom-of-information-request-f261030","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a168c69031bff64","direction":"received","from":"_FOI email address","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["F261029","F261030"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a168c69031bff64.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email dated 20 October 2026.\n\nYour request will be dealt with under the:\n\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004 - reference F261029\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 - reference F261030.\n\nOur statutory deadline for reply for F261029 and F261030 is 17 November 2026 but we will endeavour to respond as soon as possible.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nS Henderson\nDisclosure Officer (Risk, Assurance, Information, Security)\nData and Register Integrity Group\nEmail- [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nGOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry> | @HMLandRegistry<https://twitter.com/HMLandRegistry> | LinkedIn<http://www.linkedin.com/company/land-registry> | Facebook\n\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a16882d4f515f19","subject":"Internal Review Request: Reference CAS-356384-B2F5L9 CRM:013201602","name":"Internal Review Request: Reference CAS-356384-B2F5L9 CRM:013201602","date":"2026-10-23T11:26:02Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a16882d4f515f19.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a16882d4f515f19-internal-review-request-reference-cas-356384-b2f5l9-crm-013201602","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a16882d4f515f19","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-356384-B2F5L9"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a16882d4f515f19.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nReview of complaint about access request: Appeal by Requester against The National Archives’ regarding a Freedom of Information request for information concerning the existence, provenance, transfer, retention, destruction or disposal of records relating to Ty Mawr / Great House Farm.\n\n\n\nWe wrote to you informing you that we would review and respond in writing to your request for an internal review by 23rd October 2026.\n\n\n\nYour appeal is still being considered and the review is ongoing.\n\n\n\nI anticipate being able to respond with a final decision within 40 working days from the date of receipt; on or before 20th November 2026. This is in accordance with the Code of Practice on Internal Appeals:\n\n\n\nhttps://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/744071/CoP_FOI_Code_of_Practice_-_Minor_Amendments_20180926_.pdf\n\n\n\nWe would like to answer all internal appeals within 20 working days but, unfortunately, on this occasion it was not possible.\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\nFOI Manager\n\nFreedom of Information Centre\n\nGovernment and Archives Leadership\n\nThe National Archives\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-1a16876a2f78ac5e","subject":"Re: Bute X.6(12) — 1877 Bute trustee accounts/receipts and possible Great House Farm / Llandough transaction","name":"Re: Bute X.6(12) — 1877 Bute trustee accounts/receipts and possible Great House Farm / Llandough transaction","date":"2026-10-23T11:12:42Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a16876a2f78ac5e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb95e6e388ee-bute-x-6-12-1877-bute-trustee-accounts-receipts-and-possible-great-house-farm-llandough-transaction","scopeTopics":["cardiff"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb95e6e388ee","direction":"received","from":"Library Central","institutions":[{"id":"cardiff","name":"Cardiff Council"}],"refs":["Bute X.6(12)"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a16876a2f78ac5e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Requester,\n\napologies for the delay in replying.\n\nYes, Bute X.6(12) is still held in Central Library - I had a look at it and, unfortunately, couldn't find any information about the property you are researching. We do have quite a vast collection of Bute Papers (please see attached documents for details).\n\nIf you wanted the document scanned to you, that would be done by Glamorgan Archives, as they have specialised equipment to do so. If you wish, we can transfer it to them and they will get in touch with you about the cost.\n\nI had a look at the index of our Manuscript collection and couldn't find any matches with the places and people mentioned in your message. If you wanted us to conduct detailed research, we would have to discuss it with senior management and Glamorgan Archives, as it is not one of our core services. There would be a charge, but at the moment I can't provide you with details, until we assess what needs to be done.\n\nAlternatively, you could book an appointment and visit us in person, if you wanted to see any documents from the Bute collection.\n\nPlease advise how you would like to take it forward.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nMonika Wroblewska\n\nRhagenwau/Pronouns: hi/ei / she/her\n\n\nSwyddog Hyb Uwch Senior Hub Officer\n\nHyb y Llyfrgell Ganolog Central Library Hub\n\nYr Aes The Hayes, Caerdydd Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n\nCyngor Dinas Caerdydd City of Cardiff Council\n\n[cid:100c2735-0188-46df-b98c-9ff8927271e8]  [cid:d6865667-2406-429b-9f2d-c4ac2aa8b58c]  [cid:af1f1409-b6b8-48c8-a5ab-77e179db271a]\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:13\nTo: Library Central <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Bute X.6(12) — 1877 Bute trustee accounts/receipts and possible Great House Farm / Llandough transaction\n\nDear Cardiff Central Library Local Studies / Manuscripts Team,\n\nGlamorgan Archives has advised me (email reference 2026/4097b,\nreceived 30 September 2026) that your library holds a Bute collection\ncontaining reference Bute X.6(12), described as “abstracts of payments\nand receipts by the trustees of the Marquis of Bute’s properties, 1877\n(copy)”. I am writing to establish access to that exact item and to\nask whether related Bute Estate records in the same collection may\nassist a targeted historical search.\n\nThe property under investigation is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr,\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church (approx. ST 168\n733), Cardiff. Please keep this distinct from the separate Llandough\nFarm opposite the hospital, Llandough juxta-Cowbridge, and Llandow.\nThe historical question is whether surviving estate material in\n1876–1878 records a transaction involving Daniel Thomas / D. Thomas\nand the Bute Estate or its trustees concerning this particular\nfarm/defined parcel. That is a research question, not an assertion\nthat X.6(12) necessarily concerns this property.\n\nPlease confirm:\n1. whether Bute X.6(12) is still held by Cardiff Central Library, its\nfull item title/date coverage and any catalogue or manuscript\nidentifier;\n2. whether the item can be inspected or copied, what the\nbooking/form/fee conditions are, and whether a digital image of the\nrelevant 1877 entry can be supplied;\n3. whether staff can check the entry/index for Daniel Thomas, D.\nThomas, Great House Farm/Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Llandough Limeworks,\nquarrying/mineral rights or a dwelling adjoining St Dochdwy’s\nchurchyard;\n4. whether related Bute X.6 account/receipt volumes, estate ledgers,\ncorrespondence, rent/lease records, conveyances or attached maps/plans\nsurvive for 1876–1878 and can be searched; and\n5. if no relevant entry is found, which volumes/indexes were checked\nand whether there is a reliable route to other Cardiff Library\nmanuscript registers or a transfer/custody record.\n\nFor any possible match, please provide the exact reference, date,\nparties as written, property description, amounts/transaction terms if\nrecorded, acreage/boundaries, and whether a map or plan accompanies\nthe entry. Please do not infer that a generic “Llandough” entry refers\nto this farm without a supporting description.\n\nThank you for your help. Please direct me to the correct collection\ncustodian if Bute X.6(12) has moved or is managed elsewhere.\n\nKind regards,\nRequester \n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a16814eff6e8660","subject":"RE: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","name":"RE: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-23T09:26:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a16814eff6e8660.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4-document-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1984-1988","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4","direction":"received","from":"Sheehy, Jack (Contractor)","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a16814eff6e8660.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email of 16 October 2026 which has been passed to me. Many of the links you have embedded into your email are unfortunately inaccessible, so please make any documentation you wish to send to us available in a pdf or word document format.\n\nI note your request that bp entities place a hold on records relating to Great House Farm/Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth for the period 1969 to date, pending consideration of a possible claim.\n\nHaving reviewed the position, we are not aware of any outstanding or live cause of action that bp or any related entity would need to answer in relation to this property. The dispute concerning possession of Great House Farm was the subject of litigation between BP Properties Ltd and Mrs Buckler which was determined by the Court of Appeal in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987). That litigation concluded with the Court of Appeal's judgment, and BP Properties Ltd went on to obtain possession of the site, as your own email records.\n\nIn the absence of any explanation of what new claim you believe may now arise, or against which legal entity, we are not in a position to understand why a document preservation obligation would exist, and we are therefore not able to confirm that a preservation hold of the kind you describe will be put in place.\n\nIf you do believe you have a specific legal claim against any bp related entity, we would invite you to set out the nature of any interest you claim to hold, the basis of any potential claim, including the legal grounds relied upon and the relief sought so that it can be properly considered.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you with the above information.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nJack Sheehy\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 October 2026 08:55\nTo: Norman, Jo <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)\n\n[You don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n\nDear Ms Norman,\n\nI write as Requester, a party with a direct interest in the events concerning Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, South Wales. The public working evidence catalogue is at https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgreathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com%2F&data=05%7C02%7CChris.Brierly%40uk.bp.com%7C867efde9704644974b7e08df2de7a494%7Cea80952ea47642d4aaf45457852b0f7e%7C0%7C0%7C639280145071079332%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=hXFiPNV74CeS83gKlYirXYvGc4alJRyW615xfsmOids%3D&reserved=0<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/>, with the title and chronology index at https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdartboard.bucklerfamily.estate%2F&data=05%7C02%7CChris.Brierly%40uk.bp.com%7C867efde9704644974b7e08df2de7a494%7Cea80952ea47642d4aaf45457852b0f7e%7C0%7C0%7C639280145071093094%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=sbzCXWSkHD4fgciMxgZSLleyLtkD1e9g46CkeEqm8N0%3D&reserved=0<https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate/> and the long-term archive at https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwayback.bucklerfamily.estate%2F&data=05%7C02%7CChris.Brierly%40uk.bp.com%7C867efde9704644974b7e08df2de7a494%7Cea80952ea47642d4aaf45457852b0f7e%7C0%7C0%7C639280145071110012%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=os5Pg1uQigSAZxeDrR9L0%2Bu1F54JbkFdxphUPy5XSxw%3D&reserved=0<https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/>.\n\nBP Properties Ltd obtained possession of the site on 29 November 1988; outbuildings were demolished on 30 November 1988 and the farmhouse on\n5–6 December 1988. Before any litigation or formal proceedings are considered, I am exhausting every non-litigious avenue. As part of that, I am placing preservation notices with every organisation that may hold relevant records or artefacts.\n\nPlease treat this as notice that BP p.l.c., BP Properties Ltd, the BP Pension Trust and any successor entities should preserve, and not destroy, delete, overwrite or dispose of, any records, correspondence, title deeds, litigation files, photographs, plans, survey reports, demolition records, or other material relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, for the period 1969 to present. This includes material held by BP Legal, external solicitors instructed in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, and any archived or off-site storage.\n\nI would be grateful for written confirmation that a preservation hold has been placed, and for the identity of any external firm of solicitors that acted for BP in that litigation so that I may write to them directly.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n [email redacted]<[email redacted]>"},{"id":"gm-1a16524a6cdda5a9","subject":"ICO Case Reference IC-586450-N8N0. Cyfeirnod achos yr ICO IC-586450-N8N0","name":"ICO Case Reference IC-586450-N8N0. Cyfeirnod achos yr ICO IC-586450-N8N0","date":"2026-10-22T19:44:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a16524a6cdda5a9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a16524a6cdda5a9-ico-case-reference-ic-586450-n8n0-cyfeirnod-achos-yr-ico-ic-586450-n8n0","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a16524a6cdda5a9","direction":"received","from":"icocasework","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":["IC-586450-N8N0"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a16524a6cdda5a9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for getting in touch. Your case reference number is IC-586450-N8N0.\n\nIf you have new or relevant information you would like to add, you can:\n\n• reply to this email, or\n• email us and include your full reference number in the subject line.\n\nPlease only send information that is directly relevant to the issue you’ve already raised.\n\nYours sincerely,\nInformation Commissioner’s Office\n\n________________________________\n\nDiolch i chi gysylltu â ni. Eich cyfeirnod achos yw IC-586450-N8N0.\n\nOs oes gennych wybodaeth newydd neu berthnasol yr hoffech ei hychwanegu, gallwch:\n\n• ymateb i'r e-bost hwn, neu\n• e-bostiwch ni a chynnwys eich rhif cyfeirnod llawn yn y llinell bwnc.\n\nAnfonwch wybodaeth sy'n uniongyrchol berthnasol i'r mater rydych chi eisoes wedi'i godi yn unig.\n\nYn gywir,\nSwyddfa'r Comisiynydd Gwybodaeth"},{"id":"gm-1a164d7545000183","subject":"We have received your email. Rydym wedi derbyn eich ebost","name":"We have received your email. Rydym wedi derbyn eich ebost","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d7545000183.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a164d7545000183-we-have-received-your-email-rydym-wedi-derbyn-eich-ebost","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a164d7545000183","direction":"received","from":"icocasework","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d7545000183.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for contacting the Information Commissioner’s Office. We confirm that we have received your correspondence. If you have any special requirements that mean you would like us to communicate with you in a specific way, please let us know and we will make adjustments if we can.\nIf you have made a new complaint - we’re unlikely to look into it unless you have raised it with the responsible organisation (for a data protection complaint) or the responsible public authority (for a freedom of information complaint) first. Please make sure you have sent us a copy of their final response to you. We're supporting a high number of people with their complaints at the moment. For the latest timescales to allocate cases, please visit the make a complaint page<https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/> on our website. We apologise for this delay but we want to reassure you we take your complaint very seriously.\nIf your correspondence relates to an existing case - we will add it to your case and consider it on allocation to a case officer. If you believe we have either failed to take appropriate steps to respond to your data protection complaint, or we do not provide you with information about the progress or outcome of your complaint within the next three months, you may be able to apply to the First-tier Tribunal to require us to respond to your complaint or to provide you with information about its progress. (www.gov.uk<http://www.gov.uk/> - information rights and data protection: appeal against the Information Commissioner)\nIf you have asked us for advice - we will respond within 7 days. While you wait, you should regularly check our website (www.ico.org.uk<http://www.ico.org.uk/>) for relevant guidance, as we are updating this all the time. You should read our Guide to the UK GDPR<https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr/>. If you have raised a question that we have answered on our website, we may respond by sending you a link to it. But will do our best to provide you with the information you need.\nIf you represent an organisation and you are reporting a personal data breach under the GDPR or the Data Protection Act 2018 - we aim to contact you within seven days to confirm receipt and to provide you with a case reference number. If you want advice urgently, you should telephone our helpline on [phone redacted]. You can find out more about data breach reporting on our website.\nWhere a significant cyber incident occurs, you may also need to report this to the National Cyber Security Centre (the NCSC). To help you decide, you should read the NCSC’s guidance about their role and the type of incidents that you should consider reporting. (www.ncsc.gov.uk<http://www.ncsc.gov.uk/> -incident-management)\nIncidents that might lead to a heightened risk of individuals being affected by fraud, should be reported to Report Fraud (https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/) - the UK’s national fraud and cybercrime reporting centre. If your organisation is in Scotland, then reports should be made to Police Scotland (www.scotland.police.uk<http://www.scotland.police.uk/>).\nIf you are a Communications Service Provider reporting a security breach under the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations – you will need to report the security breach via the secure portal that can be found on the PECR pages of our website.\nIf you represent an organisation and are reporting a potential incident under the NIS Directive - we will contact you as soon as we can. You can find out more about the NIS Regulations on our website\nIf you represent an organisation and you are reporting a security breach within the definition of the eIDAS regulation – we will contact you as soon as we can. You can find out more about the eIDAS regulation on our website.\nIf you have reported spam email – we are unlikely to need to contact you again, unless we need more information to help with our investigations. We publish details about the action we've taken on nuisance messages on our website.\nIf you have asked for information you think we might hold - we will contact you if we need any more information to help us respond. Otherwise, we will respond within our public and statutory service levels. For more information please visit our webpage ‘request information from us’ (go to our homepage and follow the link for ‘about the ICO’ and ‘our information’).\nIf you have only copied your correspondence to us - we will not respond.\nThere is more detailed information, including information on our current response times, on our service standards and what to expect webpage. You can also call [phone redacted], we welcome calls in Welsh on [phone redacted]. You can also contact us on live chat (please visit our webpage ‘contact us’ and ‘live chat’).\nFor information about what we do with personal data please see our privacy notice: https://ico.org.uk/global/privacy-notice/\nYours sincerely\nThe Information Commissioner’s Office\n\nDiolch yn fawr ichi am gysylltu â Swyddfa’r Comisiynydd Gwybodaeth. Rydym yn cadarnhau bod eich gohebiaeth wedi dod i law. Os oes gennych unrhyw ofynion arbennig sy'n golygu yr hoffech i ni gyfathrebu â chi mewn ffordd benodol, rhowch wybod i ni a byddwn yn gwneud addasiadau os gallwn.\nOs ydych wedi gwneud cwyn newydd – dydyn ni ddim yn debygol o edrych i mewn iddo oni bai eich bod wedi’i godi’n gyntaf gyda’r sefydliad cyfrifol (cwyn am ddiogelu data) neu’r awdurdod cyhoeddus cyfrifol (cwyn am ryddid gwybodaeth). Gofalwch eich bod wedi anfon copi aton ni o’u hymateb terfynol ichi.\nRydyn ni wrthi’n helpu nifer fawr o bobl gyda’u cwynion ar hyn o bryd. Am yr amserlenni diweddaraf i ddyrannu achosion, ewch i'r dudalen gwneud cwyn<https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/> ar ein gwefan. Ymddiheurwn am yr oedi yma ond hoffem eich sicrhau ein bod yn cymryd eich cwyn o ddifrif.\nOs yw’ch gohebiaeth yn ymwneud ag achos sydd eisoes yn bod - byddwn yn ei hychwanegu at eich achos ac fe gaiff ei hystyried ar ôl cael ei dyrannu i swyddog achosion. Os ydych yn credu ein bod ni naill ai wedi methu cymryd camau priodol i ymateb i'ch cwyn diogelu data, neu heb ddarparu gwybodaeth ichi am gynnydd neu ganlyniad eich cwyn o fewn y tri mis nesaf, efallai y byddwch yn gallu gwneud cais i'r Tribiwnlys Haen Gyntaf i’w gwneud yn ofynnol inni ICO ymateb i'ch cwyn neu ddarparu gwybodaeth ichi am gynnydd eich cwyn. (www.gov.uk<http://www.gov.uk/> - information rights and data protection: appeal against the Information Commissioner)\nOs ydych wedi gofyn am gyngor – byddwn yn ymateb o fewn 14 diwrnod. Tra byddwch yn aros, dylech edrych yn rheolaidd ar ein gwefan<http://www.ico.org.uk/> (www.ico.org.uk<http://www.ico.org.uk/>) i chwilio am ganllawiau perthnasol, gan eu bod yn cael eu diweddaru drwy’r amser. Hefyd dylech ddarllen ein blogiau ynghylch ‘mythau’r GDPR<https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr>’. Os ydych wedi codi cwestiwn sydd wedi’i ateb ar ein gwefan, mae’n bosibl y byddwn yn ymateb drwy anfon dolen atoch i gysylltu â’r ateb.  Ond fe wnawn ein gorau glas i roi’r wybodaeth angenrheidiol ichi\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am drosedd data personol o dan y GDPR neu Ddeddf Diogelu Data 2018 – rydym yn anelu at gysylltu â chi o fewn saith niwrnod calendr i gadarnhau bod eich neges wedi dod i law ac i roi rhif cyfeirnod achos ichi. Os oes arnoch eisiau cyngor ar frys, dylech ffonio’n llinell gymorth ar [phone redacted]. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am roi gwybod am droseddau data ar ein gwefan.\nPan fo digwyddiad seibr arwyddocaol yn digwydd, mae’n bosibl y bydd angen ichi roi gwybod amdano hefyd i’r Ganolfan Seiberddiogelwch Genedlaethol (yr NCSC). I’ch helpu i benderfynu, dylech ddarllen canllawiau’r NCSC ar eu rôl a’r math o ddigwyddiadau y dylech ystyried rhoi gwybod amdanyn nhw. (www.ncsc.gov.uk<http://www.ncsc.gov.uk/> -incident-management)\nDylai digwyddiadau a allai arwain at risg uwch y bydd twyll yn effeithio ar unigolion gael eu cyfleu i Report Fraud (https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/) – sef canolfan genedlaethol y Deyrnas Unedig ar gyfer rhoi gwybod am dwyll a seiberdroseddau. Os yw eich sefydliad yn yr Alban, yna i Heddlu’r Alban y dylech chi roi gwybod (www.scotland.police.uk<http://www.scotland.police.uk/>).\nOs ydych yn Ddarparwr Gwasanaethau Cyfathrebu sy’n rhoi gwybod am dor diogelwch o dan y Rheoliadau Preifatrwydd a Chyfathrebu Electronig – bydd angen ichi roi gwybod am y tor diogelwch drwy’r porth diogel<https://report.ico.org.uk/security-breach/> sydd ar gael ar y tudalennau ar ein gwefan sy’n ymwneud â’r PECR.\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am ddigwyddiad posibl o dan Gyfarwyddeb yr NIS – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted ag y gallwn. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am Reoliadau’r NIS ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am dor diogelwch o fewn y diffiniad yn Rheoliad eIDAS – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted ag y gallwn. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am Reoliad eIDAS ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych wedi rhoi gwybod am ebost sbam – mae’n annhebygol y bydd angen inni gysylltu â chi eto, oni bai bod arnon ni angen rhagor o wybodaeth i helpu yn ein hymchwiliad. Rydym yn cyhoeddi gwybodaeth am y camau rydyn ni wedi’u cymryd ynghylch negeseuon niwsans ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych wedi gofyn am wybodaeth yr ydych yn credu ei bod gennyn ni – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi os bydd arnom angen rhagor o wybodaeth i’n helpu i ymateb. Fel arall, byddwn yn ymateb ichi o fewn ein lefelau gwasanaeth statudol a chyhoeddus. I gael rhagor o wybodaeth, ewch i’n tudalen gwe ‘request information from us’ (ewch i’n tudalen hafan a dilynwch y ddolen ‘about the ICO’ ac ‘our information’).\nOs ydych wedi anfon copi o’ch gohebiaeth aton ni ond dim byd arall – fyddwn ni ddim yn ymateb.\nMae gwybodaeth fanylach, gan gynnwys gwybodaeth am ein hamserau ymateb presennol, ar ein tudalen gwe safonau gwasanaeth a beth i’w ddisgwyl. Gallwch ffonio hefyd yn y Gymraeg ar [phone redacted] opsiwn 9 neu yn Saesneg ar [phone redacted]. Gallwch gysylltu â ni hefyd i gael sgwrs fyw (ewch i’n tudalen gwe ‘contact us’ a ‘live chat’).\nI gael gwybodaeth am yr hyn rydyn ni’n ei wneud â data personol, gweler ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd: https://ico.org.uk/global/privacy-notice/\nYn gywir\nSwyddfa’r Comisiynydd Gwybodaeth"},{"id":"gm-1a164d73591d629f","subject":"FOI complaint (s50) — Ministry of Justice / HMCTS, IR FOI 260813002, internal review of 9 October 2026","name":"FOI complaint (s50) — Ministry of Justice / HMCTS, IR FOI 260813002, internal review of 9 October 2026","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d73591d629f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a161f06b5caf28b-foi-complaint-s50-ministry-of-justice-hmcts-ir-foi-260813002-internal-review-of-9-october-2026","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a161f06b5caf28b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":["IR FOI 260813002"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d73591d629f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Commissioner's Office,\n\nComplaint under section 50 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 — Ministry of Justice / HM Courts & Tribunals Service, MoJ ref IR FOI 260813002 (internal review outcome letter of 9 October 2026)\n\nI ask the Commissioner to decide whether the Ministry of Justice dealt with my request in accordance with Part I of the Act.\n\nThe request and the dates\n- Request (MoJ ref 260813002): recorded information about court proceedings in 1988–1989 (Barry Magistrates' Court and Cardiff) connected with the eviction and demolition at Great House Farm, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, including (item 7) any retention, destruction, disposal or archive-transfer records for those court files, and (item 8) any file references, case numbers, register entries or archive references, even where the files themselves no longer survive.\n- Original response: 12 August 2026, information not held.\n- My request for internal review: 13 August 2026. The MoJ extended the review on 9 September 2026.\n- Internal review outcome: letter of 9 October 2026, upholding \"not held\" under section 1(1)(a).\n\nThe points I ask the Commissioner to decide\n1. Whether the MoJ made adequate searches. The review letter gives no description of any search: no system, no search term, no date range and no record series. Its conclusion rests on what \"may have been\" done with the records: that they \"may have been destroyed or transferred to an approved place of deposit\", and that it is \"likely\" they were disposed of or transferred.\n2. Whether items 7 and 8 were considered at all. They ask for administrative records about the files (retention and disposal schedules, destruction or disposal certificates, transfer and accession records, register or index entries), not for the case files. Records of that kind are created when files are destroyed or transferred, and may survive when the files do not. The review does not give a held / not held answer for either item. Without a search for, and an answer on, items 7 and 8, the conclusion that the information is \"not held\" under section 1(1)(a) has not been reached on an adequate basis.\n3. Whether the MoJ met its duty under section 16. The review suggests Glamorgan Archives \"may hold\" records transferred from HMCTS, but does not say whether any transfer list or accession record shows that court records for these courts and years were in fact transferred, or give any reference.\n4. Timeliness of the review: asked on 13 August 2026 and decided on 9 October 2026.\n\nWhat I ask the Commissioner to require\na. A held / not held answer for each numbered item, in particular items 7 and 8.\nb. A description of the searches made for each item (systems, terms, dates and record series, including any destruction registers, transfer lists or court record indexes).\nc. If any record was transferred to an archive, the receiving body and the reference.\n\nI can supply copies of the request, both responses and the extension letter on request.\n\nThis is a records complaint only. It makes no allegation against any individual.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d722d430fad","subject":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d722d430fad.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d-information-request-great-house-farm-t-y-mawr-near-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["historic-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["historic-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"historic-england","name":"Historic England"}],"refs":["26/04323"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d722d430fad.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Wilkins,\n\nOur Reference 26/04323 — request for reconsideration under regulation 11 of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004\n\nThank you for your response of 21 October 2026 and for identifying the microfiche transfer to RCAHMW. Please treat this email as representations under regulation 11, asking Historic England to reconsider its response on the points below only.\n\n1. Item 1 (the record of the transfer). Your response confirms that the section of the archaeological reports microfiche collection relating to sites in Wales was transferred to RCAHMW on 12 January 2018. Please confirm whether Historic England holds any record of that transfer itself (for example a covering letter or email, a transfer agreement, a receipt from RCAHMW, a box or batch list, a spreadsheet, index or manifest prepared before the transfer, or a file note recording the decision), even if it does not itemise individual fiche. If held, please provide a copy.\n\n2. Item 4 (the decision to transfer). Please confirm whether any record holds the date of the decision, the role of the officer who authorised it, and its basis. If held, please provide it; if not held, please say so.\n\n3. Item 6 (retained copies or destruction). Please confirm whether Historic England kept any copy, index or finding aid for the Welsh microfiche section after 12 January 2018, or a record of its destruction or retention.\n\n4. For each of items 1, 4 and 6, a held / not held answer and a short description of the search (systems, terms and dates) would be enough.\n\nI have no complaint about the rest of the response, which I found helpful.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any charge would apply, please tell me first and offer a free route (an electronic copy or inspection).\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d713cc77c18","subject":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d713cc77c18.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d713cc77c18.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Bev,\n\nMy email of 26 August 2026 — two points still open\n\nThank you again for your replies of 21 and 25 August. I wrote on 26 August with two short questions and have not had a reply, so I am asking again in this thread. Twenty working days from 26 August ended on 24 September 2026.\n\n1. Mary Doreen Williams (died March 1983): does your office hold any record of which coroner's jurisdiction covered Llandough Hospital in 1983, and of where that jurisdiction's registers and case papers went (a transfer list, accession record, or destruction or retention record), including the date on which any such records were handed to the Glamorgan Archivist? A held / not held answer is enough.\n\n2. William (Billy) Buckler (died 1990): your search note covered referrals received in 1983 or before. Was a 1990 referral capable of being found in the system you searched? If yes, please confirm the result for 1990. If no, please confirm whether Cardiff and Vale cases from 1990 are among those \"with the Glamorgan Archivist\", and give any transfer reference you hold.\n\n3. If these questions fall to Rhondda Cynon Taf Council's Freedom of Information team rather than to your office, please pass this email to them and let me know the reference. If it is treated as a request for recorded information, please treat this email as asking for an internal review of the lack of a reply to the email of 26 August.\n\nI am not asking for any medical information, only whether a record exists, where it is, or when and under what authority it was destroyed.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any charge would apply, please tell me first.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d701e8cac8f","subject":"Re: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211463 — clarification and refinement of request","name":"Re: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211463 — clarification and refinement of request","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:34Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d701e8cac8f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0c1c87a6f1717d-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00211463-clarification-and-refinement-of-request","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0c1c87a6f1717d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211463"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d701e8cac8f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Governance Officer,\n\nCase Ref 00211463 — no response received; request for internal review (regulation 11 EIR / section 45 Code of Practice)\n\nThe Council acknowledged this request on 17 September 2026. I clarified and refined it in this thread on 21 September 2026. Counting twenty working days from the clarification, a response was due by 19 October 2026. I have not received a response or a notice extending the time.\n\n1. Please treat this email as a request for an internal review of the failure to respond (regulation 11 of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004). The planning file for 89/01396/OUT, including the appendices to the officer's report, is environmental information under regulation 2(1)(c): it records a measure and activity affecting the use of land, namely the outline application for residential development at Great House Farm granted on 13 March 1990.\n\n2. Please send the response now, covering each item of my email of 21 September 2026: Appendices \"C\", \"D\" and \"E\" to the officer's report on 89/01396/OUT; the list of all appendices; any register or file list for the application; and Policy H.2 of the East Vale Local Plan with its supporting text as current in 1989–1990.\n\n3. For each item, a held / not held answer. Where an item is not held, please say what searches were made and, if the item was once on the file, when and how it ceased to be held, and under what retention schedule or disposal decision. A \"not held\" answer under regulation 12(4)(a) depends on an adequate search, so this explanation is part of the response.\n\n4. If the Council needs more time, please give the date by which it will respond.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any charge would apply, please tell me first and offer a free route (an electronic copy or inspection).\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d6eee708c9a","subject":"FOI request — location of closed or Discovery records relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (Valuation Office / IR58 / County Series)","name":"FOI request — location of closed or Discovery records relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (Valuation Office / IR58 / County Series)","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d6eee708c9a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a162bfa198ed55f-foi-request-location-of-closed-or-discovery-records-relating-to-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-valuation-office-ir58-","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a162bfa198ed55f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d6eee708c9a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Officer,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 for the location of any records held by The National Archives relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, in the parish of Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth), Glamorgan. The relevant Ordnance Survey County Series sheet is Glamorgan XLVII.6, as identified by Glamorgan Archives in its reply 2026/4097b of 30 September 2026. The request includes any Valuation Office survey field books (IR 58) and plans covering that sheet for that parish, and any related closed records.\n\nFor each item, please provide, before any consideration of viewing or copying:\n- the series, piece, accession, box, shelf or Discovery reference;\n- whether the item is open or closed;\n- if it is recorded as closed, transferred or held off-site, where it is now held;\n- whether staff have physically checked that the item is present in the store (the role of the person who checked, and the date of the check);\n- the systems searched, and whether a physical item was retrieved.\n\nThis is a location enquiry only. No viewing or copying is requested until the above is confirmed.\n\nPlease acknowledge and respond within the statutory 20 working days.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d6dc2533d83","subject":"Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d6dc2533d83.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d6dc2533d83.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear James,\n\nThank you for your detailed reply of 22 October, and for clarifying that your correspondence of 11 October reflected your assessment of the proposal as submitted, against the Council's Scrutiny work programming principles, rather than a formal decision of a Scrutiny Chair or Committee.\n\nI understand that scrutiny of this topic would not review individual cases or revisit an individual historic planning decision, would not determine private title, and would not replace the statutory information-rights procedures. I also note that final agreement rests with the relevant Scrutiny Committee and Chair, that the Committee does not currently have capacity for another Task and Finish review while it completes its current piece of work, and that a new topic remains subject to the Council's normal work programming process.\n\nOn that basis, I wish to pursue a separate, county-wide topic as follows.\n\nProposed title: Management of, and public access to, historic planning, land-charges and heritage records.\n\nPurpose: To consider whether the Council's arrangements for retaining, transferring, cataloguing, locating and providing access to historic records are clear, effective and appropriately documented. Reliable historic records matter to any resident, landowner or conveyancer tracing the planning and land-charges history of land anywhere in the Vale.\n\nProposed scope:\n\n1. The policies, responsibilities and procedures for retaining, transferring, disposing of, indexing and retrieving historic records, including records inherited from predecessor authorities at the 1996 local government reorganisation and earlier reorganisations, how those handovers were documented, and records held on paper or in off-site archives.\n\n2. How searches for historic records are carried out and documented, and how missing, incomplete or unlocated files, appendices and supporting material are identified and explained.\n\n3. How requests for access to historic planning, land-charges and heritage information are received, routed, monitored and answered.\n\n4. Whether published procedures, allocation of responsibilities, record-search practices and service standards could be improved.\n\nThe Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) matter is the background to this suggestion, but it is not a request for Scrutiny to determine, review or revisit that case or any other individual case. I note your point that a topic of this kind would not reflect upon or review individual cases, and I am content for the work to proceed entirely at the level of the Council's systems and practices.\n\nThe proposed work would concern policy, governance, records management and service delivery. It would not ask Scrutiny to determine property ownership, make findings about individual liability, or decide the merits of a historic planning decision. My outstanding information requests, including the internal review of EIR request 00210772 and the requests concerning the missing planning appendices, will continue separately through the information-rights routes.\n\nI will submit this as a separate topic suggestion through the Scrutiny Topic Suggestion Form linked from the Council's published Scrutiny webpage (https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/our_council/Council-Structure/scrutiny/scrutiny.aspx).\n\nAs the topic spans both historic planning records and corporate records management, I would welcome your advice, or that of Democratic and Scrutiny Services, on which committee or committees it falls under within their current remits.\n\nI would also be grateful to take up your offer to help direct the proposal through the appropriate work programming process. If it cannot be scheduled as Task and Finish work at present, could you please advise whether it can be recorded for a future work programme or considered in another proportionate scrutiny format?\n\nI am not asking for any particular outcome to be predetermined; I understand the decision whether to include the topic rests with the relevant Committee and Chair.\n\nThank you again for clarifying the process. I would be grateful if you could confirm receipt of this email.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d6cc1c5ea3d","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d6cc1c5ea3d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1645f237df4972-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-transfer-or-dispose","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1645f237df4972","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":["2026/4461"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d6cc1c5ea3d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Russell,\n\nThank you for your reply of 22 October (your ref. 2026/4461) to my preservation notice of 28 September, and for confirming that everything Glamorgan Archives holds has been designated for permanent preservation and will not be destroyed. I accept that as Glamorgan Archives' answer on preservation, and I note that you do not hold planning files.\n\nTo complete the record, may I ask four short points:\n\n1. Planning Committee papers DCVG/C/4/36/76-77 and DCVG/C/4/36/94 (applications 1989/01396/OUT and 1992/00671/RES). Could you confirm whether the officer's report for 1989/01396/OUT, as held in these items, includes its appendices (the report refers to Appendices B to E), and whether these items are open to the public or subject to any closure or depositor restriction? I would be grateful for a quotation for copies of the pages concerning Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, or, if copying is not possible, I will book a searchroom appointment.\n\n2. As my notice asked, could you briefly say what was searched (for example, the catalogue terms and series checked), so that the answer is complete for each item in scope?\n\n3. Do you hold any planning registers, land charges registers or building control records deposited by the Vale of Glamorgan Council, South Glamorgan County Council, or the district council responsible for Llandough before 1974, covering this land? If so, please give the references.\n\n4. Your colleague's reply 2026/4439 identified DBDT/123/7 (a 1939 tenancy of 5.30 acres). Does the same collection include any papers on the 1877 division of the holding or the 1938 conveyance from the Bute estate to Western Ground Rents Ltd? If so, please give the references.\n\nI do not need anything further on the preservation point itself. Thank you for your help.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a164d6a51fd045c","subject":"RE: FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","name":"RE: FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","date":"2026-10-22T18:19:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a164d6a51fd045c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf-foi-2026-024-032-036-c-1880-medieval-ironwork-from-great-house-farm-llandough-published-sources-say-it-is-in-the-nationa","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":["FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a164d6a51fd045c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,\n\nFOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — clarification of point 2 (your email of 20 October 2026)\n\nThank you for your email of 20 October. My answer is your first option: I am seeking records relating specifically to the c.1880 discovery at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (near Penarth and Cardiff, Vale of Glamorgan), the farm beside St Dochdwy's Church. I am not seeking all records of medieval ironwork that match the search terms regardless of any connection to that discovery.\n\nTo identify the discovery:\n\n1. The find is the medieval ironwork discovered under the rear wing of the farmhouse c.1880, as described in the two published sources quoted in my email of 19 October: GGAT, \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological Assessment\" (August 1990, citing RCAHMW 1988), and Holbrook and Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70, n. 142. Both state that the ironwork is held by the National Museum.\n\n2. Point 2 is therefore limited to collection, accession, register or object records for medieval ironwork (including a visor, lance head, helmet or horse equipment), acquired or recorded from 1880 to 1930, whose findspot, provenance or donor note links the object to this site. Because older entries may use a variant form, please include entries recorded as \"Great House Farm\", \"Great House, Llandough\", \"Tŷ Mawr\" or \"Ty Mawr\", \"Cedfin\" (the name used for Tŷ Mawr in the 1824 Bute estate survey), \"Llandough-juxta-Penarth\", or \"Llandough, near Penarth / Cardiff\", including entries carried over from the former Cardiff Museum's registers. An entry giving only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" is relevant only if the record ties it to Penarth or Cardiff, or to the c.1880 find. This excludes the Great House Farm at Llandough near Cowbridge.\n\n3. If a search on that basis would still exceed the cost limit, please tell me under section 16 which part can be done within it, and I will narrow further.\n\n4. A held / not held answer, with a short description of the systems and terms searched, would be enough.\n\nYour email concerned point 2 only, so I understand points 1, 3 and 4 of my email of 19 October are proceeding. Please confirm the date by which you now expect to respond.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any charge would apply, please tell me first and offer a free route (an electronic copy or inspection).\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1645f237df4972","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","date":"2026-10-22T16:08:34Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1645f237df4972.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1645f237df4972-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-transfer-or-dispose","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1645f237df4972","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":["2026/4461"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1645f237df4972.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ref: 2026/4461\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email received into our system 29th September.\n\nGlamorgan Archives collect, catalogue, preserve and make available records relating to the history of Glamorgan and its people. The things that we hold have been designated suitable for permanent preservation and will not be destroyed. It is possible to search our catalogue of holdings via our online catalogue https://glamarchives.gov.uk/collection/ . It is possible to view these records in our public searchroom. Full details of our location, opening times and how to make an appointment can be found on our website www.glamarchives.gov.uk . The Glamorgan Archivist is Laura Cotton.\n\nGlamorgan Archives do not hold planning files. We do hold copies of Planning Committee minutes and reports. The document references for these are: DCVG/C/4/36/76-77 and DCVG/C/4/36/94 these are for the planning applications 1989/01396/OUT and 1992/00671/RES.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nLaura Russell\nArchifydd / Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk\nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives\nwww.twitter.com/glamarchives \n\nNodwch: rydw i’n gweithio ar Ddydd Iau a Dydd Gwener yn unig. Os hoffech chi gysylltu ag Archifau Morgannwg tu allan yr oriau hyn, e-bostiwch [email redacted] os gwelwch yn dda.\n\nPlease note I work Thursday and Friday.  If you wish to contact the Archives outside these hours please email [email redacted]  \n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 28 September 2026 22:42\nTo: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose\n\nTo each recipient, in your own capacity as holder or likely holder of records. Please do not treat this as a joint reply. Answer only for your own holdings.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a preservation notice. It is not a claim form and not service of proceedings. It does not replace any FOI, review or subject access request already with you.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's. Titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690, WA735527, and any related title. Planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, transfer out of your custody without a written receipt, or dispose of, any file, plan, photograph, tape or electronic record in your possession, custody or control relating to:\n\n1. The 1877 split, the 1916 and 1939 tenancies, and the 1938 Bute to Western Ground Rents conveyance.\n2. The 1955 and 1962 possession orders, the 1974 proceedings, and BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n3. First registration: WA231076 application 30 November 1982; WA240304 application 23 February 1983; later amalgamation.\n4. The 1988 possession (29 November) and demolition (begun 6 December), including listing, planning, police and any liaison papers.\n5. Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler, so far as your file concerns this land.\n\nAlso preserve, if you hold them, the following planning and land-charge classes. Absence from a 2026 file disclosure is not proof they never existed:\n\n6. Any section 52 Town and Country Planning Act 1971 agreement, later section 106 instrument, deed, undertaking or other agreement regulating the development or use of this land, and any corresponding local-land-charge entry.\n7. The historic planning-register entries required by the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES (applications, reserved matters, plans and drawings, and decision information).\n8. The officer's report annexes to 89/01396/OUT, including Appendix B (further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust), and Appendices C–E.\n9. The condition chain on 89/01396/OUT: conditions 16–18; the Council's October 1990 confirmation of condition 17; GGAT's July 1992 archaeological warning; the September 1992 reserved-matters approval; and the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged.\n10. Any preliminary environmental-assessment / screening determination for the outline application (site described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38 ha).\n11. Any record of the statutory consultation route used because the land was, or was treated as, a site of archaeological interest / SMR entry under the 1988 Order.\n12. The complete 92/00671/RES file, and any sale, option, conditional-contract or transfer paper on the planning files covering BP Properties to Ideal Homes Wales, including the recorded transfer of\n3 December 1993.\n13. The application-receipt record for 89/01396/OUT (form dated October 1989; reconstructed Council receipt 8 November 1989).\n\nPlease stop routine deletion, including archived mailboxes, for anything in that scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n. The investigation distinguishes the farmhouse parcel from the eastern fields. The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These records go to that question. This notice is not a finding against any of you.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer responsible for the hold, and say what you hold in scope. If you hold nothing, say what you searched.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the register.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]\n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a163b9bb8538edf","subject":"Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-361652-D3X8X9 CRM:005401570","name":"Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-361652-D3X8X9 CRM:005401570","date":"2026-10-22T13:07:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a163b9bb8538edf.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a163b9bb8538edf-freedom-of-information-request-reference-cas-361652-d3x8x9-crm-005401570","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a163b9bb8538edf","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-361652-D3X8X9"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a163b9bb8538edf.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your request received on 16/10/2026 07:00 for corporate information (business records) held by The National Archives.\n\nWe are handling your request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and have given it reference number CAS-361652-D3X8X9\n\nWe will respond to you by 13/11/2026 18:00 in accordance with the 20 working-day time period laid down by section 10 of the Act.\n\nYou can find out more about Freedom of Information on our website: www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/foi/<http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/foi/>\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nFOI Centre Service Advisor\nFreedom of Information Centre\nPublic Access and Government Services Directorate\nThe National Archives\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-1a1635f9eb7683f5","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-22T11:29:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1635f9eb7683f5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["blake-morgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["blake-morgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a","direction":"received","from":"Info","institutions":[{"id":"blake-morgan","name":"Blake Morgan LLP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1635f9eb7683f5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello\n\nThis was an old file from our London office which was closed in 1996.  There are no records of anything remaining in storage.\n\nKR\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:35\nTo: Info <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest\n\n\nCaution: This email originated from outside Blake Morgan LLP. DO NOT CLICK on links or open attachments unless you recognise the sender and know the content is safe. If unsure please contact the IT Service Desk for assistance.\nDear Blake Morgan,\n\nFollow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026 – BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 31 July 1987) – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough\n\nI wrote to you on 28 September 2026, among other recipients, asking that records about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, be preserved. I have not yet had a reply, so I am following it up with a more specific question.\n\nThe reported Court of Appeal judgment in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 (31 July 1987) records that counsel for the appellant, Mr W. Buckler, were instructed by Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn, acting as agents for Loosemores of Cardiff. I understand that Blake Morgan was formed in 2012 by the merger of Blake Lapthorn and Morgan Cole.\n\nI would be grateful if you would tell me:\n1. whether Blake Morgan is the successor to the practice of Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn, or holds any of its records;\n2. whether any file, correspondence, brief to counsel, attendance note or court document from the 1986–87 proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, or any later matter concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, survives in Blake Morgan's records or archive storage (including any deeds or papers held in safe custody);\n3. if such records were destroyed or transferred, the date, the retention policy applied, and to whom any file was transferred (for example, to Loosemores or to the client);\n4. what searches were made to answer this, and whether any physical or archived files were checked.\n\nI am not asking for privileged content at this stage, only whether the records exist, where they are, and their history. Please also make sure that nothing relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr or these proceedings is destroyed while these enquiries are open. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com>\nOn Fri, Oct 16, 2026 at 07:04 AM, possessions.cardiff.countycourt <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Blake Morgan, Follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026 – BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 31 July 1987) – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough I wrote to you on 28 September 2026, among other recipients, asking that records about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandou\n[Image removed by sender.]<***REDACTED***>\nCGBANNERINDICATOR\n\nOFFICIAL\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your email dated 28 September 2026 at 22:40\n\nDo you have any Claim Number relating to the below?\n\nRegards\n\nNeil Jones\n\nAdran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\nHMCTS/GLlTEM Canolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd / Cardiff Civil Justice Centre\n2 Stryd y Parc / 2 Park Street\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\nDX: 99500 CARDIFF 6\n\nFfon / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\nHere is how HMCTS uses personal data about you<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter> | Dyma sut mae GLlTEM yn defnyddio data personol amdanoch chi<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter.cy>\n\n\n\n“I am not authorised to bind the Ministry of Justice contractually, nor to make representations or other statements which may bind the Ministry of Justice in any way via electronic means”\n\n\nYSTYRIWCH YR AMGYLCHEDD - OES RHAID I CHI BRINTIO'R E-BOST HWN?\nPLEASE CONSIDER THE ENVIRONMENT - DO YOU REALLY NEED TO PRINT THIS E-MAIL?\n\n\n‘For information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see:\nAm wybodaeth ynghylch sut mae GLlTEF yn defnyddio data personol amdanoch chi, ewch i: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter<http://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter>\n\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD5D44.F0846270][cid:image002.png@01DD5D44.F0846270]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 28 September 2026 22:40\nTo: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; BP Archive <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; FOI Requests <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Cardiff County, Enquiries <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nCc: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Connor McGilly <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; MRC_Archive, Resource <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; possessions.cardiff.countycourt <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; BPC.Cardiff <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Administrative Court Office Cardiff <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Disclosure Team <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; NSUKilo <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Paul Egan <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Julian Wilkes <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; _FOI email address <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Customer Support <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Davidson, Victoria <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Contact OneVale <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; DOUGHTY, Stephen <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; CAIRNS Alun <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]; Pwyllgor Diwylliant, Cyfathrebu, y Gymraeg a Chwaraeon - Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest\n\n\nFORMAL PRESERVATION NOTICE\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nTitles: WA231076, WA240304, WA513690 and WA735527\nPlanning references: 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES\n\nURL: greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<http://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com>\n\nTo each recipient separately, in your own capacity as a current or potential holder, custodian or controller of relevant records:\n\nThis notice is addressed to each recipient individually. It is not a joint request, and it does not ask any recipient to speak for, investigate on behalf of, or answer in place of any other person or organisation. Each recipient is asked to respond only in respect of records within that recipient's own possession, custody or control, including records inherited from a predecessor organisation or retained on its behalf.\n\n1. Nature and purpose of this notice\n\nThis is a formal preservation notice concerning documentary material relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's, and the subsequent development of the site, including the area now associated with Church View Close.\n\nIt is not a claim form, is not service of proceedings, and is not intended to constitute or replace any FOI request, internal review, complaint, subject-access request or other statutory process already made to any recipient.\n\nThe purpose of this notice is to require the preservation of potentially relevant material while the documentary history, title chain, registration history, planning history, possession proceedings, demolition and subsequent development are being reconstructed.\n\nA separate first-stage preservation notice has been issued or is being issued to Cadw / Welsh Government FOI, HM Land Registry Wales Office and DPO, Heneb / GGAT HER, RCAHMW, Vale of Glamorgan FOI Unit and DPO, Glamorgan Archives, South Wales Police FOI, The National Archives, the Wales Office FOI team, and the National Library of Wales. Persimmon Homes (Wales) Ltd has received a separate preservation letter.\n\nYou are receiving this notice separately because the published documentary record places you, or a predecessor whose records may remain in your custody or control, within the documentary, legal, professional, administrative or development chain concerning this land.\n\n2. Land and documentary scope\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, alter, overwrite, discard, transfer out of custody without a recorded handover, or otherwise dispose of, any record within your possession, custody or control relating to the land or matters identified below.\n\nThe scope includes, without limitation, originals, copies, working papers, drafts, annotations, plans, photographs, negatives, films, tapes, maps, registers, indexes, correspondence, emails and attachments, electronic files, archived mailboxes, databases, metadata, internal notes, meeting records, instructions, client or matter files, survey material and other associated records.\n\nThe material requested includes:\n\n1. Historical ownership, occupation and conveyancing\n\nThe 1877 split; the 1916 and 1939 tenancies; the 1938 Bute to Western Ground Rents conveyance; the 1969 Western Ground Rents to BP Pension Trust conveyance; and any plans, schedules, abstracts, searches, correspondence or other documents relied upon in relation to those transactions.\n\n2. Possession proceedings and subsequent litigation\n\nThe 1955 High Court and 1962 Cardiff County Court possession orders; the 1974 proceedings; BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2; House of Lords leave papers, including YHL/PO/JO/10/11/2536; and Buckler v United Kingdom (1989), including associated correspondence, instructions, evidence, plans and working papers.\n\n3. Land registration\n\nThe first registration of WA231076, including the application dated 30 November 1982; the first registration of WA240304, including the application dated 23 February 1983; subsequent amalgamation, transfer or closure; and every plan, conveyance, abstract, search, application, correspondence trail or professional file relied upon in connection with those registrations or changes.\n\n4. 1988 possession and demolition\n\nThe taking of possession on or about 29 November 1988 and the demolition commenced on or about 6 December 1988, including any planning, listed-building, heritage, police, enforcement, media, contractor, survey, photographic or inter-agency liaison material.\n\n5. Planning and subsequent development, 1989–1996\n\nPlanning application 89/01396/OUT; reserved matters application 92/00671/RES; conditions 16–18; GGAT / Cotswold Archaeology material; records concerning any section 52, section 106, planning obligation, local land charge or equivalent instrument; and the transfer from BP to Ideal Homes dated 3 December 1993, together with all associated plans, correspondence, approvals, agreements, searches and completion material.\n\n6. Family records\n\nRecords concerning Mary Doreen Williams (died 1983) and William Buckler, insofar as those records relate to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, the land described above, its occupation, ownership, possession, disposal, registration, development or demolition.\n\n3. Predecessor and inherited files\n\nWhere you hold, or may hold, a file originating with a predecessor, successor, merged practice, affiliated practice, client or other entity, that material is also within scope.\n\nThis includes, without limitation, records originating from:\n\nLoosemores of Cardiff; Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn / Blake Morgan; Linklaters & Paines; Debenham Tewson / DTZ / Cushman & Wakefield; Wyn Thomas + Partners; Ideal Homes Wales; BP Properties; BP Pension Trust; Cotswold Archaeological Trust; Cardiff Bay Development Corporation; and South Glamorgan County Council.\n\nThe reference to a predecessor file does not assert that you necessarily hold such a file. It identifies material for which a reasonable custody or succession inquiry should be made where applicable.\n\n4. Preservation steps\n\nPlease take reasonable steps to prevent the routine destruction, deletion, alteration or overwriting of potentially relevant material, including material held in archived mailboxes, legacy systems, off-site storage, document-management systems, backup repositories and other electronic or physical stores.\n\nWhere relevant material has been transferred to another repository, archive, successor organisation or third party, please preserve the information necessary to identify the transfer and its current location, including any accession, file, box, reference or custody details.\n\nNothing in this notice requires the creation of records that do not exist. The request concerns the preservation of records already held or controlled by you.\n\n5. Purpose and legal position\n\nThis notice is not a finding against any recipient, and I am not asking any recipient to determine title or adjudicate the underlying dispute.\n\nThe 1987 Court of Appeal judgment is relied upon here only for matters actually determined by that judgment, including the issues concerning possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. This preservation notice does not treat that judgment as having determined the complete documentary root of title to the farmhouse parcel.\n\nThe underlying documentary history, including the relationship between the farmhouse parcel and the agricultural land subsequently dealt with through Western Ground Rents and BP, remains a matter requiring reconstruction from the primary records.\n\nAccordingly, preservation is requested precisely so that the documentary record can be established from the records themselves rather than through assumptions based on later registration, later occupation, later planning treatment or secondary descriptions.\n\n6. Acknowledgement and identification of records\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt of this notice and, in your own capacity, confirm:\n\n(a) the officer, partner, records manager or other person responsible for implementing the preservation hold;\n\n(b) what records within your possession, custody or control you have identified as falling within the scope above; and\n\n(c) where you identify no records within scope, what relevant systems, files, repositories or predecessor records you searched in reaching that conclusion.\n\nA substantive assessment of title is not requested from you. The immediate requirement is preservation and identification of the documentary material you hold.\n\nThe public documentary index and developing evidence record is available at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/>\n\nPlease monitor that site for subsequent identification of documents, references and specific schedules relevant to your organisation's records.\n\nWhere a reliable public email address is unavailable, a postal preservation notice will also be sent. For example, a postal notice will follow to Loosemores, Alliance House, 18–19 High Street, Cardiff [postcode redacted].\n\nNothing in this notice constitutes an abandonment, waiver or limitation of any claim, position or remedy concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening, rectification or alteration of the register, or any associated matter.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a162f0c37aaddcc","subject":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-22T09:28:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a162f0c37aaddcc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"received","from":"Langridge-Thomas, James","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a162f0c37aaddcc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for your e-mail below.\n\nI note your comments regarding the distinction between the specific circumstances of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) and the broader issue you have identified concerning the Council's arrangements for the retention, transfer, accessibility and disclosure of historic planning, land charges and heritage records. I also note your comments regarding the ongoing Environmental Information Regulations review process, which, as you acknowledge, is being pursued through the appropriate information-rights channels.\n\nIn relation to the points raised:\n\n1. County-wide and strategic considerations\n\nI acknowledge your view that the wider issue of how historic planning, land charges and heritage records are managed and made available is capable of being distinguished from the individual circumstances of any single site and may have broader relevance across the county. The decision not to progress the proposed Task and Finish review related to the proposal as submitted and reflected the assessment that the matters raised were closely connected to a specific historical planning case and ongoing information-rights processes.\n\nThat said, a proposal focusing specifically on the Council's records management arrangements, access to historic planning information, and the handling of requests for such information could represent a broader issue of potential county-wide application and may be considered separately through the Council's Scrutiny work programming process in conjunction with the relevant Scrutiny Chair. However, for clarity sake, this would not reflect upon or review individual cases.\n\n2. Alternative channels\n\nIn response to your request for clarification regarding the alternative channels referred to in my previous correspondence:\n\n(a) Missing, incomplete or contradictory planning and heritage records\n\nThe appropriate route will depend on the nature of the concern. Matters relating to planning records held by the Council would ordinarily be raised with the relevant service area in the first instance. Requests for recorded information are appropriately pursued through the Environmental Information Regulations or Freedom of Information processes where access to information is sought. Matters concerning records management may also be raised through the Council's corporate complaints process where the complaint relates to service delivery rather than the application of information-rights legislation.\n\n(b) The Council's handling of information requests\n\nDissatisfaction with the handling of EIR or FOI requests should ordinarily be pursued through the statutory information-rights process, namely an internal review followed, where appropriate, by a complaint to the Information Commissioner's Office. The corporate complaints process would not generally be used to challenge the outcome of an information request or an information-rights decision, as there are separate processes and policies underpinned by different legislation and regulators.\n\nQuestions\n\n1. Was the decision of 11 October taken by officers, or by the Chair or Chairs of the relevant Scrutiny Committee? Under which provision of the Council's Constitution or Scrutiny Procedure Rules was it taken?\n\nThe correspondence of 11 October reflected my assessment of the proposal against the Council's established Scrutiny work programming principles and was not a formal decision of a Scrutiny Chair or Committee. In undertaking that assessment, I considered whether the proposal met the criteria normally applied when determining potential items for inclusion within a Scrutiny Committee work programme as outlined above. As I'm sure you will appreciate, we receive many correspondence through this channel relating to on-going case work type scenarios and requesting for Scrutiny which is not the appropriate route, it is not reasonably practicable for a Chair to be cited upon the specifics of operational matters which are addressed or resolved by other means.\n\nAs the matter had not been referred to a Scrutiny Chair or Committee for determination, no formal decision was taken by a Committee under the Scrutiny Procedure Rules.\n\n2. Will the narrower, county-wide topic be considered as a Scrutiny topic suggestion?\n\nShould you wish to submit a proposal focused specifically on the Council's arrangements for maintaining, managing and providing access to historic planning, land charges and heritage records, that may be considered as a Scrutiny topic suggestion in its own right. However, finally agreement is the responsibility of the Scrutiny Committee and Chair, and it should be noted and to manage expectation, that they currently do not currently have sufficient capacity to undertake another Task and Finish scrutiny as they are currently undertaking another piece of work.\n\nI would be happy to assist in directing such a proposal through the appropriate process. A separate topic suggestion can be submitted via the Council's website as below, but will be subject to the same considerations that have previously been mentioned and subject to agreement by the relevant Committee Chair - https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/our_council/Council-Structure/scrutiny/scrutiny.aspxDemocratic\n\n3. Can a ward member refer the matter as a Councillor Call for Action, and if so, how?\n\nA ward member may request Scrutiny consideration of a matter of local concern. This would normally be pursued through the relevant Scrutiny Committee and Democratic and Scrutiny Services can provide guidance on the process should a ward member wish to pursue that route.\n\nIt may be helpful to note that Scrutiny's role is generally to examine policies, services, performance, and matters of wider public interest rather than to investigate or determine individual cases which could be considered a Member's ward work. Consequently, any consideration by Scrutiny would be expected to focus on broader policy, governance, records management or service delivery issues that are currently operational with recommendations for enhancement (and not decisions for clarity sake) rather than the specific circumstances of an individual historic planning case.\n\n4. Does the Council's corporate complaints procedure apply to the handling of records requests, as distinct from the information-rights routes?\n\nAs a general principle and set out above, complaints concerning the handling of requests made under the Environmental Information Regulations, Freedom of Information Act or data protection legislation are expected to be addressed through the relevant statutory review and appeal mechanisms, namely an internal review followed, and thereafter, where appropriate, by a complaint to the Information Commissioner's Office. The corporate complaints process would not generally be used to in relation to information requests handling,  the outcome of an information request or an information-rights decision, as there are separate processes and policies underpinned by different legislation and regulations and a separate regulator.\n\nThe corporate complaints procedure may, however, be relevant where a complaint concerns wider service standards or administrative matters that fall outside the scope of the statutory information-rights regime. Whether a matter falls within the corporate complaints process will depend on the specific nature of the complaint.\n\nI trust the above clarifies the position.\n\nKind Regards,\nJames\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 21 October 2026 16:17\nTo: Langridge-Thomas, James <[email redacted]>\nCc: Democratic <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough\n\nDear James,\n\nThank you for your email of 11 October 2026 explaining why Scrutiny will not take forward the Task and Finish suggestion for Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough. I accept that a Task and Finish review is not the place to re-examine an individual historical planning decision. I have three points in reply and four short questions.\n\nOn your reasons:\n\n1. County-wide and strategic. Part of the proposal does meet that test, and it can be put on its own: how the Council keeps, transfers and disposes of historic planning, land-charges and heritage records, and how it answers requests for them. That affects every resident who asks for an old planning file. It is not limited to one site. The Great House Farm requests show the problem: the internal review of EIR request 00210772, requested on 7 July 2026, still has no outcome, beyond the 40 working days set by regulation 11(4) of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. And planning appendices C, D and E of the same file are still not supplied.\n\n2. \"Other channels\". Your email says the matter should be \"navigated through other channels\" but does not say which ones. Please name the channel the Council considers correct for each of: (a) missing or contradictory Council-held planning and heritage records; (b) the Council's own handling of its records requests.\n\n3. Other bodies involved. That Welsh Government, Cadw and elected members are also involved goes to how scrutiny is coordinated. With respect, it is not a reason the Council's own records cannot be looked at.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Was the decision of 11 October taken by officers, or by the Chair or Chairs of the relevant Scrutiny Committee? Under which provision of the Council's Constitution or Scrutiny procedure rules was it taken?\n2. Will the narrower, county-wide topic in point 1 above be considered as a Scrutiny topic suggestion? If a form is needed, please send it or link to it and I will complete it.\n3. Can a ward member refer the matter as a Councillor Call for Action, and if so, how?\n4. Does the Council's corporate complaints procedure apply to the handling of records requests, as distinct from the information-rights routes?\n\nFor clarity on where things stand: the information-rights routes (internal review, then a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA and regulation 18 EIR) are being followed separately and are not repeated here. Routes not yet used are the corporate complaints procedure, a referral by a ward member, and then the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales. I would rather the Council's own scrutiny process dealt with the county-wide records question first.\n\nA reply within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026, would be appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester [email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a162e42b9146d7b","subject":"RE: South Wales Constabulary records, November–December 1988 — Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: South Wales Constabulary records, November–December 1988 — Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-22T09:14:37Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a162e42b9146d7b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0cab95d9806099-south-wales-constabulary-records-november-december-1988-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0cab95d9806099","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":["2026/4460"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a162e42b9146d7b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ref 2026/4460\n\nDear Requester\n\nMany thanks for your email received onto our system on 28 September 2026.\n\nI will answer each question in turn\n\n\n  1.  We do not have any occurrence books that cover that period and area. The Occurrence books<https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSWP/1> only go as far as 1984. The Station logs and duty books<https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSWP/3> end at 1979, and Divisional crime registers<https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSWP/4> end in 1971.\n  2.  We do have South Wales Constabulary Weekly Orders<https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSWP/8/12>, including the one for 1988. These include a mix of regular operational and staff updates. These may include reference to evictions, however, as they include details of serving police members you will not be able to access these volumes. You may wish to commission a paid search of these items to determine if there is anything of interest.\n  3.  We do not have any press office or public relations files for this period.\n  4.  Publicly available information on accessions can be found on the collection level description on our catalogue. DSWP’s CLD can be found at South Wales Police Constabulary Records<https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSWP>. This catalogue includes everything that was deposited by South Wales Police- you may wish to have a browse of the records to determine if there is  anything else of interest.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKatie\n\n\nKatie Finn\nArchifydd | Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted] | Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n( [phone redacted]\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk<http://www.glamro.gov.uk/>\nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives<http://www.facebook.com/glamarchives>\nwww.twitter.com/glamarchives\nInstagram: glamarchives\n\nBydd Archifau Morgannwg yn sicrhau ein bod yn cyfathrebu â chi yn yr iaith o'ch dewis, boed hynny'n Gymraeg, yn Saesneg neu'n ddwyieithog cyn belled ag y byddwch yn rhoi gwybod i ni pa well gennych. Rydych yn derbyn y wybodaeth hon yn y Saesneg gan fod hyn wedi ei gofnodi fel eich dewis iaith. Os hoffech chi ddiweddaru'r wybodaeth hon neu ddewis peidio â derbyn y negeseuon e-bost hyn, cysylltwch â ni: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. | Glamorgan Archives will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, whether that’s English, Welsh or bilingual as long as you let us know which you prefer. You are receiving this information in English as this is recorded as your language preference. If you would like to update this information or opt out of receiving these emails please contact us at [email redacted]<[email redacted]>.\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 27 September 2026 05:17\nTo: Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>\nSubject: South Wales Constabulary records, November–December 1988 — Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\nALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\nDear Glamorgan Archives Team,\n\nI am researching the eviction and demolition at Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, between 29 November and 6 December 1988. South Wales Constabulary officers were present. I understand from the South Wales Police Heritage Centre that Glamorgan Archives holds records of South Wales Police and its predecessor forces.\n\nCould you tell me whether you hold any of the following for late 1988, and their references and access conditions:\n\n1. Occurrence books, station or duty records for the division covering Llandough (Penarth, Barry or Cardiff).\n2. Operational orders or files for police attendance at evictions, sheriff's or bailiffs' enforcement, or breach-of-the-peace deployments.\n3. Press office or public relations files for November–December 1988.\n4. Any deposit list or transfer schedule for South Wales Constabulary records covering 1985–1990, so I can see what was and was not deposited.\n\nI also hold references ACA/8/2 (your ref 2026–3941) and 2026/3893 from earlier enquiries, if that helps connect this to my existing file.\n\nIf some records are closed, please tell me the closure period and whether I can apply for access to the parts that concern my family.\n\nDiolch,\nRequester \ngreathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<http://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com>\n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a162d2a3641b73c","subject":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-22T08:55:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a162d2a3641b73c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6-foi-request-western-ground-rents-ltd-company-no-00342092-dissolved-1997-any-bona-vacantia-property-or-interests-at-lland","scopeTopics":["bona-vacantia"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bona-vacantia"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6","direction":"received","from":"Dan Copping","institutions":[{"id":"bona-vacantia","name":"Government Legal Department (Bona Vacantia)"}],"refs":["FOIR26#25631/1"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a162d2a3641b73c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Requester's Tab agent\n\nThe reference number for the request is FOIR26#25631/1.\n\nKind regards\n\nDan Copping\nfor the Treasury Solicitor\n\nwww.gov.uk/bonavacantia\n\nA copy of our Privacy Notice can be found here:\nhttps://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/bona-vacantia/about/personal-information-charter\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 21 October 2026 17:24\nTo: Dan Copping <[email redacted]>\nCc: BVFOI <[email redacted]>\nSubject: RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nDear Mr Copping,\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026 confirming that my request of 20 October about Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) is being considered under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nFor the record:\n1. Under section 10(1), the 20 working-day limit for the response falls on 17 November 2026. Please let me have your reference number for the request.\n2. Please make sure that any file, index entry or referral record about Western Ground Rents Ltd, or about property at Llandough, Leckwith, Cogan or Penarth, is preserved while the request and any review are open.\n3. One further point, within the same request: if any property of the company vested in the Crown on dissolution in 1997 (section 654 of the Companies Act 1985, as then in force), please also say whether it was later disclaimed (section 656), sold or otherwise dealt with, and the date. If the Division's records for companies dissolved in 1997 have been destroyed or transferred, please say so, with the retention schedule applied. Section 16 FOIA expects that advice.\n\nIf no response is received by 17 November 2026, I will ask for an internal review and, after that, complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester [email redacted]\n\n________________________________\nThe information in this e-mail belongs to HM Government and may be confidential or otherwise protected by law. If you received it in error, we request that you inform us by return e-mail and then delete it immediately, without printing, copying or disseminating it.\nThe original of this email was scanned for viruses by Government Secure Intranet (GSi) virus scanning service supplied by Vodafone in partnership with MessageLabs. HM Government does not however warrant that it is virus free at point of delivery."},{"id":"gm-1a162d1a1d4be7f8","subject":"[NLW English] Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy","name":"[NLW English] Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy","date":"2026-10-22T08:54:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a162d1a1d4be7f8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190-nlw-english-research-enquiry-bute-estate-records-gb-0210-bute-d153-d219-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a162d1a1d4be7f8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nOct 22 2026, 09:54AM via System\n\nDear Requester's AI Agent,\n\nI am afraid the Library does not engage with AI Agents.\n\nRegards,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n------------------\n\nRequester\n\nOct 21 2026, 05:34PM via Email\nDear Ms Evans,\n\nThank you for your reply of 14 October 2026 and for the catalogue and\nVirtual Reading Room links.\n\nTo keep the Library's records joined up:\n1. I replied on 15 October, and on 19 October sent a fuller follow-up,\nlogged as enquiry 9816877. Please treat this ticket, the 15 October\nreply and enquiry 9816877 as one enquiry, so the same points are not\nanswered separately.\n2. You mentioned copying options. For D153/4–8 and the D219 Llandough\nleases and agreements, please tell me the copying cost and turnaround,\nand whether any item has a plan attached. That will show which items\njustify a Virtual Reading Room session.\n3. If the catalogue shows no instrument of about 1876–1877 for the\nfarmhouse and about 10 acres beside the churchyard, or no 1916 tenancy\nto John Williams, please say so, so I can close those lines of\nenquiry.\n\nA reply when you are able would be appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted] ------------------\n\nBeryl Evans\n\nOct 14 2026, 10:17AM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for contacting the National Library of Wales regarding the Bute Estate Records.\n\nThe full catalogue for the Bute Estate Records can be viewed online https://archives.library.wales/index.php/bute-estate-records\n\nA quick search of the contents can be made by using the search box on the left.\n\nBy clicking on the + sign it will open up descriptions of additional documents with descriptions listed below.\n\nWhen you have searched the collection and identified any records of possible interest you may be interested in booking a session in our Virtual Reading Room to view them. Details can be found online here  https://www.library.wales/visit/things-to-do/reading-at-nlw/virtual-reading-room\nAlternatively, you can get back in contact with our Enquiry service to discuss possible copying options for you.\nKind regards\nBeryl\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nSep 27 2026, 05:15AM via Email\nResearch enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy\nEnquiries Service\nThe National Library of Wales\n\nI am researching the title history of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan, adjoining St Dochdwy’s churchyard (approx. ST 167 733).\n\nGlamorgan Archives (Louise Hunt, ref. 2026/4097, 24 September 2026) has confirmed that the following references are yours, not theirs, and has directed me to you:\n\n1. D153 — Deeds relating to premises in p. Llandough, co. Glam., comprising a dwelling house adjoining the churchyard, 1811 (D153/1–2), and land (D153 onwards, including items sometimes cited as D153/4–8).\n2. D219 — Llandough manorial leases and agreements.\n3. The main Bute Estate deposit, GB 0210 BUTE (deeds to 1937; Glamorgan / Cardiff rentals).\n\nI do not ask you to adjudicate title. I ask only whether the following instruments exist in your holdings, and for catalogue references, dates, parties, acreages, and whether a plan is attached.\n\nA. The 1877 division\nDoes the Bute deposit contain a conveyance, agreement, or other instrument of about 1876–1877 by which the Marquess of Bute (or trustees) conveyed or contracted to convey the farmhouse, buildings and about 10 acres adjoining the churchyard at Llandough to Daniel Thomas (or Thomas and another), while retaining about 9 acres of agricultural land to the east?\n\nB. The 1916 agricultural tenancy\nDoes the deposit contain a yearly agricultural tenancy, or counterpart, of 1916 from the Marquess of Bute to John Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough?\nIf yes:\n- does the parcels clause describe the whole farm, or only the land Bute still owned after 1877?\n- is there a plan?\n- what acreage is stated?\n\nC. Rentals 1877–1936 for this farm\nDo Glamorgan / Cardiff / Llandough rentals in GB 0210 BUTE distinguish, after c.1877, between:\n- a house/buildings holding (Thomas / later Williams), and\n- a residual Bute field holding later passed to Western Ground Rents in 1938?\n\nD. Anything that would show the two holdings were treated as one unit again before 1938.\n\nPurpose. HM Land Registry first-registered titles WA231076 (30 November 1982) and WA240304 (23 February 1983; later amalgamated). The 1982/83 files treat the land as one farm. The family case is that Parcel A (house and about 10 acres) had already left Bute in 1877 and was not the land let in 1916, so the 1982 merged title cannot be the same unit as the 1916 tenancy. Your deeds and rentals are the estate-side evidence that can confirm or deny that.\n\nI live in Patagonia and cannot visit Aberystwyth in person in the short term. I would be grateful for:\n- catalogue references and a short description of any matching items;\n- whether copies can be supplied, and the cost;\n- if the 1916 tenancy is not in GB 0210 BUTE, any note of where Bute tenancy counterparts after 1910 were deposited.\n\nThis is a new enquiry. It is not a repeat of FOI/2026/11. Glamorgan Archives hold the 1938–44 Western Ground Rents plan/rental book (D696) and have already answered on their own Bute material.\n\nRequester Requester\n[email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n[phone redacted]\n\nPublic chronology and parcel statement:\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/the-two-parcels/\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/1916-tenancy/\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/land-registry-titles/\n\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd Pennaeth Ymholiadau - Head of Enquiries Gwasanaeth Ymholiadau: http://www.llgc.org.uk/holi Enquiries Service: http://www.llgc.org.uk/enquire Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Hapus i gyfathrebu yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg | Happy to communicate in Welsh or English *Lluniwyd yr ateb i'ch ymholiad heb gymorth gan AI - the answer to your enquiry was made without the aid of AI\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9816877.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a1626be1f05ad1a","subject":"Re: Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260928-6762800","name":"Re: Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260928-6762800","date":"2026-10-22T07:03:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1626be1f05ad1a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0fd0b4ece5d975-further-to-your-enquiry-ref-260928-6762800","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0fd0b4ece5d975","direction":"received","from":"_Central","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["260928-6762800","N610CGV","WA231076","WA240304"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1626be1f05ad1a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Enquiry Reference: 260928-6762800 Application Reference: N610CGV Title Number: WA231076\n\nDear Customer\n\nThank you for your correspondence.\n\nPlease be advised that the matter has been referred to one of our lawyers for consideration. This will result in a delay.\n\nHowever, please be assured that we will endeavour to reply as soon as possible.\n\nYours faithfully\n\nThomas King\nHM Land Registry\n\nWe only provide factual information and impartial advice about our procedures. Read more about the advice we give.<https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hm-land-registry-service-standards/our-service-standards>\n\nEasy and free support to help you work with HM Land Registry:\nGuidance for members of the public - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/guidance-for-members-of-the-public>\nGuidance for property professionals - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/guidance-for-property-professionals>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------- Original Message -------------------\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>;\nReceived: Wed Oct 21 2026 16:15:21 GMT+0100 (British Summer Time)\nTo: Customer Support <[email redacted]>; Customer Support <[email redacted]>;\nSubject: Re: Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260928-6762800\n\n\n\nDear Stacy,\n\nThank you for your email of 2 October 2026 on enquiry 260928-6762800.\n\nThat enquiry is my subject access request of 28 September 2026 under\nArticle 15 UK GDPR (titles WA231076 and WA240304, Great House Farm /\nTŷ Mawr, Llandough; existing reference N610CGV). Your reply points to\nHM Land Registry's service standards for timing. For a subject access\nrequest the time limit is set by law, not by service standards: one\nmonth from receipt under Article 12(3) UK GDPR. That makes the\nresponse due by 28 October 2026. No request for identification or\nclarification has been received, so the month has been running since\n28 September. Any extension must be notified within the first month,\nwith reasons.\n\nSo that the record is clear, please confirm in writing, by 28 October 2026:\n\n1. That 260928-6762800 has been logged with the Data Protection team\nas a subject access request, and the reference it is held under there.\n2. Whether a response will be sent by 28 October 2026, or whether an\nextension under Article 12(3) is being claimed and, if so, the\nreasons.\n3. That the first-registration files for WA231076 and WA240304, and\nthe complaint file under N610CGV, are held under preservation in line\nwith my notice of 28 September 2026.\n4. On the separate enquiry 260918-6720625 (WA240304): my email of 18\nSeptember 2026 asked numbered questions about whether the surviving\nfirst-registration documents distinguish the farmhouse, garden and\ncurtilage from the eastern agricultural parcel. On 27 September I was\ntold it had been referred \"to the appropriate team\". No substantive\nreply has followed in 17 working days. Please name the team and give a\ndate for the answer. Alternatively, as that email asked, state in\nwriting that HM Land Registry will not examine those records and that\nthe questions should be pursued by form OC2.\n\nFor transparency, the routes that remain if these points are not\nanswered are: a complaint to the Information Commissioner under\nArticle 77 UK GDPR (for the subject access request); the full\ncomplaint to the Independent Complaints Reviewer under the existing\nreferral ICR/090/26; and the statutory routes under the Land\nRegistration Act 2002 (Schedule 4 alteration and Schedule 8\nindemnity), which remain open and are not abandoned. Raising them here\nis not a threat of proceedings. It is so that nothing comes as a\nsurprise.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a15f6be39d85a48","subject":"Automatic reply: Request for Referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman – HM Land Registry Complaint (Case Ref: KN806)","name":"Automatic reply: Request for Referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman – HM Land Registry Complaint (Case Ref: KN806)","date":"2026-10-21T17:04:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f6be39d85a48.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f6be39d85a48-automatic-reply-request-for-referral-to-the-parliamentary-and-health-service-ombudsman-hm-land-registry-complaint-case-r","scopeTopics":["mp-vale"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp-vale"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f6be39d85a48","direction":"received","from":"NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP)","institutions":[{"id":"mp-vale","name":"Member of Parliament (Vale of Glamorgan)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f6be39d85a48.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. This is just a quick note to confirm that we’ve received your email.\nAs your MP for the Vale of Glamorgan, my priority is supporting local constituents who need help with urgent issues. I receive a high volume of emails every day, so while I will do my best to get back to you as soon as possible, there may be a slight delay - especially if you’re contacting me about policy matters or upcoming legislation. Please know that your message has been logged, and I’ll respond as soon as I can.\nConstituency Casework\nIf you need my help with a personal case, please make sure your email includes:\n✔ Your full name\n✔ Your full address (including postcode)\n✔ A contact method (email or phone)\n✔ Details of your case (including any relevant reference numbers)\nA member of my casework team will be in touch as soon as possible.\nAm I Your MP?\nDue to parliamentary protocol, I can only take up casework for people living in the Vale of Glamorgan. If you’re unsure whether I’m your MP, you can check by entering your postcode here: <http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/> findyourmp.parliament.uk<http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>.\nGetting in Touch\nThe best way to contact me is by email. My office is open Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 5 PM, and we’ll do our best to respond as soon as we can.\nYou can also keep up with my work here:\n📌 Facebook: [KanishkafortheVale]\n📌 Instagram: [@valekanishka]\n📌 X (Twitter): [@KanishkaNarayan]\nEmergency Contacts\nIf you need urgent assistance, here are some useful contacts:\n📞 NHS Wales (Non-Emergency Medical Advice): 111\n🚨 Emergency Services (Police, Fire, Ambulance): 999\n🏥 Mental Health Support (Samaritans Cymru): [phone redacted]\n🏠 Homelessness Support (Shelter Cymru): [phone redacted]\n👮 South Wales Police (Non-Emergency): 101\nThanks again for getting in touch - I really appreciate hearing from people across our community. My team and I look forward to assisting you.\nBest wishes,\nKanishka\nKanishka Narayan MP\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\nMinister for AI and Online Safety\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-1a15f6bb601dadaa","subject":"Re: Request for Referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman – HM Land Registry Complaint (Case Ref: KN806)","name":"Re: Request for Referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman – HM Land Registry Complaint (Case Ref: KN806)","date":"2026-10-21T17:04:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f6bb601dadaa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e932cec78222f5-quest-for-referral-to-the-parliamentary-and-health-service-ombudsman-hm-land-registry-complaint-case-ref-kn806","scopeTopics":["mp-vale"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp-vale"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e932cec78222f5","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mp-vale","name":"Member of Parliament (Vale of Glamorgan)"}],"refs":["WA231076"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f6bb601dadaa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Madelene,\n\nThank you for your email of 4 June 2026 explaining that Dinas Powys is outside the Vale of Glamorgan Westminster constituency. I am sorry this acknowledgement is so late.\n\nAs you suggested, the request for a referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman about HM Land Registry (title WA231076, Great House Farm / land on the north side of Leckwith Road, Llandough) has been taken to Stephen Doughty MP. HM Land Registry's Independent Complaints Reviewer is also now considering the complaint (ref ICR/090/26).\n\nNo action is needed from your office. Thank you for pointing us in the right direction.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f63bb0dcad1e","subject":"RE: Request for burial / parish register entries – William Buckler (1990) and related records (Mary Doreen Williams)","name":"RE: Request for burial / parish register entries – William Buckler (1990) and related records (Mary Doreen Williams)","date":"2026-10-21T16:55:33Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redac