fonydd yn ddi-oed. Dylid ystyried unrhyw ddatganiadau neu sylwadau a wneir uchod yn rhai personol, ac nid o angenrhaid yn rhai o eiddo Bwrdd Iechyd Prifysgol Caerdydd a’r Fro, nac unrhyw ran gyfansoddol ohoni na chorff cysylltiedig. Mae cyfathrebu drwy e-bost yn amodol l fonitro. Am fwy o wybodaeth: https://cavuhb.nhs.wales/use-of-site/privacy-policy/ Cofiwch fod yn ymwybodol ei bod yn bosibl y bydd disgwyl i Bwrdd Iechyd Prifysgol Caerdydd a’r Fro roi cyhoeddusrwydd i gynnwys unrhyw ebost neu ohebiaeth a dderbynnir, yn unol ag amodau'r Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth 2000. I gael mwy o wybodaeth am Ryddid Gwybodaeth, cofiwch gyfeirio at wefan Bwrdd Iechyd Prifysgol Caerdydd a’r Fro: https://cavuhb.nhs.wales/about-us/governance-and-assurance/freedom-of-information/ We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh, and we will respond to correspondence in Welsh, and that correspondence in Welsh will not lead to delay. Confidentiality Privacy Notice: The Cardiff and Vale University Health Board Privacy Notice can be accessed on our website: https://cavuhb.nhs.wales/use-of-site/privacy-policy/ This message is strictly confidential and intended for the person or organisation to whom it is addressed. If you are not the intended recipient of the message then please notify the sender immediately. Any of the statements or comments made above should be regarded as personal and not necessarily those of Cardiff and Vale University Health Board, any constituent part or connected body. Email communication is subject to monitoring. For further information: https://cavuhb.nhs.wales/use-of-site/privacy-policy/ Please be aware that, under the terms of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, Cardiff and Vale University Health Board may be required to make public the content of any emails or correspondence received. For further information on Freedom of Information, please refer to the Cardiff and Vale University Health Board website: https://cavuhb.nhs.wales/about-us/governance-and-assurance/freedom-of-information/ ---"},{"id":"gm-1a15f63308fcfde9","subject":"Re: Access to Deceased Health Records / FOI Request – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: Access to Deceased Health Records / FOI Request – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-10-21T16:54:58Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f63308fcfde9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165fcfe194d80-access-to-deceased-health-records-foi-request-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["nhs-cav"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nhs-cav"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165fcfe194d80","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nhs-cav","name":"Cardiff and Vale University Health Board"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f63308fcfde9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Wheeler,\n\nAccess to deceased health records: William Buckler and Mary Doreen Williams\n\nThank you for your email of 21 August 2026 and for the application form and cover letter. I am sorry for the delay in replying. Requester will complete and sign the form himself, as the applicant under the Access to Health Records Act 1990.\n\nBefore he does, three points:\n1. Corrected date. The request gave William Buckler's death as \"on or about 29 May 1990\", from newspaper reports. Requester has since confirmed that William Beverly Buckler died at Llandough Hospital on 15 May 1992. Please search on that date.\n2. Whether records survive. Please tell us whether the Health Board still holds any records for these two patients (Mary Doreen Williams, born 10 August 1913, death registered March 1983; William Beverly Buckler, died 15 May 1992). If records have been destroyed under the retention schedule, please give the date and the schedule entry applied. This saves an application for records that no longer exist.\n3. Preservation. Please make sure that any surviving records for either patient are kept while the application is made and dealt with.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f62a92742020","subject":"Re: IR2026/06711 - Department for Culture, Media and Sport - Response Letter","name":"Re: IR2026/06711 - Department for Culture, Media and Sport - Response Letter","date":"2026-10-21T16:54:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f62a92742020.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a01a9ea1c9795b9-ir2026-06711-department-for-culture-media-and-sport-response-letter","scopeTopics":["dcms"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dcms"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a01a9ea1c9795b9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"dcms","name":"Department for Culture, Media and Sport"}],"refs":["FOI2026/06174","IR2026/06711"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f62a92742020.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Freedom of Information Team,\n\nYour refs: IR2026/06711 (internal review of FOI2026/06174)\n\nThank you for the internal review outcome of 19 August 2026, and I am sorry for the delay in replying.\n\nI accept that heritage functions in Wales have rested with the Welsh Office and Cadw since 1984, so a nil return may be correct. But the reason the review gives, that the property \"was demolished prior to the establishment of the Department\", does not answer the request. The request was for records about movable property and correspondence, which can date from after 1988. The Department also holds or held records inherited from its predecessors (the Department of National Heritage from 1992, and the Office of Arts and Libraries before it), as well as files for the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of Art.\n\nSo that the nil return can be relied on, please confirm:\n1. whether the searches covered records inherited from those predecessor bodies and the RCEWA files, or only records created after the Department was formed;\n2. the systems searched and the search terms used, which the review request asked for and the outcome does not give;\n3. where predecessor files have been transferred to The National Archives, the series or references, so that I can follow the review's suggestion. Section 16 FOIA expects that advice.\n\nA reply by 18 November 2026 would be appreciated. If these points cannot be answered, I will ask the Information Commissioner to consider the adequacy of the search under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f5724d2f2ce4","subject":"Re: Subject Access Request","name":"Re: Subject Access Request","date":"2026-10-21T16:41:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f5724d2f2ce4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0f2926630689c3-subject-access-request","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0f2926630689c3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1188/26","FOI 1040/26","FOI 1189/26","FOI 1264/26","FOI 719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f5724d2f2ce4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Data Protection Team,\n\nSubject access request: your email of 30 September 2026\n\nThank you for your email of 30 September 2026, and I am sorry this answer has taken time.\n\n1. The request of 20 August 2026. On 20 August 2026 an email was sent to [email redacted] headed \"Freedom of Information Request – Records relating to the deaths of William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\". Your FOI team dealt with it as FOI 1040/26 and answered on 29 September 2026. It is a Freedom of Information matter about deceased relatives, not part of this subject access request. An internal review of FOI 1040/26 was requested today. I mention it only so that the records of how it was handled can be found under item 2(b) below.\n\n2. What this subject access request covers: Requester's own personal data only, in:\n(a) any record naming or identifying him in connection with the possession and demolition at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Leckwith Road, Llandough, between 29 November and 6 December 1988, for example incident or control-room logs, duty or deployment records, pocket notebooks and correspondence;\n(b) records created in handling his requests and correspondence from 1 June 2026 to the date of your search: FOI 719/26 and internal review 1188/26, FOI 1040/26, FOI 1189/26, FOI 1264/26, and his email of 28 September 2026, including internal emails and notes that refer to him;\n(c) any record of the decision made on the crime-recording request in his email of 28 September 2026.\n\n3. Held or not held. For each item, please say whether information is held. Where it is not, please describe the search briefly: the systems and paper series searched, the search terms and date range, and whether older paper records were transferred to an archive or destroyed, with the date if recorded.\n\n4. Dates. You received identification and proof of address on 29 September 2026. Your question of 30 September was about a separate FOI matter, not the scope of this request. Our position is that it did not stop the one-month period under Article 12(3) UK GDPR, so the response is due by 29 October 2026. If you are counting from a different date, please tell me the date and the reason.\n\nNo fee is agreed. If any cost would arise, please say so first and offer a free route (an electronic copy or inspection).\n\nIf the response is not received by the due date, the next step is a complaint to the Information Commissioner under Article 77 UK GDPR.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f55aead048aa","subject":"Re: IR/26/16 - Buckler - Acknowledgement","name":"Re: IR/26/16 - Buckler - Acknowledgement","date":"2026-10-21T16:40:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f55aead048aa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ede5733d4fb7c-ir-26-16-buckler-acknowledgement","scopeTopics":["nio"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nio"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ede5733d4fb7c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nio","name":"Northern Ireland Office"}],"refs":["IR/26/16"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f55aead048aa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Freedom of Information Team,\n\nYour ref: IR/26/16 (internal review of 26FOI 103)\n\nThank you for your acknowledgement of 29 September 2026, which gives 26 October 2026 as the date for the review outcome.\n\nOne development since my review request is relevant to it. The response to 26FOI 103 (22 September 2026) said the historic Welsh Office / Cadw listing papers for Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough sit with the Welsh Government. I made that request to the Welsh Government on 28 September 2026 (ATISN 27589). On 19 October 2026 it was refused under section 14(2) FOIA as substantially similar to an earlier request, and no new papers were identified.\n\nSo that the review gives usable advice under section 16 FOIA, please:\n1. identify, if the Department holds the information, which files, series or registry references the 22 September response was referring to, and any transfer to the Welsh Government, The National Archives or elsewhere, with the date and reference;\n2. confirm the systems and file indexes searched for 26FOI 103;\n3. confirm that any records within scope are preserved while the review and any complaint to the Information Commissioner remain open.\n\nIf the outcome is not received by 26 October 2026, or does not deal with these points, I will complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f52068163c3a","subject":"Re: Request for information - ref FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough Non-SF Information","name":"Re: Request for information - ref FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough Non-SF Information","date":"2026-10-21T16:36:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f52068163c3a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13fa747f9c0dd3-quest-for-information-ref-foi2026-23272-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-non-sf-information","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13fa747f9c0dd3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":["FOI2026/23272"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f52068163c3a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Army Policy & Secretariat,\n\nYour ref: FOI2026/23272\n\nThank you for logging the request on 15 October 2026 with a response date of 9 November 2026.\n\nFor the file:\n1. My email of 16 October 2026 (sent separately, subject \"Re: FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough\") gives search identifiers and asks for preservation. Please attach it to this reference.\n2. If the search finds that records from November–December 1988 have been destroyed, please state the retention rule applied under JSP 441 (or its predecessor) and any disposal record. If records have been transferred to The National Archives or another repository, please give the reference. Section 16 FOIA expects that advice.\n3. Please confirm that the response will name the record systems and archives searched, so that a \"not held\" answer, if given, can be assessed.\n\nIf no response is received by 9 November 2026, I will ask for an internal review and then complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f50af42db702","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-j