026. The 20 working-day limit under section 10(1) FOIA and regulation 5(2) EIR fell on 16 October 2026. I have received no response to either request, and no notice extending time under regulation 7(1) EIR.\n2. For 00211484, even if my narrowing email of 28 September 2026 were treated as a fresh request, the limit would be 26 October 2026.\n3. Please confirm by return whether any extension notice was issued and, if so, its date. If none was, please tell me the date on which each response will be sent.\n4. My supplement of 18 October 2026 (village green VG41, the planning committee meeting of 19 November 1958, and council works on the VG41 land) asked to be logged separately if you prefer. Please give me its reference number and due date.\n5. Please make sure that all records within scope of these requests are preserved while they and any review remain open.\n\nIf no response to 00211483 is received by 4 November 2026, I will complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA (and regulation 18 EIR) about the failure to respond, and ask for an internal review (regulation 11) at the same time.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f48c942639bc","subject":"Re: Request for information - Ref: FOI2026/118465","name":"Re: Request for information - Ref: FOI2026/118465","date":"2026-10-21T16:26:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f48c942639bc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15877f505dbb0b-quest-for-information-ref-foi2026-118465","scopeTopics":["voa"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["voa"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15877f505dbb0b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"voa","name":"Valuation Office Agency / HMRC"}],"refs":["FOI2026/118465"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f48c942639bc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Rights Unit,\n\nYour ref: FOI2026/118465\n\nThank you for your acknowledgement of 20 October 2026.\n\nSo that the record is clear:\n1. Please confirm that FOI2026/118465 is my request of 20 October 2026 to the Valuation Office Agency ([email redacted]) about rating and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1955–1995, and that the VOA's own records are being searched.\n2. Section 10(1) FOIA requires a response within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. It is a legal limit, not an aim. The only extension the Act allows is a reasonable extension under section 10(3) to consider the public interest where a qualified exemption applies. If HMRC relies on that, the refusal notice must name the exemption by 17 November 2026 (section 17(2)).\n3. Please make sure that any valuation list entry, rating file, proposal, appeal or deletion record for the property is preserved while the request and any review are open.\n4. If the 1956, 1963 or 1973 valuation lists for the area are not held by HMRC or the VOA, please say where they are held, for example a transfer to The National Archives with its reference. Section 16 expects that advice.\n\nIf no response is received by 17 November 2026, I will ask for an internal review and then complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f47239c2d0d7","subject":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-21T16:24:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f47239c2d0d7.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6-foi-request-western-ground-rents-ltd-company-no-00342092-dissolved-1997-any-bona-vacantia-property-or-interests-at-lland","scopeTopics":["bona-vacantia"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bona-vacantia"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bona-vacantia","name":"Government Legal Department (Bona Vacantia)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f47239c2d0d7.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Copping,\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026 confirming that my request of 20 October about Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) is being considered under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nFor the record:\n1. Under section 10(1), the 20 working-day limit for the response falls on 17 November 2026. Please let me have your reference number for the request.\n2. Please make sure that any file, index entry or referral record about Western Ground Rents Ltd, or about property at Llandough, Leckwith, Cogan or Penarth, is preserved while the request and any review are open.\n3. One further point, within the same request: if any property of the company vested in the Crown on dissolution in 1997 (section 654 of the Companies Act 1985, as then in force), please also say whether it was later disclaimed (section 656), sold or otherwise dealt with, and the date. If the Division's records for companies dissolved in 1997 have been destroyed or transferred, please say so, with the retention schedule applied. Section 16 FOIA expects that advice.\n\nIf no response is received by 17 November 2026, I will ask for an internal review and, after that, complain to the Information Commissioner under section 50.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f46517f42662","subject":"RE: [2] Re: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026  — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough (TO/HF/05677/26)","name":"RE: [2] Re: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026  — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough (TO/HF/05677/26)","date":"2026-10-21T16:23:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f46517f42662.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15ee71949f5b94-2-re-supplement-to-complaint-re-served-20-september-2026-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-to-hf-05677-26","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15ee71949f5b94","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f46517f42662.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dr Wigley,\n\nComplaint ticket #628635887 (your ref TO/HF/05677/26)\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026, and for the confirmation that information caught by a request under FOIA or the EIR will not be destroyed.\n\nSo that the record is clear, four points.\n\n1. Status of the complaint. The complaint (17 September, re-served 20 September, supplement 22 September 2026) is about Cadw's administrative handling of the 1988 assessment: what was considered, what was recorded, and why no record of it now exists. That is an administrative action. The Complaints Advice Team's email of 30 September did not reject it; it said my concerns \"will be addressed by the relevant officials\". Please confirm, by 4 November 2026, whether your email of 21 October is the Welsh Government's final response to the complaint, or whether a further stage is available. If it is the final response, the complaint will be referred to the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales.\n\n2. Restriction on correspondence. Your email says further correspondence about the farm \"will be filed but not answered\" unless new evidence is raised. Please tell me which Welsh Government policy that decision is made under, the date it was made, how long it lasts and how it can be reviewed. I assume it does not apply to requests made under FOIA, the EIR or data protection law, or to the Information Rights Unit. Those will continue through the proper channels and must be answered within the statutory time limits.\n\n3. Preservation. Your confirmation covers information \"caught by a request\". The complaint and a possible Ombudsman referral are also open. Please make sure the hold also covers the categories in part D of my email of 19 October 2026 to the Information Rights Unit: the registered files identified in the internal review of ATISN 27021, any remnant of the 1988 listing file, the originals of the 29 July 1988 inspection photographs, the disposal logs and retention schedules for 1970–1997, and any transfer lists.\n\n4. Open requests. I note that ATISN 26-0009 will be answered by 6 November 2026. The section 14(2) refusal of ATISN 27589 was challenged on 19 October 2026 (part B of the same email), and I am waiting for that answer.\n\nOur position is that the Welsh Government has not shown what Cadw considered in 1988. That question remains open whatever view is taken of the correspondence.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f43e150dde4d","subject":"Automatic reply: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","name":"Automatic reply: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","date":"2026-10-21T16:20:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f43e150dde4d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f43e150dde4d-automatic-reply-response-freedom-of-information-1189-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f43e150dde4d","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1189/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f43e150dde4d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a15f43a9f1f22f6","subject":"Re: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","name":"Re: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","date":"2026-10-21T16:20:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f43a9f1f22f6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15eff3a07ac34b-sponse-freedom-of-information-1189-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15eff3a07ac34b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1188/26","1189/26","FOI 1040/26","FOI 1189/26","FOI 1264/26","FOI 719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f43a9f1f22f6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Mccarley,\n\nFOI 1189/26: preservation notice of 28 September 2026\n\nThank you for your response of 21 October 2026.\n\nI agree that the email of 28 September 2026 was not a request for information under section 8 FOIA, and it was not sent as one. It was a preservation notice: a request that South Wales Police does not destroy, transfer or dispose of records about Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, while related requests are open. Registering it as an FOI request and closing it leaves that request unanswered.\n\nThe duty does not depend on section 8. Records within the scope of open requests are protected by section 77 FOIA (and, for personal data, section 173 of the Data Protection Act 2018). The Section 46 Code of Practice on records management also expects an authority to stop routine disposal of records it knows are subject to an open request, review or complaint. The open matters are:\n- FOI 1264/26 (response due 9 November 2026);\n- internal review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26 (due 26 October 2026);\n- the internal review of FOI 1040/26 requested today;\n- my subject access request (due 29 October 2026).\n\nPlease:\n1. confirm in writing that a hold is in place on records about Great House Farm, the 1988 possession enforcement and demolition, and the deaths covered by FOI 1040/26, until those matters and any complaint to the Information Commissioner are closed;\n2. name the unit or role that owns the hold, if it is not the Data Management and Disclosure Unit;\n3. confirm that FOI 1189/26 will not be cited as a reason to treat any later request as repeated or vexatious, since it was not a request for information.\n\nA reply by 4 November 2026 would be appreciated. If no confirmation is given, I will raise the point with the Information Commissioner together with the reviews above.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f28811081705","subject":"We have received your email. Rydym wedi derbyn eich ebost","name":"We have received your email. Rydym wedi derbyn eich ebost","date":"2026-10-21T15:50:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f28811081705.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f28811081705-we-have-received-your-email-rydym-wedi-derbyn-eich-ebost","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f28811081705","direction":"received","from":"icocasework","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f28811081705.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for contacting the Information Commissioner’s Office. We confirm that we have received your correspondence. If you have any special requirements that mean you would like us to communicate with you in a specific way, please let us know and we will make adjustments if we can.\nIf you have made a new complaint - we’re unlikely to look into it unless you have raised it with the responsible organisation (for a data protection complaint) or the responsible public authority (for a freedom of information complaint) first. Please make sure you have sent us a copy of their final response to you. We're supporting a high number of people with their complaints at the moment. For the latest timescales to allocate cases, please visit the make a complaint page<https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/> on our website. We apologise for this delay but we want to reassure you we take your complaint very seriously.\nIf your correspondence relates to an existing case - we will add it to your case and consider it on allocation to a case officer. If you believe we have either failed to take appropriate steps to respond to your data protection complaint, or we do not provide you with information about the progress or outcome of your complaint within the next three months, you may be able to apply to the First-tier Tribunal to require us to respond to your complaint or to provide you with information about its progress. (www.gov.uk<http://www.gov.uk/> - information rights and data protection: appeal against the Information Commissioner)\nIf you have asked us for advice - we will respond within 7 days. While you wait, you should regularly check our website (www.ico.org.uk<http://www.ico.org.uk/>) for relevant guidance, as we are updating this all the time. You should read our Guide to the UK GDPR<https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr/>. If you have raised a question that we have answered on our website, we may respond by sending you a link to it. But will do our best to provide you with the information you need.\nIf you represent an organisation and you are reporting a personal data breach under the GDPR or the Data Protection Act 2018 - we aim to contact you within seven days to confirm receipt and to provide you with a case reference number. If you want advice urgently, you should telephone our helpline on [phone redacted]. You can find out more about data breach reporting on our website.\nWhere a significant cyber incident occurs, you may also need to report this to the National Cyber Security Centre (the NCSC). To help you decide, you should read the NCSC’s guidance about their role and the type of incidents that you should consider reporting. (www.ncsc.gov.uk<http://www.ncsc.gov.uk/> -incident-management)\nIncidents that might lead to a heightened risk of individuals being affected by fraud, should be reported to Report Fraud (https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/) - the UK’s national fraud and cybercrime reporting centre. If your organisation is in Scotland, then reports should be made to Police Scotland (www.scotland.police.uk<http://www.scotland.police.uk/>).\nIf you are a Communications Service Provider reporting a security breach under the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations – you will need to report the security breach via the secure portal that can be found on the PECR pages of our website.\nIf you represent an organisation and are reporting a potential incident under the NIS Directive - we will contact you as soon as we can. You can find out more about the NIS Regulations on our website\nIf you represent an organisation and you are reporting a security breach within the definition of the eIDAS regulation – we will contact you as soon as we can. You can find out more about the eIDAS regulation on our website.\nIf you have reported spam email – we are unlikely to need to contact you again, unless we need more information to help with our investigations. We publish details about the action we've taken on nuisance messages on our website.\nIf you have asked for information you think we might hold - we will contact you if we need any more information to help us respond. Otherwise, we will respond within our public and statutory service levels. For more information please visit our webpage ‘request information from us’ (go to our homepage and follow the link for ‘about the ICO’ and ‘our information’).\nIf you have only copied your correspondence to us - we will not respond.\nThere is more detailed information, including information on our current response times, on our service standards and what to expect webpage. You can also call [phone redacted], we welcome calls in Welsh on [phone redacted]. You can also contact us on live chat (please visit our webpage ‘contact us’ and ‘live chat’).\nFor information about what we do with personal data please see our privacy notice: https://ico.org.uk/global/privacy-notice/\nYours sincerely\nThe Information Commissioner’s Office\n\nDiolch yn fawr ichi am gysylltu â Swyddfa’r Comisiynydd Gwybodaeth. Rydym yn cadarnhau bod eich gohebiaeth wedi dod i law. Os oes gennych unrhyw ofynion arbennig sy'n golygu yr hoffech i ni gyfathrebu â chi mewn ffordd benodol, rhowch wybod i ni a byddwn yn gwneud addasiadau os gallwn.\nOs ydych wedi gwneud cwyn newydd – dydyn ni ddim yn debygol o edrych i mewn iddo oni bai eich bod wedi’i godi’n gyntaf gyda’r sefydliad cyfrifol (cwyn am ddiogelu data) neu’r awdurdod cyhoeddus cyfrifol (cwyn am ryddid gwybodaeth). Gofalwch eich bod wedi anfon copi aton ni o’u hymateb terfynol ichi.\nRydyn ni wrthi’n helpu nifer fawr o bobl gyda’u cwynion ar hyn o bryd. Am yr amserlenni diweddaraf i ddyrannu achosion, ewch i'r dudalen gwneud cwyn<https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/data-protection-complaints/> ar ein gwefan. Ymddiheurwn am yr oedi yma ond hoffem eich sicrhau ein bod yn cymryd eich cwyn o ddifrif.\nOs yw’ch gohebiaeth yn ymwneud ag achos sydd eisoes yn bod - byddwn yn ei hychwanegu at eich achos ac fe gaiff ei hystyried ar ôl cael ei dyrannu i swyddog achosion. Os ydych yn credu ein bod ni naill ai wedi methu cymryd camau priodol i ymateb i'ch cwyn diogelu data, neu heb ddarparu gwybodaeth ichi am gynnydd neu ganlyniad eich cwyn o fewn y tri mis nesaf, efallai y byddwch yn gallu gwneud cais i'r Tribiwnlys Haen Gyntaf i’w gwneud yn ofynnol inni ICO ymateb i'ch cwyn neu ddarparu gwybodaeth ichi am gynnydd eich cwyn. (www.gov.uk<http://www.gov.uk/> - information rights and data protection: appeal against the Information Commissioner)\nOs ydych wedi gofyn am gyngor – byddwn yn ymateb o fewn 14 diwrnod. Tra byddwch yn aros, dylech edrych yn rheolaidd ar ein gwefan<http://www.ico.org.uk/> (www.ico.org.uk<http://www.ico.org.uk/>) i chwilio am ganllawiau perthnasol, gan eu bod yn cael eu diweddaru drwy’r amser. Hefyd dylech ddarllen ein blogiau ynghylch ‘mythau’r GDPR<https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/guide-to-data-protection/guide-to-the-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr>’. Os ydych wedi codi cwestiwn sydd wedi’i ateb ar ein gwefan, mae’n bosibl y byddwn yn ymateb drwy anfon dolen atoch i gysylltu â’r ateb.  Ond fe wnawn ein gorau glas i roi’r wybodaeth angenrheidiol ichi\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am drosedd data personol o dan y GDPR neu Ddeddf Diogelu Data 2018 – rydym yn anelu at gysylltu â chi o fewn saith niwrnod calendr i gadarnhau bod eich neges wedi dod i law ac i roi rhif cyfeirnod achos ichi. Os oes arnoch eisiau cyngor ar frys, dylech ffonio’n llinell gymorth ar [phone redacted]. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am roi gwybod am droseddau data ar ein gwefan.\nPan fo digwyddiad seibr arwyddocaol yn digwydd, mae’n bosibl y bydd angen ichi roi gwybod amdano hefyd i’r Ganolfan Seiberddiogelwch Genedlaethol (yr NCSC). I’ch helpu i benderfynu, dylech ddarllen canllawiau’r NCSC ar eu rôl a’r math o ddigwyddiadau y dylech ystyried rhoi gwybod amdanyn nhw. (www.ncsc.gov.uk<http://www.ncsc.gov.uk/> -incident-management)\nDylai digwyddiadau a allai arwain at risg uwch y bydd twyll yn effeithio ar unigolion gael eu cyfleu i Report Fraud (https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/) – sef canolfan genedlaethol y Deyrnas Unedig ar gyfer rhoi gwybod am dwyll a seiberdroseddau. Os yw eich sefydliad yn yr Alban, yna i Heddlu’r Alban y dylech chi roi gwybod (www.scotland.police.uk<http://www.scotland.police.uk/>).\nOs ydych yn Ddarparwr Gwasanaethau Cyfathrebu sy’n rhoi gwybod am dor diogelwch o dan y Rheoliadau Preifatrwydd a Chyfathrebu Electronig – bydd angen ichi roi gwybod am y tor diogelwch drwy’r porth diogel<https://report.ico.org.uk/security-breach/> sydd ar gael ar y tudalennau ar ein gwefan sy’n ymwneud â’r PECR.\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am ddigwyddiad posibl o dan Gyfarwyddeb yr NIS – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted ag y gallwn. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am Reoliadau’r NIS ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych yn cynrychioli sefydliad a’ch bod yn rhoi gwybod am dor diogelwch o fewn y diffiniad yn Rheoliad eIDAS – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted ag y gallwn. Cewch ragor o wybodaeth am Reoliad eIDAS ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych wedi rhoi gwybod am ebost sbam – mae’n annhebygol y bydd angen inni gysylltu â chi eto, oni bai bod arnon ni angen rhagor o wybodaeth i helpu yn ein hymchwiliad. Rydym yn cyhoeddi gwybodaeth am y camau rydyn ni wedi’u cymryd ynghylch negeseuon niwsans ar ein gwefan.\nOs ydych wedi gofyn am wybodaeth yr ydych yn credu ei bod gennyn ni – byddwn yn cysylltu â chi os bydd arnom angen rhagor o wybodaeth i’n helpu i ymateb. Fel arall, byddwn yn ymateb ichi o fewn ein lefelau gwasanaeth statudol a chyhoeddus. I gael rhagor o wybodaeth, ewch i’n tudalen gwe ‘request information from us’ (ewch i’n tudalen hafan a dilynwch y ddolen ‘about the ICO’ ac ‘our information’).\nOs ydych wedi anfon copi o’ch gohebiaeth aton ni ond dim byd arall – fyddwn ni ddim yn ymateb.\nMae gwybodaeth fanylach, gan gynnwys gwybodaeth am ein hamserau ymateb presennol, ar ein tudalen gwe safonau gwasanaeth a beth i’w ddisgwyl. Gallwch ffonio hefyd yn y Gymraeg ar [phone redacted] opsiwn 9 neu yn Saesneg ar [phone redacted]. Gallwch gysylltu â ni hefyd i gael sgwrs fyw (ewch i’n tudalen gwe ‘contact us’ a ‘live chat’).\nI gael gwybodaeth am yr hyn rydyn ni’n ei wneud â data personol, gweler ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd: https://ico.org.uk/global/privacy-notice/\nYn gywir\nSwyddfa’r Comisiynydd Gwybodaeth"},{"id":"gm-1a15f285df2fb1de","subject":"Re: ICO Case Reference: IC-546505-W6P0","name":"Re: ICO Case Reference: IC-546505-W6P0","date":"2026-10-21T15:50:42Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f285df2fb1de.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fec61fb1d20afa-ico-case-reference-ic-546505-w6p0","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fec61fb1d20afa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":["1188/26","FOI 1040/26","FOI 719/26","IC-546505-W6P0"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f285df2fb1de.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Cuthbert,\n\nICO Case Reference: IC-546505-W6P0\n\nThank you for your letter of 10 August 2026, and I am sorry for the delay in replying. I understand the limits of the Commissioner's remit that you set out: the ICO does not decide maladministration, does not refer matters to other bodies, and does not decide what an authority should hold.\n\nAs you suggested, complaints will come to you one request at a time, on the FOI complaint form, with the request, the response, the internal review request and the review outcome. Internal reviews are now in progress, for example:\n- South Wales Police: internal review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26 (outcome due 26 October 2026), and an internal review of FOI 1040/26 requested today;\n- Welsh Government: an internal review of ATISN 26-0010 requested on 19 October 2026. ATISN 27589 was refused on 19 October 2026 under section 14(2), with no internal review procedure given.\n\nSo that those complaints are framed correctly, I would be grateful for answers to four points that do fall within the Commissioner's functions:\n\n1. Records management (section 46 Code and section 48 FOIA). Welsh Government has said (ATISN 27021 and its internal reviews of July 2026) that the 1988 listing file for the farm was \"most likely\" destroyed, that no destruction record could be found, and that it could not say what retention arrangements applied at the time. Will the Commissioner consider a concern about an authority's conformity with the section 46 Code of Practice on records management, separately from a section 50 complaint? If so, what form should it take and what evidence do you need?\n\n2. Records within scope of open requests. Your letter says preservation for a legal matter is outside the ICO's remit. Please confirm that where information within the scope of a live request is altered, defaced, erased, destroyed or concealed to prevent disclosure, that falls under section 77 FOIA, regulation 19 EIR or, for personal data, section 173 DPA 2018, and that the ICO is the body to report it to. How should such a concern be reported?\n\n3. Late responses. Where an authority answers after the 20 working-day limit (for example, South Wales Police answered FOI 1040/26 seven working days late), can the section 10 breach be included in the section 50 complaint about that request, or should it be reported separately?\n\n4. Case status. Please confirm that IC-546505-W6P0 is closed, so that new complaints about specific requests are not treated as duplicates of it.\n\nI would be grateful for a reply by 18 November 2026.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f27d7071dd5f","subject":"Automatic reply: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1040/26","name":"Automatic reply: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1040/26","date":"2026-10-21T15:50:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f27d7071dd5f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f27d7071dd5f-automatic-reply-response-freedom-of-information-1040-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f27d7071dd5f","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1040/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f27d7071dd5f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a15f27ac84986fc","subject":"Re: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1040/26","name":"Re: RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1040/26","date":"2026-10-21T15:49:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f27ac84986fc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ed90513b1ae67-sponse-freedom-of-information-1040-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ed90513b1ae67","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1040/26","1188/26","FOI 1040/26","FOI 1264/26","FOI 719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f27ac84986fc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Mccarley,\n\nFOI 1040/26: request for internal review\n\nThank you for your email of 29 September 2026 and the attached response to FOI 1040/26. The response says, in full, \"South Wales Police do not hold this information.\" Under your Freedom of Information Complaints Procedure, please treat this email as a request for internal review of that response. I am copying it to the review mailbox named in the procedure.\n\nGrounds\n\n1. Adequacy of search. The request (20 August 2026) asked for incident reports, sudden-death reports, referrals to the Coroner, statements and other records about two deaths: William (Billy) Buckler, late of Great House Farm, Llandough, and Mary Doreen Williams (born 10 August 1913; death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan). The response gives no description of what was searched. A one-line \"not held\" cannot be tested without one. The ICO's approach is that a not-held answer is judged on the balance of probabilities, by reference to the searches actually made.\n\n2. Corrected date. The request gave William Buckler's death as \"on or about 29 May 1990\", taken from newspaper reports. Since then, in correspondence on FOI 1264/26 (13 and 16 October 2026), I have confirmed that William Beverly Buckler died at Llandough Hospital on 15 May 1992. If the search was limited to 1990, please re-run it for May 1992, and for all name forms (William Beverly Buckler, William, Bill or Billy Buckler). If you consider that part a new request, please register it, give me the reference and the 20 working-day date, and do not treat it as a reason to delay the review of the rest.\n\n3. Timeliness. The request was received on 20 August 2026 (your email of 28 September confirms this). The 20 working-day limit under section 10(1) FOIA fell on 18 September 2026. The response was sent on 29 September 2026, seven working days late. Please record the breach in the review.\n\n4. Duty to advise (section 16 FOIA). If South Wales Police does not hold these records, the response did not say whether they were never created, were destroyed, or were transferred. Nor did it say who might hold them now, for example the Coroner's office or an archive. Section 16 and the Section 45 Code of Practice expect that advice.\n\nWhat I ask the review to provide\n\na) the systems, indexes, archives and date ranges searched, and the search terms used, for each of the two deaths;\nb) the retention period that applied to sudden-death reports and Coroner referral records from 1983 and 1990–92, and the policy or schedule it comes from;\nc) any record of the destruction or disposal of such records, with the date;\nd) whether any records of that period were transferred to Glamorgan Archives, the Coroner or any other body, and if so the reference;\ne) confirmation that any surviving record within scope will be preserved while this review, FOI 1264/26 (due 9 November 2026) and the internal review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26 (due 26 October 2026) remain open.\n\nInformation about people who have died is not personal data under section 3(2) of the Data Protection Act 2018, so section 40 FOIA does not prevent disclosure of anything found.\n\nI would be grateful for the review outcome within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026. If the review upholds the original answer without describing the searches, the next step is a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f0b3734dbbe0","subject":"RE: Epexio contact us form submission","name":"RE: Epexio contact us form submission","date":"2026-10-21T15:18:52Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f0b3734dbbe0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a07b3bf0b65e56c-epexio-contact-us-form-submission","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a07b3bf0b65e56c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":["2026/4439"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f0b3734dbbe0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Louise,\n\nThank you for your email of today (ref 2026/4439), and for reading DBDT/123/7 so carefully.\n\nYour reading is very useful. The 18 May 1939 tenancy between Western Ground Rents Ltd and John Williams concerns 5.30 acres marked pink, which is agricultural land next to the Tŷ Mawr farmhouse and Llwyn-yr-eryr. It does not mention the farmhouse or any other structure as included, and it reserves quarrying and other rights to Western Ground Rents. We note your advice to have the document interpreted by a land law specialist.\n\nYour note about DSA/14/91 is a new lead for us. A few focused questions, which I hope can be answered from the catalogue and accession records without a paid search:\n\n1. DSA/14/91 (1936 sale particulars of Llwyn-yr-eryr, Mr Charles St David Spencer): does the item include a plan? Does the lot that includes the land later let in 1939 state its tenure, the lessor and the term of the leasehold? If it can be photographed on a visit, or copied, please tell me the cost.\n\n2. Do any other deposits relating to Llwyn-yr-eryr or the Spencer family hold the head lease (or its counterpart) under which that land was held before 1938?\n\n3. DBDT/123 and the DB (Western Ground Rents) material: could you give the accession or deposit date and the depositor (at the level normally shown to users)? And are there any withdrawal or return-to-depositor entries for items in those series? We understand Glamorgan Archives keeps records of withdrawals.\n\n4. You confirm that no records of the later title history are held. For completeness, does that include the Leckwith Common / Llandough land charges and the Penarth Urban District Council and Glamorgan County Council planning committee papers for 1955–1962? Earlier cycles of our research identified those fonds as held by you.\n\nIf any of this is better handled as a formal request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, please say so and treat it as one (regulation 9, advice and assistance). A reply within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026, would be ideal.\n\nWith thanks again,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f0a3dde6b898","subject":"Automatic reply: Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","name":"Automatic reply: Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","date":"2026-10-21T15:17:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f0a3dde6b898.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f0a3dde6b898-automatic-reply-internal-review-1188-26-of-foi-719-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f0a3dde6b898","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1188/26","FOI 719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f0a3dde6b898.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a15f0a1a98c3eeb","subject":"Re: Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","name":"Re: Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","date":"2026-10-21T15:17:40Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f0a1a98c3eeb.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ed9801c58b6b2-internal-review-1188-26-of-foi-719-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ed9801c58b6b2","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1188/26","FOI 1264/26","FOI 719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f0a1a98c3eeb.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Mccarley,\n\nThank you for your email of 29 September 2026 acknowledging my request of 27 September for an internal review of FOI 719/26 (your reference 1188/26).\n\nYour email says the FOI officers will establish whether the request is valid under the Act and whether clarification is needed. For the avoidance of delay:\n\n1. This is not a new request. It is a request for internal review of the response to FOI 719/26 (16 July 2026, \"hold no information\"). Its validity follows from the original request. The Section 45 Code of Practice and ICO guidance expect a review outcome within 20 working days, which falls on 26 October 2026.\n\n2. No clarification is needed. The scope is the 1988 operational record of police attendance at the possession enforcements at Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, Penarth: the failed attempt of 29 April 1988, and the enforcement and demolition in November–December 1988.\n\n3. So that a \"not held\" answer can be tested, please include in the review outcome:\n   a) the systems, archives and date ranges searched, and the search terms used;\n   b) the retention schedule under which 1988 operational records, duty states, incident logs and occurrence books would have been kept or destroyed;\n   c) any destruction or disposal record for them;\n   d) whether any records of the period were transferred to Glamorgan Archives or elsewhere, and if so the reference.\n\n4. Please confirm that any surviving record within scope is preserved while this review, my subject access request (due 29 October 2026) and FOI 1264/26 (due 9 November 2026) remain open. I am not repeating those requests here.\n\nIf the review upholds the original answer without describing the searches, the next step is a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f0980aac7907","subject":"RE: Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 — clarification","name":"RE: Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 — clarification","date":"2026-10-21T15:17:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f0980aac7907.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ed914794badec-freedom-of-information-request-reference-cas-347296-m0v4y1-clarification","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ed914794badec","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-347296-M0V4Y1"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f0980aac7907.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Manager,\n\nThank you for your email of 1 October 2026 setting out the sequence of cases. That is helpful, and I accept it: CAS-344046 was the original enquiry, CAS-347296 the FOI request (final response 23 September 2026), and CAS-356384 the internal review requested on 23 September 2026.\n\nThree points arise from it:\n\n1. Internal review CAS-356384 was requested on 23 September 2026. Twenty working days from then is today, 21 October 2026, the period the Section 45 Code of Practice and ICO guidance treat as normal. Please confirm the date the review outcome will be issued. If it needs longer, please give the reason and a date within 40 working days (by 18 November 2026).\n\n2. I also wrote on 7 October 2026 about the review. Please confirm whether that email has been joined to CAS-356384 or logged as a separate case, and if separate, its reference.\n\n3. Your email of 1 October did not deal with paragraph 2 of my email of 30 September. That paragraph asked for my enquiry about the National Farm Survey and the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (1936–1950) to be passed to Records Enquiries under CAS-344046. My chase of 20 August had bounced from [email redacted]. Please confirm whether it has been passed on, and the reference it is held under. If it should be sent somewhere else, please say where (section 16 FOIA, advice and assistance).\n\nIf the review upholds the original response, the next step is a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA. I would rather the review settled the matter.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f094419c7eee","subject":"Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Re: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-21T15:16:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f094419c7eee.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-foi","vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi","vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"},{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f094419c7eee.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear James,\n\nThank you for your email of 11 October 2026 explaining why Scrutiny will not take forward the Task and Finish suggestion for Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough. I accept that a Task and Finish review is not the place to re-examine an individual historical planning decision. I have three points in reply and four short questions.\n\nOn your reasons:\n\n1. County-wide and strategic. Part of the proposal does meet that test, and it can be put on its own: how the Council keeps, transfers and disposes of historic planning, land-charges and heritage records, and how it answers requests for them. That affects every resident who asks for an old planning file. It is not limited to one site. The Great House Farm requests show the problem: the internal review of EIR request 00210772, requested on 7 July 2026, still has no outcome, beyond the 40 working days set by regulation 11(4) of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. And planning appendices C, D and E of the same file are still not supplied.\n\n2. \"Other channels\". Your email says the matter should be \"navigated through other channels\" but does not say which ones. Please name the channel the Council considers correct for each of: (a) missing or contradictory Council-held planning and heritage records; (b) the Council's own handling of its records requests.\n\n3. Other bodies involved. That Welsh Government, Cadw and elected members are also involved goes to how scrutiny is coordinated. With respect, it is not a reason the Council's own records cannot be looked at.\n\nQuestions:\n1. Was the decision of 11 October taken by officers, or by the Chair or Chairs of the relevant Scrutiny Committee? Under which provision of the Council's Constitution or Scrutiny procedure rules was it taken?\n2. Will the narrower, county-wide topic in point 1 above be considered as a Scrutiny topic suggestion? If a form is needed, please send it or link to it and I will complete it.\n3. Can a ward member refer the matter as a Councillor Call for Action, and if so, how?\n4. Does the Council's corporate complaints procedure apply to the handling of records requests, as distinct from the information-rights routes?\n\nFor clarity on where things stand: the information-rights routes (internal review, then a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA and regulation 18 EIR) are being followed separately and are not repeated here. Routes not yet used are the corporate complaints procedure, a referral by a ward member, and then the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales. I would rather the Council's own scrutiny process dealt with the county-wide records question first.\n\nA reply within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026, would be appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f07e4d32f435","subject":"Re: Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260928-6762800","name":"Re: Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260928-6762800","date":"2026-10-21T15:15:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f07e4d32f435.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0fd0b4ece5d975-further-to-your-enquiry-ref-260928-6762800","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0fd0b4ece5d975","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["260928-6762800","N610CGV","WA231076","WA240304"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f07e4d32f435.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Stacy,\n\nThank you for your email of 2 October 2026 on enquiry 260928-6762800.\n\nThat enquiry is my subject access request of 28 September 2026 under Article 15 UK GDPR (titles WA231076 and WA240304, Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough; existing reference N610CGV). Your reply points to HM Land Registry's service standards for timing. For a subject access request the time limit is set by law, not by service standards: one month from receipt under Article 12(3) UK GDPR. That makes the response due by 28 October 2026. No request for identification or clarification has been received, so the month has been running since 28 September. Any extension must be notified within the first month, with reasons.\n\nSo that the record is clear, please confirm in writing, by 28 October 2026:\n\n1. That 260928-6762800 has been logged with the Data Protection team as a subject access request, and the reference it is held under there.\n2. Whether a response will be sent by 28 October 2026, or whether an extension under Article 12(3) is being claimed and, if so, the reasons.\n3. That the first-registration files for WA231076 and WA240304, and the complaint file under N610CGV, are held under preservation in line with my notice of 28 September 2026.\n4. On the separate enquiry 260918-6720625 (WA240304): my email of 18 September 2026 asked numbered questions about whether the surviving first-registration documents distinguish the farmhouse, garden and curtilage from the eastern agricultural parcel. On 27 September I was told it had been referred \"to the appropriate team\". No substantive reply has followed in 17 working days. Please name the team and give a date for the answer. Alternatively, as that email asked, state in writing that HM Land Registry will not examine those records and that the questions should be pursued by form OC2.\n\nFor transparency, the routes that remain if these points are not answered are: a complaint to the Information Commissioner under Article 77 UK GDPR (for the subject access request); the full complaint to the Independent Complaints Reviewer under the existing referral ICR/090/26; and the statutory routes under the Land Registration Act 2002 (Schedule 4 alteration and Schedule 8 indemnity), which remain open and are not abandoned. Raising them here is not a threat of proceedings. It is so that nothing comes as a surprise.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f0631aeba10f","subject":"Re: RC26-0375 – thank you and three remaining points & Order for scans","name":"Re: RC26-0375 – thank you and three remaining points & Order for scans","date":"2026-10-21T15:13:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f0631aeba10f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a135bdc3ab000b2-rc26-0375-thank-you-and-three-remaining-points-order-for-scans","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a135bdc3ab000b2","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0375"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f0631aeba10f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Adam,\n\nThank you for your email of 13 October 2026 on RC26-0375, and for the clear answers on all three points. I accept point 3: archive number 6364275 relates to Great House, Bonvilston, not Great House Farm, Llandough. I am grateful that the item was physically examined.\n\n1. Scan order. Please treat this email as confirmation that we wish to order research-quality scans of archive numbers 6048945, 6048943 and 6048941, for private, non-commercial research for the family's case. The order form attached to your email has not come through on our side in a usable form. Could you either accept the order on the details below, or send the form again (a plain Word or PDF file is fine)?\n   - Name: Requester\n   - Email: [email redacted]\n   - Items: 6048945, 6048943, 6048941 (your estimate: four research-quality scans, within the fee waiver for fewer than five)\n   - Use: personal, non-commercial research\n\n2. Noted: no further information is held beyond the archive catalogue. Three short follow-up questions, which I do not think have been asked before:\n   a) Did the NMRW receive any material from Cadw (or the Welsh Office) relating to the 1988 listing or demolition of the Llandough farmhouse? A yes or no from the accessions or transfer register is enough.\n   b) Are the H.J. Thomas notes and plan of 26 April 1974 (ST 1681 7331) held complete, and is there any related correspondence or photography from that survey?\n   c) Is there a list of RAF or Ordnance Survey vertical aerial sorties that cover Llandough (around ST 168 733) between 1940 and 1990? I am asking only for the sortie list from the catalogue, not a chargeable search.\n\nIf any of these would be better made as a formal request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, please say so (regulation 9, advice and assistance) and treat it as one. A reply within 20 working days, by 18 November 2026, would be appreciated.\n\nWith thanks,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f05a4547ae7d","subject":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","name":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","date":"2026-10-21T15:12:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f05a4547ae7d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15e1f613adbd58-great-house-farm-suspected-historic-fraud","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15e1f613adbd58","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f05a4547ae7d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear L Rutter,\n\nThank you for your email of 21 October 2026, and for passing my email of 30 September 2026 to a Legal Manager.\n\nI note the CPS position: it cannot accept evidence from members of the public, and material bearing on any criminal matter is for the police. Noted: material of that kind is for the police, and none will be sent to the CPS as evidence.\n\nYour reply says the CPS \"is not involved in, and has no knowledge of\" the case. That answers the evidential point. It does not answer whether the CPS holds records. The CPS took over prosecutions in England and Wales in October 1986, and the events at Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, Penarth, include a summons arising from events at the farm on 29 April 1988, which the local press reported as withdrawn in January 1989 as out of time. Our position is that any file on that summons would have been a CPS file.\n\nI therefore make the following requests. They are requests for information, not the submission of evidence.\n\nRequest under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000\n1. Whether the CPS (including CPS Wales and any earlier CPS area office covering Glamorgan) holds any record, from 1 October 1986 to 31 December 1990, that refers to Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, BP Properties Ltd, or the summons described above.\n2. If such records once existed but are no longer held: the retention schedule that applied to magistrates' court case files of that period, and any destruction or disposal record for them.\n3. The searches made before your reply of 21 October (systems searched, terms used), so that \"no knowledge of the case\" can be understood as either \"no record held\" or \"no search made\".\n\nIf any part of this would be better framed differently, please advise under section 16 FOIA (the duty to advise and assist). Any personal data within scope should be dealt with separately as a subject access request under section 45 of the Data Protection Act 2018. Please treat this email as that request, so far as it concerns Requester's own personal data.\n\nStatutory dates: the FOIA response is due within 20 working days of receipt, by 18 November 2026; the subject access response is due within one month.\n\nFor clarity on routes: if the FOIA answer is refused or incomplete, the next steps are internal review and then a complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 50 FOIA. Any concern about the handling of this correspondence will go through the CPS Feedback and Complaints Policy, and then to the Independent Assessor of Complaints.\n\nPlease preserve any surviving 1986–1990 records within scope while this request is open.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester's Tab agent\nAI agent acting on behalf of Requester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15f01d6f789066","subject":"Request response: Wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955 (FOI2026/23886)","name":"Request response: Wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955 (FOI2026/23886)","date":"2026-10-21T15:08:38Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15f01d6f789066.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15f01d6f789066-quest-response-wartime-and-post-war-farm-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1936-1955-foi2026-23886","scopeTopics":["defra"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["defra"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15f01d6f789066","direction":"received","from":"Information Rights Team","institutions":[{"id":"defra","name":"Defra"}],"refs":["FOI2026/23886"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15f01d6f789066.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\nPlease find attached the response to your request of 20th October for information on Wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955.\nYours sincerely\nInformation Rights Team\n[email redacted]\n\n\n====================\nAttachment: Response_FOI2026_23886.pdf (text)\n====================\n                                     Seacole Building\n                                     2 Marsham Street\n                                     London                          T: [phone redacted]\n                                     [postcode redacted]                        [email redacted]\n                                                                     www.gov.uk/defra\n\n\nRequester                                                   Our ref: FOI2026/23886\nBy email: [email redacted]                             21 October 2026\n\n\n\nDear Requester,\n\n\nREQUEST FOR INFORMATION: Wartime and post-war farm records for Great\nHouse Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955\n\nThank you for your request for information of 20 October 2026 about wartime and post-\nwar farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955. We have\nhandled your request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (FOIA).\n\nYour information request and our response are set out below.\n\nWestern Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092), to which the Bute Estate\nconveyed its interest by a conveyance dated 25 December 1938, obtained a\npossession order on 4 July 1955. I am trying to establish from the records how the\nfarm was dealt with between 1936 and 1955, who took each decision, and on what\nrecord.\n\nPlease tell me whether Defra holds, and provide, the following for Great House Farm\nfor 1936–1955:\n1. any National Farm Survey or other MAF farm record for the holding, including the\n    occupier, the owner and the acreage recorded;\n2. any record of the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (or its\n    successor, the Glamorgan Agricultural Executive Committee) about the farm:\n    inspections, gradings, cultivation or other directions, supervision orders, or any\n    possession, requisition or termination of tenancy, with the date and the committee\n    or officer (by role) who made each decision;\n3. any application for, or decision on, the Minister's consent to the operation of a\n    notice to quit the holding (Agricultural Holdings Act 1948), with the date, the\n    decision and who made it;\n4. any compensation claim or payment for the land under the Compensation\n    (Defence) Act 1939 or the Agriculture Acts;\n5. any correspondence with Western Ground Rents Ltd, the Bute Estate or their\n    agents about the farm, or about the possession order of 4 July 1955 and the land\n    it covered.\n\nIf records in scope have been transferred to The National Archives (for example MAF\n32, the National Farm Survey, or the MAF 80 series of committee minutes), please\n\fgive the reference rather than treating that part as not held. If any record in scope was\ndestroyed, please give the retention or disposal schedule that applied and, where\nrecorded, the date and the authority for its destruction. If any part is held by the Welsh\nGovernment rather than by Defra, please say so.\n\nFollowing a search of our paper and electronic records, we have established that the\ninformation that you have requested is not held by Defra.\n\nWe can confirm that the information may be held by the Welsh Government, which\ncan be contacted at https://www.gov.wales/contact-welsh-government#52148\n\nWe attach an annex giving contact details should you be unhappy with the service you\nhave received.\n\nIf you have any queries about this letter please contact us.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\n\n\nInformation Rights Team\n[email redacted]\n\fAnnex\nComplaints\nIf you are unhappy with the service you have received in relation to your request you\nmay make a complaint or appeal against our decision under section 17(7) of the FOIA\nor under regulation 11 of the EIRs, as applicable, within 40 working days of the date\nof this letter. Please write to Damian Lynch, Head of Information Rights via email at\n[email redacted] and they will arrange for an internal review of your\ncase. Details of Defra’s complaints procedure are on our website.\nIf you are not content with the outcome of the internal review, section 50 of the FOIA\nand regulation 18 of the EIRs gives you the right to apply directly to the Information\nCommission’s Office (ICO) for a decision. Please note that generally the ICO cannot\nmake a decision unless you have first exhausted Defra’s own complaints procedure.\nThe ICO can be contacted using the following link:\nhttps://ico.org.uk/"},{"id":"gm-1a15eff3a07ac34b","subject":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","name":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information 1189/26","date":"2026-10-21T15:05:41Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15eff3a07ac34b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15eff3a07ac34b-sponse-freedom-of-information-1189-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15eff3a07ac34b","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1189/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15eff3a07ac34b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nYour request for information has now been considered and our response is attached.\n\nI trust that this information answers your request. Should you have any queries and wish to contact us by e-mail, please do so using the mail box [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nSouth Wales Police provides you the right to request a re-examination of your case under its review procedure (copy attached). If you decide to request such a review and having followed the Forces full process you are still dissatisfied, then you have the right to direct your comments to the Information Commissioner who will give it consideration.\n\nKind regards,\n\nClare Mccarley\nSwyddog Ymchwil ac Ansawdd Data | Freedom of Information\nRheolwr Rheoli Data a Datgeliadau | Data Management and Disclosure Unit\nPencadlys Heddlu De Cymru | South Wales Police Headquarters\nFfôn/Phone: [phone redacted] |\n[A blue circle with white lines on it  Description automatically generated]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>[A blue sign with white text  Description automatically generated]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/cyfryngau-cymdeithasol/>[A blue sign with white text  Description automatically generated]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/social-media/>\n[A logo of a police officer  Description automatically generated]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>\n[A logo with a circle and text  Description automatically generated]\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg ac yn Saesneg.\nByddwn yn ymateb yn eich iaith o ddewis.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English.\nWe will respond in your language of choice.\n\n\n\n\n\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/.\n\n\n====================\nAttachment: Response 1189_26.pdf (text)\n====================\n                                    Freedom of Information Request 1189/26\n                                            Response Date: 21st October 2026\n\nRequest\n\nRequest for a preservation notice.\n\nResponse\n\nThe Freedom of Information Act 2000 creates a statutory right of access to recorded information held by public\nauthorities. When processing requests for information under the Freedom of Information Act, public authorities have\ntwo duties to consider. Section 1(1)(a) is the duty to confirm or deny that the requested information is held, and\nSection 1(1)(b) is to the duty to communicate the requested information to the applicant.\n\nSection 8 of the Act is also relevant here, as it outlines the criteria which need to be fulfilled in order for a request to be\ndeemed ‘valid’ and therefore suitable for processing under the Act.\n\nSection 8(1) of the Act provides:\n\n(1) In this Act any reference to a “request for information” is a reference to such a request which:\n\n(a) is in writing,\n(b) states the name of the applicant and an address for correspondence,\n(c) describes the information requested.\n\nSection 84 of the Act clarifies that ‘information’ means ‘information recorded in any form’.\n\nPlease see the link below for further guidance on how to submit a valid FOI request:\n\nRecognising a request made under the Freedom of Information Act (section 8) | ICO"},{"id":"gm-1a15ee71949f5b94","subject":"RE: [2] Re: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough (TO/HF/05677/26)","name":"RE: [2] Re: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough (TO/HF/05677/26)","date":"2026-10-21T14:39:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15ee71949f5b94.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15ee71949f5b94-2-re-supplement-to-complaint-re-served-20-september-2026-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-to-hf-05677-26","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15ee71949f5b94","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15ee71949f5b94.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your further emails of 17, 20, 22, and 30 September regarding your complaint relating to Cadw’s 1988 assessment of Great House Farm.  I am sending this email as a single reply to all three of these emails.\n\nCadw is part of Welsh Government and does not therefore operate a sperate complaints process. I understand that your complaint has, however, been received and considered by the Welsh Government Complaints Advice Team and that they have responded to you on 30 September, advising that this is not a matter they can investigate under the complaints policy.\n\nIn terms of the further questions you have asked, there is again nothing further I can add to our previous replies. In particular, and as I stated in my email of 4 September, it would be inappropriate for me to speculate on the events around the listing assessment without our own contemporary evidence being available to me to substantiate precisely what occurred, and what information was and was not considered at that time.\n\nWith regard to your email of 28 September, and separately to those regarding your complaint referred to above, I can advise that all information caught by a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and/ or Environmental Information Regulations 2004 would not be destroyed and Welsh Government’s Retention and Disposal Schedule<https://www.gov.wales/welsh-government-retention-and-disposal-schedule> will otherwise be applied.\n\nA response to your Freedom of Information request of 28 September (ATSNI 27589) was provided on 19 October and your Freedom of Information request of 10 October (ATSNI 26-0009) is currently under consideration and a response will be provided by 6 November.\n\nYou have now been corresponding with officials in Cadw in respect of matters relating to Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough since 27 May 2026. We consider that you have been given appropriate responses to the matters you have raised and, as stated above, we have nothing further to add to the information and explanations which we have already provided to you.\nIn light of the fact that you are opposed to accepting the responses we have to offer, there does not appear to be any merit in continuing to correspond with you on these matters.\nShould you wish to communicate on any other matter, that has not been previously addressed, you should contact me directly using this email address.\nYour correspondence must be reasonable and to the point. Government officials will not engage further in communication that seeks to re-open matters previously addressed or those on which we are unable to provide further information. Unless new evidence is raised, any further correspondence regarding Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough will be filed but not answered.\n\nYours sincerely.\n\nAndy Wigley\n\n\n[cid:[email redacted]0F5E0]\n\nDr Andy Wigley\nPrif Arolygydd – Pennaeth Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Chief Inspector - Head of Historic Environment Inspectorate\nCadw\nDysgu, Cymunedau a Diwylliant / Learning, Communities and Culture\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nTŷ Ladywell / Ladywell House\nY Drenewydd / Newtown\nPowys\n[postcode redacted]\n\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\nFfôn symudol / Mobile: [phone redacted]\nE-bost/ Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[cid:[email redacted]0F5E0][cid:[email redacted]0F5E0]\nP Helpwch yr amgylchedd - peidiwch ag argraffu hon os nad oes gwir raid   Help our environment - only print this if really necessary\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth Gymraeg. Cewch ateb Cymraeg i bob gohebiaeth Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh. Correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not involve any delay.\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 30 September 2026 01:39\nTo: Wigley, Andy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: [2] Re: Supplement to complaint re-served 20 September 2026 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough\n\nDr Wigley / Cadw Complaints Manager,\n\nThis is not a new complaint and not a chase. It is notice for the stage-one complaint already opened under ticket #628635887: complaint of 17 September 2026, re-served on 20 September after delivery to [email redacted]<[email redacted]> was rejected, with a supplement sent on 22 September.\n\nThe complaint is that Cadw’s 1988 assessment of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth (approximately ST 1681 7331; later HER GGAT02038s), did not adequately address the historic fabric, archaeological context and information then available, and that the building was demolished in December 1988 before any listing protection was secured.\n\nI am not asking Cadw to determine title. I am asking Cadw to answer for its own role, decisions and professional handling of the 1988 assessment.\n\nWhat I seek from this complaint, if Cadw is willing to resolve it without referral to the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales, is:\n\n1. A written stage-one decision on whether Cadw’s 1988 assessment was adequate having regard to the material then available and the criteria and process applicable at the time, including the relevant 1979 GGAT excavation record concerning the Roman villa and associated early-medieval archaeology on land formerly within the farm holding.\n\n2. If Cadw concludes that the assessment was inadequate, a written acknowledgement of that finding, confined to Cadw’s own role and without determination of title or third-party liability.\n\n3. Cadw’s confirmation of whether it will ask Heneb to review HER entry GGAT02038s and, where necessary, correct or supplement the entry so that the relevant excavated archaeology is accurately recorded, rather than leaving the site classified simply as “POST MEDIEVAL – Farm” where that description is incomplete.\n\n4. Confirmation of what records from the 1988 assessment Cadw still holds, what material was destroyed, disposed of or not retained, and the applicable retention schedule or rule governing the 1988 file.\n\nI do not expect Cadw to rebuild the house or determine the separate title dispute involving HM Land Registry or any successor in title. Those matters belong to other processes.\n\nI will await the stage-one response. I will not add further correspondence to this complaint unless Cadw asks a question or the published response timescale expires.\n\nPlease treat ticket #628635887 together with the emails of 17, 20 and 22 September 2026 as the complaint. This letter adds no new grounds.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-1a15e9a1a2129ef3","subject":"RE: Epexio contact us form submission","name":"RE: Epexio contact us form submission","date":"2026-10-21T13:15:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15e9a1a2129ef3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a07b3bf0b65e56c-epexio-contact-us-form-submission","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a07b3bf0b65e56c","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":["2026/4439"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15e9a1a2129ef3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ref: 2026/4439\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your further emails received into our enquiries system 28th September.\n\nDBDT/123/7<https://canfod.glamarchives.gov.uk/en/records/DBDT/123/7> tenancy agreement between West Ground Rents Ltd and Mr John Williams, 18 May 1939.  This document relates to 5.30 acres marked in pink on the map (your photograph number 1067).  This appears to relate to agricultural land adjacent to Ty-Mawr farmhouse  and Llwyn-yr-eryr but does not make any mention of the farmhouse or other structures as being included. It reserves quarrying and other rights to Western Ground Rents Ltd.\n\nWe would advise you consult a land law legal specialist to further interpret the document.\n\nIncidentally, we note that the leasehold of the land marked on the map in the tenancy agreement DBDT/123/7, was included in the particulars of sale of Llwyn-yr-eryr by Mr Charles St David Spencer in 1936 (auction particulars are in DSA/14/91<https://canfod.glamarchives.gov.uk/en/records/DSA/14/91>).\n\nIn our previous emails we have outlined the records that we hold.  If records of a particular transaction have not been highlighted to you this is because we have not found reference to such a document within the collection.  We have suggested other repositories for you to approach but it is quite likely, as with all land, that only a small proportion of all deeds relating to Ty Mawr will be held by an archive repository.  Indeed, for the majority of properties in the geographic area that we cover, we hold no deeds so it is fortuitous that you have been able to find some relevant material within our collection.  We can confirm that we do not have any records of the later title history.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nLouise Hunt\nArchifydd / Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\nClos Parc Morgannwg\nLecwydd / Leckwith\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/<http://www.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/> www.glamarchives.gov.uk<http://www.glamarchives.gov.uk/>\nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives<http://www.facebook.com/glamarchives>\nwww.instagram.com/glamarchives<https://www.instagram.com/glamarchives/>\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a15e3779a430212","subject":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RE: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-21T11:27:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15e3779a430212.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6-foi-request-western-ground-rents-ltd-company-no-00342092-dissolved-1997-any-bona-vacantia-property-or-interests-at-lland","scopeTopics":["bona-vacantia"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bona-vacantia"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6","direction":"received","from":"Dan Copping","institutions":[{"id":"bona-vacantia","name":"Government Legal Department (Bona Vacantia)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15e3779a430212.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir/Madam\n\nThank you for your e-mail of 20th October 2026.\n\nYour request is being considered under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nWe will write to you again within 20 working days.\n\nKind regards\n\nDan Copping\nfor the Treasury Solicitor\n\nwww.gov.uk/bonavacantia\n\nA copy of our Privacy Notice can be found here:\nhttps://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/bona-vacantia/about/personal-information-charter\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:19\nTo: BVFOI <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nDear Bona Vacantia FOI Officer,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, near Penarth (historically Glamorgan; South Glamorgan from 1974 to 1996; now the Vale of Glamorgan), and of the land and woodland around it. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record of how this land changed hands, who made each decision, and on what record.\n\nBackground, from public sources:\n- Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) is reported to have bought the Bute family's urban estate in 1938. It let farm land at Llandough from 1939, and it conveyed land at Llandough to the BP Pension Trust by a conveyance recited in HM Land Registry's records as dated 31 December 1969.\n- On 26 June 1996 its members placed it in members' voluntary liquidation, together with other dormant companies whose registered office was BP House (London Gazette, issue 54455, 3 July 1996, pages\n8979 and 8982). The final meeting was called for 16 May 1997 (London Gazette, issue 54739, page 4683), and the company was dissolved in 1997.\n\nPlease tell me whether the Bona Vacantia Division (or the Treasury Solicitor, before the Government Legal Department was formed) holds any information about this company, and in particular:\n\n1. Whether any property, right or interest of Western Ground Rents Ltd was referred to your Division, or vested in the Crown as bona vacantia, on or after its dissolution. This includes freehold land, woodland, freehold reversions on leases, ground rents or rentcharges, and any reserved mines and minerals, and especially anything at Llandough, Leckwith, Cogan or Penarth.\n\n2. For any such property: when and how it came to your notice (and who referred it, if a company or public body); what was done with it (sale, transfer, disclaimer under section 656 of the Companies Act\n1985 or section 1013 of the Companies Act 2006, or retention); the date and the instrument; the buyer or transferee and the price, if a company or public body; and the record of the decision, with the role of the officer who approved it.\n\n3. Any enquiry, application or correspondence about the company's property received since 1997 (for example from HM Land Registry, a local authority, a developer, a charity or a BP group company), with its date, the enquirer if a company or public body, and your reply.\n\n4. Whether any application was made to restore the company to the register, and any letter your Division issued in connection with it.\n\n5. If your Division held records about the company that are no longer\nheld: when they were destroyed or transferred, under which retention schedule, and the record authorising that.\n\nA \"not held\" answer to any part would be just as useful as a positive one. If anything is withheld, please name the exemption relied on for each part. Copies by email are ideal.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n\n\n________________________________\nThe information in this e-mail belongs to HM Government and may be confidential or otherwise protected by law. If you received it in error, we request that you inform us by return e-mail and then delete it immediately, without printing, copying or disseminating it.\nThe original of this email was scanned for viruses by Government Secure Intranet (GSi) virus scanning service supplied by Vodafone in partnership with MessageLabs. HM Government does not however warrant that it is virus free at point of delivery."},{"id":"gm-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d","subject":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-21T11:15:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d-information-request-great-house-farm-t-y-mawr-near-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["historic-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["historic-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d","direction":"received","from":"Wilkins, Mark","institutions":[{"id":"historic-england","name":"Historic England"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15e2cfd24eaf4d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Our Reference: 26/04323\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nRe: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan:\n\nThank you for your email on 20 October 2026 in which you requested the following information related to the property above:\n\n1. The record of that transfer as it relates to this item, or to Llandough: the transfer list or schedule entry, its description, and any covering correspondence.\n\n2. How and when Historic England (or English Heritage, RCHME or the National Buildings Record before it) acquired the item: the accession or registration record, the source or depositor, and the date.\n\n3. Whether Historic England kept any copy, digital image, catalogue record or index entry of the item, or of any other material about the site, after the transfer; and if so, a copy.\n\n4. The record of the decision to include this item in the 2018 exchange: the date, the role of the officer who authorised it, and the basis.\n\n5. Any other information you hold about Great House Farm / Tŷy Mawr or its buildings, including photographs, survey notes, and any correspondence with Cadw, RCAHMW or the Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust about its listing or its demolition (1986–1989). Search terms: \"Great House Farm\", \"Tŷy Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"Penarth\".\n\n6. If anything within items 1 to 5 was held but has since been destroyed or transferred elsewhere: when, under which retention schedule, and where it went.\n\nYour request has been processed under the Environmental Information Regulations (2004).\n\nFollowing a search of our paper and electronic records I can confirm that, under the exception contained within Regulation 12(4)(a) of the EIR, I am unable to provide you with anything on this occasion, as we do not hold any information that falls within the scope of your request.\n\nHowever, we do have a record of the following:\n\nArchaeological Reports on microfiche\n\nThese reports were produced by the RCHME and a variety of organisations and copied by or for the RCHME from the 1980s onwards for research and to provide a security copy. Transferred to RCAHMW on 12 January 2018. This would have been a microfiche copy of a report produced by the RCHME or another organisation. However, we do not have an itemised list of the microfiche that was sent: we just sent the section of microfiche collection relating to sites in Wales.\n\nWe have also found a record from RACHMW Coflein which may relate to the material from us\n\nhttps://coflein.gov.uk/en/search?term=6500905&type=archive\n\n\nI am sorry that I have been unable to provide you with the information that you have asked for on this occasion. If you are unhappy with this response you may request an internal review.  Details of our review procedure are attached.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nMark Wilkins\nACCESS TO INFORMATION OFFICER\nLegal & Governance\n• T [phone redacted]\n• Historic England | Room 2/20 | The Engine House | Fire Fly Avenue | Swindon | Wiltshire | [postcode redacted]\n• [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nWe will keep a record of contact details provided by you and details of your enquiry for administrative purposes.  We will not use these details for marketing purposes and we will never sell your personal details or share your information with another organisation for marketing purposes. If you would like to know more or understand your data protection rights, please take a look at our privacy policy<https://historicengland.org.uk/terms/privacy/>\n\n\n\nEnsuring our heritage lives on and is loved for longer.\nhistoricengland.org.uk\nThis e‑mail (and any attachments) is confidential and may contain personal views which are not the views of Historic England unless specifically stated. If you have received it in error, please delete it from your system and notify the sender immediately. \n​Do not use, copy or disclose the information in any way nor act in reliance on it. Any information sent to Historic England may become publicly available. For information about our use of your personal data please visit: historicengland.org.uk/terms/privacy"},{"id":"gm-1a15e1f613adbd58","subject":"Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","name":"Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","date":"2026-10-21T11:01:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15e1f613adbd58.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15e1f613adbd58-great-house-farm-suspected-historic-fraud","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15e1f613adbd58","direction":"received","from":"Victim Liaison Cymru-Wales","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15e1f613adbd58.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nFurther to my colleague's email dated 8 October 2026, which advised that your email of 30 September 2026 had been referred to a Legal Manager for consideration, I have now received their response.\n\nI understand that you are trying to help, and I appreciate the time you have taken to raise your concerns.\n\nAs previously explained, the Crown Prosecution Service (CPS) cannot accept or consider information, evidence or other material sent directly to us by members of the public. Any information relating to a criminal investigation must be provided to the police, who are responsible for gathering and assessing evidence.\n\nThe CPS is not involved in, and has no knowledge of, the case you have referred to. Therefore, we are unable to comment on the matters you have raised or answer any questions regarding the investigation.\n\nIf you have information that you believe may be relevant or wish to raise concerns about how the matter is being dealt with, you should contact the police directly. They will be able to consider the information you provide and advise you further.\n\nI appreciate that this may not be the response you were hoping for, but I hope this explains why the CPS is unable to assist you further.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nL Rutter\nRheolwr Cyswllt Dioddefwyr / Victim Liaison Officer\nUned Cyswllt Dioddefwyr / Victim Liaison Unit\n[Gwasanaeth Erlyn y Goron / Crown Prosecution Service]\nCrown Prosecution Service, CPS Wales Area, Welsh Government Offices, Cathays Park, Cardiff [postcode redacted]. Gwasanaeth Erlyn y Goron, Ardal CPS Cymru, Llywodraeth Cymru, Parc Cathays, Caerdydd [postcode redacted].\nFfôn/Telephone: [phone redacted]\nwww.cps.gov.uk<http://www.cps.gov.uk/>"},{"id":"gm-1a15e19a4609a6ad","subject":"RE: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","name":"RE: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","date":"2026-10-21T10:54:58Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15e19a4609a6ad.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad-icr-090-26-further-formal-points-on-the-first-registration-file-and-1987-amalgamation","scopeTopics":["hmlr-icr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr-icr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad","direction":"received","from":"ICR Office Inbox","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr-icr","name":"HM Land Registry (Independent Complaints Reviewer)"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26","WA231076","WA240304"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15e19a4609a6ad.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email. In Ms St Rose’s absence, I have put your request to the ICR today. She has asked me to confirm that her decision not to investigate further was final.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nChris Jackson (Mr)\nSenior Investigation Officer\nOffice of the Independent Complaints Reviewer\n10 South Colonnade, Canary Wharf, London [postcode redacted].\nOffice telephone: [phone redacted]\nwww.icrev.org.uk<http://www.icrev.org.uk>\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:29\nTo: ICR Office Inbox <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation\n\nDear Ms St Rose,\n\nICR/090/26 – HM Land Registry, titles WA231076 and WA240304 (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough)\n\nThank you for your letter of 9 October 2026, which you kindly re-sent on 12 October after my email of 10 October crossed with it. I have read the Independent Complaints Reviewer's decision carefully and I understand that she cannot review HM Land Registry's legal decisions, assess the evidence, or revisit the 1987 litigation. I am not asking her to do any of those things.\n\nYour letter explains that the ICR \"can give a view on whether HMLR has followed its standard procedure in reviewing registration decisions and whether its complaint responses clearly and fully deal with the matters within HMLR's remit\". I respectfully ask her to reconsider on that limited basis only. HMLR's replies to me (23 March, 19 April, 25 May and 30 July 2026) did not answer three factual questions about HMLR's own records, each of which is within HMLR's remit and none of which asks HMLR or the ICR to decide who owns the land:\n1. whether HMLR's records show that any enquiry or notice was sent to the occupiers of the farmhouse before the first registrations of 1982–83, and if so to whom, at what address and on what date. The Stage 2 response says HMLR \"did not receive or were aware of any interest that you or your family may or may not have had in the land\"; it does not say whether a notice was sent;\n2. why the conveyance of 31 December 1969, relied on as the root of title, does not appear in the schedule of documents on the first-registration file released on 30 July 2026, and whether HMLR holds it under any other reference;\n3. on what application the two titles were amalgamated on 2 February 1987, and whether the record shows what was known then about the pending appeal.\n\nOne small point of record: your letter refers to the Stage 1 response as dated 19 April 2025. I believe it is dated 19 April 2026.\n\nIf the ICR will not reconsider, please confirm in writing that her decision of 9 October 2026 is final, so that I can ask my MP to consider a referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman, enclosing your letter as you suggest. A reply by 6 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nOn Mon, Oct 12, 2026 at 10:09 AM, ICR Office Inbox <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nIt appears that you have not received my letter dated 9 October 2026 which I sent on the same date. Therefore, please find that letter attached.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nDenyse St Rose\nOffice Manager and Investigations Officer\nICR Office\n\n10 South Colonnade\nCanary Wharf, London [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted] (Telephone number)\nwww.icrev.org.uk<http://www.icrev.org.uk>\n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:12\nTo: ICR Office Inbox\nSubject: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation\n\nDear Independent Complaints Reviewer,\n\nReference ICR/090/26.\n\nI hold the stage-one decision of 19 April 2026 and the stage-two decision of 25 May 2026. I also hold the schedule of 43 documents on the first-registration files released on 30 July 2026.\n\nThe family’s established case, recorded on the public wiki and under investigation, is that the 1877 arrangement took effect in 1928, transferring the full Parcel A (house and buildings, barn, stable and west-side yard, garden, northern forest and the south-east ground later registered as VG41) to the Williams family. The 1939 agreement/plan depicts Parcel B only. On the family account, the 1949 attempt to make the occupation of Parcel A permissive failed, title papers were reported missing in 1950–52, and Western Ground Rents’ 4 July 1955 enforcement of Parcel B also seized the Parcel-A forest and green under “whole farm” wording. Later documentary work is directed at corroborating or precisely mapping that account and tracing those areas into later titles.\n\nFour specific points remain unanswered and are relevant to that investigation:\n\n1. The 1969 root deed recited as the root of title does not appear on the schedule. Please confirm whether HMLR holds that deed under any other reference, or whether it was never lodged.\n2. What evidence exists on the file of notice or opportunity to object given to the occupying family (Williams / Buckler) in 1982–83.\n3. The precise legal and administrative basis for the 1987 title amalgamation that took place while the Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler were still live.\n4. Whether the inclusion of the woodland (or any land beyond the 1938\nconveyance) is regarded as a possible mistake capable of alteration or indemnity under the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice Guide 39.\n\nPlease confirm these points form part of the live investigation and state the exact start date of the ICR six-month period (so that the\n~25 November 2026 outer limit can be verified).\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a15daaa6d10bd96","subject":"Re: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","name":"Re: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","date":"2026-10-21T08:53:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15daaa6d10bd96.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526ec926276db-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-follow-up-to-my-preservation-notice-of-28-september-2026","scopeTopics":["ads"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ads"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526ec926276db","direction":"received","from":"Archaeology Data Service","institutions":[{"id":"ads","name":"Archaeology Data Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15daaa6d10bd96.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your follow up query and please find our responses further\nbelow.\n\n*Question 1: **whether the Archaeology Data Service holds any deposit,\nmetadata **record or archive identifier relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ\nMawr, **Llandough, in particular the 1990 Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological\nTrust **assessment or the 1994 Cotswold Archaeology work*\n\nThe ADS holds the following metadata records and digital resources:\n\n*a) METADATA RECORD*\n\nTy Mawr;Great House Farm.\n\n\nhttps://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/data-catalogue/resource/016dc563db84d7089594378df3a91695f0464c1064e48fc878a0172326070b02\n\n\nRecord deposited with us by *Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical\nMonuments of Wales* as part of the Coflein database of sites and monuments\nin Wales. Please see the link provided for details.\n\n\n*b) METADATA RECORD*\n\nGreat House Farm\n\n\nhttps://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/data-catalogue/resource/64c8d227d5d18a95bd506e5e8130bf4d1d4e747882d9d58a44930714cc487fb2\n\n\nRecord deposited with us by *Glamorgan-Gwent HER* (as was). Record mentions\ndemolition of the farmhouse. Please see the link provided for details.\n\n\n*c) METADATA RECORD*\n\nGREAT HOUSE FARM, LLANDOUGH\n\n\nhttps://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/data-catalogue/resource/f132b9a43fb4af027987100ac49e601336d667bcd12f5726b3726e3b1f0c2296\n\n\nRecord deposited with us by *Glamorgan-Gwent HER* (as was). Record relates\nto the GGAT 1990 excavation. Please see the link provided for details.\n\n\n*d) Published academic article*\n\nAn Early-medieval Monastic Cemetery at Llandough, Glamorgan: Excavations in\n1994\n\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.5284/1071962\n\n\nAn eprint of the publication in the journal Medieval Archaeology covering\nthe 1994 excavations by Cotswold Archaeology. This was deposited with us by\nthe *Society for Medieval Archaeology*.\n\n\n*e) Digital resource*\n\nThe Early Medieval Monastic Cemetery at Llandough, Glamorgan\n\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.5284/1000252\n\n\nDatasets from the 1994 excavations by Cotswold Archaeology that cover the\nmedieval remains encountered, deposited with us by *Cotswold Archaeology.*\n\n\n*Question 2:* *what searches were made, and whether any physical files were\nchecked*\n\nThe search was undertaken using the ADS Data Catalogue\n<https://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/data-catalogue/> and the ADS Library\n<https://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/library/index.xhtml>.\n\n\n*Question 3:* *whether anything has been destroyed or transferred elsewhere\n(and **if so, when and to whom).*\n\nAccessioning of records (metadata sets or digital resources) is recorded\nvia our Collections Management System. A review of our CMS indicates that\nno digital material has been removed from any of these resources - and\nrelating to the site in question - since deposition.\n\n\n\nPlease let us know if we can be of any further assistance.\n\n\nBest wishes,\n\nAnett Mladoniczki\n\nHelpdesk\n\n\nArchaeology Data Service <https://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/>\n\nUniversity of York, The Guildhall, St Martin's Courtyard, Coney Street,\nYork, [postcode redacted]\n\nEmail Disclaimer\n<https://www.york.ac.uk/about/legal-statements/email-disclaimer/> |  Privacy\nPolicy <https://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/privacy/>\n\n\nOn Mon, 19 Oct 2026 at 23:14, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Archaeology Data Service,\n>\n> Re: my preservation notice of 28 September 2026; your reply of 2 October\n> 2026.\n>\n> I am writing about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr,\n> Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, the subject of BP\n> Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court 1986; Court of Appeal 1987).\n> Thank you for your reply of 2 October 2026; I understand the\n> Archaeology Data Service preserves its data permanently.\n>\n> I would be grateful if you would tell me:\n> 1. whether the Archaeology Data Service holds any deposit, metadata\n> record or archive identifier relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr,\n> Llandough, in particular the 1990 Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\n> assessment or the 1994 Cotswold Archaeology work;\n> 2. what searches were made, and whether any physical files were checked;\n> 3. whether anything has been destroyed or transferred elsewhere (and\n> if so, when and to whom).\n>\n> A reply by 16 November 2026 would be much appreciated. Please also\n> make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is\n> destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n>\n> Thank you for your help.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n> \n> https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a15ba18a498992d","subject":"MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-20T23:24:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15ba18a498992d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15ba18a498992d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan,\n\nFurther to my email of last night, and so the Council can prepare, I list the questions I will ask on Thursday. All of them are based on points already raised in our correspondence.\n\n1. What consideration was my first approach given before the reply of 20 November 2025?\n2. Does the Council hold any Tŷ Mawr records besides the minute books deposited in 2002 (my email of 14 June)?\n3. Which agenda items cover the \"other matters\" your email of 11 October said would be considered in October?\n4. Who decided the meeting would be remote only, and on what date?\n5. When was the website agenda revised and republished?\n6. Where are the published arrangements for multi-location meetings (s.47, LGE(W)A 2021)?\n7. Was a physical public venue considered?\n8. When will my internal review (13 October) and narrower request (20 October) be answered, and will the review apply the EIR?\n9. Will my statement and briefing pack be received and minuted?\n10. If the remote-only decision stands, will its reasons be minuted?\n11. Which councillor is my point of contact?\n12. How do I place the wider matters on a future agenda?\n\nPlease place this with the meeting papers.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n\nOn Tue, Oct 20, 2026 at 10:05 PM, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Mr Egan,\n>\n> Thank you for your reply of 20 October, and for confirming that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to ask questions and make comments on the business on the published agenda.\n>\n> I maintain my objection that no physical venue is being offered to residents. However, with the meeting two days away, I accept the practical position. I will join by Zoom using the link you sent on 13 October and take part under the public participation item (item 4) and item 10.\n>\n> Your reply answers the last of the five points in my email of 16 October. It does not address the other four. I would be grateful for a short reply to each, before Thursday if possible:\n>\n> 1. Who decided that the meeting would be held remotely only, and on what date.\n> 2. Whether the agenda on the Council's website and noticeboards was revised after the agenda you sent me on 13 October and, if so, the date of the revised notice.\n> 3. The Council's published arrangements or policy for remote and multi-location meetings (a link is enough).\n> 4. What consideration was given to residents who wish to observe or take part in person.\n>\n> If these cannot be answered before the meeting, I ask that they be noted as outstanding and answered afterwards, and that this exchange be kept with the meeting correspondence.\n>\n> For the meeting itself, I would also be grateful if you could:\n>\n> a) Confirm the time limit for public participation, and that I will be admitted from the waiting room and invited to speak at item 4.\n> b) Circulate my supporting briefing to all councillors in advance, if you and the Chair consider that appropriate. It is at https://www.google.com/url?q=https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792617746873000&sa=E and the read-aloud statement is at https://www.google.com/url?q=https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate/meeting-script.txt&source=gmail&ust=1792617746873000&sa=E. Please also confirm whether the written statement can be kept with the minutes.\n> c) Advise how the wider context can be handled. I understand item 10 covers two specific requests, and that decisions cannot be taken under item 16 on matters not listed on the agenda. I am not asking the Council to determine title or to make findings against any person or body. If the wider history is best dealt with separately, please tell me whether a request for a properly noticed item at a future meeting should be submitted now.\n>\n> Separately, and not as part of the above: please acknowledge my internal review request of 13 October and my narrower information request of 20 October, with the dates by which I can expect replies. I would also still welcome confirmation, from my email of 16 October, that any planning files or correspondence the Council holds for 1988-1992 under refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES are being retained.\n>\n> I remain willing to take part constructively and appreciate your help in the run-up to the meeting.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Requester\n> \n> \n>\n> On Tue, Oct 20, 2026 02:31 PM, Paul Egan <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> >\n> > Dear Requester,\n> >\n> > I would advise you that the agenda published on the Council's website and on our noticeboards specifies that this will be a remote meeting and that members of the public can attend and ask me to provide a Zoom link to attend. I can confirm that you will be given a reasonable opportunity to ask questions and make comments on any item of business specified to be transacted that is on the published agenda.\n> >\n> > Kind regards,\n> >\n> > ---\n> >\n> > Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n> >\n> > Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n> >\n> > [address removed]\n> >\n> > Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> >\n> > Telephone [phone redacted]\n> >\n> > Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk <http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk>\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> > When you contact us\n> >\n> > The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\n> > email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\n> > to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> > information and/or access our facilities and services.\n> >\n> > Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other third party. Your information may however be published in the public domain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> > For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website www.llandough-cc.co.uk <http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk>\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> > The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our identity' The Council will always strive to:\n> >\n> >  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n> >\n> > · Be accountable in all our council activities\n> >\n> > · Be responsive to the needs of the community\n> >\n> > · Encourage community participation\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> >\n> > On 2026-10-16 14:31, Requester wrote:\n> >\n> > >\n> > >\n> > > Dear Mr Egan,\n> > >\n> > > Thank you for your email confirming that the Council meeting on 22 October 2026 will now be held remotely only.\n> > >\n> > > I object to the removal of the opportunity for residents to attend in person and ask that the decision be reconsidered before the meeting.\n> > >\n> > > I recognise that the Local Government and Elections (Wales) Act 2021 provides for remote meetings. My concern is not with councillors using Zoom, but with the Council deciding that there will be no physical public attendance, without explaining the reasons for that decision or how the interests of local democratic participation have been considered.\n> > >\n> > > The Welsh Government's statutory guidance for community and town councils recognises the importance of accessible meetings, public participation and transparency. It also requires councils to have regard to the guidance when exercising their relevant functions. The Act's section 48, inserting paragraph 27A into Schedule 12 of the Local Government Act 1972, requires the person presiding over an open community council meeting to give members of the public in attendance a reasonable opportunity to make representations about the business, subject to the statutory exception.\n> > >\n> > > I therefore ask the Council to:\n> > >\n> > > 1. Reconsider whether a physical venue can be made available to residents, even if all councillors participate remotely.\n> > > 2. Confirm who made the decision to change the meeting to remote-only and when it was made.\n> > > 3. Identify the Council's published arrangements or policy governing multi-location meetings and provide the relevant link or document.\n> > > 4. Explain what consideration was given to residents' ability to observe proceedings and participate effectively, and why a physical public gallery was not provided.\n> > > 5. Confirm that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to make representations during the public participation item through the Zoom meeting, in accordance with the applicable rules.\n> > >\n> > > If the Council maintains its decision, please treat this email as a request for the reasons and the relevant policy or resolution to be recorded in the public record.\n> > >\n> > > For clarity, my outstanding FOI internal review and my requests concerning the retention of historic planning records are separate matters. I do not ask the Council to determine either matter through this objection.\n> > >\n> > > I remain willing to participate constructively in the meeting. I ask only that the Council take the concerns about public access seriously and explain its decision.\n> > >\n> > > Yours sincerely,\n> > >\n> > > Requester\n> > > \n> > > \n> > >\n> > >\n> > >\n> > >\n> > > On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 06:53 AM, Paul Egan <[email redacted]> wrote:\n> > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > > Dear Requester,\n> > > >\n> > > > Thank you for your email.\n> > > >\n> > > > Can you please note that the Council meeting on 22 October will now be held remotely only and you can use the Zoom link that has already been emailed to you.\n> > > >\n> > > > Regards,\n> > > >\n> > > > ---\n> > > >\n> > > > Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n> > > >\n> > > > Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n> > > >\n> > > > [address removed]\n> > > >\n> > > > Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> > > >\n> > > > Telephone [phone redacted]\n> > > >\n> > > > Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk <http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk>\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > > When you contact us\n> > > >\n> > > > The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\n> > > > email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\n> > > > to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> > > > information and/or access our facilities and services.\n> > > >\n> > > > Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other third party. Your information may however be published in the public domain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > > For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website www.llandough-cc.co.uk <http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk>\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > > The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our identity' The Council will always strive to:\n> > > >\n> > > >  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n> > > >\n> > > > · Be accountable in all our council activities\n> > > >\n> > > > · Be responsive to the needs of the community\n> > > >\n> > > > · Encourage community participation\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > > > On 2026-10-16 09:45, Requester wrote:\n> > > >\n> > > > >\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Dear Mr Egan,\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Thank you for the agenda and Zoom link. Ahead of the 22 October meeting I would like to flag two items for the public record, both tied to the Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr material at https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E.\n> > > > >\n> > > > > First, my FOI to the Council (treated as such in your reply of 11 October) and the internal review request of 13 October remain open. I am not asking the Council to pre-judge them at the meeting; I simply ask that the review outcome or a firm date be communicated before or at the meeting so that public participation is not conducted under a section 12 refusal that has not been reviewed.\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Second, I have placed preservation requests with The National Archives, HM Land Registry, the MOD, South Wales Police and others concerning 1988 records. If the Council holds any planning files, section 52/106 instruments or correspondence from 1988-1992 relating to planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES, I would be grateful for confirmation that they are being retained pending those wider enquiries.\n> > > > >\n> > > > > I will participate through the public participation slot only.\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Title and chronology index: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n> > > > > Long-term archive: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Yours sincerely,\n> > > > >\n> > > > > Requester\n> > > > > \n> > > > > \n> > > > > [email redacted]\n> > > > >\n> > > > >\n> > > >\n> > > >\n> > >\n> > >\n> > >\n> >\n> >\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a15b80e111654ae","subject":"MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-20T22:48:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15b80e111654ae.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15b80e111654ae.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan,\n\nThank you for your reply of 20 October and for confirming that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to ask questions and make comments on business specified on the published agenda.\n\nI maintain my objection to the absence of an in-person option for members of the public. With the meeting now two days away, I will join by Zoom using the link sent on 13 October and participate constructively. This is acceptance of the practical arrangements for this meeting, not withdrawal of my objection.\n\nYour reply answers point 5 of my email of 16 October, but leaves points 1–4 unanswered. I restate them below, with one further question about the notice (question 2), and would be grateful for a brief response to each, if possible before Thursday and in any event within 20 working days of this email:\n\n1. Decision: Who decided that the meeting would be held remotely only, and on what date?\n2. Notice: Was the agenda or meeting notice sent to me on 13 October subsequently revised? If so, when was it revised, and on what date was the revised notice published on the Council's website and noticeboards?\n3. Published arrangements: Please provide a link or copy of the Council's current published arrangements for multi-location meetings, which section 47 of the Local Government and Elections (Wales) Act 2021 requires the Council to make and publish, and identify whether any revision or replacement of those arrangements applies to this meeting.\n4. Public access: What consideration was given to residents who wish to observe or participate in person, including whether a physical public venue was considered and, if so, why it was not made available?\n\nI am not suggesting that the legislation guarantees a physical venue for every meeting. My concern is how the decision was made, which published arrangements apply, and how public access was considered in this instance.\n\nIf these questions cannot be answered before Thursday, please confirm that they remain outstanding and indicate when I can expect a response, which I would ask to be no later than 20 working days from this email. Please also retain this exchange with the meeting correspondence and identify where any formal decision or resolution concerning the arrangements is recorded.\n\nArrangements for Thursday's meeting\n\na) Public participation and Item 10\n\nPlease confirm the time limit for Item 4, the procedure for being admitted from the Zoom waiting room and invited to speak, and any separate time limit or procedure for making representations when Item 10 is reached. I intend to make a brief contribution under Item 4 and to address the Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr business under Item 10, in accordance with your confirmation concerning representations on published agenda business.\n\nb) Circulation and retention of the statement\n\nPlease circulate my supporting briefing and read-aloud statement to all councillors before the meeting:\n\n- \"Meeting briefing\" (https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate/)\n- \"Read-aloud statement\" (https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate/meeting-script.txt)\n\nPlease confirm whether the written statement can be retained with the meeting papers and referred to in the minutes. If the full briefing cannot be circulated before the meeting, I would be grateful if the statement could at least be circulated and the briefing link made available to councillors.\n\nc) The wider context and any future agenda item\n\nI understand that Item 10 covers two specific requests, and that Item 16 concerns correspondence rather than decisions on unlisted business. I am not asking the Council to determine title to the land or to make findings against any person or body.\n\nThe wider history, heritage and outstanding records questions may require separate consideration. If these matters cannot properly be addressed under Item 10, please advise whether I should now submit a request for a properly notified item at a future meeting and whether any particular notice, motion or other procedure is required.\n\nSeparate information and preservation matters\n\nSeparately from the meeting arrangements, please acknowledge receipt of my internal review request of 13 October (the later of my two emails that day, which stands as sent) and my narrower information request of 20 October, and advise the anticipated response date for each. As my request of 21 September concerns land and environmental information, I would ask that the review consider it under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, which contain no cost limit equivalent to section 12 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI would also welcome confirmation of whether the Council holds planning files, section 52 or section 106 instruments, or related correspondence from 1988–1992 concerning planning references 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES and, if so, whether those records are being retained pending the wider records enquiries.\n\nThe wider experience, which I ask to be placed on record before Thursday\n\nI raise the following so that the Council has my concerns in writing ahead of the meeting:\n\n- My first approach to the Council about this matter received the reply of 20 November 2025: \"I regret to inform you that we are unable to assist with the matter you raise.\" From my side, the Council has not engaged with the substance since then, which is why I have had to escalate by formal requests, an internal review and a complaint about the handling of my correspondence.\n- When I was told the matter could be raised at a meeting, I was not told where or when that meeting would be held. Only after I asked for those details so that I could attend did the meeting become remote only. I have travelled some 7,000 miles to be present in Llandough for it.\n- The Council regularly tells residents on its public social media that it is a community council that is transparent and approachable and that will answer questions. My experience has not matched that, and I ask the Council to explain the difference.\n- For my family, raising these matters at all is difficult. Since the demolition of Great House Farm in 1988, we have lived for 38 years largely silent and in fear about it. I have already explained this to you and to councillors. A remote-only meeting, arranged after I asked to attend in person, is not accommodating of that.\n- Thursday is my family's opportunity to have these matters recorded. I ask that this message, my briefing and my statement are kept with the meeting papers, so that the minutes can later be compared with the points raised, and any points not reached can be taken forward at a future meeting.\n\nI appreciate that this is shortly before the meeting. Where a substantive answer is not possible before Thursday, a brief acknowledgement identifying what remains outstanding and when it will be addressed (within 20 working days at the latest) would be helpful.\n\nI remain willing to participate constructively and appreciate your assistance in the run-up to the meeting.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\n\nOn Tue, Oct 20, 2026 at 10:14 PM, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Mr Egan,\n>\n> Thank you for your reply of 20 October and for confirming that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to ask questions and make comments on business specified on the published agenda.\n>\n> I maintain my objection to the absence of an in-person option for members of the public. With the meeting now two days away, I will join by Zoom using the link sent on 13 October and participate constructively. This is acceptance of the practical arrangements for this meeting, not withdrawal of my objection.\n>\n> Your reply answers point 5 of my email of 16 October, but leaves points 1–4 unanswered. I restate them below, with one further question about the notice (question 2), and would be grateful for a brief response to each, if possible before Thursday and in any event within 20 working days of this email:\n>\n> 1. Decision: Who decided that the meeting would be held remotely only, and on what date?\n> 2. Notice: Was the agenda or meeting notice sent to me on 13 October subsequently revised? If so, when was it revised, and on what date was the revised notice published on the Council's website and noticeboards?\n> 3. Published arrangements: Please provide a link or copy of the Council's current published arrangements for multi-location meetings, which section 47 of the Local Government and Elections (Wales) Act 2021 requires the Council to make and publish, and identify whether any revision or replacement of those arrangements applies to this meeting.\n> 4. Public access: What consideration was given to residents who wish to observe or participate in person, including whether a physical public venue was considered and, if so, why it was not made available?\n>\n> I am not suggesting that the legislation guarantees a physical venue for every meeting. My concern is how the decision was made, which published arrangements apply, and how public access was considered in this instance.\n>\n> If these questions cannot be answered before Thursday, please confirm that they remain outstanding and indicate when I can expect a response, which I would ask to be no later than 20 working days from this email. Please also retain this exchange with the meeting correspondence and identify where any formal decision or resolution concerning the arrangements is recorded.\n>\n> Arrangements for Thursday's meeting\n>\n> a) Public participation and Item 10\n>\n> Please confirm the time limit for Item 4, the procedure for being admitted from the Zoom waiting room and invited to speak, and any separate time limit or procedure for making representations when Item 10 is reached. I intend to make a brief contribution under Item 4 and to address the Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr business under Item 10, in accordance with your confirmation concerning representations on published agenda business.\n>\n> b) Circulation and retention of the statement\n>\n> Please circulate my supporting briefing and read-aloud statement to all councillors before the meeting:\n>\n> - \"Meeting briefing\" (https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate/)\n> - \"Read-aloud statement\" (https://2026-10-22.bucklerfamily.estate/meeting-script.txt)\n>\n> Please confirm whether the written statement can be retained with the meeting papers and referred to in the minutes. If the full briefing cannot be circulated before the meeting, I would be grateful if the statement could at least be circulated and the briefing link made available to councillors.\n>\n> c) The wider context and any future agenda item\n>\n> I understand that Item 10 covers two specific requests, and that Item 16 concerns correspondence rather than decisions on unlisted business. I am not asking the Council to determine title to the land or to make findings against any person or body.\n>\n> The wider history, heritage and outstanding records questions may require separate consideration. If these matters cannot properly be addressed under Item 10, please advise whether I should now submit a request for a properly notified item at a future meeting and whether any particular notice, motion or other procedure is required.\n>\n> Separate information and preservation matters\n>\n> Separately from the meeting arrangements, please acknowledge receipt of my internal review request of 13 October (the later of my two emails that day, which stands as sent) and my narrower information request of 20 October, and advise the anticipated response date for each. As my request of 21 September concerns land and environmental information, I would ask that the review consider it under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, which contain no cost limit equivalent to section 12 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I would also welcome confirmation of whether the Council holds planning files, section 52 or section 106 instruments, or related correspondence from 1988–1992 concerning planning references 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES and, if so, whether those records are being retained pending the wider records enquiries.\n>\n> I appreciate that this is shortly before the meeting. Where a substantive answer is not possible before Thursday, a brief acknowledgement identifying what remains outstanding and when it will be addressed (within 20 working days at the latest) would be helpful.\n>\n> I remain willing to participate constructively and appreciate your assistance in the run-up to the meeting.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Requester\n> \n> "},{"id":"gm-1a15a5ea5f7f9995","subject":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-20T17:31:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15a5ea5f7f9995.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15a5ea5f7f9995.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nI would advise you that the agenda published on the Council's website \nand on our noticeboards specifies that this will be a remote meeting and \nthat members of the public can attend and ask me to provide a Zoom link \nto attend. I can confirm that you will be given a reasonable opportunity \nto ask questions and make comments on any item of business specified to \nbe transacted that is on the published agenda.\n\nKind regards,\n\n---\nPaul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n\nClerk to Llandough Community Council,\n\n[address removed]\n\nVale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone [phone redacted]\n\nWebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [1]\n\nWhen you contact us\n\nThe information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\nemail address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\nto enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\ninformation and/or access our facilities and services.\n\nYour personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \nthird party. Your information may however be published in the public \ndomain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n\nFor further information please see our full privacy notice on our \nwebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [1]\n\nThe Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \nour identity' The Council will always strive to:\n\n  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n\n· Be accountable in all our council activities\n\n· Be responsive to the needs of the community\n\n· Encourage community participation\n\nOn 2026-10-16 14:31, Requester wrote:\n\n> Dear Mr Egan,\n> \n> Thank you for your email confirming that the Council meeting on 22 \n> October 2026 will now be held remotely only.\n> \n> I object to the removal of the opportunity for residents to attend in \n> person and ask that the decision be reconsidered before the meeting.\n> \n> I recognise that the Local Government and Elections (Wales) Act 2021 \n> provides for remote meetings. My concern is not with councillors using \n> Zoom, but with the Council deciding that there will be no physical \n> public attendance, without explaining the reasons for that decision or \n> how the interests of local democratic participation have been \n> considered.\n> \n> The Welsh Government's statutory guidance for community and town \n> councils recognises the importance of accessible meetings, public \n> participation and transparency. It also requires councils to have \n> regard to the guidance when exercising their relevant functions. The \n> Act's section 48, inserting paragraph 27A into Schedule 12 of the Local \n> Government Act 1972, requires the person presiding over an open \n> community council meeting to give members of the public in attendance a \n> reasonable opportunity to make representations about the business, \n> subject to the statutory exception.\n> \n> I therefore ask the Council to:\n> \n> 1. Reconsider whether a physical venue can be made available to \n> residents, even if all councillors participate remotely.\n> 2. Confirm who made the decision to change the meeting to remote-only \n> and when it was made.\n> 3. Identify the Council's published arrangements or policy governing \n> multi-location meetings and provide the relevant link or document.\n> 4. Explain what consideration was given to residents' ability to \n> observe proceedings and participate effectively, and why a physical \n> public gallery was not provided.\n> 5. Confirm that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to make \n> representations during the public participation item through the Zoom \n> meeting, in accordance with the applicable rules.\n> \n> If the Council maintains its decision, please treat this email as a \n> request for the reasons and the relevant policy or resolution to be \n> recorded in the public record.\n> \n> For clarity, my outstanding FOI internal review and my requests \n> concerning the retention of historic planning records are separate \n> matters. I do not ask the Council to determine either matter through \n> this objection.\n> \n> I remain willing to participate constructively in the meeting. I ask \n> only that the Council take the concerns about public access seriously \n> and explain its decision.\n> \n> Yours sincerely,\n> \n> Requester\n> \n> \n> \n> On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 06:53 AM, Paul Egan <[email redacted]> \n> wrote:\n> \n> Dear Requester,\n> \n> Thank you for your email.\n> \n> Can you please note that the Council meeting on 22 October will now be \n> held remotely only and you can use the Zoom link that has already been \n> emailed to you.\n> \n> Regards,\n> \n> ---\n> Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n> \n> Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n> \n> [address removed]\n> \n> Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> \n> Telephone [phone redacted]\n> \n> Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk [1]\n> \n> When you contact us\n> \n> The information you provide (personal information such as name, \n> address,\n> email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\n> to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> information and/or access our facilities and services.\n> \n> Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \n> third party. Your information may however be published in the public \n> domain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n> \n> For further information please see our full privacy notice on our \n> website www.llandough-cc.co.uk [1]\n> \n> The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \n> our identity' The Council will always strive to:\n> \n> ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n> \n> · Be accountable in all our council activities\n> \n> · Be responsive to the needs of the community\n> \n> · Encourage community participation\n> \n> On 2026-10-16 09:45, Requester wrote:\n> \n> Dear Mr Egan,\n> \n> Thank you for the agenda and Zoom link. Ahead of the 22 October meeting \n> I would like to flag two items for the public record, both tied to the \n> Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr material at \n> https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E \n> [2].\n> \n> First, my FOI to the Council (treated as such in your reply of 11 \n> October) and the internal review request of 13 October remain open. I \n> am not asking the Council to pre-judge them at the meeting; I simply \n> ask that the review outcome or a firm date be communicated before or at \n> the meeting so that public participation is not conducted under a \n> section 12 refusal that has not been reviewed.\n> \n> Second, I have placed preservation requests with The National Archives, \n> HM Land Registry, the MOD, South Wales Police and others concerning \n> 1988 records. If the Council holds any planning files, section 52/106 \n> instruments or correspondence from 1988-1992 relating to planning refs \n> 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES, I would be grateful for confirmation \n> that they are being retained pending those wider enquiries.\n> \n> I will participate through the public participation slot only.\n> \n> Title and chronology index: \n> https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E \n> [3]\n> Long-term archive: \n> https://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E \n> [4]\n> \n> Yours sincerely,\n> \n> Requester\n> \n> \n> [email redacted]\n\n\nLinks:\n------\n[1] http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n[2] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n[3] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n[4] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E"},{"id":"gm-1a159d2b98aea981","subject":"Ref No: FOI-26-46 (Mapping information - Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff) - Acknowledgement of receipt of a request for information","name":"Ref No: FOI-26-46 (Mapping information - Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff) - Acknowledgement of receipt of a request for information","date":"2026-10-20T14:58:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a159d2b98aea981.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a159d2b98aea981-f-no-foi-26-46-mapping-information-ty-mawr-great-house-farm-red-fen-cedfin-llandough-cardiff-acknowledgement-of-receipt-","scopeTopics":["os"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["os"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a159d2b98aea981","direction":"received","from":"FOI","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":["FOI-26-46"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a159d2b98aea981.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email dated 20 October 2026.\nI apologise that you did not receive a response to your original request from our Customer Service Centre, as advised.\nThe information you have requested would normally be dealt with as part of our routine business, however, in the circumstances, we will deal with your request under the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) 2000, as requested.\nAs your request was received by Ordnance Survey on 20 October 2026 we will provide you with a response within 20 working days, as required by the FOIA, therefore by 17 November 2026 (although we will endeavour to respond as soon as we can).\nIn exceptional circumstances it may be necessary for Ordnance Survey to extend this date to consider a complex public interest argument if engaging a qualified exemption.  In such cases we will notify you of the revised date by which we would expect to provide a response.\nShould you need to contact Ordnance Survey regarding your request at any time, please quote the allocated reference number in your correspondence.\nApologies once again that you did not receive a response as promised.\nThank you for your enquiry.\n\nWith kind regards,\n\nNikki\n\nNikki Osborne for the FOI Team\nLegal Services\n[cid:image001.png@01DD60AB.E9DB4B40]\nAdanac Drive, Southampton, [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n[email redacted] | www.os.uk<http://www.os.uk/>\nFollow us: X (Twitter)<https://x.com/OrdnanceSurvey> | LinkedIn<https://www.linkedin.com/company/ordnance-survey/> | YouTube<https://www.youtube.com/@ordnancesurvey/videos> | Instagram<https://www.instagram.com/ordnancesurvey/?hl=en> | Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/osmapping/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:25\nTo: FOI <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff\n\nExternal Email: Take care with attachments & links.\n\nDear FOI Team,\n\nYour email of 30 June 2026 (Kim Furlong) - my request of 27 June 2026 about Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nThank you for your email of 30 June 2026. You wrote that my request was \"for mapping information which is dealt with as part of our routine business\", that it had been forwarded to Customer Services, and that \"Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10 working days.\" I have not received a reply from Customer Services, so I am writing to you again in this thread.\n\n1. Two parts of my email of 27 June asked for recorded information, not for advice. They asked whether Ordnance Survey holds (a) \"any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\", and (b) \"any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\". Please deal with those two parts as a request for information under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 if you consider the information environmental.\n\n2. For each of (a) and (b), please confirm or deny whether the information is held (section 1(1)(a)). The site is at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, within the area of County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW, with the map references I gave (38-1-608 and 38-1-334).\n\n3. To make (a) as precise as possible, it covers, for the large-scale (1:2,500 and 1:10,560) plans of this site published between 1950 and 1975: the revision or resurvey dates; any name sheet, name book or field revision record for the names \"Ty Mawr\", \"Great House\" or \"Great House Farm\"; and any record of who supplied or authorised a name or a change to it (for example, an owner, an occupier, a local authority or HM Land Registry), in what capacity, and when.\n\n4. If any of this has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference instead of treating that part as not held. I have found that object name books for County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW (1898-1942) are at The National Archives as OS 35/2503. Please tell me whether Ordnance Survey holds anything later of the same kind for this area. If records of this kind were destroyed, please give the disposal schedule or policy that applied and, if recorded, the date.\n\n5. If any part cannot be answered as framed, please give me advice and assistance (section 16) on how to frame it so that it can be.\n\nI would be grateful for a response within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/>\nOn Mon, Oct 19, 2026 at 10:36 PM, Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear FOI Team,\n\nYour email of 30 June 2026 - my request of 27 June 2026 about Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nThank you for your email of 30 June 2026. You wrote that my request was \"for mapping information which is dealt with as part of our routine business\", that it had been forwarded to Customer Services, and that \"Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10 working days.\" I have not received a reply from Customer Services, so I am writing to you again.\n\n1. Two parts of my email of 27 June asked for recorded information, not for advice. They asked whether Ordnance Survey holds (a) \"any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\", and (b) \"any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\". Please deal with those two parts as a request for information under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 if you consider the information environmental.\n\n2. For each of (a) and (b), please confirm or deny whether the information is held (section 1(1)(a)). The site is at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, on County Series sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6, with the map references I gave (38-1-608 and 38-1-334).\n\n3. If any of it has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference instead of treating that part as not held. I have found that object name books for the County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW (1898-1942) are at The National Archives as OS 35/2503. Please tell me whether Ordnance Survey holds anything later of the same kind for this area, such as name books or revision records for the National Grid sheets.\n\n4. If any part cannot be answered as framed, please give me advice and assistance (section 16) on how to frame it so that it can be.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\n\nThis email and any attachments are intended only for the intended recipient and may contain sensitive information. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately delete this email and inform the sender.\n\nOS email communications may be monitored to ensure the secure and effective operation of our systems and for other lawful purposes. Subject to contract: No rights are to be derived from any proposal contained in this email until a written agreement containing all necessary terms is executed between the relevant parties.\n\nThank you for your cooperation.\n\nOrdnance Survey Limited (Company Registration number 09121572)\nRegistered Office: Explorer House\nAdanac Drive\nSouthampton [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\nhttp://www.os.uk<http://www.os.uk/>"},{"id":"gm-1a1598079be2517d","subject":"Correction to my email of 20 October 2026 – Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) information request","name":"Correction to my email of 20 October 2026 – Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr) information request","date":"2026-10-20T13:29:14Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1598079be2517d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1598079be2517d-correction-to-my-email-of-20-october-2026-great-house-farm-t-mawr-information-request","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1598079be2517d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":["EIR 2004"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1598079be2517d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan,\n\nA short correction to my email of 20 October 2026 (subject \"Re: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — request for information under FOIA 2000 / EIR 2004\"), which set out a new, narrower information request.\n\n1. That email was sent as a reply to the wrong message, so my email of 13 October 2026 (01:07) appears quoted beneath it. On 13 October I asked you to disregard that email (subject \"Apologies Gentlemen - Disregard Last Email Por Favor\"), and on 16 October I sent a plain-language supplement.\n\n2. Please continue to disregard the quoted 13 October (01:07) text. It was not re-sent intentionally and forms no part of the 20 October request.\n\n3. My later email of 13 October and my email of 16 October stand as sent. The new request (items 1 to 4, above the quoted text) is unaffected.\n\nI apologise for the extra email.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1594c5dd452d5e","subject":"RE: Request for information – LGA and predecessor associations: guidance to councils on land with disputed title; any record of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","name":"RE: Request for information – LGA and predecessor associations: guidance to councils on land with disputed title; any record of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-20T12:32:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1594c5dd452d5e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ad529447920-quest-for-information-lga-and-predecessor-associations-guidance-to-councils-on-land-with-disputed-title-any-record-of-gr","scopeTopics":["lga"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["lga"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ad529447920","direction":"received","from":"FOI and DPA","institutions":[{"id":"lga","name":"Local Government Association / WLGA"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1594c5dd452d5e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your below request which is being dealt with by Freedom of Information Act.\n\nWe are reviewing your request and will respond as soon as possible and within the statutory deadline of 17 November 2026.\n\nKind regards\nFOI Team\nLGA\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 October 2026 01:19\nTo: FOI and DPA <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Request for information – LGA and predecessor associations: guidance to councils on land with disputed title; any record of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough\n\nDear Local Government Association,\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr,\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, and how public bodies\ndealt with the farm and the land around it from the 1950s onwards,\nincluding the registration of land near the farm as a village green in\n1970 and the later housing development of the farm site. My aim is to\nidentify and preserve every surviving record.\n\nI make this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, in line\nwith the LGA's published freedom of information policy. If the LGA\nconsiders that the Act does not apply to it, I would be grateful for a\nreply on a voluntary basis.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. Any guidance, circular or advice note issued to member councils by\nthe LGA, or by its predecessors (the Association of County Councils,\nthe Association of District Councils and the Association of\nMetropolitan Authorities, and their pre-1974 forerunners), between\n1965 and 2000, on:\n(a) acquiring, accepting, leasing or granting planning permission over\nland whose title was disputed or unregistered, or where an occupier\nclaimed title by possession;\n(b) registering land as a town or village green under the Commons\nRegistration Act 1965 where its ownership was disputed or unknown.\n\n2. Any record mentioning Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Western\nGround Rents Ltd, BP Properties Ltd, or the case BP Properties Ltd v\nBuckler (Court of Appeal, 1987).\n\n3. Whether the LGA holds the archives of those predecessor\nassociations and, if not, where they were deposited.\n\n4. If any of the above was held but has been destroyed or transferred:\nwhen, under which retention schedule, and on whose authority.\n\nA \"not held\" answer to any part would be just as helpful. A reply by\n17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com>\n\nThis email may include confidential information and is solely for use by the intended recipient(s). If you have received this email in error please notify the sender immediately. You must not disclose, copy, distribute or retain any part of the email message or attachments. No responsibility will be assumed by the LGA for any direct or consequential loss, financial or otherwise, damage or inconvenience, or any other obligation or liability incurred by readers relying on information contained in this email. Views and opinions expressed by the author are not necessarily those of the organisation nor should they be treated, where cited, as an authoritative statement of the law, and independent legal and other professional advice should be obtained as appropriate.\n\nVisit the Local Government Association website – www.local.gov.uk"},{"id":"gm-1a1592f05965e88d","subject":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-20T12:00:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1592f05965e88d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1592f05965e88d-information-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-near-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["historic-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["historic-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1592f05965e88d","direction":"received","from":"FOI","institutions":[{"id":"historic-england","name":"Historic England"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1592f05965e88d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Our Reference: 26/04323\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nRe: Information Request – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nThank you for your email on 20 October 2026 in which you requested the following information related to the property above:\n\n\n1. The record of that transfer as it relates to this item, or to Llandough: the transfer list or schedule entry, its description, and any covering correspondence.\n\n\n\n2. How and when Historic England (or English Heritage, RCHME or the National Buildings Record before it) acquired the item: the accession or registration record, the source or depositor, and the date.\n\n\n\n3. Whether Historic England kept any copy, digital image, catalogue record or index entry of the item, or of any other material about the site, after the transfer; and if so, a copy.\n\n\n\n4. The record of the decision to include this item in the 2018 exchange: the date, the role of the officer who authorised it, and the basis.\n\n\n\n5. Any other information you hold about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr or its buildings, including photographs, survey notes, and any correspondence with Cadw, RCAHMW or the Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust about its listing or its demolition (1986–1989). Search terms: \"Great House Farm\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"Penarth\".\n\n\n\n6. If anything within items 1 to 5 was held but has since been destroyed or transferred elsewhere: when, under which retention schedule, and where it went.\n\nYour request will be considered under the Freedom of Information Act (2000) / the Environmental Information Regulations (2004). We will be writing to you within the statutory 20 working day timeframe with a response to your request. You will be informed if this is not possible.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nAccess to Information team\n\nHistoric England\nThe Engine House\nSwindon\n[postcode redacted]\n\nWe will keep a record of contact details provided by you and details of your enquiry for administrative purposes. We will not use these details for marketing purposes and we will never sell your personal details or share your information with another organisation for marketing purposes. If you would like to know more or understand your data protection rights, please take a look at our Privacy and Cookies Policy<https://www.historicengland.org.uk/terms/privacy-cookies/>.\n\n\n\n\nEnsuring our heritage lives on and is loved for longer.\nhistoricengland.org.uk\nThis e‑mail (and any attachments) is confidential and may contain personal views which are not the views of Historic England unless specifically stated. If you have received it in error, please delete it from your system and notify the sender immediately. \n​Do not use, copy or disclose the information in any way nor act in reliance on it. Any information sent to Historic England may become publicly available. For information about our use of your personal data please visit: historicengland.org.uk/terms/privacy"},{"id":"gm-1a158ee36fed63d2","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-20T10:49:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a158ee36fed63d2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a","direction":"received","from":"possessions.cardiff.countycourt","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a158ee36fed63d2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"OFFICIAL\n\nGood morning\n\n\"Cardiff County Court Enquiries told me on 4 August 2026 that, because of the case's age, no records were held. Could you let me know the basis of that statement, so that I understand how it fits with your request for a claim\"\n\nMy colleague was not aware of your previous emails and the historical claim you are referring to.\n\nTo assist you further and ensure we locate the correct matter we ask the parties to provide the claim number. We deal with several cases each day, and the claim number will help us identify the relevant case promptly.\n\nAnswer to your emails:\n\n\nThe County Court, Family Court, Court of Protection, and the District Registries of the High Court Records Retention and Disposition Schedule is the document that is used to manage the retention and destruction of records in HMCTS.\n\n1. This schedule covers the court/tribunal records and associated administrative records held in the County Court, the Family Court, the Court of Protection and the District Registries of the High Court. It covers the records that are created and managed in line with Section 8 and Schedule 1, paragraph 4 of the Public Records Act 1958. HMCTS manages these public records on behalf of the Lord Chancellor.\n\n2. It covers the records for the different jurisdictions and courts that sit in county court buildings (County court (civil), Family court, Court of Protection and District Registries of the High Court).\n\n3. The schedule sets out how long these records should be kept (retention) and what should happen to the records when the retention period ends (disposition). It applies to records in all formats including, but not limited to, digital (for example case management systems or emails), paper and audio.\n\n4. This schedule is in the public domain and published on GOV.uk website at: https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/record-retention-and-disposition-schedules.\n\nHope this help\n\nWarmest regards,\n\nJyothi Polusani\n\nAdministration Officer\nAdran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\n\nCanolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd | 2 Stryd Y Parc | Caerdydd | [postcode redacted]\nCardiff Civil Justice Centre | 2 Park Street | Cardiff  | [postcode redacted]\n [phone redacted] [email redacted]\n\nI am not authorised to bind the Ministry of Justice contractually, nor to make representations or other statements which may bind the Ministry of Justice in any way via electronic means.\nNid oes gennyf awdurdod i rwymo’r Weinyddiaeth Gyfiawnder trwy gytundeb, na chyflwyno sylwadau neu ddatganiadau eraill a all rwymo’r Weinyddiaeth Gyfiawnder mewn unrhyw ffordd trwy ddull electronig\n\n\nFor information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see:\nAm wybodaeth ynghylch sut mae GLlTEF yn defnyddio data personol amdanoch chi, ewch i:\nwww.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 19 October 2026 23:14\nTo: possessions.cardiff.countycourt <[email redacted]>\nSubject: RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest\n\nDear Mr Jones,\n\nThank you for your email of 16 October 2026 asking whether I have a claim number relating to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026.\nI have put everything I need to ask HMCTS into this one reply.\n\n1. Claim numbers and the proceedings concerned\n\nI do not have claim numbers. The proceedings I know of concern Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, near Penarth:\n- a possession order of 2 February 1955 and a Cardiff County Court order of 11 December 1962, in proceedings in which Western Ground Rents Ltd was the party seeking possession;\n- a possession action listed on 3 July 1974;\n- the possession order enforced in November 1988 following BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court, Hollis J, July 1986; Court of Appeal [1987] EWCA Civ 2).\n\nThese details come from the published judgment and family papers, so I may be wrong on some of them.\n\n2. Surviving records\n\nCould you tell me whether any record, index entry, warrant or bailiff's return survives for these, or for the November 1988 enforcement? If not, were any transferred elsewhere (for example to a central HMCTS archive or The National Archives) or destroyed, and if so when and under which retention schedule?\n\n3. The earlier \"no records\" reply\n\nCardiff County Court Enquiries told me on 4 August 2026 that, because of the case's age, no records were held. Could you let me know the basis of that statement, so that I understand how it fits with your request for a claim number?\n\nIf any of this is better handled under my Ministry of Justice subject access request (IR 260904007), please let me know.\n\nA reply by 2 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n________________________________\n This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a15877f505dbb0b","subject":"Request for information - Ref: FOI2026/118465","name":"Request for information - Ref: FOI2026/118465","date":"2026-10-20T08:40:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15877f505dbb0b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a15877f505dbb0b-quest-for-information-ref-foi2026-118465","scopeTopics":["voa"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["voa"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a15877f505dbb0b","direction":"received","from":"Information Rights Unit","institutions":[{"id":"voa","name":"Valuation Office Agency / HMRC"}],"refs":["FOI2026/118465"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15877f505dbb0b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Our ref: FOI2026/118465\nDear Requester,\nThank you for your request, which was received on 20 October 2026.\nPlease remember to quote the reference number above if you need to contact us about this request again.\nWe aim to respond to all freedom of information requests within 20 working days. We will either send you the information you have asked for or let you know why we can't.\nIf we can't reply by 17 November 2026, we will write to let you know the reason and when you can expect a response.\nYours sincerely\nHMRC Information Rights Unit"},{"id":"gm-1a158298d6ff819a","subject":"RE: FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","name":"RE: FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","date":"2026-10-20T07:14:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a158298d6ff819a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf-foi-2026-024-032-036-c-1880-medieval-ironwork-from-great-house-farm-llandough-published-sources-say-it-is-in-the-nationa","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":["FOI 2026-024","FOI 2026-032","FOI 2026-036"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a158298d6ff819a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester\n\nBefore we can consider point 2 of your request, we would be grateful for clarification.\n\nThe searches undertaken in relation to FOI 2026-024, FOI 2026-032 and FOI 2026-036 were directed at specific records, locations and objects associated with the matters raised in those requests.\n\nPoint 2 of your current request seeks searches for \"medieval ironwork (any object type)\" using a number of place names, provenance references and donor details. As drafted, this would significantly broaden the scope of the searches previously undertaken and could encompass a substantial number of collection records.\n\nAs you will be aware, there are a number of properties named \"Great House Farm\" across Wales and \"Llandough\" is not a unique place name. In addition, Amgueddfa Cymru holds a substantial collection of medieval ironwork and it is not clear whether you are seeking records relating specifically to the alleged discovery at Great House Farm/Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff), or a broader category of collection records matching the search terms listed in your email.\n\nTo assist us in identifying the information you are seeking, please clarify:\n\n  *   whether you are seeking records relating specifically to the alleged c.1880 discovery at Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff); or\n  *   whether you are seeking all records of medieval ironwork matching any of the search terms listed in your email, regardless of whether they have any recorded connection to the alleged discovery.\n\nOnce we have received your clarification, we will be able to consider the request further.\n\nPlease note that the request will be placed on hold pending receipt of your clarification.\n\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image002.png@01DD606A.B7534330]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/amgueddfa.cymru> | museum.wales<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/museum.wales>\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 19 October 2026 23:14\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum\n\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\n\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nDear Amgueddfa Cymru FOI team,\n\nRe: FOI 2026-024 (25 August 2026), FOI 2026-032 (22 September 2026), FOI 2026-036 (5 October 2026) and your reply of 16 October 2026 on the search basis.\n\nThank you for your replies about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan. I would be grateful for help reconciling them with two published sources.\n\nYour replies, as I understand them:\n- FOI 2026-024: no records of the specific discovery (a soldier, horse, visor and lance);\n- FOI 2026-032: other archaeological discoveries at Great House Farm were identified but treated as unrelated or out of scope;\n- FOI 2026-036: no accession entry, register, day-book, donations book or correspondence dated 1875-1915 for ironwork, armour, a visor, lance or helmet from Great House / Llandough Farm, including the former Cardiff Museum registers;\n- 16 October 2026: no separate search log is held beyond what was supplied.\n\nThe published sources:\n- Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust, \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological Assessment\", August 1990 (planning files 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES): \"it is likely that some medieval ironwork which is held by the National Museum of Wales was discovered under the rear wing c 1880 (RCAHMW 1988).\"\n- Holbrook and Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70, n. 142: \"medieval ironwork was discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm c. 1880. It is now in the collections of the National Museums & Galleries of Wales.\"\n\nEither the published statements are mistaken, or the objects are recorded under a different findspot, donor name or description. I am asking only for recorded information, or confirmation that none is held:\n\n1. Please provide any record held by Amgueddfa Cymru (including correspondence with the authors or with GGAT/RCAHMW, enquiry files, or collections-management notes) that records or comments on the statement that medieval ironwork from Great House Farm is in the Museum's collections. If none is held, please say so.\n\n2. Please search the collections database and the accession registers for medieval ironwork (any object type) with any of these in the findspot, place, donor or provenance fields: \"Llandough\", \"Llandough-juxta-Penarth\", \"Great House\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Cedfin\", \"Williams of Great House\", or a Cardiff Museum donation before 1912. Please list any matches, with accession numbers and descriptions, or confirm that there are none.\n\n3. Please say whether any record identified and treated as unrelated under FOI 2026-024 or 2026-032 could correspond to the c.1880 ironwork.\n\n4. If this is better treated as a request for internal review of FOI 2026-036, please treat it as one and tell me the reference and the date by which you will reply.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days (by 16 November 2026).\n\nSupporting material: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E (evidence catalogue), https://www.google.com/url?q=https://clerk.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E and https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E"},{"id":"gm-1a156c62f0744603","subject":"FOI request — Audit Wales: external audit records of council land dealings at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1970–1996","name":"FOI request — Audit Wales: external audit records of council land dealings at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1970–1996","date":"2026-10-20T00:46:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156c62f0744603.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156c62f0744603-foi-request-audit-wales-external-audit-records-of-council-land-dealings-at-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1970-1996","scopeTopics":["audit-wales"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["audit-wales"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156c62f0744603","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"audit-wales","name":"Audit Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156c62f0744603.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Officer,\n\nI sent this request earlier today (20 October 2026) to [email redacted], which returned it as undeliverable (address unknown), so I am resending it to the address published on your Freedom of Information page.\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where they apply, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. It concerns Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan: the farm, its woodland beside Leckwith Road, village green VG41 (registered on 16 June 1970), and the land later developed as Church View Close. The farmhouse was demolished in 1988.\n\nI understand that Audit Wales holds records inherited from the Wales Audit Office and, for Welsh local government, from the District Audit Service and the Audit Commission. I am trying to establish from the records whether the external auditors examined any council dealing with this land and, if so, who examined it, when and with what result.\n\nPlease tell me whether Audit Wales holds, and provide, the following for 1970–1996, for the Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council, South Glamorgan County Council, Glamorgan County Council and the district councils that covered Llandough before 1974:\n1. any audit report, management letter, public interest report or value-for-money report that mentions Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Church View Close, village green VG41 or land at Leckwith Road, Llandough;\n2. any auditor's working papers or correspondence about any acquisition, sale, exchange, lease or registration of land there by any of those councils, including the registration of VG41;\n3. any objection by a local government elector, or any question raised at the audit of accounts, about land at Great House Farm, and the auditor's decision on it, with the date and the auditor (by role) who made it;\n4. any correspondence between the auditors and HM Land Registry, BP Properties Ltd (company no. 00699446), Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) or Ideal Homes about the land;\n5. if records of this kind for the period are no longer held, the retention or disposal schedule that applied, the date of disposal if recorded, and who authorised it, or the repository to which they were transferred.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance under section 16.\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156c125e06a456","subject":"Automatic reply: FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","name":"Automatic reply: FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","date":"2026-10-20T00:40:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156c125e06a456.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156c125e06a456-automatic-reply-foi-eir-request-defra-successor-to-maf-wartime-and-post-war-farm-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-lla","scopeTopics":["defra"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["defra"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156c125e06a456","direction":"received","from":"SM-Defra-Information Requests (DEFRA)","institutions":[{"id":"defra","name":"Defra"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156c125e06a456.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your email to the Information Rights Team in the Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra).\nThis email address is for submitting information requests that are handled under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (FOIA) and/or the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 (EIRs) only.\nRequests handled under these regimes are requests for recorded information. Any correspondence for views, explanations, or interpretations would not amount to a valid request under these regimes and would be handled as general correspondence. Guidance on how to submit an effective information request can be found on the Information Commissioner's Office website here:\nHow to write an effective request for information | ICO<https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/official-information/preparing-and-submitting-your-information-request/>\nPlease note any enquires that do not amount to an information request will need to be submitted through the webform that can be found here:\nhttps://www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-defra\nIf you are unable to use the webform for accessibility reasons, please visit:\nhttps://submit-an-enquiry-to-defra.service.gov.uk/accessibility-statement?lang=en_GB\nPostal enquiries\nWhere possible, please send your correspondence electronically through our webform. If necessary, postal enquiries can be sent to:\nMinisterial Contact Unit\nDefra\nSeacole Building\n2 Marsham Street\nLondon\n[postcode redacted]\n\nDepartment for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra) This email and any attachments is intended for the named recipient only. If you have received it in error you have no authority to use, disclose, store or copy any of its contents and you should destroy it and inform the sender. Whilst this email and associated attachments will have been checked for known viruses whilst within Defra systems we can accept no responsibility once it has left our systems. Communications on Defra's computer systems may be monitored and/or recorded to secure the effective operation of the system and for other lawful purposes."},{"id":"gm-1a156bfe07db1662","subject":"FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","name":"FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","date":"2026-10-20T00:39:37Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156bfe07db1662.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156bfe07db1662-foi-eir-request-defra-successor-to-maf-wartime-and-post-war-farm-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1936-1955","scopeTopics":["defra"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["defra"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156bfe07db1662","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"defra","name":"Defra"}],"refs":["CAS-344046","CAS-347296"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156bfe07db1662.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Defra Information Rights team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where they apply, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. It concerns Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (then Glamorgan), a farm occupied by my relatives, the Williams family, and the records of the Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries (MAF) and its Glamorgan committees, to which Defra is the successor. It is separate from my request 2026/1425E, which is on a different subject. It is linked to my enquiries with The National Archives, CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 and CAS-344046-K1S1R2.\n\nI first sent this request earlier today (20 October 2026) to [email redacted]. It was returned as undeliverable (a mail routing loop), so I am resending it to the address published on GOV.UK. Please treat this copy as the request.\n\nWestern Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092), to which the Bute Estate conveyed its interest by a conveyance dated 25 December 1938, obtained a possession order on 4 July 1955. I am trying to establish from the records how the farm was dealt with between 1936 and 1955, who took each decision, and on what record.\n\nPlease tell me whether Defra holds, and provide, the following for Great House Farm for 1936–1955:\n1. any National Farm Survey or other MAF farm record for the holding, including the occupier, the owner and the acreage recorded;\n2. any record of the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (or its successor, the Glamorgan Agricultural Executive Committee) about the farm: inspections, gradings, cultivation or other directions, supervision orders, or any possession, requisition or termination of tenancy, with the date and the committee or officer (by role) who made each decision;\n3. any application for, or decision on, the Minister's consent to the operation of a notice to quit the holding (Agricultural Holdings Act 1948), with the date, the decision and who made it;\n4. any compensation claim or payment for the land under the Compensation (Defence) Act 1939 or the Agriculture Acts;\n5. any correspondence with Western Ground Rents Ltd, the Bute Estate or their agents about the farm, or about the possession order of 4 July 1955 and the land it covered.\n\nIf records in scope have been transferred to The National Archives (for example MAF 32, the National Farm Survey, or the MAF 80 series of committee minutes), please give the reference rather than treating that part as not held. If any record in scope was destroyed, please give the retention or disposal schedule that applied and, where recorded, the date and the authority for its destruction. If any part is held by the Welsh Government rather than by Defra, please say so.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance (section 16 FOIA; regulation 9 EIR).\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156bb48de3312f","subject":"Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-20T00:34:36Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156bb48de3312f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["blake-morgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["blake-morgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"blake-morgan","name":"Blake Morgan LLP"}],"refs":["2004/12"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156bb48de3312f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Blake Morgan,<br><br>Follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026 – BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 31 July 1987) – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough<br><br>I wrote to you on 28 September 2026, among other recipients, asking that records about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, be preserved. I have not yet had a reply, so I am following it up with a more specific question.<br><br>The reported Court of Appeal judgment in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 (31 July 1987) records that counsel for the appellant, Mr W. Buckler, were instructed by Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn, acting as agents for Loosemores of Cardiff. I understand that Blake Morgan was formed in 2012 by the merger of Blake Lapthorn and Morgan Cole.<br><br>I would be grateful if you would tell me:<br>1. whether Blake Morgan is the successor to the practice of Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn, or holds any of its records;<br>2. whether any file, correspondence, brief to counsel, attendance note or court document from the 1986–87 proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, or any later matter concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, survives in Blake Morgan's records or archive storage (including any deeds or papers held in safe custody);<br>3. if such records were destroyed or transferred, the date, the retention policy applied, and to whom any file was transferred (for example, to Loosemores or to the client);<br>4. what searches were made to answer this, and whether any physical or archived files were checked.<br><br>I am not asking for privileged content at this stage, only whether the records exist, where they are, and their history. Please also make sure that nothing relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr or these proceedings is destroyed while these enquiries are open. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.<br><br>Yours sincerely,<br><br>Requester <br><br>https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 at 07:04 AM, possessions.cardiff.countycourt &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted]>[email redacted]</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><html xmlns:v=\"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml\" xmlns:o=\"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office\" xmlns:w=\"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word\" xmlns:m=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2004/12/omml\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40\">\n<head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"Microsoft Word 15 (filtered medium)\">\n<!--[if !mso]><style