mitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data.\n</div>\n\n</blockquote></div>\n</div></blockquote></div>"},{"id":"gm-1a156b774d4f98b2","subject":"Subject access request — WA231076 / WA240304 — Great House Farm, Llandough — Williams / Buckler","name":"Subject access request — WA231076 / WA240304 — Great House Farm, Llandough — Williams / Buckler","date":"2026-10-20T00:30:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b774d4f98b2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3f997bc1bf94-subject-access-request-wa231076-wa240304-great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3f997bc1bf94","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["D260928","WA231076","WA240304","WA513690","WA735527"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b774d4f98b2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Wignall,<br><br>Your reference D260928 – my subject access request (your email of 1 October 2026: statutory deadline 28 October 2026) – and a request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004<br><br>Thank you for your email of 1 October 2026. I am replying in the same thread so that everything for the Information Rights Team is in one place. Section 1 below is for the subject access request; sections 2 to 4 are a new request for information, and I would be grateful if you could pass them to whoever deals with EIR and FOI requests.<br><br>The land is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, now registered under titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690 and WA735527. Related references: my application of 15 October 2026 to alter the register (N610CGV / Z084NQV) and enquiries 261015-6844273, 260928-6762800, 260917-6718215 and 260918-6720625.<br><br>1. Subject access request D260928 – documents to include<br><br>To help you search, these are the documents on the first-registration and amalgamation files that I expect to name or concern me or my family. I ask for my own personal data in them under UK GDPR Article 15, and for the documents themselves, as information about the land, under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004:<br>(a) for WA231076 (application of 30 November 1982) and WA240304 (application of 23 February 1983): Form 1C as lodged; the 1971 abstract of title; all plans and the original title plans; form D23; the correspondence of 8 April, 12 April and 12 May 1983; the A3 application of 13 January 1984; and any notices served, with their service records;<br>(b) the amalgamation application of 2 February 1987, with its decision and completion;<br>(c) the 1994 correction applications.<br><br>I am asking for these under the subject access request and the EIR instead of ordering official copies on form OC2.<br><br>2. First-registration examination records (EIR, or FOI for anything outside the EIR)<br><br>For the first registrations of WA231076 and WA240304, and their amalgamation on 2 February 1987, please provide any recorded information showing:<br>(a) whether the Registry made any enquiry of, or sent any notice to, persons in occupation of the farmhouse, or advertised the applications; and, if so, when, to whom, at what address and under which rule;<br>(b) any requisition raised on the absence of the 31 December 1969 conveyance (Western Ground Rents Ltd to the BP Pension Trust parties) from the documents lodged, and the reply;<br>(c) any internal note or examination record referring to the occupation of the farmhouse;<br>(d) who applied for the 1987 amalgamation, the application form, the officer (by grade or role) who approved it, and any note of the pending appeal in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler.<br><br>If any examination file or record in scope has been destroyed, please give the date, the retention schedule applied and the authority for its destruction.<br><br>Some of these points are also before the Wales Office under Z084NQV. This is a request for the recorded information under the EIR; if the Wales Office answers a point first, a cross-reference to its reply is all I need for that point.<br><br>3. Earlier title, plans and later events (EIR/FOI)<br><br>Please tell me:<br>(a) whether HM Land Registry's records (including the first-registration documents for WA231076 and WA240304) identify the earlier title, plans or parcels in a way that can be matched to the Valuation Office field books for the area (The National Archives series IR 58);<br>(b) whether HM Land Registry's records refer to the 1988 demolition of the farmhouse or to the 1989–92 planning applications (Vale of Glamorgan references 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES).<br><br>4. Occupiers named in notices after March 1983<br><br>For any notice, letter, application or other record on the WA231076 and WA240304 files dated after 31 March 1983 (to 1994) that names a \"Mrs Buckler\", or any other Buckler or Williams occupier of the farmhouse, please tell me where it appears, the name and address as written, and on what evidence the Registry identified that person.<br><br>5. Address for correspondence<br><br>Please confirm that this address is the right one for future correspondence with the Information Rights Team, given the automated notice of 7 October 2026 that another Registry email address is \"no longer supported\".<br><br>For sections 2 to 4, please reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exception or exemption relied on. Please also confirm that the subject access request will be answered by 28 October 2026.<br><br>Thank you for your help.<br><br>Yours faithfully,<br><br>Requester <br><br>https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Oct 01, 2026 at 01:25 PM, _DataProtection &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted]>[email redacted]</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Requester\n<br>\n<br>Thank you for your email.\n<br>\n<br>We will handle your request in accordance with your rights under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.\n<br>\n<br>Our statutory deadline for reply is 28 October 2026, although we will endeavour to respond as soon as possible.\n<br>\n<br>Your reference is D260928.\n<br>\n<br>Yours sincerely\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>Kat Wignall\n<br>EO Disclosure Officer\n<br>Information Rights Team\n<br>Data and Register Integrity Group\n<br>Email- [email redacted] / [email redacted]\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>-----Original Message-----\n<br>From: Requester <[email redacted]>\n<br>Sent: 28 September 2026 22:42\n<br>To: _DataProtection <[email redacted]>\n<br>Cc: Wales.OfficeMail <[email redacted]>; _FOI email address <[email redacted]>\n<br>Subject: Subject access request — WA231076 / WA240304 — Great House Farm, Llandough — Williams / Buckler\n<br>\n<br>[You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n<br>\n<br>Data Protection Officer\n<br>HM Land Registry\n<br>[email redacted]\n<br>cc: [email redacted]; [email redacted] Refs already with you: N610CGV; letter of SG Haste, 30 July 2026\n<br>\n<br>Sirs/Madam,\n<br>\n<br>Subject access request under UK GDPR Article 15.\n<br>Requester: Requester.\n<br>Titles: WA231076 and WA240304 (closed). Land north of Leckwith Road, Llandough (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr).\n<br>\n<br>This is not a request for an official copy of the register. It is a request for personal data in the working file in which I am identifiable, including customer-complaint files, the pack sent to Stephen Doughty MP, and any note of my correspondence on N610CGV.\n<br>\n<br>Please also say whether the first-registration file contains personal data about Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) or William Buckler, so far as you can disclose it to me as a family representative, and what identity you require before the month starts.\n<br>\n<br>The matters to which that file goes, so you can search properly, are these. They are questions, not findings against Land Registry:\n<br>\n<br>1. First-registration applications: WA231076 on 30 November 1982 (form 1E); WA240304 on 23 February 1983 (form 1C); later amalgamation and closure of WA240304.\n<br>2. A 31 December 1969 conveyance, Western Ground Rents to BP Pension Trust, identified as a root, and whether it is on the 30 July 2026 schedule of documents surviving on the file.\n<br>3. Notice and opportunity to object in 1982–83, while Mary Williams remained in occupation of the farmhouse. Family evidence is that notification was not received until after her death on 26 March 1983.\n<br>I am seeking the notice and service record.\n<br>4. What the 1987 Court of Appeal decided (possession, limitation, October 1974 letters) and what it did not decide (documentary root of the farmhouse and garden parcel).\n<br>\n<br>The public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ .\n<br>\n<br>Please preserve the first-registration file and the complaint file. Do not start the statutory month until you have said what identification you need. Nothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the register. This is not a claim form and not service.\n<br>\n<br>Yours faithfully,\n<br>\n<br>Requester \n<br>\n<br>[email redacted]\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n<br>\n<br>We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n<br>\n<br>We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n<br>\n<br>To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n<br>\n<br>\n<br></div></blockquote></div>"},{"id":"gm-1a156b64e8e56807","subject":"ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","name":"ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","date":"2026-10-20T00:29:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b64e8e56807.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad-icr-090-26-further-formal-points-on-the-first-registration-file-and-1987-amalgamation","scopeTopics":["hmlr-icr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr-icr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr-icr","name":"HM Land Registry (Independent Complaints Reviewer)"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26","WA231076","WA240304"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b64e8e56807.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms St Rose,<br><br>ICR/090/26 – HM Land Registry, titles WA231076 and WA240304 (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough)<br><br>Thank you for your letter of 9 October 2026, which you kindly re-sent on 12 October after my email of 10 October crossed with it. I have read the Independent Complaints Reviewer's decision carefully and I understand that she cannot review HM Land Registry's legal decisions, assess the evidence, or revisit the 1987 litigation. I am not asking her to do any of those things.<br><br>Your letter explains that the ICR \"can give a view on whether HMLR has followed its standard procedure in reviewing registration decisions and whether its complaint responses clearly and fully deal with the matters within HMLR's remit\". I respectfully ask her to reconsider on that limited basis only. HMLR's replies to me (23 March, 19 April, 25 May and 30 July 2026) did not answer three factual questions about HMLR's own records, each of which is within HMLR's remit and none of which asks HMLR or the ICR to decide who owns the land:<br>1. whether HMLR's records show that any enquiry or notice was sent to the occupiers of the farmhouse before the first registrations of 1982–83, and if so to whom, at what address and on what date. The Stage 2 response says HMLR \"did not receive or were aware of any interest that you or your family may or may not have had in the land\"; it does not say whether a notice was sent;<br>2. why the conveyance of 31 December 1969, relied on as the root of title, does not appear in the schedule of documents on the first-registration file released on 30 July 2026, and whether HMLR holds it under any other reference;<br>3. on what application the two titles were amalgamated on 2 February 1987, and whether the record shows what was known then about the pending appeal.<br><br>One small point of record: your letter refers to the Stage 1 response as dated 19 April 2025. I believe it is dated 19 April 2026.<br><br>If the ICR will not reconsider, please confirm in writing that her decision of 9 October 2026 is final, so that I can ask my MP to consider a referral to the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman, enclosing your letter as you suggest. A reply by 6 November 2026 would be appreciated.<br><br>Yours sincerely,<br><br>Requester <br><br>https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Oct 12, 2026 at 10:09 AM, ICR Office Inbox &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted]>[email redacted]</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Requester \n<br>\n<br>Thank you for your email. \n<br>\n<br>It appears that you have not received my letter dated 9 October 2026 which I sent on the same date. Therefore, please find that letter attached.\n<br>\n<br>Yours sincerely\n<br>\n<br>Denyse St Rose\n<br>Office Manager and Investigations Officer\n<br>ICR Office\n<br>\n<br>10 South Colonnade\n<br>Canary Wharf, London [postcode redacted]\n<br>[phone redacted] (Telephone number)\n<br>www.icrev.org.uk\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<br>-----Original Message-----\n<br>From: Requester <[email redacted]> \n<br>Sent: 10 October 2026 20:12\n<br>To: ICR Office Inbox <[email redacted]>\n<br>Subject: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation\n<br>\n<br>Dear Independent Complaints Reviewer,\n<br>\n<br>Reference ICR/090/26.\n<br>\n<br>I hold the stage-one decision of 19 April 2026 and the stage-two decision of 25 May 2026. I also hold the schedule of 43 documents on the first-registration files released on 30 July 2026.\n<br>\n<br>The family’s established case, recorded on the public wiki and under investigation, is that the 1877 arrangement took effect in 1928, transferring the full Parcel A (house and buildings, barn, stable and west-side yard, garden, northern forest and the south-east ground later registered as VG41) to the Williams family. The 1939 agreement/plan depicts Parcel B only. On the family account, the 1949 attempt to make the occupation of Parcel A permissive failed, title papers were reported missing in 1950–52, and Western Ground Rents’ 4 July 1955 enforcement of Parcel B also seized the Parcel-A forest and green under “whole farm” wording. Later documentary work is directed at corroborating or precisely mapping that account and tracing those areas into later titles.\n<br>\n<br>Four specific points remain unanswered and are relevant to that investigation:\n<br>\n<br>1. The 1969 root deed recited as the root of title does not appear on the schedule. Please confirm whether HMLR holds that deed under any other reference, or whether it was never lodged.\n<br>2. What evidence exists on the file of notice or opportunity to object given to the occupying family (Williams / Buckler) in 1982–83.\n<br>3. The precise legal and administrative basis for the 1987 title amalgamation that took place while the Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler were still live.\n<br>4. Whether the inclusion of the woodland (or any land beyond the 1938\n<br>conveyance) is regarded as a possible mistake capable of alteration or indemnity under the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice Guide 39.\n<br>\n<br>Please confirm these points form part of the live investigation and state the exact start date of the ICR six-month period (so that the\n<br>~25 November 2026 outer limit can be verified).\n<br>\n<br>Yours faithfully,\n<br>\n<br>Requester \n<br>\n<br></div></blockquote></div>"},{"id":"gm-1a156b5af7d8295c","subject":"Automatic reply: FOI request — Valuation Office Agency: rating and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1955–1995","name":"Automatic reply: FOI request — Valuation Office Agency: rating and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1955–1995","date":"2026-10-20T00:28:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b5af7d8295c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b5af7d8295c-automatic-reply-foi-request-valuation-office-agency-rating-and-valuation-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1","scopeTopics":["voa"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["voa"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b5af7d8295c","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; hmrc.gov.uk)","institutions":[{"id":"voa","name":"Valuation Office Agency / HMRC"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b5af7d8295c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"IMPORTANT INFORMATION – PLEASE READ\nThank you for contacting the Information Rights team at the Valuation Office, part of HMRC.\nThis acknowledgement is confirmation we are progressing your request. We will only contact you if further information is needed.\nIf your request falls under the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) or Environmental Information Regulations (EIR) – We aim to respond within the statutory timescale of 20 working days following receipt of your request.\nIf your request falls under Data Protection legislation – personal information (including data held on your own property) is exempt from disclosure under the FOIA, but may be disclosed under data protection legislation. We will consider whether we can disclose information under this legislation, and if so, aim to respond within one calendar month.\nIf you have only copied your correspondence to us – we will not respond.\nIf your enquiry does not fall under any of the above legislation – Our team are unable to respond to general enquiries. We will pass any correspondence of this nature on to our Customer Service team. Should you wish to contact them directly, please fill in the form here: www.gov.uk/contact-voa<https://www.gov.uk/contact-voa>\nPWYSIG – DARLLENWCH OS GWELWCH YN DDA\nDiolch am gysylltu â'r tîm Hawliau Gwybodaeth yn y Swyddfa Brisio, rhan o Gyllid a Thollau EF.\nMae’r gydnabyddiaeth hon yn gadarnhad ein bod yn ymdrin â’ch cais. Dim ond os bydd angen gwybodaeth bellach arnom byddwn yn cysylltu â chi.\nOs yw eich cais yn dod o dan y Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth (FOIA) neu Reoliadau Gwybodaeth Amgylcheddol (EIR) – Ein nod yw ymateb cyn pen yr amserlen statudol o 20 diwrnod gwaith ar ôl derbyn eich cais.\nOs yw eich cais yn dod o dan ddeddfwriaeth Diogelu Data - Mae gwybodaeth bersonol (gan gynnwys data a gedwir am eich eiddo) wedi'i heithrio rhag cael ei ddatgelu o dan y Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth (FOIA), ond gellir ei ddatgelu o dan ddeddfwriaeth diogelu data. Byddwn yn ystyried a allwn ddatgelu gwybodaeth o dan y ddeddfwriaeth hon, ac os felly, ein nod yw ymateb cyn pen un mis calendr.\nOs mai dim ond eich gohebiaeth yr ydych wedi’i gopïo atom - ni fyddwn yn ymateb.\nOs nad yw'ch ymholiad yn dod o dan unrhyw un o'r deddfwriaethau uchod – ni all ein tîm ymateb i ymholiadau cyffredinol. Byddwn yn trosglwyddo unrhyw ohebiaeth o'r math hwn i'n tîm Gwasanaeth Cwsmeriaid. Pe byddech yn dymuno cysylltu â nhw'n uniongyrchol, llenwch y ffurflen yma: https://www.gov.uk/cysylltu-voa\n\n\nThis message and any attachments are confidential. Unless you are the intended recipient, the information must not be used, disclosed, or copied to any other person who is not entitled to receive it. If you have received this message in error, please notify the sender immediately and then delete it. The Commissioners for HM Revenue and Customs are not liable for any personal views of the sender.\n\nTo help HMRC fight cybercrime, forward suspicious emails to [email redacted] and texts to 60599. Find advice and report tax scam phone calls on GOV.UK."},{"id":"gm-1a156b4d228c23d2","subject":"FOI request — Valuation Office Agency: rating and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1955–1995","name":"FOI request — Valuation Office Agency: rating and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1955–1995","date":"2026-10-20T00:27:33Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b4d228c23d2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b4d228c23d2-foi-request-valuation-office-agency-rating-and-valuation-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1955-1995","scopeTopics":["voa"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["voa"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b4d228c23d2","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"voa","name":"Valuation Office Agency / HMRC"}],"refs":["WA231076","WA240304","WA513690","WA735527"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b4d228c23d2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Valuation Office Agency FOI team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 for recorded information held by the VOA about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan: the farmhouse and buildings (demolished in 1988), its woodland beside Leckwith Road, and the land now within HM Land Registry titles WA231076, WA240304, WA513690 and WA735527.\n\nI am trying to establish from the records who was rated or recorded as occupier or owner of the property between 1955 and 1995, and how and on whose notice entries were altered or deleted.\n\nPlease search for and provide:\n1. the valuation list entries and rating assessments for the farmhouse, buildings, woodland or land beside Leckwith Road, 1955–1990 (including the 1956, 1963 and 1973 lists), and any council tax valuation record from 1 April 1993 to 1995;\n2. any record naming the ratepayer, occupier or owner in that period, including the periods when Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) and later BP Properties Ltd (company no. 00699446) were recorded as owners;\n3. any proposal, appeal or request to alter or delete an entry for the property, including its deletion after the demolition in 1988: who made it, in what capacity, the date, and the decision;\n4. the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales records that its survey of the house on 26 April 1974 was partial because of an ownership dispute; any VOA record of a dispute about the ownership or occupation of the property, 1955–1995;\n5. any valuation relating to village green VG41, registered on 16 June 1970;\n6. if records in scope have been transferred to The National Archives or destroyed, the reference, or the retention or disposal schedule that applied and the date of disposal if recorded.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance under section 16.\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156b4a9e8729a6","subject":"FOI request — Audit Wales: external audit records of council land dealings at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1970–1996","name":"FOI request — Audit Wales: external audit records of council land dealings at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1970–1996","date":"2026-10-20T00:27:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b4a9e8729a6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b4a9e8729a6-foi-request-audit-wales-external-audit-records-of-council-land-dealings-at-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1970-1996","scopeTopics":["audit-wales"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["audit-wales"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b4a9e8729a6","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"audit-wales","name":"Audit Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b4a9e8729a6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Audit Wales FOI team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where they apply, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. It concerns Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan: the farm, its woodland beside Leckwith Road, village green VG41 (registered on 16 June 1970), and the land later developed as Church View Close. The farmhouse was demolished in 1988.\n\nI understand that Audit Wales holds records inherited from the Wales Audit Office and, for Welsh local government, from the District Audit Service and the Audit Commission. I am trying to establish from the records whether the external auditors examined any council dealing with this land and, if so, who examined it, when and with what result.\n\nPlease tell me whether Audit Wales holds, and provide, the following for 1970–1996, for the Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council, South Glamorgan County Council, Glamorgan County Council and the district councils that covered Llandough before 1974:\n1. any audit report, management letter, public interest report or value-for-money report that mentions Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Church View Close, village green VG41 or land at Leckwith Road, Llandough;\n2. any auditor's working papers or correspondence about any acquisition, sale, exchange, lease or registration of land there by any of those councils, including the registration of VG41;\n3. any objection by a local government elector, or any question raised at the audit of accounts, about land at Great House Farm, and the auditor's decision on it, with the date and the auditor (by role) who made it;\n4. any correspondence between the auditors and HM Land Registry, BP Properties Ltd (company no. 00699446), Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) or Ideal Homes about the land;\n5. if records of this kind for the period are no longer held, the retention or disposal schedule that applied, the date of disposal if recorded, and who authorised it, or the repository to which they were transferred.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance under section 16.\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156b33bce23290","subject":"FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","name":"FOI/EIR request – Defra (successor to MAF): wartime and post-war farm records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1936–1955","date":"2026-10-20T00:25:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b33bce23290.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b33bce23290-foi-eir-request-defra-successor-to-maf-wartime-and-post-war-farm-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1936-1955","scopeTopics":["defra"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["defra"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b33bce23290","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"defra","name":"Defra"}],"refs":["CAS-344046","CAS-347296"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b33bce23290.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Defra Information Rights team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where they apply, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. It concerns Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (then Glamorgan), a farm occupied by my relatives, the Williams family, and the records of the Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries (MAF) and its Glamorgan committees, to which Defra is the successor. It is separate from my request 2026/1425E, which is on a different subject. It is linked to my enquiries with The National Archives, CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 and CAS-344046-K1S1R2.\n\nWestern Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092), to which the Bute Estate conveyed its interest by a conveyance dated 25 December 1938, obtained a possession order on 4 July 1955. I am trying to establish from the records how the farm was dealt with between 1936 and 1955, who took each decision, and on what record.\n\nPlease tell me whether Defra holds, and provide, the following for Great House Farm for 1936–1955:\n1. any National Farm Survey or other MAF farm record for the holding, including the occupier, the owner and the acreage recorded;\n2. any record of the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (or its successor, the Glamorgan Agricultural Executive Committee) about the farm: inspections, gradings, cultivation or other directions, supervision orders, or any possession, requisition or termination of tenancy, with the date and the committee or officer (by role) who made each decision;\n3. any application for, or decision on, the Minister's consent to the operation of a notice to quit the holding (Agricultural Holdings Act 1948), with the date, the decision and who made it;\n4. any compensation claim or payment for the land under the Compensation (Defence) Act 1939 or the Agriculture Acts;\n5. any correspondence with Western Ground Rents Ltd, the Bute Estate or their agents about the farm, or about the possession order of 4 July 1955 and the land it covered.\n\nIf records in scope have been transferred to The National Archives (for example MAF 32, the National Farm Survey, or the MAF 80 series of committee minutes), please give the reference rather than treating that part as not held. If any record in scope was destroyed, please give the retention or disposal schedule that applied and, where recorded, the date and the authority for its destruction. If any part is held by the Welsh Government rather than by Defra, please say so.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026. If you hold no information for any part, please say so; if anything is withheld, please give the exemption relied on. If any part cannot be answered as framed, I would be grateful for advice and assistance (section 16 FOIA; regulation 9 EIR).\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156b262a532dcc","subject":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-10-20T00:24:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b262a532dcc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c-ty-mawr-great-house-farm-red-fen-cedfin-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["os"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["os"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b262a532dcc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,<br><br>Your email of 30 June 2026 (Kim Furlong) – my request of 27 June 2026 about Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, Llandough<br><br>Thank you for your email of 30 June 2026. You wrote that my request was \"for mapping information which is dealt with as part of our routine business\", that it had been forwarded to Customer Services, and that \"Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10 working days.\" I have not received a reply from Customer Services, so I am writing to you again in this thread.<br><br>1. Two parts of my email of 27 June asked for recorded information, not for advice. They asked whether Ordnance Survey holds (a) \"any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\", and (b) \"any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\". Please deal with those two parts as a request for information under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 if you consider the information environmental.<br><br>2. For each of (a) and (b), please confirm or deny whether the information is held (section 1(1)(a)). The site is at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, within the area of County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW, with the map references I gave (38-1-608 and 38-1-334).<br><br>3. To make (a) as precise as possible, it covers, for the large-scale (1:2,500 and 1:10,560) plans of this site published between 1950 and 1975: the revision or resurvey dates; any name sheet, name book or field revision record for the names \"Ty Mawr\", \"Great House\" or \"Great House Farm\"; and any record of who supplied or authorised a name or a change to it (for example, an owner, an occupier, a local authority or HM Land Registry), in what capacity, and when.<br><br>4. If any of this has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference instead of treating that part as not held. I have found that object name books for County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW (1898–1942) are at The National Archives as OS 35/2503. Please tell me whether Ordnance Survey holds anything later of the same kind for this area. If records of this kind were destroyed, please give the disposal schedule or policy that applied and, if recorded, the date.<br><br>5. If any part cannot be answered as framed, please give me advice and assistance (section 16) on how to frame it so that it can be.<br><br>I would be grateful for a response within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.<br><br>Thank you for your help.<br><br>Yours sincerely,<br><br>Requester <br><br>https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Oct 19, 2026 at 10:36 PM, Requester &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted]>[email redacted]</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear FOI Team,<br><br>Your email of 30 June 2026 – my request of 27 June 2026 about Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, Llandough<br><br>Thank you for your email of 30 June 2026. You wrote that my request was \"for mapping information which is dealt with as part of our routine business\", that it had been forwarded to Customer Services, and that \"Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10 working days.\" I have not received a reply from Customer Services, so I am writing to you again.<br><br>1. Two parts of my email of 27 June asked for recorded information, not for advice. They asked whether Ordnance Survey holds (a) \"any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\", and (b) \"any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\". Please deal with those two parts as a request for information under section 1 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 if you consider the information environmental.<br><br>2. For each of (a) and (b), please confirm or deny whether the information is held (section 1(1)(a)). The site is at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, on County Series sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6, with the map references I gave (38-1-608 and 38-1-334).<br><br>3. If any of it has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference instead of treating that part as not held. I have found that object name books for the County Series sheet Glamorgan 47 NW (1898–1942) are at The National Archives as OS 35/2503. Please tell me whether Ordnance Survey holds anything later of the same kind for this area, such as name books or revision records for the National Grid sheets.<br><br>4. If any part cannot be answered as framed, please give me advice and assistance (section 16) on how to frame it so that it can be.<br><br>Thank you for your help.<br><br>Yours sincerely,<br><br>Requester<br></div></blockquote></div>"},{"id":"gm-1a156b195dd68381","subject":"Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-20T00:24:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b195dd68381.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fd90bc1cfc812a-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["bt-archives"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bt-archives"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fd90bc1cfc812a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bt-archives","name":"BT Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b195dd68381.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Fahema,<br><br>Thank you again for your helpful reply of 10 August 2026 about the 1897 Marconi records, which I have been working through.<br><br>I have a second, separate enquiry about the same place, Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (near Penarth). The farmhouse was occupied until late 1988, when it was demolished. I am trying to establish from the records who held and occupied the property over time and what happened to its telephone service and the plant on the land.<br><br>Could you tell me whether BT Group Archives holds, or can point me to, any of the following for the period 1950 to 1990:<br>1. telephone directory entries for Great House Farm, Llandough (Cardiff and Penarth directories), with the years and the name in which the line was listed;<br>2. any wayleave agreement, consent or easement file for poles, overhead lines, cables or ducts on or across Great House Farm land, including the name or capacity of the person or company who granted it (for example, the owner or the occupier) and the date;<br>3. any record of the cessation or removal of the telephone service and plant at Great House Farm in 1988 or 1989, including who requested it, in what capacity, and the date;<br>4. any exchange, line plant or engineering records for Llandough, Leckwith Road or Penarth Road that show the farm;<br>5. if records of this kind are held by Openreach rather than by BT Group Archives, the right team at Openreach to ask, or I would be grateful if you could pass this part on;<br>6. if records of this kind for the period were not kept, or have been destroyed, the retention or disposal schedule that applied, if known.<br><br>I understand that BT is not subject to the Freedom of Information Act 2000, so this is a request for your voluntary help. Catalogue references would be ideal, and I am happy to book a searchroom visit if anything needs to be viewed in person. If nothing is held, a short note saying so would be equally helpful. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.<br><br>Kind regards,<br><br>Requester <br><br>https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Aug 10, 2026 at 04:16 PM, Requester &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted]>[email redacted]</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">---------- Forwarded message ---------<br>From: <span dir=\"auto\">&lt;<a href=\"[email redacted] target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">[email redacted]</a>&gt;</span><br>Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026, 06:54<br>Subject: RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough<br>To:  &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted] target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">[email redacted]</a>&gt;<br></div><br><br>\n\n\n\n\n\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\n<p style=\"font-family:Century Gothic;font-size:9pt;color:#5514b4;margin:5pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none\" align=\"Right\">\nGeneral<br>\n</p>\n<br>\n<div>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Dear Requester<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Thank you for your enquiry.\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">As a starting point, the following records may be of interest.\n</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">These have been digitised and can be accessed via the\n</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">via the online catalogue entry (see the PDF in the ‘Document’ field)</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">:\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f361&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">POST 30/631A</a> \n<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f529&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">POST 30/940</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f494&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">POST 878B</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f2&amp;pos=2\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCB 273/2</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f3&amp;pos=2\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCB 273/3</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Digitised images:\n<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f5+PH%2f2%2f1%2f5%2fP+5083&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCB 473/P 5083</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f5+PH%2f9%2f1%2fARC+1148&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCE 361/ARC 1148</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Occasionally, our catalogue software struggles to open large files; if you experience any problems, please let me know and I can share the digitised copies via our sharing platform</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">The following files have not been digitised but can be viewed by appointment in our searchroom:</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f5&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCB 273/5</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&amp;id=BTA%2f7+PP%2f1%2f23%2f22&amp;pos=1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TCK 89/22</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">We also hold a number of secondary sources relating to Marconi in our library, which can be consulted in our searchroom.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">I would recommend searching our online catalogue\n</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">(<a href=\"https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Default.aspx?\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Home Page</a>)</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"> to identify any other records that you think may be useful for your research. Details of how to book\n an appointment can be found on our </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">website</a>.</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Kind regards<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Fahema<u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a name=\"m_2569589454584063382_m_-5011732038997601762_OLE_LINK1\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Fahema Begum<u></u><u></u></span></b></a></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">BT Group Archives<u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">E:\n</span></span><span></span><a href=\"[email redacted] rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">[email redacted]</span></span><span></span></a><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">W:\n</span></span><span></span><a href=\"https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">bt.com/history</span></span><span></span></a><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">\n<u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><i><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Planning a research visit to the Archives? We’ve introduced a new appointment booking system - visit our\n</span></i></span><span></span><a href=\"https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span><i><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">website</span></i></span><span></span></a><span><i><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">\n for details.</span></i></span><span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></b></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span> </span></span><span><img border=\"0\" width=\"340\" height=\"107\" style=\"width:3.5416in;height:1.118in\" id=\"m_2569589454584063382m_-5011732038997601762Picture_x0020_1\" src=\"cid:ii_19fec3ce2864cff311\"></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></span></p>\n<span></span>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\">This email contains information from BT Brands that might be privileged or confidential.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><br>\n</span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\">And it&#39;s only meant for the person above. If that&#39;s not you, we&#39;re sorry - we must have sent it to you by mistake. Please email us to let us know, and don&#39;t copy or forward it\n to anyone else. Thanks. We monitor our email systems and may record all our emails.</span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\">British Telecommunications plc</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><br>\n</span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\"><a href=\"[map link redacted] target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">R/O : 1 Braham Street, London, [postcode redacted]</a></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\"> </span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\">Registered in England: No 1800000</span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e\">British Telecommunications plc is authorised and regulated by Financial Conduct Authority for the provision of consumer credit.</span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\n<div>\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm;font-size:pt\">\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"><br>\n</span></b></p>\n<p style=\"font-family:Century Gothic;font-size:9pt;color:#5514b4;margin:5pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none\" align=\"Right\">\nGeneral<br>\n</p>\nFrom:<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Requester &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted] rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">[email redacted]</a>&gt;\n<br>\n<b>Sent:</b> 06 August 2026 22:48<br>\n<b>To:</b> BTARCHIV &lt;<a href=\"[email redacted] rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">[email redacted]</a>&gt;<br>\n<b>Subject:</b> Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough<u></u><u></u></span>\n<p></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"left\" width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"0\" style=\"width:.3pt;background:#a6a6a6;padding:5.25pt 1.5pt 5.25pt 1.5pt\">\n</td>\n<td width=\"100%\" style=\"width:100.0%;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 11.25pt;background:revert!important;border:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;padding:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-align:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;width:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">\n<span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,serif;color:#212121\">You don&#39;t often get email from\n<a href=\"[email redacted] rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">[email redacted]</a>. <a href=\"https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification\" rel=\"noreferrer noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">\nLearn why this is important</a> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td width=\"75\" style=\"width:56.25pt;background:#eaeaea;padding:5.25pt 3.75pt 5.25pt 3.75pt;background:revert!important;border:revert!important;color:revert!important;direction:revert!important;display:revert!important;font-size:revert!important;height:revert!important;letter-spacing:revert!important;line-height:revert!important;margin:revert!important;opacity:revert!important;outline:revert!important;overflow:revert!important;padding:revert!important;table-layout:revert!important;text-align:revert!important;text-indent:revert!important;text-orientation:revert!important;text-overflow:revert!important;text-transform:revert!important;vertical-align:revert!important;white-space:revert!important;width:revert!important;word-break:revert!important;word-spacing:revert!important;writing-mode:revert!important;zoom:revert!important\">\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Dear BT Archives Team,<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>I am researching the General Post Office involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s South Wales wireless telegraphy experiments during 1897, particularly the experiments between Lavernock Point and Flat Holm.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>The Postal Museum has advised that the relevant GPO Telegraph Department and Engineering Department records are likely to be held by BT Archives. They confirmed that their own searches of Postal Museum holdings found no relevant records and that surviving\n telecommunications material from this period is likely to be within the collections transferred to BT Archives.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>I would be grateful if you could advise on the relevant surviving records and catalogue references.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>My research concerns:<u></u><u></u></p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nMarconi’s 1897 South Wales wireless experiments;<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nLavernock Point and Flat Holm;<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nPenarth and Llandough (near Penarth);<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nthe involvement of the GPO Telegraph Department and Engineering Department;<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nany surviving correspondence, reports, notebooks, engineering records, plans, photographs or administrative records connected with the experiments.<u></u><u></u></li></ul>\n<p>I am particularly interested in identifying any references to local residents or private individuals who assisted Marconi or GPO engineers. Family history suggests that a Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, may have assisted with the experiments\n locally. I appreciate that such a person may not appear in catalogue descriptions if he was a private individual rather than a GPO employee.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>Could you please advise whether your catalogue contains references to any of the following terms or variants:<u></u><u></u></p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nMarconi<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nGuglielmo Marconi<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nwireless telegraphy<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nSouth Wales experiments<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nLavernock<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nPenarth<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nLlandough<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nGreat House Farm<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nWilliams<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nW. Williams<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nWilliam Williams<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\nMr Williams<u></u><u></u></li></ul>\n<p>If relevant records exist, I would be grateful for the catalogue references, file descriptions and dates so that I can identify the material for further research.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>I would also appreciate any guidance on whether there are related collections, transferred Post Office records, or finding aids that may not be obvious from the online catalogue.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>Thank you very much for your assistance.<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>Kind regards,<u></u><u></u></p>\n<p>Requester<br>\n<br>\n<u></u><u></u></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div></div></div>\n</div></blockquote></div>"},{"id":"gm-1a156b0fb558e0a3","subject":"Automatic reply: Records request — Lambeth Palace Library / Church Commissioners: glebe, exchange and Bute Estate records, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ECE/6/3/372/CD27551)","name":"Automatic reply: Records request — Lambeth Palace Library / Church Commissioners: glebe, exchange and Bute Estate records, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ECE/6/3/372/CD27551)","date":"2026-10-20T00:23:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b0fb558e0a3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b0fb558e0a3-automatic-reply-records-request-lambeth-palace-library-church-commissioners-glebe-exchange-and-bute-estate-records-lland","scopeTopics":["church-of-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["church-of-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b0fb558e0a3","direction":"received","from":"Archives","institutions":[{"id":"church-of-england","name":"Church of England archives (Lambeth Palace Library)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b0fb558e0a3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your enquiry which this automated message confirms we have received.\nWe aim to send a fuller response within 10 working days, but this will depend on the nature of the enquiry, staff availability, and the volume of enquiries received.\nWe are pleased to answer routine enquiries and offer advice about sources. If your enquiry requires detailed research, we will advise you to visit in person or suggest that you employ a professional researcher.\nOur catalogues and selected images from the collections are available online<https://lambethpalacelibrary.info/collections/library-catalogues>.\nFor guidance on research for specific topics, please click here<https://lambethpalacelibrary.info/collections/research-guides>. For details about copying services, click here<https://lambethpalacelibrary.info/services/imaging-services>.\nAll readers at Lambeth Palace Library are asked to register for a new reader’s ticket for their first visit to the reading room.\nFor information about visiting, including opening times, please click here<https://lambethpalacelibrary.info/using-the-library/registering-and-booking>.\nClick here<https://www.lambethpalacelibrary.info/events> to see information about events at the Library. For information about the Library's current exhibitions click here<https://www.lambethpalacelibrary.info/exhibitions>.\nOur website is at www.lambethpalacelibrary.info<http://www.lambethpalacelibrary.info>\n\nAny information relating to your enquiry will be used only for the administrative purposes of the Library and will be stored in accordance with UK General Data Protection Regulation and the Data Protection Act 2018 will not be passed on to third parties."},{"id":"gm-1a156b0b5929168e","subject":"Records request — Lambeth Palace Library / Church Commissioners: glebe, exchange and Bute Estate records, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ECE/6/3/372/CD27551)","name":"Records request — Lambeth Palace Library / Church Commissioners: glebe, exchange and Bute Estate records, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ECE/6/3/372/CD27551)","date":"2026-10-20T00:23:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156b0b5929168e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156b0b5929168e-cords-request-lambeth-palace-library-church-commissioners-glebe-exchange-and-bute-estate-records-llandough-juxta-penarth","scopeTopics":["church-of-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["church-of-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156b0b5929168e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"church-of-england","name":"Church of England archives (Lambeth Palace Library)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156b0b5929168e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Lambeth Palace Library / Church of England Record Centre,\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, the farm next to St Dochdwy's church, which was demolished in 1988. I am trying to establish, from the records, how the land around the church and the farm was held, exchanged and transferred, and by whom.\n\nTwo catalogue entries appear to relate to church land at Llandough:\n(a) Lambeth Palace Library ECE/6/3/372/CD27551 (1 March 1890): \"Leckwith St James R with Llandough R & Cogan R. re. T. R. Thompson\";\n(b) The National Archives MAF 11/55/5333: \"Order of exchange of lands. Place: Llandough, Glamorgan. Parties: Major H H Lee and T R Thompson\" (11 September 1879).\n\nThe Bute Estate held the freehold of Great House Farm until a conveyance on sale to Western Ground Rents Ltd dated 25 December 1938 (recited in a 1965 contract).\n\nI would be grateful for your voluntary help with the following:\n1. File ECE/6/3/372/CD27551: a short description of its contents (for example, whether it concerns glebe, an exchange of land, or a sale), its extent, whether it contains any plan, and a quotation for copies of any plan or conveyance in it.\n2. Whether the Ecclesiastical Commissioners' records hold any file on the 1879 exchange between Major H. H. Lee and T. R. Thompson (MAF 11/55/5333), if it concerns Llandough-juxta-Penarth rather than Llandough near Cowbridge, or any other exchange, sale or purchase of glebe at Llandough-juxta-Penarth, with the file references.\n3. Any glebe terrier, glebe plan or tithe-related file for Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Leckwith or Cogan held in the Ecclesiastical Commissioners' or Queen Anne's Bounty records, with references.\n4. Any correspondence between the Ecclesiastical Commissioners and the Bute Estate (the Marquess of Bute or his agents) about land at Llandough or Leckwith, with references.\n5. Any manorial records for Llandough or Leckwith held by the Library or the Record Centre.\n6. Whether any record in the scope above is known to have been transferred to another repository (for example, the Representative Body of the Church in Wales after disestablishment in 1920, the National Library of Wales or Glamorgan Archives) or destroyed, with the date and the record of the transfer or destruction where held.\n\nI understand that Lambeth Palace Library and the Church Commissioners are not subject to the Freedom of Information Act 2000, so this is a request for your voluntary help, and I am happy to pay normal copying charges. Catalogue references and a short description of each item would be ideal, even without copies. If you hold nothing, a short note saying so would be equally helpful. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156ae46b1bad14","subject":"EIR request — Cwm Cydfin SSSI (0524) notification and owner/occupier records; woodland title WA735527, Llandough; Forestry Commission lease of Leckwith Woods","name":"EIR request — Cwm Cydfin SSSI (0524) notification and owner/occupier records; woodland title WA735527, Llandough; Forestry Commission lease of Leckwith Woods","date":"2026-10-20T00:20:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156ae46b1bad14.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ae46b1bad14-eir-request-cwm-cydfin-sssi-0524-notification-and-owner-occupier-records-woodland-title-wa735527-llandough-forestry-comm","scopeTopics":["nrw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nrw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ae46b1bad14","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nrw","name":"Natural Resources Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156ae46b1bad14.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear NRW Access to Information team,\n\nThis is a request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, and of the woodland between Llandough and Leckwith. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record of who owned and occupied that woodland, how it changed hands, and who decided what, when and on what record. Please search the records NRW holds, including those inherited from the Countryside Council for Wales (and, before it, the Nature Conservancy Council) and from Forestry Commission Wales.\n\nA. Cwm Cydfin SSSI (site 0524, \"Cwm Cydfin, Leckwith\", around ST 165 739)\nYour published citation gives notification dates of 1972 and 1985 and says it is not the legal copy; your boundary data records the site as last notified on 9 December 1985.\n\n1. The full legal citation and notification map, and the 1972 notification and 1985 re-notification documents.\n\n2. The list of owners and occupiers served with each notification, and any later record of the site's owners or occupiers up to 2013, including any notice or record of a change of ownership (for example around 1988 and 1994 to 1996).\n\n3. Any representations or objections received on either notification, the record of how each was decided (date, and the committee or officer role), and any record of how the 1985 boundary was fixed.\n\n4. Any management agreement, notice of proposed operations or consent application under section 28 of the Wildlife and Countryside Act 1981, and site-file correspondence with an owner or occupier, 1972 to 2013.\n\nB. Woodland at Leckwith Road, Llandough, now registered under title WA735527 (Forest of Cardiff)\nHM Land Registry records a transfer of this woodland to Forest of Cardiff (registered charity 1002867) dated 10 November 1994, and I understand that part of it was transferred to Goldsworthy Homes in 2005.\n\n5. Any woodland grant, felling licence, management plan or dedication agreement affecting this woodland, 1950 to 2010, with the owner or applicant recorded; and any record relating to the 1994 transfer to Forest of Cardiff or to the 2005 transfer of part of it.\n\nC. Forestry Commission lease of Leckwith Woods\nCardiff's published park history records that Leckwith Woods (about 109 acres given to Cardiff council by Western Ground Rents Ltd, completed in April 1942) was leased to the Forestry Commission, and that the council agreed in June 1985 to accept the surrender of the lease.\n\n6. The lease, its plan and dates; the compartment or stock maps for that woodland; and the 1985 surrender with any plan.\n\nD. Records no longer held\n\n7. If any of the above existed but is no longer held: when it was destroyed or transferred, under which retention schedule, where any transfer went (for example to The National Archives or a record office), and the record authorising it.\n\nOn personal data: where an owner or occupier was a private individual and you consider that regulation 13 applies, I would be grateful for the record with only that name redacted, and a note of whether each party was a private individual, a company or a public body. I ask for the names of companies and public bodies in full.\n\nIf any part is too wide, please tell me under regulation 9 how to narrow it rather than refusing it; Part A is my priority. A \"not held\" answer to any part is just as useful.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156adec7a23f4b","subject":"Records request – WLGA: guidance on land with disputed title; the 1996 allocation of South Glamorgan land at Llandough and Leckwith; Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr","name":"Records request – WLGA: guidance on land with disputed title; the 1996 allocation of South Glamorgan land at Llandough and Leckwith; Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr","date":"2026-10-20T00:20:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156adec7a23f4b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156adec7a23f4b-cords-request-wlga-guidance-on-land-with-disputed-title-the-1996-allocation-of-south-glamorgan-land-at-llandough-and-lec","scopeTopics":["lga"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["lga"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156adec7a23f4b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"lga","name":"Local Government Association / WLGA"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156adec7a23f4b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Welsh Local Government Association,\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, and how public bodies dealt with the farm and the land and woodland around it. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record.\n\nI understand that the WLGA may not be a public authority under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, so this is a request for your voluntary help.\n\nPlease tell me whether the WLGA holds, or knows who holds:\n\n1. Any guidance, circular or advice note issued to Welsh councils by the WLGA or its predecessors (including the Assembly of Welsh Counties and the Council of Welsh Districts), between 1974 and 2000, on acquiring, accepting or developing land whose title was disputed or unregistered, or where an occupier claimed title by possession; or on registering land as a town or village green where its ownership was disputed.\n\n2. Any record of how the land of South Glamorgan County Council at Llandough, Leckwith and Cogan was allocated between Cardiff and the Vale of Glamorgan at the reorganisation of 1 April 1996 (Local Government (Wales) Act 1994; Local Government Reorganisation (Wales) (Property etc.) Order 1996), including any agreement, schedule, or dispute referred to the associations or to the Residuary Body for Wales. Press reports from 1994 and 1995 (South Wales Echo) describe South Glamorgan County Council acquiring about 125 acres of woodland and farmland between Leckwith and Llandough from the Land Authority for Wales. I am trying to establish which successor council received that land, and on what record.\n\n3. Any record mentioning Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Properties Ltd, or the case BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 1987).\n\n4. Where the archives of the Assembly of Welsh Counties are now held. (I understand that papers of the Council of Welsh Districts are at the National Library of Wales.)\n\n5. If any of the above was held but has been destroyed or transferred: when, and under which retention policy.\n\nA short \"not held\" would be just as helpful as a positive answer. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156ad529447920","subject":"Request for information – LGA and predecessor associations: guidance to councils on land with disputed title; any record of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Request for information – LGA and predecessor associations: guidance to councils on land with disputed title; any record of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-20T00:19:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156ad529447920.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ad529447920-quest-for-information-lga-and-predecessor-associations-guidance-to-councils-on-land-with-disputed-title-any-record-of-gr","scopeTopics":["lga"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["lga"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ad529447920","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"lga","name":"Local Government Association / WLGA"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156ad529447920.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Local Government Association,\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, and how public bodies dealt with the farm and the land around it from the 1950s onwards, including the registration of land near the farm as a village green in 1970 and the later housing development of the farm site. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record.\n\nI make this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, in line with the LGA's published freedom of information policy. If the LGA considers that the Act does not apply to it, I would be grateful for a reply on a voluntary basis.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. Any guidance, circular or advice note issued to member councils by the LGA, or by its predecessors (the Association of County Councils, the Association of District Councils and the Association of Metropolitan Authorities, and their pre-1974 forerunners), between 1965 and 2000, on:\n(a) acquiring, accepting, leasing or granting planning permission over land whose title was disputed or unregistered, or where an occupier claimed title by possession;\n(b) registering land as a town or village green under the Commons Registration Act 1965 where its ownership was disputed or unknown.\n\n2. Any record mentioning Great House Farm, Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Properties Ltd, or the case BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Court of Appeal, 1987).\n\n3. Whether the LGA holds the archives of those predecessor associations and, if not, where they were deposited.\n\n4. If any of the above was held but has been destroyed or transferred: when, under which retention schedule, and on whose authority.\n\nA \"not held\" answer to any part would be just as helpful. A reply by 17 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156ad030c56a7f","subject":"FOI request — Historic England: records of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (Wales), including an item transferred to RCAHMW on 15 January 2018","name":"FOI request — Historic England: records of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (Wales), including an item transferred to RCAHMW on 15 January 2018","date":"2026-10-20T00:19:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156ad030c56a7f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ad030c56a7f-foi-request-historic-england-records-of-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-wales-including-an-item-transferred-to-rcahmw-","scopeTopics":["historic-england"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["historic-england"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ad030c56a7f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"historic-england","name":"Historic England"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156ad030c56a7f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Historic England Access to Information team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI am researching Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan. The farmhouse was surveyed in 1974 by H.J. Thomas of the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales (RCAHMW), was the subject of a listing decision by Cadw in 1988, and was demolished on 6 December 1988. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record of the building and of the decisions made about it.\n\nAlthough the site is in Wales, RCAHMW's records show that Historic England held material about it. On 10 June 2026 RCAHMW told me (their reference RC26-0205) that one of the records in its archive about the site, archive number 6500905 (creator recorded as Dr Katherine Watson), was \"Transferred from Historic England as part of an exchange of material between the two organisations\", with an accession date of 15/01/2018.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. The record of that transfer as it relates to this item, or to Llandough: the transfer list or schedule entry, its description, and any covering correspondence.\n\n2. How and when Historic England (or English Heritage, RCHME or the National Buildings Record before it) acquired the item: the accession or registration record, the source or depositor, and the date.\n\n3. Whether Historic England kept any copy, digital image, catalogue record or index entry of the item, or of any other material about the site, after the transfer; and if so, a copy.\n\n4. The record of the decision to include this item in the 2018 exchange: the date, the role of the officer who authorised it, and the basis.\n\n5. Any other information you hold about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr or its buildings, including photographs, survey notes, and any correspondence with Cadw, RCAHMW or the Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust about its listing or its demolition (1986–1989). Search terms: \"Great House Farm\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"Penarth\".\n\n6. If anything within items 1 to 5 was held but has since been destroyed or transferred elsewhere: when, under which retention schedule, and where it went.\n\nA \"not held\" answer to any part would be just as useful as a positive one. If anything is withheld, please name the exemption relied on for each part.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a156ac8b40758c6","subject":"FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"FOI request — Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, dissolved 1997): any bona vacantia property or interests at Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-10-20T00:18:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a156ac8b40758c6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6-foi-request-western-ground-rents-ltd-company-no-00342092-dissolved-1997-any-bona-vacantia-property-or-interests-at-lland","scopeTopics":["bona-vacantia"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bona-vacantia"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a156ac8b40758c6","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bona-vacantia","name":"Government Legal Department (Bona Vacantia)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a156ac8b40758c6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Bona Vacantia FOI Officer,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI am researching the history of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, near Penarth (historically Glamorgan; South Glamorgan from 1974 to 1996; now the Vale of Glamorgan), and of the land and woodland around it. My aim is to identify and preserve every surviving record of how this land changed hands, who made each decision, and on what record.\n\nBackground, from public sources:\n- Western Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092) is reported to have bought the Bute family's urban estate in 1938. It let farm land at Llandough from 1939, and it conveyed land at Llandough to the BP Pension Trust by a conveyance recited in HM Land Registry's records as dated 31 December 1969.\n- On 26 June 1996 its members placed it in members' voluntary liquidation, together with other dormant companies whose registered office was BP House (London Gazette, issue 54455, 3 July 1996, pages 8979 and 8982). The final meeting was called for 16 May 1997 (London Gazette, issue 54739, page 4683), and the company was dissolved in 1997.\n\nPlease tell me whether the Bona Vacantia Division (or the Treasury Solicitor, before the Government Legal Department was formed) holds any information about this company, and in particular:\n\n1. Whether any property, right or interest of Western Ground Rents Ltd was referred to your Division, or vested in the Crown as bona vacantia, on or after its dissolution. This includes freehold land, woodland, freehold reversions on leases, ground rents or rentcharges, and any reserved mines and minerals, and especially anything at Llandough, Leckwith, Cogan or Penarth.\n\n2. For any such property: when and how it came to your notice (and who referred it, if a company or public body); what was done with it (sale, transfer, disclaimer under section 656 of the Companies Act 1985 or section 1013 of the Companies Act 2006, or retention); the date and the instrument; the buyer or transferee and the price, if a company or public body; and the record of the decision, with the role of the officer who approved it.\n\n3. Any enquiry, application or correspondence about the company's property received since 1997 (for example from HM Land Registry, a local authority, a developer, a charity or a BP group company), with its date, the enquirer if a company or public body, and your reply.\n\n4. Whether any application was made to restore the company to the register, and any letter your Division issued in connection with it.\n\n5. If your Division held records about the company that are no longer held: when they were destroyed or transferred, under which retention schedule, and the record authorising that.\n\nA \"not held\" answer to any part would be just as useful as a positive one. If anything is withheld, please name the exemption relied on for each part. Copies by email are ideal.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days, by 17 November 2026.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563e23f35bd02","subject":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","name":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","date":"2026-10-19T22:17:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563e23f35bd02.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563e23f35bd02-your-submission-to-libanswers-was-received","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563e23f35bd02","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563e23f35bd02.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester,\n\nYour question was submitted successfully to the National Library of Wales enquiries service / Cyflwynwyd eich cwestiwn yn llwyddiannus i Wasanaeth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru\n\nDue to high demand and some resource challenges, there may be some delay in responding to enquiries at present. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nOherwydd lefel uchel y galw a rhai heriau adnoddau, bydd oedi gydag ymateb i ymholiadau ar hyn o bryd. Yr ydym yn ymddiheuro am unrhyw anghyfleuster a achosir gan hyn ac fe fyddwn yn darparu diweddariad cyn gynted ag y medrwn.\n\nWe will contact you as soon as possible. In the meantime, perhaps you can visit our FAQs <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com>\nByddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted â phosibl! Yn y cyfamser, efallai yr hoffech chi chwlio ein  FAQs  <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com> perthnasol gall ateb eich cwestiwn.\n\n\n\nWe welcome calls and correspondence in Welsh. You will receive a response in Welsh and correspondence in Welsh will not result in a delay./ Rydym yn croesawu galwadau a gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwch yn derbyn ymateb yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 19 2026, 11:13PM via Email\nEnquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth: Bute Estate records and related items (several items)\nDear Ms Evans and the Enquiries team,\n\nFurther to enquiry 9816877 (14 October 2026), and thank you for your\nhelp so far. To keep things simple, I have put everything I need from\nthe National Library into this one email.\n\n1. Bute Estate Records, 1870–1880\n\nCould you search the Bute Estate Records for the following, all for\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth:\n(a) any lease, agreement or sale of \"Cedfin\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\" or\n\"Great House\" farm between 1870 and 1880, especially to John Williams\nor to Daniel Thomas & Son (who were rated for the lime kiln and quarry\nthere in 1876);\n(b) the items referenced as D153/4–8 and D219, which Glamorgan\nArchives suggests are held by the National Library;\n(c) the conveyance of the Bute interest at Llandough to Western Ground\nRents Ltd in December 1938 (a 1965 contract refers to a conveyance on\nsale dated 25 December 1938).\n\n2. Later records of the farm\n\nWhether the Library holds any record of Great House Farm, Llandough,\nfrom the 1974 survey, the 1988 listing consideration or the demolition\nof the farmhouse in 1988, and anything that would help distinguish it\nfrom Great House, Bonvilston.\n\n3. Searches\n\nWhat searches were made, and whether physical files were checked.\n\nPlease send catalogue references, and copy costs where items exist. A\nreply by 6 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n\n------------------\n\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9901459.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a1563b141b2baa3","subject":"Automatic reply: Enquiry – original South Glamorgan \"County Treasures\" inventory: entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Automatic reply: Enquiry – original South Glamorgan \"County Treasures\" inventory: entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563b141b2baa3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563b141b2baa3-automatic-reply-enquiry-original-south-glamorgan-county-treasures-inventory-entry-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563b141b2baa3","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563b141b2baa3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your email.  Glamorgan Archives aims to answer all remote enquiries within 20 working days.  You may find our website useful, it includes information about the office along with the catalogue of our collections – https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n\n\nWe are currently receiving a large volume of enquiries, many of which are using artificial intelligence (AI) to draft the request.  The nature of these requests can make it hard for staff to identify the relevant information being requested and delay responses.  Please try to ensure that your enquiry contains a clear question so that staff can help you and other enquirers as quickly and efficiently as possible.\n**********\n\nDiolch am eich e-bost.  Mae Archifau Morgannwg yn anelu at ateb pob ymholiad o bell o fewn 20 diwrnod gwaith.  Efallai bydd ein gwefan o ddefnydd, mae’n cynnwys gwybodaeth am y swyddfa ynghyd a’r catalog o’n casgliadau - http://archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/\n\nAr hyn o bryd rydym yn derbyn nifer fawr o ymholiadau, llawer ohonynt yn defnyddio deallusrwydd artiffisial (DA) i ddrafftio'r cais.  Gall natur y ceisiadau hyn ei gwneud hi'n anodd i staff nodi'r wybodaeth berthnasol y gofynnir amdani ac oedi ymatebion.  Ceisiwch sicrhau bod eich ymholiad yn cynnwys cwestiwn clir fel y gall staff eich helpu chi ac ymholwyr eraill mor gyflym ac effeithlon â phosibl.\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a1563ab10f64fba","subject":"Follow-up to research visit request of 15 October — Bute Estate (Glamorgan), Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"Follow-up to research visit request of 15 October — Bute Estate (Glamorgan), Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563ab10f64fba.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563a9efad7a9d-follow-up-to-research-visit-request-of-15-october-bute-estate-glamorgan-llandough-juxta-penarth","scopeTopics":["mount-stuart"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mount-stuart"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563a9efad7a9d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mount-stuart","name":"Mount Stuart (Bute archive)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563ab10f64fba.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Collections team,\n\nFurther to my request of 15 October 2026, may I narrow the search to make it easier?\n\nFor Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan, I am looking for:\n1. any lease, agreement or sale of Cedfin / Tŷ Mawr / Great House farm, 1870-1880. Family papers held by the Bucklers date a division of the farm to 1877, but no document has been located;\n2. rentals or estate surveys showing the farm's tenant and acreage in the 1870s;\n3. the sale of the Bute interest at Llandough to Western Ground Rents Ltd in December 1938 (a 1965 contract refers to a conveyance on sale dated 25 December 1938).\n\nIf these papers are held at the National Library of Wales or Glamorgan Archives rather than at Mount Stuart, a pointer would be very helpful. A short list of what Mount Stuart holds for Llandough, even without copies, would also help me plan a visit. A reply by 6 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534444814000&sa=E"},{"id":"gm-1a1563aae0fa411a","subject":"Re: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough: item locations, retrieval and a copy quotation for BT 31/87651 (several items)","name":"Re: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough: item locations, retrieval and a copy quotation for BT 31/87651 (several items)","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563aae0fa411a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13aa68b250b8de-cas-359317-q8q4r9-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-item-locations-retrieval-and-a-copy-quotation-for-bt-31-87651-severa","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13aa68b250b8de","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-343481","CAS-344046","CAS-347296","CAS-356384","CAS-359317","WA231076","WA240304","WA513690"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563aae0fa411a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Records and Research team,\n\nRe: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 (14 October 2026); CAS-347296-M0V4Y1; CAS-356384-B2F5L9; CAS-344046-K1S1R2; CAS-343481-X5H3M6.\n\nThank you for the catalogue leads (Glamorgan XLVII; Penarth, IR 58) for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan. To keep things simple, I have put everything I need from The National Archives into this one email. If any part is better dealt with by your FOI team, I would be grateful if you could pass it on.\n\n1. Item references and locations\n\nMy follow-up of 16 October 2026 (sent to [email redacted], re CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9) asks for the exact item references, store locations and physical-check status of the Glamorgan XLVII.6 field book, plan and index. That request stands and I am not repeating it here; please link this email to it.\n\n2. IR 58 and the modern titles\n\nThe land is now registered at HM Land Registry under titles WA231076, WA240304, WA513690 and WA735527. I would like to know which IR 58 entries correspond to those parcels.\n\n3. Other records\n\nPlease tell me:\n(a) whether you hold any record of the 1986-87 proceedings (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler) or of the possession order enforced in November 1988;\n(b) whether you hold anything relating to Great House, Llandough, that would help distinguish it from Great House, Bonvilston (the National Monuments Record of Wales has identified its archive 6364275 as relating to Bonvilston).\n\n4. Western Ground Rents Ltd - company file and copy quotation\n\nWestern Ground Rents Ltd (company no. 00342092, incorporated 1938, dissolved 1997) should have a Board of Trade company file in the BT 31 series. I believe the reference is BT 31/87651 (parts /1 to /7), but I have not been able to confirm it in Discovery. Please could you:\n(a) confirm the correct BT 31 reference(s) for this company, or tell me if no file survives or the file is held elsewhere;\n(b) give a quotation, or a page count for each part, so that I can choose which to order first.\nI am particularly interested in any annual returns, accounts, schedules of property or correspondence from 1955 to 1982 that refer to land at Llandough, near Penarth (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr), and the company's disposals to British Petroleum Pension Trust Ltd in or around December 1969.\n\nWhere the Freedom of Information Act 2000 applies, please reply within 20 working days (by 16 November 2026). If anything is reported as not held, please say which systems were searched and whether physical retrieval was attempted.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534442407000&sa=E"},{"id":"gm-1a1563aa61190422","subject":"Records enquiry – BP Properties Ltd / BP Pension Trust: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1969–1993 (several items)","name":"Records enquiry – BP Properties Ltd / BP Pension Trust: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1969–1993 (several items)","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563aa61190422.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526f6e1b9996a-cords-enquiry-bp-properties-ltd-bp-pension-trust-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1969-1993-several-items","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526f6e1b9996a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":["WA231076","WA240304"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563aa61190422.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear BP Archive,\n\nThank you for your replies of 19 and 25 August 2026, and further to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026. To keep things simple, I have put everything I need to ask BP into this one email.\n\nI understand the BP Archive holds material only to the end of 1954 and that later records are not open to external access. I am not asking for access. I am asking whether you hold, or can identify the custodian of, the records below.\n\n1. Property records, 1969–1993\n\nRecords of BP Properties Ltd (company no. 00699446) and British Petroleum Pension Trust Ltd relating to land at Llandough, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr), 1969–1993, including:\n(a) the purchase from Western Ground Rents Ltd by conveyance recited as dated 31 December 1969, and the conveyances of 23 May 1975 and 19 November 1982, as recited in HM Land Registry's records;\n(b) the first registrations of titles WA231076 and WA240304 (1982–83) and their amalgamation on 2 February 1987;\n(c) the management of the site in the 1980s;\n(d) the 1993 transfer of the site to Ideal Homes.\n\n2. The litigation and the 1988 demolition\n\nWhether BP holds any file on BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court 1986; Court of Appeal 1987) or on the possession and demolition of the farmhouse in November–December 1988.\n\n3. Searches and retention\n\nWhat searches were made, whether physical files were checked, and whether anything has been destroyed or transferred elsewhere.\n\nA catalogue reference, or a \"not held\" with a pointer to the part of BP that would hold property-company records, would both help. A reply by 16 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nPlease also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563aa4a42a029","subject":"Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","name":"Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563aa4a42a029.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526ec926276db-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-follow-up-to-my-preservation-notice-of-28-september-2026","scopeTopics":["ads"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ads"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526ec926276db","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"ads","name":"Archaeology Data Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563aa4a42a029.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Archaeology Data Service,\n\nRe: my preservation notice of 28 September 2026; your reply of 2 October 2026.\n\nI am writing about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, the subject of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court 1986; Court of Appeal 1987). Thank you for your reply of 2 October 2026; I understand the Archaeology Data Service preserves its data permanently.\n\nI would be grateful if you would tell me:\n1. whether the Archaeology Data Service holds any deposit, metadata record or archive identifier relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, in particular the 1990 Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust assessment or the 1994 Cotswold Archaeology work;\n2. what searches were made, and whether any physical files were checked;\n3. whether anything has been destroyed or transferred elsewhere (and if so, when and to whom).\n\nA reply by 16 November 2026 would be much appreciated. Please also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563aa32adcc72","subject":"Enquiry – original South Glamorgan \"County Treasures\" inventory: entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Enquiry – original South Glamorgan \"County Treasures\" inventory: entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563aa32adcc72.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526ec443d3ca3-enquiry-original-south-glamorgan-county-treasures-inventory-entry-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526ec443d3ca3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563aa32adcc72.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Glamorgan Archives,\n\nI am researching Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan.\n\nI am looking for the original County Treasures inventory compiled by the former South Glamorgan County Council (I understand in the late 1970s), and any entry in it for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr. The later survey (2002–2007) is a different record.\n\nCould you tell me whether Glamorgan Archives holds:\n1. the original inventory, or any Llandough, Penarth or Cogan entry in it for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr;\n2. any associated survey sheet, field notes, map, photograph or draft list identifying the property;\n3. any record of amendment or deletion between the original inventory and the later survey?\n\nCatalogue references would be ideal. Search terms: \"Great House Farm\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"County Treasures\", \"South Glamorgan County Council\".\n\nA reply by 16 November 2026 would be much appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563aa0b94af1b","subject":"Glamorgan County Council deed wallet 1756 (Llandough school site)  – follow-up to FOI 00211027","name":"Glamorgan County Council deed wallet 1756 (Llandough school site)  – follow-up to FOI 00211027","date":"2026-10-19T22:14:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563aa0b94af1b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526dbb7d77751-glamorgan-county-council-deed-wallet-1756-llandough-school-site-follow-up-to-foi-00211027","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526dbb7d77751","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563aa0b94af1b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Unit,\n\nRe: FOI 00211027; your reply of 14 September 2026, which included the 1965 conveyance of the Llandough school site and the 1965 contract. The conveyance is marked as document 10 in deed wallet 1756.\n\nPlease provide copies of the other documents in that deed wallet (documents 1 to 9, and 11 onward), or a list of them if that is easier. In particular:\n(a) any abstract or summary of title (the 1965 contract, condition F, says title was to start with a conveyance on sale dated 25 December 1938);\n(b) the plan to the conveyance of 5 March 1962 by Western Ground Rents Ltd to Lakeside and Llandough Development Co Ltd, if a copy is held.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a667d5c9b9","subject":"FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","name":"FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 — c.1880 medieval ironwork from Great House Farm, Llandough: published sources say it is in the National Museum","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a667d5c9b9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf-foi-2026-024-032-036-c-1880-medieval-ironwork-from-great-house-farm-llandough-published-sources-say-it-is-in-the-nationa","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1563a58cdf4ebf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":["FOI 2026-024","FOI 2026-032","FOI 2026-036"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a667d5c9b9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Amgueddfa Cymru FOI team,\n\nRe: FOI 2026-024 (25 August 2026), FOI 2026-032 (22 September 2026), FOI 2026-036 (5 October 2026) and your reply of 16 October 2026 on the search basis.\n\nThank you for your replies about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan. I would be grateful for help reconciling them with two published sources.\n\nYour replies, as I understand them:\n- FOI 2026-024: no records of the specific discovery (a soldier, horse, visor and lance);\n- FOI 2026-032: other archaeological discoveries at Great House Farm were identified but treated as unrelated or out of scope;\n- FOI 2026-036: no accession entry, register, day-book, donations book or correspondence dated 1875-1915 for ironwork, armour, a visor, lance or helmet from Great House / Llandough Farm, including the former Cardiff Museum registers;\n- 16 October 2026: no separate search log is held beyond what was supplied.\n\nThe published sources:\n- Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust, \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological Assessment\", August 1990 (planning files 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES): \"it is likely that some medieval ironwork which is held by the National Museum of Wales was discovered under the rear wing c 1880 (RCAHMW 1988).\"\n- Holbrook and Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70, n. 142: \"medieval ironwork was discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm c. 1880. It is now in the collections of the National Museums & Galleries of Wales.\"\n\nEither the published statements are mistaken, or the objects are recorded under a different findspot, donor name or description. I am asking only for recorded information, or confirmation that none is held:\n\n1. Please provide any record held by Amgueddfa Cymru (including correspondence with the authors or with GGAT/RCAHMW, enquiry files, or collections-management notes) that records or comments on the statement that medieval ironwork from Great House Farm is in the Museum's collections. If none is held, please say so.\n\n2. Please search the collections database and the accession registers for medieval ironwork (any object type) with any of these in the findspot, place, donor or provenance fields: \"Llandough\", \"Llandough-juxta-Penarth\", \"Great House\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Cedfin\", \"Williams of Great House\", or a Cardiff Museum donation before 1912. Please list any matches, with accession numbers and descriptions, or confirm that there are none.\n\n3. Please say whether any record identified and treated as unrelated under FOI 2026-024 or 2026-032 could correspond to the c.1880 ironwork.\n\n4. If this is better treated as a request for internal review of FOI 2026-036, please treat it as one and tell me the reference and the date by which you will reply.\n\nPlease reply within 20 working days (by 16 November 2026).\n\nSupporting material: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E (evidence catalogue), https://www.google.com/url?q=https://clerk.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E and https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792534426733000&sa=E"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a5fd1f8170","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:48Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a5fd1f8170.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526f7cd0d98cb-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526f7cd0d98cb","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a5fd1f8170.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Jones,\n\nThank you for your email of 16 October 2026 asking whether I have a claim number relating to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026. I have put everything I need to ask HMCTS into this one reply.\n\n1. Claim numbers and the proceedings concerned\n\nI do not have claim numbers. The proceedings I know of concern Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, near Penarth:\n- a possession order of 2 February 1955 and a Cardiff County Court order of 11 December 1962, in proceedings in which Western Ground Rents Ltd was the party seeking possession;\n- a possession action listed on 3 July 1974;\n- the possession order enforced in November 1988 following BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court, Hollis J, July 1986; Court of Appeal [1987] EWCA Civ 2).\n\nThese details come from the published judgment and family papers, so I may be wrong on some of them.\n\n2. Surviving records\n\nCould you tell me whether any record, index entry, warrant or bailiff's return survives for these, or for the November 1988 enforcement? If not, were any transferred elsewhere (for example to a central HMCTS archive or The National Archives) or destroyed, and if so when and under which retention schedule?\n\n3. The earlier \"no records\" reply\n\nCardiff County Court Enquiries told me on 4 August 2026 that, because of the case's age, no records were held. Could you let me know the basis of that statement, so that I understand how it fits with your request for a claim number?\n\nIf any of this is better handled under my Ministry of Justice subject access request (IR 260904007), please let me know.\n\nA reply by 2 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a5d85ffa54","subject":"Enquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth: Bute Estate records and related items (several items)","name":"Enquiry 9816877 – Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr (Cedfin), Llandough-juxta-Penarth: Bute Estate records and related items (several items)","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a5d85ffa54.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526f6d8a1233b-enquiry-9816877-great-house-farm-t-mawr-cedfin-llandough-juxta-penarth-bute-estate-records-and-related-items-several-ite","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526f6d8a1233b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a5d85ffa54.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Evans and the Enquiries team,\n\nFurther to enquiry 9816877 (14 October 2026), and thank you for your help so far. To keep things simple, I have put everything I need from the National Library into this one email.\n\n1. Bute Estate Records, 1870–1880\n\nCould you search the Bute Estate Records for the following, all for Llandough-juxta-Penarth:\n(a) any lease, agreement or sale of \"Cedfin\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\" or \"Great House\" farm between 1870 and 1880, especially to John Williams or to Daniel Thomas & Son (who were rated for the lime kiln and quarry there in 1876);\n(b) the items referenced as D153/4–8 and D219, which Glamorgan Archives suggests are held by the National Library;\n(c) the conveyance of the Bute interest at Llandough to Western Ground Rents Ltd in December 1938 (a 1965 contract refers to a conveyance on sale dated 25 December 1938).\n\n2. Later records of the farm\n\nWhether the Library holds any record of Great House Farm, Llandough, from the 1974 survey, the 1988 listing consideration or the demolition of the farmhouse in 1988, and anything that would help distinguish it from Great House, Bonvilston.\n\n3. Searches\n\nWhat searches were made, and whether physical files were checked.\n\nPlease send catalogue references, and copy costs where items exist. A reply by 6 November 2026 would be appreciated.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a5b056dbb0","subject":"Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","name":"Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough – follow-up to my preservation notice of 28 September 2026","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a5b056dbb0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1526eca2820200-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-follow-up-to-my-preservation-notice-of-28-september-2026","scopeTopics":["cotswold"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cotswold"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1526eca2820200","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cotswold","name":"Cotswold Archaeology"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a5b056dbb0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Cotswold Archaeology,\n\nRe: my preservation notice of 28 September 2026.\n\nI am writing about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan, the subject of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (High Court 1986; Court of Appeal 1987). Thank you for Paolo Guarino's reply of 12 October 2026 pointing me to the 1994 report on your online reports library. This follow-up is about the underlying excavation archive for that 1994 work at the site, before the houses at Church View Close were built.\n\nI would be grateful if you would tell me:\n1. whether Cotswold Archaeology holds the excavation archive for the 1994 work (site code, context sheets, photographs, finds inventory, field records and correspondence), and whether it has been deposited with a museum or archive (and if so, where and under what accession);\n2. what searches were made, and whether any physical files were checked;\n3. whether anything has been destroyed or transferred elsewhere (and if so, when and to whom).\n\nA reply by 16 November 2026 would be much appreciated. Please also make sure that no record relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr is destroyed while these enquiries are open.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a1cfcaeb44","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a1cfcaeb44.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0bbdf18c9ea3b9-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0bbdf18c9ea3b9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a1cfcaeb44.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear HER Team,\n\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (HER 02038s) — your reply of 16 October 2026 to my schedule GHF/HENEB/2026-09-20\n\nThank you for your reply of 16 October, and for your email of 14 October confirming the physical search of the HER source file and the upload of its contents to Archwilio record 02038s.\n\nSo that nothing is asked twice: I do not repeat here anything in my complaint of 27 September 2026, which Mr Foulston is investigating, or items 1, 2, 13, 39, 42 and 48 of the schedule, which you have answered. I make this request under Heneb's arrangements for access to the Historic Environment Record and its own policy. I do not reopen the question of the Environmental Information Regulations, on which I note your position of 6 October.\n\n1. Scope of the search. Each \"not held\" answer reads \"The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\" Several items asked for records of the Trust rather than entries in the HER: for example item 12 (Cadw's inspection of 29 July 1988), item 22 (the Trust's copy of the 1974 measured survey), item 25 (the consultee response to reserved matters application 92/00671/RES), items 28 to 31 (condition compliance, the meeting of 4 May 1994, monitoring of the 1994 excavation, and the burial licence), item 32 (correspondence with Cadw on scheduling, 1993 to 1995) and item 33 (the watching brief recommended in 1990). For those items, please confirm whether the search extended beyond the HER to:\n(a) the former GGAT curatorial and planning-advice files;\n(b) the former GGAT project archives, including the archive of the August 1990 assessment \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough\";\n(c) the former GGAT paper records kept at Baglan (your answer to item 46); and\n(d) the Trust's general correspondence and administrative files.\nIf any of these was not searched, please either search it or tell me which part of Heneb holds it, so that I can ask in the right place.\n\n2. Archive locations (item 34). Does the HER event record for each intervention (1978 to 1980, 1990 and 1994, including event GGATE003875) carry an archive-holder or archive-location field? If so, please tell me what each one says.\n\n3. 1988 records (item 11). You say these are publicly available on Archwilio. Please identify which of the files in the Sources section of record 02038s are the 1988 records you mean, so that I can be sure I am reading the right documents.\n\n4. Change log (items 3 to 5). I understand that the log is an audit trail rather than a set of snapshots, and that it contains personal data. Could Heneb supply the entries for 02038s and its linked records with names and any other personal data removed, showing for each entry only the date, the table or field changed and the type of change? If the full history is too long, the entries from 20 May 2026 to date would be enough for now.\n\n5. Date of transfer (item 45). Thank you for confirming that Heneb is the record holder for the former GGAT. Item 45 also asked for the date of transfer; please give it.\n\n6. Retention and disposal (items 46 and 47). Please send the records-management or retention policy that applies to the former GGAT paper records now, while the review you mention is under way. Please also say whether Heneb, or the former GGAT, keeps a register of disposal or destruction for those records; if no such register exists, please say so.\n\n7. Preservation. As Heneb's data management policy is under review, I ask that nothing relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough is destroyed, disposed of, weeded or moved out of Heneb's custody while my enquiries and complaint remain open. This covers paper and digital records, emails and the HER change log, and in particular:\n- HER records 02038s, GGAT03586s and GGATE003872, event GGATE003875, and the HER source file;\n- the August 1990 assessment \"Land at Great House Farm, Llandough\" and its project archive;\n- the Trust's files on the 1994 excavation and on Holbrook and Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005);\n- consultation responses and correspondence on planning applications 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES;\n- correspondence with Cadw, the Vale of Glamorgan Council, BP Properties Ltd and its agents, Ideal Homes Wales Ltd and Cotswold Archaeological Trust, 1978 to 1995 and 2005.\nI asked for this in my preservation notice of 28 September 2026. I would be grateful for a short written confirmation that a hold is in place.\n\nI would be grateful for that confirmation as soon as convenient, and for the rest by 19 November 2026. If any item is unclear or too broad, please tell me and I will narrow it.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com"},{"id":"gm-1a1563a1a05563ce","subject":"Re: Welsh Government response to request for information ATISN 26-0010 (Retention & destruction schedules))","name":"Re: Welsh Government response to request for information ATISN 26-0010 (Retention & destruction schedules))","date":"2026-10-19T22:13:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1563a1a05563ce.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1537b442f27f72-welsh-government-response-to-request-for-information-atisn-26-0010-retention-destruction-schedules","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1537b442f27f72","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN 27021","ATISN 27589"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1563a1a05563ce.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Rights Unit,\n\nTo keep everything for the Welsh Government in one place, this email covers four things: (A) a request for an internal review of ATISN 26-0010; (B) ATISN 27589 (Cadw; your ref qA2496208); (C) four new requests for information; and (D) a request that records be preserved. I would be grateful if you could pass each part to the right team.\n\nA. ATISN 26-0010 – request for internal review\n\nThank you, and please pass my thanks to Emma Harvey-Woodason, for the response of 19 October 2026. I ask for an internal review on four points. Each asks only for recorded information, or for confirmation that none is held.\n\n1. Item 2 of my request asked for any recorded information on whether files in those series were destroyed, transferred or retained, and if destroyed \"the date and authority\". The response says \"any routine records would have been destroyed in line with the corporate retention schedule applied at the time\", and that it is \"equally possible\" that disposition \"would have been carried out by a predecessor body\". Please confirm whether the Welsh Government holds any record of an actual destruction, transfer or retention decision for files in those series relating to the farm, Western Ground Rents Ltd or BP Properties Ltd. If none is held, please confirm that the quoted sentences describe the likely position and not a recorded event.\n\n2. If a specific entry in a retention schedule was relied on for the sentence quoted at point 1, please provide that entry (title, version, date). If no particular entry was identified, please say so. I have noted that the current schedules are published on GOV.WALES, so I am not asking you to explain them.\n\n3. The response says that \"Before 1997, the Welsh Office or other agencies … would have had their own retention schedules.\" Does the Welsh Government hold the Welsh Office schedules for the file series in item 1 of my request? If so, please provide them. If not, please say so and, if known, where they are held.\n\n4. The response says: \"Searches were carried out to find files mentioning the farm name and the companies listed in your request.\" Please provide the record of those searches: the systems, indexes and file series searched, the search terms, the date range, and whether the index of physical registered files was included. (The internal review of ATISN 27021, dated 2 July 2026, describes searches of physical registered files, including A--CL172-06-017/1 Community of Llandough, and a wider search of files from around the 1980s–1990s.)\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, the 1988 Cadw listing file is not part of this review; it is covered by ATISN 26-0009 (response due 6 November 2026).\n\nB. ATISN 27589 (Cadw; your ref qA2496208)\n\nI note the letter of 19 October 2026 refusing ATISN 27589 under section 14(2). Three points, so that I can decide whether to ask for an internal review:\n\n1. Section 14(2) applies only to a request that is substantially similar to an earlier one. Please tell me which points of ATISN 27589 the Welsh Government considers ATISN 27021 already covered. Point 3 of ATISN 27589 asked for \"Any transfer, destruction or disposal of those files, with the schedule used and the date.\" ATISN 27021 did not ask for that.\n\n2. The letter says that no new information \"has been generated or become available\". Please confirm whether it is saying that no information is held on any point of ATISN 27589 beyond what was released under ATISN 27021, or only that it declines to search again.\n\n3. The letter sets out the right to complain to the Information Commissioner but not the internal review procedure, although it refers to the internal review of ATISN 27021. Please confirm how and by when I may ask for an internal review of ATISN 27589. I will not treat the time for asking as running until you have confirmed this.\n\nThe question in point 3 of ATISN 27589 is also being dealt with under ATISN 26-0009, so I am not making any new request about it here.\n\nC. New requests under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the Environmental Information Regulations 2004\n\nThese are new requests and not part of the review above. They concern Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan.\n\n1. Registered files. The internal review of ATISN 27021 identified registered files (including A--CL172-06-017/1 Community of Llandough, CL172-10-001/1, A--CL172-10-002/1, A--CL172-10-001/1, and six files of potential interest). I am not asking for the contents of the files. For each file, please provide the register entry or index record showing its title, opening and closing dates, and current status (retained, transferred, destroyed or not traced) and, where the entry says a file was destroyed or transferred, the date and the record of the destruction or transfer.\n\n2. Property and deeds records. The response to ATISN 26-0010 says that records of Welsh Government property, deeds and leasing are retained until the property is sold or the lease ends. Please confirm whether the Welsh Government or the Welsh Office has ever owned, leased, acquired or disposed of any interest in land at Great House Farm, Leckwith Road or village green VG41, Llandough, between 1950 and 1997, and provide any deed, lease or property file record of it. If none is held, please say so.\n\n3. Wartime farm records, 1936–1955. Please provide any recorded information held by the Welsh Government, including records inherited from the Welsh Office, about the farm in 1936–1955:\n(a) any record of the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee, or its post-war successor, about the farm, including any possession, requisition or cultivation direction;\n(b) any claim or payment under the Compensation (Defence) Act 1939;\n(c) any record naming the occupier or owner of the farm in that period.\nI understand the 1941–43 National Farm Survey is held at The National Archives (MAF 32), so I am not asking for it. If any other record has been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference rather than treating that part as not held.\n\n4. Compulsory purchase and stopping-up orders, 1950–1995. Please confirm whether the Secretary of State for Wales or the Welsh Office made or confirmed any compulsory purchase order, stopping-up order or diversion order affecting the land at Great House Farm between 1950 and 1995, and provide a copy of any such order and of the decision confirming it. ATISN 26-0010 searched under the farm name and two company names. Orders of this kind are usually titled by road or place, so please also search under \"Leckwith Road, Llandough\", \"Llandough-juxta-Penarth\" and \"Church View Close\". If such records have been transferred to The National Archives, please give the reference.\n\nIf no information is held for any part, please say so. If anything is withheld, please give the exemption or exception relied on.\n\nD. Preservation of records\n\nAs I asked on 28 September and 1 October 2026, please make sure that the following are not destroyed or weeded while ATISN 26-0009, the review in part A, the requests in part C and any complaint to the Information Commissioner remain open:\n\n1. the index of physical registered files, and the registered files themselves, referred to in the internal review of ATISN 27021 (including A--CL172-06-017/1, CL172-10-001/1, A--CL172-10-002/1, A--CL172-10-001/1 and the six files of potential interest identified in that review);\n2. any 1988 listing file for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, or any part or remnant of it;\n3. the originals of the two inspection photographs dated 29 July 1988 released under ATISN 27021, with any negatives, digital files, envelopes, captions or other information recorded with them;\n4. any disposal or destruction logs, certificates or schedules of destruction covering Welsh Office or Cadw records for 1970–1997;\n5. the retention schedules in force for those records in 1970–1997;\n6. any transfer lists to The National Archives or a Place of Deposit for those records, including any selection records made under OSP 7.\n\nPlease confirm in writing that a hold is in place for these records.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a154577a09c3329","subject":"RE: FOI — Welsh Office / Cadw papers, July–December 1988 — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — following 26FOI 103 (ATISN 27589)","name":"RE: FOI — Welsh Office / Cadw papers, July–December 1988 — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — following 26FOI 103 (ATISN 27589)","date":"2026-10-19T13:26:17Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a154577a09c3329.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a154577a09c3329-foi-welsh-office-cadw-papers-july-december-1988-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-following-26foi-103-atisn-27589","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a154577a09c3329","direction":"received","from":"Andy Wigley","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["26FOI103","ATISN27589","qA2496208"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a154577a09c3329.json","attachments":[{"name":"ATISN 27589 - 2026-10-19 - Response.pdf","title":"ATISN 27589 response (ref qA2496208): request refused under FOIA s.14(2) as a repeat of ATISN 27021","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-10-19_cadw_atisn-27589_response-s14-2.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":112190,"sha256":"0813652b6c608e40ca7db2fc6c95209c32f71704984fcfdea740781ef3df2beb"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your request which was received on 28 September 2026.\n\nPlease see attached response.\n\nYour sincerely,\n\nAndy Wigley\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD5FA6.A5431630]\n\nDr Andy Wigley\nPrif Arolygydd – Pennaeth Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Chief Inspector - Head of Historic Environment Inspectorate\nCadw\nDysgu, Cymunedau a Diwylliant / Learning, Communities and Culture\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nTŷ Ladywell / Ladywell House\nY Drenewydd / Newtown\nPowys\n[postcode redacted]\n\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\nFfôn symudol / Mobile: [phone redacted]\nE-bost/ Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[cid:image002.png@01DD5FA6.A5431630][cid:image003.png@01DD5FA6.A5431630]\nP Helpwch yr amgylchedd - peidiwch ag argraffu hon os nad oes gwir raid   Help our environment - only print this if really necessary\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth Gymraeg. Cewch ateb Cymraeg i bob gohebiaeth Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh. Correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not involve any delay.\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\n[Attached letter: “ATISN 27589 - 2026-10-19 - Response.pdf” (2 pages). Its text, extracted from the PDF, follows. The PDF itself is linked under Attachments below.]\n\nRequester                                                     Eich cyf/Your ref: ATISN 27589\nBy email:\n[email redacted]                                         Ein cyf/Our ref: qA2496208\n\n                                                                 Dyddiad/Date: 19 October 2026\n\n\n\n\nDear Requester\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough (ATISN 27589)\n\nThank you for your request for information received on 28 September 2026.\n\nWe have considered your request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nThe information you have requested was the subject of a previous request submitted by\nyou under reference (ATISN 27021), to which Welsh Government has already\nresponded, including undertaking an internal review. Following a review of your latest\nrequest, we are satisfied that it is substantially similar to the earlier request and that no\nnew information has been generated or become available since our previous response.\n\nAccordingly, Welsh Government is refusing your request under section 14(2) of the\nFreedom of Information Act 2000, which provides that a public authority is not obliged to\ncomply with a request if it is a repeated request made by the same person, where it is\nsubstantially similar to a previous request and a reasonable interval has not elapsed.\n\nFor ease of reference, the previous response, together with the outcome of the\nassociated internal review, can be found here:\n\nFOI release 27021: Great House Farm | GOV.WALES\n\nYou have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner. The Information\nCommissioner can be contacted at:\n\fInformation Commissioner’s Office,\nWycliffe House,\nWater Lane,\nWilmslow,\nCheshire,\n[postcode redacted].\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nAndy Wigley\nHead of Historic Environment Inspectorate\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (1)\n- ATISN 27589 - 2026-10-19 - Response.pdf (application/pdf, 110 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-10-19_cadw_atisn-27589_response-s14-2.pdf"},{"id":"gm-1a1537b442f27f72","subject":"Welsh Government response to request for information ATISN 26-0010 (Retention & destruction schedules))","name":"Welsh Government response to request for information ATISN 26-0010 (Retention & destruction schedules))","date":"2026-10-19T09:25:46Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1537b442f27f72.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1537b442f27f72-welsh-government-response-to-request-for-information-atisn-26-0010-retention-destruction-schedules","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1537b442f27f72","direction":"received","from":"Welsh Government FOI mailbox (Operational Effectiveness Group)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN26-0010"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1537b442f27f72.json","attachments":[{"name":"ATISN 26-0010 - Disclosure.pdf","title":"ATISN 26-0010 disclosure response: retention and destruction schedules; no files found under the farm name, Western Ground Rents Ltd or BP Properties Ltd","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-10-19_welsh-government_atisn-26-0010_disclosure-response.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":171042,"sha256":"7fca7e2b9ae5a10be76817ef5b2a8a908aa87ddd8de68c828a8d45bfb6d9a2f6"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nFurther to your recent request for information, please find disclosure response attached, sent on behalf of Emma Harvey-Woodason.\n\nKind regards\nNatalie\n\nNatalie Chant\nTîm Rheoli Busnes / Business Management Unit\nY Grŵp Effeithiolrwydd Gweithredol / Operational Effectiveness Group\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nE-bost: [email redacted] / E-mail: [email redacted]\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\n[Attached letter: “ATISN 26-0010 - Disclosure.pdf” (2 pages). Its text, extracted from the PDF, follows. The PDF itself is linked under Attachments below.]\n\nY Grŵp Effeithiolrwydd Gweithredol\nOperational Effectiveness Group\n\n\n\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]\n\nOur ref: ATISN 26-0010\nDate: 19 October 2026\n\nDear Requester\n\nATISN 26-0010\n\nThank you for your request which I received on 10 October. You asked for:\n\n   1. The retention and destruction schedules (or equivalent policy documents) that\n      applied, or still apply, to former Welsh Office / Welsh Government file series\n      covering agricultural tenancies, land ownership or compulsory purchase, rural\n      depopulation, or related policy in the period 1970–1997.\n   2. Any recorded information identifying whether files in those series that would\n      have related to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough-juxta-Penarth, or to\n      the companies Western Ground Rents Ltd or BP Properties Ltd, were\n      destroyed, transferred or retained, and if destroyed the date and authority.\n   3. Confirmation of the repositories to which any surviving pre-1997 paper files\n      from the relevant series were transferred (e.g. National Assembly / Welsh\n      Government / The National Archives / other).\nOur response\n\n   1. All Welsh Government Retention Schedules, past and present, are available\n      on the external website: Welsh Government retention and disposal schedule |\n      GOV.WALES. Before 1997, the Welsh Office or other agencies would have\n      had responsibility for areas affecting Wales and would have had their own\n      retention schedules.\n\n   2. Searches were carried out to find files mentioning the farm name and the\n      companies listed in your request. No files were found and given the date\n      range of your request, any routine records would have been destroyed in line\n      with the corporate retention schedule applied at the time. Given the date\n      range for the search, it is equally possible that records relating to this would\n      not have been transferred to Welsh Government and disposition would have\n      been carried out by a predecessor body.\n\n\n\n\n                                      Parc Cathays ● Cathays Park            [email redacted]\n                                               Caerdydd ● Cardiff   Gwefan ● website: www.llyw.cymru\n                                                        [postcode redacted]                       www.gov.wales\n\f   3. Material with historical significance from this period would have been\n      identified using the Welsh Office’s Operational Selection Policy (available on\n      TNA’s website: OSP 7 - Welsh Office 1979-1997). Historical material would\n      then have been transferred by us to The National Archives (or a designated\n      Place of Deposit) for permanent preservation at the appropriate time (this was\n      after 30 years at that time, subsequently reduced to after 20 years for WG\n      material from 2023 onwards). Records relating to Welsh Government\n      property/deeds/leasing etc. are not transferred to TNA as they are not classed\n      as “public records” like our business records are. These would be retained\n      until the property is sold or lease agreements terminated.\n\nNext steps\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with the Welsh Government’s handling of your request, you\ncan ask for an internal review within 40 working days of the date of this response.\nRequests for an internal review should be addressed to the Welsh Government’s\nFreedom of Information Officer at:\n\nInformation Rights Unit\nWelsh Government\nCathays Park\nCardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\nor e-mail: [email redacted]\n\nPlease remember to quote the ATISN reference number above.\n\nYou also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner. The\nInformation Commissioner can be contacted at:\n\nInformation Commissioner’s Office\nWycliffe House\nWater Lane\nWilmslow\nCheshire\n[postcode redacted]\n\nWebsite: www.ico.org.uk\n\nHowever, please note that the Commissioner will not normally investigate a\ncomplaint until it has been through our own internal review process.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nEmma Harvey-Woodason\nDepartmental Records Officer\nWelsh Government\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (1)\n- ATISN 26-0010 - Disclosure.pdf (application/pdf, 167 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-10-19_welsh-government_atisn-26-0010_disclosure-response.pdf"},{"id":"gm-1a15125192fffca9","subject":"Re: Chase — Vale of Glamorgan FOI 00210772 internal review — 15 October 2026","name":"Re: Chase — Vale of Glamorgan FOI 00210772 internal review — 15 October 2026","date":"2026-10-18T22:32:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15125192fffca9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cc190751565-chase-vale-of-glamorgan-foi-00210772-internal-review-15-october-2026","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cc190751565","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15125192fffca9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Unit, A short follow-up on the internal review of FOI 00210772 (request of 7 July 2026), which I asked about on 7 and 15 October 2026. I have not yet had an outcome or a date. Please send the outcome, or a firm date for it, by 30 October 2026. If I have neither by then, I may ask the Information Commissioner's Office to consider the delay under section 50 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000. While the review is pending, please confirm that records relating to planning applications 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES (including conditions 16–18 and any section 52 or section 106 agreement) are held under a hold and will not be destroyed under routine retention schedules. Yours faithfully, Requester [email redacted] Evidence catalogue: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792449148071000&sa=E On Thu, Oct 15, 2026 08:01 PM, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote: Dear FOI Unit, \n \nThis is the scheduled chase for internal review of FOI 00210772, requested on 7 July 2026 and still outstanding. \n \nPlease confirm the review outcome or a firm date. I am also concerned that records relevant to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (1988 eviction, demolition, planning and Building Preservation Notice files) may be subject to routine disposal. Please suspend any disposal of those records pending the outcome of this review. \n \nPublic working evidence catalogue:  https://greathousefarmwiki.wor dpress.com \nTitle and chronology index:  https://dartboard.bucklerfamil y.estate  and  https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfam ily.estate \nLong-term archive:  https://wayback.bucklerfamily. estate \n \nYours sincerely, \n \nRequester  \n"},{"id":"gm-1a15125176d01042","subject":"Re: 00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm","name":"Re: 00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm","date":"2026-10-18T22:32:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15125176d01042.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3fa1b0e3358b-00211484-narrowed-request-commemorative-tree-church-view-close-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3fa1b0e3358b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772","00211483","00211484"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15125176d01042.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Unit, This is a supplement to my open requests 00211484 and 00211483 (Church View Close / Great House Farm). It adds a narrow request about the village green beside Leckwith Road. If you would rather log it as a separate request, please do so and let me know the reference. It does not replace or narrow any open request, or restart their clocks. This is a request under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 (and the Freedom of Information Act 2000 for anything that is not environmental information). The council is the commons registration authority for the area. Please provide: 1. Village green VG41 (registered 16 June 1970 under the Commons Registration Act 1965): the register entry and register map; the application and any evidence or statutory declaration submitted with it; the applicant's identity; any objection or representation received; and any notice of the application sent to the occupiers of Great House Farm, which adjoined the land. 2. Glamorgan County Council planning committee, meeting of 19 November 1958: the minutes and any papers or correspondence relating to representations made by a Mrs Buckler of Great House Farm (reported, as I understand it, in the Western Mail on 20 November 1958). 3. Any council works carried out on the VG41 land or the adjoining woodland north of Leckwith Road between 1955 and 1988: dates, contractors and any record of who the council understood the owner or occupier to be. If any of these records were transferred to Glamorgan Archives, please tell me the reference rather than treating that part as not held. If a record contains third-party personal data, please redact that data rather than withhold the record. Please reply within 20 working days. I am happy to receive copies electronically. Yours faithfully, Requester [email redacted] Evidence catalogue: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792449147391000&sa=E On Mon, Sep 28, 2026 06:41 PM, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote: Information Governance Team, \nVale of Glamorgan Council \n [email redacted] \n \nSirs/Madam, \n \nCase 00211484. This narrows the request. It does not reopen 00210772. Please keep them separate. \n \nI hold dated photographs of the works. Please disclose: \n \n1. The instruction, works order or contractor record for removal of the commemorative tree on or adjoining the former Great House Farm / Church View Close land. \n2. The date of the works and who authorised them. \n3. Any note linking the tree to the Williams / Buckler family, to Mary Williams, or to the 1988 demolition. \n \nIf nothing is held, say what was searched. \n \nThe public evidence index is  https://greathousefarmwiki.wor dpress.com/  . This request is about one tree and one works record. It is not a request that you decide title. \n \nYours faithfully, \n \nRequester  \n [email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a15125143440637","subject":"Re: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211557","name":"Re: FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00211557","date":"2026-10-18T22:32:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a15125143440637.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0f2d7e013f1d97-foi-eir-request-case-ref-00211557","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0f2d7e013f1d97","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211557"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a15125143440637.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Unit, This is a supplement to my request 00211557 (Great House Farm / Church View Close). It adds one narrow request for a related heritage record. If you would rather log it as a separate request, please do so and let me know the reference. It is not meant to replace or narrow 00211557 or any of my other open requests, or to restart their clocks. Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (and the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 for anything that is environmental information), I am looking for the original County Treasures inventory compiled by the former South Glamorgan County Council (I understand in the late 1970s), specifically any entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, near Penarth. The Council's County Treasures list and 2009 Supplementary Planning Guidance describe the later survey (2002–2007), which is a different record. Please provide, if held: 1. The original list, including any Llandough, Penarth or Cogan entry for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr. 2. Any associated survey sheet, field notes, map, photograph or draft list identifying the property. 3. Any record of amendment or deletion between the original inventory and the later survey. 4. Any record of how the original inventory was circulated to the council's planning and conservation officers. Search terms: \"Great House Farm\", \"Tŷ Mawr\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"County Treasures\", \"South Glamorgan County Council\". If the records are not held, please say whether they were transferred (for example to Glamorgan Archives, with the reference) and distinguish \"not held\" from \"not found after searching\". If a record contains third-party personal data, please redact that data rather than withhold the record. Please reply within 20 working days. Yours faithfully, Requester [email redacted] Evidence catalogue: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792449146622000&sa=E On Wed, Sep 30, 2026 12:03 PM, [email redacted] wrote: \n \n Dear  Requester FREEDOM OF INFORMATION ACT 2000/ENVIRONMENTAL INFORMATION REGULATIONS 2004 - INFORMATION REQUEST Thank you for your request for information about: Great House Farm / Church View Close — s.52/land charges, planning register, EA screening, condition 16–18 chain, 92/00671/RES Your request was received on 28/09/2026 and is being considered under the terms of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the Environmental Information Regulations 2004. Your query has been given the reference 00211557. In some circumstances a fee may be payable and if that is the case we will let you know. A fees notice will be issued to you, and you will be required to pay before we will proceed to deal with your request. You should receive the information requested within 20 working days unless the Council does not hold the information or there is a reason for it to be withheld. We will write to you in any event. If you have any requirements regarding the format any information should be supplied in, e.g. the language to be used, audio, large print and so on, then if you have not already done so please let us know.  If you have any queries or concerns then please do not hesitate to contact us. Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future communications. Further information about your rights is also available from the Information Commissioner at: Information Commissioner's Office - Wales Second Floor, Churchill House Churchill Way, Cardiff [postcode redacted] [phone redacted]  [email redacted]   Yours sincerely, Information Governance Officer/ Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth Director's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau Vale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg tel / ffôn: [phone redacted] e-mail / e-bost :  [email redacted]  or  [email redacted]   Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.   Visit our Website at   www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk Ewch i'n gwefan yn   www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk   Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook Follow us on Twitter /Dilynwch ni ar Twitter   Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-1a1501db0a197d12","subject":"In Touch with Llandough!","name":"In Touch with Llandough!","date":"2026-10-18T17:44:42Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1501db0a197d12.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1501db0a197d12-in-touch-with-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1501db0a197d12","direction":"received","from":"Cllr George Carroll","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1501db0a197d12.json","textStatus":"available","text":"View this email in your browser (https://mailchi.mp/2c7176792734/in-touch-with-llandough-17666390?e=1429c2c1bb)\nTHIS TUESDAY: COMMUNITY DROP-IN EVENT\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDear Requester\n\nTracey and the team at the Merrie Harrier are very kindly hosting our next community drop-in event on Tuesday 20th October at 7.00pm.\n\nIt's very informal and all are welcome to attend.\n\nIf you just fancy popping along for a chat or if there's a specific issue you'd like to raise, everyone is welcome. Please do come along!\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/19em1Y36nJ/\nThis week, many residents have also reported disruption to postal services within Llandough.\n\nThank you to everyone who's shared their experiences.\n\nThis has been extremely helpful, as it has helped present a picture to Royal Mail bosses of current service provision within Llandough.\n\nI've raised these concerns with company bosses, asking them to investigate and provide details of action being taken to address existing problems.\n\nYou can read the full letter below.\nFAO: Royal Mail\n\n14th October 2026\n\n\nDear Michael\n\nROYAL MAIL DELIVERIES IN LLANDOUGH\n\nI am writing to you regarding the above.\n\nIn recent weeks, several Llandough residents have reported delays and reliability issues with postal services.\n\nIn one incident, a resident waited several weeks to receive a blood test form that she had ordered. The paperwork in question only arrived two weeks after the medical appointment for which it was required.\n\nAnother resident missed a pre-surgery appointment because the relevant notification arrived a week late, while a third person has reported a medical subscription arrived several days after its scheduled delivery date.\n\nFurthermore, another resident has not received any post since 7th September. Many others have reported that they have not received anything for several weeks, only for a large amount of mail to arrive all at once.\n\nRoyal Mail’s website advises customers that 2nd Class and other non-1st Class letters will be delivered every other weekday. Customers are told to expect 2nd Class mail to arrive within three weekdays. Reports from residents indicate these timescales are not being adhered to.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if you would investigate current provision in the Llandough, Penarth and Eastern Vale of Glamorgan areas, and take action to address existing issues regarding service reliability.\n\nThank you for your assistance with this, and I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nKind regards,\n\nCllr George Carroll\nElected Member\n\nLlandough ward\nVale of Glamorgan Council\nI'll provide a full update when I've received a response.\n\nWe get things done in Llandough because we work together.\n\nIf there's ever anything I can assist with, Requester, please let me know.\n\nThis is what Our Plan for Llandough is all about.\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPlans to build 250 houses on land just down from the Merrie Harrier\n\nIf you submitted representations during the consultation on the Vale of Glamorgan Replacement Local Development Plan, you will recently have received an invitation to register to speak at the public examination.\n\nThe deadline to do so is 30th October.\n\nThe RDLP includes a key site (below) to build 250 houses on land just down from the Merrie Harrier.\n\nThis will exacerbate existing congestion and safety issues at the Merrie Harrier junction.\n\nFurthermore, it will eat into farmland that creates a natural boundary between Llandough and Dinas Powys, threatening both villages' distinct, separate identities.\n\nI have registered to speak at the hearing, at which I will be speaking against the plans.\n\nI would urge as many residents as possible to do so too.\n\nThe hearings are likely to take place in Spring or Summer 2027.\n\nWe must work together to protect our green spaces and prevent inappropriate development.\n\nIt's a key part of Our Plan for Llandough.\n\nIf you have further questions, please let me know.\n\nOur community newsletter\n\nOur community newsletter ensures everyone in our village is kept up to date with what’s happening in Llandough.\n\nIt’s been going for several years, with a team of us working together to make it happen.\n\nIt wouldn’t be possible without the hard work of our volunteers.\n\nMaintaining good communication with residents is central to Our Plan for Llandough.\n\nWe do many things to help achieve this. Social media is an important way to share updates.\n\nAs is this weekly e-newsletter, that lands in subscribers’ inboxes every Sunday evening.\n\nWe also go door to door, asking residents if there’s anything they’d like to raise.\n\nYou may be surprised how many people we speak to who aren’t online.\n\nIt’s vital they’re kept in the loop.\n\nWe achieve this through a paper newsletter, that lands on every doormat in Llandough.\n\nOur aim is to build a delivery network that covers our whole village, while I fill in the gaps.\n\nIf you’d like to help, Requester, get in touch!\n\nhttps://fb.watch/v/90RqdWUG5/\n\nRail replacement bus service:\n25th October to 1st November\n\nThe Vale of Glamorgan Line between Cardiff, Barry and Bridgend will be CLOSED from 10.00pm on Sunday 25th October, reopening on Monday 2nd November.\n\nBuses will replace trains serving Cogan station during this time.\n\nNetwork Rail have advised the closure is to allow for works across the line, including renewing switches and crossings in Cogan.\n\nPassengers are advised to check before they travel and allow extra time.\n\nFurther information can be found on Transport for Wales' website.\nRAIL SERVICE UPDATES (https://tfw.wales/service-status/planned-improvement-works)\n\nFly-tipping\n\nI’m extremely grateful to the resident who sent me the above photographs of the latest fly-tipping incidents on Greenway Close and Llandough Hill.\n\nMore investment must go towards prevention, and surveillance equipment is key.\n\nI’ll continue to press the Council to deploy it at these and other hotspots across our village.\n\nIf you have any information as to who may have been responsible, Requester, please come forward.\n\nThose who disrespect our community in this way must face the consequences of their actions.\n\nCommunity coffee morning:\nFriday 23rd October\n\nBringing our village together is so important.\n\nIt builds a sense of community and creates good social opportunities too.\n\nLlandough Community Council work incredibly hard to do so through their monthly coffee mornings.\n\nEveryone from across our village is welcome.\n\nDetails of their next event, being held at 10.00am on Friday 23rd October at the Memorial Hall, can be found above.\n\nPavement repairs:\nSpencer Drive\n\nHuge thanks to the resident who contacted me about a defective pavement repair on Spencer Drive.\n\nThe resident helpfully sent a picture (top) showing the defects.\n\nI fed this in to the Council and asked them to rectify it.\n\nWithin 24 hours, the work was done!\n\nThis is teamwork in action … showing just what a great community we have in Llandough.\n\nYou can see the repairs below.\n\nChristmas Fayre:\nSaturday 14th November\n\nLlandough’s annual Christmas Fayre is set to take place on Saturday 14th November.\n\nWith many local businesses operating stalls, it’s a great way to make a start to your Christmas shopping and support our local economy.\n\nHuge thanks to Llandough Community Council for organising, it’s always a great event and this year promises to be no different.\n\nFurther details can be found above.\n\nBlocked drains\n\nBlocked drains pose a serious safety risk to our village, with the potential to cause floods and ice hazards.\n\nWhen I raised the leaks on Leckwith Road recently, the Council confirmed to me only has two gully tanker teams to maintain around 25,000 drains on its highway network.\n\nThe Council must invest in more capacity to ensure drain repairs can be carried out in a more timely manner.\n\nWatch my comments at the last Full Council meeting below.\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/1X6HBXKW5v/\n\nConcert for Remembrance:\nSaturday 14th November\n\nRemembrance is fast approaching, and this week I signed up to volunteer at the Penarth Poppy Caravan.\n\nOur community will hold our Remembrance Sunday service at St Dochdwy’s as we do every year, and further information will follow in due course.\n\nI also wanted to share details of a concert being held at All Saints Church in Penarth on Saturday 14th November to raise money for the Royal British Legion.\n\nThe concert is performed by the Sine Nomine Singers, and tickets are £12.\n\nOur Plan for Llandough!\n\n\nAs your councillor, I'm working with you all to secure a better future for Llandough. Together, we have a plan to deliver for the village.\n\nOur plan is making Llandough better by:\n\n1. Sorting out the parking problems\n2. Stamping out dog fouling\n3. Repairing our roads\n4. Stopping littering and flytipping\n5. Delivering better sports facilities\n6. Keeping the whole community involved\n\nIf you have any suggestions of what you'd like to see in Our Plan, please get in touch!\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F2c7176792734%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666390 Share (http://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F2c7176792734%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666390)\nhttps://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=15d7d1ab41&e=1429c2c1bb Forward (https://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=15d7d1ab41&e=1429c2c1bb)\n\n============================================================\nI'm hoping to reach as many people as possible with this newsletter, so please feel free to forward it to friends and neighbours.\n\nIf this email has been forwarded to you, and you would like to sign up to my newsletter, please click ** here ([email redacted]\n.\nThis email was sent to you because your email address is on my subscribers list. If you don't want to receive any more messages from me, please click below to unsubscribe.\n\nYour consent was previously given during an online or offline interaction with me or the Conservatives. If you feel this is incorrect or would like to comment, please contact me. I do not buy email lists.\n\nPromoted by Chris Kirkham on behalf of George Carroll, both of Vale of Glamorgan Conservatives, Holton House, 50 Holton Road, Barry [postcode redacted].\n\nThis email was sent to [email redacted] ([email redacted]\nwhy did I get this? (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/about?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=15d7d1ab41)     unsubscribe from this list (***REDACTED***     update subscription preferences (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/profile?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=15d7d1ab41)\nPolitician . Unit 5 Pro Copy Business Centre . Parc Ty Glas . Cardiff, Crf [postcode redacted] . USA"},{"id":"gm-1a145570b9618f41","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-10-16T15:31:20Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a145570b9618f41.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0bbdf18c9ea3b9-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0bbdf18c9ea3b9","direction":"received","from":"HER","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a145570b9618f41.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nPlease find below our response to the schedule of records requested by yourself on the 19th September 2026:\n\n1. This information is publicly available on our website, Archwilio.\n2. This information is publicly available on our website, Archwilio.\n3/4/5. The HER is a constantly evolving record and is subject to thousands of edits every day.  A change log provides an audit trail of edits and updates to tables; it does not store snapshots of the data contained within any of the tables.  We are unable to release a copy of this information because it contains personal data that is protected under UK GDPR legislation.\n6. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n7. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n8-10. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n11. This information is publicly available on our website, Archwilio.\n12. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n13.  Information pertaining to the Vale of Glamorgan’s County Treasures can be found on their website, here: https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/living/planning_and_building_control/Planning/Heritage.aspx\n14. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n15. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n16-21. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n22. The HER does not hold a copy of this document.\n23-24. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n25-33. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n34-38. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n39. This is a direct quote from Suggett, 1988, as listed on Archwilio.\n40. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n41. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n42. GGAT02038s has only a single grid reference.\n43. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n44. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n45. Heneb: The Trust for Welsh Archaeology is the record holder for the former GGAT, following merger of the four WATs in April 2024.\n46. Heneb’s data management policy is currently under review.  The former GGAT HER paper records are kept at Heneb’s Baglan office.\n47. The HER does not hold information relating to this request.\n48. Steven Foulston, HR Manager.\n\nKind regards,\n\nThe Heneb HER Team\n\n\nTîm Cofnod yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol | Historic Environment Record Team\nGwefan / Web\n​www.heneb.org.uk\n THE TRUST FOR WELSH ARCHAEOLOGY\n YMDDIRIEDOLAETH ARCHAEOLEGOL CYMRU\n​\n​Cadeirydd / Chair: Dr Carol Bell          PSG / CEO: Richard Nicholls\n \nHeneb is a Registered Organisation with the Chartered Institute for Archaeologists \nMae Heneb yn Sefydliad Cofrestredig gyda’r Chartered Institute for Archaeologists\n​\nThe Trust is both a Limited Company (1198990) and a Registered Charity (504616)\nAny of the statements or comments made above should be regarded as personal and not necessarily those of\n​Heneb. This e-mail and any files transmitted with it are confidential and intended solely for the use of the individual or\n​entity to whom they are addressed.\n​\n​Privacy Policy - Heneb\n​\n​Registered Office: Corner House, 6 Carmarthen Street, Llandeilo, Carmarthenshire, [postcode redacted]\n​Swyddfa Gofrestredig : Ty Cornel, 6 Stryd Caerfyrddin, Llandeilo, Sir Gaerfyrddin, [postcode redacted]\n\n​Cwmni Cyfyngedig (1198990) ynghyd ag Elusen Gofrestredig (504616) yw’r Ymddiriedolaeth\n​Dylai'r datganiadau neu'r sylwadau uchod gael eu trin fel rhai personol ac nid o reidrwydd fel datganiadau neu\n​​sylwadau gan Heneb. Mae'r e-bost hwn ac unrhyw ffeiliau a drosglwyddir gydag ef yn gyfrinachol ac at ddefnydd\nyr unigolyn neu'r corff y cyfeiriwyd hwy atynt yn unig.\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 19 September 2026 23:55\nTo: Barbara Rees <[email redacted]>\nCc: HER <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\nDear Calli,\n\nFurther to my email of 8 September 2026 concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, I attach a formal schedule of the records I am seeking, so that the request is easier for Heneb to work through and to allocate internally. I have also completed your online enquiry form, so the request is in your preferred channel.\n\nI appreciate a response would not fall due until 6 October, so this is not a chaser. It is to put the detail in one place and to clarify the basis of the request.\n\nOn your note of 22 May. You are right that Heneb, as a limited company, is not a public authority under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, and I do not pursue that. Two separate points remain, and I would welcome Heneb's position on each.\n\nFirst, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 apply on a different test — regulation 2(2) reaches bodies carrying out functions of public administration relating to the environment, or under the control of a public authority. If Heneb considers it falls outside that, please say so expressly with brief reasons, so that I can direct the request elsewhere.\n\nSecond, and independently, the Historic Environment Record is a statutory record: sections 194 and 195 of the Historic Environment (Wales) Act 2023 require the Welsh Ministers to maintain an HER for every local authority area and to make it available for public inspection, and Heneb keeps the south-east Wales record on their behalf. I therefore ask in the alternative that this be treated as a request for access under that regime and under Heneb's own policy.\n\nTwo things that will make this easier. If any item is too broad, please tell me which and I will narrow it rather than have the whole request refused. And if Heneb can supply, as a first step, simply a schedule or index of the records it holds for this site — without copying them — that would let me target the rest precisely and save your staff considerable time. I am content to inspect material by appointment at Baglan or at the HER, and any reasonable copying or staff-time charge can be notified to me in advance for approval.\n\nTwo small administrative points. Please confirm which legal entity now holds the records and functions formerly of Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust Ltd, and who within Heneb handles access requests of this kind.\n\nFinally, since my correspondence in May was framed more formally: my purpose is documentary. I am reconstructing the record of a farm my family occupied for generations, and I would far rather do that with Heneb's help than around it.\n\nI should say plainly that I have read GGAT's December 1993 notification to the Vale of Glamorgan that Condition 18 had not been complied with, and the recommendation that a Breach of Condition Notice be issued. Whatever else is in dispute about this site, that was the Trust doing its job properly, and I am grateful for it.\n\nThank you in advance for your time in this matter,\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\nEnc: Schedule of Records Requested, ref GHF/HENEB/2026-09-20"},{"id":"gm-1a144e8abd7a5cfa","subject":"Re: Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-16T13:31:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a144e8abd7a5cfa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a144e8abd7a5cfa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan, Thank you for your email confirming that the Council meeting on 22 October 2026 will now be held remotely only. I object to the removal of the opportunity for residents to attend in person and ask that the decision be reconsidered before the meeting. I recognise that the Local Government and Elections (Wales) Act 2021 provides for remote meetings. My concern is not with councillors using Zoom, but with the Council deciding that there will be no physical public attendance, without explaining the reasons for that decision or how the interests of local democratic participation have been considered. The Welsh Government's statutory guidance for community and town councils recognises the importance of accessible meetings, public participation and transparency. It also requires councils to have regard to the guidance when exercising their relevant functions. The Act's section 48, inserting paragraph 27A into Schedule 12 of the Local Government Act 1972, requires the person presiding over an open community council meeting to give members of the public in attendance a reasonable opportunity to make representations about the business, subject to the statutory exception. I therefore ask the Council to: 1. Reconsider whether a physical venue can be made available to residents, even if all councillors participate remotely. 2. Confirm who made the decision to change the meeting to remote-only and when it was made. 3. Identify the Council's published arrangements or policy governing multi-location meetings and provide the relevant link or document. 4. Explain what consideration was given to residents' ability to observe proceedings and participate effectively, and why a physical public gallery was not provided. 5. Confirm that I will be given a reasonable opportunity to make representations during the public participation item through the Zoom meeting, in accordance with the applicable rules. If the Council maintains its decision, please treat this email as a request for the reasons and the relevant policy or resolution to be recorded in the public record. For clarity, my outstanding FOI internal review and my requests concerning the retention of historic planning records are separate matters. I do not ask the Council to determine either matter through this objection. I remain willing to participate constructively in the meeting. I ask only that the Council take the concerns about public access seriously and explain its decision. Yours sincerely, Requester   On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 06:53 AM, Paul Egan <[email redacted]> wrote: \n Dear Requester, \n Thank you for your email. \n Can you please note that the Council meeting on 22 October will now be held remotely only and you can use the Zoom link that has already been emailed to you. \n Regards, \n --- \n Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM Clerk to Llandough Community Council, [address removed] Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted] Telephone [phone redacted] Website  www.llandough-cc.co.uk   When you contact us The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,  email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored  to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide  information and/or access our facilities and services.  Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other third party. Your information may however be published in the public domain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.   For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website  www.llandough-cc.co.uk   The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our identity' The Council will always strive to:  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making  · Be accountable in all our council activities · Be responsive to the needs of the community · Encourage community participation \n \n \n On 2026-10-16 09:45, Requester wrote: \n \n \n Dear Mr Egan, Thank you for the agenda and Zoom link. Ahead of the 22 October meeting I would like to flag two items for the public record, both tied to the Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr material at  https://www.google.com/url?q= https://greathousefarmwiki. wordpress.com&source=gmail& ust=1792226701788000&sa=E . First, my FOI to the Council (treated as such in your reply of 11 October) and the internal review request of 13 October remain open. I am not asking the Council to pre-judge them at the meeting; I simply ask that the review outcome or a firm date be communicated before or at the meeting so that public participation is not conducted under a section 12 refusal that has not been reviewed. Second, I have placed preservation requests with The National Archives, HM Land Registry, the MOD, South Wales Police and others concerning 1988 records. If the Council holds any planning files, section 52/106 instruments or correspondence from 1988-1992 relating to planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES, I would be grateful for confirmation that they are being retained pending those wider enquiries. I will participate through the public participation slot only. Title and chronology index:  https://www.google.com/url?q= https://dartboard. bucklerfamily.estate&source= gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa= E Long-term archive:  https://www.google.com/url?q= https://wayback.bucklerfamily. estate&source=gmail&ust= 1792226701788000&sa=E Yours sincerely, Requester   [email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a144b5a227786ef","subject":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","name":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","date":"2026-10-16T12:35:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a144b5a227786ef.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bfd5d432cf5-allanol-external-foi-2026-024-032-036-outstanding-item-7-recorded-basis-for-treating-already-found-records-as-unrelated-","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bfd5d432cf5","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a144b5a227786ef.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester\n\nThe information requested regarding the searches undertaken was provided in our response of 5 October 2026.\n\nAs explained in that response, Collections staff reviewed records identified through references to Great House Farm, Ty Mawr Farm and Llandough, together with records returned through associated place-name searches. Records relating to the wider Llandough area, to other locations sharing the name \"Llandough\", or to other properties bearing the name \"Great House Farm\" were also reviewed.\n\nWe also confirmed that searches of the earliest accession registers encompass the former Cardiff Museum accession records, which became part of the National Museum of Wales collection without re-accessioning.  \n\nAmgueddfa Cymru does not hold a separate search log, audit schedule or other recorded document providing further detail beyond that already supplied.\n\nWe therefore have no further recorded information to provide in relation to this matter.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n\nFOI Team\n\n\n[email redacted]\namgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 16 October 2026 09:45\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nDear Amgueddfa Cymru FOI Team,\n\nThank you for your reply of 12 October. I note that you do not hold a separate recorded basis for treating records as outside the scope of FOI 2026-024. I would be grateful if you could confirm what search terms and systems were used to reach that conclusion, and whether any predecessor records (e.g. from the former National Museum of Wales or\nGGAT) were included.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a144212a91e2ce8","subject":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-16T09:53:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a144212a91e2ce8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a144212a91e2ce8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Request