e review outcome or a firm date be communicated before or at \n> the meeting so that public participation is not conducted under a \n> section 12 refusal that has not been reviewed.\n> \n> Second, I have placed preservation requests with The National Archives, \n> HM Land Registry, the MOD, South Wales Police and others concerning \n> 1988 records. If the Council holds any planning files, section 52/106 \n> instruments or correspondence from 1988-1992 relating to planning refs \n> 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES, I would be grateful for confirmation \n> that they are being retained pending those wider enquiries.\n> \n> I will participate through the public participation slot only.\n> \n> Title and chronology index: \n> https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E \n> [2]\n> Long-term archive: \n> https://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E \n> [3]\n> \n> Yours sincerely,\n> \n> Requester\n> \n> \n> [email redacted]\n\n\nLinks:\n------\n[1] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n[2] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n[3] \nhttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n[4] http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk"},{"id":"gm-1a143eb210d4982d","subject":"Supplement and plain-language clarification to my email of 13 October 2026 (03:25 UTC)","name":"Supplement and plain-language clarification to my email of 13 October 2026 (03:25 UTC)","date":"2026-10-16T08:54:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143eb210d4982d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143eb18a1da9f7-supplement-and-plain-language-clarification-to-my-email-of-13-october-2026-03-25-utc","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143eb18a1da9f7","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143eb210d4982d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan, copied to Dr Misra,\n\nThis is a supplement to my email of 13 October 2026 (03:25 UTC, \"Apologies Gentlemen - Disregard Last Email Por Favor\"). I come from a military background, and parts of that email used the language of that world. So that nothing is misread, I restate the relevant points in plain administrative terms. All of the formal requests in that email stand as sent.\n\n1. My position. I act for my family, who are Welsh nationals and have been on this land for generations. We assert our claim to Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), in particular what the family calls Parcel A, and we ask every body that holds a record or made a decision about it to respect that claim by answering for its records, decisions and representations. We do not accept that the matter is closed, and we will not stop asking.\n\n2. \"Hostage\", \"terrorist\", \"occupation\" and \"legitimacy\". I meant that my family has been unable to obtain clear answers about its land and home for some forty years, and that public bodies should evidence what they hold and have done rather than rely on their authority alone. I am not alleging terrorism by the Council or its officers.\n\n3. \"Security group\", \"close-protection officers\" and \"army\". These referred to my professional associates and my large extended family, who support my research. No one is being asked or instructed to take any action against the Council, its members or its staff, and no one will be on its premises or on the land in any capacity other than as the law allows. I make no threat of any kind. My route is lawful and administrative: information requests, internal review, complaint and referral to the Independent Complaints Reviewer, the Information Commissioner, and the courts if necessary.\n\n4. \"Decolonise\", \"ethnic cleansing\" and \"powder keg\". These express my political view about the loss of Welsh families' land and heritage and the pace of the present process. They are my opinions, not allegations of unlawful conduct by the Council, and I do not ask the Council to adopt or answer them.\n\n5. Remarks about my personal circumstances and about third parties. These were background. They are not part of any request and need not be recorded or circulated.\n\nThe formal parts stand: the request for internal review of the section 12 response of 11 October 2026, the further information request, the subject access request, and the request for the date, venue and public-access arrangements for the 22 October meeting. I ask for a reasoned answer to each.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a143e3043559508","subject":"Automatic reply: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","name":"Automatic reply: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e3043559508.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143e3043559508-automatic-reply-foi-1264-26-non-personal-operational-records-concerning-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-november-decem","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143e3043559508","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["FOI1264"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e3043559508.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a143e2fb7f43d90","subject":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Re: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2fb7f43d90.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191-meeting-of-the-council-22-october-at-7-00pm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a136e2b51f9d191","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2fb7f43d90.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Egan,\n\nThank you for the agenda and Zoom link. Ahead of the 22 October meeting I would like to flag two items for the public record, both tied to the Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr material at https://www.google.com/url?q=https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E.\n\nFirst, my FOI to the Council (treated as such in your reply of 11 October) and the internal review request of 13 October remain open. I am not asking the Council to pre-judge them at the meeting; I simply ask that the review outcome or a firm date be communicated before or at the meeting so that public participation is not conducted under a section 12 refusal that has not been reviewed.\n\nSecond, I have placed preservation requests with The National Archives, HM Land Registry, the MOD, South Wales Police and others concerning 1988 records. If the Council holds any planning files, section 52/106 instruments or correspondence from 1988-1992 relating to planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES, I would be grateful for confirmation that they are being retained pending those wider enquiries.\n\nI will participate through the public participation slot only.\n\nTitle and chronology index: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\nLong-term archive: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate&source=gmail&ust=1792226701788000&sa=E\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a143e2f57fe17a4","subject":"Re: ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding (ATISN 26-0009)","name":"Re: ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding (ATISN 26-0009)","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2f57fe17a4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bf758e03cf3-atisn-27021-existing-records-behind-the-1988-listing-file-disposal-finding-atisn-26-0009","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bf758e03cf3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["1264/26","ATISN27021","CAS-347296","CAS-359317","N610CGV","Z084NQV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2f57fe17a4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Wigley,\n\nThank you for your reply of 15 October concerning ATISN 27021. I would be grateful if you could confirm:\n\n1. Whether any inventory, closure note, archive transfer form or disposal schedule still exists for the 1988 listing file, even if the file itself has been destroyed.\n2. The identity of any successor or predecessor body (including Cadw, the former Welsh Office, or South Glamorgan County Council) that may hold copies or related material.\n3. Any recorded reason for the disposal decision and the date it was made.\n\nI have also submitted related FOIs to the MOD (FOI2026/23272), The National Archives (CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9, CAS-347296-M0V4Y1), HM Land Registry (Z084NQV, N610CGV) and South Wales Police (FOI 1264/26), and I am corresponding with ITV Wales and the National Library of Wales about 1988 broadcast material. The public documentary index is at https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a143e2f2ef2f376","subject":"Re: FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2f2ef2f376.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bf813010f09-foi2026-23272-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bf813010f09","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2f2ef2f376.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Army Secretariat,\n\nThank you for logging my request under FOI2026/23272 with a target date of 9 November 2026.\n\nTo assist your search, the following identifiers may be relevant: the taking of possession of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth on or about 29 November 1988; demolition commenced on or about 6 December 1988; any military or inter-agency liaison concerning the site at that time; and any records relating to William Beverly Buckler or Mary Doreen Williams in connection with the land.\n\nI would also ask that any potentially relevant material be preserved pending the outcome of the request, in line with the preservation notices already issued to other bodies.\n\nThe public index is at https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com, with the chronology index at https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a143e2e7325eb79","subject":"Re: ATISN 26-0010 - Acknowledgement (Retention & disposal schedules)","name":"Re: ATISN 26-0010 - Acknowledgement (Retention & disposal schedules)","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2e7325eb79.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bfc1a6b3c2e-atisn-26-0010-acknowledgement-retention-disposal-schedules","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bfc1a6b3c2e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2e7325eb79.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Natalie / FMCO FOI Team,\n\nThank you for the acknowledgement of ATISN 26-0010 concerning retention and disposal schedules. I would be grateful for the substantive response as soon as possible, particularly in relation to any schedules covering records of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, 1988–1996.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a143e2e53836634","subject":"Re: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","name":"Re: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2e53836634.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bfcb03318bc-foi-1264-26-non-personal-operational-records-concerning-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-november-december-1988","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bfcb03318bc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["FOI1264"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2e53836634.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Byrne,\n\nThank you for your emails of 12 and 13 October 2026. I note the deadline of 9 November 2026.\n\nFor completeness, I confirm that William Beverly Buckler died at Llandough Hospital on 15 May 1992, and that information relating to a deceased person is not exempt on data-protection grounds in the same way as information about a living individual. I would be grateful if the scope of FOI 1264/26 could be read accordingly.\n\nPlease also preserve any potentially relevant material, including liaison records with other agencies concerning the 1988 possession and demolition.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a143e2e17c95ddb","subject":"Re: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","name":"Re: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","date":"2026-10-16T08:45:04Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143e2e17c95ddb.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a143bfd5d432cf5-allanol-external-foi-2026-024-032-036-outstanding-item-7-recorded-basis-for-treating-already-found-records-as-unrelated-","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a143bfd5d432cf5","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":["FOI 2026-024"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143e2e17c95ddb.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Amgueddfa Cymru FOI Team,\n\nThank you for your reply of 12 October. I note that you do not hold a separate recorded basis for treating records as outside the scope of FOI 2026-024. I would be grateful if you could confirm what search terms and systems were used to reach that conclusion, and whether any predecessor records (e.g. from the former National Museum of Wales or GGAT) were included.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a143cd83e23f32d","subject":"Re: You can search ITV Wales database on National Library of Wales website","name":"Re: You can search ITV Wales database on National Library of Wales website","date":"2026-10-16T08:21:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143cd83e23f32d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13a27945463893-you-can-search-itv-wales-database-on-national-library-of-wales-website","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13a27945463893","direction":"received","from":"Owain Meredith","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143cd83e23f32d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks for your message Requester\n\nPlease direct any further query to Nia ( enclosed)\n\nJust to note that my name is Owain not Owen\n\nThanks again\n\n\n\nOwain Meredith\n\nArchifydd ITV Cymru\nArchivist ITV Wales\n\n[phone redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n\n\n\nAr Gwen, 16 Hyd 2026 am 05:48 Requester  \nysgrifennodd:\n\n> Dear Owen and Nia,\n>\n> Thank you, Owen, for speaking with me. I have now examined the catalogue\n> information for another item held by the National Library of Wales, and it\n> helps clarify why I need to distinguish the different recordings,\n> broadcasts and later publications.\n>\n> I want to establish what happened to the reporting, what actually aired,\n> what survives, and when the material was disclosed or made publicly\n> accessible. I am raising concerns and asking questions, not asserting that\n> deliberate censorship or a special non-disclosure agreement has been proved.\n>\n> *The omissions and editorial questions*\n>\n> My principal concern is that the coverage I have seen does not convey the\n> full human circumstances of the events. In particular, three infant\n> children and the fact that my mother was pregnant at the time appear to\n> have been omitted.\n>\n> I am also concerned about the apparently abrupt edit following the\n> reference to the property as prime development land overlooking Cardiff\n> Bay. I would like to establish whether that cut appeared in the original\n> broadcast or was introduced when a later viewing copy was edited.\n>\n> There is a further personal dimension involving Nicola Heywood-Thomas, the\n> presenter identified in the material. For a period, she was like a second\n> mother to me. That connection is important to my understanding of the\n> story, although I recognise that the existence of a personal relationship\n> does not, in itself, establish what the broadcaster knew or was required to\n> include. I would like to know whether footage involving her was broadcast,\n> whether other versions survive, and whether any relevant editorial or\n> confidentiality record exists.\n>\n> *The chronology I need to reconcile*\n>\n> The following are separate events and records, and I would be grateful for\n> your help establishing their precise relationship.\n>\n>    -\n>\n>    *30 November 1988 — eviction and injunction coverage.* The National\n>    Library of Wales Watch and Listen catalogue has an item entitled *Eviction\n>    News Material, 30 November 1988*:\n>    https://gwylio-gwrando.llyfrgell.cymru/detail/507738. Its catalogue\n>    dates recording and broadcast to 30 November. It describes a one-minute HTV\n>    Wales Betacam item involving Miles Fletcher, bailiffs removing furniture,\n>    removal vans and [member of the public] leaving the farm. The abstract refers to a\n>    High Court injunction preventing demolition.\n>\n>    Crucially, the cataloguer says “Not viewed”. The tape contains\n>    unrelated clips, the position of this particular clip is unknown, and the\n>    description may have been taken from the broadcaster’s log. The record does\n>    not supply a catalogue-creation date or online-publication date.\n>    -\n>\n>    *5 December 1988 — separate demolition report.* I am investigating a\n>    distinct *Wales at Six* demolition headline/report and the associated\n>    off-transmission recording. I do not want the 30 November eviction and\n>    injunction item mistaken for the 5 December demolition coverage. I would\n>    like to establish whether the latter report aired, whether the surviving\n>    material represents the complete broadcast, and whether scripts, running\n>    orders, transmission logs or rushes survive.\n>    -\n>\n>    *6 December 1988 — demolition.* This is the recorded date of the\n>    farmhouse demolition in the heritage record. The event date should be kept\n>    separate from filming, broadcast and archival dates.\n>    -\n>\n>    *25 July 2025 — National Library of Wales YouTube publication.* The\n>    viewing copy I have identified as 4GXmR7mAas0 is associated with this\n>    publication date. The relevant link is https://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0. I\n>    understand the online publication was by the National Library of Wales, not\n>    an ITV upload. I would like the uploader and publication metadata retained\n>    and checked, and the exact relationship between this copy and the catalogue\n>    item above established.\n>    -\n>\n>    *Archive donation and digitisation.* The National Library of Wales\n>    holds ITV Wales/HTV material following the archive donation announced in\n>    2012. I would like to know whether the specific recordings under discussion\n>    were included in that transfer, and whether their individual accession,\n>    digitisation and catalogue histories are available.\n>    -\n>\n>    *My disclosure requests and subsequent contacts.* I would like the\n>    requests, responses, referrals and any internal handling records reconciled\n>    against these individual items. A later public upload does not, by itself,\n>    answer whether the footage was previously disclosed to me or when the\n>    Library’s catalogue entry became accessible online.\n>\n> I also note that Owen’s reported reference to a December 2025 YouTube\n> publication does not match the 25 July 2025 date associated with the\n> viewing copy identified above. These dates should not be assigned to the\n> same item until we establish precisely which video was meant.\n>\n> *What I would appreciate from ITV Wales*\n>\n> Please help establish:\n>\n>    1. The transmission date, programme, duration and running order for\n>    the 1988 eviction/injunction report and the separate 5 December demolition\n>    report.\n>    2. Whether ITV holds the complete broadcasts, off-transmission\n>    masters, scripts, rushes, outtakes, edit histories or other versions.\n>    3. Whether the abrupt cut around the property’s development value was\n>    present in the original broadcast or belongs to a later edit.\n>    4. Whether relevant footage involving Nicola Heywood-Thomas aired, and\n>    whether any alternative version survives.\n>    5. Whether any relevant editorial instruction, contractual restriction\n>    or case-specific non-disclosure agreement exists. I am asking whether such\n>    a record exists, not asserting that one does.\n>    6. What ITV records show about receiving, routing and handling my\n>    disclosure requests.\n>    7. Whether ITV can identify the specific items transferred to the\n>    National Library of Wales and provide any available provenance or accession\n>    information.\n>\n> I would also welcome guidance on the best way to coordinate these\n> enquiries with Beryl Evans and the National Library of Wales Enquiries\n> team, particularly concerning the creation and first online publication of\n> catalogue record 507738 and the search for separate 5 December material.\n>\n> The Library’s stated restrictions on viewing original media and reusing\n> footage may be entirely routine. They do not, by themselves, establish\n> concealment or unusual treatment. Equally, the existence of a public\n> catalogue entry does not settle the questions about broadcast completeness,\n> the history of my disclosure requests or the publication dates of\n> individual items.\n>\n> I am seeking a reliable chronology and an accurate account of the\n> surviving evidence. If any part of my understanding is mistaken, I would\n> welcome a clear correction supported by the relevant record. If a record\n> cannot be found or no longer survives, please distinguish that from a\n> question that has not yet been searched.\n>\n> Thank you for your help. Please let me know who will coordinate the\n> enquiries and which records ITV can realistically investigate.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Requester\n> \n> \n>\n>  https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n>\n>  https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and\n> https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\n> https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n>\n> On Wed, 14 Oct 2026, 12:23 Owain Meredith,   wrote:\n>\n>>\n>> https://www.library.wales/\n>>\n>> Choose Catalogue\n>> in serch box dropdown choose alln categories\n>> Tweak my results choose author ITV\n>>\n>> This shiws you everything in ITV Collection - This information has been\n>> in the public domains since 2012\n>>\n>> Owain Meredith\n>>\n>> Archifydd ITV Cymru\n>> Archivist ITV Wales\n>>\n>> [phone redacted]\n>> [phone redacted]\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> ITV plc (Registration No. 4967001) (ITV) is incorporated in England and\n>> Wales with its registered office at ITV White City, 201 Wood Lane,\n>> London [postcode redacted]\n>>  .\n>> Please visit www.itv.com for further information.\n>>\n>> This email and any attachments are intended solely for the addressee and\n>> may contain confidential, copyrighted and/or privileged information.  If\n>> you have received this message in error, please notify us and delete it.\n>> Recipients should scan the email and any attachments for their own\n>> protection.\n>>\n>> This email does not conclude a binding agreement. If there is commercial\n>> information in this email it remains subject to contract and management\n>> approval. The views or opinions presented in this email do not necessarily\n>> represent those of ITV.\n>>\n>> We reserve the right to monitor all e-mail communications, as permitted\n>> by applicable law and regulations.\n>>\n>> For details of how we process personal data, please see the privacy\n>> notices for each of ITV's business areas at http://www.itv.com/\n>> groupprivacy\n>>\n>>\n>>\n\n-- \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nITV plc (Registration No. 4967001) (ITV) is incorporated in England \nand Wales with its registered office at ITV White City, 201 Wood Lane, \nLondon [postcode redacted]. Please visit www.itv.com   for further \ninformation.\n\nThis email and any attachments are intended solely for the \naddressee and may contain confidential, copyrighted and/or privileged \ninformation.  If you have received this message in error, please notify us \nand delete it.  Recipients should scan the email and any attachments for \ntheir own protection. \n\nThis email does not conclude a binding agreement. \nIf there is commercial information in this email it remains subject to \ncontract and management approval. The views or opinions presented in this \nemail do not necessarily represent those of ITV.\n\nWe reserve the right to \nmonitor all e-mail communications, as permitted by applicable law and \nregulations.\n\nFor details of how we process personal data, please see the \nprivacy notices for each of ITV's business areas at \nhttp://www.itv.com/groupprivacy"},{"id":"gm-1a143b522328160a","subject":"Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","name":"Document preservation notice — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-16T07:55:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143b522328160a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4-document-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1984-1988","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1439902c7e1dc4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143b522328160a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Norman,\n\nI write as Requester, a party with a direct interest in the events concerning Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, South Wales. The public working evidence catalogue is at https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com, with the title and chronology index at https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and the long-term archive at https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate.\n\nBP Properties Ltd obtained possession of the site on 29 November 1988; outbuildings were demolished on 30 November 1988 and the farmhouse on 5–6 December 1988. Before any litigation or formal proceedings are considered, I am exhausting every non-litigious avenue. As part of that, I am placing preservation notices with every organisation that may hold relevant records or artefacts.\n\nPlease treat this as notice that BP p.l.c., BP Properties Ltd, the BP Pension Trust and any successor entities should preserve, and not destroy, delete, overwrite or dispose of, any records, correspondence, title deeds, litigation files, photographs, plans, survey reports, demolition records, or other material relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, for the period 1969 to present. This includes material held by BP Legal, external solicitors instructed in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, and any archived or off-site storage.\n\nI would be grateful for written confirmation that a preservation hold has been placed, and for the identity of any external firm of solicitors that acted for BP in that litigation so that I may write to them directly.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a143acd92ae8fc5","subject":"Enquiry — barrister or chambers involvement in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Great House Farm, Llandough, 1984–1988)","name":"Enquiry — barrister or chambers involvement in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (Great House Farm, Llandough, 1984–1988)","date":"2026-10-16T07:46:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143acd92ae8fc5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1439f0c75c3ab1-enquiry-barrister-or-chambers-involvement-in-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough-1984-1988","scopeTopics":["legal-regulators"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["legal-regulators"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1439f0c75c3ab1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"legal-regulators","name":"Legal regulators"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143acd92ae8fc5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am researching the BP Properties Ltd v Buckler litigation. The public working evidence catalogue is at https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com and the chronology index at https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate. I would be grateful for any guidance on tracing barristers or chambers that may have acted in that matter, and for preservation of any relevant records.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr research\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nhttps://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate\nhttps://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate"},{"id":"gm-1a143ac62b958bb0","subject":"Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993)","name":"Enquiry and preservation notice — surveyors and valuation records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (1969–1993)","date":"2026-10-16T07:45:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a143ac62b958bb0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1439902e39b2d0-enquiry-and-preservation-notice-surveyors-and-valuation-records-for-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-1969","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1439902e39b2d0","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a143ac62b958bb0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear RICS,\n\nI am researching Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, South Wales. The public working evidence catalogue is at https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com, with the title and chronology index at https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and the long-term archive at https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate.\n\nThe site passed through Western Ground Rents Limited (1938), the BP Pension Trust / BP Properties Ltd (1969), and was subject to possession proceedings culminating in demolition in November–December 1988. Valuation Office field books, National Farm Survey / CWAEC records and other survey material are already the subject of enquiries with The National Archives.\n\nPlease advise whether RICS holds any central or member records, practice archives, or guidance relating to surveyors or valuers who may have worked on this site between 1969 and 1993, and whether any preservation notice is appropriate for member files.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a14386a609c7540","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-16T07:04:17Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a14386a609c7540.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a","direction":"received","from":"possessions.cardiff.countycourt","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a14386a609c7540.json","textStatus":"available","text":"OFFICIAL\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your email dated 28 September 2026 at 22:40\n\nDo you have any Claim Number relating to the below?\n\nRegards\n\n\nNeil Jones\n\nAdran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\nHMCTS/GLlTEM Canolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd / Cardiff Civil Justice Centre\n2 Stryd y Parc / 2 Park Street\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\nDX: 99500 CARDIFF 6\n\nFfon / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\nHere is how HMCTS uses personal data about you  | Dyma sut mae GLlTEM yn defnyddio data personol amdanoch chi \n\n\n\n“I am not authorised to bind the Ministry of Justice contractually, nor to make representations or other statements which may bind the Ministry of Justice in any way via electronic means”\n\n\nYSTYRIWCH YR AMGYLCHEDD - OES RHAID I CHI BRINTIO'R E-BOST HWN?\nPLEASE CONSIDER THE ENVIRONMENT - DO YOU REALLY NEED TO PRINT THIS E-MAIL?\n\n\n‘For information on how HMCTS uses personal data about you please see:\nAm wybodaeth ynghylch sut mae GLlTEF yn defnyddio data personol amdanoch chi, ewch i: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter \n\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD5D44.F0846270][cid:image002.png@01DD5D44.F0846270]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOFFICIAL\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 28 September 2026 22:40\nTo: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; BP Archive  ; FOI Requests  ; Cardiff County, Enquiries  ; [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Connor McGilly  ; MRC_Archive, Resource  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; possessions.cardiff.countycourt  ; BPC.Cardiff  ; Administrative Court Office Cardiff  ; Disclosure Team  ; NSUKilo  ; Paul Egan  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Julian Wilkes  ; [email redacted]; _FOI email address  ; [email redacted]; Customer Support  ; Davidson, Victoria  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Contact OneVale  ; [email redacted]; DOUGHTY, Stephen  ; CAIRNS Alun  ; [email redacted]; Pwyllgor Diwylliant, Cyfathrebu, y Gymraeg a Chwaraeon - Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest\n\n\nFORMAL PRESERVATION NOTICE\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nTitles: WA231076, WA240304, WA513690 and WA735527\nPlanning references: 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES\n\nURL: greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com \n\nTo each recipient separately, in your own capacity as a current or potential holder, custodian or controller of relevant records:\n\nThis notice is addressed to each recipient individually. It is not a joint request, and it does not ask any recipient to speak for, investigate on behalf of, or answer in place of any other person or organisation. Each recipient is asked to respond only in respect of records within that recipient's own possession, custody or control, including records inherited from a predecessor organisation or retained on its behalf.\n\n1. Nature and purpose of this notice\n\nThis is a formal preservation notice concerning documentary material relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's, and the subsequent development of the site, including the area now associated with Church View Close.\n\nIt is not a claim form, is not service of proceedings, and is not intended to constitute or replace any FOI request, internal review, complaint, subject-access request or other statutory process already made to any recipient.\n\nThe purpose of this notice is to require the preservation of potentially relevant material while the documentary history, title chain, registration history, planning history, possession proceedings, demolition and subsequent development are being reconstructed.\n\nA separate first-stage preservation notice has been issued or is being issued to Cadw / Welsh Government FOI, HM Land Registry Wales Office and DPO, Heneb / GGAT HER, RCAHMW, Vale of Glamorgan FOI Unit and DPO, Glamorgan Archives, South Wales Police FOI, The National Archives, the Wales Office FOI team, and the National Library of Wales. Persimmon Homes (Wales) Ltd has received a separate preservation letter.\n\nYou are receiving this notice separately because the published documentary record places you, or a predecessor whose records may remain in your custody or control, within the documentary, legal, professional, administrative or development chain concerning this land.\n\n2. Land and documentary scope\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, alter, overwrite, discard, transfer out of custody without a recorded handover, or otherwise dispose of, any record within your possession, custody or control relating to the land or matters identified below.\n\nThe scope includes, without limitation, originals, copies, working papers, drafts, annotations, plans, photographs, negatives, films, tapes, maps, registers, indexes, correspondence, emails and attachments, electronic files, archived mailboxes, databases, metadata, internal notes, meeting records, instructions, client or matter files, survey material and other associated records.\n\nThe material requested includes:\n\n1. Historical ownership, occupation and conveyancing\n\nThe 1877 split; the 1916 and 1939 tenancies; the 1938 Bute to Western Ground Rents conveyance; the 1969 Western Ground Rents to BP Pension Trust conveyance; and any plans, schedules, abstracts, searches, correspondence or other documents relied upon in relation to those transactions.\n\n2. Possession proceedings and subsequent litigation\n\nThe 1955 High Court and 1962 Cardiff County Court possession orders; the 1974 proceedings; BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2; House of Lords leave papers, including YHL/PO/JO/10/11/2536; and Buckler v United Kingdom (1989), including associated correspondence, instructions, evidence, plans and working papers.\n\n3. Land registration\n\nThe first registration of WA231076, including the application dated 30 November 1982; the first registration of WA240304, including the application dated 23 February 1983; subsequent amalgamation, transfer or closure; and every plan, conveyance, abstract, search, application, correspondence trail or professional file relied upon in connection with those registrations or changes.\n\n4. 1988 possession and demolition\n\nThe taking of possession on or about 29 November 1988 and the demolition commenced on or about 6 December 1988, including any planning, listed-building, heritage, police, enforcement, media, contractor, survey, photographic or inter-agency liaison material.\n\n5. Planning and subsequent development, 1989–1996\n\nPlanning application 89/01396/OUT; reserved matters application 92/00671/RES; conditions 16–18; GGAT / Cotswold Archaeology material; records concerning any section 52, section 106, planning obligation, local land charge or equivalent instrument; and the transfer from BP to Ideal Homes dated 3 December 1993, together with all associated plans, correspondence, approvals, agreements, searches and completion material.\n\n6. Family records\n\nRecords concerning Mary Doreen Williams (died 1983) and William Buckler, insofar as those records relate to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, the land described above, its occupation, ownership, possession, disposal, registration, development or demolition.\n\n3. Predecessor and inherited files\n\nWhere you hold, or may hold, a file originating with a predecessor, successor, merged practice, affiliated practice, client or other entity, that material is also within scope.\n\nThis includes, without limitation, records originating from:\n\nLoosemores of Cardiff; Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn / Blake Morgan; Linklaters & Paines; Debenham Tewson / DTZ / Cushman & Wakefield; Wyn Thomas + Partners; Ideal Homes Wales; BP Properties; BP Pension Trust; Cotswold Archaeological Trust; Cardiff Bay Development Corporation; and South Glamorgan County Council.\n\nThe reference to a predecessor file does not assert that you necessarily hold such a file. It identifies material for which a reasonable custody or succession inquiry should be made where applicable.\n\n4. Preservation steps\n\nPlease take reasonable steps to prevent the routine destruction, deletion, alteration or overwriting of potentially relevant material, including material held in archived mailboxes, legacy systems, off-site storage, document-management systems, backup repositories and other electronic or physical stores.\n\nWhere relevant material has been transferred to another repository, archive, successor organisation or third party, please preserve the information necessary to identify the transfer and its current location, including any accession, file, box, reference or custody details.\n\nNothing in this notice requires the creation of records that do not exist. The request concerns the preservation of records already held or controlled by you.\n\n5. Purpose and legal position\n\nThis notice is not a finding against any recipient, and I am not asking any recipient to determine title or adjudicate the underlying dispute.\n\nThe 1987 Court of Appeal judgment is relied upon here only for matters actually determined by that judgment, including the issues concerning possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. This preservation notice does not treat that judgment as having determined the complete documentary root of title to the farmhouse parcel.\n\nThe underlying documentary history, including the relationship between the farmhouse parcel and the agricultural land subsequently dealt with through Western Ground Rents and BP, remains a matter requiring reconstruction from the primary records.\n\nAccordingly, preservation is requested precisely so that the documentary record can be established from the records themselves rather than through assumptions based on later registration, later occupation, later planning treatment or secondary descriptions.\n\n6. Acknowledgement and identification of records\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt of this notice and, in your own capacity, confirm:\n\n(a) the officer, partner, records manager or other person responsible for implementing the preservation hold;\n\n(b) what records within your possession, custody or control you have identified as falling within the scope above; and\n\n(c) where you identify no records within scope, what relevant systems, files, repositories or predecessor records you searched in reaching that conclusion.\n\nA substantive assessment of title is not requested from you. The immediate requirement is preservation and identification of the documentary material you hold.\n\nThe public documentary index and developing evidence record is available at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nPlease monitor that site for subsequent identification of documents, references and specific schedules relevant to your organisation's records.\n\nWhere a reliable public email address is unavailable, a postal preservation notice will also be sent. For example, a postal notice will follow to Loosemores, Alliance House, 18–19 High Street, Cardiff [postcode redacted].\n\nNothing in this notice constitutes an abandonment, waiver or limitation of any claim, position or remedy concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening, rectification or alteration of the register, or any associated matter.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a1430a4a93a8002","subject":"Re: You can search ITV Wales database on National Library of Wales website","name":"Re: You can search ITV Wales database on National Library of Wales website","date":"2026-10-16T04:06:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1430a4a93a8002.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13a27945463893-you-can-search-itv-wales-database-on-national-library-of-wales-website","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13a27945463893","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1430a4a93a8002.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Owen and Nia,\n\nThank you, Owen, for speaking with me. I have now examined the catalogue\ninformation for another item held by the National Library of Wales, and it\nhelps clarify why I need to distinguish the different recordings,\nbroadcasts and later publications.\n\nI want to establish what happened to the reporting, what actually aired,\nwhat survives, and when the material was disclosed or made publicly\naccessible. I am raising concerns and asking questions, not asserting that\ndeliberate censorship or a special non-disclosure agreement has been proved.\n\n*The omissions and editorial questions*\n\nMy principal concern is that the coverage I have seen does not convey the\nfull human circumstances of the events. In particular, three infant\nchildren and the fact that my mother was pregnant at the time appear to\nhave been omitted.\n\nI am also concerned about the apparently abrupt edit following the\nreference to the property as prime development land overlooking Cardiff\nBay. I would like to establish whether that cut appeared in the original\nbroadcast or was introduced when a later viewing copy was edited.\n\nThere is a further personal dimension involving Nicola Heywood-Thomas, the\npresenter identified in the material. For a period, she was like a second\nmother to me. That connection is important to my understanding of the\nstory, although I recognise that the existence of a personal relationship\ndoes not, in itself, establish what the broadcaster knew or was required to\ninclude. I would like to know whether footage involving her was broadcast,\nwhether other versions survive, and whether any relevant editorial or\nconfidentiality record exists.\n\n*The chronology I need to reconcile*\n\nThe following are separate events and records, and I would be grateful for\nyour help establishing their precise relationship.\n\n   -\n\n   *30 November 1988 — eviction and injunction coverage.* The National\n   Library of Wales Watch and Listen catalogue has an item entitled *Eviction\n   News Material, 30 November 1988*:\n   https://gwylio-gwrando.llyfrgell.cymru/detail/507738. Its catalogue\n   dates recording and broadcast to 30 November. It describes a one-minute HTV\n   Wales Betacam item involving Miles Fletcher, bailiffs removing furniture,\n   removal vans and [member of the public] leaving the farm. The abstract refers to a\n   High Court injunction preventing demolition.\n\n   Crucially, the cataloguer says “Not viewed”. The tape contains unrelated\n   clips, the position of this particular clip is unknown, and the description\n   may have been taken from the broadcaster’s log. The record does not supply\n   a catalogue-creation date or online-publication date.\n   -\n\n   *5 December 1988 — separate demolition report.* I am investigating a\n   distinct *Wales at Six* demolition headline/report and the associated\n   off-transmission recording. I do not want the 30 November eviction and\n   injunction item mistaken for the 5 December demolition coverage. I would\n   like to establish whether the latter report aired, whether the surviving\n   material represents the complete broadcast, and whether scripts, running\n   orders, transmission logs or rushes survive.\n   -\n\n   *6 December 1988 — demolition.* This is the recorded date of the\n   farmhouse demolition in the heritage record. The event date should be kept\n   separate from filming, broadcast and archival dates.\n   -\n\n   *25 July 2025 — National Library of Wales YouTube publication.* The\n   viewing copy I have identified as 4GXmR7mAas0 is associated with this\n   publication date. The relevant link is https://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0. I\n   understand the online publication was by the National Library of Wales, not\n   an ITV upload. I would like the uploader and publication metadata retained\n   and checked, and the exact relationship between this copy and the catalogue\n   item above established.\n   -\n\n   *Archive donation and digitisation.* The National Library of Wales holds\n   ITV Wales/HTV material following the archive donation announced in 2012. I\n   would like to know whether the specific recordings under discussion were\n   included in that transfer, and whether their individual accession,\n   digitisation and catalogue histories are available.\n   -\n\n   *My disclosure requests and subsequent contacts.* I would like the\n   requests, responses, referrals and any internal handling records reconciled\n   against these individual items. A later public upload does not, by itself,\n   answer whether the footage was previously disclosed to me or when the\n   Library’s catalogue entry became accessible online.\n\nI also note that Owen’s reported reference to a December 2025 YouTube\npublication does not match the 25 July 2025 date associated with the\nviewing copy identified above. These dates should not be assigned to the\nsame item until we establish precisely which video was meant.\n\n*What I would appreciate from ITV Wales*\n\nPlease help establish:\n\n   1. The transmission date, programme, duration and running order for the\n   1988 eviction/injunction report and the separate 5 December demolition\n   report.\n   2. Whether ITV holds the complete broadcasts, off-transmission masters,\n   scripts, rushes, outtakes, edit histories or other versions.\n   3. Whether the abrupt cut around the property’s development value was\n   present in the original broadcast or belongs to a later edit.\n   4. Whether relevant footage involving Nicola Heywood-Thomas aired, and\n   whether any alternative version survives.\n   5. Whether any relevant editorial instruction, contractual restriction\n   or case-specific non-disclosure agreement exists. I am asking whether such\n   a record exists, not asserting that one does.\n   6. What ITV records show about receiving, routing and handling my\n   disclosure requests.\n   7. Whether ITV can identify the specific items transferred to the\n   National Library of Wales and provide any available provenance or accession\n   information.\n\nI would also welcome guidance on the best way to coordinate these enquiries\nwith Beryl Evans and the National Library of Wales Enquiries team,\nparticularly concerning the creation and first online publication of\ncatalogue record 507738 and the search for separate 5 December material.\n\nThe Library’s stated restrictions on viewing original media and reusing\nfootage may be entirely routine. They do not, by themselves, establish\nconcealment or unusual treatment. Equally, the existence of a public\ncatalogue entry does not settle the questions about broadcast completeness,\nthe history of my disclosure requests or the publication dates of\nindividual items.\n\nI am seeking a reliable chronology and an accurate account of the surviving\nevidence. If any part of my understanding is mistaken, I would welcome a\nclear correction supported by the relevant record. If a record cannot be\nfound or no longer survives, please distinguish that from a question that\nhas not yet been searched.\n\nThank you for your help. Please let me know who will coordinate the\nenquiries and which records ITV can realistically investigate.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n\n\n https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n\n https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nhttps://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nOn Wed, 14 Oct 2026, 12:23 Owain Meredith, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n>\n> https://www.library.wales/\n>\n> Choose Catalogue\n> in serch box dropdown choose alln categories\n> Tweak my results choose author ITV\n>\n> This shiws you everything in ITV Collection - This information has been in\n> the public domains since 2012\n>\n> Owain Meredith\n>\n> Archifydd ITV Cymru\n> Archivist ITV Wales\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n> [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> ITV plc (Registration No. 4967001) (ITV) is incorporated in England and\n> Wales with its registered office at ITV White City, 201 Wood Lane, London\n> [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted].\n> Please visit www.itv.com for further information.\n>\n> This email and any attachments are intended solely for the addressee and\n> may contain confidential, copyrighted and/or privileged information.  If\n> you have received this message in error, please notify us and delete it.\n> Recipients should scan the email and any attachments for their own\n> protection.\n>\n> This email does not conclude a binding agreement. If there is commercial\n> information in this email it remains subject to contract and management\n> approval. The views or opinions presented in this email do not necessarily\n> represent those of ITV.\n>\n> We reserve the right to monitor all e-mail communications, as permitted by\n> applicable law and regulations.\n>\n> For details of how we process personal data, please see the privacy\n> notices for each of ITV's business areas at http://www.itv.com/groupprivac\n> y\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a141ffbc39607dd","subject":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","name":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","date":"2026-10-15T23:57:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141ffbc39607dd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141ffbc39607dd-your-submission-to-libanswers-was-received","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141ffbc39607dd","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141ffbc39607dd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester,\n\nYour question was submitted successfully to the National Library of Wales enquiries service / Cyflwynwyd eich cwestiwn yn llwyddiannus i Wasanaeth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru\n\nDue to high demand and some resource challenges, there may be some delay in responding to enquiries at present. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nOherwydd lefel uchel y galw a rhai heriau adnoddau, bydd oedi gydag ymateb i ymholiadau ar hyn o bryd. Yr ydym yn ymddiheuro am unrhyw anghyfleuster a achosir gan hyn ac fe fyddwn yn darparu diweddariad cyn gynted ag y medrwn.\n\nWe will contact you as soon as possible. In the meantime, perhaps you can visit our FAQs <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com>\nByddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted â phosibl! Yn y cyfamser, efallai yr hoffech chi chwlio ein  FAQs  <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com> perthnasol gall ateb eich cwestiwn.\n\n\n\nWe welcome calls and correspondence in Welsh. You will receive a response in Welsh and correspondence in Welsh will not result in a delay./ Rydym yn croesawu galwadau a gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwch yn derbyn ymateb yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 16 2026, 12:53AM via Email\nNew FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nFreedom of Information / Enquiries Service,\n\nThis is a new request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is\noutside the scope of FOI/2026/09 and its internal review, which\nconcerned Bute series including D153 and D205 and the 1877\ntransaction. It is also separate from my enquiry of 27 September and\nfollow-up of 10 October 2026 on D153/1–8.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm\ncalled Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and\nCardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood\nbeside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge),\nand the Great Houses at nearby Llandow and Aberthin. For example,\n\"Manors of Llandough and St Mary Church\" (Penrice and Margam Estate\nRecords, 1619–1704) appears to be the Cowbridge Llandough; please\nconfirm if you know otherwise.\nPlease do not send or rely on records for the Cowbridge-area places.\nIf an entry says only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" and the parish\ncannot be told, please say so rather than assume.\n\nPart 1 — S7, Survey of the lands of William Herbert, kt, dec., in the\nlordships or manors of Dinas Powys, Cogan, Llandough and others,\nJanuary 1610.\nPlease tell me:\n(a) Whether S7 contains an entry for Great House or any holding in\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, and the folio.\n(b) The name of the holder or tenant recorded, the tenure (freehold,\ncopyhold, leasehold) and any rent or acreage given.\n(c) Whether S7 is digitised or filmed, and the cost of a copy of only\nthose folios.\n\nPart 2 — Cardiff MSS on Microfilm (CARDMFS), filmed 1980–1984.\nGlamorgan Archives (ref 2026/4097b) identified Bute X.6(12), abstracts\nof payments and receipts by the Bute trustees, 1877 (copy), at Cardiff\nLibrary.\nPlease tell me:\n(a) Whether Bute X.6(12), or any Bute X.6 item, is on the CARDMFS\nmicrofilm, and the reel and frame reference.\n(b) If so, how I can obtain a copy of the entries relating to\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth or Daniel Thomas, and the cost.\n\nPart 3 — A lease of Great House said to date from 1667.\nThe family's account (not yet supported by a document) is that the\nWilliams family took Great House, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, in 1667 on\na lease for 999 years. Great House is described in published sources\nas a freehold of the Vaughan family from the 16th to the late 18th\ncentury, after which it came to the Bute estate. Please tell me\nwhether the Bute Estate Records, including the Herbert and Windsor\nfamily papers within them, or any other NLW collection, hold:\n(a) Any lease, counterpart lease, assignment or enrolment,\nc.1660–1675, of Great House or any messuage in\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, to any person named Williams, or for a term\nof 999 years (or any other long term).\n(b) Any later deed, abstract of title, schedule or rental that recites\nor refers to a lease of Great House for 999 years or for a long term.\n(c) The conveyance or other instrument by which the Bute estate (or\nthe Windsor family before it) acquired Great House from the Vaughan\nfamily or its heirs, with its date and reference, and whether it\nrecites any lease or tenancy then outstanding.\n(d) Any Vaughan of Llandough family papers, and where they are held if\nnot at NLW.\n\nIf you consider any of this reasonably accessible by other means under\nsection 21, please say exactly where and how.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester \n\n\n------------------\n\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9890384.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a141fc6af762916","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Bute Estate records — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — ticket #9816877","name":"Re: [NLW English] Bute Estate records — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — ticket #9816877","date":"2026-10-15T23:53:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141fc6af762916.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141fc5ee03da4f-nlw-english-bute-estate-records-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-ticket-9816877","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141fc5ee03da4f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141fc6af762916.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Evans,\n\nThank you for your reply of 14 October and for the catalogue and Virtual Reading Room links. I will search the Bute catalogue myself and book a session if I find candidate items.\n\nOne point before that: my requests concern preservation as much as access. Several of the records in issue are unique 17th- and 19th-century items, and I am concerned that routine disposal, weeding or transfer could remove them before they can be examined. Please confirm that no Bute Estate Records relating to Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Great House / Tŷ Mawr, Daniel Thomas, John Williams, or the 1875–1880 transaction have been reported missing, withdrawn, transferred or disposed of, and that any relevant retention or disposal schedule will be applied with this correspondence in mind.\n\nIf you hold any recorded information on the location or physical-check status of the 1610 Herbert survey S7 or Bute X.6(12) beyond the catalogue links already supplied, please state it.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141fc481dbd2e5","subject":"New FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"New FOI request (outside FOI/2026/09) — 1610 Herbert survey S7 and Cardiff MSS microfilm of Bute X.6(12) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-15T23:53:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141fc481dbd2e5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141fc4254e01d4-new-foi-request-outside-foi-2026-09-1610-herbert-survey-s7-and-cardiff-mss-microfilm-of-bute-x-6-12-llandough-juxta-pena","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141fc4254e01d4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141fc481dbd2e5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information / Enquiries Service,\n\nThis is a new request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is outside the scope of FOI/2026/09 and its internal review, which concerned Bute series including D153 and D205 and the 1877 transaction. It is also separate from my enquiry of 27 September and follow-up of 10 October 2026 on D153/1–8.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm called Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and Cardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood beside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge), and the Great Houses at nearby Llandow and Aberthin. For example, \"Manors of Llandough and St Mary Church\" (Penrice and Margam Estate Records, 1619–1704) appears to be the Cowbridge Llandough; please confirm if you know otherwise.\nPlease do not send or rely on records for the Cowbridge-area places. If an entry says only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" and the parish cannot be told, please say so rather than assume.\n\nPart 1 — S7, Survey of the lands of William Herbert, kt, dec., in the lordships or manors of Dinas Powys, Cogan, Llandough and others, January 1610.\nPlease tell me:\n(a) Whether S7 contains an entry for Great House or any holding in Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and the folio.\n(b) The name of the holder or tenant recorded, the tenure (freehold, copyhold, leasehold) and any rent or acreage given.\n(c) Whether S7 is digitised or filmed, and the cost of a copy of only those folios.\n\nPart 2 — Cardiff MSS on Microfilm (CARDMFS), filmed 1980–1984.\nGlamorgan Archives (ref 2026/4097b) identified Bute X.6(12), abstracts of payments and receipts by the Bute trustees, 1877 (copy), at Cardiff Library.\nPlease tell me:\n(a) Whether Bute X.6(12), or any Bute X.6 item, is on the CARDMFS microfilm, and the reel and frame reference.\n(b) If so, how I can obtain a copy of the entries relating to Llandough-juxta-Penarth or Daniel Thomas, and the cost.\n\nPart 3 — A lease of Great House said to date from 1667.\nThe family's account (not yet supported by a document) is that the Williams family took Great House, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, in 1667 on a lease for 999 years. Great House is described in published sources as a freehold of the Vaughan family from the 16th to the late 18th century, after which it came to the Bute estate. Please tell me whether the Bute Estate Records, including the Herbert and Windsor family papers within them, or any other NLW collection, hold:\n(a) Any lease, counterpart lease, assignment or enrolment, c.1660–1675, of Great House or any messuage in Llandough-juxta-Penarth, to any person named Williams, or for a term of 999 years (or any other long term).\n(b) Any later deed, abstract of title, schedule or rental that recites or refers to a lease of Great House for 999 years or for a long term.\n(c) The conveyance or other instrument by which the Bute estate (or the Windsor family before it) acquired Great House from the Vaughan family or its heirs, with its date and reference, and whether it recites any lease or tenancy then outstanding.\n(d) Any Vaughan of Llandough family papers, and where they are held if not at NLW.\n\nIf you consider any of this reasonably accessible by other means under section 21, please say exactly where and how.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141fc0a480f714","subject":"FOI — location and content only — Glamorgan hearth tax rolls E 179/221/297 and E 179/221/294 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"FOI — location and content only — Glamorgan hearth tax rolls E 179/221/297 and E 179/221/294 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-15T23:53:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141fc0a480f714.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141fc044669fbd-foi-location-and-content-only-glamorgan-hearth-tax-rolls-e-179-221-297-and-e-179-221-294-llandough-juxta-penarth","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141fc044669fbd","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-347296","CAS-356384"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141fc0a480f714.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is a location and content request only. It is separate from CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 and its review CAS-356384-B2F5L9.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm called Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and Cardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood beside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge), and the Great Houses at nearby Llandow and Aberthin.\nPlease do not send or rely on records for the Cowbridge-area places. If an entry says only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" and the parish cannot be told, please say so rather than assume.\n\nRecords:\n1. E 179/221/297 — Glamorgan hearth tax assessment, c.1663–1667 (possibly 1666), roll of 105 rotulets.\n2. E 179/221/294 — Glamorgan hearth tax assessment, [1671], roll of 45 rotulets.\n\nPlease tell me:\n(a) For each roll, which rotulet or membrane covers the parish of Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Dinas Powys hundred), if this is recorded in any finding aid, schedule or index you hold.\n(b) Whether any finding aid, index or transcript you hold lists the householders named for Llandough-juxta-Penarth in either roll, and if so, those names and their hearth counts.\n(c) Whether either roll is digitised or available on microfilm, and the cost and route for ordering a copy of only that entry.\n\nIf you consider any of this reasonably accessible by other means under section 21, please say exactly where and how, so I can obtain it.\n\nI am not asking to book a reading room visit.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141cd3cb54a9b5","subject":"Location and content request — Glamorgan land tax assessments DBJ/O/90-94 (1691–1707) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth — not a viewing request","name":"Location and content request — Glamorgan land tax assessments DBJ/O/90-94 (1691–1707) — Llandough-juxta-Penarth — not a viewing request","date":"2026-10-15T23:02:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cd3cb54a9b5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cd290288f4c-location-and-content-request-glamorgan-land-tax-assessments-dbj-o-90-94-1691-1707-llandough-juxta-penarth-not-a-viewing-","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cd290288f4c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cd3cb54a9b5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Glamorgan Archives,\n\nThis is a location and content request only, under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. I am not asking to book a searchroom visit. It is separate from refs 2026/3793, 2026/4097, 2026/4097b and 2026/4274.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm called Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and Cardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood beside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge), and the Great Houses at nearby Llandow and Aberthin.\nPlease do not send or rely on records for the Cowbridge-area places. If an entry says only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" and the parish cannot be told, please say so rather than assume.\n\nPart 1 — Glamorgan land tax, DBJ/O/90-94, assessments and receipts, 1691–1707 (NRA 5219).\nPlease tell me:\n1. Which items in DBJ/O/90-94 cover the parish of Llandough-juxta-Penarth or the Dinas Powys hundred, and for which years.\n2. Whether any catalogue, index or transcript you hold names the proprietors and occupiers listed for Llandough-juxta-Penarth in those years. If so, please supply those names and sums.\n3. The cost of a staff search or copy limited to those entries only.\n\nPart 2 — A lease of Great House said to date from 1667.\nThe family's account (not yet supported by a document) is that the Williams family took Great House, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, in 1667 on a lease for 999 years. Great House is described in published sources as a freehold of the Vaughan family from the 16th to the late 18th century, after which it came to the Bute estate. Please tell me whether you hold:\n4. Any lease, counterpart lease, assignment or enrolment, c.1660–1675, of Great House or any messuage in Llandough-juxta-Penarth, to any person named Williams, or for a term of 999 years (or any other long term).\n5. Any later deed, abstract of title, schedule or rental (including in the Bute, DBDT or Western Ground Rents material) that recites or refers to a lease of Great House for 999 years or for a long term.\n6. The conveyance by which the Bute estate (or the Windsor family) acquired Great House from the Vaughan family or its heirs, or any copy, abstract or reference to it.\n7. Any Vaughan of Llandough family papers.\n\nThe aim is to establish who owned and occupied Great House from 1667 onward and on what tenure, and to test the family's 1667 date.\n\nIf you consider any of this reasonably accessible by other means under section 21, please say exactly where and how.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141cd2ab07bcb5","subject":"Automatic reply: [External] Research visit request — Bute Estate (Glamorgan) records, 1667 and 1875–1880 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"Automatic reply: [External] Research visit request — Bute Estate (Glamorgan) records, 1667 and 1875–1880 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-15T23:02:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cd2ab07bcb5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cd2ab07bcb5-automatic-reply-external-research-visit-request-bute-estate-glamorgan-records-1667-and-1875-1880-llandough-juxta-penarth","scopeTopics":["mount-stuart"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mount-stuart"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cd2ab07bcb5","direction":"received","from":"Collections","institutions":[{"id":"mount-stuart","name":"Mount Stuart (Bute archive)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cd2ab07bcb5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your kind enquiry to the Mount Stuart Trust Collections Team.\n\nPlease note that we are currently unable to respond to general external enquiries. We anticipate reviewing this position in January 2027.\n\nDuring this time, we are still able to assist with the following:\n\nReproductions & Permissions: where we already hold the requested image of a Collections item, we can process these as usual, and will be in touch to reply in due course. The Bute Collection at Mount Stuart is privately owned, and permission is essential for the reproduction of images or information, whether for private study or for commercial publication. Please supply as much detail as possible for your reproduction or permission request (e.g. type of use, synopsis of publication, publisher, print run, language,\nand distribution area). Conditions for permission will be supplied on receipt of your request.\n\nLoan Requests: please send these to [email redacted] and we will be in touch.\nResearch Visits: these remain available by 3-weeks' advance appointment with our Collections Team. These are charged at £20 per day.\n\nCollections Viewings: these remain available to book as usual - please find the 2027 dates available for these on our website What's On page .\nPlease note we are not able to respond to family history or genealogical enquiries at this time. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and appreciate your understanding.\n\n\nThank you again for your interest in the Collections at Mount Stuart.\n\nBest wishes,\nThe Collections Team\nMount Stuart Trust\n\nDisclaimer\n\nThe information contained in this communication from the sender is confidential. It is intended solely for use by the recipient and others authorized to receive it. If you are not the recipient, you are hereby notified that any disclosure, copying, distribution or taking action in relation of the contents of this information is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful.\n\nThis email has been scanned for viruses and malware, and may have been automatically archived by Mimecast, a leader in email security and cyber resilience. Mimecast integrates email defenses with brand protection, security awareness training, web security, compliance and other essential capabilities. Mimecast helps protect large and small organizations from malicious activity, human error and technology failure; and to lead the movement toward building a more resilient world. To find out more, visit our website."},{"id":"gm-1a141ccee6dea9c9","subject":"Research visit request — Bute Estate (Glamorgan) records, 1667 and 1875–1880 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","name":"Research visit request — Bute Estate (Glamorgan) records, 1667 and 1875–1880 — Llandough-juxta-Penarth","date":"2026-10-15T23:01:51Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141ccee6dea9c9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141ccdfba02bb7-search-visit-request-bute-estate-glamorgan-records-1667-and-1875-1880-llandough-juxta-penarth","scopeTopics":["mount-stuart"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mount-stuart"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141ccdfba02bb7","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mount-stuart","name":"Mount Stuart (Bute archive)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141ccee6dea9c9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Collections Team,\n\nI would like to book a research visit to the Bute Archive at Mount Stuart. I understand that you are not taking general enquiries until January 2027, so this is a research visit request only. Please send me the Reader Registration Form and Reading Room Regulations, and your available dates (I can give at least three weeks' notice).\n\nPLEASE NOTE: DUPLICATE PLACE AND FARM NAMES IN GLAMORGAN\nGlamorgan has two parishes called Llandough, and each had a farm called Great House.\nIN SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Penarth (Llandough near Penarth and Cardiff), hundred of Dinas Powys. Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood beside St Dochdwy's church, approx. ST 168 733.\nOUT OF SCOPE: Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge (Llandough near Cowbridge), and the Great Houses at nearby Llandow and Aberthin.\nPlease do not prepare records for the Cowbridge-area places. If an item says only \"Llandough\" or \"Great House\" and the parish cannot be told, please flag it rather than assume.\n\nTo help you prepare, these are the records I hope to consult, all for Llandough-juxta-Penarth:\n\n1. Bute Estate (Glamorgan) accounts, rentals, trustees' papers or correspondence for 1875–1880, especially anything recording a payment from Daniel Thomas (or Daniel Thomas & Son) or a disposal of land at Llandough in 1877.\n2. Any Herbert, Windsor or Bute deeds, surveys, rentals or court records for the manor of Llandough for c.1660–1680, especially 1667, naming the holder of Great House.\n3. Any lease of Great House to the Williams family, or any lease of it for 999 years. The family's account is that such a lease was granted in 1667; no copy has yet been found.\n4. The conveyance by which the Bute estate acquired Great House from the Vaughan family or its heirs (late 18th century), and any abstract of title reciting leases then outstanding.\n5. Any later index, schedule or abstract of title for Bute land at Llandough that would show when Great House left or stayed in the estate.\n\nIf none of these are held at Mount Stuart, or they are at the National Library of Wales or Cardiff, a one-line confirmation would save a wasted journey.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141cc6d72f8f62","subject":"Re: Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 - incomplete location response under FOIA","name":"Re: Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 - incomplete location response under FOIA","date":"2026-10-15T23:01:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cc6d72f8f62.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cc67c7f3f3b-sponse-to-national-archives-enquiry-case-number-cas-359317-q8q4r9-incomplete-location-response-under-foia","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cc67c7f3f3b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-359317"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cc6d72f8f62.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Team,\n\nThank you for the reply of 14 October 2026 under case CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9.\n\nThe reply provides Discovery catalogue search links for Glamorgan XLVII and Penarth field books. It does not answer the location request.\n\nPlease treat this as a follow-up under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the s.45 code. The original request was a location request only. I am still not asking for a copy, a screen-room appointment, or production until location and physical-check status are confirmed.\n\nPlease state, for the Valuation Office field book, plan and index covering Ordnance Survey sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6 for the parish of Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan):\n\n1. The series, piece and item references (IR 58, IR 121, IR 124, IR 125, IR 126, IR 127, IR 128 or successor).\n2. The accession, box, shelf or other store location used by staff.\n3. The Discovery catalogue identifier.\n4. Whether a member of staff has physically checked that the item is in that location: yes, no, or not answered. If yes, who, date, and which store.\n5. Whether the item is open, closed or retained by another department, and if closed the series and FOI route.\n6. The systems searched, and whether a physical file or plan was retrieved rather than a catalogue-only search.\n\nA catalogue-only answer is incomplete unless the systems and physical-check status are stated. Please quote the statutory deadline for this follow-up.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141cc467cf9491","subject":"Re: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 and CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 — preservation flag: Valuation Office field books and National Farm Survey / CWAEC records for Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 and CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 — preservation flag: Valuation Office field books and National Farm Survey / CWAEC records for Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-15T23:01:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cc467cf9491.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cc4128fb719-cas-359317-q8q4r9-and-cas-347296-m0v4y1-preservation-flag-valuation-office-field-books-and-national-farm-survey-cwaec-re","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cc4128fb719","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-347296","CAS-359317"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cc467cf9491.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Team,\n\nTwo cases are live: CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 (Valuation Office field book, plan and index, Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough-juxta-Penarth) and CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 (National Farm Survey / MAFF and Glamorgan CWAEC records, c.1936-1950, including Compensation (Defence) Act 1939 material).\n\nThis is not a new request. It is a preservation flag. The 1988 demolition removed the building; the paper trail is what remains. I am concerned that routine disposal or weeding of IR 58 / IR 121-128 series material, MAFF National Farm Survey records, or CWAEC cultivation and compensation files could remove items before location and physical-check status are confirmed.\n\nPlease confirm: (1) whether any retention or disposal schedule has been or will be applied to these series in relation to this holding; (2) whether any item has been reported missing, transferred or destroyed; (3) the physical-check status of the Glamorgan XLVII.6 field book and plan as previously requested.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a141cc245e1dbc5","subject":"Chase — Vale of Glamorgan FOI 00210772 internal review — 15 October 2026","name":"Chase — Vale of Glamorgan FOI 00210772 internal review — 15 October 2026","date":"2026-10-15T23:01:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cc245e1dbc5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141cc190751565-chase-vale-of-glamorgan-foi-00210772-internal-review-15-october-2026","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141cc190751565","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cc245e1dbc5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Unit,\n\nThis is the scheduled chase for internal review of FOI 00210772, requested on 7 July 2026 and still outstanding.\n\nPlease confirm the review outcome or a firm date. I am also concerned that records relevant to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (1988 eviction, demolition, planning and Building Preservation Notice files) may be subject to routine disposal. Please suspend any disposal of those records pending the outcome of this review.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n"},