\n\nByddwn yn ymateb i geisiadau’r Ddeddf Diogelu Data o fewn mis a cheisiadau’r Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth o fewn ugain niwrnod gwaith.\n\nYn y cyfamser, efallai cewch ateb i’ch ymholiad yn www.gov.uk/land-registry.cy<http://www.gov.uk/land-registry.cy>\n\nOs ydych wedi defnyddio un o’n cyfeiriadau ebost, awgrymwn eich bod yn defnyddio’n Ffurflen Gysylltu ar gyfer unrhyw ohebiaeth yn y dyfodol i’n helpu i gyfeirio’ch ymholiad yn y ffordd fwyaf effeithlon.\n\nCedwir diogelwch a chyfrinachedd yr holl ddata personol yn unol â’n Siarter Gwybodaeth Bersonol<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy>.\n\nDarllenwch ragor am ein safonau gwasanaeth<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about-our-services.cy> .\n\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a141cb5de1ebfc1","subject":"Z084NQV / N610CGV – WA240304 and WA231076 – application to alter the register (Schedule 4 LRA 2002) and follow-up on the 1983 first registration","name":"Z084NQV / N610CGV – WA240304 and WA231076 – application to alter the register (Schedule 4 LRA 2002) and follow-up on the 1983 first registration","date":"2026-10-15T23:00:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a141cb5de1ebfc1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a141af7e036c3a1-z084nqv-n610cgv-wa240304-and-wa231076-application-to-alter-the-register-schedule-4-lra-2002-and-follow-up-on-the-1983-fi","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a141af7e036c3a1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26","N610CGV","Z084NQV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a141cb5de1ebfc1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear HM Land Registry,\n\nReferences: N610CGV; Z084NQV (error investigation application); enquiries 260917-6718215, 260928-6762800, 260929-6766714, 261007-6799563.\nTitles: WA240304 (closed) and WA231076.\nLand: north side of Leckwith Road, Llandough (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr).\n\n1. What this email is\n\n(a) It asks the Registrar to consider alteration of the register under Schedule 4 to the Land Registration Act 2002, and indemnity under Schedule 8. Please add it to Z084NQV.\n(b) It supplements my emails of 30 July, 12 August, 16 September (points 1 to 14), 18 September, 27 September and 7 October 2026. Where a point repeats an earlier question I say so. Those questions remain unanswered. Points marked NEW have not been put to the Registry before.\n(c) It is limited to the first registration of WA240304 in 1983 and what followed to 1987. It does not deal with the 1982 application or the eastern land, and I waive nothing on either.\n\nYour enquiry 260917-6714796 says the Registry can no longer service mail sent to individual addresses. Please treat this email as received on the date sent and confirm receipt against Z084NQV.\n\nCopies go to the Independent Complaints Reviewer (ICR/090/26), Stephen Doughty MP, who raised this matter with the Registry, and Llandough Community Council, which holds related local records.\n\nI am not asking you to decide who owns the land. I am asking what the Registry examined, what it relied on and what its records show. The dates come from your schedule of 30 July 2026, your letters of 23 March, 19 April and 25 May 2026, and the WA231076 register accessed on 19 September 2026.\n\nPublic working evidence catalogue: https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\nTitle and chronology index: https://dartboard.bucklerfamily.estate and https://bpvsbuckler.bucklerfamily.estate\nLong-term archive: https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate\n\n2. The 1983 record on your own schedule\n\n- 23 February 1983: form 1C application from Linklaters & Paines (WA240304 item 11), and a register edition of the same date (item 10).\n- 26 March 1983: Mary Williams, the occupier of the farmhouse, died.\n- 8 April 1983: form D23 (\"inside exam\") and a Linklaters & Paines letter (WA240304 item 7).\n- 12 April 1983: customer correspondence (item 4), plus undated letters (item 5).\n- 12 May 1983: several letters between Linklaters & Paines and the Registry (WA231076 item 16).\n- 13 January 1984: form A3 application (item 15) and a new register edition (item 23).\n- 22 May 1984: BP's writ for possession. This is chronology only, not evidence of what the Registry knew in 1983.\n- 2 February 1987: application to amalgamate (WA231076 item 14). Your schedule says the WA240304 copy of the form has \"no annotation on it\".\n\n3. Points arising\n\n3.1 Root of title and class of title. Raised before: my email of 16 September (points 10 and 13) and my ICR referral. NEW detail: your stage one letter says a full documentary title commencing with a good root at least 15 years old should normally establish title. It then concluded a good root was shown and that BP Pension Trust acquired the land in 1969. That conclusion rests on the recital in the 1975 conveyance, which refers to a conveyance of 31 December 1969. The 1969 deed itself is not on your schedule. The recited root was about 13 years 2 months old on 23 February 1983. The letter also quotes the 1975 recital as giving the year as \"One thousand One hundred and sixty nine\". Please confirm the original reads 1969. Please say which documents the Registry relied on as the root, whether any exception or alternative procedure was used (and under which provision of the 1925 Act), why absolute title was accepted, and the class of title first entered for WA240304.\n\n3.2 The 1971 abstract. Raised before: 30 July, 12 August and 16 September (points 1 and 8). Your letter says a 1971 abstract was lodged with the WA231076 application and that the Registry \"had sight of\" one for WA240304. Neither schedule lists it. NEW: a 1971 abstract cannot evidence a conveyance of 1975. What evidenced that conveyance?\n\n3.3 Extent and plans. Raised before in part: 18 September. NEW: WA240304 item 1 is a plan to the conveyance of 23 May 1975, but item 13 is a plan \"to conveyance dated 23 February 1975\". Please reconcile those dates and say which plan governed the registration. The WA231076 register records that the 1975 conveyance plan is \"filed under WA240304\", which is now a closed title. Please supply the original title plan (item 9) and both plans. Please also identify the land conveyed in 1975 and the vendors' \"Retained Land\", the capacity in which each vendor conveyed, and how the extents of the two titles related immediately before amalgamation, including any overlap. The register also records that a new filed plan was substituted on 5 January 1995. Please supply the plan it replaced and confirm the extent did not change.\n\n3.4 The occupier and what the Registry knew. Raised before in part: 16 September (points 4 and 12), 27 September, and ICR/090/26. Mary Williams was in actual occupation of the farmhouse in February and March 1983. The history includes the 1955 order against Frederick Buckler alone, the 1962 order against Frederick and Mary for the farmhouse and garden (not enforced), and the 1974 county court action in which Mary pleaded ownership, which was part-heard and never concluded. NEW: stage two says the Registry \"were unaware of any dispute that was possibly ongoing\". Yet WA240304 holds an inside examination (D23) and letters of 8 and 12 April 1983, and WA231076 holds letters between the applicant's solicitors and the Registry of 12 May 1983. Please say what enquiry was made of the occupier (Land Registration Act 1925 s.70(1)(g)), what inspection was done, and what those letters said about occupation, possession proceedings or the 1974 action. Please supply the D23 examination record.\n\n3.5 The solicitors' certificate. Raised before: 30 July and 16 September (points 2 and 9). Stage one relied on certificate wording from form FR1. The 1983 application was on form 1C. Please supply form 1C as lodged and say what it certified about any question or doubt affecting title.\n\n3.6 Notice and caution. Raised before: my email of 27 September (the family's case) and ICR/090/26. NEW: stage two says my family could have applied for a caution. That requires knowing of the application. Please produce every notice and service record for WA240304, as sent, showing the title it concerned, the addressee's name, the address, the date and any proof of delivery. A notice addressed to Mary Williams and issued or received after 26 March 1983 went to a person who had died. If it went to \"Mrs Williams\" at the property, I ask whether that was the right name and the right household. I am not asserting that this happened. I am asking for the record.\n\n3.7 The 1987 judgment and the amalgamation. Raised before: 16 September (point 14) and ICR/090/26. Stage one said it is not for the Registrar to look behind decisions of the Court. The Court of Appeal considered adverse possession, the 1962 order and the 1974 letters. As I read it, it did not review the Registry's examination of title, the documents supplied or the notices. Please say precisely what HMLR says that judgment established and which parts of its 1983 process it says the judgment answers. NEW: please provide the application, decision and completion dates of the amalgamation, the instrument and plans relied on, the power used, and whether the registered extent changed or only the structure of the register. HMLR has also given the closure of WA240304 as 1987 (the amalgamation) and as 2005 (your email of 21 September 2026, enquiry 260919-6726246). Please state the actual date and the entry that records it.\n\n3.8 What the complaint decisions examined. Raised before: ICR/090/26. The itemised schedule reached me on 30 July 2026, after both decisions. NEW: stage two says the reviewer examined \"the evidence lodged in support of the application\". Please confirm which original first-registration documents each decision-maker examined, whether the absence of the 1969 conveyance was identified, and provide the recorded basis for the conclusions reached.\n\n3.9 The 1994 corrections. NEW to the Registry (raised only with the ICR). WA231076 items 12 and 22 are applications \"to correct the title\", dated 20 January 1994 and 13 October 1994. Stage one and stage two found no evidence of a mistake. Please say what was corrected, on whose application, under what authority, on what evidence, and whether the registered extent changed, including land derived from WA240304.\n\n4. Schedule 4 (mistake and rectification) and Schedule 8 (indemnity). NEW\n\nA. Mistake. I understand Schedule 4 now governs alteration of the register as it stands, including entries made in 1983 under the 1925 Act. The Registrar may alter the register to correct a mistake (paragraph 5(a)). Practice Guide 39 gives \"including too much land in a registered title\" as an example. I say there is a possible mistake in the 1983 entry in two respects: absolute title entered on a root that is not on the file (3.1 and 3.2), and an extent fixed by plans that do not reconcile (3.3). Please state whether HMLR accepts either as a mistake.\n\nB. Possession and proper care. Practice Guide 39 (sections 1.3 and 1.4) says a registered proprietor in possession is protected unless it caused or contributed to the mistake by fraud or lack of proper care, or unless it would be unjust not to correct. Possession means physical possession. Please say who is in physical possession of the land affected. Practice Guide 39 (appendix 12.3.1) gives as an example a solicitor on a first registration who fails to lodge all the documents in their possession. Please say whether the applicant's solicitors lodged every document in their possession in 1983, including the 1969 conveyance and the abstract, and whether HMLR considers that bears on this protection. I do not assert that anything was withheld.\n\nC. Class of title and overriding interests. Practice Guide 39 (section 1.1) says an alteration can give effect to an estate, right or interest not affected by registration where land is registered with good leasehold, possessory or qualified title. If the root evidence supported no more than that, the class entered may itself be the mistake. Section 1.2 says an alteration reflecting an overriding interest is not rectification. Please say whether HMLR accepts that an occupier's rights in 1983 could be recorded without that being rectification, and how it would deal with them.\n\nD. Indemnity and process. Please confirm Z084NQV is being treated as a formal application for alteration, or tell me what form and fee are required (Practice Guide 39 section 2.1; rule 13 of the Land Registration Rules 2003). Practice Guide 39 says anyone may apply, and the fee may be refunded where the Registry caused the error. Indemnity time runs for six years from when the claimant knew or should have known of the claim (Schedule 8 paragraph 8). The family first saw the file schedule on 30 July 2026. Please confirm HMLR will treat any claim as in time. Please also give your consent under Schedule 8 paragraph 3 to reasonable costs, including copy fees at £11 per document. Where indemnity is not available, please consider whether a payment for maladministration is appropriate (Practice Guide 39 section 11).\n\n5. Anticipated responses\n\n- \"The amalgamation was administrative tidying.\" Points 3.3 and 3.7 ask whether it altered the registered extent. Points 3.1 and 3.2 go to the examination of title, not to the structure of the register.\n- \"The missing documents' contents are unknown, so absence of evidence is not evidence of absence.\" That is why I ask for the files to be read and the examination record produced.\n- \"The Registry may rely on the solicitors' certificate.\" Please produce the certificate actually given on form 1C (3.5).\n- \"The registrar may approve a title open to objection where the holding is unlikely to be disturbed (section 13 of the 1925 Act, and section 9(3) of the 2002 Act).\" If HMLR relied on that discretion, please identify the defect considered, the contemporaneous evidence supporting the opinion that the holding would not be disturbed, and the recorded reasons for approving the title. Please also explain how the occupier's rights under section 70(1)(g) were examined before they were treated as undisclosed.\n\n6. Requests\n\n(a) Confirm these points are added to Z084NQV, and confirm receipt of this email.\n(b) Answer each numbered point and A to D, or say the record is not held.\n(c) Provide copies of the WA240304 register as first registered, form 1C as lodged, form D23, the letters of 8 and 12 April 1983 and 12 May 1983, the A3 application of 13 January 1984 and the register edition, the 1971 abstract, both plans, the original title plan, every notice and service record, the amalgamation application with its decision and completion dates, and the two 1994 correction applications. If copies cannot be emailed, please give the OC2 / HC1 wording and the address for each.\n(d) Reply within 20 working days.\n\nPlease also keep every document on both first-registration files and every related internal record, in line with my preservation notices of 3 June and 28 September 2026.\n\nTo the Independent Complaints Reviewer: please confirm whether you will consider this additional material in ICR/090/26, or whether I should raise it separately.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a13fd8c7589dabc","subject":"RE. ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding (ATISN 26-0009)","name":"RE. ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding (ATISN 26-0009)","date":"2026-10-15T13:55:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13fd8c7589dabc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13fd8c7589dabc-atisn-27021-existing-records-behind-the-1988-listing-file-disposal-finding-atisn-26-0009","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13fd8c7589dabc","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13fd8c7589dabc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nATISN 26-0009 - Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nThank you for your latest request which I received on 10 October.  You asked for:\n\n\n  1.  Any existing file inventory, closure note, archive catalogue entry, transfer list, disposal authority, retention schedule, weeding/destruction record, archival receipt, email/minute/note recording the search or basis for the conclusion,  or record showing whether the file remained held or was transferred on/after 6 December 1988.\n  2.  The recorded date and responsible role/unit for any documented disposal or transfer decision.\n  3.  If neither 1 or 2 exist, distinguish an actual contemporaneous disposal decision/log from the present-day inability to locate the file, identifying the repositories, indices and systems searched for this focused request.\n\nYou will receive a response by 6 November 2026.  If you have any queries about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future correspondence.\n\nThe request you sent me contains personal information about you - for example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your personal information and all other information relating to your request for three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your personal information will then be disposed of securely.\n\nUnder data protection legislation, you have the right:\n\n•              to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access it\n•              to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\n•              to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\n•              for (in certain circumstances) your data to be ‘erased’\n•              to (in certain circumstances) data portability\n•              to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\n\nFor further information about the information which the Welsh Government holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR, please see contact details below:\n\nData Protection Officer\nWelsh Government\nCathays Park\nCARDIFF\n[postcode redacted]\nEmail:    [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nThe contact details for the Information Commissioner’s Office are:\n\nWycliffe House\nWater Lane\nWilmslow\nCheshire\n[postcode redacted]\n\nWebsite: www.ico.org.uk<http://www.ico.org.uk>\n\nAny information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh Government’s Disclosure Log (at https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en).\n\nYours sincerely\n\nAndy Wigley\n\n\n[cid:[email redacted]967400]\n\nDr Andy Wigley\nPrif Arolygydd – Pennaeth Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Chief Inspector - Head of Historic Environment Inspectorate\nCadw\nDysgu, Cymunedau a Diwylliant / Learning, Communities and Culture\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nTŷ Ladywell / Ladywell House\nY Drenewydd / Newtown\nPowys\n[postcode redacted]\n\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\nFfôn symudol / Mobile: [phone redacted]\nE-bost/ Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[cid:[email redacted]967400][cid:[email redacted]967400]\nP Helpwch yr amgylchedd - peidiwch ag argraffu hon os nad oes gwir raid   Help our environment - only print this if really necessary\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth Gymraeg. Cewch ateb Cymraeg i bob gohebiaeth Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh. Correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not involve any delay.\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-1a13fa747f9c0dd3","subject":"Request for information - ref FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough Non-SF Information","name":"Request for information - ref FOI2026/23272 - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough Non-SF Information","date":"2026-10-15T13:01:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13fa747f9c0dd3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13fa747f9c0dd3-quest-for-information-ref-foi2026-23272-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-non-sf-information","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13fa747f9c0dd3","direction":"received","from":"Army Secretariat","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13fa747f9c0dd3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\nYour request has been logged under our reference FOI2026/23272 and the target date for response is 09 November 2026.\nYours sincerely,\nArmy Policy & Secretariat\nDid you know you can now submit your FOI request to us through our webform, which can be found here:\nhttp://submit-freedom-of-information-request.service.mod.uk/start-now"},{"id":"gm-1a13aff7c0c5d8b4","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-10-14T15:19:37Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13aff7c0c5d8b4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a07efa0b6b10900-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a07efa0b6b10900","direction":"received","from":"HER","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13aff7c0c5d8b4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear sir,\n\nThe information held in the HER source file has now been digitised and uploaded to Archwilio and is accessible via record 02038s as PDF files shown in the Sources section of the record.  This includes a copy of Suggett, 1988 as held by the HER.  Having undertaken a physical search of our records, I can confirm that no further information is held within the HER source file.\n\nWe will respond to your additional points raised on 19th September by 21st October.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nTîm Cofnod yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol | Historic Environment Record Team\nGwefan / Web\n​www.heneb.org.uk\n THE TRUST FOR WELSH ARCHAEOLOGY\n YMDDIRIEDOLAETH ARCHAEOLEGOL CYMRU\n​\n​Cadeirydd / Chair: Dr Carol Bell          PSG / CEO: Richard Nicholls\n \nHeneb is a Registered Organisation with the Chartered Institute for Archaeologists \nMae Heneb yn Sefydliad Cofrestredig gyda’r Chartered Institute for Archaeologists\n​\nThe Trust is both a Limited Company (1198990) and a Registered Charity (504616)\nAny of the statements or comments made above should be regarded as personal and not necessarily those of\n​Heneb. This e-mail and any files transmitted with it are confidential and intended solely for the use of the individual or\n​entity to whom they are addressed.\n​\n​Privacy Policy - Heneb\n​\n​Registered Office: Corner House, 6 Carmarthen Street, Llandeilo, Carmarthenshire, [postcode redacted]\n​Swyddfa Gofrestredig : Ty Cornel, 6 Stryd Caerfyrddin, Llandeilo, Sir Gaerfyrddin, [postcode redacted]\n\n​Cwmni Cyfyngedig (1198990) ynghyd ag Elusen Gofrestredig (504616) yw’r Ymddiriedolaeth\n​Dylai'r datganiadau neu'r sylwadau uchod gael eu trin fel rhai personol ac nid o reidrwydd fel datganiadau neu\n​​sylwadau gan Heneb. Mae'r e-bost hwn ac unrhyw ffeiliau a drosglwyddir gydag ef yn gyfrinachol ac at ddefnydd\nyr unigolyn neu'r corff y cyfeiriwyd hwy atynt yn unig.\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 10 October 2026 20:14\nTo: HER <[email redacted]>\nSubject: RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\nHER Officer,\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough - your letter of 6 October 2026, request of 8 September 2026 (GGAT02038s)\n\nThank you. I note that you point to Archwilio record 02038s and that you will reply separately on the 19 September 2026 email.\n\nThe 8 September request asked for the HER source file, not only the online summary. Archwilio 02038s does not supply:\n1. the complete entry text on armour or medieval ironwork found under the rear wing or floor about 1880, with every source code; 2. a copy or transcript of the RCAHMW / Suggett 1988 material on the file; 3. any museum accession, letter, or catalogue slip naming where the ironwork went; 4. any recorded distinction between the c.1880 rear-wing ironwork, the\n1979 villa iron south of the church, and the 1994 cemetery iron girdle (Burial 631).\n\nPlease give the record location before any viewing is discussed:\nseries, accession, box, shelf, and catalogue id for the source file behind 02038s, and whether staff physically checked that the item is there (who, date, store). I am not requesting a screen-room viewing.\n\nIf any of the four items is not held, please name the systems searched and whether the physical source file was retrieved (EIR reg.5 and reg.9; reg.14 if you refuse).\n\nPlease also give a date for the separate reply on the 19 September email. The 8 September request was answered on day 20. An extension of the 19 September points should be notified if you need beyond 20 working days from 6 October.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a13aa68b250b8de","subject":"Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 CRM:022001165","name":"Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-359317-Q8Q4R9 CRM:022001165","date":"2026-10-14T13:42:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13aa68b250b8de.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13aa68b250b8de-sponse-to-national-archives-enquiry-case-number-cas-359317-q8q4r9-crm-022001165","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13aa68b250b8de","direction":"received","from":"RESO Records Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-359317"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13aa68b250b8de.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear  Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nWe may hold records related to your enquiry. The map you mention is listed in our catalogue.\n\nI have searched our catalogue  for records using Glamorgan XLVII as search terms. You can view the results of the search here and try some similar searches yourself.\n\nSearch results: (Glamorgan AND XLVII) AND 6 | The National Archives \n\nPenarth field books ….\n Search results: penarth | The National Archives \n\nFurther advice about using Valuation Office records can be found here….\n Land use, value and ownership: Valuation Office Survey 1910-1915 - The National Archives \n\nRecords are represented in our online catalogue by a title, a reference and a brief description. When you search our catalogue using keywords you are searching across these titles and descriptions, rather than the contents of the records themselves.\n\nBy clicking on any search result, you can see whether the record is available online or if you need to visit us to view the original. You can also request copies of records from their catalogue description page.\n\nIf the record is held by another archive, you will need to contact them directly to find out how you can access it.\n\nYou can also watch this video  for more advice on using our online catalogue.\n\nYou are welcome to visit us  to continue your research here in person, where access to our records is free of charge. Before you visit, please check our website for information regarding our opening hours  and ID requirements , and videos with tips on how to handle and photograph original documents .\n\nIf you are unable to visit, or would like someone to pursue this research on your behalf, please see the available paid search options  on our website.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nMichael McGrady\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk \n\nPlease complete our brief, three question survey  to let us know what you think about your recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n\nEnquiry:\n[You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\nFreedom of Information Team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is a\nlocation request only. I am not asking for a copy of the plan, a\nscreen-room appointment, or production of the item until the location\nand physical-check status are confirmed.\n\nContext. Glamorgan Archives, in reply 2026/4097b of 30 September 2026,\nidentified Ordnance Survey sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6 as the sheet\nrelevant to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and\ndirected me to the Valuation Office Survey 1910-1915 maps held by The\nNational Archives.\n\nPlease state, for the Valuation Office field book, plan, and index\ncovering that sheet for the parish of Llandough\n(Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan):\n\n1. The series, piece, and item references (including any IR 58, IR\n121, IR 124, IR 125, IR 126, IR 127, IR 128 or successor reference\nthat applies).\n2. The accession, box, shelf, or other store location used by your staff.\n3. The Discovery catalogue identifier.\n4. Whether a member of staff has physically checked that the item is\nin that location: yes, no, or not answered. If yes, who checked it and\non what date, and which store.\n5. Whether the item is open, closed, or retained by another\ndepartment, and if closed the series and the FOI route for a closed\nrecord.\n6. The systems searched, and whether a physical file or plan was\nretrieved rather than a catalogue-only search.\n\nI am not asking you to interpret ownership or to comment on any legal\nproceedings. Please treat a “not held” answer as incomplete unless you\nname the systems searched and whether a physical item was retrieved.\n\nPlease quote this email as the request and give the statutory deadline.\n\n\nRequester \n\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-1a13a11f16d19b46","subject":"In Touch with Llandough!","name":"In Touch with Llandough!","date":"2026-10-14T11:00:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13a11f16d19b46.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a13a11f16d19b46-in-touch-with-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a13a11f16d19b46","direction":"received","from":"Cllr George Carroll","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13a11f16d19b46.json","textStatus":"available","text":"View this email in your browser (https://mailchi.mp/e61374125296/in-touch-with-llandough-17666383?e=1429c2c1bb)\nUPDATE: FIREWORKS\nRESPONSE FROM POLICE AND COUNCIL\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDear Requester\n\nFireworks continue to cause unacceptable noise disturbances in our community.\n\nI raised the issue at Full Council on Monday, emphasising the importance of both the Council and the Police working together.\n\nYou can watch my comments here.  (https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1JExrTZK3w/)\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/v/1JExrTZK3w/\n\nOn Wednesday, our village experienced another incident.\n\nIt is clear neither the police nor the Vale of Glamorgan Council have taken sufficient action to date to address this problem.\n\nBoth authorities have failed to fulfill their duties to protect our community.\n\nI've written to both authorities to raise serious concerns.\n\nYou can read my letter below.\nFAO: South Wales Police\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n\n8th October 2026\n\n\nDear both\n\nIllegal firework usage in Llandough\n\nI’m saddened to report that another firework related incident took place in Llandough last night.\n\nThis is impacting some of the most vulnerable members of our community, causing distress to the elderly, small children and animals.\n\nIt is apparent that those responsible for setting off fireworks are not residents and instead come into the community from outside.\n\nA lack of action to date is sending a message to those responsible that their behaviour is acceptable and will be tolerated.\n\nThere have been several instances in which fireworks have been set off past 11.00pm at night, in direct contravention of the law. There may also be other laws and regulations that have been broken.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if you would:\n\n- Outline full details of all firework-related incidents in the Llandough ward reported to your respective authorities within the past 24 months;\n\n- Confirm all actions that were taken following those incidents to address the problems reported;\n\n- Outline all actions proposed by your authorities to prevent inappropriate firework usage in the Llandough ward in future;\n\n- Confirm all measures available to your respective authorities to detain and apprehend the individuals responsible for inappropriate firework usage in the Community of Llandough as well as any restrictions that may be imposed to prohibit those individuals from entering the Community boundary; and\n\n- Confirm details of any powers conferred on your respective authorities which enable you to introduce additional regulations or byelaws to impose stricter restrictions prohibiting firework usage within the Community of Llandough.\n\nI have not copied this message to our PSCOs because they are not responsible for operational decisions, and as such it would be unfair to attribute blame to them for the failure to address this problem.\n\nHowever, I reiterate my request for your respective authorities to meet with me at the earliest convenience to discuss this ongoing problem, with an invitation also extended to our PCSOs.\n\nThank you for your consideration of this matter, and I look forward to your prompt response.\n\nKind regards,\n\nCllr George Carroll\nElected member\n\nLlandough ward\nVale of Glamorgan Council\nI'm pleased to report both authorities responded promptly.\n\nThe Police have confirmed a Problem Oriented Police Plan is being developed in conjunction with our PCSOs.\n\nThe Inspector has confirmed he'll update me in due course, with further escalation promised if this proves insufficient.\n\nThe Council too have agreed to take part in a multi-agency meeting to address the problem.\n\nThe time for discussion has long passed.\n\nWe need to see surveillance and enforcement, so that those responsible for these disturbances know their behaviour will not be tolerated.\n\nAs a community, it's vital we keep up the pressure.\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNEXT WEEK: Penlan Road\ntemporary traffic lights\n\nTemporary traffic lights will be in place on Penlan Road on Tuesday 13th October to allow for Welsh Water works to be carried out safely.\n\nThey will operate from 9.30am to 2.30pm.\n\nThe lights will be situated outside the Memorial Hall, with Spencer Drive and Cogan Pill Road also impacted.\n\nThe bus stops outside the Hall will be suspended due to proximity to the works.\n\nAccess will be maintained for residents at all times.\n\nIf anyone has further questions, please let me know.\n\nPlease see below for further information.\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Eqf5imB1i/\n\nLlandough Hospital meadow\n\nI've received many enquiries about the Llandough Hospital meadow, access to which has been restricted.\n\nI've contacted the Health Board about this, as I know many residents enjoy using this route.\n\nThey've confirmed it has been fenced off as a temporary measure following misuse of the site.\n\nThey do not intend to close it permanently, but have restricted access while safety arrangements are reviewed.\n\nA fortnight ago, I requested a likely timescale.\n\nThe person I spoke with said they were unable to provide one at present, but said they'd request an update.\n\nI've chased them on this.\n\nIf anyone has further questions, please let me know.\n\nThe meadow has been a good benefit to our community and I’m pressing for it to be opened again as soon as possible.\n\nPenarth Road water leak\n\nProblems like the Penarth Road water leak require different agencies to work together.\n\nThe manhole from which the water is emanating is BT's responsibility, but the fault causing the leak is Welsh Water's responsibility.\n\nThe Council is in charge of highway safety, so they must make sure the algae forming in the discharge is cleared to prevent a slip hazard.\n\nAll responsible bodies must work together to fulfil their responsibilities, rather than blame each other.\n\nI emphasised this to the Council this week.\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/19dhRQfogP/\n\nChristmas Fayre\nSaturday 14th November\n\nLlandough’s annual Christmas Fayre is set to take place on Saturday 14th November.\n\nWith many local businesses operating stalls, it’s a great way to make a start to your Christmas shopping and support our local economy.\n\nHuge thanks to Llandough Community Council for organising, it’s always a great event and this year promises to be no different.\n\nFurther details can be found above.\n\nCommunity drop-in event:\n20th October\n\nOur next community drop-in event takes place at the Merrie Harrier on 20th October.\n\nLike the last one, it'll start at 7.00pm.\n\nThe pub is a key asset to our community.\n\nTracey and the team do a lot for us - help return the favour by lending them your support.\n\nYou can see some of their midweek offers below!\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/1EM9z5wbMs/\n\nOur Plan for Llandough!\n\n\nAs your councillor, I'm working with you all to secure a better future for Llandough. Together, we have a plan to deliver for the village.\n\nOur plan is making Llandough better by:\n\n1. Sorting out the parking problems\n2. Stamping out dog fouling\n3. Repairing our roads\n4. Stopping littering and flytipping\n5. Delivering better sports facilities\n6. Keeping the whole community involved\n\nIf you have any suggestions of what you'd like to see in Our Plan, please get in touch!\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2Fe61374125296%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666383 Share (http://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2Fe61374125296%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666383)\nhttps://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=587f910676&e=1429c2c1bb Forward (https://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=587f910676&e=1429c2c1bb)\n\n============================================================\nI'm hoping to reach as many people as possible with this newsletter, so please feel free to forward it to friends and neighbours.\n\nIf this email has been forwarded to you, and you would like to sign up to my newsletter, please click ** here ([email redacted]\n.\nThis email was sent to you because your email address is on my subscribers list. If you don't want to receive any more messages from me, please click below to unsubscribe.\n\nYour consent was previously given during an online or offline interaction with me or the Conservatives. If you feel this is incorrect or would like to comment, please contact me. I do not buy email lists.\n\nPromoted by Chris Kirkham on behalf of George Carroll, both of Vale of Glamorgan Conservatives, Holton House, 50 Holton Road, Barry [postcode redacted].\n\nThis email was sent to [email redacted] ([email redacted]\nwhy did I get this? (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/about?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=587f910676)     unsubscribe from this list (***REDACTED***     update subscription preferences (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/profile?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=587f910676)\nPolitician . Unit 5 Pro Copy Business Centre . Parc Ty Glas . Cardiff, Crf [postcode redacted] . USA"},{"id":"gm-1a139da7cf491974","subject":"Request for information ATISN 26-0010 - Acknowledgement (Retention & disposal schedules)","name":"Request for information ATISN 26-0010 - Acknowledgement (Retention & disposal schedules)","date":"2026-10-14T09:59:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a139da7cf491974.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a139da7cf491974-quest-for-information-atisn-26-0010-acknowledgement-r