e the right to \nmonitor all e-mail communications, as permitted by applicable law and \nregulations.\n\nFor details of how we process personal data, please see the \nprivacy notices for each of ITV's business areas at \nhttp://www.itv.com/groupprivacy"},{"id":"gm-1a139b57592cf670","subject":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-14T09:19:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a139b57592cf670.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e03138143e763-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e03138143e763","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a139b57592cf670.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nBeryl Evans\n\nOct 14 2026, 10:18AM via System\n\nPlease see my other reply today.\n\nKind regards\n\nBeryl\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nSep 27 2026, 05:12AM via Email\nGreat House Farm, Llandough\n\nSirs/ Ma'ams,\n\n\nI need to correct a date I have used in earlier correspondence about Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, titles WA231076 and WA240304.\n\n\nI had treated 1983 as the year the two titles were merged. That was wrong. HM Land Registry’s own letter of 23 March 2026 (Lisa Griffiths, ref N610CGV) separates the two acts.\n1982–83 was first registration of two live titles, not a merger.\n30 November 1982: application to first-register WA231076. The Court of Appeal later treated BP Properties Ltd as registered proprietors of “the farm” from November 1982.\n23 February 1983: application to first-register a second title, WA240304.\n26 March 1983: Mary Williams died. On the family’s case, notice of those applications did not reach us until after her death, while the family was in mourning. She had no window in which to object. The family was not in a position to use any window that arrived after that.\nThose two titles remained separate through first instance.\n24 July 1986: Hollis J. Both titles were still live. The judgment language treats Great House Farm as one holding. It had not been one holding on the register. On the family’s case it had not been one holding since the 1877 split: Parcel A (house, buildings, garden/yard and about 10 acres, the Thomas/Williams line) and Parcel B (the eastern fields retained by Bute and later WGR/BP).\n2 February 1987: application to amalgamate the two titles. WA240304 was then closed and registration continued under WA231076. That is the merge. It was made after the 1986 ruling and before the Court of Appeal gave judgment on 31 July 1987.\nSo 1983 is silent first registration of a second title while Mary was still in Parcel A, or had only just died. 1987 is the administrative merger, carried out while the appeal was still open.\nThis was not a dispute about a single land parcel that BP already owned. Mary was on Parcel A, which the family says she owned, with occupation on that house parcel running in the family from at least 1667. BP, and WGR before it from 1949, were the neighbouring interest on Parcel B. From 1949 onwards the family’s case is that those neighbours ran a decades-long series of tenancy offers, “whole farm” wording, possession orders and the 1974 letters to make her occupation of her own parcel look permissive, and to make both parcels look like one estate they had acquired. They never produced a conveyance of Parcel A. What they had was an unfounded claim that her occupancy was permissive.\nPlease treat any earlier letter from me that said the titles merged in 1983 as corrected by this email. The dates that matter are:\n1982/83 — first registration of two titles, without the occupier being heard;\n24 July 1986 — first-instance judgment describing one farm while two titles still stood;\n2 February 1987 — amalgamation, before the appeal ended;\n31 July 1987 — Court of Appeal.\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nRequester\nRefs where relevant: N610CGV; 260919-6726246; titles WA231076 and WA240304.\n\nRequester \ngreathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com <http://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com>\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n\nBeryl Evans Rheolwr Gwasanaethau Ymchwil Research Services Manager Gwasanaeth Ymholiadau: https://www.llyfrgell.cymru/gwasanaethau/ymholiadau/ymholiadau-llgc Enquiries Service: https://www.library.wales/services/enquiries/nlw-enquiries Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Ffacs/Fax: [phone redacted]\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9816931.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a139b4ba7873d07","subject":"[NLW English] Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy","name":"[NLW English] Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy","date":"2026-10-14T09:18:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a139b4ba7873d07.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190-nlw-english-research-enquiry-bute-estate-records-gb-0210-bute-d153-d219-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a139b4ba7873d07.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nBeryl Evans\n\nOct 14 2026, 10:17AM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for contacting the National Library of Wales regarding the Bute Estate Records.\n\nThe full catalogue for the Bute Estate Records can be viewed online https://archives.library.wales/index.php/bute-estate-records\n\nA quick search of the contents can be made by using the search box on the left.\n\nBy clicking on the + sign it will open up descriptions of additional documents with descriptions listed below.\n\nWhen you have searched the collection and identified any records of possible interest you may be interested in booking a session in our Virtual Reading Room to view them. Details can be found online here  https://www.library.wales/visit/things-to-do/reading-at-nlw/virtual-reading-room\nAlternatively, you can get back in contact with our Enquiry service to discuss possible copying options for you.\nKind regards\nBeryl\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nSep 27 2026, 05:15AM via Email\nResearch enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — 1877 split and 1916 tenancy\nEnquiries Service\nThe National Library of Wales\n\nI am researching the title history of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan, adjoining St Dochdwy’s churchyard (approx. ST 167 733).\n\nGlamorgan Archives (Louise Hunt, ref. 2026/4097, 24 September 2026) has confirmed that the following references are yours, not theirs, and has directed me to you:\n\n1. D153 — Deeds relating to premises in p. Llandough, co. Glam., comprising a dwelling house adjoining the churchyard, 1811 (D153/1–2), and land (D153 onwards, including items sometimes cited as D153/4–8).\n2. D219 — Llandough manorial leases and agreements.\n3. The main Bute Estate deposit, GB 0210 BUTE (deeds to 1937; Glamorgan / Cardiff rentals).\n\nI do not ask you to adjudicate title. I ask only whether the following instruments exist in your holdings, and for catalogue references, dates, parties, acreages, and whether a plan is attached.\n\nA. The 1877 division\nDoes the Bute deposit contain a conveyance, agreement, or other instrument of about 1876–1877 by which the Marquess of Bute (or trustees) conveyed or contracted to convey the farmhouse, buildings and about 10 acres adjoining the churchyard at Llandough to Daniel Thomas (or Thomas and another), while retaining about 9 acres of agricultural land to the east?\n\nB. The 1916 agricultural tenancy\nDoes the deposit contain a yearly agricultural tenancy, or counterpart, of 1916 from the Marquess of Bute to John Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough?\nIf yes:\n- does the parcels clause describe the whole farm, or only the land Bute still owned after 1877?\n- is there a plan?\n- what acreage is stated?\n\nC. Rentals 1877–1936 for this farm\nDo Glamorgan / Cardiff / Llandough rentals in GB 0210 BUTE distinguish, after c.1877, between:\n- a house/buildings holding (Thomas / later Williams), and\n- a residual Bute field holding later passed to Western Ground Rents in 1938?\n\nD. Anything that would show the two holdings were treated as one unit again before 1938.\n\nPurpose. HM Land Registry first-registered titles WA231076 (30 November 1982) and WA240304 (23 February 1983; later amalgamated). The 1982/83 files treat the land as one farm. The family case is that Parcel A (house and about 10 acres) had already left Bute in 1877 and was not the land let in 1916, so the 1982 merged title cannot be the same unit as the 1916 tenancy. Your deeds and rentals are the estate-side evidence that can confirm or deny that.\n\nI live in Patagonia and cannot visit Aberystwyth in person in the short term. I would be grateful for:\n- catalogue references and a short description of any matching items;\n- whether copies can be supplied, and the cost;\n- if the 1916 tenancy is not in GB 0210 BUTE, any note of where Bute tenancy counterparts after 1910 were deposited.\n\nThis is a new enquiry. It is not a repeat of FOI/2026/11. Glamorgan Archives hold the 1938–44 Western Ground Rents plan/rental book (D696) and have already answered on their own Bute material.\n\nRequester Requester\n[email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n[phone redacted]\n\nPublic chronology and parcel statement:\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/the-two-parcels/\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/1916-tenancy/\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/land-registry-titles/\n\n------------------\n\nBeryl Evans Rheolwr Gwasanaethau Ymchwil Research Services Manager Gwasanaeth Ymholiadau: https://www.llyfrgell.cymru/gwasanaethau/ymholiadau/ymholiadau-llgc Enquiries Service: https://www.library.wales/services/enquiries/nlw-enquiries Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Ffacs/Fax: [phone redacted]\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9816877.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a1393f92a4eae63","subject":"Fwd: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","name":"Fwd: MEETING OF THE COUNCIL - 22 OCTOBER AT 7.00PM","date":"2026-10-14T07:10:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1393f92a4eae63.txt","threadSlug":"g