ou wish to complain\n> about any aspect of the handling of your request, then you should contact\n> us in the first instance and we will undertake an internal review.\n>\n>  If after the internal review you wish to complain further then you can\n> complain to the Information Commissioners Office http://www.ico.gov.uk and\n> request a decision notice.\n>\n> The other matters you include in your email will be considered at the\n> October meeting of the council and I will let you have the views of the\n> council after the meeting.\n>\n>  Kind regards,\n> ---\n> Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n>\n> Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n>\n> [address removed]\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n>\n> Telephone [phone redacted]\n>\n> Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> When you contact us\n>\n> The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\n> email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\n> to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> information and/or access our facilities and services.\n>\n> Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other\n> third party. Your information may however be published in the public domain\n> if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n>\n>\n>\n> For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website\n> www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our\n> identity' The Council will always strive to:\n>\n>  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n>\n> · Be accountable in all our council activities\n>\n> · Be responsive to the needs of the community\n>\n> · Encourage community participation\n>\n>\n> On 2026-09-21 03:59, Requester wrote:\n>\n> Dr Misra,\n>\n> Thank you for replying, and for doing so promptly and at a weekend. Good\n> drills Sir. What an honour. I know you and the Council serve as volunteers,\n> and I am grateful for the time.\n>\n> Let me set out plainly what I am asking of the Council, which is narrow.\n> If you'll allow me?\n>\n> I am not asking your Council to revisit Mr Egan's answer of 14 June 2026.\n> He explained that the minute books from 1982 onwards were deposited with\n> Glamorgan Archives in 2002, and I am pursuing those there.\n>\n> What I am asking about is what that answer did not cover. Llandough\n> Community Council is a public authority under Schedule 1, Part II,\n> paragraph 7(b) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000. The Act applies to\n> the recorded information set out below generally; the Environmental\n> Information Regulations 2004 apply in addition to any part of it that is\n> environmental information.\n>\n> PART ONE — REQUEST FOR RECORDED INFORMATION\n>\n> 1. Whether the Council holds any recorded information created after the\n> 2002 deposit — minutes, correspondence, reports, emails, photographs or\n> files of any kind — concerning Great House Farm (Ty Mawr) / Church View\n> Close, the village green in front of St Dochdwy's including registered\n> green VG 41, or the roadside verge by the churchyard wall.\n>\n> 2. Whether the Council holds any photographs, postcards or images of the\n> farm, the barn, the green or the church surroundings, of any date.\n>\n> 3. Whether the Council holds any recorded information showing what, if\n> anything, transferred to it from Penarth Town Council at the 1982\n> reorganisation, and any recorded information identifying where the pre-1982\n> Llandough community records were deposited.\n>\n> If the answer to any of these is that no such information is held, I would\n> be content with a short statement to that effect — but I do need it stated.\n> Section 1(1)(a) of the Act requires the Council to confirm or deny whether\n> the information is held.\n>\n> Section 10 (and regulation 5 of the EIR) allows twenty working days from\n> receipt, which on my request of 20 September 2026 I calculate as 16 October\n> 2026.\n>\n> If the Council is refusing, section 17 (and regulation 14) requires a\n> written refusal notice identifying the exemption or exception relied on;\n> section 17(7) requires the Council to give particulars of any complaints\n> procedure it operates, or to state that it has none, and to notify me of my\n> right to apply to the Information Commissioner; and regulation 11 gives a\n> right to an internal review of any refusal under the EIR.\n>\n> \"We have nothing more to add\" does not meet those requirements. If the\n> period passes without a compliant response I will have no option but to\n> complain to the Information Commissioner.\n>\n> PART TWO — MATTERS FOR THE COUNCIL'S DISCRETION\n>\n> These are not part of the request above and carry no deadline. They are\n> simply things I would be grateful for.\n>\n> A. I am not asking for the name or contact details of any individual. I am\n> asking whether the Council would be willing to pass my details to any\n> former member, former clerk or long-standing resident who might remember\n> the village between the 1950s and the 1990s, leaving it entirely to them\n> whether to contact me. I appreciate the Council may have data protection or\n> administrative reasons for declining, and I would not press it.\n>\n> B. Whether the Council would be willing to table this correspondence at a\n> meeting and minute it. I am content for it to be tabled in full.\n>\n> C. Whether the Council would consider, in due course, whether an\n> interpretation board or a plaque near the green would be appropriate. The\n> excavation on the land beneath Church View Close recorded 1,026 burials,\n> described in the published report as by far the largest early medieval\n> burial population so far recovered from Wales, above a Roman villa and an\n> Iron Age roundhouse. That history belongs to Llandough as much as to my\n> family, and there is nothing on the ground that records it. I would be glad\n> to give the Council or the community a short talk on the documentary\n> record, without charge, if that would be useful.\n>\n> I should be grateful for a response to items 1 to 3 by 16 October 2026.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester \n> \n>\n>\n> On Sun, 20 Sept 2026, 18:31 Mo Misra, <[email redacted]>\n> wrote:\n>\n> > Dear Requester,\n> >\n> > Thanks for your email of 20th September 2026.\n> >\n> > I note that our Clerk, Paul Egan, has already directed you to all the\n> > information we have on the matter as indicated in paragraph 6 of your\n> > email.\n> >\n> > We have nothing more to add.\n> >\n> > Best regards\n> >\n> > Dr M C Misra,\n> > Chair Llandough Community Council\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a130cebc8f7e302","subject":"RE: FOI — location only — Valuation Office Survey 1910, OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough / Great House Farm","name":"RE: FOI — location only — Valuation Office Survey 1910, OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough / Great House Farm","date":"2026-10-12T15:50:02Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a130cebc8f7e302.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1060d79ae529a6-foi-location-only-valuation-office-survey-1910-os-glamorgan-xlvii-6-llandough-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1060d79ae529a6","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a130cebc8f7e302.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nBased on the information you have provided, we believe that this is the Valuation Office map covering the property you have referred to: https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C1667398 (IR 131/4/96).\n\nUnfortunately, there is no way of identifying the relevant IR field book on our catalogue without additional information. We would need the income tax parish and the assessment number, which we would expect to be found via the map linked above (IR 131/4/96). We have checked the Genealogist website which has digitised some of these records, but its coverage appears not to include Glamorgan.\n\nWe have made a guess that the income tax parish is Penarth, but we would still need the assessment number of the individual farm in order to identify the right field book: https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/results/r/1?_q=penarth&_cr=IR%2058&_dss=range&_ro=any&_srt=1)\n\nYour options for accessing information from IR 131/4/96 is to either travel to Kew to review it and ascertain the field book number yourself, or to request a paid search by TNA staff, or hire an independent researcher.\n\nDetails on the options available for paid research can be found via the following pages:\n\nhttps://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/paying-for-research/\n\nA public authority is allowed to charge fees for access to information under section 9 of the FOI Act. The prices we charge are set out by the Fees Regulations under the Public Records Act (1958), and are based on recovering the costs of providing the services. Fees are typically charged for research and provision of information within open records in TNA's collection.\n\nInformation on booking a visit to The National Archives and how to register for a reader's ticket can be found here: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/visit/researching-here/booking-a-visit-to-view-documents/\n\nIf you are able to identify the relevant records from our catalogue to which your enquiry below relates, you are welcome to request information regarding their production history or any other recorded metadata held in relation to them. Please submit a new request to [email redacted]\n\nWe hope this advice is of assistance in your research.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nFOI Manager\nFreedom of Information Centre\nThe National Archives\n\n--------------\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:15\nTo: Contact Centre <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI — location only — Valuation Office Survey 1910, OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough / Great House Farm\n\n[You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\nFreedom of Information Team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is a location request only. I am not asking for a copy of the plan, a screen-room appointment, or production of the item until the location and physical-check status are confirmed.\n\nContext. Glamorgan Archives, in reply 2026/4097b of 30 September 2026, identified Ordnance Survey sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6 as the sheet relevant to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and directed me to the Valuation Office Survey 1910-1915 maps held by The National Archives.\n\nPlease state, for the Valuation Office field book, plan, and index covering that sheet for the parish of Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan):\n\n1. The series, piece, and item references (including any IR 58, IR 121, IR 124, IR 125, IR 126, IR 127, IR 128 or successor reference that applies).\n2. The accession, box, shelf, or other store location used by your staff.\n3. The Discovery catalogue identifier.\n4. Whether a member of staff has physically checked that the item is in that location: yes, no, or not answered. If yes, who checked it and on what date, and which store.\n5. Whether the item is open, closed, or retained by another department, and if closed the series and the FOI route for a closed record.\n6. The systems searched, and whether a physical file or plan was retrieved rather than a catalogue-only search.\n\nI am not asking you to interpret ownership or to comment on any legal proceedings. Please treat a “not held” answer as incomplete unless you name the systems searched and whether a physical item was retrieved.\n\nPlease quote this email as the request and give the statutory deadline.\n\nRequester \n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-1a130b2a317f8aa2","subject":"Re: Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","name":"Re: Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","date":"2026-10-12T15:19:34Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a130b2a317f8aa2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5-mary-doreen-williams-death-registration-request-passed-from-vale-of-glamorgan-registration-service-on-30-september-2026","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a130b2a317f8aa2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Yes, please pass on.\nThank you.\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 12 Oct 2026, 09:35 Denham, Karen (Registrars), <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your email regarding Mary Doreen Williams\n>\n>\n>\n> 1 Cardiff Register Office does not hold the registration of death for Mary\n> Doreen Williams\n>\n> 2 The indexes that were search were FREEBMD where the reference number\n> VOLUME 28 PAGE NO 3029 comes up. Note. If you quote this to our head office\n> based in Southport they can do the certificate from there for you\n>\n>\n>\n> In 1983 South Glamorgan was a vast area so the registration could be in\n> any district. If you would like I will pass this on to our team at the\n> Glamorgan Archives and they can tell you which register office that you\n> would need to contact but advised previously it is better to get a copy of\n> the certificate from our head office as we definitely do not hold the\n> record for Mary Doreen Williams here with us in Cardiff.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n> Karen\n>\n>\n>\n> *Karen Denham*\n>\n> Dirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar &\n> Nationality Officer\n>\n> Ebost/Email: [email redacted] / [email redacted]\n>\n> Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n> www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 10 October 2026 20:14\n> *To:* Denham, Karen (Registrars)  \n> *Subject:* Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed\n> from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026\n>\n>\n>\n>  *EXTERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take\n> care when clicking links.\n>  *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch\n> ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Ms Denham,\n>\n> Mary Doreen Williams: death registration\n>\n> On 30 September 2026 the Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service told me\n> they could not find a death record for Mary Doreen Williams in the Vale,\n> and that they had passed my request to Cardiff. I have not had a reply from\n> Cardiff.\n>\n> Please could you:\n>\n> 1. confirm whether Cardiff Register Office holds a registration of death\n> for Mary Doreen Williams;\n> 2. if it does, tell me how I can obtain a certified copy and the fee; and\n> 3. if it does not, tell me which indexes and registers were searched, so\n> that I can search the GRO death index for the correct registration district.\n>\n> If you need further details to carry out the search (approximate date or\n> place of death, date of birth, last address), please tell me what you need\n> and I will supply it. I am asking as a family member and I need the\n> registration for estate administration.\n>\n> Thank you for your help.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester \n> \n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> The Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We\n> will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as\n> long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not\n> lead to delay.\n>\n> Privileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If\n> you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for\n> delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this\n> message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly\n> notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your\n> employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.\n> Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not\n> relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of\n> Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail\n> sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils\n> Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other\n> than the addressee.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> Mae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog.\n> Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni\n> pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n>\n> Mae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y\n> neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r\n> neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges.\n> Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy\n> e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi\n> neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon.\n> Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y\n> neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir\n> Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff\n> unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan\n> system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu\n> harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a130a221be37fde","subject":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","name":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","date":"2026-10-12T15:01:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a130a221be37fde.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-filtered-schedule-still-not-supplied-unanswered-points-from-foi-2026-032-correct","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a130a221be37fde.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nIn relation to the \"filtered schedule\", as previously explained, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold a separate recorded document identifying, item by item, which search results were excluded following review. The review was undertaken by staff using the records and search results identified during the handling of the request. No separate audit schedule, review log or equivalent record of exclusion decisions was created.\n\nIn relation to MS 3360/3, following further review we have confirmed that the page previously supplied does not relate to the property that was the subject of FOI 2026-036. While the document refers to a property known as \"Great House\", it relates to a holding in the Parish of Llanfair and not to Great House Farm/Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff), which was the subject of your request. The document should therefore be regarded as outside the scope of FOI 2026-036.\n\nWe do not hold any further recorded information linking MS 3360/3 to Great House Farm/Tŷ Mawr, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff).\n\nIn relation to Ref 13.2, our position remains unchanged. The collections record describes the item as a \"Waterwheel from Llandough Farm (opposite hospital)\". No further location information has been identified within that record.\n\nWe have no further recorded information to provide in relation to these matters.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n\nFOI Team\n\n[email redacted]\namgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 10 October 2026 20:14\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nDear FOI Team,\n\nFOI 2026-036 — your letter of 7 October 2026\n\nThank you. I note three points from that letter.\n\n1. You do not hold a separate recorded document listing, item by item, which search results were excluded. Please state which systems were searched for that schedule (collections database, search-export, review log, email, paper file) and whether a physical file was retrieved, and by whom and on what date. A not-held answer is incomplete without that (FOIA s.16).\n\n2. MS 3360/3: the page already supplied records Great House as part of the 1924 Llandough Estate sale particulars, occupied by W.G. Thomas & Sons, about 202 acres, Parish of Llanfair, homestead in the Village of Llandough. Please confirm whether the catalogue or the page itself names which Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth or Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge). If that is not on the page or in the catalogue entry, say so.\n\n3. Ref 13.2 is recorded as a waterwheel from Llandough Farm (opposite hospital). I treat that as the Penarth hospital site, not the farmhouse demolished on 6 December 1988, unless a further recorded field says otherwise.\n\nI am not asking for a new search or for a document you say you do not hold. I am asking for the systems searched and the physical-file check on the not-held point, and the parish identification if it is already on the page or catalogue entry.\n\nCofion,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1309dc33154ec9","subject":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","name":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","date":"2026-10-12T14:56:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1309dc33154ec9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1309dc33154ec9-allanol-external-foi-2026-024-032-036-outstanding-item-7-recorded-basis-for-treating-already-found-records-as-unrelated-","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1309dc33154ec9","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1309dc33154ec9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nIn relation to your request for the recorded basis on which records were treated as outside the scope of FOI 2026-024, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold a separate search log, file note, internal note or other recorded document setting out the rationale for that assessment.\n\nThe original response was based on searches which identified no records relating to the reported discovery described in your request, namely the alleged discovery of a soldier, horse remains and associated armour at Great House Farm, Llandough. While searches identified records relating to other archaeological finds from Church Farm and archaeological investigations at Great House Farm, staff concluded that those records did not relate to the specific discovery described in your request and therefore fell outside its scope. No separate record of that assessment was created.  We have since provided you with the records referred to as being from Church Farm.\n\nNo records remain withheld.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n\nFOI Team\n\n\n\n[email redacted]\namgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n \n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 10 October 2026 20:11\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nDear FOI Team,\n\nThank you for the disclosures under FOI 2026-032 (22 September) and\n2026-036 (5 October).\n\nOn 25 August 2026 you stated that searches had located records of “other archaeological discoveries at Great House Farm and Church Farm”\nwhich were withheld as “not in scope”. On 26 August I asked for those records and, specifically, the recorded basis for calling them unrelated (item 7).\n\nThat question remains unanswered. The later disclosures released certain Church Farm and other-site material but still did not supply the internal note, search-log entry or other record that justified the original classification.\n\nI therefore request:\n\n1. The recorded basis (search log, file note, email or other document) that led the Museum to treat the already-found Great House Farm / Church Farm records as unrelated or out of scope on 25 August 2026.\n2. If no such written basis exists, an explicit statement to that effect.\n3. Confirmation that the full set of records located in the August searches has now been disclosed or, if any remain withheld, the precise exemption relied upon for each.\n\nPlease treat this as a request for the information that should have been provided under the internal review of 2026-024. This is for the completeness of the evidence library on the public record.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a13016d4fe95bfd","subject":"RE: Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material","name":"RE: Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material","date":"2026-10-12T12:29:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a13016d4fe95bfd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eaa835381426-quest-for-any-retained-copy-of-the-1994-llandough-great-house-farm-archaeological-material","scopeTopics":["cotswold"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cotswold"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eaa835381426","direction":"received","from":"Paolo Guarino","institutions":[{"id":"cotswold","name":"Cotswold Archaeology"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a13016d4fe95bfd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester, \n\nI can see that the report is available online on the Cotswold Archaeology website. Please follow this link: https://reports.cotswoldarchaeology.co.uk/ -  select 'Keyword', enter 'Llandough' in the available field and then press 'search'. The report should appear below the map and you should see the option to download it on the right-hand side.\n\nI hope this helps,  but please let me know if you have any issues with downloading the report\n\nBest Regards\n\nPaolo\n\n\nPaolo Guarino\nPost Excavation Manager\n_______________________________________________________________________________________\nT[phone redacted]|M[phone redacted]\nABuilding 11, Cotswold Business Park, Cirencester, [postcode redacted]. \n► Access our latest monograph here — \"The Wreck of the London\", the maritime recovery of a 17th century warship.\n© Cotswold Archaeology Ltd. The contents of this email and any attached files are confidential. If you have received this in error please delete it and notify the sender. \nRegistered Company: (England) 2362531. Registered Charity: 1001653. Registered Office: Building 11, Cotswold Business Park, Cirencester, Gloucestershire, [postcode redacted]. \n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: enquiries <[email redacted]> \nSent: 12 October 2026 12:59\nTo: Publications managers <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FW: Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]> \nSent: 10 October 2026 20:14\nTo: enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material\n\nDear Cotswold Archaeology,\n\nA preservation notice has already been served. I request confirmation whether you hold any retained copy of the 1994 early-medieval cemetery excavation archive or report relating to the redevelopment of land formerly part of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and, if so, the terms on which a copy may be obtained.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , "},{"id":"gm-1a12fa8ff526287b","subject":"RE: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","name":"RE: FOI 1264/26 - non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","date":"2026-10-12T10:29:20Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12fa8ff526287b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a12fa8ff526287b-foi-1264-26-non-personal-operational-records-concerning-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-november-december-1988","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a12fa8ff526287b","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["1264/26","719/26","FOI1264"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12fa8ff526287b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThank you for your email pertaining to FOI request 1264/26.\n\nA response will be provided to yourself within 20 working days, the deadline for which is 09/11/2026.\n\nKind Regards,\n\n\n\n\n\nOwen Byrne\n\n\n\nSwyddog Cymorth Ymchwil a Datgelu| Research and Data Quality Officer\n\n\n\nRheolwr Rheoli Data a Datgeliadau | Data Management and Disclosure Unit\n\n\n\nPencadlys Heddlu De Cymru | South Wales Police Headquarters\n\n\n\n\n: [phone redacted] | Ext: 26660\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:14\nTo: Freedom of Information <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI/EIR request — non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988\n\nDear South Wales Police Information Rights Team,\n\nPlease treat this as a request under the Freedom of Information Act\n2000 for recorded information, excluding personal data and excluding any material for which the appropriate handling route is the separate subject-access request already open. The site is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church, Cardiff (approx. ST 168 733), and the period is 1 November to 31 December 1988 inclusive.\n\nPlease search the relevant South Wales Constabulary / predecessor-force and successor holdings, including any transferred records available to the Force, for existing non-personal records that refer to the site or the events associated with its possession and demolition. Relevant record types, if held, include:\n1. incident or occurrence logs and control-room records; 2. deployment, duty or operational logs and any record identifying whether officers attended; 3. correspondence between police, the local authority, landowner/developer, court enforcement officers or other public bodies about the site; 4. any recorded liaison or request for police assistance connected with possession, eviction, demolition, public order or the handling of complaints; and 5. records-transfer, retention or disposal entries for the relevant operational record series, if the responsive records are no longer held.\n\nI am not asserting that a police deployment or a particular incident record necessarily exists. If no responsive record is located, please state that result and identify, so far as reasonably practicable, the record systems, index/series, date range and site/name variants searched. Please distinguish “not found in the systems searched” from a contemporaneous record showing that a file was destroyed or transferred. If transferred, please identify the receiving repository and reference where recorded. If any information is withheld, identify the specific statutory basis and release reasonably separable non-exempt information.\n\nThe existing SAR and internal review under ref. 719/26 are separate processes. If a record contains personal data, please do not disclose it through this FOI route; please identify it only as necessary to explain the FOIA decision and continue to handle personal data through the live SAR. This FOI request is not asking South Wales Police to determine ownership or to decide whether an offence occurred.\n\nPlease confirm receipt, the request reference, and the statutory response date.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a12f9954040af76","subject":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","name":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","date":"2026-10-12T10:12:17Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12f9954040af76.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd-your-communication-with-companies-house-ref-coh2382411x","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[],"refs":["COH2382411X"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12f9954040af76.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Customer,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nPlease find the following links for the dissolved companies\n\nWESTERN GROUND RENTS LIMITED\nCompany number 09760885\nWESTERN GROUND RENTS LIMITED filing history - Find and update company information - GOV.UK<https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/09760885/filing-history>\n\nBP PROPERTIES LIMITED\nCompany number 00699446\nBP PROPERTIES LIMITED filing history - Find and update company information - GOV.UK<https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/00699446/filing-history?page=8>\n\nPERSIMMON HOMES (WALES) LIMITED\nCompany number 00461464\nPERSIMMON HOMES (WALES) LIMITED overview - Find and update company information - GOV.UK<https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/00461464>\n\n\nFree access to digital company data and images is available from the Companies House Service: https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/<https://beta.companieshouse.gov.uk/>.\n\nAlternatively, any document can be accessed from the Companies House records.  However, there is an administration charge to cover costs.\n\nThe charge for a search is as follows:\n\n£3 per document required. This can be posted or emailed.\n\n£3 for a list of past and present directors. This list would not contain resignations prior to 1991.\n£3 for a list of mortgage/charge/debent"},{"id":"gm-1a12f9732739a69e","subject":"RE: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","name":"RE: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","date":"2026-10-12T10:09:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12f9732739a69e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad-icr-090-26-further-formal-points-on-the-first-registration-file-and-1987-amalgamation","scopeTopics":["hmlr-icr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr-icr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad","direction":"received","from":"ICR Office Inbox","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr-icr","name":"HM Land Registry (Independent Complaints Reviewer)"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12f9732739a69e.json","attachments":[{"name":"ICR09026-Blank letter R7-01102026.pdf","title":"ICR09026-Blank letter R7-01102026.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/2026-10-09_icr_hmlr-complaint-icr-090-26-letter.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":169508,"sha256":"84e36c1dfc1588f0d14656a0ca1cc546519d3b0447160d049b3a122795e8b5a5"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester \n\nThank you for your email. \n\nIt appears that you have not received my letter dated 9 October 2026 which I sent on the same date. Therefore, please find that letter attached.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nDenyse St Rose\nOffice Manager and Investigations Officer\nICR Office\n\n10 South Colonnade\nCanary Wharf, London [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted] (Telephone number)\nwww.icrev.org.uk\n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester   \nSent: 10 October 2026 20:12\nTo: ICR Office Inbox  \nSubject: ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation\n\nDear Independent Complaints Reviewer,\n\nReference ICR/090/26.\n\nI hold the stage-one decision of 19 April 2026 and the stage-two decision of 25 May 2026. I also hold the schedule of 43 documents on the first-registration files released on 30 July 2026.\n\nThe family’s established case, recorded on the public wiki and under investigation, is that the 1877 arrangement took effect in 1928, transferring the full Parcel A (house and buildings, barn, stable and west-side yard, garden, northern forest and the south-east ground later registered as VG41) to the Williams family. The 1939 agreement/plan depicts Parcel B only. On the family account, the 1949 attempt to make the occupation of Parcel A permissive failed, title papers were reported missing in 1950–52, and Western Ground Rents’ 4 July 1955 enforcement of Parcel B also seized the Parcel-A forest and green under “whole farm” wording. Later documentary work is directed at corroborating or precisely mapping that account and tracing those areas into later titles.\n\nFour specific points remain unanswered and are relevant to that investigation:\n\n1. The 1969 root deed recited as the root of title does not appear on the schedule. Please confirm whether HMLR holds that deed under any other reference, or whether it was never lodged.\n2. What evidence exists on the file of notice or opportunity to object given to the occupying family (Williams / Buckler) in 1982–83.\n3. The precise legal and administrative basis for the 1987 title amalgamation that took place while the Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler were still live.\n4. Whether the inclusion of the woodland (or any land beyond the 1938\nconveyance) is regarded as a possible mistake capable of alteration or indemnity under the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice Guide 39.\n\nPlease confirm these points form part of the live investigation and state the exact start date of the ICR six-month period (so that the\n~25 November 2026 outer limit can be verified).\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12f404420e3087","subject":"RE: Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","name":"RE: Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","date":"2026-10-12T08:34:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12f404420e3087.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5-mary-doreen-williams-death-registration-request-passed-from-vale-of-glamorgan-registration-service-on-30-september-2026","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5","direction":"received","from":"Denham, Karen (Registrars)","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12f404420e3087.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\nThank you for your email regarding Mary Doreen Williams\n\n1 Cardiff Register Office does not hold the registration of death for Mary Doreen Williams\n2 The indexes that were search were FREEBMD where the reference number VOLUME 28 PAGE NO 3029 comes up. Note. If you quote this to our head office based in Southport they can do the certificate from there for you\n\nIn 1983 South Glamorgan was a vast area so the registration could be in any district. If you would like I will pass this on to our team at the Glamorgan Archives and they can tell you which register office that you would need to contact but advised previously it is better to get a copy of the certificate from our head office as we definitely do not hold the record for Mary Doreen Williams here with us in Cardiff.\n\nKind Regards\nKaren\n\nKaren Denham\nDirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar & Nationality Officer\nEbost/Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nFfon/Tel: [phone redacted]\nwww.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk<http://www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:14\nTo: Denham, Karen (Registrars) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\nDear Ms Denham,\n\nMary Doreen Williams: death registration\n\nOn 30 September 2026 the Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service told me they could not find a death record for Mary Doreen Williams in the Vale, and that they had passed my request to Cardiff. I have not had a reply from Cardiff.\n\nPlease could you:\n\n1. confirm whether Cardiff Register Office holds a registration of death for Mary Doreen Williams;\n2. if it does, tell me how I can obtain a certified copy and the fee; and\n3. if it does not, tell me which indexes and registers were searched, so that I can search the GRO death index for the correct registration district.\n\nIf you need further details to carry out the search (approximate date or place of death, date of birth, last address), please tell me what you need and I will supply it. I am asking as a family member and I need the registration for estate administration.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a12c11105793977","subject":"In Touch with Llandough!","name":"In Touch with Llandough!","date":"2026-10-11T17:44:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12c11105793977.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a12c11105793977-in-touch-with-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a12c11105793977","direction":"received","from":"Cllr George Carroll","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12c11105793977.json","textStatus":"available","text":"View this email in your browser (https://mailchi.mp/237c8aa90f9a/in-touch-with-llandough-17666381?e=1429c2c1bb)\nUPDATE: FIREWORKS\nRESPONSE FROM POLICE AND COUNCIL\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDear Requester\n\nFireworks continue to cause unacceptable noise disturbances in our community.\n\nI raised the issue at Full Council on Monday, emphasising the importance of both the Council and the Police working together.\n\nYou can watch my comments here.  (https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1JExrTZK3w/)\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/v/1JExrTZK3w/\n\nOn Wednesday, our village experienced another incident.\n\nIt is clear neither the police nor the Vale of Glamorgan Council have taken sufficient action to date to address this problem.\n\nBoth authorities have failed to fulfill their duties to protect our community.\n\nI've written to both authorities to raise serious concerns.\n\nYou can read my letter below.\nFAO: South Wales Police\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n\n8th October 2026\n\n\nDear both\n\nIllegal firework usage in Llandough\n\nI’m saddened to report that another firework related incident took place in Llandough last night.\n\nThis is impacting some of the most vulnerable members of our community, causing distress to the elderly, small children and animals.\n\nIt is apparent that those responsible for setting off fireworks are not residents and instead come into the community from outside.\n\nA lack of action to date is sending a message to those responsible that their behaviour is acceptable and will be tolerated.\n\nThere have been several instances in which fireworks have been set off past 11.00pm at night, in direct contravention of the law. There may also be other laws and regulations that have been broken.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if you would:\n\n- Outline full details of all firework-related incidents in the Llandough ward reported to your respective authorities within the past 24 months;\n\n- Confirm all actions that were taken following those incidents to address the problems reported;\n\n- Outline all actions proposed by your authorities to prevent inappropriate firework usage in the Llandough ward in future;\n\n- Confirm all measures available to your respective authorities to detain and apprehend the individuals responsible for inappropriate firework usage in the Community of Llandough as well as any restrictions that may be imposed to prohibit those individuals from entering the Community boundary; and\n\n- Confirm details of any powers conferred on your respective authorities which enable you to introduce additional regulations or byelaws to impose stricter restrictions prohibiting firework usage within the Community of Llandough.\n\nI have not copied this message to our PSCOs because they are not responsible for operational decisions, and as such it would be unfair to attribute blame to them for the failure to address this problem.\n\nHowever, I reiterate my request for your respective authorities to meet with me at the earliest convenience to discuss this ongoing problem, with an invitation also extended to our PCSOs.\n\nThank you for your consideration of this matter, and I look forward to your prompt response.\n\nKind regards,\n\nCllr George Carroll\nElected member\n\nLlandough ward\nVale of Glamorgan Council\nI'm pleased to report both authorities responded promptly.\n\nThe Police have confirmed a Problem Oriented Police Plan is being developed in conjunction with our PCSOs.\n\nThe Inspector has confirmed he'll update me in due course, with further escalation promised if this proves insufficient.\n\nThe Council too have agreed to take part in a multi-agency meeting to address the problem.\n\nThe time for discussion has long passed.\n\nWe need to see surveillance and enforcement, so that those responsible for these disturbances know their behaviour will not be tolerated.\n\nAs a community, it's vital we keep up the pressure.\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNEXT WEEK: Penlan Road\ntemporary traffic lights\n\nTemporary traffic lights will be in place on Penlan Road on Tuesday 13th October to allow for Welsh Water works to be carried out safely.\n\nThey will operate from 9.30am to 2.30pm.\n\nThe lights will be situated outside the Memorial Hall, with Spencer Drive and Cogan Pill Road also impacted.\n\nThe bus stops outside the Hall will be suspended due to proximity to the works.\n\nAccess will be maintained for residents at all times.\n\nIf anyone has further questions, please let me know.\n\nPlease see below for further information.\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Eqf5imB1i/\n\nLlandough Hospital meadow\n\nI've received many enquiries about the Llandough Hospital meadow, access to which has been restricted.\n\nI've contacted the Health Board about this, as I know many residents enjoy using this route.\n\nThey've confirmed it has been fenced off as a temporary measure following misuse of the site.\n\nThey do not intend to close it permanently, but have restricted access while safety arrangements are reviewed.\n\nA fortnight ago, I requested a likely timescale.\n\nThe person I spoke with said they were unable to provide one at present, but said they'd request an update.\n\nI've chased them on this.\n\nIf anyone has further questions, please let me know.\n\nThe meadow has been a good benefit to our community and I’m pressing for it to be opened again as soon as possible.\n\nPenarth Road water leak\n\nProblems like the Penarth Road water leak require different agencies to work together.\n\nThe manhole from which the water is emanating is BT's responsibility, but the fault causing the leak is Welsh Water's responsibility.\n\nThe Council is in charge of highway safety, so they must make sure the algae forming in the discharge is cleared to prevent a slip hazard.\n\nAll responsible bodies must work together to fulfil their responsibilities, rather than blame each other.\n\nI emphasised this to the Council this week.\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/19dhRQfogP/\n\nChristmas Fayre\nSaturday 14th November\n\nLlandough’s annual Christmas Fayre is set to take place on Saturday 14th November.\n\nWith many local businesses operating stalls, it’s a great way to make a start to your Christmas shopping and support our local economy.\n\nHuge thanks to Llandough Community Council for organising, it’s always a great event and this year promises to be no different.\n\nFurther details can be found above.\n\nCommunity drop-in event:\n20th October\n\nOur next community drop-in event takes place at the Merrie Harrier on 20th October.\n\nLike the last one, it'll start at 7.00pm.\n\nThe pub is a key asset to our community.\n\nTracey and the team do a lot for us - help return the favour by lending them your support.\n\nYou can see some of their midweek offers below!\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/1EM9z5wbMs/\n\nOur Plan for Llandough!\n\n\nAs your councillor, I'm working with you all to secure a better future for Llandough. Together, we have a plan to deliver for the village.\n\nOur plan is making Llandough better by:\n\n1. Sorting out the parking problems\n2. Stamping out dog fouling\n3. Repairing our roads\n4. Stopping littering and flytipping\n5. Delivering better sports facilities\n6. Keeping the whole community involved\n\nIf you have any suggestions of what you'd like to see in Our Plan, please get in touch!\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F237c8aa90f9a%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666381 Share (http://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F237c8aa90f9a%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666381)\nhttps://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=e9a2251b74&e=1429c2c1bb Forward (https://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=e9a2251b74&e=1429c2c1bb)\n\n============================================================\nI'm hoping to reach as many people as possible with this newsletter, so please feel free to forward it to friends and neighbours.\n\nIf this email has been forwarded to you, and you would like to sign up to my newsletter, please click ** here ([email redacted]\n.\nThis email was sent to you because your email address is on my subscribers list. If you don't want to receive any more messages from me, please click below to unsubscribe.\n\nYour consent was previously given during an online or offline interaction with me or the Conservatives. If you feel this is incorrect or would like to comment, please contact me. I do not buy email lists.\n\nPromoted by Chris Kirkham on behalf of George Carroll, both of Vale of Glamorgan Conservatives, Holton House, 50 Holton Road, Barry [postcode redacted].\n\nThis email was sent to [email redacted] ([email redacted]\nwhy did I get this? (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/about?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=e9a2251b74)     unsubscribe from this list (***REDACTED***     update subscription preferences (https://facebook.us19.list-manage.com/profile?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=daad00f7e3&e=1429c2c1bb&c=e9a2251b74)\nPolitician . Unit 5 Pro Copy Business Centre . Parc Ty Glas . Cardiff, Crf [postcode redacted] . USA"},{"id":"gm-1a12ad2c5353945c","subject":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"RE: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-11T11:56:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12ad2c5353945c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"received","from":"Langridge-Thomas, James","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12ad2c5353945c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for your e-mail below and your request for Scrutiny to consider the topic suggested as part of it's Task and Finish work.\n\nUnfortunately, on this occasion we will be unable to consider the request for several reasons:\n\n1. The purpose of Task and Finish is to review existing policy Council considerations and identify areas for future policy direction at a strategic level impacting on a county wide basis. These topics are purposefully strategic in manner, and are based upon areas that Committees determine to have the most positive impact.\n\n2. In addition to the above, the purpose of Scrutiny is not to review evidence related to individual historical decisions and make subsequent recommendations, particularly related to planning, which should be navigated through other channels.\n\n3. We are aware through other correspondence to which you have copied us into that there are ongoing concerns being raised through a variety of channels including Welsh Government, CADW, MSs and MPs, and as such it would not be appropriate for a Scrutiny Task and Finish to add an additional layer of stakeholders and complexity in exploring the issues; notwithstanding points 1 and 2 raised.\n\nKind Regards,\nJames\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 October 2026 20:15\nTo: Democratic <[email redacted]>\nCc: FOI Unit <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough\n\nDemocratic and Scrutiny Services\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n[email redacted]\n\ncc: [email redacted] (for information only — this is not a new FOI request)\n\nDear Democratic and Scrutiny Services,\n\nScrutiny Topic Suggestion / request for a focused Task and Finish Review\n\nI am a resident with a long-standing family connection to Great House Farm (Tÿ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth. A public documentary archive of the site is maintained at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nI request that the Council consider a focused Scrutiny Topic Suggestion leading to a Task and Finish Review (or other appropriate scrutiny mechanism) concerning the Council-held planning, heritage, environmental and public-authority record relating to Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr / Church View Close.\n\nProposed scope (within the Council’s remit):\n\n• the Council-held planning, heritage, environmental and public-authority record relating to Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr / Church View Close; • the chronology of Council decisions, records and responses from the mid-twentieth century onwards; • identification of missing, contradictory or unresolved Council-held records and, where appropriate, referral to the body with the relevant jurisdiction; • consideration of the site’s heritage and historical record, including its proposed interpretation in the Tÿ Mawr replica museum project in Puerto Madryn, Chubut; and • recommendations within the Council’s powers, without asking the Council to determine private title, criminal liability or matters reserved to courts or other public bodies.\n\nThis is an evidence-review and accountability route. It is not a request for the Council to decide private title or liability.\n\nI am happy to complete the online Scrutiny Topic Suggestion Form if preferred, or to supply any further information the Democratic Services team requires.\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt and indicate the process and timescale for consideration.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12a57b87f563cc","subject":"Re: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — request for information under FOIA 2000 / EIR 2004","name":"Re: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — request for information under FOIA 2000 / EIR 2004","date":"2026-10-11T09:42:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12a57b87f563cc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0c1e36871ebfd1-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-request-for-information-under-foia-2000-eir-2004","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0c1e36871ebfd1","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12a57b87f563cc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email of  21 September 2026 making a request for \ninformation.\n\nWe are treating your correspondence as a request for information under \nthe Freedom of Information Act 2000 (the act).\n\nUnder the provisions of the act and as defined by \"The Freedom of \nInformation and Data Protection (Appropriate Limit and Fees) Regulations \n2004\" (the regulations) , an authority is not obliged to comply with a \nrequest for information if the authority estimates that the cost of \ncomplying with the request would exceed the \"appropriate limit\".  This \nappropriate limit is set by the regulations at £450 for our type of \nauthority.\n\nIn the regulations our staff time is valued at £25 per hour.  This has \nthe effect of imposing a time limit of 18 hours of staff time for \nactivities specified in the regulations.\n\n  The regulations make the following activities by an authority countable \ntowards the cost limit.\n\n  \t* determining whether it holds the information,\n\n  \t* locating the information, or a document which may contain the \ninformation,\n\n  \t* retrieving the information, or a document which may contain the \ninformation, and\n\n  \t* extracting the information from a document containing it.\n\n  We have estimated the time and therefore costs as provided by the \nregulations, and in doing so have taken into account the above \nactivities.\n\n  We estimate that this work will take in excess of 18 hours of effort by \nour staff. As we have a significant amount of documents on file from the \nperiod 2002-2016 where minutes are in documents rather than published on \nthe website or in archives.\n\n  We estimate this will exceed the limit provided for by the regulations \nand therefore your request is refused on the grounds provided for under \nsection 12 of the act.\n\nOur estimate of time is based on the requirement to search all minutes \nof the council and its committees for a period of 14 years. It is \nestimated that it will take about 20 minutes to read each set of minutes \nof which there are estimated to 224 sets of minutes. It is considered \nthat this is likely to take about 10 minutes to assess each set of \nminutes a total of over 2240 minutes which equates to 37 hours.\n\n  We may may be able to provide some information if you are able to \nreduce or refine your request to bring the cost of compliance under the \nregulations limit.  We suggest that you could limit the time frame of \nminutes that we would need to look through. For example 2002-2006.\n\n  Please contact us if you would like to refine your request.\n\n  If you are not satisfied with this response or you wish to complain \nabout any aspect of the handling of your request, then you should \ncontact us in the first instance and we will undertake an internal \nreview.\n\n  If after the internal review you wish to complain further then you can \ncomplain to the Information Commissioners Office http://www.ico.gov.uk \n[1] and request a decision notice.\n\nThe other matters you include in your email will be considered at the \nOctober meeting of the council and I will let you have the views of the \ncouncil after the meeting.\n\n  Kind regards,\n---\nPaul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n\nClerk to Llandough Community Council,\n\n[address removed]\n\nVale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone [phone redacted]\n\nWebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [2]\n\nWhen you contact us\n\nThe information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\nemail address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\nto enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\ninformation and/or access our facilities and services.\n\nYour personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \nthird party. Your information may however be published in the public \ndomain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n\nFor further information please see our full privacy notice on our \nwebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [2]\n\nThe Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \nour identity' The Council will always strive to:\n\n  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n\n· Be accountable in all our council activities\n\n· Be responsive to the needs of the community\n\n· Encourage community participation\n\nOn 2026-09-21 03:59, Requester wrote:\n\n> Dr Misra,\n> \n> Thank you for replying, and for doing so promptly and at a weekend. \n> Good drills Sir. What an honour. I know you and the Council serve as \n> volunteers, and I am grateful for the time.\n> \n> Let me set out plainly what I am asking of the Council, which is \n> narrow. If you'll allow me?\n> \n> I am not asking your Council to revisit Mr Egan's answer of 14 June \n> 2026. He explained that the minute books from 1982 onwards were \n> deposited with Glamorgan Archives in 2002, and I am pursuing those \n> there.\n> \n> What I am asking about is what that answer did not cover. Llandough \n> Community Council is a public authority under Schedule 1, Part II, \n> paragraph 7(b) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000. The Act applies \n> to the recorded information set out below generally; the Environmental \n> Information Regulations 2004 apply in addition to any part of it that \n> is environmental information.\n> \n> PART ONE -- REQUEST FOR RECORDED INFORMATION\n> \n> 1. Whether the Council holds any recorded information created after the \n> 2002 deposit -- minutes, correspondence, reports, emails, photographs \n> or files of any kind -- concerning Great House Farm (Ty Mawr) / Church \n> View Close, the village green in front of St Dochdwy's including \n> registered green VG 41, or the roadside verge by the churchyard wall.\n> \n> 2. Whether the Council holds any photographs, postcards or images of \n> the farm, the barn, the green or the church surroundings, of any date.\n> \n> 3. Whether the Council holds any recorded information showing what, if \n> anything, transferred to it from Penarth Town Council at the 1982 \n> reorganisation, and any recorded information identifying where the \n> pre-1982 Llandough community records were deposited.\n> \n> If the answer to any of these is that no such information is held, I \n> would be content with a short statement to that effect -- but I do need \n> it stated. Section 1(1)(a) of the Act requires the Council to confirm \n> or deny whether the information is held.\n> \n> Section 10 (and regulation 5 of the EIR) allows twenty working days \n> from receipt, which on my request of 20 September 2026 I calculate as \n> 16 October 2026.\n> \n> If the Council is refusing, section 17 (and regulation 14) requires a \n> written refusal notice identifying the exemption or exception relied \n> on; section 17(7) requires the Council to give particulars of any \n> complaints procedure it operates, or to state that it has none, and to \n> notify me of my right to apply to the Information Commissioner; and \n> regulation 11 gives a right to an internal review of any refusal under \n> the EIR.\n> \n> \"We have nothing more to add\" does not meet those requirements. If the \n> period passes without a compliant response I will have no option but to \n> complain to the Information Commissioner.\n> \n> PART TWO -- MATTERS FOR THE COUNCIL'S DISCRETION\n> \n> These are not part of the request above and carry no deadline. They are \n> simply things I would be grateful for.\n> \n> A. I am not asking for the name or contact details of any individual. I \n> am asking whether the Council would be willing to pass my details to \n> any former member, former clerk or long-standing resident who might \n> remember the village between the 1950s and the 1990s, leaving it \n> entirely to them whether to contact me. I appreciate the Council may \n> have data protection or administrative reasons for declining, and I \n> would not press it.\n> \n> B. Whether the Council would be willing to table this correspondence at \n> a meeting and minute it. I am content for it to be tabled in full.\n> \n> C. Whether the Council would consider, in due course, whether an \n> interpretation board or a plaque near the green would be appropriate. \n> The excavation on the land beneath Church View Close recorded 1,026 \n> burials, described in the published report as by far the largest early \n> medieval burial population so far recovered from Wales, above a Roman \n> villa and an Iron Age roundhouse. That history belongs to Llandough as \n> much as to my family, and there is nothing on the ground that records \n> it. I would be glad to give the Council or the community a short talk \n> on the documentary record, without charge, if that would be useful.\n> \n> I should be grateful for a response to items 1 to 3 by 16 October 2026.\n> \n> Regards,\n> \n> Requester \n> \n> \n> On Sun, 20 Sept 2026, 18:31 Mo Misra, <[email redacted]> \n> wrote:\n> \n>> Dear Requester,\n>> \n>> Thanks for your email of 20th September 2026.\n>> \n>> I note that our Clerk, Paul Egan, has already directed you to all the\n>> information we have on the matter as indicated in paragraph 6 of your\n>> email.\n>> \n>> We have nothing more to add.\n>> \n>> Best regards\n>> \n>> Dr M C Misra,\n>> Chair Llandough Community Council\n\n\nLinks:\n------\n[1] http://www.ico.gov.uk/\n[2] http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk"},{"id":"gm-1a12773fe97fcf89","subject":"Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","name":"Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","date":"2026-10-10T20:14:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12773fe97fcf89.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988-personal-research","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71","direction":"received","from":"Viewers Requests","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12773fe97fcf89.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Viewer Requests\n\n-This is an automated response-\n\nThank you for your email to ITV Viewers Requests - this service is only for\nviewers wishing to obtain copies of ITV programmes past and present.\n\nFor any other query or questions about ITV or its content please contact\nour\n\nViewer Services team at:  [email redacted] , who will be very happy\nto answer your enquiry.\n\n\n   -\n\n   For copies of ITV programmes please complete the following viewer\n   request order form.\n\n\n\n   -\n\n   Only digital files of the programmes can be supplied (no DVDs etc)\n\n\n\n   -\n\n   All orders are subject to payment, to cover the cost to supply the\n   content -\n\n\nPrice List Per Programme\n\nUp to 15 mins: £70\n\nUp to 30 mins £95\n\nUp to 60 mins £145\n\nUp to 90 mins £195\n\nOver 90 mins £245\n\nPlease note that due to the large volume of requests only fully completed\nforms will be accepted and only complete programmes can be supplied (not\nclips of programmes)\n\n\n\nViewers Request Form (Please click and complete)\n<https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeYsGJiLW2WZND1dioj56n4iSAln1uhkXJ2XTs0tnNXlgv0aw/viewform?usp=sf_link>\n\n\n\nThank You\n\nITV Viewer Requests\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \nViewers Requests | *ITV plc*\n[email redacted]\n\nITV plc Head Office Tel [phone redacted] itv.com <http://www.itv.com/>\n\nPlease consider the environment before printing this email\n\n-- \n <https://www.itv.com/>\n\n\n\nITV plc (Registration No. 4967001) (ITV) is \nincorporated in England and Wales with its registered office at ITV White \nCity, 201 Wood Lane, London [postcode redacted]. Please visit www.itv.com \n<http://www.itv.com/> for further information.\n\nThis email and any \nattachments are intended solely for the addressee and may contain \nconfidential, copyrighted and/or privileged information.  If you have \nreceived this message in error, please notify us and delete it.  Recipients \nshould scan the email and any attachments for their own protection. \n\nThis \nemail does not conclude a binding agreement.  The views or opinions \npresented in this email do not necessarily represent those of ITV.\n\nWe \nreserve the right to monitor all e-mail communications, as permitted by \napplicable law and regulations.\n\n\n\nFor details of how we process personal \ndata, please see the privacy notices for each of ITV's business areas at \nhttp://www.itv.com/groupprivacy <http://www.itv.com/groupprivacy>"},{"id":"gm-1a12773e9d5ce9a8","subject":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","name":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988 (personal research)","date":"2026-10-10T20:14:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12773e9d5ce9a8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988-personal-research","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12773e9d5ce9a8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear ITV Viewers Requests,\n\nI am researching the events surrounding Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church, Cardiff (approx. ST 168 733). Demolition of the farmhouse reportedly began on 6 December 1988. I already hold a partial clip and am trying to identify the complete surviving ITV news item/programme and any associated production record.\n\nPlease search, or advise how best to search, ITV’s archive for regional or national news coverage filmed or transmitted in late November and December 1988 concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, farmhouse possession/demolition, or the adjoining site. Relevant records may be indexed by the demolition, local authority, land dispute or reporter rather than the farm name.\n\nIf a match is found, please provide:\n1. programme/news-item title, transmission date/time, regional service and archive reference;\n2. whether a complete transmitted segment, original camera footage/rushes, outtakes, narration/script, running order, transmission log or production correspondence survives;\n3. available duration/format and whether a viewing or research copy can be supplied;\n4. cost, lead time, rights/licensing terms and any limits on personal research use; and\n5. if no match is found, the index searched and any alternative archive or successor custodian you recommend.\n\nI am not asking for a determination of title or permission to republish without the appropriate rights. I am seeking to identify and preserve the source record for personal historical research, and can provide the partial clip’s details if that will assist the search.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12773e4fb72e7c","subject":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","name":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","date":"2026-10-10T20:14:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12773e4fb72e7c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11b2364b1e069e-great-house-farm-suspected-historic-fraud","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11b2364b1e069e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12773e4fb72e7c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Victim Liaison Cymru,\n\nThank you for your email of 8 October 2026 acknowledging receipt of my 30 September correspondence and confirming it has been passed to a CPS manager.\n\nI note the apology for the delay in acknowledgement. Please keep me informed of any further progress or if additional information is required.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12773e2d476f70","subject":"Re: Enquiry — does D153/1–8 contain a c.1875–1880 Llandough-juxta-Penarth instrument?","name":"Re: Enquiry — does D153/1–8 contain a c.1875–1880 Llandough-juxta-Penarth instrument?","date":"2026-10-10T20:14:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12773e2d476f70.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ac815c712ae7c-enquiry-does-d153-1-8-contain-a-c-1875-1880-llandough-juxta-penarth-instrument","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ac815c712ae7c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12773e2d476f70.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Louise Hunt,\n\nThank you for your email of 6 October 2026 (ref 2026/4274).\n\nI note that D153/1–8 is held at the National Library of Wales and will pursue that route with them. I also note your clarification that DRA/11/120 (formerly D/DRa 11/120) relates to Elder’s Navigation Colliery, Maesteg, and is not relevant to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth.\n\nThe reference originated from earlier research notes; I will not pursue it further with Glamorgan Archives.\n\nThank you for the clear direction.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12773e24efe302","subject":"Re: RC26-0375 (gan gynnwys RC26-0353, -0368, a -0371) - Ty Mawr/ Great House, Llandough, Cardiff - Further response","name":"Re: RC26-0375 (gan gynnwys RC26-0353, -0368, a -0371) - Ty Mawr/ Great House, Llandough, Cardiff - Further response","date":"2026-10-10T20:14:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a12773e24efe302.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11178b91ab138c-rc26-0375-gan-gynnwys-rc26-0353-0368-a-0371-ty-mawr-great-house-llandough-cardiff-further-response","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11178b91ab138c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0353","RC26-0375"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a12773e24efe302.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Adam Coward,\n\nThank you for your detailed further response of 6 October 2026 under RC26-0375.\n\nI note the confirmation of the extensive searches undertaken, the nil returns on internal administrative records, the identification of the publicly accessible NMR items, and the offer of fee-waived scans for Archive 6048945.\n\nI will review the points against the earlier requests and catalogue the outcome. If any residual clarification is required on a specific item, I will write separately.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273e9401107d9","subject":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","name":"Your submission to LibAnswers was received.","date":"2026-10-10T19:16:14Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273e9401107d9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273e9401107d9-your-submission-to-libanswers-was-received","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273e9401107d9","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273e9401107d9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester,\n\nYour question was submitted successfully to the National Library of Wales enquiries service / Cyflwynwyd eich cwestiwn yn llwyddiannus i Wasanaeth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru\n\nDue to high demand and some resource challenges, there may be some delay in responding to enquiries at present. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nOherwydd lefel uchel y galw a rhai heriau adnoddau, bydd oedi gydag ymateb i ymholiadau ar hyn o bryd. Yr ydym yn ymddiheuro am unrhyw anghyfleuster a achosir gan hyn ac fe fyddwn yn darparu diweddariad cyn gynted ag y medrwn.\n\nWe will contact you as soon as possible. In the meantime, perhaps you can visit our FAQs <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com>\nByddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted â phosibl! Yn y cyfamser, efallai yr hoffech chi chwlio ein  FAQs  <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com> perthnasol gall ateb eich cwestiwn.\n\n\n\nWe welcome calls and correspondence in Welsh. You will receive a response in Welsh and correspondence in Welsh will not result in a delay./ Rydym yn croesawu galwadau a gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwch yn derbyn ymateb yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nOct 10 2026, 08:14PM via Email\nRe: Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — D153/1-8 check requested\nEnquiries Service\nThe National Library of Wales\n\nFollow-up to my research enquiry of 27 September 2026 (Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219)\n\nGlamorgan Archives has told me (ref 2026/4274, 6 October 2026) that D153/1-8 are held by the Library and that I should ask you. This is a research enquiry, not a request for a reading-room booking.\n\nThe property is Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ST 168 733), adjoining St Dochdwy's churchyard. It is not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge.\n\nPlease would you check the full sequence D153/1-8, including endorsements, dockets and any attached plans, for any document dated c.1875-1880 relating to that property. The catalogue titles may not name the parties. I am looking for any agreement, lease, counterpart, award, conveyance or plan involving:\n\n- Daniel Thomas / D. Thomas & Son;\n- Llandough Limeworks;\n- John Williams or Thomas Williams;\n- the Bute Estate or the Trustees of the Marquess of Bute;\n- quarrying, minerals, lime, sidings, compensation or reparation;\n- the dwelling adjoining the churchyard (I note your catalogue entry for D153/1-2, 1811).\n\nIf such an item exists, please give the exact reference, date, document type, parties as written, property description and acreage, whether a plan is attached, and whether a copy can be supplied and at what cost.\n\nIf nothing in D153/1-8 matches, please say so, and say which other Bute series (including D219) you would check next. I have not yet had a substantive reply to my enquiry of 27 September; I would be grateful for a date by which I can expect one.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n------------------\n\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9869940.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a1273e1e7a70b6f","subject":"Automatic reply: Great House Farm, Llandough — HMLR ref N610CGV — follow-up on Ministry of Justice reply and casework log","name":"Automatic reply: Great House Farm, Llandough — HMLR ref N610CGV — follow-up on Ministry of Justice reply and casework log","date":"2026-10-10T19:15:40Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273e1e7a70b6f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273e1e7a70b6f-automatic-reply-great-house-farm-llandough-hmlr-ref-n610cgv-follow-up-on-ministry-of-justice-reply-and-casework-log","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273e1e7a70b6f","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273e1e7a70b6f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n\n• Your full postal address\n\n• Your contact telephone number\n\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in Parliament, it will be dealt with as appropriate.\n\n\nMinisterial Business\n\nIf you are contacting me in my capacity as a Minister at the FCDO, you will need to redirect your email to to [email redacted]<[email redacted]>, or alternatively contact your own MP – you can find who that is at https://members.parliament.uk/FindYourMP\n\n\nThank you for taking the time to contact me.\n\nFor information about how we use your personal data, see our Privacy Notice<https://www.stephendoughty.wales/privacynotice>.\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nStephen\n\n\nStephen Doughty MP / AS\nMember of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth // Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nHouse of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-1a1273de327c97d5","subject":"Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","name":"Scrutiny Topic Suggestion / Task and Finish request — Council-held planning, heritage and public-authority record for Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-10-10T19:15:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273de327c97d5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc-scrutiny-topic-suggestion-task-and-finish-request-council-held-planning-heritage-and-public-authority-record-for-great-h","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149d647cb33dc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273de327c97d5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Democratic and Scrutiny Services\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n[email redacted]\n\ncc: [email redacted] (for information only — this is not a new FOI request)\n\nDear Democratic and Scrutiny Services,\n\nScrutiny Topic Suggestion / request for a focused Task and Finish Review\n\nI am a resident with a long-standing family connection to Great House Farm (Tÿ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth. A public documentary archive of the site is maintained at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nI request that the Council consider a focused Scrutiny Topic Suggestion leading to a Task and Finish Review (or other appropriate scrutiny mechanism) concerning the Council-held planning, heritage, environmental and public-authority record relating to Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr / Church View Close.\n\nProposed scope (within the Council’s remit):\n\n• the Council-held planning, heritage, environmental and public-authority record relating to Great House Farm / Tÿ Mawr / Church View Close;\n• the chronology of Council decisions, records and responses from the mid-twentieth century onwards;\n• identification of missing, contradictory or unresolved Council-held records and, where appropriate, referral to the body with the relevant jurisdiction;\n• consideration of the site’s heritage and historical record, including its proposed interpretation in the Tÿ Mawr replica museum project in Puerto Madryn, Chubut; and\n• recommendations within the Council’s powers, without asking the Council to determine private title, criminal liability or matters reserved to courts or other public bodies.\n\nThis is an evidence-review and accountability route. It is not a request for the Council to decide private title or liability.\n\nI am happy to complete the online Scrutiny Topic Suggestion Form if preferred, or to supply any further information the Democratic Services team requires.\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt and indicate the process and timescale for consideration.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273de2fb6e40c","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough — HMLR ref N610CGV — follow-up on Ministry of Justice reply and casework log","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough — HMLR ref N610CGV — follow-up on Ministry of Justice reply and casework log","date":"2026-10-10T19:15:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273de2fb6e40c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11a41c4126f155-great-house-farm-llandough-hmlr-ref-n610cgv-follow-up-on-ministry-of-justice-reply-and-casework-log","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11a41c4126f155","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":["26FOI103","ICR/090/26","N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273de2fb6e40c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Doughty,\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough — HM Land Registry ref N610CGV — follow-up\n\nThank you for your office's forwarding on 18 September of the letter from HM Land Registry's Chief Executive and Chief Land Registrar. I understand your office is still waiting for a reply from the Ministry of Justice.\n\nCould your office please:\n\n1. tell me whether the Ministry of Justice has replied, and if not, when your office last chased it;\n2. confirm that my emails of 27 and 28 September 2026 have been received and logged as casework, since earlier messages were reported as not found; and\n3. let me have a caseworker's name and a direct reply address, so that I do not have to rely on the general inbox.\n\nFor your information, the Independent Complaints Reviewer has opened an investigation (ICR/090/26), the Wales Office internal review of 26FOI 103 is due by 26 October 2026, and HM Land Registry's subject access reply is due by 28 October 2026. I am not asking you to intervene in any of those processes, only to press the Ministry of Justice for the reply your office is waiting on.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273cfaf46ca4d","subject":"FOI — location only — Valuation Office Survey 1910, OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough / Great House Farm","name":"FOI — location only — Valuation Office Survey 1910, OS Glamorgan XLVII.6, Llandough / Great House Farm","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cfaf46ca4d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1060d79ae529a6-foi-location-only-valuation-office-survey-1910-os-glamorgan-xlvii-6-llandough-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1060d79ae529a6","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cfaf46ca4d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Team,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is a location request only. I am not asking for a copy of the plan, a screen-room appointment, or production of the item until the location and physical-check status are confirmed.\n\nContext. Glamorgan Archives, in reply 2026/4097b of 30 September 2026, identified Ordnance Survey sheet Glamorgan XLVII.6 as the sheet relevant to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and directed me to the Valuation Office Survey 1910-1915 maps held by The National Archives.\n\nPlease state, for the Valuation Office field book, plan, and index covering that sheet for the parish of Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan):\n\n1. The series, piece, and item references (including any IR 58, IR 121, IR 124, IR 125, IR 126, IR 127, IR 128 or successor reference that applies).\n2. The accession, box, shelf, or other store location used by your staff.\n3. The Discovery catalogue identifier.\n4. Whether a member of staff has physically checked that the item is in that location: yes, no, or not answered. If yes, who checked it and on what date, and which store.\n5. Whether the item is open, closed, or retained by another department, and if closed the series and the FOI route for a closed record.\n6. The systems searched, and whether a physical file or plan was retrieved rather than a catalogue-only search.\n\nI am not asking you to interpret ownership or to comment on any legal proceedings. Please treat a “not held” answer as incomplete unless you name the systems searched and whether a physical item was retrieved.\n\nPlease quote this email as the request and give the statutory deadline.\n\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273cf6624c0a9","subject":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","name":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cf6624c0a9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-filtered-schedule-still-not-supplied-unanswered-points-from-foi-2026-032-correct","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cf6624c0a9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,\n\nFOI 2026-036 — your letter of 7 October 2026\n\nThank you. I note three points from that letter.\n\n1. You do not hold a separate recorded document listing, item by item, which search results were excluded. Please state which systems were searched for that schedule (collections database, search-export, review log, email, paper file) and whether a physical file was retrieved, and by whom and on what date. A not-held answer is incomplete without that (FOIA s.16).\n\n2. MS 3360/3: the page already supplied records Great House as part of the 1924 Llandough Estate sale particulars, occupied by W.G. Thomas & Sons, about 202 acres, Parish of Llanfair, homestead in the Village of Llandough. Please confirm whether the catalogue or the page itself names which Llandough (Llandough-juxta-Penarth or Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge). If that is not on the page or in the catalogue entry, say so.\n\n3. Ref 13.2 is recorded as a waterwheel from Llandough Farm (opposite hospital). I treat that as the Penarth hospital site, not the farmhouse demolished on 6 December 1988, unless a further recorded field says otherwise.\n\nI am not asking for a new search or for a document you say you do not hold. I am asking for the systems searched and the physical-file check on the not-held point, and the parish identification if it is already on the page or catalogue entry.\n\nCofion,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273cf0b865c62","subject":"Location request — Llandough-juxta-Penarth parish, vestry and tithe records — Great House / Ty Mawr — not a viewing request","name":"Location request — Llandough-juxta-Penarth parish, vestry and tithe records — Great House / Ty Mawr — not a viewing request","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cf0b865c62.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1158080de15320-location-request-llandough-juxta-penarth-parish-vestry-and-tithe-records-great-house-ty-mawr-not-a-viewing-request","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1158080de15320","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cf0b865c62.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Glamorgan Archives,\n\nLocation request only. I am not asking to book a screen room.\n\nProperty: Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (not Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge). Working description, not a finding: two parcels; Mary Williams owned the house and garden parcel.\n\nPlease state whether you hold, and if so the series, accession, box, shelf and CALM reference, for:\n1. Llandough-juxta-Penarth vestry minutes and churchwardens' accounts covering 1870–1930 that name Great House, Ty Mawr, or a Williams occupier or owner;\n2. the tithe apportionment and map for the parish, and the plot number or numbers for that holding;\n3. any enclosure award for the parish that names the holding.\n\nPlease also say whether staff have physically checked that the item is in the stated place (who, date, store). If not held, name the systems searched and whether a physical file was retrieved.\n\nThis is a request for recorded information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000, s.1 and s.16.\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273cec9f65619","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cec9f65619.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a07efa0b6b10900-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a07efa0b6b10900","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cec9f65619.json","textStatus":"available","text":"HER Officer,\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough — your letter of 6 October 2026, request of 8 September 2026 (GGAT02038s)\n\nThank you. I note that you point to Archwilio record 02038s and that you will reply separately on the 19 September 2026 email.\n\nThe 8 September request asked for the HER source file, not only the online summary. Archwilio 02038s does not supply:\n1. the complete entry text on armour or medieval ironwork found under the rear wing or floor about 1880, with every source code;\n2. a copy or transcript of the RCAHMW / Suggett 1988 material on the file;\n3. any museum accession, letter, or catalogue slip naming where the ironwork went;\n4. any recorded distinction between the c.1880 rear-wing ironwork, the 1979 villa iron south of the church, and the 1994 cemetery iron girdle (Burial 631).\n\nPlease give the record location before any viewing is discussed: series, accession, box, shelf, and catalogue id for the source file behind 02038s, and whether staff physically checked that the item is there (who, date, store). I am not requesting a screen-room viewing.\n\nIf any of the four items is not held, please name the systems searched and whether the physical source file was retrieved (EIR reg.5 and reg.9; reg.14 if you refuse).\n\nPlease also give a date for the separate reply on the 19 September email. The 8 September request was answered on day 20. An extension of the 19 September points should be notified if you need beyond 20 working days from 6 October.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273ceb33ceda8","subject":"Re: Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — D153/1-8 check requested","name":"Re: Research enquiry — Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219: Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth — D153/1-8 check requested","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273ceb33ceda8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190-search-enquiry-bute-estate-records-gb-0210-bute-d153-d219-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-juxta-penarth-d153-1-8-check","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0d4d42318ac190","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273ceb33ceda8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Enquiries Service The National Library of Wales Follow-up to my research enquiry of 27 September 2026 (Bute Estate records GB 0210 BUTE / D153 / D219) Glamorgan Archives has told me (ref 2026/4274, 6 October 2026) that D153/1-8 are held by the Library and that I should ask you. This is a research enquiry, not a request for a reading-room booking. The property is Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth (ST 168 733), adjoining St Dochdwy's churchyard. It is not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge. Please would you check the full sequence D153/1-8, including endorsements, dockets and any attached plans, for any document dated c.1875-1880 relating to that property. The catalogue titles may not name the parties. I am looking for any agreement, lease, counterpart, award, conveyance or plan involving: - Daniel Thomas / D. Thomas & Son; - Llandough Limeworks; - John Williams or Thomas Williams; - the Bute Estate or the Trustees of the Marquess of Bute; - quarrying, minerals, lime, sidings, compensation or reparation; - the dwelling adjoining the churchyard (I note your catalogue entry for D153/1-2, 1811). If such an item exists, please give the exact reference, date, document type, parties as written, property description and acreage, whether a plan is attached, and whether a copy can be supplied and at what cost. If nothing in D153/1-8 matches, please say so, and say which other Bute series (including D219) you would check next. I have not yet had a substantive reply to my enquiry of 27 September; I would be grateful for a date by which I can expect one. Regards, Requester   On Sun, Sep 27, 2026 01:15 AM, Requester <[email redacted]> wrote: Enquiries Service \nThe National Library of Wales \n \nI am researching the title history of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough-juxta-Penarth, Glamorgan, adjoining St Dochdwy’s churchyard (approx. ST 167 733). \n \nGlamorgan Archives (Louise Hunt, ref. 2026/4097, 24 September 2026) has confirmed that the following references are yours, not theirs, and has directed me to you: \n \n1. D153 — Deeds relating to premises in p. Llandough, co. Glam., comprising a dwelling house adjoining the churchyard, 1811 (D153/1–2), and land (D153 onwards, including items sometimes cited as D153/4–8). \n2. D219 — Llandough manorial leases and agreements. \n3. The main Bute Estate deposit, GB 0210 BUTE (deeds to 1937; Glamorgan / Cardiff rentals). \n \nI do not ask you to adjudicate title. I ask only whether the following instruments exist in your holdings, and for catalogue references, dates, parties, acreages, and whether a plan is attached. \n \nA. The 1877 division \nDoes the Bute deposit contain a conveyance, agreement, or other instrument of about 1876–1877 by which the Marquess of Bute (or trustees) conveyed or contracted to convey the farmhouse, buildings and about 10 acres adjoining the churchyard at Llandough to Daniel Thomas (or Thomas and another), while retaining about 9 acres of agricultural land to the east? \n \nB. The 1916 agricultural tenancy \nDoes the deposit contain a yearly agricultural tenancy, or counterpart, of 1916 from the Marquess of Bute to John Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough? \nIf yes: \n- does the parcels clause describe the whole farm, or only the land Bute still owned after 1877? \n- is there a plan? \n- what acreage is stated? \n \nC. Rentals 1877–1936 for this farm \nDo Glamorgan / Cardiff / Llandough rentals in GB 0210 BUTE distinguish, after c.1877, between: \n- a house/buildings holding (Thomas / later Williams), and \n- a residual Bute field holding later passed to Western Ground Rents in 1938? \n \nD. Anything that would show the two holdings were treated as one unit again before 1938. \n \nPurpose. HM Land Registry first-registered titles WA231076 (30 November 1982) and WA240304 (23 February 1983; later amalgamated). The 1982/83 files treat the land as one farm. The family case is that Parcel A (house and about 10 acres) had already left Bute in 1877 and was not the land let in 1916, so the 1982 merged title cannot be the same unit as the 1916 tenancy. Your deeds and rentals are the estate-side evidence that can confirm or deny that. \n \nI live in Patagonia and cannot visit Aberystwyth in person in the short term. I would be grateful for: \n- catalogue references and a short description of any matching items; \n- whether copies can be supplied, and the cost; \n- if the 1916 tenancy is not in GB 0210 BUTE, any note of where Bute tenancy counterparts after 1910 were deposited. \n \nThis is a new enquiry. It is not a repeat of FOI/2026/11. Glamorgan Archives hold the 1938–44 Western Ground Rents plan/rental book (D696) and have already answered on their own Bute material. \n \nRequester Requester \n [email redacted] [phone redacted] \n \nPublic chronology and parcel statement: \n https://greathousefarmwiki. wordpress.com/the-two-parcels/ \n https://greathousefarmwiki. wordpress.com/1916-tenancy/ \n https://greathousefarmwiki. wordpress.com/land-registry- titles/"},{"id":"gm-1a1273ce9fdd7187","subject":"Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","name":"Mary Doreen Williams — death registration — request passed from Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service on 30 September 2026","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273ce9fdd7187.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5-mary-doreen-williams-death-registration-request-passed-from-vale-of-glamorgan-registration-service-on-30-september-2026","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11a41ac938b1a5","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273ce9fdd7187.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Denham,\n\nMary Doreen Williams: death registration\n\nOn 30 September 2026 the Vale of Glamorgan Registration Service told me they could not find a death record for Mary Doreen Williams in the Vale, and that they had passed my request to Cardiff. I have not had a reply from Cardiff.\n\nPlease could you:\n\n1. confirm whether Cardiff Register Office holds a registration of death for Mary Doreen Williams;\n2. if it does, tell me how I can obtain a certified copy and the fee; and\n3. if it does not, tell me which indexes and registers were searched, so that I can search the GRO death index for the correct registration district.\n\nIf you need further details to carry out the search (approximate date or place of death, date of birth, last address), please tell me what you need and I will supply it. I am asking as a family member and I need the registration for estate administration.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273cb43accb34","subject":"Welsh Government / former Welsh Office – retention and destruction schedules for pre-1997 file series (agricultural tenancy, land, rural policy)","name":"Welsh Government / former Welsh Office – retention and destruction schedules for pre-1997 file series (agricultural tenancy, land, rural policy)","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cb43accb34.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11ea981f52fcb9-welsh-government-former-welsh-office-retention-and-destruction-schedules-for-pre-1997-file-series-agricultural-tenancy-l","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11ea981f52fcb9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["26FOI103","ATISN27021","ATISN27589"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cb43accb34.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Welsh Government FOI team,\n\nI refer to the live requests ATISN 27021 and ATISN 27589 (Cadw listing material) and to the Wales Office response under 26FOI 103 / IR/26/16.\n\nSeparately from those listing-specific requests, I request under the Freedom of Information Act:\n\n1. The retention and destruction schedules (or equivalent policy documents) that applied, or still apply, to former Welsh Office / Welsh Government file series covering agricultural tenancies, land ownership or compulsory purchase, rural depopulation, or related policy in the period 1970–1997.\n2. Any recorded information identifying whether files in those series that would have related to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough-juxta-Penarth, or to the companies Western Ground Rents Ltd or BP Properties Ltd, were destroyed, transferred or retained, and if destroyed the date and authority.\n3. Confirmation of the repositories to which any surviving pre-1997 paper files from the relevant series were transferred (e.g. National Assembly / Welsh Government / The National Archives / other).\n\nThis request is distinct from ATISN 27021 and ATISN 27589 and should not be merged with them. Please confirm the statutory response date.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , "},{"id":"gm-1a1273cb2bcfb5f4","subject":"FOI/2026/09 and subsequent correspondence – thank you and one remaining point","name":"FOI/2026/09 and subsequent correspondence – thank you and one remaining point","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273cb2bcfb5f4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eaa0af2e3861-foi-2026-09-and-subsequent-correspondence-thank-you-and-one-remaining-point","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eaa0af2e3861","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273cb2bcfb5f4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear NLW FOI / Enquiries team,\n\nThank you for the internal-review outcome and the searches of the Bute Estate series (including D153 and D205).\n\nPlease confirm whether any further Bute Estate or related classmarks have been identified since the July 2026 searches that relate to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough, the 1877 agreement, the 1916 tenancy, or the 1938–39 sale.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , "},{"id":"gm-1a1273c992f2cba8","subject":"Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material","name":"Request for any retained copy of the 1994 Llandough / Great House Farm archaeological material","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c992f2cba8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eaa835381426-quest-for-any-retained-copy-of-the-1994-llandough-great-house-farm-archaeological-material","scopeTopics":["cotswold"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cotswold"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eaa835381426","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cotswold","name":"Cotswold Archaeology"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c992f2cba8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Cotswold Archaeology,\n\nA preservation notice has already been served. I request confirmation whether you hold any retained copy of the 1994 early-medieval cemetery excavation archive or report relating to the redevelopment of land formerly part of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and, if so, the terms on which a copy may be obtained.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , "},{"id":"gm-1a1273c98299ae92","subject":"FOI2026/09019 — clarification of the non-Special-Forces remainder and existing retention/search records","name":"FOI2026/09019 — clarification of the non-Special-Forces remainder and existing retention/search records","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c98299ae92.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb8cc384c312-foi2026-09019-clarification-of-the-non-special-forces-remainder-and-existing-retention-search-records","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb8cc384c312","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c98299ae92.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ministry of Defence FOI Team,\n\nI am writing about FOI2026/09019 and the related outstanding correspondence. I understand that the Ministry relied on section 23(5) in relation to Special Forces material. This message does not ask you to confirm or deny whether Special Forces information is held. I am narrowing the outstanding information request to non-Special-Forces information that can be considered separately, without prejudicing the current internal review or the related subject-access request.\n\nFor Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, and the period 1 November–31 December 1988, please disclose any recorded information held by non-Special-Forces parts of the Ministry concerning:\n1. any request, assessment or record of Military Aid to the Civil Authorities (MACA) relating to the location or relevant events;\n2. any incident, deployment, duty-log, correspondence or administrative record held by regular Army, Territorial Army or Royal Military Police units that records activity relating to that location and period; and\n3. any existing search record, case note, retention schedule, transfer list or disposal entry that explains how the non-Special-Forces portion of FOI2026/09019 was searched or what happened to potentially responsive records.\n\nPlease identify, at a level that can properly be disclosed, which non-Special-Forces departments, record systems, date ranges and catalogue/file series were searched for these points. Where responsive information is not held, please distinguish the result of a search from a record showing prior destruction, transfer or disposal; if a transfer or disposal entry exists, provide its date, reference and destination where recorded.\n\nPlease process any severable non-exempt information without treating the section 23(5) response on Special Forces as applying automatically to every non-Special-Forces record. If this narrower scope needs a new reference under your process, please tell me and register only the genuinely new element as a separate request; please do not restart or close the existing request or internal review as a result of this clarification.\n\nThis is an information request, not a request for the Ministry to decide title or the merits of any civil proceedings. It also does not ask you to disclose personal data through FOIA; the separate subject-access route remains separate.\n\nPlease confirm receipt and the applicable response date for any part registered as a new request.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273c96995be9b","subject":"Preservation / access request – historical BP Properties / BP Pension Trust files relating to Great House Farm / Llandough 1982–1988","name":"Preservation / access request – historical BP Properties / BP Pension Trust files relating to Great House Farm / Llandough 1982–1988","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:04Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c96995be9b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eaa7a327d405-preservation-access-request-historical-bp-properties-bp-pension-trust-files-relating-to-great-house-farm-llandough-1982-","scopeTopics":["linklaters"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["linklaters"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eaa7a327d405","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"linklaters","name":"Linklaters"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c96995be9b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Records / Archive team,\n\nI refer to the preservation notice already served. I now request confirmation of:\n\n1. Whether any client files, pleadings, instructions, disclosure schedules, title abstracts, HMLR correspondence or plans relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr / Llandough for the period 1982–1988 remain in your custody or have been transferred to an archive.\n2. The retention / destruction status of those files and any client/matter reference.\n\nYours sincerely,\nRequester , "},{"id":"gm-1a1273ca4744a906","subject":"Automatic reply: FOI/EIR request — non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","name":"Automatic reply: FOI/EIR request — non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273ca4744a906.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273ca4744a906-automatic-reply-foi-eir-request-non-personal-operational-records-concerning-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-november-d","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273ca4744a906","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273ca4744a906.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a1273c9321bad3b","subject":"ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding","name":"ATISN 27021 — existing records behind the 1988 listing-file disposal finding","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c9321bad3b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb8afe818123-atisn-27021-existing-records-behind-the-1988-listing-file-disposal-finding","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb8afe818123","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c9321bad3b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Cadw / Welsh Government Complaints Manager and Chief Inspector,\n\nI refer to the internal-review outcomes of 2, 10 and 29 July 2026 and the Chief Inspector’s letters of 27 August and 4 September 2026 concerning the 1988 Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr listing file for Llandough-juxta-Penarth.\n\nThe previous responses said the file had “most likely” been destroyed, that no destruction record could be found, and that Cadw could not say what retention arrangements applied 38 years ago. I am not asking you to repeat the response or recreate a record that does not exist. I ask whether any pre-existing recorded information remains that supports or qualifies the “most likely destroyed” conclusion or documents the file’s lifecycle.\n\nPlease disclose any existing file inventory, closure note, archive catalogue entry, transfer list, disposal authority, retention schedule, weeding/destruction record, archival receipt, email/minute/note recording the search or basis for the conclusion, or record showing whether the file remained held or was transferred on/after 6 December 1988. Please provide the recorded date and responsible role/unit for any documented disposal or transfer decision.\n\nIf no additional record is held, please distinguish an actual contemporaneous disposal decision/log from the present-day inability to locate the file. Identify repositories, indices and systems searched for this focused request. If any information is withheld, cite the statutory basis and disclose reasonably separable information.\n\nPlease preserve any extant records within scope while the related complaint and disclosure routes remain active. This is a request for recorded information, not a request to decide title, possession or the legal effect of the 1987 proceedings. This is a focused request for additional recorded information, not an appeal or a request to reopen the merits of the earlier complaint. If it falls outside the scope or closure status of ATISN 27021, please register it as a new FOI request, cross-reference ATISN 27021 for context, and confirm the new reference and statutory response date. If you consider the requested material already covered by the earlier request/response, please identify the precise part of the prior request/response that dealt with each category and tell me how the additional points will be handled.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273c8e61a8b71","subject":"Thank you for your email Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988","name":"Thank you for your email Re: Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988","date":"2026-10-10T19:14:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c8e61a8b71.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71-thank-you-for-your-email-re-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273c8e61a8b71","direction":"received","from":"Clipsales Mailbox","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c8e61a8b71.json","textStatus":"available","text":"This inbox is for clients wishing to licence ITV programme, sport and regional news footage, for broadcast and commercial purposes only. For personal/academic research requests, please email  [email redacted] Our stills library is represented by  Shutterstock                                                    *Important Information* The ITV Clip Sales team will try to respond to your email as quickly as possible but please note -  Emails relating to brand new projects may have a wait of up to 5 working days for a reply. Existing projects can expect up to 3 days.  Our office hours are 9am - 5pm --  Follow us on:          Registered Office: ITV Global Distribution Ltd ITV White City 201 Wood Lane London [postcode redacted] Company:    2203983  VAT Reg No: GB 197 0041 67 www.itvarchive.com   \n \n ITV plc (Registration No. 4967001) (ITV) is incorporated in England and Wales with its registered office at ITV White City, 201 Wood Lane, London [postcode redacted]. Please visit  www.itv.com  for further information. This email and any attachments are intended solely for the addressee and may contain confidential, copyrighted and/or privileged information.  If you have received this message in error, please notify us and delete it.  Recipients should scan the email and any attachments for their own protection.  This email does not conclude a binding agreement.  The views or opinions presented in this email do not necessarily represent those of ITV. We reserve the right to monitor all e-mail communications, as permitted by applicable law and regulations. For details of how we process personal data, please see the privacy notices for each of ITV's business areas at  http://www.itv.com/ groupprivac y"},{"id":"gm-1a1273c7c57cc83b","subject":"FOI/EIR request — non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","name":"FOI/EIR request — non-personal operational records concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, November–December 1988","date":"2026-10-10T19:13:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c7c57cc83b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb8e953ebec9-foi-eir-request-non-personal-operational-records-concerning-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-november-december-1988","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb8e953ebec9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c7c57cc83b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear South Wales Police Information Rights Team,\n\nPlease treat this as a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 for recorded information, excluding personal data and excluding any material for which the appropriate handling route is the separate subject-access request already open. The site is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church, Cardiff (approx. ST 168 733), and the period is 1 November to 31 December 1988 inclusive.\n\nPlease search the relevant South Wales Constabulary / predecessor-force and successor holdings, including any transferred records available to the Force, for existing non-personal records that refer to the site or the events associated with its possession and demolition. Relevant record types, if held, include:\n1. incident or occurrence logs and control-room records;\n2. deployment, duty or operational logs and any record identifying whether officers attended;\n3. correspondence between police, the local authority, landowner/developer, court enforcement officers or other public bodies about the site;\n4. any recorded liaison or request for police assistance connected with possession, eviction, demolition, public order or the handling of complaints; and\n5. records-transfer, retention or disposal entries for the relevant operational record series, if the responsive records are no longer held.\n\nI am not asserting that a police deployment or a particular incident record necessarily exists. If no responsive record is located, please state that result and identify, so far as reasonably practicable, the record systems, index/series, date range and site/name variants searched. Please distinguish “not found in the systems searched” from a contemporaneous record showing that a file was destroyed or transferred. If transferred, please identify the receiving repository and reference where recorded. If any information is withheld, identify the specific statutory basis and release reasonably separable non-exempt information.\n\nThe existing SAR and internal review under ref. 719/26 are separate processes. If a record contains personal data, please do not disclose it through this FOI route; please identify it only as necessary to explain the FOIA decision and continue to handle personal data through the live SAR. This FOI request is not asking South Wales Police to determine ownership or to decide whether an offence occurred.\n\nPlease confirm receipt, the request reference, and the statutory response date.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273c7b1a2cacf","subject":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988","name":"Archive search request — Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff — December 1988","date":"2026-10-10T19:13:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c7b1a2cacf.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb9014d1ea5f-archive-search-request-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-cardiff-december-1988","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb9014d1ea5f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c7b1a2cacf.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear ITV Archive,\n\nI am researching the events surrounding Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church, Cardiff (approx. ST 168 733). Demolition of the farmhouse reportedly began on 6 December 1988. I already hold a partial clip and am trying to identify the complete surviving ITV news item/programme and any associated production record.\n\nPlease search, or advise how best to search, ITV’s archive for regional or national news coverage filmed or transmitted in late November and December 1988 concerning Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, farmhouse possession/demolition, or the adjoining site. Relevant records may be indexed by the demolition, local authority, land dispute or reporter rather than the farm name.\n\nIf a match is found, please provide:\n1. programme/news-item title, transmission date/time, regional service and archive reference;\n2. whether a complete transmitted segment, original camera footage/rushes, outtakes, narration/script, running order, transmission log or production correspondence survives;\n3. available duration/format and whether a viewing or research copy can be supplied;\n4. cost, lead time, rights/licensing terms and any limits on personal research use; and\n5. if no match is found, the index searched and any alternative archive or successor custodian you recommend.\n\nI am not asking for a determination of title or permission to republish without the appropriate rights. I am seeking to identify and preserve the source record, and can provide the partial clip’s details if that will assist the search.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273c7920043b3","subject":"Bute X.6(12) — 1877 Bute trustee accounts/receipts and possible Great House Farm / Llandough transaction","name":"Bute X.6(12) — 1877 Bute trustee accounts/receipts and possible Great House Farm / Llandough transaction","date":"2026-10-10T19:13:56Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273c7920043b3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11eb95e6e388ee-bute-x-6-12-1877-bute-trustee-accounts-receipts-and-possible-great-house-farm-llandough-transaction","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11eb95e6e388ee","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273c7920043b3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Cardiff Central Library Local Studies / Manuscripts Team,\n\nGlamorgan Archives has advised me (email reference 2026/4097b, received 30 September 2026) that your library holds a Bute collection containing reference Bute X.6(12), described as “abstracts of payments and receipts by the trustees of the Marquis of Bute’s properties, 1877 (copy)”. I am writing to establish access to that exact item and to ask whether related Bute Estate records in the same collection may assist a targeted historical search.\n\nThe property under investigation is Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy’s Church (approx. ST 168 733), Cardiff. Please keep this distinct from the separate Llandough Farm opposite the hospital, Llandough juxta-Cowbridge, and Llandow. The historical question is whether surviving estate material in 1876–1878 records a transaction involving Daniel Thomas / D. Thomas and the Bute Estate or its trustees concerning this particular farm/defined parcel. That is a research question, not an assertion that X.6(12) necessarily concerns this property.\n\nPlease confirm:\n1. whether Bute X.6(12) is still held by Cardiff Central Library, its full item title/date coverage and any catalogue or manuscript identifier;\n2. whether the item can be inspected or copied, what the booking/form/fee conditions are, and whether a digital image of the relevant 1877 entry can be supplied;\n3. whether staff can check the entry/index for Daniel Thomas, D. Thomas, Great House Farm/Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, Llandough Limeworks, quarrying/mineral rights or a dwelling adjoining St Dochdwy’s churchyard;\n4. whether related Bute X.6 account/receipt volumes, estate ledgers, correspondence, rent/lease records, conveyances or attached maps/plans survive for 1876–1878 and can be searched; and\n5. if no relevant entry is found, which volumes/indexes were checked and whether there is a reliable route to other Cardiff Library manuscript registers or a transfer/custody record.\n\nFor any possible match, please provide the exact reference, date, parties as written, property description, amounts/transaction terms if recorded, acreage/boundaries, and whether a map or plan accompanies the entry. Please do not infer that a generic “Llandough” entry refers to this farm without a supporting description.\n\nThank you for your help. Please direct me to the correct collection custodian if Bute X.6(12) has moved or is managed elsewhere.\n\nKind regards,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a8a3ded5fd","subject":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","name":"RE: Your Communication with Companies House, Ref: COH2382411X","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a8a3ded5fd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd-your-communication-with-companies-house-ref-coh2382411x","scopeTopics":[],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":[],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1273a8a3ded5fd","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[],"refs":["COH2382411X"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a8a3ded5fd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"The Companies House Enquiries Team has received your email.\nA response will be with you shortly.\nPlease note our opening hours - Monday - Friday 08.30 - 18.00 excluding Bank Holidays\n\n\nMae Tim Ymholiadau Ty'r Cwmniau wedi derbyn eich neges e-bost.\nAnfonir ateb atoch cyn bo hir.\nNodwch ein horiau agor - Llun - Gwener 08.30 - 18.00  ac eithrio Gwyliau Banc\n\n\n[Companies House Footer Image]\n\nFor details on how your personal data is handled by Companies House, please see our privacy policy -https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/companies-house/about/personal-information-charter\n\nThis message and any attachments are intended for the persons named as addressees only and may contain confidential information. In addition they may be protected by copyright. If you receive it in error, notify us, delete it and do not make use of or copy it. You must not copy, disseminate or otherwise distribute or publish this message, except for the purposes for which this message is intended, without our consent. Please note that this e-mail has been created in the knowledge that Internet e-mail is not a 100% secure communications medium. We advise that you understand and accept this lack of security when e-mailing us. For company information, guidance and how to file documents online, please visit our website www.companieshouse.gov.uk. This message has been scanned for viruses"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a71e6cec27","subject":"RC26-0375 — order for scans: Archives 6048945, 6048943 and 6048941","name":"RC26-0375 — order for scans: Archives 6048945, 6048943 and 6048941","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a71e6cec27.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11f562b7880f36-rc26-0375-order-for-scans-archives-6048945-6048943-and-6048941","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11f562b7880f36","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0375"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a71e6cec27.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Adam / NMR Enquiries team,\n\nThank you for the further response of 6 October 2026 under RC26-0375.\n\nI note your position that the requests of 8, 15, 17 and 20 September are treated as fully answered, that searches of registered files and the NMRW archive (including term-based, spatial and manual uncatalogued checks) identified no administrative or operational records beyond the Coflein material for NPRN 20182, and that no information is being withheld.\n\nI now wish to order the free research-quality scans you indicated are available for small personal non-commercial orders of fewer than five scans:\n\n1. Archive 6048945 (Suggett post-demolition note — one page, front and back — two scans).\n2. Archive 6048943 (H. J. Thomas 1974 investigator notes / sketch plan).\n3. Archive 6048941 (ink plan with 12 December 1988 additions), if a standalone scan is available in addition to the copy reproduced in the GGAT 1990 assessment.\n\nPlease confirm the order form already supplied remains valid, or attach a fresh LES08 form, and confirm the fee waiver applies to this order.\n\nI am not reopening the FOI points treated as closed under section 21.\n\nYours faithfully,\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a47146ed2d","subject":"ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","name":"ICR/090/26 – further formal points on the first-registration file and 1987 amalgamation","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a47146ed2d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad-icr-090-26-further-formal-points-on-the-first-registration-file-and-1987-amalgamation","scopeTopics":["hmlr-icr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr-icr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef587a83fad","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr-icr","name":"HM Land Registry (Independent Complaints Reviewer)"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a47146ed2d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Independent Complaints Reviewer,\n\nReference ICR/090/26.\n\nI hold the stage-one decision of 19 April 2026 and the stage-two decision of 25 May 2026. I also hold the schedule of 43 documents on the first-registration files released on 30 July 2026.\n\nThe family’s established case, recorded on the public wiki and under investigation, is that the 1877 arrangement took effect in 1928, transferring the full Parcel A (house and buildings, barn, stable and west-side yard, garden, northern forest and the south-east ground later registered as VG41) to the Williams family. The 1939 agreement/plan depicts Parcel B only. On the family account, the 1949 attempt to make the occupation of Parcel A permissive failed, title papers were reported missing in 1950–52, and Western Ground Rents’ 4 July 1955 enforcement of Parcel B also seized the Parcel-A forest and green under “whole farm” wording. Later documentary work is directed at corroborating or precisely mapping that account and tracing those areas into later titles.\n\nFour specific points remain unanswered and are relevant to that investigation:\n\n1. The 1969 root deed recited as the root of title does not appear on the schedule. Please confirm whether HMLR holds that deed under any other reference, or whether it was never lodged.\n2. What evidence exists on the file of notice or opportunity to object given to the occupying family (Williams / Buckler) in 1982–83.\n3. The precise legal and administrative basis for the 1987 title amalgamation that took place while the Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler were still live.\n4. Whether the inclusion of the woodland (or any land beyond the 1938 conveyance) is regarded as a possible mistake capable of alteration or indemnity under the Land Registration Act 2002 and Practice Guide 39.\n\nPlease confirm these points form part of the live investigation and state the exact start date of the ICR six-month period (so that the ~25 November 2026 outer limit can be verified).\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a44bf86340","subject":"FOI/EIR 00211557 and earlier requests – formal chase of three missing planning appendices (C, D and E)","name":"FOI/EIR 00211557 and earlier requests – formal chase of three missing planning appendices (C, D and E)","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a44bf86340.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef64335cb7c-foi-eir-00211557-and-earlier-requests-formal-chase-of-three-missing-planning-appendices-c-d-and-e","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef64335cb7c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772","00211463","00211483","00211484","00211557"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a44bf86340.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,\n\nI refer to the partial disclosures already made and to the still-open requests concerning Great House Farm / Tý Mawr / Church View Close (including 00210772, 00211463, 00211483, 00211484 and 00211557).\n\nThe planning report’s Appendices C, D and E remain missing. These form part of the public planning record for the site and are required for the completeness of the evidence library. Please:\n\n1. Identify the three missing appendices by their original reference or description.\n2. Either disclose them in full or state the precise exemption relied upon for each.\n3. Confirm the statutory response date for FOI/EIR 00211557 remains on or about 26 October 2026.\n\nThis is a chase of existing open requests for the public record. It does not ask the Council to determine private title or liability.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a3966769ad","subject":"RC26-0375 – thank you and three remaining points","name":"RC26-0375 – thank you and three remaining points","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a3966769ad.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef8ffb95c24-rc26-0375-thank-you-and-three-remaining-points","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef8ffb95c24","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0375"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a3966769ad.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear National Monuments Record team,\n\nThank you for the consolidated reply of 29 September / 6 October 2026 (RC26-0375) and for confirming that the requests of 8, 15, 17 and 20 September are now treated as fully answered.\n\nThree points remain:\n\n1. Please supply the free scans of NMR 6048945, 6048943 and 6048941 as indicated.\n2. Confirm whether any accession data, transfer note or provenance record exists for the material held under NPRN 20182 (beyond the statement that none is held in registered files).\n3. Confirm whether the emergency-recording case previously catalogued under the wrong place-name (Bonvilston) has now been correctly linked.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a37f30c0ce","subject":"RE: 2026/4274 — thank you; D153 at NLW; source of DRA/11/120 note","name":"RE: 2026/4274 — thank you; D153 at NLW; source of DRA/11/120 note","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a37f30c0ce.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123ef991df48ff-2026-4274-thank-you-d153-at-nlw-source-of-dra-11-120-note","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123ef991df48ff","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a37f30c0ce.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Louise / Glamorgan Archives,\n\nThank you for your reply of 6 October 2026 under reference 2026/4274.\n\nI note and accept:\n\n1. D153/1–8 is held at the National Library of Wales. I will pursue that sequence with NLW (catalogue entry for deeds in p. Llandough including the dwelling adjoining the churchyard, 1811, D153/1–2).\n\n2. DRA/11/120 (formerly D/DRa 11/120) forms part of the Elder’s Navigation Colliery, Maesteg series (DRA/11/1–293) and does not relate to Llandough-juxta-Penarth or to Tynywain. I will not treat it as evidence for this site.\n\nThe DRA/11/120 form appeared in secondary notes I was checking; your correction is helpful and I will mark it as a wrong reference for this research.\n\nNo further action is requested from Glamorgan Archives on those two points. I remain grateful for the earlier 2026/4097 searches and copy offers.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a1273a35d066961","subject":"FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","name":"FOI 2026-024 / 032 / 036 – outstanding item 7: recorded basis for treating already-found records as “unrelated / not in scope”","date":"2026-10-10T19:11:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a1273a35d066961.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a123efb2856da1d-foi-2026-024-032-036-outstanding-item-7-recorded-basis-for-treating-already-found-records-as-unrelated-not-in-scope","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a123efb2856da1d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a1273a35d066961.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,\n\nThank you for the disclosures under FOI 2026-032 (22 September) and 2026-036 (5 October).\n\nOn 25 August 2026 you stated that searches had located records of “other archaeological discoveries at Great House Farm and Church Farm” which were withheld as “not in scope”. On 26 August I asked for those records and, specifically, the recorded basis for calling them unrelated (item 7).\n\nThat question remains unanswered. The later disclosures released certain Church Farm and other-site material but still did not supply the internal note, search-log entry or other record that justified the original classification.\n\nI therefore request:\n\n1. The recorded basis (search log, file note, email or other document) that led the Museum to treat the already-found Great House Farm / Church Farm records as unrelated or out of scope on 25 August 2026.\n2. If no such written basis exists, an explicit statement to that effect.\n3. Confirmation that the full set of records located in the August searches has now been disclosed or, if any remain withheld, the precise exemption relied upon for each.\n\nPlease treat this as a request for the information that should have been provided under the internal review of 2026-024. This is for the completeness of the evidence library on the public record.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a12523a7927c6ca","subject":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","name":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","date":"2026-10-10T09:27:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamil