610CGV Title No: WA231076","name":"Further to Your Enquiry: Ref: 260917-6718215 ABR No: N610CGV Title No: WA231076","date":"2026-10-10T07:23:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a124b25060d556f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a124b25060d556f-further-to-your-enquiry-ref-260917-6718215-abr-no-n610cgv-title-no-wa231076","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a124b25060d556f","direction":"received","from":"_Central","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["N610CGV","Z084NQV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a124b25060d556f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Enquiry Reference: 260917-6718215 Application Reference: N610CGV Title Number: WA231076\n\nDear Customer\n\nThank you for your enquiry.\n\n\nThe matter you have contacted us about has already been raised by yourself and an application has been captured internally by HM Land Registry to investigate and correct any error that may have been made.\n\nPlease note the application reference - Z084NQV\n\n\n\n\nYours faithfully\n\nKaty\nHM Land Registry\n\nWe only provide factual information and impartial advice about our procedures. Read more about the advice we give.<https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hm-land-registry-service-standards/our-service-standards>\n\nEasy and free support to help you work with HM Land Registry:\nGuidance for members of the public - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/guidance-for-members-of-the-public>\nGuidance for property professionals - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/guidance-for-property-professionals>\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a120c63de6587c0","subject":"New response to your FOI request - BP vs Buckler 1987","name":"New response to your FOI request - BP vs Buckler 1987","date":"2026-10-09T13:07:04Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a120c63de6587c0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a120c63de6587c0-new-response-to-your-foi-request-bp-vs-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":["nactso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nactso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a120c63de6587c0","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"nactso","name":"Counter Terrorism Policing (NaCTSO)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a120c63de6587c0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request 'BP vs Buckler 1987' that you made to National Counter Terrorism Security Office.\n