eviewer)"}],"refs":["ICR/090/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a11fdabbb6d199f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nFurther to my colleague's email below, please find my letter of today's date attached.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nDenyse St Rose\nOffice Manager and Investigations Officer\nICR Office\n\n10 South Colonnade\nCanary Wharf, London [postcode redacted]\n[Title: phone - Description: phone-icon]  [phone redacted]\n[Title: website - Description: website-icon]  www.icrev.org.uk \n\n\nFrom: ICR Office Inbox\nSent: 28 September 2026 12:44\nTo: Requester  \nSubject: Your complaint about HM Land Registry - referral to ICR Office\n\nDear Requester\n\nI am writing to acknowledge receipt of:\n\n1.) Your email of 26 September titled \"Great House Farm, Llandough\" with 9 attachments.\n\n2.) Your email of 27 September titled \"Great House Farm, Llandough\" providing correction of a date quoted in your earlier correspondence.\n\n3.) Your email of 27 September titled \"Referral to the Independent Complaints Reviewer - HM Land Registry, titles WA231076 / WA240304 (Llandough)\"\n\nThank you for setting out the details of the complaint you have about HM Land Registry (HMLR). Your correspondence and request for an independent review will be passed to an investigation officer here at the ICR Office. They will consider what you have said and discuss your complaint with the Independent Complaints Reviewer.\n\nThe investigation officer will contact you in the next ten working days.\n\nYour referral has been allocated reference number ICR/090/26.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nVicky Applegate\nOffice Administrator\nIndependent Complaints Reviewers Office\n10 South Colonnade\nCanary Wharf\nLondon\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[email redacted] \n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a11fa854d35e082","subject":"FREEDOM OF INFORMATION ACT (FOIA) INTERNAL REVIEW","name":"FREEDOM OF INFORMATION ACT (FOIA) INTERNAL REVIEW","date":"2026-10-09T07:54:44Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a11fa854d35e082.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11fa854d35e082-freedom-of-information-act-foia-internal-review","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11fa854d35e082","direction":"received","from":"NSUKilo","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a11fa854d35e082.json","attachments":[{"name":"IR FOI 260813002 Requester Response.pdf","title":"IR FOI 260813002 Requester Response.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/2026-10-09_moj_ir-foi-260813002-internal-review-response.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":136101,"sha256":"ff9e9ec343722bc96ab3eb4b3a43b5627253ab53d186d263f5ece9101611fd22"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"OFFICIAL\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nThank you for your Internal Review request dated the 13 August 2026 regarding request FOI 260813002.\n\nPlease find attached a letter with the outcome of the review.\n\nThanks\n\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n\n\nOFFICIAL"},{"id":"gm-1a11c210b3442ac5","subject":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"RE: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-10-08T15:28:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a11c210b3442ac5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e9889be4e6a","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a11c210b3442ac5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon.  I acknowledge receipt of your e-mail below.  I can also confirm that Planning and Environment Decisions Wales (PEDW) does not hold any information or records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth or planning applications 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.  All PEDW’s electronic records have been searched.  PEDW does not have a paper file repository.\nIsabel Nethell\n\nPennaeth Gweithrediadau/Head of Operations\nPenderfyniadau Cynllunio a’r Amgylchedd / Planning & Environment Decisions Wales\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nCP2, Parc Cathays, Caerdydd, [postcode redacted] / CP2, Cathays Park, Cardiff, [postcode redacted]\nFfôn / Phone: [phone redacted]\nE-bost / E-mail:  [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n[A logo for a company  AI-generated content may be incorrect.]\n\n\nPenderfyniadau Cynllunio ac Amgylchedd Cymru | LLYW.CYMRU<https://llyw.cymru/penderfyndiadau-cynllunio-ac-amgylchedd-cymru?_ga=2.118801417.1086042177.1633691770-684163877.1633354991> / Planning and Environment Decisions Wales | GOV.WALES<https://gov.wales/planning-and-environment-decisions-wales>\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 28 September 2026 22:40\nTo: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; BP Archive <[email redacted]>; FOI Requests <[email redacted]>; Cardiff County, Enquiries <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Connor McGilly <[email redacted]>; MRC_Archive, Resource <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Disclosure Team <[email redacted]>; NSUKilo <[email redacted]>; Paul Egan <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Julian Wilkes <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; _FOI email address <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; Customer Support <[email redacted]>; Davidson, Victoria <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Contact OneVale <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; DOUGHTY, Stephen <[email redacted]>; CAIRNS Alun <[email redacted]>; Correspondence/Gohebiaeth - HF <[email redacted]>; Pwyllgor Diwylliant, Cyfathrebu, y Gymraeg a Chwaraeon - Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee <[email redacted]>; Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>; PEDW – Cwynion / Complaints <[email redacted]>; FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest\n\n\nFORMAL PRESERVATION NOTICE\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth\nTitles: WA231076, WA240304, WA513690 and WA735527\nPlanning references: 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES\n\nURL: greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com<http://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/>\n\nTo each recipient separately, in your own capacity as a current or potential holder, custodian or controller of relevant records:\n\nThis notice is addressed to each recipient individually. It is not a joint request, and it does not ask any recipient to speak for, investigate on behalf of, or answer in place of any other person or organisation. Each recipient is asked to respond only in respect of records within that recipient's own possession, custody or control, including records inherited from a predecessor organisation or retained on its behalf.\n\n1. Nature and purpose of this notice\n\nThis is a formal preservation notice concerning documentary material relating to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's, and the subsequent development of the site, including the area now associated with Church View Close.\n\nIt is not a claim form, is not service of proceedings, and is not intended to constitute or replace any FOI request, internal review, complaint, subject-access request or other statutory process already made to any recipient.\n\nThe purpose of this notice is to require the preservation of potentially relevant material while the documentary history, title chain, registration history, planning history, possession proceedings, demolition and subsequent development are being reconstructed.\n\nA separate first-stage preservation notice has been issued or is being issued to Cadw / Welsh Government FOI, HM Land Registry Wales Office and DPO, Heneb / GGAT HER, RCAHMW, Vale of Glamorgan FOI Unit and DPO, Glamorgan Archives, South Wales Police FOI, The National Archives, the Wales Office FOI team, and the National Library of Wales. Persimmon Homes (Wales) Ltd has received a separate preservation letter.\n\nYou are receiving this notice separately because the published documentary record places you, or a predecessor whose records may remain in your custody or control, within the documentary, legal, professional, administrative or development chain concerning this land.\n\n2. Land and documentary scope\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, alter, overwrite, discard, transfer out of custody without a recorded handover, or otherwise dispose of, any record within your possession, custody or control relating to the land or matters identified below.\n\nThe scope includes, without limitation, originals, copies, working papers, drafts, annotations, plans, photographs, negatives, films, tapes, maps, registers, indexes, correspondence, emails and attachments, electronic files, archived mailboxes, databases, metadata, internal notes, meeting records, instructions, client or matter files, survey material and other associated records.\n\nThe material requested includes:\n\n1. Historical ownership, occupation and conveyancing\n\nThe 1877 split; the 1916 and 1939 tenancies; the 1938 Bute to Western Ground Rents conveyance; the 1969 Western Ground Rents to BP Pension Trust conveyance; and any plans, schedules, abstracts, searches, correspondence or other documents relied upon in relation to those transactions.\n\n2. Possession proceedings and subsequent litigation\n\nThe 1955 High Court and 1962 Cardiff County Court possession orders; the 1974 proceedings; BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2; House of Lords leave papers, including YHL/PO/JO/10/11/2536; and Buckler v United Kingdom (1989), including associated correspondence, instructions, evidence, plans and working papers.\n\n3. Land registration\n\nThe first registration of WA231076, including the application dated 30 November 1982; the first registration of WA240304, including the application dated 23 February 1983; subsequent amalgamation, transfer or closure; and every plan, conveyance, abstract, search, application, correspondence trail or professional file relied upon in connection with those registrations or changes.\n\n4. 1988 possession and demolition\n\nThe taking of possession on or about 29 November 1988 and the demolition commenced on or about 6 December 1988, including any planning, listed-building, heritage, police, enforcement, media, contractor, survey, photographic or inter-agency liaison material.\n\n5. Planning and subsequent development, 1989–1996\n\nPlanning application 89/01396/OUT; reserved matters application 92/00671/RES; conditions 16–18; GGAT / Cotswold Archaeology material; records concerning any section 52, section 106, planning obligation, local land charge or equivalent instrument; and the transfer from BP to Ideal Homes dated 3 December 1993, together with all associated plans, correspondence, approvals, agreements, searches and completion material.\n\n6. Family records\n\nRecords concerning Mary Doreen Williams (died 1983) and William Buckler, insofar as those records relate to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, the land described above, its occupation, ownership, possession, disposal, registration, development or demolition.\n\n3. Predecessor and inherited files\n\nWhere you hold, or may hold, a file originating with a predecessor, successor, merged practice, affiliated practice, client or other entity, that material is also within scope.\n\nThis includes, without limitation, records originating from:\n\nLoosemores of Cardiff; Robbins Olivey & Blake Lapthorn / Blake Morgan; Linklaters & Paines; Debenham Tewson / DTZ / Cushman & Wakefield; Wyn Thomas + Partners; Ideal Homes Wales; BP Properties; BP Pension Trust; Cotswold Archaeological Trust; Cardiff Bay Development Corporation; and South Glamorgan County Council.\n\nThe reference to a predecessor file does not assert that you necessarily hold such a file. It identifies material for which a reasonable custody or succession inquiry should be made where applicable.\n\n4. Preservation steps\n\nPlease take reasonable steps to prevent the routine destruction, deletion, alteration or overwriting of potentially relevant material, including material held in archived mailboxes, legacy systems, off-site storage, document-management systems, backup repositories and other electronic or physical stores.\n\nWhere relevant material has been transferred to another repository, archive, successor organisation or third party, please preserve the information necessary to identify the transfer and its current location, including any accession, file, box, reference or custody details.\n\nNothing in this notice requires the creation of records that do not exist. The request concerns the preservation of records already held or controlled by you.\n\n5. Purpose and legal position\n\nThis notice is not a finding against any recipient, and I am not asking any recipient to determine title or adjudicate the underlying dispute.\n\nThe 1987 Court of Appeal judgment is relied upon here only for matters actually determined by that judgment, including the issues concerning possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. This preservation notice does not treat that judgment as having determined the complete documentary root of title to the farmhouse parcel.\n\nThe underlying documentary history, including the relationship between the farmhouse parcel and the agricultural land subsequently dealt with through Western Ground Rents and BP, remains a matter requiring reconstruction from the primary records.\n\nAccordingly, preservation is requested precisely so that the documentary record can be established from the records themselves rather than through assumptions based on later registration, later occupation, later planning treatment or secondary descriptions.\n\n6. Acknowledgement and identification of records\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt of this notice and, in your own capacity, confirm:\n\n(a) the officer, partner, records manager or other person responsible for implementing the preservation hold;\n\n(b) what records within your possession, custody or control you have identified as falling within the scope above; and\n\n(c) where you identify no records within scope, what relevant systems, files, repositories or predecessor records you searched in reaching that conclusion.\n\nA substantive assessment of title is not requested from you. The immediate requirement is preservation and identification of the documentary material you hold.\n\nThe public documentary index and developing evidence record is available at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nPlease monitor that site for subsequent identification of documents, references and specific schedules relevant to your organisation's records.\n\nWhere a reliable public email address is unavailable, a postal preservation notice will also be sent. For example, a postal notice will follow to Loosemores, Alliance House, 18–19 High Street, Cardiff [postcode redacted].\n\nNothing in this notice constitutes an abandonment, waiver or limitation of any claim, position or remedy concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening, rectification or alteration of the register, or any associated matter.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-1a11b2364b1e069e","subject":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","name":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud","date":"2026-10-08T10:50:58Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a11b2364b1e069e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a11b2364b1e069e-great-house-farm-suspected-historic-fraud","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a11b2364b1e069e","direction":"received","from":"Victim Liaison Cymru-Wales","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a11b2364b1e069e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email dated 30 September 2026.  Please accept our apologies that you have not received an acknowledgement until now.  Your email has been passed to a CPS manager for her advice, and we will return to you when we receive that advice.\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\nA Allabarton\n\nA Allabarton\nRheolwr Cyswllt Dioddefwyr / Victim Liaison Officer\nUned Cyswllt Dioddefwyr / Victim Liaison Unit\n[Gwasanaeth Erlyn y Goron / Crown Prosecution Service]\nCrown Prosecution Service, CPS Wales Area, Welsh Government Offices, Cathays Park, Cardiff [postcode redacted]. Gwasanaeth Erlyn y Goron, Ardal CPS Cymru, Llywodraeth Cymru, Parc Cathays, Caerdydd [postcode redacted].\nFfôn/Telephone: [phone redacted]\nwww.cps.gov.uk<http://www.cps.gov.uk/>"},{"id":"gm-1a11ad2b22443cb9","subject":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","name":"RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","date":"2026-10-08T09:22:51Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a11ad2b22443cb9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-filtered-schedule-still-not-supplied-unanswered-points-from-foi-2026-032-correct","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a11ad2b22443cb9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nThe Museum has reviewed the material held under reference MS 3360/3 and has already provided the relevant page identified during that review.\n\nThere is no catalogue record identifying Great House Farm within this document. Following additional research by Collections staff, one page within the larger document was identified as relating to Great House Farm and was supplied to you.\n\nThe information contained on that page has already been disclosed and summarised in our previous correspondence. No further recorded information relating to Great House Farm has been identified within the material held under reference MS 3360/3.\n\nWe therefore have nothing further to add on this matter.\n\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image002.png@01DD570E.F8BD0A00]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/amgueddfa.cymru> | museum.wales<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/museum.wales>\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 07 October 2026 18:10\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction\n\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\n\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\n\nFOI Team,\n\nThank you for the clarification.\n\nYour email of 7 October materially clarifies the position, and I have now corrected my records to distinguish the different Llandough farmsteads.\n\nRef 13.2 — Llandough Farm opposite the hospital\n\nI understand and accept the distinction in your catalogue description:\n\n“Waterwheel from Llandough Farm (opposite hospital)”\n\nThis refers to the separate Llandough Farm in the Llandough near Penarth/Cardiff locality, not to Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr. I am not seeking to attribute the waterwheel to Great House Farm.\n\nI will therefore treat Ref 13.2 as a separate Llandough Farm record unless a primary Museum record expressly establishes otherwise.\n\nMS 3360/3 — Great House / Llandough Estate\n\nThe more significant clarification is the information you have now supplied from MS 3360/3.\n\nYou state that the page records that:\n\n  *   “Great House” formed part of the Llandough Estate sale particulars of 1924;\n  *   it was occupied by W.G. Thomas & Sons;\n  *   it comprised approximately 202 acres;\n  *   it was situated in the Parish of Llanfair; and\n  *   the homestead was situated in the Village of Llandough.\n\nThose particulars provide a much more specific identification than the earlier catalogue description.\n\nI am particularly interested in the combination of Llandough Estate + Parish of Llanfair + Village of Llandough + approximately 202 acres + W.G. Thomas & Sons.\n\nCould you therefore confirm one narrow point from the record already examined:\n\nDoes the MS 3360/3 page or plan itself contain any further recorded identifier which identifies which historical Llandough is meant — for example the specific place-name form, neighbouring farms, estate owner, parish/benefice wording, acreage breakdown, plan number, tenant information, road, church or other geographical feature?\n\nI am not asking the Museum to make a new identification or to provide an opinion. I am asking only whether such information is actually recorded in the page or plan you have already examined.\n\nThere is an important reason for keeping this distinction precise. There are two different farmsteads in the Llandough near Penarth/Cardiff locality relevant to the Museum's records:\n\n  1.  Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, beside St Dochdwy's Church; and\n  2.  Llandough Farm, separately described by the Museum as “opposite hospital”.\n\nThey must not be treated as alternative names for one farm.\n\nThere is also a separate question concerning the Museum's wording “Llandough Church Farm” in the 1858 provenance of accession 63.24. I now understand that this should not automatically be equated with either of the above merely because it contains the word Llandough. Unless the underlying historical evidence expressly identifies the 1858 “Church Farm”, I will continue to record that identity as unresolved.\n\nFiltered schedule\n\nI also accept your clarification that the Museum does not hold a separate recorded audit schedule showing, item by item, which search results staff excluded after reviewing the results.\n\nI therefore do not ask the Museum to create such a schedule.\n\nFor the purposes of the record, I will instead distinguish between:\n\n  *   records positively identified as Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr;\n  *   records positively identified as the separate Llandough Farm opposite the hospital;\n  *   records from other Llandoughs, including Llandough-juxta-Cowbridge;\n  *   and source-specific records whose location remains unresolved.\n\nThe new MS 3360/3 particulars are sufficiently distinctive to make the underlying page and plan an important identification source, so I would be grateful for confirmation of whether any further geographical identifier is actually recorded there.\n\nThank you again for the clarification.\n\nCofion,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 7 Oct 2026, 08:11 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nIn relation to the filtered schedule, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold a separate recorded document identifying, item by item, which search results were excluded following review. Search results were reviewed by staff to determine whether they related to the location specified in your request, and the outcome of that review was reflected in our response of 5 October 2026. We do not hold a separate audit schedule of those decisions.\n\nIn relation to MS 3360/3, the relevant page was previously supplied in response to FOI 2026-032. That page records that \"Great House\" formed part of the Llandough Estate sale particulars of 1924, was occupied by W.G. Thomas & Sons, comprised approximately 202 acres, was situated in the Parish of Llanfair, and describes the homestead as being situated in the Village of Llandough. No additional recorded information identifying the holding has been identified within the material reviewed.\n\nIn relation to Ref 13.2, the collections record describes the item as a \"Waterwheel from Llandough Farm (opposite hospital)\". No further location information has been identified within the record.\n\nWe trust this clarifies the position.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\nFOI Team\n[email redacted]<http://museumwales.ac.uk/>\namgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 07 October 2026 05:29\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: RE: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nDear FOI Team,\n\nFOI 2026-036 – response of 5 October 2026\n\nThank you for the letter. I note the additional records identified (Ref 13.2 waterwheel and the page of MS 3360/3).\n\nWhat remains unanswered\nOn 27 September I corrected the place names in the FOI 2026-032 pack, identifying at least PAS 2022.18.1 (NGR SS9934672805) and a separate Great House Farm entry at Llandow as belonging to different properties. Your reply of 28 September accepted the distinction: the collections system does not group by similar names, no recorded cross-attribution is held, and those hits arose from the search rather than catalogue overlap.\n\nThe 5 October letter does not supply a cleaned / filtered schedule showing which of the FOI 2026-032 items survive that filter. Until that is provided, the cross-reference still carries the Cowbridge and Llandow material. That is the point left open on 28 September and still open now.\n\nWhat you have not said\nYou have not stated, item by item, which of the earlier schedule entries are now excluded as relating to Great House Farm near Cowbridge or Great House Farm, Llandow. You have not confirmed the parish of the page of MS 3360/3 that you identify as relating to Great House Farm (which Llandough, and any vendor / tenant / acreage / parcel detail that identifies the holding). You have not confirmed whether Ref 13.2 (waterwheel collected 1 April 1979 from “Llandough Farm”, donor Wales and West Housing Association) is recorded as the Penarth site opposite the hospital, or as the farmhouse demolished by BP on 6 December 1988.\n\nPlease therefore supply:\n1. A filtered schedule of the FOI 2026-032 records that remain after exclusion of all items relating to Great House Farm / Llandough near Cowbridge and to Great House Farm, Llandow. For each surviving entry:\naccession or archive number, title, date, and one-line description.\n2. Explicit parish confirmation for the page of MS 3360/3 identified as relating to Great House Farm: which Llandough, and any vendor / tenant / acreage / parcel detail that identifies the holding.\n3. Confirmation whether Ref 13.2 is recorded as the Penarth site opposite the hospital, or as the farmhouse demolished by BP on 6 December 1988.\n\nThese are requests for recorded information already within the searches undertaken. I am not seeking new searches or opinions. The unanswered point is the filter that you accepted was necessary on 28 September but have not yet applied in a disclosed schedule.\n\nCofion,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a117581dc9c1a2b","subject":"Re: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","name":"Re: FOI 2026-036 – Great House Farm, Llandough – filtered schedule still not supplied; unanswered points from FOI 2026-032 correction","date":"2026-10-07T17:10:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a117581dc9c1a2b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-filtered-schedule-still-not-supplied-unanswered-points-from-foi-2026-032-correct","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a1149cc3b8ce394","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a117581dc9c1a2b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"FOI Team,\n\nThank you for the clarification.\n\nYour email of 7 October materially clarifies the position, and 