 Organisation with the Chartered Institute for Archaeologists \nMae Heneb yn Sefydliad Cofrestredig gyda’r Chartered Institute for Archaeologists\n​\nThe Trust is both a Limited Company (1198990) and a Registered Charity (504616)\nAny of the statements or comments made above should be regarded as personal and not necessarily those of\n​Heneb. This e-mail and any files transmitted with it are confidential and intended solely for the use of the individual or\n​entity to whom they are addressed.\n​\n​Privacy Policy - Heneb\n​\n​Registered Office: Corner House, 6 Carmarthen Street, Llandeilo, Carmarthenshire, [postcode redacted]\n​Swyddfa Gofrestredig : Ty Cornel, 6 Stryd Caerfyrddin, Llandeilo, Sir Gaerfyrddin, [postcode redacted]\n\n​Cwmni Cyfyngedig (1198990) ynghyd ag Elusen Gofrestredig (504616) yw’r Ymddiriedolaeth\n​Dylai'r datganiadau neu'r sylwadau uchod gael eu trin fel rhai personol ac nid o reidrwydd fel datganiadau neu\n​​sylwadau gan Heneb. Mae'r e-bost hwn ac unrhyw ffeiliau a drosglwyddir gydag ef yn gyfrinachol ac at ddefnydd\nyr unigolyn neu'r corff y cyfeiriwyd hwy atynt yn unig.\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 08 September 2026 04:06\nTo: HER <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\nHER Officer (Heneb: Glamorgan-Gwent),\n\nThis is a request for recorded information under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 and, so far as applicable, the Freedom of Information Act 2000, and under the public-access duty to the historic environment record.\n\nI request the full HER source file for Great House Farm, Llandough (GGAT02038s and any linked event or find records), specifically:\n\n1. The complete text of the entry or entries that refer to armour or medieval ironwork found under the rear wing / floor c.1880, including every source code and footnote.\n\n2. A copy or transcript of the RCAHMW / Suggett 1988 material held on the HER file (GGAT’s 1990 assessment cites “RCAHMW 1988” for the museum attribution).\n\n3. Any museum accession number, letter, or catalogue slip on the file that identifies where the ironwork went.\n\n4. Any distinction on the file between:\n   (a) the c.1880 rear-wing ironwork;\n   (b) iron from the 1979 villa excavation south of the church;\n   (c) the 1994 cemetery iron girdle (Burial 631) later examined by the National Museum of Wales.\n\nPlease send electronic copies. I am an interested person researching the documented history of this site, not a commercial applicant.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>"},{"id":"gm-1a10d0150abced55","subject":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-10-05T16:59:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a10d0150abced55.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e8f80ef591718-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-scrutiny"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-scrutiny"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e8f80ef591718","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a10d0150abced55.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Chris,\n\nI flew back.\n\ngreathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com\n\nRequester\n\nOn Monday, 5 October 2026, Franks, Christopher P (Cllr) <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Diolch.\n>\n>\n>\n> I will indeed say a prayer and have already done so,\n>\n>\n>\n> Chris\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 28 September 2026 18:29\n> *To:* Franks, Christopher P (Cllr)  \n> *Subject:* Great House Far