pondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0f7dbf9dec61a9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0f7dbf9dec61a9-foi-welsh-office-cadw-papers-july-december-1988-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-following-26foi-103-atisn-27589","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0f7dbf9dec61a9","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["26FOI103","ATISN27589"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0f7dbf9dec61a9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nATISN 27589 - Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n\n\nThank you for your request which I received on 29 September.  You asked for:\n\n\n\n  1.  Any consideration, between 1 July and 31 December 1988, of listing, spot-listing or emergency listing of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's (approx. ST 168 733).\n  2.  Any inspection, photograph, minute or note of the building, or of its demolition, in that period. Possession was taken on 29 November 1988. Demolition of the farmhouse began on 6 December 1988.\n  3.  Any transfer, destruction or disposal of those files, with the schedule used and the date.\n\n\n\nYou will receive a response by 26 October 2026.  If you have any queries about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future correspondence.\n\n\n\nThe request you sent me contains personal information about you - for example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your personal information and all other information relating to your request for three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your personal information will then be disposed of securely.\n\n\n\nUnder data protection legislation, you have the right:\n\n\n\n•              to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access it\n\n•              to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\n\n•              to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\n\n•              for (in certain circumstances) your data to be ‘erased’\n\n•              to (in certain circumstances) data portability\n\n•              to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\n\n\n\nFor further information about the information which the Welsh Government holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR, please see contact details below:\n\n\n\nData Protection Officer\n\nWelsh Government\n\nCathays Park\n\nCARDIFF\n\n[postcode redacted]\n\nEmail:    [email redacted]\n\n\n\nThe contact details for the Information Commissioner’s Office are:\n\n\n\nWycliffe House\n\nWater Lane\n\nWilmslow\n\nCheshire\n\n[postcode redacted]\n\n\n\nWebsite: www.ico.org.uk\n\n\n\nAny information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh Government’s Disclosure Log (at https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en).\n\n\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\n\nAndy Wigley\n\n\n\nDr Andy Wigley\n\nPrif Arolygydd – Pennaeth Arolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Chief Inspector - Head of Historic Environment Inspectorate\n\nCadw\n\nDysgu, Cymunedau a Diwylliant / Learning, Communities and Culture\n\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n\nTŷ Ladywell / Ladywell House\n\nY Drenewydd / Newtown\n\nPowys\n\n[postcode redacted]\n\n\n\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\nFfôn symudol / Mobile: [phone redacted]\n\nE-bost/ Email: [email redacted] / [email redacted]\n\n\n\n Helpwch yr amgylchedd - peidiwch ag argraffu hon os nad oes gwir raid   Help our environment - only print this if really necessary\n\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth Gymraeg. Cewch ateb Cymraeg i bob gohebiaeth Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh. Correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not involve any delay.\n\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 28 September 2026 22:42\nTo: Freedom of Information Officer <[email redacted]>\nCc: [email redacted]\nSubject: FOI — Welsh Office / Cadw papers, July–December 1988 — Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough — following 26FOI 103\n\n\n\nFreedom of Information\n\nWelsh Government\n\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\ncc: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> — so 26FOI 103 stays on the same fact\n\n\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\n\n\nRequest under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nRequester: Requester.\n\n\n\nWales Office, in 26FOI 103 dated 22 September 2026, said historic Welsh Office / Cadw listing papers for this house sit with you. This is that request. I am not asking you to decide title.\n\n\n\nPlease disclose recorded information held by the Welsh Government or by Cadw as part of it concerning:\n\n\n\n1. Any consideration, between 1 July and 31 December 1988, of listing, spot-listing or emergency listing of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's (approx. ST 168 733).\n\n2. Any inspection, photograph, minute or note of the building, or of its demolition, in that period. Possession was taken on 29 November 1988. Demolition of the farmhouse began on 6 December 1988.\n\n3. Any transfer, destruction or disposal of those files, with the schedule used and the date.\n\n\n\nIf nothing is held, please say what was searched, including Cadw listing files, Welsh Office inherited files, and any index of destroyed building records.\n\n\n\nThe public evidence index is https://eur01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgreathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com%2F&data=05%7C02%7CFreedom.ofinformation%40gov.wales%7Ce029caee52814a3b432208df1da95c68%7Ca2cc36c592804ae78887d06dab89216b%7C0%7C0%7C639262285389715752%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=xkALWerkSzniYZhge00mFdOGmXpaU1i9ZVJTPzZeRKM%3D&reserved=0<https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/>\n\n. The investigation distinguishes Parcel A (farmhouse, garden, buildings and yard — the family's maintained freehold) from Parcel B (eastern fields — not presently disputed). The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide whether the documentary root of Parcel A was ever established. These papers go to that question. They are not a finding against Cadw.\n\n\n\nPlease confirm the reference and the 20 working-day date, and preserve anything in scope.\n\n\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation or reopening. This is not a claim form.\n\n\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybod