faithfully,\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nSep 28 2026, 10:42PM via Email\nPreservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose\nTo each recipient, in your own capacity as holder or likely holder of\nrecords. Please do not treat this as a joint reply. Answer only for\nyour own holdings.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a preservation notice. It is not a claim form and not service\nof proceedings. It does not replace any FOI, review or subject access\nrequest already with you.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining\nSt Dochdwy's. Titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690, WA735527,\nand any related title. Planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, transfer out of your custody\nwithout a written receipt, or dispose of, any file, plan, photograph,\ntape or electronic record in your possession, custody or control\nrelating to:\n\n1. The 1877 split, the 1916 and 1939 tenancies, and the 1938 Bute to\nWestern Ground Rents conveyance.\n2. The 1955 and 1962 possession orders, the 1974 proceedings, and BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n3. First registration: WA231076 application 30 November 1982; WA240304\napplication 23 February 1983; later amalgamation.\n4. The 1988 possession (29 November) and demolition (begun 6\nDecember), including listing, planning, police and any liaison papers.\n5. Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler, so\nfar as your file concerns this land.\n\nAlso preserve, if you hold them, the following planning and\nland-charge classes. Absence from a 2026 file disclosure is not proof\nthey never existed:\n\n6. Any section 52 Town and Country Planning Act 1971 agreement, later\nsection 106 instrument, deed, undertaking or other agreement\nregulating the development or use of this land, and any corresponding\nlocal-land-charge entry.\n7. The historic planning-register entries required by the Town and\nCountry Planning General Development Order 1988 for 89/01396/OUT and\n92/00671/RES (applications, reserved matters, plans and drawings, and\ndecision information).\n8. The officer's report annexes to 89/01396/OUT, including Appendix B\n(further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust), and\nAppendices C–E.\n9. The condition chain on 89/01396/OUT: conditions 16–18; the\nCouncil's October 1990 confirmation of condition 17; GGAT's July 1992\narchaeological warning; the September 1992 reserved-matters approval;\nand the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged.\n10. Any preliminary environmental-assessment / screening determination\nfor the outline application (site described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38\nha).\n11. Any record of the statutory consultation route used because the\nland was, or was treated as, a site of archaeological interest / SMR\nentry under the 1988 Order.\n12. The complete 92/00671/RES file, and any sale, option,\nconditional-contract or transfer paper on the planning files covering\nBP Properties to Ideal Homes Wales, including the recorded transfer of\n3 December 1993.\n13. The application-receipt record for 89/01396/OUT (form dated\nOctober 1989; reconstructed Council receipt 8 November 1989).\n\nPlease stop routine deletion, including archived mailboxes, for\nanything in that scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n. The investigation distinguishes the farmhouse parcel from the\neastern fields. The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession,\nlimitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the\ndocumentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These records go to that\nquestion. This notice is not a finding against any of you.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer responsible for the hold, and say\nwhat you hold in scope. If you hold nothing, say what you searched.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title,\nregistration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the\nregister.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]\n\n------------------\n\nThank you for using the National Library of Wales Enquiry Service.\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9823416.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a0f250d8b44a046","subject":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud — further information and request for consideration","name":"Re: Great House Farm / suspected historic fraud — further information and request for consideration","date":"2026-09-30T12:36:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0f250d8b44a046.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ee493c00fb442-great-house-farm-suspected-historic-fraud-further-information-and-request-for-consideration","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ee493c00fb442","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cps","name":"Crown Prosecution Service"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0f250d8b44a046.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr/Ms Rutter,\n\nFurther to my email of earlier today and your message of 29 September 2026.\n\nI am writing to place further material and context before the Victim\nLiaison Unit so that CPS Cymru-Wales has the information necessary to\nidentify any existing record or referral and, where appropriate, to ensure\nthat the material reaches the prosecutor or team responsible for\nconsidering it.\n\nI am not asking the CPS to determine the underlying civil title to the\nproperty. The issue I am raising is whether the documentary history gives\nrise to potential criminal offences, whether those matters warrant\ninvestigation, and, if a private prosecution is subsequently instituted,\nwhether the circumstances are such that the Director's power under section\n6(2) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985 should be considered.\n\n1. Police engagement and current references\n\nOn 28 September 2026 I submitted a formal crime-recording request to South\nWales Police ([email redacted]), copied to Stephen Doughty\nMP for constituency-record purposes only.\n\nThe request asks South Wales Police to record, or explain in writing why\nthey will not record, a report concerning suspected fraud and related\nconcealment in the creation and subsequent use of registered title to the\nformer Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough. It identifies, in particular,\nthe first-registration application for WA231076 dated 30 November 1982, the\napplication for WA240304 dated 23 February 1983, and matters arising from\nthe subsequent 1987 proceedings.\n\nI also have a live Subject Access Request with South Wales Police\nconcerning the 1988 eviction and demolition and related personal data.\n\nI previously reported suspected irregularities concerning the 1982\nregistration to HM Land Registry (reference 260202-5732372). Further HM\nLand Registry enquiry references include 260929-6766714 and related\nreferences generated in September 2026.\n\nIf a Report Fraud reference is issued, I will provide it immediately. For\npresent purposes, I ask that the South Wales Police crime-recording request\nand the HM Land Registry report of suspected registration irregularities be\ntreated as the principal current investigative references.\n\n2. Documentary title sequence and suspected criminality\n\nThe public evidence index is available at:\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nThe material assembled there identifies a documentary sequence which, in my\npresent assessment, raises questions as to whether the family's historic\nproprietary interest in the farmhouse parcel was displaced through the use\nof records, possession evidence and registration material relating to a\ndifferent or wider parcel, and whether subsequent registration and dealings\nthen relied upon that resulting title position.\n\nFor convenience, I refer on the website to this as the \"synthetic title\"\nissue. That is a description of the documentary pattern I have identified,\nrather than an assumption that criminal liability has already been\nestablished.\n\nThe distinction is important because the 1987 Court of Appeal proceedings\nconcerned possession, limitation and the October 1974 correspondence. My\nconcern is that those proceedings did not determine the underlying\ndocumentary root of title to the farmhouse parcel now represented by the\nregistered title history.\n\n3. 1955 possession order and the neighbouring parcel\n\nA further issue requiring examination is the relationship between the 1955\npossession order and the land historically occupied and claimed by the\nWilliams/Buckler family.\n\nMy evidence indicates that the 1955 order related to a neighbouring parcel\nrather than the family's core farmhouse holding. I am concerned that\nsubsequent possession and development activity may nevertheless have\ntreated that order, or the associated possession history, as extending to\nland outside the parcel to which it actually related.\n\nRecent excavation and works on the former family land make this a live\nevidential issue. I ask that the underlying order, plans, descriptions and\nsubsequent land use be considered against the documentary title sequence\nrather than assuming that the parcels were identical.\n\n4. Possible loss or destruction of relevant records\n\nI hold dated photographs concerning works which removed a commemorative\ntree planted by my great-grandfather on or adjoining the former Great House\nFarm / Church View Close land.\n\nI have made a narrowed FOI request to the Vale of Glamorgan Council (case\n00211484) seeking the instruction, works order, authorisation and any\nrecord linking the tree to the Williams/Buckler family or to the 1988\ndemolition.\n\nMore generally, I am concerned that parts of the planning and land-history\nrecord which could bear upon the ownership history are incomplete or\nunavailable. I am not presently asking the CPS to draw an inference from\nthat absence. I ask that any potentially relevant records held by public\nauthorities or other custodians be identified and preserved while the\npolice and other investigations are ongoing.\n\n5. Existing correspondence and preservation\n\nI have maintained a continuous documentary record of communications\nconcerning these issues with:\n\n- South Wales Police, including FOI, SAR, crime-recording and preservation\ncorrespondence;\n- HM Land Registry and the Independent Complaints Reviewer (ICR/090/26);\n- Cadw, Heneb, RCAHMW, Glamorgan Archives, National Library of Wales and\nother heritage bodies; and\n- Vale of Glamorgan Council, including FOI requests and internal reviews.\n\nPreservation requests/notices have also been made to principal\nrecord-holders where I consider material may be relevant, so that\npotentially significant evidence is not inadvertently destroyed,\ntransferred or disposed of while these matters are being examined.\n\n6. Request to CPS Cymru-Wales\n\nI respectfully ask CPS Cymru-Wales to:\n\n(a) note the South Wales Police crime-recording request of 28 September\n2026 and HM Land Registry reference 260202-5732372 as the present principal\nreferences, with any subsequent police or Report Fraud reference to be\nadded when available;\n\n(b) ensure that the material is considered by the appropriate CPS\nprosecutor or team if it is referred for prosecutorial consideration,\nincluding consideration of whether the alleged documentary conduct raises\nsufficiently serious or complex criminal issues to require specialist\ncasework;\n\n(c) note that, should a private prosecution subsequently be instituted, I\nmay make a specific request for the CPS to consider the Director's power\nunder section 6(2) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985; and\n\n(d) advise me of the appropriate procedure for making such a request, and\nthe evidence CPS would require, if that stage is reached.\n\nI appreciate that the CPS does not itself conduct the police investigation.\nMy purpose at this stage is to ensure that the potential prosecutorial\ndimension is properly identified and that the present material is capable\nof being matched to any police investigation or later referral.\n\nI remain ready to provide an indexed evidential bundle comprising the 1955\nand 1974 material, historical conveyances and plans, HM Land Registry\ndocumentation for WA231076, WA240304 and related titles, relevant court\nrecords, chronology, and photographs concerning the former property and\nsubsequent works. The website provides a public index to much of this\nmaterial.\n\nI note the previous deadline of 13 October 2026. I will provide any South\nWales Police crime/incident reference or Report Fraud reference as soon as\nit is allocated.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/"},{"id":"gm-1a0f2422e78895e9","subject":"Re: death certificate","name":"Re: death certificate","date":"2026-09-30T12:20:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0f2422e78895e9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e7d2841902574-death-certificate","scopeTopics":["cardiff-reg"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff-reg"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","thre