 redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0f1f90f797cce7","direction":"received","from":"Cllr George Carroll","institutions":[{"id":"vale-scrutiny","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council (Scrutiny)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0f1f90f797cce7.json","textStatus":"available","text":"View this email in your browser (https://mailchi.mp/848bae40f8ee/in-touch-with-llandough-17666143?e=1429c2c1bb)\nNEXT SUNDAY: ROAD CLOSURES\nFOR CARDIFF HALF MARATHON\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDear Requester\n\nRoad closures will affect our community on the morning of Sunday 4th October for the Cardiff Half Marathon.\n\nPenarth Road, Barry Road and Cogan Spur will all be closed, as the marathon course runs along these roads.\n\nLlandough Hill will also be closed, to prevent vehicles diverted via Penlan Road from inadvertently trying to access Penarth Road while it's shut.\nDiversions will be in place, and you can see the full road closure map above.\n\nThe closures will operate between 9am and 12pm.\n\nFurther details can be found at the Cardiff Half Marathon website here.  (https://www.cardiffhalfmarathon.co.uk/event-info/road-closures/)\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/1BzkRccTvm/\n\nIf you have further questions, Requester, please let me know.\n\n\n**\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNext community litter pick\n\nOur last community litter pick has had great feedback.\n\nI've even had a couple of messages asking when the next one is taking place!\n\nLlandough Community Council organise these events throughout the year, but they usually put them on hold during the winter, due to lack of interest.\n\nBut given the enthusiasm, I thought it best to harness it!\n\nWe discussed it at last week's Community Council meeting, and I'm exploring organising another in the coming weeks.\n\nI'll need to liaise with the Vale Council to arrange equipment, but the Community Council are on board and have said they'll help.\n\nIf you're interested in taking part, Requester, drop me a message!\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/v/1KDWx1SUjX/\n\nLicensing Service of\nRevd Phil Maudsley\n\nI had a wonderful evening on Tuesday at the Licensing Service of Reverend Phil Maudsley, the new Penarth Ministry Area lead.\n\nIt was great to see many members of our community there, including Llandough Community Council Chair Mo Misra, Reverend Susannah Griffin and lots of other residents.\n\nPhil and his family have recently moved to South Wales from North Yorkshire, and I look forward to working with him.\n\nI know everyone in Llandough will join me in welcoming them to our community.\n\nGreenway Close verge\n\nWhen I was out in our village recently, a Greenway Close resident raised the overgrowth on the nearby verge.\n\nAs you'll see from the first picture, it was in need of attention.\n\nI raised with the Council. And I'm pleased to report it's now been cut back.\n\nThanks so much to the resident for coming over and raising this.\n\nIt helped ensure it was cleared.\n\nAs I always say, we're a team in Llandough.\n\nBy all chipping in, we make our village better for everyone.\n\nIf you ever spot anything that needs attention, Requester, do let me know!\n\nPreventing car thefts\n\nI spoke with two people who've recently purchased Faraday boxes while I was out meeting residents this week.\n\nWith attempted car thefts reported in our village in recent months, police have advised everyone with keyless fobs to keep them in a Faraday pouch or box as a security measure.\n\nIt's a sensible precaution and a small expense to protect your car.\n\nIt was good to see people following the advice.\n\nIf you require further information, please drop me a message.\n\nCommunity drop-in event:\n20th October\n\nOur next community drop-in event takes place at the Merrie Harrier on 20th October.\n\nLike the last one, it'll start at 7.00pm.\n\nThe pub is a key asset to our community.\n\nTracey and the team do a lot for us - help return the favour by lending them your support.\n\nYou can see some of their midweek offers below!\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/share/r/1EM9z5wbMs/\n\nOur Plan for Llandough!\n\n\nAs your councillor, I'm working with you all to secure a better future for Llandough. Together, we have a plan to deliver for the village.\n\nOur plan is making Llandough better by:\n\n1. Sorting out the parking problems\n2. Stamping out dog fouling\n3. Repairing our roads\n4. Stopping littering and flytipping\n5. Delivering better sports facilities\n6. Keeping the whole community involved\n\nIf you have any suggestions of what you'd like to see in Our Plan, please get in touch!\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F848bae40f8ee%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666143 Share (http://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fmailchi.mp%2F848bae40f8ee%2Fin-touch-with-llandough-17666143)\nhttps://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=dbf7d36859&e=1429c2c1bb Forward (https://us19.forward-to-friend.com/forward?u=7b7a08284cdbc1f69f5b0afd8&id=dbf7d36859&e=1429c2c1bb)\n\n============================================================\nI'm hoping to reach as many people as possible with this newsletter, so please feel free to forward it to friends and neighbours.\n\nIf this email has been forwarded to you, and you would like to sign up to my newsletter, please click ** here ([email redacted]\n.\nThis email was sent to you because your email address is on my subscribers list. If you don't want to receive any more messages from me, please click below to unsubscribe.\n\nYour consent was previously given during an online or offline interaction with me or the Conservatives. If you feel this is incorrect or would like to comment, please contact me. I do not buy email lists.\n\nPromoted by Chris Kirkham on behalf of George Carroll, both of Vale of Glamorgan Conservatives, Holton House, 50 Holton Road, Barry [post