rection":"received","from":"NIO FOI","institutions":[{"id":"nio","name":"Northern Ireland Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ed9a03118aab9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\nThank you for your enquiry of 28/09/26 to the Wales Office.\n\n\nWe acknowledge receipt of your preservation notice.\n\nPlease note that as your correspondence asks to preserve records and does\nnot request recorded information, under section 8(1) of the FOI Act 2000 it\nis not being processed as a request for information. Should you wish to\nrequest copies of or access to any specific records held by the authority,\nplease respond to this email detailing the specific recorded information\nyou require.\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nFreedom of Information Team\n\n\n[image: image.png]\n\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 28 September 2026 22:42\nTo: [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n[email redacted]; [email redacted];\n[email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n[email redacted]; [email redacted];\n[email redacted]; [email redacted];\n[email redacted]; Wales Office FOI <\n[email redacted]>; [email redacted]\nSubject: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do\nnot destroy, transfer or dispose\n\nTo each recipient, in your own capacity as holder or likely holder of\nrecords. Please do not treat this as a joint reply. Answer only for your\nown holdings.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a preservation notice. It is not a claim form and not service of\nproceedings. It does not replace any FOI, review or subject access request\nalready with you.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St\nDochdwy's. Titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690, WA735527, and any\nrelated title. Planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, transfer out of your custody without a\nwritten receipt, or dispose of, any file, plan, photograph, tape or\nelectronic record in your possession, custody or control relating to:\n\n1. The 1877 split, the 1916 and 1939 tenancies, and the 1938 Bute to\nWestern Ground Rents conveyance.\n2. The 1955 and 1962 possession orders, the 1974 proceedings, and BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n3. First registration: WA231076 application 30 November 1982; WA240304\napplication 23 February 1983; later amalgamation.\n4. The 1988 possession (29 November) and demolition (begun 6 December),\nincluding listing, planning, police and any liaison papers.\n5. Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler, so far as\nyour file concerns this land.\n\nAlso preserve, if you hold them, the following planning and land-charge\nclasses. Absence from a 2026 file disclosure is not proof they never\nexisted:\n\n6. Any section 52 Town and Country Planning Act 1971 agreement, later\nsection 106 instrument, deed, undertaking or other agreement regulating the\ndevelopment or use of this land, and any corresponding local-land-charge\nentry.\n7. The historic planning-register entries required by the Town and Country\nPlanning General Development Order 1988 for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES\n(applications, reserved matters, plans and drawings, and decision\ninformation).\n8. The officer's report annexes to 89/01396/OUT, including Appendix B\n(further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust), and Appendices\nC–E.\n9. The condition chain on 89/01396/OUT: conditions 16–18; the Council's\nOctober 1990 confirmation of condition 17; GGAT's July 1992 archaeological\nwarning; the September 1992 reserved-matters approval; and the 1993–94\npapers on whether condition 18 had been discharged.\n10. Any preliminary environmental-assessment / screening determination for\nthe outline application (site described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38 ha).\n11. Any record of the statutory consultation route used because the land\nwas, or was treated as, a site of archaeological interest / SMR entry under\nthe 1988 Order.\n12. The complete 92/00671/RES file, and any sale, option,\nconditional-contract or transfer paper on the planning files covering BP\nProperties to Ideal Homes Wales, including the recorded transfer of\n3 December 1993.\n13. The application-receipt record for 89/01396/OUT (form dated October\n1989; reconstructed Council receipt 8 November 1989).\n\nPlease stop routine deletion, including archived mailboxes, for anything in\nthat scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n. The investigation distinguishes the farmhouse parcel from the eastern\nfields. The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the\nOctober 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of the\nfarmhouse parcel. These records go to that question. This notice is not a\nfinding against any of you.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer responsible for the hold, and say what\nyou hold in scope. If you hold nothing, say what you searched.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration,\nconcealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the register.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]\n________________________________\n This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the\naddressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not\npermitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies\nand inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure\nmedium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone\nelse. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in\nresponse to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender\nor the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry\nof Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content\nmay be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not\nbroken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n________________________________\nMae’r e-bost hwn (ac unrhyw atodiad) wedi’i fwriadu at sylw’r derbynnydd\n(derbynwyr) yn unig. Ni chaniateir i unrhyw un ei ddefnyddio, ei ddatgelu,\nei gadw na gwneud copi ohono heb awdurdod. Os nad chi yw’r unigolyn y mae’r\ne-bost wedi’i fwriadu ar ei gyfer, dilëwch bob copi, os gwelwch yn dda a\nrhowch wybod i’r anfonwr drwy anfon e-bost yn ôl. Nid yw anfon negeseuon\ne-bost ar y rhyngrwyd yn ddull diogel o gyfathrebu. Gallai rhywun arall\nagor a darllen unrhyw ymateb i’r neges hon. Cofiwch hyn wrth benderfynu\nanfon deunydd mewn ymateb i'r neges hon drwy e-bost. Gall y Weinyddiaeth\nCyfiawnder fonitro, cofnodi a chadw'r e-bost hwn (pa un ai chi yw'r anfonwr\nynteu’r derbynnydd). Mae’n bosib y defnyddir meddalwedd monitro / atal\nnegeseuon e-bost, a gellir darllen cynnwys yr e-bost ar unrhyw adeg. Mae\ngennych gyfrifoldeb i sicrhau nad ydych yn torri unrhyw gyfreithiau wrth\ngreu neu anfon negeseuon e-bost a’u cynnwys ymlaen. Wrth adael Mewnrwyd\nDdiogel y Llywodraeth, nid oedd unrhyw feirws yn gysylltiedig â’r e-bost\nhwn. Mae’n ddigon posibl y bydd unrhyw ohebiaeth drwy’r GSi yn cael ei\nlogio, ei monitro a/neu ei chofnodi yn awtomatig am resymau cyfreithiol."},{"id":"gm-1a0ed9801c58b6b2","subject":"Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","name":"Internal Review 1188/26 of FOI 719/26","date":"2026-09-29T14:35:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ed9801c58b6b2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ed9801c58b6b2-internal-review-1188-26-of-foi-719-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addr