sses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9fa2e406d0af","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9fa2e406d0af.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester,\n\nYour question was submitted successfully to the National Library of Wales enquiries service / Cyflwynwyd eich cwestiwn yn llwyddiannus i Wasanaeth Ymholiadau Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru\n\nDue to high demand and some resource challenges, there may be some delay in responding to enquiries at present. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will provide an update as soon as possible.\n\nOherwydd lefel uchel y galw a rhai heriau adnoddau, bydd oedi gydag ymateb i ymholiadau ar hyn o bryd. Yr ydym yn ymddiheuro am unrhyw anghyfleuster a achosir gan hyn ac fe fyddwn yn darparu diweddariad cyn gynted ag y medrwn.\n\nWe will contact you as soon as possible. In the meantime, perhaps you can visit our FAQs <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com>\nByddwn yn cysylltu â chi cyn gynted â phosibl! Yn y cyfamser, efallai yr hoffech chi chwlio ein  FAQs  <http://national-library-wales.libanswers.com> perthnasol gall ateb eich cwestiwn.\n\n\n\nWe welcome calls and correspondence in Welsh. You will receive a response in Welsh and correspondence in Welsh will not result in a delay./ Rydym yn croesawu galwadau a gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwch yn derbyn ymateb yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nSep 28 2026, 10:42PM via Email\nPreservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose\nTo each recipient, in your own capacity as holder or likely holder of\nrecords. Please do not treat this as a joint reply. Answer only for\nyour own holdings.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a preservation notice. It is not a claim form and not service\nof proceedings. It does not replace any FOI, review or subject access\nrequest already with you.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining\nSt Dochdwy's. Titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690, WA735527,\nand any related title. Planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, transfer out of your custody\nwithout a written receipt, or dispose of, any file, plan, photograph,\ntape or electronic record in your possession, custody or control\nrelating to:\n\n1. The 1877 split, the 1916 and 1939 tenancies, and the 1938 Bute to\nWestern Ground Rents conveyance.\n2. The 1955 and 1962 possession orders, the 1974 proceedings, and BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n3. First registration: WA231076 application 30 November 1982; WA240304\napplication 23 February 1983; later amalgamation.\n4. The 1988 possession (29 November) and demolition (begun 6\nDecember), including listing, planning, police and any liaison papers.\n5. Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler, so\nfar as your file concerns this land.\n\nAlso preserve, if you hold them, the following planning and\nland-charge classes. Absence from a 2026 file disclosure is not proof\nthey never existed:\n\n6. Any section 52 Town and Country Planning Act 1971 agreement, later\nsection 106 instrument, deed, undertaking or other agreement\nregulating the development or use of this land, and any corresponding\nlocal-land-charge entry.\n7. The historic planning-register entries required by the Town and\nCountry Planning General Development Order 1988 for 89/01396/OUT and\n92/00671/RES (applications, reserved matters, plans and drawings, and\ndecision information).\n8. The officer's report annexes to 89/01396/OUT, including Appendix B\n(further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust), and\nAppendices C–E.\n9. The condition chain on 89/01396/OUT: conditions 16–18; the\nCouncil's October 1990 confirmation of condition 17; GGAT's July 1992\narchaeological warning; the September 1992 reserved-matters approval;\nand the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged.\n10. Any preliminary environmental-assessment / screening determination\nfor the outline application (site described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38\nha).\n11. Any record of the statutory consultation route used because the\nland was, or was treated as, a site of archaeological interest / SMR\nentry under the 1988 Order.\n12. The complete 92/00671/RES file, and any sale, option,\nconditional-contract or transfer paper on the planning files covering\nBP Properties to Ideal Homes Wales, including the recorded transfer of\n3 December 1993.\n13. The application-receipt record for 89/01396/OUT (form dated\nOctober 1989; reconstructed Council receipt 8 November 1989).\n\nPlease stop routine deletion, including archived mailboxes, for\nanything in that scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n. The investigation distinguishes the farmhouse parcel from the\neastern fields. The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession,\nlimitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the\ndocumentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These records go to that\nquestion. This notice is not a finding against any of you.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer responsible for the hold, and say\nwhat you hold in scope. If you hold nothing, say what you searched.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title,\nregistration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the\nregister.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]\n\n------------------\n\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9823416.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f8374f5ca52","subject":"Automatic reply: Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","name":"Automatic reply: Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f8374f5ca52.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f7f0377a51b-automatic-reply-subject-access-crime-recording-request-and-search-note-on-719-26-great-house-farm-llandough-1988","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f7f0377a51b","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f8374f5ca52.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n\n• Your full postal address\n\n• Your contact telephone number\n\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in Parliament, it will be dealt with as appropriate.\n\n\nMinisterial Business\n\nIf you are contacting me in my capacity as a Minister at the FCDO, you will need to redirect your email to to [email redacted]<[email redacted]>, or alternatively contact your own MP – you can find who that is at https://members.parliament.uk/FindYourMP\n\n\nThank you for taking the time to contact me.\n\nFor information about how we use your personal data, see our Privacy Notice<https://www.stephendoughty.wales/privacynotice>.\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nStephen\n\n\nStephen Doughty MP / AS\nMember of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth // Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nHouse of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f80450c11d1","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f80450c11d1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f7c642730d3-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-transfer-or-dispose","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f7c642730d3","direction":"received","from":"_DataProtection","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f80450c11d1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for contacting HM Land Registry. This is an automated response to confirm that we have received your correspondence. We aim to formally provide an acknowledgement within three working days. If you have any special requirements that mean you would like us to communicate with you in a specific way, please let us know and we will make adjustments if we can.\n\n\nIf you are contacting us in respect of any matters relating to property registration or have a general customer enquiry – Our team are unable to respond to any general registration enquiries or provide updates on any property applications. Please redirect your customer enquiry to our Customer Support colleagues, using any of the methods below:\n\n  *   Online contact form: HM Land Registry Contact Us form<https://customerhelp.landregistry.gov.uk/guide-page-external/?stepid=2b31bc48-eb96-eb11-b1ac-002248413956>\n\n\n  *   Website - www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/contact-hm-land-registry>\n\n\n  *   Telephone\n\n\n     *   English language [phone redacted]\n\n     *   Welsh language [phone redacted]\n\n\nTelephone lines are open between 08:00 and 17:00 Monday to Thursday. This does not include Bank Holidays.\n\n\n  *   Post - HM Land Registry Citizen Centre\n\nPO Box 74\n\nGloucester\n[postcode redacted]\n\n\nThere is no direct contact e-mail address for Customer Support. Please use the online contact form and any responses will be issued via e-mail.\n\n\nIf you have made a request under the Freedom of Information Act or Environmental Information Regulations–The statutory timescale for response is 20 working days following receipt of your request.\n\n\nIf you have made a request in relation to your data rights, for example, a subject access request for personal data – The statutory timescale for response is one calendar month following receipt of your request.\n\n\nPlease note that where personal data is held on our register, it is exempt from the right of subject access under UK GDPR.\n\n\n\nWhere any personal data is held on record for a registered title, the exemption provided at Schedule 2, Part 1, Paragraph 5(1) of the Data Protection Act 2018 would be engaged. \n\n \n\nThis states: \n\n \n\n“5(1) The listed GDPR provisions do not apply to personal data consisting of information that the controller is obliged by an enactment to make available to the public, to the extent that the application of those provisions would prevent the controller from complying with that obligation.” \n\n\nPlease see the section below titled 'Register information and your data protection rights' for further explanation.\n\n\nIf you have only copied your correspondence to us - we will not respond.\n\n\nYours sincerely\n\n\n\nInformation Rights Team\n\nHM Land Registry\n\n\nRegister information and your data protection rights    \n\n   \n\nData protection law permits HM Land Registry to use personal data for our official purposes.\n\n\n\nThe lawful basis for HM Land Registry processing personal data under the United Kingdom (UK) General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) is that it is necessary to enable us to perform our public task of the registration of land and property (Article 6(1)(e) of UK GDPR). This is defined in the Land Registration Act 2002. \n\n\n\nParagraph 5 of Schedule 2 Part 1 of the Data Protection Act 2018 provides the following exemption from the specified UK GDPR provisions:\n\n\n\n“The listed UK GDPR provisions do not apply to personal data consisting of information that the controller is obliged by an enactment to make available to the public, to the extent that the application of those provisions would prevent the controller from complying with that obligation.”    \n\n\n\nThe Land Registration Act 2002 is the principal legislation governing land registration in England and Wales. It sets out provisions for the keeping of a register of title to land and requirements for its administration by HM Land Registry under a Chief Land Registrar.\n\n\nThe Chief Land Registrar is required by the Land Registration Act 2002 and to make register information (including any documents held on the register of title) available to the public, therefore the following data protection provisions do not apply:\n\n  *   the requirement to provide ‘privacy notices’ to individuals\n\n  *   the requirement to provide personal data in response to subject access requests\n\n  *   the requirement to rectification\n\n  *   the requirement to comply with requests to erasure (right to be ‘forgotten’)\n\n  *   most of the principles of UK GDPR\n\nPlease visit our website for further information about our registers:\n\n\n\nwww.gov.uk/get-information-about-property-and-land<http://www.gov.uk/get-information-about-property-and-land>\n\n  \n\nFor further information in relation to your rights and how HMLR processes personal data please refer to our Personal Information Charter:\n\n\n\nwww.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter<http://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter>\n\n\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7f0377a51b","subject":"Automatic reply: Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","name":"Automatic reply: Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7f0377a51b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f7f0377a51b-automatic-reply-subject-access-crime-recording-request-and-search-note-on-719-26-great-house-farm-llandough-1988","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f7f0377a51b","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7f0377a51b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7e7f60e6fd","subject":"FOI — Welsh Office / Cadw papers, July–December 1988 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — following 26FOI 103","name":"FOI — Welsh Office / Cadw papers, July–December 1988 — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — following 26FOI 103","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7e7f60e6fd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3f9730cdedac-foi-welsh-office-cadw-papers-july-december-1988-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-following-26foi-103","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3f9730cdedac","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["26FOI103"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7e7f60e6fd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information\nWelsh Government\n[email redacted]\ncc: [email redacted] — so 26FOI 103 stays on the same fact\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nRequest under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\nRequester: Requester.\n\nWales Office, in 26FOI 103 dated 22 September 2026, said historic Welsh Office / Cadw listing papers for this house sit with you. This is that request. I am not asking you to decide title.\n\nPlease disclose recorded information held by the Welsh Government or by Cadw as part of it concerning:\n\n1. Any consideration, between 1 July and 31 December 1988, of listing, spot-listing or emergency listing of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's (approx. ST 168 733).\n2. Any inspection, photograph, minute or note of the building, or of its demolition, in that period. Possession was taken on 29 November 1988. Demolition of the farmhouse began on 6 December 1988.\n3. Any transfer, destruction or disposal of those files, with the schedule used and the date.\n\nIf nothing is held, please say what was searched, including Cadw listing files, Welsh Office inherited files, and any index of destroyed building records.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . The investigation distinguishes Parcel A (farmhouse, garden, buildings and yard — the family's maintained freehold) from Parcel B (eastern fields — not presently disputed). The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide whether the documentary root of Parcel A was ever established. These papers go to that question. They are not a finding against Cadw.\n\nPlease confirm the reference and the 20 working-day date, and preserve anything in scope.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation or reopening. This is not a claim form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7f43bbc6e7","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7f43bbc6e7.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["cotswold"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cotswold"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"cotswold","name":"Cotswold Archaeology"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7f43bbc6e7.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your enquiry we will pass this onto the relevant team. Whilst they will endeavour to respond as soon as possible it may take up to one working week before you hear from them. If the matter is urgent, please call [phone redacted]\n\nKind Regards,\nEnquiries"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7d82dd5650","subject":"Record now public — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — 1987 case, 1988 demolition, 2026 disclosure","name":"Record now public — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — 1987 case, 1988 demolition, 2026 disclosure","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7d82dd5650.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f77fcdf6f43-cord-now-public-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-1987-case-1988-demolition-2026-disclosure","scopeTopics":["itv"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["itv"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f77fcdf6f43","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"itv","name":"ITV Archive"}],"refs":["00210772","26FOI103","N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7d82dd5650.json","textStatus":"available","text":"News desks,\n\nI am not asking you to adopt a legal conclusion. I am asking you to look at a primary record that is now public, before more of it is lost.\n\nhttps://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nWhat the record shows, as distinct from what is still a question:\n\nGreat House Farm / Tŷ Mawr stood by St Dochdwy's, Llandough. Possession was taken on 29 November 1988. Demolition of the farmhouse began on 6 December 1988. The land is now Church View Close. The current registered proprietor of WA231076 is Persimmon Homes (Wales) Ltd. First-registration applications were made on 30 November 1982 (WA231076) and 23 February 1983 (WA240304, later closed into WA231076).\n\nBP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 decided possession, limitation and the effect of letters in October 1974. It did not decide whether the documentary root of the farmhouse and garden was ever established. The family's investigation is that the house and garden were a separate parcel from the eastern fields, and that later papers used \"whole farm\" for both. That is a working reconstruction, set out on the site with the documents and the gaps. It is not a judgment.\n\nThis month, on the disclosure side, not as findings: Wales Office answered 26FOI 103 and pointed 1988 listing papers to the Welsh Government. A Vale of Glamorgan internal review requested on 7 July (00210772) has no outcome. HM Land Registry file N610CGV is with the Independent Complaints Reviewer. A replica of the house is being built in the Welsh settlement in Patagonia as a museum, not as restitution.\n\nContemporary reporting described the 1988 scene in the language of a battleground. I can supply documents and a named contact.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7d5ec760dd","subject":"Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","name":"Subject access, crime-recording request, and search note on 719/26 — Great House Farm, Llandough, 1988","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7d5ec760dd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3f9bfedd9297-subject-access-crime-recording-request-and-search-note-on-719-26-great-house-farm-llandough-1988","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3f9bfedd9297","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7d5ec760dd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information / Data Management / Crime Recording\nSouth Wales Police\n[email redacted]\ncc: Stephen Doughty MP — constituency record only. Please do not treat the copy as a further request to the MP.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is separate from the internal review of 719/26 sent on the morning of 27 September 2026. Please do not merge them.\n\nI am not asking you to decide the civil claim. I am asking you to apply the recording rules, and to disclose personal data.\n\n1. Subject access, UK GDPR Article 15. Personal data you hold about me, Requester, arising from the eviction and demolition at Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, between 29 November and 6 December 1988, and from later correspondence including 719/26 and the request of 20 August 2026 concerning the deaths of William Buckler and Mary Doreen Williams. Say what identification you need before the month starts.\n\n2. Crime recording. Please record, or explain in writing why you will not record, a report of suspected fraud and concealment in the creation and use of title to that land, including first registration of WA231076 (application 30 November 1982) and WA240304 (application 23 February 1983), and the 1987 proceedings. The question is whether a crime record should be opened. It is not a request that you find the civil title.\n\n3. Search note on 719/26. “No records held” for a documented multi-officer operation in November–December 1988 still requires a note of systems searched, years searched, and whether South Wales Constabulary paper has gone to Glamorgan Archives. That note can sit with the internal review. I ask for it here so the crime-recording decision is not made without it.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These are evidential questions. They are not a finding against any officer.\n\nPlease preserve any 1988 operational file, pocket book, custody record or transfer list. Nothing in this letter abandons any claim. This is not a claim form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7c642730d3","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","date":"2026-09-28T21:42:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7c642730d3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f7c642730d3-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-transfer-or-dispose","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f7c642730d3","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7c642730d3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7a29892868","subject":"00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm","name":"00211484 — narrowed request — commemorative tree, Church View Close / Great House Farm","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7a29892868.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3fa1b0e3358b-00211484-narrowed-request-commemorative-tree-church-view-close-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3fa1b0e3358b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772","00211484"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7a29892868.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Information Governance Team,\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n[email redacted]\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nCase 00211484. This narrows the request. It does not reopen 00210772. Please keep them separate.\n\nI hold dated photographs of the works. Please disclose:\n\n1. The instruction, works order or contractor record for removal of the commemorative tree on or adjoining the former Great House Farm / Church View Close land.\n2. The date of the works and who authorised them.\n3. Any note linking the tree to the Williams / Buckler family, to Mary Williams, or to the 1988 demolition.\n\nIf nothing is held, say what was searched.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . This request is about one tree and one works record. It is not a request that you decide title.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7a146cba39","subject":"FOI/EIR — Great House Farm / Church View Close — s.52/land charges, planning register, EA screening, condition 16–18 chain, 92/00671/RES — new request, not 00210772","name":"FOI/EIR — Great House Farm / Church View Close — s.52/land charges, planning register, EA screening, condition 16–18 chain, 92/00671/RES — new request, not 00210772","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:55Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7a146cba39.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e2492937ce6-foi-eir-great-house-farm-church-view-close-s-52-land-charges-planning-register-ea-screening-condition-16-18-chain-92-006","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e2492937ce6","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772","00211463","00211484"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7a146cba39.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Information Governance Team\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n[email redacted]\ncc: [email redacted]\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nNew request under FOIA 2000 and/or EIR 2004. Do not treat this as a reopening or expansion of 00210772, 00211463 or 00211484. Those cases stay as they are.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Leckwith Road, Llandough, later Church View Close.\nApplications: 89/01396/OUT (outline granted 13 March 1990) and 92/00671/RES.\n\nI already have, or have already asked for, the officer's report, Policy H.2 text, Appendices C–E, the decision notices, and the general archaeological-condition papers. This request is confined to classes that those earlier requests did not name.\n\nPlease disclose recorded information held, or confirm item by item if not held:\n\n1. Section 52 / later section 106 / land charges\nAny agreement under section 52 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1971, any later section 106 instrument, any deed, undertaking or other agreement regulating the development or use of this land, and any corresponding entry on the local land charges register. Search legal, planning and land-charges holdings, not only the 2026 planning-file scan. If none is held, say so expressly. That is an open records question, not a conclusion that none existed.\n\n2. Historic planning register\nThe planning-register entries that the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 required the authority to keep for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES: the applications, reserved-matters applications, plans and drawings, and relevant decision information. If the 2026 file disclosure is incomplete against that register, say what the register still lists and what is missing from the file.\n\n3. Appendix B\nAppendix B to the officer's report on 89/01396/OUT: the further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust. Case 00211463 asked for C, D and E and for a list of annexes. It did not ask for B by that description. If B is not held, say when it left the file, under what retention rule, and whether any copy survives elsewhere.\n\n4. Condition 16–18 chain\nNamed papers, not a general search:\n(a) conditions 16, 17 and 18 as issued on the 13 March 1990 permission;\n(b) the Council's October 1990 confirmation of condition 17;\n(c) GGAT's archaeological warning of July 1992;\n(d) the September 1992 reserved-matters approval, and whether any further archaeological condition was attached;\n(e) the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged, including GGAT's December 1993 letters recommending a breach-of-condition notice.\n\n5. Environmental assessment / screening\nAny preliminary environmental-assessment determination, screening opinion, or recorded decision that an environmental statement was or was not required for 89/01396/OUT. The application site is described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38 hectares. I am not asserting that an environmental statement was required. I am asking whether the Council made and recorded the determination at all.\n\n6. Archaeological-interest consultation route\nAny record of the statutory consultation route actually used because the land was recorded in the county Sites and Monuments Record, or was treated as a \"site of archaeological interest\" under the 1988 Order. I am not asking you to treat SMR status as automatic proof of a particular duty. I am asking what route was used.\n\n7. Application receipt date\nThe Council's receipt record for 89/01396/OUT. The application form is dated October 1989. The reconstructed planning record gives 8 November 1989 as receipt of the application and plans. Please supply the date-stamped receipt, validation or register entry.\n\n8. 92/00671/RES completeness and applicant standing\n(a) A file list or register for 92/00671/RES showing what the reserved-matters file originally contained.\n(b) Any sale, option, conditional-contract or authority-to-apply paper on the planning files covering the change from BP Properties (1989 outline applicant) to Ideal Homes Wales (appearing on the 1992 reserved-matters trail), including the recorded BP-to-Ideal Homes transfer of 3 December 1993.\nThis is a documentary interest/authority question. It is not an allegation that the 1992 application was invalid.\n\nIf a record is not held, say so for that item. If it was destroyed, transferred or archived, give the date, the schedule, and any surviving catalogue. Search planning, legal, land charges and archived/scanned holdings.\n\nPlease give a new reference and the 20 working-day date. Preserve anything in scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . I am not asking the Council to decide title.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f7a1a4fa353","subject":"Subject access request — WA231076 / WA240304 — Great House Farm, Llandough — Williams / Buckler","name":"Subject access request — WA231076 / WA240304 — Great House Farm, Llandough — Williams / Buckler","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f7a1a4fa353.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e3f997bc1bf94-subject-access-request-wa231076-wa240304-great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e3f997bc1bf94","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f7a1a4fa353.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Data Protection Officer\nHM Land Registry\n[email redacted]\ncc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]\nRefs already with you: N610CGV; letter of SG Haste, 30 July 2026\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nSubject access request under UK GDPR Article 15.\nRequester: Requester.\nTitles: WA231076 and WA240304 (closed). Land north of Leckwith Road, Llandough (Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr).\n\nThis is not a request for an official copy of the register. It is a request for personal data in the working file in which I am identifiable, including customer-complaint files, the pack sent to Stephen Doughty MP, and any note of my correspondence on N610CGV.\n\nPlease also say whether the first-registration file contains personal data about Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) or William Buckler, so far as you can disclose it to me as a family representative, and what identity you require before the month starts.\n\nThe matters to which that file goes, so you can search properly, are these. They are questions, not findings against Land Registry:\n\n1. First-registration applications: WA231076 on 30 November 1982 (form 1E); WA240304 on 23 February 1983 (form 1C); later amalgamation and closure of WA240304.\n2. A 31 December 1969 conveyance, Western Ground Rents to BP Pension Trust, identified as a root, and whether it is on the 30 July 2026 schedule of documents surviving on the file.\n3. Notice and opportunity to object in 1982–83, while Mary Williams remained in occupation of the farmhouse. Family evidence is that notification was not received until after her death on 26 March 1983. I am seeking the notice and service record.\n4. What the 1987 Court of Appeal decided (possession, limitation, October 1974 letters) and what it did not decide (documentary root of the farmhouse and garden parcel).\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ .\n\nPlease preserve the first-registration file and the complaint file. Do not start the statutory month until you have said what identification you need. Nothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the register. This is not a claim form and not service.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f79f658c66c","subject":"Request for Internal Review — 26FOI 103 — response dated 22 September 2026","name":"Request for Internal Review — 26FOI 103 — response dated 22 September 2026","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f79f658c66c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e4fb51bacf452-quest-for-internal-review-26foi-103-response-dated-22-september-2026","scopeTopics":["wales-office"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["wales-office"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e4fb51bacf452","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"wales-office","name":"Wales Office"}],"refs":["26FOI103"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f79f658c66c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Team\nWales Office\nGwydyr House\nWhitehall\nLondon [postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]\n\ncc: [email redacted] — the mailbox that sent the acknowledgement and the response\n\nDear Sir or Madam,\n\nRequest for Internal Review — 26FOI 103 — response dated 22 September 2026\nRequester: Requester\n\nI request an internal review of the handling and substance of 26FOI 103.\n\nThis is an FOI review only. I am not asking the Wales Office to determine title, to reopen BP Properties Ltd v Buckler, or to adopt any party's case on the land. I am asking whether the letter of 22 September 2026 answered the request that was made, and whether the search described in it was adequate.\n\nA. What is already on this file\n\n1. 29 August 2026 — I asked the Wales Office for recorded information about Great House Farm. Your letter of 22 September quotes the request as five points. I adopt that quotation. The points were:\n\n- records of any communication or outreach between Cadw, or its predecessor functions, and the Office of the Secretary of State for Wales / Welsh Office concerning Great House Farm during July–December 1988;\n- records of any recommendation, briefing, submission, notification or formal appeal concerning the protection or listing of Great House Farm submitted to the Secretary of State;\n- records of any communications with the occupiers and owners of the property before the refusal decision of 5 December 1988;\n- any surviving destruction, disposal, transfer or accession documentation relating to the Great House Farm 1988 assessment file, including certificates, dockets, lists, database entries, retention schedules, disposal authorities or other contemporaneous records held by the Welsh Office, its predecessors, Cadw, or any repository to which relevant records were transferred;\n- information regarding a decision made in relation to Great House Farm in 1988, including the evidence that was used to support that decision.\n\n2. 8 September 2026 — acknowledgement from NIO FOI ([email redacted]), recording the request date as 29/08/26. It named no officer and described no search.\n\n3. 22 September 2026 — covering email from the same NIO FOI mailbox, attaching “26FOI 103 - Buckler - Response.pdf”. The covering email contained no substance. The letter is signed Freedom of Information Team, Wales Office, and directs any review to [email redacted].\n\nThis review is within the two calendar months stated in that letter. The deadline you gave is 22 November 2026.\n\nB. What the letter actually says, and what it does not\n\nThe operative paragraph is this:\n\n“We have carried out a search of our digital records and have determined that the Wales Office does not hold the information requested. Any paper files previously held by the former Welsh Office relating to this matter would have been transferred to the National Assembly for Wales in 1999, and subsequently to the Welsh Government in 2007.”\n\nThat paragraph does not answer the request. The gaps are these.\n\n1. Digital records only. The letter says a search of digital records. It does not say that paper, microfilm, card indexes, transfer lists, accession registers, or destruction schedules were searched. A 1988 Welsh Office file is a paper file. A search confined to current digital holdings cannot find it, and cannot find the transfer or destruction docket that the fourth bullet asked for.\n\n2. “Would have been transferred” is not a search result. It is an assumption about devolution. It is not a statement that a transfer list was consulted, that a file for this house appears on that list, or that the file was received in Cardiff. “Would have been” covers three different outcomes: transferred, destroyed, or still here under another description. The letter does not distinguish them.\n\n3. The fourth bullet asked for the transfer, disposal and accession records themselves. Those records, if they exist, are Wales Office records of what left the building. They are not the assessment file. Pointing me to the Welsh Government does not answer a request for the docket, the list, the database entry or the disposal authority. Those may still be held here even if the file went to Cardiff. The letter does not say they were searched for.\n\n4. The five bullets are not answered one by one. There is no finding on communications with Cadw; no finding on any briefing or appeal to the Secretary of State; no finding on communications with occupiers and owners before 5 December 1988; no finding on the evidence said to have supported a 1988 decision. A single sentence that digital records do not hold “the information requested” does not show that each limb was searched.\n\n5. The letter uses “the refusal decision of 5 December 1988” only because I used it. It does not say whether that decision is recognised, whether a file for it was identified, or whether the decision is one of the papers “which would have been transferred”. Silence on a dated decision is not a not-held finding.\n\n6. “You may therefore wish” is not section 16 advice. Section 16 requires advice and assistance so far as reasonable. A reasonable step, where the department asserts a transfer, is to give the receiving body's file reference, the date of transfer, and the series. None is given. If the intention was section 21 (information reasonably accessible elsewhere), that exemption is not named, and the conditions are not addressed. A suggestion that I write to [email redacted] is not a section 21 notice.\n\n7. “Does not hold” is stated as a conclusion. The search described cannot support it. A not-held finding under section 1 requires a search capable of finding the information. A search of digital records, plus an assumption about 1999, is not that search.\n\n8. The request was answered from a Northern Ireland Office mailbox. The letter is in the name of the Wales Office. The review must be of the Wales Office search. Please confirm it will not be taken by the person who signed the 22 September letter.\n\nC. What the reviewing officer is asked to determine\n\n1. What was searched, by name: digital systems, paper series, transfer lists, accession registers, destruction schedules, Gwydyr House holdings, and any index of files passed to the National Assembly in 1999 or to the Welsh Government in 2007. If a location was not searched, say so.\n\n2. For each of the five bullets, a separate finding: held, not held after the searches at (1), transferred (with date, recipient and reference), or destroyed (with date and disposal authority).\n\n3. Whether any transfer, disposal or accession record relating to a Great House Farm 1988 assessment file is held by this department, as distinct from the assessment file itself.\n\n4. Whether any record of a decision on or about 5 December 1988, or of communications with the occupiers or owners before that date, was identified even as an index entry.\n\n5. If information is held and is not to be disclosed, a section 17 notice naming the exemption. Do not replace that notice with a referral.\n\n6. If the review maintains that the file went to Cardiff, the transfer reference. Without it, the referral is an assertion.\n\nD. Scope, so the review is not narrowed again\n\nThe window is July–December 1988. Possession of Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, adjoining St Dochdwy's, was taken on 29 November 1988. Demolition of the farmhouse began on 6 December 1988. The refusal date in the request is 5 December 1988. Those dates fix the search. They do not ask you to decide the land.\n\nI have made a parallel request to the Welsh Government, following the referral. That does not discharge 26FOI 103. A file can have been transferred and the transfer docket can still be here. Both questions were asked. Only one was gestured at.\n\nE. Why these records are in scope, without asking you to decide title\n\nThe public index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/\n\nThe investigation distinguishes Parcel A (farmhouse, garden, buildings and yard — the family's maintained freehold interest out of the Bute estate) from Parcel B (eastern fields). Later papers use “whole farm”. BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of Parcel A. Whether the Secretary of State or Cadw looked at this house in the week it was refused and pulled down is a records question. It is not a request that you adopt the family's case.\n\nF. Preservation\n\nPlease preserve any record that may fall within 26FOI 103 while this review is open, including transfer lists, destruction schedules and anything due for routine disposal. Do not transfer or destroy in-scope material without a written receipt that can be disclosed on the review.\n\nG. Reservation\n\nThis letter does not waive any position on title, registration, concealment, limitation, or any later reopening. It is an internal review under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is not a claim form and is not service of proceedings.\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt, give the review reference, and state the date by which the review will be completed. ICO guidance is that an internal review should normally be completed within 20 working days.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f79f062df99","subject":"Formal concern, preservation and subject access — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — remedy before escalation","name":"Formal concern, preservation and subject access — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — remedy before escalation","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f79f062df99.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e2089441e30-formal-concern-preservation-and-subject-access-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-remedy-before-escalation","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e2089441e30","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772","00211463","00211484"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f79f062df99.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Victoria Davidson\nMonitoring Officer and Head of Legal and Democratic Services\nVale of Glamorgan Council\n[email redacted]\nAlso: [email redacted]; [email redacted]\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a formal concern, a preservation notice, and a subject access request. It is the opportunity to remedy before the Information Commissioner and, if the internal processes end without remedy, the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales.\n\nI am not asking the Council to decide title. I am asking it to deal with its own records and its own delay.\n\n1. Complete the internal review of FOI/EIR 00210772, requested 7 July 2026, acknowledged 10 July 2026, further apology 11 September 2026, chased 5 August, 1 September and 22 September 2026. There is still no outcome. That is past a reasonable period. An ICO complaint confined to that delay is drafted. A completed review would deal with the point.\n\n2. Preserve planning, building-control, housing, legal, local-land-charge and land records for Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough, titles WA231076 and WA240304, Church View Close, and the 1988 demolition (possession 29 November 1988; demolition begun 6 December 1988). Stop routine destruction of those files. That hold includes, if held:\n   - any section 52 TCPA 1971 / later section 106 / deed / undertaking and the matching land-charge entry;\n   - the 1988 GDO planning-register entries for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES;\n   - officer-report Appendices B–E (B = further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust);\n   - conditions 16–18 and the 1990–94 discharge papers, including the October 1990 confirmation of condition 17 and the 1993–94 dispute over condition 18;\n   - any environmental-assessment / screening determination for the outline application;\n   - the complete 92/00671/RES file and any BP–Ideal Homes sale, option or conditional-contract paper on the planning files, including the recorded transfer of 3 December 1993.\nA separate FOI/EIR for those classes will follow and must not be folded into 00210772, 00211463 or 00211484.\n\n3. Subject access under UK GDPR Article 15: personal data you hold about me, Requester, in those files, and about Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler so far as the law allows a relative to see it. Say what identification you need before the month starts.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . The investigation distinguishes Parcel A (farmhouse, garden, buildings and yard — the family's maintained freehold) from Parcel B (eastern fields — not presently disputed). The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of Parcel A. Council papers on planning and demolition go to that question. They are not a finding against any officer.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening or reparations. This is not a claim form.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer for the hold, and give a date for the 00210772 outcome.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f79e1673b53","subject":"Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","name":"Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy, transfer or dispose","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f79e1673b53.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9e1e5a4586bf-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-transfer-or-dispose","scopeTopics":["cadw","glamorgan","heneb","hmlr","nlw","rcahmw","swp","tna","vale-foi","wales-office"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw","glamorgan","heneb","hmlr","nlw","rcahmw","swp","tna","vale-foi","wales-office"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9e1e5a4586bf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"},{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"},{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"},{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"},{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"},{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"},{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"},{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"},{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"},{"id":"wales-office","name":"Wales Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f79e1673b53.json","textStatus":"available","text":"To each recipient, in your own capacity as holder or likely holder of records. Please do not treat this as a joint reply. Answer only for your own holdings.\n\nSirs/Madam,\n\nThis is a preservation notice. It is not a claim form and not service of proceedings. It does not replace any FOI, review or subject access request already with you.\n\nLand: Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth, adjoining St Dochdwy's. Titles WA231076, WA240304 (closed), WA513690, WA735527, and any related title. Planning refs 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES.\n\nPlease preserve, and do not destroy, transfer out of your custody without a written receipt, or dispose of, any file, plan, photograph, tape or electronic record in your possession, custody or control relating to:\n\n1. The 1877 split, the 1916 and 1939 tenancies, and the 1938 Bute to Western Ground Rents conveyance.\n2. The 1955 and 1962 possession orders, the 1974 proceedings, and BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n3. First registration: WA231076 application 30 November 1982; WA240304 application 23 February 1983; later amalgamation.\n4. The 1988 possession (29 November) and demolition (begun 6 December), including listing, planning, police and any liaison papers.\n5. Mary Doreen Williams (died 26 March 1983) and William Buckler, so far as your file concerns this land.\n\nAlso preserve, if you hold them, the following planning and land-charge classes. Absence from a 2026 file disclosure is not proof they never existed:\n\n6. Any section 52 Town and Country Planning Act 1971 agreement, later section 106 instrument, deed, undertaking or other agreement regulating the development or use of this land, and any corresponding local-land-charge entry.\n7. The historic planning-register entries required by the Town and Country Planning General Development Order 1988 for 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES (applications, reserved matters, plans and drawings, and decision information).\n8. The officer's report annexes to 89/01396/OUT, including Appendix B (further GGAT comments after discussions with the Trust), and Appendices C–E.\n9. The condition chain on 89/01396/OUT: conditions 16–18; the Council's October 1990 confirmation of condition 17; GGAT's July 1992 archaeological warning; the September 1992 reserved-matters approval; and the 1993–94 papers on whether condition 18 had been discharged.\n10. Any preliminary environmental-assessment / screening determination for the outline application (site described as about 3.4 acres / 1.38 ha).\n11. Any record of the statutory consultation route used because the land was, or was treated as, a site of archaeological interest / SMR entry under the 1988 Order.\n12. The complete 92/00671/RES file, and any sale, option, conditional-contract or transfer paper on the planning files covering BP Properties to Ideal Homes Wales, including the recorded transfer of 3 December 1993.\n13. The application-receipt record for 89/01396/OUT (form dated October 1989; reconstructed Council receipt 8 November 1989).\n\nPlease stop routine deletion, including archived mailboxes, for anything in that scope.\n\nThe public evidence index is https://greathousefarmwiki.wordpress.com/ . The investigation distinguishes the farmhouse parcel from the eastern fields. The 1987 Court of Appeal decided possession, limitation and the October 1974 letters. It did not decide the documentary root of the farmhouse parcel. These records go to that question. This notice is not a finding against any of you.\n\nPlease acknowledge, name the officer responsible for the hold, and say what you hold in scope. If you hold nothing, say what you searched.\n\nNothing in this letter abandons any claim concerning title, registration, concealment, limitation, reopening or alteration of the register.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f70cad764a3","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:41:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f70cad764a3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"Administrative Court Office Cardiff","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f70cad764a3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Your email has been safely received by the Cardiff Administrative Court Team; please retain this email as confirmation that your document/query has been received.\nWe aim to respond to emails between 5 & 10 working days unless they are urgent. Please refrain from chasing for a response unless your query relates to a hearing taking place in the next 2 working days or you have been waiting more than 10 days for a response.\nTop Tips\n1.      Send your documents once and do not duplicate a copy in the Post/DX/Fax – this reply is your confirmation that your email has been received.\n2.      If your documents have already been placed on CE-File, your email containing them is not necessary and will be disregarded.\n3.      Do not send emails which exceed 20Mb.\n4.      Do not forget to include case number and full party names on all court documents\n\nCourt finder – For Court addresses and information\nFind a Court or Tribunal - GOV.UK<https://www.find-court-tribunal.service.gov.uk/>\nForm finder – For Court forms (including the Court fees leaflet)\nhttp://hmctsformfinder.justice.gov.uk/HMCTS/FormFinder.do\nHearing information - Will be published on the Court and Tribunal Hearings service\nhttps://www.court-tribunal-hearings.service.gov.uk/summary-of-publications?locationId=115\n\nPlease note that Court staff are not legally trained and therefore cannot advise on the appropriate route of appeal. We strongly recommend that you seek independent legal advice as per below.\n\n\nFurther Assistance\nIf you require help completing forms or understanding legal procedures, the following resources may be helpful:\n•    Citizens Advice Bureau (Royal Courts of Justice)\nStaff are legally trained and can assist with form completion and general guidance.\nYou may also contact your local Citizens Advice Bureau.\n•    Support Through Court\nFor issues beyond their remit, please refer to their signposting-guide-2024.pdf<https://supportthroughcourt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/signposting-guide-2024.pdf>.\n•    RCJ Advice Bureau\nOffers free legal advice to litigants.\nWebsite: https://www.rcjadvice.org.uk/\n•    LawWorks\nHelps locate free legal advice clinics near you.\nWebsite: https://www.lawworks.org.uk/legal-advice-individuals/find-legal-advice-clinic-near-you\n•    Gov.uk\nAdditional legal resources and guidance: www.gov.uk<http://www.gov.uk>\n\nThank you for your cooperation, patience, and support.\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f6c2b44ca09","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:40:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f6c2b44ca09.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"BPC.Cardiff","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f6c2b44ca09.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Derbyniwyd eich neges gan y llys ac fe ddelir â hi cyn gynted â phosibl. Your message has been received by the court and will be dealt with as soon as possible.\n\nThankyou for your email - please note this email address is to be used for Appeals and any party in a High Court matter who is not legally represented (Litigant In Person)\n\nIf you are a Solicitor or Barrister or Legal Representative then please take note of the information below:\n\nThe Court has received your correspondence below, we will not upload your request on to CMS nor take any action. As per Practice Direction 51O, this must be uploaded via CE-File.\n\nPlease also note that sending duplicate submissions via email or hard copy (unless directed by the court) is unnecessary and will not be actioned. This also consumes staff resources that could be better utilised elsewhere.\n\nPlease note for Business and Property Courts in Wales: -\n\nFrom 30 April 2019, professional users must file all documents and submissions through CE-Filing.\n\nPlease note for Kings’s Bench in Cardiff: -\n\nFrom 18 October 2021, professional users must file all documents and submissions through CE-Filing.\n\nFurther guidance can be found on the gov.uk website<https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ce-file-system-information-and-support-advice> (https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ce-file-system-information-and-support-advice); including on how to register as a user, the payment of fees, security and data protection, as well as the five simple steps required to use the system, and where to go for further help.\n\nIf you are experiencing problem in accessing CE-File persistently, please contact [email redacted]<[email redacted]> to report them.\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f6ce603c498","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:40:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f6ce603c498.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f6ce603c498.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n\n• Your full postal address\n\n• Your contact telephone number\n\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in Parliament, it will be dealt with as appropriate.\n\n\nMinisterial Business\n\nIf you are contacting me in my capacity as a Minister at the FCDO, you will need to redirect your email to to [email redacted]<[email redacted]>, or alternatively contact your own MP – you can find who that is at https://members.parliament.uk/FindYourMP\n\n\nThank you for taking the time to contact me.\n\nFor information about how we use your personal data, see our Privacy Notice<https://www.stephendoughty.wales/privacynotice>.\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nStephen\n\n\nStephen Doughty MP / AS\nMember of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth // Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nHouse of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f5f3cb3556b","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:40:02Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f5f3cb3556b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["linklaters"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["linklaters"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"Data Protection","institutions":[{"id":"linklaters","name":"Linklaters"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f5f3cb3556b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your email. Please note that our usual turnaround time for a response is 24 hours.\n\nIf your query is related to Linklater s privacy notices and policies, please see our Privacy Portal >.\n\nAny business communication sent by or on behalf of Linklaters LLP or one of its affiliated firms or other entities (together \"Linklaters\") is confidential and may be privileged or otherwise protected. If you receive it in error please inform us and then delete it immediately from your system. You should not copy it or disclose its contents to anyone. Please be aware that messages sent to and from Linklaters may be monitored for reasons of security, to protect our business, and to ensure compliance with legal and regulatory obligations and our internal policies. Emails are not a secure method of communication, can be intercepted and cannot be guaranteed to be error free. Anyone who communicates with us by email is taken to understand and accept the above.\n\nLinklaters LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England and Wales with registered number OC326345. It is a law firm authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority (www.sra.org.uk), with SRA ID: 460682. The term partner in relation to Linklaters LLP is used to refer to a member of Linklaters LLP or an employee or consultant of Linklaters LLP or any of its affiliated firms or entities with equivalent standing and qualifications. Please refer to www.linklaters.com/regulation for important information on our regulatory position. A list of Linklaters LLP members together with a list of those non-members who are designated as partners and their professional qualifications, may be inspected at our registered office, 20 Ropemaker St, London [postcode redacted] and such persons are either solicitors or registered foreign lawyers.\n\nWe take your privacy seriously. For information about how we process your personal data, please see our Global Privacy Notice at www.linklaters.com/en/legal-notices/privacy-notice."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","subject":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","name":"Automatic reply: Preservation notice — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — do not destroy records — Matter of public interest","date":"2026-09-28T21:39:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0e9f5e78576a4c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c-automatic-reply-preservation-notice-great-house-farm-t-mawr-llandough-do-not-destroy-records-matter-of-public-interest","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0e9f5e78576a4c","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0e9f5e78576a4c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am eich e-bost at Benderfyniadau Cynllunio a Amgylchedd Cymru (PCAC). Nod PEDW yw ymateb i Adborth/Cwynion o fewn 20 diwrnod gwaith o'r diwrnod derbyn. Os yw eich e-bost yn gŵyn am benderfyniad arolygydd, nodwch nad oes gan PEDW awdurdod i newid y penderfyniad. Dim ond ar ôl her gyfreithiol lwyddiannus yn y Llysoedd y gellir gwneud hyn. Mae dyddiad cau ar gyfer gwneud her neu geisio adolygiad barnwrol. Cofiwch y dyddiad cau ar gyfer yr her gan na all y Llysoedd ei ymestyn. Terfynau amser; Apeliadau Cynllunio – 6 wythnos o ddyddiad y penderfyniad Apeliadau Gorfodi – 28 diwrnod o ddyddiad y penderfyniad Cais am Adolygiad Barnwrol – 3 mis Thank you for your e-mail to Planning and Environment Decisions Wales (PEDW). PEDW aim to respond to Feedback/Complaints within 20 working days from day of receipt. If your e-mail is a complaint about an Inspectors decision please note that PEDW has no authority to change the decision. This can only be done after a successful legal challenge in the Courts. There is a deadline for making a challenge or seeking a judicial review. Please be mindful of the challenge deadline as the Courts cannot extend it. Deadlines; Planning Appeals – 6 weeks from date of decision Enforcement Appeals – 28 days from date of decision Application for Judicial Review – 3 months\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-1a0e9f5c