ncil's actions and omissions.\n\nIn particular, I ask the Council to determine:\n\n   1. Whether its officers discharged the heritage and planning\n   responsibilities applicable at the time.\n   2. Whether any failure occurred in relation to the identification,\n   protection, recording or investigation of Great House Farm.\n   3. Whether the Council's handling of the 1989 planning application\n   appropriately addressed the recent demolition of the building.\n   4. Whether any relevant records have been lost or destroyed and, if so,\n   when and under what retention arrangements.\n   5. What procedural lessons arise from the case.\n\nI also request disclosure of the relevant non-exempt records identified\nduring the complaint investigation, where these are not otherwise\navailable. I recognise that requests for specific recorded information may\nneed to be dealt with separately under the appropriate information-access\nregime.\n\nI have only recently been able to examine and correlate the surviving\nplanning, archaeological and heritage documentation sufficiently to\nidentify these issues. I therefore ask that the Council accepts the\ncomplaint for investigation notwithstanding the age of the events concerned.\n\nPlease acknowledge receipt and confirm the complaint reference and the\nofficer responsible for its investigation.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n\n\nRequester \n\n"},{"id":"gm-1a0ad6441e1b82e9","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-09-17T03:23:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ad6441e1b82e9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ad615441a4131-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ad615441a4131","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ad6441e1b82e9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Royal Commission,\n\nI am researching the demolition of Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr),\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth, in December 1988 (HER reference GGAT02038s / ST\n1681 7331).\n\nI am seeking to establish whether the Royal Commission was consulted or\nnotified before the farmhouse was demolished.\n\nContemporary reports from 3 December 1988 state that Cadw was considering\nemergency protection/listing of Great House Farm and that a Cadw inspection\nwas being arranged, including discussion with the Royal Commission for\nAncient and Historical Monuments.\n\nThe farmhouse was then demolished on 6 December 1988.\n\nI understand that the statutory framework at the time included provisions\nconcerning the recording of historic buildings before authorised\ndemolition. I would therefore be grateful if you could check your records\nand confirm:\n\n   1.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission received any notification, consultation,\n   referral or request for advice concerning Great House Farm before its\n   demolition in December 1988.\n   2.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission was asked to inspect, photograph, record or\n   otherwise document the building before demolition.\n   3.\n\n   Whether any correspondence exists between the Royal Commission, Cadw,\n   the local planning authority, BP Properties Ltd, or their representatives\n   concerning the proposed demolition.\n   4.\n\n   Whether the Royal Commission was given an opportunity to complete or\n   supplement its earlier recording of the farmhouse before demolition.\n   5.\n\n   Whether your records contain any photographs, measured drawings,\n   reports, field notes or other documentation relating specifically to the\n   farmhouse immediately before its demolition.\n   6.\n\n   If records exist, I would be grateful for the relevant reference numbers\n   and, where possible, copies.\n\nFor context, the Royal Commission had already recorded Great House Farm\narchitecturally in 1974. Contemporary material indicates that the building\nwas subsequently under consideration for emergency listing shortly before\nits destruction.\n\nThere is also an important chronology concerning the occupation and\npossession of the property: my late father William Buckler had lodged\nEuropean Commission of Human Rights application 14464/88 on 3 May 1988; BP\nobtained possession on 29 November 1988; demolition began on 6 December\n1988; and the Strasbourg application was registered on 12 December 1988.\n\nI am not asking the Royal Commission to express an opinion on the ownership\ndispute or the legality of the demolition. I am simply seeking to\nestablish, from your records, whether the Commission was notified or\nconsulted and what opportunity, if any, it was given to record the building\n(our home since 1667) before it was destroyed?\n\nGiven the historical and archaeological significance subsequently\nidentified at the site, I would particularly appreciate confirmation of\nwhether any pre-demolition recording was requested or undertaken.\n\nRegards\n\n\n,\n\n\nRequester \n\n"},{"id":"gm-1a0ad45d2d2ec97a","subject":"FAO: Barry Preservation Society / the Civic Trust","name":"FAO: Barry Preservation Society / the Civic Trust","date":"2026-09-17T02:50:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ad45d2d2ec97a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ad4529e6b01dd-fao-barry-preservation-society-the-civic-trust","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ad4529e6b01dd","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ad45d2d2ec97a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Freedom of Information Officer,\n\nI am researching the 1989 planning application for the development\nsubsequently known as Church View Close, Llandough-juxta-Penarth.\n\nThe planning officer's report records that representations were received\nfrom the *Barry Preservation Society* and the *Civic Trust*, but the report\ndoes not reproduce the substance of those representations.\n\nPlease provide copies of all records held by the Council relating to the\nrepresentation made by the *Barry Preservation Society* in connection with\nthat planning application, including:\n\n   1. The original letter, objection or representation submitted by the\n   Barry Preservation Society.\n   2. Any covering letter, acknowledgement or correspondence concerning its\n   submission.\n   3. Any internal Council correspondence referring to or summarising the\n   Society's representations.\n   4. Any plans, photographs or supporting material submitted by the\n   Society.\n   5. Any correspondence concerning the *retention, preservation,\n   alteration or demolition of Great House Farm farmhouse*.\n   6. Any subsequent correspondence between the Council and the Barry\n   Preservation Society concerning Great House Farm or the development.\n\nI am particularly seeking the Society's *original 1989 comments about Great\nHouse Farm farmhouse*, rather than a later summary of them.\n\nThe organisation is referred to in later Vale of Glamorgan Council records\nas the *Barry Preservation Society*, including its participation in the\nCouncil's Conservation Area Advisory Group. It also appears in historical\npublications as the *Barry Preservation Society and Civic Trust*.\n\nIf the original representation is no longer held, please state that\nexplicitly and provide any surviving reference, file number, minute,\nextract or other record that identifies what was submitted and when.\n\nPlease search the complete planning file and associated correspondence\nrather than relying solely on the published officer report.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a0ac85f438ad450","subject":"Enquiry — does D153/1–8 contain a c.1875–1880 Llandough-juxta-Penarth instrument?","name":"Enquiry — does D153/1–8 contain a c.1875–1880 Llandough-juxta-Penarth instrument?","date":"2026-09-16T23:20:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ac85f438ad450.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ac815c712ae7c-enquiry-does-d153-1-8-contain-a-c-1875-1880-llandough-juxta-penarth-instrument","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ac815c712ae7c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ac85f438ad450.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Archivist,\nPlease would you check whether D153/1–8 contains any document dated\nc.1875–1880 relating to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough-juxta-Penarth\n(ST 168 733), adjoining St Dochdwy’s churchyard.\nThis is not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge.\n\nI am looking for an agreement, lease, counterpart, award, conveyance or\nrelated plan involving any of:\n\nDaniel Thomas / D. Thomas & Son\n\nLlandough Limeworks\n\nJohn Williams / Thomas Williams\n\nthe Bute Estate or the Trustees of the Marquess of Bute\n\nquarrying, minerals, lime, sidings, compensation or reparation\n\nthe dwelling adjoining the churchyard\nPlease inspect the full sequence D153/1–8, not only items already described\nas D153/4–8.\n\nCatalogue titles may not name the parties. Endorsements, dockets and plans\nshould be checked.\n\nIf such an item exists, please give:\n\nthe exact reference\ndate\ndocument type\nparties as written\nproperty description and acreage\nwhether a plan is attached\nwhether a copy can be supplied, and at what cost\n\nAlso is there any item in D153/1–8 dated 1875–1880 naming Thomas Williams,\nJohn Williams, Daniel Thomas, Llandough Limeworks, or the dwelling by St\nDochdwy’s?\n\nPlease confirm D/DRa 11/120 is Tynywain, Llanedeyrne, and not\nLlandough-juxta-Penarth/ Llandough Cardiff.\n\nI do not need a searchroom booking at this stage.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a0ac6f29f89eaf9","subject":"2 of 2 - Unanswered clarification — N610CGV / WA231076 & WA240304 — emails of 26 May, 2–3 June, 30 July and 12 August 2026","name":"2 of 2 - Unanswered clarification — N610CGV / WA231076 & WA240304 — emails of 26 May, 2–3 June, 30 July and 12 August 2026","date":"2026-09-16T22:56:00Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ac6f29f89eaf9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ac6dc899f582c-2-of-2-unanswered-clarification-n610cgv-wa231076-wa240304-emails-of-26-may-2-3-june-30-july-and-12-august-2026","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ac6dc899f582c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ac6f29f89eaf9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Mr Haste,\n\nThis supplements my email of 16 September 2026 on N610CGV / WA231076 and\nWA240304. It is not a complaint, not a request to reopen stage 2, and not a\nFOIA request. Please treat points 8–14 with points 1–7 as one live enquiry\n(also your customer-support refs 260812-6561894 and 260812-6565153).\n\n8. 1971 abstract as listed on the DL, versus the document itself\n\nMs Takeuchi’s letter of 19 April 2026 stated that “an abstract of title\nlisted dated 1971 was lodged” and that the deeds were listed on the form\nDL. Your 30 July schedule has an A13-DL (WA231076 item 17) but no separate\n1971 abstract.\n\nPlease confirm:\nwhether item 17 still lists a 1971 abstract;\n\nif it does, whether the abstract itself is still held, and under which item;\n\nif the abstract is listed but no longer held, when and how it left the file.\n\n9. Form 1E / Form 1C / FR1\nMs Takeuchi referred to certificates on Form FR1. Your 30 July letter\nidentifies Form 1E (30 November 1982, item 13) and, for WA240304, Form 1C\n(item 11).\n\nPlease confirm:\nwhether an FR1 also survives for either title;\nwhether 1E and 1C are the first-registration application forms;\n\nwhether the wording “not aware of any question or doubt affecting the\ntitle” appears on 1E, on 1C, on an FR1, or on none of them.\n\n10. The 31 December 1969 Western Ground Rents conveyance\n\nMs Takeuchi and Ms Griffiths treated the 31 December 1969 conveyance\n(Western Ground Rents Ltd to the BP Pension Trust parties) as the root\nrecited in the 1975 and 1982 conveyances. That 1969 deed does not appear as\nan item on the 30 July schedule.\n\nPlease confirm whether the 1969 conveyance:\n\nis held (give title and item number);\nwas only recited and never lodged; or\nwas lodged and is no longer held.\n11. Paper files and the February 2026 scan\nMs Griffiths wrote on 13 February 2026 that she had “ordered the historic\npaper files of the first registration” and was awaiting scanning.\n\nPlease confirm:\nwhether those paper files were retrieved and scanned in full;\n\nwhether the originals are still held, and where;\n\nwhether the 30 July list is the complete surviving set from that retrieval;\n\nthe procedure under Land Registration Act 2002 s.66 for inspection of the\noriginals, as distinct from paid OC2 copies.\n\n12. Examiner material already identified\nYour 30 July list includes WA240304 item 7: “Application form D23 (inside\nexam) and letter dated 8 April 1983 from Linklaters & Paines.” That is\nexaminer/requisition material.\n\nPlease confirm what the D23 and the 8 April 1983 letter concern, or state\nthat you will not read them and that they should be requested as OC2 items.\nIdentify any other surviving examiner notes, requisitions or file notes for\neither title.\n\n13. Class of title and cautions at first registration\n\nPlease confirm, from the surviving register editions you listed (including\nWA240304 item 10, 23 February 1983, and WA231076 item 23, 13 January 1984):\n\nthe class of title first granted on each title (absolute / possessory /\nqualified);\n\nwhether any caution, notice, restriction or inhibition was entered at or\nbefore completion of first registration.\n\nMr Gill’s letter of 25 May 2026 said no caution was received from my\nfamily. I am asking what the register editions themselves show, not for a\nrestatement of that conclusion.\n\n14. Amalgamation\nWA231076 item 14 is an application to amalgamate dated 2 February 1987.\nPlease confirm that WA240304 was wholly absorbed into WA231076, or identify\nany part of the closed title that was not.\n\nI do not need the complaints outcome repeated. I need numbered answers to\n1–14, or a written statement that HM Land Registry refuses to examine the\ndocuments it has listed.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\nN610CGV — WA231076 / WA240304\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nDate: Wed, 16 Sept 2026, 23:48\nSubject: Unanswered clarification — N610CGV / WA231076 & WA240304 — emails\nof 26 May, 2–3 June, 30 July and 12 August 2026\nTo: <[email redacted]>\nCc: <[email redacted]>\n\n\nMr Haste,\n\nI refer to your letter of 30 July 2026 (N610CGV) and to my emails of 26\nMay, 2 June, 3 June (clarification, physical inspection, and preservation),\n30 July and 12 August 2026.\n\nThis is not a complaint and not a request to reopen the stage 2 review\nconcluded by Mr Gill on 25 May 2026. It is a request that HM Land Registry\nanswer the factual questions already put, which remain unanswered.\nYour 30 July letter listed documents still held. It did not answer what\nthose documents contain, nor the earlier questions that listing was meant\nto enable.\nPlease answer each of the following. If a point cannot be answered without\nreading a listed item, say so and name the item number.\n\n1. 1971 abstract of title\nEarlier correspondence referred to a 1971 abstract lodged with first\nregistration. It does not appear as a separate item in your 30 July\nschedule. Confirm whether it:\nsurvives as a separate document;\nforms part of a listed item (give the title and item number); or\n\nis no longer held.\n\n2. “No question or doubt” certificate\nEarlier correspondence referred to a certificate that the applicant’s\nsolicitors were “not aware of any question or doubt affecting the title.”\nConfirm whether that wording appears in Form 1E dated 30 November 1982\n(WA231076 item 13), in another surviving document (identify it), or is no\nlonger held.\n\n3. Marriage certificate relied on by Mr Gill\nMr Gill’s letter of 25 May 2026 stated that identity was established\nbecause “there is a marriage certificate to show this.” Confirm whether\nthat certificate:\n\nwas lodged on the first-registration file;\nis one of the items listed on 30 July (give number); or\nis not held by HM Land Registry and was asserted from some other source.\n\n4. Contents of the surviving first-registration records\nConfirm whether any of the documents listed on 30 July 2026 for WA231076 or\nWA240304 contain any reference to:\nMary Williams / Mary Buckler;\nFred Buckler;\nWilliam (Billy) Buckler;\nTy Mawr / Great House Farm, farmhouse, garden or curtilage;\nany person other than the applicant asserting ownership, occupation or\nanother interest;\n\npossession proceedings, litigation, objection, caution, competing claim, or\nany question or doubt as to title.\nIf any such reference exists, identify the title and item number. If none\nexists in the surviving records, confirm that fact in writing.\n\n5. Physical check\nOn 3 June 2026 I asked to inspect the physical files, or scans if the\noriginals are not accessible. That request has not been answered. Please\nconfirm:\n\nwhether the originals of the 30 July items still exist in physical form;\n\nwhere they are held;\n\nthe procedure, identification and fee for inspection; and\n\nif originals have been destroyed or are not produced for inspection, the\ndate and manner of destruction or the reason inspection is refused.\n\n6. Form OC2\nTo avoid an unnecessarily broad application, identify the item numbers from\nyour 30 July schedule that comprise the surviving first-registration\nrecord, in particular:\n\nForm 1E (WA231076 item 13);\nA13-DL list of documents lodged (item 17);\n19 November 1982 conveyance (item 4);\nLinklaters & Paines correspondence (WA231076 items 16 and 18; WA240304\nitems 4, 5 and 7);\n\nForm 1C and 23 May 1975 conveyance (WA240304 items 11 and 12);\nA28 / draft entries;\n\nthe 1971 abstract, if it survives;\nany examiner’s notes, requisitions, memoranda or file notes that survive.\nIf any of those categories do not survive, say which.\n\n7. Preservation\nYour 30 July letter stated the listed documents “will remain on file.”\nPlease confirm that none of the WA231076 or WA240304 first-registration\nmaterial, including scans or microfiche, will be destroyed while these\nquestions and any OC2 application remain outstanding.\n\nI asked these questions so that HM Land Registry would either confirm the\ncontents of its own listed records or state that it will not examine them.\nA further inventory, a direction to Form OC2, or a restatement that the\ncomplaints procedure is closed is not an answer.\n\nI would be grateful for a numbered reply to points 1–7.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nN610CGV — WA231076 / WA240304"},{"id":"gm-1a0ac6892f9e1222","subject":"Unanswered clarification — N610CGV / WA231076 & WA240304 — emails of 26 May, 2–3 June, 30 July and 12 August 2026","name":"Unanswered clarification — N610CGV / WA231076 & WA240304 — emails of 26 May, 2–3 June, 30 July and 12 August 2026","date":"2026-09-16T22:48:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0ac6892f9e1222.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0ac666bcf3aff9-unanswered-clarification-n610cgv-wa231076-wa240304-emails-of-26-may-2-3-june-30-july-and-12-august-2026","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0ac666bcf3aff9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0ac6892f9e1222.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Mr Haste,\n\nI refer to your letter of 30 July 2026 (N610CGV) and to