person other than the applicant asserting ownership, occupation or\nanother interest;\n\npossession proceedings, litigation, objection, caution, competing claim, or\nany question or doubt as to title.\nIf any such reference exists, identify the title and item number. If none\nexists in the surviving records, confirm that fact in writing.\n\n5. Physical check\nOn 3 June 2026 I asked to inspect the physical files, or scans if the\noriginals are not accessible. That request has not been answered. Please\nconfirm:\n\nwhether the originals of the 30 July items still exist in physical form;\n\nwhere they are held;\n\nthe procedure, identification and fee for inspection; and\n\nif originals have been destroyed or are not produced for inspection, the\ndate and manner of destruction or the reason inspection is refused.\n\n6. Form OC2\nTo avoid an unnecessarily broad application, identify the item numbers from\nyour 30 July schedule that comprise the surviving first-registration\nrecord, in particular:\n\nForm 1E (WA231076 item 13);\nA13-DL list of documents lodged (item 17);\n19 November 1982 conveyance (item 4);\nLinklaters & Paines correspondence (WA231076 items 16 and 18; WA240304\nitems 4, 5 and 7);\n\nForm 1C and 23 May 1975 conveyance (WA240304 items 11 and 12);\nA28 / draft entries;\n\nthe 1971 abstract, if it survives;\nany examiner’s notes, requisitions, memoranda or file notes that survive.\nIf any of those categories do not survive, say which.\n\n7. Preservation\nYour 30 July letter stated the listed documents “will remain on file.”\nPlease confirm that none of the WA231076 or WA240304 first-registration\nmaterial, including scans or microfiche, will be destroyed while these\nquestions and any OC2 application remain outstanding.\n\nI asked these questions so that HM Land Registry would either confirm the\ncontents of its own listed records or state that it will not examine them.\nA further inventory, a direction to Form OC2, or a restatement that the\ncomplaints procedure is closed is not an answer.\n\nI would be grateful for a numbered reply to points 1–7.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\nN610CGV — WA231076 / WA240304"},{"id":"gm-1a0a9a25c2761e75","subject":"RE: Catalogue check – ERC RCS2/1/1777 “Great House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston”","name":"RE: Catalogue check – ERC RCS2/1/1777 “Great House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston”","date":"2026-09-16T09:52:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0a9a25c2761e75.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0a6ba8235d6122-catalogue-check-erc-rcs2-1-1777-great-house-ty-mawr-bonvilston","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0a6ba8235d6122","direction":"received","from":"NMR Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0a9a25c2761e75.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am eich ymholiad. Byddwn yn ceisio ymateb cyn pen 15 diwrnod gwaith.  Rydym wedi gohirio ein gwasanaeth chwilio a blaenoriaeth ar hyn o bryd oherwydd prinder staff. Ymddiheuriadau am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achosir.\n\nYn y cyfamser, gallai’r wybodaeth isod fod yn ddefnyddiol i chi:\n\nI gael gwybodaeth am safleoedd hanesyddol yng Nghymru a chael manylion am yr hyn sydd yn ein harchifau, ewch i’n cronfa ddata a’n catalog, https://coflein.gov.uk/cy/\n\nOs yn bosibl, rydym yn argymell eich bod yn trefnu apwyntiad i ymweld â’n llyfrgell ac ystafell chwilio<https://cbhc.gov.uk/gwasanaethau/> ein harchif, os hoffech weld deunydd yr archif â’ch llygaid eich hun a thynnu lluniau heb orfod talu amdanynt. Yn gyffredinol, mae gwneud hynny’n gynt ac yn rhatach o lawer nag archebu sganiau o bell.\n\nMae llawer o’n delweddau digidol ar gael i’w lawrlwytho, eu prynu a’u trwyddedu yn syth o Coflein. Mae canllawiau ynghylch sut mae gwneud hynny i’w gweld yn y fideo byr hwn: Lawrlwytho delweddau o Coflein<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JYJmCNrRFqY> Os nad yw’r ddelwedd yr ydych yn chwilio amdani ar gael drwy’r system hon, y rheswm am hynny’n aml fydd cyfyngiadau hawlfraint, ac efallai y byddwch am chwilio am ddelwedd amgen sydd ar gael, os yw hynny’n bosibl.\n\n\nThank you for your enquiry.  We will endeavour to respond within 15 working days.  Please note, we have currently suspended our Priority Enquiry Service due to staff shortage. We apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\nIn the meantime, you may find the information below helpful:\n\nFor information on historic sites in Wales and details of archive holdings see our database and catalogue, https://coflein.gov.uk/en/\n\nWhere possible we recommend that you make an appointment to visit our archive search room and library<https://rcahmw.gov.uk/services/> to view archive material in person and take photos without charge.  This is generally much quicker and cheaper than ordering scans remotely.\n\nMany of our digital images are available to download, purchase and licence directly from Coflein.  Guidance on how to do this can be seen in this short video: Downloading images from Coflein (youtube.com)<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gKpL61F1M2w&t=3s>  If the image which you want is not available via this system, this is often due to copyright restrictions and you may wish to identify an alternative image which is available, if possible.\n\n\n\n\nNMR Enquiries\nYmholiadau Cyhoeddus I Public Enquiries\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 15 September 2026 21:22\nTo: NMR Enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Catalogue check – ERC RCS2/1/1777 “Great House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston”\n\nDear NMR / RCAHMW cataloguing team,\n\nPlease could you check whether Emergency Recording case RCS2/1/1777 is correctly assigned.\n\nThe Coflein description reads:\n\nGreat House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston – measured drawings, copies of historic maps, photographic material description and location plan received in the course of Emergency Recording case RCS2/1/1777, filed in nprn order.\n\nThere are two distinct Vale of Glamorgan sites with that name:\n\n1. Ty Mawr / Great House, Bonvilston – still standing, Grade II (Cadw 13603), south side of the A48 opposite St Mary’s Church.\n\n2. Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth) – NPRN 20182, ST1681073310, demolished 6 December 1988. RCAHMW already holds NMR Site Files for it (plan with additions dated 12/12/1988; Suggett account; press cuttings).\n\nEmergency Recording of measured drawings, historic maps and photographs is the pattern one would expect for the Llandough demolition, not for the surviving Bonvilston house. Adjacent ERC case RCS2/1/1776 is also of that period.\n\nCould you confirm from the location plan / map copies / photographs in the RCS2/1/1777 bundle whether the site is Bonvilston (A48 / church opposite) or Llandough (St Dochdwy / farm group)? If it is Llandough, please re-link the file to NPRN 20182.\n\nHappy to supply further identifiers if useful.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a0a6bb6d43d5b5f","subject":"Catalogue check – ERC RCS2/1/1777 “Great House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston”","name":"Catalogue check – ERC RCS2/1/1777 “Great House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston”","date":"2026-09-15T20:21:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0a6bb6d43d5b5f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0a6ba8235d6122-catalogue-check-erc-rcs2-1-1777-great-house-ty-mawr-bonvilston","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0a6ba8235d6122","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0a6bb6d43d5b5f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear NMR / RCAHMW cataloguing team,\n\nPlease could you check whether Emergency Recording case RCS2/1/1777 is\ncorrectly assigned.\n\nThe Coflein description reads:\n\nGreat House (Ty Mawr), Bonvilston – measured drawings, copies of historic\nmaps, photographic material description and location plan received in the\ncourse of Emergency Recording case RCS2/1/1777, filed in nprn order.\n\nThere are two distinct Vale of Glamorgan sites with that name:\n\n1. Ty Mawr / Great House, Bonvilston – still standing, Grade II (Cadw\n13603), south side of the A48 opposite St Mary’s Church.\n\n2. Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth) – NPRN 20182, ST1681073310,\ndemolished 6 December 1988. RCAHMW already holds NMR Site Files for it\n(plan with additions dated 12/12/1988; Suggett account; press cuttings).\n\nEmergency Recording of measured drawings, historic maps and photographs is\nthe pattern one would expect for the Llandough demolition, not for the\nsurviving Bonvilston house. Adjacent ERC case RCS2/1/1776 is also of that\nperiod.\n\nCould you confirm from the location plan / map copies / photographs in the\nRCS2/1/1777 bundle whether the site is Bonvilston (A48 / church opposite)\nor Llandough (St Dochdwy / farm group)? If it is Llandough, please re-link\nthe file to NPRN 20182.\n\nHappy to supply further identifiers if useful.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a0a07619dc77c41","subject":"FOI request - Case Ref/ 00211027","name":"FOI request - Case Ref/ 00211027","date":"2026-09-14T15:07:52Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0a07619dc77c41.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0a07619dc77c41-foi-request-case-ref-00211027","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0a07619dc77c41","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211027"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0a07619dc77c41.json","attachments":[{"name":"Conveyance dated 11 June 1965.pdf","title":"Conveyance dated 11 June 1965.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/1965-06-11_vale-foi-00211027_conveyance-11-june-1965.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":2993988,"sha256":"a09d100e5b4689175fbc13fe9eda3b3cffbd6485fbe910ef7bc48eee4c2119bd"},{"name":"1965 Contract.pdf","title":"1965 Contract.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/1965-00-00_vale-foi-00211027_contract-for-sale-llandough-school-site.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":16676219,"sha256":"f7265dcdd788e5c9ce91136e5629651cb929bb09bdf4e9ffa78a3a0f17b2f511"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your request for information about Llandough Primary School and your further enquires around whom you within the Information Governance team you have been corresponding with.\n\nYou asked\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004, I request copies of records relating to the acquisition of the land used for the construction of Llandough Primary School.\n\nSpecifically, I request:\n\n■ The transfer deed, conveyance or other legal instrument by which the Council acquired the land.\n\n■ The purchase price or consideration paid for the land.\n\n■ If the land was gifted, transferred at nominal value or below market value, records explaining the basis for that arrangement.\n\n■ Any valuation reports obtained before acquisition.\n\n■ Any agreements, correspondence or meeting minutes between the Council and BP (or any BP subsidiary, trust or associated company) concerning the transfer of the land.\n\n■ Any Cabinet, Committee or Council reports authorising the acquisition.\n\n■ Any planning agreements or obligations connected with the transfer.\n\nIf any of the requested information is already publicly available, please provide the relevant links or document references.\n\nYou then issued further correspondence requesting:\n\nOn 14 July 2026 you acknowledged my FOI/EIR request (Case Ref 00211027) concerning the acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School.\n\nI replied the same day asking for the name of the officer who sent the acknowledgement. I have received no further response or substantive reply.\n\nOur Response\n\nThe transfer deed, conveyance or other legal instrument by which the Council acquired the land\nThe Council holds a conveyance dated 11 June 1965 made between:\n1.            Lakeside and Llandough Development Company Limited;\n2.            Western Ground Rents Limited; and\n3.            The Glamorgan County Council.\nA scanned copy of the conveyance and its plan is attached (“the 1965 Conveyance”).\n\nThe purchase price or consideration paid for the land\nThe consideration recorded in the 1965 Conveyance is £16,800.\n\nIf the land was gifted, transferred at nominal value or below market value, records explaining the basis of that arrangement\nThe 1965 Conveyance records a purchase for £16,800. No record has been located within the papers held by Legal Services indicating that the land was gifted or transferred at nominal value or below market value.\n\nAny valuation reports obtained before acquisition\nSearches were undertaken with Legal Services and Estates Department. No valuation report relating to the acquisition has been identified. The Council does not hold any valuation report falling within the scope of this request.\n\nAny agreements, correspondence or meeting minutes between the Council and BP, or any BP subsidiary, trust or associated company, concerning the transfer\nNo agreements, correspondence or meeting minutes between the Council and BP or any BP subsidiary, trust or associated company relating to the acquisition of the land have been identified.\n\nAny Cabinet, Committee or Council reports authorising the acquisition\nThe Council has not identified any Cabinet, Committee or Council reports within its current records management systems which fall within the scope of your request. Given the age of the acquisition, any surviving historic records may have been transferred to Glamorgan Archives. You may wish to contact Glamorgan Archives directly regarding records from this period.\n\nAny planning agreements or obligations connected with the transfer\nNo planning agreement or planning obligation connected with the 1965 Conveyance has been identified within the title deeds held by Legal Services or, within the Planning Departments records.\n\nWe have considered this aspect of your correspondence under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\nThe Council’s Information Governance Team deal with requests on a collective basis and all requests will be considered by different officers. The requests are dealt with via a generic e-mail account so that all officers in the Team can consider correspondence.  There are several reasons why the Information Governance Team work in this way.  One reason is to ensure that correspondence is considered as soon as possible and to ensure that messages or e-mails are not sent to individuals and overlooked within our systems overall.  The information requested is also considered to constitute the personal data of a member of staff and disclosure would amount to disclosure to the world at large. Therefore the Council is unable to provide the name of the individual officer, because it is not considered that there is a lawful basis that would make disclosure fair or necessary in the circumstances.  The Council's correspondence is issued on behalf of the authority, and requests for information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 are made to the Council as a public authority rather than to individual officers. It is not necessary to know the identity of a particular officer in order to submit a valid request for information.\nIf you are dissatisfied with the handling of your request, you have the right to ask for an internal review. Internal review requests should be made within 40 working days of the date of receipt of the response to your original letter and should be addressed to:\nc/o The Monitoring Officer – [email redacted]\n\nOr by post to The Monitoring Officer, Civic Offices, Holton Road, Barry, [postcode redacted].\n\nPlease remember to quote the reference number above in any future communications.\n\nIf you are not content with the outcome of the internal review, you have the right to apply directly to the Information Commissioner for a decision.\n\nThe Information Commissioner can be contacted at:\nInformation Commissioner's Office - Wales\nSecond Floor, Churchill House\nChurchill Way,\nCardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted] / Fax:[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]\n\nKind regards\n\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ntel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-1a09f8df7298670a","subject":"FW: DBDT79/1 – physical examination of the original","name":"FW: DBDT79/1 – physical examination of the original","date":"2026-09-14T10:51:33Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a09f8df7298670a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a03f5d330ba15ad-fw-dbdt79-1-physical-examination-of-the-original","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a03f5d330ba15ad","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a09f8df7298670a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"My apologies, I sent the below email without attaching the digital photography order form.  Please find it attached here instead.\n\nLouise Hunt\nArchifydd / Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\nClos Parc Morgannwg\nLecwydd / Leckwith\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] \n\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/  www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.instagram.com/glamarchives \n\nFrom: Hunt, Louise On Behalf Of Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg\nSent: 14 September 2026 11:49\nTo: Requester  \nSubject: RE: DBDT79/1 – physical examination of the original\n\nRef: 2026/3893\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email received into our enquiries system 27th August relating to the deed in our collection with document reference DBDT/79/1.\n\nThe catalogue description for DBDT/79/1 had a few small errors which have now been corrected.  In answer to your questions:\n\n\n  1.  Parties and date – Does the original name the Marquess of Bute and Mr John Williams, and is it dated May 1877?\n\nThe document is a counterpart lease dated 2 May 1877 between the Trustees of the Will of the late Marquess of Bute and Mr John Williams of Newport.\n\n  1.  Property description – Exact wording of the land and premises. Does it expressly locate the property in Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff?\n\n‘All that piece or parcel of land with the messuage or tenement and outbuildings thereto now being erected and built or part thereof by the said lesee, situate, lying and being in Pembroke Terrace in the parish of St John the Baptist, Cardiff containing by admeasurement sixty-nine feet or thereabouts on the north side thereof, thirty-one feet or thereabouts on the east and west sides thereof and sixty-nine feet six inches or thereaboutson the south side thereof bounded on the north by land of the Marquess of Bute, on the east by Pembroke Terrace aforesaid, on the south by land demised to David Price and on the west by land of Mr John William Vachell.’\n\n  1.  Llandough / other references – Any mention (body text, plan, schedule, endorsements or annotations) of Llandough, Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr, Western Ground Rents, or any locality outside Pembroke Terrace?\n\nThere is no mention of Llandough, Great House Farm or Ty Mawr or any other property outside of Pembroke Terrace.\n\n  1.  Marginal plan – Does the plan identify the location sufficiently? If procedures allow, please supply a digital image or scan of the plan.\n\nThe plan clearly shows a property on Pembroke Terrace.  We can provide a digital copy if you require it at a charge of £15.60 (inclusive of VAT).  Please find attached a digital photography order form.\n\n  1.  Further identifying details – Any adjoining owners, plot numbers, parish, street numbers, measurements, previous ownership, rent, consideration, or cross-references to other instruments.\n\nSee above for full description.  There is no further information included.\nWe hope that this answers your questions in relation to this document but please do let us know if you would like order a digital copy.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nLouise Hunt\nArchifydd / Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\nClos Parc Morgannwg\nLecwydd / Leckwith\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] \n\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/  www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.instagram.com/glamarchives \n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir)