ddresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a098384b56819b4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a09844850e7a165.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\n\nI have been liaising a lot with local authorities in South Wales the last\nyear regarding my interest in Llandough.\n\nThis is a line of enquiry I wish to open about a separate matter. I am\nwriting on behalf of a US-based company to explore the possibility of\nestablishing a unique satellite office in South Wales.\n\nThe interest is in discussing a potential Commercial Guardianship Tenancy\nor alternative lease arrangement for Lavernock Battery and Fort.\n\nI understand that management and ownership of the site involve multiple\nstakeholders, and I am reaching out to gauge your initial interest in such\nan arrangement.\n\nThis proposal is a scenario that solves a common issue for this heritage\nand coastal site—preventing dereliction, vandalism, and weathering through\nactive, professional occupation.\n\n## Why a Commercial Guardianship?\nRather than a traditional commercial takeover, the type of agreement would\nhave a responsible custodians on site. Guardianship tenancies are not new\nto Councils in Wales.\n\nOccupancy would provide:\n\n* Active Security & Maintenance: A regular physical presence on-site to\ndeter anti-social behavior and immediately flag structural or environmental\nissues.\n\n* Preservation of Heritage: respect the Scheduled Ancient Monument status\nof the structures. Any workspace configuration would be entirely\nlow-impact, fully reversible, and designed to protect the historical\nintegrity of the architecture.\n\n* Sympathetic Integration: mindful of the surrounding Lavernock Point\nNature Reserve and local businesses. Small team to operate quietly,\nensuring zero disruption to local wildlife, public footpaths, or\nneighboring holiday operations.\n\nI believe that breathing new life into these historic structures through a\ncontrolled, professional occupancy could be an excellent model for\nsustainable heritage preservation.\n\nI welcome the opportunity to discuss this concept with you and my US\nbusiness associates, to see if a mutual arrangement could be reached. Could\nyou please let me know if this is a proposal your organisations would be\nopen to exploring?\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nWarm regards,\n\nRequester \n\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a090fd50150bcee","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough – Request 00210772 – Internal Review – Formal Chase","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough – Request 00210772 – Internal Review – Formal Chase","date":"2026-09-11T15:01:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a090fd50150bcee.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a05eaa94c597908-great-house-farm-llandough-request-00210772-internal-review-formal-chase","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a05eaa94c597908","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a090fd50150bcee.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe are sorry for the delay in providing you with a substantive update in this matter.  You asked for an internal review in particular because you had concerns about whether or not substantive enough searches had been carried out.  We wrote to you on 5th August 2026 advising that further enquiries regarding the searches was being made with service areas. We advised you those enquiries were not quite complete.\n\nService areas have reverted, and further historical documentation has been found.  Unfortunately, we are still sifting through it to determine its relevance to your request.  It is also not necessarily Council documentation but is nonetheless in the Council’s possession therefore, anything that may be relevant to your request also requires the Council to consider whether or not it should consult with 3rd parties and if necessary consult with them.  We are undertaking the review of the documentation to determine relevance and whether we need to consult with third parties.  We intend to try and update you further by the end of next week with a clearer time frame of when we may be able to respond substantively about this other documentation and indeed provide copies of anything we feel able to.\n\nWe are grateful to you for your patience and apologise for the time it is taking.\n\nRegards\n\n\nInformation Governance Officer/ / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nLegal & Democratic Services /Gwasanaethau Cyfreithol a Democrataidd\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted]/[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 01 September 2026 21:32\nTo: FOI Unit <[email redacted]>\nCc: Franks, Christopher P (Cllr) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough – Request 00210772 – Internal Review – Formal Chase\n\nInformation Governance Team,\n\nI refer again to the internal review of Case Ref 00210772 (Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough), requested on 7 July 2026 and acknowledged by you on 10 July 2026.\nOn 5 August 2026 you wrote that further enquiries were ongoing and that you would provide a further update by Friday 14 August 2026.\n\nOn 14 August 2026 I chased and requested the completed internal review decision by close of business on 24 August 2026.\nNo response or update has been received.\n\nThe Environmental Information Regulations 2004 require that internal reviews be completed promptly and within a reasonable time. The delay is now substantial and exceeds both the statutory expectation and the deadlines you yourselves set.\n\nPlease issue the completed internal review decision within 5 working days of this email (i.e. by close of business on Tuesday 8 September 2026).\n\nIf a substantive response is not received by that date I will escalate the matter to the Information Commissioner’s Office for non-compliance with the EIR timescales.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a08bb3809f8a66b","subject":"Escalation — Llandough ward member silence: Great House Farm / Church View Close and removal of commemorative tree","name":"Escalation — Llandough ward member silence: Great House Farm / Church View Close and removal of commemorative tree","date":"2026-09-10T14:23:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a08bb3809f8a66b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a08ba0ae4dec885-escalation-llandough-ward-member-silence-great-house-farm-church-view-close-and-removal-of-commemorative-tree","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a08ba0ae4dec885","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a08bb3809f8a66b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Councillor Burnett,\n\nI write to you as Leader of the Vale of Glamorgan Council because the\nelected member for Llandough, Councillor George D. D. Carroll, has not\nanswered a sequence of written enquiries spanning more than six months. I\nam going above him for that reason alone. I am not asking you to adjudicate\nthe historic title dispute. I am asking that a constituent with a\ndocumented family interest in the ward receive a reply that the ward member\nhas declined to give.\n\nI understand that elected members do not have a line manager in the\nemployment sense. Councillor Carroll is Leader of the Conservative Group.\nYou are the political head of the authority. After the ward member and the\nMonitoring Officer, you are the proper next addressee.\n\nWhy I am writing to you rather than waiting further\n\n1. Councillor Carroll has not sent a single substantive reply to me at\n[email redacted].\n2. On 27 July 2026 I filed a formal complaint about that silence (copied to\nhim, Democratic Services and the Monitoring Officer).\n3. On 12 August 2026 Victoria Davidson, Monitoring Officer, wrote that the\nmatter fell outside the Corporate Concerns and Complaints Policy and that\nshe had not identified a Code of Conduct breach. That determination did not\nrequire him to respond. It left the original questions unanswered.\n4. I followed up with the Monitoring Officer on 12 August, 21 August and 24\nAugust 2026. The position did not change.\n5. I copied Councillor Carroll again on 28 August 2026 (joint letter with\nStephen Doughty MP). Still no reply from him.\n\nThe questions he has not answered include a simple, current, ward-level\none: who removed the tree my great-grandfather planted to mark the family’s\nclaim, as recorded in the Collection of Wales / archival image. That is a\nlocal enquiry a ward member can signpost to Parks, Highways, Planning or\nthe landowner. It is not a request that he retry BP Properties Ltd v\nBuckler.\n\nFrom his public output, Councillor Carroll appears to concentrate on\nblocked drains, potholes and similar highway defects. Those matters matter.\nThe correspondence I sent him is of a different character: heritage,\nplanning and enforcement records, the 1988 demolition of Great House Farm\n(Ty Mawr), now Church View Close, and the removal of a commemorative tree.\nI accept that may be outside the type of casework he usually handles. That\nis why a short, honest reply — even if only to say the questions sit with\nnamed officers, and to pass the tree query to the correct department —\nwould have been sufficient. Silence is not.\n\nRecorded approaches to Councillor Carroll ([email redacted])\n\nAll sent. No substantive reply on any of them.\n\n- 16 February 2026 — “Title Fraud and Procedural Concealment – Church View\nClose, Llandough (formerly Great House Farm / Ty Mawr)”. Planning and\nrecord-keeping gaps; 1988 demolition.\n- 4 May 2026 — follow-up on BP v Buckler 1987; ITV footage; request for\nattention as Llandough councillor.\n- 3 May 2026 — joined the public “George Carroll for Llandough” Facebook\ngroup (approved). Not a substitute for a council-email reply.\n- 9 May 2026 — a wider formal notice also addressed to\n[email redacted]. That address bounced. Subsequent mail used\nthe correct gdcarroll@ address.\n- 7 June 2026 — “Church View Close, Llandough”. 1988 events from public\nrecords, family testimony and media.\n- 25 June 2026 — “Great House Farm, Llandough”. Asked whether he had\nreviewed the earlier concerns and whether any discussion was possible.\n- 13 July 2026 — “Great House Farm / Church View Close”. Full timeline\nrestated. Ten-working-day request. Explicit question: who removed the tree\nmy great-grandfather planted to commemorate the ownership claim, as shown\nin the Collection of Wales archive image.\n- 27 July 2026 — formal complaint to [email redacted],\ncopied to Councillor Carroll, Democratic Services and the Monitoring\nOfficer.\n- 28 August 2026 — further letter to Councillor Carroll and Stephen Doughty\nMP on the same site.\n\nWhat I am asking you to do\n\n1. Note that the ward member has not answered, and that the complaint\nprocess produced no requirement that he do so.\n\n2. Ask Councillor Carroll, or the relevant Director, to provide a short\nwritten reply on the tree: which department or landowner authorised or\ncarried out its removal, on what date, and under what power or works order\n— or to confirm that the Council holds no such record.\n\n3. Identify the correct officer contact for heritage, trees and historic\nplanning records at Church View Close / former Great House Farm, so I am\nnot left circling a silent ward inbox.\n\n4. Confirm whether the Council will treat a documented family connection to\na demolished historic farmstead in the ward as a legitimate basis for a\nreply, even where the correspondent is not presently resident in Llandough.\n\nThe thesis of my concern is that the lawfare/ warfare that systematically\nattempted to make our occupancy permissive as early as the 40's (with my\ngrandmothers statement of title being stolen, a failed attempt to get us\ninto a tenancy afterwards, and ambiguity in a 1955 order for another parcel\nwe leased and defaulted on, which later meant it was able to be\nmisinterpreted to make it appear our parcel of land (now Church View Close)\nwas part of theirs, like it was in 1916 - 1928) is a racket. The ownership\ndispute was a problem created. The reaction followed and the solution was\nto focus on possession. And so in 1987 BP were awarded possession with what\nwas a defective title chain.\n\nI do not expect you to reopen 1987 litigation. I do expect the authority,\nonce the ward member has been given months and a formal complaint, to\nanswer a factual question about a tree on land in that ward. Because that\ntree was part of a long list of evidence supporting our ownership claim.\n\nI can supply the original emails and the 27 July complaint in full if\nDemocratic Services does not already have them. See attached the\naforementioned tree planting ceremy image. I also enclose a draft chancery\ncourt allocation so you can understand the legal arguments.\n\nDue to a lot of suspicious and conveniently timed deaths in our family,\nsurrounding this case, like my grandmother dying in the 2 weeks she will\nhave had to challenge BP quietly registering our land parcel in their names\nin 1983, without declaring our ownership claim, which was never\nexstinguished as the first 1974 court case was ajourned. Or my fathers\ndeath after his appeal of the 1987 ruling was dismissed on grounds of\n\"heads BP win, tails we lose\". Followed by ECHR rejection citing BP own the\nland, despite BP only seeking possession and never seeking or gaining\nownership.\n\nI have a trove of evidence and I am collecting more and investigating and\nin talks with CPS and Fraud Police and MoJ and Land Registry. The initial\nthing I would like from you is the record of the removal of the tree we\nplanted. The picture attached depicts its location. I'd like to know who\nremoved it and when it was removed?\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a08a8783f2b6b56","subject":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-09-10T08:55:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a08a8783f2b6b56.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"received","from":"Denham, Karen (Registrars)","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a08a8783f2b6b56.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Requester\nThank you for your email. As I stated in my last email we only hold the record for William Buckler in 1990. I have found Mary Doreen Williams in 1983 on FREEBMD with that volume and page number and it clearly states her name as this. I have also tried with my colleagues in the Barry Register Office and they don’t hold the record there either and they have done a search on various names also. With regards to your email of the 21st August 2026 we cannot comment on individual cases and that is the case for the solicitor. We can only supply copies of the certificates that you are trying to locate. With regards to Mary Doreen Williams as I explained it best to get this certificate from our head office as they hold all the records for England and Wales and you just need to give them the volume and the page number that you have. If you would like to purchase the copy of William Bucklers death certificate then you can either apply online or give us a call on [phone redacted] and we can take the order and payment from you. I am sorry that I cannot be of more help to you.\n\nKind Regards\nKaren\n\nKaren Denham\nDirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar & Nationality Officer\nEbost/Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nFfon/Tel: [phone redacted]\nwww.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk<http://www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 09 September 2026 17:29\nTo: Denham, Karen (Registrars) <[email redacted]>\nCc: Registrars Office / Swyddfa'r Cofrestrydd <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\n*** EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links. ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni. *** . Dear Karen,\n\nThank you for your emails of 21 August and 9 September 2026.\n\nYour 9 September message repeats the 21 August reply and does not address my follow-up of 21 August 2026 (13:31), which attached the only document I hold for Mary Doreen Williams and asked specific questions about the March 1983 registration. I set out below only those points that fall within the Register Office.\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler — entry you confirm you hold\nPlease confirm in writing that:\n(a) Cardiff Register Office holds the death entry;\n(b) the entry will be retained and will not be destroyed;\n(c) the registration particulars needed to order a certified copy, namely exact date of death, district, volume and page (or equivalent register reference).\n\nI will consider placing the order. Please confirm whether you need anything further from me before I pay (priority £38.50 or standard £12.50).\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams — entry you say you cannot locate\nI already supplied:\n- full name: Mary Doreen Williams\n- date of birth: 10 August 1913\n- death registered: March 1983, South Glamorgan\n- GRO index: Volume 28, Page 3029\n- supporting document attached to my 21 August email\n\nPlease confirm:\n(a) whether that 21 August attachment was received and reviewed;\n(b) whether the search included Volume 28, Page 3029 for March 1983, South Glamorgan;\n(c) which indexes and years were searched, and under which name variants (Mary, Doreen, Mary D, Williams);\n(d) if Cardiff does not hold the entry, which office should hold a March 1983 South Glamorgan death, or whether I should order from GRO using Vol 28 / Page 3029;\n(e) if the entry is found, whether the index or register shows anything unusual for March 1983 (for example a gap between date of death and date of registration, or any other feature visible on the face of the record).\n\nPoint (e) is a request about the registration record only. I am not asking the Register Office to comment on title, planning, or any other matter outside civil registration.\n\nI would be grateful for a written reply to each of 1(a)–(c) and 2(a)–(e).\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a087009ed6a2a98","subject":"Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-09-09T16:29:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a087009ed6a2a98.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a087009ed6a2a98.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Karen,\n\nThank you for your emails of 21 August and 9 September 2026.\n\nYour 9 September message repeats the 21 August reply and does not address\nmy follow-up of 21 August 2026 (13:31), which attached the only document I\nhold for Mary Doreen Williams and asked specific questions about the March\n1983 registration. I set out below only those points that fall within the\nRegister Office.\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler — entry you confirm you hold\nPlease confirm in writing that:\n(a) Cardiff Register Office holds the death entry;\n(b) the entry will be retained and will not be destroyed;\n(c) the registration particulars needed to order a certified copy, namely\nexact date of death, district, volume and page (or equivalent register\nreference).\n\nI will consider placing the order. Please confirm whether you need anything\nfurther from me before I pay (priority £38.50 or standard £12.50).\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams — entry you say you cannot locate\nI already supplied:\n- full name: Mary Doreen Williams\n- date of birth: 10 August 1913\n- death registered: March 1983, South Glamorgan\n- GRO index: Volume 28, Page 3029\n- supporting document attached to my 21 August email\n\nPlease confirm:\n(a) whether that 21 August attachment was received and reviewed;\n(b) whether the search included Volume 28, Page 3029 for March 1983, South\nGlamorgan;\n(c) which indexes and years were searched, and under which name variants\n(Mary, Doreen, Mary D, Williams);\n(d) if Cardiff does not hold the entry, which office should hold a March\n1983 South Glamorgan death, or whether I should order from GRO using Vol 28\n/ Page 3029;\n(e) if the entry is found, whether the index or register shows anything\nunusual for March 1983 (for example a gap between date of death and date of\nregistration, or any other feature visible on the face of the record).\n\nPoint (e) is a request about the registration record only. I am not asking\nthe Register Office to comment on title, planning, or any other matter\noutside civil registration.\n\nI would be grateful for a written reply to each of 1(a)–(c) and 2(a)–(e).\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-1a086f0f8c32285b","subject":"FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-09-09T16:12:14Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a086f0f8c32285b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a08046912368e30-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a08046912368e30","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a086f0f8c32285b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch,\n\nI myself am at the mercy of having to leave no stone unturned with this and\nmust explore all avenues because much has eventually come to light, but not\neasily with other institutions.\n\nI have encountered parties trying opt out of FOI even GDPR and SAR. Then\ntrying to refer me to other agencies before conducting a search. Then total\ndenial any result were found. Even lying to me. Then a search but negligent\nand incompetently. Then I've actually had to show snippeted of my copies of\nrecords they should hold. Then I've had to insist on internal reviews to be\nsure of what was searched matched what I asked. I've even had conditional\nacceptances whereby even my last employer, of my last of my 22 years in\nOath, the Vale of Glamorgan Council, asked for what I had before they'd\nshow me what they had. Or other oddities.\n\nI know with what happened in the last century with our farmhouse involved a\nlot of scandle, in order to disposses us of our country treasure 800 year\nold home, which we owned, before being removed by force from the land we\nstill own, and demolishing our home since 1667 to develop 20 houses in its\nplace, which the entire community petitioned when the plan was just 13\nhouses, and on a roman villa and monestry and medieval burial site, which\nauthories knew full well was there. I'm just trying to get answers for my\nfamily and to understand what exactly happened in a fact find and on an\nevidence basis. But the Llandough councillors refusal to respond and the\nnon response from MPs is a further outrage on what is already a very\nsensitive subject. My surviving family who didn't die in mysterious ways at\nconvenient times during all this, have been too terrified to speak up or\nout again about any of this, living like hostages under the occupying\nBritish, suffering in silence for the last 38 straight years. And the land\nregistry responses also raise more questions. Many local authorities take\nthe maximum time to respond at each interval. Our family are having to\nre-live a horrendous ordeal, to even say anything about our home and lands\ntrue history and herritage and the defective title upon which 20 family\nhomes now exist.\n\nThe narrative and public records are all very wrong and misleading and\ndeceiving. I have corroborating family testimony confirming records were\nremoved/ stolen and not just from our home but the public library. Many\ninstitutions report gaps in records and cannot account for destroyed/\nmissing records.\n\nSo I thank you in advance for your co-operation in this matter. I believe a\ncollective effort will mean a lot should the Senedd authorise a public\nenquiry or my family get justice. But this was and still is a matter of\nnational public interest.\n\nMarconi was staying with us at our home there, in 1897, while conducting\nthe successful experiment of radio at Lavernock Point.  Meanwhile Cardiff\nCouncil refuse to even put the inventors name on the statue of the radio at\nCardiff Bay because Cardiff is now a city of sanctuary and Marconi was\nright wing politically. And alledgedly an anti semite, but my research from\nthat also suggests that wasn't the case. I'm actually having to depend on\nGermanies spy's accounts of what happened between my family and Marconi due\nto the Brit'ish States concealment and rewriting of history.\n\nWe should remember, especially as Welsh under British occupancy and rule,\nthat the British Establishment invented concentration work camps. And is\nrenowned for ethnically cleansing entire races of indigenous. What my\nfamily and our history and herritage and culture and language were\nsubjected to for the last century, was nothing short of that.\n\nI enclose for your interest ITV footage, unaired/ gatekept, of our home\nbeing looted of all our furniture we got from Cardiff Castle. While my baby\nsister was made to watch. It's believed the BP Bailiffs were in fact\nundercover soldiers.\n\nThe complete story and chronology has not been told. It appears to begin\nwith Cedwyn the giant/ St Cedwyn. A 2,200 year old iron age round house.\n\nThe 1820 church wasn't the first built. And I find it highly suspect CADW\nrejected our 800 year old county treasure home next door, from receiving\nGrade II listing status so it couldn't be demolished, whereas the church,\nalso rebuilt again in the 1840's I believe, was awarded Grade II in 1989.\n\nThere's not even a park bench plaque to Marconi there or a tourist\ninformation board for the rich history and herritage. Church View Close,\nLlandough constitutes a terrorist cell/ network/ concentration work camp.\nThis should be an outrage to any historian. Which isn't my field, I'm just\na military cyber warfare professional.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\n\nOn Tue, 8 Sept 2026, 10:14 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> I note your position and can confirm that FOI:2026-032 will remain open\n> and will be processed separately from FOI:2026-036.\n>\n>\n>\n> In all honesty, my suggestion that FOI:2026-036 replace FOI:2026-032 was\n> not made with a view to aggregating the requests or considering the\n> application of a section 12 exemption. It was intended as an administrative\n> measure to avoid duplication of work and correspondence for a small\n> collections team where two requests cover substantially the same subject\n> matter.\n>\n>\n>\n> However, I note that you wish the requests to remain separate and we will\n> proceed on that basis.\n>\n>\n>\n> Also, to confirm, the internal review of FOI:2026-024 will continue\n> independently.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 08 September 2026 13:17\n> *To:* FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> This email comes from outside the organisation.\n>\n> Do not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected\n> to receive.\n>\n> FOI Team,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email concerning FOI:2026-036.\n>\n>\n>\n> I do not agree that FOI:2026-032 should be closed or treated as replaced.\n>\n>\n>\n> The three matters are distinct and should remain so.\n>\n>\n>\n> Internal review of FOI 2026-024\n>\n> This remains a review of how the original 27 July request was interpreted\n> and searched. I confirm it is separate. Nothing in FOI:2026-036 is a\n> comment on that review.\n>\n>\n>\n> FOI 2026-032 (your letter of 26 August 2026; also written by you as FOI\n> 2026-32)\n>\n> This is the request you yourselves extracted from my 26 August email. Its\n> subject is the records your searches for FOI 2026-024 had already\n> identified: the “other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House\n> Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough” and the Church Farm, Llandough finds which you\n> excluded from 2026-024 as out of scope. You registered that as a new\n> request and gave a response date of 23 September 2026. That request has not\n> been withdrawn. Those records have already been located. They do not\n> require a new collection-wide trawl.\n>\n>\n>\n> FOI:2026-036 (my email of 8 September 2026). This is a new request. It is\n> not a restatement of 2026-032. It has additional limbs:\n>\n>\n>\n> a schedule of every object, archive file, accession, loan, enquiry or\n> correspondence record indexed, provenanced or otherwise recorded as from\n> Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Llandough Farm;\n>\n>\n>\n> the Church Farm schedule only so far as already retrieved in the 2026-024\n> search, and without a new full trawl;\n>\n>\n>\n> predecessor accession, register, day-book, donations-book and\n> correspondence searches for 1875–1915 (Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of\n> Natural History / National Museum of Wales) for ironwork, armour, visor,\n> lance, helmet, “armour from Llandough”, or a find from Great House /\n> Llandough Farm;\n>\n>\n>\n> object records for Llandough ironwork not labelled “visor” or “lance” but\n> associated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing / dairy.\n>\n>\n>\n> If it assists you administratively, I have no objection to a single letter\n> that answers both 2026-032 and 2026-036, provided that:\n>\n> a. FOI 2026-032 is not closed, withdrawn or treated as superseded;\n>\n>\n>\n> b. the records already identified in the 2026-024 search are scheduled and\n> disclosed as a discrete part of that letter, and that part is provided by\n> the date you gave for 2026-032 (23 September 2026);\n>\n>\n>\n> c. the additional limbs of 2026-036 remain live and are answered on the\n> 2026-036 timescale;\n>\n>\n>\n> d. the two requests are not aggregated so as to refuse either under\n> section 12;\n>\n> e. the internal review of FOI 2026-024 continues independently.\n>\n>\n>\n> The purpose of 2026-036 was to obtain the records you had already found\n> and set aside, together with the predecessor-register and full-site\n> schedule work that 2026-024 did not cover. It was not an invitation to\n> extinguish 2026-032 or to restart the clock on material already retrieved.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please confirm that FOI 2026-032 remains open on the terms above.\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> On Tue, 8 Sept 2026, 06:08 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\n> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> I note that this request covers the same subject matter as FOI:2026-032\n> and extends the scope of the information requested in that case.\n>\n>\n>\n> In order to avoid duplication and ensure that we provide a single,\n> comprehensive response, our intention is to treat FOI:2026-036 as replacing\n> FOI:2026-032 and to close FOI:2026-032 accordingly.\n>\n>\n>\n> Unless we hear from you to the contrary within the next few working days,\n> we will proceed on that basis and respond to the broader request contained\n> in FOI:2026-036.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please note that your request for an internal review of FOI:2026-024\n> remains a separate matter and will continue to be considered independently.\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 08 September 2026 04:05\n> *To:* FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> This email comes from outside the organisation.\n>\n> Do not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected\n> to receive.\n>\n> FOI Team,\n>\n>\n>\n> This is a new request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is not\n> a repeat of FOI 2026-024 and it is not a comment on the internal review of\n> that request.\n>\n>\n>\n> In your letter of 25 August 2026 (FOI 2026-024) you stated:\n>\n>\n>\n>   “For completeness, our searches identified records relating to other\n> archaeological finds from Church Farm, Llandough and to other\n> archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr),\n> Llandough. These records do not relate to, nor are they otherwise\n> associated with, the discovery described in your request. We have therefore\n> not considered them to fall within the scope of this request.”\n>\n>\n>\n> I now request those records.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please provide:\n>\n>\n>\n> 1. A schedule of every object, archive file, accession, loan, enquiry or\n> correspondence record that Amgueddfa Cymru holds which is indexed,\n> provenanced or otherwise recorded as from Great House Farm / Ty Mawr /\n> Llandough Farm, Llandough (Penarth / Vale of Glamorgan). For each entry:\n> accession or archive number, object or file title, date of acquisition or\n> creation, donor or excavator if recorded, and a one-line description.\n>\n>\n>\n> 2. The same schedule for Church Farm, Llandough, but only so far as the\n> records were retrieved in the 2026-024 search and can be identified without\n> a new full trawl.\n>\n>\n>\n> 3. Any accession, register entry, day-book, donations book or\n> correspondence in the collections of Amgueddfa Cymru or of its predecessor\n> Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of Natural History / National Museum of\n> Wales, dated 1875–1915, recording ironwork, armour, a visor, a lance, a\n> helmet, “armour from Llandough”, or a find from Great House / Llandough\n> Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n>    Published sources which state that such ironwork is in the National\n> Museum, and which therefore make a search of predecessor registers\n> reasonable, are:\n>\n>\n>\n>    • GGAT, Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological\n> Assessment, August 1990 (planning file 89/01396/OUT and 92/00671/RES): “it\n> is likely that some medieval ironwork which is held by the National Museum\n> of Wales was discovered under the rear wing c 1880 (RCAHMW 1988).”\n>\n>\n>\n>    • Holbrook & Thomas, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70 n. 142:\n> “medieval ironwork was discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm\n> c. 1880. It is now in the collections of the National Museums & Galleries\n> of Wales.”\n>\n>\n>\n>    I note that the National Museum of Wales was not founded until 1907. If\n> a find of c.1880 entered a public collection in Cardiff it would have done\n> so through the earlier municipal museum. Please search those predecessor\n> accession registers, not only the post-1907 NMW database.\n>\n>\n>\n> 4. Any object record for Llandough ironwork that is not labelled “visor”\n> or “lance” but is or was associated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing /\n> dairy (the room identified on H. J. Thomas’s 1974 RCAHMW plan).\n>\n>\n>\n> Please treat this as a request for recorded information only.\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a086c4776891280","subject":"Extension - Our reference:  260813002 FOI IR","name":"Extension - Our reference:  260813002 FOI IR","date":"2026-09-09T15:23:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a086c4776891280.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a086c4776891280-extension-our-reference-260813002-foi-ir","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a086c4776891280","direction":"received","from":"NSUKilo","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":["260813002"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a086c4776891280.json","attachments":[{"name":"260813002 – FOI IR extension letter.pdf","title":"260813002 – FOI IR extension letter.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-09-09_moj_260813002_foi-ir-extension-letter.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":129491,"sha256":"ed23a948b3931e5c2885304274b705a0b0cbface365c893d4d98d292e994ae5d"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\nPlease see attached the extension letter for your request (our reference: 260813002).\n\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\n\n\nKnowledge and Information Liaison Officer\n\nNational Support Unit\n\nHM Courts and Tribunals Service\n\n\n[cid:9a37e32a-3027-4c11-82c1-06eef6b0f164]\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-1a0865e98e7a5dcd","subject":"FW: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"FW: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-09-09T13:31:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0865e98e7a5dcd.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-fw-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"received","from":"Denham, Karen (Registrars)","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0865e98e7a5dcd.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Requester\nThank you for your email regarding William Buckler and Mary Doreen Williams death certificates. I have done a search in our indexes and I can confirm that we hold the record for William Buckler but unfortunately I cannot locate the death entry for Mary Doreen Williams. If you would like to purchase the certificate of William Buckler with us then you can either pay £38.50 and you can come and collect it from our office the following day after payment or we can send it out to you first class the following day after payment and will be with you in a couple of days. You can also choose from our standard service which is £12.50 and this is sent out in the post in fifteen days. You can place the order online and we will call you for payment or you can contact us on [phone redacted] and we can take the order and payment from you.  Alternatively you can contact our head office quoting the volume and the page numbers and they will do them from there for you. Their contact telephone number is [phone redacted]. Or alternatively you can email them on Order a birth, death, marriage or civil partnership certificate - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/order-copy-birth-death-marriage-certificate>. I hope all this information helps.\n\nKind Regards\nKaren\n\n\nKaren Denham\nDirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar & Nationality Officer\n\nEbost/Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nFfon/Tel: [phone redacted]\nY Swyddfa Gofrestru, Archifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg. Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted]\nThe Register Office, Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\nwww.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk<http://www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 20 August 2026 20:34\nTo: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Registrars Office / Swyddfa'r Cofrestrydd <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\nDear Register Office,\n\nI wish to obtain certified copies of the death certificates for the following individuals:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital\n   - Aged 41\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Likely registered in the Vale of Glamorgan / South Glamorgan district\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise the correct office holding each entry, the application process, current fees (standard and priority), payment methods, and any additional information required to locate the entries accurately.\n\nI am happy to complete any formal application forms and provide identification if needed.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-1a08615a61a60215","subject":"Opening of BP vs Buckler 1987","name":"Opening of BP vs Buckler 1987","date":"2026-09-09T12:12:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a08615a61a60215.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a08615a61a60215-opening-of-bp-vs-buckler-1987","scopeTopics":["cps"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cps"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a08615a61a60215","direction":"received","from":"Victim Liaison 