 1988 = Unpublished Records relating to Great House\n> Farm prepared by R F Suggett, December 1988.\n>\n>    (GGAT, Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological\n> Assessment, August 1990.)\n>\n>\n>\n> 2. The same statement is repeated in Holbrook & Thomas, “An Early-medieval\n> Monastic Cemetery at Llandough, Glamorgan”, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005),\n> p. 70 n. 142:\n>\n>\n>\n>    “Mention should also be made of the fact that medieval ironwork was\n> discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm c. 1880. It is now in\n> the collections of the National Museums & Galleries of Wales.”\n>\n>\n>\n> 3. The Heneb / Archwilio HER entry for Great House Farm (GGAT02038s)\n> records armour / medieval ironwork found under the rear-wing floor c.1880\n> and attributes the note to RCAHMW.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please therefore provide:\n>\n>\n>\n> A. The full text of R F Suggett’s December 1988 unpublished records\n> relating to Great House Farm, including every page or card that mentions\n> ironwork, armour, a visor, a lance, a helmet, a burial, a soldier, a horse,\n> a museum, or a find under the floor or rear wing / dairy.\n>\n>\n>\n> B. Any earlier NMR / RCAHMW survey notes, correspondence or drawings that\n> Suggett was using (including H. J. Thomas’s 1974 survey of the house,\n> updated December 1988), insofar as they mention the c.1880 find or the\n> destination of the objects.\n>\n>\n>\n> C. Any record of the source of Suggett’s statement that the ironwork “is\n> held by the National Museum of Wales” — for example a letter, accession\n> note, conversation record, or museum catalogue reference.\n>\n>\n>\n> D. Any later NMR / Coflein / correspondence file that confirms, corrects\n> or withdraws that museum attribution.\n>\n>\n>\n> E. File references, NPRNs and any copy letters sent to or received from\n> the National Museum of Wales / Amgueddfa Cymru, GGAT, Cadw or the Vale of\n> Glamorgan concerning this find.\n>\n>\n>\n> I am not asking for advice or for a new interpretation. I am asking for\n> the recorded information that underpins the 1988 sentence now cited as fact\n> in the planning file and in Medieval Archaeology.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please supply electronic copies where held. If any item is already\n> published on Coflein, a catalogue link and reference is enough.\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a081cc2fcfedcab","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-09-08T16:13:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a081cc2fcfedcab.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a07ef67ca845e50-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a07ef67ca845e50","direction":"received","from":"NMR Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a081cc2fcfedcab.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon.\n\nThank you for your request.\n\nWe will respond to your enquiry within twenty working days.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRhodri Lewis\n\n\n\n\nNMR Enquiries\nYmholiadau Cyhoeddus I Public Enquiries\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 08 September 2026 04:03\nTo: NMR Enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\nNational Monuments Record / FOI Officer,\n\nThis is a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, so far as the records concern the historic environment, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nI request copies of recorded information held by RCAHMW / the National Monuments Record of Wales relating to a reported discovery of ironwork or “armour” under the rear wing of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan (approx. ST 1681 7331; SMR / HER GGAT02038s; NMR NPRN associated with Great House Farm).\n\nThe published citations which identify RCAHMW as the source, and which state that the objects are at the National Museum of Wales, are:\n\n1. RCAHMW, December 1988 — “Unpublished Records relating to Great House Farm prepared by R F Suggett, December 1988.” This is the source cited in the Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust assessment lodged on planning application 89/01396/OUT (and carried into 92/00671/RES):\n\n   “it is likely that some medieval ironwork which is held by the National Museum of Wales was discovered under the rear wing c 1880 (RCAHMW 1988).”\n\n   Bibliography: RCAHMW 1988 = Unpublished Records relating to Great House Farm prepared by R F Suggett, December 1988.\n   (GGAT, Land at Great House Farm, Llandough: An Archaeological Assessment, August 1990.)\n\n2. The same statement is repeated in Holbrook & Thomas, “An Early-medieval Monastic Cemetery at Llandough, Glamorgan”, Medieval Archaeology 49 (2005), p. 70 n. 142:\n\n   “Mention should also be made of the fact that medieval ironwork was discovered under the rear wing of Great House Farm c. 1880. It is now in the collections of the National Museums & Galleries of Wales.”\n\n3. The Heneb / Archwilio HER entry for Great House Farm (GGAT02038s) records armour / medieval ironwork found under the rear-wing floor c.1880 and attributes the note to RCAHMW.\n\nPlease therefore provide:\n\nA. The full text of R F Suggett’s December 1988 unpublished records relating to Great House Farm, including every page or card that mentions ironwork, armour, a visor, a lance, a helmet, a burial, a soldier, a horse, a museum, or a find under the floor or rear wing / dairy.\n\nB. Any earlier NMR / RCAHMW survey notes, correspondence or drawings that Suggett was using (including H. J. Thomas’s 1974 survey of the house, updated December 1988), insofar as they mention the c.1880 find or the destination of the objects.\n\nC. Any record of the source of Suggett’s statement that the ironwork “is held by the National Museum of Wales” — for example a letter, accession note, conversation record, or museum catalogue reference.\n\nD. Any later NMR / Coflein / correspondence file that confirms, corrects or withdraws that museum attribution.\n\nE. File references, NPRNs and any copy letters sent to or received from the National Museum of Wales / Amgueddfa Cymru, GGAT, Cadw or the Vale of Glamorgan concerning this find.\n\nI am not asking for advice or for a new interpretation. I am asking for the recorded information that underpins the 1988 sentence now cited as fact in the planning file and in Medieval Archaeology.\n\nPlease supply electronic copies where held. If any item is already published on Coflein, a catalogue link and reference is enough.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>"},{"id":"gm-1a0817bd1497136e","subject":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-09-08T14:45:46Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0817bd1497136e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["cardiff-reg"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff-reg"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"received","from":"Registration Service","institutions":[{"id":"cardiff-reg","name":"Cardiff / Vale Register Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0817bd1497136e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello Requester\n\nWe have been unable to find records for either of the requested certificates.  Please contact Cardiff to request as deaths between 1990 and 1996 in LLandough are held at Cardiff and South Glamorgan covered the Vale and Cardiff.\n\nMany thanks\nMichelle\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 20 August 2026 20:34\nTo: Registration Service  ; [email redacted]\nSubject: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\nDear Register Office,\n\nI wish to obtain certified copies of the death certificates for the following individuals:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital\n   - Aged 41\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Likely registered in the Vale of Glamorgan / South Glamorgan district\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise the correct office holding each entry, the application process, current fees (standard and priority), payment methods, and any additional information required to locate the entries accurately.\n\nI am happy to complete any formal application forms and provide identification if needed.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a08127fe562a418","subject":"RE: FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-09-08T13:14:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a08127fe562a418.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a08046912368e30-foi-2026-036-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a08046912368e30","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a08127fe562a418.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nI note your position and can confirm that FOI:2026-032 will remain open and will be processed separately from FOI:2026-036.\n\nIn all honesty, my suggestion that FOI:2026-036 replace FOI:2026-032 was not made with a view to aggregating the requests or considering the application of a section 12 exemption. It was intended as an administrative measure to avoid duplication of work and correspondence for a small collections team where two requests cover substantially the same subject matter.\n\nHowever, I note that you wish the requests to remain separate and we will proceed on that basis.\n\nAlso, to confirm, the internal review of FOI:2026-024 will continue independently.\n\n\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image003.png@01DD3F9B.8F47A1A0]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/amgueddfa.cymru> | museum.wales<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/museum.wales>\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 08 September 2026 13:17\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: FOI: 2026-036 - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\n\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nFOI Team,\n\nThank you for your email concerning FOI:2026-036.\n\nI do not agree that FOI:2026-032 should be closed or treated as replaced.\n\nThe three matters are distinct and should remain so.\n\nInternal review of FOI 2026-024\nThis remains a review of how the original 27 July request was interpreted and searched. I confirm it is separate. Nothing in FOI:2026-036 is a comment on that review.\n\nFOI 2026-032 (your letter of 26 August 2026; also written by you as FOI 2026-32)\nThis is the request you yourselves extracted from my 26 August email. Its subject is the records your searches for FOI 2026-024 had already identified: the \"other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough\" and the Church Farm, Llandough finds which you excluded from 2026-024 as out of scope. You registered that as a new request and gave a response date of 23 September 2026. That request has not been withdrawn. Those records have already been located. They do not require a new collection-wide trawl.\n\nFOI:2026-036 (my email of 8 September 2026). This is a new request. It is not a restatement of 2026-032. It has additional limbs:\n\na schedule of every object, archive file, accession, loan, enquiry or correspondence record indexed, provenanced or otherwise recorded as from Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Llandough Farm;\n\nthe Church Farm schedule only so far as already retrieved in the 2026-024 search, and without a new full trawl;\n\npredecessor accession, register, day-book, donations-book and correspondence searches for 1875-1915 (Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of Natural History / National Museum of Wales) for ironwork, armour, visor, lance, helmet, \"armour from Llandough\", or a find from Great House / Llandough Farm;\n\nobject records for Llandough ironwork not labelled \"visor\" or \"lance\" but associated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing / dairy.\n\nIf it assists you administratively, I have no objection to a single letter that answers both 2026-032 and 2026-036, provided that:\na. FOI 2026-032 is not closed, withdrawn or treated as superseded;\n\nb. the records already identified in the 2026-024 search are scheduled and disclosed as a discrete part of that letter, and that part is provided by the date you gave for 2026-032 (23 September 2026);\n\nc. the additional limbs of 2026-036 remain live and are answered on the 2026-036 timescale;\n\nd. the two requests are not aggregated so as to refuse either under section 12;\ne. the internal review of FOI 2026-024 continues independently.\n\nThe purpose of 2026-036 was to obtain the records you had already found and set aside, together with the predecessor-register and full-site schedule work that 2026-024 did not cover. It was not an invitation to extinguish 2026-032 or to restart the clock on material already retrieved.\n\nPlease confirm that FOI 2026-032 remains open on the terms above.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nOn Tue, 8 Sept 2026, 06:08 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nI note that this request covers the same subject matter as FOI:2026-032 and extends the scope of the information requested in that case.\n\nIn order to avoid duplication and ensure that we provide a single, comprehensive response, our intention is to treat FOI:2026-036 as replacing FOI:2026-032 and to close FOI:2026-032 accordingly.\n\nUnless we hear from you to the contrary within the next few working days, we will proceed on that basis and respond to the broader request contained in FOI:2026-036.\n\nPlease note that your request for an internal review of FOI:2026-024 remains a separate matter and will continue to be considered independently.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware    Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[https://mail.google.com/mail/?ui=2&ik=1b3dc17d38&attid=0.3&th=1a080e71d83376c5&view=fimg&fur=ip&rm=1a080e71d83376c5&sz=w1600-h1000&attbid=ANGjdJ_E7YWjX8HausrpKD0FtVJqhGs-ffaR93kGuLiVVs6mZueMRTHSsJFQekY8murFYHqpjVdZZ5yPdnn1NQZtSQqjA7Cu1C7XGAWK1Gw-zFRVRhOjiaIcsddIbqM&disp=emb&realattid&zw]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 08 September 2026 04:05\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\n\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nFOI Team,\n\nThis is a new request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000. It is not a repeat of FOI 2026-024 and it is not a comment on the internal review of that request.\n\nIn your letter of 25 August 2026 (FOI 2026-024) you stated:\n\n  \"For completeness, our searches identified records relating to other archaeological finds from Church Farm, Llandough and to other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. These records do not relate to, nor are they otherwise associated with, the discovery described in your request. We have therefore not considered them to fall within the scope of this request.\"\n\nI now request those records.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n1. A schedule of every object, archive file, accession, loan, enquiry or correspondence record that Amgueddfa Cymru holds which is indexed, provenanced or otherwise recorded as from Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Llandough Farm, Llandough (Penarth / Vale of Glamorgan). For each entry: accession or archive number, object or file title, date of acquisition or creation, donor or excavator if recorded, and a one-line description.\n\n2. The same schedule for Church Farm, Llandough, but only so far as the records were retrieved in the 2026-024 search and can be identified without a new full trawl.\n\n3. Any accession, register entry, day-book, donations book or correspondence in the collections of Amgueddfa Cymru or of its predecessor Cardiff Museum / Welsh Museum of Natural History / National Museum of Wales, dated 1875-1915, recording ironwork, armour, a visor, a lance, a helmet, \"armour from Llandough\", or a find from Great House / Llandough Farm.\n\n   Published sources which state that such ironwork is in the National Museum, and which therefore make a search of predecessor registers reasonable, are:\n\n   * GGAT, Land at Great House Farm, 