work not labelled “visor” or “lance” but\nassociated with the farmhouse floor or rear wing / dairy.\n\nIf it assists you administratively, I have no objection to a single letter\nthat answers both 2026-032 and 2026-036, provided that:\na. FOI 2026-032 is not closed, withdrawn or treated as superseded;\n\nb. the records already identified in the 2026-024 search are scheduled and\ndisclosed as a discrete part of that letter, and that part is provided by\nthe date you gave for 2026-032 (23 September 2026);\n\nc. the additional limbs of 2026-036 remain live and are answered on the\n2026-036 timescale;\n\nd. the two requests are not aggregated so as to refuse either under section\n12;\ne. the internal review of FOI 2026-024 continues independently.\n\nThe purpose of 2026-036 was to obtain the records you had already found and\nset aside, together with the predecessor-register and full-site schedule\nwork that 2026-024 did not cover. It was not an invitation to extinguish\n2026-032 or to restart the clock on material already retrieved.\n\nPlease confirm that FOI 2026-032 remains open on the terms above.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]\n\nOn Tue, 8 Sept 2026, 06:08 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> I note that this request covers the same subject matter as FOI:2026-032\n> and extends the scope of the information requested in that case.\n>\n>\n>\n> In order to avoid duplication and ensure that we provide a single,\n> comprehensive response, our intention is to treat FOI:2026-036 as replacing\n> FOI:2026-032 and to close FOI:2026-032 accordingly.\n>\n>\n>\n> Unless we hear from you to the contrary within the next few working days,\n> we will proceed on that basis and respond to the broader request contained\n> in FOI:2026-036.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please note that your request for an internal review of FOI:2026-024\n> remains a separate matter and will continue to be considered independently.\n>\n