r monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation For the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer<http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer>\n\nCroesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at oedi.  Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e Cymraeg neu'n ddwyieithog. Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person(au) a enwyd yn unig a gall gynnwys deunydd sensitif neu ddeunydd sy wedi'i farcio hyd at 'CYFYNGEDIG' a dylid ei thrin yn unol a hynny. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi'r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopio neu'i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych wedi derbyn y neges ar gam a wnewch roi gwybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae modd cofnodi a/neu fonitro holl negeseuon GCSX yn unol a'r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol.  \nI weld yr ymwadiad llawn ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual. This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain sensitive or protectively marked material up to RESTRICTED and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a037cf4054f6219","subject":"FOI - 2026-024 - Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"FOI - 2026-024 - Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-08-25T07:25:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a037cf4054f6219.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a037cf4054f6219-foi-2026-024-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a037cf4054f6219","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a037cf4054f6219.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your request for information received on 27 July 2026 concerning records relating to a reported discovery at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including a soldier, horse remains and items described as a visor and lance.\n\nAmgueddfa Cymru has undertaken searches of its collections management systems, accession records and associated documentation.\n\nWe have not identified any records relating to the acquisition, accession, donation, transfer or deposit of a medieval visor, lance, helmet or other item of armour associated with Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. We have also not identified records relating to the specific discovery described in your request, including records of associated human or animal remains, reburial records, excavation reports, watching briefs or discovery reports.\n\nAccordingly, under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response is that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.\n\nFor completeness, our searches identified records relating to other archaeological finds from Church Farm, Llandough and to other archaeological discoveries recorded at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. These records do not relate to, nor are they otherwise associated with, the discovery described in your request. We have therefore not considered them to fall within the scope of this request.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with this response, you may request an internal review by writing to [email redacted]<[email redacted]> within 40 working days of the date of this letter.\n\n\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image002.png@01DD346B.41DF6F50]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/amgueddfa.cymru> | museum.wales<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/museum.wales>\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 27 July 2026 02:22\nTo: FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\nSubject: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - FOI - Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n\nThis email comes from outside the organisation.\n\nDo not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected to receive.\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\nDear Freedom of Information Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nA published local history account states that, during works to replace the stone floor of the dining room at Great House Farm (also known as Ty Mawr), Llandough, Cardiff, the remains of a soldier and his horse were discovered beneath the floor.\n\n The remains were subsequently re-buried in the churchyard, and the soldier's visor and lance were given to the National Museum of Wales (Amgueddfa Cymru).\n\nI therefore request the following recorded information held by Amgueddfa Cymru:\n\nAny records relating to the acquisition, accession, donation, transfer or deposit of a medieval visor, lance, helmet, or other items of armour associated with Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Llandough.\n\nThe accession number(s), date of acquisition or transfer, name of the donor or transferring body, and any provenance or discovery notes linked to these objects.\n\nAny catalogue entries, object records, or internal correspondence concerning the above items.\n\nAny records of associated human or animal remains from the same discovery, including notes on reburial.\n\nAny related excavation, watching-brief, or discovery reports held by the Museum.\n\nIf any of the requested information is already publicly available (for example via the Museum's online collections database), I would be grateful if you could simply provide the relevant accession numbers or catalogue links.\n\nPlease treat this as a request for recorded information only. I am not seeking advice or opinion.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory timescale.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n[cid:image003.jpg@01DD346B.41DF6F50]"},{"id":"gm-1a035df692bb0640","subject":"Re: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-24T22:23:48Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a035df692bb0640.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016607283cece4-enquiry-regarding-historical-deaths-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["nhs-cav"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nhs-cav"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016607283cece4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nhs-cav","name":"Cardiff and Vale University Health Board"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a035df692bb0640.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Gentleman! 🙏🏻\n\nOn Mon, 24 Aug 2026, 16:16 Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance), <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Glad I could help you, best of luck with your further enquiries.\n>\n> Tim\n>\n> Sent from Outlook for iOS  \n> ------------------------------\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* Monday, 24 August 2026 19:20:53\n> *To:* Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance) <\n> [email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FW: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n> WARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening\n> attachments.\n>\n> Tim,\n>\n> It's been pleasure.\n> God bless you.\n> Good drills.\n>\n> Requester \n> [phone redacted]\n>\n> On Mon, 24 Aug 2026, 06:16 Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance), <\n> [email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> My responses in red below.\n>\n>\n>\n> Tim\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 24 August 2026 10:11\n> *To:* Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance) <\n> [email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FW: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n> WARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening\n> attachments.\n>\n>\n>\n> Mr Knifton,\n>\n> Thank you for confirming that, having read the points, you confirm that\n> this is the correct position.\n>\n> Before the matter is closed, I would be grateful if I could clarify one\n> important point about the scope of that confirmation, as I do not wish the\n> correspondence to be capable of being interpreted more broadly than the\n> searches actually undertaken.\n>\n> My understanding is that your confirmation means that *no records were\n> found for William Buckler or Mary Doreen Williams on the specific current\n> registration systems searched by your registration team*, and that the\n> Medical Examiner Service itself has no predecessor records because that\n> service did not exist at the time of either death. Correct as explained\n> in my original email.\n>\n> It does *not*, however, mean that searches have established that no\n> historical records ever existed in relation to either death, nor that all\n> records formerly held by the South Glamorgan Health Authority or its\n> constituent hospitals and services have been searched and found not to\n> exist. Unless there is something I am misunderstanding? I want to be sure I\n> don't overlook any traces of evidence.  Correct, this would be the Health\n> Board (Cardiff & Vale or C&V) to determine if records still exist.\n>\n> In particular, as I understand the position you have confirmed, the\n> following remain separate questions outside the scope of the current\n> systems search:\n>\n>    - whether hospital records relating to William Buckler's admission and\n>    death at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990 were created and, if\n>    so, whether any survive with Cardiff and Vale University Health Board or an\n>    archive; For C&V to confirm\n>    - whether equivalent medical, hospital or health-authority records\n>    relating to Mary Doreen Williams were created and, if so, where any\n>    surviving records are held; For C&V to confirm\n>    - whether either death was referred to a coroner or involved a\n>    post-mortem, inquest or other separate investigation; For coroner’s\n>    office to confirm\n>    - whether any relevant records formerly held by the South Glamorgan\n>    Health Authority were transferred to a successor body or archive; and For\n>    C&V to confirm\n>    - where records no longer survive, whether they were destroyed under\n>    an applicable retention and disposal process. They would have been\n>    completed many years ago but this would be for the responsible Health Body\n>    to confirm.\n>\n> I appreciate that these matters may fall outside your office's remit and I\n> am not asking you to undertake those searches yourself. I simply want to\n> ensure that the documentary record accurately distinguishes *\"no records\n> found on the systems searched\"* from *\"no historical records ever existed\n> or survive anywhere within the former health-authority system.\"*\n>\n> If that distinction is correct, I would be grateful for your confirmation.\n> I will then pursue the surviving-record and archival questions with the\n> appropriate successor bodies.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> *Requester * \n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, 24 Aug 2026, 05:42 Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance), <\n> [email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> You’re very welcome and glad I could be of some further assistance.\n>\n>\n>\n> As requested, reading the points as set out in your email below, this is\n> the correct position.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> *Tim Knifton, MSc Gwybodeg Iechyd/Health Informatics*\n>\n> *Rheolwr Rheoli Gwybodaeth/**Information Governance Manager*\n>\n> Partneriaeth Cydwasanaethau GIG Cymru/NHS Wales Shared Services\n> Partnership\n>\n> e-bost/ email: *[email redacted]  *\n>\n> Rhyngrwyd • Internet:* https://nwssp.nhs.wales/\n>  *\n>\n> Twitter: @nwssp\n>\n>\n>\n> Mae PCGC yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu Saesneg.\n>\n> NWSSP welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English.\n>\n>\n>\n> *'Mae'r e-bost hwn ac unrhyw ffeiliau sy'n cyd-fynd gyda’r e-bost hwn,\n> ddim ond ar gyfer defnydd priodol y derbynnydd/ion, a gall gynnwys\n> gwybodaeth sy'n freintiedig, yn gyfrinachol neu eithriedig rhag cael ei\n> ddatgelu. Os nad yw'r darllenydd yn dderbynnydd a fwriadwyd i dderbyn yr\n> e-bost, gwaherddir unrhyw ddatgeliad, dosbarthiad neu unrhyw gamau eraill y\n> cymerwyd neu sydd heb gael eu cymryd gan ddibynnu arno, a gallai fod yn\n> anghyfreithlon. Os ydych wedi derbyn yr e-bost hwn trwy gamgymeriad,\n> dilewch o'ch system ac yn rhowch wybod i'r anfonwr ar unwaith. Bydd y sawl\n> sy’n datgelu unrhyw wybodaeth heb awdurdod i ddatgelu’r wybodaeth a\n> gynhwysir yn yr e-bost yn cael eu gwahardd yn llym.’*\n>\n>\n>\n> *‘**This e-mail and any files that accompany it are intended only for the\n> appropriate use of the addressee/s, and may contain information that is\n> privileged, confidential or exempt from disclosure. If the reader is not an\n> intended recipient, any disclosure, distribution or any action taken or\n> omitted to be taken in reliance on it, is prohibited and may be unlawful.\n> If you have received this e-mail in error, please delete it from your\n> system and notify the sender immediately. Any unauthorised disclosure of\n> the information contained in this e-mail is strictly prohibited, as is use\n> or application of its contents other than for its intended purpose’*\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 24 August 2026 09:39\n> *To:* Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance) <\n> [email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FW: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n> WARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening\n> attachments.\n>\n>\n>\n> Mr Knifton,\n>\n> Very good of you. Thank you for your detailed response and for taking the\n> time to clarify the position. I have passed my concerned to the National\n> Crime Agency too.\n>\n> I appreciate the confirmation that the All Wales Medical Examiner Service\n> did not exist at the time of either death and that, consequently, it would\n> not hold predecessor records relating to deaths in 1983 or 1990.\n>\n> I am also grateful that you asked the registration team to conduct a\n> search and confirmed that no records were found for either individual on\n> the systems searched.\n>\n> For the purposes of maintaining an accurate documentary record, I would be\n> grateful if you could clarify one final point. My objective is to\n> distinguish clearly between records which were never held by the present\n> organisation, records which once existed but have since been destroyed, and\n> records which may survive with a successor body or archive.\n>\n> As I understand your response, the position is as follows:\n>\n>    - the Medical Examiner Service holds no relevant historical records\n>    because the service was not established until 2019;\n>    - the primary care registration system and the records searched by\n>    your registration team contain no records for either William Buckler or\n>    Mary Doreen Williams;\n>    - any original hospital or health-authority records relating to these\n>    deaths would have fallen under the former South Glamorgan Health Authority\n>    and its applicable records-management arrangements;\n>    - surviving hospital records relating to William Buckler's death at\n>    Llandough Hospital may therefore be held by, or have passed to, Cardiff and\n>    Vale University Health Board or another successor/archive repository;\n>    - records relating to any coroner referral, post-mortem or inquest, if\n>    such events occurred, may have been held separately; and\n>    - GP records may have been destroyed under applicable retention\n>    arrangements, although the present search has not identified a specific\n>    destruction record for either individual.\n>\n> If that is an accurate summary of your position, no further action is\n> required from your office. I would simply be grateful for confirmation,\n> particularly that the statement that no records were found does not amount\n> to confirmation that no historical records ever existed elsewhere within\n> the former South Glamorgan Health Authority system.\n>\n> Thank you again for clarifying the historical position and for identifying\n> Cardiff and Vale University Health Board, Glamorgan Archives and the\n> coroner's records as the more appropriate avenues for further enquiry.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> *Requester *\n> \n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, 24 Aug 2026, 04:56 Tim Knifton (NWSSP - Information Governance), <\n> [email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email. As the main contact for Freedom of Information,\n> I have not seen your request previously but I will explain what I can in\n> regards to your original request:\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *I am writing to enquire whether any records or references are held in\n> relation to the following historical deaths that occurred in the Cardiff &\n> Vale / Llandough area: 1. William (Billy) Buckler    - Died at Llandough\n> Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41    - Reported cause: heart attack\n> 2. Mary Doreen Williams    - Born 10 August 1913    - Death registered\n> March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029) Although these pre-date the\n> current Medical Examiner Service, I would be grateful if you could advise\n> whether any legacy records, referrals, or related documentation exist, or\n> direct me to the appropriate archive or department that may hold such\n> information.*\n>\n>\n>\n> The All Wales Medical Examiner Service was introduced on a non-statutory\n> basis in 2019. It operated across Wales to provide independent scrutiny of\n> deaths that were not referred to a coroner so deaths in 1983 and 1990 would\n> not apply in this case. The service became statutory on 9 September 2024,\n> when the death certification reforms came into force in England and Wales.\n> From that date, independent scrutiny by a Medical Examiner became a legal\n> requirement before registration of all non-coronial deaths. Therefore, for\n> deaths in 1983/1990, there would have been no Medical Examiner Service.\n> Death certification would have been carried out by the attending doctor,\n> with referrals made to the coroner where required under the rules that\n> existed at the time. The Medical Examiner system only arrived many decades\n> later.\n>\n>\n>\n> If both deaths occurred in Secondary Care, Hospitals do maintain records\n> of deaths that occurred in their facilities, but these are not generally\n> public records.\n>\n>\n>\n> The official legal record of a death is the death certificate registered\n> with the local registrar and held by the General Register Office (GRO). In\n> Wales, you can obtain copies of death certificates dating back before 1983\n> if the death was registered.  Hospital medical records are usually retained\n> under NHS records management policies and may still exist for deaths in\n> 1983, but access is restricted because they contain confidential medical\n> information.\n>\n>\n>\n> If you are researching a specific death from 1990 at Llandough Hospital,\n> possible sources are:\n>\n>\n>\n>    1. Death certificate from the General Register Office.\n>    2. Glamorgan Archives for historical NHS administrative records.\n>    3. The relevant NHS body that inherited Llandough Hospital records,\n>    now part of Cardiff and Vale University Health Board.\n>    4. Coroner's records, if an inquest was held.\n>\n>\n>\n> In 1990, Llandough Hospital was still an NHS hospital managed through the\n> local health authority system. This was under the South Glamorgan Health\n> Authority, which was responsible for hospitals in the Cardiff and Vale area\n> before NHS trusts were created in the early 1990s and now the Cardiff &\n> Vale University Health Board.\n>\n>\n>\n> They can be contacted here:\n>\n>\n>\n> Health Records - Cardiff and Vale University Health Board\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> GP records are generally retained for a long period. Under current NHS\n> records management guidance, GP records are typically kept for 10 years\n> after a patient's death before being destroyed so these records would be\n> out of scope.\n>\n>\n>\n> I have asked our registration team to search both patients and there are\n> no records found for either patients due to the time elapsed.\n>\n>\n>\n> Further comments have been provided below in red for reference.\n>\n>\n>\n