val policy, schedule or instruction relied upon in concluding that records of this age would no longer be held. I note that the current publicly available County Court Records Retention and Disposition Schedule specifies relatively short retention periods for possession action cases. I should therefore be grateful if you could identify the historical policy, schedule or instruction that governed the records relating to these proceedings and, if possible, indicate when they would have been scheduled for destruction or transfer.\n  5.  Does HMCTS hold any administrative record of the destruction or transfer of the relevant files, such as destruction registers, certificates, transfer schedules or equivalent records?\n  6.  Were any records relating to these proceedings transferred to another repository, including The National Archives, Glamorgan Archives, or any other archive? If so, I should be grateful if you would provide the destination, date and any available reference.\n  7.  Even if the original case files no longer survive, do any registers, indexes or other administrative records remain recording the existence, progress or disposal of proceedings involving the Williams family, the Buckler family, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Pension Trust Ltd, BP Properties Ltd, or Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough?\n\nThe proceedings in question include the High Court possession proceedings of 1955 (including enforcement on or around 4 July 1955), the Cardiff County Court proceedings culminating in the possession order of 11 December 1962 before Judge Temple Morris QC, and the Cardiff County Court proceedings of 1974, including the part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974, the application for leave to enforce in September 1974, and the subsequent correspondence concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement.\n\nI have already been making enquiries of HM Land Registry. However, my present request concerns the court's own records, the searches undertaken in relation to those records, and any surviving administrative record of their retention, destruction or transfer.\n\nIf the information requested is not held within the Enforcement Section, I should be grateful if this enquiry could be forwarded to the appropriate court manager, records officer or other HMCTS team responsible for historical court records, and if you could kindly confirm that this has been done.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to your substantive reply addressing each of the points above.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n[address redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nOn Tue, 4 Aug 2026, 09:43 Cardiff County, Enquiries, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nGood afternoon,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nDue to the age of this case, we wouldn’t currently hold any existing records for it, in line with our procedures. I can confirm we have conducted a search on our internal case management system, which has not produced any results. We are not privy to any other systems upon which we could conduct a search on the details you provide.\n\nIt might be worth contacting Land Registry to see if they hold any details on this:\n\n\nHM Land Registry Citizen Centre\nPO Box74\nGloucester\n[postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\n\nThank you.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nPhoebe Owen\n\nAdministration Officer\nAdran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\nCanolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd | 2 Stryd Y Parc | Caerdydd | [postcode redacted]\nCardiff Civil Justice Centre | 2 Park Street | Cardiff[map link redacted]  | [postcode redacted][map link redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 03 August 2026 21:01\nTo: Cardiff County, Enquiries <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI wrote to you on 10 June 2026 requesting access to historical court records relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan. I have not received a response.\n\nI am seeking confirmation of whether any surviving court records exist relating to possession, title, and related proceedings involving the Williams / Buckler family and the successive parties asserting title through Western Ground Rents Ltd and subsequently BP Pension Trust Ltd / BP Properties Ltd.\n\nThe proceedings and related matters I am seeking to identify include:\n\n  *   High Court possession proceedings and the possession order of 1955, including any related enforcement records (including the enforcement action concerning the agricultural land on or around 4 July 1955);\n  *   Cardiff County Court proceedings of 1962, resulting in the possession order dated 11 December 1962 (before Judge Temple Morris QC), including any related claim for mesne profits;\n  *   Cardiff County Court proceedings commenced in 1974, including the part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974 at which Mary Williams asserted ownership and relied upon adverse possession / limitation arguments, the application for leave to enforce in September 1974, and subsequent correspondence concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement in October and November 1974;\n  *   The subsequent Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] 55 P & CR 337.\n\nI request confirmation of whether any surviving records remain, including (but not limited to):\n\n  *   pleadings;\n  *   statements of case;\n  *   orders;\n  *   warrants;\n  *   correspondence;\n  *   exhibits;\n  *   judgments;\n  *   case files;\n  *   registers or indexes referring to these proceedings or the property.\n\nIf records remain, please advise the procedure for obtaining copies or arranging inspection, including any applicable fees.\n\nIf no records remain, please confirm what searches have been undertaken, which repositories or record systems have been checked, and whether any destruction, retention, or transfer records exist relating to these procee