ynnwys unrhyw e-bost neu ohebiaeth a dderbynnir, yn inol ag amodau’r Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth 2000.\n\nPlease be aware that, under the terms of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership may be required to make public the content of any emails or correspondence received.\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD3197.A1ECB410][cid:image002.png@01DD3197.A1ECB410] [cid:image003.png@01DD3197.A1ECB410]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 20 August 2026 20:33\nTo: SouthWalesCentral MedicalExaminersOffice (Gen126594) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\nWARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening attachments.\n\nDear Medical Examiner Service (South Wales Central),\n\nI am writing to enquire whether any records or references are held in relation to the following historical deaths that occurred in the Cardiff & Vale / Llandough area:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Reported cause: heart attack\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nAlthough these pre-date the current Medical Examiner Service, I would be grateful if you could advise whether any legacy records, referrals, or related documentation exist, or direct me to the appropriate archive or department that may hold such information.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a02ad595fc3aeac","subject":"Ty Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Ty Mawr, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-08-22T18:57:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a02ad595fc3aeac.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a02ad4c2f0fd6e3-ty-mawr-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a02ad4c2f0fd6e3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02ad595fc3aeac.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Glamorgan Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to make a targeted archive research enquiry concerning the\nDBDT collection and any related Bute, Mountjoy or Western Ground Rents\nmaterial held by Glamorgan Archives.\n\nI am investigating the historic title, occupation and parcel\nboundaries of *Great\nHouse Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough*, particularly evidence concerning a\npossible historical division of the farm between land retained by the Bute\nEstate and land allegedly sold or transferred to *Daniel Thomas*.\n\nA family witness account describes a specific arrangement under which\napproximately ten acres, including the farmhouse, were allegedly sold by\nthe Bute Estate to Daniel Thomas, while a separate portion of approximately\nnine acres remained under the Bute Estate. The account further describes\nquarrying on the Thomas-held land and an agreement under which the freehold\nwould eventually pass to the occupying family when quarrying ceased.\n\nI appreciate that this account requires verification against the original\ndocumentary record. I am therefore seeking to identify the relevant deeds,\nagreements, plans and subsequent title documents.\n1. Verification of specific DBDT catalogue entries\n\nPlease confirm the exact property description, parties and date of the\nfollowing catalogue entries, and, if possible, provide a digital copy or\nscan of the opening parties clause and any attached or marginal plan:\n\n   -\n\n   *DBDT10/19* – Lease (counterpart), described in the catalogue as\n   concerning land and messuages in Bute Street, Cardiff, from trustees of the\n   late Marquess of Bute to Mr Daniel Thomas, October 1850.\n   -\n\n   *DBDT10/20* – Agreement for a building lease of premises in Bute Town,\n   Cardiff, involving the same parties, June 1849.\n\nI understand from the catalogue descriptions that these items concern\nCardiff rather than Llandough. My purpose is to establish whether the *Daniel\nThomas named in these instruments can be identified sufficiently to\ndetermine whether he is the same individual later connected with the\nLlandough lime works and land interests*, or whether these are unrelated\ntransactions involving another person of the same name.\n\nPlease also advise whether either document contains information identifying\nDaniel Thomas by residence, occupation, estate, trusteeship or other\ndistinguishing details.\n2. Targeted search for a Bute–Daniel Thomas transaction at or near Llandough\n\nPlease search the catalogue descriptions and indexes available to Glamorgan\nArchives for any deed, conveyance, exchange, sale, transfer, lease,\nagreement, plan or related instrument involving:\n\n   - *Daniel Thomas*;\n   - *Alfred Thomas*;\n   - the *Marquess of Bute*;\n   - trustees of the Marquess of Bute;\n   - the *Bute Estate*;\n\nand land at or near:\n\n   - *Llandough*;\n   - *Great House Farm / Great House / Tŷ Mawr*;\n   - adjoining land or parcels that may subsequently have formed part of\n   the farm.\n\nI am particularly interested in transactions dating from approximately *1876\nto 1878*, but would be grateful for references to earlier or later\ndocuments where they form part of the same chain of title.\n\nIn particular, I am seeking evidence capable of confirming or disproving\nwhether any defined parcel of land was conveyed by the Bute Estate to\nDaniel Thomas.\n3. Quarrying, lime works and any conditional reversion or transfer\n\nPlease identify any relevant records concerning land at Llandough or Great\nHouse Farm that refer to:\n\n   - quarrying;\n   - quarries or quarry land;\n   - lime works or lime kilns;\n   - mineral rights;\n   - removal of quarrying machinery;\n   - reduction or cessation of rent as land was quarried;\n   - termination of quarrying;\n   - a future conveyance, reversion, surrender or transfer of a freehold\n   interest when quarrying ceased.\n\nThe particular issue I am investigating is whether an agreement existed\nunder which occupation or ownership of a defined parcel was intended to\nchange when quarrying operations came to an end.\n4. Daniel Thomas, Alfred Thomas and the Llandough lime works\n\nPlease identify any documents linking *Daniel Thomas*, or his son *Alfred\nThomas (later Lord Pontypridd)*, with:\n\n   - land at Llandough;\n   - the Llandough lime works or lime kilns;\n   - quarrying operations;\n   - Great House Farm or adjoining agricultural land;\n   - any freehold or leasehold interest in the area.\n\nI would be particularly interested in estate papers, correspondence,\nconveyances, wills, probate-related estate records, rentals, rent books,\nabstracts of title and plans that may trace what became of any Daniel\nThomas interest after his death or thereafter.\n5. Subsequent title and occupation\n\nPlease identify any abstracts of title, estate maps, conveyances,\ncorrespondence, tenancy records or other material that may assist in\nestablishing:\n\n   1. what happened to any freehold interest held by Daniel Thomas or his\n   estate;\n   2. whether such an interest was ever conveyed, surrendered or\n   transferred back to the Bute Estate or another party;\n   3. whether the Bute Estate later reacquired any relevant parcel;\n   4. whether later parties, including *Mountjoy Ltd* or *Western Ground\n   Rents Ltd*, acquired title to land previously held by Daniel Thomas or\n   his successors;\n   5. the basis on which later tenancies described as covering the \"whole\"\n   of Great House Farm were granted.\n\nI am also interested in any material linking these title questions with the\noccupation of the farm by the *Williams family*.\n6. Plans and parcel boundaries\n\nA separate line of research concerns the possibility that historic legal\nboundaries passed through or between different parts of the Great House\nFarm complex.\n\nAccordingly, please identify any:\n\n   - estate maps;\n   - conveyance plans;\n   - tenancy plans;\n   - quarry plans;\n   - large-scale plans;\n   - boundary plans;\n   - valuation plans;\n\nthat show Great House Farm, the farmhouse, garden, stables, outbuildings or\nadjoining parcels.\n\nI am particularly interested in documents that could establish whether\ndifferent parts of the historic building complex fell within different\nlegal parcels.\n\nI appreciate that some of these requests may require staff research beyond\na standard enquiry. My immediate priority is to obtain *the relevant\ncatalogue references and confirmation of what material exists*. If more\ndetailed searching or document retrieval is necessary, please let me know\nthe applicable procedure, estimated cost and whether a formal paid research\nrequest would be required.\n\nIf relevant documents have been digitised, I would be grateful for details\nof the cost of obtaining copies. Otherwise, please advise whether they can\nbe consulted in person and whether any restrictions or advance ordering\nrequirements apply.\n\nThank you for your assistance. The documents identified through this\nenquiry may be important to reconstructing the historical chain of title\nand occupation of Great House Farm, Llandough from the nineteenth century\nonwards.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n*Requester *"},{"id":"gm-1a025349254f12f0","subject":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T16:43:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a025349254f12f0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"received","from":"Coroner Admin","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a025349254f12f0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am eich e-bost.  Ein nod yw darparu ymateb o fewn 7 niwrnod gwaith.\n\nThank you for your email.  We aim to provide a response within 7 working days.\n\nCroesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at oedi.  Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e Cymraeg neu'n ddwyieithog. Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person(au) a enwyd yn unig a gall gynnwys deunydd sensitif neu ddeunydd sy wedi'i farcio hyd at 'CYFYNGEDIG' a dylid ei thrin yn unol a hynny. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi'r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopio neu'i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych wedi derbyn y neges ar gam a wnewch roi gwybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae modd cofnodi a/neu fonitro holl negeseuon GCSX yn unol a'r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol.  \nI weld yr ymwadiad llawn ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual. This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain sensitive or protectively marked material up to RESTRICTED and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a0253421f267d4d","subject":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T16:42:48Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0253421f267d4d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0253421f267d4d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Bev,\n\nThank you for checking the system and for your prompt and helpful reply.\n\nI am grateful for the clarification regarding the historical position of\nCardiff and Vale cases prior to 2002, and I will now pursue enquiries with\nGlamorgan Archives.\n\nBefore I do so, I would be grateful if I could clarify one point concerning\nthe result of your search, particularly in relation to my grandmother, Mary\nDoreen Williams.\n\nMy purpose is not simply genealogical. I am attempting to reconstruct and\nforensically assess the historical circumstances surrounding her death in\n1983, and there is information concerning the circumstances before and\naround her death which I am seeking to reconcile against the surviving\nofficial documentary record.\n\nCould you therefore please confirm whether your statement that you are\n\"unable to locate any details\" means only that neither individual appears\nin the records or computerised/indexed system currently available to your\noffice, or whether your office is able positively to state that neither\ndeath was ever referred to the coroner?\n\nIn particular, if you are able to clarify, I would be grateful to know\nwhether the absence of a record in your system excludes, or does not\nexclude, the historical existence of:\n\n   - a report of the death to a coroner;\n   - a preliminary coroner's enquiry;\n   - a post-mortem examination;\n   - an inquest;\n   - correspondence with the police, hospital or other authority;\n   - a case file or register subsequently transferred to an archive or\n   destroyed in accordance with an applicable retention policy.\n\nI appreciate that you may not hold the historical records themselves. I am\nnot asking you to speculate about the circumstances of either death. I am\nsimply seeking to ensure that I correctly understand the evidential\nsignificance of the negative search result before proceeding to the archive.\n\nIf possible, I would also be grateful if you could confirm the name of the\ncoroner jurisdiction or office responsible for Llandough/Llandough Hospital\nin March 1983, when Mary Doreen Williams died, and whether you know which\nbody would have inherited or transferred that jurisdiction's surviving\nrecords.\n\nFor completeness, if there are any records held off-system, legacy indexes,\npaper registers, accession records or transfer information which are not\nsearchable through the system you checked, I would be grateful if you could\nlet me know whether those exist and who now holds them.\n\nI appreciate your assistance. I am trying to establish the documentary\nfacts carefully and avoid drawing conclusions before the relevant records\nhave been located or ruled out.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 05:14 Coroner Admin, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Good morning, Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your prompt reply.\n>\n> I have checked our system for any records relating to the two cases you\n> have asked information for.\n>\n> Unfortunately, I am unable to locate any details on the Late Mr William\n> Buckler or the late Mary Doreen Williams.\n>\n> Cardiff and Vale cases prior to 2002 should be with the Glamorgan\n> Archivist, you can contact them on Tel; [phone redacted] or\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> I hope this information helps and I wish you the best in your search.\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n> Bev\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 21 August 2026 08:47\n> *To:* Coroner Admin <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n> Bev,\n>\n> Thank you for clarifying the position regarding the Freedom of Information\n> Act.\n>\n> I understand that coroners and their records are not subject to the FOI\n> access regime. I am therefore not seeking to pursue the matter as an FOI\n> request if that is not the appropriate route.\n>\n> My primary purpose is to establish whether either of these deaths was ever\n> referred to the coroner and, if so, whether any surviving record exists and\n> what lawful route is available for an interested family member to obtain\n> information from it.\n>\n> I would therefore be grateful if you could clarify the following, insofar\n> as you are able:\n>\n>    1. Whether your office has any record or index indicating that either\n>    William (Billy) Buckler, who died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May\n>    1990, or Mary Doreen Williams, whose death was registered in March 1983 in\n>    South Glamorgan (Vol. 28, p. 3029), was reported to or dealt with by the\n>    coroner;\n>    2. If either death was the subject of a coroner's investigation,\n>    whether an inquest, post-mortem examination or other coroner's\n>    investigation took place;\n>    3. Whether any historical record relating to either death remains in\n>    the custody of the coroner's service, or whether such records have been\n>    transferred to another archive, authority or successor body;\n>    4. If records exist but cannot be disclosed directly, what procedure\n>    is available for a descendant or other interested person to establish the\n>    basic factual information concerning the case;\n>    5. If your office has no record whatsoever of either death, whether\n>    that means that no coroner's record exists, or simply that the surviving\n>    records are no longer held by your office.\n>\n> I am particularly interested in establishing the documentary chain rather\n> than necessarily seeking disclosure of confidential medical information. A\n> confirmation that a death was, or was not, referred to the coroner would\n> itself be useful.\n>\n> If you are not the appropriate office to answer these historical-record\n> questions, I would be grateful if you could identify the relevant archive,\n> successor body or other custodian to whom I should direct the enquiry.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester \n>\n> \n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 04:33 Coroner Admin, <[email redacted]>\n> wrote:\n>\n> Good morning, Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your e-mail dated 20/08/2026.\n>\n>\n>\n> Although appointed and paid for by local councils, the coroner is not a\n> local government officer but holds office under the Crown.\n>\n>\n>\n> Coroners are not designated as public authorities under the Freedom of\n> Information Act 2000 and therefore their records are not subject to the\n> information access regime of this Act.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please let me know if I can be of further assistance.\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n> Bev Morgan\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 20 August 2026 20:34\n> *To:* Coroner Admin <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Coroner’s Office,\n>\n> I am writing under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and as an\n> interested person to request any records held by the South Wales Central\n> Coroner’s Service relating to the following two deaths:\n>\n> 1. William (Billy) Buckler\n>    - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n>    - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n>    - Reported cause: heart attack\n>    - Funeral 5 June 1990, Bethesda Chapel, Dinas Powys; interment St\n> Michael’s Church, Michaelston-le-Pit\n>\n> 2. Mary Doreen Williams\n>    - Born 10 August 1913\n>    - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n>\n> Please advise whether either death was reported to the Coroner, whether a\n> post-mortem or inquest was held, and what documentation (reports, police\n> referrals, hospital communications, etc.) remains available. Please also\n> confirm the procedure, identification required, any fees, and timescales\n> for release to next-of-kin or interested persons.\n>\n> I can supply further identifying details, proof of interest, and\n> contemporary newspaper cuttings / family notes upon request.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n> Requester \n> \n>\n>\n>\n> Croesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at\n> oedi. Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e. Cymraeg neu'n\n> ddwyieithog\n>\n> Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person / pobl enwedig yn unig. Gall gynnwys\n> gwybodaeth bersonol, sensitif neu gyfrinachol. Os nad chi yw'r person a\n> enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi’r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a\n> enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopïo neu’i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson\n> arall. Os ydych chi wedi derbyn y neges ar gam, rhowch wybod i'r sawl sy\n> wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae'n bosibl y bydd holl negeseuon yn cael\n> eu cofnodi a/neu fonitro unol â’r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol. I ddarllen yr\n> ymwadiad llawn, ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding with us in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual\n>\n> This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may\n> contain personal, sensitive or confidential material and should be handled\n> accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive\n> it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone\n> else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the\n> sender immediately. All traffic may be subject to recording and/or\n> monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation For the full disclaimer\n> please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer\n>\n>\n>\n> Croesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at\n> oedi. Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e. Cymraeg neu'n\n> ddwyieithog\n>\n> Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person / pobl enwedig yn unig. Gall gynnwys\n> gwybodaeth bersonol, sensitif neu gyfrinachol. Os nad chi yw'r person a\n> enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi’r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a\n> enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopïo neu’i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson\n> arall. Os ydych chi wedi derbyn y neges ar gam, rhowch wybod i'r sawl sy\n> wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae'n bosibl y bydd holl negeseuon yn cael\n> eu cofnodi a/neu fonitro unol â’r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol. I ddarllen yr\n> ymwadiad llawn, ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding with us in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual\n>\n> This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may\n> contain personal, sensitive or confidential material and should be handled\n> accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive\n> it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone\n> else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the\n> sender immediately. All traffic may be subject to recording and/or\n> monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation For the full disclaimer\n> please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a02529c981f4434","subject":"Re: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T16:31:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a02529c981f4434.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02529c981f4434.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you. You star!\n\nPlease ensure the record isn't destroyed.\n\nAll I have for my nan is the attached.\n\nCould you tell me any more about March 1983 and if there's any anomalies or\nanything out of the ordinary?\n\nI have a statement from my grandmother about her title deeds going missing\nfrom her home by an unsavory character. And then she died in the 2 week\nwindow she will have had to challenge her land being registered in another\nparties name, at the land registry.\n\nHer title was merged with the adjacent plot of land in that timeframe too.\nWhich was also possessed from our family with equal contestability. The\nland in question has already had 20 homes developed on it (Church View\nClose, Llandough) and is now proceeding to flatten woodland and develop 133\nhomes (planning approved) with no mention of title chain defect. And I\nguess the council for Llandough refuses to respond to the concern I'm\nraising because of a bias in the project to develop homes on our land. Our\nownership claim has never been estinguished by a court. Their ownership\nclaim not ruled on either. It's our land since 1667. They have just awarded\nthemselves possession of our land in their courts because my grandmother\nwas unable to present her title deed. A public library copy went missing\ntoo. But the court ruling was ajourned.\n\nI'm horrified at the council and MP. The long standing council clerk for\nLlandough recently retired, I guess in relation to this. I was also lied to\nfor months by various departments like CADW.  This is a genuine concern.\nAnd matter of public and national interest as they are also concealing the\nfact of our lands archelogical and hostorical significants. Including a\nRoman villa, 1,026 medieval burials and grange, a monestry too. And prior\nto our home being abruptly demolished with all our evidence inside, which\nCADW and the council (who failed to do a demolish stop order) looked away,\nMarconi stayed with us while inventing radio and Peerless Jim fought his\nfirst fight in our barn and much else.\n\nWe are a very dispossessed family and the subject of decades of crimes\nbeing committed against us. Proceedural unfairness, court mistakes. But it\nreally is a matter of public and national interest. And police dismissed\ninvestigating the 20 years of evidence I've collected within 3 hours of\nreceiving it.\n\nMy family all remain too terrified to speak up or out. After everyone who\nhas challenged the occupation of my ancestral birthland and childhood home\nhas died. My fathers death, conveniently before planning was approved on\nthe 20 houses.\n\nI would encourage you not to keep this information to yourself.\n\nI'm a bona fide war veteran and left my military career with full honours.\nI finished my 22 years in Oath in 2024 and my last employed is the Vale of\nGlamorgan council under which I provided adult care.\n\nI am sorry to burden you with all this, but seeing as your one of the few\nwhos provided me any help or answers in my enquiry, I take the opportunity\nto entrust this information to you.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\nBuckler/ Williams Family Estate\nhttps://bucklerfamily.estate\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 05:11 Denham, Karen (Registrars), <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Hi Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your email regarding William Buckler and Mary Doreen\n> Williams death certificates. I have done a search in our indexes and I can\n> confirm that we hold the record for William Buckler but unfortunately I\n> cannot locate the death entry for Mary Doreen Williams. If you would like\n> to purchase the certificate of William Buckler with us then you can either\n> pay £38.50 and you can come and collect it from our office the following\n> day after payment or we can send it out to you first class the following\n> day after payment and will be with you in a couple of days. You can also\n> choose from our standard service which is £12.50 and this is sent out in\n> the post in fifteen days. You can place the order online and we will call\n> you for payment or you can contact us on [phone redacted] and we can take the\n> order and payment from you.  Alternatively you can contact our head office\n> quoting the volume and the page numbers and they will do them from there\n> for you. Their contact telephone number is [phone redacted]. Or alternatively\n> you can email them on Order a birth, death, marriage or civil partnership\n> certificate - GOV.UK\n> <https://www.gov.uk/order-copy-birth-death-marriage-certificate>. I hope\n> all this information helps.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n> Karen\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *Karen Denham*\n>\n> Dirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar &\n> Nationality Officer\n>\n>\n>\n> Ebost/Email: [email redacted] / [email redacted]\n>\n> Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n> Y Swyddfa Gofrestru, Archifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg. Lecwydd,\n> Caerdydd [postcode redacted]\n>\n> The Register Office, Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith,\n> Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n>\n> www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 20 August 2026 20:34\n> *To:* [email redacted]; Registrars Office /\n> Swyddfa'r Cofrestrydd <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n>  *EXTERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take\n> care when clicking links.\n>  *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch\n> ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Register Office,\n>\n> I wish to obtain certified copies of the death certificates for the\n> following individuals:\n>\n> 1. William (Billy) Buckler\n>    - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital\n>    - Aged 41\n>    - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n>    - Likely registered in the Vale of Glamorgan / South Glamorgan district\n>\n> 2. Mary Doreen Williams\n>    - Born 10 August 1913\n>    - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n>\n> Please advise the correct office holding each entry, the application\n> process, current fees (standard and priority), payment methods, and any\n> additional information required to locate the entries accurately.\n>\n> I am happy to complete any formal application forms and provide\n> identification if needed.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n> Requester \n> \n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> The Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We\n> will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as\n> long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not\n> lead to delay.\n>\n> Privileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If\n> you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for\n> delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this\n> message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly\n> notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your\n> employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.\n> Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not\n> relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of\n> Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail\n> sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils\n> Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other\n> than the addressee.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> Mae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog.\n> Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni\n> pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n>\n> Mae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y\n> neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r\n> neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges.\n> Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy\n> e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi\n> neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon.\n> Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y\n> neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir\n> Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff\n> unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan\n> system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu\n> harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a02362b84644d27","subject":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T08:14:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a02362b84644d27.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"received","from":"Coroner Admin","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02362b84644d27.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning, Requester\nThank you for your prompt reply.\nI have checked our system for any records relating to the two cases you have asked information for.\nUnfortunately, I am unable to locate any details on the Late Mr William Buckler or the late Mary Doreen Williams.\nCardiff and Vale cases prior to 2002 should be with the Glamorgan Archivist, you can contact them on Tel; [phone redacted] or [email redacted] \nI hope this information helps and I wish you the best in your search.\nKind Regards\nBev\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 21 August 2026 08:47\nTo: Coroner Admin  \nSubject: Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\n\nBev,\n\nThank you for clarifying the position regarding the Freedom of Information Act.\n\nI understand that coroners and their records are not subject to the FOI access regime. I am therefore not seeking to pursue the matter as an FOI request if that is not the appropriate route.\n\nMy primary purpose is to establish whether either of these deaths was ever referred to the coroner and, if so, whether any surviving record exists and what lawful route is available for an interested family member to obtain information from it.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if you could clarify the following, insofar as you are able:\n\n  1.  Whether your office has any record or index indicating that either William (Billy) Buckler, who died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, or Mary Doreen Williams, whose death was registered in March 1983 in South Glamorgan (Vol. 28, p. 3029), was reported to or dealt with by the coroner;\n  2.  If either death was the subject of a coroner's investigation, whether an inquest, post-mortem examination or other coroner's investigation took place;\n  3.  Whether any historical record relating to either death remains in the custody of the coroner's service, or whether such records have been transferred to another archive, authority or successor body;\n  4.  If records exist but cannot be disclosed directly, what procedure is available for a descendant or other interested person to establish the basic factual information concerning the case;\n  5.  If your office has no record whatsoever of either death, whether that means that no coroner's record exists, or simply that the surviving records are no longer held by your office.\n\nI am particularly interested in establishing the documentary chain rather than necessarily seeking disclosure of confidential medical information. A confirmation that a death was, or was not, referred to the coroner would itself be useful.\n\nIf you are not the appropriate office to answer these historical-record questions, I would be grateful if you could identify the relevant archive, successor body or other custodian to whom I should direct the enquiry.\n\nThank you again for your assistance.\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 04:33 Coroner Admin,  > wrote:\nGood morning, Requester\nThank you for your e-mail dated 20/08/2026.\n\nAlthough appointed and paid for by local councils, the coroner is not a local government officer but holds office under the Crown.\n\nCoroners are not designated as public authorities under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and therefore their records are not subject to the information access regime of this Act.\n\nPlease let me know if I can be of further assistance.\nKind Regards\nBev Morgan\n\n\nFrom: Requester  >\nSent: 20 August 2026 20:34\nTo: Coroner Admin  >\nSubject: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\nDear Coroner’s Office,\n\nI am writing under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and as an interested person to request any records held by the South Wales Central Coroner’s Service relating to the following two deaths:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Reported cause: heart attack\n   - Funeral 5 June 1990, Bethesda Chapel, Dinas Powys; interment St Michael’s Church, Michaelston-le-Pit\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise whether either death was reported to the Coroner, whether a post-mortem or inquest was held, and what documentation (reports, police referrals, hospital communications, etc.) remains available. Please also confirm the procedure, identification required, any fees, and timescales for release to next-of-kin or interested persons.\n\nI can supply further identifying details, proof of interest, and contemporary newspaper cuttings / family notes upon request.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nCroesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at oedi. Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e. Cymraeg neu'n ddwyieithog\n\nMae'r neges ar gyfer y person / pobl enwedig yn unig. Gall gynnwys gwybodaeth bersonol, sensitif neu gyfrinachol. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi’r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopïo neu’i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych chi wedi derbyn y neges ar gam, rhowch wybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae'n bosibl y bydd holl negeseuon yn cael eu cofnodi a/neu fonitro unol â’r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol. I ddarllen yr ymwadiad llawn, ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad \n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding with us in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual\n\nThis transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain personal, sensitive or confidential material and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation For the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer \n\nCroesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at oedi.  Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e Cymraeg neu'n ddwyieithog. Mae'r neges ar gyfer y person(au) a enwyd yn unig a gall gynnwys deunydd sensitif neu ddeunydd sy wedi'i farcio hyd at 'CYFYNGEDIG' a dylid ei thrin yn unol a hynny. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi'r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopio neu'i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych wedi derbyn y neges ar gam a wnewch roi gwybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae modd cofnodi a/neu fonitro holl negeseuon GCSX yn unol a'r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol.  \nI weld yr ymwadiad llawn ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual. This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain sensitive or protectively marked material up to RESTRICTED and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a0236237188e9b4","subject":"Re: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close – Request for clarification (12 Aug)","name":"Re: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close – Request for clarification (12 Aug)","date":"2026-08-21T08:13:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0236237188e9b4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0235a6860385cb-complaint-failure-to-respond-failure-to-deal-properly-with-case-cllr-george-carroll-llandough-great-house-farm-church-vi","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0235a6860385cb","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0236237188e9b4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Davidson,\n\nI refer to my email of 12 August 2026 seeking clarification of the basis\nfor your determination that there was no evidence indicating a possible\nbreach of the Members’ Code of Conduct.\n\nI have not yet received a response. Please confirm whether a reply is still\nintended and the expected timescale.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a02361876a70fbf","subject":"Formal Governance and Integrity Notification — Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough","name":"Formal Governance and Integrity Notification — Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough","date":"2026-08-21T08:13:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a02361876a70fbf.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0235a869f9b1ef-formal-governance-and-integrity-notification-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0235a869f9b1ef","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02361876a70fbf.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Madam,\n\nI write to give formal notice of documentary evidence which, if correctly\nunderstood, raises a potentially material question concerning the\nhistorical identity, ownership and/or title to land formerly known as *Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, subsequently developed for residential\npurposes including *Church View Close*.\n\nThis correspondence is intended as a *governance and integrity notification*.\nIt is not an FOI or EIR request, nor am I asking the Council at this stage\nto accept my allegations or conclusions as established fact.\n1. The land and subsequent development\n\nThe land concerned is the former Great House Farm / Ty Mawr site at\nLlandough.\n\nThe site was subsequently developed for residential use. Planning and\nassociated administrative decisions were therefore made in circumstances in\nwhich ownership of the relevant land appears to have been treated as\nsufficiently established for those purposes.\n\nI am notifying the Council because documentary evidence now assembled\nappears to raise a material question as to whether the historical title\nposition was in fact conclusively established, and whether that question\nwas adequately identified, examined and recorded within the Council's\nadministrative and planning records.\n2. Potential title-chain discrepancy\n\nThe documentary record presently available to me indicates a historical\ndispute concerning the land involving my grandmother and the\nWilliams/Buckler family on one side and BP-related entities on the other.\n\nMy understanding of the available records is that:\n\n   - proceedings in 1974 did not result in a final judicial determination\n   conclusively establishing the underlying title in the manner subsequently\n   assumed;\n   - a further hearing listed for *31 October 1974* did not proceed\n   substantively;\n   - the land was subsequently registered in the name of BP-related\n   entities around *1982*;\n   - my grandmother died in *1983*, without, on the evidence presently\n   available to me, a final judicial determination of the underlying ownership\n   dispute or compensation resolving the family's claim;\n   - the subsequent *1987 Court of Appeal proceedings, BP Properties Ltd v\n   Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2*, did not, in my assessment, constitute a\n   comprehensive adjudication of every underlying historical title question\n   now arising from the documentary record.\n\nI emphasise that I am *not asking the Council to determine the civil title\nitself*. Rather, I am asking whether the Council has properly established\nwhat was actually determined by the courts, what remained disputed, what\ndocumentary basis was relied upon for treating title as settled, and\nwhether that distinction was properly reflected in its own records and\ndecision-making.\n\nThat distinction is important.\n3. Documentary evidence\n\nI have assembled documentary material concerning the historical title\nchain, court proceedings, registration history, conveyances and associated\nrecords, together with a chronological record of notifications and\nresponses.\n\nThe core documentary evidence can be supplied to the Council immediately.\n\nSome of the underlying material and references have also been raised in\nprevious correspondence with the Council and other public bodies. I\ntherefore request that this notification be considered alongside the\nrelevant material already held on Council files, rather than treated as an\nisolated new allegation.\n4. Authorities previously notified\n\nThe matter has previously been raised with, among others:\n\n   - the Planning Department — from 31 January 2026 and subsequently;\n   - the Council's FOI / Information Governance function, including case\n   *00210772*;\n   - Councillor George Carroll — through multiple contacts between February\n   and July 2026;\n   - Corporate Complaints / the Monitoring Officer — including\n   correspondence dated 27 July 2026 and the determination dated 12 August\n   2026;\n   - Cadw and the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments\n   of Wales (RCAHMW);\n   - other public bodies involved in the continuing documentary and\n   evidential trail.\n\nI am concerned that the substantive governance question identified above\nhas not yet been independently addressed.\n5. Matters requiring independent examination\n\nIn particular, I request that the Council establish:\n\n   1.\n\n   *Whether the historical title dispute was ever conclusively determined\n   by a competent court*, distinguishing between orders concerning\n   possession, proceedings concerning particular issues, and an actual final\n   determination of the underlying title.\n   2.\n\n   *What documentary evidence the Council historically relied upon when\n   treating ownership of the relevant land as established* for planning,\n   development, conveyancing or other administrative purposes.\n   3.\n\n   *Whether the Council's planning and administrative records contain any\n   recognition of the historical dispute*, including any consideration of\n   competing title claims or unresolved matters affecting the identity or\n   ownership of the land.\n   4.\n\n   *Whether any independent review of these issues has previously been\n   undertaken*, and if so, by whom, on what terms, and with what\n   conclusions.\n   5.\n\n   *Whether any current Council officer involved in reviewing this\n   notification has previously participated materially in the decisions,\n   complaints, correspondence or investigations now under examination*,\n   and, if so, what arrangements will be made to ensure genuine independence.\n   6.\n\n   *Whether the Council considers that any governance, record-keeping,\n   planning or public-confidence issue remains outstanding*, irrespective\n   of the ultimate determination of civil title.\n\n6. Why independent examination is warranted\n\nThe fact that the land has subsequently been developed does not, by itself,\nresolve the historical documentary question.\n\nIf the evidence demonstrates that a material title issue was overlooked,\nmisunderstood or inadequately recorded, that may have implications\nextending beyond the original ownership dispute, including the accuracy and\nintegrity of public records and the basis upon which subsequent\nadministrative decisions were made.\n\nConversely, if the Council considers that the historical record\nconclusively resolves the matter, I ask that it identify *the specific\ndocumentary and judicial basis for that conclusion*.\n\nThat is why I am requesting an independent examination rather than asking\nindividual officers who have previously dealt with the matter simply to\nreaffirm earlier positions.\n7. Formal request\n\nI therefore formally request that the Council:\n\n*a.* acknowledge this notification and identify the officer or function\nresponsible for independently reviewing it;\n\n*b.* confirm how that review will be kept independent of officers who have\npreviously dealt substantively with the matter;\n\n*c.* identify the principal Council records and documentary evidence that\nwill be considered;\n\n*d.* determine whether the historical title issue described above has\npreviously been properly examined and recorded;\n\n*e.* identify any material governance or administrative issue that remains\noutstanding; and\n\n*f.* provide a written response setting out the process to be followed and\nthe anticipated timescale.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am *not asking the Council to accept that\nfraud, unlawful dispossession or defective title has been established*. I\nam notifying the Council that documentary evidence appears to raise a\npotentially material question concerning the historical identity and/or\ntitle to land upon which subsequent development took place, and I am asking\nthe Council to establish whether that question has ever been properly\nexamined.\n\nIf the Council considers that determination of the underlying civil title\nfalls outside its functions, I would nevertheless ask it to address the\nseparate governance question: *whether its own historical records and\ndecision-making properly identified and dealt with the title issue on the\nevidence available to it.*\n\nThis is a *formal governance and integrity notification*, not an FOI or EIR\nrequest.\n\nI would be grateful for written acknowledgement and confirmation of the\nprocess and timescale for an independent determination.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n*Requester *\n\nLife Member"},{"id":"gm-1a0236015e69de3d","subject":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"RE: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T08:11:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0236015e69de3d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"received","from":"Denham, Karen (Registrars)","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0236015e69de3d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi Requester\nThank you for your email regarding William Buckler and Mary Doreen Williams death certificates. I have done a search in our indexes and I can confirm that we hold the record for William Buckler but unfortunately I cannot locate the death entry for Mary Doreen Williams. If you would like to purchase the certificate of William Buckler with us then you can either pay £38.50 and you can come and collect it from our office the following day after payment or we can send it out to you first class the following day after payment and will be with you in a couple of days. You can also choose from our standard service which is £12.50 and this is sent out in the post in fifteen days. You can place the order online and we will call you for payment or you can contact us on [phone redacted] and we can take the order and payment from you.  Alternatively you can contact our head office quoting the volume and the page numbers and they will do them from there for you. Their contact telephone number is [phone redacted]. Or alternatively you can email them on Order a birth, death, marriage or civil partnership certificate - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/order-copy-birth-death-marriage-certificate>. I hope all this information helps.\n\nKind Regards\nKaren\n\n\nKaren Denham\nDirprwy Gofrestrydd a Swyddog Dinasyddiaeth / Deputy Registrar & Nationality Officer\n\nEbost/Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> / [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nFfon/Tel: [phone redacted]\nY Swyddfa Gofrestru, Archifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg. Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted]\nThe Register Office, Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\nwww.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk<http://www.cardiffregisteroffice.co.uk/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 August 2026 20:34\nTo: [email redacted]; Registrars Office / Swyddfa'r Cofrestrydd <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\nDear Register Office,\n\nI wish to obtain certified copies of the death certificates for the following individuals:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital\n   - Aged 41\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Likely registered in the Vale of Glamorgan / South Glamorgan district\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise the correct office holding each entry, the application process, current fees (standard and priority), payment methods, and any additional information required to locate the entries accurately.\n\nI am happy to complete any formal application forms and provide identification if needed.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. W