yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg. Ni fydd gohebu gyda ni yn y Gymraeg yn achosi oedi.\n\nI’m not able to understand Welsh. However NWSSP welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English. We welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding with us in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\n\n\nMae’r neges hon yn gyfrinachol. Os nad chi yw’r derbynnydd y bwriedid y neges a rei gyfer, rhowch wybod I’r anfonwr yn ddioed. Dylid ystyried unrhyw ddatganiadau neu sylwadau a wneir uchod yn rhai personol, ac nid o angenrhaid yn rhai o eiddo Partneriaeth Cydwasanaethau GIG Cymru, nac unrhyw ran gyfansoddol ohoni na chorff cysylltiedig.\n\nThis message is confidential. If you are not the intended recipient of the message then please notify the sender immediately. Any of the statements or comments made above should be regarded as personal and not necessarily those of the NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership any constituent part or connected body.\n\n\n\nCofiwch fod yn ymwybodol ei bod yn bosibl y bydd disgwyl Partneriaeth Cydwasanaethau GIG Cymru roi cyhoeddusrwydd I gynnwys unrhyw e-bost neu ohebiaeth a dderbynnir, yn inol ag amodau’r Ddeddf Rhyddid Gwybodaeth 2000.\n\nPlease be aware that, under the terms of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership may be required to make public the content of any emails or correspondence received.\n\n[cid:303e049b-f298-4540-bc6e-92c0aa914ae0][cid:e8b9a5d1-5774-4a76-8b69-8e6903a12f07] [cid:6cd3059a-3f58-4d97-8934-55a051078076]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 21 August 2026 08:44\nTo: SouthWalesCentral MedicalExaminersOffice (Gen126594) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\nWARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening attachments.\n\n\nMichelle,\n\nThanks for your prompt response.\n\nI'd like to request an internal review of the handling of my enquiry and, insofar as it constitutes a Freedom of Information request, of the conclusion that no relevant records are held.\n\nI am not challenging the conclusion simply because it is inconvenient to my enquiry. Rather, I would like to establish whether an adequate search was undertaken before the conclusion was reached.\n\nYour latest response states that the Medical Examiner Service would not hold “any records whatsoever” or have “any knowledge” of these patients. Given that the deaths occurred in 1983 and 1990, before the establishment of the current Medical Examiner Service, I would be grateful if the internal review could specifically establish whether the search extended beyond current Medical Examiner records to any relevant predecessor, legacy or transferred records.\n\nIn particular, could the review please confirm:\n\n  1.  What records and information systems were searched;\n\n  2.  Whether any legacy or predecessor records relating to the medical examination or certification of deaths were considered;\n\n  3.  Whether records relating to Llandough Hospital, where William Buckler is recorded as having died in approximately May 1990, are held by the Medical Examiner Service, NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership, another NHS body, or an archive to which you have access or knowledge;\n\n  4.  Whether any records concerning referrals to a coroner, inquests, post-mortems or other investigations into these deaths would have been held separately from Medical Examiner records;\n\n  5.  Whether the possibility of records having been transferred to an archive or successor organisation was considered;\n\n  6.  Whether the statement that no records are held means that no relevant records are held by the South Wales Central Medical Examiner Service specifically, or that searches have established that no such records are held anywhere within NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership; and\n\n  7.  If the records are not held by your organisation, whether you can identify the appropriate current custodian or archive for any surviving historical records.\n\nFor clarity, the individuals concerned are:\n\n  *   William (Billy) Buckler – died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41; and\n  *   Mary Doreen Williams – born 10 August 1913; death registered in March 1983, South Glamorgan, Vol. 28, p. 3029.\n\nI would be grateful if this could be treated as a formal internal review rather than simply a further general enquiry.\n\nI would also ask that the review be undertaken by someone who was not responsible for the original response, where practicable.\n\nMy purpose is to establish a reliable documentary record and, in particular, to distinguish between:\n\n(a) records which do not exist;\n\n(b) records which once existed but have been destroyed;\n\n(c) records which exist but are held by another organisation; and\n\n(d) records which are held within NHS Wales or a predecessor organisation but were not identified by the original search.\n\nI would be grateful for confirmation of the review and, where applicable, the relevant FOI reference number.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 04:33 SouthWalesCentral MedicalExaminersOffice (Gen126594), <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nGood morning\n\nWe would not hold any records whatsoever or have any knowledge of these patients.\n\nMany thanks\n\nMichelle\n\n\n\n\n\nSwyddfa Ganolog De Cymru South Wales Central Office\n\nGwasanaeth Archwilio Meddygol Cymru Gyfan  All Wales Medical Examiners Service\n\nPartneriaeth Cydwasanaethau GIG Cymru  NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership\n\nFfon Telephone:  [phone redacted]\n\nE-bost  Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nGwefan Website:  https://nwssp.nhs.wales/ourservices/medical-examiner-service/\n\n\n\nMae Partneriaeth Cydwasanaethau GIG Cymru yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg.\n\nNHS Wales Shared Services welcomes correspondence in Welsh.\n\nDw