If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a02349abab2e950","subject":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Re: FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-21T07:47:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a02349abab2e950.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02349abab2e950.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Bev,\n\nThank you for clarifying the position regarding the Freedom of Information\nAct.\n\nI understand that coroners and their records are not subject to the FOI\naccess regime. I am therefore not seeking to pursue the matter as an FOI\nrequest if that is not the appropriate route.\n\nMy primary purpose is to establish whether either of these deaths was ever\nreferred to the coroner and, if so, whether any surviving record exists and\nwhat lawful route is available for an interested family member to obtain\ninformation from it.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if you could clarify the following, insofar\nas you are able:\n\n   1.\n\n   Whether your office has any record or index indicating that either\n   William (Billy) Buckler, who died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May\n   1990, or Mary Doreen Williams, whose death was registered in March 1983 in\n   South Glamorgan (Vol. 28, p. 3029), was reported to or dealt with by the\n   coroner;\n   2.\n\n   If either death was the subject of a coroner's investigation, whether an\n   inquest, post-mortem examination or other coroner's investigation took\n   place;\n   3.\n\n   Whether any historical record relating to either death remains in the\n   custody of the coroner's service, or whether such records have been\n   transferred to another archive, authority or successor body;\n   4.\n\n   If records exist but cannot be disclosed directly, what procedure is\n   available for a descendant or other interested person to establish the\n   basic factual information concerning the case;\n   5.\n\n   If your office has no record whatsoever of either death, whether that\n   means that no coroner's record exists, or simply that the surviving records\n   are no longer held by your office.\n\nI am particularly interested in establishing the documentary chain rather\nthan necessarily seeking disclosure of confidential medical information. A\nconfirmation that a death was, or was not, referred to the coroner would\nitself be useful.\n\nIf you are not the appropriate office to answer these historical-record\nquestions, I would be grateful if you could identify the relevant archive,\nsuccessor body or other custodian to whom I should direct the enquiry.\n\nThank you again for your assistance.\n\nRegards,\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 04:33 Coroner Admin, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Good morning, Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your e-mail dated 20/08/2026.\n>\n>\n>\n> Although appointed and paid for by local councils, the coroner is not a\n> local government officer but holds office under the Crown.\n>\n>\n>\n> Coroners are not designated as public authorities under the Freedom of\n> Information Act 2000 and therefore their records are not subject to the\n> information access regime of this Act.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please let me know if I can be of further assistance.\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n> Bev Morgan\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 20 August 2026 20:34\n> *To:* Coroner Admin <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler\n> (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Coroner’s Office,\n>\n> I am writing under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and as an\n> interested person to request any records held by the South Wales Central\n> Coroner’s Service relating to the following two deaths:\n>\n> 1. William (Billy) Buckler\n>    - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n>    - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n>    - Reported cause: heart attack\n>    - Funeral 5 June 1990, Bethesda Chapel, Dinas Powys; interment St\n> Michael’s Church, Michaelston-le-Pit\n>\n> 2. Mary Doreen Williams\n>    - Born 10 August 1913\n>    - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n>\n> Please advise whether either death was reported to the Coroner, whether a\n> post-mortem or inquest was held, and what documentation (reports, police\n> referrals, hospital communications, etc.) remains available. Please also\n> confirm the procedure, identification required, any fees, and timescales\n> for release to next-of-kin or interested persons.\n>\n> I can supply further identifying details, proof of interest, and\n> contemporary newspaper cuttings / family notes upon request.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n> Requester \n> \n>\n>\n> Croesawn ohebu yn Gymraeg a fydd gohebu yn y Gymraeg ddim yn arwain at\n> oedi. Rhowch wybod inni beth yw'ch dewis iaith e.e. C