-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["nhs-cav"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nhs-cav"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016607283cece4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nhs-cav","name":"Cardiff and Vale University Health Board"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a02347a33c4f856.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Michelle,\n\nThanks for your prompt response.\n\nI'd like to request an internal review of the handling of my enquiry and,\ninsofar as it constitutes a Freedom of Information request, of the\nconclusion that no relevant records are held.\n\nI am not challenging the conclusion simply because it is inconvenient to my\nenquiry. Rather, I would like to establish whether an adequate search was\nundertaken before the conclusion was reached.\n\nYour latest response states that the Medical Examiner Service would not\nhold “any records whatsoever” or have “any knowledge” of these patients.\nGiven that the deaths occurred in 1983 and 1990, before the establishment\nof the current Medical Examiner Service, I would be grateful if the\ninternal review could specifically establish whether the search extended\nbeyond current Medical Examiner records to any relevant predecessor, legacy\nor transferred records.\n\nIn particular, could the review please confirm:\n\n   1.\n\n   What records and information systems were searched;\n   2.\n\n   Whether any legacy or predecessor records relating to the medical\n   examination or certification of deaths were considered;\n   3.\n\n   Whether records relating to Llandough Hospital, where William Buckler is\n   recorded as having died in approximately May 1990, are held by the Medical\n   Examiner Service, NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership, another NHS body,\n   or an archive to which you have access or knowledge;\n   4.\n\n   Whether any records concerning referrals to a coroner, inquests,\n   post-mortems or other investigations into these deaths would have been held\n   separately from Medical Examiner records;\n   5.\n\n   Whether the possibility of records having been transferred to an archive\n   or successor organisation was considered;\n   6.\n\n   Whether the statement that no records are held means that no relevant\n   records are held by the South Wales Central Medical Examiner Service\n   specifically, or that searches have established that no such records are\n   held anywhere within NHS Wales Shared Services Partnership; and\n   7.\n\n   If the records are not held by your organisation, whether you can\n   identify the appropriate current custodian or archive for any surviving\n   historical records.\n\nFor clarity, the individuals concerned are:\n\n   - William (Billy) Buckler – died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29\n   May 1990, aged 41; and\n   - Mary Doreen Williams – born 10 August 1913; death registered in March\n   1983, South Glamorgan, Vol. 28, p. 3029.\n\nI would be grateful if this could be treated as a formal internal review\nrather than simply a further general enquiry.\n\nI would also ask that the review be undertaken by someone who was not\nresponsible for the original response, where practicable.\n\nMy purpose is to establish a reliable documentary record and, in\nparticular, to distinguish between:\n\n(a) records which do not exist;\n\n(b) records which once existed but have been destroyed;\n\n(c) records which exist but are held by another organisation; and\n\n(d) records which are held within NHS Wales or a predecessor organisation\nbut were not identified by the original search.\n\nI would be grateful for confirmation of the review and, where applicable,\nthe relevant FOI reference number.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 04:33 SouthWalesCentral MedicalExaminersOffice\n(Gen1