ffice (Gen126594)  \nSubject: Re: Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important \nWARNING: External email – take care before clicking links or opening attachments.\n\n\nDear Michelle,\n\nThank you for your prompt response and for clarifying that the South Wales Central Medical Examiner Service does not hold records dating back to these deaths.\n\nI appreciate your advice regarding the registrars' offices. I will follow that route.\n\nFor completeness, could you please clarify whether, in addition to the registration records, you would expect any historical records relating to these deaths — for example, medical certificates of cause of death, coroner's referrals or inquest records, or archived hospital records — to be held by another NHS body, the coroner's service, or an archive rather than the registrars?\n\nIn particular, I am trying to establish the documentary trail surrounding:\n\n  *   William (Billy) Buckler, who died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990; and\n  *   Mary Doreen Williams, whose death was registered in March 1983 in South Glamorgan (Vol. 28, p. 3029).\n\nI understand that the Medical Examiner Service itself did not exist at the time, so I am simply trying to identify the correct historical custodian of any surviving records.\n\nThank you again for pointing me in the right direction.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nRequester\n\n\n\nOn Fri, 21 Aug 2026, 03:55 SouthWalesCentral MedicalExaminersOffice (Gen126594),  > wrote:\nGood morning\n\nThank you for your email\n\nUnfortunately, we do not hold ay records dating back this far and Data Protection would not allow us to release these either if they were held.\n\nYou would therefore need to contact the registrars office in Cardiff and the Vale of Glamorgan who may be able to assist you further.\n\nKind regards\n\nMichelle\n\n\nMicehlle Burnett\nMES Operations Support Officer