nol a hynny. Os nad chi yw'r person a enwyd (neu os nad oes gyda chi'r awdurdod i'w derbyn ar ran y person a enwyd) chewch chi ddim ei chopio neu'i defnyddio, neu'i datgelu i berson arall. Os ydych wedi derbyn y neges ar gam a wnewch roi gwybod i'r sawl sy wedi anfon y neges ar unwaith. Mae modd cofnodi a/neu fonitro holl negeseuon GCSX yn unol a'r ddeddfwriaeth berthnasol.  \nI weld yr ymwadiad llawn ewch i http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/ymwadiad\n\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay. Let us know your language choice if Welsh or bilingual. This transmission is intended for the named addressee(s) only and may contain sensitive or protectively marked material up to RESTRICTED and should be handled accordingly. Unless you are the named addressee (or authorised to receive it for the addressee) you may not copy or use it, or disclose it to anyone else. If you have received this transmission in error please notify the sender immediately. All traffic including GCSx may be subject to recording and/or monitoring in accordance with relevant legislation.\nFor the full disclaimer please access http://www.rctcbc.gov.uk/disclaimer"},{"id":"gm-1a020aafa05a15da","subject":"Automatic reply: Freedom of Information Request – Records relating to the deaths of William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Automatic reply: Freedom of Information Request – Records relating to the deaths of William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:34:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aafa05a15da.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a020aafa05a15da-automatic-reply-freedom-of-information-request-records-relating-to-the-deaths-of-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-wi","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a020aafa05a15da","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aafa05a15da.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-1a020aae35f6979f","subject":"FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"FOI / Records Request – Deaths of William (Billy) Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:34:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aae35f6979f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d-foi-records-request-deaths-of-william-billy-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["rct"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rct"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165faa913f91d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rct","name":"Coroner's Service (RCT Council)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aae35f6979f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Coroner’s Office,\n\nI am writing under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and as an interested\nperson to request any records held by the South Wales Central Coroner’s\nService relating to the following two deaths:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Reported cause: heart attack\n   - Funeral 5 June 1990, Bethesda Chapel, Dinas Powys; interment St\nMichael’s Church, Michaelston-le-Pit\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise whether either death was reported to the Coroner, whether a\npost-mortem or inquest was held, and what documentation (reports, police\nreferrals, hospital communications, etc.) remains available. Please also\nconfirm the procedure, identification required, any fees, and timescales\nfor release to next-of-kin or interested persons.\n\nI can supply further identifying details, proof of interest, and\ncontemporary newspaper cuttings / family notes upon request.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a020aac15169bb2","subject":"Access to Deceased Health Records / FOI Request – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Access to Deceased Health Records / FOI Request – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:34:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aac15169bb2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165fcfe194d80-access-to-deceased-health-records-foi-request-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["nhs-cav"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nhs-cav"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165fcfe194d80","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nhs-cav","name":"Cardiff and Vale University Health Board"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aac15169bb2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Health Records Manager,\n\nI am writing to request access to any health records held by Cardiff and\nVale University Health Board (including Llandough Hospital) relating to the\nfollowing deceased persons, under the Access to Health Records Act 1990\nand/or the Freedom of Information Act 2000 where applicable:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Reported cause of death: heart attack\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise what records remain available, the correct application\nprocess for deceased patients’ records, any forms or identification\nrequired, applicable fees, and expected timescales. I am happy to provide\nfurther details and proof of relationship/interest as needed.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a020aaa1787776d","subject":"Freedom of Information Request – Records relating to the deaths of William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Freedom of Information Request – Records relating to the deaths of William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:34:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aaa1787776d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0165feee8e5161-freedom-of-information-request-records-relating-to-the-deaths-of-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0165feee8e5161","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aaa1787776d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Freedom of Information Team,\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request any recorded\ninformation held by South Wales Police relating to the deaths of the\nfollowing individuals:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Reported cause: heart attack\n   - Contemporary newspaper reports refer to the circumstances of his death\nand prior eviction proceedings involving BP Properties.\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease search for any incident reports, sudden-death reports, referrals to\nthe Coroner, statements, or other relevant documentation. If the cost limit\nwould be exceeded, please advise which elements can be provided within the\nlimit or how the request can be refined.\n\nI am happy to provide further identifying details if required.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a020aa7634d2f36","subject":"Request for burial / parish register entries – William Buckler (1990) and related records (Mary Doreen Williams)","name":"Request for burial / parish register entries – William Buckler (1990) and related records (Mary Doreen Williams)","date":"2026-08-20T19:33:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aa7634d2f36.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016600b59eb32a-quest-for-burial-parish-register-entries-william-buckler-1990-and-related-records-mary-doreen-williams","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016600b59eb32a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aa7634d2f36.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Glamorgan Archives,\n\nI am researching the deaths and burial arrangements of the following\nindividuals and would be grateful for any assistance with parish / burial\nregisters or related records in your custody:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital, aged 41\n   - Interred at St Michael’s Church, Michaelston-le-Pit (funeral service\nat Bethesda Chapel, Dinas Powys on 5 June 1990)\n   - Contemporary reports confirm burial at St Michael’s rather than the\nfamily resting place at Llandough.\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n   - Any burial or related parish entries that may connect her to the\nLlandough / Michaelston / Dinas Powys area or the Buckler family would be\nof interest.\n\nPlease advise what registers or indexes are held for St Michael’s,\nMichaelston-le-Pit and nearby parishes for the relevant periods, the\nprocedure for obtaining copies or transcripts, any research service fees,\nand how best to proceed.\n\nThank you for your help.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a020aa597cd85af","subject":"Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Application for copy death certificates – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:33:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aa597cd85af.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016601f861000b-application-for-copy-death-certificates-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["cardiff-reg"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff-reg"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016601f861000b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cardiff-reg","name":"Cardiff / Vale Register Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aa597cd85af.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Register Office,\n\nI wish to obtain certified copies of the death certificates for the\nfollowing individuals:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died on or about 29 May 1990 at Llandough Hospital\n   - Aged 41\n   - Late of Great House Farm, Llandough\n   - Likely registered in the Vale of Glamorgan / South Glamorgan district\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nPlease advise the correct office holding each entry, the application\nprocess, current fees (standard and priority), payment methods, and any\nadditional information required to locate the entries accurately.\n\nI am happy to complete any formal application forms and provide\nidentification if needed.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a020aa32bfe4b8e","subject":"Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","name":"Enquiry regarding historical deaths – William Buckler (1990) and Mary Doreen Williams (1983)","date":"2026-08-20T19:33:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a020aa32bfe4b8e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a016607283cece4-enquiry-regarding-historical-deaths-william-buckler-1990-and-mary-doreen-williams-1983","scopeTopics":["nhs-cav"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nhs-cav"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a016607283cece4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nhs-cav","name":"Cardiff and Vale University Health Board"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a020aa32bfe4b8e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Medical Examiner Service (South Wales Central),\n\nI am writing to enquire whether any records or references are held in\nrelation to the following historical deaths that occurred in the Cardiff &\nVale / Llandough area:\n\n1. William (Billy) Buckler\n   - Died at Llandough Hospital on or about 29 May 1990, aged 41\n   - Reported cause: heart attack\n\n2. Mary Doreen Williams\n   - Born 10 August 1913\n   - Death registered March 1983, South Glamorgan (Vol 28, Page 3029)\n\nAlthough these pre-date the current Medical Examiner Service, I would be\ngrateful if you could advise whether any legacy records, referrals, or\nrelated documentation exist, or direct me to the appropriate archive or\ndepartment that may hold such information.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a01f6ea24d7be5f","subject":"Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 CRM:007302424","name":"Freedom of Information Request: Reference CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 CRM:007302424","date":"2026-08-20T13:47:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a01f6ea24d7be5f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a01f6ea24d7be5f-freedom-of-information-request-reference-cas-347296-m0v4y1-crm-007302424","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a01f6ea24d7be5f","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-347296"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a01f6ea24d7be5f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nThank you for your enquiry of 13/08/2026 regarding a review of:\n\n\n\nWe are handling your request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\n\n\nFrom our initial assessment it is clear that we will not be able to answer your request without further clarification. Under section 1(3) of the Act, a public authority need not comply with a request unless any further information reasonably required to locate the information is supplied.\n\n\n\nIn order to progress your request, we require clarification on the scope of your request.\n\n\n\nThe FOI Centre has received a request for the following:\n\n\n\nMy request was deliberately framed more broadly than a simple catalogue search for the words “Great House Farm”, “Ty Mawr”, “Llandough” or “Cedfin”. I specifically asked The National Archives to identify recorded information concerning the existence, transfer, retention, destruction, disposal or absence of records, including records that might not be catalogued under the property's later or local names.\n\n\n\nYour response confirms only that you searched the PRO and RW series using:\n\n\n\n“Great House Farm” OR “Ty Mawr” OR Llandough OR Cedfin\n\n\n\ncombined with “Glamorgan”, and that this produced no catalogue results.\n\n\n\nYou also correctly state that Discovery searches catalogue titles and descriptions rather than the contents of records. That qualification is important, because it means the search described cannot establish that relevant records did not exist, were never transferred, or were destroyed.\n\n\n\nIn particular, your response does not appear to address the other categories expressly identified in my request, including searches or recorded information relating to:\n\n\n\n  *   Western Ground Rents Ltd;\n\n  *   BP Pension Trust Ltd;\n\n  *   BP Properties Ltd;\n\n  *   Mountjoy Ltd;\n\n  *   the proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2;\n\n  *   the 1982–1983 registration and associated government or administrative records;\n\n  *   the 1980–1988 public campaign and governmental correspondence;\n\n  *   the 1988 eviction and demolition;\n\n  *   Cadw or central-government communications concerning the property;\n\n  *   European Commission of Human Rights Application 14464/88;\n\n  *   records concerning transfer, destruction or disposal of potentially relevant material; and\n\n  *   HMC9/311 or related archival references.\n\n\n\nThese alternative lines of enquiry are intentional. The purpose is to establish whether relevant information can be identified through the government bodies, corporate entities, court proceedings, administrative processes and archival transfers associated with the property, rather than relying solely upon the modern name by which the property is known.\n\n\n\nI am conducting corresponding enquiries with other repositories and public bodies. This is specifically intended to triangulate the documentary history where records may have been catalogued under a different creator, department, legal proceeding, estate, corporate body or administrative function.\n\n\n\nI therefore ask that you do not treat the absence of a Discovery keyword hit as an answer to the substantive questions raised.\n\n\n\nPlease clarify:\n\n\n\n  1.  Whether the searches undertaken were limited to the PRO and RW catalogue series and the four property/location search terms identified in your email.\n\n\n\n  1.  Whether The National Archives searched for the named corporate bodies, court proceedings and application references identified in my request, rather than only searching the property names.\n\n\n\n  1.  Whether The National Archives holds any recorded transfer, accession, disposal, destruction or retention information indicating that records concerning the relevant property, estate, companies, litigation or government involvement were transferred elsewhere, destroyed, or otherwise disposed of.\n\n\n\n  1.  If such information is not held, whether this is because no such records are held, because no relevant records were ever transferred to TNA, or because TNA's catalogue/search systems contain no discoverable description of them.\n\n\n\n  1.  Whether HMC9/311 or related series have been checked, or whether that reference falls outside the search undertaken.\n\n\n\n  1.  Whether there are central-government, court, departmental or administrative records relating to the litigation and entities identified above which may contain references to the property without using “Great House Farm”, “Ty Mawr”, “Llandough” or “Cedfin” in the catalogue description.\n\n\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am not asking The National Archives to infer the contents of uncatalogued records or to undertake an unlimited research project. I am asking for confirmation of the recorded information held by TNA concerning the existence, provenance, transfer, retention, destruction or disposal of potentially relevant records, and for the searches undertaken to locate that information.\n\n\n\nThat distinction is particularly important because a catalogue search returning no result is not equivalent to a finding that no relevant historical, governmental or archival records existed.\n\n\n\nI would therefore be grateful if this could be reconsidered as a response to the scope of the original FOI enquiry rather than treated solely as a request for assistance with a Discovery keyword search.\n\n\n\nI am continuing parallel enquiries with the National Library of Wales, Glamorgan Archives, Cadw, RCAHMW, HM Land Registry and other relevant bodies. The purpose of these enquiries is to establish the documentary chain independently and to identify where records were created, transferred, retained or potentially destroyed.\n\n\n\nAn acknowledgment email was sent on 17/08/2026, informing you we are handling your request under the FOI Act and that the request has been given a reference number: CAS-347296-M0V4Y1.\n\n\n\nToday (20/08/2026) we have received the following:\n\n\n\nI wrote to you on 12 August 2026 with a follow-up refining my earlier enquiry concerning National Farm Survey / MAFF records relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan (Williams / Buckler family interest).\n\n\n\nI have not yet received a substantive reply to that follow-up and would be grateful for an update on progress and the expected timescale for a full response.\n\n\n\nIn addition, please expand the scope of the search to include any records held relating to the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (“War Ag” / CWAEC) and Great House Farm / the relevant land at Llandough, covering approximately 1936–1950 (with particular focus on 1939–1945). This should include, where held:\n\nAny orders, notices or decisions taking possession of, directing cultivation of, or otherwise requisitioning land forming part of Great House Farm (or the specific parcel now associated with Llandough Motor Sales / Llandough Trading Estate).\n\n\n\nAny compensation claims, assessments, payments or settlements under the Compensation (Defence) Act 1939 or related wartime legislation, including the identity of the recipient(s).\n\n\n\nRelevant minutes, correspondence or case files of the Glamorgan CWAEC concerning the farm or land in question.\n\n\n\nAny related material in the MAF series that links the National Farm Survey entries with wartime agricultural possession or compensation.\n\n\n\nI hold original documents recording compensation payments in connection with this land and am seeking to identify the wartime status of the holding and the party recognised as entitled to compensation.\n\n\n\nPlease link this expanded request to the existing case reference CAS-344046-K1S1R2 so that the searches can be coordinated.\n\n\n\nPlease can you clarify if the above (received on 20/08/2026) should be treated as clarification on the scope of your FOI request referenced CAS-347296 or a separate research enquiry about the collection.\n\n\n\nPlease provide as much information possible as this will assist us in providing a more guided response and possibly assist you in getting the information you require.\n\n\n\nPlease send your clarification by reply this email, or by contacting:\n\n\n\nFOI Centre\nThe National Archives\nKew\nRichmond\nSurrey\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n\n\nWe have now placed your request on hold until we receive clarification from you. Please quote the reference number CAS-347296-M0V4Y1 in all correspondence.\n\n\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with the handling of your request or the decision which has been reached, you have the right to ask for an internal review. Internal review requests must be submitted within two months of the date of this response and should be addressed to:\n\n\n\nQuality Manager\nThe National Archives\nKew\nRichmond\nSurrey\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nPlease mark your complaint clearly. You have the right to ask the Information Commissioner to investigate any aspect of your complaint. However, please note that the Information Commissioner is likely to expect internal complaints procedures to have been exhausted before beginning his investigation.\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\n\n\nFOI Assessor\nFreedom of Information Centre\n\nThe National Archives\n\n\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-1a01e48dc17d6fe1","subject":"Case reference: CAS-344046-K1S1R2","name":"Case reference: CAS-344046-K1S1R2","date":"2026-08-20T08:28:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a01e48dc17d6fe1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a01e3fccbc7ca9a-case-reference-cas-344046-k1s1r2","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a01e3fccbc7ca9a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-344046"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a01e48dc17d6fe1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Records Enquiries Team,\n\nCase reference: CAS-344046-K1S1R2\nI wrote to you on 12 August 2026 with a follow-up refining my earlier\nenquiry concerning National Farm Survey / MAFF records relating to Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan (Williams / Buckler\nfamily interest).\n\nI have not yet received a substantive reply to that follow-up and would be\ngrateful for an update on progress and the expected timescale for a full\nresponse.\n\nIn addition, please expand the scope of the search to include any records\nheld relating to the Glamorgan War Agricultural Executive Committee (“War\nAg” / CWAEC) and Great House Farm / the relevant land at Llandough,\ncovering approximately 1936–1950 (with particular focus on 1939–1945). This\nshould include, where held:\nAny orders, notices or decisions taking possession of, directing\ncultivation of, or otherwise requisitioning land forming part of Great\nHouse Farm (or the specific parcel now associated with Llandough Motor\nSales / Llandough Trading Estate).\n\nAny compensation claims, assessments, payments or settlements under the\nCompensation (Defence) Act 1939 or related wartime legislation, including\nthe identity of the recipient(s).\n\nRelevant minutes, correspondence or case files of the Glamorgan CWAEC\nconcerning the farm or land in question.\n\nAny related material in the MAF series that links the National Farm Survey\nentries with wartime agricultural possession or compensation.\n\nI hold original documents recording compensation payments in connection\nwith this land and am seeking to identify the wartime status of the holding\nand the party recognised as entitled to compensation.\n\nPlease link this expanded request to the existing case reference\nCAS-344046-K1S1R2 so that the searches can be coordinated.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to your reply.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-1a01e2dfd62ab056","subject":"RE: Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-08-20T07:58:38Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a01e2dfd62ab056.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa5759a198dbff-complaint-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa5759a198dbff","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a01e2dfd62ab056.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning Requester\n\nThank you for your email below and for the additional information provided.\nWe have now made further enquiries on your behalf and will be in touch once a full response has been received.\n\nKind regards,\n\n[cid:image002.jpg@01DD3082.20159530]\nOffice of Stephen Doughty MP / AS\nLabour and Co-operative Member of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth\nLlafur a Cydweithredol Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nWestminster / San Steffan | [phone redacted] | House of Commons, London, [postcode redacted]\nEmail / E-bost                      | [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nWebsite / Gwefan                | www.stephendoughty.wales<http://www.stephendoughty.wales/>\n\nFor information about how we use your personal data, see our Privacy Notice<https://www.stephendoughty.wales/privacynotice>.\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 05 August 2026 12:52\nTo: DOUGHTY, Stephen <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nThis is brilliant we are now in communications.\n\nYour theory maybe correct.\n\nDo you see the attached?\n\nI believe I have discovered fraud and consealment in information the court relied on for the ruling in landmark legal case BP vs Buckler 1987. My fathers and families case.\n\nI am preparing my evidence for legal ajudication. I believe in 1983 the land registry made a mistake by excluding our claim to what is now Church View Close, Llandough. Partly due to information being witheld/ concealed from them.\n\nMore details in the attached documents. I believe this is a matter of public interest.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\n\nOn Wed, 5 Aug 2026, 08:20 DOUGHTY, Stephen, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email of July 27. We are sorry that you have not received a reply to your earlier emails – we have searched our systems, and despite you receiving auto-replies as mentioned, we haven’t been able to find any of the messages you sent on the dates listed below. Were there large or multiple attachments perhaps? Sometimes this can prevent messages from coming through to us.\nIn order to assess whether we can assist, could you please send a summary outline of your case/concerns - to make sure this gets through - and then follow up with any supporting information?\n\nKind regards\n\nOffice of Stephen Doughty MP\n\n[cid:image003.jpg@01DD3082.20159530]\nOffice of Stephen Doughty MP\nLabour and Co-operative Member of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth\nTel: [phone redacted] | Address: House of Commons, London, [postcode redacted]\nEmail             | [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nWebsite         | www.stephendoughty.wales<http://www.stephendoughty.wales>\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 27 July 2026 22:27\nTo: DOUGHTY, Stephen <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nStephen Doughty MP,\n\nWith great regret I am writing to lodge a formal complaint about the failure of your office to provide any substantive response to my repeated correspondence concerning historic land, planning, enforcement, heritage and related public-interest matters at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (now Church View Close).\n\nI am a constituent (address below) with a legitimate and long-standing family interest in the site. The issues raised include alleged defective notices, loss of opportunity to contest enforcement leading to demolition in 1988, heritage/regulatory oversight, planning and title records, and related transparency failures.\n\nDespite multiple contacts, I have received only automated acknowledgements and no substantive reply.\n\n### Full correspondence log with your office ([email redacted]<[email redacted]>)\n\n| Date       | Subject / Key content                                                                 | Response received          |\n|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|\n| 29 May 2026 | Formal disclosure notice & litigation hold / FOIA-EIR style request on historic significance, planning and displaced family records | Automated acknowledgement only |\n\n| 31 May 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying address and further detail                              | None substantive           |\n\n| 12 Jun 2026 | “Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)” – detailed personal/historical letter with attachments | Automated acknowledgement only |\n\n| 12 Jun 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying full name, address and contact details                  | None substantive           |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | Complaint of maladministration (defective notice, enforcement process, loss of opportunity) copied to you | Automated acknowledgement only |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying full personal details and references                    | None substantive           |\n\n| 13 Jul 2026 | Follow-up on previous emails regarding historical records, council involvement and transparency; request for update and confirmation of review | None                       |\n\n### What I am asking for\n\n1. A full written response addressing the points raised in the logged emails.\n2. Confirmation whether your office has reviewed the matter and what, if any, assistance or representation you are able to offer.\n\n3. A clear reply within **14 days** of the date of this email.\n\nI have retained the full original emails and attachments and can supply them on request. Please acknowledge receipt of this formal complaint.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted][map link redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[phone redacted]\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data.\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-1a01defc69b6c0b4","subject":"Re: Reading Room request","name":"Re: Reading Room request","date":"2026-08-20T06:50:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a01defc69b6c0b4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0073ad95b3bb32-ading-room-request","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-1a0073ad95b3bb32","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a01defc69b6c0b4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Bethany,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI understand that the BP Archive contains material up to the end of 1954,\nbut that post-1954 material is currently unavailable for external access.\nMy original enquiry did include the later BP acquisition, litigation and\nregistration records, so I understand that those parts of my request cannot\ncurrently be accessed.\n\nI would therefore like to clarify what *pre-1955 material concerning Great\nHouse Farm / Ty Mawr* is held within the accessible BP Archive.\n\nThe reason this is particularly relevant is that Great House Farm was\nsubsequently acquired by *BP Pension Trust Ltd from Western Ground Rents in\n1969*, and became the subject of *BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA\nCiv 2*. I am researching the underlying root of title and the history of\nthe family's occupation before *2 February 1955*, which is a critical date\nin the subsequent dispute.\n\nCould you please search the pre-1955 BP Archive holdings for Great House\nFarm / Ty Mawr, Llandough, including references under:\n\n   - Great House Farm / Great House / Ty Mawr\n   - Llandough\n   - Western Ground Rents Ltd\n   - Mountjoy Ltd\n   - Bute Estate / Llandough Estate\n   - Williams\n   - Buckler\n\nIn particular, I am looking for any surviving copies or references to:\n\n   - the *1916 yearly tenancy agreement* between the Bute Estate and John\n   Williams;\n   - the *1924 Llandough Estate sale particulars — DSA/6/701*;\n   - the *1938 Great House Farm auction particulars — GD/LA/15/255 and\n   DSA/6/1158*;\n   - the *1938 conveyance from Mountjoy Ltd to Western Ground Rents*;\n   - the *1949 agreement or correspondence* concerning Frederick Buckler\n   and Mary Williams taking over the occupation;\n   - the *1953 judgment concerning rent arrears* at Great House Farm; and\n   - any *notice to quit issued before 2 February 1955*.\n\nI would also be interested in any pre-1955 *plans, title descriptions,\nschedules of deeds, abstracts of title or other records* showing how the\nfarmhouse, garden, farmyard, cottages and agricultural land were described\nor treated.\n\nI appreciate that some of these documents may have originated with the Bute\nEstate, Mountjoy or Western Ground Rents rather than BP itself. What I am\ntrying to establish is whether any such historical material is present\nwithin the BP Archive, or whether the BP Archive has catalogue references\nidentifying material which may have subsequently formed part of the title\nhistory of the property.\n\nIf the answer is that the BP Archive contains *no pre-1955 material\nrelating to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr*, I would be grateful if you could\nconfirm that explicitly. If you can identify relevant catalogue references\neven where the underlying document is not held, those references would also\nbe very useful.\