ler families;\n   - possession proceedings and enforcement, particularly 1955, 1962 and\n   1974–1988;\n   - property acquisition, title investigation and disposal;\n   - conveyances, title deeds, abstracts of title and schedules of deeds;\n   - estate-management correspondence;\n   - property, site and boundary plans;\n   - Land Registry correspondence and registration, particularly 1982–1983.\n\nThe relevant period is approximately *1955–1988*, with particular emphasis\non *1962–1983*.\nThree priority categories\n\nIf relevant material survives, I would particularly like to identify the\nfollowing, in this order:\n\n*1. The BP Properties Ltd / BP Pension Trust Ltd property file for Great\nHouse Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough*\n\nIn particular, any acquisition/title file containing the original property\ndescription, conveyances, title investigation, schedules of deeds, property\nplans, boundary plans or correspondence identifying exactly which land and\nbuildings BP considered to form the property.\n\n*2. The legal/property file relating to the 1962 possession proceedings and\nsubsequent enforcement/re-entry*\n\nIn particular, any BP legal correspondence, instructions to solicitors,\nplans, property descriptions or internal documents identifying the land and\nbuildings to which the possession order was understood to apply.\n\n*3. The 1982–1983 title/registration/consolidation file*\n\nIn particular, correspondence, plans, conveyances, title investigation and\nLand Registry material concerning the registration or amalgamation of the\nrelevant parcels, including any documentation showing how the\nhouse-and-garden, eastern cottages and western farm/barn/stables/courtyard\nareas were treated.\n\nIf these exact files do not survive, I would be very grateful for the\nnearest surviving files, alternative references or catalogue entries\ncovering the same transactions.\nAccess\n\nI would also appreciate advice on:\n\n   - whether the relevant records are available for public research;\n   - whether they can be viewed in person at the BP Archive at the\n   University of Warwick;\n   - whether advance appointment or reader registration is required;\n   - whether particular records require advance retrieval;\n   - whether copies or digital reproductions can be ordered; and\n   - whether any relevant records are subject to closure or other access\n   restrictions.\n\nI am happy to provide further information, including the relevant court\ncase reference, property names, dates and Land Registry title numbers, if\nthis would assist the archivist in identifying the records.\nResearch purpose\n\nI am particularly interested in *contemporary BP documentation rather than\nlater summaries*, because the central research question is what BP itself\nunderstood the property's legal identity, boundaries and constituent\nparcels to be at the relevant dates.\n\nThank you very much for any assistance you can provide.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-1a0043078b268da8","subject":"Please update the status of your request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","name":"Please update the status of your request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","date":"2026-08-15T06:51:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0043078b268da8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-1a0043078b268da8-please-update-the-status-of-your-request-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-from-the-williams-buckler-fami","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-