 (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fd2730a7c87340","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a00198b4da13afc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Information Governance Team,\n\nI refer to the internal review of Case Ref 00210772 (Great House Farm / Ty\nMawr, Llandough) which I requested on 7 July 2026.\n\nOn 5 August 2026 you acknowledged that the matter remained outstanding\nbeyond the 20-working-day statutory period and stated that further\nenquiries with service areas were ongoing. You indicated a further update\nor decision would be provided.\n\nAs of the close of business on Friday 14 August 2026 no substantive\nresponse or decision has been received.\n\nThis is a formal chase. The Environmental Information Regulations 2004\nrequire that internal reviews be completed promptly and, in any event,\nwithin a reasonable time. The delay is now significant.\n\nPlease provide the completed internal review decision within 5 working days\nof this email (i.e. by close of business on Monday 24 August 2026).\n\nIf a full response is not received by that date I may escalate the matter\nto the Information Commissioner’s Office for non-compliance with the\nstatutory timescales under the EIR, which I do not care to do.\n\nPlease also confirm, as part of the outstanding review or by way of further\ndisclosure under the same reference:\n\n1. Whether the Council (as local planning authority) considered issuing a\nBuilding Preservation Notice under section 58 of the Town and Country\nPlanning Act 1971 (or any equivalent provision) in respect of Great House\nFarm at any time between July and December 1988.\n\n2. If it was considered, who decided against it and on what grounds.\n\n3. If it was not considered, why not, given that the building was under\nactive bailiff enforcement, partial demolition of outbuildings had already\noccurred, and Cadw had publicly stated on 3 December 1988 that listing was\nunder active consideration.\n\nA Building Preservation Notice would have provided interim protection at\nthe critical moment. Its absence is material to the internal review of the\noriginal response and to the wider handling of the case.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\nWilliams/ Buckler Family Estate\n\n---\n\nReady to create/update as a Gmail draft if you want.\n\nOn Wed, 5 Aug 2026, 12:03 FOI Unit, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> We apologise for the delay in replying, for information further enquiries\n> are being made with service areas in light of the concerns you have raised\n> with the original response.  Those enquiries are not quite complete yet.\n> We will write to you further by Friday 14th August 2026 with a further\n> update.\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Information Governance Officer/ / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\n>\n> Legal & Democratic Services /Gwasanaethau Cyfreithol a Democrataidd\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\n>\n> e-mail / e-bost: [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you\n> really need to.*\n>\n> *Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod\n> gwir angen.*\n>\n>\n>\n> Visit our Website at *www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n> <http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>*\n>\n> Ewch i'n gwefan yn *www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n> <http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>*\n>\n>\n>\n> *Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n> <https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>*\n>\n> *Follow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n> <http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>*\n>\n>\n>\n> Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 01 August 2026 16:23\n> *To:* FOI Unit <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Information Governance Team,\n>\n>\n>\n> On 7 July 2026 I requested an internal review of the Council’s response to\n> my Environmental Information Regulations request (Case Ref 00210772).\n>\n> You acknowledged this on 10 July 2026 and stated you were reviewing my\n> concerns and would be in touch further as soon as possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> Over 20 working days have now passed with no further update or decision.\n>\n> Please provide the outcome of the internal review, or a clear timescale\n> for when it will be issued, within 5 working days.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a00192410acc9e9","subject":"Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)","name":"Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)","date":"2026-08-14T18:39:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a00192410acc9e9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834-cadw-failures-revised-report-10-august-2026","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a00192410acc9e9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Amy,\n\nThank you for confirming receipt and for confirming that the revised report\ndated 10 August 2026 will be treated as the operative version in place of\nthe previous edition.\n\nI appreciate that you need to consult colleagues and that annual leave may\naffect the timetable. Friday 28 August is noted.\n\nSee attached an A.I analysis of the evidence and chronology I hold. Which\nmight assist your departments internal review of this matter too.\n\nI look forward to receiving the substantive response when you return.\n\nRegards,\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nWilliams / Buckler Family Estate\n\nOn Fri, 14 Aug 2026, 12:18 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for the email, we shall use this revised report (10th August\n> 26) instead of the previous version.\n>\n>\n>\n> I am just checking with colleagues and will collate a response. However,\n> given annual leave (including my own) a response may have a slight delay.\n>\n>\n>\n> On my return to work, I will endeavour to respond by Friday 28th August.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy Longford\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 10 August 2026 22:46\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Cc:* Cadw Planning <[email redacted]>;\n> [email redacted]; DOUGHTY, Stephen <\n> [email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)\n>\n>\n>\n> Sirs/Ma'ams,\n>\n> I write further to my email of 9 August 2026 submitting a review\n> concerning Cadw’s 1988 assessment of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n>\n> Please find attached (and linked below) a revised edition of the report,\n> dated 10 August 2026. This version has been carefully restructured to\n> present the same evidence in a more measured and administratively focused\n> form. It is offered as a request for historical record correction, archival\n> explanation, and administrative acknowledgement rather than as a forensic\n> challenge.\n>\n> The revised document:\n>\n> • Clearly states what it is and is not;\n> • Sets out the surviving independent evidence (principally the H.J. Thomas\n> RCAHMW survey of 1974);\n> • Notes the near-total absence of Cadw’s 1988 working papers confirmed in\n> ATISN 27021;\n> • Asks only for realistic, achievable administrative steps: explanation of\n> the archival position, reflection of the surviving evidence in the Historic\n> Environment Record, acknowledgement of the records gap, and consideration\n> of a local heritage marker.\n>\n> It does not claim unlawfulness, seek compensation from Cadw, or demand a\n> public inquiry.\n>\n> I hope this revised presentation is more palatable and will assist the\n> relevant bodies in providing a constructive response.\n>\n> I look forward to your substantive response.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester\n> \n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd\n> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu\n> eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon\n> ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn\n> Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh\n> Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh\n> Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the\n> Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice\n> <https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en>\n> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your\n> privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\n>"},{"id":"gm-1a0015c1d2cc29c1","subject":"Re: FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-08-14T17:40:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-1a0015c1d2cc29c1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa-foi-2026-020-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-1a0015c1d2cc29c1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"FOI Team,\n\nThank you for your detailed response and for undertaking the additional\nenquiries.\n\nI appreciate the further information you have provided concerning the\nsearches undertaken. However, I would like to request an internal review\nunder the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nMy concern is not simply that no objects have been identified. It is\nwhether the searches undertaken have fully addressed the scope of my\noriginal request, particularly the documentary evidence concerning the\nprovenance, acquisition, transfer, ownership, identification and dispersal\nof material originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr).\n\nI would be grateful if the internal review could consider the following\npoints.\n\n*1. Information identified concerning Great House Farm*\n\nYour response states that the additional enquiries identified “some\ninformation relating generally to Great House Farm and the surrounding\narea”.\n\nPlease could you identify what categories of information this refers to\nand, where it is not exempt, provide the relevant recorded information or\nexplain where it can be accessed?\n\nThis appears potentially relevant to the original request even if it does\nnot itself identify furniture or household objects.\n\n*2. Scope of the archived electronic search*\n\nYou state that the Information Technology team reviewed “archived\nelectronic systems and records retained by the Museum”.\n\nPlease could the review clarify:\n\n   - which archived systems were searched;\n   - the approximate date ranges covered;\n   - whether historical email or correspondence archives were searched;\n   - whether legacy collections-management databases were searched;\n   - whether databases or systems preceding the current CMS were searched;\n   and\n   - whether any archived systems were unavailable, incomplete or incapable\n   of being searched.\n\n*3. Correspondence and administrative records*\n\nMy original request expressly sought correspondence concerning the\nidentification, recovery, ownership or location of objects, as well as\ncorrespondence with the Bute Estate, Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle and\nother public authorities.\n\nYour response refers generally to “associated collection documentation” and\n“administrative records”, but does not make clear whether historical\ncorrespondence files were specifically searched.\n\nPlease could the internal review establish whether searches were made of:\n\n   - curator correspondence;\n   - departmental correspondence files;\n   - donor correspondence;\n   - acquisition correspondence;\n   - disposal correspondence;\n   - loan correspondence;\n   - provenance correspondence;\n   - correspondence with Cardiff Council;\n   - correspondence with Cardiff Castle;\n   - correspondence with the Bute Estate;\n   - correspondence with other museums or public authorities; and\n   - any relevant institutional or external correspondence indexes.\n\n*4. Search terms*\n\nThank you for identifying many of the search terms used.\n\nPlease could the internal review confirm whether the search also included\ncombinations and variants involving:\n\n   - “Bute Estate”\n   - “Bute”\n   - “Cardiff Castle”\n   - “Cardiff Council”\n   - “Great House Farm”\n   - “Ty Mawr”\n   - “Great House”\n   - “Llandough”\n   - “Buckler”\n   - “Williams”\n   - “Mary Williams”\n   - “Mary Doreen Williams”\n   - “household effects”\n   - “contents”\n   - “furniture”\n   - “furnishings”\n   - “heirlooms”\n   - “fixtures”\n   - “estate”\n   - “dispersal”\n   - “recovery”\n   - “provenance”\n   - “ownership”\n   - “transfer”\n   - “demolition”\n\nI appreciate that historical records may not have been consistently\nindexed, which is why I would be grateful for confirmation of the\nmethodology used.\n\n*5. Transfer, disposal and destruction*\n\nYour response states:\n\n“We are also not aware of any relevant collection records relating to such\nmaterial having been transferred to another institution or destroyed.”\n\nPlease could the internal review clarify whether this conclusion is based\nupon:\n\na. a search of transfer/accession-out records;\n\nb. a review of retention and disposal records;\n\nc. enquiries with relevant collections staff;\n\nd. review of archival transfer documentation; or\n\ne. institutional knowledge rather than a documentary search.\n\nI am particularly interested in distinguishing between “no record exists”\nand “no record was identified in the systems searched”.\n\n*6. The original request concerning external institutions*\n\nThe original request was deliberately framed broadly because the question\nconcerns possible dispersal of the contents of a demolished historic\nproperty.\n\nIt expressly included records concerning Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\nthe Bute Estate, museums, Arts Council England, DCMS, RCEWA and other\npublic authorities.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if the review could confirm whether records\nof communications or transactions involving those bodies were searched\nwithin Amgueddfa Cymru's records, rather than simply searching the Museum's\nobject catalogue for Great House Farm objects.\n\n*7. Advice and assistance*\n\nYou have stated that Cardiff Council and Cardiff Castle “would appear to be\nthe organisations most likely to hold records relating to furniture,\nfurnishings or other movable property associated with Great House Farm”.\n\nI appreciate that you cannot transfer another authority's records to me.\nHowever, could you please provide any further information available to the\nMuseum as to *which particular department, collection, archive or record\nseries at Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle is most likely to contain such\nmaterial*?\n\nThat would materially assist me in directing subsequent FOI and archival\nenquiries.\n\nI am grateful for the additional work already undertaken. I am requesting\nthe internal review because I would like the record to be clear as to\nprecisely what was searched, what information was identified, and what the\nnegative result does and does not establish.\n\nI am not asking Amgueddfa Cymru to determine any allegation concerning the\nhistorical ownership of Great House Farm. The purpose of the review is\nsimply to ensure that the documentary search corresponds fully with the\nscope of the original FOI request.\n\nPlease treat this email as my formal request for an internal review of FOI\n2026-020.\n\nRegards,\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nWilliams / Buckler Family Estate\n\nOn Fri, 14 Aug 2026, 05:43 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> Following receipt of your query, Amgueddfa Cymru undertook further\n> enquiries to satisfy itself that no information had been overlooked when\n> responding to your request.\n>\n>\n>\n> These enquiries included a review of records held across the Museum's\n> collections and a review of archived electronic systems and records by the\n> Museum's Information Technology team. The review considered all collections\n> management systems used by the Museum, including those most likely to\n> contain information falling within the scope of your request.\n>\n>\n>\n> For the History collections, searches were undertaken of the Collections\n> Management System (CMS), accession files, donor indexes, location indexes\n> and associated collection documentation. Searches were carried out using\n> terms including \"Great House Farm\", \"Ty Mawr\", \"Llandough\", \"Buckler\" and\n> \"Bute\". Additional consideration was given to acquisition records,\n> provenance information and associated administrative records.\n>\n>\n>\n> For the Art collections, searches were undertaken within the collections\n> management system across description, comments, acquisition notes and place\n> fields using the terms \"Ty Mawr\", \"Great House Farm\", \"Great House\",\n> \"Williams\", \"Buckler\", \"Llandough\" and combinations of those terms. No\n> additional paper archives relating to Great House Farm, Ty Mawr, Great\n> House or Buckler were identified.\n>\n>\n>\n> The Museum's Information Technology team also reviewed archived electronic\n> systems and records retained by the Museum.\n>\n>\n>\n> These enquiries identified some information relating generally to Great\n> House Farm and the surrounding area. However, no information was identified\n> concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms or other\n> movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. We\n> did not identify any inventories, catalogues, acquisition records, disposal\n> records, loan records, provenance files, ownership records, photographs,\n> correspondence or other records falling within categories 1 to 9 of your\n> request.\n>\n>\n>\n> We are also not aware of any relevant collection records relating to such\n> material having been transferred to another institution or destroyed.\n>\n>\n>\n> Accordingly, having completed these additional enquiries, Amgueddfa Cymru\n> remains satisfied that it does not hold recorded information within the\n> scope of your request and our response under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom\n> of Information Act 2000 remains unchanged.\n>\n> In relation to your request for advice and assistance, Cardiff Council and\n> Cardiff Castle would appear to be the organisations most likely to hold\n> records relating to furniture, furnishings or other movable property\n> associated with Great House Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n> If you remain dissatisfied with this response, you may request an internal\n> review within 40 working days of the date of this email.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 03 August 2026 17:29\n> *To:* FOI Requests <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff\n> Castle Furniture\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> This email comes from outside the organisation.\n>\n> Do not click links or open attachments unless it is an email you expected\n> to receive.\n>\n> Dear FOI Team,\n>\n> Thank you for your response.\n>\n> I note your position that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold recorded\n> information within the scope of my request.\n>\n> However, I would be grateful if you could clarify the searches undertaken\n> to reach that conclusion.\n>\n> In particular, please confirm:\n>\n>    - Which collections management systems, databases and \"associated\n>    records\" were searched.\n>    - Whether searches extended beyond accessioned objects to include\n>    acquisition files, provenance files, curator correspondence, donor files,\n>    temporary custody records, unaccessioned material, photographs and\n>    administrative records.\n>    - The search terms used (for example: \"Great House Farm\", \"Ty Mawr\",\n>    \"Llandough\", \"Williams\", \"Buckler\", \"Bute Estate\" and any other relevant\n>    variants).\n>    - Whether any potentially relevant records have been transferred to\n>    another institution or destroyed in accordance with a retention policy.\n>\n> My original request was not limited to identifying surviving objects. It\n> also sought records relating to their provenance, acquisition, transfer,\n> ownership, photographs and correspondence. This reflects the fact that the\n> contents of Great House Farm may have been dispersed following the\n> property's demolition, meaning relevant records could exist even if no\n> objects were ultimately accessioned by the Museum.\n>\n> If, following those searches, Amgueddfa Cymru remains satisfied that no\n> recorded information is held, I would be grateful for confirmation of that\n> position.\n>\n> Finally, if you are aware of another public authority that is more likely\n> to hold records falling within the scope of my request, I would appreciate\n> your advice in accordance with your duty to provide advice and assistance.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, 3 Aug 2026, 10:39 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\n> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your request for information received on 2nd July 2026,\n> concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other\n> movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> Following searches of the Museum's collections management systems and\n> associated records, Amgueddfa Cymru has not identified any furniture,\n> furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms or other movable property\n> recorded as originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> Accordingly, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold recorded information falling\n> within the scope of items 1 to 9 of your request relating to such objects.\n>\n> For clarity:\n>\n>    - We have not identified any objects of the type described in your\n>    request as originating from Great House Farm.\n>    - We have not identified inventories, catalogues, acquisition records,\n>    disposal records, loan records, provenance files, ownership records,\n>    photographs, correspondence, reports, memoranda or related records\n>    concerning such objects within the scope of your request.\n>    - We have not identified any records relating to the identification,\n>    recovery, ownership or location of furniture or household effects from\n>    Great House Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n> We note your references to archaeological material from land associated\n> with Great House Farm. However, archaeological finds are outside the scope\n> of this response because they do not fall within your request for\n> furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable\n> property. We understand that archaeological material is the subject of a\n> separate information request and will be dealt with separately.\n>\n>\n>\n> Under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response\n> is therefore that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 20:51\n> *To:* [email redacted]\n> *Cc:* [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI Requests <\n> [email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> National Library of Wales <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff\n> Castle Furniture\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making t