mail unless you really need to.\n> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n> National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it\n> are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are\n> addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this\n> email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions,\n> conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do\n> not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither\n> given nor endorsed by it.\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n>\n>\n> Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\n> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n> National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it\n> are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are\n> addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this\n> email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions,\n> conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do\n> not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither\n> given nor endorsed by it.\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ff65cb074e6c9d","subject":"RE: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close","name":"RE: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close","date":"2026-08-12T14:24:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ff65cb074e6c9d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa56f91e54c219-complaint-failure-to-respond-failure-to-deal-properly-with-case-cllr-george-carroll-llandough-great-house-farm-church-vi","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa56f91e54c219","direction":"received","from":"Davidson, Victoria","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ff65cb074e6c9d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\nThank you for your email regarding Councillor George Carroll and for setting out the background to your concerns relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, now Church View Close.\nI acknowledge receipt of your correspondence and have carefully considered the matters you have raised.\nHaving reviewed your complaint, I do not consider that it falls within the scope of the Vale of Glamorgan Council's Corporate Concerns and Complaints Policy. The substance of your correspondence relates to historic planning, enforcement, land ownership, heritage and record keeping matters dating back several decades, together with requests for review, explanation and further investigation of those matters.\nThe Corporate Concerns and Complaints Policy is not intended to provide a mechanism for challenging or revisiting decisions where there is a separate statutory process or right of appeal; seeking changes to properly made decisions, policies or legislation; pursuing matters which are not the responsibility of the Council; promoting a particular cause or campaign; or addressing matters for which alternative legal or regulatory processes exist.\nYou have also requested that the matter be considered by me as the Monitoring Officer as a potential breach of the Member’s Code of Conduct by Councillor Carroll.\nThe role of the Monitoring Officer in this context is limited to considering whether there is evidence that a member has failed to comply with the statutory Members’s Code of Conduct. Having reviewed the information you have provided, I have not identified evidence which would indicate a breach of the Members Code of Conduct.\nAccordingly, the issues raised will not be progressed under the Council's Corporate Concerns and Complaints Policy as they fall outside the scope of that procedure. I do not consider there is sufficient evidence to justify referral of the matter for consideration under the Members’s Code of Conduct. No further action will therefore be taken by me in my capacity as the Council’s Monitoring Officer in relation to this complaint.\nI appreciate that this response may be disappointing. However, I trust it clarifies the Council's position and the limits of the Corporate Complaints Procedure and the Monitoring Officer's role in the context of the matters you raise.\nYours sincerely,\n\nVictoria Davidson\nMonitoring Officer/Head of Legal & Democratic Services / Rheolydd Gweithredol, Gwasanaethau Cyfreithiol\nManagement Team - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ntel / ffôn:\nmob / sym: [phone redacted]\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n\nConsider the environment.. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<http://en-gb.facebook.com/valeofglamorganlife>\nFollow us on Instagram / Dilynwch ni ar Instagram<https://www.instagram.com/vog_council>\nFollow us on LinkedIn / Dilynwch ni ar LinkedIn<https://www.linkedin.com/company/vale-of-glamorgan-council>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD2A6D.C6BF2380]<https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/our_council/achieving_our_vision/Corporate-Plan.aspx>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 27 July 2026 22:22\nTo: [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; Carroll, George D (Cllr) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\nDear Monitoring Officer / Corporate Complaints Team,\n\nWith great regret I am writing to make a complaint about the persistent failure of Councillor George D. D. Carroll (Llandough ward) to respond substantively to my repeated and reasonable correspondence concerning historic land, planning, enforcement, heritage and related public-interest matters at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (now Church View Close), Vale of Glamorgan.\n\nI have a legitimate and long-standing family interest in the site (Williams/Buckler family connection documented from the 17th century). See attached.\n\nThe issues raised include alleged defective notices, loss of opportunity to contest enforcement leading to demolition in 1988, heritage/regulatory oversight, planning and title records, and related transparency failures.\n\nDespite multiple contacts over several months, I have received no substantive replies from Cllr Carroll. This constitutes a failure to respond and a failure to deal with the case properly.\n\n### Full correspondence log with Cllr George Carroll ([email redacted]<[email redacted]>)\n\n| Date       | Subject / Key content                                                                 | Response received |\n|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 16 Feb 2026 | Potential gaps in Council planning/record-keeping for Great House Farm (demolished 1988); title fraud and procedural issues relating to Church View Close | None |\n\n| 4 May 2026  | Request regarding BP vs Buckler 1987; shared media/evidence; request for attention as Llandough councillor | None |\n\n| 7 Jun 2026  | “Church View Close, Llandough” – piecing together 1988 events from public records, family testimony and media | None |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | “Great House Farm, Llandough” – enquiry whether prior concerns on family dispossession had been reviewed; request for any progress or discussion | None |\n\n| 13 Jul 2026 | “Great House Farm/ Church View Close” – formal follow-up listing the above timeline, restating legitimate interest (family roots since 1667), noting absence of replies, requesting detailed response within 10 working days, and raising the removed commemorative tree | None |\n\n### Remedy sought\n\n1. A full written response from Cllr Carroll addressing the points raised in the logged emails, within 10–15 working days.\n\n2. Confirmation that this complaint has been logged under the Council’s corporate complaints procedure and/or referred to the Monitoring Officer / Standards Committee as appropriate for any potential breach of the councillor Code of Conduct (failure to respond / failure to deal properly with a case).\n\n3. Written confirmation of the process and timescale for investigation and response.\n\nI have retained the full original emails and attachments and can supply them on request. Please acknowledge receipt of this formal complaint.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19ff5eec7294b507","subject":"Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-344046-K1S1R2 CRM:021100306","name":"Response to National Archives enquiry. Case number CAS-344046-K1S1R2 CRM:021100306","date":"2026-08-12T12:24:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ff5eec7294b507.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ff5eec7294b507-sponse-to-national-archives-enquiry-case-number-cas-344046-k1s1r2-crm-021100306","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ff5eec7294b507","direction":"received","from":"RESO Records Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-343481","CAS-344046"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ff5eec7294b507.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear  Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nRecords relating to the transfer, retention or destruction of material can be found on our catalogue within the record series created by the Public Record Office (departmental code PRO) and The National Archives (departmental code RW).\n\nI have searched our catalogue, via the advanced search page  for records using (\"Great House Farm\" OR \"Ty Mawr\" OR Llandough OR Cedfin) AND Glamorgan as search terms within the file series PRO and RW. As you can see here, this search did not yield any results . You can try some similar searches yourself.\n\nI recommend you consult our guides to searching for records relating land and maps  and civil court records  to assist with other aspects of your enquiry. These guides will help you to use our catalogue , or other online sources, effectively and focus your search.\n\nRecords are represented in our online catalogue by a title, a reference and a brief description. When you search our catalogue using keywords you are searching across these titles and descriptions, rather than the contents of the records themselves.\n\nBy clicking on any search result, you can see whether the record is available online or if you need to visit us to view the original. You can also request copies of records from their catalogue description page.\n\nIf the record is held by another archive, you will need to contact them directly to find out how you can access it.\n\nYou can also watch this video  for more advice on using our online catalogue.\n\nYou are welcome to visit us  to continue your research here in person, where access to our records is free of charge. Before you visit, please check our website for information regarding our opening hours  and ID requirements , and videos with tips on how to handle and photograph original documents .\n\nIf you are unable to visit, or would like someone to pursue this research on your behalf, please see the available paid search options  on our website.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nSarah Abbott\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk \n\nPlease complete our brief, three question survey  to let us know what you think about your recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important \n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\nDear Patricia Reynolds,\n\nThank you for your response of 30 July 2026 (Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6).\n\nI note your advice that The National Archives is not the primary repository for the material described in my original enquiry. However, my enquiry also concerns whether The National Archives holds any recorded information relating to the existence, transfer, retention, destruction, or absence of such records.\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000, I request confirmation of any recorded information held by The National Archives relating to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough (Glamorgan), including historical references under alternative descriptions such as Cedfin or equivalent contemporary descriptions.\n\nSpecifically, please confirm whether The National Archives holds:\n\n  1.  Manorial and estate records\n\nAny catalogue entries, Manorial Documents Register information, finding aids, transfer records, or related documentation concerning:\n\n  *   the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan);\n\n  *   pre-1667 references to occupants, customary tenants, holdings, surveys, rentals, terriers, or court rolls;\n\n  *   Vaughan family estate holdings at Llandough;\n\n  *   Great House Farm / Ty Mawr or any earlier description of the holding.\n\nPlease include any references to HMC9/311 or related archival series.\n\n  1.  Records concerning disposal, destruction, or transfer of records\n\nAny recorded information showing:\n\n  *   whether records relating to Great House Farm, Llandough, the Bute Estate, Vaughan family papers, or associated land records were ever transferred to The National Archives;\n\n  *   whether any such records were destroyed, and if so:\n\n     *   what records were destroyed;\n\n     *   when they were destroyed;\n\n     *   under which retention schedule, disposal authority, or policy;\n\n     *   which body authorised or carried out the destruction.\n\nIf no such records are held, please confirm whether any disposal or transfer records indicate that relevant material was never deposited or was destroyed elsewhere.\n\n  1.  Legal and court records\n\nAny central court records, indexes, correspondence, or administrative records concerning:\n\n  *   possession or title disputes involving Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n\n  *   Western Ground Rents Ltd;\n\n  *   BP Pension Trust Ltd;\n\n  *   BP Properties Ltd;\n\n  *   Mountjoy Ltd;\n\n  *   the proceedings connected with BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2.\n\n  1.  Estate transfers and ownership records\n\nAny government-held correspondence, files, or records relating to:\n\n  *   the Bute Estate;\n\n  *   the 1938 sale or transfer of Great House Farm;\n\n  *   Western Ground Rents Ltd acquisition;\n\n  *   BP Pension Trust/BP Properties involvement;\n\n  *   any government department involvement in the property.\n\n  1.  Family correspondence and related records\n\nAny correspondence, reports, enquiries, or administrative records held by The National Archives involving:\n\n  *   Mary Williams;\n\n  *   Fred Buckler;\n\n  *   William Buckler;\n\n  *   the Williams/Buckler family;\n\n  *   Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n\n  *   Bute Estate representatives;\n\n  *   Western Ground Rents;\n\n  *   BP entities.\n\n  1.  1980–1988 period and demolition/eviction matters\n\nAny records concerning:\n\n  *   the public campaign regarding Great House Farm;\n\n  *   parliamentary correspondence or government enquiries;\n\n  *   the 1988 eviction/demolition;\n\n  *   Cadw or government communications;\n\n  *   European Commission of Human Rights Application 14464/88 (Buckler v United Kingdom).\n\nIf any relevant information is held, please provide catalogue references, descriptions, and access arrangements.\n\nIf no relevant information is held, please confirm:\n\n  *   the searches undertaken;\n\n  *   the catalogues, databases, and record series searched;\n\n  *   whether any relevant records were ever held and subsequently transferred, destroyed, or disposed of.\n\nI am pursuing parallel enquiries with the National Library of Wales, Glamorgan Archives and other repositories. This request is specifically directed at recorded information held by The National Archives.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\n\nOn Thu, 30 Jul 2026, 10:56 Contact Centre,  > wrote:\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nI'm afraid we are not the right place to come to for your enquiry. We hold historical records sent to us by central government departments and law courts for permanent preservation. I regret, therefore, that I'm unable to help you with your enquiry.\n\nI suggest you contact The National Library of Wales .\n\nI wish you every success with your research.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nPatricia Reynolds\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk \n\nPlease complete our brief, three question survey  to let us know what you think about your recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted] . Learn why this is important \n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded information held by the National Library of Wales:\nAny manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\nAny estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings) that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\nAny catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the family’s holding at this property.\nPlease confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state the exemption(s) relied upon.\n\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nRequester \n\n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------