or historical record correction, archival\n> explanation, and administrative acknowledgement rather than as a forensic\n> challenge.\n>\n> The revised document:\n>\n> • Clearly states what it is and is not;\n> • Sets out the surviving independent evidence (principally the H.J. Thomas\n> RCAHMW survey of 1974);\n> • Notes the near-total absence of Cadw’s 1988 working papers confirmed in\n> ATISN 27021;\n> • Asks only for realistic, achievable administrative steps: explanation of\n> the archival position, reflection of the surviving evidence in the Historic\n> Environment Record, acknowledgement of the records gap, and consideration\n> of a local heritage marker.\n>\n> It does not claim unlawfulness, seek compensation from Cadw, or demand a\n> public inquiry.\n>\n> I hope this revised presentation is more palatable and will assist the\n> relevant bodies in providing a constructive response.\n>\n> I look forward to your substantive response.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester\n> \n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ff079027ee0614","subject":"Acknowledgement from the Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee","name":"Acknowledgement from the Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee","date":"2026-08-11T10:58:02Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ff079027ee0614.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ff079027ee0614-acknowledgement-from-the-culture-communications-cymraeg-and-sport-committee","scopeTopics":["senedd"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["senedd"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ff079027ee0614","direction":"received","from":"Pwyllgor Diwylliant, Cyfathrebu, y Gymraeg a Chwaraeon - Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee","institutions":[{"id":"senedd","name":"Senedd"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ff079027ee0614.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your correspondence and for sharing the forensic review of Cadw's 1988 assessment of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough. I acknowledge the strength of feeling expressed in your letter and recognise the longstanding concerns that you and your family have raised.\n\nThe Committee’s role is to scrutinise the work of the Welsh Government and associated public bodies, including holding ministers and public authorities to account for their policies, administration and use of public resources. However, the Committee does not have a remit to investigate, adjudicate upon, or oversee individual complaints or dispute. Nor does it have the powers to reopen historical decisions or direct public bodies to undertake investigations into specific matters.\n\nThe Committee is therefore unable to take on an oversight role in relation to the issues you raise or to intervene in these matters.\n\nThe matters you raise appear principally to concern the actions and decision-making processes of Cadw in relation to a specific historical assessment. Cadw are responsible for responding to requests for information about their records and decision-making processes, and for considering any representations made regarding the accuracy or completeness of the historical record.\n\nThank you again for writing to the Committee.\n\nKind regards,\n\nHaidee\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD2983.C251FAB0]\nHaidee James[cid:image002.png@01DD2983.C251FAB0]\nAil Glerc, Pwyllgor Diwylliant, Cyfathrebu, y Gymraeg a Chwaraeon, Senedd Cymru\nSecond Clerk, Culture, Communications, Cymraeg and Sport Committee, Welsh Parliament\n[phone redacted] Rhagenwau|Pronouns: hi – she/her\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 10 August 2026 22:46\nTo: [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; DOUGHTY, Stephen <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)\n\nSirs/Ma'ams,\n\nI write further to my email of 9 August 2026 submitting a review concerning Cadw’s 1988 assessment of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nPlease find attached (and linked below) a revised edition of the report, dated 10 August 2026. This version has been carefully restructured to present the same evidence in a more measured and administratively focused form. It is offered as a request for historical record correction, archival explanation, and administrative acknowledgement rather than as a forensic challenge.\n\nThe revised document:\n\n• Clearly states what it is and is not;\n• Sets out the surviving independent evidence (principally the H.J. Thomas RCAHMW survey of 1974);\n• Notes the near-total absence of Cadw’s 1988 working papers confirmed in ATISN 27021;\n• Asks only for realistic, achievable administrative steps: explanation of the archival position, reflection of the surviving evidence in the Historic Environment Record, acknowledgement of the records gap, and consideration of a local heritage marker.\n\nIt does not claim unlawfulness, seek compensation from Cadw, or demand a public inquiry.\n\nI hope this revised presentation is more palatable and will assist the relevant bodies in providing a constructive response.\n\nI look forward to your substantive response.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19feeb428c9f92d6","subject":"Follow-up – Outstanding information request (Great House Farm, Llandough) – originally sent 20 June 2026","name":"Follow-up – Outstanding information request (Great House Farm, Llandough) – originally sent 20 June 2026","date":"2026-08-11T02:43:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19feeb428c9f92d6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19feeb273de10513-follow-up-outstanding-information-request-great-house-farm-llandough-originally-sent-20-june-2026","scopeTopics":["dwrcymru"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dwrcymru"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19feeb273de10513","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"dwrcymru","name":"Dwr Cymru Welsh Water"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19feeb428c9f92d6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Environmental Information Requests Team,\n\nI am writing to follow up on my request for recorded information concerning\nGreat House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\nI first emailed Dŵr Cymru on 20 June 2026 (to [email redacted]) requesting\naccess to any records held relating to water supply accounts, billing\nhistory, and correspondence concerning the property.\n\nI sent a reminder to the same address on 1 August 2026. I have received no\nacknowledgement or response to either message.\n\nPlease confirm:\n\nWhether my original request has been received and logged.\n\nWhether it is being handled under the Environmental Information Regulations\n2004.\n\nWhen I may expect a substantive response (or a formal refusal if the\ninformation is considered outside the scope of the Regulations).\n\nI would be grateful for a reply within the next 10 working days. If a\ndifferent internal reference or contact point is now handling the matter,\nplease let me know.\n\nThank you for your attention.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n"},{"id":"gm-19feda3903937e59","subject":"Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)","name":"Re: CADW failures – Revised Report (10 August 2026)","date":"2026-08-10T21:45:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19feda3903937e59.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834-cadw-failures-revised-report-10-august-2026","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19feda3903937e59.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'ams,\n\nI write further to my email of 9 August 2026 submitting a review concerning\nCadw’s 1988 assessment of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nPlease find attached (and linked below) a revised edition of the report,\ndated 10 August 2026. This version has been carefully restructured to\npresent the same evidence in a more measured and administratively focused\nform. It is offered as a request for historical record correction, archival\nexplanation, and administrative acknowledgement rather than as a forensic\nchallenge.\n\nThe revised document:\n\n• Clearly states what it is and is not;\n• Sets out the surviving independent evidence (principally the H.J. Thomas\nRCAHMW survey of 1974);\n• Notes the near-total absence of Cadw’s 1988 working papers confirmed in\nATISN 27021;\n• Asks only for realistic, achievable administrative steps: explanation of\nthe archival position, reflection of the surviving evidence in the Historic\nEnvironment Record, acknowledgement of the records gap, and consideration\nof a local heritage marker.\n\nIt does not claim unlawfulness, seek compensation from Cadw, or demand a\npublic inquiry.\n\nI hope this revised presentation is more palatable and will assist the\nrelevant bodies in providing a constructive response.\n\nI look forward to your substantive response.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\n[email redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fec61fb1d20afa","subject":"ICO Case Reference: IC-546505-W6P0","name":"ICO Case Reference: IC-546505-W6P0","date":"2026-08-10T15:54:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fec61fb1d20afa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fec61fb1d20afa-ico-case-reference-ic-546505-w6p0","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fec61fb1d20afa","direction":"received","from":"icocasework","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":["IC-546505-W6P0"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fec61fb1d20afa.json","attachments":[{"name":"Letter to SB.pdf","title":"Letter to SB.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-08-10_ico_ic-546505-w6p0_letter.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":92770,"sha256":"fe1c863b6f90445d43b6df29e8f52a9b5fe9414dfcac0b81c3fdb2bd4d661574"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"10 August 2026\n\nDear Requester,\n\nOur reference: IC-546505-W6P0\n\nThank you for your correspondence of 21 July 2026.\n\nPlease find a letter attached in response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nElla Cuthbert\nLead Case Officer\nInformation Commissioner's Office\n\nInformation Commissioner’s Office, Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire [postcode redacted]\nT. [phone redacted] ico.org.uk<https://ico.org.uk/> twitter.com/iconews<https://twitter.com/iconews>\nPlease consider the environment before printing this email.\n\nFor information about what we do with personal data see our privacy notice at www.ico.org.uk/privacy-notice<https://www.ico.org.uk/privacy-notice>."},{"id":"gm-19feb187184eaca3","subject":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-08-10T09:54:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19feb187184eaca3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fd90bc1cfc812a-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["bt-archives"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bt-archives"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fd90bc1cfc812a","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; bt.com)","institutions":[{"id":"bt-archives","name":"BT Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19feb187184eaca3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"General\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your enquiry.\n\nAs a starting point, the following records may be of interest. These have been digitised and can be accessed via the via the online catalogue entry (see the PDF in the 'Document' field):\nPOST 30/631A<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f361&pos=1>\nPOST 30/940<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f529&pos=1>\nPOST 878B<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f2+CEN%2fCEN3%2f1%2f1%2f494&pos=1>\nTCB 273/2<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f2&pos=2>\nTCB 273/3<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f3&pos=2>\n\nDigitised images:\nTCB 473/P 5083<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f5+PH%2f2%2f1%2f5%2fP+5083&pos=1>\nTCE 361/ARC 1148<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f5+PH%2f9%2f1%2fARC+1148&pos=1>\n\nOccasionally, our catalogue software struggles to open large files; if you experience any problems, please let me know and I can share the digitised copies via our sharing platform\n\n\nThe following files have not been digitised but can be viewed by appointment in our searchroom:\nTCB 273/5<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f3+BT1%2f11+RES%2fRES3%2f3%2f5&pos=1>\nTCK 89/22<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Record.aspx?src=CalmView.Catalog&id=BTA%2f7+PP%2f1%2f23%2f22&pos=1>\n\n\nWe also hold a number of secondary sources relating to Marconi in our library, which can be consulted in our searchroom.\n\n\nI would recommend searching our online catalogue (Home Page<https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/CalmView/Default.aspx?>) to identify any other records that you think may be useful for your research. Details of how to book an appointment can be found on our website<https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives>.\n\n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n\nFahema\n\n\n\nFahema Begum\n\nBT Group Archives\n\nE: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nW: bt.com/history<https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history>\n\nPlanning a research visit to the Archives? We've introduced a new appointment booking system - visit our website<https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives> for details.\n\n [cid:image001.png@01DD28B6.9AC8C230]\nThis email contains information from BT Brands that might be privileged or confidential.\nAnd it's only meant for the person above. If that's not you, we're sorry - we must have sent it to you by mistake. Please email us to let us know, and don't copy or forward it to anyone else. Thanks. We monitor our email systems and may record all our emails.\nBritish Telecommunications plc\nR/O : 1 Braham Street, London, [postcode redacted]\n\nRegistered in England: No 1800000\nBritish Telecommunications plc is authorised and regulated by Financial Conduct Authority for the provision of consumer credit.\n\n\n\nGeneral\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 06 August 2026 22:48\nTo: BTARCHIV <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nDear BT Archives Team,\n\nI am researching the General Post Office involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's South Wales wireless telegraphy experiments during 1897, particularly the experiments between Lavernock Point and Flat Holm.\n\nThe Postal Museum has advised that the relevant GPO Telegraph Department and Engineering Department records are likely to be held by BT Archives. They confirmed that their own searches of Postal Museum holdings found no relevant records and that surviving telecommunications material from this period is likely to be within the collections transferred to BT Archives.\n\nI would be grateful if you could advise on the relevant surviving records and catalogue references.\n\nMy research concerns:\n\n  *   Marconi's 1897 South Wales wireless experiments;\n  *   Lavernock Point and Flat Holm;\n  *   Penarth and Llandough (near Penarth);\n  *   the involvement of the GPO Telegraph Department and Engineering Department;\n  *   any surviving correspondence, reports, notebooks, engineering records, plans, photographs or administrative records connected with the experiments.\n\nI am particularly interested in identifying any references to local residents or private individuals who assisted Marconi or GPO engineers. Family history suggests that a Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, may have assisted with the experiments locally. I appreciate that such a person may not appear in catalogue descriptions if he was a private individual rather than a GPO employee.\n\nCould you please advise whether your catalogue contains references to any of the following terms or variants:\n\n  *   Marconi\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi\n  *   wireless telegraphy\n  *   South Wales experiments\n  *   Lavernock\n  *   Penarth\n  *   Llandough\n  *   Great House Farm\n  *   Williams\n  *   W. Williams\n  *   William Williams\n  *   Mr Williams\n\nIf relevant records exist, I would be grateful for the catalogue references, file descriptions and dates so that I can identify the material for further research.\n\nI would also appreciate any guidance on whether there are related collections, transferred Post Office records, or finding aids that may not be obvious from the online catalogue.\n\nThank you very much for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n"},{"id":"gm-19fe7d6c11e21130","subject":"Re: CADW failures","name":"Re: CADW failures","date":"2026-08-09T18:43:58Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fe7d6c11e21130.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834-cadw-failures","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fe7c63edda5834","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fe7d6c11e21130.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'ams,\n\nI write on behalf of my household; the Williams / Buckler Family of what\nonce was Great House in Llandough, Cardiff. I formally submit the attached\nforensic review dated 9 August 2026 concerning Cadw’s 1988 assessment of\nGreat House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, the subsequent demolition, and the\nnear-total absence of contemporary decision records confirmed in ATISN\n27021.\n\nThe report sets out the surviving documentary evidence, the compressed\nemergency process of December 1988, the independent professional record\n(including the H.J. Thomas RCAHMW survey and post-demolition notes), and\ntwenty specific questions arising from Cadw’s own disclosures. It does not\nassert criminal wrongdoing; it identifies material evidential gaps and\nrequests administrative accountability.\n\nI respectfully request that the addressed bodies:\n\nProvide a full account of the 1988 processes, answering the questions in\nSection 8 of the report so far as records and institutional knowledge\npermit.\n\nConfirm whether the H.J. Thomas RCAHMW survey was held, accessed or\nconsidered.\n\nIssue a public statement acknowledging the record-keeping gap for an\nirreversible heritage decision.\n\nConsider formal administrative acknowledgement of process deficiencies and\nappropriate annotation of the National Heritage List / Coflein / HER\nentries.\n\nPreserve and accession remaining material, including the two July 1988\nphotographs.\n\nI ask Vale of Glamorgan Council to disclose any surviving records relating\nto Building Preservation Notice consideration in November–December 1988,\nand RCAHMW / HER custodians to update the relevant entries to reflect the\nindependent professional evidence and the missing Cadw assessment record.\n\nI look forward to your substantive response within a reasonable timeframe.\nPlease cooperate in this matter. Our family have been heavily displaced,\ndispossessed and justice delayed/ denied for decades. Having already taken\nit to ECHR all avenues for recourse appeared to have expired. That was\nuntil I discovered, what I believe to be, fraud and consealment. Which is\nwhy I am calling for this case to be reopened, revisted and investigated by\nlocal authorities as a matter of public interest.\n\nAs it stands with this case the law has become a monument to injustice, as\nthe practical application of property law resulted in the inhumane\ntreatment of my family. And for authority to be authority, legitimacy is\nparamount. And I question a lot of the legitimacy in the decisions and\nactions of the authorities in this matter. I seek in good faith to remedy\nthis entire matter so that it can be put behind us all. And so that the\naccount of what happened at that location, is accurate and no longer\nremains so inaccuracte, fragmented and concealsed.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 09:10 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for your email, apologies for the delay in responding I have\n> been on annual leave. To answer your queries I must refer you back to my\n> previous emails of the 10th 3rd and 2nd July.\n>\n>\n>\n> I appreciate your concerns and desires to find the information. However, I\n> can confirm that all records were checked for the information you requested\n> and we hold no further information or a record of the destruction. Cadw’s\n> inspector advised, based on his experience, that he understood the practice\n> was to either transfer records to the RCAHMW or destroy them under the\n> Public Records Act 1958. We have no record of any transfer lists, accession\n> records, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records\n> relating to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW.  The\n> photograph provides the only documentary evidence that Great House Farm was\n> visited by Cadw and did not meet the criteria as it was not included on the\n> list.\n>\n>\n>\n> To be clear, we do not have any further information which would help with\n> your search for the relevant information. If you remain dissatisfied with\n> this response you have the right to complain to the Information\n> Commissioner. The Information Commissioner can be contacted at:\n>\n> Information Commissioner’s Office,\n>\n> Wycliffe House,\n>\n> Water Lane,\n>\n> Wilmslow,\n>\n> Cheshire,\n>\n> [postcode redacted].\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 15 July 2026 18:28\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Ms Longford,\n>\n> Before responding to my earlier email, please may I add the following to\n> my enquiry, even if you require addition time to respond due to this\n> addition to my enquiry;\n>\n> In addition to my email of 2 July, there are a small number of further\n> points which I would be grateful if you could address as they arise\n> directly from comparing the original response with the internal review.\n>\n> The original response of 11 June 2026 stated:\n>\n> \"Any other associated records would have been either transferred to the\n> Royal Commission on the Ancient & Historical Monuments of Wales for\n> permanent preservation, or destroyed under the Public Record Act 1958.\"\n>\n> However, the internal review of 2 July 2026 states instead that:\n>\n> \"There is also no evidence that any relevant files have been transferred\n> to the RCAHMW.\"\n>\n> and\n>\n> \"It is possible that the file was destroyed before it was ever updated on\n> our electronic filing system.\"\n>\n> These appear to be materially different positions.\n>\n> Accordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n>\n>    1. What evidence supported the original statement that any associated\n>    records would have been transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the\n>    Public Records Act 1958?\n>    2. Following the internal review, does Welsh Government now accept\n>    that there is no evidence that any relevant records were transferred to the\n>    RCAHMW?\n>    3. Does Welsh Government hold any transfer lists, accession records,\n>    archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating\n>    to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW?\n>    4. If no such documentation exists, on what evidential basis was the\n>    original statement regarding transfer to the RCAHMW made?\n>    5. Likewise, if there is no destruction register, disposal log or\n>    audit trail relating to the relevant file, on what evidential basis has\n>    destruction been suggested?\n>\n> Finally, the original response stated as fact that Great House Farm was\n> visited by Cadw inspectors and did not meet the statutory listing criteria.\n> The internal review, however, confirms that no assessment, report or case\n> file has been located.\n>\n> Could you therefore identify the documentary evidence upon which that\n> conclusion was based, or alternatively confirm whether the statement in the\n> original response was an inference drawn from the existence of the two\n> photographs rather than from any surviving assessment records.\n>\n> These points are intended simply to clarify the historical record and to\n> reconcile what appear to be two materially different explanations contained\n> within the original response and the internal review.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance, and I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n>\n>  & Life Member\n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 23:41 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> 👍🏻\n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will\n> review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17\n> th July.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 21:01\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review\n> of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House\n> Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> I appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the\n> explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n>\n> However, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and\n> the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could\n> clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n>\n> *1. Documentary basis of the original response*\n>\n> The original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and\n> assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the\n> statutory listing criteria.\n>\n> The internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file\n> relating to that decision has been located and further states that any\n> relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the\n> electronic records system.\n>\n> Please therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original\n> response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the\n> listing criteria.\n>\n> Specifically:\n>\n>    - Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n>    - If so, please identify that record.\n>    - If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n>\n> *2. The inspection of 29 July 1988*\n>\n> The original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n>\n> Please confirm:\n>\n>    - whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing\n>    inspection;\n>    - whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n>    - whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks,\n>    photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n>    - if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have\n>    been destroyed.\n>\n> *3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed*\n>\n> The review states that it is possible documentation dating from around\n> 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n>\n> Please clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n>\n>    - documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n>    - records management documentation such as retention schedules,\n>    destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n>    - a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n>\n> If no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please\n> confirm this.\n>\n> *4. Scope of the searches*\n>\n> Please confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing\n> files to include, where appropriate:\n>\n>    - ministerial correspondence;\n>    - senior officials' correspondence;\n>    - legal files;\n>    - inspector's working papers;\n>    - site visit records;\n>    - archaeological or conservation files;\n>    - policy records; and\n>    - correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of\n>    Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n>\n> If any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you\n> could identify which.\n>\n> *5. Welsh Government's position*\n>\n> Finally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's\n> position regarding Great House Farm.\n>\n> Does the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n>\n>    - that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n>    - that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n>    - that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration\n>    took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n>\n> If none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful if\n> you could explain what the Welsh Government's position is.\n>\n> These questions arise directly from the original response and the internal\n> review and are intended to clarify the historical record rather than seek\n> the creation of new information.\n>\n> I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:10 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Please see attached my review of your request noted ATISN 27021.\n>\n> Please let me know if you have any questions or queries.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy Longford\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 June 2026 09:10\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> I suspected so.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thanks Amy.\n>\n>\n>\n> I look forward.\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Tue, 16 Jun 2026, 05:08 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the quick response and for confirming your position. I\n> totally understand and whilst the letters may appear formal, there are set\n> templates to use for a review, I will bear this in mind whilst taking this\n> forward.\n>\n>\n>\n> Just to let you know, I have had initial conversations internally which I\n> will continue. I will keep you updated as best as I can.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 June 2026 05:38\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for the acknowledgement letter and for handling the internal\n> review.\n>\n> For the record, my communications with Cadw have been enquiries and\n> requests for information under FOI/EIR (ATISN 27021), specifically\n> regarding the statutory listing history, assessments and related records\n> (including the 1988 inspection photographs) for the building known as Great\n> House Farm / Ty Mawr / Church View Close. I subsequently requested an\n> internal review of the response provided.\n>\n> This was not framed or intended as a formal complaint. I would therefore\n> be grateful if the matter could be treated and recorded as an information\n> request and internal review under FOI/EIR, rather than as a complaint.\n>\n> My enquiries concern Cadw's functions in relation to the listing and\n> assessment of the building only.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n\n>\n> Life Member: Royal Corps of Signals\n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, 15 Jun 2026, 12:44 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for your email requesting an internal review of you EOI\n> request, I will be the case officer dealing with the review, please see the\n> attached acknowledgement letter with key dates. Any questions, please let\n> me know and I will do my best to help.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd yn\n> esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich\n> preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb\n> yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg\n> yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this\n> email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the\n> protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Gover