omorrow to\nresearch Great House Farm (Ty Mawr/Cedfin/Cydfin), Llandough, and our\nWilliams and Buckler family history. If possible, I would be very grateful\nif the following material could be prepared in advance.\n\nI appreciate that some references below may relate to connected collections\nor require confirmation of the correct repository. Where a reference is not\nheld by Glamorgan Archives, we would be grateful if you could advise\nwhether you hold any related material, copies, cross-references or\ncatalogue information, or direct us to the appropriate repository.\n\nThe records requested are as follows:\n\n   - DB/E/1–2 – David Stewart survey of the Marquess of Bute's Glamorgan\n   estates, including Great House Farm alias Cedfin, Llandough, together with\n   any related maps or accompanying material.\n   - D160/1–4 – Agreements between Lambert Williams and the Bute Estate\n   (1818–1835).\n   - Any copies, related material or cross-references connected with NLW\n   D219 (Llandough manorial leases and agreements, including Ty Mawr/Cydfin\n   references).\n   - D153/4–8 – Records relating to the 1876 severance of land formerly\n   part of Great House Farm for Llandough Limeworks, including associated\n   plans.\n   - DSA/6/701 – Parts of the Llandough Estate, 9 October 1924.\n   - DSA/6/1158 – Great House Farm, Llandough, 15 November 1938, including\n   sale particulars, plans and associated papers.\n   - GD/LA/15/255 – Great House Farm sale particulars (1938), if held.\n   - DXJF/64/27–32, including DXJF/64/30–32 – Nancy Buckler / Nancy Buckler\n   Williams sketch and notes of the former layout of Llandough.\n   - DCOWHS material containing references to the Buckler family.\n   - DBDT catalogue reference relating to the July 1877 counterpart lease\n   from the Trustees of the late Marquess of Bute to John Williams, if held.\n   - Cardiff Rural District Council records relating to Great House Farm or\n   Ty Mawr.\n   - CVG/C/1/52.\n   - DCVG/PL planning records relating to Great House Farm, demolition,\n   redevelopment or Church View Close.\n   - Any relevant DRA records, including DRA 418–420 or DRA 5/31.\n   - UDPE/S/1/68 – Original four plans and accompanying documents.\n   - Any estate maps, sale plans, surveys, tithe maps, OS maps or boundary\n   plans showing Great House Farm/Ty Mawr.\n   - Any records relating to Western Ground Rents Ltd, Mountjoy Ltd, BP\n   Pension Trust Ltd, BP Properties Ltd, or any leases, conveyances, rent\n   books, tenancy agreements, possession records or related correspondence\n   concerning Great House Farm and the Williams/Buckler family.\n\nIf any of the above records contain associated bundles, schedules,\nenclosures, oversized plans or documents stored separately from the\nprincipal reference, we would be grateful if these could also be identified.\n\nWe would also appreciate advice as to whether Glamorgan Archives holds any\nuncatalogued or recently deposited material relating to Great House Farm,\nTy Mawr, the above families, or the ownership and occupation history of the\nsite between 1875 and 1988.\n\nMy reader's ticket number is *2004093*.\n\nThank you very much for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nRequester \n\nOn Wed, 5 Aug 2026, 07:04 Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> 2026/3309\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> As you are requesting information relating to records held at the National\n> Library of Wales, you will need to contact the Library directly.  Contact\n> details can be found here\n> <https://www.library.wales/about-nlw/about-us/contact-us>.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Rhian Diggins\n>\n> Uwch Archifydd / Senior Archivist\n>\n>\n>\n> Archifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 27 July 2026 18:56\n> *To:* Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Mo