n>"},{"id":"gm-19fd161c3adc555d","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-08-05T10:04:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fd161c3adc555d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa4b5a70ee940a-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa4b5a70ee940a","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fd161c3adc555d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"2026/3309\n\nDear Requester.\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nAs you are requesting information relating to records held at the National Library of Wales, you will need to contact the Library directly.  Contact details can be found here .\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRhian Diggins [cid:image001.jpg@01DD24CA.2E3D0E90]\nUwch Archifydd / Senior Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] \nhttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 27 July 2026 18:56\nTo: Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg  \nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\nALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded information held by the National Library of Wales:\nAny manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\nAny estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings) that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\nAny catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the family’s holding at this property.\nPlease confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state the exemption(s) relied upon.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19fd081a42485a6e","subject":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","name":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","date":"2026-08-05T05:59:44Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fd081a42485a6e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fd081a42485a6e-new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-from-the-williams-buckler-family","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fd081a42485a6e","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fd081a42485a6e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request '1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family' that you made to Ministry of Defence.\n\nTo view the response, click on the link below.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/1988_dispossession_of_great_hous?nocache=incoming-3507980#incoming-3507980\n\nWhen you get there, please update the status to say if the response contains any useful information.\n\nAlthough all responses are automatically published, we depend on you, the original requester, to evaluate them.\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhatDoTheyKnow is a project of mySociety run by a small team of staff and\ndedicated volunteers.\n\nmySociety is a charity that believes that information should be accessible to everyone.\nIf this is important to you, please consider donating to help us do more:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/donate\n\nFind out more about how we handle your data at:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/help/privacy\n\nmySociety is a registered charity in England and Wales (1076346), and a limited\ncompany (03277032)"},{"id":"gm-19fcf6f5f7a5a80a","subject":"Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request – Historical Court Records and Administrative Records Relating to William (\"Billy\") Buckler (1988–1989)","name":"Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request – Historical Court Records and Administrative Records Relating to William (\"Billy\") Buckler (1988–1989)","date":"2026-08-05T01:00:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fcf6f5f7a5a80a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fcf68c9ca9324b-freedom-of-information-act-2000-request-historical-court-records-and-administrative-records-relating-to-william-billy-bu","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fcf68c9ca9324b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fcf6f5f7a5a80a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir/Madam,\n\nThis is a separate Freedom of Information request under the Freedom of\nInformation Act 2000.\n\nIt is distinct from my earlier request under your reference 260607013\n(submitted 7 June 2026), which concerned the location and access options\nfor historical court records relating to Great House Farm, Mary\nWilliams/Buckler, Western Ground Rents and BP (focusing on the 1915, 1955\nand 1962 possession proceedings and title/equitable interest evidence).\n\nThis new request is limited solely to records of the hearing (or hearings)\nat Barry Magistrates Court in late January 1989 at which the Crown\nProsecution Service withdrew the charge arising from the allegation of 29\nApril 1988 as being “out of time.”\n\nI write under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 to request recorded\ninformation relating to criminal proceedings involving *William Beverly\n(\"Billy\") Buckler* arising from events connected with the eviction and\ndemolition of *Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan*,\nduring 1988–1989.\n\nI am seeking administrative and recorded information concerning the\nhandling of these proceedings, rather than personal data contained within\nindividual case files.\n\nSpecifically, I request copies of, or access to, any recorded information\nheld concerning:\n\n   1.\n\n   The prosecution in which a charge dating from *29 April 1988* alleging\n   threatening words or behaviour was withdrawn because the proceedings were\n   considered *\"out of time.\"*\n   2.\n\n   Any records identifying:\n   - the court in which that decision was made;\n      - the date of the hearing;\n      - the prosecutor involved (reported contemporaneously as *Mr Jeff\n      Clarke*);\n      - the legal basis upon which the summons was determined to be out of\n      time.\n   3.\n\n   Records relating to Billy Buckler's appearances before the courts\nduring *January–March\n   1989*, including any surviving:\n   - cause lists;\n      - court registers;\n      - hearing lists;\n      - minute books;\n      - court log books;\n      - bench records;\n      - administrative case records;\n      - listing records;\n      - prosecution correspondence;\n      - disposal records; or similar recorded information.\n   4.\n\n   Records concerning the proceedings heard in *Cardiff on or about 23\n   March 1989*, including recorded information showing:\n   - the charges before the court;\n      - which charges were proceeded with;\n      - which charges were withdrawn or discontinued;\n      - the sentence imposed;\n      - any recorded fine;\n      - any credit given for time already spent in custody.\n   5.\n\n   Records concerning charges arising from the *November 1988 eviction of\n   Great House Farm*, including allegations of assault and wanton and\n   furious driving.\n   6.\n\n   Any recorded information concerning:\n   - remand or custody records;\n      - warrants;\n      - bail conditions;\n      - injunction-related court administration;\n      - any order restricting Billy Buckler from approaching Great House\n      Farm.\n   7.\n\n   Any retention, destruction or disposal records relating to the above\n   court files, including:\n   - destruction schedules;\n      - retention schedules;\n      - disposal certificates;\n      - archive transfer records;\n      - accession records;\n      - file movement records;\n      - records identifying when and under what authority any files were\n      destroyed or transferred.\n   8.\n\n   Any file references, case numbers, register entries or archive\n   references relating to these proceedings, even where the substantive files\n   no longer survive.\n\nIf any of the requested information has been transferred to another body,\nsuch as the relevant archive service or another part of HM Courts &\nTribunals Service or the Ministry of Justice, please identify the receiving\nbody and any known reference numbers.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please specify the exemption relied upon,\nexplain why it applies, and disclose all reasonably segregable information.\n\nIf some parts of this request are more readily available than others, I\nwould be grateful if those could be disclosed without waiting for the\nremainder.\n\nRegards,\n\n\nRequester \n\n"},{"id":"gm-19fcdd76e23e36ee","subject":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-08-04T17:34:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fcdd76e23e36ee.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fcdd76e23e36ee.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Owen,\n\nThank you for your email of 4 August 2026 and for confirming that a search\nof your internal case management system has been carried out with no\nresults identified.\n\nMy request was not limited to whether records are currently held on that\nsystem. It also sought confirmation of what searches (if any) were made of\nhistorical paper records, indexes and finding aids, and what became of the\ncourt records relating to the proceedings I identified.\n\nYou state that, due to the age of the case, the court would not currently\nhold records \"in line with our procedures.\" I should be grateful if you\nwould clarify the basis for that statement by addressing the following\npoints:\n\n   1.\n\n   What is the precise name of the internal case management system that was\n   searched, and what period of records does it cover?\n   2.\n\n   Were any surviving paper finding aids or historical records examined,\n   including cause books, order books, registers of judgments or orders,\n   warrant books, index cards, or any other historical indexes maintained by\n   Cardiff County Court, Cardiff Civil Justice Centre, or their predecessors?\n   3.\n\n   Were any archived or off-site repositories under HMCTS control\n   considered or searched?\n   4.\n\n   Please identify the records retention, disposal or archival policy,\n   schedule or instruction relied upon in concluding that records of this age\n   would no longer be held. I note that the current publicly available County\n   Court Records Retention and Disposition Schedule specifies relatively short\n   retention periods for possession action cases. I should therefore be\n   grateful if you could identify the historical policy, schedule or\n   instruction that governed the records relating to these proceedings and, if\n   possible, indicate when they would have been scheduled for destruction or\n   transfer.\n   5.\n\n   Does HMCTS hold any administrative record of the destruction or transfer\n   of the relevant files, such as destruction registers, certificates,\n   transfer schedules or equivalent records?\n   6.\n\n   Were any records relating to these proceedings transferred to another\n   repository, including The National Archives, Glamorgan Archives, or any\n   other archive? If so, I should be grateful if you would provide the\n   destination, date and any available reference.\n   7.\n\n   Even if the original case files no longer survive, do any registers,\n   indexes or other administrative records remain recording the existence,\n   progress or disposal of proceedings involving the Williams family, the\n   Buckler family, Western Ground Rents Ltd, BP Pension Trust Ltd, BP\n   Properties Ltd, or Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough?\n\nThe proceedings in question include the High Court possession proceedings\nof 1955 (including enforcement on or around 4 July 1955), the Cardiff\nCounty Court proceedings culminating in the possession order of 11 December\n1962 before Judge Temple Morris QC, and the Cardiff County Court\nproceedings of 1974, including the part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974, the\napplication for leave to enforce in September 1974, and the subsequent\ncorrespondence concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement.\n\nI have already been making enquiries of HM Land Registry. However, my\npresent request concerns the court's own records, the searches undertaken\nin relation to those records, and any surviving administrative record of\ntheir retention, destruction or transfer.\n\nIf the information requested is not held within the Enforcement Section, I\nshould be grateful if this enquiry could be forwarded to the appropriate\ncourt manager, records officer or other HMCTS team responsible for\nhistorical court records, and if you could kindly confirm that this has\nbeen done.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to your substantive reply\naddressing each of the points above.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n[address redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]\n\nOn Tue, 4 Aug 2026, 09:43 Cardiff County, Enquiries, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> Due to the age of this case, we wouldn’t currently hold any existing\n> records for it, in line with our procedures. I can confirm we have\n> conducted a search on our internal case management system, which has not\n> produced any results. We are not privy to any other systems upon which we\n> could conduct a search on the details you provide.\n>\n>\n>\n> It might be worth contacting Land Registry to see if they hold any details\n> on this:\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry Citizen Centre\n>\n> PO Box74\n>\n> Gloucester\n>\n> [postcode redacted]\n>\n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n>\n> Phoebe Owen\n>\n>\n>\n> Administration Officer\n>\n> Adran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\n>\n> Canolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd | 2 Stryd Y Parc | Caerdydd | [postcode redacted]\n>\n> Cardiff Civil Justice Centre | 2 Park Street | Cardiff\n> [map link redacted]\n> | [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 03 August 2026 21:01\n> *To:* Cardiff County, Enquiries <\n> [email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n>\n>\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I wrote to you on 10 June 2026 requesting access to historical court\n> records relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of\n> Glamorgan. I have not received a response.\n>\n> I am seeking confirmation of whether any surviving court records exist\n> relating to possession, title, and related proceedings involving the\n> Williams / Buckler family and the successive parties asserting title\n> through Western Ground Rents Ltd and subsequently BP Pension Trust Ltd / BP\n> Properties Ltd.\n>\n> The proceedings and related matters I am seeking to identify include:\n>\n>    - High Court possession proceedings and the possession order of 1955,\n>    including any related enforcement records (including the enforcement action\n>    concerning the agricultural land on or around 4 July 1955);\n>    - Cardiff County Court proceedings of 1962, resulting in the\n>    possession order dated 11 December 1962 (before Judge Temple Morris QC),\n>    including any related claim for mesne profits;\n>    - Cardiff County Court proceedings commenced in 1974, including the\n>    part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974 at which Mary Williams asserted ownership\n>    and relied upon adverse possession / limitation arguments, the application\n>    for leave to enforce in September 1974, and subsequent correspondence\n>    concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement in October and\n>    November 1974;\n>    - The subsequent Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v\n>    Buckler [1987] 55 P & CR 337.\n>\n> I request confirmation of whether any surviving records remain, including\n> (but not limited to):\n>\n>    - pleadings;\n>    - statements of case;\n>    - orders;\n>    - warrants;\n>    - correspondence;\n>    - exhibits;\n>    - judgments;\n>    - case files;\n>    - registers or indexes referring to these proceedings or the property.\n>\n> If records remain, please advise the procedure for obtaining copies or\n> arranging inspection, including any applicable fees.\n>\n> If no records remain, please confirm what searches have been undertaken,\n> which repositories or record systems have been checked, and whether any\n> destruction, retention, or transfer records exist relating to these\n> proceedings.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n> [address redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [location redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [email redacted]\n> ------------------------------\n> This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the\n> addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not\n> permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies\n> and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure\n> medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone\n> else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in\n> response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender\n> or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry\n> of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content\n> may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not\n> broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fcd855ebb650b6","subject":"The National Archives Satisfaction Survey","name":"The National Archives Satisfaction Survey","date":"2026-08-04T16:04:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fcd855ebb650b6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fcd855ebb650b6-the-national-archives-satisfaction-survey","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fcd855ebb650b6","direction":"received","from":"The National Archives Survey","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-344122"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fcd855ebb650b6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Your Views Satisfaction Survey \n \n \n \n                                       Hello  Requester* Buckler \n Please click the following link to complete the survey about your enquiry \n Email sent to ICO - Buckler vs United Kingdom \n  which has our reference  \n CAS-344122-V1D0G3 \n \n \n \n START SURVEY \n \n \n \n   \n Customer Service and Complaints Team \n     W:  nationalarchives.gov.uk \nTwitter: @UkNatArchives \nThe National Archives, Kew, Richmond, Surrey [postcode redacted] \n Or copy paste the URL below into your internet browser. \n https://emea.dcv.ms/lgc2hyd30s \n \n \n This is a system generated email, please do not reply to it. The survey link in this email is unique to its recipient. Please do not forward this email. If you would like to unsubscribe and stop receiving these emails, click  unsubscribe ."},{"id":"gm-19fccccd723ad697","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-08-04T12:43:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fccccd723ad697.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa","direction":"received","from":"Cardiff County, Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fccccd723ad697.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nDue to the age of this case, we wouldn’t currently hold any existing records for it, in line with our procedures. I can confirm we have conducted a search on our internal case management system, which has not produced any results. We are not privy to any other systems upon which we could conduct a search on the details you provide.\n\nIt might be worth contacting Land Registry to see if they hold any details on this:\n\n\nHM Land Registry Citizen Centre\nPO Box74\nGloucester\n[postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\n\nThank you.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nPhoebe Owen\n\nAdministration Officer\nAdran Gorfodi / Enforcement Section\nCanolfan Llysoedd Sifil Caerdydd | 2 Stryd Y Parc | Caerdydd | [postcode redacted]\nCardiff Civil Justice Centre | 2 Park Street | Cardiff  | [postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 03 August 2026 21:01\nTo: Cardiff County, Enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff\n\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI wrote to you on 10 June 2026 requesting access to historical court records relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan. I have not received a response.\n\nI am seeking confirmation of whether any surviving court records exist relating to possession, title, and related proceedings involving the Williams / Buckler family and the successive parties asserting title through Western Ground Rents Ltd and subsequently BP Pension Trust Ltd / BP Properties Ltd.\n\nThe proceedings and related matters I am seeking to identify include:\n\n  *   High Court possession proceedings and the possession order of 1955, including any related enforcement records (including the enforcement action concerning the agricultural land on or around 4 July 1955);\n  *   Cardiff County Court proceedings of 1962, resulting in the possession order dated 11 December 1962 (before Judge Temple Morris QC), including any related claim for mesne profits;\n  *   Cardiff County Court proceedings commenced in 1974, including the part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974 at which Mary Williams asserted ownership and relied upon adverse possession / limitation arguments, the application for leave to enforce in September 1974, and subsequent correspondence concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement in October and November 1974;\n  *   The subsequent Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] 55 P & CR 337.\n\nI request confirmation of whether any surviving records remain, including (but not limited to):\n\n  *   pleadings;\n  *   statements of case;\n  *   orders;\n  *   warrants;\n  *   correspondence;\n  *   exhibits;\n  *   judgments;\n  *   case files;\n  *   registers or indexes referring to these proceedings or the property.\n\nIf records remain, please advise the procedure for obtaining copies or arranging inspection, including any applicable fees.\n\nIf no records remain, please confirm what searches have been undertaken, which repositories or record systems have been checked, and whether any destruction, retention, or transfer records exist relating to these proceedings.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n\nRequester \n\n[address redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-19fc9371a7c7b307","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-08-03T20:00:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc9371a7c7b307.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc9358eecc11aa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc9371a7c7b307.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Madam,\n\nI wrote to you on 10 June 2026 requesting access to historical court\nrecords relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of\nGlamorgan. I have not received a response.\n\nI am seeking confirmation of whether any surviving court records exist\nrelating to possession, title, and related proceedings involving the\nWilliams / Buckler family and the successive parties asserting title\nthrough Western Ground Rents Ltd and subsequently BP Pension Trust Ltd / BP\nProperties Ltd.\n\nThe proceedings and related matters I am seeking to identify include:\n\n   -\n\n   High Court possession proceedings and the possession order of 1955,\n   including any related enforcement records (including the enforcement action\n   concerning the agricultural land on or around 4 July 1955);\n   -\n\n   Cardiff County Court proceedings of 1962, resulting in the possession\n   order dated 11 December 1962 (before Judge Temple Morris QC), including any\n   related claim for mesne profits;\n   -\n\n   Cardiff County Court proceedings commenced in 1974, including the\n   part-heard hearing of 3 July 1974 at which Mary Williams asserted ownership\n   and relied upon adverse possession / limitation arguments, the application\n   for leave to enforce in September 1974, and subsequent correspondence\n   concerning the proposed unilateral licence arrangement in October and\n   November 1974;\n   -\n\n   The subsequent Court of Appeal proceedings in BP Properties Ltd v\n   Buckler [1987] 55 P & CR 337.\n\nI request confirmation of whether any surviving records remain, including\n(but not limited to):\n\n   - pleadings;\n   - statements of case;\n   - orders;\n   - warrants;\n   - correspondence;\n   - exhibits;\n   - judgments;\n   - case files;\n   - registers or indexes referring to these proceedings or the property.\n\nIf records remain, please advise the procedure for obtaining copies or\narranging inspection, including any applicable fees.\n\nIf no records remain, please confirm what searches have been undertaken,\nwhich repositories or record systems have been checked, and whether any\ndestruction, retention, or transfer records exist relating to these\nproceedings.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nRequester \n\n\n[address redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fc87529c174081","subject":"Re: FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-08-03T16:29:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc87529c174081.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa-foi-2026-020-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc87529c174081.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear FOI Team,\n\nThank you for your response.\n\nI note your position that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold recorded\ninformation within the scope of my request.\n\nHowever, I would be grateful if you could clarify the searches undertaken\nto reach that conclusion.\n\nIn particular, please confirm:\n\n   - Which collections management systems, databases and \"associated\n   records\" were searched.\n   - Whether searches extended beyond accessioned objects to include\n   acquisition files, provenance files, curator correspondence, donor files,\n   temporary custody records, unaccessioned material, photographs and\n   administrative records.\n   - The search terms used (for example: \"Great House Farm\", \"Ty Mawr\",\n   \"Llandough\", \"Williams\", \"Buckler\", \"Bute Estate\" and any other relevant\n   variants).\n   - Whether any potentially relevant records have been transferred to\n   another institution or destroyed in accordance with a retention policy.\n\nMy original request was not limited to identifying surviving objects. It\nalso sought records relating to their provenance, acquisition, transfer,\nownership, photographs and correspondence. This reflects the fact that the\ncontents of Great House Farm may have been dispersed following the\nproperty's demolition, meaning relevant records could exist even if no\nobjects were ultimately accessioned by the Museum.\n\nIf, following those searches, Amgueddfa Cymru remains satisfied that no\nrecorded information is held, I would be grateful for confirmation of that\nposition.\n\nFinally, if you are aware of another public authority that is more likely\nto hold records falling within the scope of my request, I would appreciate\nyour advice in accordance with your duty to provide advice and assistance.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 3 Aug 2026, 10:39 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your request for information received on 2nd July 2026,\n> concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other\n> movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> Following searches of the Museum's collections management systems and\n> associated records, Amgueddfa Cymru has not identified any furniture,\n> furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms or other movable property\n> recorded as originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> Accordingly, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold recorded information falling\n> within the scope of items 1 to 9 of your request relating to such objects.\n>\n> For clarity:\n>\n>    - We have not identified any objects of the type described in your\n>    request as originating from Great House Farm.\n>    - We have not identified inventories, catalogues, acquisition records,\n>    disposal records, loan records, provenance files, ownership records,\n>    photographs, correspondence, reports, memoranda or related records\n>    concerning such objects within the scope of your request.\n>    - We have not identified any records relating to the identification,\n>    recovery, ownership or location of furniture or household effects from\n>    Great House Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n> We note your references to archaeological material from land associated\n> with Great House Farm. However, archaeological finds are outside the scope\n> of this response because they do not fall within your request for\n> furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable\n> property. We understand that archaeological material is the subject of a\n> separate information request and will be dealt with separately.\n>\n>\n>\n> Under section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response\n> is therefore that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 20:51\n> *To:* [email redacted]\n> *Cc:* [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI Requests <\n> [email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> National Library of Wales <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff\n> Castle Furniture\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fc87049b7e047c","subject":"Re: Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","name":"Re: Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","date":"2026-08-03T16:23:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc87049b7e047c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47-follow-up-foi-eir-case-ref-00211027-llandough-primary-school","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211027"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc87049b7e047c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nThank you for your response.\n\nMy query regarding the substantive FOI/EIR request is separate from my\nrequest for the identity of the officer who acknowledged my correspondence.\n\nI asked for the name of the officer who sent the acknowledgement email.\nYour reply does not answer that request. Instead, it refers to the team's\ngeneral practice of issuing correspondence collectively.\n\nIf the information is held and you are refusing to disclose it, please\nissue a formal refusal notice identifying the relevant statutory basis for\nwithholding it and advising me of my review rights.\n\nIf no individual officer's name is recorded or held in relation to the\nacknowledgement, please confirm that expressly.\n\nOtherwise, please provide the information requested.\n\nI look forward to your response.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Mon, 3 Aug 2026, 12:02 FOI Unit, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> Our apologies that you did not receive a response to your email requesting\n> the name of the officer who had acknowledged your request. We have\n> previously advised that due to the Information Governance Team working\n> collaboratively, and requests being managed collectively across the team,\n> rather than by individual officers. Correspondence is not issued under\n> individual names.\n>\n>\n>\n> In regards to this request, we are still working on it. Your request was\n> received on 13 July 2026 therefore, the 20 working days timeframe has not\n> yet elapsed. We aim to respond no later than 10 August 2026 and will write\n> to you as soon as possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Information Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\n>\n> Director's Office - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\n>\n> tel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\n>\n> e-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you\n> really need to.*\n>\n> *Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod\n> gwir angen.*\n>\n>\n>\n> Visit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n>\n> Ewch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n> <https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\n>\n> Follow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n> <http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n>\n>\n>\n> Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 01 August 2026 16:25\n> *To:* FOI Unit <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary\n> School)\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Information Governance Team,\n>\n>\n>\n> On 14 July 2026 you acknowledged my FOI/EIR request (Case Ref 00211027)\n> concerning the acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School.\n>\n>\n>\n> I replied the same day asking for the name of the officer who sent the\n> acknowledgement. I have received no further response or substantive reply.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please now provide either the information requested or a formal response\n> (including any refusal notice) within 5 working days. The statutory\n> deadline has passed.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fc825d17ea5d49","subject":"RE: Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","name":"RE: Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","date":"2026-08-03T15:02:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc825d17ea5d49.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47-follow-up-foi-eir-case-ref-00211027-llandough-primary-school","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211027"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc825d17ea5d49.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nOur apologies that you did not receive a response to your email requesting the name of the officer who had acknowledged your request. We have previously advised that due to the Information Governance Team working collaboratively, and requests being managed collectively across the team, rather than by individual officers. Correspondence is not issued under individual names.\n\nIn regards to this request, we are still working on it. Your request was received on 13 July 2026 therefore, the 20 working days timeframe has not yet elapsed. We aim to respond no later than 10 August 2026 and will write to you as soon as possible.\n\nKind regards\n\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ntel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 01 August 2026 16:25\nTo: FOI Unit <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)\n\nDear Information Governance Team,\n\nOn 14 July 2026 you acknowledged my FOI/EIR request (Case Ref 00211027) concerning the acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School.\n\nI replied the same day asking for the name of the officer who sent the acknowledgement. I have received no further response or substantive reply.\n\nPlease now provide either the information requested or a formal response (including any refusal notice) within 5 working days. The statutory deadline has passed.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>"},{"id":"gm-19fc7d9d48f162aa","subject":"FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"FOI 2026-020 - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-08-03T13:39:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc7d9d48f162aa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa-foi-2026-020-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc7d9d48f162aa","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc7d9d48f162aa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your request for information received on 2nd July 2026, concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nFollowing searches of the Museum's collections management systems and associated records, Amgueddfa Cymru has not identified any furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms or other movable property recorded as originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nAccordingly, Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold recorded information falling within the scope of items 1 to 9 of your request relating to such objects.\nFor clarity:\n\n  *   We have not identified any objects of the type described in your request as originating from Great House Farm.\n  *   We have not identified inventories, catalogues, acquisition records, disposal records, loan records, provenance files, ownership records, photographs, correspondence, reports, memoranda or related records concerning such objects within the scope of your request.\n  *   We have not identified any records relating to the identification, recovery, ownership or location of furniture or household effects from Great House Farm.\n\nWe note your references to archaeological material from land associated with Great House Farm. However, archaeological finds are outside the scope of this response because they do not fall within your request for furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property. We understand that archaeological material is the subject of a separate information request and will be dealt with separately.\n\nUnder section 1(1)(a) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, our response is therefore that Amgueddfa Cymru does not hold the requested information.\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image002.png@01DD2355.40BD4100]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\namgueddfa.cymru<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/amgueddfa.cymru> | museum.wales<applewebdata://288FE56C-5BFC-474C-ADB3-A1017EF25E69/museum.wales>\n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 02 July 2026 20:51\nTo: [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI Requests <[email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; National Library of Wales <[email redacted]>\nSubject: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 Request\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items we received from Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.  Weather it be museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts from our land in Llandough.\n\nSpecifically, I request copies of all:\n\n  1.  Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n  2.  Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n  3.  Provenance files and ownership records.\n  4.  Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House Farm.\n  5.  Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership or location of such items.\n  6.  Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great House Farm furniture or household effects.\n  7.  Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in connection with these items.\n  8.  Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great House Farm.\n  9.  Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n\nFor context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still gathering actionable intelligence.\n\nI appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n\nI am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle, museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom of Information Act.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest test where required.\n\nIf another public authority is more likely to hold the requested information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or advise me accordingly.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester "},{"id":"gm-19fc7331f99b2d8b","subject":"Response to your request (our reference 260702090 - SAR)","name":"Response to your request (our reference 260702090 - SAR)","date":"2026-08-03T10:37:20Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc7331f99b2d8b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc7331f99b2d8b-sponse-to-your-request-our-reference-260702090-sar","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc7331f99b2d8b","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown)","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc7331f99b2d8b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\n\n\nPlease see the attached response to your request (our reference 260702090 - SAR).\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\nOperational Support - Knowledge and Information Liaison Officer\n\nNational Support Unit | HMCTS\n\ngov.uk/hmcts<http://www.gov.uk/hmcts>\n\n\n\n[Picture 725930249, Picture]\n\nHere is how HMCTS users your data<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter>\n\n\n\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents."},{"id":"gm-19fc40e3ff740538","subject":"FAO: Dr Driver: Aerial Discoveries & a Buried History","name":"FAO: Dr Driver: Aerial Discoveries & a Buried History","date":"2026-08-02T19:58:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc40e3ff740538.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc40b846363f4e-fao-dr-driver-aerial-discoveries-a-buried-history","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc40b846363f4e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc40e3ff740538.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dr. Driver,\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I wanted first to offer my sincere\ncongratulations to you and the RCAHMW team on your recent aerial\ndiscoveries. There is something almost magical about the way a sustained\nspell of dry, sunny weather can strip back the concealment of centuries —\nrevealing sites of profound historical importance that grass and topsoil\nhave kept hidden from view for generations. It is a powerful reminder of\nhow much of our past lies just beneath the surface, waiting for the right\nconditions to bring it back into the light.\n\nI write to you, however, about a site whose concealment has not been\nbotanical, but bureaucratic and procedural. My family’s history — that of\nGreat House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan — has been covered\nup not by grass, but by what I can only describe, with careful precision,\nas a major scandal of documentary disappearance, procedural irregularity,\nand the systematic obscuring of a separate legal title.\n\nThe farm, which stood beside St Dochdwy’s Church from at least the 13th\ncentury (and possibly as early as 1215), was home to the Williams family\nfrom 1667 and later the Buckler line. In 1876, the Bute Estate severed 33\nacres for the Llandough Limeworks. Family testimony, supported by estate\nrecords, indicates that following this severance, the farmhouse, garden and\ncurtilage may have been treated as a separate legal parcel — a freehold\ndistinct from the surrounding agricultural leasehold. Yet this distinction,\nif it existed, was progressively obscured through decades of litigation,\nmissing title deeds, and what appears to have been a conflation of two\ndistinct legal interests.\n\nBy the time of the 1987 Court of Appeal decision in BP Properties Ltd v\nBuckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2, the question of historical title had never been\njudicially determined. The court ruled on possession and the effect of a\n1974 unilateral licence on adverse possession; it did not rule on whether\nthe Williams family held a separate freehold to the farmhouse plot. The\noriginal Land Registry first-registration bundle (WA231076 / WA240304)\nremains inaccessible following an FOI refusal. The 1971 Ordnance Survey\nrecords have not been examined for descriptor shifts. And the 1667\ntransaction deed — a 999-year lease, effectively a virtual freehold — has\nnever been located.\n\nThe farm was demolished in December 1988. A 1994 rescue excavation by\nCotswold Archaeological Trust revealed 1,026 early-medieval inhumation\nburials — the largest such population yet recovered from Wales — yet the\ndemolition proceeded without archaeological condition. The RCAHMW’s own\n1974 floor plan (ST 16817331, H.W. Thomas) documented late 17th–19th\ncentury features shortly before the final litigation. LiDAR data now show\nanomalous features near the former site that may indicate a far larger\nRoman landscape than previously understood.\n\nWhat I am asking, Dr. Driver, is whether the RCAHMW — with its unique\nstatutory role in recording and protecting the historic environment of\nWales — might look again at this site, not with a drone or an aerial\ncamera, but with the same forensic attention to buried evidence that your\nteam applies to cropmarks. The grass that covers your aerial sites is\nhonest; it can be burned away by a hot summer. The concealment surrounding\nGreat House Farm is of a different order entirely — it lies in missing\ndocuments, inaccessible registries, and a litigation record that addressed\npossession while never determining title.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to share the full reconstructed chronology\n(Version 7.0) with you, and to discuss whether RCAHMW records, surveys, or\ncartographic archives might hold the key to uncovering what was truly lost\nat Llandough.\n\nWith warm regards and renewed congratulations on your aerial survey\nsuccesses,\n\n\n\nOn behalf of the Restored House of Williams / Buckler Family Estate\n\nGreat House, Manor of Llandough, Cardiff\n\n📧 [email redacted]\n\n📞 [phone redacted]\n\n---\n\nP.S. — I have attached my notes."},{"id":"gm-19fc00520f23a353","subject":"Automatic reply: Follow-up – FOI Request 719/26 (Great House Farm / 1988 Dispossession)","name":"Automatic reply: Follow-up – FOI Request 719/26 (Great House Farm / 1988 Dispossession)","date":"2026-08-02T01:09:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc00520f23a353.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fc00520f23a353-automatic-reply-follow-up-foi-request-719-26-great-house-farm-1988-dispossession","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fc00520f23a353","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc00520f23a353.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Diolch am gysylltu â'r Tîm Rhyddid Gwybodaeth yn Heddlu De Cymru. Dyma neges i gadarnhau ein bod wedi cael eich gohebiaeth. Peidiwch ag ymateb i'r neges e-bost hon.\n\nRydym yn delio â nifer mawr o geisiadau ar hyn o bryd, yn ogystal ag ôl-groniad. Er ein bod yn gwneud pob ymdrech i ymateb i geisiadau o fewn y terfyn amser o 20 diwrnod gwaith, gall fod oedi wrth ddelio â rhai o'r ceisiadau o ganlyniad i hyn.\n\nMae'n ddrwg gennym am unrhyw anghyfleustra a achoswyd.\n\nThank you for contacting the Freedom of Information (FOI) Team at South Wales Police. This message is to confirm that we have received your correspondence. Please do not reply to this email.\n\nPlease be advised that we are currently dealing with a high volume of requests as well as a backlog. Whilst we make every effort to respond to all requests within the 20 working day deadline, there may be delays in the handling some of the requests as a result.\n\nWe apologise for any inconvenience caused.\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-19fc004c0026ba19","subject":"Follow-up – FOI Request 719/26 (Great House Farm / 1988 Dispossession)","name":"Follow-up – FOI Request 719/26 (Great House Farm / 1988 Dispossession)","date":"2026-08-02T01:09:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fc004c0026ba19.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbdf07c28ad2ef-follow-up-foi-request-719-26-great-house-farm-1988-dispossession","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbdf07c28ad2ef","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["719/26"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fc004c0026ba19.json","textStatus":"available","text":"FOI Team,\nOn 16 July 2026 you issued a response to my FOI request 719/26 stating that\nno records were held.\n\nThe same day I replied requesting clarification, noting that [redacted] video footage (including ITV material) showing police presence at Llandough in\n1988 in connection with the events at Great House Farm.\n\nI have received no further reply.\nPlease now either:\n\nConfirm a further search has been conducted and provide any additional\nrecords identified, or\n\nExplain the basis on which the original “no records” response stands in\nlight of the contemporaneous video evidence.\n\nA response within 5 working days would be appreciated.\n\nSee attached some screen shots from the ITV Cymru Wales footage showing my\nmum, [member of the public], with what seems to be a South Wales Police officer (I\nthink color ID 2715), from that final confrontation/enforcement period in\nearly December 1988 (almost certainly 5–6 December).\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Army Sergeant)\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fbdedaf33b1171","subject":"Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","name":"Follow-up – FOI/EIR Case Ref 00211027 (Llandough Primary School)","date":"2026-08-01T15:24:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fbdedaf33b1171.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47-follow-up-foi-eir-case-ref-00211027-llandough-primary-school","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbdeca9328ad47","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00211027"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fbdedaf33b1171.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Governance Team,\n\nOn 14 July 2026 you acknowledged my FOI/EIR request (Case Ref 00211027)\nconcerning the acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School.\n\nI replied the same day asking for the name of the officer who sent the\nacknowledgement. I have received no further response or substantive reply.\n\nPlease now provide either the information requested or a formal response\n(including any refusal notice) within 5 working days. The statutory\ndeadline has passed.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fbdec2253d70c5","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-08-01T15:23:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fbdec2253d70c5.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbdeb4b1e102b8-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbdeb4b1e102b8","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fbdec2253d70c5.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Governance Team,\n\nOn 7 July 2026 I requested an internal review of the Council’s response to\nmy Environmental Information Regulations request (Case Ref 00210772).\nYou acknowledged this on 10 July 2026 and stated you were reviewing my\nconcerns and would be in touch further as soon as possible.\n\nOver 20 working days have now passed with no further update or decision.\nPlease provide the outcome of the internal review, or a clear timescale for\nwhen it will be issued, within 5 working days.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fbdeab0292488c","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough FOI","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough FOI","date":"2026-08-01T15:21:41Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fbdeab0292488c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fbde9f8e40e11e-great-house-farm-llandough-foi","scopeTopics":["dwrcymru"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dwrcymru"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fbde9f8e40e11e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"dwrcymru","name":"Dwr Cymru Welsh Water"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fbdeab0292488c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Governance Team,\n\nI wrote to you on 20 June 2026 requesting recorded information held by Dŵr\nCymru relating to water supply accounts, billing history, and\ncorrespondence concerning Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\nMore than 40 days have now passed with no acknowledgement or response.\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 / Environmental Information\nRegulations 2004, a response is required within 20 working days.\n\nPlease confirm receipt of my original request and provide either:\n\nThe information requested, or\nA formal refusal notice with the reasons and your internal review details.\n\nI look forward to your reply within 5 working days.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester\n[email redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fb8ffbdbe5e1d9","subject":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-31T16:26:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb8ffbdbe5e1d9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb8ffbdbe5e1d9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Mathilde,\n\nThank you for clarifying the search methodology. Your explanation is\nhelpful, particularly the distinction between records appearing in the\nPostal Museum catalogue and records physically held at BT Archives.\n\nBefore I proceed to BT Archives, I would like to make sure I understand the\nlimits of the search correctly and avoid unnecessarily duplicating it.\n\nThere are a few further points which I would be grateful if you could\nclarify.\n\n*1. Date range*\n\nWas the search for the various names and locations conducted across the\nsurrounding period, or was material effectively assessed only against the\n1897 demonstration?\n\nCould you confirm whether *1895–1900*, including 1896, 1898, 1899 and 1900,\nwas searched?\n\nThis is important because I am investigating not only the demonstration\nitself but also possible preparations beforehand and correspondence or\nreports afterwards.\n\n*2. Catalogue results which were considered unrelated*\n\nYou mentioned that some results appeared for terms including Penarth,\nwireless demonstrations, GPO Telegraph Department, Engineering Department\nand Williams, but that they were considered unrelated after examination of\ntheir catalogue descriptions.\n\nWould it be possible to provide the *catalogue reference numbers and\ndescriptions of those records*, even where you consider them unrelated,\ntogether with the reason they were excluded?\n\nI would prefer to examine those references myself rather than inadvertently\noverlooking something that may become relevant when considered alongside\nother records.\n\n*3. Scope of the catalogue*\n\nYou have explained that the physical archives were not separately checked\nbecause the information is recorded on the archival cataloguing system.\n\nCould you confirm whether this means that *all existing Postal Museum\narchival holdings, including uncatalogued or incompletely catalogued\nmaterial, are represented in the system searched*, or whether there are\ncategories of physical material which may not yet be represented?\n\n*4. Restricted, closed or unprocessed material*\n\nWere any records identified which could potentially relate to the subject\nbut which were unavailable because they were restricted, closed,\nuncatalogued, unprocessed or otherwise inaccessible?\n\nIf so, I would be grateful for the relevant reference numbers and any\napplicable access restrictions.\n\n*5. Records transferred to BT Archives*\n\nYou explained that relevant telecommunications material appearing in the\ncatalogue is held at BT Archives.\n\nCould you confirm whether the Postal Museum retains any *transfer records,\naccession records, finding aids or other information identifying the\nparticular GPO/Telegraph/Engineering records which were transferred to BT\nArchives*?\n\nIf there are catalogue references which would help BT Archives locate the\nunderlying material, I would be very grateful for those.\n\n*6. The Williams connection*\n\nThe purpose of the search for Williams is not to establish that Mr Williams\nwas a Post Office employee.\n\nThe family tradition concerns *a local Mr Williams of Great House Farm,\nLlandough near Penarth*, who may have assisted Marconi locally.\nConsequently, a relevant record might describe him as a local resident,\nlandowner, farmer, host, assistant, carrier, messenger, proprietor or other\nprivate individual rather than as Post Office personnel.\n\nCould you therefore confirm whether the search for Williams included\nreferences of this kind, rather than only Post Office employees or\npersonnel records?\n\nSimilarly, were variants such as *Mr Williams, W. Williams, William\nWilliams and Williams* considered?\n\n*7. Preparatory and follow-up records*\n\nCould the search also be considered in terms of records concerning:\n\n   - preparations for the South Wales experiments;\n   - arrangements made with local residents or property owners;\n   - visits to or use of private premises;\n   - transport or movement of equipment;\n   - correspondence immediately before or after the experiments;\n   - follow-up reports;\n   - subsequent demonstrations or experiments in the area;\n   - photographs, plans, maps or other material which might identify\n   locations or participants.\n\nI appreciate that you may ultimately conclude that none of these are held\nby the Postal Museum. I am simply trying to establish precisely what\nevidence has and has not survived, and where the relevant archival trail\nnow leads.\n\nFinally, if the Postal Museum has any *contemporary publications,\nnewspaper-cutting collections, photographs, finding aids or other material\nconcerning the South Wales Marconi experiments*, even where they do not\nspecifically mention Great House Farm or Mr Williams, I would be grateful\nfor those references as well.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. Your clarification has helped\nconsiderably in narrowing the search, and I appreciate your taking the time\nto establish exactly what the Postal Museum catalogue can and cannot tell\nme.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester  \n\nOn Fri, 31 Jul 2026, 11:04 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> I searched our archive’s catalogued, for all catalogued and uncatalogued\n> items, using the following keywords:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm\n>    - Llandough\n>    - Lavernock\n>\n> *Result*: no item is held in our archives using these words in the\n> description.\n>\n> Concerning the below keywords:\n>\n>    - Penarth\n>    - wireless demonstrations\n>    - GPO Telegraph Department\n>    - Engineering Department\n>    - Williams / Mr Williams\n>\n> *Result*: Some items held in our archives came up with those keywords,\n> but when reading the description field on our catalogue, they turned out to\n> be unrelated to the 1897 wireless telegraphy demonstration. Most were dated\n> to before or after 1897. Many came up on our online catalogue, but they are\n> held at BT Archives, therefore, we won’t have any more information. This is\n> what I meant by ‘nothing relevant came up’ – despite corresponding keyword,\n> the dates or the content aren’t related to your enquiry.\n>\n> The physical archives were not checked as all information on our files are\n> recorded on our archival cataloguing system, which is what I used to search\n> information and keyword. Because the few records that seemed relevant are\n> held at BT Archives, only they can inform you of the digitised or\n> non-digitised status of the items.\n>\n> Although the items held at BT Archives come up in our archival cataloguing\n> system, you would need to contact directly for more information.\n>\n> For your questions in 4. On the link with Mr Williams, nothing came up\n> about people who participated to the demonstrations.\n>\n> You can search our online catalogue here:\n> https://catalogue.postalmuseum.org/\n>\n> And here is the link to the catalogue of BT Archives:\n> https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/Calmview/\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 29 July 2026 14:41\n> *To:* Archives <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Mathilde,\n>\n> Thank you for your further reply and for carrying out the searches.\n>\n> I appreciate your assistance, but I would like to clarify the scope and\n> conclusions of the search, as several points remain unresolved.\n>\n> Firstly, I should correct one detail: the individual I am researching is *\n> Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough near Penarth*, not \"Mr\n> William\". The surname is significant because family history suggests that\n> my great-grandfather, Mr Williams of Great House Farm, assisted Guglielmo\n> Marconi during the 1897 South Wales wireless experiments.\n>\n> I fully understand that the absence of a result within the Postal Museum\n> catalogue does not necessarily mean that no such person or record existed.\n> However, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n>\n>    1. *Search methodology*\n>\n> Could you confirm exactly which catalogue collections, series, or record\n> groups were searched for:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough (Penarth)\n>    - Llandough\n>    - Lavernock\n>    - Marconi\n>    - wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n>    - GPO Telegraph Department\n>    - Engineering Department\n>    - Williams / Mr Williams\n>\n>\n>    2. *Scope of the negative result*\n>\n> When you state that \"nothing relevant came up\", does this mean:\n>\n>    - no indexed catalogue entries were found in Postal Museum collections;\n>    - no digitised records were found;\n>    - or that physical archival holdings were also checked?\n>\n>\n>    3. *Records relating to GPO personnel*\n>\n> You mentioned that most Marconi and Telegraph Department records are held\n> at BT Archives. Could you confirm whether the Postal Museum holds any\n> catalogue references, finding aids, or transferred-record information\n> indicating where the relevant GPO engineering correspondence, reports,\n> notebooks, or staff records may have been moved?\n>\n>    4. *The Williams connection*\n>\n> The question I am trying to establish is not necessarily whether Mr\n> Williams was a Post Office employee. He may instead have been the\n> owner/occupier of Great House Farm who assisted Marconi locally.\n>\n> Could you therefore confirm whether your search included references to:\n>\n>    - private individuals assisting demonstrations;\n>    - hosts or local contacts connected with Marconi's experiments;\n>    - correspondence mentioning residents of Llandough, Penarth, or\n>    Lavernock?\n>\n> I appreciate that the absence of a catalogue entry cannot prove that an\n> event or person did not exist, particularly where local residents or\n> private landowners were involved.\n>\n> My aim is simply to establish the evidential trail: whether the Mr\n> Williams mentioned in contemporary accounts can be identified, and whether\n> surviving records connect him with Great House Farm and Marconi's\n> experiments.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance. I would be grateful for any further\n> clarification on the above points before I proceed to BT Archives and\n> Glamorgan Archives.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 10:32 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> I searched for all files related to the key words Great House Farm,\n> Llandough, Lavernock, wireless demonstration. Nothing relevant came up. For\n> Marconi and the Telegraph Departments, all the files would be held at BT\n> Archives.\n>\n>\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n>\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n>\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 29 July 2026 14:04\n> *To:* Archives <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Mathilde,\n>\n> Thank you very much for taking the time to carry out these searches and\n> for your detailed response.\n>\n> I appreciate the clarification regarding the distinction between Great\n> House Farm, Llandough near Penarth and the similarly named location near\n> Cowbridge. The Penarth/Llandough/Lavernock area is the location of interest.\n>\n> Your advice regarding BT Archives is very helpful, and I will follow this\n> up with them, as the surviving GPO Telegraph and wireless records appear\n> likely to be held there.\n>\n> I am also grateful for the information about the Post Office family\n> history records. My main interest is not that Mr Williams was necessarily a\n> Post Office employee, but whether the individual mentioned in contemporary\n> accounts as assisting Marconi at Great House Farm can be identified. Family\n> history passed down through my great grandfather's line suggests that a Mr\n> Williams of Great House Farm assisted Marconi during his South Wales\n> experiments, and I am trying to establish whether this can be connected to\n> my ancestor.\n>\n> If possible, could you let me know whether the search you carried out\n> included any of the following terms or collections, as this may help me\n> understand the scope of the search:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm (Llandough/Penarth)\n>    - Llandough\n>    - Lavernock\n>    - Marconi\n>    - wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n>    - GPO Telegraph Department / Engineering Department\n>\n> I will also contact Glamorgan Archives, as you suggest, since local\n> newspapers, estate records, or correspondence may contain information not\n> held in the national collections.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance. Your guidance has helped narrow down\n> where the relevant evidence is most likely to survive.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:31 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. I will do my best to check if we have\n> surviving records of this demonstration, although most of the records about\n> telecommunications were transferred to BT Archives so they might have more\n> information than us: https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge)\n>\n> I couldn’t find any record mentioning Great House Farm, Llandough. For\n> Penarth, there were some results but they were all dated much later than\n> the demonstration. We have many records on Cardiff, which you can find on\n> our online catalogue Here, but nothing relevant seemed to have come up.\n>\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>\n> Nothing came up for Lavernock either, the locations are too precise for\n> this type of records to have reached our archives. I searched for ‘wireless\n> demonstration’ and POST 88 Series titled ‘Post Office: Wireless Telegraphy\n> and Telephony’ mentions such events, but all the files are kept in BT\n> Archives.\n>\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>\n> Almost all the files related to Marconi are held in BT Archives.\n>\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> I couldn’t find any specific file about a Mr William from Great House\n> Farm, but the main records we have that are useful for family history\n> research are the Appointment Books, and the pension and gratuity records.\n> We also have Establishment Books and staff magazines that can be helpful\n> too. You can find more information about what we hold here:\n> https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/family-history/\n>  Please bear in mind that most villages, small towns, hamlets, etc. such as\n> Llandough had business that ran a postal service, and these people were not\n> directly employed by the Post Office, therefore, we won’t have any\n> information. If Mr Williams had another business, he was likely not\n> employed by the Post Office. A local archive might hold newspaper cuttings\n> or other information about this person: https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n> You are welcome to visit our archives, but I believe most of the records\n> and information you are looking for will be held at BT Archives. You can\n> contact them directly to organise an appointment.\n>\n>\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n>\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n>\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 24 July 2026 16:17\n> *To:* Booking Support Team <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> Dear Archive Team,\n>\n> I am conducting historical research into the General Post Office's\n> involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's wireless demonstrations in South Wales\n> during 1897.\n>\n> Post Office Ltd has advised that your archive is the most likely\n> repository for surviving historic GPO records relating to this period.\n>\n> I would be grateful if you could search for any records relating to:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge).\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> If records relating specifically to Mr Williams cannot be located, I would\n> also appreciate details of any records identifying GPO personnel, visitors\n> or local residents connected with the demonstrations, as these may help\n> establish the historical context.\n>\n> If another archive holds any of these records, I would be grateful if you\n> could advise where I should direct my enquiry.\n>\n> Mr Williams of Great House Farm was my great grandad. I am trying to\n> ascertain if the Mr Williams post office worker, mentioned helping Marconi\n> in the article, was the same man as my great grandfather. I am also looking\n> for any more connections between my family, my former home and Marconi and\n> the radio experiments at lavernock point. Which I understand were already\n> underway before Marconi arrived to South Wales.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and assistance. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> \n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fb87d48d3858f8","subject":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-31T14:03:56Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb87d48d3858f8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e","direction":"received","from":"Archives","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb87d48d3858f8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nI searched our archive's catalogued, for all catalogued and uncatalogued items, using the following keywords:\n\n  *   Great House Farm\n  *   Llandough\n  *   Lavernock\nResult: no item is held in our archives using these words in the description.\nConcerning the below keywords:\n\n  *   Penarth\n  *   wireless demonstrations\n  *   GPO Telegraph Department\n  *   Engineering Department\n  *   Williams / Mr Williams\nResult: Some items held in our archives came up with those keywords, but when reading the description field on our catalogue, they turned out to be unrelated to the 1897 wireless telegraphy demonstration. Most were dated to before or after 1897. Many came up on our online catalogue, but they are held at BT Archives, therefore, we won't have any more information. This is what I meant by 'nothing relevant came up' - despite corresponding keyword, the dates or the content aren't related to your enquiry.\nThe physical archives were not checked as all information on our files are recorded on our archival cataloguing system, which is what I used to search information and keyword. Because the few records that seemed relevant are held at BT Archives, only they can inform you of the digitised or non-digitised status of the items.\nAlthough the items held at BT Archives come up in our archival cataloguing system, you would need to contact directly for more information.\nFor your questions in 4. On the link with Mr Williams, nothing came up about people who participated to the demonstrations.\nYou can search our online catalogue here: https://catalogue.postalmuseum.org/\nAnd here is the link to the catalogue of BT Archives: https://www.digitalarchives.bt.com/Calmview/\nI hope this helps,\nBest regards,\nMathilde\nMathilde Jourdan\nArchives Assistant\nThe Postal Museum | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\nT: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Facebook channel]<https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Twitter Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]<https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Instgram Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]<https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Youtube Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]<https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n\n[cid:image005.png@01DD20FD.1D906540]\nThe Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust. Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 29 July 2026 14:41\nTo: Archives <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n\nDear Mathilde,\n\nThank you for your further reply and for carrying out the searches.\n\nI appreciate your assistance, but I would like to clarify the scope and conclusions of the search, as several points remain unresolved.\n\nFirstly, I should correct one detail: the individual I am researching is Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough near Penarth, not \"Mr William\". The surname is significant because family history suggests that my great-grandfather, Mr Williams of Great House Farm, assisted Guglielmo Marconi during the 1897 South Wales wireless experiments.\n\nI fully understand that the absence of a result within the Postal Museum catalogue does not necessarily mean that no such person or record existed. However, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n\n  1.  Search methodology\n\nCould you confirm exactly which catalogue collections, series, or record groups were searched for:\n\n  *   Great House Farm, Llandough (Penarth)\n  *   Llandough\n  *   Lavernock\n  *   Marconi\n  *   wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n  *   GPO Telegraph Department\n  *   Engineering Department\n  *   Williams / Mr Williams\n\n  1.  Scope of the negative result\n\nWhen you state that \"nothing relevant came up\", does this mean:\n\n  *   no indexed catalogue entries were found in Postal Museum collections;\n  *   no digitised records were found;\n  *   or that physical archival holdings were also checked?\n\n  1.  Records relating to GPO personnel\n\nYou mentioned that most Marconi and Telegraph Department records are held at BT Archives. Could you confirm whether the Postal Museum holds any catalogue references, finding aids, or transferred-record information indicating where the relevant GPO engineering correspondence, reports, notebooks, or staff records may have been moved?\n\n  1.  The Williams connection\n\nThe question I am trying to establish is not necessarily whether Mr Williams was a Post Office employee. He may instead have been the owner/occupier of Great House Farm who assisted Marconi locally.\n\nCould you therefore confirm whether your search included references to:\n\n  *   private individuals assisting demonstrations;\n  *   hosts or local contacts connected with Marconi's experiments;\n  *   correspondence mentioning residents of Llandough, Penarth, or Lavernock?\n\nI appreciate that the absence of a catalogue entry cannot prove that an event or person did not exist, particularly where local residents or private landowners were involved.\n\nMy aim is simply to establish the evidential trail: whether the Mr Williams mentioned in contemporary accounts can be identified, and whether surviving records connect him with Great House Farm and Marconi's experiments.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. I would be grateful for any further clarification on the above points before I proceed to BT Archives and Glamorgan Archives.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 10:32 Archives, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nI searched for all files related to the key words Great House Farm, Llandough, Lavernock, wireless demonstration. Nothing relevant came up. For Marconi and the Telegraph Departments, all the files would be held at BT Archives.\n\nI hope this helps,\n\nBest regards,\n\nMathilde\n\nMathilde Jourdan\nArchives Assistant\nThe Postal Museum | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted][map link redacted]\nT: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Facebook channel]<https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Twitter Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]<https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Instgram Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]<https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Youtube Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]<https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n\n[cid:image005.png@01DD20FD.1D906540]\nThe Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust. Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 29 July 2026 14:04\nTo: Archives <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n\nDear Mathilde,\n\nThank you very much for taking the time to carry out these searches and for your detailed response.\n\nI appreciate the clarification regarding the distinction between Great House Farm, Llandough near Penarth and the similarly named location near Cowbridge. The Penarth/Llandough/Lavernock area is the location of interest.\n\nYour advice regarding BT Archives is very helpful, and I will follow this up with them, as the surviving GPO Telegraph and wireless records appear likely to be held there.\n\nI am also grateful for the information about the Post Office family history records. My main interest is not that Mr Williams was necessarily a Post Office employee, but whether the individual mentioned in contemporary accounts as assisting Marconi at Great House Farm can be identified. Family history passed down through my great grandfather's line suggests that a Mr Williams of Great House Farm assisted Marconi during his South Wales experiments, and I am trying to establish whether this can be connected to my ancestor.\n\nIf possible, could you let me know whether the search you carried out included any of the following terms or collections, as this may help me understand the scope of the search:\n\n  *   Great House Farm (Llandough/Penarth)\n  *   Llandough\n  *   Lavernock\n  *   Marconi\n  *   wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n  *   GPO Telegraph Department / Engineering Department\n\nI will also contact Glamorgan Archives, as you suggest, since local newspapers, estate records, or correspondence may contain information not held in the national collections.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. Your guidance has helped narrow down where the relevant evidence is most likely to survive.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:31 Archives, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your enquiry. I will do my best to check if we have surviving records of this demonstration, although most of the records about telecommunications were transferred to BT Archives so they might have more information than us: https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\n\n  *   Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge)\nI couldn't find any record mentioning Great House Farm, Llandough. For Penarth, there were some results but they were all dated much later than the demonstration. We have many records on Cardiff, which you can find on our online catalogue Here, but nothing relevant seemed to have come up.\n\n  *   Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless demonstration sites.\nNothing came up for Lavernock either, the locations are too precise for this type of records to have reached our archives. I searched for 'wireless demonstration' and POST 88 Series titled 'Post Office: Wireless Telegraphy and Telephony' mentions such events, but all the files are kept in BT Archives.\n\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\nAlmost all the files related to Marconi are held in BT Archives.\n\n  *   GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these demonstrations.\nSee above.\n\n  *   Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\nSee above.\n\n  *   Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay at the property.\nI couldn't find any specific file about a Mr William from Great House Farm, but the main records we have that are useful for family history research are the Appointment Books, and the pension and gratuity records. We also have Establishment Books and staff magazines that can be helpful too. You can find more information about what we hold here:  https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/family-history/  Please bear in mind that most villages, small towns, hamlets, etc. such as Llandough had business that ran a postal service, and these people were not directly employed by the Post Office, therefore, we won't have any information. If Mr Williams had another business, he was likely not employed by the Post Office. A local archive might hold newspaper cuttings or other information about this person: https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\nYou are welcome to visit our archives, but I believe most of the records and information you are looking for will be held at BT Archives. You can contact them directly to organise an appointment.\n\nI hope this helps,\n\nBest regards,\n\nMathilde\n\nMathilde Jourdan\nArchives Assistant\nThe Postal Museum | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted][map link redacted]\nT: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Facebook channel]<https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Twitter Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]<https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Instgram Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]<https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[Youtube Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]<https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n\n[cid:image005.png@01DD20FD.1D906540]\nThe Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust. Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 24 July 2026 16:17\nTo: Booking Support Team <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nDear Archive Team,\n\nI am conducting historical research into the General Post Office's involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's wireless demonstrations in South Wales during 1897.\n\nPost Office Ltd has advised that your archive is the most likely repository for surviving historic GPO records relating to this period.\n\nI would be grateful if you could search for any records relating to:\n\n  *   Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge).\n  *   Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless demonstration sites.\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n  *   GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these demonstrations.\n  *   Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n  *   Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay at the property.\n\nIf records relating specifically to Mr Williams cannot be located, I would also appreciate details of any records identifying GPO personnel, visitors or local residents connected with the demonstrations, as these may help establish the historical context.\n\nIf another archive holds any of these records, I would be grateful if you could advise where I should direct my enquiry.\n\nMr Williams of Great House Farm was my great grandad. I am trying to ascertain if the Mr Williams post office worker, mentioned helping Marconi in the article, was the same man as my great grandfather. I am also looking for any more connections between my family, my former home and Marconi and the radio experiments at lavernock point. Which I understand were already underway before Marconi arrived to South Wales.\n\nThank you for your time and assistance. I look forward to your response.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nRequester\n\n"},{"id":"gm-19fb429942d0c479","subject":"Re: Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464","name":"Re: Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464","date":"2026-07-30T17:54:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb429942d0c479.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fb3502cda71764-sponse-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas-343481-x5h3m6-crm-016207464","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fb3502cda71764","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-343481"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb429942d0c479.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Patricia Reynolds,\n\nThank you for your response of 30 July 2026 (Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6).\n\nI note your advice that The National Archives is not the primary repository\nfor the material described in my original enquiry. However, my enquiry also\nconcerns whether The National Archives holds any recorded information\nrelating to the existence, transfer, retention, destruction, or absence of\nsuch records.\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000, I request confirmation of any\nrecorded information held by The National Archives relating to Great House\nFarm / Ty Mawr, Llandough (Glamorgan), including historical references\nunder alternative descriptions such as Cedfin or equivalent contemporary\ndescriptions.\n\nSpecifically, please confirm whether The National Archives holds:\n\n   1. *Manorial and estate records*\n\nAny catalogue entries, Manorial Documents Register information, finding\naids, transfer records, or related documentation concerning:\n\n   - the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan);\n   - pre-1667 references to occupants, customary tenants, holdings,\n   surveys, rentals, terriers, or court rolls;\n   - Vaughan family estate holdings at Llandough;\n   - Great House Farm / Ty Mawr or any earlier description of the holding.\n\nPlease include any references to HMC9/311 or related archival series.\n\n   2. *Records concerning disposal, destruction, or transfer of records*\n\nAny recorded information showing:\n\n   - whether records relating to Great House Farm, Llandough, the Bute\n   Estate, Vaughan family papers, or associated land records were ever\n   transferred to The National Archives;\n   - whether any such records were destroyed, and if so:\n      - what records were destroyed;\n      - when they were destroyed;\n      - under which retention schedule, disposal authority, or policy;\n      - which body authorised or carried out the destruction.\n\nIf no such records are held, please confirm whether any disposal or\ntransfer records indicate that relevant material was never deposited or was\ndestroyed elsewhere.\n\n   3. *Legal and court records*\n\nAny central court records, indexes, correspondence, or administrative\nrecords concerning:\n\n   - possession or title disputes involving Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n   - Western Ground Rents Ltd;\n   - BP Pension Trust Ltd;\n   - BP Properties Ltd;\n   - Mountjoy Ltd;\n   - the proceedings connected with *BP Properties Ltd v Buckler* [1987]\n   EWCA Civ 2.\n\n\n   4. *Estate transfers and ownership records*\n\nAny government-held correspondence, files, or records relating to:\n\n   - the Bute Estate;\n   - the 1938 sale or transfer of Great House Farm;\n   - Western Ground Rents Ltd acquisition;\n   - BP Pension Trust/BP Properties involvement;\n   - any government department involvement in the property.\n\n\n   5. *Family correspondence and related records*\n\nAny correspondence, reports, enquiries, or administrative records held by\nThe National Archives involving:\n\n   - Mary Williams;\n   - Fred Buckler;\n   - William Buckler;\n   - the Williams/Buckler family;\n   - Great House Farm / Ty Mawr;\n   - Bute Estate representatives;\n   - Western Ground Rents;\n   - BP entities.\n\n\n   6. *1980–1988 period and demolition/eviction matters*\n\nAny records concerning:\n\n   - the public campaign regarding Great House Farm;\n   - parliamentary correspondence or government enquiries;\n   - the 1988 eviction/demolition;\n   - Cadw or government communications;\n   - European Commission of Human Rights Application 14464/88 (Buckler v\n   United Kingdom).\n\nIf any relevant information is held, please provide catalogue references,\ndescriptions, and access arrangements.\n\nIf no relevant information is held, please confirm:\n\n   - the searches undertaken;\n   - the catalogues, databases, and record series searched;\n   - whether any relevant records were ever held and subsequently\n   transferred, destroyed, or disposed of.\n\nI am pursuing parallel enquiries with the National Library of Wales,\nGlamorgan Archives and other repositories. This request is specifically\ndirected at recorded information held by The National Archives.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\n\nOn Thu, 30 Jul 2026, 10:56 Contact Centre, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Thank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n>\n> I'm afraid we are not the right place to come to for your enquiry. We hold\n> historical records sent to us by central government departments and law\n> courts for permanent preservation. I regret, therefore, that I'm unable to\n> help you with your enquiry.\n>\n> I suggest you contact The National Library of Wales\n> <https://www.library.wales/>.\n>\n> I wish you every success with your research.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Patricia Reynolds\n>\n> Remote Enquiries Duty Officer\n> www.nationalarchives.gov.uk\n>\n> Please complete our brief, three question survey\n> <https://emea.dcv.ms/1PncPtnWn7> to let us know what you think about your\n> recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n>\n> *Enquiry:*\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n>\n> *EXTERNAL*: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded\n> information held by the National Library of Wales:\n> Any manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents\n> for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that\n> list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later\n> known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\n> Any estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or\n> surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings)\n> that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of\n> land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\n> Any catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify\n> pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the\n> family’s holding at this property.\n> Please confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the\n> relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or\n> advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state\n> the exemption(s) relied upon.\n>\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n>\n> Requester \n>\n> Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\n> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n> National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it\n> are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are\n> addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this\n> email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions,\n> conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do\n> not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither\n> given nor endorsed by it.\n> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fb3a2fbd127319","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-30T15:27:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb3a2fbd127319.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb3a2fbd127319.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dr Roberts,\n\nThank you for your response and for confirming the internal review outcome.\n\nI acknowledge the clarification provided regarding the searches undertaken,\nincluding reference to the Bute Estate series D153, D205 and D219, and the\napplication of section 21 in relation to publicly accessible catalogue\nmaterial.\n\nHowever, I would like to clarify one remaining point for the record.\n\nMy concern throughout this request has not been whether the Library holds\nphysical furniture or objects as collection items. My request was\nspecifically for recorded information relating to furniture, furnishings,\nfixtures, household effects and movable property connected with Great House\nFarm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nThe questions I sought answers to were therefore about the existence of\nrecords such as inventories, valuations, estate correspondence, fixture\nrecords, transfers, disposals, provenance information and references within\nrelevant archival collections.\n\nTo avoid any misunderstanding, could you please confirm specifically:\n\n   1. Whether the Bute Estate series D153, D205 and D219 were searched only\n   for references to the property name (for example \"Ty Mawr\", \"Great House\n   Farm\" or \"Llandough\"), or whether searches were also undertaken for related\n   terms such as:\n\n\n   - inventory;\n   - valuation;\n   - contents;\n   - furniture;\n   - furnishings;\n   - fixtures;\n   - household effects;\n   - sale;\n   - transfer;\n   - disposal.\n\n\n   2.\n\n   Whether any archival collections other than the identified Bute Estate\n   series were considered relevant and searched.\n   3.\n\n   Whether the Library holds, or has confirmed it does not hold, any:\n\n\n   - household inventories;\n   - estate valuations;\n   - tenant records;\n   - correspondence regarding contents or fixtures;\n   - records of removal, disposal or transfer of items;\n   - photographs or descriptions of household contents connected with Ty\n   Mawr/Llandough.\n\n\n   4. If no such records were identified, please confirm that this\n   conclusion is based on searches undertaken across the relevant archival\n   collections, rather than solely on the absence of catalogue descriptions\n   containing the property name.\n\nI appreciate that archival catalogues do not always describe individual\nitems or subjects in detail. However, the purpose of this clarification is\nto establish precisely what searches were undertaken and what records were\nconsidered, so that there is a clear and accurate record of the Library’s\nposition.\n\nI am grateful for the assistance provided so far and would appreciate a\nspecific response to each point above.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\nOn Thu, 30 Jul 2026, 10:41 National Library of Wales, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> --# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Owain Roberts\n>\n> Jul 30 2026, 02:41PM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your message of acknowledgement.\n>\n> Kind regards and best wishes,\n>\n> Dr Owain Rhys Roberts\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> Jul 29 2026, 02:10PM via Email\n> Dear Dr Roberts,\n> Thank you for the detailed internal review outcome of FOI/2026/09 dated 29\n> July 2026.\n> I note the clarification of the searches undertaken (including Bute Estate\n> series D153, D205 and D219), the rationale for limiting terms to the\n> property name, and the application of section 21 to the publicly accessible\n> catalogue and Reading Room material.\n> This closes the internal review from my side. I will proceed via the\n> Library’s normal catalogue and Reading Room services for the identified\n> estate records.\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Owain Roberts\n>\n> Jul 29 2026, 11:21AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Please find attached the outcome of the internal review that you requested\n> on the 20 July 2026. I can confirm that the internal review considered the\n> clarification that you provided on the 20 July 2026.\n>\n> Regards,\n> Dr Owain Rhys Roberts\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09-Internal_Review_Outcome.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4534050&type=0&key=f13df66d89dd9bb9040b52659665094b>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 08:37PM via Email\n> Ms Daniel,\n>\n> Further to my internal review request, I would like to provide a short\n> clarification regarding the scope of my original FOI request.\n>\n> Having reviewed my original request submitted on 3 July 2026, I wish to\n> emphasise that the request was expressly for recorded information, not\n> merely for physical objects held within NLW collections.\n>\n> The original request specifically sought:\n> inventories, catalogues and asset registers;\n> acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records;\n> provenance files and ownership records;\n> photographs;\n> correspondence concerning identification, recovery, ownership or location;\n> internal reports, legal advice and memoranda;\n> correspondence involving the Buckler or Williams families;\n> correspondence with Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, museums and other public\n> bodies.\n>\n> Therefore, my concern is not that NLW does not hold furniture as part of a\n> collection. I understand that point. My concern is whether relevant\n> documentary records were searched across appropriate archival collections\n> where references to such items may exist.\n>\n> For example, where NLW holds Bute Estate material relating to Ty\n> Mawr/Llandough, I would appreciate confirmation as to whether those\n> collections were searched for incidental references to:\n> household inventories;\n> fixtures;\n> valuations;\n> estate correspondence;\n> transfers or disposals;\n> provenance information;\n> references to occupants or contents of the farmhouse.\n>\n> This clarification is provided to assist the internal review and ensure the\n> original request is considered in its full context.\n> I appreciate the catalogue references already provided and look forward to\n> confirmation of the searches undertaken.\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 08:35PM via Email\n> Ms Daniel,\n>\n> Thank you for your response dated 20 July 2026 regarding FOI/2026/09 and\n> for identifying the catalogue references relating to Ty Mawr/Llandough\n> within the Bute Estate collections.\n>\n> I would like to request an internal review, as I believe the response may\n> have interpreted the scope of my request too narrowly.\n>\n> My request was for:\n>\n> \"All recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques,\n> fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House\n> Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items received from Bute\n> Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.\"\n>\n> I appreciate that the National Library of Wales does not collect furniture\n> as a category of object and therefore may not hold the physical items\n> themselves. However, my request was not limited to physical objects or\n> acquisition files. It sought *all recorded information* relating to such\n> items.\n>\n> This could include, for example:\n>\n> - inventories;\n> - valuations;\n> - estate correspondence;\n> - fixture schedules;\n> - probate references;\n> - sale catalogues;\n> - photographs;\n> - tenancy records;\n> - references within Bute Estate papers;\n> - records of transfer, removal or disposal.\n>\n> The response confirms that NLW holds significant Bute Estate material\n> relating to Ty Mawr, including maps, leases and deeds. However, it does not\n> clarify whether those wider collections were searched for references to the\n> farmhouse contents, fixtures, or related estate administration records.\n>\n> Could the internal review please clarify:\n>\n> 1.\n>\n> What collections and record series were searched in responding to this\n> request?\n> 2.\n>\n> Were searches undertaken beyond acquisition files, including within Bute\n> Estate papers and related archival collections?\n> 3.\n>\n> Were terms such as:\n>\n>\n> - Great House Farm;\n> - Ty Mawr;\n> - Llandough;\n> - fixtures;\n> - inventory;\n> - valuation;\n> - contents;\n> - furnishings;\n> - sale;\n> - transfer;\n>\n> used as part of the search?\n>\n> 4. If no relevant records are held, could you please confirm the\n> searches undertaken and the basis for that conclusion?\n>\n> The reason this distinction matters is that my wider research concerns the\n> documentary history of the farmhouse and garden plot following changes\n> affecting Ty Mawr/Llandough after the 19th century. Records relating to\n> fixtures, valuations, inventories or estate administration may provide\n> important historical context, regardless of whether the physical items\n> themselves remain.\n>\n> I am not asking NLW to determine ownership or provide a legal opinion. I am\n> seeking confirmation that all relevant archival holdings have been\n> considered and that the request has been searched against the appropriate\n> collections.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance. I look forward to the outcome of the\n> internal review.\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Attached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4517166&type=0&key=5afe8f6fd61ea76cddc027c015f0bfb2>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> I am writing in response to your recent application for information held\n> by the Library\n>\n> (Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n>\n> You will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n>\n> Best wishes,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Cwestiwn gwreiddiol\n>\n> Jul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\n> Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Thank you for using the National Library of Wales Enquiry Service.\n>\n>\n> This email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n>\n> Read our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fb3917287520aa","subject":"Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/SH","name":"Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/SH","date":"2026-07-30T15:08:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb3917287520aa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fb20f21f899949-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-sh","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fb20f21f899949","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":["N610CGV"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb3917287520aa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mr Haste,\n\nThank you for your letter of 30 July 2026 (reference N610CGV) and for\nidentifying the surviving records held in relation to titles WA231076 and\nWA240304.\n\nI am not seeking to reopen HM Land Registry’s complaints procedure or to\nask for any previous decision to be reconsidered. This is a separate\nrequest for clarification arising from the additional information in your\nletter.\n\nYour letter is the first to set out in detail which first-registration\nrecords survive. It therefore enables a number of factual questions that\ncould not previously be asked with precision.\n\nFirst, earlier correspondence referred to a 1971 abstract of title having\nbeen lodged with the first registration applications. That document does\nnot appear as a separate item in the schedule you have provided. Could you\nplease confirm whether:\n\nthe 1971 abstract of title survives as a separate document;\n\nit forms part of one of the listed items (and if so, which); or\n\nit is no longer held.\n\nSecond, earlier correspondence referred to a certificate given with the\nfirst registration application in which the applicant’s solicitors stated\nthey were “not aware of any question or doubt affecting the title”. Your\nschedule identifies the surviving first-registration application as Form 1E\n(item 13 for WA231076). Could you please confirm whether that certificate\nforms part of the surviving Form 1E, and if not, identify the surviving\ndocument in which it appears.\n\nThe purpose of this enquiry is solely to establish what information is\nactually contained in the surviving first-registration records you have\nlisted.\n\nCould you therefore confirm whether those records — including the\nfirst-registration application, the A13/DL list of documents lodged, the\ncorrespondence with Linklaters & Paines, any related applications, and any\nsurviving examiner’s notes, file notes, memoranda or internal\ncorrespondence — contain any reference to:\n\nMary Williams (also known as Mrs Buckler);\n\nFred Buckler;\n\nTy Mawr;\n\nGreat House Farm;\n\nany assertion by another person that they owned, occupied, or claimed an\ninterest in the land;\n\nany ownership dispute, possession proceedings, litigation, or competing\nclaim affecting the land;\n\nany issue, doubt, objection, caution, competing interest, or other matter\naffecting title.\n\nIn particular, could you confirm whether any of the surviving\nfirst-registration records contain any indication that another party\nasserted ownership of, or claimed an interest in, the land before first\nregistration was completed for either title.\n\nIf any such reference exists, please identify the document or item number\nin which it appears.\n\nIf no such references appear anywhere in the surviving records, a simple\nconfirmation of that fact would be sufficient.\n\nIf these questions cannot be answered without inspection of the documents\nthemselves, please confirm that and identify which specific documents are\ncapable of answering them, so that any Form OC2 application can be limited\nto those documents alone.\n\nThis request concerns only the factual contents of the records identified\nin your letter of 30 July 2026.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to your reply.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nRequester \n\n and Life Memeber\n\nOn Thu, 30 Jul 2026, 05:06 Wales.OfficeMail, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\n> document by post.\n>\n> Ymholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r\n> ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais\n> rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni\n> chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n>\n> Mae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg\n> y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y\n> ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho\n> i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun\n> at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir\n> EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd\n> rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Diben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy’n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: “Marchnad eiddo o’r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy”.\n>\n> Rydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe’ch cynghorir mai chi sy’n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna’i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n>\n> I weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fb3502cda71764","subject":"Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464","name":"Response to enquiry at The National Archives. Case number CAS-343481-X5H3M6 CRM:016207464","date":"2026-07-30T13:56:38Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb3502cda71764.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fb3502cda71764-sponse-to-enquiry-at-the-national-archives-case-number-cas-343481-x5h3m6-crm-016207464","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fb3502cda71764","direction":"received","from":"Contact Centre","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":["CAS-343481"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb3502cda71764.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for contacting The National Archives of the United Kingdom.\n\nI'm afraid we are not the right place to come to for your enquiry. We hold historical records sent to us by central government departments and law courts for permanent preservation. I regret, therefore, that I'm unable to help you with your enquiry.\n\nI suggest you contact The National Library of Wales .\n\nI wish you every success with your research.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nPatricia Reynolds\n\nRemote Enquiries Duty Officer\nwww.nationalarchives.gov.uk \n\nPlease complete our brief, three question survey  to let us know what you think about your recent contact. Your views are important in helping us improve our service.\n\nEnquiry:\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this is important \n\nEXTERNAL: This email originates from outside of The National Archives.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded information held by the National Library of Wales:\nAny manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents for the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that list or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later known as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\nAny estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or surveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings) that mention a lease, renewal, confirmation, surrender, or new grant of land at Great House Farm / Llandough around or before 1667.\nAny catalogue descriptions, finding aids, or indexes that identify pre-1667 deeds, court-roll entries, or estate surveys referring to the family’s holding at this property.\nPlease confirm whether such material is held and, if so, provide the relevant catalogue references and any available descriptions or copies (or advise on access arrangements). If any information is exempt, please state the exemption(s) relied upon.\n\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nRequester \n\nPlease don't print this e-mail unless you really need to. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- National Archives Disclaimer This email and any files transmitted with it are intended solely for the use of the individual(s) to whom they are addressed. If you are not the intended recipient and have received this email in error, please notify the sender and delete the email. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message and attachments that do not relate to the official business of The National Archives are neither given nor endorsed by it. ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------"},{"id":"gm-19fb34242da57298","subject":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-30T13:41:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb34242da57298.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb34242da57298.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nOwain Roberts\n\nJul 30 2026, 02:41PM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your message of acknowledgement.\n\nKind regards and best wishes,\n\nDr Owain Rhys Roberts\n------------------\n\nRequester\n\nJul 29 2026, 02:10PM via Email\nDear Dr Roberts,\nThank you for the detailed internal review outcome of FOI/2026/09 dated 29\nJuly 2026.\nI note the clarification of the searches undertaken (including Bute Estate\nseries D153, D205 and D219), the rationale for limiting terms to the\nproperty name, and the application of section 21 to the publicly accessible\ncatalogue and Reading Room material.\nThis closes the internal review from my side. I will proceed via the\nLibrary’s normal catalogue and Reading Room services for the identified\nestate records. ------------------\n\nOwain Roberts\n\nJul 29 2026, 11:21AM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nPlease find attached the outcome of the internal review that you requested on the 20 July 2026. I can confirm that the internal review considered the clarification that you provided on the 20 July 2026.\n\nRegards,\nDr Owain Rhys Roberts\n\nAttached Files\n\n-FOI2026-09-Internal_Review_Outcome.pdf <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4534050&type=0&key=f13df66d89dd9bb9040b52659665094b>\n\n------------------\n\nRequester\n\nJul 20 2026, 08:37PM via Email\nMs Daniel,\n\nFurther to my internal review request, I would like to provide a short\nclarification regarding the scope of my original FOI request.\n\nHaving reviewed my original request submitted on 3 July 2026, I wish to\nemphasise that the request was expressly for recorded information, not\nmerely for physical objects held within NLW collections.\n\nThe original request specifically sought:\ninventories, catalogues and asset registers;\nacquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records;\nprovenance files and ownership records;\nphotographs;\ncorrespondence concerning identification, recovery, ownership or location;\ninternal reports, legal advice and memoranda;\ncorrespondence involving the Buckler or Williams families;\ncorrespondence with Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, museums and other public\nbodies.\n\nTherefore, my concern is not that NLW does not hold furniture as part of a\ncollection. I understand that point. My concern is whether relevant\ndocumentary records were searched across appropriate archival collections\nwhere references to such items may exist.\n\nFor example, where NLW holds Bute Estate material relating to Ty\nMawr/Llandough, I would appreciate confirmation as to whether those\ncollections were searched for incidental references to:\nhousehold inventories;\nfixtures;\nvaluations;\nestate correspondence;\ntransfers or disposals;\nprovenance information;\nreferences to occupants or contents of the farmhouse.\n\nThis clarification is provided to assist the internal review and ensure the\noriginal request is considered in its full context.\nI appreciate the catalogue references already provided and look forward to\nconfirmation of the searches undertaken. ------------------\n\nRequester\n\nJul 20 2026, 08:35PM via Email\nMs Daniel,\n\nThank you for your response dated 20 July 2026 regarding FOI/2026/09 and\nfor identifying the catalogue references relating to Ty Mawr/Llandough\nwithin the Bute Estate collections.\n\nI would like to request an internal review, as I believe the response may\nhave interpreted the scope of my request too narrowly.\n\nMy request was for:\n\n\"All recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques,\nfixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House\nFarm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items received from Bute\nEstate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.\"\n\nI appreciate that the National Library of Wales does not collect furniture\nas a category of object and therefore may not hold the physical items\nthemselves. However, my request was not limited to physical objects or\nacquisition files. It sought *all recorded information* relating to such\nitems.\n\nThis could include, for example:\n\n- inventories;\n- valuations;\n- estate correspondence;\n- fixture schedules;\n- probate references;\n- sale catalogues;\n- photographs;\n- tenancy records;\n- references within Bute Estate papers;\n- records of transfer, removal or disposal.\n\nThe response confirms that NLW holds significant Bute Estate material\nrelating to Ty Mawr, including maps, leases and deeds. However, it does not\nclarify whether those wider collections were searched for references to the\nfarmhouse contents, fixtures, or related estate administration records.\n\nCould the internal review please clarify:\n\n1.\n\nWhat collections and record series were searched in responding to this\nrequest?\n2.\n\nWere searches undertaken beyond acquisition files, including within Bute\nEstate papers and related archival collections?\n3.\n\nWere terms such as:\n\n\n- Great House Farm;\n- Ty Mawr;\n- Llandough;\n- fixtures;\n- inventory;\n- valuation;\n- contents;\n- furnishings;\n- sale;\n- transfer;\n\nused as part of the search?\n\n4. If no relevant records are held, could you please confirm the\nsearches undertaken and the basis for that conclusion?\n\nThe reason this distinction matters is that my wider research concerns the\ndocumentary history of the farmhouse and garden plot following changes\naffecting Ty Mawr/Llandough after the 19th century. Records relating to\nfixtures, valuations, inventories or estate administration may provide\nimportant historical context, regardless of whether the physical items\nthemselves remain.\n\nI am not asking NLW to determine ownership or provide a legal opinion. I am\nseeking confirmation that all relevant archival holdings have been\nconsidered and that the request has been searched against the appropriate\ncollections.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to the outcome of the\ninternal review. ------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nJul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nAttached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n\nRegards,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nAttached Files\n\n-FOI2026-09.pdf <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4517166&type=0&key=5afe8f6fd61ea76cddc027c015f0bfb2>\n\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nJul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nI am writing in response to your recent application for information held by the Library\n \n(Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n \nYou will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n\nBest wishes,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nJul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\nGreat House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 Request\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items we received from Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.  Weather it be museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts from our land in Llandough. \n\nSpecifically, I request copies of all:\n-Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n-Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n-Provenance files and ownership records.\n-Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House Farm.\n-Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership or location of such items.\n-Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great House Farm furniture or household effects.\n-Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in connection with these items.\n-Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great House Farm.\n-Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n\nFor context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still gathering actionable intelligence. \n\nI appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n\nI am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle, museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom of Information Act.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest test where required.\n\nIf another public authority is more likely to hold the requested information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or advise me accordingly.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n\nThank you for using the National Library of Wales Enquiry Service.\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-19fb20f21f899949","subject":"Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/SH","name":"Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/SH","date":"2026-07-30T08:05:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fb20f21f899949.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fb20f21f899949-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-sh","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fb20f21f899949","direction":"received","from":"Wales.OfficeMail","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fb20f21f899949.json","attachments":[{"name":"Correspondence.pdf","title":"Schedule of first-registration documents WA231076 / WA240304","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-07-30_hmlr_first-registration-schedule.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":186813,"sha256":"d8ef59d252154e6ff8258cce4780cd1ca47be804ad9e9d65e893c09d6d02eafa"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n\nThe document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed document by post.\n\nYmholiad, nodyn atgoffa neu lythyr swyddogol gan Gofrestrfa Tir EM yw'r ddogfen atodedig. Nid cylchlythyr yw hi ac mae'n ymwneud naill ai â chais rydych wedi ei gyflwyno i ni neu ag eiddo y mae gennych fudd ynddo. Ni chaiff copi papur o'r ohebiaeth ei anfon atoch.\n\nMae'r ddogfen ar ffurf 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) sy'n dyblygu golwg y fersiwn copi caled. Bydd angen Adobe Acrobat Reader arnoch i agor y ddogfen. Os nad yw Adobe Acrobat Reader gennych yn barod, gallwch ei lwytho i lawr am ddim o www.adobe.com. Sylwch na fydd modd ichi ychwanegu testun at unrhyw ddogfen y mae'n rhaid ichi ei llenwi a dychwelyd i Gofrestrfa Tir EM gan ei bod ar ffurf PDF. Ar ôl ichi lenwi unrhyw ddogfen o'r fath bydd rhaid ichi ei dychwelyd trwy'r post.\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n\n\n\n\n\nDiben Cofrestrfa Tir EF yw gwarchod perchnogaeth eich tir a darparu gwasanaethau a data sy'n sail i farchnad eiddo effeithlon a gwybodus. Ein gweledigaeth yw: \"Marchnad eiddo o'r radd flaenaf fel rhan o economi ffyniannus a dyfodol cynaliadwy\".\n\nRydym yn gwirio pob neges ac atodiad am firysau hysbys. Fodd bynnag, fe'ch cynghorir mai chi sy'n gyfrifol am unrhyw atodiadau y byddwch yn eu hagor. Os ydych wedi cael yr ebost hwn trwy ddamwain, rhowch wybod i ni ac yna'i ddileu, os gwelwch yn dda.\n\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg.\n\nI weld sut mae Cofrestrfa Tir EF yn trin eich gwybodaeth bersonol, darllenwch ein Siarter gwybodaeth bersonol: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.cy.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (1)\n- Correspondence.pdf (application/pdf, 182 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-07-30_hmlr_first-registration-schedule.pdf"},{"id":"gm-19fae1bcda03af34","subject":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-29T13:41:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fae1bcda03af34.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fae1bcda03af34.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mathilde,\n\nThank you for your further reply and for carrying out the searches.\n\nI appreciate your assistance, but I would like to clarify the scope and\nconclusions of the search, as several points remain unresolved.\n\nFirstly, I should correct one detail: the individual I am researching is *Mr\nWilliams of Great House Farm, Llandough near Penarth*, not \"Mr William\".\nThe surname is significant because family history suggests that my\ngreat-grandfather, Mr Williams of Great House Farm, assisted Guglielmo\nMarconi during the 1897 South Wales wireless experiments.\n\nI fully understand that the absence of a result within the Postal Museum\ncatalogue does not necessarily mean that no such person or record existed.\nHowever, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n\n   1. *Search methodology*\n\nCould you confirm exactly which catalogue collections, series, or record\ngroups were searched for:\n\n   - Great House Farm, Llandough (Penarth)\n   - Llandough\n   - Lavernock\n   - Marconi\n   - wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n   - GPO Telegraph Department\n   - Engineering Department\n   - Williams / Mr Williams\n\n\n   2. *Scope of the negative result*\n\nWhen you state that \"nothing relevant came up\", does this mean:\n\n   - no indexed catalogue entries were found in Postal Museum collections;\n   - no digitised records were found;\n   - or that physical archival holdings were also checked?\n\n\n   3. *Records relating to GPO personnel*\n\nYou mentioned that most Marconi and Telegraph Department records are held\nat BT Archives. Could you confirm whether the Postal Museum holds any\ncatalogue references, finding aids, or transferred-record information\nindicating where the relevant GPO engineering correspondence, reports,\nnotebooks, or staff records may have been moved?\n\n   4. *The Williams connection*\n\nThe question I am trying to establish is not necessarily whether Mr\nWilliams was a Post Office employee. He may instead have been the\nowner/occupier of Great House Farm who assisted Marconi locally.\n\nCould you therefore confirm whether your search included references to:\n\n   - private individuals assisting demonstrations;\n   - hosts or local contacts connected with Marconi's experiments;\n   - correspondence mentioning residents of Llandough, Penarth, or\n   Lavernock?\n\nI appreciate that the absence of a catalogue entry cannot prove that an\nevent or person did not exist, particularly where local residents or\nprivate landowners were involved.\n\nMy aim is simply to establish the evidential trail: whether the Mr Williams\nmentioned in contemporary accounts can be identified, and whether surviving\nrecords connect him with Great House Farm and Marconi's experiments.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. I would be grateful for any further\nclarification on the above points before I proceed to BT Archives and\nGlamorgan Archives.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 10:32 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> I searched for all files related to the key words Great House Farm,\n> Llandough, Lavernock, wireless demonstration. Nothing relevant came up. For\n> Marconi and the Telegraph Departments, all the files would be held at BT\n> Archives.\n>\n>\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n>\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n>\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 29 July 2026 14:04\n> *To:* Archives <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Mathilde,\n>\n> Thank you very much for taking the time to carry out these searches and\n> for your detailed response.\n>\n> I appreciate the clarification regarding the distinction between Great\n> House Farm, Llandough near Penarth and the similarly named location near\n> Cowbridge. The Penarth/Llandough/Lavernock area is the location of interest.\n>\n> Your advice regarding BT Archives is very helpful, and I will follow this\n> up with them, as the surviving GPO Telegraph and wireless records appear\n> likely to be held there.\n>\n> I am also grateful for the information about the Post Office family\n> history records. My main interest is not that Mr Williams was necessarily a\n> Post Office employee, but whether the individual mentioned in contemporary\n> accounts as assisting Marconi at Great House Farm can be identified. Family\n> history passed down through my great grandfather's line suggests that a Mr\n> Williams of Great House Farm assisted Marconi during his South Wales\n> experiments, and I am trying to establish whether this can be connected to\n> my ancestor.\n>\n> If possible, could you let me know whether the search you carried out\n> included any of the following terms or collections, as this may help me\n> understand the scope of the search:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm (Llandough/Penarth)\n>    - Llandough\n>    - Lavernock\n>    - Marconi\n>    - wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n>    - GPO Telegraph Department / Engineering Department\n>\n> I will also contact Glamorgan Archives, as you suggest, since local\n> newspapers, estate records, or correspondence may contain information not\n> held in the national collections.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance. Your guidance has helped narrow down\n> where the relevant evidence is most likely to survive.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:31 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. I will do my best to check if we have\n> surviving records of this demonstration, although most of the records about\n> telecommunications were transferred to BT Archives so they might have more\n> information than us: https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge)\n>\n> I couldn’t find any record mentioning Great House Farm, Llandough. For\n> Penarth, there were some results but they were all dated much later than\n> the demonstration. We have many records on Cardiff, which you can find on\n> our online catalogue Here, but nothing relevant seemed to have come up.\n>\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>\n> Nothing came up for Lavernock either, the locations are too precise for\n> this type of records to have reached our archives. I searched for ‘wireless\n> demonstration’ and POST 88 Series titled ‘Post Office: Wireless Telegraphy\n> and Telephony’ mentions such events, but all the files are kept in BT\n> Archives.\n>\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>\n> Almost all the files related to Marconi are held in BT Archives.\n>\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> I couldn’t find any specific file about a Mr William from Great House\n> Farm, but the main records we have that are useful for family history\n> research are the Appointment Books, and the pension and gratuity records.\n> We also have Establishment Books and staff magazines that can be helpful\n> too. You can find more information about what we hold here:\n> https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/family-history/\n>  Please bear in mind that most villages, small towns, hamlets, etc. such as\n> Llandough had business that ran a postal service, and these people were not\n> directly employed by the Post Office, therefore, we won’t have any\n> information. If Mr Williams had another business, he was likely not\n> employed by the Post Office. A local archive might hold newspaper cuttings\n> or other information about this person: https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n> You are welcome to visit our archives, but I believe most of the records\n> and information you are looking for will be held at BT Archives. You can\n> contact them directly to organise an appointment.\n>\n>\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n>\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n>\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 24 July 2026 16:17\n> *To:* Booking Support Team <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> Dear Archive Team,\n>\n> I am conducting historical research into the General Post Office's\n> involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's wireless demonstrations in South Wales\n> during 1897.\n>\n> Post Office Ltd has advised that your archive is the most likely\n> repository for surviving historic GPO records relating to this period.\n>\n> I would be grateful if you could search for any records relating to:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge).\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> If records relating specifically to Mr Williams cannot be located, I would\n> also appreciate details of any records identifying GPO personnel, visitors\n> or local residents connected with the demonstrations, as these may help\n> establish the historical context.\n>\n> If another archive holds any of these records, I would be grateful if you\n> could advise where I should direct my enquiry.\n>\n> Mr Williams of Great House Farm was my great grandad. I am trying to\n> ascertain if the Mr Williams post office worker, mentioned helping Marconi\n> in the article, was the same man as my great grandfather. I am also looking\n> for any more connections between my family, my former home and Marconi and\n> the radio experiments at lavernock point. Which I understand were already\n> underway before Marconi arrived to South Wales.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and assistance. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> \n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fae13bff92ee94","subject":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-29T13:32:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fae13bff92ee94.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e","direction":"received","from":"Archives","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fae13bff92ee94.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nI searched for all files related to the key words Great House Farm, Llandough, Lavernock, wireless demonstration. Nothing relevant came up. For Marconi and the Telegraph Departments, all the files would be held at BT Archives.\n\nI hope this helps,\n\nBest regards,\n\nMathilde\n\nMathilde Jourdan\nArchives Assistant\nThe Postal Museum | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\nT: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:[email redacted] \n[Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Facebook channel] [Twitter Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel] [Instgram Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel] [Youtube Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel] \n\n[cid:image005.png@01DD1F65.E5CB0B30]\nThe Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust. Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 29 July 2026 14:04\nTo: Archives  \nSubject: Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n\nDear Mathilde,\n\nThank you very much for taking the time to carry out these searches and for your detailed response.\n\nI appreciate the clarification regarding the distinction between Great House Farm, Llandough near Penarth and the similarly named location near Cowbridge. The Penarth/Llandough/Lavernock area is the location of interest.\n\nYour advice regarding BT Archives is very helpful, and I will follow this up with them, as the surviving GPO Telegraph and wireless records appear likely to be held there.\n\nI am also grateful for the information about the Post Office family history records. My main interest is not that Mr Williams was necessarily a Post Office employee, but whether the individual mentioned in contemporary accounts as assisting Marconi at Great House Farm can be identified. Family history passed down through my great grandfather's line suggests that a Mr Williams of Great House Farm assisted Marconi during his South Wales experiments, and I am trying to establish whether this can be connected to my ancestor.\n\nIf possible, could you let me know whether the search you carried out included any of the following terms or collections, as this may help me understand the scope of the search:\n\n  *   Great House Farm (Llandough/Penarth)\n  *   Llandough\n  *   Lavernock\n  *   Marconi\n  *   wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n  *   GPO Telegraph Department / Engineering Department\n\nI will also contact Glamorgan Archives, as you suggest, since local newspapers, estate records, or correspondence may contain information not held in the national collections.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. Your guidance has helped narrow down where the relevant evidence is most likely to survive.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:31 Archives,  > wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your enquiry. I will do my best to check if we have surviving records of this demonstration, although most of the records about telecommunications were transferred to BT Archives so they might have more information than us: https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\n\n  *   Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge)\nI couldn't find any record mentioning Great House Farm, Llandough. For Penarth, there were some results but they were all dated much later than the demonstration. We have many records on Cardiff, which you can find on our online catalogue Here, but nothing relevant seemed to have come up.\n\n  *   Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless demonstration sites.\nNothing came up for Lavernock either, the locations are too precise for this type of records to have reached our archives. I searched for 'wireless demonstration' and POST 88 Series titled 'Post Office: Wireless Telegraphy and Telephony' mentions such events, but all the files are kept in BT Archives.\n\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\nAlmost all the files related to Marconi are held in BT Archives.\n\n  *   GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these demonstrations.\nSee above.\n\n  *   Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\nSee above.\n\n  *   Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay at the property.\nI couldn't find any specific file about a Mr William from Great House Farm, but the main records we have that are useful for family history research are the Appointment Books, and the pension and gratuity records. We also have Establishment Books and staff magazines that can be helpful too. You can find more information about what we hold here:  https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/family-history/  Please bear in mind that most villages, small towns, hamlets, etc. such as Llandough had business that ran a postal service, and these people were not directly employed by the Post Office, therefore, we won't have any information. If Mr Williams had another business, he was likely not employed by the Post Office. A local archive might hold newspaper cuttings or other information about this person: https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\nYou are welcome to visit our archives, but I believe most of the records and information you are looking for will be held at BT Archives. You can contact them directly to organise an appointment.\n\nI hope this helps,\n\nBest regards,\n\nMathilde\n\nMathilde Jourdan\nArchives Assistant\nThe Postal Museum | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted] \nT: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:[email redacted] \n[Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Facebook channel] [Twitter Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel] [Instgram Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel] [Youtube Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel] \n\n[cid:image005.png@01DD1F65.E5CB0B30]\nThe Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust. Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n\n\nFrom: Requester  >\nSent: 24 July 2026 16:17\nTo: Booking Support Team  >\nSubject: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted] . Learn why this is important \n\nDear Archive Team,\n\nI am conducting historical research into the General Post Office's involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's wireless demonstrations in South Wales during 1897.\n\nPost Office Ltd has advised that your archive is the most likely repository for surviving historic GPO records relating to this period.\n\nI would be grateful if you could search for any records relating to:\n\n  *   Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge).\n  *   Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless demonstration sites.\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n  *   GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these demonstrations.\n  *   Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n  *   Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay at the property.\n\nIf records relating specifically to Mr Williams cannot be located, I would also appreciate details of any records identifying GPO personnel, visitors or local residents connected with the demonstrations, as these may help establish the historical context.\n\nIf another archive holds any of these records, I would be grateful if you could advise where I should direct my enquiry.\n\nMr Williams of Great House Farm was my great grandad. I am trying to ascertain if the Mr Williams post office worker, mentioned helping Marconi in the article, was the same man as my great grandfather. I am also looking for any more connections between my family, my former home and Marconi and the radio experiments at lavernock point. Which I understand were already underway before Marconi arrived to South Wales.\n\nThank you for your time and assistance. I look forward to your response.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nRequester\n\n"},{"id":"gm-19fadfee3efc0929","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-29T13:09:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fadfee3efc0929.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fadfee3efc0929.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dr Roberts,\nThank you for the detailed internal review outcome of FOI/2026/09 dated 29\nJuly 2026.\nI note the clarification of the searches undertaken (including Bute Estate\nseries D153, D205 and D219), the rationale for limiting terms to the\nproperty name, and the application of section 21 to the publicly accessible\ncatalogue and Reading Room material.\nThis closes the internal review from my side. I will proceed via the\nLibrary’s normal catalogue and Reading Room services for the identified\nestate records.\nYours sincerely,\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:23 National Library of Wales, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> --# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Owain Roberts\n>\n> Jul 29 2026, 11:21AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Please find attached the outcome of the internal review that you requested\n> on the 20 July 2026. I can confirm that the internal review considered the\n> clarification that you provided on the 20 July 2026.\n>\n> Regards,\n> Dr Owain Rhys Roberts\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09-Internal_Review_Outcome.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4534050&type=0&key=f13df66d89dd9bb9040b52659665094b>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 08:37PM via Email\n> Ms Daniel,\n>\n> Further to my internal review request, I would like to provide a short\n> clarification regarding the scope of my original FOI request.\n>\n> Having reviewed my original request submitted on 3 July 2026, I wish to\n> emphasise that the request was expressly for recorded information, not\n> merely for physical objects held within NLW collections.\n>\n> The original request specifically sought:\n> inventories, catalogues and asset registers;\n> acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records;\n> provenance files and ownership records;\n> photographs;\n> correspondence concerning identification, recovery, ownership or location;\n> internal reports, legal advice and memoranda;\n> correspondence involving the Buckler or Williams families;\n> correspondence with Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, museums and other public\n> bodies.\n>\n> Therefore, my concern is not that NLW does not hold furniture as part of a\n> collection. I understand that point. My concern is whether relevant\n> documentary records were searched across appropriate archival collections\n> where references to such items may exist.\n>\n> For example, where NLW holds Bute Estate material relating to Ty\n> Mawr/Llandough, I would appreciate confirmation as to whether those\n> collections were searched for incidental references to:\n> household inventories;\n> fixtures;\n> valuations;\n> estate correspondence;\n> transfers or disposals;\n> provenance information;\n> references to occupants or contents of the farmhouse.\n>\n> This clarification is provided to assist the internal review and ensure the\n> original request is considered in its full context.\n> I appreciate the catalogue references already provided and look forward to\n> confirmation of the searches undertaken.\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 08:35PM via Email\n> Ms Daniel,\n>\n> Thank you for your response dated 20 July 2026 regarding FOI/2026/09 and\n> for identifying the catalogue references relating to Ty Mawr/Llandough\n> within the Bute Estate collections.\n>\n> I would like to request an internal review, as I believe the response may\n> have interpreted the scope of my request too narrowly.\n>\n> My request was for:\n>\n> \"All recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques,\n> fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House\n> Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items received from Bute\n> Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.\"\n>\n> I appreciate that the National Library of Wales does not collect furniture\n> as a category of object and therefore may not hold the physical items\n> themselves. However, my request was not limited to physical objects or\n> acquisition files. It sought *all recorded information* relating to such\n> items.\n>\n> This could include, for example:\n>\n> - inventories;\n> - valuations;\n> - estate correspondence;\n> - fixture schedules;\n> - probate references;\n> - sale catalogues;\n> - photographs;\n> - tenancy records;\n> - references within Bute Estate papers;\n> - records of transfer, removal or disposal.\n>\n> The response confirms that NLW holds significant Bute Estate material\n> relating to Ty Mawr, including maps, leases and deeds. However, it does not\n> clarify whether those wider collections were searched for references to the\n> farmhouse contents, fixtures, or related estate administration records.\n>\n> Could the internal review please clarify:\n>\n> 1.\n>\n> What collections and record series were searched in responding to this\n> request?\n> 2.\n>\n> Were searches undertaken beyond acquisition files, including within Bute\n> Estate papers and related archival collections?\n> 3.\n>\n> Were terms such as:\n>\n>\n> - Great House Farm;\n> - Ty Mawr;\n> - Llandough;\n> - fixtures;\n> - inventory;\n> - valuation;\n> - contents;\n> - furnishings;\n> - sale;\n> - transfer;\n>\n> used as part of the search?\n>\n> 4. If no relevant records are held, could you please confirm the\n> searches undertaken and the basis for that conclusion?\n>\n> The reason this distinction matters is that my wider research concerns the\n> documentary history of the farmhouse and garden plot following changes\n> affecting Ty Mawr/Llandough after the 19th century. Records relating to\n> fixtures, valuations, inventories or estate administration may provide\n> important historical context, regardless of whether the physical items\n> themselves remain.\n>\n> I am not asking NLW to determine ownership or provide a legal opinion. I am\n> seeking confirmation that all relevant archival holdings have been\n> considered and that the request has been searched against the appropriate\n> collections.\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance. I look forward to the outcome of the\n> internal review.\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Attached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4517166&type=0&key=5afe8f6fd61ea76cddc027c015f0bfb2>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> I am writing in response to your recent application for information held\n> by the Library\n>\n> (Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n>\n> You will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n>\n> Best wishes,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Cwestiwn gwreiddiol\n>\n> Jul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\n> Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Thank you for using the National Library of Wales Enquiry Service.\n>\n>\n> This email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n>\n> Read our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fadfaf94c2ee98","subject":"Automatic reply: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Automatic reply: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-29T13:05:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fadfaf94c2ee98.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94b41e012a821-automatic-reply-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94b41e012a821","direction":"received","from":"Archives","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fadfaf94c2ee98.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for your message. We will respond to your enquiry in a timely manner within 10 working days (or sooner if you are booking an appointment in the next 10 days).\n\n\nThe Archive is open 10:00-16:30 Wednesdays-Fridays (except on bank holidays) and the second Saturday of each month. If you wish to view original archive material, we recommend you book in advance via: https://catalogue.postalmuseum.org/ (you must be signed in), or by email.\n\n\nWith kind regards,\n\n\nTPM Archive Team\n\n\nDid you know we're a charity? There are lots of ways you can get involved in our work. To find out more visit: www.postalmuseum.org/support-us<http://www.postalmuseum.org/support-us>"},{"id":"gm-19fadf9d61fc9aca","subject":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-29T13:04:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fadf9d61fc9aca.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e-marconi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["postal-museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["postal-museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f94ad9e6597d2e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"postal-museum","name":"The Postal Museum"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fadf9d61fc9aca.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Mathilde,\n\nThank you very much for taking the time to carry out these searches and for\nyour detailed response.\n\nI appreciate the clarification regarding the distinction between Great\nHouse Farm, Llandough near Penarth and the similarly named location near\nCowbridge. The Penarth/Llandough/Lavernock area is the location of interest.\n\nYour advice regarding BT Archives is very helpful, and I will follow this\nup with them, as the surviving GPO Telegraph and wireless records appear\nlikely to be held there.\n\nI am also grateful for the information about the Post Office family history\nrecords. My main interest is not that Mr Williams was necessarily a Post\nOffice employee, but whether the individual mentioned in contemporary\naccounts as assisting Marconi at Great House Farm can be identified. Family\nhistory passed down through my great grandfather's line suggests that a Mr\nWilliams of Great House Farm assisted Marconi during his South Wales\nexperiments, and I am trying to establish whether this can be connected to\nmy ancestor.\n\nIf possible, could you let me know whether the search you carried out\nincluded any of the following terms or collections, as this may help me\nunderstand the scope of the search:\n\n   - Great House Farm (Llandough/Penarth)\n   - Llandough\n   - Lavernock\n   - Marconi\n   - wireless telegraphy demonstrations (1897)\n   - GPO Telegraph Department / Engineering Department\n\nI will also contact Glamorgan Archives, as you suggest, since local\nnewspapers, estate records, or correspondence may contain information not\nheld in the national collections.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. Your guidance has helped narrow down\nwhere the relevant evidence is most likely to survive.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 07:31 Archives, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. I will do my best to check if we have\n> surviving records of this demonstration, although most of the records about\n> telecommunications were transferred to BT Archives so they might have more\n> information than us: https://www.bt.com/about/bt/our-history/bt-archives\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge)\n>\n> I couldn’t find any record mentioning Great House Farm, Llandough. For\n> Penarth, there were some results but they were all dated much later than\n> the demonstration. We have many records on Cardiff, which you can find on\n> our online catalogue Here, but nothing relevant seemed to have come up.\n>\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>\n> Nothing came up for Lavernock either, the locations are too precise for\n> this type of records to have reached our archives. I searched for ‘wireless\n> demonstration’ and POST 88 Series titled ‘Post Office: Wireless Telegraphy\n> and Telephony’ mentions such events, but all the files are kept in BT\n> Archives.\n>\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>\n> Almost all the files related to Marconi are held in BT Archives.\n>\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>\n> See above.\n>\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> I couldn’t find any specific file about a Mr William from Great House\n> Farm, but the main records we have that are useful for family history\n> research are the Appointment Books, and the pension and gratuity records.\n> We also have Establishment Books and staff magazines that can be helpful\n> too. You can find more information about what we hold here:\n> https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/family-history/\n>  Please bear in mind that most villages, small towns, hamlets, etc. such as\n> Llandough had business that ran a postal service, and these people were not\n> directly employed by the Post Office, therefore, we won’t have any\n> information. If Mr Williams had another business, he was likely not\n> employed by the Post Office. A local archive might hold newspaper cuttings\n> or other information about this person: https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n> You are welcome to visit our archives, but I believe most of the records\n> and information you are looking for will be held at BT Archives. You can\n> contact them directly to organise an appointment.\n>\n>\n>\n> I hope this helps,\n>\n>\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Mathilde\n>\n>\n>\n> *Mathilde Jourdan*\n>\n> Archives Assistant\n>\n> *The Postal Museum* | 15-20 Phoenix Place | London [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> T: [phone redacted] | Archive enquiries: [phone redacted]  | E:\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> [image: Facebook Icon - click to open a new browser window showing the\n> Postal Museum Facebook channel]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Twitter Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Twitter channel]\n> <https://twitter.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Instgram Icon - click to\n> open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Instragram channel]\n> <https://www.instagram.com/thepostalmuseum/>[image: Youtube Icon - click\n> to open a new browser window showing the Postal Museum Youtube channel]\n> <https://www.youtube.com/thepostalmuseum>\n>\n>\n>\n> The Postal Museum is the public identity of the Postal Heritage Trust.\n> Registered as a charity in England and Wales. Registered Charity Number\n> 1102360. Company Number 4896056\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 24 July 2026 16:17\n> *To:* Booking Support Team <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Marconi, Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> Dear Archive Team,\n>\n> I am conducting historical research into the General Post Office's\n> involvement in Guglielmo Marconi's wireless demonstrations in South Wales\n> during 1897.\n>\n> Post Office Ltd has advised that your archive is the most likely\n> repository for surviving historic GPO records relating to this period.\n>\n> I would be grateful if you could search for any records relating to:\n>\n>    - Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth, Cardiff (not Great House\n>    Farm, Llandough near Cowbridge).\n>    - Llandough, Penarth, Lavernock and the surrounding wireless\n>    demonstration sites.\n>    - Guglielmo Marconi's 1897 demonstrations.\n>    - GPO Telegraph or Engineering Department records concerning these\n>    demonstrations.\n>    - Correspondence, reports, notebooks, diaries, staff lists, expense\n>    claims, photographs or plans relating to engineers or officials present.\n>    - Any references to Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, who\n>    family history suggests assisted Marconi before, during or after his stay\n>    at the property.\n>\n> If records relating specifically to Mr Williams cannot be located, I would\n> also appreciate details of any records identifying GPO personnel, visitors\n> or local residents connected with the demonstrations, as these may help\n> establish the historical context.\n>\n> If another archive holds any of these records, I would be grateful if you\n> could advise where I should direct my enquiry.\n>\n> Mr Williams of Great House Farm was my great grandad. I am trying to\n> ascertain if the Mr Williams post office worker, mentioned helping Marconi\n> in the article, was the same man as my great grandfather. I am also looking\n> for any more connections between my family, my former home and Marconi and\n> the radio experiments at lavernock point. Which I understand were already\n> underway before Marconi arrived to South Wales.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and assistance. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> \n>"},{"id":"gm-19fadf79c5d8412c","subject":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-07-29T12:59:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fadf79c5d8412c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fadf79c5d8412c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Longford,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nI note your confirmation that Cadw holds no transfer lists, accession\nrecords, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records\nrelating to Great House Farm were transferred to the RCAHMW, and that Cadw\nalso holds no record of their destruction. I also note that the suggestion\nthat records may have been transferred or destroyed is based upon an\ninspector's understanding of historic practice rather than documentary\nevidence relating to this case.\n\nHowever, there remain a small number of points on which I would be grateful\nfor clarification.\n\n   1.\n\n   The original response of 11 June stated that associated records \"would\n   have been either transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the Public\n   Records Act 1958\". As no transfer or destruction documentation has been\n   identified, on what evidential basis was that statement made?\n   2.\n\n   Does the Welsh Government now accept that it holds no documentary\n   evidence that any records relating to Great House Farm were transferred to\n   the RCAHMW?\n   3.\n\n   Contemporary press reports concerning the proposed protection of Great\n   House Farm referred to consultation with other departments and bodies\n   before a decision was reached. During this correspondence I therefore asked\n   whether searches extended to correspondence with other departments,\n   external bodies and related records. Although you have confirmed wider\n   searches were undertaken, no such records have been identified. Could you\n   therefore confirm whether the Welsh Government's position is that it holds\n   no surviving correspondence, memoranda, consultation records or other\n   documents relating to any such consultations concerning Great House Farm?\n   4.\n\n   Is the Welsh Government's position therefore that, apart from the two\n   photographs dated 29 July 1988, no inspection report, recommendation,\n   consultation correspondence, assessment, case file or associated\n   documentation relating to the 1988 consideration of Great House Farm\n   survives?\n\nThese questions are intended solely to clarify the historical record and to\nreconcile the original response with the findings of the internal review.\n\nThank you for your assistance, and I look forward to your reply.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 29 Jul 2026, 09:10 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for your email, apologies for the delay in responding I have\n> been on annual leave. To answer your queries I must refer you back to my\n> previous emails of the 10th 3rd and 2nd July.\n>\n>\n>\n> I appreciate your concerns and desires to find the information. However, I\n> can confirm that all records were checked for the information you requested\n> and we hold no further information or a record of the destruction. Cadw’s\n> inspector advised, based on his experience, that he understood the practice\n> was to either transfer records to the RCAHMW or destroy them under the\n> Public Records Act 1958. We have no record of any transfer lists, accession\n> records, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records\n> relating to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW.  The\n> photograph provides the only documentary evidence that Great House Farm was\n> visited by Cadw and did not meet the criteria as it was not included on the\n> list.\n>\n>\n>\n> To be clear, we do not have any further information which would help with\n> your search for the relevant information. If you remain dissatisfied with\n> this response you have the right to complain to the Information\n> Commissioner. The Information Commissioner can be contacted at:\n>\n> Information Commissioner’s Office,\n>\n> Wycliffe House,\n>\n> Water Lane,\n>\n> Wilmslow,\n>\n> Cheshire,\n>\n> [postcode redacted].\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 15 July 2026 18:28\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Ms Longford,\n>\n> Before responding to my earlier email, please may I add the following to\n> my enquiry, even if you require addition time to respond due to this\n> addition to my enquiry;\n>\n> In addition to my email of 2 July, there are a small number of further\n> points which I would be grateful if you could address as they arise\n> directly from comparing the original response with the internal review.\n>\n> The original response of 11 June 2026 stated:\n>\n> \"Any other associated records would have been either transferred to the\n> Royal Commission on the Ancient & Historical Monuments of Wales for\n> permanent preservation, or destroyed under the Public Record Act 1958.\"\n>\n> However, the internal review of 2 July 2026 states instead that:\n>\n> \"There is also no evidence that any relevant files have been transferred\n> to the RCAHMW.\"\n>\n> and\n>\n> \"It is possible that the file was destroyed before it was ever updated on\n> our electronic filing system.\"\n>\n> These appear to be materially different positions.\n>\n> Accordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n>\n>    1. What evidence supported the original statement that any associated\n>    records would have been transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the\n>    Public Records Act 1958?\n>    2. Following the internal review, does Welsh Government now accept\n>    that there is no evidence that any relevant records were transferred to the\n>    RCAHMW?\n>    3. Does Welsh Government hold any transfer lists, accession records,\n>    archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating\n>    to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW?\n>    4. If no such documentation exists, on what evidential basis was the\n>    original statement regarding transfer to the RCAHMW made?\n>    5. Likewise, if there is no destruction register, disposal log or\n>    audit trail relating to the relevant file, on what evidential basis has\n>    destruction been suggested?\n>\n> Finally, the original response stated as fact that Great House Farm was\n> visited by Cadw inspectors and did not meet the statutory listing criteria.\n> The internal review, however, confirms that no assessment, report or case\n> file has been located.\n>\n> Could you therefore identify the documentary evidence upon which that\n> conclusion was based, or alternatively confirm whether the statement in the\n> original response was an inference drawn from the existence of the two\n> photographs rather than from any surviving assessment records.\n>\n> These points are intended simply to clarify the historical record and to\n> reconcile what appear to be two materially different explanations contained\n> within the original response and the internal review.\n>\n> Thank you again for your assistance, and I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n>\n>  & Life Member\n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 23:41 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> 👍🏻\n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will\n> review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17\n> th July.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 21:01\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review\n> of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House\n> Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> I appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the\n> explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n>\n> However, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and\n> the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could\n> clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n>\n> *1. Documentary basis of the original response*\n>\n> The original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and\n> assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the\n> statutory listing criteria.\n>\n> The internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file\n> relating to that decision has been located and further states that any\n> relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the\n> electronic records system.\n>\n> Please therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original\n> response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the\n> listing criteria.\n>\n> Specifically:\n>\n>    - Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n>    - If so, please identify that record.\n>    - If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n>\n> *2. The inspection of 29 July 1988*\n>\n> The original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n>\n> Please confirm:\n>\n>    - whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing\n>    inspection;\n>    - whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n>    - whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks,\n>    photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n>    - if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have\n>    been destroyed.\n>\n> *3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed*\n>\n> The review states that it is possible documentation dating from around\n> 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n>\n> Please clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n>\n>    - documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n>    - records management documentation such as retention schedules,\n>    destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n>    - a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n>\n> If no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please\n> confirm this.\n>\n> *4. Scope of the searches*\n>\n> Please confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing\n> files to include, where appropriate:\n>\n>    - ministerial correspondence;\n>    - senior officials' correspondence;\n>    - legal files;\n>    - inspector's working papers;\n>    - site visit records;\n>    - archaeological or conservation files;\n>    - policy records; and\n>    - correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of\n>    Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n>\n> If any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you\n> could identify which.\n>\n> *5. Welsh Government's position*\n>\n> Finally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's\n> position regarding Great House Farm.\n>\n> Does the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n>\n>    - that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n>    - that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n>    - that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration\n>    took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n>\n> If none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful if\n> you could explain what the Welsh Government's position is.\n>\n> These questions arise directly from the original response and the internal\n> review and are intended to clarify the historical record rather than seek\n> the creation of new information.\n>\n> I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:10 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Please see attached my review of your request noted ATISN 27021.\n>\n> Please let me know if you have any questions or queries.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy Longford\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 June 2026 09:10\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> I suspected so.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thanks Amy.\n>\n>\n>\n> I look forward.\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> On Tue, 16 Jun 2026, 05:08 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the quick response and for confirming your position. I\n> totally understand and whilst the letters may appear formal, there are set\n> templates to use for a review, I will bear this in mind whilst taking this\n> forward.\n>\n>\n>\n> Just to let you know, I have had initial conversations internally which I\n> will continue. I will keep you updated as best as I can.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 June 2026 05:38\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for the acknowledgement letter and for handling the internal\n> review.\n>\n> For the record, my communications with Cadw have been enquiries and\n> requests for information under FOI/EIR (ATISN 27021), specifically\n> regarding the statutory listing history, assessments and related records\n> (including the 1988 inspection photographs) for the building known as Great\n> House Farm / Ty Mawr / Church View Close. I subsequently requested an\n> internal review of the response provided.\n>\n> This was not framed or intended as a formal complaint. I would therefore\n> be grateful if the matter could be treated and recorded as an information\n> request and internal review under FOI/EIR, rather than as a complaint.\n>\n> My enquiries concern Cadw's functions in relation to the listing and\n> assessment of the building only.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n\n>\n> Life Member: Royal Corps of Signals\n>\n>\n>\n> On Mon, 15 Jun 2026, 12:44 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for your email requesting an internal review of you EOI\n> request, I will be the case officer dealing with the review, please see the\n> attached acknowledgement letter with key dates. Any questions, please let\n> me know and I will do my best to help.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth C