n Welsh. Any correspondence\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\n>\n> Sganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth\n> Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich\n> data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd\n> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu\n> eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon\n> ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn\n> Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh\n> Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh\n> Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the\n> Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice\n> <https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en>\n> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your\n> privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence\n> received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will\n> not lead to a delay in responding.\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fadc8628eb9d17","subject":"RE: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"RE: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-07-29T12:10:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fadc8628eb9d17.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fadc8628eb9d17.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nMany thanks for your email, apologies for the delay in responding I have been on annual leave. To answer your queries I must refer you back to my previous emails of the 10th 3rd and 2nd July.\n\nI appreciate your concerns and desires to find the information. However, I can confirm that all records were checked for the information you requested and we hold no further information or a record of the destruction. Cadw’s inspector advised, based on his experience, that he understood the practice was to either transfer records to the RCAHMW or destroy them under the Public Records Act 1958. We have no record of any transfer lists, accession records, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW.  The photograph provides the only documentary evidence that Great House Farm was visited by Cadw and did not meet the criteria as it was not included on the list.\n\nTo be clear, we do not have any further information which would help with your search for the relevant information. If you remain dissatisfied with this response you have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner. The Information Commissioner can be contacted at:\n\nInformation Commissioner’s Office,\n\nWycliffe House,\n\nWater Lane,\n\nWilmslow,\n\nCheshire,\n[postcode redacted].\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n\nAmy Longford IHBC MRTPI\nUwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n/ Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\nAmgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\nCadw\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]<http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n[https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]<http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\nYmunwch â Cadw<https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\nJoin Cadw<https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 15 July 2026 18:28\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n\nMs Longford,\n\nBefore responding to my earlier email, please may I add the following to my enquiry, even if you require addition time to respond due to this addition to my enquiry;\n\nIn addition to my email of 2 July, there are a small number of further points which I would be grateful if you could address as they arise directly from comparing the original response with the internal review.\n\nThe original response of 11 June 2026 stated:\n\n\"Any other associated records would have been either transferred to the Royal Commission on the Ancient & Historical Monuments of Wales for permanent preservation, or destroyed under the Public Record Act 1958.\"\n\nHowever, the internal review of 2 July 2026 states instead that:\n\n\"There is also no evidence that any relevant files have been transferred to the RCAHMW.\"\n\nand\n\n\"It is possible that the file was destroyed before it was ever updated on our electronic filing system.\"\n\nThese appear to be materially different positions.\n\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n\n  1.  What evidence supported the original statement that any associated records would have been transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the Public Records Act 1958?\n  2.  Following the internal review, does Welsh Government now accept that there is no evidence that any relevant records were transferred to the RCAHMW?\n  3.  Does Welsh Government hold any transfer lists, accession records, archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW?\n  4.  If no such documentation exists, on what evidential basis was the original statement regarding transfer to the RCAHMW made?\n  5.  Likewise, if there is no destruction register, disposal log or audit trail relating to the relevant file, on what evidential basis has destruction been suggested?\n\nFinally, the original response stated as fact that Great House Farm was visited by Cadw inspectors and did not meet the statutory listing criteria. The internal review, however, confirms that no assessment, report or case file has been located.\n\nCould you therefore identify the documentary evidence upon which that conclusion was based, or alternatively confirm whether the statement in the original response was an inference drawn from the existence of the two photographs rather than from any surviving assessment records.\n\nThese points are intended simply to clarify the historical record and to reconcile what appear to be two materially different explanations contained within the original response and the internal review.\n\nThank you again for your assistance, and I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\n & Life Member\n\nOn Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 23:41 Requester, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\n👍🏻\n\nOn Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17th July.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 02 July 2026 21:01\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n\nDear Ms Longford,\n\nThank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nI appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n\nHowever, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n\n1. Documentary basis of the original response\n\nThe original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the statutory listing criteria.\n\nThe internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file relating to that decision has been located and further states that any relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n\nPlease therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the listing criteria.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n  *   Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n  *   If so, please identify that record.\n  *   If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n\n2. The inspection of 29 July 1988\n\nThe original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n\nPlease confirm:\n\n  *   whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing inspection;\n  *   whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n  *   whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks, photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n  *   if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have been destroyed.\n\n3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed\n\nThe review states that it is possible documentation dating from around 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n\nPlease clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n\n  *   documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n  *   records management documentation such as retention schedules, destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n  *   a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n\nIf no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please confirm this.\n\n4. Scope of the searches\n\nPlease confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing files to include, where appropriate:\n\n  *   ministerial correspondence;\n  *   senior officials' correspondence;\n  *   legal files;\n  *   inspector's working papers;\n  *   site visit records;\n  *   archaeological or conservation files;\n  *   policy records; and\n  *   correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n\nIf any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you could identify which.\n\n5. Welsh Government's position\n\nFinally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's position regarding Great House Farm.\n\nDoes the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n\n  *   that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n  *   that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n  *   that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n\nIf none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful if you could explain what the Welsh Government's position is.\n\nThese questions arise directly from the original response and the internal review and are intended to clarify the historical record rather than seek the creation of new information.\n\nI look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:10 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nPlease see attached my review of your request noted ATISN 27021.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or queries.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy Longford\n\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n\nAmy Longford IHBC MRTPI\nUwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n/ Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\nAmgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\nCadw\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]<http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n[https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]<http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\nYmunwch â Cadw<https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\nJoin Cadw<https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 June 2026 09:10\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\nI suspected so.\n\nThanks Amy.\n\nI look forward.\n\nRequester\n\nOn Tue, 16 Jun 2026, 05:08 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for the quick response and for confirming your position. I totally understand and whilst the letters may appear formal, there are set templates to use for a review, I will bear this in mind whilst taking this forward.\n\nJust to let you know, I have had initial conversations internally which I will continue. I will keep you updated as best as I can.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 June 2026 05:38\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n\nMs Longford,\n\nThank you for the acknowledgement letter and for handling the internal review.\n\nFor the record, my communications with Cadw have been enquiries and requests for information under FOI/EIR (ATISN 27021), specifically regarding the statutory listing history, assessments and related records (including the 1988 inspection photographs) for the building known as Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Church View Close. I subsequently requested an internal review of the response provided.\n\nThis was not framed or intended as a formal complaint. I would therefore be grateful if the matter could be treated and recorded as an information request and internal review under FOI/EIR, rather than as a complaint.\n\nMy enquiries concern Cadw's functions in relation to the listing and assessment of the building only.\n\nRegards,\nRequester \n\nLife Member: Royal Corps of Signals\n\nOn Mon, 15 Jun 2026, 12:44 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nMany thanks for your email requesting an internal review of you EOI request, I will be the case officer dealing with the review, please see the attached acknowledgement letter with key dates. Any questions, please let me know and I will do my best to help.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n\nAmy Longford IHBC MRTPI\nUwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n/ Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\nAmgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\nCadw\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]<http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n[https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]<http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\nYmunwch â Cadw<https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\nJoin Cadw<https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email wa