he family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa579a3ae1c297","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fa579a3ae1c297.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please quickly read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\n\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n• Your full postal address\n• Your contact telephone number\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in Parliament, it will be dealt with as appropriate.\n\nThank you for taking the time to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nStephen\n\n[X]\nStephen Doughty MP / AS\nMember of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth // Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nHouse of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19fa5794010d81c7","subject":"Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Complaint - Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-07-27T21:26:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fa5794010d81c7.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa5759a198dbff-complaint-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa5759a198dbff","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fa5794010d81c7.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Stephen Doughty MP,\n\nWith great regret I am writing to lodge a formal complaint about the\nfailure of your office to provide any substantive response to my repeated\ncorrespondence concerning historic land, planning, enforcement, heritage\nand related public-interest matters at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr),\nLlandough (now Church View Close).\n\nI am a constituent (address below) with a legitimate and long-standing\nfamily interest in the site. The issues raised include alleged defective\nnotices, loss of opportunity to contest enforcement leading to demolition\nin 1988, heritage/regulatory oversight, planning and title records, and\nrelated transparency failures.\n\nDespite multiple contacts, I have received only automated acknowledgements\nand no substantive reply.\n\n### Full correspondence log with your office (\n[email redacted])\n\n| Date       | Subject / Key content\n                         | Response received          |\n|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|\n| 29 May 2026 | Formal disclosure notice & litigation hold / FOIA-EIR style\nrequest on historic significance, planning and displaced family records |\nAutomated acknowledgement only |\n\n| 31 May 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying address and further detail\n                          | None substantive           |\n\n| 12 Jun 2026 | “Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)” –\ndetailed personal/historical letter with attachments | Automated\nacknowledgement only |\n\n| 12 Jun 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying full name, address and\ncontact details                  | None substantive           |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | Complaint of maladministration (defective notice,\nenforcement process, loss of opportunity) copied to you | Automated\nacknowledgement only |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | Reply to auto-reply supplying full personal details and\nreferences                    | None substantive           |\n\n| 13 Jul 2026 | Follow-up on previous emails regarding historical records,\ncouncil involvement and transparency; request for update and confirmation\nof review | None                       |\n\n### What I am asking for\n\n1. A full written response addressing the points raised in the logged\nemails.\n2. Confirmation whether your office has reviewed the matter and what, if\nany, assistance or representation you are able to offer.\n\n3. A clear reply within **14 days** of the date of this email.\n\nI have retained the full original emails and attachments and can supply\nthem on request. Please acknowledge receipt of this formal complaint.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fa5752dc501f03","subject":"Automatic reply: Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close","name":"Automatic reply: Complaint –