you for your email. I am currently away from the office until the 27th July 2026.\n\nFor urgent matters please contact Vicci Rowlands at [email redacted]. or Henry Brown [email redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fa574a3151e1b8","subject":"Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close","name":"Complaint – Failure to Respond / Failure to Deal Properly with Case – Cllr George Carroll (Llandough) – Great House Farm / Church View Close","date":"2026-07-27T21:21:51Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fa574a3151e1b8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa56f91e54c219-complaint-failure-to-respond-failure-to-deal-properly-with-case-cllr-george-carroll-llandough-great-house-farm-church-vi","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa56f91e54c219","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fa574a3151e1b8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Monitoring Officer / Corporate Complaints Team,\n\nWith great regret I am writing to make a complaint about the persistent\nfailure of Councillor George D. D. Carroll (Llandough ward) to respond\nsubstantively to my repeated and reasonable correspondence concerning\nhistoric land, planning, enforcement, heritage and related public-interest\nmatters at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (now Church View Close),\nVale of Glamorgan.\n\nI have a legitimate and long-standing family interest in the site\n(Williams/Buckler family connection documented from the 17th century). See\nattached.\n\nThe issues raised include alleged defective notices, loss of opportunity to\ncontest enforcement leading to demolition in 1988, heritage/regulatory\noversight, planning and title records, and related transparency failures.\n\nDespite multiple contacts over several months, I have received no\nsubstantive replies from Cllr Carroll. This constitutes a failure to\nrespond and a failure to deal with the case properly.\n\n### Full correspondence log with Cllr George Carroll (\n[email redacted])\n\n| Date       | Subject / Key content\n                         | Response received |\n|------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 16 Feb 2026 | Potential gaps in Council planning/record-keeping for Great\nHouse Farm (demolished 1988); title fraud and procedural issues relating to\nChurch View Close | None |\n\n| 4 May 2026  | Request regarding BP vs Buckler 1987; shared\nmedia/evidence; request for attention as Llandough councillor | None |\n\n| 7 Jun 2026  | “Church View Close, Llandough” – piecing together 1988\nevents from public records, family testimony and media | None |\n\n| 25 Jun 2026 | “Great House Farm, Llandough” – enquiry whether prior\nconcerns on family dispossession had been reviewed; request for any\nprogress or discussion | None |\n\n| 13 Jul 2026 | “Great House Farm/ Church View Close” – formal follow-up\nlisting the above timeline, restating legitimate interest (family roots\nsince 1667), noting absence of replies, requesting detailed response within\n10 working days, and raising the removed commemorative tree | None |\n\n### Remedy sought\n\n1. A full written response from Cllr Carroll addressing the points raised\nin the logged emails, within 10–15 working days.\n\n2. Confirmation that this complaint has been logged under the Council’s\ncorporate complaints procedure and/or referred to the Monitoring Officer /\nStandards Committee as appropriate for any potential breach of the\ncouncillor Code of Conduct (failure to respond / failure to deal properly\nwith a case).\n\n3. Written confirmation of the process and timescale for investigation and\nresponse.\n\nI have retained the full original emails and attachments and can supply\nthem on request. Please acknowledge receipt of this formal complaint.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]\n[email redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19fa4c0e80385108","subject":"Re: FOI","name":"Re: FOI","date":"2026-07-27T18:05:33Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fa4c0e80385108.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea150513c39427-foi","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea150513c39427","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fa4c0e80385108.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Disclosure Team,\n\nSee attached.\n\nI look forward to your reply,\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\nWilliams/Buckler Family Heir & Successor\n[phone redacted]\n\nOn Mon, 8 Jun 2026, 04:10 Disclosure Team,  \nwrote:\n\n> Morning,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n> As you are requesting information which may be held in archived records,\n> we need further information in order to deal with your request.\n>\n>\n>\n> If you haven’t already, please could you provide the full name, full date\n> of birth and any other relevant information e.g. date of\n> conviction/imprisonment, name of prison, prisoner number, region where\n> individual resided before imprisonment. We will have a better chance of\n> finding the information you seek if you include as much detail as possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> You may wish to note that it is a general policy of the Ministry of\n> Justice (MoJ) not to disclose, to a third party, personal information about\n> another living person. This is because the MoJ has obligations under the\n> Data Protection Act and in law generally to protect this information. Your\n> request for personal information has been considered in line with our\n> obligations under the Freedom of Information Act. In the event that we hold\n> the information you request, we will require the written authority of the\n> Data Subject of the information you want the information about. If the\n> individual is now deceased, we will require a copy of official\n> documentation confirming that they are deceased such as death certificate.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: signature_1893814455]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Disclosure Team*\n>\n> Security and Information Directorate\n>\n> Service Transformation Group\n>\n> Ministry of Justice\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 07 June 2026 10:03\n> *To:* Disclosure Team  \n> *Subject:* FOI\n>\n>\n>\n> Sirs,\n>\n> Please will you locate/access probate records for Mary Williams (d. March\n> 1983), Great House Farm, Llandough—any wills, affidavits, or ownership\n> claims referenced?\n>\n> Thanks,\n>\n> Requester\n> ------------------------------\n> This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the\n> addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not\n> permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies\n> and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure\n> medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone\n> else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in\n> response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender\n> or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry\n> of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content\n> may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not\n> broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n>"},{"id":"gm-19fa4b936d896588","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-07-27T17:57:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19fa4b936d896588.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19fa4b5a70ee940a-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19fa4b5a70ee940a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19fa4b936d896588.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 I request the following recorded\ninformation held by the National Library of Wales:\nAny manorial court rolls, surveys, rentals, terriers, or related documents\nfor the Manor of Llandough (Glamorgan) covering the period c.1600–1670 that\nlist or refer to occupants, customary tenants, or holders of land later\nknown as Great House Farm (or equivalent contemporary descriptions).\nAny estate papers, correspondence, leases, rentals, account books, or\nsurveys of the Vaughan family of Llandough (or related Vaughan holdings)\nt