e Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-22T15:07:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f8a5e4cfb0620e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["cardiff-univ"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff-univ"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"received","from":"Special Collections","institutions":[{"id":"cardiff-univ","name":"Cardiff University Special Collections"}],"refs":["1897"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f8a5e4cfb0620e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nWe have searched the catalogues and the accessions register of our university records for the topics you have listed below but did not find any results. The full list of Cardiff University Archives<https://archiveshub.jisc.ac.uk/search/locations/7ece46db-5242-3590-988f-f23ea40100df> can be searched on Archives Hub.\n\nCathays Branch and Heritage Library<https://cardiffhubs.co.uk/hub/cathays-branch-and-heritage-library/> has books in its library collection<https://cardiff.spydus.co.uk/cgi-bin/spydus.exe/ENQ/OPAC/BIBWRKENQ?ENTRY=marconi&ENTRY_NAME=BS&ENTRY_TYPE=K&SORTS=SQL_REL_WRK&GQ=marconi&NRECS=10&QRY=&QRYTEXT=Full+catalogue+%28Work%29&_SPQ=2> relating to Marconi that may be relevant to your research. They also hold local newspapers which may be of interest.\n\nAll the best,\n\nAnna\n\n\nCasgliadau Arbennig ac Archifau / Special Collections and Archives\n\nGwasanaeth Llyfrgell y Brifysgol | University Library Service\n\nPrifysgol Caerdydd | Cardiff University\n\n\n\nEbost | Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nGwefan | Website: <https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections> https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections\n\nX/Instagram: @CUSpecialColls\n\nMae'r llyfrgell yn gwerthfawrogi eich adborth. Cymerwch funud i ddweud wrthym yn ddienw sut ydyn ni'n gwneud<https://forms.office.com/e/EaUeP2bfDx>. The library values your feedback. Please take a minute to tell us anonymously <https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj> how we are doing.<https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj>\n\n[cid:1aa2a364-439b-47ed-82f8-0d276129a192]\nMae’r Brifysgol yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at unrhyw oedi.\n\nThe University welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 21 July 2026 13:44\nTo: Special Collections <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\n\nDear Special Collections and Archives Team,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI appreciate your confirmation that Cardiff University does not hold records from the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office.\n\nTo clarify, my enquiry was not limited to official GPO records. I was also seeking to establish whether your collections contain any references to:\n\n  *   Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough;\n  *   Guglielmo Marconi's stay in Cardiff or Llandough in 1897;\n  *   the Lavernock wireless experiments;\n  *   photographs, correspondence, personal papers, local history collections or donated archives mentioning these subjects.\n\nCould you please confirm whether searches were carried out for those subjects, or whether your response relates solely to official GPO records?\n\nMany thanks for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nRequester\n\n & Life Member\n\nOn Tue, 21 Jul 2026, 06:44 Special Collections, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nWe do not hold any records from the Cardiff Post Office/General Post Office in our collection. As the local authority repository, Glamorgan Archives is the most likely place to hold relevant archives from Cardiff and Penarth. Their catalogue<https://glamarchives.gov.uk/collection/> can be searched on their website.\n\nAll the best,\n\nSpecial Collections and Archives Team\n\n\nCasgliadau Arbennig ac Archifau / Special Collections and Archives\n\nGwasanaeth Llyfrgell y Brifysgol | University Library Service\n\nPrifysgol Caerdydd | Cardiff University\n\n\n\nEbost | Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nGwefan | Website: <https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections> https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections\n\nX/Instagram: @CUSpecialColls\n\nMae'r llyfrgell yn gwerthfawrogi eich adborth. Cymerwch funud i ddweud wrthym yn ddienw sut ydyn ni'n gwneud<https://forms.office.com/e/EaUeP2bfDx>. The library values your feedback. Please take a minute to tell us anonymously <https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj> how we are doing.<https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj>\n\n[cid:9cffe1e0-aa7e-4aaa-8b56-2365a6c1aff5]\nMae’r Brifysgol yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at unrhyw oedi.\n\nThe University welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 July 2026 20:40\nTo: Special Collections <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\nThank you for your prompt response and for checking the University calendars.\n\nTo clarify: my request was not about University College / Cardiff University Engineering Department academic staff. It specifically concerned my great-grandfather Mr. Williams in the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office (GPO) Engineering Department around 1897, and any records of his assistance to Marconi’s wireless experiments at Lavernock Point (as referenced in contemporary newspaper reports). See attached.\n\nI would be grateful if you could confirm whether your archives hold any GPO-related material, or advise on the correct contact within Cardiff University (or elsewhere) for Post Office engineering records from that period.\n\nThank you again for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n & Life Member\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n[address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted][map link redacted]\n\nOn Thu, 16 Jul 2026, 12:40 Special Collections, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nWe checked the calendars of the University College of South Wales and Monmouthshire, predecessor to Cardiff University, which list its academic staff. We did not find any Engineering staff with the surname Williams for 1896/97, 1897/98, or 1898/99.\n\nThese calendars are available online to view:\nUniversity calendar, 1896-97<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074502420>, Engineering staff listed on image 51.\nUniversity calendar, 1897-98<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074402420>, Engineering staff listed on image 47.\nUniversity calendar, 1898-99<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074302420>, Engineering staff listed on image 47.\n\nAll the best,\n\nSpecial Collections and Archives Team\n\n\nCasgliadau Arbennig ac Archifau / Special Collections and Archives\n\nGwasanaeth Llyfrgell y Brifysgol | University Library Service\n\nPrifysgol Caerdydd | Cardiff University\n\n\n\nEbost | Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nGwefan | Website: <https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections> https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections\n\nX/Instagram: @CUSpecialColls\n\nMae'r llyfrgell yn gwerthfawrogi eich adborth. Cymerwch funud i ddweud wrthym yn ddienw sut ydyn ni'n gwneud<https://forms.office.com/e/EaUeP2bfDx>. The library values your feedback. Please take a minute to tell us anonymously <https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj> how we are doing.<https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj>\n\n[cid:388d7efe-87a8-483f-a2f3-9737d96ea5b7]\nMae’r Brifysgol yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at unrhyw oedi.\n\nThe University welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 July 2026 01:44\nTo: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; Special Collections <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]> <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\nExternal email to Cardiff University - Take care when replying/opening attachments or links.\nNid ebost mewnol o Brifysgol Caerdydd yw hwn - Cymerwch ofal wrth ateb/agor atodiadau neu ddolenni.\n\n\n\nDear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams, who worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office around 1897.\n\nSpecifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence, reports, or mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the 120-foot pole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary newspaper reports from May 1897.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n  *   Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff engineering department circa 1897.\n  *   Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s demonstrations.\n  *   Any other relevant historical files from the GPO telegraph/engineering teams.\n\nMy full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted][map link redacted] Contact: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> Relationship: Great Grandson\n\nI am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not to be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of Glamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after Marconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n\nI am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member"},{"id":"gm-19f89db67d0404c4","subject":"RE: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","name":"RE: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-22T12:44:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f89db67d0404c4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f89db67d0404c4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"2026/3194\n\nDear Requester.\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nI have searched our catalogue and I can confirm that Glamorgan Archives does not hold any records relating to engineering activities at Cardiff Post Office, nor to Marconi’s experiments at Lavernock Point, or any material concerning connections between the Post Office’s engineering team / Mr Williams and these events.\n\nI’m sorry that I failed to clarify this fully in my previous email.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRhian Diggins [cid:image001.jpg@01DD19E0.3D5A4E00]\nUwch Archifydd / Senior Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nhttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 21 July 2026 17:17\nTo: Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\nALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\nMs Diggins,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI appreciate your clarification that Glamorgan Archives does not hold records of past Post Office employees. However, my request was broader than personnel records alone.\n\nI was also seeking any historical records held by Glamorgan Archives relating to:\n\n  *   Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office engineering activities around 1897;\n  *   the Marconi wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point and tests to Flat Holm;\n  *   correspondence, reports, photographs, deposited collections or other references mentioning the Cardiff engineering team or “Mr Williams” in connection with these events.\n\nCould you please confirm whether Glamorgan Archives has searched its catalogues or collections for these broader categories of records, rather than only employee records?\n\nIf no relevant records are held, I would be grateful for confirmation of the searches undertaken and any catalogue references checked, so that I can direct my research appropriately.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\nOn Tue, 21 Jul 2026, 12:00 Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\n2026/3098\nDear Requester.\nThank you for your email, received into our postal system on 16 July 2026.\nGlamorgan Archives does not hold records of past employees of the Post Office. We suggest that you contact the Postal Museum and Archives<https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/> for further information on your grandfather’s time working at Cardiff Post Office in 1897.\nI’m sorry that we can’t be of any further help on this occasion.\nYours sincerely,\nRhian Diggins [cid:image001.jpg@01DD19E0.3D5A4E00]\nUwch Archifydd / Senior Archivist\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nhttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 July 2026 01:45\nTo: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>; [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nSubject: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\nALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\nDear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams, who worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office around 1897.\n\nSpecifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence, reports, or mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the 120-foot pole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary newspaper reports from May 1897.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n  *   Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff engineering department circa 1897.\n  *   Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s demonstrations.\n  *   Any other relevant historical files from the GPO telegraph/engineering teams.\n\nMy full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted][map link redacted] Contact: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> Relationship: Great Grandson\n\nI am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not to be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of Glamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after Marconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n\nI am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member\n\n**********************************************************************\n\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n\n**********************************************************************\n\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19f89b3285482a8a","subject":"FOI2026/06174 - Department for Culture, Media and Sport - Response Letter","name":"FOI2026/06174 - Department for Culture, Media and Sport - Response Letter","date":"2026-07-22T12:00:47Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f89b3285482a8a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f89b3285482a8a-foi2026-06174-department-for-culture-media-and-sport-response-letter","scopeTopics":["dcms"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dcms"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f89b3285482a8a","direction":"received","from":"FOI Team","institutions":[{"id":"dcms","name":"Department for Culture, Media and Sport"}],"refs":["FOI2026/06174"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f89b3285482a8a.json","attachments":[{"name":"_FOI2026_06174.pdf","title":"_FOI2026_06174.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-07-22_dcms_foi2026-06174_response.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":136855,"sha256":"c53f4d343823af5fe435476150a3747a1d194123fca4f1dbadaac36a1b35147a"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Our Ref: FOI2026/06174\nPlease see the attached letter from the Department for Culture, Media and Sport.\nKind regards,\nMinisterial Support Team\nDepartment for Culture, Media and Sport"},{"id":"gm-19f85b7a66dba6f2","subject":"Automatic reply: Buckler vs United Kingdom","name":"Automatic reply: Buckler vs United Kingdom","date":"2026-07-21T17:27:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f85b7a66dba6f2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f85b6062fea189-automatic-reply-buckler-vs-united-kingdom","scopeTopics":["sfo"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["sfo"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f85b6062fea189","direction":"received","from":"Public Enquiries SFO","institutions":[{"id":"sfo","name":"Serious Fraud Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f85b7a66dba6f2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you for contacting the Serious Fraud Office (SFO).\n\nTo comply with our privacy notice SFO Privacy Policy - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sfo-privacy-policy>, your information will not be retained if there is no business requirement to hold it.\nWe will not respond to your query if it relates to the following matters:\nSuspicious contact from the SFO: If you have been contacted by someone purporting to be from the SFO, please consult our guidance Is the message I’ve had from the SFO genuine? - GOV.UK.<https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/is-the-message-ive-had-from-the-sfo-genuine>.\nReferrals: We investigate and prosecute the most serious economic crimes only. Information about this can be found on our website:  Serious Fraud Office - GOV.UK.<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/serious-fraud-office> We cannot accept any referrals outside our remit or pass this information onto other agencies. This should instead be reported to the police by calling 101 or Report Fraud<https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/>. We do not handle visas or immigration matters.\nReferrals in relation to serious economic crime: We cannot accept any referrals into this inbox. If you want to make a referral, please refer to the secure online reporting form on our website Serious Fraud Office - GOV.UK<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/serious-fraud-office> instead.\nFollows ups on your referral: If you have not heard from us within 20 working days please assume that your allegation(s) or complaint(s) do not meet the statutory remit of the SFO.\nJob Opportunities at the SFO: These are advertised here Civil Service Jobs - GOV.UK<https://www.civilservicejobs.service.gov.uk/csr/index.cgi>. We cannot reply to requests for work experience.\nMedia queries: Information for journalists, about how to get in touch with our media team, is on our website.\nSFO new phone number: Our new public enquiries phone number is:[phone redacted]\nThis is an automated email. Please do not reply to this email.\nWe won't stop fighting serious fraud, bribery and corruption.\nThe information in this email and any attachments is confidential and may be subject to legal professional privilege. Unless you are the intended recipient or their representative you may not read, copy, distribute, use or retain anything in this message. If this message is not meant for you, please notify the sender immediately.\n\nEmails sent to and from Serious Fraud Office (SFO) computer systems will be monitored and recorded for lawful purposes. The SFO is not liable for any personal views of the sender.\n\nSerious Fraud Office, 2 - 4 Cockspur Street, London [postcode redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19f85b59ef763361","subject":"Buckler vs United Kingdom","name":"Buckler vs United Kingdom","date":"2026-07-21T17:24:59Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f85b59ef763361.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f858eac3b093ec-buckler-vs-united-kingdom","scopeTopics":["ico"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["ico"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f858eac3b093ec","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"ico","name":"Information Commissioner's Office"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f85b59ef763361.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Madam,\n\nI am requesting your urgent assistance and referral to the appropriate\noversight bodies regarding serious and ongoing difficulties obtaining\nhistoric records required for my family’s claim concerning Great House Farm\n(Tŷ Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan.\n\nI want to be clear that I am not asking you to determine the underlying\nownership dispute. That is a matter for legal adjudication. I am requesting\nassistance to ensure that the documentary evidence required for a fair\nlegal determination is identified, preserved and made available.\n\nThe Information Commissioner’s Office has advised that this matter requires\nreferral through my Member of Parliament. Who doesn't reply. The Llandough\ncouncillor doesn't reply. I follow up monthly and nothing. The council\nclerk for Llandough initially refused to cooperate then retired. CADW\ninitially lied to me too.\n\nAfter more than a year of attempting to obtain records through Freedom of\nInformation requests, Environmental Information Regulations requests,\narchive enquiries and correspondence with relevant bodies, I have\nencountered repeated difficulties which are preventing proper assessment of\nmy family’s claim. South Wales Police say they don't hold records yet they\nwere reported by ITV and other news outlets as being heavily involved in\nthe dispossession of our land and home in 1988. Before our 80p year old\nhome was abruptly demolished and our land and home since 1667 seized .\nAlong with all our furniture, artwork etc, originally from Cardiff castle.\nProperty and reference information\n\nThe matter concerns:\n\n*Great House Farm / Tŷ Mawr*\nLlandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nRelevant Land Registry titles:\n\n   - WA231076\n   - WA240304\n\nHistoric Ordnance Survey references:\n\n   - 38-1-608\n   - 38-1-334\n\nThere appear to be significant gaps in the documentary chain concerning the\ntransition from historic family occupation, later possession arrangements,\nregistration, and subsequent transfer of interests.\n\nMy family’s understanding is that there may have been separate interests\nrelating to the occupied farmhouse/plot and surrounding leased land.\nClarification of the documentary evidence concerning historic title,\noccupation, registration and possession is therefore essential.\n\nA key unresolved issue is the evidential gap between historic occupation\nand the later registration position, including the documents relied upon\nwhen registration occurred and the subsequent handling of title\ndocumentation.\n\nI also note Marconi stayed with us while inventing radio. A Roman villa and\nmonestry existed there too and has never been formally even attempted to be\ndiscovered. Its home to one of the largest medieval burial sites, also no\ncoverage of that exhivation before 20 houses were built on our stolen land.\nMy nan conveniently died while BP registered our land in their names\nin1983. My dad conveniently died after his appeal of landmark legal case BP\nvs Buckler 1987 was dismissed and his ECHR rejected and then planning\npermission approved.\n\nI'm a former military cyber and electronic warfare professional, in\naddition to being my dads son, nans grandson and child from this\ndispossession in 1988. Which included what maybe SAS undercover as BP\nBailiffs. Both ripping me from my birthland and demolishing it in front of\nus. Along with 2 toddlers siblings and my pregnant mum, who's shoulder they\ndislocated while she served them an injuction to prevent them demolishing\nor stealing our property.\n\nFraud unravels all. And the limitation is from discovery not occurance of\nit. I alledge fraud. Fraud and consealment. BP should have least told the\nland registry we challenged their claim with our claim to the land.\nRecords requiring identification, preservation and disclosure\n\nThe records required include, but are not limited to:\nLand ownership and registration\n\n   - The complete title registration files and supporting documents for\n   WA231076 and WA240304.\n   - Application documents submitted for registration.\n   - Supporting deeds, conveyances, evidence of title, correspondence and\n   internal notes.\n   - Any records showing how historic interests were considered during\n   registration.\n   - Records concerning Western Ground Rents, BP Pension Trust Ltd and BP\n   Properties Ltd.\n\nCourt and legal records\n\n   - Records relating to possession proceedings from 1955.\n   - Records relating to the 1962 County Court possession order.\n   - Documents connected with:\n\n*BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2*\n\nIncluding:\n\n   - pleadings;\n   - exhibits;\n   - correspondence;\n   - administrative records;\n   - any associated court documents.\n\nOccupation and possession records\n\n   - Correspondence and documents relating to occupation/licence\n   arrangements around 1974.\n   - Records concerning communications with members of the Williams/Buckler\n   family.\n   - Notices, agreements, applications and internal decision records.\n\nPublic authority and heritage records\n\n   -\n\n   Council records relating to Great House Farm.\n   -\n\n   Police records relating to events surrounding the property, where held.\n   -\n\n   Cadw records including:\n   - inspection records;\n      - listing consideration records;\n      - photographs dated 29 July 1988;\n      - demolition-related correspondence.\n   -\n\n   Archaeological records including:\n   - 1978–1980 investigations;\n      - 1994 excavations;\n      - reports;\n      - correspondence;\n      - site records;\n      - photographs.\n\nDemolition records\n\nAll records relating to the demolition of Great House Farm in December\n1988, including:\n\n   - permissions;\n   - correspondence;\n   - photographs;\n   - reports;\n   - decision records.\n\nConcerns regarding record handling\n\nMy concern is not simply that some records are unavailable. The concern is\nthat repeated requests have resulted in responses which:\n\n   - do not address the information requested;\n   - answer different questions from those asked;\n   - fail to explain what searches were undertaken;\n   - state that records cannot be located without identifying where\n   searches were carried out;\n   - describe records as missing, unavailable or destroyed without\n   explaining:\n      - when this occurred;\n      - under what retention policy;\n      - who authorised disposal;\n      - whether alternative copies exist.\n\nThis creates a serious barrier to obtaining legal advice and pursuing a\nlawful determination of my family’s claim.\nRequest for intervention\n\nI respectfully request assistance with:\n\n   1. Referral through the appropriate ICO escalation route.\n   2. Ensuring relevant public bodies conduct documented and comprehensive\n   searches.\n   3. Obtaining explanations for any records stated to be missing,\n   destroyed or unavailable.\n   4. Ensuring potentially relevant records are preserved.\n   5. Raising concerns regarding historic public record management with the\n   appropriate oversight bodies.\n\nThe relevant oversight routes may include:\n\n   - Information Commissioner’s Office (FOI/EIR compliance);\n   - Audit Wales (public body governance and accountability);\n   - Welsh public services complaints mechanisms;\n   - National Archives (public records management);\n   - Independent Office for Police Conduct, where appropriate;\n   - Any other appropriate authority where evidence indicates further\n   action is required.\n\nUrgency\n\nThis matter is urgent because the continuing absence of documentary\nevidence is preventing proper legal assessment of the claim. I am concerned\nthat further delay may prejudice my family’s ability to seek legal remedies\nwithin applicable limitation periods.\n\nI can provide:\n\n   - a complete chronology of requests and responses;\n   - FOI reference numbers;\n   - copies of correspondence;\n   - evidence indexes;\n   - supporting historical documentation.\n\nI request confirmation within 10 working days that this matter has been\nreviewed and that appropriate referrals have been made.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\n----\n\nAppendix A — Great House Farm (Tŷ Mawr), Llandough — Evidence Access,\nRecords and Disclosure Chronology\n\nDate / Period\n\nEvent / Issue\n\nRecords required / outstanding\n\nRelevant body / holder\n\nDisclosure concern\n\n1667 onwards\n\nFamily occupation and claimed historic interest in Great House Farm / Tŷ\nMawr\n\nHistoric deeds, title evidence, manorial records, estate records,\noccupation evidence\n\nNational Library of Wales, Glamorgan Archives, private estates, Land\nRegistry\n\nDocumentary chain required to establish historic occupation and interests\n\nPre-1876\n\nFamily occupation and relationship with surrounding leased land\n\nLease documents, rent records, estate correspondence, maps\n\nEstate archives / Glamorgan Archives / NLW\n\nNeed clarification of distinction between occupied holding and leased\nsurrounding land\n\n1876\n\nBute estate/Llandough Limeworks changes affecting surrounding land interests\n\nConveyances, leases, maps, estate records\n\nEstate archives, NLW, archives\n\nNeed clarification of land boundaries and interests created\n\n1897\n\nMarconi wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point; claimed Cardiff\nPost Office engineering connection\n\nEmployment records, Post Office/GPO records, correspondence, technical\nrecords\n\nBT Archives / National Archives / GPO records\n\nRelevant historical context; records sought\n\n1938\n\nAuction catalogue referring to property and alleged \"vacant possession\"\n\nAuction papers, catalogue, purchaser records, correspondence\n\nArchives / estate records\n\nClarification required as family occupation appears to have continued\n\n1950s\n\nAlleged continued occupation and dispute over possession\n\nRent records, notices, correspondence, court documents\n\nLandowners, courts, archives\n\nEvidence needed regarding legal basis of possession claims\n\n1955\n\nPossession proceedings\n\nClaim documents, pleadings, evidence, orders, correspondence\n\nCourt archives\n\nFull records required\n\n1962\n\nCounty Court possession order\n\nCourt file, order, evidence relied upon\n\nCourt archive\n\nNeed complete context and documents relied upon\n\n1969\n\nWestern Ground Rents / BP Pension Trust involvement\n\nConveyances, transfers, title documents, correspondence\n\nLand Registry, company records, archives\n\nNeed chain of ownership/interests\n\nEarly 1970s\n\nAlleged change in occupation/legal status\n\nCorrespondence, internal notes, notices\n\nBP-related entities, council, archives\n\nClarification of decisions affecting occupation\n\n1971\n\nAlleged Ordnance Survey descriptor changes\n\nOS historical mapping records and revision information\n\nOrdnance Survey\n\nNeed confirmation of mapping history\n\n1974\n\nLicence/occupation correspondence involving \"Mrs Buckler\"\n\nAll letters, agreements, internal correspondence, decision records\n\nBP-related bodies / council / archives\n\nNeed clarification of legal basis and parties involved\n\n1978–1980\n\nArchaeological investigations\n\nExcavation reports, photographs, correspondence, site records\n\nGlamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust / RCAHMW / Cadw\n\nComplete archive required\n\n1982\n\nLand Registry registration\n\nFull application bundle for WA231076\n\nHM Land Registry\n\nCritical issue: supporting evidence and documents used for registration\n\n1982 onwards\n\nWA231076 title history\n\nTitle documents, filed deeds, correspondence, applications\n\nHM Land Registry\n\nFOI confirmed registration but underlying evidence requires clarification\n\n1980s\n\nLand Registry title changes / later title WA240304\n\nComplete title history and supporting documents\n\nHM Land Registry\n\nNeed complete chain\n\n1987\n\nBP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2\n\nPleadings, exhibits, transcripts, correspondence, administrative records\n\nCourt archives\n\nRequired for understanding legal issues determined\n\n29 July 1988\n\nCadw photographs/inspection material\n\nPhotographs, inspection notes, listing consideration records\n\nCadw\n\nCadw confirmed photographs but wider record availability unclear\n\n1988\n\nDemolition of Great House Farm (December 1988)\n\nPermissions, notices, correspondence, photographs, reports\n\nCouncil, Cadw, archives\n\nNeed complete decision trail\n\n1994\n\nArchaeological excavations\n\nReports, photographs, archive material\n\nArchaeological bodies / RCAHMW\n\nNeed complete record\n\n2025–2026\n\nFOI/EIR requests commenced\n\nAll requests and responses\n\nMultiple public bodies\n\nRepeated issues with incomplete answers\n\n2025–2026\n\nRequests to archives, councils, heritage bodies, Land Registry and others\n\nSearch records, explanations, retention policies\n\nRelevant organisations\n\nNeed details of searches undertaken\n\n2025–2026\n\nLand Registry FOI response (reference previously noted: F260213)\n\nRegistration confirmation and refusal of bundle disclosure\n\nHM Land Registry\n\nNeed alternative access route to filed documents\n\n2025–2026\n\nCadw correspondence\n\nListing/demolition records\n\nCadw\n\nRecords reportedly incomplete/pre-digitisation gaps\n\n2025–2026\n\nRCAHMW correspondence\n\nHeld archive material (14 archive items referenced)\n\nRCAHMW\n\nNeed identification/access to all relevant records\n\n2025–2026\n\nGlamorgan Archives response\n\nArchive searches regarding demolition/legal records\n\nGlamorgan Archives\n\nNeed clarity on search scope\n\n2025–2026\n\nVale of Glamorgan Council responses\n\nCouncil records\n\nCouncil\n\nNeed confirmation of departments searched\n\n2025–2026\n\nSouth Wales Police records request\n\nIncident/event records if held\n\nSouth Wales Police\n\nNeed search explanation and retention information\n\n2025–2026\n\nITV archive footage issue\n\nBroadcast/archive material relating to events\n\nITV\n\nNeed archive request route; not FOI-accessible\n\n2026\n\nICO advice\n\nReferral through MP route\n\nICO\n\nEscalation required\n\n\nOutstanding disclosure questions;\n\nWhat documents were submitted to HM Land Registry to create title WA231076?\n\nWhat evidence of title was accepted?\n\nWhat happened to any earlier deeds or documentary evidence?\n\nWhy were some records unavailable when requested?\n\nWere any relevant records destroyed?\n\nIf destroyed:\n\nwhen?\n\nby whom?\n\nunder what retention policy?\n\nwith what authorisation?\n\nWere duplicate copies retained elsewhere?\n\nWhich departments, databases, archives and physical collections were\nsearched?\n\nWho conducted those searches?\n\nAre any records currently subject to preservation holds?"},{"id":"gm-19f8577ab13fc619","subject":"Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","name":"Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-21T16:17:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f8577ab13fc619.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f8577ab13fc619.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Diggins,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI appreciate your clarification that Glamorgan Archives does not hold\nrecords of past Post Office employees. However, my request was broader than\npersonnel records alone.\n\nI was also seeking any historical records held by Glamorgan Archives\nrelating to:\n\n   - Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office engineering activities\n   around 1897;\n   - the Marconi wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point and\n   tests to Flat Holm;\n   - correspondence, reports, photographs, deposited collections or other\n   references mentioning the Cardiff engineering team or “Mr Williams” in\n   connection with these events.\n\nCould you please confirm whether Glamorgan Archives has searched its\ncatalogues or collections for these broader categories of records, rather\nthan only employee records?\n\nIf no relevant records are held, I would be grateful for confirmation of\nthe searches undertaken and any catalogue references checked, so that I can\ndirect my research appropriately.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester \n\nOn Tue, 21 Jul 2026, 12:00 Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> 2026/3098\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email, received into our postal system on 16 July 2026.\n>\n>\n>\n> Glamorgan Archives does not hold records of past employees of the Post\n> Office.  We suggest that you contact the Postal Museum and Archives\n> <https://www.postalmuseum.org/collections/the-archive/> for further\n> information on your grandfather’s time working at Cardiff Post Office in\n> 1897.\n>\n>\n>\n> I’m sorry that we can’t be of any further help on this occasion.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Rhian Diggins\n>\n> Uwch Archifydd / Senior Archivist\n>\n>\n>\n> Archifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 16 July 2026 01:45\n> *To:* [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>; FOI /\n> Rhyddid Gwybodaeth <[email redacted]>; [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]\n> *Subject:* Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr.\n> Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi\n> Lavernock Experiments\n>\n>\n>\n> *EXTERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care\n> when clicking links.\n> *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal\n> wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n>\n> I am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act\n> 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams,\n> who worked in the engineering department of 