TERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take\n> care when clicking links.\n>  *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch\n> ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n>\n> I am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act\n> 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams,\n> who worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office /\n> General Post Office around 1897.\n>\n> Specifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence,\n> reports, or mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s\n> wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the\n> 120-foot pole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary\n> newspaper reports from May 1897.\n>\n> Please provide:\n>\n>    - Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff\n>    engineering department circa 1897.\n>    - Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s\n>    demonstrations.\n>    - Any other relevant historical files from the GPO\n>    telegraph/engineering teams.\n>\n> My full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of\n> Glamorgan, [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> Contact: [email redacted] Relationship: Great Grandson\n>\n> I am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams\n> of Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not\n> to be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of\n> Glamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after\n> Marconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n>\n> I am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for\n> your assistance.\n>\n> Best regards,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>  & Life Member\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> The Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We\n> will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as\n> long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not\n> lead to delay.\n>\n> Privileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If\n> you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for\n> delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this\n> message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly\n> notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your\n> employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.\n> Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not\n> relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of\n> Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail\n> sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils\n> Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other\n> than the addressee.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> Mae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog.\n> Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni\n> pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n>\n> Mae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y\n> neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r\n> neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges.\n> Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy\n> e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi\n> neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon.\n> Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y\n> neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir\n> Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff\n> unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan\n> system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu\n> harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f81088a9c5371a","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture 2/2","name":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture 2/2","date":"2026-07-20T19:37:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f81088a9c5371a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f81087a6d94d66-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture-2-2","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f81087a6d94d66","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f81088a9c5371a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Daniel,\n\nFurther to my internal review request, I would like to provide a short\nclarification regarding the scope of my original FOI request.\n\nHaving reviewed my original request submitted on 3 July 2026, I wish to\nemphasise that the request was expressly for recorded information, not\nmerely for physical objects held within NLW collections.\n\nThe original request specifically sought:\ninventories, catalogues and asset registers;\nacquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records;\nprovenance files and ownership records;\nphotographs;\ncorrespondence concerning identification, recovery, ownership or location;\ninternal reports, legal advice and memoranda;\ncorrespondence involving the Buckler or Williams families;\ncorrespondence with Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, museums and other public\nbodies.\n\nTherefore, my concern is not that NLW does not hold furniture as part of a\ncollection. I understand that point. My concern is whether relevant\ndocumentary records were searched across appropriate archival collections\nwhere references to such items may exist.\n\nFor example, where NLW holds Bute Estate material relating to Ty\nMawr/Llandough, I would appreciate confirmation as to whether those\ncollections were searched for incidental references to:\nhousehold inventories;\nfixtures;\nvaluations;\nestate correspondence;\ntransfers or disposals;\nprovenance information;\nreferences to occupants or contents of the farmhouse.\n\nThis clarification is provided to assist the internal review and ensure the\noriginal request is considered in its full context.\nI appreciate the catalogue references already provided and look forward to\nconfirmation of the searches undertaken.\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 20 Jul 2026, 13:11 National Library of Wales, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> --# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Attached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4517166&type=0&key=5afe8f6fd61ea76cddc027c015f0bfb2>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> I am writing in response to your recent application for information held\n> by the Library\n>\n> (Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n>\n> You will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n>\n> Best wishes,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Cwestiwn gwreiddiol\n>\n> Jul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\n> Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd Pennaeth Ymholiadau - Head of Enquiries Gwasanaeth\n> Ymholiadau: http://www.llgc.org.uk/holi Enquiries Service:\n> http://www.llgc.org.uk/enquire Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Hapus i\n> gyfathrebu yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg | Happy to communicate in Welsh or\n> English *Lluniwyd yr ateb i'ch ymholiad heb gymorth gan AI - the answer to\n> your enquiry was made without the aid of AI\n>\n>\n> This email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n>\n> Read our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f81066fb7a3f1a","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: [NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-20T19:35:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f81066fb7a3f1a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f81066fb7a3f1a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Daniel,\n\nThank you for your response dated 20 July 2026 regarding FOI/2026/09 and\nfor identifying the catalogue references relating to Ty Mawr/Llandough\nwithin the Bute Estate collections.\n\nI would like to request an internal review, as I believe the response may\nhave interpreted the scope of my request too narrowly.\n\nMy request was for:\n\n\"All recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques,\nfixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House\nFarm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items received from Bute\nEstate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.\"\n\nI appreciate that the National Library of Wales does not collect furniture\nas a category of object and therefore may not hold the physical items\nthemselves. However, my request was not limited to physical objects or\nacquisition files. It sought *all recorded information* relating to such\nitems.\n\nThis could include, for example:\n\n   - inventories;\n   - valuations;\n   - estate correspondence;\n   - fixture schedules;\n   - probate references;\n   - sale catalogues;\n   - photographs;\n   - tenancy records;\n   - references within Bute Estate papers;\n   - records of transfer, removal or disposal.\n\nThe response confirms that NLW holds significant Bute Estate material\nrelating to Ty Mawr, including maps, leases and deeds. However, it does not\nclarify whether those wider collections were searched for references to the\nfarmhouse contents, fixtures, or related estate administration records.\n\nCould the internal review please clarify:\n\n   1.\n\n   What collections and record series were searched in responding to this\n   request?\n   2.\n\n   Were searches undertaken beyond acquisition files, including within Bute\n   Estate papers and related archival collections?\n   3.\n\n   Were terms such as:\n\n\n   - Great House Farm;\n   - Ty Mawr;\n   - Llandough;\n   - fixtures;\n   - inventory;\n   - valuation;\n   - contents;\n   - furnishings;\n   - sale;\n   - transfer;\n\nused as part of the search?\n\n   4. If no relevant records are held, could you please confirm the\n   searches undertaken and the basis for that conclusion?\n\nThe reason this distinction matters is that my wider research concerns the\ndocumentary history of the farmhouse and garden plot following changes\naffecting Ty Mawr/Llandough after the 19th century. Records relating to\nfixtures, valuations, inventories or estate administration may provide\nimportant historical context, regardless of whether the physical items\nthemselves remain.\n\nI am not asking NLW to determine ownership or provide a legal opinion. I am\nseeking confirmation that all relevant archival holdings have been\nconsidered and that the request has been searched against the appropriate\ncollections.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to the outcome of the\ninternal review.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 20 Jul 2026, 13:11 National Library of Wales, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> --# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> Attached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - FOI2026-09.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4517166&type=0&key=5afe8f6fd61ea76cddc027c015f0bfb2>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n>\n> Jul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> I am writing in response to your recent application for information held\n> by the Library\n>\n> (Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n>\n> You will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n>\n> Best wishes,\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Cwestiwn gwreiddiol\n>\n> Jul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\n> Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Iwan ap Dafydd Pennaeth Ymholiadau - Head of Enquiries Gwasanaeth\n> Ymholiadau: http://www.llgc.org.uk/holi Enquiries Service:\n> http://www.llgc.org.uk/enquire Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Hapus i\n> gyfathrebu yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg | Happy to communicate in Welsh or\n> English *Lluniwyd yr ateb i'ch ymholiad heb gymorth gan AI - the answer to\n> your enquiry was made without the aid of AI\n>\n>\n> This email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n>\n> Read our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f804bf3f50c1c0","subject":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"[NLW English] Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-20T16:11:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f804bf3f50c1c0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-nlw-english-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f804bf3f50c1c0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nJul 20 2026, 05:10PM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nAttached is the response to your recent Freedom of Information request.\n\nRegards,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nAttached Files\n\n-FOI2026-09.pdf  \n\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\nJul 03 2026, 11:45AM via System\n\nDear Requester,\n\nI am writing in response to your recent application for information held by the Library\n \n(Ref FOI/2026/09) received here at the Library on 3 July, 2026\n \nYou will receive a reply within 20 working days, being 31 July, 2026\n\nBest wishes,\n\nIwan ap Dafydd\n\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nJul 02 2026, 08:51PM via Email\nGreat House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 Request\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items we received from Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.  Weather it be museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts from our land in Llandough. \n\nSpecifically, I request copies of all:\n-Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n-Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n-Provenance files and ownership records.\n-Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House Farm.\n-Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership or location of such items.\n-Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great House Farm furniture or household effects.\n-Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in connection with these items.\n-Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great House Farm.\n-Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n\nFor context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still gathering actionable intelligence. \n\nI appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n\nI am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle, museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom of Information Act.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest test where required.\n\nIf another public authority is more likely to hold the requested information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or advise me accordingly.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester \n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n\nIwan ap Dafydd Pennaeth Ymholiadau - Head of Enquiries Gwasanaeth Ymholiadau: http://www.llgc.org.uk/holi Enquiries Service: http://www.llgc.org.uk/enquire Ffon/Tel: [phone redacted] Hapus i gyfathrebu yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg | Happy to communicate in Welsh or English *Lluniwyd yr ateb i'ch ymholiad heb gymorth gan AI - the answer to your enquiry was made without the aid of AI\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9603180.\n\nRead our privacy policy."},{"id":"gm-19f8028f054c6958","subject":"Re: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","name":"Re: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","date":"2026-07-20T15:33:14Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f8028f054c6958.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9-phso-case-ref-c-2205633","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f8028f054c6958.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\n\nI'll chase up my MP for a response. I was chasing the MP for Vale of\nGlamorgan and he didn't respond for months. When his office finally did it\nwas only to say the county lines had been redrawn and that I would need to\ncontact the MP for Cardiff instead. So I've contacted him and waited weeks,\nfollowed up and am still waiting weeks. This is a complex and collosal case\nand I am giving everyone the benefit of the doubt with the time taken to\ntake a position on the matter.\n\nOnce I've heard back from the MP I will say I require this of him, if not\nalready done.\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 20 Jul 2026 at 08:34, Phso Enquiries <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> We can consider complaints about HMCTS referred by your MP. However, we\n> are unable to access any website you may create due to our security policy.\n> Instead, we require you to provide the formal complaint responses you have\n> received from HMCTS, as well as a completed complaint form.\n>\n>\n>\n> Once we have received and reviewed these documents, we will contact you\n> regarding the next steps in the process. Kindly refrain from sending links\n> to websites or any additional information beyond what has been requested.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *Anita Eastham*\n>\n> *Intake Caseworker *\n>\n> Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman\n>\n> T: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f7f4e2bf47fca2","subject":"RE: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","name":"RE: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","date":"2026-07-20T11:34:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f7f4e2bf47fca2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9-phso-case-ref-c-2205633","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9","direction":"received","from":"Phso Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f7f4e2bf47fca2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your email.\n\nWe can consider complaints about HMCTS referred by your MP. However, we are unable to access any website you may create due to our security policy. Instead, we require you to provide the formal complaint responses you have received from HMCTS, as well as a completed complaint form.\n\nOnce we have received and reviewed these documents, we will contact you regarding the next steps in the process. Kindly refrain from sending links to websites or any additional information beyond what has been requested.\n\nYours Sincerely,\n\n\nAnita Eastham\nIntake Caseworker\nParliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman\nT: [phone redacted]\nE: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nW: www.ombudsman.org.uk<http://www.ombudsman.org.uk/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 16 July 2026 20:39\nTo: Phso Enquiries <[email redacted]>; PHSO Enquiries <[email redacted]>; Phso Enquiries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nMs Eastham,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI believe there has been a misunderstanding regarding the nature of my complaint.\n\nI am not asking the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman to review judicial decisions made in the Great House Farm litigation, nor am I seeking an investigation into the merits of the original court proceedings.\n\nMy complaint concerns alleged maladministration by HM Courts & Tribunals Service in its present-day handling of my complaint, including defective complaint handling, inaccurate statements regarding court records, failures to investigate apparent inconsistencies, and the resulting loss of my opportunity to pursue appropriate remedies.\n\nYour email states that complaints about HMCTS fall within your remit once the HMCTS complaints procedure has been completed and an MP referral has been obtained. That is precisely the route I am following.\n\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if you could confirm that, once I have exhausted the HMCTS complaints process and obtained the required MP referral, the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman will consider my complaint insofar as it concerns administrative failings by HMCTS, rather than the judicial decisions themselves.\n\nI would appreciate confirmation that this is the correct procedure. Also feel free to call to discuss as this is a collosal and complex case. I'm assembling a website with a chronological timeline and I'll place the supporting evidence I find on it. Including my last year of FOI's.\n\nWe can always revisit this as we near to my evidence and claims being legally adjudicated. I just want other departments and agencies to co operate beforehand which might be better than afterwards. As you might have a completly different opinion about the case with the evidence before you.\n\nI actually appear to be in receipt of a lot of evidence the state doesn't and vice versa. Which is why I am seeking cooperation, so as we can collectively fill in the mysteries of this whole case.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member\n\nOn Thu, 16 Jul 2026, 11:44 Phso Enquiries, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester Bucker\n\nThank you for your email with the subject heading ‘ complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough).\n\nOur remit covers complaints where someone believes they've been treated unfairly or received poor service from NHS organisations or from UK government departments and their associated public organisations.\n\nIf the complaint involves public health services in Wales, this will usually fall under the remit of the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales: https://www.ombudsman.wales/\n\nSimilarly, if the complaint is related to how a solicitor or legal professional has handled a case, it is likely to fall under the jurisdiction of the Legal Ombudsman: https://www.legalombudsman.org.uk/\n\nIf your complaint is about HMCTS then you will need to complete the full complaints process and provide us with the formal response with an MP’s referral.  You can follow the link below for further information on the full complaint process:\n\nhttps://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/complaints-procedure\n\nIf your concerns are primarily about judicial decisions and potential violations of his rights under the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR). As the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman (PHSO) does not have the remit to investigate judicial decisions, you could consider the following options:\n\n  1.  Judicial Reviews and Appeals:\nYou will need to seek independent legal advice about the possibility of appealing the decisions or applying for a judicial review. Legal professionals can guide you on the feasibility of further legal action.\n  2.  European Court of Human Rights (ECtHR):\nIf you believe your rights under the ECHR have been violated, you may wish to bring his case to the ECtHR. You will need to review the criteria for applying to the ECtHR at the court’s official website: https://www.echr.coe.int/.\n  3.  Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC):\nThe EHRC provides guidance and support concerning human rights and discrimination issues in England, Scotland, and Wales. You can contact them for information or assistance: https://www.equalityhumanrights.com/en.\n  4.  Citizens Advice:\nFor free, impartial advice, you could approach Citizens Advice, which may guide you on your next steps, including accessing pro bono legal services: https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/.\nI hope you find this information useful.\n\nYours Sincerely,\n\n\nAnita Eastham\nIntake Caseworker\nParliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman\nT: [phone redacted]\nE: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nW: www.ombudsman.org.uk<http://www.ombudsman.org.uk/>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe’re changing our name. Later this year we will become the Public Service Ombudsman. This will make it easier for people to find us and understand what we do. The service we provide will remain the same. Visit our website<https://www.ombudsman.org.uk/about-us/who-we-are/new-name-new-chapter> to find out more."},{"id":"gm-19f7eb0d36022a14","subject":"RE: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","name":"RE: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-20T08:42:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f7eb0d36022a14.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"received","from":"FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f7eb0d36022a14.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good Morning Ms Buckler\n\nThank you for your email below.\n\nWe have made some enquiries regarding this, and feel this is best responded to by Glamorgan Archives rather then through the Freedom of Information process.\n\nThey are aware of this request, and have asked that you make an official request through them, they have also agreed this would be best answered by them.\n\nThey can be contacted by emailing [email redacted]  or phoning [phone redacted]. Their website can be found by following this link: Home - Glamorgan Archives .\n\nThank you again for contacting Cardiff Council, and if you have any further queries please don’t hesitate in contacting us.\n\n\nKind Regards\n\nGwasanaeth Cais am Wybodaeth / Information Request Service\nLlywodraethu Gwybodaeth / Information Governance\nCyngor Caerdydd / Cardiff Council\nYstafell 118, Neuadd y Sir, Glanfa'r Iwerydd CAERDYDD [postcode redacted]\nRoom 118, County Hall, Atlantic Wharf CARDIFF [postcode redacted]\nFfôn / Tel: Working From Home\nE-bost / Email: [email redacted]  / [email redacted] \n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester  >\nSent: 16 July 2026 01:45\nTo: [email redacted] ; [email redacted] ; [email redacted] ; Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg  >; FOI / Rhyddid Gwybodaeth  >; [email redacted] ; [email redacted] ; [email redacted] ; [email redacted] \nSubject: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\n\nDear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams, who worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office around 1897.\n\nSpecifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence, reports, or mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the 120-foot pole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary newspaper reports from May 1897.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n  *   Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff engineering department circa 1897.\n  *   Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s demonstrations.\n  *   Any other relevant historical files from the GPO telegraph/engineering teams.\n\nMy full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted] Contact: [email redacted]  Relationship: Great Grandson\n\nI am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not to be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of Glamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after Marconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n\nI am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member\n\n**********************************************************************\n\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n\n**********************************************************************\n\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19f6fb6d6595006e","subject":"BP vs Buckler 1987 (fraud & Consealment)","name":"BP vs Buckler 1987 (fraud & Consealment)","date":"2026-07-17T10:54:40Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6fb6d6595006e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6fb3c8d4c11bc-bp-vs-buckler-1987-fraud-consealment","scopeTopics":["senedd"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["senedd"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6fb3c8d4c11bc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"senedd","name":"Senedd"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6fb6d6595006e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"*Editor / Investigations Desk*\n\nDear Editor,\n\nI am writing to ask your investigations team to examine what I believe is a\nsignificant public-interest story involving one of the most influential\nadverse possession cases in modern English and Welsh property law: *BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler [1987] 2 EGLR 168* (also reported as *(1988) 55 P\n& CR 337*).\n\nThis Court of Appeal decision continues to be cited in legal textbooks and\ncase law. It established that a unilateral letter from the paper title\nowner granting a rent-free licence could prevent adverse possession, even\nwhere the occupier had not expressly accepted it. The case has shaped\nproperty law for almost forty years.\n\nMy concern is not simply with the legal judgment itself.\n\nIt is with what surrounded it.\n\nFor several years I have been investigating the history of my family's\noccupation of *Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth*, and the events\nleading to the litigation. Through hundreds of Freedom of Information\nrequests, archive searches, Land Registry enquiries, historical research\nand correspondence with public authorities, I have uncovered what I believe\nare serious inconsistencies, missing records and evidence of institutional\nconcealment that deserve independent scrutiny.\n\nAmong the matters that I believe warrant investigation are:\n\n   - Whether material evidence relating to the occupation and ownership of\n   Great House Farm was withheld or never presented.\n   - The circumstances surrounding the registration of title by BP\n   interests in 1982 despite the long-running dispute.\n   - Missing or unexplained historical records across multiple public\n   bodies.\n   - Whether public authorities have failed to preserve records concerning\n   a nationally significant legal case.\n   - Whether subsequent institutions have frustrated attempts to obtain\n   records through Freedom of Information legislation.\n   - The wider implications if a leading legal precedent was built upon an\n   incomplete or inaccurate factual record.\n\nMy investigation has revealed repeated examples of authorities either\nclaiming records do not exist, directing me elsewhere, or providing\ndocuments unrelated to the requests made. Numerous archives acknowledge\ngaps where relevant material would ordinarily be expected.\n\nI have also experienced what I believe to be persistent obstruction. My\nelected representatives have failed to engage despite repeated requests.\nComplaints have been redirected without investigation. During my enquiries,\na court employee whom I challenged over contradictory information left\ntheir position shortly afterwards. While I cannot infer the reason for that\ndeparture, the wider pattern has made it exceptionally difficult to\nestablish an accurate historical record.\n\nThis story extends far beyond a private family dispute.\n\nIt concerns:\n\n   - whether powerful institutions have been properly held accountable;\n   - preservation of public records;\n   - transparency within government;\n   - the development of UK property law;\n   - the treatment of ordinary families in litigation against major\n   corporations;\n   - and whether historical injustices can remain effectively hidden\n   because records disappear over time.\n\nThe human story is equally compelling.\n\nMy family lived through decades of litigation, uncertainty and eventual\ndisplacement. The farmhouse was ultimately demolished, ending centuries of\nfamily association with the property. Much of my family—particularly the\nwomen—have lived with the consequences for generations and remain reluctant\nto speak publicly because of the trauma. My brother and I are now\nattempting to reconstruct the historical record before more evidence\ndisappears.\n\nThe property itself has remarkable historical significance. Great House\nFarm has connections with the historic Bute Estate, archaeological\ndiscoveries including Roman remains, and local accounts associated with the\npioneering wireless experiments at Lavernock Point during the Marconi era.\nYet the legal battle that made national case law has largely eclipsed that\nwider history.\n\nThis investigation is supported by:\n\n   - extensive documentary evidence;\n   - Land Registry correspondence;\n   - Freedom of Information responses from multiple public authorities;\n   - archive references from national and local repositories;\n   - court documents;\n   - historical maps;\n   - newspaper reports;\n   - and a detailed chronology spanning more than a century.\n\nI have also recorded my testimony explaining the evidence, chronology and\nimpact on my family: https://youtu.be/XuArB_vYWWA?si=O7TL2i5ocU3vn5fG\n\nI am prepared to provide your journalists with a fully indexed evidence\narchive, original source documents, timelines, witness information where\navailable, and copies of all official correspondence.\n\nI am *not* asking your newspaper to accept my conclusions without question.\n\nI am asking you to investigate.\n\nIf my concerns are unfounded, they should be capable of being disproved\nthrough proper scrutiny. If they are substantiated, they raise serious\nquestions about one of the UK's leading property law authorities,\ninstitutional accountability, public record keeping and the treatment of an\nordinary family whose story has never properly been told.\n\nThis is not simply a historical dispute.\n\nIt is a story about how legal precedents are created, how power operates,\nwhether the historical record can be trusted, and whether ordinary citizens\ncan ever obtain accountability decades after the events in question.\n\nI believe it is exactly the kind of investigation that serves the public\ninterest.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to speak with one of your investigative\njournalists and provide unrestricted access to the evidence I have\nassembled.\n\n*Yours faithfully,*\n\n*Requester*\n, \n\n\n[phone redacted]\n\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19f6c6fbe8b1063b","subject":"Re: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","name":"Re: PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","date":"2026-07-16T19:38:10Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6c6fbe8b1063b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9-phso-case-ref-c-2205633","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6c6fbe8b1063b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Eastham,\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nI believe there has been a misunderstanding regarding the nature of my\ncomplaint.\n\nI am not asking the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman to review\njudicial decisions made in the Great House Farm litigation, nor am I\nseeking an investigation into the merits of the original court proceedings.\n\nMy complaint concerns alleged maladministration by HM Courts & Tribunals\nService in its present-day handling of my complaint, including defective\ncomplaint handling, inaccurate statements regarding court records, failures\nto investigate apparent inconsistencies, and the resulting loss of my\nopportunity to pursue appropriate remedies.\n\nYour email states that complaints about HMCTS fall within your remit once\nthe HMCTS complaints procedure has been completed and an MP referral has\nbeen obtained. That is precisely the route I am following.\n\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if you could confirm that, once I have\nexhausted the HMCTS complaints process and obtained the required MP\nreferral, the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman will consider my\ncomplaint insofar as it concerns administrative failings by HMCTS, rather\nthan the judicial decisions themselves.\n\nI would appreciate confirmation that this is the correct procedure. Also\nfeel free to call to discuss as this is a collosal and complex case. I'm\nassembling a website with a chronological timeline and I'll place the\nsupporting evidence I find on it. Including my last year of FOI's.\n\nWe can always revisit this as we near to my evidence and claims being\nlegally adjudicated. I just want other departments and agencies to co\noperate beforehand which might be better than afterwards. As you might have\na completly different opinion about the case with the evidence before you.\n\nI actually appear to be in receipt of a lot of evidence the state doesn't\nand vice versa. Which is why I am seeking cooperation, so as we can\ncollectively fill in the mysteries of this whole case.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member\n\nOn Thu, 16 Jul 2026, 11:44 Phso Enquiries, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester Bucker\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email with the subject heading ‘ complaint of\n> maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of\n> opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough).\n>\n> Our remit covers complaints where someone believes they've been treated\n> unfairly or received poor service from NHS organisations or from *UK\n> government* departments and their associated public organisations.\n>\n> If the complaint involves public health services in *Wales*, this will\n> usually fall under the remit of the *Public Services Ombudsman for Wales*:\n> https://www.ombudsman.wales/\n>\n> Similarly, if the complaint is related to how a solicitor or legal\n> professional has handled a case, it is likely to fall under the\n> jurisdiction of the *Legal Ombudsman*: https://www.legalombudsman.org.uk/\n>\n> If your complaint is about HMCTS then you will need to complete the full\n> complaints process and provide us with the formal response with an MP’s\n> referral.  You can follow the link below for further information on the\n> full complaint process:\n>\n>\n> https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/complaints-procedure\n>\n> If your concerns are primarily about judicial decisions and potential\n> violations of his rights under the European Convention on Human Rights\n> (ECHR). As the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman (PHSO) *does\n> not have the remit* to investigate judicial decisions, you could consider\n> the following options:\n>\n>    1. Judicial Reviews and Appeals:\n>    You will need to seek independent legal advice about the possibility\n>    of appealing the decisions or applying for a judicial review. Legal\n>    professionals can guide you on the feasibility of further legal action.\n>    2. European Court of Human Rights (ECtHR):\n>    If you believe your rights under the ECHR have been violated, you may\n>    wish to bring his case to the ECtHR. You will need to review the criteria\n>    for applying to the ECtHR at the court’s official website:\n>    https://www.echr.coe.int/.\n>    3. Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC):\n>    The EHRC provides guidance and support concerning human rights and\n>    discrimination issues in England, Scotland, and Wales. You can contact them\n>    for information or assistance: https://www.equalityhumanrights.com/en.\n>    4. Citizens Advice:\n>    For free, impartial advice, you could approach Citizens Advice, which\n>    may guide you on your next steps, including accessing pro bono legal\n>    services: https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/.\n>\n> I hope you find this information useful.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *Anita Eastham*\n>\n> *Intake Caseworker *\n>\n> Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman\n>\n> T: [phone redacted]\n>\n> E: [email redacted]\n>\n> W: www.ombudsman.org.uk\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> We’re changing our name. Later this year we will become the Public Service\n> Ombudsman. This will make it easier for people to find us and understand\n> what we do. The service we provide will remain the same. Visit our website\n> <https://www.ombudsman.org.uk/about-us/who-we-are/new-name-new-chapter>\n> to find out more.\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f6b96957251a99","subject":"Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","name":"Re: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-16T15:40:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6b96957251a99.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["cardiff-univ"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cardiff-univ"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"received","from":"Special Collections","institutions":[{"id":"cardiff-univ","name":"Cardiff University Special Collections"}],"refs":["1897"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6b96957251a99.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nWe checked the calendars of the University College of South Wales and Monmouthshire, predecessor to Cardiff University, which list its academic staff. We did not find any Engineering staff with the surname Williams for 1896/97, 1897/98, or 1898/99.\n\nThese calendars are available online to view:\nUniversity calendar, 1896-97<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074502420>, Engineering staff listed on image 51.\nUniversity calendar, 1897-98<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074402420>, Engineering staff listed on image 47.\nUniversity calendar, 1898-99<https://librarysearch.cardiff.ac.uk/permalink/44WHELF_CAR/1gk9lnh/alma9912321074302420>, Engineering staff listed on image 47.\n\nAll the best,\n\nSpecial Collections and Archives Team\n\n\nCasgliadau Arbennig ac Archifau / Special Collections and Archives\n\nGwasanaeth Llyfrgell y Brifysgol | University Library Service\n\nPrifysgol Caerdydd | Cardiff University\n\n\n\nEbost | Email: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nGwefan | Website: <https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections> https://www.cardiff.ac.uk/special-collections\n\nX/Instagram: @CUSpecialColls\n\nMae'r llyfrgell yn gwerthfawrogi eich adborth. Cymerwch funud i ddweud wrthym yn ddienw sut ydyn ni'n gwneud<https://forms.office.com/e/EaUeP2bfDx>. The library values your feedback. Please take a minute to tell us anonymously <https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj> how we are doing.<https://forms.office.com/e/nJvk6p63zj>\n\n[cid:388d7efe-87a8-483f-a2f3-9737d96ea5b7]\nMae’r Brifysgol yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at unrhyw oedi.\n\nThe University welcomes correspondence in Welsh or English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 16 July 2026 01:44\nTo: [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>; Special Collections <[email redacted]>; [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments\n\nExternal email to Cardiff University - Take care when replying/opening attachments or links.\nNid ebost mewnol o Brifysgol Caerdydd yw hwn - Cymerwch ofal wrth ateb/agor atodiadau neu ddolenni.\n\n\n\nDear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams, who worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office / General Post Office around 1897.\n\nSpecifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence, reports, or mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s wireless telegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the 120-foot pole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary newspaper reports from May 1897.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n  *   Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff engineering department circa 1897.\n  *   Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s demonstrations.\n  *   Any other relevant historical files from the GPO telegraph/engineering teams.\n\nMy full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted] Contact: [email redacted]<[email redacted]> Relationship: Great Grandson\n\nI am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not to be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of Glamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after Marconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n\nI am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for your assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member"},{"id":"gm-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9","subject":"PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","name":"PHSO Case Ref: C-2205633","date":"2026-07-16T14:43:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9-phso-case-ref-c-2205633","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9","direction":"received","from":"Phso Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6b62c2ddc9ed9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester Bucker\n\nThank you for your email with the subject heading ' complaint of maladministration - defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough).\n\nOur remit covers complaints where someone believes they've been treated unfairly or received poor service from NHS organisations or from UK government departments and their associated public organisations.\n\nIf the complaint involves public health services in Wales, this will usually fall under the remit of the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales: https://www.ombudsman.wales/\n\nSimilarly, if the complaint is related to how a solicitor or legal professional has handled a case, it is likely to fall under the jurisdiction of the Legal Ombudsman: https://www.legalombudsman.org.uk/\n\nIf your complaint is about HMCTS then you will need to complete the full complaints process and provide us with the formal response with an MP's referral.  You can follow the link below for further information on the full complaint process:\n\nhttps://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/complaints-procedure\n\nIf your concerns are primarily about judicial decisions and potential violations of his rights under the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR). As the Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman (PHSO) does not have the remit to investigate judicial decisions, you could consider the following options:\n\n  1.  Judicial Reviews and Appeals:\nYou will need to seek independent legal advice about the possibility of appealing the decisions or applying for a judicial review. Legal professionals can guide you on the feasibility of further legal action.\n  2.  European Court of Human Rights (ECtHR):\nIf you believe your rights under the ECHR have been violated, you may wish to bring his case to the ECtHR. You will need to review the criteria for applying to the ECtHR at the court's official website: https://www.echr.coe.int/.\n  3.  Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC):\nThe EHRC provides guidance and support concerning human rights and discrimination issues in England, Scotland, and Wales. You can contact them for information or assistance: https://www.equalityhumanrights.com/en.\n  4.  Citizens Advice:\nFor free, impartial advice, you could approach Citizens Advice, which may guide you on your next steps, including accessing pro bono legal services: https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/.\nI hope you find this information useful.\n\nYours Sincerely,\n\n\nAnita Eastham\nIntake Caseworker\nParliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman\nT: [phone redacted]\nE: [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nW: www.ombudsman.org.uk<http://www.ombudsman.org.uk/>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe're changing our name. Later this year we will become the Public Service Ombudsman. This will make it easier for people to find us and understand what we do. The service we provide will remain the same. Visit our website<https://www.ombudsman.org.uk/about-us/who-we-are/new-name-new-chapter> to find out more."},{"id":"gm-19f6a82d65fb8e13","subject":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information Request 719/26","name":"RESPONSE Freedom of Information Request 719/26","date":"2026-07-16T10:39:43Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6a82d65fb8e13.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f6a82d65fb8e13-sponse-freedom-of-information-request-719-26","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f6a82d65fb8e13","direction":"received","from":"Freedom of Information","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6a82d65fb8e13.json","attachments":[{"name":"Response 719_26.pdf","title":"Response 719_26.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/2026-07-16_wp1300_south-wales-police-response-to-foi-request-719-26.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":180775,"sha256":"d6b3e44366c13a29726979ebc178a59de96bef9174b565f1d9b6315a92107c41"},{"name":"Complaints Procedure.pdf","title":"Complaints Procedure.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/2026-07-16_swp_foi-complaints-procedure-fb8e13.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":197535,"sha256":"dfd117b0cd39876f45800c6a11e7d8ed5d5c99affd11942a3aa83dbd29bc3a8a"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning,\n\nYour request for information has now been considered and our response is attached.\n\nI trust that this information answers your request. Should you have any queries and wish to contact us by e-mail, please do so using the mail box [email redacted] .\n\nSouth Wales Police provides you the right to request a re-examination of your case under its review procedure (copy attached). If you decide to request such a review and having followed the Forces full process you are still dissatisfied, then you have the right to direct your comments to the Information Commissioner who will give it consideration.\n\nKind regards,\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DD1517.B743FC20]<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>\n\n\nSamantha Jones\nSwyddog Ymchwil ac Ansawdd Data| Research and Data Quality Officer\nRheolwr Rheoli Data a Datgeliadau | Data Management and Disclosure Unit\nPencadlys Heddlu De Cymru | South Wales Police Headquarters\n*: [phone redacted] | Ext: 26660\n[cid:image002.jpg@01DD1517.B743FC20]<http://fb.me/swpolice>\n[cid:image003.jpg@01DD1517.B743FC20]<https://www.instagram.com/swpolice/>\n[cid:image004.jpg@01DD1517.B743FC20]<https://twitter.com/swpolice>\n[cid:image005.jpg@01DD1517.B743FC20]<https://www.youtube.com/user/swptv>\n\n\n\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad ?'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk<https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/>, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don't require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk<https://www.south-wales.police.uk/>, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu'r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-19f6861eda31b943","subject":"Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","name":"Freedom of Information / Historical Records Request - Mr. Williams, Cardiff Post Office Engineering Department, 1897 Marconi Lavernock Experiments","date":"2026-07-16T00:44:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f6861eda31b943.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0-freedom-of-information-historical-records-request-mr-williams-cardiff-post-office-engineering-department-1897-marconi-la","scopeTopics":["glamorgan","tna"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan","tna"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f682ed8be4fae0","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"},{"id":"tna","name":"The National Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f6861eda31b943.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Information Rights / Archives Team,\n\nI am writing to request information under the Freedom of Information Act\n2000 (or equivalent records access) regarding my grandfather, Mr. Williams,\nwho worked in the engineering department of the Cardiff Post Office /\nGeneral Post Office around 1897.\n\nSpecifically, I seek any records, personnel files, correspondence, reports,\nor mentions confirming his involvement in Guglielmo Marconi’s wireless\ntelegraphy experiments at Lavernock Point (including erecting the 120-foot\npole and related tests to Flat Holm). This relates to contemporary\nnewspaper reports from May 1897.\n\nPlease provide:\n\n   - Any personnel or service records for Mr. Williams in the Cardiff\n   engineering department circa 1897.\n   - Documents referencing \"Mr. Williams\" in connection with Marconi’s\n   demonstrations.\n   - Any other relevant historical files from the GPO telegraph/engineering\n   teams.\n\nMy full name: Requester Address: [address redacted], Vale of\nGlamorgan, [postcode redacted] Contact: [email redacted] Relationship: Great\nGrandson\n\nI am ultimately seeking any record about my great grandfather Mr Williams\nof Great House Farm, Llandough, Cardiff (formerly Vale of Glamorgan). Not\nto be confused with Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge, Vale of\nGlamorgan. And his role in the Marconi experiment. And before and after\nMarconis stay with our family in our home in 1897.\n\nI am happy to provide further identification if required. Thank you for\nyour assistance.\n\nBest regards,\n\nRequester \n\n & Life Member"},{"id":"gm-19f66d1ec71a417f","subject":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-07-15T17:27:40Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f66d1ec71a417f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f66d1ec71a417f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ms Longford,\n\nBefore responding to my earlier email, please may I add the following to my\nenquiry, even if you require addition time to respond due to this addition\nto my enquiry;\n\nIn addition to my email of 2 July, there are a small number of further\npoints which I would be grateful if you could address as they arise\ndirectly from comparing the original response with the internal review.\n\nThe original response of 11 June 2026 stated:\n\n\"Any other associated records would have been either transferred to the\nRoyal Commission on the Ancient & Historical Monuments of Wales for\npermanent preservation, or destroyed under the Public Record Act 1958.\"\n\nHowever, the internal review of 2 July 2026 states instead that:\n\n\"There is also no evidence that any relevant files have been transferred to\nthe RCAHMW.\"\n\nand\n\n\"It is possible that the file was destroyed before it was ever updated on\nour electronic filing system.\"\n\nThese appear to be materially different positions.\n\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify the following:\n\n   1.\n\n   What evidence supported the original statement that any associated\n   records would have been transferred to the RCAHMW or destroyed under the\n   Public Records Act 1958?\n   2.\n\n   Following the internal review, does Welsh Government now accept that\n   there is no evidence that any relevant records were transferred to the\n   RCAHMW?\n   3.\n\n   Does Welsh Government hold any transfer lists, accession records,\n   archive schedules or other documentation recording whether records relating\n   to Great House Farm were ever transferred to the RCAHMW?\n   4.\n\n   If no such documentation exists, on what evidential basis was the\n   original statement regarding transfer to the RCAHMW made?\n   5.\n\n   Likewise, if there is no destruction register, disposal log or audit\n   trail relating to the relevant file, on what evidential basis has\n   destruction been suggested?\n\nFinally, the original response stated as fact that Great House Farm was\nvisited by Cadw inspectors and did not meet the statutory listing criteria.\nThe internal review, however, confirms that no assessment, report or case\nfile has been located.\n\nCould you therefore identify the documentary evidence upon which that\nconclusion was based, or alternatively confirm whether the statement in the\noriginal response was an inference drawn from the existence of the two\nphotographs rather than from any surviving assessment records.\n\nThese points are intended simply to clarify the historical record and to\nreconcile what appear to be two materially different explanations contained\nwithin the original response and the internal review.\n\nThank you again for your assistance, and I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\n & Life Member\n\nOn Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 23:41 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> 👍🏻\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n>> Dear Requester,\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Many thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will\n>> review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17\n>> th July.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Kind Regards\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Amy\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n>> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 21:01\n>> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n>> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Dear Ms Longford,\n>>\n>> Thank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal\n>> review of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great\n>> House Farm, Llandough.\n>>\n>> I appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the\n>> explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n>>\n>> However, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and\n>> the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could\n>> clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n>>\n>> *1. Documentary basis of the original response*\n>>\n>> The original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and\n>> assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the\n>> statutory listing criteria.\n>>\n>> The internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file\n>> relating to that decision has been located and further states that any\n>> relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the\n>> electronic records system.\n>>\n>> Please therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original\n>> response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the\n>> listing criteria.\n>>\n>> Specifically:\n>>\n>>    - Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n>>    - If so, please identify that record.\n>>    - If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n>>\n>> *2. The inspection of 29 July 1988*\n>>\n>> The original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n>>\n>> Please confirm:\n>>\n>>    - whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing\n>>    inspection;\n>>    - whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n>>    - whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field\n>>    notebooks, photographic registers or other associated records were created;\n>>    and\n>>    - if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have\n>>    been destroyed.\n>>\n>> *3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed*\n>>\n>> The review states that it is possible documentation dating from around\n>> 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n>>\n>> Please clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n>>\n>>    - documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n>>    - records management documentation such as retention schedules,\n>>    destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n>>    - a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n>>\n>> If no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please\n>> confirm this.\n>>\n>> *4. Scope of the searches*\n>>\n>> Please confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing\n>> files to include, where appropriate:\n>>\n>>    - ministerial correspondence;\n>>    - senior officials' correspondence;\n>>    - legal files;\n>>    - inspector's working papers;\n>>    - site visit records;\n>>    - archaeological or conservation files;\n>>    - policy records; and\n>>    - correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of\n>>    Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n>>\n>> If any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you\n>> could identify which.\n>>\n>> *5. Welsh Government's position*\n>>\n>> Finally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's\n>> position regarding Great House Farm.\n>>\n>> Does the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n>>\n>>    - that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n>>    - that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n>>    - that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration\n>>    took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n>>\n>> If none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful\n>> if you could explain what the Welsh Government's position is.\n>>\n>> These questions arise directly from the original response and the\n>> internal review and are intended to clarify the historical record rather\n>> than seek the creation of new information.\n>>\n>> I look forward to your response.\n>>\n>> Yours sincerely,\n>>\n>> Requester\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> On Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:10 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>>\n>> Dear Requester\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Please see attached my review of your request noted ATISN 27021.\n>>\n>> Please let me know if you have any questions or queries.\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Kind Regards\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Amy Longford\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>>\n>> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>>\n>> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>>\n>> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>>\n>> Cadw\n>> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n>> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n>> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>>\n>> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n>> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>>\n>>\n>>\n>> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasan