oner's Office - Wales\n\nSecond Floor, Churchill House\n\nChurchill Way,\n\nCardiff\n\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted] \n\n[email redacted] \n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInformation Governance Officer/ Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\n\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\n\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\n\ntel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\n\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or [email redacted]\n\n \n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\n\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\n \n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n\n \n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n\nFollow us on Twitter /Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n\n \n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-19f5ca04c185d24f","subject":"Re: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"Re: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-13T17:57:16Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f5ca04c185d24f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc-allanol-external-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f5ca04c185d24f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Yes please.\n\nI am trying to gather all information.\nMine and my families claim to ownership of the land was never extinguished,\nas confirmed by the land registry recently. This land is my birthplace and\nI am the heir and successor to the claim. I was in the home when we were\ndispossessed of it and when it was demolished in front of us in 1988.\n\nSo this is not just an enquiry from a member of the public. This concerns\nmy interest in the land and my personal story and data.\n\nThank you in advance for any assistance you can provide.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n & Life Member\n[phone redacted]\n\nOn Mon, 13 Jul 2026, 08:07 FOI Requests, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> We note that your request was addressed to Cardiff Council, with Amgueddfa\n> Cymru copied into the correspondence. Please confirm whether you intended\n> this request to be made to Amgueddfa Cymru as well.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Cofion cynnes,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware Description\n> automatically generated]\n>\n> *FOI Team*\n>\n> [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n>\n> amgueddfa.cymru | museum.wales\n>\n>\n>\n> *Rhif elusen* | Charity number 525774\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 20:51\n> *To:* [email redacted]\n> *Cc:* [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI Requests <\n> [email redacted]>; [email redacted]; [email redacted];\n> National Library of Wales <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff\n> Castle Furniture\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important <https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n>\n> *Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n>\n> Sir/Madam,\n>\n> I am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n>\n> I seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\n> antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from *Great\n> House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\n> from *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\n> museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\n> from our land in Llandough.\n>\n> Specifically, I request copies of all:\n>\n>    1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n>    2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n>    3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n>    4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House\n>    Farm.\n>    5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership\n>    or location of such items.\n>    6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great\n>    House Farm furniture or household effects.\n>    7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n>    connection with these items.\n>    8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n>    to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n>    House Farm.\n>    9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n>    Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n>    Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n>    other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n>\n> For context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\n> Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\n> possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\n> possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\n> gathering actionable intelligence.\n>\n> I appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\n> authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\n> directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n>\n> I am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\n> Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\n> house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\n> items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\n> museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\n> return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\n> reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\n> context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\n> of Information Act.\n>\n> If any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\n> and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\n> test where required.\n>\n> If another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\n> information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\n> advise me accordingly.\n>\n> I look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n>\n> Yours faithfully,\n>\n> Requester \n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f5c9be805341e9","subject":"Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/KH","name":"Re: Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/KH","date":"2026-07-13T17:52:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f5c9be805341e9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5c2d9b170845d-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-kh","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5c2d9b170845d","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f5c9be805341e9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks. I did too.\nI've not heard from them yet though.\nIf you could nudge them I'd appreciate.\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 13 Jul 2026, 12:52 Coventry.OfficeMail, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from\n> HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application\n> you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No\n> paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n>\n> The document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the\n> appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to\n> open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can\n> be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is\n> in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete\n> and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed\n> document by post.\n>\n>\n>\n> HM Land Registry’s purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: “A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future”.\n>\n> We check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n>\n> To see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f5c2d9b170845d","subject":"Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/KH","name":"Your Ref: EDD Our Ref: WA231076/A/216/KH","date":"2026-07-13T15:51:56Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f5c2d9b170845d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5c2d9b170845d-your-ref-edd-our-ref-wa231076-a-216-kh","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5c2d9b170845d","direction":"received","from":"Coventry.OfficeMail","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f5c2d9b170845d.json","attachments":[{"name":"Correspondence.pdf","title":"N610CGV letter (WA231076)","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-07-13_hmlr_n610cgv_letter.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":213339,"sha256":"5c193fa242fd991c17d06102a5304980b5c3bf3ee66486d1ae8f3f889714cbde"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"The document attached is an official requisition, reminder or letter from HM Land Registry. It is not a circular and relates either to an application you have lodged with us or a property in which you have an interest. No paper copy of the item of correspondence will be sent to you.\n\nThe document is in 'Portable Document Format' (PDF) which replicates the appearance of the hard copy version. You will need Adobe Acrobat Reader to open the document. If you do not already have Adobe Acrobat Reader it can be installed free from www.adobe.com. Please note that as the document is in PDF format you cannot add text to any document that you need to complete and return to HM Land Registry. You will have to return any such completed document by post.\n\n\n\nHM Land Registry's purpose is to protect your land ownership and provide services and data that underpin an efficient and informed property market. Our vision is: \"A world-leading property market as part of a thriving economy and a sustainable future\".\n\nWe check all mail and attachments for known viruses. However, you are advised that you open any attachments at your own risk. If you have received this email and it was not intended for you, please let us know, then delete it.\n\nWe welcome correspondence in English and Welsh.\n\nTo see how HM Land Registry treats your personal information, read our Personal information charter: www.gov.uk/government/organisations/land-registry/about/personal-information-charter.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (1)\n- Correspondence.pdf (application/pdf, 208 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-07-13_hmlr_n610cgv_letter.pdf"},{"id":"gm-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc","subject":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","name":"RE: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture","date":"2026-07-13T11:06:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc-allanol-external-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["museum"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["museum"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc","direction":"received","from":"FOI Requests","institutions":[{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f5b28bbe6ecdbc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe note that your request was addressed to Cardiff Council, with Amgueddfa Cymru copied into the correspondence. Please confirm whether you intended this request to be made to Amgueddfa Cymru as well.\n\n\nCofion cynnes,\n\n[A picture containing text, tableware, plate, dishware  Description automatically generated]\nFOI Team\n[cid:image002.png@01DD12C0.19C36700]\n[email redacted] \namgueddfa.cymru  | museum.wales \n\nRhif elusen | Charity number 525774\n\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 02 July 2026 20:51\nTo: [email redacted]\nCc: [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; FOI Requests  ; [email redacted]; [email redacted]; National Library of Wales  \nSubject: ALLANOL/EXTERNAL - Great House Farm, Llandough | Cardiff Castle Furniture\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted] . Learn why this is important \n\nFreedom of Information Act 2000 Request\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings, antiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating from Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including any and all items we received from Bute Estate, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff Council.  Weather it be museums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts from our land in Llandough.\n\nSpecifically, I request copies of all:\n\n  1.  Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n  2.  Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n  3.  Provenance files and ownership records.\n  4.  Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House Farm.\n  5.  Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership or location of such items.\n  6.  Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great House Farm furniture or household effects.\n  7.  Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in connection with these items.\n  8.  Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great House Farm.\n  9.  Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n\nFor context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of Great House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic possessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's possible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still gathering actionable intelligence.\n\nI appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the authority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is directly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n\nI am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in Patagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the house, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving items from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle, museums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful return or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the reconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as context for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom of Information Act.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon and explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest test where required.\n\nIf another public authority is more likely to hold the requested information, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or advise me accordingly.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester "},{"id":"gm-19f59b3f9816c96a","subject":"Automatic reply: Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)","name":"Automatic reply: Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)","date":"2026-07-13T04:19:49Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f59b3f9816c96a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f59b3f9816c96a-automatic-reply-great-house-farm-llandough-now-church-view-close","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f59b3f9816c96a","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f59b3f9816c96a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please quickly read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\n\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n• Your full postal address\n• Your contact telephone number\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in Parliament, it will be dealt with as appropriate.\n\nThank you for taking the time to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nStephen\n\n[X]\nStephen Doughty MP / AS\nMember of Parliament for Cardiff South and Penarth // Aelod Seneddol dros Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth\nHouse of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19f59b3800abf5de","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)","date":"2026-07-13T04:19:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f59b3800abf5de.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f59b21c55b2e9c-great-house-farm-llandough-now-church-view-close","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f59b21c55b2e9c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f59b3800abf5de.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Stephen Doughty MP,\n\nI am writing to follow up on my previous email regarding Great House Farm,\nLlandough, and the concerns