story, and\nrelated issues.\n\nFor your reference, here is a summary of my prior correspondence to you:\nEmail Date Key Points Raised\n16 Feb 2026 • Potential gaps in Council planning and record-keeping for\nGreat House Farm (demolished 1988) • Title fraud and procedural concealment\nrelating to Church View Close (formerly Great House Farm / Ty Mawr)\n4 May 2026 • Setting aside BP vs Buckler 1987 case (stolen paper title,\nidentity fraud, court mistakes, procedural unfairness) • Shared ITV footage\nlink and request for attention as Llandough Councillor\n7 Jun 2026 • Church View Close, Llandough – piecing together 1988 events\nfrom public records, family testimony, and media\n25 Jun 2026 • Enquiry whether you had reviewed prior concerns on family\ndispossession from land in Llandough; request for any progress or discussion\n\nI'd also like to know who removed the tree my great grandad planted to\ncommemorate our ownership claim. As per the image in the collection of\nWales archive.\n\nI have not received substantive replies to these points. As the elected\nCouncillor for Llandough, you have a public duty to respond to reasonable\nenquiries from those with a legitimate interest in the ward in a timely\nmanner (typically within 10–15 working days per standard local authority\nexpectations).\n\nI would appreciate your detailed response to the above at your earliest\nconvenience, ideally within the next 10 working days.\n\nThank you for your attention. I look forward to your reply.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester "},{"id":"gm-19f59994bf7f2993","subject":"Fwd: Request for information regarding acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School","name":"Fwd: Request for information regarding acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School","date":"2026-07-13T03:50:46Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f59994bf7f2993.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5994af5fb93e1-fwd-request-for-information-regarding-acquisition-of-land-for-llandough-primary-school","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5994af5fb93e1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f59994bf7f2993.json","textStatus":"available","text":"---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Requester  \nDate: Mon, 13 Jul 2026, 00:49\nSubject: Request for information regarding acquisition of land for\nLlandough Primary School\nTo:  \n\n\nSirs/ Ma'am,\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004, I request copies of records\nrelating to the acquisition of the land used for the construction of\nLlandough Primary School.\n\nSpecifically, I request:\n\n■ The transfer deed, conveyance or other legal instrument by which the\nCouncil acquired the land.\n\n■ The purchase price or consideration paid for the land.\n\n■ If the land was gifted, transferred at nominal value or below market\nvalue, records explaining the basis for that arrangement.\n\n■ Any valuation reports obtained before acquisition.\n\n■ Any agreements, correspondence or meeting minutes between the Council and\nBP (or any BP subsidiary, trust or associated company) concerning the\ntransfer of the land.\n\n■ Any Cabinet, Committee or Council reports authorising the acquisition.\n\n■ Any planning agreements or obligations connected with the transfer.\n\nIf any of the requested information is already publicly available, please\nprovide the relevant links or document references.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n[address redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19f5997d36b27f89","subject":"Request for information regarding acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School","name":"Request for information regarding acquisition of land for Llandough Primary School","date":"2026-07-13T03:49:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f5997d36b27f89.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f5994af5fb93e1-quest-for-information-regarding-acquisition-of-land-for-llandough-primary-school","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f5994af5fb93e1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f5997d36b27f89.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004, I request copies of records\nrelating to the acquisition of the land used for the construction of\nLlandough Primary School.\n\nSpecifically, I request:\n\n■ The transfer deed, conveyance or other legal instrument by which the\nCouncil acquired the land.\n\n■ The purchase price or consideration paid for the land.\n\n■ If the land was gifted, transferred at nominal value or below market\nvalue, records explaining the basis for that arrangement.\n\n■ Any valuation reports obtained before acquisition.\n\n■ Any agreements, correspondence or meeting minutes between the Council and\nBP (or any BP subsidiary, trust or associated company) concerning the\ntransfer of the land.\n\n■ Any Cabinet, Committee or Council reports authorising the acquisition.\n\n■ Any planning agreements or obligations connected with the transfer.\n\nIf any of the requested information is already publicly available, please\nprovide the relevant links or document references.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n[address redacted]\n[phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19f4ced2ae8529da","subject":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-07-10T16:47:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f4ced2ae8529da.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f4ced2ae8529da.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Ms Longford,\n\nThank you for your response and for the time taken to clarify Cadw's\ncurrent position regarding ATISN 27021.\nI note your confirmation that:\n\nGreat House Farm was inspected for statutory listing on 29 July 1988;\nthe two photographs formed part of that listing assessment;\nthe \"YYY\" code on the reverse of the photographs indicated that the\nbuilding did not meet the listing criteria;\nno official listing file has been located; and\napart from the two photographs, no further records have been identified.\nI am grateful for those clarifications.\n\nAs this request is being considered under the Environmental Information\nRegulations 2004 (and, where applicable, the Freedom of Information Act\n2000), and bearing in mind the EIR's presumption in favour of disclosure, I\nwould be grateful for one further clarification regarding the scope of the\nsearches undertaken.\n\nContemporary newspaper reports from December 1988 indicate that Cadw was\nactively engaged with a number of parties during its consideration of Great\nHouse Farm. These reports refer to:\n\nCadw considering emergency (\"spot\") listing;\ndiscussions with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical\nMonuments of Wales;\ncomments made by a Cadw spokesperson explaining why the building did not\nsatisfy the listing criteria; and\npublic statements regarding the architectural and archaeological\nsignificance of the site.\n\nGiven those contemporary reports, could you please confirm whether the\nsearches undertaken for ATISN 27021 specifically included records such as:\n\ninternal memoranda;\ninspector-to-management correspondence;\nbriefing notes;\nfile notes and telephone notes;\nmeeting records;\npress office files, media briefings or press releases;\ncorrespondence with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical\nMonuments of Wales;\ncorrespondence with the Welsh Office;\ncorrespondence with the local planning authority, conservation officers or\nother public bodies;\nministerial submissions or briefing papers; and\nany other correspondence, whether internal or external, relating to the\nconsideration of Great House Farm for statutory listing.\n\nThe public interest in ensuring that all environmental information has been\nidentified is considerable. Great House Farm was a site with a recorded\nhistory extending over approximately 800 years, associated with the\nhistoric manor of Llandough, incorporating significant historic fabric\nincluding the coach house and outbuildings, and lying within the wider\ncontext of the Marconi wireless experiments at Lavernock. It had also been\nthe subject of a 1974 public petition concerning its preservation and, as\nconfirmed by Cadw, was sufficiently significant in 1988 to warrant\nconsideration for emergency (\"spot\") listing. These factors underline the\nimportance of establishing whether any additional environmental information\nrelating to Cadw's assessment survives.\n\nFinally, if the official listing file and/or any associated correspondence\nonce existed but are no longer held, I would be grateful if you could\nclarify Cadw's records management position by confirming:\nwhether any retention schedule applied to those records;\n\nwhether any authorised destruction took place;\nwhether any destruction certificate, disposal log or other records\nmanagement documentation exists;\nif no such documentation exists, whether this is because no destruction\nrecord was created or because any such record is itself no longer held.\n\nMy intention is simply to establish whether any further environmental\ninformation relating to Cadw's consideration of Great House Farm survives\nbeyond the two inspection photographs already disclosed.\nThank you again for your assistance, and I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Fri, 10 Jul 2026, 08:57 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the below email and follow up questions, for clarity I\n> have responded to each in turn. I hope this helps provide the clarity you\n> are looking for.\n>\n>\n>\n>    1. *Documentary basis of the original response *\n>\n> The two photographs illustrate that the building was inspected for listing\n> and ‘yyy’ reference on the reverse of the photograph was the coding at the\n> time to signify that the building did not met the criteria to be listed.\n>\n>    2. *The inspection of 29th July 1988*\n>\n> The photographs are dated 29/07/1988 and would have been taken as part of\n> the listing assessment. The practice was to keep all photographs separate\n> from the official file in a cabinet. No official file containing additional\n> information has been located and the Records Department have indicated that\n> the documentation from 1988 has, most likely, been destroyed.\n>\n>    3. *Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed. *\n>\n> No destruction record exists. An official in the Records Department\n> provided this advice based on their experience and understanding of the\n> records within their management.\n>\n>    4. *Scope of the searches *\n>\n> I can confirm that the searches included all 8 categories\n>\n>    5. *Welsh Government’s position.*\n>\n> I can confirm that the building was considered for listing, however other\n> than the 2 photographs provided, no other records survive.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Amy Longford IHBC MRTPI*\n>\n> Uwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n>\n> / Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\n>\n> Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\n>\n> Cadw\n> Llywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\n> Ffôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]\n> <http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> [image: https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]\n> <http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Ymunwch â Cadw <https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n>\n> Join Cadw <https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 04 July 2026 03:41\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> 👍🏻\n>\n>\n>\n> On Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will\n> review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17\n> th July.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 21:01\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review\n> of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House\n> Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> I appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the\n> explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n>\n> However, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and\n> the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could\n> clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n>\n> *1. Documentary basis of the original response*\n>\n> The original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and\n> assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the\n> statutory listing criteria.\n>\n> The internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file\n> relating to that decision has been located and further states that any\n> relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the\n> electronic records system.\n>\n> Please therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original\n> response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the\n> listing criteria.\n>\n> Specifically:\n>\n>    - Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n>    - If so, please identify that record.\n>    - If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n>\n> *2. The inspection of 29 July 1988*\n>\n> The original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n>\n> Please confirm:\n>\n>    - whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing\n>    inspection;\n>    - whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n>    - whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks,\n>    photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n>    - if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have\n>    been destroyed.\n>\n> *3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed*\n>\n> The review states that it is possible documentation dating from around\n> 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n>\n> Please clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n>\n>    - documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n>    - records management documentation such as retention schedules,\n>    destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n>    - a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n>\n> If no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please\n> confirm this.\n>\n> *4. Scope of the searches*\n>\n> Please confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing\n> files to include, where appropriate:\n>\n>    - ministerial correspondence;\n>    - senior officials' correspondence;\n>    - legal files;\n>    - inspector's working papers;\n>    - site visit records;\n>    - archaeological or conservation files;\n>    - policy records; and\n>    - correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of\n>    Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n>\n> If any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you\n> could identify which.\n>\n> *5. Welsh Government's position*\n>\n> Finally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's\n> position regarding Great House Farm.\n>\n> Does the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n>\n>    - that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n>    - that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n>    - that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration\n>    took place because the relevant records are unavailable?