Status":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f4be37a086c06e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; gov.wales)","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f4be37a086c06e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nMany thanks for the below email and follow up questions, for clarity I have responded to each in turn. I hope this helps provide the clarity you are looking for.\n\n\n  1.  Documentary basis of the original response\n\nThe two photographs illustrate that the building was inspected for listing and ‘yyy’ reference on the reverse of the photograph was the coding at the time to signify that the building did not met the criteria to be listed.\n\n  1.  The inspection of 29th July 1988\n\nThe photographs are dated 29/07/1988 and would have been taken as part of the listing assessment. The practice was to keep all photographs separate from the official file in a cabinet. No official file containing additional information has been located and the Records Department have indicated that the documentation from 1988 has, most likely, been destroyed.\n\n  1.  Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed.\n\nNo destruction record exists. An official in the Records Department provided this advice based on their experience and understanding of the records within their management.\n\n  1.  Scope of the searches\n\nI can confirm that the searches included all 8 categories\n\n  1.  Welsh Government’s position.\n\nI can confirm that the building was considered for listing, however other than the 2 photographs provided, no other records survive.\n\n\n\nKind Regards\n\n\n\nAmy\n\n\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n\nAmy Longford IHBC MRTPI\nUwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n/ Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\nAmgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\nCadw\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]<http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n[https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]<http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\nYmunwch â Cadw<https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\nJoin Cadw<https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 04 July 2026 03:41\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n👍🏻\n\nOn Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17th July.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 02 July 2026 21:01\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n\nDear Ms Longford,\n\nThank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nI appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n\nHowever, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n\n1. Documentary basis of the original response\n\nThe original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the statutory listing criteria.\n\nThe internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file relating to that decision has been located and further states that any relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n\nPlease therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the listing criteria.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n  *   Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n  *   If so, please identify that record.\n  *   If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n\n2. The inspection of 29 July 1988\n\nThe original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n\nPlease confirm:\n\n  *   whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing inspection;\n  *   whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n  *   whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks, photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n  *   if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have been destroyed.\n\n3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed\n\nThe review states that it is possible documentation dating from around 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n\nPlease clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n\n  *   documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n  *   records management documentation such as retention schedules, destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n  *   a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n\nIf no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please confirm this.\n\n4. Scope of the searches\n\nPlease confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing files to include, where appropriate:\n\n  *   ministerial correspondence;\n  *   senior officials' correspondence;\n  *   legal files;\n  *   inspector's working papers;\n  *   site visit records;\n  *   archaeological or conservation files;\n  *   policy records; and\n  *   correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n\nIf any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you could identify which.\n\n5. Welsh Government's position\n\nFinally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's position regarding Great House Farm.\n\nDoes the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n\n  *   that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n  *   that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n  *   that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n\nIf none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful if you could explain what the Welsh Government's position is.\n\nThese questions arise directly from the original response and the internal review and are intended to clarify the historical record rather than seek the creation of new information.\n\nI look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:10 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester\n\nPlease see attached my review of your request noted ATISN 27021.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or queries.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy Longford\n\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/59wkfSM/Cadw-large.png]\n\nAmy Longford IHBC MRTPI\nUwch Arolygydd Adeiladau Hanesyddol, Parciau a Gerddi\n/ Senior Inspector of Historic Buildings, Parks and Gardens\nAmgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment\nCadw\nLlywodraeth Cymru / Welsh Government\nFfôn / Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n[https://i.ibb.co/CVwfkw2/Cadw-er-lles-pawb.png]<http://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\n[https://i.ibb.co/NxJvcfW/For-us-all-to-keep.png]<http://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\nYmunwch â Cadw<https://www.aelodaethcadw.gwasanaeth.llyw.cymru/>\nJoin Cadw<https://www.cadwmembership.service.gov.wales/>\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 June 2026 09:10\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\nI suspected so.\n\nThanks Amy.\n\nI look forward.\n\nRequester\n\nOn Tue, 16 Jun 2026, 05:08 , <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nDear Requester,\n\nMany thanks for the quick response and for confirming your position. I totally understand and whilst the letters may appear formal, there are set templates to use for a review, I will bear this in mind whilst taking this forward.\n\nJust to let you know, I have had initial conversations internally which I will continue. I will keep you updated as best as I can.\n\nKind Regards\n\nAmy\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 16 June 2026 05:38\nTo: Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw) <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n\n\nMs Longford,\n\nThank you for the acknowledgement letter and for handling the internal review.\n\nFor the record, my communications with Cadw have been enquiries and requests for information under FOI/EIR (ATISN 27021), specifically regarding the statutory listing history, assessments and related records (including the 1988 inspection photographs) for the building known as Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Church View Close. I subsequently requested an internal review of the response provided.\n\nThis was not framed or intended as a formal complaint. I would therefore be grateful if the matter could be treated and recorded a