ases were searched.\nWhether searches extended beyond the Planning Register itself.\nWhether search terms or keywords were used and, if so, what they were.\nWhether date restrictions were applied.\nWhether any information was identified but withheld.\n\nInformation not held\nWhere the Council concludes that information is not held, I respectfully\nrequest that the review explains:\nwhich reasonable searches were undertaken before reaching that conclusion;\nwhether the information never existed;\nwhether it was transferred elsewhere;\nwhether it was destroyed;\nif destroyed, the applicable retention schedule and date of destruction;\nif transferred, the destination repository.\nInformation withheld\n\nIf any information has been withheld under the Environmental Information\nRegulations, I request that the review identifies:\nthe precise Regulation relied upon;\nthe reasons why that exception applies;\nwhere required, the public interest considerations;\nwhether partial disclosure or redaction was considered.\n\nPlanning Register\nThe response relies upon Regulation 6(1)(b) on the basis that planning\ninformation is publicly available.\n\nI would therefore appreciate clarification as to whether the online\nPlanning Register contains the complete planning files, including:\n\nofficer reports;\ncommittee reports;\nconsultation responses;\ninternal memoranda;\ncorrespondence;\namendments;\nsupporting plans;\ntechnical reports;\nconditions;\nenforcement material (if any);\narchived documents.\nIf it does not, I request disclosure of any remaining environmental\ninformation held by the Council.\nGIS information\n\nThe response states that my request for GIS information lacked sufficient\ndetail.\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I seek copies of any GIS datasets or historic\nmapping held by the Council relating to Great House Farm/Ty Mawr, including\nwhere available:\n\nparcel boundaries;\nplanning polygons;\nhistoric base mapping;\naerial imagery;\nhighway extents;\nrights of 