 / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f3cd95eeea3854","subject":"EIR request - Case Ref/ 00210772","name":"EIR request - Case Ref/ 00210772","date":"2026-07-07T13:51:39Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f3cd95eeea3854.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f3cd95eeea3854-eir-request-case-ref-00210772","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f3cd95eeea3854","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f3cd95eeea3854.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your request for information about Great House Farm, Williams/Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan and the further clarification that was received on the 7th June. Your request has been processed under the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nThe Council's Planning records have been reviewed and the Planning department has provided the following response:\n\nIn line with your clarification that was received on the 7th June, searches have been undertaken by the Council's Planning department in relation to the historic Great House Farm / Ty Mawr estate in Llandough. This includes land adjacent to and including Church View Close and the north side of Leckwith Road, with particular reference to the area identified within Land Registry title WA231076 and the timeframe indicated from 1875 onwards, where records exist.\n\nWe have been advised that the links to the planning records relating to the redevelopment of the site during the 1980s-1990s have previously been provided by colleagues in the Planning department. These records, including associated documentation, are publicly available via the Council's Planning Register and can be accessed using the relevant application reference numbers at View or Comment on a Planning Application<https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/living/planning_and_building_control/Planning/Planning-Applications/View-or-Comment-on-a-Planning-Application.aspx>.\nThis information is therefore excepted under Regulation 6(1)(b) of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 - information already publicly available and easily accessible by other means.\n\nWhilst planning files may contain some archaeological information, it is also noted that archaeological records for the Vale of Glamorgan are maintained by Heneb (formerly Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust). We suggest that you contact Heneb directly to access relevant records. Details on how to contact them can be found at Heneb - The Trust for Welsh Archaeology<https://heneb.org.uk/>. To the extent that the Council does not hold further archaeological reports beyond those contained within planning files, Regulation 12(4)(a) of the Environmental Information Regulations 2004 (information not held) applies.\n\nFollowing searches of Planning records, no additional information has been identified within the scope of your request. You asked whether any records may have been transferred to Glamorgan Archives or otherwise. It is possible that historic material of this nature may be held externally, and you may therefore wish to contact Glamorgan Archives directly. Details on how to contact them can be found at https://glamarchives.gov.uk/contact/.\n\nFrom the clarification provided, the Council has been unable to identify which specific GIS datasets are being sought. Please provide further clarification regarding this and once received, we will consider this element further.\n\nAs previously advised, the Council does not hold records relating to the legal case of BP Properties Ltd v Buckler. Neither the Vale of Glamorgan Council nor its predecessor authorities were parties to that case, which appears to have been a private legal matter. Accordingly, information relating to those proceedings is not held by the Council.\n\nIf you are dissatisfied with the handling of your request, you have the right to ask for an internal review. Internal review requests should be made within 40 working days of the date of receipt of the response to your original letter and should be addressed to:\nc/o The Monitoring Officer - [email redacted]\nOr by post to The Monitoring Officer, Civic Offices, Holton Road, Barry, [postcode redacted].\n\nPlease remember to quote the reference number above in any future communications.\n\nIf you are not content with the outcome of the internal review, you have the right to apply directly to the Information Commissioner for a decision.\n\nThe Information Commissioner can be contacted at:\nInformation Commissioner's Office - Wales\nSecond Floor, Churchill House\nChurchill Way,\nCardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted] / Fax:[phone redacted]\n[email redacted]\n\nYours sincerely\n\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ntel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-19f2c63fc6c744db","subject":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","name":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","date":"2026-07-04T09:09:37Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f2c63fc6c744db.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f2c63fc6c744db-new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-from-the-williams-buckler-family","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f2c63fc6c744db","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f2c63fc6c744db.json","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request '1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family' that you made to Ministry of Defence.\n\nTo view the response, click on the link below.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/1988_dispossession_of_great_hous?nocache=incoming-3471357#incoming-3471357\n\nWhen you get there, please update the status to say if the response contains any useful information.\n\nAlthough all responses are automatically published, we depend on you, the original requester, to evaluate them.\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhatDoTheyKnow is a project of mySociety run by a small team of staff and\ndedicated volunteers.\n\nmySociety is a charity that believes that information should be accessible to everyone.\nIf this is important to you, please consider donating to help us do more:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/donate\n\nFind out more about how we handle your data at:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/help/privacy\n\nmySociety is a registered charity in England and Wales (1076346), and a limited\ncompany (03277032)"},{"id":"gm-19f2b0086c4cb09a","subject":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-07-04T02:41:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f2b0086c4cb09a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":["ATISN27021"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f2b0086c4cb09a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"👍🏻\n\nOn Fri, 3 Jul 2026, 12:00 ,   wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for the email. This is a courtesy response to say that I will\n> review your questions below and aim to get a response back to you by the 17\n> th July.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Amy\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 02 July 2026 21:01\n> *To:* Longford, Amy (LCC - Cadw)  \n> *Subject:* Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Ms Longford,\n>\n> Thank you for your letter of 2 July 2026 responding to the internal review\n> of my Freedom of Information request (ATISN 27021) concerning Great House\n> Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> I appreciate the additional searches undertaken during the review and the\n> explanation provided regarding the physical record series examined.\n>\n> However, having considered both the original response of 11 June 2026 and\n> the outcome of the internal review, I would be be grateful if you could\n> clarify a number of points which appear to remain unresolved.\n>\n> *1. Documentary basis of the original response*\n>\n> The original response stated that Great House Farm was visited and\n> assessed by Cadw inspectors and that the building did not satisfy the\n> statutory listing criteria.\n>\n> The internal review now confirms that no assessment, report or case file\n> relating to that decision has been located and further states that any\n> relevant file may have been destroyed before being entered onto the\n> electronic records system.\n>\n> Please therefore identify the documentary basis upon which the original\n> response concluded that the property was assessed and found not to meet the\n> listing criteria.\n>\n> Specifically:\n>\n>    - Is that conclusion derived from a surviving record?\n>    - If so, please identify that record.\n>    - If not, please explain how that conclusion was reached.\n>\n> *2. The inspection of 29 July 1988*\n>\n> The original disclosure included two photographs dated 29 July 1988.\n>\n> Please confirm:\n>\n>    - whether those photographs were taken as part of a formal listing\n>    inspection;\n>    - whether they formed part of a wider inspection file;\n>    - whether any inspection notes, recommendation forms, field notebooks,\n>    photographic registers or other associated records were created; and\n>    - if such records once existed, whether they are now believed to have\n>    been destroyed.\n>\n> *3. Basis for the statement that records may have been destroyed*\n>\n> The review states that it is possible documentation dating from around\n> 1988 was destroyed before being entered onto the electronic records system.\n>\n> Please clarify whether that statement is based upon:\n>\n>    - documentary evidence relating specifically to Great House Farm;\n>    - records management documentation such as retention schedules,\n>    destruction registers or disposal logs; or\n>    - a general understanding of historic records management practices.\n>\n> If no destruction records exist for the relevant file series, please\n> confirm this.\n>\n> *4. Scope of the searches*\n>\n> Please confirm whether searches extended beyond the registered listing\n> files to include, where appropriate:\n>\n>    - ministerial correspondence;\n>    - senior officials' correspondence;\n>    - legal files;\n>    - inspector's working papers;\n>    - site visit records;\n>    - archaeological or conservation files;\n>    - policy records; and\n>    - correspondence with external organisations, including the Vale of\n>    Glamorgan Council, the former Welsh Office and other heritage bodies.\n>\n> If any of these categories were not searched, I would be grateful if you\n> could identify which.\n>\n> *5. Welsh Government's position*\n>\n> Finally, I would be appreciate clarification of the Welsh Government's\n> position regarding Great House Farm.\n>\n> Does the Welsh Government's position now amount to one of the following:\n>\n>    - that Great House Farm was never considered for statutory protection;\n>    - that it was considered, but the records no longer survive; or\n>    - that it is no longer possible to determine whether consideration\n>    took place because the relevant records are unavailable?\n>\n> If none of those accurately reflects your position, I would be grateful if\n> you could explain what the Welsh Government'