02T19:51:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f246285263cd25.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e-great-house-farm-llandough-cardiff-castle-furniture","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f1c45aa603989e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f246285263cd25.json","textStatus":"available","text":"*Freedom of Information Act 2000 Request*\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nI am making this request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nI seek all recorded information held concerning furniture, furnishings,\nantiques, fixtures, heirlooms and other movable property originating\nfrom *Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough*, including any and all items we received\nfrom *Bute Estate*, *Cardiff Castle*, *Cardiff Council. * Weather it be\nmuseums, archives or any other public body. I know museums have artifacts\nfrom our land in Llandough.\n\nSpecifically, I request copies of all:\n\n   1. Inventories, catalogues and asset registers.\n   2. Acquisition, disposal, loan and transfer records.\n   3. Provenance files and ownership records.\n   4. Photographs of items identified as originating from Great House Farm.\n   5. Correspondence concerning the identification, recovery, ownership or\n   location of such items.\n   6. Internal reports, legal advice and memoranda relating to Great House\n   Farm furniture or household effects.\n   7. Correspondence mentioning the Buckler or Williams families in\n   connection with these items.\n   8. Records concerning any efforts by Cardiff Council or Cardiff Castle\n   to trace, recover or secure items believed to have originated from Great\n   House Farm.\n   9. Correspondence with the Bute Estate, museums, the Department for\n   Culture, Media and Sport, the Reviewing Committee on the Export of Works of\n   Art and Objects of Cultural Interest (RCEWA), Arts Council England or any\n   other public authority regarding objects from Great House Farm.\n\nFor context, I am allegeing that my family was unlawfully dispossessed of\nGreat House Farm through fraud, and that furniture and other historic\npossessions belonging to the family were consequently dispersed. It's\npossible the bailiffs from BP were also SAS soldiers. We are still\ngathering actionable intelligence.\n\nI appreciate that the Freedom of Information Act does not require the\nauthority to determine the merits of that allegation. However, it is\ndirectly relevant to understanding why I seek the recorded information.\n\nI am currently developing a full-scale replica of Great House Farm in\nPatagonia, Argentina as a museum dedicated to preserving the history of the\nhouse, its occupants and its contents. Should records identify surviving\nitems from the farm, whether held by Cardiff Council, Cardiff Castle,\nmuseums or other public institutions, I intend to pursue their lawful\nreturn or transfer so they may ultimately be reunited with the\nreconstructed Great House Farm museum. This statement is provided solely as\ncontext for my request and does not seek a determination under the Freedom\nof Information Act.\n\nIf any information is withheld, please identify each exemption relied upon\nand explain why it applies, including the outcome of any public interest\ntest where required.\n\nIf another public authority is more likely to hold the requested\ninformation, I would be grateful if you would transfer the request or\nadvise me accordingly.\n\nI look forward to your response within the statutory time limit.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester "},{"id":"gm-19f2461b853376c3","subject":"Re: Buckler - 260607013 - FOI - response","name":"Re: Buckler - 260607013 - FOI - response","date":"2026-07-02T19:50:09Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f2461b853376c3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f18a3ec528e53f-buckler-260607013-foi-response","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f18a3ec528e53f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f2461b853376c3.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nSee below.\nGood day.\n\nRequester \n[phone redacted]\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Thu, 2 Jul 2026, 08:48 Disclosure Team,  \nwrote:\n\n> OFFICIAL - SENSITIVE\n>\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email. Please can you send your proof of address in a\n> different format, as we are unable to open it.\n>\n>\n>\n> On receipt of this information, we will continue to process your request.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: signature_1893814455]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Disclosure Team*\n>\n> Security and Information Directorate\n>\n> Service Transformation Group\n>\n> Ministry of Justice\n>\n>\n>\n> OFFICIAL - SENSITIVE\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 01 July 2026 22:24\n> *To:* Disclosure Team  \n> *Subject:* Re: Buckler - 260607013 - FOI - response\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: Image removed by sender.]\n>  \n>\n> account-statement_2026-07-01_2026-07-01_en-gb_586dc5.pdf\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> See attached,\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [phone redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> On Wed, 1 Jul 2026, 07:31 Disclosure Team,  \n> wrote:\n>\n> OFFICIAL\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email.\n>\n>\n>\n> Your request has been handled in line with data protection legislation as\n> a Subject Access Request (SAR) for your personal information. In order for\n> us to process your request we require further information as detailed below.\n>\n>\n>\n> *Verifying Identity*\n>\n>\n>\n> The Ministry of Justice (MoJ) is committed to protecting your personal\n> data and keeping it secure. One of the key safeguards we use is verifying\n> the identity of anyone who requests access to personal data. This ensures\n> that only you can access your information through a SAR.\n>\n> To process your request, we ask that you provide two forms of\n> identification.\n>\n>    1. *Photo ID* – This should clearly show your face, such as a passport\n>    or driving licence.\n>\n>\n>    2. *Proof of Address* – This should show your full name and current\n>    address, such as a utility bill (e.g. electricity, gas, water,\n>    telephone/broadband), council tax bill, or a bank/credit card statement.\n>    These documents must be dated within the last six months.\n>\n> You can use your driving licence as proof of your current address, but\n> you’ll still need to provide an additional photo ID (such as your\n> passport).\n>\n>\n>\n> We do not use photo ID to confirm your likeness but because the process\n> for obtaining photo ID involves additional safeguards that help us confirm\n> your identity with greater confidence. This is a necessary and\n> proportionate step to make sure your data remains secure.\n>\n> You can find more information about how we handle personal data in our Personal\n> Information Charter\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> On receipt of this information, we will continue to process your request.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> [image: signature_1893814455]