rrespondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f1aa5d5d6d832e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thank you\n\nRequester\n\nOn Tue, 30 Jun 2026, 07:50 FOI,   wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email of 27 June 2026, requesting information from\n> Ordnance Survey in accordance with the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA)\n> 2000, in relation to the historical depiction of a property and surrounding\n> land historically referred to as Ty Mawr / Great House Farm.\n>\n>\n>\n> Having reviewed your request, in our view this does not appear to be a\n> request for information as defined under the Freedom of Information Act\n> (2000).  A valid request for recorded information will be treated as a\n> request under the FOIA, unless it is a routine enquiry or for information\n> that is dealt with as part of our routine business.\n>\n>\n>\n> We consider your request to be for mapping information which is dealt with\n> as part of our routine business.  As a result, rather than dealing with\n> this as an FOI request, we have forwarded your email to our Customer\n> Services team as we feel they will be better able to deal with your\n> request. Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10\n> working days.\n>\n> In the mean-time, we do have some information about Historical mapping on\n> our website: Historical map archives | About us | OS\n>  .\n>\n> You can call customer Services on [phone redacted], or contact them via Live\n> Chat   which is available\n> Monday to Friday 08:00 -18:00 (except for Bank Holidays). Outside of\n> these hours, you can use the Contact Us\n>   form or email\n> [email redacted].\n>\n>\n>\n> Yours sincerely\n>\n>\n>\n> *Kim Furlong for the FOI Team*\n>\n> Legal Services\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Adanac Drive, Southampton, [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n>\n> www.os.uk | *[email redacted]  *\n>\n> Follow us: X (Twitter)   | LinkedIn\n>   | YouTube\n>   | Instagram\n>   | Facebook\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 27 June 2026 16:56\n> *To:* FOI  \n> *Subject:* Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff\n>\n>\n>\n> *External Email:* Take care with attachments & links.\n>\n>\n>\n> Ordnance Survey Historical Enquiries Team,\n>\n>\n>\n> I am writing to request information regarding historical Ordnance Survey\n> mapping and naming conventions for a specific area in Llandough, near\n> Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (Wales).\n>\n>\n>\n> I am researching the historical depiction of a property and surrounding\n> land historically referred to as Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, and I am\n> trying to understand how its labelling and placement may have changed\n> across Ordnance Survey map editions.\n>\n>\n>\n> Specific mapping references\n>\n> The area I am examining includes the following Ordnance Survey historical\n> map references:\n>\n> 38-1-608\n>\n> 38-1-334\n>\n>\n>\n> I am also comparing Ordnance Survey map editions from approximately the\n> 1950s through to the early 1970s.\n>\n>\n>\n> Mapping issue being investigated\n>\n> From comparing available historical map editions, I have observed the\n> following:\n>\n>\n>\n> Earlier Ordnance Survey maps (pre-1950s / early 1950s) appear to\n> consistently show the name Ty Mawr / Great House Farm in one field or\n> parcel location.\n>\n>\n>\n> In later editions (circa early 1970s), the label “Ty Mawr” appears to\n> shift position between adjacent parcels, and the descriptor “Farm” appears\n> to be applied or positioned differently than in earlier mapping.\n>\n>\n>\n> There also appears to be a change in how the surrounding land parcels are\n> labelled or visually grouped.\n>\n>\n>\n> What I am seeking clarification on\n>\n> Could you please advise:\n>\n>\n>\n> Whether Ordnance Survey records show any map revision notes, resurvey\n> information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or\n> label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\n>\n> Whether changes such as the movement of a name between adjacent parcels\n> would typically result from:\n>\n>\n>\n> resurvey work or updated field recording\n>\n> cartographic generalisation or redraw practices\n>\n> changes in naming conventions or feature classification\n>\n> Whether OS holds any guidance or archival material explaining how estate\n> names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across\n> map editions in this period\n>\n>\n>\n> Which historical Ordnance Survey editions or map series would best show\n> the most accurate progression of naming and label placement for this\n> specific site\n>\n>\n>\n> If possible, I would also appreciate guidance on accessing any archived\n> mapping sheets or revision history material relevant to this location.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your assistance. I appreciate your time in helping clarify\n> how Ordnance Survey mapping practices evolved during this period.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n>\n\n>\n\n>\n>\n> This email and any attachments are intended only for the intended\n> recipient and may contain sensitive information. If you are not the\n> intended recipient, please immediately delete this email and inform the\n> sender.\n>\n> OS email communications may be monitored to ensure the secure and\n> effective operation of our systems and for other lawful purposes. Subject\n> to contract: No rights are to be derived from any proposal contained in\n> this email until a written agreement containing all necessary terms is\n> executed between the relevant parties.\n>\n> Thank you for your cooperation.\n>\n> Ordnance Survey Limited (Company Registration number 09121572)\n> Registered Office: Explorer House\n> Adanac Drive\n> Southampton [postcode redacted]\n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n> http://www.os.uk\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f1aa2455a19a61","subject":"Re: Buckler - 260607013 - FOI - response","name":"Re: Buckler - 260607013 - FOI - response","date":"2026-06-30T22:24:29Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f1aa2455a19a61.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f18a3ec528e53f-buckler-260607013-foi-response","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f18a3ec528e53f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f1aa2455a19a61.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks.\n\nAnd finally,\n\nI am writing now to make a Subject Access Request under Article 15 of the\nUK General Data Protection Regulation and the Data Protection Act 2018.\n\nI wish to obtain copies of any personal data that the Ministry of Justice,\nHM Courts & Tribunals Service, or any relevant department holds about me, *Requester*, whether in electronic or paper records.\n\nIn particular, I am seeking any personal data relating to the events\nsurrounding the possession and eviction proceedings connected with Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan. As a young child, I was\npresent in the farmhouse during the eviction and enforcement action\ninvolving BP and court bailiffs. I understand there were reports at the\ntime that specialist security personnel may also have been involved. If any\nrecords identify me, refer to my presence, welfare, or involvement, I\nrequest copies of those records.\n\nI also request any persona