edge and Information Liaison Officer\nNational Support Unit | HMCTS\ngov.uk/hmcts<http://www.gov.uk/hmcts>\n\n[HM Courts & Tribunals Service logo]\nHere is how HMCTS users your data<https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/hm-courts-and-tribunals-service/about/personal-information-charter>\n\n\n________________________________\nThis e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents.\n\n\nOFFICIAL - FOR PUBLIC RELEASE"},{"id":"gm-19f18269393340ea","subject":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-06-30T10:50:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f18269393340ea.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c-ty-mawr-great-house-farm-red-fen-cedfin-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["os"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["os"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c","direction":"received","from":"FOI","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f18269393340ea.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nThank you for your email of 27 June 2026, requesting information from Ordnance Survey in accordance with the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) 2000, in relation to the historical depiction of a property and surrounding land historically referred to as Ty Mawr / Great House Farm.\n\nHaving reviewed your request, in our view this does not appear to be a request for information as defined under the Freedom of Information Act (2000).  A valid request for recorded information will be treated as a request under the FOIA, unless it is a routine enquiry or for information that is dealt with as part of our routine business.\n\nWe consider your request to be for mapping information which is dealt with as part of our routine business.  As a result, rather than dealing with this as an FOI request, we have forwarded your email to our Customer Services team as we feel they will be better able to deal with your request. Our Customer Services Team will aim to respond to you within 10 working days.\nIn the mean-time, we do have some information about Historical mapping on our website: Historical map archives | About us | OS<https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/about/historical-map-archives>.\nYou can call customer Services on [phone redacted], or contact them via Live Chat<https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/contact-us> which is available Monday to Friday 08:00 -18:00 (except for Bank Holidays). Outside of these hours, you can use the Contact Us<https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/contact-us> form or email [email redacted]<[email redacted]>.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nKim Furlong for the FOI Team\nLegal Services\n\n[cid:image003.png@01DD0886.9570A410]\n\nAdanac Drive, Southampton, [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\nwww.os.uk<http://www.os.uk/> | [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nFollow us: X (Twitter)<https://x.com/OrdnanceSurvey> | LinkedIn<https://www.linkedin.com/company/ordnance-survey/> | YouTube<https://www.youtube.com/@ordnancesurvey/videos> | Instagram<https://www.instagram.com/ordnancesurvey/?hl=en> | Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/osmapping/>\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 27 June 2026 16:56\nTo: FOI <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff\n\nExternal Email: Take care with attachments & links.\n\nOrdnance Survey Historical Enquiries Team,\n\nI am writing to request information regarding historical Ordnance Survey mapping and naming conventions for a specific area in Llandough, near Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan (Wales).\n\nI am researching the historical depiction of a property and surrounding land historically referred to as Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, and I am trying to understand how its labelling and placement may have changed across Ordnance Survey map editions.\n\nSpecific mapping references\nThe area I am examining includes the following Ordnance Survey historical map references:\n38-1-608\n38-1-334\n\nI am also comparing Ordnance Survey map editions from approximately the 1950s through to the early 1970s.\n\nMapping issue being investigated\nFrom comparing available historical map editions, I have observed the following:\n\nEarlier Ordnance Survey maps (pre-1950s / early 1950s) appear to consistently show the name Ty Mawr / Great House Farm in one field or parcel location.\n\nIn later editions (circa early 1970s), the label “Ty Mawr” appears to shift position between adjacent parcels, and the descriptor “Farm” appears to be applied or positioned differently than in earlier mapping.\n\nThere also appears to be a change in how the surrounding land parcels are labelled or visually grouped.\n\nWhat I am seeking clarification on\nCould you please advise:\n\nWhether Ordnance Survey records show any map revision notes, resurvey information, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or label placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\nWhether changes such as the movement of a name between adjacent parcels would typically result from:\n\nresurvey work or updated field recording\ncartographic generalisation or redraw practices\nchanges in naming conventions or feature classification\nWhether OS holds any guidance or archival material explaining how estate names or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across map editions in this period\n\nWhich historical Ordnance Survey editions or map series would best show the most accurate progression of naming and label placement for this specific site\n\nIf possible, I would also appreciate guidance on accessing any archived mapping sheets or revision history material relevant to this location.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I appreciate your time in helping clarify how Ordnance Survey mapping practices evolved during this period.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\n\n\n\nThis email and any attachments are intended only for the intended recipient and may contain sensitive information. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately delete this email and inform the sender.\n\nOS email communications may be monitored to ensure the secure and effective operation of our systems and for other lawful purposes. Subject to contract: No rights are to be derived from any proposal contained in this email until a written agreement containing all necessary terms is executed between the relevant parties.\n\nThank you for your cooperation.\n\nOrdnance Survey Limited (Company Registration number 09121572)\nRegistered Office: Explorer House\nAdanac Drive\nSouthampton [postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\nhttp://www.os.uk<http://www.os.uk/>"},{"id":"gm-19f09cb101e038e4","subject":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","name":"Ty Mawr/ Great House Farm/ Red Fen (Cedfin), Llandough, Cardiff","date":"2026-06-27T15:55:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f09cb101e038e4.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c-ty-mawr-great-house-farm-red-fen-cedfin-llandough-cardiff","scopeTopics":["os"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["os"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f09c8c7ddc8f3c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"os","name":"Ordnance Survey"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f09cb101e038e4.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ordnance Survey Historical Enquiries Team,\n\nI am writing to request information regarding historical Ordnance Survey\nmapping and naming conventions for a specific area in Llandough, near\nPenarth, Vale of Glamorgan (Wales).\n\nI am researching the historical depiction of a property and surrounding\nland historically referred to as Ty Mawr / Great House Farm, and I am\ntrying to understand how its labelling and placement may have changed\nacross Ordnance Survey map editions.\n\nSpecific mapping references\nThe area I am examining includes the following Ordnance Survey historical\nmap references:\n38-1-608\n38-1-334\n\nI am also comparing Ordnance Survey map editions from approximately the\n1950s through to the early 1970s.\n\nMapping issue being investigated\nFrom comparing available historical map editions, I have observed the\nfollowing:\n\nEarlier Ordnance Survey maps (pre-1950s / early 1950s) appear to\nconsistently show the name Ty Mawr / Great House Farm in one field or\nparcel location.\n\nIn later editions (circa early 1970s), the label “Ty Mawr” appears to shift\nposition between adjacent parcels, and the descriptor “Farm” appears to be\napplied or positioned differently than in earlier mapping.\n\nThere also appears to be a change in how the surrounding land parcels are\nlabelled or visually grouped.\n\nWhat I am seeking clarification on\nCould you please advise:\n\nWhether Ordnance Survey records show any map revision notes, resurvey\ninformation, or internal documentation explaining changes in naming or\nlabel placement for this area between approximately 1950 and 1975\nWhether changes such as the movement of a name between adjacent parcels\nwould typically result from:\n\nresurvey work or updated field recording\ncartographic generalisation or redraw practices\nchanges in naming conventions or feature classification\nWhether OS holds any guidance or archival material explaining how estate\nnames or farm names were assigned, repositioned, or reinterpreted across\nmap editions in this period\n\nWhich historical Ordnance Survey editions or map series would best show the\nmost accurate progression of naming and label placement for this specific\nsite\n\nIf possible, I would also appreciate guidance on accessing any archived\nmapping sheets or revision history material relevant to this location.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I appreciate your time in helping clarify\nhow Ordnance Survey mapping practices evolved during this period.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\n"},{"id":"gm-19f08cdd7e768c7f","subject":"Enquiry re: Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough – Plot references 36.792 & 70/1.334 (Williams / Buckler family, 1876 acquisition)\r\n","name":"Enquiry re: Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough – Plot references 36.792 & 70/1.334 (Williams / Buckler family, 1876 acquisition)\r\n","date":"2026-06-27T11:18:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f08cdd7e768c7f.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f08007fe391d18-enquiry-re-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-plot-references-36-792-70-1-334-williams-buckler-family-1876-acquisition","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f08007fe391d18","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f08cdd7e768c7f.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\n\nI am writing regarding historical records for *Great House Farm (Ty Mawr)*\non the north side of Leckwith Road, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan (title\nWA231076 / formerly WA240304 accordingly to Land Registry FOI).\n\nMy family (Williams, later Buckler) are believed to have held the land,\nwith acquisition around *1876*. I have two OS map references for the same\nplot:\n\n   - *36.792* (1952 edition)\n   - *70 / 1.334* (earlier revision, associated with \"Ty-mawr\" labelling)\n\nI would be grateful if you could search your collections for any deeds,\nconveyances, manorial records, tithe/apportionment documents, valuations,\nor estate papers linking these plot references (or the farm) to the\n*Williams* or *Buckler* family.\n\nAlso relevant: connections to *Western Ground Rents Limited*, *Bute Estate*,\nor *BP Pension Trust* / predecessors in the 1969–1980s period.\n\nAny details on access, copies, or visit requirements would be appreciated.\nReference: Requester, [email redacted].\n\nA family member there could also visit if there's anything.\n\nThank you,\n\n\nRequester "},{"id":"gm-19f00f36b33fb6f8","subject":"Automatic reply: Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","name":"Automatic reply: Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","date":"2026-06-25T22:42:50Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f00f36b33fb6f8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19f00f36b33fb6f8-automatic-reply-automatic-reply-complaint-of-maladministration-defective-notice-enforcement-process-and-loss-of-opportun","scopeTopics":["mp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19f00f36b33fb6f8","direction":"received","from":"DOUGHTY, Stephen","institutions":[{"id":"mp","name":"Member of Parliament"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f00f36b33fb6f8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello,\n\nThank you for your email. Please quickly read this automatic response, which serves as notice that your message has been received.\n\nI receive hundreds of emails every week, and although I intend to reply as quickly as I can to all, I prioritise those that raise immediate problems and urgent cases.\n\n\nCasework\n\nThere is a strict protocol that means Members of Parliament may only provide assistance to their own constituents. This means you must live in the constituency of Cardiff South and Penarth in order for me to assist.\n\nPlease therefore ensure that you have included:\n\n• Your full name\n• Your full postal address\n• Your contact telephone number\n• Any relevant reference numbers\n\nParliamentary Business\n\nIf your email relates to my work in