n> Dde Caerdydd a Phenarth*\n> *House of Commons, Westminster, London, [postcode redacted]*\n> *Tel: [phone redacted] | Email: [email redacted]\n> <[email redacted]>*\n>\n>\n> UK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended\n> recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and\n> delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is\n> not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability\n> is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail.\n> This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used\n> for sensitive data.\n>"},{"id":"gm-19f00928c04bfc52","subject":"Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-25T20:57:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19f00928c04bfc52.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ef7671c783f5d5-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ef7671c783f5d5","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19f00928c04bfc52.json","textStatus":"available","text":"George,\n\nHave you had an opportunity to look into any of the concerns I have raised\nwith you regarding my family's dispossession from land at Llandough?\n\nMight we be able to achieve even the smallest task together in trying to\nunravel what I allege may have involved fraud, concealment, mistakes, or\nother wrongdoing surrounding my family's loss of possession of land there?\n\nIt is land that my family claimed to own, and that claim has never, to my\nknowledge, been extinguished or determined against us by a court.\n\nThe possibility of errors relating to my grandmother's and father's deaths,\ncourt mistakes, Land Registry mistakes, the dismissal of my father's appeal\nagainst the 1987 ruling, the rejection of the ECHR application, and Cadw's\ninaction do not alter the central point: my family's claim to ownership of\nthe land itself has never been properly adjudicated upon or defeated.\n\nI may even have an interest in Church View Close. I am raising concerns\nabout what could amount to a major scandal in the manner in which my family\nand I were dispossessed of land there. Your lack of response, together with\na number of unusual or contradictory responses I have received from other\nparties connected with the matter, has not reassured me that there is a\nwillingness to examine these issues openly.\n\nIf evidence was destroyed, if mistakes were made, or if fraud or\nconcealment occurred, I am sure you would prefer to assist in establishing\nthe truth rather than be perceived as defending or perpetuating any\nwrongdoing.\n\nWould you at least be willing to help with the more limited task of\nidentifying when the tree planted by my family was removed? From what I can\ngather, the tree planting commemorated our claim to absolute title over our\nplot of land. Its removal could arguably represent the destruction of\nevidence connected with that claim.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n"},{"id":"gm-19efdbb70ed76424","subject":"Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","name":"Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","date":"2026-06-25T07:42:35Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"