] | Email: [email redacted]\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19efdbacc43cd375","subject":"Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","name":"Automatic reply: Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","date":"2026-06-25T07:42:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19efdbacc43cd375.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19efdbacc43cd375-automatic-reply-complaint-of-maladministration-defective-notice-enforcement-process-and-loss-of-opportunity-great-house-","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19efdbacc43cd375","direction":"received","from":"Phso Enquiries","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19efdbacc43cd375.json","textStatus":"available","text":"This is an automated response to confirm we have received your email.\n\n\n\nPlease read the section which relates to why you have contacted us.\n\n\n\nYou are bringing or have a complaint with us.\n\n\n\n  1.  If you are bringing a complaint to us and this is your first contact:\n\n\n\nWe are sorry that you have had reason to contact us. The best way to submit your complaint to us is to complete our complaint form. You can complete the complaint form online , or you can get copies of our Parliamentary and Health forms (including large print format) on our website. \n\n\n\nIf you are unsure if your complaint is ready for us to look at, you can find out more on our website .\n\n\n\nIf you need a different format such as a different language or Braille, or if you need any further support to help you get your complaint to us, you can call us on [phone redacted]. We can also provide paper copies of the forms. Our opening hours are Monday to Thursday 9am to 4pm, Friday 8.30am to 12pm\n\n2. If you have an existing case with us:\n\n\n\nYour email will be added to your case and your caseworker will usually be in contact with you     within one month.\n\n\n\n3. If you are making an FOI request:\n\n\n\nPlease resend your email to [email redacted] .\n\n\nYou are contacting us from an organisation or MP's office:\n\n\n\n  1.  If you are providing records or a response to enquiries on a case, your email will be added to the case and if necessary, the caseworker will be in contact with you.\n\n\n\n  1.  If you have a general query, you will be responded to within one month.\n\n\n\nIf you are emailing about any of the following, please redirect your email:\n\n\n     *   Recruitment – [email redacted] \n     *   Invoicing – [email redacted] \n\n\nWe’re changing our name. Later this year we will become the Public Service Ombudsman. This will make it easier for people to find us and understand what we do. The service we provide will remain the same. Visit our website  to find out more."},{"id":"gm-19efdb9d4ad37c98","subject":"Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","name":"Complaint of maladministration – defective notice, enforcement process, and loss of opportunity (Great House Farm, Llandough)","date":"2026-06-25T07:41:14Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19efdb9d4ad37c98.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19efdb5116ec642f-complaint-of-maladministration-defective-notice-enforcement-process-and-loss-of-opportunity-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19efdb5116ec642f","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19efdb9d4ad37c98.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman,\n\nI wish to submit a complaint of maladministration concerning the handling\nof enforcement and associated administrative processes relating to my\nfamily’s former residence and land at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr),\nLlandough, Vale of Glamorgan, culminating in its demolition in December\n1988.\n\nThis complaint is not a request to reopen any court judgment. It concerns\nthe *administrative conduct of public bodies*, including notice procedures,\nenforcement execution, and heritage-related decision-making.\n1. Defective and misleading notice process\n\nI believe that formal notices issued during the relevant period were\nmaterially defective, including being addressed to “Mrs Buckler” rather\nthan the legal occupier, Mary Williams.\n\nThis created a situation where the intended recipient was not properly\nidentified in their correct legal capacity, which I believe resulted in a *loss\nof meaningful opportunity to respond, challenge, or seek suspension of\nenforcement action* at the relevant time.\n2. Loss of opportunity to contest enforcement\n\nAs a result of the above notice issues, I believe the family was deprived\nof a genuine opportunity to take timely legal or procedural steps to\nprevent or delay enforcement action, including demolition.\n\nThis constitutes, in my view, procedural unfairness in the administration\nof enforcement.\n3. Heritage and regulatory oversight concerns\n\nI also believe that relevant public authorities had knowledge of the\nhistorical and archaeological significance of the site, including Roman and\nearly medieval features, but failed to take adequate protective action\nprior to demolition.\n\nThis raises concerns of *regulatory failure in the exercise of statutory\nheritage responsibilities*.\n4. Irreversible loss and harm\n\nThe outcome of these processes was the complete demolition of the property\nin December 1988, resulting in:\n\n   - irreversible loss of a long-occupied family home\n   - destruction of potential historical and archaeological material\n   - loss of personal and family property and records\n\nI believe this outcome resulted from administrative failings rather than a\nfair and properly informed process.\n------------------------------\n5. What I am asking the Ombudsman to do\n\nI am requesting that the Ombudsman:\n\n   1. Investigate whether there was maladministration in:\n      - service of notices and identification of the correct legal occupier\n      - execution of enforcement actions\n      - handling of heritage-related responsibilities by relevant\n      authorities\n   2. Determine whether these actions caused a loss of opportunity to\n   prevent or challenge demolition.\n   3. Consider whether a finding of maladministration is appropriate, and\n   whether this should lead to:\n      - a formal apology\n      - a recommendation for ex gratia compensation\n      - any further remedial or restorative measures within the Ombudsman’s\n      remit\n\n------------------------------\n6. Supporting material\n\nI am in the process of obtaining further documentary evidence via Freedom\nof Information requests and archival sources, including:\n\n   - enforcement and court execution records\n   - local authority and heritage body correspondence\n   - any relevant ministerial communications\n\nI will provide these as they become available.\n------------------------------\n\nI submit this complaint in good faith and seek an independent review of\nadministrative fairness and decision-making, not a reopening of any\njudicial determination.\n\nRegards, Requester"},{"id":"gm-19eee71b973f9c75","subject":"RE: FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-22T08:28:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19eee71b973f9c75.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ee6a2303d483b9-foi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ee6a2303d483b9","direction":"received","from":"Disclosure Team","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19eee71b973f9c75.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning,\n\nWe are processing your request under reference 260607013. The deadline for the response is 6 July.\n\nKind regards\n\n[signature_1893814455]\n\nDisclosure Team\nSecurity and Information Directorate\nService Transformation