mation <[email redacted]>\nSubject: FOI follow up\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nDid you receive my FOI recently?\nI don't see a reply.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\nYmateb nad yw'n Argyfwng\\ Non-Emergency Response\n\nOes angen i chi siarad â'r heddlu ond nid oes angen ymateb brys arnoch? Gallwch roi gwybod am fater drwy ein gwefan https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk, neu ffonio 101. Gallwch ddefnyddio 101 i roi gwybod am achosion nad ydynt yn rhai brys i unrhyw heddlu yng Nghymru a Lloegr. Mewn argyfwng, ffoniwch 999 bob amser.\n\nDo you need to speak to the police but don’t require an emergency response? You can make a report via our website https://www.south-wales.police.uk, or call 101. 101 can be used to report a non-emergency to any force in Wales and England. In an emergency always dial 999.\n\nCymorth Iaith Gymraeg\\Welsh Language Support\n\nMae Heddlu De Cymru yn croesawu derbyn gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Byddwn yn ateb gohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nSouth Wales Police welcomes receiving correspondence in Welsh and English. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\nYmwadiad Heddlu De Cymru\\South Wales Police Disclaimer\n\nGallai defnyddio neu ddatgelu’r neges e-bost hon heb awdurdod fod yn anghyfreithlon. Gallwch weld ein datganiad cyfrinachedd yn: https://www.heddlu-de-cymru.police.uk/cy-GB/heddluoedd/heddlu-de-cymru/ardaloedd/amdanom-ni/amdanom-ni/datganiad-cyfrinachedd-e-bost/\".\n\nUnauthorised use or disclosure of this email may be unlawful. View our confidentiality statement at https://www.south-wales.police.uk/police-forces/south-wales-police/areas/about-us/about-us/email-confidentiality-statement/."},{"id":"gm-19ee6a61b242cb74","subject":"FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-20T20:08:25Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ee6a61b242cb74.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ee6a51312a8311-foi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["dwrcymru"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dwrcymru"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ee6a51312a8311","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"dwrcymru","name":"Dwr Cymru Welsh Water"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ee6a61b242cb74.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dŵr Cymru / Welsh Water Information Governance Team,\n\nI am writing to request access to any records held by Dŵr Cymru relating to\nwater supply accounts, billing history, and correspondence associated with\nthe following property and occupants:\n\nGreat House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough, near Cardiff (Vale of Glamorgan)\nAny accounts registered in the names of Williams and/or Buckler families\nassociated with this address or adjoining holdings\nThis request is made under the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK\nGDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018, and where applicable under the\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\n1. Information requested\nPlease provide copies of all records held, including but not limited to:\nAccount and billing records\nHistorical and active water supply account details for the property\nNames of account holders associated with the address\nBilling statements, arrears records, and payment history\nAny changes of account holder or tenancy-related updates\nCorrespondence and operational records\nAny letters, notices, or internal correspondence relating to:\n\nwater supply restriction\ndisconnection or proposed disconnection\nenforcement actions for non-payment\nAny instructions received internally to restrict, reduce, or disconnect\nwater supply\nOperational or legal instructions\nAny records of:\n\ndisconnection orders\nenforcement decisions\nvisits or inspections related to supply interruption\nThe identity (job role or department) of any person who authorised such\naction\nHistorical records\nAny archived or legacy records (including pre-digital systems) relating to\nthe above property and family names\n\n2. Time period\nPlease search records from the earliest date available up to the present\nday, or until records cease to exist.\n\n3. Clarification of identity\nIf required for record matching, please note that the property may appear\nunder variations of:\nGreat House Farm\nTy Mawr\nLlandough (Penarth / Cardiff / Vale of Glamorgan)\n\n4. Form of response\nWhere possible, I would prefer:\nDigital copies (PDF or scanned documents)\nCopies of correspondence logs or account summaries\nIndex references to archived material if full copies cannot be provided\n\n5. Personal data request\nWhere personal data is involved, I understand this request may be processed\nas a Subject Access Request, and I consent to any reasonable identity\nverification required.\n\nThis request is made for historical and research purposes relating to\nproperty and family records.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ee6a35491d857a","subject":"FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"FOI: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-20T20:05:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ee6a35491d857a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ee6a2303d483b9-foi-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ee6a2303d483b9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ee6a35491d857a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/Ma'am,\n\nDid you receive a FOI from me recently?\nRef: Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nI don't see a suitable response.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ee000e6f3b9032","subject":"[NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","name":"[NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","date":"2026-06-19T13:10:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ee000e6f3b9032.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea148fc3e83020-nlw-english-subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-bute-estates-daniel-thomas","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea148fc3e83020","direction":"received","from":"National Library of Wales","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ee000e6f3b9032.json","textStatus":"available","text":"--# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n------------------\n\nRhydian Davies\n\nJun 19 2026, 02:10PM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your reply.The only specific reference that  appears in the Bute Estate Collection is for file D153/1-8.\n\nDeeds relating to premises in p. Llandough, co. Glam., comprising a dwelling house adjoining the churchyard, 1811 (D153/1-2), land (19 a.) for a brick and tile works at Cogan Pill, 1875 (D153/3) and land (33 a.), formerly part of Great House Farm, for the Llandough Limeworks (33 a.), 1876-1912 (D153/4-8). Plan engrossed on D153/3 (1875) and 4 (1876).\n\nTy Mawr is mentioned in the Llandough documents from within the collection, this could be translated to Large House or Great House, but this is only speculation\n\nD 219. Llandough manorial leases and agreements,\n \n\nThe deeds include leases of the farm of Cydfin Farm or Ty Mawr Farm, (107 a.), 1552-1824 (D219/1, 4-5, 8, et seq.), the tmt and lands called Upper Cogan Pill, with the fishery there, 1790 (D219/6), Llandough Farm (166 a.), 1824-32 (D219/9-13), Cogan Pill Farm (153 a.), 1824-8 (D219/14-17), Corners Well (107 a.), Lower Cogan Pill (24 a.) and Green Sayes (71 a.), 1824-6 (D219/18-20), and Cogan Farm (320 a.), 1824 (D219/21), all in p. llandough\n\n \n\nOtherwise you would be required to visit the Library to  search through the rental books and other documents that may be of interest to  locate any documentation relating  to Great House Farm\n\n \n\nIf you wish to have copies of the documents I have listed, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nRegards\n\nRhydian\n------------------\n\nRequester\n\nJun 13 2026, 03:25AM via Email\nMr Davies / Reading Rooms Team,\n\nThank you for your response and the guidance provided.\n\nI would be grateful if you could clarify, from your catalogue and holdings,\nwhich specific Bute Estate classmarks or reference numbers relate to:\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough\nWilliams family (John and Mary Williams) owner/ tenancy/occupation records\nGaps in Bute records for the property title (1850 - 1950)\nBuckler family association with the property\nAny associated estate maps, rent books, leases, or correspondence relating\nto the property\nAny relevant material in the Bute Estate collection connected to land\ntransactions affecting the site\n\nAt this stage I am not requesting copies or scans, but simply the specific\ncatalogue references / classmarks for relevant material held in your\ncollections.\n\nI'm in Argentina and unable to visit in person, so having the correct\nreferences will allow me to identify and prioritise any relevant material\nthrough your catalogue system.\n\nI'm here at the Welsh Settlement: Patagonia, looking to reconstruct a\nreplica of Great House Farm. Any assistance from my community back there\nwould be appreciated, as this is a massive undertaking.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant) ------------------\n\nRhydian Davies\n\nJun 12 2026, 10:36AM via System\n\nDear Requester\n\nThank you for your enquiry. At the Library we have the Bute Estate Records, to help you with your search I have included a link to the catalogue entry. You maybe able to identify what documents would be relevant to the property.\n\nhttps://archives.library.wales/index.php/bute-estate-records\n\nIf you wish to locate maps relating to the Bute Estate, you can locate the details through our main catalogue. To carry out this search,use the link provided below\n\nhttps://discover.library.wales/discovery/search?vid=44WHELF_NLW:44WHELF_NLW_NUI\n\nClick on Advanced Search, under 'Search Filters' you will see the word Title with a downward pointing arrow, click on this, from the drop screen menu  choose Classmark.\n\nType in Bute as you search term and click on the search button. A result page should show 290 results for you. \n\nAnother search you are able to carry out would be through the main catalogue again, but this time include 'Bute Estate' in the search box and then on the results page,you can choose map on the resource type filter which appears on the left hand side of the page.\n\nWe also produce a leaflet for 'Sources for the History of Houses' and have included a copy in the attachment.\n\nI hope the above information will prove helpful. If you wish to visit the Library or require any further assistance, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nRegards\n\n \n\nRhydian Davies\n\nSwyddog Ystafelloedd Darllen/Reading Rooms Officer\n\nRhif Ffon/Tel No [phone redacted]\n\nAttached Files\n\n-Sources_for_the_History_of_Houses.pdf <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4450175&type=0&key=a6341c1d39a4789d88d32de76913afb7>\n\n------------------\n\nCwestiwn gwreiddiol\n\nJun 07 2026, 09:54AM via Email\nSubject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)\n\nDear Enquiries,\n\nPlease search and advise on/provide access to: Bute Estate collections, maps, title references, family papers, or manuscripts relating to Great House Farm, Llandough; Daniel Thomas quarry deal/swap; John/Mary Williams occupation/ownership claims.\n\nFor generational land history and reparations research. Copies/fees welcome.\n\n\n\n\nRequester\n\n\n------------------\n\nSwyddog Ystafelloedd Darllen/Reading Rooms Officer Ffon/Tel [phone redacted] E-bost/E-mail [email redacted]\n\n\n\nThis email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9541987.\n\nRead our privacy policy. <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>"},{"id":"gm-19ecf7b0321e4086","subject":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","name":"Re: REVIEW of EOI ATISN 27021","date":"2026-06-16T08:10:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ecf7b0321e4086.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ecbf50d494e1ce-view-of-eoi-atisn-27021","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence