ontact us again.\n\nKind regards\nPlanning team\n\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk \nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk \n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook \nFollow us on Instagram / Dilynwch ni ar Instagram \nFollow us on LinkedIn / Dilynwch ni ar LinkedIn \n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DCFCA4.5288DED0]"},{"id":"gm-19ec7ff513ef0b99","subject":"Follow up","name":"Follow up","date":"2026-06-14T21:17:38Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ec7ff513ef0b99.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ec7fdd4aa96df1-follow-up","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ec7fdd4aa96df1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ec7ff513ef0b99.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Paul,\n\nI also just heard of your service and commitment to Llandough and the fact\nyour leaving. https://www.facebook.com/share/v/18qEQJC9B4/\n\nAnd with that, I appreciate your earlier email even more. And thank you\nagain.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ec73b2adf27745","subject":"Re: Great House Farm","name":"Re: Great House Farm","date":"2026-06-14T17:43:23Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ec73b2adf27745.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e3900c32c4c541-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e3900c32c4c541","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ec73b2adf27745.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Mr Egan,\n\nThank you for your response and for confirming that the Council's minute\nbooks from 1982 onwards were deposited with Glamorgan Archives in 2002.\n\nI note your reliance upon Section 21 FOIA in respect of records already\naccessible through Glamorgan Archives. I shall pursue those records\ndirectly with the archive.\n\nHowever, my request was not limited to council minutes. I also requested\ndisclosure of any correspondence, clerk's notes, memoranda, photographs,\nmaps, plans, committee papers, archived files or other records held by the\nCouncil concerning:\n\nTy Mawr (Great House Farm), Llandough;\nthe associated farm lands;\nthe Williams family;\nBilly Buckler, [member of the public] and members of the Buckler family;\nBP Properties Ltd v Buckler and related matters.\n\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if you could clarify:\n\nWhether the Council presently holds any records responsive to the above\nrequest other than the deposited minute books;\nIf such records exist, whether they remain in the Council's possession or\nwere transferred to another archive or repository;\nIf no such records are held, whether this is because they were never\ncreated, were transferred elsewhere, or were subsequently destroyed;\nWhether the Council retains any record of Billy Buckler addressing the\nCouncil, whether in minutes, correspondence, agenda papers, clerk's notes\nor any other form.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am content to receive a simple confirmation\nof whether such records are held and their location, rather than requiring\nthe Council to undertake extensive historical research.\n\nThank you for your assistance and I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester \nCyber & Electronic Warfare Professsional\nLife Member: Royal Corps of Signals\n\n\n\nOn Sun, 14 Jun 2026, 13:04 Paul Egan, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n> I have undertaken a reasonable search of our records and would advise you\n> as follows:\n>\n> a) The minutes of all council minutes for the period in question were\n> deposited in the Glamorgan Records Office in 2002. These cover the period\n> from 1982 when Llandough Community Council was first formed. Prior to that\n> time, the community of Llandough was included in the remit of Penarth Town\n> Council. The relevant web-link which shows the information held is :\n> perihttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/od\n>\n> b) You are able to visit the Glamorgan Records Office in Cardiff by\n> appointment and the web-link to find details of their location is:\n> https://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n>\n> Section 21 of the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) is an absolute\n> exemption that allows public authorities to refuse a request if the\n> requested information is already reasonably accessible to the applicant by\n> other means. This avoids duplicating effort and prevents authorities from\n> acting as personal research services.\n>\n> c) I would suggest that you access the Llandough Community Council's\n> website for historical information about the community of Llandough -\n> web-link is :\n>\n> https://www.llandough-cc.co.uk/Buildings_of_Significance_in_our_Community_25590.aspx\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n>\n> Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n>\n> [address removed]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> Telephone [phone redacted]\n>\n> Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> When you contact us\n>\n> The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\n> email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\n> to enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> information and/or access our facilities and services.\n>\n> Your personal information will be not shared or provided to any other\n> third party. Your information may however be published in the public domain\n> if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n>\n>\n>\n> For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website\n> www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our\n> identity' The Council will always strive to:\n>\n>  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n>\n> · Be accountable in all our council activities\n>\n> · Be responsive to the needs of the community\n>\n> · Encourage community participation\n>\n>\n> On 2026-05-18 04:12, Requester wrote:\n>\n> Mr Egan,\n>\n> Further to my previous correspondence, I understand that matters\n> concerning the property and family were discussed by Llandough Community\n> Council in or around 1988 and that my late father William \"Billy\" Buckler\n> addressed the Council.\n>\n> I am attempting to reconstruct the historical chain of occupation,\n> ownership, administration and public record concerning the property, family\n> and associated farm lands.\n>\n> https://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n>\n> Accordingly, I request disclosure of all records held by Llandough\n> Community Council, regardless of date, concerning:\n>\n>    - Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough;\n>    - the associated farm lands and any connected parcels;\n>    - the Williams family and successors in occupation;\n>    - Billy Buckler, [member of the public] and members of the Buckler family;\n>    - historical ownership, occupation, tenancy, possession, planning,\n>    access, acquisition, disposal, development, disputes or representations;\n>    - BP v Buckler and related matters;\n>    - any meetings in which Billy Buckler addressed the Council.\n>\n> This request includes, but is not limited to:\n>\n>    - minute books;\n>    - agendas;\n>    - correspondence;\n>    - maps;\n>    - plans;\n>    - asset registers;\n>    - committee papers;\n>    - land schedules;\n>    - photographs;\n>    - memoranda;\n>    - clerk notes;\n>    - archived files;\n>    - transferred records;\n>    - records held by third-party archives on the Council's behalf.\n>\n> If records predating the present Council are not held, please confirm:\n>\n>    1. Whether older records were transferred elsewhere;\n>    2. The archive location;\n>    3. Whether records were destroyed and under what retention policy;\n>    4. The earliest records held concerning the property.\n>\n> My understanding is that family occupation and acquisition history extends\n> substantially earlier, potentially to the seventeenth century, and I am\n> seeking to establish the documentary chain.\n>\n> I am confident that our claim to the fee simple absolute manorial title\n> still stands and no amount of time, fraud, purgergy, court \"mistakes\", gaps\n> in records, demolition of our home, erasure of history (like Marconi\n> staying with us while inventing radio), acts of terrorism, human rights\n> violations, lawfare, nor proceedural unfairness and supression or\n> witholding of information and possible murder of members of my family has\n> changed that fact. It appears our title was stolen and this is a position\n> grandmother held until 1982 when she conveniently died in the 2 week window\n> she had to challenge BP's registrstion of our land in their name with the\n> land registry.\n>\n> ITV also recently declassified and published coverage too:\n>\n> https://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n>\n> This is a terrorist/ hostage situation so far as I see. My dispossessed\n> family are your hostages not constituents. They are too frightened to even\n> speak up about this matter. I require of your department some effort to\n> revisit your postion.\n>\n> My research tells me that the councillor at the time said, prior to my\n> father's death, that the situation with BP would result in a death. I\n> believe that was concerning the conflict with Bailiffs, Police and possibly\n> SAS.\n>\n> I have submitted a FOI to the MOD too. The Ministry of Justice are also on\n> notice and imply this matter is being investigated.\n>\n> If not me, who? If not now, when?\n>\n> My address is [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted].\n> If you care to visit or write or deliver items, please do so to that\n> address.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n>\n> Requester Esq. \n>\n> On Thu, 20 Nov 2025, 05:42 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Paul,\n>\n> I understand.\n> Thanks for your reply nevertheless.\n>\n> Requester\n> [phone redacted]\n>\n> On Thu, 20 Nov 2025, 04:40 Paul Egan, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n>\n> Hi Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> I regret to inform you that we are unable to assist with the matter you\n> raise.\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Paul\n>\n>\n>\n> Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n>\n> Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n>\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> [address removed]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n> Telephone [phone redacted]\n>\n> Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> When you contact us\n>\n> The information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\n> email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored to\n> enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\n> information and/or access our facilities and services. Your personal\n> information will be not shared or provided to any other third party. Your\n> information may however be published in the public domain if you require\n> the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n>\n>\n>\n> For further information please see our full privacy notice on our website\n> www.llandough-cc.co.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving our\n> identity' The Council will always strive to:\n>\n>  ·  *Be open and accessible in all our decision making*\n>\n> · *Be accountable in all our council activities*\n>\n> · *Be responsive to the needs of the community*\n>\n> · *Encourage community participation*\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 14 November 2025 12:49\n> *To:* [email redacted]\n> *Subject:* BP vs Buckler\n>\n>\n>\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\n> assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\n> Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> My family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for\n> generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of\n> our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply affected.\n> Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\n> inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\n> corporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\n> considerations relating to the site.\n>\n> I have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\n> requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\n> historical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\n> historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n>\n> My interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\n> significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\n> stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\n> this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n>\n> By way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\n> Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\n> simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\n> would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n> *Requester*\n> [address redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [location redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> [postcode redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ec6e0894a49c27","subject":"Re: Great House Farm","name":"Re: Great House Farm","date":"2026-06-14T16:04:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ec6e0894a49c27.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e3900c32c4c541-great-house-farm","scopeTopics":["llandough"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["llandough"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e3900c32c4c541","direction":"received","from":"Paul Egan","institutions":[{"id":"llandough","name":"Llandough Community Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ec6e0894a49c27.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nI have undertaken a reasonable search of our records and would advise \nyou as follows:\n\na) The minutes of all council minutes for the period in question were \ndeposited in the Glamorgan Records Office in 2002. These cover the \nperiod from 1982 when Llandough Community Council was first formed. \nPrior to that time, the community of Llandough was included in the remit \nof Penarth Town Council. The relevant web-link which shows the \ninformation held is : perihttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/od\n\nb) You are able to visit the Glamorgan Records Office in Cardiff by \nappointment and the web-link to find details of their location is: \nhttps://glamarchives.gov.uk/\n\nSection 21 of the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) is an absolute \nexemption that allows public authorities to refuse a request if the \nrequested information is already reasonably accessible to the applicant \nby other means. This avoids duplicating effort and prevents authorities \nfrom acting as personal research services.\n\nc) I would suggest that you access the Llandough Community Council's \nwebsite for historical information about the community of Llandough - \nweb-link is :\n\nhttps://www.llandough-cc.co.uk/Buildings_of_Significance_in_our_Community_25590.aspx\n\nKind regards,\n\nPaul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n\nClerk to Llandough Community Council,\n\n[address removed]\n\nVale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n\nTelephone [phone redacted]\n\nWebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [4]\n\nWhen you contact us\n\nThe information you provide (personal information such as name, address,\nemail address, phone number, organisation) will be processed and stored\nto enable us to contact you and respond to your correspondence, provide\ninformation and/or access our facilities and services.\n\nYour personal information will be not shared or provided to any other \nthird party. Your information may however be published in the public \ndomain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n\nFor further information please see our full privacy notice on our \nwebsite www.llandough-cc.co.uk [4]\n\nThe Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \nour identity' The Council will always strive to:\n\n  ·  Be open and accessible in all our decision making\n\n· Be accountable in all our council activities\n\n· Be responsive to the needs of the community\n\n· Encourage community participation\n\nOn 2026-05-18 04:12, Requester wrote:\n\n> Mr Egan,\n> \n> Further to my previous correspondence, I understand that matters \n> concerning the property and family were discussed by Llandough \n> Community Council in or around 1988 and that my late father William \n> \"Billy\" Buckler addressed the Council.\n> \n> I am attempting to reconstruct the historical chain of occupation, \n> ownership, administration and public record concerning the property, \n> family and associated farm lands.\n> \n> https://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n> \n> Accordingly, I request disclosure of all records held by Llandough \n> Community Council, regardless of date, concerning:\n> \n> * Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough;\n> * the associated farm lands and any connected parcels;\n> * the Williams family and successors in occupation;\n> * Billy Buckler, [member of the public] and members of the Buckler family;\n> * historical ownership, occupation, tenancy, possession, planning, \n> access, acquisition, disposal, development, disputes or \n> representations;\n> * BP v Buckler and related matters;\n> * any meetings in which Billy Buckler addressed the Council.\n> \n> This request includes, but is not limited to:\n> \n> * minute books;\n> * agendas;\n> * correspondence;\n> * maps;\n> * plans;\n> * asset registers;\n> * committee papers;\n> * land schedules;\n> * photographs;\n> * memoranda;\n> * clerk notes;\n> * archived files;\n> * transferred records;\n> * records held by third-party archives on the Council's behalf.\n> \n> If records predating the present Council are not held, please confirm:\n> \n> * Whether older records were transferred elsewhere;\n> * The archive location;\n> * Whether records were destroyed and under what retention policy;\n> * The earliest records held concerning the property.\n> \n> My understanding is that family occupation and acquisition history \n> extends substantially earlier, potentially to the seventeenth century, \n> and I am seeking to establish the documentary chain.\n> \n> I am confident that our claim to the fee simple absolute manorial title \n> still stands and no amount of time, fraud, purgergy, court \"mistakes\", \n> gaps in records, demolition of our home, erasure of history (like \n> Marconi staying with us while inventing radio), acts of terrorism, \n> human rights violations, lawfare, nor proceedural unfairness and \n> supression or witholding of information and possible murder of members \n> of my family has changed that fact. It appears our title was stolen and \n> this is a position grandmother held until 1982 when she conveniently \n> died in the 2 week window she had to challenge BP's registrstion of our \n> land in their name with the land registry.\n> \n> ITV also recently declassified and published coverage too:\n> \n> https://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n> \n> This is a terrorist/ hostage situation so far as I see. My dispossessed \n> family are your hostages not constituents. They are too frightened to \n> even speak up about this matter. I require of your department some \n> effort to revisit your postion.\n> \n> My research tells me that the councillor at the time said, prior to my \n> father's death, that the situation with BP would result in a death. I \n> believe that was concerning the conflict with Bailiffs, Police and \n> possibly SAS.\n> \n> I have submitted a FOI to the MOD too. The Ministry of Justice are also \n> on notice and imply this matter is being investigated.\n> \n> If not me, who? If not now, when?\n> \n> My address is [address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan, [postcode redacted]. \n> If you care to visit or write or deliver items, please do so to that \n> address.\n> \n> Kind regards,\n> \n> Requester Esq. \n> \n> On Thu, 20 Nov 2025, 05:42 Requester, <[email redacted]> \n> wrote:\n> Paul,\n> \n> I understand.\n> Thanks for your reply nevertheless.\n> \n> Requester\n> [phone redacted]\n> \n> On Thu, 20 Nov 2025, 04:40 Paul Egan, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n> \n> Hi Requester,\n> \n> I regret to inform you that we are unable to assist with the matter you \n> raise.\n> \n> Regards,\n> \n> Paul\n> \n> Paul R. Egan BA, Chartered MCIPD, CiLCA, F. Inst. LM, FIPSM\n> \n> Clerk to Llandough Community Council,\n> \n> [address removed]\n> \n> Vale of Glamorgan [postcode redacted]\n> \n> Telephone [phone redacted]\n> \n> Website www.llandough-cc.co.uk [2]\n> \n> When you contact us\n> \n> The information you provide (personal information such as name, \n> address, email address, phone number, organisation) will be processed \n> and stored to enable us to contact you and respond to your \n> correspondence, provide information and/or access our facilities and \n> services. Your personal information will be not shared or provided to \n> any other third party. Your information may however be published in the \n> public domain if you require the Council to discuss the matter raised.\n> \n> For further information please see our full privacy notice on our \n> website www.llandough-cc.co.uk [2]\n> \n> The Council's mission statement is 'Serving our community, preserving \n> our identity' The Council will always strive to:\n> \n> ·  _Be open and accessible in all our decision making_\n> \n> · _Be accountable in all our council activities_\n> \n> · _Be responsive to the needs of the community_\n> \n> · _Encourage community participation_\n> \n> From: Requester <[email redacted]>\n> Sent: 14 November 2025 12:49\n> To: [email redacted]\n> Subject: BP vs Buckler\n> \n> Sir/Ma'am,\n> \n> I am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request \n> your assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my \n> family: _BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987)_, relating to Great House \n> Farm, Llandough.\n> \n> My family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for \n> generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss \n> of our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply \n> affected. Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant \n> procedural inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered \n> questions regarding corporate identity, unverified service of key \n> documents, and heritage considerations relating to the site.\n> \n> I have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am \n> requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies--legal, \n> historical, or governmental--who may be able to independently review \n> the historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n> \n> My interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage \n> significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo \n> Marconi stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I \n> believe this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n> \n> By way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed \n> Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is \n> simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I \n> would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n> \n> Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your \n> response.\n> \n> Yours sincerely,\n> \n> Requester\n> [address redacted] [3]\n> [location redacted] [3]\n> [postcode redacted] [3]\n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n\n\nLinks:\n------\n[1] \n[map link redacted]\n[2] http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk/\n[3] \n[map link redacted]\n[4] http://www.llandough-cc.co.uk"},{"id":"gm-19ec1b189ca60ba8","subject":"Re: Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-06-13T15:54:57Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ec1b189ca60ba8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ebb2140ec50bbf-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ebb2140ec50bbf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ec1b189ca60ba8.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks.\n\nIs this Helen Huggins using Helen Huggins email?\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester \n\nLife Member of Royal Corps of Signals\n\nOn Fri, 12 Jun 2026, 06:19 Huggins, Helen,  \nwrote:\n\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your emails, requesting information on the above mentioned\n> site. I can confirm, I have done a search on the site and the two\n> applications that may be of relevance, for the information you are seeking\n> are noted below.  Please be advised that this information is available via\n> our online planning register\n>   and\n> maps\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> I trust this is of assistance, however, if you require anything further,\n> please do not hesitate to contact us again.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n> Planning team\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you\n> really need to.*\n>\n> *Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod\n> gwir angen.*\n>\n>\n>\n> Visit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n>\n> Ewch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n>  \n>\n> Follow us on Instagram / Dilynwch ni ar Instagram\n>  \n>\n> Follow us on LinkedIn / Dilynwch ni ar LinkedIn\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>  \n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ebecbc88416257","subject":"Re: [NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","name":"Re: [NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","date":"2026-06-13T02:24:46Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ebecbc88416257.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea148fc3e83020-nlw-english-subject-research-enquiry-great-house-farm-llandough-williams-buckler-bute-estates-daniel-thomas","scopeTopics":["nlw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["nlw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea148fc3e83020","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"nlw","name":"National Library of Wales"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ebecbc88416257.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Mr Davies / Reading Rooms Team,\n\nThank you for your response and the guidance provided.\n\nI would be grateful if you could clarify, from your catalogue and holdings,\nwhich specific Bute Estate classmarks or reference numbers relate to:\n\nGreat House Farm, Llandough\nWilliams family (John and Mary Williams) owner/ tenancy/occupation records\nGaps in Bute records for the property title (1850 - 1950)\nBuckler family association with the property\nAny associated estate maps, rent books, leases, or correspondence relating\nto the property\nAny relevant material in the Bute Estate collection connected to land\ntransactions affecting the site\n\nAt this stage I am not requesting copies or scans, but simply the specific\ncatalogue references / classmarks for relevant material held in your\ncollections.\n\nI'm in Argentina and unable to visit in person, so having the correct\nreferences will allow me to identify and prioritise any relevant material\nthrough your catalogue system.\n\nI'm here at the Welsh Settlement: Patagonia, looking to reconstruct a\nreplica of Great House Farm. Any assistance from my community back there\nwould be appreciated, as this is a massive undertaking.\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester (Ret'd Sergenant)\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, 12 Jun 2026, 06:36 National Library of Wales, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> --# Teipiwch eich ateb uwchben y llinell hon #--\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Rhydian Davies\n>\n> Jun 12 2026, 10:36AM via System\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. At the Library we have the Bute Estate\n> Records, to help you with your search I have included a link to the\n> catalogue entry. You maybe able to identify what documents would be\n> relevant to the property.\n>\n> https://archives.library.wales/index.php/bute-estate-records\n>\n> If you wish to locate maps relating to the Bute Estate, you can locate the\n> details through our main catalogue. To carry out this search,use the link\n> provided below\n>\n>\n> https://discover.library.wales/discovery/search?vid=44WHELF_NLW:44WHELF_NLW_NUI\n>\n> Click on Advanced Search, under 'Search Filters' you will see the word\n> Title with a downward pointing arrow, click on this, from the drop screen\n> menu  choose Classmark.\n>\n> Type in Bute as you search term and click on the search button. A result\n> page should show 290 results for you.\n>\n> Another search you are able to carry out would be through the main\n> catalogue again, but this time include 'Bute Estate' in the search box and\n> then on the results page,you can choose map on the resource type filter\n> which appears on the left hand side of the page.\n>\n> We also produce a leaflet for 'Sources for the History of Houses' and have\n> included a copy in the attachment.\n>\n> I hope the above information will prove helpful. If you wish to visit the\n> Library or require any further assistance, please do not hesitate to\n> contact me.\n>\n> Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Rhydian Davies\n>\n> Swyddog Ystafelloedd Darllen/Reading Rooms Officer\n>\n> Rhif Ffon/Tel No [phone redacted]\n>\n> Attached Files\n>\n>    - Sources_for_the_History_of_Houses.pdf\n>    <https://national-library-wales.libanswers.com/loaderTicket?fid=4450175&type=0&key=a6341c1d39a4789d88d32de76913afb7>\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Cwestiwn gwreiddiol\n>\n> Jun 07 2026, 09:54AM via Email\n> Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler,\n> Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)\n>\n> Dear Enquiries,\n>\n> Please search and advise on/provide access to: Bute Estate collections,\n> maps, title references, family papers, or manuscripts relating to Great\n> House Farm, Llandough; Daniel Thomas quarry deal/swap; John/Mary Williams\n> occupation/ownership claims.\n>\n> For generational land history and reparations research. Copies/fees\n> welcome.\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> ------------------------------\n>\n> Swyddog Ystafelloedd Darllen/Reading Rooms Officer Ffon/Tel [phone redacted]\n> E-bost/E-mail [email redacted]\n>\n>\n> This email is sent from LibAnswers in relationship to ticket #9541987.\n>\n> Read our privacy policy.\n> <https://springshare.com/privacy.html>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ebdfdb031db09a","subject":"Automatic reply: Automatic reply: Great House Farm, Llandough (now Church View Close)","name":"Automatic reply: Automa