bsurd or nonsense.\nBut I say in advance, I'm a former military cyber and electronic warfare\nprofessional, I left my career in the Royal Signals with full honours. I've\ncompleted 22 years in Oath, I'm bona fide. And my last employer in 2024 was\nthe Welsh Government/ Vale of Glamorgan Council. Via the direct payment\nadult care scheme. It's not UFO's or aliens. Although my military records\nwill confirm I did do an attachment at the undeground UFO city in Coresham.\nOn the official secrets act. But it wasn't as exiting or interesting as\nthat sounds. I was just routine circuits and managing cryptography to\nWhitehall.\nI write to you because I would like the conditions to be more favourable so\nthat I might actually get to enjoy my home there, as your constituent. I\ntry and try and try to speak to MP's and I've been ignored for decades. In\n2007 when I came out of uniform I could go an have a cup of tea with John\nSmith and talk. He ripped me off and all the soldiers I employed in my\nfirst company, saying that the £14Billion project at St Athan would happen\nand we should all buy houses there. Mine was 40 Lombard Street. Not only\nwas all that \"Biggest single investment in Wales\" a sham. But my morgage\ncompany (Manchester Building Society) didn't honour a payment holiday, made\nme repay it as an arrears. Which I did. Then demanded £3.5k for admin for\nletters they sent. I offered £2k. They they wired back my payment for\narrears, took possession of my house, billed me for the auction shortfall\nmany multiple times the \"arrears\" I'd already paid. Then tried to place\nthat as a lien on my nans house, who wasn't even a guarantor. I still don't\nhave my house back. But the omnibusman did side with me/ my family. I want\nmy house back! Also there's no record of me ever even having owned it. But\nI did 2006 - 2012.\nMy grandad Ray Smith, Chief Superintendent Gordon Spikings in the TV series\nDempsey and Makepeace, bought the house we have there in Dinas Powys, after\nfilming in the Exodus movie with Paul Newman, so I'm told. Again I'd love\nto be there at our house, but things just get more insane.\nMy 36 day old boy was then abducted in 2013, from Stockeld Park in Leeds. I\nwas then forced into exile until 2022 after reporting video evidence I\nobtained of rituals being performed on him, which resulted in 3 lots of\npolice, 5 military and a helicopter being sent to try kidnapping and\nsilencing me. I escaped/ evaded as I'm a military warfare professional and\nalso no charges or warrants existed.  I have since had no choice but to\nconsidered myself a counter officer in a literal civil war waged on me and\nus. My sons whereabouts or status still unknown, is he even still alive? ..\nif so he has been kept from me and my family since his abduction. It's\ngoing on 13 years and its inhumane. ECHR also won't reply. My former MP\nwouldn't even sign the EDM for father's to have rights in 2014.\nSo I remarried and started a new family. I literally gave up fighting the\ndemonic realm you call UK, after about 8 years of the state sponsored\neffort to cover that up.  Nobody, to this day: year 13, has provided me\nwith the only answer I have asked since my 36 day old boys abduction from\nmy former home in Stockeld Park Leeds in 2013: How and where is my son? All\nthe ownus is placed on me to pay for a blood test, pay lawyers, pay this\nand that. If alive, my son is abducted and held hostage. I'm not paying his\nabductors or abusers or the regime holding him hostage or forcing him\nfatherless when he's not. The decade+ long campaign to frame, criminalise,\ndiscredit, kidnap, silence, ostracise, alienate, ignore me on this matter\nis abhorrent. It's a depth of evil beyond anything else I've known. Was he\nmurdered? What happened after he was abducted? It is the most insane\nsituation how all that has happened since he was taken was just campaign\nafter campaign to kidnap and silence me. The other witness at my home that\nday. Another soldier I served with, who brought his infant daughter to meet\nmine, hasn't even ever been asked for a statement.\nAfter exhonoration, a clear DBS and returning from exile and New York in\n2022; to care for my nan (who was on end of life due to vaccines, with no\ncarers able to sufficiently reach Monknash from Barry) I was expected to\nsleep in a tent for a year, which I did, after not being able to afford\nhousing abroad and in UK too,  at such short notice of return. All the\nwhile 97 Afghans were being secrely housed outside our 11 home village up\nthe road in St Athan airbase. And given tens of times more tax I was\nexpected to pay per year, to help them get started.\nOne afghan was in the garden where my ill grandmother lay dying from\nvsccine poisoning while one afghan was in the garden trying to steal my\ndog. I reported and complained. Like with my housing denial of asistant\ncomplaint. And both were ignored or fobbed off. I already keep my daughter\noff that island, after Southport and other incidents. But I also have\nexported my dog off that small (formerly pale) island too, to my wife and\ndaughter at our place in the Caribbean. Which was another huge scandal of\nextortion and racketeering which I again reported to my MP and nothing\nhappened.\nI also raised concerns arms or illegals might have been being smuggled into\nMonknash beach. Our families former livery yard there since 2009, received\nan abrupt termination of our lease and we had to move. After a lot of\nsuspicious activity at the beach car park and beach we controlled there.\nWhich I have on CCTV and my axon bodycam recordings. So I say again, I\nwould like to exist on my ancestral birthland as an indigenous Briton. With\nmy young family. But I find it untenable and have to fly in and out like\nits an active war zone there. To keep myself and my family safe.\nAnd in all instances it appears to be the British State waging civil war on\nus. I was shot at one time before while I was back, on the top road of\nBarry. Driving between my grandparents former house in Dinas Powys and my\nnan at my mums former place in Monknash. The craziness just doesn't end. I\ndared to have a McDonald's too and they racketeer there too, charging for\nbags after you make your order and drive forward. When they either need to\nbe provided for free or you need to at least be asked. When I safely make\nit back abroad and off that lawless island, which involved me building\nmyself my own man-portable ocean pack packraft as a contingency to get my\ndog out too, after legal export attempts were unlawfully hindered last\nminute (like with the notary in Milton Keynes) I have to spend weeks even\nmonths clawing back money I get scammed out of.\nBy things like my former car insurance company in Bristol, or the airline\nchanging my flight last minute and charging me hundreds extra falsy saying\nI requested the change and if I didn't like it I would need to cancel. I\nspent months going through their regulators in Europe to get that back.\nIt's a perilous experience for me in Britain. It's literally like another\ntour of the middle east to get in and out unscathed. And takes too long to\nbe made whole after making it safely off those shores and open borders,\nexcept to the boxed in, kill boxed Britons trying to exit  with our pets,\nmoney, children and businesses.\nI have no doubt you're busy, but I do require your consideration on all of\nthe above. But more importantly possible fraud, concealment, and even\nmilitary action I might have discovered, used against my family, to\nbrutally dispossess us of our former 800 year old home in Llandough back in\n1988—a home we owned and occupied since 1667.\nI enclose the ECHR but also my criticism of it in a separate PDF. I am\nstill research this case and the scandals don't end. I just unearthing more\nand more and its looking very damning for both the UK Govenrment and BP.\nI was a child in this 1988 battlefield and warzone. I was inside the house\nwhen poleaxes hacked our windows and BP bailiffs began demolishing our\n800-year-old home while we and our pregnant mother were still inside.\nI am now 41 years old. I have studied this case and collected evidence for\n20 years, alongside my military career in cyber and electronic warfare. I\nam now a life member of the Royal Signals and left my career with full\nhonors. I also completed the last of my 22 years of service under oath,\nemployed under the Vale Council and Welsh Government in 2024 within adult\ncare. I am bona fide. This followed eight years in exile on a Caribbean\nisland between those two periods of employment, after I exposed another\nmajor scandal in Yorkshire in 2013.\nI am now working to formally collect and present evidence. I am very\ndisappointed by the gatekeeping, lies, obstruction, and continued\nwithholding of information from various departments like Cadw, the National\nArchives, and the Vale Council. Furthermore, regarding the information I\nhave received, I am horrified by the gaps in records, peculiar\ncircumstances, missing information, and the general inaccessibility of\npublic records.\nI am just trying to understand what happened here; I require the whole\ntruth. I will put the evidence in chronological order on a website that\ncannot be taken offline, censored, or removed. The source code will be\nbacked up to a 1,000-year film in a Scandinavian mine as part of GitHub’s\nArctic Code Vault program. With this clear reconstruction of the evidence\nand story, I can also seek legal adjudication and remedy.\nWe maintain our absolute claim to the land, which was passed from my\ngrandmother to my father, and then to me and my expanding family. As you\nare well aware, fraud and concealment unravel everything, which I suspect\nthey will in this case.\nIf you could instruct all parties to be more forthcoming with records held\non me, my family, and our former family home since 1667, we would be most\ngrateful.\nThus far, I see a clear miscarriage of justice, court mistakes, and\nprocedural unfairness. BP and the British Government/United Kingdom were\nsynonymous in 1987 too, as part of that £7 billion deal.\nI believe this case involving my family may have been part of a larger\nnationwide campaign that likely happened to many other families.\nFurthermore, having recently worked closely with law firms in London on the\nPCP car finance scandal, I see a parallel in this matter, with my family's\ncase serving as a catalyst.\nFrom what I can gather so far from the information and family testimony I\nhave (including five aunties, my dad, an uncle, my mum, and cousins), my\nworking theory is that my grandad, Frederick Buckler, pawned his wife's (my\nnan, Mrs. Williams) virtual freehold to the surrounding farmland. However,\nthe house, garden, and immediate land may have been a separate plot to\nwhich we did obtain absolute title from Bute following a quarrying deal,\nwhich granted permission for quarrying/limeworks in exchange for that title.\nThat title was later stolen from our house. I have the criminal's name, and\nI suspect there is a police record of him. There were numerous court\nhearings where Mary won, but she was later unable to present the title\n(though its prior existence was not denied). The copy from the public\nlibrary was gone too. My mum's testimony states she went back to retrieve\nthe index card almost immediately afterward, but that had been taken as\nwell. Consequently, the dispossession escalated, with BP registering our\nland in their names at the Land Registry in 1983. This was entirely based\non the office being willfully ignorant (I am currently in talks with them)\nand BP withholding information.\nAdditionally, my grandmother’s convenient death occurred within the\ntwo-week window she would have had to challenge BP merging her stolen title\ninto their surrounding land title. Later, in 1987 (the landmark case *BP\nvs. Buckler*, 1987), the judge is quoted as saying my nan \"conceived the\nnotion\" she owned it. He claimed that had she challenged BP's license\nletters, the outcome would have been different. Yet, she is well-documented\nas challenging the BP Pension Trust in the press, via a petition with 1,100\nsignatures, and in the 1975 conveyance. The judge then claimed that even if\nshe challenged them, it would not count because the plaintiff was BP\nProperties, not the BP Pension Trust, asserting they were two separate\ncompanies. Thus, BP won possession.\nHowever, no court has ever ruled against our claim of ownership, and we\nhave never willingly surrendered it. No court has ever ruled that BP owns\nit. When my dad appealed that ruling, arguing that the BP Pension Trust\nshould have been the plaintiff, the same judge dismissed his appeal by\nstating that BP Pension and BP Properties were effectively the same\ncompany. It was a \"heads they win, tails we lose\" scenario.\nI believe the possession of our surrounding farmland is dubious and highly\narguable. I recognize that my grandmother, a disabled widow and pensioner,\ndid not have it in her to single-handedly defend everything against three\nBP companies, their predecessor Western Ground Rents (whom Parliament even\nnoted on the record as crooks), and the bias of its shareholder, the\nBritish Government.\nBut the possession of our home and garden is an outright outrage—not just\ndue to the human rights violations and the possible use of the military\nafter Thatcher told the Land Registry to look the other way, as Cadw and\nmany others appear to have done. The press also labeled us squatters and\nsuppressed reports. I only recently obtained the ITV report from 1988,\nwhich—even if not actively suppressed for over three decades—fails to\nmention that my mum was pregnant with three toddlers when her shoulder was\ndislocated while serving the invaders a writ after the siege.\nOur home and garden were evidently a separate plot. In the worst-case\nscenario, we should have been granted an easement or thoroughfare across\nthe surrounding land to access our home and garden. Instead, we faced\nfraud, concealment, procedural unfairness, court \"mistakes,\" and willful\nignorance—such as the Land Registry looking at the 1974 land dispute case\nto verify BP's claim without acknowledging that our land was actively in\ndispute.\nFurthermore, the Land Registry claims the 1987 ruling justifies their\nactions in 1983, yet the 1987 ruling relies on their actions from 1983. The\n1987 ruling is also retrospective in how it validates the invalid license\nletters from 1974. The only class in this entire act came from my disabled,\nwidow-pensioner grandmother, and my terminally ill dad before his\nconveniently timed death following his dismissed appeal, demolished home,\ndetention without charge, violated human rights (being ripped from his\nhospital bed), and blocked ECHR access.\nWill you take this on? Will you instruct the Senedd to launch a public\ninquiry into this?\nI am speaking through a immense amount of trauma to report this to you. We\nhave never received any counseling or reparations following these events.\nMy family has not dared to speak up or out because they remain terrorized.\nMy younger sister, now 40 years old, had nightmares earlier this year when\nI brought it up with her. My mum and aunties experience meltdowns and\nshutdowns whenever I try to discuss it with them.\nIf the SAS was deployed against my family in 1988 and we had known, I might\nnot have chosen to play a part in rescuing those two SAS soldiers from an\nIraqi prison and execution in 2005—an operation I believe I was deeply\ninvolved in, if not instrumental to.\nRight now, it feels as though my family is being held hostage. The 20\nhouses built on our land could be construed as accommodation for an\noccupying network. Consider the fact that this land is Wales's largest and\nmost significant burial site, home to a Roman villa and a monastery, the\nplace where Marconi stayed with us while inventing the radio, and where\nPeerless Jim fought his first fight in our barn. The fact that none of this\nis marked with so much as a park bench plaque above ground only affirms\nwhat I am saying.\nIn the National Eisteddfod, we have a ceremony where a sword is withdrawn\nthree times, and each time the crowd is asked, \"Is there peace?\" If the\ncrowd answers yes, the sword is resheathed. As a certified, experienced\nmilitary commander and warfare professional, I believe it is asked three\ntimes so you can look into the eyes of the people to see if they are\nanswering under duress, such as at gunpoint.\nInterestingly, that ceremony now feels hijacked and insincere, as people\nare being attacked in Britain, yet the crowd still declares peace. In WWII,\nthe ceremony was canceled during air raids and bombings because crowds\ncould not sincerely say there was peace.\nI am Welsh—an indigenous, white Welsh Christian national. When I visit my\nfamily and see them suffer meltdowns or nightmares just discussing this\ncase, I know there is no peace. My sword, metaphorically speaking, is not\nbeing resheathed. This is not to say I am going to hijack a BP fuel truck\nand drive it in flames into the properties on our land; I am bona fide and\noperate with honor. But I am certainly not standing for this situation.\nNothing could be done about this for the last few decades, nor during the\n20 years I have spent collecting evidence to understand it. But two things\nhave changed: I discovered extensive evidence of fraud and concealment, and\nwe are now in the age of recursive, self-improving AI—and I am a cyber and\nelectronic warfare professional.\nI do not even have to depend solely on traditional methods anymore. Last\nweek, my system of AI tools discovered a social media comment from many\nyears ago mentioning a photo of our farm inside the disabled toilet of a\npub. I sent someone there, and low and behold, it was still on the wall: a\nclear aerial image of the Roman villa remains, taken between the demolition\nof our home and the construction of the 20 houses.\nI believe that with proper cooperation, I can reconstruct the timeline of\nthis story with all supporting evidence for the public record. While the\nBritish state continues to erase and suppress our place in\nhistory—including Marconi, Peerless Jim, the Roman villa (possibly where\nMagnus Maximus once resided), and the monastery beneath it—the Welsh\nsettlement here in Argentina actively celebrates Welsh culture and history.\nThis is why I intend to build an augmented reality tour guide for\nLlandough, Wales. I am confident I can regularly get boots on the ground\nthere to see what once stood, despite the current lack of physical\ninformation. I have at least 50 personnel back home invested in my business\nwho would love to support this. I am also intent on forming a *Colonia\nLlandough* or *New Llandough* here, with an exact replica of Great House\nFarm at its center, alongside a potential Netflix documentary to tell the\nstory right.\nIt is vital to me and the public that this story be told accurately while\nthe previous generation of my family is still alive to participate.\nRegards,\nRequester \n\nLife Member: Royal Corps of Signals\nOBO Williams/Buckler Estate (Est. 1667)\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz"},{"id":"gm-19ebb30b74546fa8","subject":"[NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","name":"[NLW English] Subject: Research Enquiry - Great House Farm, Llandough (Williams/Buckler, Bute Estates, Daniel Thomas)","date":"2026-06-12T09:36:31Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ebb30b74546fa8.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea148fc3e83020-nlw-english-subject-research-enquiry-great-ho