terest.\n  5.  Any records discussing the age, architectural significance, archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n  6.  Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n  7.  Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or representations seeking preservation of the building.\n  8.  Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nYou will receive a response by 25 June 2026. If you have any queries about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future correspondence (ATISN 27021).\n\nThe request you sent me contains personal information about you - for example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your personal information and all other information relating to your request for three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your personal information will then be disposed of securely.\n\nUnder data protection legislation, you have the right:\n\n\n  *   to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access it\n  *   to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\n  *   to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\n  *   for (in certain circumstances) your data to be ‘erased’\n  *   to (in certain circumstances) data portability\n  *   to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\n\nFor further information about the information which the Welsh Government holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR, please see contact details below:\n\nData Protection Officer\nWelsh Government\nCathays Park\nCARDIFF\n[postcode redacted]\nEmail: [email redacted] \n\nThe contact details for the Information Commissioner’s Office are:\n\nWycliffe House\nWater Lane\nWilmslow\nCheshire\n[postcode redacted]\nWebsite: www.ico.org.uk \n\nAny information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh Government’s Disclosure Log (at https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en).\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nMike Weatherhead\n\nArweinydd Tîm Gwaith Achosion / Casework Team Leader\nPolisi a Gwarchod / Policy and Protection\nArolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment Inspectorate\nCadw\n\nFrom: Requester  >\nSent: 28 May 2026 06:29\nTo: Freedom of Information Officer  >; Listed Buildings / Adeiladau Rhestredig  >\nSubject: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n\nDear Freedom of Information Officer,\n\nI am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw concerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\n\nI request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\n\n  1.  Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n  2.  Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or reports concerning the building.\n  3.  Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or protection of the property.\n  4.  Any records explaining why the building was not added to the statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n  5.  Any records discussing the age, architectural significance, archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n  6.  Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n  7.  Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or representations seeking preservation of the building.\n  8.  Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than an explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\n\nIf any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I would be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the records.\n\nI would prefer the information in electronic form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester Esq. . Heir & Successors of Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Llandough\n\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<”https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy”> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice  explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (3)\n- Doc 1. 1988-07-29 - Great House Farmhouse, Llandough - survey photo.pdf (application/pdf, 232 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-06-11_welsh-government_atisn-27021_doc1-1988-07-29-farmhouse-survey-photo.pdf\n- Doc 2. 1988-07-29 - Barn at Great House Farmhouse, Llandough - survey photo.pdf (application/pdf, 240 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-06-11_welsh-government_atisn-27021_doc2-1988-07-29-barn-survey-photo.pdf\n- ATISN 27021 - 2026-06-11 - Response Letter.pdf (application/pdf, 117 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-06-11_welsh-government_atisn-27021_response-letter.pdf"},{"id":"gm-19eb75ec2e0a1cdc","subject":"RE: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","name":"RE: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-06-11T15:48:19Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19eb75ec2e0a1cdc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-tenancy-records-f","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19eb75ec2e0a1cdc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"2026 / 2475, 2482, 2503\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nThank you for your emails received 5-8 June.\n\nLlandough came under Cardiff Rural District Council, 1875-1974. The plans held here have been listed and are available to search on our catalogue . There are no plans listed for Great House Farm. After this date the area come under Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council. Although some records are held for the council (catalogue available here: DCVG ) these do not include plans. No plans have been deposited by either Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council or its successor authority Vale of Glamorgan County Borough Council. We suggest that you contact them directly: planning@valeofglamorgan. gov.uk .\n\nCorrespondence received from the farm may have been reported during committee meetings: Vale of Glamorgan County Borough Council can be viewed online: CVG , and Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council: DCVG .\n\nWe do not hold any records of BP Properties Ltd or BP Pension Trust. The BP Archive (1840-2001) is held at Warwick University, and can be contacted: [email redacted] \n\nA catalogue to the Bute Estate records held here can be searched: DB .\n\nTithe maps can be searched online: Tithe Maps of Wales - Home .\n\nRate valuation books, 1956-1992 are here: DCVG/T/1 \n\nThere is a small Western Ground Rents Ltd Collection, consisting of three volumes, c1938-1944: D696 . However, a search of our catalogue for ‘Western Ground Rents’ will help you to locate records throughout our collections, searching for ‘Western Ground Rents AND Thomas’ may help you to identify records relating to the agreement with Daniel Thomas. A similar method can be employed to combine other search terms which will help you to identify records of relevance to your search.\n\nIf you would like to visit the Archives to view these records then details of our opening times and location can be found on our website , although please note that we are closed to the public 16-18 June to allow staff to undertake essential work on the collection. Booking is advised and if you are able to provide a list of the documents you would like to consult we will have them ready for your arrival. If you have not visited us before you will be required to register; for this we ask you bring along two forms of identification - one showing your name (e.g. driving licence, passport) and another showing your address (e.g. a recent bill or official letter).\n\nI hope you find this information useful.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nHannah Price\nArchifydd | Archivist\n\nNodwch fy mod yn gweithio o Ddydd Llun tan Ddydd Iau.  Os hoffwch gysylltu â’r Archifau tu allan i’r oriau yma danfonwch e-bost [email redacted]  | Please note I work Mondays to Thursdays. If you wish to contact the Archives outside these hours please email [email redacted] \nArchifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted] | Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n( [phone redacted]\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.twitter.com/glamarchives\nInstagram: glamarchives\n\nBydd Archifau Morgannwg yn sicrhau ein bod yn cyfathrebu â chi yn yr iaith o'ch dewis, boed hynny'n Gymraeg, yn Saesneg neu'n ddwyieithog cyn belled ag y byddwch yn rhoi gwybod i ni pa well gennych. Rydych yn derbyn y wybodaeth hon yn y Saesneg gan fod hyn wedi ei gofnodi fel eich dewis iaith. Os hoffech chi ddiweddaru'r wybodaeth hon neu ddewis peidio â derbyn y negeseuon e-bost hyn, cysylltwch â ni: [email redacted] . | Glamorgan Archives will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, whether that’s English, Welsh or bilingual as long as you let us know which you prefer. You are receiving this information in English as this 