ble to send us the exact references? They could possibly include a document/manuscript number that could help locating any materials in question.\n\nLastly, I had a brief look at materials held by our partner, Glamorgan Archives. One of the records that came up is the below:\n[cid:74a57f3b-c0e1-483b-aba1-464a9ee48fbd]\nI think it would be worth contacting them (Contact - Glamorgan Archives<https://glamarchives.gov.uk/contact/>) and asking if they have any more documents relating to the house.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nMonika Wroblewska\n\nRhagenwau/Pronouns: hi/ei / she/her\n\n\nSwyddog Hyb Uwch Senior Hub Officer\n\nHyb y Llyfrgell Ganolog Central Library Hub\n\nYr Aes The Hayes, Caerdydd Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n\nCyngor Dinas Caerdydd City of Cardiff Council\n\n[cid:22e6516e-3bef-4048-b52e-44daa00578e7]  [cid:40562fed-af06-45f3-8dcf-724362b4bebe]  [cid:35320d82-e8ff-457e-968f-bb4709586dd3]\n\n________________________________\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 07 June 2026 10:05\nTo: Libraries <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\n\nSirs,\n\nPlease help me locate a copy of Daniel Thomas/Bute Estates deed/swap for Great House Farm (referenced in quarry deal histories) and any late 1800's / early 1900s materials or Williams family files.\n\nRegards\n\n\nRequester\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to 