 - Further Details of Archives","name":"Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Further Details of Archives","date":"2026-06-10T19:39:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19eb30bb29961396.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan-further-details-of-archives","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19eb30bb29961396.json","textStatus":"available","text":"On Wed, 10 Jun 2026, 10:06 Dr Adam Coward,  \nwrote:\n\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your further enquiry. I have checked the accessions\n> information for the archive items which we hold related to the site.\n> Unfortunately, there is no accessions data for the items in the NMR Site\n> File collection. This is because most of the information was either created\n> (in the case of notes and drawing from site visits) or collected (in the\n> case of the newspaper cuttings) by RCAHMW staff in the course of their\n> duties. Having examined the records themselves, however, I do note that\n> Archive Number 6048942 *may* have come from a Mrs Buckler (‘Mrs Buckler?’\n> is handwritten under the account). There is also a note at the bottom of\n> Archive Number 6048945 that ‘Correspondence between C.N. Johns and Mrs\n> Buckler, Great House Farm, has been lost since 1986/87’, although I have\n> been unable to find any other record of this correspondence either in our\n> records or our archive catalogue, having carried out both digital and\n> physical searches, including searching through the RCAHMW administrative\n> files in the archive (some of which are not yet open to the public).\n>\n>\n>\n> With regard to the first three records in the list, I include what\n> accessions details are available below:\n>\n> Archive Number\n>\n> creator or originating body\n>\n> accession source\n>\n> accession date\n>\n> 6524751\n>\n> Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\n>\n> Donation\n>\n> 20/03/2019\n>\n> 6416853\n>\n>  Cotswold Archaeology\n>\n> Donation\n>\n> 30/05/2014\n>\n> 6500905\n>\n> Dr Katherine Watson\n>\n> Transferred from Historic England as part of an exchange of material\n> between the two organisations\n>\n> 15/01/2018\n>\n>\n>\n> With regards to which records mention things like ownership and the\n> dispute, most of the newspaper article clippings naturally discuss it.\n> Archive Number 6048942 provides a short history of the site and notes the\n> family’s residence there and Archive Number 6048945 notes that ‘The house\n> remained partially recorded because of problems created by an ownership\n> dispute. The house and farm buildings were suddenly and completely\n> destroyed by B. P. Properties Ltd. on 6th December 1988 amid considerable\n> local controversy’. If you would like further details about the content of\n> these records, they can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the\n> National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday. Scans of\n> records can also be requested, using the attached order form. We also do\n> offer a limited document summary service. Please see our price list for\n> details.\n>\n>\n>\n> In addition to these 14 records, we may hold some historical aerial\n> photography which may include the site. This would likely include vertical\n> aerial photography taken from a high altitude by the Royal Air Force and/or\n> Ordnance survey from the 1940s to the turn of the 21st century. If you\n> would like to request a search of our historic aerial photography\n> collections, please provide details for your search, such as any location\n> or time-period parameters. Please note that we do charge for these\n> searches. Please see the attached price list for details.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam Coward\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dr Adam Coward\n>  Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,  Aberystwyth,  [postcode redacted]\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n> [email redacted]  |  [email redacted]\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk    |  www.rcahmw.gov.uk\n>  \n> Noddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru  |  Sponsored by Welsh Government\n> [image: Facebook]\n>  \n> [image: Twitter]  \n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i\n> gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis\n> iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a\n> ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y\n> Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn\n> defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n> ​​​​\n> Under the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the\n> right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the\n> Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To\n> ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive\n> correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information\n> will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all\n> future communication. Thank you.\n> ​\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19eb30b008362973","subject":"Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Further Details of Archives","name":"Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Further Details of Archives","date":"2026-06-10T19:38:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19eb30b008362973.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan-further-details-of-archives","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19eb30b008362973.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Adam,\n\nThanks.\n\nI'm at the Welsh Settlement in Patagonia to reconstruct a replica of our\nformer 10 bed court house/manor house. If I haven't said already. I will\ntry to respond to this, but forgive me in advance as my times limited am\nI'm sure yours is. And this is deeply traumatic. I am still the only one in\nmy family half able and willing to speak up and out about this.\n\nMy grandmother was only Mrs Buckler for a short time, from her marriage in\n1935 until she changed her name back to Mrs Williams, as I understand — if\nshe was ever Mrs Buckler at all. Since her Williams name and \"Williams\nTitle\" (as the courts cite) were important to her ancestral and hereditary\nland claim. Whereas the dead legal name Mrs Buckler, with no such rights as\nthe indigenous living woman on her ancestral birthland, did have rights.\nAnd the courts' and BP's and land registries' use of Mrs Buckler as her\nname, long after it ceased to exist, I believe is at least a mistake.\nConsidering it falls within the context of a campaign to dispossess this\ndisabled widow's pension and us of our family home and land since 1667, I\nwould say that mistake and distinction ought to be corrected on the public\nrecord. I would like to know the procedure where it concerns your\ndepartment. Or if a note can be made of this on the files where the mistake\nexists. If it exists. I will be happy to provide her death certificate as\nMrs Williams and so forth, if helpful.\n\nThe other matter is the fact of the 1975 and 1983 conveyance of two titles\nand merging of two titles. Both were treated as the surrounding farmland\nand leased and defaulted on the lease of the surrounding farmland. But if\nit were indeed the case that Mrs Williams had absolute title of her\nfarmhouse and garden, aside from the 999-year lease of surrounding farmland\nacquired in 1667, then the above conveyances show that her land and home\nwere unlawfully absorbed into the land BP acquired and gained possession\nof, treating her home and garden as one and the same when they were not.\nOwnership was never ruled on. BP sought possession and never gained a\nruling on ownership.\n\nSo Mrs Williams and our family's home and garden and ownership claim and\nplot appears to not have been extinguished, but instead possession of our\nhome and garden appears to have been taken by force — possibly military\ntoo, not just police — as if our home and garden were subject to the\npossession of the surrounding farmland. Confusion caused may stem from BP\nwithholding the fact Mary was challenging their claim of ownership of her\nland and garden from the land registry in 1983.\n\nMary conveniently died the fortnight she had to challenge BP merging her\ntitle into theirs. The land registry also appears to have used the invalid\nMrs Buckler name from her 1935 marriage, disregarding the name change\nreversion, to validate the name Mrs Buckler on BP's licence letters offered\nin 1974. To which were allegedly not rejected despite Mary going to the\npapers to expressly reject as per the 1974 article and expressly rejected\naccess in 1975 during the conveyance. The land registry also would have had\nto depend on the 1974 quashed and earlier adjourned court documents to\ncorroborate BP's filings, but allege to have not seen or known the land was\ndisputed by Mary Williams and my family, while depending on court documents\nexplicitly detailing that Mary Williams and my family were challenging BP.\nThe 1974 licence letters, wrongly validated retrospectively in 1987, as did\nthe land registry try to validate their actions in 1983 using a ruling 4\nyears later as their defence. BP lost in 1974. The challenge of ownership\ncould not be ruled on in their favour nor ruled against in Mary's. Nor did\nthey win possession. The press sided with Mary. The courts to an extent\ntoo, saying she couldn't present title, which isn't to say it didn't exist.\nAnd we won in the hearts and minds of the 1100+ people who petitioned BP in\n1974. Their licence letters afterwards, after my nan conveniently didn't\nget her audience and ruling in her favour with the court for the second\ntime that year due to adjourning and squashing, appear to have been\nbackdated. And lacked validity due to the 1975 conveyance where BP\nthemselves clearly did not leave Mary alone as their own licence terms.\nNotwithstanding the name was wrong on them. Notwithstanding Mary did\nexplicitly reject them publicly and in the 1975 conveyance.\n\nA series of institutional failures and court mistakes and procedural\nunfairness and fraud appears to have occurred, notwithstanding the\nconvenient timed death of my grandmother in the 2-week window to challenge\nBP's registering of our home and garden and land in their names in 1983. Or\nthe convenient death of my father after his appeal of the 1987 ruling was\ndismissed and his ECHR blocked and his property abruptly destroyed. ITV\nfailing to report that 24 hours before that abrupt demolition us 3 children\nand pregnant mum were inside. ITV footage suppressed until late last year\nalong with much other media, still suppressed.\n\nI don't say all this to offload the trauma of it all onto you. I say all\nthis to say that I am still a constituent of this community and my family\nhad standing in this community and county since 1667 and still do with our\ncurrent house we have in the neighbouring town, since the 50's. Which my\ngrandad Ray Smith purchased after starring in Exodus with Paul Newman. And\nfor 38 years we have, all of us, been utterly deceived by headlines saying\nwe were squatters being evicted. Or like in 1987 the judge said Mary\nWilliams \"conceived the notion she owned\". Her paper title was stolen from\nher so far as I understand in my research so far. She still appears to have\ndefeated the attempts to dispossess our family of our home in the early to\nlater half of the 1900's due to a copy of the paper in the public library.\nWhich in later cases could not be presented as that went missing too. Which\nin later court cases, despite paper title not being able to be presented,\nstill did not defeat or extinguish our ownership claim due to our long\nstanding. And to this day our ownership claim has not been lawfully or\nlegally extinguished or surrendered or transferred or sold by the inheritor\nof the Williams Title i.e. Mrs Williams, or her heirs or successors i.e. my\nlate father and now my cousins, 5 aunties, tens of cousins, and brothers\nand sisters.\n\nOur family is now a small army. And all of this information is surfacing\nand assembling and is painting a very damning picture of the reality there.\nThere's literal theatre going on there. The authority is lacking\nlegitimacy. This false reality is the only thing that has been conceived or\nimagined and on the basis of BP perjury, fraud and concealment. My dad\nreported fraud prior to his conveniently timed death too and I don't see it\nwas ever actioned then.\n\nThe situation is untenable. I appreciate your help but I am receiving a lot\nof snivelling, delaying/stalling, gatekeeping, legally defensive, carefully\nworded responses as to what information is and is not held. And what\ninformation is/is not disclosed to me. Notwithstanding gaps in records.\nWith none of you seeming to hear me when I say I am a military cyber and\nelectronic warfare professional and certified and experienced military\ncommander and leader. I was the child in this village, which I am still not\nfeeling the warmth from, 38 years later. And I have been examining this\nwhole matter and collecting my evidence for the best part of 20 years.\n\nLast month CADW alleged to have nothing to do with this and I had to send\nthem a newspaper clipping explicitly quoting them, with their affiliation\nto this case. Much of what I collected over the last 2 decades has gone\nmissing. Including Parliamentary records of this case: moved, destroyed,\ninaccessible to journalists and researchers or their security\nclassification changed for increased inaccessibility.\n\nI would encourage every self-proclaimed authority there, to not dig\nyourselves into deeper holes to protect institutional failures here. The\nNetflix documentary of all this will come. The replica of the farm here in\nPatagonia will no longer just be a museum to tell the story of the farm.\nBut will now include the 1988 possible military action/ siege against my\nfamily, disguised as a civil proceeding. And the perversion of the course\nof justice and suppression of this thereafter.\n\nThis is a scandal. Not just controversial.\nLet's be real. Here's what I can gather so far:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared\n\nMy family remain in authority.\nAs our claim is legitimate.\nNo force. No stealth/secrecy. NO LICENCE.\n\nBP and the British State claims lack legitimacy here. And force,\nstealth/secrecy and illegitimate licence was used.\n\nNow please, provide me the records you hold on me, my family estate, in\ntrust, and this case. The full truth. Without further delay. Or ambiguity.\n\nIt's unreasonable to expect me to pay admission to your records. Let alone\nfly 7,000 miles to view them. Or the artifacts in the museums looted from\nour stolen land. And so forth. Co-operate with me on this because your all\non notice for allegations of fraud and supression of information and\ndestruction of evidence. As a regime. Or possible terrorist network/ cell\nor failed 80's coup. Nothing theorised about what you lot are all doing\nthere with this case, would much surprise me any more. Except maybe acting\nmore forthcoming and transparently. Public servants and public records\nshould be public and private citizens and private lives should remain\nprivate. This entire dialoug my family are having with your govenrment is\nthe inverse whereby Vale of Glamorgan and others ask what it is I'm doing\nor know, while gatekeeping and keeping private information held on me and\nmy family and case. Not historic, but my actual physical self, who was in\nthat house while it was demolished while we still resided in it. Refusing\nto leave with one simple term: rule on ownership. No ruling was made we\ndidn't own it. No ruling was made BP did. Our forceful removal and the\nlawfare was and still is absurd and an ongoing crime against our humanity.\n\nI am simply building a chronological timeline of events to try to\naccurately re-tell this story for family, history/heritage and later legal\nadjudication and press and media. https://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nI'm not hijacking a BP fuel truck and driving it into those 20 houses on\nour land and standing on the truck with a naked flame making demands. I'm\njust asking you and your regime, respectfully and kindly, to just release\nthe files. You and other departments. In full. Without further delay or\nransom or conditions.\n\nI will be including in each slide and statement in the above website all\nthe supporting evidence. https://wayback.datro.xyz\n\nAnd this is all open source:\nhttps://github.com/unclehowell/datro/tree/bpvsbuckler so anyone can submit\na pull request with edits suggested. Which is how I would encourage and\ninfluence over mistakes I make, to be addressed. Seeing as we are now\nalgocratic and technologcal. This makes the narrative democratic and\ntransparent and not perverted and supressed.\n\nMy family hold the access keys to this repo in allodium. Which could be\nconditionally entrusted to the Welsh Government once it stops being so\nscandalous on this matter. And resembles a legitimate fiduciary and\nauthority to my indigenous family, on our ancestral birthland. I literally\nhave to fly in and out of my own county like it's a war zone now. Because\nof all this hybrid warfare. Like another tour of Iraq. And see my\ngenerationally traumatised family held hostage by terrorists, after the\n1988 act of terrorism we endured, still being covered up, is like seeing\nthe SAS soldiers I helped break out the Iraq prison, days before their\nexecution. The parallels are uncanny. And the irony is it was SAS that\nappear to have dispossessed our family for BP and Thatcher. Had I known\nthis I might have not helped save those two SAS soldiers from execution in\n2005. The depth of evil to have sent me to save the same people who\nsabotaged my family, goes some way to proving the demonic realm occupying\nand ruling their. Redeem yourselves already. For the love of God.\n\n99% of MP's refused to sign an EDM to condemn decapitating Christians last\nyear. Notwithstanding anyone with a flag resembling the colors of the four\nhorsemen of the apocalypse are already decapitating Britons on British\nisles. Michael Jones set up this Welsh Settlement in Argentina in 1786\nspecifically, as his followers recount, due to the \"decapitation committee\".\n\nI would, as a former employee of the Welsh Government/Vale of Glamorgan\nCouncil up until 2024 (adult care), having left my military career with\nfull honours (and am still bonafide), stop going down this path of this\nBrit'ish cultural, heritage and historic erasure and replacement of us all,\nspecifically Christian indigenous white Welsh, on our ancestral land, with\nour history and heritage. I'm married to a Dominican, my brother married a\nphiilipino; my family's race has changed from all white to mixed in a\nsingle generation with my nephews and neice and daughter now all half\nAfrican, philippino and Dominican. As a family we could not have embraced\nor advocated multiculturalism or diversity or being Brit'ish, any more. But\nour own culture, story, history and heritage in this case, must be told,\nKNOWN and able to be celebrated too. No more of this supression and\npersecution. It's already a stretch that I'm not discussing this all in\nWelsh. I'm still inclined to refrain from discussing this further in\nEnglish.\n\nOur farm was where Peerless Jim, 1906 featherweight champion, had his first\nfight. Where Marconi invented radio. Where a Roman Villa stands. Where our\nformer (Grade II listed — as it should have been, had CADW not failed the\nnation) 800-year-old former coach/manorial/court/farm house once stood.\nWhere a monastery exists. Where we called our family home since 1667. It's\npossible Magnus Maximus might have even been at the Roman Villa on our\nland.\n\nThe fact the tree we planted to commemorate our ownership has been removed\ntoo, without our claim of ownership being extinguished or defeated. And our\nhome [destruction of property and evidence]. And what's been built over us,\nburying us alive, while we're still all alive and breathing is, so far as I\ncan see, no plaque to commemorate Marconi. No notice or tourist board to\ncommemorate the Roman Villa and Monastery. Or the fact it's Wales' largest\nand most significant burial site ever recorded. This is therefore all\nalien. It's the action of imperialism and/or a terrorist cell/camp to house\nits officers/PoWs/hostages... following militant acts of terrorism,\ntheft/looting, human rights violations, propaganda, suppression of evidence\nand information.\n\nI have reported all this to my churches here in Patagonia and South Wales.\nAnd American societies that celebrate Welsh culture and heritage and\nhistory. The embarrassment and scandal here is no side of history to be on.\nWales has political eruptions in decolonisation/devolution now too.\nNotwithstanding the uprising in right wingers and indigenous rights for\nindigenous Britons.\n\nLayering injustice upon injustice to disguise earlier injustices in this\ncase, is not going to keep working for another decade. And I don't believe\nit's any side of history to be on.\n\nMy intentions here are in good faith. I'm merly working to get the websites\nup and organise the evidence chronologically. So there's a centralised\narchive. And prepare it all for legal adjudication. Try to get a ruling on\nland ownership as it's never been ruled on (only possession was). And if a\nplaque can be erected in Llandough all the better. I would like to arrange\nguided augmented reality tours of Llandough to our land there. And I'm\nalready here to reconstruct a replica of Great House Farm here in\nArgentina. With wax models of Peerless Jim and Marconi and so forth.\n\nLegal reparations for my family is something we seek to pursue, but\nnarrative justice too. This will be expensive.\n\nI have written to the ministry of interior in Argentina to seek land with\nthe same absolute title status as we held in Wales, which cannot be\nreturned to make us whole, no matter the reparations, since that superior\ntitle type no longer exists on British Isles under UK or Welsh law, so far\nas I understand.\n\nThis is all an ambitious undertaking. I require of you, my community,\nchurches and government, support and cooperation. There's nobility in my\ndirection forward from this. To gatekeep, suppress, withhold and ransom\ninformation and extort is dishonourable. As it brings the very values your\ninstitutes proclaim to instill, into disrepute. And I won't play or pay to\nplay part in that. My chosen direction forward does not require me to, nor\ndoes it depend on your assistance if you are unwilling to fully assist. My\ndirection forward from this will happen either way and obstructions to my\nendeavours will only place those hindering what I propose into further\ndishonour in my estimation.\n\nIt will actually take a lot of work on the part of the alleged authorities\nthere, to redeem yourselves. My transparency on this matter is one such an\nopportunity. And I don't much feel the olive branch I extend here, to the\nalleged authorities and fiduciaries there, is much being reciprocated thus\nfar. This isn't to cast aspersions on your department in particular, but\ndealings thus far with CADW and land registry, MP and councillors and even\nmy former employer Vale Council, does not fill me with confidence this\nmulti-generational attempt to starve and bury my family out of existence,\nis far from over.\n\nIt's literally a demonic realm occupying and ruling back there. And no\nwonder at all I've spent most of my adult life overseas. This case is also\none of many. My 36 day old son was abducted and filmed being\nritualistacally abused.\n\nIt's not within my family to play this role of  prisoners of war or\nhostages under the tyranny of the evil men back there. It has, at best, the\nunder duress (V.C) women and children and pets of our family, that haven't\nmanaged to liberate, who remain. That isn't constituency or membership to a\nsociety or citizenship. They're still terrorised into silence. Behold that\nwhich you call citizens. Further to this I remind you of the Eisteddfod\nceremony: is there peace, is there peace, is there peace. And the sword is\nreshiethed each time the crowd say yes, there's peace. Well I contest in\nthat when visit and ask is there peace and my family say yes. It's a\nquestion that is asked 3 times specifically so that seeing beyond their\nanswer is possible. To see beyond the answer hostages at gunpoint give, in\norder to see the duress.\n\nTheir reinactment of our customs and rituals in our culture, means nothing\nbut pagentry now, to many people. The actors literally said there was peace\n3 times while bombs fell on the event and the crowd were ushered into air\nraid shelters. Which is the point I'm trying to convey about how being so\ndisconnected from reality can look. I'm not unsheathing a sword and looking\ninto my families eyes and asking is there peace 3 times before projecting\nforce on those holding them hostage, because it's so far beyond that point\nalready. And the demonic realm there is so malignant and systemic. I can\nonly appeal to others there my proposal for an alternate direction forward\nto climb out of this hell. With the replica museum reconstruction here in\nPatagonia and Augmented reality tour and plaque back there in Llandough.\nAnd while you might say write to your MP or Councillor. They ignore this.\nThey're acting possessed by this scandal and demonic realm too.\n\nToday my younger sister, despite her nightmares about all this, visited the\nlocal library and read me this extract from the Glamorgan Village Book:\n\n\"Visitors to the farm saw how people lived in the past, how they made their\nbutter, cheese and beer and dried pork, and sent their sheep's wool to the\nwoollen mill at Lock's Mill Hill for spinning into yarn. They saw the\ncheese drying rooms hollowed out of a solid wall and the bedroom where in\nearlier centuries monks took rest on their travels. Marconi too slept here\nin a four poster bed whilst working with his experiments in wireless\ntelegraphy between Flat Holm and Lavernock Point.\"\n\nI also spoke to my aunty Mary Godfrey last night. And son Mark Godfrey. And\nother extended family yesterday. We all know the injustice we have and\ncontinue to endure. We are just wondering if the regime has changed at all\nfrom Thatcher and the terrorists who waged war on us 38 years ago.\nUltimately it sucks to all be buried alive under this mountain of scandal,\nfraud, deceipt, propergander and falsified records etc for almost 4\ndecades. Has this regime occupying and ruling no mercy, if it hasn't\nchanged since Thatcher?\n\nI also note while this act of terrorism was occurring on us, which ITV\nsomewhat reported on, regardless of the abrupt edits/cuts and failure to\nreport my mum was pregnant and the existence of us three children inside\nthe house, let alone that footage being supressed for 3+ decades. I do note\nthat another Welsh journalist was in Lybia at the same time where Ghadaffi\nwas telling the Welsh journalist that Thatcher was a terrorist and killing\nus indigenous Britons, while we were simultaniously being terorrised and\nkilled and our land and home looted and destroyed. Thatcher did also tell\nthe land registry to look the other way as BP registered our land in their\nnames. Another conveniently supressed report. Had they been shown side by\nside in 1988, and my existence as a human child, inside the house been at\nleast mentioned, non of this would have happened.\n\nI don't know if you can fathom the scale of injustice we feel in this\nmatter. Not only am I the only one of my family not in enough of  vodaka\nfuelled rage scale of rage or generationally traumatised into silence about\nthis. But I don't have vices, I'm bona fide, left my professional career\nwith full honours and I'm a former Vale of Glamorgan employee, completing\nmy 22 years in Oath that same year in 2024. If you and I are not able to at\nleast find an end of this snake to pick it up by, at least the right end,\nwhat hope is there?\n\nOf all the departments I've spoken to thus far I feel you're email today\nhas been the most helpful. And I hope that what I've conveyed to you and\nyour regime about our families position on this matter has been helpful to\nyou also.\n\nDo with this information what you will too. I've said all I can say to you\nAdam.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester Esq.\nWilliams/Buckler Family\n\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 10 Jun 2026, 10:06 Dr Adam Coward, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your further enquiry. I have checked the accessions\n> information for the archive items which we hold related to the site.\n> Unfortunately, there is no accessions data for the items in the NMR Site\n> File collection. This is because most of the information was either created\n> (in the case of notes and drawing from site visits) or collected (in the\n> case of the newspaper cuttings) by RCAHMW staff in the course of their\n> duties. Having examined the records themselves, however, I do note that\n> Archive Number 6048942 *may* have come from a Mrs Buckler (‘Mrs Buckler?’\n> is handwritten under the account). There is also a note at the bottom of\n> Archive Number 6048945 that ‘Correspondence between C.N. Johns and Mrs\n> Buckler, Great House Farm, has been lost since 1986/87’, although I have\n> been unable to find any other record of this correspondence either in our\n> records or our archive catalogue, having carried out both digital and\n> physical searches, including searching through the RCAHMW administrative\n> files in the archive (some of which are not yet open to the public).\n>\n>\n>\n> With regard to the first three records in the list, I include what\n> accessions details are available below:\n>\n> Archive Number\n>\n> creator or originating body\n>\n> accession source\n>\n> accession date\n>\n> 6524751\n>\n> Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\n>\n> Donation\n>\n> 20/03/2019\n>\n> 6416853\n>\n>  Cotswold Archaeology\n>\n> Donation\n>\n> 30/05/2014\n>\n> 6500905\n>\n> Dr Katherine Watson\n>\n> Transferred from Historic England as part of an exchange of material\n> between the two organisations\n>\n> 15/01/2018\n>\n>\n>\n> With regards to which records mention things like ownership and the\n> dispute, most of the newspaper article clippings naturally discuss it.\n> Archive Number 6048942 provides a short history of the site and notes the\n> family’s residence there and Archive Number 6048945 notes that ‘The house\n> remained partially recorded because of problems created by an ownership\n> dispute. The house and farm buildings were suddenly and completely\n> destroyed by B. P. Properties Ltd. on 6th December 1988 amid considerable\n> local controversy’. If you would like further details about the content of\n> these records, they can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the\n> National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday. Scans of\n> records can also be requested, using the attached order form. We also do\n> offer a limited document summary service. Please see our price list for\n> details.\n>\n>\n>\n> In addition to these 14 records, we may hold some historical aerial\n> photography which may include the site. This would likely include vertical\n> aerial photography taken from a high altitude by the Royal Air Force and/or\n> Ordnance survey from the 1940s to the turn of the 21st century. If you\n> would like to request a search of our historic aerial photography\n> collections, please provide details for your search, such as any location\n> or time-period parameters. Please note that we do charge for these\n> searches. Please see the attached price list for details.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam Coward\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dr Adam Coward\n>  Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,  Aberystwyth,  [postcode redacted]\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n> [email redacted]  |  [email redacted]\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk <https://cbhc.