r (Great House), Llandough,\n> associated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records.\n> My family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House\n> Farm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our\n> ownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling\n> of ownership, only possession.\n>\n> It's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And\n> when BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title,\n> my nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry\n> window to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and\n> document/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his\n> appeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR\n> request blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from\n> stopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed\n> force officers and possible SAS.\n>\n> https://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\n>\n> I understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of\n> Wales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations\n> and planning files, including references already identified as:\n>\n> • Great House Farm HER site entry – GGAT03586s\n> • Land at Great House Farm HER event entry – GGATE003872\n> • The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\n>\n> Please provide copies of, or access to:\n>\n>    1. All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House\n>    Estate, Llandough including:\n>\n> • surveys\n> • reports\n> • site notes\n> • photographs\n> • maps\n> • aerial imagery\n> • GIS layers\n> • archive material\n> • annotations\n> • title references\n> • occupancy references\n> • landscape records\n> • archaeological observations.\n>\n>    2. All internal and external correspondence involving:\n>\n> • RCAHMW / NMRW\n> • Cadw\n> • GGAT / Heneb\n> • Vale of Glamorgan Council\n> • BP Properties Ltd\n> • developers\n> • planning authorities\n> • landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\n>\n>    3. Any documents discussing:\n>\n> • estate ownership\n> • occupation history\n> • family occupation or association\n> • agricultural use\n> • commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\n> • estate boundaries\n> • title history\n> • acquisition history\n> • disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\n> • estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title\n> alteration.\n>\n>    4. Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872,\n>    including the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\n>    5. Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or\n>    family associations, including references to the Williams family where\n>    present within archives.\n>    6. Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance,\n>    dates and retention schedules.\n>    7. File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further\n>    related material not already listed.\n>\n> Please provide information electronically where possible.\n>\n> If any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and\n> provide the public interest assessment.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [address redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19eb1a3f62dd725e","subject":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Further Details of Archives","name":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Further Details of Archives","date":"2026-06-10T13:05:48Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19eb1a3f62dd725e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan-further-details-of-archives","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19eb1a3f62dd725e","direction":"received","from":"Dr Adam Coward","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19eb1a3f62dd725e.json","attachments":[{"name":"LES16 Price List 2026.pdf","title":"LES16 Price List 2026.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les16-price-list-2026.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":304904,"sha256":"08666a9e23e13caa10704047249ed2130af5ce2169c2136f4ae6e5f967d3c4a7"},{"name":"LES17 Licence Fees 2026.pdf","title":"LES17 Licence Fees 2026.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les17-licence-fees-2026.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":315620,"sha256":"6c2e0f5ed166bd822b1b3ead71cf29341ab4c352f04651e6c88149e17526a37e"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThank you for your further enquiry. I have checked the accessions information for the archive items which we hold related to the site. Unfortunately, there is no accessions data for the items in the NMR Site File collection. This is because most of the information was either created (in the case of notes and drawing from site visits) or collected (in the case of the newspaper cuttings) by RCAHMW staff in the course of their duties. Having examined the records themselves, however, I do note that Archive Number 6048942 may have come from a Mrs Buckler (‘Mrs Buckler?’ is handwritten under the account). There is also a note at the bottom of Archive Number 6048945 that ‘Correspondence between C.N. Johns and Mrs Buckler, Great House Farm, has been lost since 1986/87’, although I have been unable to find any other record of this correspondence either in our records or our archive catalogue, having carried out both digital and physical searches, including searching through the RCAHMW administrative files in the archive (some of which are not yet open to the public).\n\nWith regard to the first three records in the list, I include what accessions details are available below:\nArchive Number\ncreator or originating body\naccession source\naccession date\n6524751\nGlamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust\nDonation\n20/03/2019\n6416853\n Cotswold Archaeology\nDonation\n30/05/2014\n6500905\nDr Katherine Watson\nTransferred from Historic England as part of an exchange of material between the two organisations\n15/01/2018\n\nWith regards to which records mention things like ownership and the dispute, most of the newspaper article clippings naturally discuss it. Archive Number 6048942 provides a short history of the site and notes the family’s residence there and Archive Number 6048945 notes that ‘The house remained partially recorded because of problems created by an ownership dispute. The house and farm buildings were suddenly and completely destroyed by B. P. Properties Ltd. on 6th December 1988 amid considerable local controversy’. If you would like further details about the content of these records, they can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday. Scans of records can also be requested, using the attached order form. We also do offer a limited document summary service. Please see our price list for details.\n\nIn addition to these 14 records, we may hold some historical aerial photography which may include the site. This would likely include vertical aerial photography taken from a high altitude by the Royal Air Force and/or Ordnance survey from the 1940s to the turn of the 21st century. If you would like to request a search of our historic aerial photography collections, please provide details for your search, such as any location or time-period parameters. Please note that we do charge for these searches. Please see the attached price list for details.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAdam Coward\n\n\n\nDr Adam Coward\n Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 09 June 2026 01:20\nTo: Dr Adam Coward <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Details of Archives\n\n\nDear Dr Coward,\n\nThank you for your assistance to date and for providing access to the Coflein archive listings relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nHaving reviewed your correspondence carefully, I note that RCAHMW holds fourteen archive records associated with the site.\n\nTo assist my research, I would be grateful if you could provide, for each of the fourteen archive records, any information held regarding:\n\n• full archive title; • archive number; • creator or originating body; • accession source; • accession date; • provenance; • date range covered; • physical format (photograph, report, microfiche, survey, map, drawing, etc.); • extent (number of pages, images, sheets, frames, etc.); • descriptive notes not visible on the public catalogue; • related archive references.\n\nIn addition, I would be grateful if you could confirm whether any of the fourteen archives contain references to:\n\n• ownership of Great House Farm; • occupiers or tenants; • the Williams family; • Daniel Thomas; • Bute Estate land transactions; • estate boundaries; • farm buildings before demolition; • archaeological surveys; • BP Properties Ltd; • planning consultations; • oral history; • commemorative tree planting; • historic photographs of the farm and surrounding land.\n\nYou previously confirmed that RCAHMW does not hold correspondence relating to the site. Could you also confirm whether any related material exists outside the fourteen listed archives, including:\n\n• aerial photographs; • survey photographs; • field notebooks; • unpublished reports; • HER-linked records; • transferred archives; • accession files; • provenance files; • curator notes; • associated collections indexed under alternative site names.\n\nAs part of my research into the history, occupation and documentary record of Great House Farm, I would also be grateful if you could advise whether any archive accession records identify the person, organisation or authority that deposited the material with RCAHMW.\n\nFinally, if any material has been 