ence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea65acab5ea0dc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea9c008785ee13.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Dr Coward,\n\nThank you for your assistance to date and for providing access to the\nCoflein archive listings relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nHaving reviewed your correspondence carefully, I note that RCAHMW holds\nfourteen archive records associated with the site.\n\nTo assist my research, I would be grateful if you could provide, for each\nof the fourteen archive records, any information held regarding:\n\n• full archive title; • archive number; • creator or originating body; •\naccession source; • accession date; • provenance; • date range covered; •\nphysical format (photograph, report, microfiche, survey, map, drawing,\netc.); • extent (number of pages, images, sheets, frames, etc.); •\ndescriptive notes not visible on the public catalogue; • related archive\nreferences.\n\nIn addition, I would be grateful if you could confirm whether any of the\nfourteen archives contain references to:\n\n• ownership of Great House Farm; • occupiers or tenants; • the Williams\nfamily; • Daniel Thomas; • Bute Estate land transactions; • estate\nboundaries; • farm buildings before demolition; • archaeological surveys; •\nBP Properties Ltd; • planning consultations; • oral history; •\ncommemorative tree planting; • historic photographs of the farm and\nsurrounding land.\n\nYou previously confirmed that RCAHMW does not hold correspondence relating\nto the site. Could you also confirm whether any related material exists\noutside the fourteen listed archives, including:\n\n• aerial photographs; • survey photographs; • field notebooks; •\nunpublished reports; • HER-linked records; • transferred archives; •\naccession files; • provenance files; • curator notes; • associated\ncollections indexed under alternative site names.\n\nAs part of my research into the history, occupation and documentary record\nof Great House Farm, I would also be grateful if you could advise whether\nany archive accession records identify the person, organisation or\nauthority that deposited the material with RCAHMW.\n\nFinally, if any material has been transferred to another repository, please\nidentify the repository and any relevant catalogue references.\n\nMany thanks for your assistance.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester | bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nOn Mon, 8 Jun 2026, 05:30 Dr Adam Coward, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Good morning,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email. The full list of archives which we hold related\n> to the site can be seen here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/sites/20182/archives. Fuller information about\n> the archives can be seen by clicking on the red ‘Archive Number’ for each\n> entry in the list, which will take you to the specific entry for it on our\n> catalogue. This will include information such as titles, dates, and\n> descriptions, albeit we may not have information such as dates for all\n> items.\n>\n>\n>\n> All the best,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dr Adam Coward\n>  Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,  Aberystwyth,  [postcode redacted]\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n> [email redacted]  |  [email redacted]\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk <https://cbhc.gov.uk/>  |  www.rcahmw.gov.uk\n> <https://rcahmw.gov.uk/>\n> Noddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru  |  Sponsored by Welsh Government\n> [image: Facebook]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/Royal-Commission-on-the-Ancient-and-Historical-Monuments-of-Wales-146120328739808>\n> [image: Twitter] <https://www.twitter.com/rcahmwales>\n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i\n> gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis\n> iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a\n> ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y\n> Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn\n> defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n> ​​​​\n> Under the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the\n> right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the\n> Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To\n> ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive\n> correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information\n> will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all\n> future communication. Thank you.\n> ​\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 05 June 2026 06:04\n> *To:* Dr Adam Coward <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family,\n> Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam,\n>\n>\n>\n> Might I please get the full archive list with titles, dates and\n> descriptions if you don't already have it. Of the 14 files you cited.\n>\n>\n>\n> ownership\n>\n> occupiers\n>\n> estate history\n>\n> photographs before demolition\n>\n> farm buildings\n>\n> oral history\n>\n> surveys undertaken before development\n>\n>\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> On Thu, 28 May 2026, 11:47 Dr Adam Coward, <[email redacted]>\n> wrote:\n>\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. As noted in my email of 26 November last,\n> while we cannot advise you on a legal case or undertake a review of\n> historical decisions, we do hold information and archives related to Great\n> House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> The site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments\n> Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n>\n>\n>\n> We hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can\n> be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales,\n> which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to\n> view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so\n> that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material\n> is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search\n> Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff\n> to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit. However,\n> I have located an electronic copy of Archive Number 6524751, which can be\n> accessed here:\n> https://www.walesher1974.org/her/app/php/herumd.php?group=GGAT&level=3&docid=301361628\n>\n>\n>\n> While it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order\n> form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of\n> some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would\n> require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many\n> of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be\n> able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research.\n> Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the\n> permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging\n> to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> Finally, I have confirmed with our Records Manager that we do not hold any\n> correspondence related to the site.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you again for your enquiry.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam Coward\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *Dr Adam Coward*\n>\n> * Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager*\n>\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,\n>\n>  Aberystwyth,\n>\n>  [postcode redacted]\n>\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>  |\n>\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk <https://cbhc.gov.uk/>\n>\n> |\n>\n>  www.rcahmw.gov.uk <https://rcahmw.gov.uk/>\n>\n> *Noddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru *\n>\n> |\n>\n> * Sponsored by Welsh Government*\n>\n> [image: Facebook]\n> <https://www.facebook.com/Royal-Commission-on-the-Ancient-and-Historical-Monuments-of-Wales-146120328739808>\n>\n> [image: Twitter] <https://www.twitter.com/rcahmwales>\n>\n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\n>\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Yn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i\n> gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis\n> iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a\n> ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y\n> Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn\n> defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n>\n> ​​​​\n>\n> Under the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the\n> right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the\n> Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To\n> ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive\n> correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information\n> will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all\n> future communication. Thank you.\n> ​\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 20 May 2026 22:11\n> *To:* unclehowell <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of\n> Glamorgan\n>\n>\n>\n> Sir / Madam,\n>\n> To all those whom it concerns, BCC'd into this email.\n>\n> I write to request disclosure under the Freedom of Information Act 2000\n> and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n>\n> This request concerns Great House Farm / Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough,\n> associated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records.\n> My family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House\n> Farm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our\n> ownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling\n> of ownership, only possession.\n>\n> It's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And\n> when BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title,\n> my nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry\n> window to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and\n> document/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his\n> appeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR\n> request blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from\n> stopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed\n> force officers and possible SAS.\n>\n> https://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\n>\n> I understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of\n> Wales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations\n> and planning files, including references already identified as:\n>\n> • Great House Farm HER site entry – GGAT03586s\n> • Land at Great House Farm HER event entry – GGATE003872\n> • The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\n>\n> Please provide copies of, or access to:\n>\n>    1. All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House\n>    Estate, Llandough including:\n>\n> • surveys\n> • reports\n> • site notes\n> • photographs\n> • maps\n> • aerial imagery\n> • GIS layers\n> • archive material\n> • annotations\n> • title references\n> • occupancy references\n> • landscape records\n> • archaeological observations.\n>\n>    2. All internal and external correspondence involving:\n>\n> • RCAHMW / NMRW\n> • Cadw\n> • GGAT / Heneb\n> • Vale of Glamorgan Council\n> • BP Properties Ltd\n> • developers\n> • planning authorities\n> • landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\n>\n>    3. Any documents discussing:\n>\n> • estate ownership\n> • occupation history\n> • family occupation or association\n> • agricultural use\n> • commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\n> • estate boundaries\n> • title history\n> • acquisition history\n> • disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\n> • estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title\n> alteration.\n>\n>    4. Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872,\n>    including the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\n>    5. Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or\n>    family associations, including references to the Williams family where\n>    present within archives.\n>    6. Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance,\n>    dates and retention schedules.\n>    7. File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further\n>    related material not already listed.\n>\n> Please provide information electronically where possible.\n>\n> If any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and\n> provide the public interest assessment.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [address redacted]\n> [map link redacted]\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ea9bca7953e41d","subject":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-09T00:16:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea9bca7953e41d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea1524cf133911-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea1524cf133911","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea9bca7953e41d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"David,\n\nBore Da / Good Morning,\n\nWill do. And thanks for your prompt reply.\n\nPlease also clarify whether any searches were undertaken beyond deeds and\ntitle documents, as my enquiry extends to a wider range of historical\nmaterials relating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough.\n\nFamily records and longstanding local accounts indicate that a copy of the\nconveyance or land transfer associated with Daniel Thomas and the Bute\nEstate may at one time have been available through Cardiff's library or\nlocal studies collections. The Williams family relied upon documentary\nevidence relating to the farm during disputes concerning occupation and\nownership during the twentieth century, and family members consistently\nreferred to such records.\n\nI therefore respectfully request that Cathays Branch and Heritage Library,\nor the appropriate Cardiff Council department, undertake or arrange a\nsearch of any relevant holdings, including:\n\n• Local studies collections and vertical files. • Heritage and local\nhistory indexes. • Newspaper cuttings collections. • Photographic\ncollections. • Map collections. • Catalogue entries and accession records.\n• References to Great House Farm, Ty Mawr, Llandough. • References to\nDaniel Thomas, the Bute Estate, quarry agreements, land exchanges, or\nconveyances. • References to John Williams, Mary Williams, or other members\nof the Williams family associated with the farm. • Records indicating\nwhether any such material was transferred to Glamorgan Archives or another\nrepository.\n\nIn particular, if any relevant material was formerly held by Cardiff\nLibraries or Cardiff Council but subsequently transferred, withdrawn,\nre-catalogued, or otherwise relocated, I would be grateful for any\ninformation identifying where those records are now held and any catalogue\nreferences that may assist my research.\n\nIf this request would be more appropriately handled under the Freedom of\nInformation Act 2000 or Environmental Information Regulations 2004, please\ntreat it accordingly or transfer it internally to the relevant department.\n\nThe purpose of my enquiry is to identify surviving historical records\nrelating to Great House Farm and the Williams family's connection to the\nproperty. Any guidance, references, finding aids, catalogue entries, or\narchive references would be greatly appreciated.\n\nThank you for your assistance. I look forward to hearing from you.\n\nDiolch yn fawr, Regards,\n\nRequester Esq.\nWilliams/ Buckler Family Researcher and Representative |\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nOn Mon, 8 Jun 2026, 06:26 Library Cathays, <[email redacted]>\nwrote:\n\n> Bore Da / Good Morning\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Unfortunately we don’t hold any material/deeds  for Great House Farm ,\n>  however the Glamorgan Archives does  have that information.\n>\n> The website is : Home - Glamorgan Archives <https://glamarchives.gov.uk/>\n>\n>\n>\n> Hope this helps and let me know if I can be of further assistance\n>\n>\n>\n> David Thomas\n>\n>\n>\n> Library Assistant\n>\n>\n>\n> Llyfrgell Cangen a Treftadaeth Cathays  / Cathays Branch and Heritage\n> Library\n>\n> Cyngor Caerdydd / Cardiff Council\n>\n> E-bost/E-mail: [email redacted] /\n> [email redacted]\n>\n> Ffôn/Tel: [phone redacted]\n>\n> Fairoak Road, [postcode redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> The Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We\n> will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as\n> long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not\n> lead to delay.\n>\n> Privileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If\n> you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for\n> delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this\n> message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly\n> notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your\n> employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.\n> Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not\n> relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of\n> Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail\n> sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils\n> Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other\n> than the addressee.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> Mae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog.\n> Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni\n> pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n>\n> Mae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y\n> neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r\n> neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges.\n> Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy\n> e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi\n> neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon.\n> Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y\n> neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir\n> Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff\n> unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan\n> system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu\n> harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 07 June 2026 10:05\n> *To:* Libraries <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Llandough\n>\n>\n>\n>  *EXTERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take\n> care when clicking links.\n>  *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch\n> ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Sirs,\n>\n> Please help me locate a copy of Daniel Thomas/Bute Estates deed/swap for\n> Great House Farm (referenced in quarry deal histories) and any late 1800's\n> / early 1900s materials or Williams family files.\n>\n> Regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ea68e30b0fad04","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-06-08T09:26:33Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea68e30b0fad04.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea1524cf133911-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea1524cf133911","direction":"received","from":"Library Cathays","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea68e30b0fad04.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Bore Da / Good Morning\n\nThank you for your enquiry.\n\n\nUnfortunately we don’t hold any material/deeds  for Great House Farm ,  however the Glamorgan Archives does  have that information.\nThe website is : Home - Glamorgan Archives \n\nHope this helps and let me know if I can be of further assistance\n\nDavid Thomas\n\nLibrary Assistant\n\nLlyfrgell Cangen a Treftadaeth Cathays  / Cathays Branch and Heritage Library\nCyngor Caerdydd / Cardiff Council\nE-bost/E-mail: [email redacted]  / [email redacted] \nFfôn/Tel: [phone redacted]\nFairoak Road, [postcode redacted]\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind. Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************\n\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 07 June 2026 10:05\nTo: Libraries  \nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough\n\n EXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\n ALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\n\n\nSirs,\n\nPlease help me locate a copy of Daniel Thomas/Bute Estates deed/swap for Great House Farm (referenced in quarry deal histories) and any late 1800's / early 1900s materials or Williams family files.\n\nRegards\n\n\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ea65acab5ea0dc","subject":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Details of Archives","name":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan - Details of Archives","date":"2026-06-08T08:30:15Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea65acab5ea0dc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea65acab5ea0dc-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan-details-of-archives","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea65acab5ea0dc","direction":"received","from":"Dr Adam Coward","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea65acab5ea0dc.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Good morning,\n\nThank you for your email. The full list of archives which we hold related to the site can be seen here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/sites/20182/archives. Fuller information about the archives can be seen by clicking on the red ‘Archive Number’ for each entry in the list, which will take you to the specific entry for it on our catalogue. This will include information such as titles, dates, and descriptions, albeit we may not have information such as dates for all items.\n\nAll the best,\n\nAdam\n\n\n\nDr Adam Coward\n Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 05 June 2026 06:04\nTo: Dr Adam Coward <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nAdam,\n\nMight I please get the full archive list with titles, dates and descriptions if you don't already have it. Of the 14 files you cited.\n\nownership\noccupiers\nestate history\nphotographs before demolition\nfarm buildings\noral history\nsurveys undertaken before development\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\nOn Thu, 28 May 2026, 11:47 Dr Adam Coward, <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>> wrote:\nGood afternoon,\n\nThank you for your enquiry. As noted in my email of 26 November last, while we cannot advise you on a legal case or undertake a review of historical decisions, we do hold information and archives related to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nThe site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n\nWe hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit. However, I have located an electronic copy of Archive Number 6524751, which can be accessed here: https://www.walesher1974.org/her/app/php/herumd.php?group=GGAT&level=3&docid=301361628\n\nWhile it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research. Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n\nFinally, I have confirmed with our Records Manager that we do not hold any correspondence related to the site.\n\nThank you again for your enquiry.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAdam Coward\n\n\n[cid:image001.png@01DCF729.2DDB7870]\nDr Adam Coward\n Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road,\n Aberystwyth,\n [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]<tel:+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n |\n[email redacted]<[email redacted]>\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk<https://cbhc.gov.uk/>\n|\n www.rcahmw.gov.uk<https://rcahmw.gov.uk/>\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru\n|\n Sponsored by Welsh Government\n[Facebook]<https://www.facebook.com/Royal-Commission-on-the-Ancient-and-Historical-Monuments-of-Wales-146120328739808>\n[Twitter]<https://www.twitter.com/rcahmwales>\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\n\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n​​​​\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSent: 20 May 2026 22:11\nTo: unclehowell <[email redacted]<[email redacted]>>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n\nSir / Madam,\n\nTo all those whom it concerns, BCC'd into this email.\n\nI write to request disclosure under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nThis request concerns Great House Farm / Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough, associated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records. My family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House Farm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our ownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling of ownership, only possession.\n\nIt's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And when BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title, my nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry window to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and document/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his appeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR request blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from stopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed force officers and possible SAS.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\n\nI understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of Wales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations and planning files, including references already identified as:\n\n• Great House Farm HER site entry – GGAT03586s\n• Land at Great House Farm HER event entry – GGATE003872\n• The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\n\nPlease provide copies of, or access to:\n\n  1.  All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House Estate, Llandough including:\n\n• surveys\n• reports\n• site notes\n• photographs\n• maps\n• aerial imagery\n• GIS layers\n• archive material\n• annotations\n• title references\n• occupancy references\n• landscape records\n• archaeological observations.\n\n  1.  All internal and external correspondence involving:\n\n• RCAHMW / NMRW\n• Cadw\n• GGAT / Heneb\n• Vale of Glamorgan Council\n• BP Properties Ltd\n• developers\n• planning authorities\n• landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\n\n  1.  Any documents discussing:\n\n• estate ownership\n• occupation history\n• family occupation or association\n• agricultural use\n• commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\n• estate boundaries\n• title history\n• acquisition history\n• disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\n• estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title alteration.\n\n  1.  Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872, including the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\n  2.  Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or family associations, including references to the Williams family where present within archives.\n  3.  Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance, dates and retention schedules.\n  4.  File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further related material not already listed.\n\nPlease provide information electronically where possible.\n\nIf any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and provide the public interest assessment.\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nRequester\n\n[address redacted][map link redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19ea6115dd775a77","subject":"RE: FOI","name":"RE: FOI","date":"2026-06-08T07:10:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea6115dd775a77.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea150513c39427-foi","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea150513c39427","direction":"received","from":"Disclosure Team","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea6115