t House Farm, Llandough (Mary Williams/Buckler, 1950s-1990s)","date":"2026-06-07T08:52:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea148a9088115e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea1459e1ca52e1-eir-request-historic-water-supply-records-for-great-house-farm-llandough-mary-williams-buckler-1950s-1990s","scopeTopics":["dwrcymru"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["dwrcymru"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea1459e1ca52e1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"dwrcymru","name":"Dwr Cymru Welsh Water"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea148a9088115e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear EIR Team,\n\nUnder the Environmental Information Regulations, please provide all records\nof water supply applications, connections, refusals, correspondence, or\nservice issues for Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth/Cardiff),\nparticularly involving my late gran Mary Williams or our Buckler family in\nthe 1900s-1980s. Include any notes on dairy operations, health impacts, or\nestate disputes (Western Ground Rents/Bute).\n\nThis supports family historical research into occupation and equitable\ntitle claims tied to a Daniel Thomas quarry deal. Thank you.\n\n\nRegards,\n\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ea130f935c7bc9","subject":"Formal Request for Information & Litigation Hold – Great House Farm Dispossession 1988 (Williams/Buckler Family, Titles WA231076/WA240304)","name":"Formal Request for Information & Litigation Hold – Great House Farm Dispossession 1988 (Williams/Buckler Family, Titles WA231076/WA240304)","date":"2026-06-07T08:26:41Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea130f935c7bc9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea12fc5bb465a4-formal-request-for-information-litigation-hold-great-house-farm-dispossession-1988-williams-buckler-family-titles-wa2310","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea12fc5bb465a4","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea130f935c7bc9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Legal/Compliance Team,\n\nAs heir of Mary Williams (d. 1983) and on behalf of the Williams family, I\nformally request all information held by BP Properties (or successors)\nrelating to Great House Farm, Llandough, including the 1988\neviction/demolition.\n\nSpecifically: deeds, leases, conveyance documents (post-Daniel Thomas\nquarry deal), correspondence with family/council/Cadw/police, rent records\nshowing house ownership vs. defaulted farmland lease, court files (BP v\nBuckler 1987), and any internal notes on adverse possession or family\nclaims.\n\nThis is a formal disclosure request in support of ongoing restitution.\nLitigation hold required on all files. Reference my prior notice of 15 May\n2026.\n\nI await your full response within statutory timescales where applicable.\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19ea12f74d5c8e44","subject":"FOI/EIR Request – 1988 Police/Bailiff Involvement in Dispossession at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (Ref: Buckler/Williams Family, BP Properties)\r\n","name":"FOI/EIR Request – 1988 Police/Bailiff Involvement in Dispossession at Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough (Ref: Buckler/Williams Family, BP Properties)\r\n","date":"2026-06-07T08:25:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea12f74d5c8e44.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea129e59750f6b-foi-eir-request-1988-police-bailiff-involvement-in-dispossession-at-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-ref-buckler-willi","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea129e59750f6b","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea12f74d5c8e44.json","textStatus":"available","text":"FOI Team / South Wales Police,\n\nI am Requester (heir/successor of Mary Williams, d. 1983), writing\nformally under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and Data Protection\nlegislation regarding the 1988 dispossession/eviction at Great House Farm\n(Ty Mawr / Church View Close area), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan.\n\nPlease provide all held records, correspondence, incident logs, statements,\nphotographs, or reports from 1900-1993 concerning:\n- Police attendance/support for bailiffs at the property (including\nchainsaw incident, barricading, sledgehammers).\n- Any involvement with BP Properties, Western Ground Rents, or Bute Estate\nsuccessors.\n- Mentions of Williams/Buckler family occupancy, Mary Williams' prior\nclaims, quarry deal with Daniel Thomas, house ownership vs. leased farmland.\n- Any complaints, use of force, or outcomes.\n- Any association/ collaboration with military forces, officers, defence\nstaff/ personnel regarding my families eviction in 1988\n\nHere's a YouTube on what I theorise on what happened at the address\nhttps://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared\n\nI request a litigation hold on all related files. Full details available on\nrequest.\n\nThank you,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19ea0ec0e669738a","subject":"Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough – Further Evidence of 1988 Involvement & Request for Comprehensive Records (Ref: Previous Enquiries incl. 21 May 2026)","name":"Great House Farm / Ty Mawr, Llandough – Further Evidence of 1988 Involvement & Request for Comprehensive Records (Ref: Previous Enquiries incl. 21 May 2026)","date":"2026-06-07T07:11:24Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea0ec0e669738a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea0e48eaddf4d1-great-house-farm-ty-mawr-llandough-further-evidence-of-1988-involvement-request-for-comprehensive-records-ref-previous-e","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea0e48eaddf4d1","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea0ec0e669738a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Cadw Team / Mr Michael Weatherhead / Listed Buildings Team,\n\nThank you for your assistance to date with my enquiries regarding Great\nHouse Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, including the heritage assessment\nmaterials provided on 21 May 2026.\n\nThis is a matter of profound personal and historic importance to the\nWilliams/Buckler family descendants. Mary Williams maintained until her\ndeath in 1983 that the family held ownership of the house following\narrangements with Daniel Thomas involving the quarry on the land, with the\nsurrounding farmland subject to a lease that defaulted. The family had\noccupied the property for centuries, with strong local and press\nrecognition of their longstanding connection.\n\nI attach a copy of a contemporary newspaper article from the *South Wales\nEcho* dated 3 December 1988 (\"History fight to save farm\" by Peter Bibby).\nIt reports that officials from Cadw were actively considering an appeal to\nthe Secretary of State for Wales to protect the farmhouse as a listed\nbuilding. A Cadw spokeswoman is quoted on evaluating spot-listing and\nemergency procedures due to its historic significance (parts potentially\ndating to the 12th-13th century), with plans for an inspector's site visit\nand discussion with the Royal Commission on Ancient and Historical\nMonuments. This occurred amid the family's legal battle and imminent\ndemolition.\n\nIn light of this clear evidence of Cadw's involvement at the critical time,\nI would be most grateful for a thorough review and full disclosure of *all*\nheld records, correspondence, assessments, site notes, photographs,\ninternal memos, or communications relating to Great House Farm / Ty Mawr\nfrom the 1970s to 1990s. This includes any listing considerations, heritage\nevaluations, interactions with the Vale of Glamorgan Council, BP\nProperties, or the family, and details of any records transferred to other\narchives (such as RCAHMW or Glamorgan Archives).\n\nI appreciate Cadw’s focused remit on the historic environment and kindly\nrequest that searches extend across all relevant teams and archives to\nensure nothing is overlooked. This would greatly assist our efforts to\ndocument and substantiate the family’s historic position in this sensitive\nmatter.\n\nThank you once again for your understanding and support. I look forward to\nyour substantive response at the earliest opportunity, and remain available\nfor any clarification that may assist.\n\nKind regards,\n\n*Requester* bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz [address redacted] [postcode redacted] (On\nbehalf of the Williams / Buckler family descendants)"},{"id":"gm-19ea0c4734421b17","subject":"Re: EIR/FOI request - 00210772 (Great House Farm / Church View Close, Llandough) – Further Clarification and Request for Full Disclosure","name":"Re: EIR/FOI request - 00210772 (Great House Farm / Church View Close, Llandough) – Further Clarification and Request for Full Disclosure","date":"2026-06-07T06:28:08Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea0c4734421b17.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea0ab674d60971-eir-foi-request-00210772-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-further-clarification-and-request-for-full-disclos","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea0ab674d60971","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":["00210772"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea0c4734421b17.json","textStatus":"available","text":"FOI Unit / Evelyn Morgan / Information Governance Team,\n\nThank you for your email dated 2 June 2026 and for the assistance provided\nso far in relation to reference 00210772.\n\nI appreciate the Council's efforts to support this important family matter\nand note your confirmation that no records are held regarding the private\nlegal proceedings in *BP Properties Ltd v Buckler*.\n\nAs background, this case related to the longstanding claims of my\nWilliams/Buckler family to ownership of Great House Farm (Ty Mawr). My\ngrandmother Mary Williams maintained until her conveniently timed death in\n1983 (in the 2 week window to challenge BP's registration of our home and\nland since 1667, in their names) that our family held ownership of the\nhouse following arrangements with Daniel Thomas involving the quarry, with\nthe surrounding farmland subject to a lease that defaulted.\n\nThere was a conveyance for the surrounding land and attempt to merge our\nfarmhouse and garden into that single plot in 1975. Which was challenged by\nmy nan. Something HM Land Registry correspondence (titles WA231076 and\nWA240304, first registered to BP Properties Limited in 1982/1983)\nreferences these conveyances and the Court of Appeal decision, which may\nassist in narrowing relevant planning and heritage searches.\n\nTo enable your Planning, Heritage, and other relevant teams to conduct\nthorough searches without further delay, I confirm that enquiries should\ncover the historic Great House Farm / Ty Mawr estate in Llandough (adjacent\nto and including areas now known as Church View Close, north side of\nLeckwith Road, title WA231076). This includes any planning permissions,\nheritage assessments, demolition records (circa 1988), tenancy notations,\nenvironmental information, or correspondence from 1875 onwards.\n\nI am keen to receive a full and timely response within the statutory\ntimeframe, drawing on all information the Council holds across departments.\nThis is of profound personal and historic importance to the Williams family\ndescendants as we seek to document and substantiate our family's position.\nShould any records have been transferred to Glamorgan Archives or handled\nin any other way, details of this would be most helpful.\n\nThank you once again for your understanding and support in this sensitive\nmatter. I look forward to your substantive reply at the earliest\nopportunity.\n\nKind regards,\n\n*Requester Esq. * bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz [address redacted],\n[location redacted] [postcode redacted] (On behalf of the Williams / Buckler family\ndescendants)"},{"id":"gm-19ea094cbd60e976","subject":"Planning Permission Church View Close, Llandough","name":"Planning Permission Church View Close, Llandough","date":"2026-06-07T05:36:05Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea094cbd60e976.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea093332b5eb64-planning-permission-church-view-close-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea093332b5eb64","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea094cbd60e976.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir/Madam,\n\nUnder the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004, I request copies of records\nrelating to Great House Farm (Ty Mawr), Llandough, near Cardiff.\n\nI am specifically seeking:\n\n   1.\n\n   Planning applications, permissions, refusals, conditions, appeals, and\n   related correspondence concerning the demolition of Great House Farm and\n   subsequent residential development.\n   2.\n\n   Any archaeological assessments, surveys, reports, briefs, watching\n   briefs, excavation reports, or heritage impact assessments relating to the\n   site.\n   3.\n\n   Any correspondence between the Council, Cadw, BP Properties, BP,\n   developers, archaeologists, the Royal Commission, or other public bodies\n   concerning:\n   - Great House Farm;\n      - its historic significance;\n      - archaeological discoveries;\n      - listing or scheduling considerations;\n      - demolition proposals.\n   4.\n\n   Any records discussing reported Roman remains, medieval remains,\n   monastic remains, burials, architectural fragments, or other archaeological\n   features associated with the site.\n   5.\n\n   Any records relating to emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation,\n   or protection measures considered for Great House Farm during the 1980s.\n   6.\n\n   Any committee minutes, officer reports, recommendations, or briefing\n   papers relating to planning decisions affecting the site.\n\nIf some records are held in archives or under a different authority, please\nadvise where they may be located.\n\nI would prefer the information in electronic format.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\nRequester\n\nhttps://bpvsbuckler.datro.xyz"},{"id":"gm-19ea053997d422b9","subject":"Church View Close, Llandough","name":"Church View Close, Llandough","date":"2026-06-07T04:24:53Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ea053997d422b9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ea03340a417829-church-view-close-llandough","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ea03340a417829","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ea053997d422b9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nI'm piecing together something I experienced in Llandough in 1988. From\npublic record, my research and family testemony. And media.\n\nThis is ongoing but here's a video of where my mind at is so far. It's\nlooking very aweful. I just thought I'd share this to invite you to\ncomment/ advise on any of this case.\n\nMy family seem to have been murdered into silence. But have never\nsurrendered claim to land in Llandough. Our home, my home, since 1667.\n\nI am trying to communicate this story and please understand its\nchallenging. There's trauma, anger/ upset and it's fragmented across family\nand various historic govenrment archives. It's collosal and multi\ngenerational too.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/INfFOLndny0?feature=shared\n\nWebsite below. I will work to get all these evidence onto this website so\nthere's a chrononical timeline and central location for the evidence.\n\nThis matter is unresolved in many ways and I feel it needs to be handled. I\nfeel it's unacceptable all this could have been allowed to have happened\nand gone on and buried or ignored for decades.\n\nFor authority to be authority there in South Wales, there must be\nlegitimacy. Be legitimate about this is all I ask.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz"},{"id":"gm-19e979aac22f31e1","subject":"Great House Farm - Williams/ Buckler","name":"Great House Farm - Williams/ Buckler","date":"2026-06-05T11:45:56Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e979aac22f31e1.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e97980e4c37546-great-house-farm-williams-buckler","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e97980e4c37546","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e979aac22f31e1.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nI am researching land ownership history relating to Llandough (Great House\nFarm / Ty Mawr area) and surrounding parcels.\nI am specifically seeking:\n\nBute Estate records for Llandough / Penarth / Cardiff outskirts\n\nAny conveyances, land exchanges, or “swap” agreements involving the Bute\nestate and a Daniel Thomas (late 1800s–early 1900s)\n\nAny quarrying agreements or mineral extraction leases connected to the\nproperty (including conditions of land reversion after quarrying)\n\nAny records of Western Ground Rents taking over Bute estate interests circa\nearly 1900s\n\nPlease advise:\n\nWhether such records exist in your catalogue\n\nWhich reference numbers or collections I should request\n\nWhether any material is restricted or off-site\nI am particularly interested in estate papers, deeds, correspondence, and\nmaps relating to land transfers or long leases.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester Esq. "},{"id":"gm-19e962b283bf7b5d","subject":"Automatic reply: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Automatic reply: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-06-05T05:04:28Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e962b283bf7b5d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75f4626d91a56-automatic-reply-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75f4626d91a56","direction":"received","from":"Dr Adam Coward","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e962b283bf7b5d.json","textStatus":"available","text":"﻿﻿﻿\nDiolch am eich neges. Rwyf allan o'r swyddfa yn erbyn 8 Mehefin 2026. Atebaf e-byst ar ôl dod yn ôl.\n\nOs oes brys, e-bostiwch [email redacted].\n\nThank you for your message.  I am away from the office until 8 June 2026. I will answer e-mails on my return.\n\nIf urgent, please email [email redacted].\n\nCofion gorau / Best wishes,\nDr Adam N. Coward"},{"id":"gm-19e962ac81eaa2a2","subject":"Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-06-05T05:04:06Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e962ac81eaa2a2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e6f0e4a747d5bc-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e6f0e4a747d5bc","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e962ac81eaa2a2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Adam,\n\nMight I please get the full archive list with titles, dates and\ndescriptions if you don't already have it. Of the 14 files you cited.\n\nownership\noccupiers\nestate history\nphotographs before demolition\nfarm buildings\noral history\nsurveys undertaken before development\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Thu, 28 May 2026, 11:47 Dr Adam Coward,  \nwrote:\n\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your enquiry. As noted in my email of 26 November last,\n> while we cannot advise you on a legal case or undertake a review of\n> historical decisions, we do hold information and archives related to Great\n> House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> The site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments\n> Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n>\n>\n>\n> We hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can\n> be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales,\n> which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to\n> view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so\n> that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material\n> is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search\n> Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff\n> to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit. However,\n> I have located an electronic copy of Archive Number 6524751, which can be\n> accessed here:\n> https://www.walesher1974.org/her/app/php/herumd.php?group=GGAT&level=3&docid=301361628\n>\n>\n>\n> While it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order\n> form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of\n> some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would\n> require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many\n> of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be\n> able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research.\n> Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the\n> permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging\n> to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> Finally, I have confirmed with our Records Manager that we do not hold any\n> correspondence related to the site.\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you again for your enquiry.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam Coward\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dr Adam Coward\n>  Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,  Aberystwyth,  [postcode redacted]\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n> [email redacted]  |  [email redacted]\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk    |  www.rcahmw.gov.uk\n>  \n> Noddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru  |  Sponsored by Welsh Government\n> [image: Facebook]\n>  \n> [image: Twitter]  \n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i\n> gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis\n> iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a\n> ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y\n> Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn\n> defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n> ​​​​\n> Under the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the\n> right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the\n> Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To\n> ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive\n> correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information\n> will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all\n> future communication. Thank you.\n> ​\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 20 May 2026 22:11\n> *To:* unclehowell  \n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of\n> Glamorgan\n>\n>\n>\n> Sir / Madam,\n>\n> To all those whom it concerns, BCC'd into this email.\n>\n> I write to request disclosure under the Freedom of Information Act 2000\n> and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n>\n> This request concerns Great House Farm / Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough,\n> associated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records.\n> My family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House\n> Farm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our\n> ownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling\n> of ownership, only possession.\n>\n> It's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And\n> when BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title,\n> my nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry\n> window to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and\n> document/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his\n> appeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR\n> request blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from\n> stopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed\n> force officers and possible SAS.\n>\n> https://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\n>\n> I understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of\n> Wales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations\n> and planning files, including references already identified as:\n>\n> • Great House Farm HER site entry – GGAT03586s\n> • Land at Great House Farm HER event entry – GGATE003872\n> • The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\n>\n> Please provide copies of, or access to:\n>\n>    1. All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House\n>    Estate, Llandough including:\n>\n> • surveys\n> • reports\n> • site notes\n> • photographs\n> • maps\n> • aerial imagery\n> • GIS layers\n> • archive material\n> • annotations\n> • title references\n> • occupancy references\n> • landscape records\n> • archaeological observations.\n>\n>    2. All internal and external correspondence involving:\n>\n> • RCAHMW / NMRW\n> • Cadw\n> • GGAT / Heneb\n> • Vale of Glamorgan Council\n> • BP Properties Ltd\n> • developers\n> • planning authorities\n> • landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\n>\n>    3. Any documents discussing:\n>\n> • estate ownership\n> • occupation history\n> • family occupation or association\n> • agricultural use\n> • commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\n> • estate boundaries\n> • title history\n> • acquisition history\n> • disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\n> • estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title\n> alteration.\n>\n>    4. Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872,\n>    including the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\n>    5. Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or\n>    family associations, including references to the Williams family where\n>    present within archives.\n>    6. Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance,\n>    dates and retention schedules.\n>    7. File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further\n>    related material not already listed.\n>\n> Please provide information electronically where possible.\n>\n> If any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and\n> provide the public interest assessment.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n>\n>\n> Requester\n>\n> [address redacted]\n>  \n>"},{"id":"gm-19e96061aaa9978b","subject":"Re: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","name":"Re: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-06-05T04:24:02Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e96061aaa9978b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-tenancy-records-f","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e96061aaa9978b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Hannah,\n\nThank you for your detailed reply and for identifying the records relating\nto Great House Farm and the Buckler family.\n\nHaving reviewed the descriptions, I am not yet certain that the 1938 Great\nHouse Farm sale catalogue relates to the same Great House Farm, Llandough\nthat later became the subject of the BP litigation involving the Buckler\nfamily. I will investigate this further.\n\nMy current research is focused on the ownership, occupation and legal\nhistory of Great House Farm, Llandough, particularly during the twentieth\ncentury and in connection with BP Properties, BP Pension Trust, tenancy\narrangements, conveyancing, planning matters and any records that may help\nestablish the chain of title. 1800/1900's too.\n\nCould you please advise whether Glamorgan Archives holds, or is aware of,\nany records relating to:\n\n   - BP Properties Ltd;\n   - BP Pension Trust;\n   - Great House Farm, Llandough (near Penarth);\n   - conveyances, tenancy agreements or estate management records\n   concerning the property;\n   - planning applications, redevelopment proposals or demolition records\n   relating to Great House Farm;\n   - correspondence between public bodies and the owners or occupiers of\n   the property;\n   - any records that may assist in tracing ownership or occupation between\n   the 1870s and the late 1980s.\n\nI would also be grateful if you could advise whether any estate maps, tithe\nmaps, valuation records, rating records or other archival sources might\nhelp establish the historical ownership and occupation of the property.\n\nThank you again for your assistance. Your reply was meaningful and\nappreciated.\n\nKind regards,\n\nRequester\n\n\nOn Thu, 4 Jun 2026, 13:04 Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg, <\n[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> 2026/2372\n>\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for your email received on 1 June.\n>\n>\n>\n> Staff have searched the catalogue for the Great House Farm, Llandough and\n> the Buckler family with the following results:\n>\n>\n>\n> *Collection* Stephenson & Alexander, Auctioneers and Chartered Surveyors,\n> Records\n>\n> *Document reference* DSA/6/1158\n> <https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSA/6/1158>\n>\n> *Title* Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge.\n>\n> *Date* 15 Nov 1938\n>\n> *Extent* 1 booklet\n>\n> *Description* Auctioneer: Herbert R. Thomas, Cowbridge;\n> Owner: D.J. Jenkins. [See DSA/10/14 Item 2332]\n> Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge.\n> 1 lot.\n> 1 plan.\n> Note on cover ‘Sold for £5,500 to Mr L.D. Thomas, Porthcawl’. Notes on the\n> second page of the particulars as to acreage and calculations as to value.\n>\n>\n>\n> *Collection* Stephenson & Alexander, Auctioneers and Chartered Surveyors,\n> Records\n>\n> *Document reference* DSA/6/701\n> <https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DSA/6/701>\n>\n> *Title* Parts of the* Llandough* Estate\n>\n> *Date* 9 Oct 1924\n>\n> *Extent* 1 booklet and 2 papers fixed to each other\n>\n> *Description* Auctioneer: Gottwaltz & Perry of 11 High St., Cardiff, in\n> conjunction with Yorwerth and Thomas of High St., Cowbridge.\n> Parts of the Llandough Estate in the parishes of Llanfair and St Hilary\n> Owner: Sidney Hutchinson Byass. [See DSA/10/10 Item 268]\n> Parts of The Llandough Estate (1500a.) comprising:\n> Pen-yr-heol, Saer’s, accommodation land near Byrclwydd, Great House, The\n> Herberts, Church Farm, The Rectory Farm, Fish Weir, Gigman Mill, Howe Mill,\n> Prior’s Hill (partly in p. of St. Hilary), Penyrheol Cottage, 1-4 Talbot\n> Terrace and Tithe cottages, St. Marychurch, Forge Cottage near The\n> Herberts, Abernant Cottage opposite Keeper’s Lodge and School Cottage near\n> Llanfair School, the wheelwright’s shop and timber shed on the Herbert’s\n> Corner, freehold lands and gardens all in the p. of Llanfair.\n> 29 lots.\n> 2 prints of the two plans, both with markings.\n> Pencil markings on the particulars.\n> Schedule of lands coloured brown on plan `A´ annexed adjacent to the plans\n> added\n> On front cover ‘Stephenson & Alexander Private’ and some pencil notes.\n>\n>\n>\n> *Collection *Corbett Family of Cogan Pill Papers\n>\n> *Document reference* DXJF/64/30\n> <https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/records/DXJF/64/27-32/30>\n>\n> *Title* Llandough [juxta-Penarth] sketch of former layout of part of\n> village by Mrs. Nancy Buckler of Great House Farm, Llandough, with notes\n>\n> *Date(s)*\n>\n> *Date* n.d. [c. 1950]\n>\n> *Date range* 1945-1955\n>\n> *Level* Item\n>\n> *Extent* 1 card, 1 paper\n>\n>\n>\n> A catalogue to the records of the councils and planning 