ICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-06-04T16:04:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e9360fb1d8918b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-tenancy-records-f","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e9360fb1d8918b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"2026/2372\n\nDear Mr Buckler,\n\nThank you for your email received on 1 June.\n\nStaff have searched the catalogue for the Great House Farm, Llandough and the Buckler family with the following results:\n\nCollection Stephenson & Alexander, Auctioneers and Chartered Surveyors, Records\nDocument reference DSA/6/1158 \nTitle Great House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge.\nDate 15 Nov 1938\nExtent 1 booklet\nDescription Auctioneer: Herbert R. Thomas, Cowbridge;\nOwner: D.J. Jenkins. [See DSA/10/14 Item 2332]\nGreat House Farm, Llandough, Cowbridge.\n1 lot.\n1 plan.\nNote on cover ‘Sold for £5,500 to Mr L.D. Thomas, Porthcawl’. Notes on the second page of the particulars as to acreage and calculations as to value.\n\nCollection Stephenson & Alexander, Auctioneers and Chartered Surveyors, Records\nDocument reference DSA/6/701 \nTitle Parts of the Llandough Estate\nDate 9 Oct 1924\nExtent 1 booklet and 2 papers fixed to each other\nDescription Auctioneer: Gottwaltz & Perry of 11 High St., Cardiff, in conjunction with Yorwerth and Thomas of High St., Cowbridge.\nParts of the Llandough Estate in the parishes of Llanfair and St Hilary\nOwner: Sidney Hutchinson Byass. [See DSA/10/10 Item 268]\nParts of The Llandough Estate (1500a.) comprising:\nPen-yr-heol, Saer’s, accommodation land near Byrclwydd, Great House, The Herberts, Church Farm, The Rectory Farm, Fish Weir, Gigman Mill, Howe Mill, Prior’s Hill (partly in p. of St. Hilary), Penyrheol Cottage, 1-4 Talbot Terrace and Tithe cottages, St. Marychurch, Forge Cottage near The Herberts, Abernant Cottage opposite Keeper’s Lodge and School Cottage near Llanfair School, the wheelwright’s shop and timber shed on the Herbert’s Corner, freehold lands and gardens all in the p. of Llanfair.\n29 lots.\n2 prints of the two plans, both with markings.\nPencil markings on the particulars.\nSchedule of lands coloured brown on plan `A´ annexed adjacent to the plans added\nOn front cover ‘Stephenson & Alexander Private’ and some pencil notes.\n\nCollection Corbett Family of Cogan Pill Papers\nDocument reference DXJF/64/30 \nTitle Llandough [juxta-Penarth] sketch of former layout of part of village by Mrs. Nancy Buckler of Great House Farm, Llandough, with notes\nDate(s)\nDate n.d. [c. 1950]\nDate range 1945-1955\nLevel Item\nExtent 1 card, 1 paper\n\nA catalogue to the records of the councils and planning committees for Vale of Glamorgan County Borough Council can be viewed online: CVG/C/1/52 , and Vale of Glamorgan Borough Council: DCVG/PL .\n\nNone of the above listed records are held electronically, so we will not be able to provide it to you by email. As you are based in Dinas Powys you are very welcome to visit the Archives to view the planning files and identify any relevant records yourself. We are open to the public Tuesday-Thursday 9:30-12:30, 13:30-16:30. Booking is advised and if you are able to provide a list of the documents you would like to consult we will have them ready for your arrival. If you have not visited us before you will be required to register; for this we ask you bring along two forms of identification - one showing your name (e.g. driving licence, passport) and another showing your address (e.g. a recent bill or official letter).\n\nNote that we will be closed 16-18 June to allow staff to undertake essential work on the collection.\n\nDetails of tenancy can be identified by searching the census, this is held at The National Archives . Ownership can be traced by contacting the Land Registry .\n\nWith regards to assessments carried out by CADW , you should contact them directly.\n\nI hope you find this information useful.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nHannah Price\nArchifydd | Archivist\n\nNodwch fy mod yn gweithio o Ddydd Llun tan Ddydd Iau.  Os hoffwch gysylltu â’r Archifau tu allan i’r oriau yma danfonwch e-bost [email redacted]  | Please note I work Mondays to Thursdays. If you wish to contact the Archives outside these hours please email [email redacted] \nArchifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted] | Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n( [phone redacted]\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.twitter.com/glamarchives\nInstagram: glamarchives\n\nBydd Archifau Morgannwg yn sicrhau ein bod yn cyfathrebu â chi yn yr iaith o'ch dewis, boed hynny'n Gymraeg, yn Saesneg neu'n ddwyieithog cyn belled ag y byddwch yn rhoi gwybod i ni pa well gennych. Rydych yn derbyn y wybodaeth hon yn y Saesneg gan fod hyn wedi ei gofnodi fel eich dewis iaith. Os hoffech chi ddiweddaru'r wybodaeth hon neu ddewis peidio â derbyn y negeseuon e-bost hyn, cysylltwch â ni: [email redacted] . | Glamorgan Archives will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, whether that’s English, Welsh or bilingual as long as you let us know which you prefer. You are receiving this information in English as this is recorded as your language preference. If you would like to update this information or opt out of receiving these emails please contact us at [email redacted] .\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19e8de970db88555","subject":"Request for Preservation of Records – WA231076 / WA240304 (First Registration Files)","name":"Request for Preservation of Records – WA231076 / WA240304 (First Registration Files)","date":"2026-06-03T14:35:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e8de970db88555.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e8de794edda2e0-quest-for-preservation-of-records-wa231076-wa240304-first-registration-files","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e8de794edda2e0","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e8de970db88555.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir or Madam,\nFurther to my ongoing requests concerning first registration files WA231076\nand WA240304, I am writing to request that all relevant records relating to\nthese matters are preserved.\nThis includes, where applicable:\nfirst registration application files and associated bundles\nFR1 forms and supporting title documentation\nexaminer’s notes and internal handling records\nrequisitions, correspondence, and workflow records\nany indexes or metadata relating to file contents\nany archived, scanned, or microfiche versions of the above\nThis request is made on the basis that I am currently engaging with\nstatutory information access routes (including FOI and inspection\nprocedures), and may make further related requests.\nAccordingly, I would be grateful if confirmation could be provided that no\nrelevant records will be destroyed or deleted while these processes are\nongoing or reasonably anticipated.\nThis is not a complaint or request for reconsideration of any decision, but\na request to ensure preservation of relevant records pending lawful\ninformation access.\nYours faithfully,\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19e8c6ff570c0bf0","subject":"Re: last email","name":"Re: last email","date":"2026-06-03T07:43:27Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e8c6ff570c0bf0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e8c6f80bd64bee-last-email","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e8c6f80bd64bee","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e8c6ff570c0bf0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Please ignore my last email.\nIt was not meant for FOI, but another of your departments. Which I have\nmyself forwarded to that relevant department.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Wed, 3 Jun 2026, 04:09 Requester,   wrote:\n\n> Dear Sir / Madam,\n>\n> We are writing to formally request access to inspect the archived first\n> registration application files relating to:\n>\n> WA231076\n> WA240304\n>\n> This request concerns the full first registration case files, including\n> all supporting documentation, correspondence, internal notes, and any\n> associated index map search material.\n>\n> I am specifically requesting permission to:\n> Inspect the physical archived files (or digital scans if the originals are\n> not accessible)\n> Review all documents submitted in support of the applications\n>\n> Review any examiner notes, requisitions, or internal annotations made\n> during processing\n>\n> Identify any records of third-party claims, disputes, objections, or\n> references to adverse occupation or competing claims\n> Confirm whether any such material was present on the file at the time of\n> registration\n> If the files are no longer held in physical form, please confirm:\n>\n> the date and manner of destruction (if applicable), or\n>\n> whether they have been digitised or transferred to another archive location\n> If inspection is not possible, I would be grateful if you could instead\n> provide certified copies of the complete file contents.\n>\n> Please also confirm the procedure for arranging an appointment for\n> inspection, including any identification or fees required.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester and heirs of Mary Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough C/O\n> [address redacted] [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n>"},{"id":"gm-19e8c6c9e41fb0ec","subject":"WA231076 / WA240304 – request to confirm scope of first registration file records","name":"WA231076 / WA240304 – request to confirm scope of first registration file records","date":"2026-06-03T07:39:48Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e8c6c9e41fb0ec.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e8c5f645277041-wa231076-wa240304-request-to-confirm-scope-of-first-registration-file-records","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e8c5f645277041","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e8c6c9e41fb0ec.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs / Madam,\n\nFurther to my previous correspondence regarding first registration files\nWA231076 and WA240304, I am seeking a narrow clarification to ensure my\nunderstanding of the record set is accurate before any further request is\nmade under statutory access routes.\n\nI am seeking confirmation of the composition and scope of the first\nregistration file(s), specifically what material is held, recorded, or\nidentifiable as forming part of the application record at the time of\nregistration.\n\nTo avoid duplication or misunderstanding, could you please confirm the\nfollowing factual points only in relation to the actual file contents held\nby HM Land Registry:\nWhether a complete first registration application file is still held for\nWA231076 and WA240304, including any supporting bundle of documents\nsubmitted at the time of registration.\n\nWhether the file(s) include an index, schedule, or equivalent record\nidentifying the documents that formed part of the application (whether\nretained or not retained).\n\nWhether the file(s) contain any recorded material of any kind (including\ncorrespondence, requisitions, internal notes, or annotations) relating to\nany dispute, objection, or competing claim concerning the property known as\nGreat House Farm / Ty Mawr.\n\nWhether the file(s) contain any notation indicating that documents were\n“not retained”, “copy filed”, or otherwise recorded as not forming part of\nthe permanent archive.\n\nThis request is limited strictly to confirmation of the existence and scope\nof records held, rather than a request for reassessment of historical\nmatters or legal conclusions.\n\nI would be grateful if this clarification can be provided so that any\nsubsequent FOI or inspection request can be properly scoped to the actual\nrecords held.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester Esq.\nHeir & Successor to Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Llandough, Vale of\nGlamorgan C/O [address redacted] [postcode redacted], United Kingdom\n\nOn Tue, 2 Jun 2026, 01:56 Requester, <[email redacted]> wrote:\n\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am writing to request clarification regarding first registration files\n> relating to title WA231076 and WA240304.\n>\n> This request is not a complaint, request for reconsideration, or\n> application for rectification. I am seeking only clarification of the\n> documents and records held on the first registration file(s), and the\n> material relied upon in the registration process.\n>\n> Please confirm and/or provide the following:\n>\n> The full list of documents and evidence held on the first registration\n> file(s) for WA231076 and WA240304, including the application form (FR1),\n> transfer/conveyance deed(s), and any supporting abstract, epitome, or\n> statement of title.\n>\n> Whether any requisitions, objections, cautions, notices, or third-party\n> claims were received or recorded during the first registration process.\n>\n> Whether the file contains any correspondence, notes, or other documents of\n> any description referring to a dispute, competing claim, or challenge\n> concerning Mary Williams / Mary Buckler or Great House Farm / Ty Mawr.\n>\n> Whether any personal documents (including but not limited to identity,\n> marital, or probate records) relating to Mary Williams / Mary Buckler were\n> submitted as part of the application or retained on file, and if so whether\n> they were relied upon in the registration decision.\n>\n> A schedule or index of the documentary evidence relied upon to support\n> first registration, including any statement that copies were not retained\n> or are no longer held.\n>\n> Whether any document referred to in the registration process is noted as\n> “copy filed”, “not retained”, or similarly annotated.\n>\n> If this request is not the appropriate route for access to the above\n> material, please advise on the correct procedure for inspection or\n> obtaining copies of the first registration file contents.\n>\n> Regards,\n>\n> Requester Esq. \n>"},{"id":"gm-19e8c530bebecd78","subject":"Ref: WA231076 /  WA240304","name":"Ref: WA231076 /  WA240304","date":"2026-06-03T07:11:52Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e8c530bebecd78.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e8c522b6abd40e-f-wa231076-wa240304","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e8c522b6abd40e","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e8c530bebecd78.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nWe are writing to formally request access to inspect the archived first\nregistration application files relating to:\n\nWA231076\nWA240304\n\nThis request concerns the full first registration case files, including all\nsupporting documentation, correspondence, internal notes, and any\nassociated index map search material.\n\nI am specifically requesting permission to:\nInspect the physical archived files (or digital scans if the originals are\nnot accessible)\nReview all documents submitted in support of the applications\n\nReview any examiner notes, requisitions, or internal annotations made\nduring processing\n\nIdentify any records of third-party claims, disputes, objections, or\nreferences to adverse occupation or competing claims\nConfirm whether any such material was present on the file at the time of\nregistration\nIf the files are no longer held in physical form, please confirm:\n\nthe date and manner of destruction (if applicable), or\n\nwhether they have been digitised or transferred to another archive location\nIf inspection is not possible, I would be grateful if you could instead\nprovide certified copies of the complete file contents.\n\nPlease also confirm the procedure for arranging an appointment for\ninspection, including any identification or fees required.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester and heirs of Mary Williams of Great House Farm, Llandough C/O\n[address redacted] [postcode redacted], United Kingdom"},{"id":"gm-19e8c5136785a166","subject":"","name":"","date":"2026-06-03T07:09:52Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e8c5136785a166.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e8c4ad3afa8c66","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e8c4ad3afa8c66","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api