utory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n  5.  Any records discussing the age, architectural significance, archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n  6.  Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n  7.  Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or representations seeking preservation of the building.\n  8.  Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nYou will receive a response by 25 June 2026. If you have any queries about this request, please do not hesitate to contact me at the address below.  Please remember to quote the reference number above in any future correspondence (ATISN 27021).\n\nThe request you sent me contains personal information about you - for example, your name and address. The Welsh Government will be the data processor for this information and, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation, it will be processed in order to fulfil our public task and meet our legal obligations under the Act to provide you with a response. We will only use this personal information to deal with your request and any matters which arise as a result of it. We will keep your personal information and all other information relating to your request for three years from the date on which your request is finally closed.  Your personal information will then be disposed of securely.\n\nUnder data protection legislation, you have the right:\n\n\n  *   to be informed of the personal data we hold about you and to access it\n  *   to require us to rectify inaccuracies in that data\n  *   to (in certain circumstances) object to or restrict processing\n  *   for (in certain circumstances) your data to be 'erased'\n  *   to (in certain circumstances) data portability\n  *   to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) who is our independent regulator for data protection\n\nFor further information about the information which the Welsh Government holds and its use, or if you wish to exercise your rights under the GDPR, please see contact details below:\n\nData Protection Officer\nWelsh Government\nCathays Park\nCARDIFF\n[postcode redacted]\nEmail: [email redacted] \n\nThe contact details for the Information Commissioner's Office are:\n\nWycliffe House\nWater Lane\nWilmslow\nCheshire\n[postcode redacted]\nWebsite: www.ico.org.uk \n\nAny information released under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or Environmental Information Regulations 2004 will be listed in the Welsh Government's Disclosure Log (at https://gov.wales/about/open-government/freedom-of-information/responses/?lang=en).\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nMike Weatherhead\n\nArweinydd Tîm Gwaith Achosion / Casework Team Leader\nPolisi a Gwarchod / Policy and Protection\nArolygiaeth yr Amgylchedd Hanesyddol / Historic Environment Inspectorate\nCadw\n\nFrom: Requester  >\nSent: 28 May 2026 06:29\nTo: Freedom of Information Officer  >; Listed Buildings / Adeiladau Rhestredig  >\nSubject: Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n\nDear Freedom of Information Officer,\n\nI am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw concerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr), Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\n\nI request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\n\n  1.  Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n  2.  Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or reports concerning the building.\n  3.  Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or protection of the property.\n  4.  Any records explaining why the building was not added to the statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n  5.  Any records discussing the age, architectural significance, archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n  6.  Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n  7.  Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or representations seeking preservation of the building.\n  8.  Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than an explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\n\nIf any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I would be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the records.\n\nI would prefer the information in electronic form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester Esq. . Heir & Successors of Mary Williams, Great House Farm, Llandough\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice  explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding.\nSganiwyd y neges hon am bob feirws hysbys wrth iddi adael Llywodraeth Cymru. Mae Llywodraeth Cymru yn cymryd o ddifrif yr angen i ddiogelu eich data. Os cysylltwch â Llywodraeth Cymru, mae ein hysbysiad preifatrwydd<\"https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=cy\"> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice  explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-19e86b0757252ef2","subject":"Request for Clarification of Correspondence – Title WA231076","name":"Request for Clarification of Correspondence – Title WA231076","date":"2026-06-02T04:56:11Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e86b0757252ef2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e861826be48ecb-quest-for-clarification-of-correspondence-title-wa231076","scopeTopics":["hmlr"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["hmlr"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e861826be48ecb","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"hmlr","name":"HM Land Registry"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e86b0757252ef2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Ma'am,\n\nI am writing to request clarification regarding first registration files\nrelating to title WA231076 and WA240304.\n\nThis request is not a complaint, request for reconsideration, or\napplication for rectification. I am seeking only clarification of the\ndocuments and records held on the first registration file(s), and the\nmaterial relied upon in the registration process.\n\nPlease confirm and/or provide the following:\n\nThe full list of documents and evidence held on the first registration\nfile(s) for WA231076 and WA240304, including the application form (FR1),\ntransfer/conveyance deed(s), and any supporting abstract, epitome, or\nstatement of title.\n\nWhether any requisitions, objections, cautions, notices, or third-party\nclaims were received or recorded during the first registration process.\n\nWhether the file contains any correspondence, notes, or other documents of\nany description referring to a dispute, competing claim, or challenge\nconcerning Mary Williams / Mary Buckler or Great House Farm / Ty Mawr.\n\nWhether any personal documents (including but not limited to identity,\nmarital, or probate records) relating to Mary Williams / Mary Buckler were\nsubmitted as part of the application or retained on file, and if so whether\nthey were relied upon in the registration decision.\n\nA schedule or index of the documentary evidence relied upon to support\nfirst registration, including any statement that copies were not retained\nor are no longer held.\n\nWhether any document referred to in the registration process is noted as\n“copy filed”, “not retained”, or similarly annotated.\n\nIf this request is not the appropriate route for access to the above\nmaterial, please advise on the correct procedure for inspection or\nobtaining copies of the first registration file contents.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester Esq. "},{"id":"gm-19e853c4c0a17b82","subject":"Re: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","name":"Re: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-06-01T22:09:41Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e853c4c0a17b82.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-tenancy-records-f","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e853c4c0a17b82.json","textStatus":"available","text":"What is your name please?\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Mon, 1 Jun 2026, 10:52 FOI Unit,   wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you for the below. We note its contents in relation to Freedom of\n> Information however, we wrote to you (copy attached) seeking clarification\n> on a previous request received by you which relates to the same matter.\n>\n>\n>\n> We are unable to progress your request until this clarification has been\n> received.\n>\n>\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Information Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\n>\n> Director's Office - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\n>\n> tel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\n>\n> e-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you\n> really need to.*\n>\n> *Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod\n> gwir angen.*\n>\n>\n>\n> Visit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n>\n> Ewch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n>  \n>\n> Follow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 29 May 2026 19:48\n> *To:* Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg  \n> *Subject:* FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic\n> Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for\n> Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)\n>\n>\n>\n> *LEGAL NOTICE TO RECIPIENTS:*\n>\n> *Take notice that this request is issued in anticipation of formal legal\n> proceedings and the filing of an official report regarding systemic\n> institutional fraud, land misconduct, and the unlawful concealment of\n> historic preservation data. You are under a strict legal duty to preserve\n> all physical and electronic records, metadata, correspondence, maps, and\n> erased files relating to this site. Any spoliation, deletion, or\n> withholding of data will be cited in subsequent court filings.*\n>\n> Dear Freedom of Information Officer,\n>\n> *RE: Information Request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the\n> Environmental Information Regulations 2004*\n>\n> I am writing to request access to historical records, internal\n> correspondence, planning briefs, and assessments held by your organization\n> regarding *Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth/Cardiff* (demolished\n> December 1988), and the historical occupancy of the *Buckler family*.\n>\n> *Statutory Mandate on Accessibility & Charging Fees:*\n> I am aware that previous attempts to locate this data have resulted in\n> directives to visit physical archives in person or use paywalled,\n> commercial third-party web portals. Please be advised of the following\n> statutory obligations:\n>\n>    1. Under *EIR Regulation 8*, fees cannot act as an unreasonable\n>    barrier or deterrent to access. Because my family was historically\n>    displaced from this site and I am executing this request remotely, forcing\n>    physical attendance or demanding payment constitutes an unlawful obstacle.\n>    2. Public authorities are required to supply information in the format\n>    requested. I require all documents to be delivered *digitally via\n>    email attachment or secure electronic download link, free of charge*,\n>    as specified by the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) guidelines for\n>    data already held electronically.\n>\n> Please provide all recorded information matching the following points:\n>\n> *1. Tenant/Ownership Identification and the 1880 Report*\n>\n>    - Any documents, archival notes, or registry indexes citing the\n>    William/ *Buckler family line* (who occupied and farmed the house\n>    across four generations).\n>    - Clarification on whether my family members were formally cited as\n>    the legal owners, long-term tenants, or registered reporters of the 1880\n>    discovery under the dining room floor.\n>    - Any explicit records indicating *gaps, deleted metadata, or missing\n>    volumes* in your authority’s archive concerning the tenancy,\n>    land-dispute maps, or agricultural heritage of Great House Farm between\n>    1950 and 1989.\n>\n> *2. Statutory Protection and Cadw’s Assessments*\n>\n>    - Given that the site's extreme archaeological value (a\n>    1st-to-4th-century Roman precursor villa and a massive early medieval\n>    monastic settlement) was verified by rescue operations as early as 1979,\n>    what are the recorded reasons why *Cadw failed to place a statutory\n>    Schedule or Protection Order* on the standing fabric of Great House\n>    Farm before its demolition?\n>    - All internal correspondence, risk assessments, or ministerial briefs\n>    evaluating the preservation value of the sub-medieval direct-entry\n>    farmhouse core before it was levelled.\n>\n> *3. Planning Approvals and Local Authority Governance*\n>\n>    - All minutes, planning committee files, and consultation responses\n>    from the local authority that granted planning permission and housing\n>    development rights on this specific acreage.\n>    - Direct information explaining *how the council approved planning\n>    permission* for a private housing development in light of the\n>    documented historical evidence surrounding the immediate parish boundary.\n>\n> *4. Institutional Concealment and Historical \"Ignorance\"*\n>\n>    - Records showing exactly *where and at what stage of the planning\n>    process this archaeological evidence should have been brought up but was\n>    not*, which ultimately allowed developers and public bodies to claim\n>    they were unaware of the land's deep significance until after the farmhouse\n>    was destroyed and housing development began.\n>    - Any environmental impact assessments, historic environment register\n>    (HER) lookups, or developer briefs filed between 1980 and 1990 regarding\n>    the footprint of Great House Farm.\n>\n> If any part of this request is refused under the guise of commercial\n> sensitivity or archival limitations, you are required by law to state the\n> exact statutory exemption applied and provide a formal internal review\n> pathway.\n>\n> I expect your response within the statutory 20-working-day timeframe.\n>\n> Kind regards,\n>\n> *Requester *\n> *[address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan*\n>\n>\n>\n> ---------- Forwarded message ----------\n> From: FOI Unit 