ty’s archive concerning the tenancy, land-dispute\n   maps, or agricultural heritage of Great House Farm between 1950 and 1989.\n\n2. Statutory Protection and Cadw’s Assessments\n\n   - Given that the site's extreme archaeological value (a\n   1st-to-4th-century Roman precursor villa and a massive early medieval\n   monastic settlement) was verified by rescue operations as early as 1979,\n   what are the recorded reasons why Cadw failed to place a statutory\n   Schedule or Protection Order on the standing fabric of Great House Farm\n   before its demolition?\n   - All internal correspondence, risk assessments, or ministerial briefs\n   evaluating the preservation value of the sub-medieval direct-entry\n   farmhouse core before it was levelled.\n\n3. Planning Approvals and Local Authority Governance\n\n   - All minutes, planning committee files, and consultation responses from\n   the local authority that granted planning permission and housing\n   development rights on this specific acreage.\n   - Direct information explaining how the council approved planning\n   permission for a private housing development in light of the documented\n   historical evidence surrounding the immediate parish boundary.\n\n4. Institutional Concealment and Historical \"Ignorance\"\n\n   - Records showing exactly where and at what stage of the planning\n   process this archaeological evidence should have been brought up\nbut was not,\n   which ultimately allowed developers and public bodies to claim they were\n   unaware of the land's deep significance until after the farmhouse was\n   destroyed and housing development began.\n   - Any environmental impact assessments, historic environment register\n   (HER) lookups, or developer briefs filed between 1980 and 1990 regarding\n   the footprint of Great House Farm.\n\nIf any part of this request is refused under the guise of commercial\nsensitivity or archival limitations, you are required by law to state the\nexact statutory exemption applied and provide a formal internal review\npathway.\nI expect your response within the statutory 20-working-day timeframe.\nKind regards,\n*Requester *\n*[address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan*"},{"id":"gm-19e750cbad1114c0","subject":"Automatic reply: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","name":"Automatic reply: FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-05-29T18:43:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e750cbad1114c0.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e750cbad1114c0-automatic-reply-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-t","scopeTopics":["heneb"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["heneb"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e750cbad1114c0","direction":"received","from":"Barbara Rees","institutions":[{"id":"heneb","name":"Heneb (formerly GGAT) / Historic Environment Record"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e750cbad1114c0.json","textStatus":"available","text":"My next working day is Wednesday, 10th June 2026.\n\nDiolch."},{"id":"gm-19e750c31e2fcf5e","subject":"FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","name":"FORMAL DISCLOSURE NOTICE & LITIGATION HOLD: Historic Significance, Planning Approvals, and Displaced Family Tenancy Records for Great House Farm, Llandough (FOIA/EIR Request)","date":"2026-05-29T18:43:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e750c31e2fcf5e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9-formal-disclosure-notice-litigation-hold-historic-significance-planning-approvals-and-displaced-family-tenancy-records-f","scopeTopics":["cadw","museum","vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw","museum","vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e75029f91a5bd9","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"},{"id":"museum","name":"Amgueddfa Cymru - Museum Wales"},{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e750c31e2fcf5e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"LEGAL NOTICE TO RECIPIENTS:\n*Take notice that this request is issued in anticipation of formal legal\nproceedings and the filing of an official report regarding systemic\ninstitutional fraud, land misconduct, and the unlawful concealment of\nhistoric preservation data. You are under a strict legal duty to preserve\nall physical and electronic records, metadata, correspondence, maps, and\nerased files relating to this site. Any spoliation, deletion, or\nwithholding of data will be cited in subsequent court filings.*\nDear Freedom of Information Officer,\nRE: Information Request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and the\nEnvironmental Information Regulations 2004\nI am writing to request access to historical records, internal\ncorrespondence, planning briefs, and assessments held by your organization\nregarding Great House Farm, Llandough, near Penarth/Cardiff (demolished\nDecember 1988), and the historical occupancy of the Buckler family.\nStatutory Mandate on Accessibility & Charging Fees:\nI am aware that previous attempts to locate this data have resulted in\ndirectives to visit physical archives in person or use paywalled,\ncommercial third-party web portals. Please be advised of the following\nstatutory obligations:\n\n   1. Under EIR Regulation 8, fees cannot act as an unreasonable barrier or\n   deterrent to access. Because my family was historically displaced from this\n   site and I am executing this request remotely, forcing physical attendance\n   or demanding payment constitutes an unlawful obstacle.\n   2. Public authorities are required to supply information in the format\n   requested. I require all documents to be delivered digitally via email\n   attachment or secure electronic download link, free of charge, as\n   specified by the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) guidelines for\n   data already held electronically.\n\nPlease provide all recorded information matching the following points:\n1. Tenant/Ownership Identification and the 1880 Report\n\n   - Any documents, archival notes, or registry indexes citing the\nWilliam/ Buckler\n   family line (who occupied and farmed the house across four generations).\n   - Clarification on whether my family members were formally cited as the\n   legal owners, long-term tenants, or registered reporters of the 1880\n   discovery under the dining room floor.\n   - Any explicit records indicating gaps, deleted metadata, or missing\n   volumes in your authority’s archive concerning the tenancy, land-dispute\n   maps, or agricultural heritage of Great House Farm between 1950 and 1989.\n\n2. Statutory Protection and Cadw’s Assessments\n\n   - Given that the site's extreme archaeological value (a\n   1st-to-4th-century Roman precursor villa and a massive early medieval\n   monastic settlement) was verified by rescue operations as early as 1979,\n   what are the recorded reasons why Cadw failed to place a statutory\n   Schedule or Protection Order on the standing fabric of Great House Farm\n   before its demolition?\n   - All internal correspondence, risk assessments, or ministerial briefs\n   evaluating the preservation value of the sub-medieval direct-entry\n   farmhouse core before it was levelled.\n\n3. Planning Approvals and Local Authority Governance\n\n   - All minutes, planning committee files, and consultation responses from\n   the local authority that granted planning permission and housing\n   development rights on this specific acreage.\n   - Direct information explaining how the council approved planning\n   permission for a private housing development in light of the documented\n   historical evidence surrounding the immediate parish boundary.\n\n4. Institutional Concealment and Historical \"Ignorance\"\n\n   - Records showing exactly where and at what stage of the planning\n   process this archaeological evidence should have been brought up\nbut was not,\n   which ultimately allowed developers and public bodies to claim they were\n   unaware of the land's deep significance until after the farmhouse was\n   destroyed and housing development began.\n   - Any environmental impact assessments, historic environment register\n   (HER) lookups, or developer briefs filed between 1980 and 1990 regarding\n   the footprint of Great House Farm.\n\nIf any part of this request is refused under the guise of commercial\nsensitivity or archival limitations, you are required by law to state the\nexact statutory exemption applied and provide a formal internal review\npathway.\nI expect your response within the statutory 20-working-day timeframe.\nKind regards,\n*Requester *\n*[address redacted], Vale of Glamorgan*\n------------------------------\nOnce you send this, the 20-working-day statutory clock begins. If you want,\nI can help you draft a specific complaint letter template to the\nInformation Commissioner's Office (ICO) in case they try to ignore this\nnotice or try to charge you anyway. Would that be useful for your legal\npreparation?"},{"id":"gm-19e746788a06645c","subject":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","name":"New response to your FOI request - 1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family","date":"2026-05-29T15:43:22Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e746788a06645c.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e746788a06645c-new-response-to-your-foi-request-1988-dispossession-of-great-house-farm-llandough-from-the-williams-buckler-family","scopeTopics":["mod"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mod"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e746788a06645c","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"mod","name":"Ministry of Defence"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e746788a06645c.json","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request '1988 Dispossession of Great House Farm, Llandough from the Williams/ Buckler Family' that you made to Ministry of Defence.\n\nTo view the response, click on the link below.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/1988_dispossession_of_great_hous?nocache=incoming-3431830#incoming-3431830\n\nWhen you get there, please update the status to say if the response contains any useful information.\n\nAlthough all responses are automatically published, we depend on you, the original requester, to evaluate them.\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhatDoTheyKnow is a project of mySociety run by a small team of staff and\ndedicated volunteers.\n\nmySociety is a charity that believes that information should be accessible to everyone.\nIf this is important to you, please consider donating to help us do more:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/donate\n\nFind out more about how we handle your data at:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/help/privacy\n\nmySociety is a registered charity in England and Wales (1076346), and a limited\ncompany (03277032)"},{"id":"gm-19e734bf04ad6799","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-29T10:33:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e734bf04ad6799.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c-great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e734bf04ad6799.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ref: 2026/2370\n\nDear Requester,\n\nThank you for your further email.\n\nFull details of our holdings can be found on our catalogue so you are welcome to search the records we hold to see if anything may be of use to you: Glamorgan Archives Catalogue . If you come across anything that you think might help we would be pleased to provide a quote for producing digital copies of the records for you.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nLouise Hunt\nArchifydd / Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg / Glamorgan Archives\nClos Parc Morgannwg\nLecwydd / Leckwith\nCaerdydd / Cardiff\n[postcode redacted]\n\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] \n\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk/  www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.instagram.com/glamarchives \n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19e705a9ba774e00","subject":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Re: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-28T20:50:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e705a9ba774e00.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c-great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e705a9ba774e00.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks Katie,\nI am at the Welsh Settlement in Argentina. Where I will be safer, seeing as\nevery member in my family which challenged the official narrative here are\ndead. Any assistance appreciated. I believe my disabled widow nan inherited\nthe fee simple absolute (and Manorial) title from the Marquess  of Bute, a\ndeal family before us made with Daniel Thomas and the Marquess of Bute. I\nbelieve Marconi staying with us while inventing the radio or boxer\n'Peerless' Jim Driscoll fighting his first boxing match at our barns, or\nwhen we did a tree planting ceremony (customary when obtaining land) with\nthe whole town there to witness and photo evidence in the nations\ncollection of wales, it was because we'd become the absolute and manorial\ntitle holders. My nan maintained this position in all court proceedings and\nin the local press. Like a 1978 interview and article which was suppressed.\nI also noticed ITV quietly declassified covering this 1988 story. Much like\nlittle to no evidence of the 1974 news coverage exists (which the courts\ndocument as having occured, wherby the public and press sided with my nan).\nAnd more suppressed evidence exists which I am trying to get declassified\ntoo. It appears her title was stolen and ended up in the hands of Western\nGround Rents and later BP who bought it from them. Who then tried and\nfailed to get my widow pensioner nan to play the role of her tenant and pay\nthem. Failing this they appear to have replaced us and the 800 year old\nfarmhouse they demolished, with 23 houses and people who would pay their\namortizations and virtual/ lifetime freeholds.   I am simply trying to put\ntogether this story which is evidently supressed and fragmented and has\ngaps. This is not just for my family , but the injustice to us indigenous\nand our history and herritage by the British State and BP is horrific. We\nappear to have been erazed of the face of the planet, but we're not . We're\nstill here Yma o Hyd and we seek answers. So if you could kindly do\neverything in your power to assist, so that this matter is put to rest I'd\nappreciate. Regards, Requester\n\n>\n>\n> Dear Requester\n>\n>\n>\n> Many thanks for your email received onto our system on 27 May 2026\n>\n>\n>\n> I have taken a look at our catalogue and we do not have a petition\n> relating to ‘Great House’ or Ty Mawr’ farm. If you are interested in\n> finding other documents that relate you can carry out searches on our\n> catalogue, Glamorgan Archives Catalogue <https://glamorgan.epexio.com/en/>.\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> If you do find something that you would like to see, you are welcome to\n> view it for free at Glamorgan Archives. We are open Tuesday-Thursday,\n> 0930-1230 and 1330-1630. Please book an appointment in advance to ensure\n> that there is space to accommodate you in the searchroom.\n>\n>\n>\n> Please let me know if you have any further queries\n>\n>\n>\n> Best wishes\n>\n>\n>\n> Katie\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Katie Finn\n>\n> Archifydd | Archivist\n>\n>\n>\n> Archifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted] | Glamorgan\n> Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n>\n> ( [phone redacted]\n>\n> www.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk\n> <http://www.glamro.gov.uk/>\n>\n> www.facebook.com/glamarchives\n>\n> www.twitter.com/glamarchives\n>\n> Instagram: glamarchives\n>\n>\n>\n> *Bydd Archifau Morgannwg yn sicrhau ein bod yn cyfathrebu â chi yn yr\n> iaith o'ch dewis, boed hynny'n Gymraeg, yn Saesneg neu'n ddwyieithog cyn\n> belled ag y byddwch yn rhoi gwybod i ni pa well gennych. Rydych yn derbyn y\n> wybodaeth hon yn y Saesneg gan fod hyn wedi ei gofnodi fel eich dewis\n> iaith. Os hoffech chi ddiweddaru'r wybodaeth hon neu ddewis peidio â derbyn\n> y negeseuon e-bost hyn, cysylltwch â ni: [email redacted]\n> <[email redacted]>. *| *Glamorgan Archives will ensure that we\n> communicate with you in the language of your choice, whether that’s\n> English, Welsh or bilingual as long as you let us know which you prefer.\n> You are receiving this information in English as this is recorded as your\n> language preference. If you would like to update this information or opt\n> out of receiving these emails please contact us at [email redacted]\n> <[email redacted]>.*\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n> *Sent:* 26 May 2026 17:42\n> *To:* Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg <[email redacted]>\n> *Subject:* Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\n>\n>\n>\n> *EXTERNAL:* This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care\n> when clicking links.\n> *ALLANOL:* Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal\n> wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sirs/Ma'am, Please cite the link displaying the record of petition of\n> demolition of great house farm in Llandough near Penarth. I have a\n> newspaper article from 1978 citing the petition. It says 1,000 signatures,\n> in other references it says 1700. Regards, Requester\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> The Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We\n> will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as\n> long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not\n> lead to delay.\n>\n> Privileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If\n> you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for\n> delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this\n> message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly\n> notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your\n> employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.\n> Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not\n> relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of\n> Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it. All e-mail\n> sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils\n> Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other\n> than the addressee.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>\n> Mae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog.\n> Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni\n> pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n>\n> Mae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y\n> neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r\n> neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges.\n> Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy\n> e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi\n> neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon.\n> Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y\n> neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir\n> Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff\n> unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan\n> system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu\n> harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n>\n> **********************************************************************\n>"},{"id":"gm-19e6f0e4a747d5bc","subject":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RC26-0205 - Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-28T14:47:37Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e6f0e4a747d5bc.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e6f0e4a747d5bc-rc26-0205-great-house-farm-williams-buckler-family-llandough-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e6f0e4a747d5bc","direction":"received","from":"Dr Adam Coward","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC26-0205"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e6f0e4a747d5bc.json","attachments":[{"name":"LES08 Order Form 2021.docx","title":"RC26-0205 order form 2021","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les08-order-form-2021.docx","mime":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","bytes":142468,"sha256":"291e3be8baf22b8f7e538ffd565e2a16462b66f5679c94ac3d72093816a18335"},{"name":"LES16 Price List 2026.pdf","title":"RC26-0205 price list 2026","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les16-price-list-2026.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":304904,"sha256":"08666a9e23e13caa10704047249ed2130af5ce2169c2136f4ae6e5f967d3c4a7"},{"name":"LES17 Licence Fees 2026.pdf","title":"RC26-0205 licence fees 2026","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les17-licence-fees-2026.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":315620,"sha256":"6c2e0f5ed166bd822b1b3ead71cf29341ab4c352f04651e6c88149e17526a37e"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThank you for your enquiry. As noted in my email of 26 November last, while we cannot advise you on a legal case or undertake a review of historical decisions, we do hold information and archives related to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nThe site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n\nWe hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit. However, I have located an electronic copy of Archive Number 6524751, which can be accessed here: https://www.walesher1974.org/her/app/php/herumd.php?group=GGAT&level=3&docid=301361628\n\nWhile it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research. Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n\nFinally, I have confirmed with our Records Manager that we do not hold any correspondence related to the site.\n\nThank you again for your enquiry.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAdam Coward\n\n\n\nDr Adam Coward\n Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 20 May 2026 22:11\nTo: unclehowell <[email redacted]>\nSubject: Great House Farm, Williams/ Buckler Family, Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan\n\n\nSir / Madam,\n\nTo all those whom it concerns, BCC'd into this email.\n\nI write to request disclosure under the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and, where applicable, the Environmental Information Regulations 2004.\n\nThis request concerns Great House Farm / Ty Mawr (Great House), Llandough, associated estate lands, historic occupation and related heritage records. My family is Buckler and before that Williams, and we occupied Great House Farm from 1667 until our forceful dispossession of it in 1988.  Without our ownership ever having been estiguished and without BP ever having a ruling of ownership, only possession.\n\nIt's alledged our fee simple absolute and manorial title was stolen. And when BP registered our lands in their names in 1982, with our stolen title, my nan who challenged this all her life, during the 2 week land registry window to challenge BP's registration, which they achieved via purgergy and document/ identity fraud, she conveniently died. As my father did after his appeal of the 1987 mistake ruling was mistakely dismissed and his ECHR request blocked and home abruptly demolished, which he was prevented from stopping having been hospitalised and arrested without charges by armed force officers and possible SAS.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/0eXOoj7eUCo?si=hcgSA2pFgEE943HG\n\nI understand records may exist within the National Monuments Record of Wales, Historic Environment Record archives, archaeological consultations and planning files, including references already identified as:\n\n* Great House Farm HER site entry - GGAT03586s\n* Land at Great House Farm HER event entry - GGATE003872\n* The 1990 archaeological assessment commissioned by BP Properties Ltd.\n\nPlease provide copies of, or access to:\n\n  1.  All records concerning Great House Farm / Ty Mawr / Great House Estate, Llandough including:\n\n* surveys\n* reports\n* site notes\n* photographs\n* maps\n* aerial imagery\n* GIS layers\n* archive material\n* annotations\n* title references\n* occupancy references\n* landscape records\n* archaeological observations.\n\n  1.  All internal and external correspondence involving:\n\n* RCAHMW / NMRW\n* Cadw\n* GGAT / Heneb\n* Vale of Glamorgan Council\n* BP Properties Ltd\n* developers\n* planning authorities\n* landowners, estate representatives or consultants.\n\n  1.  Any documents discussing:\n\n* estate ownership\n* occupation history\n* family occupation or association\n* agricultural use\n* commemorative tree planting or memorial planting\n* estate boundaries\n* title history\n* acquisition history\n* disputes concerning ownership, heritage status or land use\n* estate restructuring, extinguishment, compulsory acquisition or title alteration.\n\n  1.  Copies of all material linked to GGAT03586s and GGATE003872, including the archaeological assessment and associated correspondence.\n  2.  Any records identifying historic occupants, proprietors, tenants or family associations, including references to the Williams family where present within archives.\n  3.  Metadata identifying file creators, accession history, provenance, dates and retention schedules.\n  4.  File indexes, archive references or schedules identifying further related material not already listed.\n\nPlease provide information electronically where possible.\n\nIf any material is withheld, please identify the exemption relied upon and provide the public interest assessment.\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nRequester\n\n[address redacted]\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAttachments (3)\n- LES08 Order Form 2021.docx (application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document, 139 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les08-order-form-2021.docx\n- LES16 Price List 2026.pdf (application/pdf, 298 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les16-price-list-2026.pdf\n- LES17 Licence Fees 2026.pdf (application/pdf, 308 KB): https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/foi/2026-05-28_rcahmw_rc26-0205_les17-licence-fees-2026.pdf"},{"id":"gm-19e6ee02fd184d16","subject":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"RE: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-28T13:57:21Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e6ee02fd184d16.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c-great-house-farm-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["glamorgan"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["glamorgan"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e65254e89ffc8c","direction":"received","from":"Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg","institutions":[{"id":"glamorgan","name":"Glamorgan Archives"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e6ee02fd184d16.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Ref 2026/2336\n\nDear Requester\n\nMany thanks for your email received onto our system on 27 May 2026\n\nI have taken a look at our catalogue and we do not have a petition relating to ‘Great House’ or Ty Mawr’ farm. If you are interested in finding other documents that relate you can carry out searches on our catalogue, Glamorgan Archives Catalogue .\n\nIf you do find something that you would like to see, you are welcome to view it for free at Glamorgan Archives. We are open Tuesday-Thursday, 0930-1230 and 1330-1630. Please book an appointment in advance to ensure that there is space to accommodate you in the searchroom.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any further queries\n\nBest wishes\n\nKatie\n\n\nKatie Finn\nArchifydd | Archivist\n\nArchifau Morgannwg, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Lecwydd, Caerdydd [postcode redacted] | Glamorgan Archives, Clos Parc Morgannwg, Leckwith, Cardiff [postcode redacted]\n( [phone redacted]\nwww.archifaumorgannwg.gov.uk / www.glamarchives.gov.uk \nwww.facebook.com/glamarchives \nwww.twitter.com/glamarchives\nInstagram: glamarchives\n\nBydd Archifau Morgannwg yn sicrhau ein bod yn cyfathrebu â chi yn yr iaith o'ch dewis, boed hynny'n Gymraeg, yn Saesneg neu'n ddwyieithog cyn belled ag y byddwch yn rhoi gwybod i ni pa well gennych. Rydych yn derbyn y wybodaeth hon yn y Saesneg gan fod hyn wedi ei gofnodi fel eich dewis iaith. Os hoffech chi ddiweddaru'r wybodaeth hon neu ddewis peidio â derbyn y negeseuon e-bost hyn, cysylltwch â ni: [email redacted] . | Glamorgan Archives will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, whether that’s English, Welsh or bilingual as long as you let us know which you prefer. You are receiving this information in English as this is recorded as your language preference. If you would like to update this information or opt out of receiving these emails please contact us at [email redacted] .\n\n\n\nFrom: Requester  \nSent: 26 May 2026 17:42\nTo: Glamro / Swyddfa Cofnodion Morgannwg  \nSubject: Great House Farm, Llandough, Nr Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan\n\nEXTERNAL: This email originated from outside Cardiff Council, take care when clicking links.\nALLANOL: Daw'r e-bost hwn o'r tu allan i Gyngor Caerdydd, cymerwch ofal wrth glicio ar ddolenni.\n\nSirs/Ma'am, Please cite the link displaying the record of petition of demolition of great house farm in Llandough near Penarth. I have a newspaper article from 1978 citing the petition. It says 1,000 signatures, in other references it says 1700. Regards, Requester\n\n**********************************************************************\nThe Council welcomes correspondence in Welsh, English or bilingually. We will ensure that we communicate with you in the language of your choice, as long as you let us know which you prefer. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to delay.\n\nPrivileged/Confidential Information may be contained in this message. If you are not the addressee indicated in this message (or responsible for delivery of the message to such person), you may not copy or deliver this message to anyone. In such case, you should destroy this message and kindly notify the sender by reply email. Please advise immediately if you or your employer does not consent to Internet email for messages of this kind.  Opinions, conclusions and other information in this message that do not relate to the official business of the Council of the City and County of Cardiff shall be understood as neither given nor endorsed by it.  All e-mail sent to or from this address will be processed by Cardiff County Councils Corporate E-mail system and may be subject to scrutiny by someone other than the addressee.\n**********************************************************************\nMae’r Cyngor yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg, Saesneg neu’n ddwyieithog. Byddwn yn cyfathrebu â chi yn ôl eich dewis, dim ond i chi roi gwybod i ni pa un sydd well gennych. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi.\n\nMae'n bosibl bod gwybodaeth gyfrinachol yn y neges hon. Os na chyfeirir y neges atoch chi'n benodol (neu os nad ydych chi'n gyfrifol am drosglwyddo'r neges i'r person a enwir), yna ni chewch gopio na throsglwyddo'r neges. Mewn achos o'r fath, dylech ddinistrio'r neges a hysbysu'r anfonwr drwy e-bost ar unwaith. Rhowch wybod i'r anfonydd ar unwaith os nad ydych chi neu eich cyflogydd yn caniatau e-bost y Rhyngrwyd am negeseuon fel hon. Rhaid deall nad yw'r safbwyntiau, y casgliadau a'r wybodaeth arall yn y neges hon nad ydynt yn cyfeirio at fusnes swyddogol Cyngor Dinas a Sir Caerdydd yn cynrychioli barn y Cyngor Sir nad yn cael sel ei fendith. Caiff unrhyw negeseuon a anfonir at, neu o'r cyfeiriad e-bost hwn eu prosesu gan system E-bost Gorfforaethol Cyngor Sir Caerdydd a gallant gael eu harchwilio gan rywun heblaw'r person a enwir.\n**********************************************************************"},{"id":"gm-19e6e41dcb8faf97","subject":"Clarification required - FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00210772","name":"Clarification required - FOI/EIR request - Case Ref/ 00210772","date":"2026-05-28T11:04:26Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e6e41dcb8faf97.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e6e41dcb8faf97-clarification-required-foi-eir-request