w.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n\n \n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n\nFollow us on Twitter /Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n\n \n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-19e6d0f67fdd15d6","subject":"Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-28T05:29:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e6d0f67fdd15d6.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e6d0b384495afa-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e6d0b384495afa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e6d0f67fdd15d6.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Freedom of Information Officer,\n\nI am requesting information held by the Welsh Government and/or Cadw\nconcerning Great House Farm (also known as Great House or Ty Mawr),\nLlandough, Vale of Glamorgan, prior to its demolition in 1988.\n\nI request copies of any recorded information held relating to:\n\n   1. Any consideration of the property for statutory listing.\n   2. Any listing assessments, surveys, inspections, recommendations or\n   reports concerning the building.\n   3. Any correspondence between Cadw, Welsh Office officials, local\n   authorities, conservation bodies, archaeological organisations or owners\n   concerning the historic significance, preservation, demolition or\n   protection of the property.\n   4. Any records explaining why the building was not added to the\n   statutory list of buildings of special architectural or historic interest.\n   5. Any records discussing the age, architectural significance,\n   archaeological significance or surviving historic fabric of the building.\n   6. Any records concerning emergency listing, spot-listing, preservation\n   notices or other forms of protection considered for the property.\n   7. Any records held relating to public campaigns, petitions or\n   representations seeking preservation of the building.\n   8. Any photographs, plans, surveys or architectural records held by Cadw\n   or the Welsh Government relating to Great House Farm.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt, I am seeking recorded information rather than\nan explanation or opinion created for the purpose of this request.\n\nIf any of the requested information is held by another public authority, I\nwould be grateful if you could advise which authority is likely to hold the\nrecords.\n\nI would prefer the information in electronic form.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nRequester Esq. . Heir & Successors of Mary Williams,\nGreat House Farm, Llandough"},{"id":"gm-19e6d0e9c0d4c68d","subject":"Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","name":"Great House Farm/ Church View Close, Llandough, nr. Penarth, Vale of Glamorgan","date":"2026-05-28T05:28:54Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e6d0e9c0d4c68d.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e6d0b384495afa-great-house-farm-church-view-close-llandough-nr-penarth-vale-of-glamorgan","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classific