ernment-privacy-notice/?lang=cy\"> yn esbonio sut rydym yn defnyddio eich gwybodaeth a sut rydym yn diogelu eich preifatrwydd. Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg. Byddwn yn anfon ateb yn Gymraeg i ohebiaeth a dderbynnir yn Gymraeg ac ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn arwain at oedi. ----------------- On leaving the Welsh Government this email was scanned for all known viruses. The Welsh Government takes the protection of your data seriously. If you contact the Welsh Government then our Privacy Notice<https://gov.wales/about/welsh-government-privacy-notice/?lang=en> explains how we use your information and the ways in which we protect your privacy. We welcome receiving correspondence in Welsh. Any correspondence received in Welsh will be answered in Welsh and corresponding in Welsh will not lead to a delay in responding."},{"id":"gm-19e34218ade65c61","subject":"BP vs Buckler, Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"BP vs Buckler, Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2026-05-17T04:11:13Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e34218ade65c61.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e341a533604469-bp-vs-buckler-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e341a533604469","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e34218ade65c61.json","textStatus":"available","text":"To whom it may concern,\n\nI am writing as the child of [member of the public] and William (“Billy”) Buckler\nregarding the destruction of Great House Farm, Llandough, and the\nlong-running dispute surrounding BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987].\n\nI have compiled a substantial historical archive, including newspaper\nreports, court references, family testimony, archaeological material,\nestate history, and public records relating to Great House Farm (“Ty\nMawr”), a site associated with medieval, monastic, and Roman occupation.\n\nThe archive is currently being made into a website at:\n\nbpvsbuckler.datro.xyz\n\nThe material raises serious unresolved questions regarding:\n\n• The treatment of us Williams/Buckler family’s longstanding occupation and\nasserted ownership claims. • The repeated use of possession proceedings\nwithout a full adjudication of superior title. • Missing or allegedly\nsuppressed title documentation connected to Bute estate transfers and later\ntransactions. • The demolition of an allegedly medieval structure during an\nactive heritage controversy. • Whether the archaeological significance of\nthe site was fully disclosed during planning and demolition processes. •\nThe wider public interest and cultural significance of the site and its\ndestruction.\n\nIt's looking to me like my family actually did obtain fee simple absolute\nand manorial title. Then it was stolen and attempts were made by the\npossessor of the stolen title, to make my family lessee's / tenants as we\nwere when we were on the virtual freehold (999 year lease) aquired in 1667.\nThereafter it appears to be a death of a thousand cuts of proceedural\nunfairness, audacity, fraud, court \"mistakes\" , purgery and more.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4GXmR7mAas0?feature=shared\n\nContemporaneous newspaper coverage from the 1970s and 1980s demonstrates\nthat these concerns were publicly known at the time, including heritage\nobjections, petitions, and public claims of ancestral ownership.\n\nI am requesting:\n\n   1. Review and preservation consideration of all surviving records\n   connected to Great House Farm.\n   2. Clarification as to whether any formal heritage review or\n   investigation into the demolition process was ever completed.\n   3. Guidance regarding access to archival and planning materials relevant\n   to the site.\n   4. Consideration of whether this matter warrants renewed historical or\n   heritage examination.\n\nI appreciate that some claims remain disputed or unproven, and I am not\nasking recipients to accept every allegation as established fact. However,\nI believe the totality of the historical material warrants serious review\nrather than dismissal.\n\nI would be grateful for acknowledgement of receipt and guidance on the\nappropriate next steps.\n\nKind regards,\n\n\nRequester Esq. \n\nManor of Llandough, Vale of Glamorgan"},{"id":"gm-19e25a1176cfb6e2","subject":"Our Reference: LPB/26/0781","name":"Our Reference: LPB/26/0781","date":"2026-05-14T08:36:04Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19e25a1176cfb6e2.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19e25a1176cfb6e2-our-reference-lpb-26-0781","scopeTopics":["swp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["swp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19e25a1176cfb6e2","direction":"received","from":"South Wales Police Commissioner - GM","institutions":[{"id":"swp","name":"South Wales Police"}],"refs":["0781"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19e25a1176cfb6e2.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester,\n\nThank you for your e-mail received 10 May 2026, addressed to the South Wales Police and Crime Commissioner.\n\nThe Commissioner and her Team very much welcome correspondence from the public and use this to aid our understanding of the