nt for the Vale of Glamorgan\n\nMinister for AI and Online Safety\n\n\n\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19c18e1c1372897b","subject":"Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)","name":"Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)","date":"2026-02-01T11:06:12Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19c18e1c1372897b.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19c18bfd989eabaf-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1987-a-dinistr-great-house-farm-llandough-formal-request-for-","scopeTopics":["cadw","senedd"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw","senedd"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19c18bfd989eabaf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"},{"id":"senedd","name":"Senedd"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19c18e1c1372897b.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Aelodau Anrhydeddus y Senedd,\n\nRwy’n ysgrifennu atoch i dynnu eich sylw at yr hyn yr wyf yn ei ystyried yn\nanghyfiawnder hanesyddol difrifol, yn ymwneud â’m teulu, y Bucklers, a\ndinistr Great House Farm yn Llandough — safle fferm a chartref o dros 800\nmlynedd o hanes, gan gynnwys cysylltiadau mynachaidd a chysylltiad\nuniongyrchol â Guglielmo Marconi yn ystod datblygiad cynnar radio.\n\nMae’r mater hwn yn codi cwestiynau difrifol ynghylch hawliau tir,\ngweithdrefnau cyfreithiol, cofrestru tir, a hawliau dynol yng Nghymru.\n\nEr enghraifft, mewn datganiad i’r wasg yn 1974, dywedodd fy nain yn\ngyhoeddus: *“It’s my home.”* Mae’r datganiad hwn, sydd yn fater o gofnod\ncyhoeddus, yn gwrth-ddweud yn uniongyrchol ganfyddiad Llys Apêl 1987 yn *BP\nv Buckler*, lle dywedwyd ei bod wedi bod yn “ddistaw” ac wedi derbyn\ntrwydded BP a gyhoeddwyd yn 1974.\n\nYn yr un achos, gwrthodwyd apêl fy nhad ar y sail bod BP Pension Trust Ltd\na BP Properties Ltd yn “effeithiol yr un cwmni”. Fodd bynnag, yn y\ndyfarniad yr oedd yn ei herio, nododd y barnwr nad oedd ymatebion fy nain i\nBP Pension Trust Ltd yn cyfrif gan mai BP Properties Ltd oedd yr hawlydd,\nac mai cwmnïau ar wahân oeddent. Yn ymarferol, roedd hyn yn arwain at\nsefyllfa “pen y cwmni’n ennill, cynffon y teulu’n colli”.\n\nYn sgil hyn, cafodd fy nhad ei dynnu o’i wely ysbyty, ei garcharu heb\ngyhuddiad, a gosodwyd gorchymyn atal arno i’w atal rhag meddiannu ac\namddiffyn ein fferm 800 oed rhag cael ei dymchwel. Cafodd ei gais i’r Llys\nHawliau Dynol Ewropeaidd ei rwystro cyn iddo farw yn 1991, yn ddim ond 41\noed.\n\nAr y sail hon, rwy’n gofyn yn ffurfiol am *Ddeiseb i sefydlu Ymchwiliad\nCyhoeddus* i’r achos hwn, fel mater o ddwyn tir hanesyddol ac o dorri\nhawliau dynol yng Nghymru.\n\nRwy’n weithiwr proffesiynol ym maes seiber a rhyfela electronig milwrol.\nMae technolegau AI pwerus bellach ar gael i bob un ohonom, ac nid oes\nunrhyw reswm technegol pam na ellid archwilio’r mater hwn yn llawn ac yn\ndrylwyr. Mae’r hyn a ddigwyddodd i’m teulu yn ymddangos fel anghyfiawnder\ndwys, aml-genhedlaethol, ac yn debyg i ffurf ar “lawfare”, lle y trinwyd fy\nnheulu fel llafur di-dâl i gynnal ased tir hyd nes yr oedd yn gyfleus i’w\nariannu. Mae’n arwyddocaol bod bron pob cam yn ein herbyn wedi digwydd ar\nyr eiliad olaf posibl.\n\nCeir honiadau bod sylw sylweddol yn y wasg yn 1974 o blaid fy nain a’n\nteulu, ynghyd â deiseb o tua 1,700 o bobl yn ceisio atal dymchwel y fferm.\nYmhellach, mae’n ymddangos bod CADW wedi methu ag ymyrryd lle dylai’r safle\nfod wedi cael statws Adeilad Rhestredig Gradd II.\n\nNid wyf yn sicr a gofnodwyd erioed yn briodol yn y Gofrestrfa Tir fod y tir\n— a gofrestrwyd gan BP yn 1982 — dan anghydfod. Yn fy nealltwriaeth i,\ncafodd ei drin fel pe na bai mewn anghydfod o gwbl. Nid oes unrhyw lys wedi\npenderfynu’n derfynol mai BP oedd perchnogion cyfreithiol y tir; cafodd\nhynny ei honni yn hytrach na’i brofi.\n\nMae hefyd fater pwysig o hanes diwylliannol. Arhosodd Marconi gyda’n teulu\nyn y fferm wrth iddo ddatblygu radio. Mae cynghorwyr a’r plwyf yn Llandough\nyn gwrthod cydnabod hyn. Rwy’n deall bod Marconi yn cael ei ystyried yn\nwleidyddol eithafol ar y dde, ac, fel y gwelir yn achos y cerflun radio ym\nMae Caerdydd, mae ei rôl hanesyddol yn cael ei hailysgrifennu. Mae’n\nrhesymol tybio bod ein teulu wedi cael ei ddal mewn ymgyrch wleidyddol\nehangach o’r chwith yn erbyn y dde, ac mai am roi llety i Marconi y bu i ni\nwynebu canlyniadau canrif o hyd — problemau nad oedd yn bodoli yn y tair\ncanrif flaenorol yr oeddem wedi byw ar y fferm.\n\nRoedd mam Marconi hefyd yn Jamerson o gwmni wisgi Gwyddelig Jameson. Rwy’n\ngofyn i chi gynnal eich ymchwil eich hun, gwneud eich ymholiadau eich hun,\na dod i’ch casgliadau eich hun — ond yn anad dim, peidiwch â chaniatáu i\nhanes gael ei ailysgrifennu yma.\n\nMae fy nheulu bellach yn archwilio opsiynau ar gyfer siarad cyhoeddus,\nhawliau stori, a dogfennaeth. Yn nhermau cysylltiadau teuluol: fy nhaid\noedd Ray Smith o Dempsey and Makepeace; mae fy modryb yn Shan Cothi; a\ndechreuodd fy ewythr y band Tigertailz.\n\nRwy’n disgrifio’r sefyllfa hon fel gwarthus. Mae fy nheulu’n mynnu\ncyfiawnder am gael ein dadleoli a’n dwyn o’n tir a’n heiddo gan y Sefydliad\nPrydeinig a BP, gyda phrin unrhyw amddiffyniad dan y gyfraith. Rydym yn\ndeulu Cymreig brodorol, Cymraeg eu hiaith, wedi byw yng Nghaerdydd, Bro\nMorgannwg, a’r fferm yn Llandough ers cannoedd o flynyddoedd.\n\nO’r hyn y gallaf ei gasglu, ceir dwsinau o achosion posibl o dwyll a\nchuddio gwybodaeth, sy’n golygu nad yw statud cyfyngiadau yn berthnasol o\nreidrwydd. I’r rhai sy’n cefnogi dad-drefedigaethu Cymru ac annibyniaeth,\nprin y ceir enghraifft gliriach na *BP v Buckler (1987)* o’r hyn a\nddigwyddodd i deulu ffermio Cymreig wrth herio’r Wladwriaeth Brydeinig a\nchorfforaeth fawr. Nid yw eraill wedi codi’r mater hwn, yn bennaf oherwydd\ntrawma cenhedlaethol.\n\nRwyf wedi profi fy hun. Gadewais fy ngyrfa filwrol gydag anrhydedd, gan\ngwblhau fy llw 22 mlynedd. Cefais fy nghyflogi’n bona fide gan Gyngor Bro\nMorgannwg a Llywodraeth Cymru hyd at 2024. Gwasanaethais mewn rhyfeloedd yn\ny Dwyrain Canol. Fodd bynnag, nid yw’r anghyfiawnder fferm yn fater unigol.\n\nYn 2013, cafodd fy mab 36 diwrnod oed ei gipio, ac nid wyf erioed wedi ei\nweld ers hynny. Cafodd tŷ ei ddwyn oddi arnaf (40 Lombard Street, Y Barri).\nYn 2023, cefais fy ngadael i gysgu mewn pabell tra roedd bron i 100 o\nAfghanistaniaid yn cael eu lletya’n dawel wrth ymyl ein pentref o 11 tŷ,\ntra roedd yn rhaid imi aros yno i ofalu am fy nain gan na allai gofalwyr ei\nchyrraedd.\n\nO ganlyniad, rwyf bellach yn byw yn yr hyn a elwir yn Setliad Cymreig yn yr\nAriannin. Rwyf wedi fy nisodli ac wedi fy dadleoli i’r eithaf. Serch hynny,\nrwy’n ddiolchgar fy mod wedi goroesi gyda’m rhyddid, fy mywyd, a’m henw da\nyn gymharol gyfan. Serch hynny, hoffwn fod wedi aros yng Nghymru, fel\nCymro, gyda safon a chynhaliaeth bywyd deg.\n\nMae fy ngwraig a minnau’n amharod i ganiatáu i’n merch hyd yn oed gamu ar\nYnysoedd Prydain o ystyried yr hyn a glywn sy’n digwydd yno. Yn 2024,\nallforiais hyd yn oed fy nghi o Abertawe i’n heiddo yn y Caribî ar ôl i\nunigolyn Afghanistan fod yng ngardd fy nheulu yng Nghymru, gan geisio ei\nddwyn.\n\nGofynnaf i’r Senedd gymryd y mater hwn o ddifrif, ac ystyried sefydlu\nYmchwiliad Cyhoeddus llawn, tryloyw ac annibynnol. Nid er budd fy nheulu yn\nunig y mae hyn, ond er uniondeb hanes, cyfiawnder tir, a hawliau dynol yng\nNghymru.\n\nYn gywir,\n\n*Requester*\n\n*----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*\n\nSirs/Ma'am,\n\nI am writing to you regarding a significant historical injustice involving\nmy family, the Bucklers, and the destruction of Great House Farm (an\n800-year-old site of monastic and Marconi history).\n\nFor example, in a 1974 press statement my grandmother said publically 'It's\nmy home'—that directly contradicts the 1987 Court of Appeal ruling that she\nwas 'silent' and accepted of BP license issued in 1974. My dad's appeal for\nthe BP vs Buckler 1987 case also got dismissed on grounds both BP Pension\nTrust Ltd and BP Properties Ltd were effectively the same company. But in\nthe ruling he was appealing, the judge said that my nans replies to BP\nPensions Trust Ltd didn't count as BP Properties Ltd were the claimant, and\nthe two were seperate companies. So it was heads they win, tails we lose.\nMy dad was ripped from his hospital bed, jailed without charge and slapped\nwith a restraining order to keep him from occupying and defending our 800\nyear old farm from being bulldozed down. His ECHR request blocked before he\ndied in 1991 aged just 41.\n\nI am requesting a *Petition for a Public Inquiry* into this case as a\nmatter of historical land theft and human rights violations in Wales.\n\nI'm a military cyber and electronic warfare professional. We all have very\npowerful AI technology at our disposal which can make light work out of all\nof this. My family suffered an incredible injustice. It also appears to be\nmulti-generational warfare/ lawfare. Whereby we were treated as free labour\nto upkeep the asset of the land and property until it was ripe to be cashed\nin. I say this as every action against us seemed to be last minute.\n\nThere was allegedly press covering the 74 case and supporting my nan and\nfamily and farm. There was a petition of 1700 people trying to defend us\nand the farm from demolishment. CADW looked the other way when it should\nhave been a Grade II listed building. I could go on and on and on.\n\nI'm not even sure the land registry recorded that our land, being\nregistered in 1982 by BP , was in dispute. I believe it was treated as if\nit wasn't dispited. No court actually definitively determined that BP were\nthe landowners. It was just asserted.\n\nMarconi stayed with our family at our farm when inventing radio. The\ncouncillors and parish at Llandough won't even acknowledge this. I\nunderstand Marconi was far right and so, like the radio statute at Cardiff\nBay has confirmed, he is being re-written out of history.  It stands to\nreason that our family was caught in this political campaign of left vs\nright. And for helping Marconi we found ourselves experiencing a century of\nproblems afterwards. Which didn't exist for the 3 centuries we were at our\nfarm before letting far right marconi stay with us. Marconi's mother was\nalso Jamerson of the Irish Whiskey company.\n\nDo your own homework. Make your own enquiries. Draw your own conclusions.\n\n But please do not let history be rewritten here. My family are exploring\noptions for public speaking, story rights, and a documentary etc.\n\nMy grandfather was Ray Smith, of Dempsey and Makepeace. My aunty Shan\nCothi. My uncle started the band tigertailz.\n\nThis is an outrage and my family demands justice for being displaced and\nstolen from, land and property, by the British Establishment/ BP -  with\nlittle to no protections under law. And we're indigenous to the land,\nWelsh, Welsh speaking, Welsh family. Resident in Cardiff / Vale and that\nfarm in Llandough for HUNDREDS OF YEARS.\n\nThere's tens of counts of fraud and concealment from what I can gather.\nWhich means the statute of limitation doesn't apply in this instance. I\nknow some are in favour of Wales decolonising and gaining independence. I\nthink there's no better example of BP vs Buckler 1987 and what has happened\nto my family. Nobody else will bring this up because there's generational\ntrauma. Notwithstanding we, a welsh farming family, are speaking up and\nagainst the British State and BP.\n\nBut I've proven myself. Leaving my military career with honours. Finishing\nmy 22 years Oath, bona fide, employed by the Vale of Glamorgan Council,\nWelsh Government until 2024. I served in the wars in the middle east. I\ndon't know what is going on, on that island. But the farm injustice isn't\nthe only matter. My 36 day old son was abducted in 2013 and I've never seen\nhim since. I had a house stolen (40 Lombard Street, Barry). And in 2023 I\nwas left to sleep in a tent, while almost 100 afghans were secretly housed\nnext to our 11 home village. Where I had to be to care for my grandmother,\nas no carers couldn't reach her. So I'm currently at the Welsh Settlement\nin Argentina. So I'm as displaced and replaced as I can be to cater for the\ninsanity that's going on, on that island. And grateful I've managed to\nsurvive it all with my liberty and life and reputation somewhat still\nintact. But I would have actually liked to have remained in Wales as a\nWelshman. And have some quality and standard of life. My wife and I are\nreluctant for our daughter to even step foot on the British Isles with what\nwe're hearing that's going on there lately. And I even exported my dog from\nSwansea to our place in the Caribbean in 2024 after an afghan was in my\nfamily's garden in Wales, trying to steal him.\n\nI look forward to your reply,\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester"},{"id":"gm-19c18ddabaa11323","subject":"Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)","name":"Cais am Ddeiseb ac Ymchwiliad Cyhoeddus: Achos Buckler v BP (1987) a Dinistr Great House Farm, Llandough / Formal Request for Inquiry: The Great House Farm Dispossession (BP vs Buckler)","date":"2026-02-01T11:01:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19c18ddabaa11323.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19c18bfd989eabaf-cais-am-ddeiseb-ac-ymchwiliad-cyhoeddus-achos-buckler-v-bp-1987-a-dinistr-great-house-farm-llandough-formal-request-for-","scopeTopics":["senedd"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["senedd"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19c18bfd989eabaf","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"senedd","name":"Senedd"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19c18ddabaa11323.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Aelodau Anrhydeddus y Senedd,\n\nRwy’n ysgrifennu atoch i dynnu eich sylw at yr hyn yr wyf yn ei ystyried yn\nanghyfiawnder hanesyddol difrifol, yn ymwneud â’m teulu, y Bucklers, a\ndinistr Great House Farm yn Llandough — safle fferm a chartref o dros 800\nmlynedd o hanes, gan gynnwys cysylltiadau mynachaidd a chysylltiad\nuniongyrchol â Guglielmo Marconi yn ystod datblygiad cynnar radio.\n\nMae’r mater hwn yn codi cwestiynau difrifol ynghylch hawliau tir,\ngweithdrefnau cyfreithiol, cofrestru tir, a haw