 correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19c035a275e5a494.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19c035a275e5a494-new-response-to-your-foi-request-freedom-of-information-request-administrative-records-for-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19c035a275e5a494","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19c035a275e5a494.json","textStatus":"available","text":"You have a new response to the Freedom of Information request 'Freedom of Information Request – Administrative Records for BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1974)' that you made to HM Courts and Tribunals Service.\n\nTo view the response, click on the link below.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/freedom_of_information_request_a_2133?nocache=incoming-3289580#incoming-3289580\n\nWhen you get there, please update the status to say if the response contains any useful information.\n\nAlthough all responses are automatically published, we depend on you, the original requester, to evaluate them.\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhatDoTheyKnow is a project of mySociety run by a small team of staff and\ndedicated volunteers.\n\nmySociety is a charity that believes that information should be accessible to everyone.\nIf this is important to you, please consider donating to help us do more:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/donate\n\nFind out more about how we handle your data at:\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/help/privacy\n\nmySociety is a registered charity in England and Wales (1076346), and a limited\ncompany (03277032)"},{"id":"gm-19c0357a12530057","subject":"For the Attention of Group General Counsel – BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2","name":"For the Attention of Group General Counsel – BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2","date":"2026-01-28T06:43:18Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19c0357a12530057.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19c033a551662faa-for-the-attention-of-group-general-counsel-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1987-ewca-civ-2","scopeTopics":["bp"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["bp"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19c033a551662faa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"bp","name":"BP"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19c0357a12530057.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Group General Counsel,\n\nI am writing in connection with the historical case of BP Properties Ltd v\nBuckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2, involving my late grandmother, Mrs. Buckler, and\nlater my father as parties.\n\nThis is a courtesy notification rather than the initiation of any formal\nproceedings. In reviewing family records and related documents, I have\nuncovered substantial evidence suggesting material inconsistencies in the\nfacts presented during the original 1974 proceedings and the 1987 appeal.\nThese include questions around BP Properties Ltd's title and capacity to\nissue the 1974 unilateral licence at the time it was granted, as the\nunderlying ownership dispute appears to have been adjourned without\nresolution. Additionally, there are indications of procedural\nirregularities, such as the characterization of Mrs. Buckler's responses\n(including her assertion of ownership), inconsistent treatment of corporate\nentities (BP Pension Trust Ltd and BP Properties Ltd), and potential\nunsubstantiated claims regarding public or media involvement that\ninfluenced the case's direction.\n\nThese findings raise concerns under the Limitation Act 1980 s.32 regarding\ndeliberate concealment or fraud, as well as broader issues of procedural\nfairness that could warrant reopening the matter under CPR 52.30 (Taylor v\nLawrence principles). I am in the process of compiling a full evidential\ndossier and consulting on potential next steps, which may include a formal\napplication to the Court of Appeal.\n\nGiven the case's significance in land law precedent and BP's historical\ncontext as a partially state-owned entity at the time, I recognize this\ncould carry reputational implications today. Before pursuing any public\navenues—such as sharing the story via social media, documentary formats, or\nlegal escalation—I believe it is appropriate to extend BP the opportunity\nfor early, private dialogue. I am open to exploring a mutually agreeable\nresolution, potentially including confidential terms, to address the\nperceived historical injustices without further publicity or litigation.\n\nI would appreciate confirmation of receipt and an indication within 14 days\nas to whether BP is prepared to engage in preliminary discussions. This\nwould allow me to determine the most constructive path forward.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester [phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19c0355441d65c0a","subject":"Confirm your FOI request to HM Courts and Tribunals Service","name":"Confirm your FOI request to HM Courts and Tribunals Service","date":"2026-01-28T06:40:45Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19c0355441d65c0a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19c0355441d65c0a-confirm-your-foi-request-to-hm-courts-and-tribunals-service","scopeTopics":["moj"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["moj"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19c0355441d65c0a","direction":"received","from":"(name not shown; whatdotheyknow.com)","institutions":[{"id":"moj","name":"Ministry of Justice / HMCTS"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19c0355441d65c0a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Requester,\n\nYou just tried to sign up to WhatDoTheyKnow, when you already have an account. Your name and password have been left as they previously were. Please click on the link below.\n\nThen your FOI request to HM Courts and Tribunals Service will be sent and published.\n\nhttps://www.whatdotheyknow.com/c/8hvhnz06816ks0fo5rb\n\n-- the WhatDoTheyKnow team"},{"id":"gm-19beaed885848f36","subject":"BP vs Buckler 1987 - FOI Request","name":"BP vs Buckler 1987 - FOI Request","date":"2026-01-23T12:56:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19beaed885848f36.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19beae659165d179-bp-vs-buckler-1987-foi-request","scopeTopics":["cadw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["cadw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19beae659165d179","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"cadw","name":"Welsh Government / Cadw"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19beaed885848f36.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sirs/ Ma'am,\n\nI am writing to make a request under the Freedom of Information Act 2000.\n\nAt your earliest convenience please would you provide me copies of all\ninformation held by Cadw relating to Great House Farm, formerly occupied by\nmy Buckler / Williams family, which was subject to a refusal to list and\nsubsequent demolition in or around the late 1980s.\n\nSpecifically, I request disclosure of the following:\n\n1. All records, assessments, reports, site visit notes, photographs,\ndesk-based evaluations, or recommendations produced by or for Cadw in\nrelation to Great House Farm, including any material connected to decisions\nnot to list the building.\n\n2. All internal correspondence (including letters, memoranda, emails, and\nbriefing notes) held by Cadw that relate to:\nThe heritage significance of Great House Farm\n\n3. The decision not to list the building\nAny consideration of archaeological, historical, or associative significance\nAny communications between Cadw and third parties (including local\nauthorities, developers, landowners, or commercial entities) concerning\nGreat House Farm prior to demolition\n\n4. Records of any archaeological notifications, alerts, or discoveries\nassociated with Great House Farm, whether before or after demolition,\nincluding references to artefacts later recovered during excavations in the\nearly 1990s.\n\n5. Any documentation referring to historical associations between Great\nHouse Farm and early radio or wireless experimentation, including any\nmention of Guglielmo Marconi or related activity in the Cardiff Bay /\nLavernock / surrounding area that may have been considered or dismissed.\n\n6. Policy or guidance documents in force at the time (1980s) that governed\nCadw’s criteria for listing historic farmhouses or buildings with\nassociative historical value.\n\n7. If any information is withheld, please specify the exemption relied upon\nand provide the reasoning as required under the Act.\n\nI would prefer to receive the information electronically, by email.\n\nPlease confirm receipt of this request too.\n\nI understand that under the Freedom of Information Act you're required to\nrespond within 20 working days. It's not that urgent so please take the\ntime you need, within reason, and keep me updated where possible.\n\nAnd if you have any questions, queries or concerns please feel free to\nreach out to me too.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[phone redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[address redacted], [postcode redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19bc5168b3c427e9","subject":"Fwd: FW: BP vs Buckler","name":"Fwd: FW: BP vs Buckler","date":"2026-01-16T04:35:44Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19bc5168b3c427e9.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa-fwd-fw-bp-vs-buckler","scopeTopics":["senedd"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["senedd"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"senedd","name":"Senedd"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19bc5168b3c427e9.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\n\nI have something below you maybe interested in.\n\nI used the latest AI models to unveil consealment and fraud and miscarriage\nof just. Which led my family to be forced off our 800 year old farm in the\nlate 80's.\n\nThis means I can re open this case and sue. And I want to. So does my\nfamily. The latest AI estimate some £40M in damages for my family if what\nI've unveiled can be won in a court of law.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[phone redacted]\n\n\n\n\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP) <[email redacted]>\nDate: Mon, 17 Nov 2025, 06:59\nSubject: FW: BP vs Buckler\nTo: [email redacted] <[email redacted]>\n\n\nDear Soin,\n\n\n\nThank you for your email to Kanishka Narayan MP and for passing on your\nconcerns. [location redacted] unfortunately does not fall within the Vale of\nGlamorgan Parliamentary Constituency and Parliamentary protocol states that\nKanishka is unable to assist anyone outside his constituency.\n\n\n\nI would like to recommend contacting your MP, Stephen Doughty. His contact\ndetails are:\n\n\n\nPhone Number: [phone redacted]\n\nEmail Address: [email redacted]\n\n\n\nI hope they are able to assist you.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nMadelene\n\n\n\n\n*Madelene Larsson Constituency Support Manager, Kanishka Narayan MP*\n\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\nParliamentary Under-Secretary of State in the Department for Science,\nInnovation and Technology\n\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended\nrecipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and\ndelete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is\nnot permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability\nis accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail.\nThis e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used\nfor sensitive data.\n\n\n\n\n\n*From:* Requester <[email redacted]>\n*Sent:* 14 November 2025 12:49\n*To:* NARAYAN, Kanishka (MP) <[email redacted]>\n*Subject:* BP vs Buckler\n\n\n\nSir/Ma'am,\n\nI am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\nassistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nMy family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for generations.\nThe events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of our home and\nland, and left several members of my family deeply affected. Recent\nresearch I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\ninconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\ncorporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\nconsiderations relating to the site.\n\nI have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\nrequesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\nhistorical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\nhistorical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n\nMy interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\nsignificance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\nstayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\nthis should form part of our preserved historical record.\n\nBy way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\nForces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\nsimply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\nwould be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\n\n*Requester*\n[address redacted]\n[map link redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[map link redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\n[map link redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended\nrecipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and\ndelete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is\nnot permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability\nis accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail.\nThis e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used\nfor sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19b4d56cf360e7aa","subject":"Re: Information Request - BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) - Request Reference 00209998","name":"Re: Information Request - BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) - Request Reference 00209998","date":"2025-12-23T22:31:30Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19b4d56cf360e7aa.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19b4bcae026b0a3a-information-request-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1987-request-reference-00209998","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19b4bcae026b0a3a","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19b4d56cf360e7aa.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hi,\n\nThanks.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n\nOn Tue, 23 Dec 2025, 12:19 FOI Unit,   wrote:\n\n> Dear Requester\n>\n> We are writing to introduce ourselves as the Council’s Information\n> Governance Team, who handle requests for information. Your request\n> regarding the above matter has been referred to us by the Council’s Legal\n> Services Department.\n>\n> We note that your request relates to a historic matter from 1987. As such,\n> it may take some time for us to check records and consider any information\n> that may be held. Please be aware that, due to the time that has passed,\n> the Council may no longer hold information relating to this matter. If this\n> is the case, we will do our best to offer advice that may assist you in\n> continuing your enquiries.\n>\n> We will write to you again as soon as possible. In the meantime, if you\n> have any further questions or need clarification, please don’t hesitate to\n> get in touch.\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n>\n>\n> Information Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\n>\n> Director's Office - Resources / Swyddfa’r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\n>\n> Vale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\n>\n> tel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\n>\n> e-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or\n> [email redacted]\n>\n>\n>\n> *Consider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you\n> really need to.*\n>\n> *Ystyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod\n> gwir angen.*\n>\n>\n>\n> Visit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk\n>\n> Ewch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk\n>\n>\n>\n> Find us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook\n>  \n>\n> Follow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter\n>  \n>\n>\n>\n> Correspondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y\n> Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg.\n>\n>\n>"},{"id":"gm-19b4bcae026b0a3a","subject":"Information Request - BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) - Request Reference 00209998","name":"Information Request - BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987) - Request Reference 00209998","date":"2025-12-23T15:19:01Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19b4bcae026b0a3a.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19b4bcae026b0a3a-information-request-bp-properties-ltd-v-buckler-1987-request-reference-00209998","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19b4bcae026b0a3a","direction":"received","from":"FOI Unit","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19b4bcae026b0a3a.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Dear Requester\n\nWe are writing to introduce ourselves as the Council's Information Governance Team, who handle requests for information. Your request regarding the above matter has been referred to us by the Council's Legal Services Department.\n\nWe note that your request relates to a historic matter from 1987. As such, it may take some time for us to check records and consider any information that may be held. Please be aware that, due to the time that has passed, the Council may no longer hold information relating to this matter. If this is the case, we will do our best to offer advice that may assist you in continuing your enquiries.\n\nWe will write to you again as soon as possible. In the meantime, if you have any further questions or need clarification, please don't hesitate to get in touch.\nKind regards\n\nInformation Governance Officer / Swyddog Llywodraethu Gwybodaeth\nDirector's Office - Resources / Swyddfa'r Cyfarwyddwr - Adnoddau\nVale of Glamorgan Council / Cyngor Bro Morgannwg\ntel / ffôn: [phone redacted]\ne-mail / e-bost: [email redacted] or [email redacted]<[email redacted]>\n\nConsider the environment. Please don't print this e-mail unless you really need to.\nYstyriwch yr amgylchedd. Peidiwch ag argraffu'r neges hon oni bai fod gwir angen.\n\nVisit our Website at www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk<http://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/>\nEwch i'n gwefan yn www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk<http://www.bromorgannwg.gov.uk/>\n\nFind us on Facebook / Cewch ddod o hyd i ni ar Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/valeofglamorgancouncil>\nFollow us on Twitter / Dilynwch ni ar Twitter<http://twitter.com/vogcouncil>\n\nCorrespondence is welcomed in Welsh or English / Croesewir Gohebiaeth yn y Gymraeg neu yn Saesneg."},{"id":"gm-19ac0ef3af79f19e","subject":"Re: RC25-0464 - Information related to Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"Re: RC25-0464 - Information related to Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2025-11-26T16:11:32Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ac0ef3af79f19e.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ac0350c6c1fde3-rc25-0464-information-related-to-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ac0350c6c1fde3","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC25-0464"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ac0ef3af79f19e.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Thanks for your prompt and detailed response. Most diligent of you.\nSincerely appreciated. Good drills.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[phone redacted]\n\n\nOn Wed, 26 Nov 2025, 09:48 Dr Adam Coward,  \nwrote:\n\n> Good afternoon,\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you very much for your enquiry. While we cannot advise you on a\n> legal case or undertake a review of historical decisions, pleas note that\n> we do hold information and archives related to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n>\n>\n> The site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments\n> Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n>\n>\n>\n> We hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here:\n> https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can\n> be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales,\n> which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to\n> view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so\n> that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material\n> is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search\n> Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff\n> to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit.\n>\n>\n>\n> While it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order\n> form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of\n> some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would\n> require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many\n> of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be\n> able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research.\n> Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the\n> permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging\n> to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n>\n>\n>\n> In addition to the information and records which we hold, there are\n> several related records in the Historic Environment Record maintained by\n> Heneb, which related to excavations, mostly concerning the cemetery/burial\n> site:\n>\n>    -\n>    https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03584s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n>    -\n>    https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03583s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n>    -\n>    https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03586s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n>    -\n>    https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03585s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n>\n>\n>\n> Thank you very much again for your enquiry.\n>\n>\n>\n> Sincerely,\n>\n>\n>\n> Adam Coward\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> Dr Adam Coward\n>  Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\n> Ffordd Penglais | Penglais Road,  Aberystwyth,  [postcode redacted]\n> [phone redacted] <+44%20(0)%201970%20621%20216>\n> [email redacted]  |  [email redacted]\n> www.cbhc.gov.uk    |  www.rcahmw.gov.uk\n>  \n> Noddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru  |  Sponsored by Welsh Government\n> [image: Facebook]\n>  \n> [image: Twitter]  \n>\n> Rydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\n>\n> We welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n>\n>\n>\n> Yn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i\n> gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis\n> iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a\n> ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y\n> Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn\n> defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\n> ​​​​\n> Under the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the\n> right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the\n> Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To\n> ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive\n> correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information\n> will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all\n> future communication. Thank you.\n> ​\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n>\n> *From:* Requester  \n> *Sent:* 14 November 2025 12:49\n> *To:* [email redacted]\n> *Subject:* BP vs Buckler\n>\n>\n>\n> You don't often get email from [email redacted]. Learn why this\n> is important  \n>\n> Sir/Ma'am,\n>\n> I am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\n> assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\n> Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n>\n> My family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for\n> generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of\n> our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply affected.\n> Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\n> inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\n> corporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\n> considerations relating to the site.\n>\n> I have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\n> requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\n> historical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\n> historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n>\n> My interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\n> significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\n> stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\n> this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n>\n> By way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\n> Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\n> simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\n> would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n>\n> Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n>\n> Yours sincerely,\n>\n>\n> *Requester*\n> [address redacted]\n>  \n> [location redacted]\n>  \n> [postcode redacted]\n>  \n> Tel: [phone redacted]\n>"},{"id":"gm-19ac0350c6c1fde3","subject":"RC25-0464 - Information related to Great House Farm, Llandough","name":"RC25-0464 - Information related to Great House Farm, Llandough","date":"2025-11-26T12:48:03Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ac0350c6c1fde3.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19ac0350c6c1fde3-rc25-0464-information-related-to-great-house-farm-llandough","scopeTopics":["rcahmw"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["rcahmw"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19ac0350c6c1fde3","direction":"received","from":"Dr Adam Coward","institutions":[{"id":"rcahmw","name":"RCAHMW (Royal Commission)"}],"refs":["RC25-0464"],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ac0350c6c1fde3.json","attachments":[{"name":"LES16 Price List 2025.pdf","title":"LES16 Price List 2025.pdf","url":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/pdf/evidence/2025-11-26_rcahmw_les16-price-list-2025.pdf","mime":"application/pdf","bytes":217630,"sha256":"3dbdfc8e1e0b28455f17f9a8afadae11b6f18e8c3c202286e2aee70789a1a1ae"}],"textStatus":"available","text":"Good afternoon,\n\nThank you very much for your enquiry. While we cannot advise you on a legal case or undertake a review of historical decisions, pleas note that we do hold information and archives related to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nThe site entry and description for the site in the National Monuments Record of Wales can be seen online on Coflein, here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182.\n\nWe hold 14 archives related to the site, a list of which can be seen here: https://coflein.gov.uk/en/site/20182/archives?size=25. These archives can be viewed in our Search Room, located in the National Library of Wales, which is open Tuesday through Thursday, 9:30-16:30. If you would like to view the material in person, I would advise arranging with us beforehand so that we can prepare the material ahead of your visit. Some of the material is on microfiche and as we do not have a microfiche reader in the Search Room, we will need to liaise with the National Library Reading Room staff to try to negotiate the use of their machines ahead of your visit.\n\nWhile it is possible to order scans of material using the attached order form, we may be unable to provide research-quality scans or photographs of some of the material, such as the material on microfiche, which would require high-resolution scanning at a cost of £20 per scan. Moreover,  many of these records remain under third-party copyright, and we would only be able to provide scans or copies for personal, non-commercial research. Other uses, such as use in a legal case or report would likely require the permission of the copyright holder(s). I would therefore advise arranging to view the material in person rather than ordering scans, if possible.\n\nIn addition to the information and records which we hold, there are several related records in the Historic Environment Record maintained by Heneb, which related to excavations, mostly concerning the cemetery/burial site:\n\n  *   https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03584s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n  *   https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03583s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n  *   https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03586s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n  *   https://archwilio.org.uk/arch/query/page.php?watprn=GGAT03585s&dbname=ggat&tbname=core\n\nThank you very much again for your enquiry.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAdam Coward\n\n\n\nDr Adam Coward\n Rheolwr Llyfrgell ac Ymholiadau | Library and Enquiries Manager\nFfordd Penglais | Penglais Road, Aberystwyth, [postcode redacted]\n[phone redacted]\n[email redacted] | [email redacted]\nwww.cbhc.gov.uk | www.rcahmw.gov.uk\nNoddir gan Lywodraeth Cymru | Sponsored by Welsh Government\nRydym yn croesawu gohebiaeth yn Gymraeg a Saesneg. Ni fydd gohebu yn Gymraeg yn peri oedi.\nWe welcome correspondence in Welsh and English. Corresponding in Welsh will not lead to any delay.\n\nYn unol â Rheoliadau Safonau'r Gymraeg (Rhif 2) 2016, mae gennych hawl i gyfathrebu a gohebu â Chomisiwn Brenhinol Henebion Cymru yn eich dewis iaith. Er mwyn sicrhau ein bod yn cyflawni’r hawl, rhowch wybod i ni a ydych yn dymuno derbyn gohebiaeth a/neu alwadau ffôn oddi wrthym yn y Gymraeg. Bydd yr wybodaeth hon yn cael ei chofnodi gennym ni, a byddwn yn defnyddio'r iaith o’ch dewis ym mhob cyfathrebu yn y dyfodol. Diolch.\nUnder the Welsh Language Standards (No. 2) Regulations 2016, you have the right to communicate and correspond with the Royal Commission on the Ancient and Historical Monuments of Wales in your preferred language. To ensure we uphold this right, please let us know whether you wish to receive correspondence and/or telephone calls from us in Welsh. This information will be recorded by us, and we will use your preferred language in all future communication. Thank you.\n​\nFrom: Requester <[email redacted]>\nSent: 14 November 2025 12:49\nTo: [email redacted]\nSubject: BP vs Buckler\n\nYou don't often get email from [email redacted]<[email redacted]>. Learn why this is important<https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification>\n\nSir/Ma'am,\n\nI am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your assistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler (1987), relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nMy family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for generations. The events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of our home and land, and left several members of my family deeply affected. Recent research I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural inconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding corporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage considerations relating to the site.\n\nI have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am requesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies-legal, historical, or governmental-who may be able to independently review the historical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n\nMy interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage significance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi stayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe this should form part of our preserved historical record.\n\nBy way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed Forces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is simply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I would be grateful for your guidance on the correct avenues to pursue.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nRequester\n[address redacted]\n[location redacted]\n[postcode redacted]\nTel: [phone redacted]"},{"id":"gm-19ab140a8f4f1727","subject":"Re: BP vs Buckler","name":"Re: BP vs Buckler","date":"2025-11-23T15:06:34Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19ab140a8f4f1727.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa-bp-vs-buckler","scopeTopics":["vale-foi"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["vale-foi"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"vale-foi","name":"Vale of Glamorgan Council"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19ab140a8f4f1727.json","textStatus":"available","text":"George,\n\nSee attached.\n\nRegards,\n\nRequester\n[phone redacted]\n\n\n\nOn Fri, 14 Nov 2025 at 15:24, Carroll, George D (Cllr)\n  wrote:\n>\n> Hi Requester\n>\n> Thank you for copying me in on this.\n>\n> If you'd like to discuss, please let me know.\n>\n> All the best,\n>\n> George\n> ________________________________\n> From: Requester  \