s I can.\n\nConstituency Casework\n\nIf you need my help with a personal case, please make sure your email includes:\n✔ Your full name\n✔ Your full address (including postcode)\n✔ A contact method (email or phone)\n✔ Details of your case (including any relevant reference numbers)\n\nA member of my casework team will be in touch as soon as possible.\n\nAm I Your MP?\n\nDue to parliamentary protocol, I can only take up casework for people living in the Vale of Glamorgan. If you’re unsure whether I’m your MP, you can check by entering your postcode here: findyourmp.parliament.uk<http://findyourmp.parliament.uk/>.\n\nGetting in Touch\n\nThe best way to contact me is by email. My office is open Monday to Friday, 9 AM to 5 PM, and we’ll do our best to respond as soon as we can.\n\nYou can also keep up with my work here:\n📌 Facebook: [KanishkafortheVale]\n📌 Instagram: [@valekanishka]\n📌 X (Twitter): [@KanishkaNarayan]\n\nEmergency Contacts\n\nIf you need urgent assistance, here are some useful contacts:\n📞 NHS Wales (Non-Emergency Medical Advice): 111\n🚨 Emergency Services (Police, Fire, Ambulance): 999\n🏥 Mental Health Support (Samaritans Cymru): [phone redacted]\n🏠 Homelessness Support (Shelter Cymru): [phone redacted]\n👮 South Wales Police (Non-Emergency): 101\n\nThanks again for getting in touch—I really appreciate hearing from people across our community. My team and I look forward to assisting you.\n\nBest wishes,\nKanishka\n\n\nKanishka Narayan MP\nMember of Parliament for the Vale of Glamorgan\nParliamentary Private Secretary to the Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs\n\n\n\n\n\nUK Parliament Disclaimer: this e-mail is confidential to the intended recipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender and delete it from your system. Any unauthorised use, disclosure, or copying is not permitted. This e-mail has been checked for viruses, but no liability is accepted for any damage caused by any virus transmitted by this e-mail. This e-mail address is not secure, is not encrypted and should not be used for sensitive data."},{"id":"gm-19a8269a3f41e059","subject":"Automatic reply: BP vs Buckler","name":"Automatic reply: BP vs Buckler","date":"2025-11-14T12:49:07Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19a8269a3f41e059.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19a8269a3f41e059-automatic-reply-bp-vs-buckler","scopeTopics":["phso"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["phso"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19a8269a3f41e059","direction":"received","from":"++Content","institutions":[{"id":"phso","name":"Parliamentary and Health Service Ombudsman"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19a8269a3f41e059.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Hello\n\nThank you for your message. This is an automatic reply to let you know we have received your email.\n\nWe aim to get back to you within two working days.\n\nIf you are contacting us about a new or active complaint, please resend your email to [email redacted].\n\nIf you are contacting us about an issue with the online complaint form, please resend your email to [email redacted].\n\nKind regards\nContent team"},{"id":"gm-19a826918b90ec23","subject":"BP vs Buckler","name":"BP vs Buckler","date":"2025-11-14T12:48:36Z","dateStatus":"email-date-from-original-message","category":"Case correspondence (original email, redacted)","evidenceVersion":"1.0.0","source":"Wayback case-mail API: redacted copy of the original email","sourceUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/mail/gm-19a826918b90ec23.txt","threadSlug":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa-bp-vs-buckler","scopeTopics":["mp-vale"],"recordType":"correspondence","tags":["mp-vale"],"sourcePath":null,"classificationNote":"Ingested from the family's Gmail (verified case correspondence); email addresses, phone numbers and private addresses redacted.","threadId":"gt-19a8249da6b74faa","direction":"sent","from":"Requester","institutions":[{"id":"mp-vale","name":"Member of Parliament (Vale of Glamorgan)"}],"refs":[],"jsonUrl":"https://wayback.bucklerfamily.estate/api/message/gm-19a826918b90ec23.json","textStatus":"available","text":"Sir/Ma'am,\n\nI am your constituent, living [location redacted]. I am writing to request your\nassistance in reviewing a historic legal matter involving my family: *BP\nProperties Ltd v Buckler (1987)*, relating to Great House Farm, Llandough.\n\nMy family lived on, cared for and claimed to own that farm for generations.\nThe events surrounding the 1987 case resulted in the loss of our home and\nland, and left several members of my family deeply affected. Recent\nresearch I have undertaken has revealed significant procedural\ninconsistencies, historical irregularities, unanswered questions regarding\ncorporate identity, unverified service of key documents, and heritage\nconsiderations relating to the site.\n\nI have attached a short report summarising SOME of these issues. I am\nrequesting your help in identifying the appropriate bodies—legal,\nhistorical, or governmental—who may be able to independently review the\nhistorical record to ensure fairness, accuracy, and transparency.\n\nMy interest is not solely personal; Great House Farm has a heritage\nsignificance to Wales, including documented accounts that Guglielmo Marconi\nstayed there while experimenting with early radio technology. I believe\nthis should form part of our preserved historical record.\n\nBy way of background, I am a veteran and have served both in the Armed\nForces and recently with the Vale of Glamorgan Council. My intention is\nsimply to seek clarity, proper review, and justice where appropriate. I\nwould be 